window.BOOKS_DATA = {"seriesTitle":"The Harry Potter Chronicles","seriesSubtitle":"An Alternate Universe Saga","generatedAt":"2026-11-10T08:16:55.1681422Z","books":[{"id":"book-1","title":"Book 1: The Boy Who Was Loved","subtitle":"From Privet Drive to the Grand Alliance","badge":"Complete","sourceFile":"Harry Potter Fan Fiction - Book 1.docx","lastModified":"2026-11-10T08:16:46.2337178Z","fileSize":2823509,"wordCount":163228,"chapterCount":154,"chapters":[{"num":1,"origNum":1,"title":"The Boy Who Was Loved","wordCount":3578,"paragraphs":["\u003cstrong\u003eNumber Four, Privet Drive\u003c/strong\u003e","The crisp morning air of November had settled over Privet Drive, a street dedicated to uniformity and respectable mediocrity. But inside Number Four, something decidedly un-mediocre was happening: breakfast was a symphony of warmth, the clatter of cutlery, and soft laughter.","Petunia Dursley, with her horse-like face softened by maternal contentment, slid a plate piled high with fluffy pancakes across the polished oak table. \u0026quot;Eat up, Harry dear,\u0026quot; she encouraged, a gentle smile creasing her lips. \u0026quot;You have a big day ahead of you with your school play practice.\u0026quot;","Eleven-year-old Harry Potter, small for his age but with a cheerful, slightly mischievous glint in his bright green eyes, beamed. His perpetually messy black hair seemed to defy gravity, a feature Petunia had long ago stopped trying to tame. He was wearing an impossibly soft, hand-knitted sweater, courtesy of Aunt Petunia\u0027s relentless needlework.","\u0026quot;Thanks, Aunt Petunia!\u0026quot; Harry dug in, thoroughly enjoying the maple syrup-drenched stack.","Across from him, Dudley Dursley—a large, blonde boy who was, despite his size, surprisingly agile—was meticulously buttering a piece of toast. Dudley looked less like the spoiled bully of another timeline and more like a boisterous but good-natured older cousin.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t forget, Harry,\u0026quot; Dudley mumbled through a mouthful of toast, \u0026quot;after practice, we\u0027re building that new LEGO castle, right?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Absolutely,\u0026quot; Harry confirmed, his mouth full. \u0026quot;The instruction book is about a mile long, we\u0027ll need all day.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley, a man whose neck was still practically non-existent but whose temper was notably less volatile, cleared his throat from behind the morning newspaper. \u0026quot;See here, Harry,\u0026quot; he said, folding the paper to reveal a glowing headline about local business expansion. \u0026quot;I’m proud of you, son. Keep working hard in school. Dudley, you make sure he gets to the practice on time, understand?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, Dad,\u0026quot; Dudley replied dutifully.","\u003cstrong\u003eA Confluence of Worlds\u003c/strong\u003e","The story of how Harry came to be loved rather than reviled was simple: Petunia Evans had never truly severed ties with her sister, Lily. When the news of the Potters\u0027 tragedy reached them via an unusually dressed man and a huge, whiskered giant, the grief was overwhelming, but the lingering familial bond was stronger. Petunia had wept not for the strangeness of the circumstance, but for the loss of her only sister and the sudden, heartbreaking responsibility of a nephew.","She had taken the little boy into her arms, and Vernon, seeing his wife\u0027s genuine sorrow and determination, had swallowed his discomfort with the \u0027unnatural\u0027 and stood by her. Harry, a quiet, wide-eyed baby, was simply a child who needed a home. The Dursleys, in their own peculiar, conventional way, had grown to love him as their own.","They were still intensely \u003cem\u003enormal\u003c/em\u003e. They hated anything that stood out, any hint of eccentricity. They hadn\u0027t told Harry about his parents\u0027 true fate, preferring to tell him that his mother and father had been killed in a tragic, but very mundane, car accident. They focused on nurturing a secure, stable, and completely magic-free environment.","Harry was happy. He excelled in school, loved building models with Dudley, and cherished the warm, protective bubble the Dursleys had created for him.","However, sometimes, strange things happened.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Small Incidents\u003c/strong\u003e","One summer afternoon, when Dudley\u0027s favourite balloon had drifted over the tall garden hedge, Harry had simply wished it back, and it had popped right back into Dudley\u0027s hand, deflated but safe. Both boys had stared at it, then at each other, and Dudley had simply shrugged it off as a lucky gust of wind.","Another time, when Petunia had accidentally shrunk Harry\u0027s new trousers in the wash, they had mysteriously stretched back to the perfect size the moment he tried them on again. Petunia had praised the quality of the tailoring, and Harry had quietly kept his secret.","These strange occurrences were rare, easy to dismiss, and never mentioned. The Dursleys, after all, had created a life of comforting denial.","But on this crisp November morning, a new, undeniable irregularity was about to puncture their carefully constructed reality.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Owl Post\u003c/strong\u003e","As Harry finished his last pancake, a sudden, sharp tapping sounded at the kitchen window. It wasn\u0027t the sound of a branch or a bird; it was a deliberate, insistent rap.","Vernon Dursley lowered his newspaper with a frown of annoyance. \u0026quot;What in the blazes is that?\u0026quot;","Perched on the window ledge, looking utterly unimpressed by the neat lawn below, was a large, tawny owl. In its beak, it clutched an envelope made of heavy, creamy parchment, sealed with a crest Petunia instantly recognized and felt a cold wave of dread wash over her.","Harry, fascinated, hopped off his chair. \u0026quot;Aunt Petunia, look! It’s a real owl!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t open the window, Harry,\u0026quot; Petunia said sharply, her voice thin. She walked over quickly, pulling the curtains shut as if the sheer sight of the bird was enough to contaminate their home.","The owl simply hooted once, dropped the letter onto the exterior window sill with an audible \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e, and soared away.","Vernon, who had followed his wife, peered out the edge of the curtains, his face pale. \u0026quot;It\u0027s one of \u003cem\u003ethose\u003c/em\u003e letters, Petunia. I told you, this was bound to happen.\u0026quot;","Harry looked confusedly between his aunt and uncle. \u0026quot;What letter? Is it a petition for the neighbourhood watch?\u0026quot;","Petunia took a deep, shaky breath, fighting down the memories of a brilliant red flash and a small, laughing baby. She couldn\u0027t shield him forever. She turned, forcing a small, reassuring smile for Harry\u0027s benefit, though her hand trembled as she reached for the cold, thick envelope resting on the sill.","She handed it to Harry. The address, written in elegant, emerald-green ink, read:","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eMr. H. Potter\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eThe Smallest Bedroom\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003e4, Privet Drive\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eLittle Whinging, Surrey\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Vernon mumbled, folding his arms across his massive chest, his protective instincts overriding his deep-seated fear of the strange. \u0026quot;Go on, boy. Open it. Let\u0027s see what all the fuss is about.\u0026quot;","Harry\u0027s fingers, usually steady when assembling intricate LEGO pieces, fumbled slightly as he broke the heavy wax seal. The parchment felt cool and important beneath his touch. Dudley and Vernon leaned forward eagerly, their curiosity momentarily overcoming their aversion to the unexplained. Petunia, however, retreated slightly, her eyes fixed on the letter as if expecting it to explode.","Harry slid out the inner letter, unfolding it to reveal a page covered in the same elegant script. He began to read aloud, his voice a mixture of nervousness and awe:","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eHOGWARTS SCHOOL OF WITCHCRAFT AND WIZARDRY\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eHeadmaster: Albus Dumbledore (Order of Merlin, First Class, Grand Sorc., Chief Warlock, Supreme Mugwump, International Confed. of Wizards)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eDear Mr. Potter,\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eWe are pleased to inform you that you have been accepted at Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry. Please find enclosed a list of all necessary books and equipment.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eTerm begins on 1 September. We await your owl by no later than 31 July.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eYours sincerely,\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eMinerva McGonagall, Deputy Headmistress\u003c/strong\u003e","A profound silence descended upon the kitchen. Dudley was the first to break it.","\u0026quot;Witchcraft and... Wizardry?\u0026quot; he echoed, his voice rising in disbelief. He looked at the letter, then at Harry, then at his parents. \u0026quot;Is this a joke? Did Piers set this up?\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley\u0027s face had gone from pale to a dangerous shade of puce. His non-existent neck seemed to swell. \u0026quot;This is \u003cem\u003erubbish\u003c/em\u003e!\u0026quot; he roared, slamming his huge hand onto the table. \u0026quot;A school of... of \u003cem\u003emagic\u003c/em\u003e? Utter nonsense! We told you, Petunia—car crash, utterly normal car crash! There is no such thing as magic!\u0026quot;","Petunia, though visibly shaken, surprised them all by remaining calm. She looked directly at Vernon, her eyes filled with a deep, resolute sorrow.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; she said, her voice quiet but firm, \u0026quot;you know that\u0027s not true. You saw the evidence on our doorstep. You saw the \u003cem\u003eflash\u003c/em\u003e in the papers. And you remember... Lily.\u0026quot; Her voice caught on her sister\u0027s name.","Harry looked back and forth between them, his heart pounding a frantic rhythm against his ribs. \u0026quot;Aunt Petunia? What are you talking about? Magic? My mum and dad—wasn\u0027t it a car crash?\u0026quot;","Petunia walked slowly over to Harry, gently taking the heavy parchment from his hand. She held it for a moment, tracing the ornate crest with a trembling finger.","\u0026quot;No, Harry,\u0026quot; she whispered, meeting his bright green eyes, eyes so much like his mother\u0027s. \u0026quot;It wasn\u0027t a car crash. They were... they were extraordinary people. They were witches and wizards. And you, my dear boy, you are too.\u0026quot;","She looked at the acceptance letter, her face a complicated tapestry of grief, regret, and fierce, protective love. \u0026quot;And it seems,\u0026quot; she finished, holding the letter up to him, \u0026quot;that they want you to go home.\u0026quot;","Harry stared at his aunt, the word \u0027extraordinary\u0027 echoing in the sudden, weighty silence. It wasn\u0027t the mention of magic that shocked him as much as the quiet dismantling of his foundational life story. Car crash. Safe, mundane, car crash. A lie, carefully maintained for ten years.","Dudley, still leaning forward, looked less disbelieving and more utterly bewildered. \u0026quot;Mum? Dad? You knew about this? Why didn\u0027t you ever say anything?\u0026quot;","Vernon, having partially recovered from his outburst, sighed heavily and ran a hand over his slick hair. The anger had drained away, replaced by a deep, weary acceptance of the inevitable. He looked at Petunia, who merely nodded, a silent command passing between them.","\u0026quot;We wanted to protect you, Harry,\u0026quot; Vernon said, his voice now surprisingly gentle. He looked at the boy he had, against all his natural instincts, come to think of as a son. \u0026quot;We wanted you to be \u003cem\u003enormal\u003c/em\u003e. Safe.\u0026quot;","Petunia sat down, pulling Harry close, the crisp parchment of the Hogwarts letter caught between them. \u0026quot;Your mother, Lily... she was a kind and brilliant woman. When she and your father, James, were killed, it wasn\u0027t a car crash, Harry. They were killed by a terrible, dark wizard. A man who wanted power above all else. They died protecting you.\u0026quot;","She paused, taking a visible breath to steady her voice. \u0026quot;And somehow, Harry, you survived him. That man, that dark wizard, he vanished the night he attacked your family. You were brought to us with a warning—that you might still be in danger.\u0026quot;","Harry absorbed the words, his mind racing. A wizard? Dark magic? Protection? It was impossible, and yet, the letter felt real, the owl was real, and his Aunt Petunia’s grief was absolutely real. He looked up at her, his bright green eyes wide. \u0026quot;So... the strange things... like the balloon, and my trousers...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Magic, dear,\u0026quot; Petunia confirmed with a faint, sorrowful smile. \u0026quot;It was always going to happen. You have her gift.\u0026quot;","The clock on the mantelpiece chimed noon, marking a sudden, dramatic shift in the Dursleys\u0027 household reality. The conversation had drifted into quiet explanations—Petunia revealing small, bittersweet memories of Lily\u0027s childhood sparks of magic, and Vernon admitting he\u0027d always feared this day. Harry was quiet, holding the list of necessary equipment, a mixture of excitement and profound confusion churning in his stomach.","Suddenly, the front door rattled violently, almost leaping off its hinges. A sound like a small, localised earthquake reverberated through the house, followed by a series of booming, impatient knocks.","\u0026quot;Good heavens!\u0026quot; Vernon exclaimed, jumping up from his chair. \u0026quot;Who in blazes is that? The Jehovah\u0027s Witnesses couldn\u0027t make that much noise!\u0026quot;","Petunia paled, recognizing the signature lack of subtlety. \u0026quot;It\u0027s him, Vernon. I recognize the thud.\u0026quot;","Before Vernon could even reach the door, it flew inward with a magnificent crash, splintering against the wall.","Filling the doorway, almost completely blocking the light, stood a man of colossal proportions. He was easily twice the height of Vernon and three times his width, a towering figure with a wild tangle of black hair and beard that obscured most of his face. He wore a coat that seemed to be made of various animal pelts and held a massive, flower-patterned umbrella in one hand.","He sniffed loudly, his eyes scanning the incredibly tidy living room before settling on Harry.","\u0026quot;Ah, there yeh are, Harry!\u0026quot; the giant rumbled, his voice like grinding stones. He stepped over the ruined door, completely oblivious to the chaos he had caused. \u0026quot;Knew I\u0027d find yeh eventually. Name\u0027s Rubeus Hagrid, Keeper of Keys and Grounds at Hogwarts, o\u0027 course.\u0026quot;","Hagrid paused, taking in the scene: the polished oak table, the remaining stack of pancakes, the hand-knitted sweater Harry wore, and the trio of Dursleys sitting unusually close to the boy.","\u0026quot;Yeh look like a healthy lad,\u0026quot; Hagrid continued, scratching his enormous beard. His gaze lingered on Harry\u0027s comfortable surroundings, then settled on Petunia. \u0026quot;And yeh must be Petunia, Lily\u0027s sister. Dumbledore said yeh were the only family he had left, but I didn\u0027t expect much... usually Muggles don\u0027t treat our kind too well.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley, though terrified, managed to puff out his chest slightly. \u0026quot;We are his family, sir! And we treat him perfectly well!\u0026quot;","Hagrid squinted. He looked at Harry, who was clinging to Petunia\u0027s side, then at the intact state of Harry’s nose, the bright, cheerful quality of his clothes, and the absence of any obvious signs of neglect. He compared this image to the one Dumbledore had sketched: a sad, possibly malnourished orphan being grudgingly sheltered.","Hagrid looked back at the Dursleys, a deeply confused expression crossing his face. \u0026quot;Well, I\u0027ll be boiled in treacle. Yeh... yeh actually look like yeh care for him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Of course, we care for him!\u0026quot; Petunia said hotly, rising to face the giant. \u0026quot;He is my sister\u0027s son! He is \u003cem\u003eour\u003c/em\u003e nephew! We gave him a home and a family, something no one else was going to do in your ridiculous world, and we love him dearly!\u0026quot;","Vernon stepped forward, positioning himself squarely in front of Petunia. \u0026quot;Now see here, Hagrid or whatever your name is! You\u0027ve just confirmed everything we feared! This is exactly why we didn\u0027t want him involved with that... that freakishness! We have raised him to be a good, well-adjusted boy, and now you burst in here and tell him his whole life is a lie!\u0026quot;","Harry, thoroughly overwhelmed, tugged on Petunia\u0027s hand. \u0026quot;Aunt Petunia, Uncle Vernon—\u0026quot;","Hagrid’s face softened considerably as he looked at the family unit. He saw genuine, albeit fiercely conventional, affection. He took a hesitant step back, running a hand through his hair. \u0026quot;I... I beg yer pardon. I was sent to fetch Harry and explain things, see. Dumbledore thought yeh hadn\u0027t told him anything.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We just did,\u0026quot; Petunia snapped, pointing a trembling finger at the Hogwarts letter on the table. \u0026quot;Five minutes before you arrived and ruined our front door.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Hagrid said, deflating slightly. He looked at the shattered door with a sheepish expression. \u0026quot;Right. Well. Good then. Less for me ter do.\u0026quot; He looked at Harry. \u0026quot;So yeh know about yer mum and dad then? James and Lily?\u0026quot;","Harry nodded slowly. \u0026quot;They were killed by a dark wizard. They were protecting me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That\u0027s right, Harry,\u0026quot; Hagrid confirmed, his voice regaining its warmth and volume. \u0026quot;And that dark wizard—Lord Voldemort—he vanished that night. And you, little Harry, you\u0027re famous! You\u0027re the reason he\u0027s gone! You\u0027re the Boy Who Lived!\u0026quot;","Hagrid paused, taking in the blank looks from the Dursleys and the awestruck expression on Harry\u0027s face. He pulled a slightly squashed cake out of an inner pocket of his coat.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Hagrid said, handing the cake to Harry. \u0026quot;Happy Birthday, Harry. And now that yer ready, we\u0027d better get to London. We\u0027ve got a lot of shopping ter do before term starts.\u0026quot;","The departure from Number Four, Privet Drive, was less of an exit and more of an evacuation, thanks to the massive figure of Rubeus Hagrid. Vernon Dursley, after a brief, furious argument about property damage and the impossibility of attending a \u0026quot;school for freaks,\u0026quot; had been subdued by Petunia\u0027s fierce determination.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s going,\u0026quot; she\u0027d stated simply, her voice brooking no argument. \u0026quot;He needs to know his own world, Vernon. But he is \u003cem\u003enot\u003c/em\u003e going alone.\u0026quot;","Thus, the entire Dursley family—Vernon, Petunia, and Dudley—found themselves squeezed into Vernon’s company car, following Hagrid, who rode a colossal, purring motor-cycle down the M25, attracting stares and near-accidents all the way to London.","\u003cstrong\u003eDiagon Alley: A Family Trip\u003c/strong\u003e","Hagrid led them to a grimy, ordinary-looking pub called the Leaky Cauldron. Stepping inside felt like crossing a threshold. The pub was dark, low-ceilinged, and filled with extraordinary people—witches in pointed hats, wizards discussing cauldrons, and even a tiny, shivering man nursing a pint who looked suspiciously like he was wearing a bat for a waistcoat.","The Dursleys, true to form, looked profoundly uncomfortable. Vernon kept his eyes fixed firmly on the floor, Petunia held Harry’s hand tightly, and even Dudley, despite his natural boisterousness, kept silent, his eyes darting nervously around the room.","Hagrid ushered them quickly through the pub and out into a small, rubbish-filled courtyard. He pulled out his massive pink umbrella, tapped a sequence of bricks in the wall, and the world shimmered. The bricks dissolved, revealing an ancient, cobbled street curving out of sight, lined with shops selling everything from quills to broomsticks.","Harry gasped, completely overwhelmed by the vibrant, magical energy of Diagon Alley. Dudley finally found his voice.","\u0026quot;Bloody hell,\u0026quot; he whispered, his eyes wide with genuine awe.","\u0026quot;Welcome, Harry,\u0026quot; Hagrid rumbled proudly. \u0026quot;To Diagon Alley.\u0026quot;","Petunia leaned down to Harry, her grip still tight. \u0026quot;Stay close, dear. And don’t touch anything.\u0026quot; Vernon, meanwhile, looked ill, trying desperately to reconcile this incredible, bewildering street with his conventional worldview.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Visit to Gringotts\u003c/strong\u003e","Their first stop was a towering, snow-white marble building that overshadowed everything else: Gringotts Wizarding Bank.","\u0026quot;Gringotts,\u0026quot; Hagrid explained, leading them up the silver steps. \u0026quot;Run by goblins, the cleverest folk outside of Hogwarts. Best keep yer voices down.\u0026quot;","Inside, the spectacle was even more unnerving. Short, stern-faced goblins in the cashier’s cage eyed them suspiciously. Vernon, ever the man of business, tried to assert control.","\u0026quot;Now, see here, Hagrid,\u0026quot; Vernon huffed, smoothing his jacket. \u0026quot;As Harry’s guardian, I need to open a temporary account for his schooling, or perhaps set up a direct debit. I’ll be paying for his things, of course. Full tuition, books, the lot.\u0026quot;","Hagrid paused, a look of surprise washing over his heavily-bearded face. \u0026quot;Oh, well, that’s... decent of yeh, Vernon, but there’s no need for that. Harry’s parents saw to it. James and Lily weren’t poor, yer know.\u0026quot;","He pulled a rather crumpled, official-looking key from his pocket. \u0026quot;They left a good bit of gold for Harry. Enough to get him through school and then some.\u0026quot;","Vernon and Petunia exchanged a look—a blend of surprise and deep, complex relief.","\u0026quot;Right then,\u0026quot; Vernon muttered, slightly deflated but clearly appreciative of the unexpected financial relief. \u0026quot;Lead the way, then.\u0026quot;","They followed a stern-looking goblin named Griphook deep into the earth, riding a terrifyingly fast, rickety cart through a labyrinth of twisting, underground tunnels. Dudley screamed once, mistaking a stalactite for a monster.","When they finally arrived at vault number 687, Griphook opened the heavy door. Harry looked inside and stopped breathing. Piled high in glittering heaps were gold Galleons, silver Sickles, and bronze Knuts. The vault was practically overflowing.","Dudley whistled. \u0026quot;Wow. That’s a \u003cem\u003elot\u003c/em\u003e of money, Harry.\u0026quot;","Vernon, who lived and breathed fiscal solvency, stared, dumbstruck by the sheer, magnificent amount of wealth. Petunia, however, saw beyond the gold. She saw the foresight and love of her sister and brother-in-law.","Harry tentatively picked up a handful of coins, the cold gold feeling heavy and real.","Petunia stepped forward, resting a hand on Harry’s shoulder. She looked directly at the gold, then back at her nephew.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; she said, her voice clear and earnest, cutting through the cavernous silence of the vault. \u0026quot;This is yours. Every single piece of it. Your mother and father wanted you to have it, and you will use it for your school, for your books, for whatever you need to succeed in their world.\u0026quot;","She paused, then added firmly, \u0026quot;But I want you to understand one thing, Harry. While you are home, while you are under our roof—and you always will be—you will not spend a single dime of this. We feed you, we clothe you, and we love you. That is our responsibility. Your money is for your future. Ours is for your present. Do you understand?\u0026quot;","Harry’s bright green eyes, which had been fixed on the gold, now looked up at his aunt, suddenly wet with unshed tears. He understood. It wasn\u0027t just about money; it was about unconditional care.","Hagrid, who had been leaning against the vault entrance, shifted his massive frame. His shaggy beard couldn’t hide the genuine emotion that crossed his face. He sniffed loudly, pulling a spotted handkerchief from his pocket and dabbing at his eyes.","\u0026quot;By the dusty bones o’ my grandfather,\u0026quot; Hagrid rumbled, his voice thick. \u0026quot;I... I haven’t seen a family stand by a young wizard like that in fifty years. Petunia, Vernon... that’s a fine thing you’re doin’.\u0026quot;","Vernon merely nodded gruffly, trying to conceal the redness creeping up his neck. \u0026quot;Well, he’s family, isn’t he? Now come on, Petunia. Let’s get out of this underground rat-run. Harry, get whatever you need.\u0026quot;","Harry, heart full and the burden of his independence suddenly lifted by their protective declaration, gathered a small pouch of gold. He smiled at his family, a genuine, luminous smile.","\u0026quot;Thanks, Aunt Petunia,\u0026quot; he whispered. \u0026quot;Thanks, Uncle Vernon.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":2,"origNum":2,"title":"A Trunk Full of Wonders","wordCount":1732,"paragraphs":["The return journey from the depths of Gringotts was much more cheerful, fueled by the glittering prospect of the day ahead. Hagrid, now thoroughly convinced of the Dursleys\u0027 genuine, if unconventional, affection for Harry, treated them with a gruff respect, even apologizing \u003cem\u003eagain\u003c/em\u003e for the door. Vernon, in turn, relaxed slightly, the financial burden of Harry’s schooling unexpectedly lifted.","\u0026quot;Right then, first things first,\u0026quot; Hagrid announced, leading them back up the marble steps and out into the bustling alley. \u0026quot;We need yer uniform, Harry. Robes, of course. Don’t want ter show up lookin’ like a Muggle.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eMadam Malkin’s Robes for All Occasions\u003c/strong\u003e","They stopped before a shop with a sign reading \u0027Madam Malkin\u0027s Robes for All Occasions\u0027. Inside, it was bright and busy. A plump, smiling woman in mauve robes met them at the door.","\u0026quot;Hogwarts, dear?\u0026quot; she asked Harry, her eyes twinkling. \u0026quot;Got another young man being fitted up right now.\u0026quot;","Harry was ushered toward the back of the shop where a pale, pointed-faced boy with sleek, white-blond hair was standing on a footstool while a second witch pinned up his long, black robes.","\u0026quot;Hello,\u0026quot; the boy said, eyeing Harry with cool, slightly bored curiosity.","\u0026quot;Hello,\u0026quot; Harry replied, climbing onto the neighboring stool.","The pale boy launched into conversation without preamble, his tone precise and superior. \u0026quot;Hogwarts too? My father’s next door buying my books and Mother’s up the street looking at wands. Then I’m dragging them off to look at racing brooms. I don’t see why first-years can’t have their own. I think I shall bully Father into getting me one and smuggling it in somehow.\u0026quot;","Harry, whose idea of extreme fun was flying his kite on the local hill, merely nodded politely. He looked over toward the Dursleys, who were clustered near the entrance, clearly trying to blend into the wallpaper. Petunia’s mouth was a tight line; Vernon looked ready to explode with pent-up conventional outrage. Dudley, for once, seemed too engrossed by a display of glittery, amethyst-colored robes to pay much attention to the snobbish boy.","\u0026quot;Have you got your own house-elf yet?\u0026quot; the blond boy continued, apparently mistaking Harry’s silence for rapt attention. \u0026quot;I hear some of the older families still use them. And what are your parents like? Are they \u003cem\u003eour\u003c/em\u003e kind?\u0026quot;","Harry paused, a flicker of irritation rising. The boy spoke as if there were only two kinds of people, and he was obviously the better one.","\u0026quot;My parents are dead,\u0026quot; Harry stated simply, his voice quiet.","The boy’s face didn’t soften, but he shifted slightly. \u0026quot;Oh, sorry,\u0026quot; he said, but it sounded distinctly insincere. \u0026quot;I mean, are they witches and wizards? Because you wouldn’t want to mix with the wrong sort. I think the Ministry should be much stricter about who they let in. What house are you hoping to be in? I know I’ll be in Slytherin. All the best wizards are.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don’t know yet,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;I’m still learning about all of this.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well, you’ll find out soon enough. Anyway, I think I’ll go and find Father. See you at Hogwarts, I suppose.\u0026quot;","He stepped off the stool and sauntered out. Madam Malkin finished Harry’s hem, and he quickly paid with his new Galleons.","\u0026quot;Well, \u003cem\u003ethat\u003c/em\u003e was an unpleasant little piece of work,\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley muttered under his breath as Harry rejoined them. \u0026quot;Sticking his nose up at everyone. Typical snob.\u0026quot;","Petunia gave a fierce, protective squeeze to Harry’s arm. \u0026quot;Don’t you pay any attention to people like that, Harry. He has terrible manners. And he’s probably only half your size without all that hair gel.\u0026quot;","Harry smiled, feeling a rush of warmth. In their own loud, judgmental way, the Dursleys were firmly on his side.","\u003cstrong\u003eA Feathered Friend\u003c/strong\u003e","With the uniform sorted, Hagrid insisted they make a stop. \u0026quot;Now, Harry, yer birthday was only yesterday, and I never got yer a proper present. Dumbledore gave me some gold to get yer somethin’ nice.\u0026quot;","He led them to Eeylops Owl Emporium, a dark shop smelling of straw and wet feathers, filled with soft rustles and glowing yellow eyes.","\u0026quot;An owl?\u0026quot; Harry whispered, eyes wide with delight.","Hagrid beamed. \u0026quot;Every wizard needs an owl! Great for sending letters, good company, clever as anything.\u0026quot;","Petunia looked at the various owls with a mixture of fascinated distaste. \u0026quot;An owl, Vernon. In the house.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Better than a bat,\u0026quot; Vernon grumbled, but he was staring at a magnificent Snowy Owl with undeniable awe.","Hagrid pointed to the Snowy Owl. \u0026quot;There’s a beautiful one, Harry. A proper hunter, too. Just the thing.\u0026quot;","Harry was about to agree when Vernon Dursley cleared his throat, adjusting his tie.","\u0026quot;See here, Hagrid,\u0026quot; Vernon said, his voice surprisingly firm. \u0026quot;You may have been sent here by the Headmaster of your… institution, but Harry is \u003cem\u003eour\u003c/em\u003e nephew. We’ve been meaning to get him a proper, substantial birthday gift, and frankly, a bit of pocket money isn\u0027t cutting it.\u0026quot; He looked at Petunia, who nodded sharply in agreement. \u0026quot;We’ll pitch in. Half of that one, Petunia, what d’you say?\u0026quot;","Petunia smiled, a rare, genuine curve of her lips. \u0026quot;More than half, Vernon. The delivery of a living creature, and one that is meant to be a companion, is a joint family responsibility.\u0026quot;","Harry looked from Hagrid to the Dursleys, feeling his throat tighten again. He knew they’d already bought him a magnificent, state-of-the-art telescope for his birthday, currently hidden in the cupboard under the stairs. This was more than a gift; it was a gesture of deep, visible acceptance of his new life.","\u0026quot;Well, I’ll be,\u0026quot; Hagrid muttered, looking deeply pleased. He accepted Vernon’s offer of a thick roll of Muggle cash (which Vernon insisted on exchanging for wizard gold at a nearby currency exchange).","Harry walked out of the shop carrying a large cage containing the spectacular Snowy Owl. She had luminous amber eyes and a quiet, dignified presence.","\u0026quot;I’ll call her Hedwig,\u0026quot; Harry announced, clutching the cage handle tightly.","\u003cstrong\u003eOllivanders: Makers of Fine Wands Since 382 B.C.\u003c/strong\u003e","The last, and most important, stop was Ollivanders. The shop was narrow, shabby, and utterly silent. Inside, the air was dust-filled and the silence felt ancient, broken only by the tinkling bell above the door.","An old man with wide, pale eyes that seemed to glow in the gloom appeared instantly. \u0026quot;Good afternoon,\u0026quot; he said. \u0026quot;Ah, yes. Harry Potter. It seems only yesterday your mother was in here, buying her first wand. Eleven inches, swishy, made of willow, nice for charm work.\u0026quot; He paused, his pale eyes flickering to Petunia. \u0026quot;And you, Petunia, you were so jealous. You always refused to step foot in here until now.\u0026quot;","Petunia visibly recoiled, her hand gripping Vernon’s jacket. Vernon, for his part, looked profoundly spooked by the old man’s unnerving memory.","\u0026quot;And your father, James,\u0026quot; Ollivander continued, ignoring the Dursleys. \u0026quot;Eleven inches, mahogany, excellent for transfiguration. A touch more power than the willow.\u0026quot;","He turned his attention entirely to Harry, his eyes fixed on the faint, lightning-bolt scar hidden under Harry’s fringe. \u0026quot;I wonder,\u0026quot; he murmured, stepping back and pulling a long measuring tape from his pocket. \u0026quot;Which is the right one for you? Let’s see.\u0026quot;","The ensuing half hour was a chaotic, frustrating mess of rejected wands. Harry tried wands of holly, oak, fir, and beech. The shop grew hotter, the air thicker. One wand made all the boxes on the shelf explode. Another caused the floorboards to creak ominously. Vernon Dursley, leaning against the counter, began to look visibly worried. Dudley was bored, and Petunia was pale with strain.","\u0026quot;Oh, dear,\u0026quot; Ollivander muttered, snatching back a wand of cedar. \u0026quot;No, no, no. Definitely not.\u0026quot;","He disappeared into the back and returned with a single box. \u0026quot;I wonder,\u0026quot; he whispered, his voice low and excited. \u0026quot;Holly, eleven inches, nice and supple, and containing a single phoenix feather.\u0026quot;","Harry took the wand. The moment his fingers closed around the smooth wood, a powerful, sudden warmth flooded his body, starting at his fingertips and spreading throughout his limbs. A shower of brilliant, golden sparks erupted from the tip of the wand, illuminating the dusty, silent shop.","Harry felt a rush of pure, exhilarating power. It felt \u003cem\u003eright\u003c/em\u003e.","The Dursleys, who had braced themselves for another disaster, stared.","Dudley’s jaw dropped. \u0026quot;Whoa.\u0026quot;","Vernon, who had never believed in magic, or rather, had always forcefully denied it, took a staggering step back. He saw the golden light, the unmistakable, beautiful energy, and the look of sheer relief and belonging on Harry’s face. His fear and denial finally fractured, replaced by a stunned, heavy recognition.","Petunia, however, reacted with a deep, silent sob. She watched the golden light dance around Harry—her nephew, her sister’s son—and saw Lily, brilliant and powerful, standing there instead. The guilt of all the years of forced denial, the quiet grief for the extraordinary life her sister had lived, and the fierce joy that Harry was finally finding his own path, all combined. She covered her mouth with her hand, tears silently streaming down her face.","Ollivander, oblivious to the family drama, beamed. \u0026quot;Curious! Very curious!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What’s curious?\u0026quot; Harry asked, still basking in the warmth of the magic.","\u0026quot;I remember every wand I’ve ever sold, Mr. Potter. The phoenix whose tail feather resides in your wand gave another feather. Only one other. It is curious that you should be destined for this wand, when its brother gave the feather for the wand that gave you that scar.\u0026quot;","Harry stared. \u0026quot;Who owned that wand?\u0026quot;","Ollivander’s voice dropped to a dramatic whisper. \u0026quot;The dark wizard who shall not be named.\u0026quot;","The name hung in the air, a shadow momentarily obscuring the golden light. Petunia took Harry’s hand, her own trembling.","\u0026quot;Thank you,\u0026quot; Harry said quickly, handing over the required gold. He gripped the box containing his wand, feeling the immense weight of destiny and the lightness of new possibility. He looked at his family—Vernon, now merely stunned; Dudley, awestruck; and Petunia, openly weeping but smiling through her tears.","The magic was real. The danger was real. But so was the love surrounding him.","The trip back to Number Four, Privet Drive, was quieter than the journey out, Hedwig perched regally in her cage, the only sound the faint rustle of her feathers. The Dursleys had seen a glimpse of Harry’s terrifying, wonderful new life, and they knew, with absolute certainty, that they could never turn their backs on it."]},{"num":3,"origNum":3,"title":"The Last Night at Number Four","wordCount":1014,"paragraphs":["The days following the trip to Diagon Alley settled into a strange, anticipatory rhythm at Number Four, Privet Drive. The Dursleys’ home, once a bastion of extreme normalcy, now housed a silent, spectacular Snowy Owl named Hedwig, a trunk full of mysterious robes and books, and an eleven-inch wand of holly and phoenix feather.","Harry spent most of his time reading his schoolbooks—\u003cem\u003eA History of Magic\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem\u003eMagical Drafts and Potions\u003c/em\u003e, and, most thrillingly, \u003cem\u003eQuidditch Through the Ages\u003c/em\u003e. The Dursleys, having accepted the unavoidable reality of Harry’s magical life, kept a respectful distance from his possessions, occasionally peering over his shoulder at the drawings of magical creatures in \u003cem\u003eFantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them\u003c/em\u003e.","One evening, Petunia found Harry staring intently at the last piece of parchment Hagrid had left him: his train ticket.","\u0026quot;What is it, dear?\u0026quot; she asked, sitting beside him on the sofa.","Harry held out the stiff, red ticket.HOGWARTS EXPRESS","Platform Nine and Three-Quarters","King\u0027s Cross Station","Term begins 1 September","\u0026quot;It\u0027s the ticket,\u0026quot; Harry said, frowning. \u0026quot;But I don\u0027t understand how I\u0027m supposed to get there. Hagrid just handed it to me.\u0026quot;","Petunia took the ticket, her lips moving silently as she read the unusual destination. \u0026quot;Platform Nine and Three-Quarters? Harry, there\u0027s no such platform at King\u0027s Cross. Vernon and I used to go through King\u0027s Cross often on our way to the coast—the platforms are numbered sequentially, up to eleven, I think. There\u0027s definitely no nine and three-quarters.\u0026quot;","Vernon, who had been ostentatiously polishing his car in the drive but was listening intently through the open window, came inside, wiping his hands on a rag. He took the ticket from Petunia, his brow furrowed in concentration.","\u0026quot;This is ridiculous!\u0026quot; he scoffed, though his voice lacked its usual bombast. \u0026quot;Do they expect the boy to sprout wings and fly there? No mention of a time, a specific carriage, or even how one finds a fraction of a platform!\u0026quot;","He paced the living room, the polished floor creaking under his weight. He stopped, looking at Harry\u0027s hopeful, slightly anxious face.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon declared, throwing the ticket onto the table. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t you worry about it for a minute, Harry. We\u0027ll take you. We\u0027ll all go. King\u0027s Cross is a major station; they must have some kind of special area, or perhaps Hagrid simply gave you a cryptic address to protect the secret.\u0026quot;","He straightened his waistcoat, his characteristic determination returning. \u0026quot;We will drive you to King\u0027s Cross on the first of September, locate Platform Nine, and then we will ask, clearly and firmly, where this... \u0027Platform Nine and Three-Quarters\u0027 is. We will not let you miss your train, understand? We will figure it out.\u0026quot;","Petunia gave Vernon a look of deep gratitude. Harry smiled, a heavy weight lifting from his chest. The comfort of having his family handle the logistics of the unexplainable was profound.","The Last Evening","August dissolved into the last day of the month. Harry\u0027s trunk, now packed with his robes, books, and cauldron, sat heavily in the hallway, looking completely out of place. Hedwig was asleep in her cage on the dining table, having been given strict instructions not to wake Vernon before 6 a.m.","Dinner was a quiet affair. Petunia had baked Harry\u0027s favourite treacle tart, a tradition she reserved for special occasions. Dudley, usually a whirlwind of noise and appetite, was unusually subdued.","After dessert, Petunia called Harry into the living room, where a meticulously wrapped, rectangular parcel sat on the coffee table.","\u0026quot;It\u0027s from us, Harry,\u0026quot; she said softly, gesturing for him to open it.","It was a book, bound in soft, worn leather. Harry opened it tentatively. It wasn\u0027t a school book, or a book of Muggle history, but a photo album. The first page contained a photograph, preserved perfectly, of a woman with bright green eyes and brilliant red hair laughing as she held a tiny, messy-haired baby aloft. Lily.","Harry traced the image with his finger. Petunia had spent the last week gathering every single photograph she had of her sister and her family, photographs she hadn\u0027t dared look at for ten years. There were pictures of Lily and James at their wedding, Lily and Petunia as girls on a beach holiday, and several blurry, wonderful photos of James playing with baby Harry.","\u0026quot;Your mother... she was never one for keeping secrets from the camera,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, tears welling in her eyes. \u0026quot;She sent these to me, before... before the end. We thought you ought to have them.\u0026quot;","Harry couldn\u0027t speak. He clutched the album to his chest, the weight of his parents\u0027 lost lives feeling suddenly tangible and warm.","Vernon cleared his throat gruffly from the doorway. \u0026quot;Right, well, don\u0027t want the boy staying up all night on his last evening, Petunia.\u0026quot; He walked into the room, holding a brightly coloured packet. \u0026quot;This is from Dudley. He bought it himself.\u0026quot;","It was a large bag of mixed sweets, the kind Harry loved but was usually only allowed in moderation.","Dudley shuffled his feet, refusing to meet Harry\u0027s gaze. \u0026quot;Just... you might need them for the train,\u0026quot; he mumbled, his face red. He then walked over and, in a supremely uncharacteristic move, gave Harry a quick, clumsy hug. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t get into trouble, Harry. Write us a letter, alright?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will, Dudley,\u0026quot; Harry promised, hugging the sweets and the photo album tightly. \u0026quot;And thank you.\u0026quot;","As Harry went upstairs to his room, he paused on the landing, looking back down. Vernon Dursley had his arm around Petunia\u0027s shoulder, and Petunia was leaning into him, quietly crying, the weight of the next day finally pressing down on them. They looked smaller, older, and fiercely, undeniably his family.","Harry retreated to his bed, placing the photo album under his pillow and Hedwig\u0027s cage beside the window. He was leaving. He was going to learn magic. But he was not leaving his home; he was merely going to school. He smiled into the darkness, ready for the adventure, secure in the knowledge that he had a loving, if loudly unconventional, family waiting for his return."]},{"num":4,"origNum":4,"title":"Platform Nine and Three-Quarters","wordCount":2706,"paragraphs":["The first of September dawned crisp and cool, a perfect day for a journey. The Dursley household was a controlled chaos of last-minute checks. Vernon Dursley, despite his continued grumbling about the impracticality of the whole affair, had meticulously planned the route to King\u0027s Cross. Petunia, pale but resolute, hovered anxiously, ensuring Harry had everything he needed.","By eight o’clock, Harry’s heavy trunk was loaded into the boot of Vernon’s car, Hedwig’s cage (covered with a thick blanket to keep her quiet and the public unaware) sat on the back seat, and the Dursleys, including a surprisingly eager Dudley, were on their way.","They arrived at the vast, sooty expanse of King\u0027s Cross Station well before the clock struck ten-thirty. The station was a confusing tangle of rushing commuters, ringing phones, and loud announcements.","Vernon Dursley, ever the man of efficiency, quickly located Platforms Nine and Ten. He glared at the gap between them, a solid brick wall supporting a steel arch.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; he announced, puffing out his chest. \u0026quot;Platform Nine and Ten. No Nine and Three-Quarters. Just as I suspected, this entire operation is run by nincompoops.\u0026quot;","Petunia looked worriedly at the blank brick wall. \u0026quot;Vernon, you can’t think the letter was wrong. Hagrid said…\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hagrid is a giant who destroys front doors, Petunia! We’ll ask a guard,\u0026quot; Vernon said, marching determinedly toward a man in a black uniform.","The guard, a tired-looking man with a large moustache, merely stared when Vernon bellowed, \u0026quot;Excuse me, where is Platform Nine and Three-Quarters?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Nine and three-quarters?\u0026quot; the guard repeated blankly, scratching his head. \u0026quot;Are you having a laugh, mate? Nine is there, Ten is there. No in-betweens.\u0026quot;","Vernon returned to his family, his face a furious red. Harry felt a knot of panic tighten in his stomach. He was going to miss his train.","Just as Harry’s anxiety reached its peak, Dudley nudged his uncle and pointed.","\u0026quot;Dad, look,\u0026quot; Dudley whispered, his eyes wide.","Approaching the barrier between Platforms Nine and Ten was a strange, bustling cluster of people. There was a plump woman with flaming red hair and a kind face, a tall, thin man with glasses, and five children, all with varying shades of the same bright red hair. They were pushing luggage trolleys piled high with trunks—trunks exactly like Harry’s. And, most tellingly, perched atop the trunks, were cages containing several owls.","The Dursleys watched, transfixed, as the older boys began to talk to the red-headed woman.","\u0026quot;Right, Percy, you go first,\u0026quot; the woman said.","A gangly boy with a prefect badge on his chest took a running start toward the solid brick barrier and, with a sudden, silent shimmer, \u003cem\u003evanished\u003c/em\u003e.","Vernon Dursley’s jaw dropped so far it nearly hit his waistcoat. Petunia gasped, clutching Harry’s arm so tightly it hurt.","\u0026quot;Merlin’s beard,\u0026quot; Hagrid had muttered that phrase a lot, and it seemed appropriate now.","Vernon recovered quickly, his businessman’s instinct for securing information overriding his conventional shock.","\u0026quot;Follow them,\u0026quot; he commanded in a low, urgent voice. \u0026quot;Petunia, Dudley, you take the luggage. Harry, stick with me.\u0026quot;","Vernon pushed his trolley, loaded with Harry’s trunk and Hedwig’s cage, toward the little group, which was now down to the plump woman, a girl, and two identical-looking boys.","\u0026quot;Excuse me!\u0026quot; Vernon said loudly, adjusting his tie and offering his most commanding smile. \u0026quot;Vernon Dursley. Pleased to make your acquaintance. I couldn’t help but notice… well, the trunks, you see. And the owls.\u0026quot;","The woman, who Harry recognized as kind, looked surprised. \u0026quot;Oh, hello. I’m Molly Weasley. Yes, we’re heading to Hogwarts. Are you… are you a Muggle?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am, yes,\u0026quot; Vernon admitted gruffly. \u0026quot;And this is my wife, Petunia, and our son, Dudley. And this,\u0026quot; he placed a hand firmly on Harry’s shoulder, \u0026quot;is our nephew, Harry. He’s going to Hogwarts for the first time, and we, ah, we appear to have misplaced the platform.\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley’s kind face broke into a broad, genuine smile. \u0026quot;Oh, dear, a first-timer! Bless him. It’s tricky if you don’t know. King’s Cross is a nightmare. Welcome, Harry. And thank you for bringing him, Mr. Dursley. It’s lovely to see a Muggle family so supportive.\u0026quot;","Vernon, who had expected either confusion or condemnation, puffed up with pride at the compliment. \u0026quot;Well, he’s family, Mrs. Weasley. We look after our own. So, this… vanishing trick?\u0026quot;","Molly chuckled. \u0026quot;It’s no trick, dear. It’s magic. You simply walk straight at the barrier between Platforms Nine and Ten. Don’t stop, and don’t be afraid of hitting the wall. It sounds like madness, but it works.\u0026quot;","Vernon stared at the wall. He looked back at Harry, then at his wife, then at Dudley. The protective resolve he’d found in Diagon Alley hardened.","\u0026quot;Right. Dudley, come here.\u0026quot; Vernon pushed the trolley a few feet away from the Weasleys. \u0026quot;We’ll go first. Make sure it’s safe for your cousin.\u0026quot;","Dudley, still wide-eyed with awe at the prospect of walking through a wall, nodded bravely.","\u0026quot;Ready, son?\u0026quot; Vernon whispered, gripping the trolley handle.","\u0026quot;Ready, Dad.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley, pillar of conventionality, took a deep breath, fixed his eyes on the spot where the prefect had vanished, and, with a powerful shove of the trolley, he and Dudley charged straight at the solid brick barrier.","\u003cem\u003eFwoomp.\u003c/em\u003e","They were gone.","Petunia gasped, a mixture of fear and profound relief washing over her.","\u0026quot;See?\u0026quot; Molly Weasley said gently. \u0026quot;Nothing to it.\u0026quot;","Petunia turned to Harry, her hand smoothing down his messy hair. Her eyes, so often narrowed in disapproval, were shining with pride and a fierce, sorrowful love.","\u0026quot;Go on, Harry,\u0026quot; she whispered, kissing his forehead. \u0026quot;You go. You find your uncle and cousin. Have a wonderful time. And remember—you write to us \u003cem\u003eevery\u003c/em\u003e week. Do you hear me?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will, Aunt Petunia,\u0026quot; Harry promised, his voice thick with emotion.","He seized the handle of his own trunk trolley. Petunia stepped up beside him, placing her hand gently over his on the handle.","\u0026quot;We’ll go together, dear,\u0026quot; she said, her voice firm. \u0026quot;Just like family.\u0026quot;","They began to walk. The noise of the station faded behind them. The brick wall rushed closer, yet Harry felt no sense of dread, only an exhilarating sense of rightness, of coming home.","At the very last moment, just as impact seemed certain, the solid brick wall shimmered. The trolley struck it, and instead of a sickening crash, a huge, curving wrought-iron archway, bearing the sign \u003cem\u003ePlatform Nine and Three-Quarters\u003c/em\u003e, appeared before them.","Harry stepped onto a smoky, crowded platform, the air filled with the smell of coal smoke and excited chatter. Towering over them, bright scarlet and steaming, was the Hogwarts Express.","Vernon and Dudley were standing a few feet away, both looking slightly ruffled but profoundly impressed. Vernon’s face, though still pale, was lit with a triumphant smile.","\u0026quot;Told you we’d figure it out, boy!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, adjusting his jacket.","Petunia looked around the platform, taking in the hundreds of excited students, the magnificent train, and the sheer, intoxicating chaos of the magical world. She looked at Harry, his face glowing with happiness and excitement, and squeezed his hand one last time.","\u0026quot;Go on, Harry,\u0026quot; she said softly. \u0026quot;Find a compartment. This is where your journey begins.\u0026quot;","Vernon quickly reclaimed the luggage trolley, his expression a mixture of pride and anxiety. \u0026quot;Right, now that we\u0027ve managed to navigate this… this farce of an entry system, let\u0027s find the boy a seat. Weasley told me the train leaves in ten minutes.\u0026quot;","The platform was dense with people, trunks, and owls. Vernon Dursley, however, was not about to be defeated by a few hundred wizards. He seized Harry’s trunk and, with a powerful, protective grunt, muscled a path down the crowded corridor toward the back of the train carriages.","Dudley, still buzzing from the shock of walking through a solid wall, proved surprisingly useful. Being large and blonde, he spotted an empty compartment near the back of the train first.","\u0026quot;Here, Harry! This one’s empty!\u0026quot; Dudley called, opening the door.","Vernon hoisted the heavy trunk onto the luggage rack with a final, exasperated grunt of effort. Petunia settled Hedwig’s covered cage gently onto the seat.","The four of them stood crammed in the small compartment, the sudden silence heavy with all the unsaid emotions of the past few weeks.","\u0026quot;Right then,\u0026quot; Vernon said, clearing his throat loudly and avoiding eye contact. He meticulously adjusted the collar of Harry’s new, slightly too-large school robes. \u0026quot;Well, you have your trunk. You have your owl. You have your ticket. Don’t, ah, don’t talk to strangers. And if anyone tries to put a hex on you,\u0026quot; he lowered his voice to a conspiratorial whisper, \u0026quot;tell them your uncle is a successful Drill Executive and will be having words with their Headmaster.\u0026quot;","The ludicrousness of the threat made Harry smile, even as the true sting of separation hit him.","Petunia stepped forward, her face working hard to maintain composure. She pulled Harry into a tight, fierce embrace.","\u0026quot;You be careful, Harry,\u0026quot; she whispered into his ear, her voice tight with unshed tears. \u0026quot;Don’t forget us. Don’t forget who loves you. If that school isn’t good enough, you come straight home. You call for us. We will come.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I hear you, Aunt Petunia,\u0026quot; Harry whispered back, hugging her just as fiercely.","She pulled back, wiping a tear from her cheek with a sharp movement. Dudley, who had been watching the scene with unusual seriousness, stepped up. He wasn\u0027t one for speeches, but he was good at direct action. He simply gripped Harry\u0027s shoulder, squeezed it hard, and nodded once.","\u0026quot;Write,\u0026quot; Dudley commanded, his voice gruff.","\u0026quot;I will,\u0026quot; Harry promised.","Vernon placed a heavy hand on Harry\u0027s other shoulder, his expression a complicated mix of pride and anxiety. \u0026quot;You remember what we taught you, Harry. Manners, diligence, and keep your elbows off the table. Now, go on. Go and be... extraordinary. We love you, son.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I love you too!\u0026quot; Harry called out, a lump rising in his throat as his family hurried out of the compartment and onto the platform.","He watched through the window as they stood together—Vernon, massive and protective; Petunia, elegant and tearful; and Dudley, towering over them, waving frantically. The train whistle blew a long, mournful blast.","The train gave a great, shuddering lurch, and slowly began to move. The Dursleys grew smaller and smaller, their bright, conventional clothes slowly fading into the distance.","Harry sank back into his seat, a profound, comfortable sense of belonging settling over him, even as he was carried further away. He was alone now, but not abandoned.A New Companion","The train rattled on, pulling out of the station and into the green, unfamiliar countryside. Harry watched the neat fields and distant hills rush by. He settled back, pulling the photo album the Dursleys had given him from his school bag, and gazing at the image of his mother and father, feeling their presence alongside the recent warmth of his aunt, uncle, and cousin.","A little while later, just as the train rounded a bend, the compartment door slid open, and a boy with bright red hair, long nose, and freckles stood there. He looked nervous and slightly embarrassed.","\u0026quot;Excuse me,\u0026quot; the boy mumbled, gesturing down the corridor. \u0026quot;Is anyone sitting here? Everywhere else is full.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, come in,\u0026quot; Harry said, quickly tucking his photo album away.","The boy slid into the seat opposite Harry. He had an awkward, gangly build, and his school robes, though new, looked a bit too short for him.","\u0026quot;I’m Ron,\u0026quot; the boy said. \u0026quot;Ron Weasley.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Harry Potter,\u0026quot; Harry replied, offering his hand.","Ron stared, his freckled face going suddenly white. He looked from Harry\u0027s messy black hair to his hand, then back to Harry\u0027s forehead, which he was obviously trying to peek under the fringe.","\u0026quot;So—so it’s really you?\u0026quot; Ron stammered.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry confirmed, a little embarrassed by the intensity of the stare.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Ron breathed, leaning back and pulling out a slightly squashed packet of sandwiches. \u0026quot;I thought Seamus was having me on. You really have got the—you know…\u0026quot; Ron jabbed his finger vaguely at his own forehead.","Harry sighed and pulled back his fringe slightly, revealing the thin, lightning-bolt scar.","Ron stared, awestruck. \u0026quot;Is that where You-Know-Who...?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry said, pulling his fringe back down.","They quickly settled into conversation, the initial strangeness replaced by the comfortable camaraderie of two boys on the cusp of a great adventure. Ron, who was excited and knowledgeable about the magical world, explained Quidditch, the different houses, and his own large family. Harry, in turn, told Ron about his Muggle life, emphasizing the unexpected support the Dursleys had shown him in accepting his magical destiny.","The hours passed quickly. They ate the sandwiches Ron’s mother had packed—a rather unappetizing blend of corned beef—and the sweets Dudley had bought Harry, which included a mountain of Drooble\u0027s Best Blowing Gum and Bertie Bott\u0027s Every Flavor Beans. They attempted (and failed) to change Ron’s rat, Scabbers, into a golden goblet, an endeavor that merely resulted in Scabbers gnawing nervously on a crust of bread.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Know-It-All\u003c/strong\u003e","They were deep into a discussion about the merits of various broomsticks when the compartment door slid open again. Standing there was a girl who was already wearing her new Hogwarts robes. She had a bossy voice, a great deal of bushy brown hair, and large, slightly prominent front teeth.","\u0026quot;Has anyone seen a toad?\u0026quot; she demanded, looking severely at their empty compartment. \u0026quot;Neville’s lost his. He’s quite upset.\u0026quot;","Ron immediately shook his head. Harry shrugged.","The girl’s eyes fell upon the spell Ron had been attempting. She marched over, her nose practically touching the textbook.","\u0026quot;Oh, are you doing magic? Let’s see then.\u0026quot;","Ron, feeling immediately challenged, cleared his throat and pointed his wand at Scabbers again.","\u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eSunshine, daises, butter mellow, turn this stupid, fat rat yellow\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; he muttered.","A quick flash of light later, and Scabbers remained resolutely grey, if slightly more frantic in his chewing.","The girl sighed dramatically and gave them a look of profound disappointment. \u0026quot;Are you sure that’s a real spell? Well, it’s not very good, is it? I’ve tried a few simple ones myself, and they’ve all worked for me. Nobody in my family is magic at all, it was ever such a surprise when I got my letter, but I was so pleased, of course, I’ve learned all the set books by heart, naturally. You two should probably be getting your robes on, we’ll be arriving soon.\u0026quot;","She then turned her attention to Harry. Her large eyes fixed on his scar.","\u0026quot;You’re Harry Potter,\u0026quot; she stated, not asked. \u0026quot;I read all about you in \u003cem\u003eModern Magical History\u003c/em\u003e. And you’re Ron Weasley.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You don’t need to tell us who you are,\u0026quot; Ron muttered darkly, \u0026quot;We know.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You do?\u0026quot; she asked, looking marginally surprised.","\u0026quot;We heard you asking around for the toad,\u0026quot; Ron clarified.","\u0026quot;Oh, right,\u0026quot; the girl said, her cheeks turning a little pink. \u0026quot;Well, I’m Hermione Granger. And if you two would like to try some \u003cem\u003eproper\u003c/em\u003e spells, I’d be happy to show you. You’re going to need to practice, you know, if you’re going to catch up.\u0026quot;","She paused, then added briskly, \u0026quot;Come on, Harry, you’ve got a chip on your glasses.\u0026quot;","She pointed her wand at Harry’s glasses.","\u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eOculus Reparo\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; she commanded, and the tiny chip Harry had acquired on his round spectacles that morning mended with a sudden \u003cem\u003epop\u003c/em\u003e.","She beamed with self-satisfaction. \u0026quot;That’s better. Now, I suggest you both get changed. I’m going to go and check on Neville’s toad again. You really should put your robes on. We’re nearly there.\u0026quot;","With that, Hermione Granger swept out of the compartment, leaving a profound silence in her wake.","Ron stared after her, dumbfounded. \u0026quot;Whatever house I’m in,\u0026quot; he finally declared, stuffing the remaining sweets into his pocket, \u0026quot;I hope she’s not in it. Honestly.\u0026quot;","The last hour of the journey passed in a flurry of activity. Ron and Harry changed into their new Hogwarts robes, the black fabric feeling heavy and distinctly magical. The train slowed, the whistle blew one final, echoing time, and they pulled into a small, dark station shrouded in mist and the gloom of early evening.","Outside the window, a sign proclaimed: \u003cem\u003eHogsmeade\u003c/em\u003e."]},{"num":5,"origNum":5,"title":"The Stone and the Chamber","wordCount":857,"paragraphs":["\u003cstrong\u003eThe Boat Ride Across the Lake\u003c/strong\u003e","The black fleet of enchanted boats glided silently across the mirror-dark surface of the Great Lake, carrying the first-years toward the towering silhouette of Hogwarts Castle. Every window blazed with amber torchlight against the Scottish night. Beside Harry, Ron was craning his neck in awe, while across the gunwale, Hermione Granger was whispering a frantic recitation of Hogwarts: A History under her breath to steady her nerves.","When the Sorting Hat was dropped onto Harry’s head inside the Great Hall, a whisper rippled from the high table to the house benches. The ancient leather brim slipped down over his forehead, and a dry,crackling voice spoke directly into his mind.","\u0026quot;Curious,\u0026quot; the Hat murmured. \u0026quot;Plenty of courage, yes. A sharp mind, and a fierce, unshakeable loyalty to those who love you. You do not hunger for glory to prove yourself, Harry Potter, because you already know who you are. Best be—GRYFFINDOR!\u0026quot;","The scarlet-and-gold table erupted. Joining Hermione and Ron at the bench, Harry felt the first true click of destiny settling into place: three utterly different minds forging a single, inseparable front.","\u003cstrong\u003eLetters from Privet Drive and the Philosopher\u0027s Stone\u003c/strong\u003e","Unlike his classmates, whose parents sent the occasional tin of fudge, Harry received weekly, heavily underlined dispatches from Number Four, Privet Drive. Vernon Dursley treated Hogwarts as an eccentric boarding school requiring rigorous oversight. When Harry made the Gryffindor Quidditch team as the youngest Seeker in a century, Vernon wrote back demanding to know whether the school provided comprehensive personal-injury coverage for aerial sports—before enclosing a clipping on fighter-pilot reflexes and telling Harry to \u0026quot;flatten the competition.\u0026quot;","At Christmas, Hedwig required the assistance of three school owls to drag in the Dursleys\u0027 hamper: a crate of Marks \u0026amp; Spencer shortbread, four tins of Quality Street, a woollen jumper knitted by Petunia in sensible navy blue, and a note from Dudley asking if Harry had fought any \u0026quot;proper monsters\u0026quot; yet.","He nearly got his wish that spring. Alongside Ron and Hermione, Harry uncovered the secret guarded beneath the third-floor corridor—the Philosopher’s Stone. Through Hagrid’s three-headed dog, Devil’s Snare, winged keys, and McGonagall’s giant chessboard, it was Hermione’s cool logic and Ron’s sacrificial bravery that cleared the path for Harry to step into the final chamber alone.","There, facing Professor Quirrell and the parasitic face of Lord Voldemort, Harry discovered the true nature of the shield inside his blood. When Quirrell’s hands blistered and burned to ash against Harry’s skin, it was not merely an ancient echo of Lily Potter’s sacrifice ten years gone; it was a living ward, fed and renewed every single day by the roof Petunia had kept over his head and the family that cherished him. When Harry woke in the Hospital Wing, Dumbledore’s eyes twinkled with quiet wonder at a boy whose heart had zero cracks for the Dark Lord to exploit.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Flying Car and the Dial-Up Detective\u003c/strong\u003e","Their second year tested that resilience in ways none of them anticipated. After a rogue house-elf named Dobby sealed the barrier at Platform Nine and Three-Quarters, Harry and Ron made the spectacularly ill-advised decision to fly Arthur Weasley’s enchanted Ford Anglia to Scotland.","The Howler Ron received from Molly Weasley was deafening, but the registered letter Harry received from Vernon Dursley two days later could have peeled paint off the dungeon walls. Vernon was not angry that a car had flown; he was apoplectic that two twelve-year-olds had stripped the gearbox of a classic British motorcar and driven it into a tree without third-party insurance.","Soon, however, the humor vanished beneath the cold terror of the Chamber of Secrets. When Muggle-born students began turning up petrified and the walls of the castle ran with warnings written in blood, Harry’s sudden ability to speak Parseltongue made him an outcast to half the school.","Over the Christmas holidays, Harry wrote home about the attacks and the whispers of a monster hidden in the plumbing. At Number Four, Dudley took the crisis personally. Spending three afternoons in his school’s newly installed computer room over a screeching dial-up modem, Dudley printed out forty-two pages on mythical serpents, welder’s goggles, and industrial drain-clearing acid, mailing the binder to Hogwarts with a sticky note reading: \u0026quot;Hit it in the eyes, Harry. Everything hates getting poked in the eyes.\u0026quot;","When Hermione herself was petrified in the spring—clutching a torn library page naming the Basilisk—something cold and immovable locked into place inside Harry’s chest. He sat by her motionless hand in the Hospital Wing every evening until he and Ron followed the trail into the depths of the Chamber.","Confronting the preserved memory of Tom Riddle and the sixty-foot King of Serpents, Harry pulled the ruby-hilted Sword of Gryffindor from the Sorting Hat, drove it through the roof of the Basilisk’s mouth, and plunged a venomous fang straight into the heart of Riddle’s diary—saving Ginny Weasley’s life and bringing Hermione back to them. When Hermione threw her arms around his neck in the Great Hall that night, Harry held on a fraction longer than a twelve-year-old friend strictly needed to, neither of them quite ready to let go."]},{"num":6,"origNum":6,"title":"The Prisoner and the Time-Turner","wordCount":3378,"paragraphs":["\u003cstrong\u003eThe Whistle and the Wraiths\u003c/strong\u003e","By the end of their third summer, the shadow of the past had crept directly onto the manicured lawns of Surrey. Sirius Black had escaped from Azkaban, and both the Muggle news and the Ministry of Magic whispered that he was hunting Harry.","Petunia Dursley was beside herself. Knowing what she knew of the night in Godric’s Hollow, the name Black conjured every nightmare of her sister’s murder. Before driving Harry to King’s Cross, Vernon presented him with a heavy-duty anodized aluminium survival torch, while Petunia pinned an ear-splitting orange mountain-rescue whistle inside his cloak pocket, making him swear on his life to blow it if he saw a large black dog.","Yet the true terror of third year proved not to be the fugitive in the shadows, but the guards stationed at the gates: the Dementors of Azkaban. Under the gentle, weary tutelage of Professor Remus Lupin—the quietest of his father’s old friends—Harry spent his winter evenings learning the Patronus Charm. Where other wizards struggled to find a single memory bright enough to hold back the fog of despair, Harry had an entire arsenal: Sunday roasts at Privet Drive, Dudley cheering from the sidelines, Ron’s crooked grin, and the warmth of Hermione’s hand steady on his sleeve.","On a breathless, moonlit night in June, every lie of the past twelve years shattered inside the dusty walls of the Shrieking Shack. Standing between Lupin and a gaunt, half-mad Sirius Black, Harry, Ron, and Hermione watched Ron’s pet rat, Scabbers, twist into the trembling form of Peter Pettigrew—the true traitor who had sold James and Lily to Voldemort and framed Sirius for the crime.","When the full moon rose, Pettigrew slipped into the dark and the Dementors closed in across the lake. It was Harry who conjured a blinding silver stag across the water to drive hundreds of Dementors back—and it was Hermione’s secret Time-Turner, spun three turns backward in the dark, that allowed the two of them to race against the chimes of midnight, rescue Buckbeak from the executioner’s axe, and fly Sirius Black to freedom from the highest tower of the castle.","\u003cstrong\u003eA Chaos of Revelations\u003c/strong\u003e","The cold air of the grounds hit Harry and Hermione, sharp and invigorating, after their frantic, time-bending journey. They stopped just outside the heavy, stone doors leading to the Hospital Wing. The weight of what they had just done—rescuing two innocent lives, defying the Ministry, and bending the very fabric of time—settled heavily between them.","Harry looked at Hermione, her bushy hair slightly askew, her face flushed with adrenaline and triumph. She looked immensely brave and immensely beautiful.","Hermione was looking at him, too. She didn\u0027t have her usual, serious expression; instead, her eyes were shining with a brilliant, wild happiness.","\u0026quot;We did it, Harry,\u0026quot; she whispered, her voice barely audible. \u0026quot;We actually did it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Couldn\u0027t have done it without you, Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry replied, a genuine, powerful surge of emotion making his voice thick. \u0026quot;You\u0027re the most brilliant witch I know.\u0026quot;","Hermione\u0027s face softened, and before Harry could say anything else, she surged forward, wrapping her arms around his neck. It wasn\u0027t a friendly hug; it was an embrace born of shared danger and profound relief. Her lips met his in a firm, confident, and slightly breathless kiss.","Harry, utterly surprised, felt the warmth of the moment flood through him. He instinctively wrapped his arms around her waist, deepening the kiss, a clear realization dawning in his mind: this felt more right than anything else in the whole, unbelievable world.","The moment of perfect bliss was shattered by two immediate, loud, and utterly disparate reactions.","The door to the Hospital Wing opened silently, and \u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore\u003c/strong\u003e swept in from the corridor, wearing a magnificent set of emerald-green robes and an expression of serene, slightly bemused curiosity. He stopped dead, his blue eyes twinkling furiously over his half-moon spectacles as he took in the sight of his two youngest heroes locked in a passionate embrace.","\u0026quot;My word,\u0026quot; Dumbledore murmured, his voice booming slightly in the quiet corridor, though his expression was that of a proud grandfather who had just found a pair of rare, delightful magical beetles. \u0026quot;That\u0027s certainly a more aggressive approach to celebrating a successful Time-Turner operation than I had anticipated. Ten points to Gryffindor for initiative, I think, though perhaps a deduction for public display.\u0026quot;","Simultaneously, inside the hospital wing, \u003cstrong\u003eRon Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e, propped up in his bed recovering from a broken leg (courtesy of Sirius Black\u0027s escape attempt), had a direct view of the doorway. He had been quietly sulking, feeling useless, when the door opened to reveal the scene.","\u0026quot;Oi! Harry! Hermione!\u0026quot; Ron bellowed from his bed, his voice cracking with a mixture of shock and sheer \u003cem\u003eeww\u003c/em\u003e factor. \u0026quot;Blimey! Not on school grounds! Honestly, you two are mental! Get a room! But... also... good job, mate! Told you she was the smart one!\u0026quot;","Harry and Hermione sprang apart as if simultaneously hit by a Bludger, both scarlet-faced.","Dumbledore merely leaned on his walking stick, his eyes gleaming. \u0026quot;Do carry on,\u0026quot; he said pleasantly, gesturing for them to enter. \u0026quot;No need to cease excellent relationship building on my account. Mr. Weasley, I trust your enthusiasm for their... \u003cem\u003eliaison\u003c/em\u003e... means you are recovering well?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well, yeah, Headmaster,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled, looking delighted for his friend but also visibly repulsed. \u0026quot;Just... kissing. It\u0027s just so \u003cem\u003emooshy\u003c/em\u003e. Still, Hermione\u0027s face looked really happy, Harry. It suits her. But seriously, Harry, I can see your tongue! Put it away!\u0026quot;","Hermione promptly hid her face in her hands.","Dumbledore walked into the ward, his robes rustling, and gave Ron a knowing look. \u0026quot;Ah, the chaos of first love, Mr. Weasley. It is often a confusing mixture of triumph, disgust, and overwhelming noise. A truly magnificent magic of its own, is it not?\u0026quot;","He turned back to the flustered pair standing in the doorway, who were now attempting to straighten their robes and avoid eye contact with each other.","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, clapping his hands together briskly. \u0026quot;Before you two begin arguing about whether or not to tell your Aunt Petunia about the time-travel element of your evening, perhaps you should come in. Professor Snape is currently attempting to explain the necessity of adhering to school rules to Professor McGonagall, and I suspect a touch of youthful, chaotic romance is exactly what is needed to lighten the mood.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eReturn to Privet Drive: The Great Revelation\u003c/strong\u003e","The transition from the magical chaos of Hogwarts back to the stifling normalcy of Privet Drive was always jarring, but this summer, it felt different. Harry\u0027s trunk, now containing a massive, sleek Firebolt broomstick (carefully disguised with a blanket and a complex series of silencing charms), was the most extraordinary piece of luggage ever to cross the threshold of Number Four.","Vernon Dursley, having driven a significantly larger, rented van to King’s Cross to accommodate the new cargo, was deeply suspicious.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t tell me that great lump is another magical animal, Harry,\u0026quot; he grumbled, eyeing the covered broom with immense distrust as he wrestled it up the stairs. \u0026quot;We just got used to that blasted owl. The neighbours are already asking about the funny-looking cat with the flattened nose that keeps trying to eat Hedwig.\u0026quot; (Vernon was, of course, referring to Crookshanks, who had tried to hitch a ride in the Firebolt packaging).","Petunia, however, was focused on Harry. He looked tired but radiant, and the constant fear of Sirius Black’s shadow had lifted from her shoulders.","That evening, after a dinner of Petunia’s roast chicken (which Harry immediately realized lacked the distinct taste of house-elf magic), Harry knew he had to tell them. He couldn\u0027t keep the truth about Sirius Black—a truth that completely vindicated Lily and James’s friendship—to himself.","He sat his aunt and uncle down in the living room, Dudley settling in a nearby armchair, unusually attentive.","\u0026quot;Aunt Petunia, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry began, taking a deep breath. \u0026quot;There’s something important you need to know about the man who was supposed to have betrayed my parents. Sirius Black.\u0026quot;","Petunia immediately tensed. \u0026quot;The murderer? Harry, what on earth are you talking about? Has he escaped again?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is innocent,\u0026quot; Harry stated firmly, looking directly at them. \u0026quot;He was framed. The real traitor was Peter Pettigrew, one of my father\u0027s other friends. He was the one who betrayed them to Voldemort, and he framed Sirius, who was wrongly sent to Azkaban.\u0026quot;","A heavy silence descended. Vernon stared, his mouth opening and closing like a fish. Petunia, however, looked stricken, her face paling rapidly.","\u0026quot;Innocent?\u0026quot; she whispered, the word thick with ten years of misplaced grief and resentment. \u0026quot;All this time, we thought... Lily’s friend…\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pettigrew was hiding as a rat for twelve years—Ron’s rat, actually,\u0026quot; Harry explained quickly, trying to distill the monumental truth into simple terms. \u0026quot;Sirius is my godfather. He’s the one who was supposed to be my guardian if anything happened. Hermione and I—we helped him escape the Ministry and the Dementors. He\u0027s safe now, but he\u0027s a fugitive.\u0026quot;","Dudley, who had been following the narrative of a man turning into a rat with rapt attention, whistled. \u0026quot;Blimey. Like a proper detective story, Harry.\u0026quot;","Petunia slowly rose and walked over to the mantelpiece, leaning on it heavily. \u0026quot;James and Lily... they had a friend, a guardian, who didn\u0027t betray them?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s right, Aunt Petunia. Sirius was their best friend. He would never have hurt them. He wanted to take me in that night, but Hagrid had already been sent by Dumbledore.\u0026quot;","The relief that washed over Petunia was tangible, a profound easing of an old, deep sorrow. She turned, her eyes wet but clear. \u0026quot;Your father’s best friend. God. You have a godfather, Harry.\u0026quot;","Vernon, always practical, cleared his throat. \u0026quot;Right. Well, that\u0027s certainly a more satisfactory explanation than \u0027dark wizard.\u0027 So, this Black is still on the run? That means he’ll be wanting to contact you, won\u0027t he?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He already has,\u0026quot; Harry admitted, trying to keep the excitement out of his voice. \u0026quot;He sent me a letter, and... he sent me a gift.\u0026quot;","Harry dashed out to the hall, retrieved the Firebolt, and brought it back, gently unwrapping the blanket.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Firebolt Presentation\u003c/strong\u003e","The polished mahogany gleamed under the living room lights. The magnificent, sleek broomstick, with its finely wrought kick-stand and its whisper-smooth finish, looked like a futuristic racing machine that had somehow materialized in the middle of their conventional room.","Harry carefully held it up for them. \u0026quot;This is the Firebolt. It\u0027s the fastest racing broom in the world. Sirius gave it to me.\u0026quot;","Dudley immediately surged forward, his jaw slack with pure, unadulterated awe. \u0026quot;That\u0027s... that is absolutely brilliant, Harry! Can it go fast?\u0026quot;","Vernon, who had a deep appreciation for quality engineering and speed, was utterly unable to hide his reaction. He bent down, his massive hands hovering near the bristles, which were as straight as a razor’s edge.","\u0026quot;Look at the streamlining, Petunia,\u0026quot; Vernon muttered, utterly forgetting his aversion to magic. \u0026quot;The pitch on the twigs, it’s practically aerodynamic! A clean machine. Harry, how fast does this… thing… go?\u0026quot;","Harry grinned, feeling a swell of pride that had nothing to do with magic and everything to do with showing off his new \u0027car\u0027 to his family.","\u0026quot;It can do one hundred and fifty miles per hour in ten seconds, Uncle Vernon. And it has an unbreakable balancing charm.\u0026quot;","Vernon straightened up, his face a mixture of shock, jealousy, and immense, grudging respect. \u0026quot;One hundred and fifty miles per hour,\u0026quot; he repeated, shaking his head. \u0026quot;On a stick. I have to drive to work every day, Harry. One hundred and fifty miles per hour.\u0026quot;","Petunia walked over, placing a hand on the Firebolt\u0027s smooth wood. Her fear was still there, but it was now tempered by the understanding that this magnificent, dangerous object was a gift of fierce, protective love from the friend who hadn\u0027t betrayed her sister.","\u0026quot;Well, it\u0027s very kind of him, Harry,\u0026quot; Petunia said, her voice softer than usual. \u0026quot;It\u0027s a wonderful gift. But you will \u003cem\u003enot\u003c/em\u003e be flying that thing over Privet Drive, do you understand? The neighbours will talk, and I have a reputation to maintain.\u0026quot;","Harry laughed, the sound warm and genuine. The Dursleys, in their own loud, conventional way, had accepted his entire, unbelievable life. He had a secret godfather, a magical inheritance, and the fastest broom in the world—and they were only worried about the neighbours.","He had never felt so securely, and wonderfully, home.","The summer weeks unfolded in the usual Dursley fashion—predictably scheduled, meticulously tidy, and punctuated by Vernon\u0027s loud pronouncements on local politics. Harry settled into the comfortable routine, the dramatic events of the past year now safely contained within his memories and the thick volumes of his school trunk. He spent his mornings tending to Hedwig and the Firebolt (still disguised under a blanket in his room), and his afternoons building extravagant LEGO structures with Dudley, who now viewed Harry’s magical pursuits with a kind of proud, vicarious thrill.","One Saturday morning, several weeks into the holidays, Petunia tiptoed into Harry\u0027s room just after nine. She wanted to wake him quietly so they could discuss the planting of the new roses before Vernon got too involved.","Harry was curled up under his duvet, his perpetually messy hair falling across his forehead. He looked utterly peaceful. Petunia reached out to gently shake his shoulder when he shifted and mumbled something into his pillow.","She paused, leaning closer.","\u0026quot;\u003cem\u003e…Hermione…\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The name was whispered, a soft, sleepy sigh. Petunia straightened up, a slow, gentle smile spreading across her face. \u003cem\u003eHermione.\u003c/em\u003e A girl\u0027s name. A school friend, clearly. The brilliant witch Harry relied on so much. Petunia knew from his letters that a girl with a fierce brain and bushy hair was instrumental to his adventures. But the \u003cem\u003etone\u003c/em\u003e of the whisper suggested something much warmer than mere academic partnership.","Petunia smoothed the duvet and backed silently out of the room, leaving Harry to his dreams. She had a feeling this new development was going to make the summer \u003cem\u003emuch\u003c/em\u003e more interesting.","When Harry finally came downstairs, showered and dressed, the kitchen was already buzzing. Vernon was reading the paper, Dudley was attempting to balance a sugar cube on his nose, and Petunia was laying out a magnificent breakfast of sausages, eggs, and toast.","The moment Harry walked in, all three Dursleys looked up, their expressions a strange mixture of casual innocence and barely-contained mischief.","\u0026quot;Morning, Harry dear,\u0026quot; Petunia chirped, her voice unusually bright. \u0026quot;Sleep well?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Very well, thanks, Aunt Petunia,\u0026quot; Harry replied, grabbing a plate.","\u0026quot;Good, good,\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, lowering his paper slightly to fix Harry with a curious eye. \u0026quot;A good night’s rest is vital for a growing boy, especially one who spends all his time flying around on… on that \u003cem\u003ething\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Dudley abandoned his sugar cube attempt and leaned in conspiratorially. \u0026quot;Yeah, Harry, did you have any good dreams?\u0026quot;","Harry shrugged, trying to ignore the sudden, intense focus of his family. \u0026quot;Just the usual.\u0026quot;","Petunia placed a glass of orange juice squarely in front of him. \u0026quot;Oh, really? I thought I heard you talking in your sleep, Harry. You seemed to be rather enjoying yourself. You were saying a name…\u0026quot;","Harry froze, spoon halfway to his mouth. He looked at his aunt, whose smile was now bordering on predatory.","\u0026quot;A name?\u0026quot; Harry tried to sound confused, but the flush creeping up his neck gave him away.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Vernon announced, putting the paper down with a decisive \u003cem\u003ethwack\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;A girl’s name, I believe. Starts with an H. \u003cem\u003eHermione\u003c/em\u003e, wasn’t it, Petunia?\u0026quot;","Petunia sighed dramatically. \u0026quot;It was, Vernon. Such a lovely name. Who is this \u003cem\u003eHermione\u003c/em\u003e, Harry? Is she the one who fixes your spectacles?\u0026quot;","Harry stared at them. He was used to their loud, conventional interrogations about grades or clean shoes, but this was new territory: \u003cem\u003eromantic\u003c/em\u003e interrogation. There was no escape.","He sighed, running a hand through his hair. \u0026quot;She’s… she’s Hermione Granger. She’s one of my best friends. She’s in Gryffindor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ah, a \u003cem\u003efriend\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; Vernon said, exchanging a look with Petunia that clearly meant: \u003cem\u003eHe’s lying.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;A very clever friend, Petunia tells me,\u0026quot; Dudley added, already enjoying the drama. \u0026quot;The one who makes sure you don’t get eaten by three-headed dogs?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, her,\u0026quot; Harry mumbled. \u0026quot;And she’s just… a friend.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just a friend who you mumble about in your sleep,\u0026quot; Petunia pointed out, her eyes twinkling. \u0026quot;And if she’s just a friend, Harry, then you won’t mind telling us what exactly happened \u003cem\u003eafter\u003c/em\u003e you rescued that fugitive godfather of yours, just before you returned to the Hospital Wing, will you? I gather there was some… \u003cem\u003eexcitement\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","Harry\u0027s jaw dropped. They couldn\u0027t possibly know. Only Dumbledore, Ron, and perhaps the Fat Lady knew!","\u0026quot;How did you—?\u0026quot;","Vernon cut him off with a deep, knowing chuckle. \u0026quot;Your friend, Ron Weasley, sent you an owl, didn’t he? A short note, full of poorly spelled advice about ‘not getting all mooshy on the train.’ We assume, Harry, that he was referring to your Hermione.\u0026quot;","Harry slumped back in his chair, utterly defeated. His big, loud, intrusive, and observant family had pieced it together. He was cornered.","He took a deep breath and, in a rush of words, confessed everything: the risky mission, the relief, the moment of shared triumph outside the Hospital Wing, and the sudden, surprising, exhilarating kiss.","He finished his story, avoiding eye contact and bracing himself for the inevitable explosion of Dursley conventional outrage—or, worse, Vernon’s thunderous lecture on the necessity of proper courtship.","Instead, a profound, heavy silence settled over the kitchen.","Dudley was the first to react. He looked from Harry, to Petunia, to Vernon, and then back to Harry, his face splitting into a colossal, delighted grin.","\u0026quot;You kissed her, Harry?\u0026quot; Dudley crowed. \u0026quot;The smart one! Brilliant! Did you use tongue?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;DUDLEY!\u0026quot; Petunia shrieked, instantly abandoning her mischievous veneer for pure, maternal shock.","Vernon Dursley, however, was staring at Harry with a look of stunned admiration that Harry had never seen before. He slowly picked up his fork and began to butter a piece of toast, his voice low and utterly sincere.","\u0026quot;Well, I’ll be,\u0026quot; Vernon muttered, shaking his head slightly. \u0026quot;The boy saves the hippogriff, rescues the family friend, and then, at the height of the drama, he manages to… to secure the girl. Efficient, Harry. Very efficient. Good hustle, son.\u0026quot;","Petunia, having recovered from her initial shock, walked over and gripped Harry’s shoulders firmly, her expression a mix of fierce pride and sudden anxiety.","\u0026quot;A kiss, Harry? A proper, mutual kiss? Did she seem happy? Is she a good girl? Does she have a sensible family? What did she say afterward? You didn\u0027t just rush off, did you? You should have offered her a cup of tea! Did you hold her hand on the way back? You must tell me everything about this girl!\u0026quot;","She turned to Vernon, her eyes wide. \u0026quot;Vernon! Our Harry! He’s only thirteen, and he’s already… already \u003cem\u003ewooing\u003c/em\u003e the cleverest girl in the year! We need to make sure he takes her out somewhere nice. Do they have restaurants in that world of yours? He needs to be a gentleman!\u0026quot;","Vernon beamed, puffed up with vicarious pride. \u0026quot;He’s a Potter, Petunia. They know how to get what they want. You just make sure she’s properly fed when she visits, Petunia. Nothing wrong with buttering up the future family, eh?\u0026quot;","Harry, utterly overwhelmed by their enthusiastic, loud, and completely non-judgmental acceptance of his romantic revelation, could only stare. He had expected shame, but he got \u003cem\u003echeers\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;It was just a kiss, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry managed to say. \u0026quot;We haven’t even talked about it.\u0026quot;","Petunia waved her hand dismissively. \u0026quot;Nonsense, Harry. A kiss after a near-death experience is a declaration, dear. Now, you’ll write to her today, won’t you? You tell her that your Aunt Petunia sends her very best wishes and that we would be delighted to host her for tea if she’s ever in the area. Make sure you use your best handwriting!\u0026quot;","Harry smiled, shaking his head. In a world full of terrifying magic and dark lords, the greatest, most wonderful surprise was the unwavering, loud, and entirely supportive love of his completely, ridiculously normal family."]},{"num":7,"origNum":7,"title":"The Triwizard Tournament","wordCount":1947,"paragraphs":["The summer that followed Harry\u0027s third year passed in a whirlwind of Firebolt practice (conducted in secret at the local park under the guise of \u0027extreme jogging\u0027), enthusiastic letters from Sirius, and the Dursleys\u0027 increasingly complex and noisy attempts to matchmake Harry and Hermione. They insisted Harry include detailed descriptions of Hermione\u0027s activities in his letters, prompting Harry to write increasingly vague, yet factual, updates on her academic achievements.","The fourth year began with the excitement of the \u003cstrong\u003eQuidditch World Cup\u003c/strong\u003e, an event the Dursleys, surprisingly, insisted on attending. Vernon, intrigued by the \u0027scale of the business operation,\u0027 spent the entire trip loudly complaining about the lack of proper stadium seating and the absence of a visible scoreboard, while Dudley and Harry were simply awestruck by the spectacle. The appearance of the \u003cstrong\u003eDark Mark\u003c/strong\u003e shortly thereafter sobered everyone, reminding them of the ever-present danger.","The year continued with the announcement of the \u003cstrong\u003eTriwizard Tournament\u003c/strong\u003e and the arrival of students from Beauxbatons and Durmstrang. Harry, despite his reluctance, found himself chosen as the unexpected fourth champion. The Dursleys, upon hearing the news via an indiscreet front-page article in the \u003cem\u003eDaily Prophet\u003c/em\u003e that Hagrid sent them, immediately called the school, with Vernon demanding to speak to the Board of Governors about the \u0027clear dereliction of duty\u0027 involved in forcing a fourteen-year-old into a death match. Their over-the-top, loud support only increased Harry\u0027s determination to survive.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe First Task: A Kiss Before the Dragons\u003c/strong\u003e","The day of the First Task—retrieving a golden egg from a nesting mother dragon—was shrouded in nervous energy. Harry had spent the last week agonizing over the logistics, primarily because he couldn\u0027t use his Firebolt without revealing his godfather\u0027s status. He eventually settled on a complex summoning charm, practiced endlessly with Hermione\u0027s patient coaching.","He was now waiting in the Champions’ tent, the thick canvas muffling the roars of the crowd and the terrifying snarls of the dragon outside. He was dressed in his tournament robes, trying to keep his hands from shaking. Viktor Krum, the Durmstrang champion, was doing impressive warm-up calisthenics, occasionally glancing at Harry with professional respect. Fleur Delacour, the Beauxbatons champion, paced elegantly. Cedric Diggory, the Hogwarts champion, was nervously twirling his wand.","The tent flap suddenly opened, and Hermione Granger slipped inside. She looked frantic, her face pale, her bushy hair slightly wild. She immediately spotted Harry and rushed over, ignoring the three other champions.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; she breathed, grabbing his arms. \u0026quot;You looked so pale leaving the Hall! I\u0027ve been so worried! Are you ready? Did you remember what I told you? Use a powerful, focused concentration! Don\u0027t panic!\u0026quot;","Harry was overwhelmed by the sheer force of her concern. \u0026quot;I know, Hermione, I know. I\u0027ve got it. I\u0027m just... nervous.\u0026quot;","She looked into his bright green eyes, the anxiety on her face melting into a look of fierce, protective adoration. She knew, better than anyone, the kind of selfless courage he possessed, and she couldn\u0027t bear the thought of him facing this alone.","\u0026quot;You\u0027ll be brilliant, Harry,\u0026quot; she whispered. \u0026quot;You always are.\u0026quot;","And then, just as she had outside the Hospital Wing, she surged forward. This time, the kiss was more confident, more desperate, and far longer. Harry instantly responded, his hands moving to cup her face, all the fear and pressure of the dragons outside vanishing in the sudden, exhilarating rush of her presence. The world narrowed down to the sound of her rapid breathing and the scent of parchment and vanilla.","The profound silence that followed was not due to the kiss itself, but to the sudden, collective intake of breath from the five adults and students who had just entered the tent.","The tent flap opened silently a second time to admit the judges and a delegation of champions.","\u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore\u003c/strong\u003e, Headmaster, stopped stock-still, his silver beard seeming to glow in the dim light. \u003cstrong\u003eProfessor McGonagall\u003c/strong\u003e, stern and practical, nearly dropped her clipboard. The three other champions—\u003cstrong\u003eKrum\u003c/strong\u003e, \u003cstrong\u003eFleur\u003c/strong\u003e, and \u003cstrong\u003eCedric\u003c/strong\u003e—also froze, witnessing the very public, very non-academic display of affection.","Harry and Hermione sprang apart, looking exactly like they had outside the Hospital Wing a year prior: flushed, rumpled, and caught red-handed.","Dumbledore, ever the picture of eccentric calm, was the first to speak, his eyes twinkling furiously.","\u0026quot;Ah! Mr. Potter, Miss Granger! Excellent timing, or perhaps, excellent \u003cem\u003elack\u003c/em\u003e of timing. I do apologize for the interruption, but the Ministry officials insisted we confirm the readiness of the champions before... well, before any further \u0027private consultations\u0027 could take place.\u0026quot;","Professor McGonagall’s lips were a thin, disapproving line, but the corner of her mouth twitched. \u0026quot;Potter! Miss Granger! You are in the champions\u0027 tent! Five points from Gryffindor for conduct unbecoming a champion, and ten points \u003cem\u003eback\u003c/em\u003e to Gryffindor for exhibiting a truly remarkable Patronus-level strength of feeling in the face of imminent dragon fire!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot; Dumbledore agreed, nodding sagely. \u0026quot;A truly potent love charm, Minerva. I suspect Mr. Potter is fully prepared now. His motivation is clearly... \u003cem\u003eheightened\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Viktor Krum, who had been watching the passionate reunion, looked neither jealous nor angry. He merely adjusted his coat, a slow, respectful smile spreading across his face. He recognized the intensity of Hermione’s emotion and knew, without a doubt, he couldn\u0027t compete with that kind of devotion.","\u0026quot;Vehrry emotional, Herr Potter,\u0026quot; Krum rumbled, his thick accent making the compliment sound genuinely impressed. \u0026quot;Gerrl is clearly vrrry fond. You must win, Herr Potter. For the gerrl.\u0026quot;","Fleur Delacour, momentarily forgetting her own elegance, put her hands on her hips, her eyes wide. \u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eMon Dieu\u003c/em\u003e! You ‘ave a moment \u003cem\u003elike zat\u003c/em\u003e before facing a dragon? You are mad, \u003cem\u003en’est-ce pas\u003c/em\u003e? But also… \u003cem\u003etrès romantique\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Cedric Diggory, ever the gentleman, merely grinned, shaking his head. \u0026quot;Well done, Harry. Looks like you’ve already won the biggest prize. Now, go get that egg!\u0026quot;","Harry, completely mortified but undeniably buoyed by the kiss and his friends\u0027 reactions, could only nod mutely.","Hermione, however, instantly recovered her academic composure, though her cheeks were still scarlet. She straightened her robes with a furious snap.","\u0026quot;Headmaster,\u0026quot; she said, her voice trembling slightly. \u0026quot;I was merely providing Harry with final, vital, non-verbal encouragement. I will wait outside. Good luck, Harry. I\u0027ll see you when you have the egg!\u0026quot;","She shot Harry one last, intense look of love and urgency, then marched out of the tent with remarkable dignity, leaving the four champions and the two Headmasters in a state of amused confusion.","Dumbledore watched her go, then placed a gentle, reassuring hand on Harry\u0027s shoulder. \u0026quot;Well, Mr. Potter. If ever there was a reason to ensure you return safely, that was it. Good luck. We shall await your triumphant—and hopefully intact—return.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eFlight Against the Horntail\u003c/strong\u003e","Five minutes later, the cannon boomed and Harry stepped out into the rocky enclosure. The roar of the stadium vanished behind the rush of blood in his ears—and the lingering warmth of Hermione’s lips. Across the arena crouched the Hungarian Horntail, fifty feet of black scales, spiked tail, and yellow eyes fixed on the clutch of eggs beneath her belly.","Harry didn\u0027t hesitate. He raised his wand and bellowed, \u0026quot;Accio Firebolt!\u0026quot;","When the broom streaked out of the castle sky and slammed into his palm, Harry vaulted into the air with an athleticism that brought the entire stadium to its feet. He didn\u0027t merely dodge the jet of white-hot dragon fire; he flew like a boy who had someone waiting for him on the ground. Diving vertically at breakneck speed, he feinted left, drew the Horntail’s lunge high, and snatched the golden egg from the nest without a single scratch on his robes.","In the weeks that followed, while the rest of the castle obsessed over invitations to the Yule Ball, Harry and Hermione retreated to an empty classroom on the fourth floor to decode the wailing screech of the golden egg. It was Hermione who deduced that the sound was Mermish—which only sang clearly underwater—and it was Harry who awkwardly, earnestly asked her to the Yule Ball while she was neck-deep in parchment.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Yule Ball and the Black Lake\u003c/strong\u003e","On Christmas night, when Hermione descended the marble staircase in periwinkle-blue silk robes, her hair tamed into elegant waves, even Ron stopped chewing long enough to stare. For four blissful hours, the tournament didn\u0027t exist. Viktor Krum, true to his word in the tent, raised a goblet to them from the head table with a solemn nod of respect.","That warmth carried them to the freezing morning of February twenty-fourth, when Harry stood on the wooden pier of the Black Lake, swallowed a handful of slimy grey Gillyweed, and plunged into the icy depths—because the thing the judges had stolen from him to anchor to the statue at the bottom of the merpeople’s village was Hermione.","Cutting her bonds with a sharp Relashio and refusing to leave Fleur’s little sister Gabrielle behind, Harry broke the surface gasping for air. Wrapped in thick woollen blankets on the shore, Hermione buried her freezing nose into the crook of his neck, whispering furiously that he was a noble, reckless idiot while refusing to let go of his hand.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Maze and the Graveyard\u003c/strong\u003e","By the twenty-fourth of June, the sky over the Quidditch pitch was clear and bruised with twilight. Twenty-foot hedges had swallowed the turf, forming a shifting, silent labyrinth. Inside the stands sat Sirius (disguised as a shaggy black hound at Hermione’s feet) and the Dursleys, whom Dumbledore had personally seated in the front box after Vernon threatened to write to his Member of Parliament.","Tied for first place, Harry and Cedric Diggory entered the maze first. Through Boggarts, Blast-Ended Skrewts, and an Imperiused Viktor Krum, the hedges seemed to breathe with malice. When Harry freed Cedric from the jaws of a giant Acromantula at the center of the maze, neither boy was willing to claim the gleaming blue Triwizard Cup alone.","\u0026quot;Together,\u0026quot; Harry panted. \u0026quot;On three.\u0026quot;","They grabbed the handles. The world hooked behind Harry’s navel and wrenched them out of the warm June night.","They didn\u0027t land on the Hogwarts lawn. They slammed onto the cold, overgrown grass of a dark graveyard in Little Hangleton. Before either boy could orient himself, a cloaked figure emerged from the shadows of the yew trees, cradling abundled, scaly thing in its arms, and a high, merciless voice sliced through the night:","\u0026quot;Kill the spare.\u0026quot;","A flash of green light burst from Wormtail’s wand. Cedric Diggory fell backward onto the grass, his grey eyes wide and empty against the stars.","Pinned against the marble headstone of Tom Riddle Senior, Harry was forced to watch the nightmare become flesh. Bone of the father, flesh of the servant, and blood sliced from Harry’s own arm—Lord Voldemort rose from the stone cauldron, tall, skeletal, and terrible, pressing his bone-white finger to Wormtail’s arm to summon the Death Eaters.","Yet when Voldemort forced Harry to duel and their spells collided in midair, a golden web of Priori Incantatem locked their twin wand cores together. From the tip of Voldemort’s wand spilled the luminous echoes of his victims: Cedric, Frank Bryce, Bertha Jorkins—and finally, Lily and James Potter.","\u0026quot;Hold on, Harry,\u0026quot; his father’s shade commanded, his voice fierce with pride. \u0026quot;When the connection breaks, run to the Portkey!\u0026quot;","Harry wrenched his wand upward, dodged a hail of curses behind the tombstones, seized Cedric’s wrist, and summoned the Triwizard Cup into his hand. They crashed back onto the grass of the Hogwarts pitch to the sound of brass bands that died into horrified screams as Dumbledore wrenched Harry off Cedric’s body, Moody—revealed within the hour as Barty Crouch Junior—dragged Harry toward the castle, and the fragile peace of the Wizarding World shattered forever."]},{"num":8,"origNum":8,"title":"The Silent Return","wordCount":1413,"paragraphs":["The end of the Triwizard Tournament did not bring the glory the Dursleys had loudly anticipated. It brought only a hollow, ringing silence.","The events of the graveyard—the return of Lord Voldemort, the flash of green light, the lifeless eyes of Cedric Diggory—had shattered the triumphant narrative of Harry’s fourth year. He had returned to Hogwarts clutching Cedric’s body, his spirit fractured in a way that no amount of treacle tart or Gryffindor camaraderie could easily fix.","The journey home on the Hogwarts Express was a stark contrast to the previous years. There were no exploding snap games, no sampling of Bertie Bott’s beans, and no excited chatter about the summer holidays. Harry sat staring out the window, his face pale and drawn, watching the magical countryside bleed into the grey, industrial outskirts of Muggle London. He felt cold, a deep, marrow-seeping chill that had nothing to do with the weather.","Hermione sat beside him, her hand gripping his tightly. She hadn\u0027t left his side since he had been released from the Hospital Wing. She didn\u0027t speak; she simply offered a grounding, physical presence, an anchor in the storm of his trauma. Ron sat opposite, looking grim and unusually serious, casting worried glances at his best friend.","When the train hissed into Platform Nine and Three-Quarters, the steam clearing to reveal the bustling crowd of parents, Harry felt a surge of nausea. He wasn\u0027t ready to pretend. He wasn\u0027t ready to be the \u0026quot;Boy Who Lived.\u0026quot; He just wanted to disappear.","They stepped onto the platform. The noise was deafening, but to Harry, it sounded underwater.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot;","The voice was unmistakable. Booming over the heads of several terrified first-years was Vernon Dursley. He was standing near the barrier, wearing a checked suit that was loud enough to wake the dead, with Petunia and Dudley flanking him.","Usually, Vernon would have been waving a large handkerchief or shouting about the parking fees. But as Harry pushed his trolley closer, the Dursleys fell silent.","Vernon’s bluster died in his throat. He looked at the boy he had raised—the boy who usually came back from school with a few scrapes and a cheeky grin—and saw a stranger. Harry looked haunted. His skin was grey, his eyes were dull and unseeing, and he held himself with a brittle stiffness, as if one wrong move would cause him to shatter.","Petunia Dursley, whose maternal instincts had been honed sharp by years of protecting Harry from a world she barely understood, felt a cold hand clutch her heart. She recognized that look. She had seen it on her sister’s face during the first war. It was the look of someone who had looked death in the face and survived, but left a piece of themselves behind.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, stepping forward and ignoring the bustle of wizards around her.","Harry stopped. He looked at his aunt, his uncle, and his cousin. He tried to smile, tried to summon the mask of the brave Gryffindor, but it crumbled.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m back,\u0026quot; he rasped, his voice sounding like it hadn\u0027t been used in days.","Dudley, who had been ready to ask if Harry had fought any more dragons, took a step back, his face falling. \u0026quot;You look terrible, Harry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dudley!\u0026quot; Vernon snapped, though his heart wasn\u0027t in the reprimand. He looked at Harry, his large mustache twitching. \u0026quot;Right. Well. Let\u0027s get you to the car. We... we made your favourite roast. And I bought a new fan for your room. It\u0027s been a scorcher.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded numbly. \u0026quot;Thanks, Uncle Vernon.\u0026quot;","He made to move past them, to blindly follow the routine of returning to Privet Drive, when a hand stopped him. Hermione had not let go.","She stood there, her bushy hair wild, her trunk heavy at her feet, looking small but fiercely determined. She looked from Harry’s broken expression to the confused, worried faces of the Dursleys.","She took a deep breath. This was the moment. She had written to her own parents that morning, explaining everything. Now, she had to convince the most conventionally stubborn family in Britain.","\u0026quot;Mr. and Mrs. Dursley?\u0026quot; Hermione said, her voice clear and trembling only slightly.","Vernon blinked, looking down at her. He recognized the name, of course. This was the girl. The \u003cem\u003ekisser\u003c/em\u003e. The smart one.","\u0026quot;Miss Granger,\u0026quot; Vernon said, trying to regain his composure. \u0026quot;We\u0027ve heard... a great deal about you. Efficient work with the dragon, I hear.\u0026quot;","Hermione didn\u0027t smile. \u0026quot;Thank you. But I need to ask you something. Something very important.\u0026quot;","She stepped closer to Petunia, instinctively sensing who held the real power in the family matters.","\u0026quot;Harry isn\u0027t alright,\u0026quot; Hermione said softly, her eyes pleading. \u0026quot;Something terrible happened at the end of the Tournament. He... he shouldn\u0027t be alone right now. If he goes back to his room, to the quiet... I\u0027m afraid he\u0027ll drown in it.\u0026quot;","Petunia looked at the girl, then back at her nephew, who was staring at his shoes, shoulders hunched. She saw the tremor in Harry\u0027s hands.","\u0026quot;I want to come with you,\u0026quot; Hermione stated, her chin lifting with Gryffindor courage. \u0026quot;I want to stay at Privet Drive. Just for a few weeks. Until he\u0027s... until he\u0027s back with us. I can sleep on the floor. I won\u0027t be any trouble. I just need to make sure he\u0027s safe.\u0026quot;","Vernon’s eyebrows shot up into his hairline. \u0026quot;Stay? At Number Four? A young lady? In the same house? Now see here, Miss Granger, we are a respectable family—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia cut in, her voice sharp.","She was looking at Hermione with a strange expression. She saw the fierce, unyielding loyalty in the girl’s brown eyes. It was the same loyalty Lily had once shown her friends. But more than that, she saw that this girl—this Muggle-born witch—loved Harry as much as they did.","Petunia looked at Harry again. He hadn\u0027t objected. He was leaning slightly toward Hermione, as if she were the only thing keeping him upright.","\u0026quot;He needs her,\u0026quot; Petunia said quietly.","\u0026quot;But Petunia!\u0026quot; Vernon sputtered, lowering his voice to a frantic whisper. \u0026quot;The neighbours! A girl staying over! And where will she sleep? We haven\u0027t prepped the guest room! And what about... \u003cem\u003emagic\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She stays,\u0026quot; Petunia said, her tone brokering no argument. She turned to Hermione. \u0026quot;You will sleep in the guest room. You will keep your wand hidden at all times. And you will help with the washing up.\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a breath she felt she’d been holding since the Third Task. \u0026quot;Yes. Yes, of course. Thank you, Mrs. Dursley.\u0026quot;","Vernon sighed, a long, deflating sound of a man accepting that his life was no longer his own. He looked at Harry, then at Hermione, and finally grunted.","\u0026quot;Right. Well. Don\u0027t just stand there blocking the platform entrance. Dudley, take Miss Granger\u0027s trunk. Harry, you take the owl. I suppose we can squeeze everyone in if we move the spare tyre.\u0026quot;","Dudley, surprisingly, didn\u0027t complain. He grabbed the handle of Hermione’s trunk. \u0026quot;You\u0027re the one who figured out the egg clue, right?\u0026quot; he asked Hermione, looking impressed.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Hermione said, giving him a small, weak smile.","\u0026quot;Cool,\u0026quot; Dudley muttered. \u0026quot;Harry told me. Said you were brilliant.\u0026quot;","They made their way out of the station to the car park. The journey back to Surrey was cramped and quiet. Harry sat in the back between Dudley and Hermione. He didn\u0027t speak, but halfway down the M25, he reached out and took Hermione\u0027s hand again.","Vernon watched them in the rearview mirror. He saw the grief etched into his nephew’s face, but he also saw the way the girl squeezed his hand, and the way Harry’s breathing seemed to steady just a fraction.","Vernon cleared his throat, gripping the steering wheel. \u0026quot;Bit of a traffic jam up ahead,\u0026quot; he announced loudly, trying to fill the silence with normality. \u0026quot;Councils are digging up the roads again. Absolute incompetence.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;We\u0027ll be home soon, Harry,\u0026quot; Petunia said from the front seat, her voice unusually soft. \u0026quot;We\u0027re all going home.\u0026quot;","As the car turned onto the pristine, uniform tarmac of Privet Drive, Harry looked at the house that had always been his sanctuary—his loud, fiercely protective suburban refuge, and now, with Hermione beside him and the Dursleys standing guard, an unshakeable fortress against the gathering dark.","He wasn\u0027t okay. But as the engine cut out and the silence of the suburbs settled around them, he knew he wouldn\u0027t have to face the nightmares alone."]},{"num":9,"origNum":9,"title":"The Incident Report","wordCount":1465,"paragraphs":["The silence at Number Four, Privet Drive, had a texture to it. It was thick and heavy, like a wool blanket in a heatwave.","Three days had passed since Harry and Hermione had arrived. Three days of quiet meals, where the only sounds were the scrape of cutlery and the ticking of the grandfather clock. Three days of Hermione hovering by Harry’s side like a bushy-haired bodyguard, intercepting well-meaning questions from Vernon with a sharp shake of her head.","Harry spent most of the time sitting in the garden, staring at the prize-winning begonias without really seeing them. He felt hollowed out, as if the portkey had transported not just his body back to Hogwarts, but his soul to somewhere else entirely.","The Dursleys were trying. They really were. Vernon had refrained from shouting at the news, and Dudley had actually offered Harry the remote control during \u003cem\u003eThe Great British Bake Off\u003c/em\u003e—a gesture of unprecedented sacrifice. But the tension was unsustainable.","It broke on a Thursday evening, during a dinner of shepherd’s pie.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Vernon began, his voice booming slightly too loud in the quiet kitchen. He stabbed a pea with his fork. \u0026quot;The school. Hogwarts. They... they handle these sorts of things, do they? Grief counseling? Post-traumatic support? Or is it all just waving sticks and hoping for the best?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly, not looking up from his plate.","\u0026quot;I’m just asking, Harry!\u0026quot; Vernon blustered, his face turning a mild pink. \u0026quot;You come back looking like you’ve gone twelve rounds with a heavyweight boxer, shaking like a leaf, and this one—\u0026quot; he gestured at Hermione with his fork \u0026quot;—won’t tell us a blasted thing. We have a right to know. We are your guardians, for heaven\u0027s sake! If there was an accident...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It wasn\u0027t an accident,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","Hermione’s hand instantly shot out, covering Harry’s on the table. \u0026quot;Harry, you don\u0027t have to.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice trembling but gaining strength. He looked up, meeting his uncle\u0027s eyes, then his aunt\u0027s. \u0026quot;I do. You need to know why I might... why I might be dangerous to be around.\u0026quot;","Petunia set her glass down. Her face was pale, her lips pressed into a thin white line. She sensed it—the shadow that had haunted her childhood was back.","\u0026quot;Tell us,\u0026quot; Petunia said softly.","Harry took a breath. It felt like inhaling broken glass.","\u0026quot;The tournament... the final task was a maze. Cedric Diggory and I... we got to the cup at the same time. We decided to take it together. A Hogwarts victory.\u0026quot;","Harry’s hand gripped the tablecloth. Hermione squeezed his other hand so hard her knuckles were white.","\u0026quot;But the cup was a portkey. It didn\u0027t take us back to the school. It took us to a graveyard. Little Hangleton.\u0026quot;","Petunia let out a small, strangled gasp. She knew the name. She had seen it in Lily’s old letters, the place where the Riddle family had lived.","\u0026quot;There was a man there,\u0026quot; Harry continued, his voice monotone, reciting the facts like a police report to keep the emotions at bay. \u0026quot;Peter Pettigrew. And... a thing. A baby, but not a baby. Voldemort.\u0026quot;","Vernon flinched at the name. Dudley stopped eating entirely.","\u0026quot;Pettigrew... he killed Cedric.\u0026quot;","The words hung in the air, absolute and terrible.","\u0026quot;Just like that?\u0026quot; Vernon whispered, his bluster completely gone. \u0026quot;A boy? A student?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just like that,\u0026quot; Harry said, staring at the shepherd’s pie. \u0026quot;The Killing Curse. Cedric didn\u0027t stand a chance. He was just... spare.\u0026quot;","Tears began to leak from Harry’s eyes, though his face remained still.","\u0026quot;Then they used my blood. They used a bone from his father\u0027s grave. They gave him a body. He’s back, Aunt Petunia. Lord Voldemort is back. He called his followers. The Death Eaters. They were all there. And then... we dueled.\u0026quot;","He explained the Priori Incantatem, the echoes of his parents, the desperate run to the cup, and the return with Cedric’s body. When he finished, the kitchen was silent, save for the hum of the refrigerator.","\u0026quot;He’s back,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered. She wasn\u0027t looking at Harry; she was looking out the window, into the gathering dark of the suburban street, as if expecting to see hooded figures on the manicured lawn. \u0026quot;After all this time. Lily’s murderer.\u0026quot;","Harry finally looked at them, his vision blurred. \u0026quot;So you see... I couldn\u0027t save Cedric. And now he\u0027s back, and he’ll come for me again. I shouldn\u0027t be here. I’m putting you all in danger.\u0026quot;","His composure cracked. He buried his face in his hands, his shoulders shaking with silent sobs. \u0026quot;It was my fault. I told Cedric to take the cup with me. If I hadn\u0027t... if I’d just been selfish...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Stop it.\u0026quot;","It wasn\u0027t Hermione who spoke. It was Petunia.","She stood up, walked around the table, and did something she had never done in fourteen years. She pulled Harry’s chair back, wrapped her thin arms around his shoulders, and pulled his messy head against her waist.","\u0026quot;You listen to me, Harry James Potter,\u0026quot; she said, her voice fierce and trembling. \u0026quot;You are a child. You are fourteen years old. You faced a monster that grown wizards are terrified to whisper about. It is \u003cem\u003enot\u003c/em\u003e your fault.\u0026quot;","Hermione was crying now, silently, her hand still clutching Harry’s. She moved her chair closer, leaning her head on Harry’s shoulder, creating a protective barrier on his other side.","\u0026quot;Petunia’s right, Harry,\u0026quot; Hermione choked out. \u0026quot;It was Voldemort. Only Voldemort. You brought Cedric home. You brought him home to his parents. That matters.\u0026quot;","Harry sobbed into his aunt’s apron, the grief finally breaking the dam. He felt Hermione’s warmth on one side and the surprising, bony strength of his aunt on the other.","Across the table, Vernon Dursley was turning a deep, dangerous shade of purple. But for the first time, his rage wasn\u0027t directed at Harry.","\u0026quot;Criminal,\u0026quot; Vernon muttered, his large hands clenched into fists on the table. \u0026quot;Absolutely criminal negligence! They send you to a school—a boarding school!—and they let a maniac resurrect himself in a graveyard? Where was the security? Where was this Dumbledore?\u0026quot;","He stood up, pacing the small kitchen floor, the floorboards creaking.","\u0026quot;A boy died? A young man with a future? And they just... what? Sent you home with a pat on the head?\u0026quot; Vernon roared, his eyes flashing. \u0026quot;If this were a proper institution, I’d sue them into the ground! I’d have the Board of Governors up on charges of manslaughter!\u0026quot;","He stopped pacing and looked at Harry, who was still being held by Petunia and Hermione. Vernon’s expression softened, the anger replaced by a grim, bulldog determination.","\u0026quot;You listen to me, boy,\u0026quot; Vernon said firmly. \u0026quot;You say this... this maniac is back. You say he’s after you.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded against Petunia’s stomach.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon said, adjusting his trousers. \u0026quot;Then he’ll have to get past us first. I don\u0027t care about his magic wands or his hooded friends. We are law-abiding citizens, and this is \u003cem\u003emy\u003c/em\u003e house.\u0026quot;","He looked at Dudley. \u0026quot;Dudley, go and check all the window latches. The downstairs ones too.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;On it, Dad,\u0026quot; Dudley said, standing up immediately. He looked at Harry. \u0026quot;I’ve still got that cricket bat, Harry. The heavy one. I’ll keep it under my bed. Just in case.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good lad,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded. He looked at Hermione. \u0026quot;And you, Miss Granger. You’re the smart one. If there are... precautions... magical alarms or whatever you call them... can you set them up? Without blowing up the kitchen?\u0026quot;","Hermione wiped her eyes, looking at Vernon with genuine surprise and gratitude. \u0026quot;Yes, Mr. Dursley. I can cast Muggle-Repelling charms—er, well, Dark Wizard repelling charms—and protective enchantments around the perimeter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Do it,\u0026quot; Vernon commanded. \u0026quot;Tonight. I want this place tighter than Fort Knox.\u0026quot;","Petunia smoothed Harry’s hair, her touch awkward but gentle. She looked at her husband, then down at her nephew.","\u0026quot;He won\u0027t touch you here, Harry,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, a fierce promise in her voice. \u0026quot;My sister gave her life to put that blood protection on you. And as long as you can call this house home... as long as we are your family... you are safe.\u0026quot;","Harry pulled away slightly, wiping his face with his sleeve. He looked around the kitchen. The Dursleys weren\u0027t wizards. They couldn\u0027t cast spells. Vernon’s plan to sue Voldemort was ridiculous, and Dudley’s cricket bat wouldn\u0027t stop a Killing Curse.","But looking at Vernon checking the back door locks, Dudley rushing upstairs to secure the perimeter, and Petunia and Hermione standing guard over him... Harry felt something shift in his chest.","The crushing weight of the graveyard didn\u0027t vanish, but for the first time since grabbing the Portkey, he felt like he wasn\u0027t carrying it entirely alone.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his voice sounding a little more like his own. \u0026quot;Okay.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":10,"origNum":10,"title":"The Guards of Azkaban","wordCount":1625,"paragraphs":["The immediate panic in the kitchen following Harry\u0027s confession began to subside, replaced by a calculated, siege-mentality planning session led by Vernon. However, Harry raised a hand, interrupting his uncle\u0027s muttered calculations about the cost of reinforcing the window bars with goblin-wrought iron.","\u0026quot;You don\u0027t need to turn the house into a fortress, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice steadying. \u0026quot;He can\u0027t touch me here. Not at Number Four.\u0026quot;","Vernon paused, a half-eaten sausage on his fork. \u0026quot;And why is that? Is the maniac allergic to suburbia?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s the magic my mother left,\u0026quot; Harry explained, glancing at Petunia. \u0026quot;Dumbledore explained it to me. Because Aunt Petunia took me in... because she’s my mother’s blood... as long as I can call this place home, I’m safe. Voldemort can’t track me here. He can’t touch me here. The protection doesn\u0027t break until I come of age at seventeen.\u0026quot;","The room went quiet. Hermione, who had been anxiously shredding a napkin, suddenly gasped, her hand flying to her mouth.","\u0026quot;Of course!\u0026quot; she exclaimed, her eyes widening. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eThe Bond of Blood!\u003c/em\u003e Professor Flitwick mentioned it in passing during Charms theory, but I’d completely forgotten! It’s ancient magic, Harry. It’s the strongest shield there is. As long as you return here once a year, the protection renews.\u0026quot;","Petunia looked down at her hands, a strange, melancholy expression on her face. The \u0026quot;choice\u0026quot; she had made fourteen years ago—to take in the nephew she barely knew—had not just given him a roof; it had built an impenetrable wall against the darkness that killed her sister.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Vernon said, digesting this information with a sharp nod. \u0026quot;We are... strategically essential to your survival?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;You are.\u0026quot;","Vernon puffed out his chest, looking immensely pleased. \u0026quot;Well. That settles it. You’re staying put. If this Lord Thingy tries to step foot on my lawn, he’ll have to answer to ancient magic \u003cem\u003eand\u003c/em\u003e the Neighbourhood Watch. We’ll be fine.\u0026quot;","The weeks that followed settled into a humid, stifling routine. July melted into a sweltering August. Hermione eventually had to return to her own parents, though the departure was a tearful affair involving a three-way hug between her, Harry, and Petunia (who pressed a tin of homemade shortbread into Hermione\u0027s hands, telling her to \u0026quot;keep her strength up\u0026quot;).","Without Hermione, the house felt quieter, but the fear had receded. Harry and Dudley spent the suffocatingly hot evenings wandering the neighbourhood. Their relationship had evolved into a comfortable, easy camaraderie. They no longer needed to talk much; they just walked, united by the secret knowledge that the world was much bigger and darker than the manicured hedges of Little Whinging suggested.","One evening, they were cutting across the play park on their way back from the corner shop. The air was heavy and still, the kind of weather that promised a storm. Dudley was complaining about his diet—Vernon had put the whole family on a regime of grapefruit and cottage cheese in solidarity with Dudley’s school boxing weight requirements.","\u0026quot;I’m telling you, Harry,\u0026quot; Dudley groaned, kicking a stone. \u0026quot;If I don\u0027t get a burger soon, I might actually eat the cricket bat.\u0026quot;","Harry chuckled. \u0026quot;I think Aunt Petunia’s hidden a stash of chocolate in the washing machine. I saw her—\u0026quot;","He stopped.","The laughter died in his throat. The humid summer air, which had been sticky and oppressive seconds ago, suddenly vanished. In its place came a bone-cracking, unnatural cold. The streetlamps flickered and died. The stars were swallowed by an encroaching, suffocating darkness.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Dudley’s voice was high and trembling. \u0026quot;What’s happening? Why is it so cold?\u0026quot;","Harry knew that cold. He felt it in his chest, a hollow, sucking sensation that dragged every happy memory he possessed into a void.","\u0026quot;Dudley, run,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his hand diving for his wand. \u0026quot;Run home!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t see!\u0026quot; Dudley panicked, stumbling backward. \u0026quot;Harry, I can\u0027t see anything! It feels like... like I\u0027ll never be happy again.\u0026quot;","Two towering, cloaked figures glided out of the shadows of the alleyway. They made no sound, but their presence screamed of despair. They were Dementors. Here. In Little Whinging.","One of them swept toward Harry, its rotted, scabbed hand reaching out. The other drifted toward Dudley, who was curled on the ground, whimpering, his hands over his ears.","Harry felt the familiar scream rising in his mind—his mother’s voice. But he pushed it down. He looked at Dudley—his cousin, his brother, the boy who had bought him sweets for the train and offered him a cricket bat for protection.","\u0026quot;NO!\u0026quot; Harry roared.","He pointed his holly wand directly at the gliding horrors. He didn\u0027t think of a memory; he thought of the kitchen table at Number Four. He thought of Petunia hugging him after the graveyard. He thought of Vernon threatening to sue a Dark Lord. He thought of \u003cem\u003ehome\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eEXPECTO PATRONUM!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","It wasn\u0027t a wisp. It was a blinding, solid eruption of silver light. The great stag, Prongs, burst from the tip of Harry’s wand, brighter than the moon. It charged the Dementor nearest Harry, tossing it aside with its antlers, then galloped toward Dudley, driving the second creature back into the darkness.","The Dementors, faced with the overwhelming power of the charm, fled into the night.","The silver light faded. The streetlamps flickered back on. The humid summer heat returned with a rush.","Harry stood panting, his wand still raised. Dudley was lying on the tarmac, shaking violently, his face grey and clammy.","\u0026quot;Duds?\u0026quot; Harry scrambled over, hauling his massive cousin to a sitting position. \u0026quot;Dudley, talk to me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cold,\u0026quot; Dudley chattered, his teeth clicking together. \u0026quot;So cold. Heard... heard things inside my head.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Come on,\u0026quot; Harry grunted, pulling Dudley’s arm over his shoulder. \u0026quot;We’re going home. Just walk. Left foot, right foot.\u0026quot;","It was a slow, agonizing stumble back to Number Four. By the time they reached the front door, Harry was exhausted, and Dudley was barely conscious. Harry didn\u0027t bother with the key; he hammered on the wood with his fist.","\u0026quot;Uncle Vernon! Aunt Petunia!\u0026quot;","The door was wrenched open almost instantly. Vernon stood there, looking irate at the noise, but his expression shattered the moment he saw them.","\u0026quot;Dudley!\u0026quot; Petunia shrieked, rushing past Vernon to grab her son’s other arm. \u0026quot;Oh my goodness! He’s freezing! Vernon, help him!\u0026quot;","Together, they wrestled the semi-conscious Dudley into the living room and dumped him onto the sofa. He was pale, sweating, and clutching his chest.","\u0026quot;What happened?\u0026quot; Vernon demanded, turning on Harry. He wasn\u0027t shouting in anger; his voice was tight with fear. \u0026quot;Was it... was it \u003cem\u003ehim\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry gasped, collapsing into an armchair. He was shaking from the after-effects of the spell. \u0026quot;Not Voldemort. Dementors.\u0026quot;","Petunia stopped fussing over Dudley and froze. She turned slowly to look at Harry. \u0026quot;Dementors? In Little Whinging? The guards of Azkaban?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Two of them,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;They came out of nowhere. They went for Dudley. They... they feed on happiness. That’s why he’s like that.\u0026quot;","Vernon looked at his son, who was rocking back and forth, muttering about being cold. The protective rage that filled Vernon’s face was terrifying to behold.","\u0026quot;They attacked my son?\u0026quot; Vernon growled. \u0026quot;Monsters? Here?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I drove them off,\u0026quot; Harry said quickly, looking at his uncle, bracing for the blame. \u0026quot;I used the Patronus Charm. It’s the only thing that stops them. I had to use magic, Uncle Vernon. I’m sorry. I know I’m not allowed, but—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You’re sorry?\u0026quot; Vernon interrupted, his voice rising. \u0026quot;You’re \u003cem\u003esorry\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","He crossed the room in two strides. Harry flinched, expecting a blow or a lecture about the neighbours.","Instead, Vernon’s heavy hand landed on Harry’s shoulder—not to shake him, but to grip him in a solid, grounding squeeze.","\u0026quot;You saved his life, didn\u0027t you?\u0026quot; Vernon said gruffly, staring into Harry\u0027s eyes.","\u0026quot;I... I think so,\u0026quot; Harry stammered. \u0026quot;They would have... kissed him. Taken his soul.\u0026quot;","Petunia let out a whimper, clutching Dudley’s hand tighter.","\u0026quot;Then don\u0027t you dare apologize,\u0026quot; Vernon stated firmly. \u0026quot;You did exactly what a man should do. You protected your family.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Harry,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, tears streaming down her face as she looked from Dudley to Harry. \u0026quot;Thank you. You saved him.\u0026quot;","Harry slumped back in the chair, a wave of relief washing over him that was stronger than any Patronus. They didn\u0027t care about the Statute of Secrecy. They didn\u0027t care about the \u0026quot;abnormality.\u0026quot; They cared that he had stood his ground.","Suddenly, a tawny owl swooped through the open living room window, dropping a parchment envelope on top of the television before soaring out again.","Vernon eyed the letter suspiciously. \u0026quot;Who\u0027s that from? The Thank-You committee?\u0026quot;","Harry picked it up, his hands shaking. He recognized the seal.","\u0026quot;It\u0027s the Ministry,\u0026quot; Harry said, his heart sinking as he tore it open. He scanned the text, his face draining of color.","\u0026quot;What is it?\u0026quot; Petunia asked sharply.","\u0026quot;I\u0027ve been expelled,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, the paper trembling in his hands. \u0026quot;For using magic in front of a Muggle. They\u0027re sending someone to snap my wand.\u0026quot;","Vernon snatched the letter from Harry’s hand. He read it, his face turning from pale concern to a deep, violent shade of puce. The vein in his temple began to throb.","\u0026quot;Expelled?\u0026quot; Vernon roared, shaking the parchment. \u0026quot;For saving my son from soul-sucking monsters? SNAP YOUR WAND?\u0026quot;","He ripped the letter in half and threw it on the floor.","\u0026quot;Let them come!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed at the ceiling. \u0026quot;Let them try! I\u0027ll give them a piece of my mind! I\u0027ll tell them exactly what happened! You saved Dudley! If those bureaucrats think they can punish a boy for being a hero, they\u0027ll have to get through me first! Petunia, get the chocolate! Harry, you sit there. Nobody is snapping anything tonight!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":11,"origNum":11,"title":"The Witness for the Defense","wordCount":1209,"paragraphs":["The chaos in the living room of Number Four was interrupted not by another owl, but by the sudden, silent appearance of Albus Dumbledore in the middle of the hearth rug.","Vernon Dursley, who had been midway through a diatribe about writing a strongly worded letter to the Prime Minister, stopped dead. Petunia let out a shriek, clutching a throw pillow.","\u0026quot;Good evening,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said pleasantly, adjusting his half-moon spectacles as he surveyed the shredded remains of the Ministry letter on the carpet. \u0026quot;I see the news has arrived. Excellent shredding technique, Vernon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You!\u0026quot; Vernon stepped forward, shielding his family. \u0026quot;You\u0027re the Headmaster! You’re the one who’s supposed to keep him safe! And now they want to snap his wand because he saved \u003cem\u003emy\u003c/em\u003e son?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Ministry can be... precipitate,\u0026quot; Dumbledore admitted, his voice calm but his eyes hard. \u0026quot;However, the situation is salvageable. There will be a disciplinary hearing on the twelfth of August.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll be there,\u0026quot; Vernon declared, pulling up his trousers. \u0026quot;I’ll represent him. I’ve handled contract disputes with tougher sharks than wizards.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am afraid that is not possible,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said gently. \u0026quot;The Wizengamot does not permit Muggles in the courtroom, with very few exceptions.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exceptions?\u0026quot; Petunia asked sharply.","\u0026quot;Witnesses,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. He turned his blue eyes toward the sofa where Dudley was still wrapped in blankets, sipping hot chocolate. \u0026quot;Harry is charged with performing magic in the presence of a Muggle. The defense relies entirely on proving that the use of magic was necessary to preserve life. For that, we need the person whose life was preserved.\u0026quot;","Dudley looked up, his face pale but his jaw set. \u0026quot;Me? You want me to go to the magic court?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do, Dudley,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. \u0026quot;And we shall be accompanied by another witness who saw the event. Mrs. Arabella Figg.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The cat lady?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, bewildered. \u0026quot;She\u0027s a wizard?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A Squib,\u0026quot; Harry corrected automatically, \u0026quot;someone born into a wizard family but without magic.\u0026quot;","Vernon looked torn between his desire to storm the Ministry himself and the realization that his son was the key to Harry’s freedom. He walked over to the sofa and placed a heavy hand on Dudley’s shoulder.","\u0026quot; rigorous cross-examination, son,\u0026quot; Vernon said gravely. \u0026quot;Stick to the facts. Don\u0027t let them intimidate you. Remember, we Dursleys don\u0027t crack.\u0026quot;","Dudley nodded slowly. He looked at Harry. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll go. He saved me. I\u0027m not letting them snap his wand.\u0026quot;","The morning of the hearing was a blur of travel. Harry, Dudley, Mrs. Figg (wearing a carpet-patterned dressing gown over her clothes), and Dumbledore traveled via a Portkey that felt like a hook behind the navel, depositing them in the Atrium of the Ministry of Magic.","Dudley stuck close to Harry, his eyes wide as he took in the golden fountain, the paper airplanes zooming overhead, and the sheer scale of the underground city. Unlike Diagon Alley, which was chaotic and vibrant1, this place felt cold and imposing.","\u0026quot;Just tell the truth, Big D,\u0026quot; Harry whispered as they descended in the lift toward the Department of Mysteries.","\u0026quot;I will,\u0026quot; Dudley muttered, adjusting the tie Vernon had forced him to wear.","The courtroom was a dungeon-like chamber with stone benches rising high on all sides. Harry was seated in a chair with chains that rattled ominously. Dumbledore conjured chintz armchairs for himself, Dudley, and Mrs. Figg.","Cornelius Fudge, the Minister for Magic, looked down from the high bench, wearing a lime-green bowler hat and a sneer.","\u0026quot;Disciplinary hearing of the twelfth of August,\u0026quot; Fudge boomed. \u0026quot;Into offenses committed by Harry James Potter... interrogationers: Cornelius Oswald Fudge, Minister for Magic...\u0026quot;","The trial began with Fudge attempting to railroad Harry, dismissing his claim of Dementors as a fantasy concocted by a boy seeking attention.","\u0026quot;Dementors? In Little Whinging?\u0026quot; Fudge scoffed, looking around at the Wizengamot members. \u0026quot;I ask you! It is highly likely the boy simply cast the charm to impress his Muggle cousin and concocted this story to cover his tracks!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have a witness,\u0026quot; Dumbledore interjected smoothly. \u0026quot;Two, in fact.\u0026quot;","Mrs. Figg was called first. She gave a nervous but determined account of the cold and the \u0026quot;running crouching things,\u0026quot; though Fudge tried to dismiss her testimony as vague.","\u0026quot;And the second witness?\u0026quot; Fudge asked impatiently. \u0026quot;Another Squib you\u0027ve dug up, Dumbledore?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. \u0026quot;The Muggle cousin in question. Dudley Dursley.\u0026quot;","A ripple of murmuring broke out across the courtroom. Wizards and witches craned their necks to stare at Dudley, who stood up. He looked large, terrified, and painfully normal in his school trousers and blazer.","Fudge stared. \u0026quot;A Muggle? In Courtroom Ten? Preposterous! He cannot see Dementors, Dumbledore! His testimony is worthless!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He cannot see them,\u0026quot; Dumbledore agreed. \u0026quot;But he can feel them. Mr. Dursley, if you would?\u0026quot;","Dudley stepped forward. He looked at the rows of staring wizards, then at Fudge, who looked remarkably like a man Vernon would have complained about at a dinner party.","\u0026quot;I didn\u0027t see them,\u0026quot; Dudley said, his voice trembling slightly before finding the volume he used on the rugby pitch. \u0026quot;But everything went dark. And cold. Really cold. Like... like it was winter, but inside me.\u0026quot;","The courtroom went silent.","\u0026quot;I felt...\u0026quot; Dudley paused, struggling for the words. \u0026quot;I felt like I was never going to be happy again. I heard... I heard screaming inside my head. And then I fell down. I couldn\u0027t get up.\u0026quot;","Fudge looked unsettled. \u0026quot;Boyish dramatics! You were likely just—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I couldn\u0027t move!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted, his Dursley temper flaring. He pointed a shaking finger at Harry. \u0026quot;He saved me! There was a silver light—a stag. It chased the cold away. If Harry hadn\u0027t done that magic, I\u0027d still be on the ground! He carried me home!\u0026quot;","Dudley glared at the Minister. \u0026quot;My dad says you\u0027re trying to punish him for being a hero. And my dad is usually right about bureaucrats.\u0026quot;","Stunned silence followed this declaration. Madam Bones, a monocled witch with a stern face, looked from Dudley to Harry with a new expression—respect.","\u0026quot;The witness describes the effects of a Dementor attack perfectly,\u0026quot; Madam Bones stated, her voice booming. \u0026quot;No Muggle could invent such a description.\u0026quot;","Fudge spluttered, but the tide had turned. The testimony of a Muggle boy—who had clearly been terrified and protected by his wizard cousin—was undeniable.","\u0026quot;Those in favor of clearing the accused of all charges?\u0026quot; Madam Bones asked.","More than half the hands shot up.","\u0026quot;Cleared of all charges,\u0026quot; Fudge announced through gritted teeth.","Harry let out a breath, slumping in the chained chair. He looked at Dudley, who was wiping sweat from his forehead but grinning weakly.","As they walked out of the courtroom, Dumbledore placed a hand on Dudley’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;A very brave thing to do, Mr. Dursley,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said quietly. \u0026quot;Your aunt and uncle should be very proud.\u0026quot;","Dudley shrugged, his face red. \u0026quot;He\u0027s family,\u0026quot; Dudley mumbled, echoing the sentiment his father had used in the Gringotts vault four years prior2. \u0026quot;Besides, he\u0027s got to teach me how to fight those things. I\u0027m not letting a floating cloak take me down again.\u0026quot;","Harry smiled, a genuine, relieved smile. He was free. And for the first time, the worlds of Privet Drive and Hogwarts didn\u0027t feel like they were at war—they were on the same side."]},{"num":12,"origNum":12,"title":"The Mending of Summer","wordCount":1011,"paragraphs":["The remainder of the summer holidays at Number Four, Privet Drive, underwent a remarkable transformation. The house, usually a bastion of aggressive normalcy1, became a strange, revolving door of magical rehabilitation.","Harry’s acquittal at the Ministry had lifted a crushing weight from his shoulders, and the Dursleys, buoyed by their victory over the \u0026quot;bureaucratic nincompoops\u0026quot; of the wizarding government, relaxed considerably. Vernon even framed the letter confirming Harry\u0027s clearance (after taping it back together) and placed it in the downstairs loo, right next to his certificates for Drill Salesmanship.","But it was the visits that truly brought the color back to Harry’s cheeks.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Weasley Invasion\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron Weasley arrived via the Floo Network on a Tuesday evening, tumbling out of the Dursleys\u0027 pristine electric fireplace in a cloud of soot.","\u0026quot;Sorry! Sorry!\u0026quot; Ron coughed, brushing ash off his robes as Petunia shrieked and snatched a dustpan. \u0026quot;Dad connected the grate for the evening. Hello, Harry! Hello, Mr. and Mrs. Dursley! Alright, Big D?\u0026quot;","Dinner that night was a cultural exchange program that would have baffled the United Nations. Vernon, feeling magnanimous after his \u0026quot;legal victory,\u0026quot; decided to educate Ron on the marvels of engineering.","\u0026quot;You see, Ron,\u0026quot; Vernon explained, gesturing with a forkful of roast potato, \u0026quot;it\u0027s not about trapping a dragon in a box. It\u0027s electricity. Circuits. Fuses. If a fuse blows, the lights go out. No incantations required.\u0026quot;","Ron stared at the toaster on the counter with unblinking reverence. \u0026quot;So... the bread pops up... without a spell? It just \u003cem\u003eknows\u003c/em\u003e when it\u0027s brown?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a timer, Ron,\u0026quot; Dudley explained around a mouthful of peas. \u0026quot;It’s a spring.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Genius,\u0026quot; Ron breathed. \u0026quot;Dad would go spare if he saw this. And this... \u0027television\u0027. You just watch Muggles living inside the box?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They aren\u0027t \u003cem\u003ein\u003c/em\u003e the box, Weasley,\u0026quot; Vernon chuckled, pouring himself a glass of wine. He looked at Harry, his eyes crinkling. \u0026quot;Your friend is a bit simple about the basics, isn\u0027t he, Harry? But he has a healthy appetite. I respect that.\u0026quot;","Harry grinned, feeling a warmth in his chest that had been missing for months. \u0026quot;Yeah, Uncle Vernon. He\u0027s great.\u0026quot;","Petunia, meanwhile, kept piling food onto Ron’s plate, evidently deciding that the best way to thank the boy who had been Harry’s best friend for four years was to ensure he couldn\u0027t physically walk out the door.","\u003cstrong\u003eHermione’s Strategy Sessions\u003c/strong\u003e","Hermione’s visits were less chaotic but equally restorative. She arrived by Muggle taxi, carrying a stack of books and a clipboard.","She and Harry sat in the garden, with Petunia bringing them trays of lemonade and sandwiches every hour. Hermione had taken it upon herself to help Harry process the events of the graveyard not just emotionally, but logically—her way of coping.","\u0026quot;So, the protection held,\u0026quot; Hermione murmured, cross-referencing a heavy tome on ancient wards. \u0026quot;And the Patronus you cast... Harry, it’s remarkable. To drive off two Dementors after... well, after everything.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I had help,\u0026quot; Harry said, watching Dudley wrestle with the lawnmower nearby. \u0026quot;Knowing they were behind me... knowing I wasn\u0027t alone here. It made the difference.\u0026quot;","Petunia, pruning her roses nearby, paused. She looked at Harry—his green eyes bright again, his posture relaxed, the haunted look of the graveyard finally gone. He looked like a normal fifteen-year-old boy, chatting with his girlfriend (Petunia was still convinced, despite their protests) in the summer sun.","\u0026quot;He looks better, doesn\u0027t he?\u0026quot; Petunia said softly to herself.","Vernon, who had just come out to inspect the lawn, nodded. \u0026quot;He’s got his spark back. Good thing, too. Can’t have him moping about when he needs to go back and show that Voldy-whatsit who’s boss.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePlatform Nine and Three-Quarters\u003c/strong\u003e","The first of September arrived with a crisp, golden morning. The journey to King\u0027s Cross was loud and cheerful. The fear that had gripped them in July—the fear of hidden monsters and dark lords—had been replaced by a fierce, protective solidarity.","When they reached the barrier between platforms nine and ten, the station was packed. Harry spotted the Weasleys’ red hair in the distance, and the bushy mane of Hermione.","Vernon parked the trolley. He turned to Harry, placing a hand on his shoulder.","\u0026quot;Right, Harry,\u0026quot; Vernon said, his voice gruff but warm. \u0026quot;You’ve got your trunk. You’ve got your owl. And you’ve got your head screwed on right this time.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thanks, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry said.","\u0026quot;Listen to me,\u0026quot; Vernon lowered his voice, glancing around at the passing commuters. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t pretend to understand half of what goes on in that mad world of yours. But I know this: You’re a fighter. You took down that snake-faced maniac once, and you survived him again. If he gives you any trouble... well, give him hell from the Dursleys.\u0026quot;","Harry laughed, a true, loud sound. \u0026quot;I will.\u0026quot;","Petunia stepped forward. She smoothed his collar, her eyes glistening. She didn\u0027t see the Boy Who Lived; she saw the baby she had found on her doorstep, grown into a young man who had saved her son.","\u0026quot;Be careful, Harry,\u0026quot; she whispered, kissing his cheek. \u0026quot;And eat properly. No skipping meals just because you\u0027re busy saving the world.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I promise, Aunt Petunia.\u0026quot;","Then, it was Dudley’s turn. The large boy, who had grown from a boisterous, toast-stealing childhood playmate into a fiercely loyal older cousin, held out a massive hand.","\u0026quot;See you next summer, Harry,\u0026quot; Dudley said, shaking Harry\u0027s hand firmly. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll keep practicing with the punching bag. In case those Dementor things come back. I\u0027ll be ready.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You will be, Big D,\u0026quot; Harry smiled. \u0026quot;Keep the cricket bat handy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Will do.\u0026quot;","Harry grabbed the handle of his trunk. He looked back at them one last time—Vernon checking his watch, Petunia dabbing her eyes, Dudley giving a thumbs-up. They were his family. His loud, normal, exasperating, wonderful family.","With a final wave, Harry turned and walked through the barrier. He was ready for the Fifth Year. He was ready for the Order, for Umbridge, and for Voldemort. Because for the first time in his life, he wasn\u0027t just fighting for the wizarding world. He was fighting for his home."]},{"num":13,"origNum":13,"title":"The Fortress of the Mind","wordCount":1022,"paragraphs":["The return to Hogwarts for Harry’s fifth year was marked by a darkening horizon. The Ministry of Magic was interfering at Hogwarts in the pink, toad-like form of Dolores Umbridge, and the corridors whispered with rumors of the Dark Lord’s return. But for Harry, the true war was being fought in the dungeon office of Severus Snape.","Albus Dumbledore had ordered the lessons immediately. Voldemort had realized the connection between his mind and Harry’s, and he was beginning to probe.","\u0026quot;Occlumency, Potter,\u0026quot; Snape sneered, pacing the dim room filled with jars of floating slime. \u0026quot;The magical defense of the mind against external penetration. An obscure branch of magic, but a highly necessary one.\u0026quot;","Harry stood in the center of the room, clutching his wand. He felt a familiar knot of tension, but unlike in previous years, it wasn\u0027t the lonely anxiety of an orphan. He had Vernon’s voice in his head telling him to \u003cem\u003estand his ground\u003c/em\u003e, and Petunia’s promise that he was safe.","\u0026quot;The Dark Lord is highly skilled at Legilimency,\u0026quot; Snape said softly, turning to face Harry. His black eyes were cold and empty. \u0026quot;He can extract feelings and memories from another person\u0027s mind. He can provoke visions. He can torture you to madness.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m ready,\u0026quot; Harry said, bracing himself.","\u0026quot;We shall see,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. He raised his wand. \u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eLegilimens!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The world dissolved.","Harry wasn\u0027t in the dungeon anymore. He was rushing through a kaleidoscope of memories, but they weren\u0027t the memories Snape—or Voldemort—might have expected to find in a neglected orphan.","He was five years old, sitting on the kitchen counter while Petunia, humming softly, pressed a plaster onto his scraped knee1.","He was eleven, watching Vernon Dursley roar at Hagrid, not out of hatred for magic, but out of a fierce, misguided desire to protect Harry from \u0026quot;freakishness\u0026quot;2.","He was sitting on his bed, opening a bag of sweets Dudley had bought him with his own pocket money3.","He was standing in the Gringotts vault, listening to Petunia tell him that their money was for his present, and his gold was for his future4.","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Harry yelled in the real world. He pushed back with everything he had, not using a spell, but using the sheer weight of those memories.","He stumbled back into the desk, gasping for air. The dungeon swam back into focus.","Snape was lowering his wand, looking at Harry with an expression of profound, unsettled confusion. He had expected to see the abuse and neglect he assumed Petunia Evans would inflict on James Potter\u0027s son. He had expected a pampered, arrogant prince or a broken, mistreated wretch.","He had not expected to see Petunia Dursley looking at Harry with the same fierce love she had once reserved only for her own son.","\u0026quot;Sentimental drivel,\u0026quot; Snape sneered, though his voice lacked its usual bite. He looked shaken. \u0026quot;You wear your heart on your sleeve, Potter. You allow your mind to be cluttered with... domestic mediocrity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s not mediocrity,\u0026quot; Harry panted, wiping sweat from his forehead. \u0026quot;It’s my family.\u0026quot;","Snape’s lip curled. \u0026quot;Your family,\u0026quot; he repeated, the word tasting like poison. \u0026quot;Petunia Evans. The woman who envied magic so much she nearly burst. You think that—that \u003cem\u003edomesticity\u003c/em\u003e will save you from the Dark Lord?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It saved me in the graveyard,\u0026quot; Harry retorted hotly. \u0026quot;And it saved me this summer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Clear your mind!\u0026quot; Snape barked, regaining his composure. \u0026quot;Potter, you are not trying! The Dark Lord will not pause to admire your aunt’s needlework or your uncle’s blustering shouts! He will tear through those memories and find what he seeks! Again!\u0026quot;","The training continued for weeks, becoming more rigorous and brutal as the winter snows melted. Snape was relentless. He attacked Harry’s mind before Harry could even raise his wand. He forced Harry to relive the graveyard, the humiliation of Umbridge’s detentions, and the fear of the corridor in the Department of Mysteries.","\u0026quot;Focus, Potter!\u0026quot; Snape shouted one evening in March, after Harry had been knocked to his knees for the fifth time. \u0026quot;You are lazy! You are arrogant! You rely on luck and the misplaced affection of Muggles to survive!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am not lazy!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, scrambling up.","\u0026quot;Then prove it! \u003cem\u003eLegilimens!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The spell hit Harry like a physical blow.","He was back in the kitchen at Privet Drive. Vernon was reading the paper. The owl tapped on the window. The letter arrived5.","The scene shifted. He was in Diagon Alley, feeling the warmth of the phoenix wand, seeing Petunia crying tears of pride6.","He was at King\u0027s Cross, Vernon Dursley pushing his trolley, charging at the barrier to ensure Harry made his train7.","\u003cem\u003eGET OUT!\u003c/em\u003e","Harry didn\u0027t just push this time; he shoved. He channeled the feeling of the Firebolt his godfather had sent 8, the taste of Petunia’s treacle tart 9, and the solid grip of Vernon’s hand on his shoulder10.","\u003cem\u003eProtago!\u003c/em\u003e","The Shield Charm erupted from Harry’s mind. It collided with Snape’s mental probe and rebounded.","Suddenly, Harry wasn\u0027t in his own head. He was looking into Snape’s.","A young, greasy-haired boy was crying in a corner while a man shouted.","A teenage Snape was being hexed by James Potter.","Snape was standing on a hill, begging Dumbledore to hide them all... to hide Lily.","Harry gasped, the connection breaking instantly. He fell backward onto the stone floor, shaking violently.","Snape staggered back against his shelves, a jar of dead cockroaches crashing to the floor. His face was white with rage.","\u0026quot;OUT!\u0026quot; Snape roared, pointing a trembling finger at the door. \u0026quot;GET OUT, POTTER!\u0026quot;","Harry scrambled for his bag, his heart hammering against his ribs. He had seen it. He had seen the loneliness that defined Snape’s life—a sharp, jagged contrast to the loud, messy, protective love that Harry had come to know at Privet Drive.","He ran from the dungeon, the door slamming shut behind him. He hadn\u0027t mastered Occlumency, not really. But he had learned something just as important: his mind wasn\u0027t a fortress of stone and solitude like Snape\u0027s. It was a home, filled with people, and that made it harder to break, but also much, much harder to hide."]},{"num":14,"origNum":14,"title":"A Cobra in the Corridor","wordCount":1130,"paragraphs":["The nightmare didn\u0027t feel like a nightmare. It felt like a broadcast.","Harry was asleep in the Gryffindor dormitory, but in his mind, he was slithering low along a stone floor. He felt the cold hardness of the tiles against his scaled belly. He felt a hunger that wasn\u0027t for food, but for violence.","Ahead, a man was sitting in a corridor, guarding a heavy wooden door. It was Mr. Weasley.","Harry—or the snake—reared back. He struck. The fangs sank into flesh. The man shouted, collapsing in a pool of blood. The urge to strike again was overwhelming, sickeningly pleasurable.","\u0026quot;HARRY!\u0026quot;","Harry woke with a scream that tore his throat raw, thrashing in his sheets. His scar was on fire.","\u0026quot;Harry! What is it?\u0026quot; Ron was standing over him, looking terrified in the moonlight.","\u0026quot;Your dad,\u0026quot; Harry gasped, clutching his forehead, his stomach heaving with the phantom sensation of the snake\u0027s venom. \u0026quot;Ron, your dad. He\u0027s been bitten. It’s bad. There was blood everywhere. We need help!\u0026quot;","The next hour was a blur of panic and frantic movement. Professor McGonagall was summoned, then Dumbledore. Harry explained the vision, fighting the nausea of the \u0026quot;connection\u0026quot; Snape had warned him about.","But it worked. Dumbledore sent a warning to the Ministry immediately. Arthur Weasley was found, bleeding but alive, and rushed to St. Mungo’s.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Letter Home\u003c/strong\u003e","Once the immediate crisis had passed and word arrived that Arthur would survive, Harry sat in the quiet of the Gryffindor common room. He needed to tell them. He couldn\u0027t just disappear for Christmas without explaining why.","He pulled out a piece of parchment and wrote quickly.","\u003cem\u003eDear Aunt Petunia and Uncle Vernon,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eSomething happened last night. I had a vision—like a dream, but real. Voldemort’s snake attacked Ron’s dad at the Ministry. Because I saw it, they found him in time. He’s going to make it, but it was close.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThe Weasleys are all going to stay together for Christmas while Mr. Weasley recovers. Mrs. Weasley is in a state. I think... I think I should be with them. They\u0027ve been so good to me, and Ron is really shaken up. Is it okay if I don\u0027t come back to Privet Drive for the holidays? I want to help look after them.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eI’ll be careful. I promise.\u003c/em\u003e","Love,","Harry","Hedwig returned less than twelve hours later, carrying a thick envelope. It contained a letter written on Vernon’s best company stationery.","\u003cem\u003eHarry,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWe received your update. A snake? Inside a government building? It sounds like their security protocols are as shambolic as their judicial system. Absolutely unacceptable workplace hazards.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eHowever, your aunt and I agree. You are a Dursley, and Dursleys stand by their friends. The Weasleys were decent enough to host you for that World Cup business, and the boy—Ron—was polite enough when he came through the fireplace (mostly).\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eYou stay with them. Support the family. That is your duty. We will hold the fort here. Dudley sends his regards and says he hopes Mr. Weasley has a \u0026quot;speedy recovery\u0026quot; (I believe he is also relieved he won\u0027t have to share his selection box).\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eStay safe. Keep your head down. And if you see that snake again, tell someone immediately. Don\u0027t try to wrestle it.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eUncle Vernon \u0026amp; Aunt Petunia\u003c/em\u003e","Harry lowered the letter, a warm lump in his throat. They understood. They always understood now.","\u003cstrong\u003eChristmas at the Burrow\u003c/strong\u003e","Three days before Christmas, Harry arrived at the Burrow. It was a stark contrast to the pristine, snow-dusted silence of Privet Drive. The Burrow was a riot of noise, color, and anxious energy.","Mrs. Weasley met him at the door, pulling him into a hug that threatened to crack his ribs.","\u0026quot;Oh, Harry, dear! Thank you!\u0026quot; she sobbed into his shoulder. \u0026quot;Arthur told us... if you hadn\u0027t seen him... if you hadn\u0027t woken up...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m just glad he\u0027s okay, Mrs. Weasley,\u0026quot; Harry mumbled, patting her back awkwardly.","The house was packed. Bill and Charlie were back, Fred and George were testing Volatile Skiving Snackboxes in the kitchen, and Ginny was helping decorate the tree with live fairies.","Arthur Weasley, pale and bandaged but cheerful, was sitting by the fire in the living room.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Arthur beamed, waving his good arm. \u0026quot;The man of the hour! Or should I say, the Seer of the hour? Come in, come in. Have a mince pie. Molly\u0027s made about three hundred.\u0026quot;","Harry sat down, but he couldn\u0027t quite relax. The joy of the Weasleys felt fragile. Every time he looked at Arthur’s bandages, he remembered the taste of blood in his mouth. He remembered the \u003cem\u003epleasure\u003c/em\u003e the snake had felt.","Later that evening, the house settled down. The wind howled outside, rattling the windowpanes. Harry found himself sitting at the scrubbed kitchen table with Ron and Hermione, who had arrived earlier that afternoon.","\u0026quot;Did you tell your aunt and uncle?\u0026quot; Hermione asked quietly, tracing the wood grain of the table.","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Harry said, taking a sip of tea. \u0026quot;They were great about it. Uncle Vernon is mostly angry about the Ministry\u0027s lack of pest control.\u0026quot;","Ron snorted into his mug. \u0026quot;Mental, your uncle. But... nice. In a loud way.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He said I should stay,\u0026quot; Harry continued, looking at the fire. \u0026quot;He said it\u0027s my duty to stand by my friends.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s right,\u0026quot; Hermione said softly. \u0026quot;But Harry... are you okay? With the... the vision?\u0026quot;","Harry hesitated. He wanted to tell them how terrified he was. He wanted to tell them that he felt dirty, contaminated, like he was carrying a piece of Voldemort inside him. He wanted to tell them that he was terrified he might attack them next.","But then he looked at the Christmas cards strung up on the mantle. Among the magical ones that moved and squeaked, there was a stiff, rectangular card with a picture of a snowman on it. It was from the Dursleys.","\u003cem\u003eWe Dursleys don\u0027t crack,\u003c/em\u003e Vernon had told Dudley.","Harry straightened up. He had two families now. One here, full of magic and warmth, and one in Surrey, full of stubborn, Muggle grit. Both of them were counting on him.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m okay,\u0026quot; Harry lied, but his voice was firmer. \u0026quot;I just want to have a good Christmas. For Mr. Weasley.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We will, mate,\u0026quot; Ron said, clapping him on the back. \u0026quot;Fred and George are planning to bewitch the garden gnomes to sing carols. It\u0027ll be brilliant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Or a disaster,\u0026quot; Hermione pointed out, though she was smiling.","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Ron grinned. \u0026quot;A Weasley Christmas.\u0026quot;","Harry smiled back. The shadow of the snake was still there, coiled in the back of his mind, but surrounded by the warmth of the Burrow and the distant, steadfast support of Privet Drive, he felt strong enough to keep it at bay. At least for the holidays."]},{"num":15,"origNum":15,"title":"A Silent Night at the Burrow","wordCount":955,"paragraphs":["The Burrow had finally fallen silent. The wind that had been battering the crooked chimney stacks earlier in the evening had died down to a soft, rhythmic whistling, like the house itself was breathing in its sleep.","The sleeping arrangements had been shuffled to accommodate the guests. With Percy estranged from the family, his room on the second floor sat empty and silent. Mrs. Weasley had made it up for Harry, insisting that he needed the peace and quiet after his ordeal. It was a small, tidy room, smelling faintly of old parchment and floor polish—a stark contrast to the chaotic warmth of Ron’s attic bedroom, but Harry was grateful for the solitude. He needed the space to think, to try and erect the mental walls Snape had demanded he build.","Hermione was bunking in with Ginny on the first floor. Ron was in the attic. Mr. and Mrs. Weasley were exhausted and asleep in their room, the stress of St. Mungo\u0027s finally taking its toll.","Harry lay in Percy’s narrow single bed, staring at the ceiling. He wasn\u0027t asleep. Every time he closed his eyes, he saw the flash of fangs or the green light of the graveyard. He felt like a radio tuned to a frequency of horror, waiting for the next broadcast. He turned over, punching his pillow, trying to force his mind to clear, to focus on the Dursleys’ Christmas card or the game of Exploding Snap he’d played with Ron earlier.","Downstairs, the grandfather clock chimed the half-hour. Twelve-thirty.","On the first floor, in the room she shared with Ginny, Hermione’s eyes snapped open. She hadn\u0027t been sleeping either. She had been lying rigid, listening to the soft exhales of Ginny on the other side of the room. Her mind was racing with defensive spells, ancient protection charms, and the terrified look she had seen in Harry’s eyes when he thought no one was watching.","She couldn\u0027t stand it. The separation felt wrong. It felt dangerous.","She slipped out of bed, her bare feet making no sound on the rug. She grabbed her dressing gown, wrapping it tight around her shivering frame, and crept out onto the landing. The Burrow creaked and groaned, familiar and comforting, but tonight the shadows seemed to stretch a little longer than usual.","She climbed the stairs to the second floor, her hand trailing lightly on the banister. She stopped outside Percy’s door. Her heart was hammering against her ribs, not from fear, but from a desperate, overwhelming need to be near him—to prove to herself, and to him, that he was still there, still whole.","She pushed the door open. It swung inward with a faint squeak.","Harry jerked upright in bed, his hand diving instinctively for his wand on the nightstand.","\u0026quot;Who\u0027s there?\u0026quot; he whispered, his voice hoarse with sleep and adrenaline.","\u0026quot;It\u0027s me,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered back.","Harry lowered his wand, exhaling a long, shaky breath. \u0026quot;Hermione?\u0026quot;","She stepped inside, closing the door softly behind her. The moonlight filtering through the window illuminated her silhouette—her bushy hair a halo, her expression anxious and vulnerable.","\u0026quot;I couldn\u0027t sleep,\u0026quot; she said, her voice barely audible in the quiet room. \u0026quot;I kept thinking about... about everything. About you being up here alone.\u0026quot;","Harry sat up a little straighter, pulling the duvet up. \u0026quot;I\u0027m okay, Hermione. Really.\u0026quot;","She shook her head, taking a step closer to the bed. \u0026quot;You\u0027re not. And neither am I.\u0026quot;","She paused, twisting the fabric of her dressing gown in her hands. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t want to be down there. I want... I wanted to spend the night with you.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at her. In the dim light, he didn\u0027t see the bossy prefect or the brilliant witch. He saw the girl who had stood by him when the rest of the school turned their backs, the girl who had faced a werewolf for him, the girl who had walked into the Dursleys\u0027 kitchen and demanded a place in his home.","The isolation of Percy’s room, which had felt like a sanctuary, suddenly felt like a prison cell. He realized he didn\u0027t want to be alone either.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. He shifted over, pressing himself against the cold wall to make room on the narrow mattress. \u0026quot;Yeah. Okay.\u0026quot;","Hermione didn\u0027t hesitate. She shed her dressing gown and climbed into the bed.","The moment she settled beside him, the cold knot of fear in Harry’s chest unraveled. It was instant. She turned on her side, facing him, and he instinctively wrapped his arms around her waist, pulling her close.","She buried her face in his chest, her hands gripping the back of his t-shirt. He buried his face in her hair, inhaling the familiar scent of vanilla and ink. They fit together perfectly, a puzzle solved in the dark.","There was no space between them. They held on with a desperation that spoke of near-misses and future terrors. It was a hold that said \u003cem\u003eI am here\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eYou are real\u003c/em\u003e. It was tight, suffocatingly close, blocking out the draft from the window, the shadows in the corner, and the nightmares waiting in the dark. Not even air could pass between them.","\u0026quot;Safe,\u0026quot; Hermione breathed against his skin, her voice thick with emotion.","\u0026quot;Safe,\u0026quot; Harry echoed.","For the first time since the vision of the snake, the buzzing in Harry’s scar faded into silence. The connection to Voldemort was drowned out by the overwhelming, tangible reality of Hermione Granger in his arms.","Entangled in each other\u0027s warmth, surrounded by the quiet creaks of the Burrow, their breathing slowly synchronized. The tension left their bodies, replaced by a heavy, profound exhaustion. Within minutes, they were both asleep, anchored to the world by nothing but each other."]},{"num":16,"origNum":16,"title":"The Gryffindor Pretzel","wordCount":1014,"paragraphs":["The sun was barely peeking over the frosty hills surrounding the Burrow, casting a pale, wintery light through the window of Percy’s room. Inside, the single bed was currently defying the laws of physics. It contained two teenagers, a duvet, and approximately eight limbs, all woven together in a knot so complex it would have baffled a sailor.","Harry was lying on his back, one arm pinned under Hermione, the other draped protectively over her head. Hermione was sprawled almost entirely on top of him, her face buried in his neck, one leg thrown over his hips, and her bushy hair creating a thermal insulation layer that covered them both. They were, for all intents and purposes, a single, snoring organism. A Gryffindor Pretzel.","The peace was shattered at exactly 7:30 AM.","The door creaked open. Ron Weasley, hair sticking up at right angles and rubbing sleep from his eyes, shuffled in.","\u0026quot;Oi, Harry,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled, yawning. \u0026quot;Mum says breakfast is ready. She’s made those sausages you like and...\u0026quot;","Ron stopped. He blinked. He rubbed his eyes and looked again.","The shape in the bed didn\u0027t look like Harry. It looked like a multi-headed, bushy-haired beast with four feet.","Ron’s brain short-circuited. He let out a noise that could only be described as a high-pitched, strangled squeal—a sound usually reserved for terrified piglets or Mandrakes being uprooted.","\u0026quot;AIIIIEEEEEE!\u0026quot;","The reaction from the rest of the house was instantaneous and military-grade.","\u0026quot;HARRY!\u0026quot; Mrs. Weasley screamed from the kitchen.","\u0026quot;Wands out!\u0026quot; Fred roared from the landing.","The thunder of footsteps on the stairs sounded like a stampede of hippogriffs. The door to Percy’s room, which Ron had left ajar, was kicked fully open with a crash.","\u0026quot;GET AWAY FROM HIM!\u0026quot; George bellowed, leaping into the room, wand raised, ready to hex a Death Eater.","\u0026quot;Protect the family!\u0026quot; Fred shouted, diving in right behind him, brandishing a spatula he’d been holding.","Mrs. Weasley came next, clutching her chest. \u0026quot;Is it the snake? Is he having another vision?\u0026quot;","And finally, Arthur Weasley—fully healed thanks to a particularly potent dose of Blood-Replenishing Potion and Phoenix tears the healers had administered the night prior—jogged in, looking pale but alert, wand at the ready.","\u0026quot;I’ve got him! Everyone stay back!\u0026quot; Arthur commanded, looking around for the attacker.","The room fell into a stunned, vibrating silence.","Six pairs of Weasley eyes landed on the bed.","Harry and Hermione, jolted awake by the screaming, the door-kicking, and the threat of spatula-based violence, scrambled to sit up.","Or rather, they \u003cem\u003etried\u003c/em\u003e to.","Harry jerked upward, but Hermione’s arm was trapped under his back, anchoring him down. Hermione tried to roll away, but her leg was tangled in the sheets and Harry’s ankles.","\u0026quot;Wha—? Who\u0027s attacking?\u0026quot; Harry yelled, blindly grabbing for his glasses and accidentally poking Hermione in the ear.","\u0026quot;Ouch! Harry, that\u0027s my head!\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, trying to extricate her hair from his armpit.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m stuck!\u0026quot; Harry panicked. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t move my left leg!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That\u0027s because I\u0027m lying on it!\u0026quot;","They flailed for a solid five seconds—a chaotic blur of limbs, pajamas, and panic—before finally untangling themselves and sitting up, side-by-side, red-faced, and breathless. They looked like two deer caught in the headlights of a very loud, very ginger lorry.","The Weasleys lowered their wands (and the spatula).","Fred stared. Then, a slow, wicked grin spread across his face.","\u0026quot;Well, well, well,\u0026quot; Fred drawled, lowering the spatula. \u0026quot;False alarm, everyone. Unless we\u0027re counting aggressive snuggling as a Dark Art.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I thought he was being strangled!\u0026quot; Ron squeaked, his face a brilliant shade of crimson, pointing a trembling finger at the bed. \u0026quot;I walked in and... and... look at them! It was a pretzel! A Harry-Hermione pretzel!\u0026quot;","George leaned against the doorframe, chuckling. \u0026quot;I must say, Harry, your defensive technique has improved. The \u0027Human Shield\u0027 strategy. Very bold.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We... I... She...\u0026quot; Harry stammered, his face burning so hot he thought he might set the duvet on fire. \u0026quot;She couldn\u0027t sleep! It was cold! We just... fell asleep!\u0026quot;","Hermione, whose hair had doubled in size due to static electricity and sheer embarrassment, pulled the duvet up to her chin. \u0026quot;It was purely... purely structural support! For nightmares!\u0026quot;","Mrs. Weasley, whose heart rate was slowly returning to normal, looked from Harry to Hermione. Her expression shifted from terrified mother to Scandalized Matron to something overwhelmingly soft.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; she breathed, her hand going to her cheek. \u0026quot;Oh, bless you both.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bless them?\u0026quot; Ron spluttered. \u0026quot;Mum! They were... they were \u003cem\u003eknitted\u003c/em\u003e together!\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley, realizing there was no snake and no Voldemort, simply blinked, looking delightfully confused. \u0026quot;So... no one is bleeding? And the snake is not back?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just a python grip, Dad,\u0026quot; George quipped.","\u0026quot;Right. Good. Excellent,\u0026quot; Arthur beamed, tucking his wand away. \u0026quot;Well! Glad to see everyone is... comfortable. Very comfortable. Shall we, ah, give them a moment to... untie themselves?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m writing to Ginny,\u0026quot; Fred announced loudly to the room. \u0026quot;She owes me five galleons. She bet Easter, I said Christmas.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I did not bet!\u0026quot; Ginny’s voice drifted up from the stairs, sounding amused. \u0026quot;And I knew he was in there! Who do you think opened the door for her?\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a small, mortified squeak and buried her face in her hands.","\u0026quot;OUT!\u0026quot; Mrs. Weasley suddenly shooed everyone, clapping her hands. \u0026quot;Out, out, out! Give them some privacy to get dressed! Breakfast is getting cold! Fred, put that spatula down!\u0026quot;","She herded her husband and sons out of the room. Ron cast one last, traumatized look at the bed before being shoved into the hallway by George.","\u0026quot;Use protection!\u0026quot; Fred called out cheerfully just before the door slammed shut. \u0026quot;By which I mean a Shield Charm, of course!\u0026quot;","Silence returned to Percy\u0027s room.","Harry and Hermione sat there for a long moment, listening to the thundering footsteps retreat downstairs.","Harry looked at Hermione. Hermione peered through her fingers at Harry.","\u0026quot;Structural support?\u0026quot; Harry asked, his lips twitching.","\u0026quot;Oh, shut up, Harry,\u0026quot; Hermione groaned, turning scarlet. But she was smiling. And despite the chaos, the fear of the night before felt a million miles away."]},{"num":17,"origNum":17,"title":"The Ostrich Maneuver","wordCount":705,"paragraphs":["The journey from Percy\u0027s room to the kitchen felt less like walking down stairs and more like walking the plank. Harry and Hermione, now fully dressed (though Hermione’s hair was still vibrating with static electricity), hesitated at the bottom step.","The smell of frying bacon and Mrs. Weasley’s baking was usually welcoming, but today it carried the ominous scent of impending social doom.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re going to be unbearable, aren\u0027t they?\u0026quot; Harry whispered, adjusting his glasses.","\u0026quot;Worse,\u0026quot; Hermione whimpered. \u0026quot;Fred and George are involved. It will be a strategic campaign of humiliation.\u0026quot;","They pushed the door open.","The kitchen fell silent. It was a crowded affair. Mr. and Mrs. Weasley were at the stove, Ron was studiously staring at his toast, Ginny was smirking into her pumpkin juice, and the twins were leaning against the sink with identical, predatory grins. Sitting at the end of the table were Bill Weasley, looking amused, and Fleur Delacour, who looked radiant and entirely too interested.","\u0026quot;Ah!\u0026quot; Fred announced, clapping his hands. \u0026quot; The happy couple descends from their nest!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Morning, lovebirds,\u0026quot; George added, pulling out two chairs with an exaggerated flourish. \u0026quot;We\u0027ve saved you the seats nearest the radiator. Don\u0027t want you getting cold again. We know how much you struggle with... \u003cem\u003ethermal regulation\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Harry and Hermione sat down, keeping their eyes fixed firmly on the tablecloth.","\u0026quot;Sausage, dear?\u0026quot; Mrs. Weasley asked, bustling over and dropping three sausages onto Harry\u0027s plate with a wink. \u0026quot;You\u0027ll need your energy.\u0026quot;","Harry choked on his own saliva.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Bill said, leaning back in his chair and grinning at Harry. \u0026quot;I hear you\u0027ve been taking defensive fortification lessons. Fred tells me you\u0027ve mastered the \u0027Full Body Bind\u0027 without even using a wand.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It wasn\u0027t like that!\u0026quot; Harry protested, his face heating up. \u0026quot;I told you, she was just cold!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Very cold,\u0026quot; George nodded sagely. \u0026quot; Arctic , one might say. It’s a miracle you both survived without hypothermia. Good thing you generated so much... friction.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;GEORGE!\u0026quot; Mrs. Weasley shouted, though she was hiding a smile behind a tea towel.","Then, Fleur Delacour cleared her throat. She flipped her silvery-blonde hair over her shoulder and fixed Hermione with a critical, yet oddly approving, gaze.","\u0026quot;I think it is very sweet,\u0026quot; Fleur declared, her French accent cutting through the snickering. \u0026quot;But, \u0027Ermione, I must ask a question of technique.\u0026quot;","Hermione looked up, terrified. \u0026quot;Y-yes?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In France,\u0026quot; Fleur said, buttering a piece of toast delicately, \u0026quot;when we visit a gentleman\u0027s bedchamber in the middle of the night, there is usually a protocol. Tell me, did you at least kiss \u0027im before you jumped into bed? Or are British girls always so... direct?\u0026quot;","The table erupted. Ron spat pumpkin juice onto his plate. Ginny howled. Even Mr. Weasley’s shoulders were shaking.","Hermione turned a color that didn\u0027t exist in nature. It wasn\u0027t just red; it was a deep, nuclear crimson that seemed to radiate heat. She looked like a tomato that had held its breath for a week.","She opened her mouth to speak, but no sound came out. The sheer mortification was too much for human speech.","Desperate for cover, she did the only thing she could think of. She turned to her left, grabbed the front of Harry’s jumper, and buried her entire face into his chest, hiding from the world in the fabric of his Weasley sweater.","\u0026quot;Awwww!\u0026quot; Ginny cooed.","The kitchen exploded with laughter. Harry, now acting as a human shield for the second time that morning, awkwardly patted Hermione’s bushy hair while turning bright pink himself.","\u0026quot;Look at that!\u0026quot; Fred shouted over the noise, pointing a sausage at them. \u0026quot;Classic defensive posture! Head in the sand—or in the sweater, as it were!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I name this move!\u0026quot; George bellowed, raising his goblet of juice. \u0026quot;The Ostrich!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Ostrich!\u0026quot; Bill cheered, clinking his glass against George\u0027s.","\u0026quot;Stop it!\u0026quot; came a muffled, high-pitched voice from inside Harry’s jumper. \u0026quot;I am not an ostrich!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re a little bit of an ostrich, Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, grinning despite himself as the Weasleys cheered around them.","\u0026quot;I hate this house,\u0026quot; she grumbled into his chest, but she didn\u0027t let go. In fact, she held on tighter, proving that while she might be an ostrich, she was definitely Harry’s ostrich."]},{"num":18,"origNum":18,"title":"The Mirror and the Trap","wordCount":1077,"paragraphs":["The dungeon air was cool, but Harry was sweating. He stood in the center of Snape’s office, his wand raised, his breathing controlled.","\u0026quot;Again,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice devoid of its usual sneer. He looked tired, but his eyes were sharp. \u0026quot;Do not get complacent, Potter. The Dark Lord is relentless. \u003cem\u003eLegilimens!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The invasion was instant. A black spear of thought pierced Harry\u0027s mind, seeking the soft, vulnerable memories of fear. But Harry didn\u0027t panic. He didn\u0027t scramble.","He built the wall.","He didn\u0027t use stone or steel. He used the feeling of Petunia’s hand on his shoulder in the kitchen. He used Vernon’s roar of defense at the Ministry. He used the warmth of the Burrow and the \u0026quot;Ostrich\u0026quot; maneuver that had made the Weasleys laugh. He constructed a fortress of belonging.","The black spear struck the memory of Hermione’s hug and shattered.","Snape staggered back, his wand arm dropping. He looked at Harry, blinking rapidly, as if he had just walked into a glass door.","\u0026quot;You pushed me out,\u0026quot; Snape said softly, a note of genuine disbelief in his voice. \u0026quot;Complete expulsion. Not a shield, Potter... a battering ram.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I told you,\u0026quot; Harry said, lowering his wand, feeling a surge of triumphant exhaustion. \u0026quot;I\u0027m not alone in my head anymore.\u0026quot;","Snape straightened his robes, regaining his composure. He looked at Harry with a strange, unreadable expression—perhaps seeing, for the first time, the formidable wizard the boy was becoming, rather than just James Potter\u0027s son.","\u0026quot;Adequate,\u0026quot; Snape muttered. \u0026quot;Surprisingly... adequate. That will be all for tonight.\u0026quot;","The true test came two weeks later, in the dead of night.","Harry was asleep in the dormitory, the curtains of his four-poster drawn tight. The castle was silent, the grounds bathed in June moonlight.","Then, the pain hit.","It wasn\u0027t a dream. It was a summons. His scar seared white-hot, splitting his skull open. The dormitory vanished.","\u003cem\u003eHe was walking down a long, dark corridor. The Department of Mysteries. He knew this place. He walked through the black door, into the circular room, through the door of time...\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eAnd there, at the bottom of the stone pit, was a figure.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eSirius.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eSirius was on his knees. Voldemort was standing over him, his wand drawn. Cruciatus. Sirius screamed, the sound echoing off the stone benches. \u0026quot;Give it to me, Black! Take it down!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I\u0027ll never... get it...\u0026quot; Sirius gasped.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eVoldemort raised his wand again. \u0026quot;Maybe young Potter will be more cooperative when he sees your corpse...\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","Harry woke with a gasp, sitting bolt upright in bed. His pajamas were soaked in cold sweat. His scar was throbbing so hard it felt like it was bleeding.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Neville’s sleepy voice came from across the room. \u0026quot;Is it... is it him?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Harry choked out, clutching his forehead. \u0026quot;He’s got Sirius. He’s got him in the Department of Mysteries. He’s torturing him.\u0026quot;","The panic rose in his chest, hot and suffocating. \u003cem\u003esave him save him save him.\u003c/em\u003e The urge to run, to find a Thestral, to fly to London immediately, was overwhelming. It was exactly what he would have done a year ago.","But Harry Potter was not the same boy who had faced the dragon alone. He had been trained. He had a family. And he had a gift he hadn\u0027t forgotten.","\u003cem\u003eUse the mirror.\u003c/em\u003e","The thought cut through the panic like a knife. Sirius had given him the two-way mirror at Christmas. \u003cem\u003eIf you need me, Harry, just say my name.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry didn\u0027t run for the door. He scrambled to the foot of his bed, throwing open the lid of his trunk. He dug frantically through his robes, past the Marauder\u0027s Map, past the Invisibility Cloak, until his fingers closed around the cool, heavy glass of the square mirror.","He sat cross-legged on the floor, ignoring the pounding in his head. He held the mirror up to his face. He looked into his own terrified green eyes reflected in the glass.","\u0026quot;Sirius Black,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his voice trembling. \u0026quot;Sirius Black.\u0026quot;","For a second, nothing happened. Harry’s heart hammered against his ribs. \u003cem\u003eHe’s not there. He’s dying. It’s too late.\u003c/em\u003e","Then, the surface of the mirror clouded over. The reflection of the dormitory dissolved.","A face appeared.","It was Sirius. But he wasn\u0027t bleeding. He wasn\u0027t screaming. He was looking slightly flushed, holding a fork halfway to his mouth, with a napkin tucked into his collar.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Sirius said, chewing quickly and swallowing. He looked concerned. \u0026quot;Everything alright? It\u0027s nearly midnight.\u0026quot;","Harry stared. He let out a sound that was half-laugh, half-sob. The relief was so intense it made him dizzy.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re... you\u0027re eating?\u0026quot; Harry stammered.","\u0026quot;Lamb stew,\u0026quot; Sirius confirmed, holding up the fork. \u0026quot;Remus made it. Why? What’s happened? You look pale.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I saw you,\u0026quot; Harry gasped, wiping sweat from his eyes. \u0026quot;In my head. Voldemort... he showed me a vision. He was torturing you at the Ministry. In the Department of Mysteries. It felt so real, Sirius. I thought... I thought you were dying.\u0026quot;","Sirius’s face darkened instantly. The playfulness vanished, replaced by the hard, dangerous look of a man who had survived Azkaban.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s trying to bait you,\u0026quot; Sirius growled. \u0026quot;He knows we\u0027re close. He wanted you to rush to the Ministry to \u0027save\u0027 me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a trap,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, the realization settling in. \u0026quot;He wanted me to come and get the prophecy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And you didn\u0027t fell for it,\u0026quot; Sirius said, a fierce pride in his eyes. \u0026quot;You checked. You used the mirror. You used your head, Harry. That\u0027s my boy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is Remus there?\u0026quot; Harry asked, his hands finally stopping their shaking.","\u0026quot;Right here, Harry,\u0026quot; Remus Lupin’s voice came from the mirror, and his scarred face appeared next to Sirius’s. \u0026quot;You did the right thing. Stay at Hogwarts. Stay safe. We will alert Dumbledore immediately that Voldemort is trying to plant false visions.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Harry breathed, clutching the mirror tight. \u0026quot;Okay. I\u0027m staying put.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go back to sleep, Harry,\u0026quot; Sirius said gently. \u0026quot;I\u0027m safe. Grimmauld Place is unplottable. He can\u0027t get me here. And thanks to you... he won\u0027t get you tonight either.\u0026quot;","The connection faded, returning Harry to his own reflection. He sat there for a long moment in the dark dormitory, holding the mirror to his chest.","Voldemort had tried to use Harry’s love for his godfather as a weapon. But he had forgotten that love wasn\u0027t just a weakness; it was a communication channel. And tonight, the trap had snapped shut on empty air."]},{"num":19,"origNum":19,"title":"The Trap Sprung","wordCount":1080,"paragraphs":["The plan was madness, but it was \u003cem\u003eGryffindor\u003c/em\u003e madness.","After the conversation in the mirror, Harry hadn\u0027t gone back to sleep. He had stayed up with Sirius and Remus, formulating a counter-strike. Voldemort wanted Harry in the Department of Mysteries. He wanted the prophecy. If Harry didn\u0027t show, Voldemort would keep trying, keep baiting, perhaps targeting the Weasleys or Hermione next.","\u0026quot;We go,\u0026quot; Harry had told Sirius through the glass. \u0026quot;We spring the trap. But we do it on our terms. He thinks I\u0027m a panicked child running to save you. He won\u0027t expect me to be ready.\u0026quot;","Sirius, eyes gleaming with a reckless mix of Marauder mischief and Black family ferocity, had agreed. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll alert the Order. We\u0027ll be right behind you. Don\u0027t engage until we get there, Harry. Keep them talking.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Hall of Prophecy\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry walked down the aisle of towering shelves, the glass orbs glowing faintly in the gloom. Behind him walked Ron, Hermione, Neville, Ginny, and Luna. They weren\u0027t creeping; they were marching.","\u0026quot;This is it,\u0026quot; Harry said, stopping at row 97. \u0026quot;The one he wants.\u0026quot;","He reached out and took the small, dusty glass orb.","Immediately, the shadows around them lengthened. Twelve black-cloaked figures emerged from the darkness, their faces obscured by masks, blocking every exit.","Lucius Malfoy stepped forward, his voice dripping with triumphant malice. \u0026quot;Very good, Potter. Now, give it to me.\u0026quot;","Harry didn\u0027t tremble. He didn\u0027t back away. He held the prophecy casually, tossing it slightly in the air and catching it, his expression bored.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t think I will, Lucius,\u0026quot; Harry said calmly.","Malfoy froze. The use of his first name—and the utter lack of fear in the boy’s voice—was wrong. The script was broken.","\u0026quot;You are in a precarious position, Potter,\u0026quot; Bellatrix Lestrange shrieked from the shadows. \u0026quot;Look at you! Little baby Potter, playing with things he doesn\u0027t understand!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I understand plenty,\u0026quot; Harry retorted, his eyes scanning the perimeter, noting the positions of the Death Eaters. \u0026quot;I understand that you\u0027re hiding behind masks because you\u0027re afraid. I understand that your master is obsessed with a glass ball because he\u0027s insecure.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;How dare you!\u0026quot; Bellatrix screamed, raising her wand.","\u0026quot;Wait!\u0026quot; Lucius snapped. \u0026quot;We need the prophecy whole!\u0026quot; He turned back to Harry. \u0026quot;You are surrounded, boy. Give it to me, and perhaps we shall let your little friends go.\u0026quot;","Harry checked his watch. \u0026quot;You know, usually, this is the part where I yell and run. But I think I\u0027ll wait. My ride is almost here.\u0026quot;","Lucius narrowed his eyes. \u0026quot;What are you talking ab—\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The air in the chamber exploded with white smoke. High above, doors banged open. Figures in bright robes plummeted from the darkness, landing on the floor between the students and the Death Eaters.","Sirius Black, Remus Lupin, Alastor Moody, Tonks, and Kingsley Shacklebolt stood tall, wands drawn.","\u0026quot;Stay away from my godson,\u0026quot; Sirius barked, a savage grin on his face.","\u0026quot;Now!\u0026quot; Harry yelled.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eREDUCTO!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The six members of the D.A. fired not at the Death Eaters, but at the shelves. The towering structures groaned and tipped. Thousands of prophecies crashed to the floor, exploding in a chaotic cloud of pearly ghosts and glass shards.","In the confusion, the battle began.","It was chaos, but controlled chaos. Harry fought differently this time. He didn\u0027t panic. He moved with the efficiency Vernon had praised and the mental discipline Snape had drilled into him. He deflected a curse from Dolohov, sent a Stunner back that clipped the Death Eater’s shoulder, and spun to cover Neville.","\u0026quot;Harry! Go!\u0026quot; Sirius roared, dueling two Death Eaters at once, laughing as he parried their strikes.","\u0026quot;Not without you!\u0026quot; Harry shouted back, shielding Hermione from a falling shelf.","The battle drifted toward the dais with the ancient stone archway—the Veil.","Harry found himself fighting back-to-back with Sirius. It felt effortless. They moved like a single unit, Harry covering Sirius’s blind spots, Sirius blasting obstacles out of Harry’s path.","\u0026quot;Nice one, Harry!\u0026quot; Sirius yelled, ducking a jet of green light. \u0026quot;You fight like your father!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I fight better!\u0026quot; Harry retorted, disarming Malfoy with a sharp flick of his wrist.","Then, the temperature dropped. Bellatrix Lestrange scrambled atop the dais. Her face was twisted in a rictus of hate, her eyes fixed on Sirius, who was distracted by Macnair.","Harry saw it. He didn\u0027t need a vision; he saw the shift in her stance, the way she raised her wand, the malicious intent gathering in her eyes. It was the moment from his nightmares, the moment the world ripped apart.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eAvada—\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Bellatrix screamed.","Sirius turned, his eyes widening, too slow to dodge.","But Harry was ready. He didn\u0027t scream. He didn\u0027t freeze. He acted with the sheer, brute force of his will, channeling every ounce of his magical core.","He didn\u0027t cast a Shield Charm. He cast a physical banishing charm, not at Bellatrix, but at Sirius.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eDEPULSO!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The spell hit Sirius square in the chest. It didn\u0027t hurt him, but it launched him backward with the force of a cannonball. He flew five feet to the left, crashing hard onto the stone floor just as the jet of green light hissed through the space where his heart had been a second before.","The Killing Curse struck the Veil harmlessly, dissipating into the tattered cloth.","Bellatrix froze, her mouth open in shock. She had missed.","Sirius scrambled up, winded but alive. He looked at the Veil, then at Harry, realizing exactly how close he had come to falling through.","\u0026quot;You missed, Bella!\u0026quot; Harry shouted, stepping in front of his godfather, his wand pointed directly at Bellatrix’s heart. \u0026quot;He\u0027s not going anywhere!\u0026quot;","Bellatrix screamed in frustration, raising her wand again, but she was too late.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eExpelliarmus!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","It wasn\u0027t just Harry. It was Harry and Sirius together. Their twin red beams hit Bellatrix simultaneously. She was lifted off her feet and thrown backward, crashing into the stone steps of the dais, her wand clattering away into the darkness.","Sirius stood up, dusting off his robes. He looked at Harry, his grey eyes shining with a fierce, overwhelming pride. He reached out, gripping Harry’s shoulder hard enough to bruise.","\u0026quot;That,\u0026quot; Sirius breathed, his voice shaking slightly, \u0026quot;was a very close shave. Thank you, Harry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I told you,\u0026quot; Harry panted, adrenaline coursing through him. \u0026quot;I\u0027m prepared.\u0026quot;","Before they could celebrate, a high, cold voice echoed through the chamber, stopping every duel in the room.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eYou have failed me, Bella...\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;"]},{"num":20,"origNum":20,"title":"The Fortress Holds","wordCount":1175,"paragraphs":["The dust from the Hall of Prophecy had barely settled when Harry felt it.","It wasn\u0027t a pain in his scar, but a cold, heavy pressure in the air, a vacuum where happiness used to be. It was calling to him from the floors above.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Sirius asked, gripping Harry\u0027s shoulder, his face smeared with dust but alive.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s here,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice flat and hard. \u0026quot;In the Atrium.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re coming with you,\u0026quot; Remus said, stepping forward.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry ordered, turning to face them. \u0026quot;Secure the Death Eaters. Make sure Bellatrix doesn\u0027t wake up. This is between him, Dumbledore, and me.\u0026quot;","Without waiting for an argument, Harry sprinted for the lifts.","When the golden grilles opened onto the Atrium, the polished dark wood floor was empty. The golden Fountain of Magical Brethren stood silent.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter,\u0026quot; a high, cold voice whispered.","Lord Voldemort stepped out of the fireplace, green flames licking at his black robes. His red eyes locked onto Harry’s. \u0026quot;You have been a very troublesome child tonight. You robbed me of my prophecy. You robbed me of my servant\u0027s kill.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m not a child anymore,\u0026quot; Harry said, his wand held steady. \u0026quot;And you\u0027re not scary. You\u0027re just a bully with a wand.\u0026quot;","Voldemort’s eyes narrowed. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eAvada\u003c/em\u003e—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was foolish to come here tonight, Tom,\u0026quot; a calm voice echoed through the vast hall.","The air shimmered, and Albus Dumbledore appeared near the fountain. He looked ancient and terrible, radiating a power that made the very air vibrate.","\u0026quot;Dumbledore!\u0026quot; Voldemort spat, turning his wand on the Headmaster.","The duel that followed was unlike anything Harry had ever seen. It was a clash of titans. Dumbledore animated the statues of the fountain to shield Harry, while Voldemort conjured snakes of living fire that consumed the air. Water whipped like whips, silver shields shattered curses, and the sound of magic colliding was like thunder trapped in a box.","Voldemort, realizing he could not beat Dumbledore through brute force, vanished.","For a second, the Atrium was silent.","Then, Harry screamed.","It wasn\u0027t physical pain. It was an invasion. He fell to his knees, his wand clattering to the floor. His mind was suddenly flooded with icy, serpentine hatred.","\u003cem\u003eYou are weak,\u003c/em\u003e Voldemort’s voice hissed inside his skull. \u003cem\u003eYou are nothing. Let me in. Let me kill the old man through you.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry gasped, clawing at the floor. The pain was blinding. Voldemort was trying to seize control of his body, to use him as a puppet.","\u003cem\u003eLook at you,\u003c/em\u003e Voldemort taunted. \u003cem\u003eFull of grief. Full of fear.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry gritted out.","He didn\u0027t try to block the pain. He didn\u0027t try to hide. Instead, he opened the doors of his mind wide. But he didn\u0027t show Voldemort fear.","He showed him the Dursleys standing in front of him at the Ministry hearing.","He showed him Hermione sleeping in his arms at the Burrow, the feeling of absolute safety.","He showed him Sirius laughing as he ate stew in the mirror.","He showed him the Weasleys cheering \u0026quot;The Ostrich.\u0026quot;","He filled his mind with the one thing Voldemort could not understand, could not touch, and could not stand: \u003cem\u003eBelonging.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eGET OUT!\u003c/em\u003e Harry roared in his own mind.","He didn\u0027t just push; he struck. He weaponized his love and his family into a mental spear and drove it straight into the intruder.","In the physical world, Harry threw his head back and yelled.","A shadow was violently ejected from Harry’s body. It flew backward, hitting the floor and rolling, materializing back into the form of Voldemort. The Dark Lord scrambled to his feet, clutching his chest, looking at Harry with genuine shock and agony. He had not just been blocked; he had been burned.","At that exact moment, the fireplaces along the walls flared green.","Cornelius Fudge, still in his pajamas and cloak, stumbled out, followed by two Aurors. He stopped dead. His jaw dropped.","He looked at the destroyed fountain. He looked at Harry Potter, standing tall and fierce. He looked at Dumbledore. And finally, he looked at the snake-faced man standing at the end of the hall.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s back,\u0026quot; Fudge whispered, his face draining of all color. \u0026quot;Lord Voldemort. He\u0027s... he\u0027s actually back.\u0026quot;","Voldemort sneered, looking from Dumbledore to the Minister. With a swirl of his cloak and a crack like a whip, he Disapparated.","But the secret was out. The denial was over.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Headmaster\u0027s Office\u003c/strong\u003e","An hour later, the silence of Dumbledore’s office was a soothing balm after the cacophony of the Ministry. Fawkes the phoenix trilled softly from his perch.","Harry sat in a chair, holding a cup of tea. He was exhausted, but he felt strangely light. Sirius was alive. The world knew the truth.","Dumbledore sat behind his desk, looking at Harry with an expression of immense pride. Standing by the window, looking out at the dark grounds, was Severus Snape.","\u0026quot;Tonight was a turning point, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly. \u0026quot;You did not just save your godfather. You forced the Ministry to open its eyes. And you faced Voldemort and survived.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I didn\u0027t just survive,\u0026quot; Harry said, looking at his tea. \u0026quot;I hurt him. When he tried to possess me... he was scared.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot; Dumbledore nodded. \u0026quot;He sought to exploit what he perceived as your weakness—your emotions. He did not realize that your heart, nurtured as it has been by your family and friends, is a weapon he cannot withstand.\u0026quot;","Snape turned from the window. His black robes swished as he walked toward the desk. He looked down at Harry, his dark eyes searching.","\u0026quot;The Dark Lord is a master Legilimens,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice low. \u0026quot;I have known wizards of great power who crumbled under his mental assault in seconds. To expel him... and to do so with such violence that he was physically repelled...\u0026quot;","Snape paused. He looked at Harry, and for the first time in five years, the sneer was entirely absent.","\u0026quot;I did not think you capable of such discipline, Potter,\u0026quot; Snape admitted, the words clearly tasting strange in his mouth. \u0026quot;I believed your attachments to be a liability. It appears... I was mistaken.\u0026quot;","Harry looked up, meeting the Potions Master\u0027s gaze. \u0026quot;You told me to clear my mind, Professor. But I couldn\u0027t. So I filled it instead. With the people who care about me.\u0026quot;","Snape held his gaze for a moment longer, then gave a stiff, singular nod.","\u0026quot;An unorthodox technique,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;But... undeniably effective. Your mother would have been... impressed.\u0026quot;","It was the closest thing to a compliment Severus Snape had ever given.","Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;Go to bed, Harry. You have earned a lie-in. And I suspect a certain bushy-haired friend of yours is currently pacing a hole in the Gryffindor common room carpet waiting for you.\u0026quot;","Harry stood up, setting his cup down. \u0026quot;Goodnight, Professor Dumbledore. Goodnight, Professor Snape.\u0026quot;","As he walked to the door, he touched the two-way mirror in his pocket. He was tired, yes. But he wasn\u0027t afraid. Voldemort was back, but Harry Potter was ready. And he wasn\u0027t alone."]},{"num":21,"origNum":21,"title":"Validations and Victories","wordCount":789,"paragraphs":["The end of the term arrived with a strange sense of calm. The castle, usually buzzing with rumors, had fallen into a respectful silence around Harry. He wasn\u0027t just the Boy Who Lived anymore; he was the Boy Who Fought Off the Dark Lord (Again) and lived to tell the tale.","When the Hogwarts Express pulled into King’s Cross, the Dursleys were waiting. Vernon was wearing a new, particularly loud checked jacket, and he greeted Harry with a handshake that nearly dislocated his shoulder.","\u0026quot;Good to see you, son,\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, ignoring the stares of passing wizards. \u0026quot;You look... battle-hardened. A bit skinny, though. Petunia, we need to get some steak into him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He looks tired, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia fussed, patting Harry’s cheek. \u0026quot;Let\u0027s get you home.\u0026quot;","The drive back to Surrey was filled with Dudley’s recounting of his boxing championship (he had won the regional semi-final) and Vernon’s complaints about the motorway traffic. It was wonderfully, beautifully mundane.","When they finally settled into the kitchen at Number Four—Harry with a large glass of iced lemonade—he reached into his rucksack.","\u0026quot;I have something to show you,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;Two things, actually.\u0026quot;","First, he pulled out a copy of the \u003cem\u003eDaily Prophet\u003c/em\u003e he had picked up at the station. He slapped it onto the polished oak table1.","The headline screamed in moving block letters: \u003cstrong\u003eFUDGE RESIGNS! MINISTER BOWS OUT IN DISGRACE.\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Hah!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted, slamming his hand down on the table so hard the coasters jumped. \u0026quot;I knew it! The man was a charlatan!\u0026quot;","He snatched the paper, reading the article with gleeful vindication.","\u0026quot;‘\u003cem\u003eAdmitted to misleading the public\u003c/em\u003e’... ‘\u003cem\u003eGross negligence regarding the return of He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named\u003c/em\u003e’... ‘\u003cem\u003eFailure to secure the Dementors\u003c/em\u003e’...\u0026quot; Vernon read aloud, his voice rising in triumph.","He looked up at Harry, his face flushed with satisfaction. \u0026quot;This is the man who tried to put you on trial, Harry! The one who tried to snap your wand for saving Dudley! And now look at him. Resigning in disgrace while you’re still standing.\u0026quot;","Vernon tossed the paper back onto the table, looking immensely pleased with the workings of justice.","\u0026quot;It’s heads rolling, that’s what it is,\u0026quot; Vernon declared. \u0026quot;Incompetence always catches up with you, Petunia. I told you. You can’t run a government—magic or otherwise—by ignoring the facts. Good riddance to him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It gets better,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;Or, well, I hope you think so.\u0026quot;","He reached back into his bag and pulled out a heavy parchment envelope sealed with the Hogwarts crest.","\u0026quot;My O.W.L. results came in just before I left,\u0026quot; Harry said, handing the envelope to Petunia. \u0026quot;I wasn\u0027t sure how I\u0027d do. I mean, with the visions, and the Occlumency lessons, and the... well, the battling.\u0026quot;","Petunia opened the envelope with trembling fingers. She pulled out the parchment, her eyes scanning the list of grades. Her mouth formed a perfect ‘O’.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; she breathed. \u0026quot;Look.\u0026quot;","She laid the parchment flat.","\u003cstrong\u003eHARRY JAMES POTTER - ORDINARY WIZARDING LEVEL RESULTS\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eAstronomy:\u003c/strong\u003e Acceptable","\u003cstrong\u003eCare of Magical Creatures:\u003c/strong\u003e Exceeds Expectations","\u003cstrong\u003eCharms:\u003c/strong\u003e Exceeds Expectations","\u003cstrong\u003eDefense Against the Dark Arts:\u003c/strong\u003e Outstanding","\u003cstrong\u003eHerbology:\u003c/strong\u003e Exceeds Expectations","\u003cstrong\u003eHistory of Magic:\u003c/strong\u003e Dreadful (Harry winced; he had passed out during that one).","\u003cstrong\u003ePotions:\u003c/strong\u003e Exceeds Expectations","\u003cstrong\u003eTransfiguration:\u003c/strong\u003e Exceeds Expectations","\u0026quot;Outstanding?\u0026quot; Vernon read, peering over her shoulder. \u0026quot;In Defense Against the Dark Arts? Well, I should bloody well hope so! You’ve been practicing on the job!\u0026quot;","He looked at Harry, shaking his head in genuine amazement.","\u0026quot;You managed this,\u0026quot; Vernon said, tapping the paper, \u0026quot;while that Umbridge woman was breathing down your neck? While a dark wizard was trying to break into your brain? And while you were organizing a secret defense club?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I had good teachers,\u0026quot; Harry said, thinking of Sirius and Remus.","\u0026quot;You have grit, Harry,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected him, his chest puffing out with pride. \u0026quot;Seven O.W.L.s. You passed seven exams in the middle of a war. That is... well, that is extraordinary.\u0026quot;","Petunia was beaming, her eyes shining with tears. She looked at the results, then at Harry. She remembered the little boy she had taken in, the one she had worried would be crushed by the weight of his legacy2.","\u0026quot;You worked so hard,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered. \u0026quot;Your mother... Lily was always top of her class. She would be so proud of you, Harry. And so are we.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Top marks!\u0026quot; Dudley cheered, raising his glass of diet lemonade. \u0026quot;Does this mean you can do the magic to clean my room now?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No magic outside of school, Dudley,\u0026quot; Harry laughed.","\u0026quot;Worth a shot,\u0026quot; Dudley shrugged.","Vernon stood up, looking at the newspaper headline about the toppled Minister and the exam results of his nephew.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon announced decisively. \u0026quot;This calls for a celebration. Petunia, forget the salad. We’re ordering Chinese. And Harry—get the menus. You’ve earned the crispy duck.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":22,"origNum":22,"title":"Protocol and Panic","wordCount":867,"paragraphs":["The summer heatwave had turned the upstairs of Number Four, Privet Drive, into a slow-baking oven. Harry lay sprawled on top of his duvet, wearing only his pajama bottoms, one arm dangling off the side of the bed.","It was 2:00 AM. The house was silent, save for the rhythmic, chainsaw-like snoring of Vernon Dursley vibrating through the wall from the master bedroom.","Harry was drifting in that heavy, hazy space between sleep and wakefulness when he heard the door click.","He didn\u0027t reach for his wand this time. He knew that sound. It wasn\u0027t the stealthy creep of a threat; it was the hesitant, soft step of someone trying very hard not to squeak a floorboard.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; A whisper cut through the dark.","Harry blinked his eyes open, groggy. \u0026quot;Mione?\u0026quot;","Hermione was standing by his bed. She was wearing a pair of oversized t-shirt pajamas, her hair tied back in a messy bun. She looked nervous, shifting her weight from foot to foot, but there was a determined set to her jaw that Harry recognized. It was the same look she wore before answering a particularly difficult question in Transfiguration.","\u0026quot;I couldn\u0027t sleep,\u0026quot; she whispered, the standard excuse falling from her lips.","Harry smiled sleepily, shifting over to the wall to make space on the narrow mattress. \u0026quot;Come on, then. The Ostrich awaits.\u0026quot;","Hermione didn\u0027t move immediately. She took a deep breath. In the silence, Harry could almost hear the echo of Fleur Delacour’s voice from Christmas morning: \u003cem\u003e“Did you at least kiss ‘im before you jumped into bed?”\u003c/em\u003e","Hermione stepped forward. But instead of climbing under the duvet, she leaned down.","Harry’s eyes widened slightly as her face came closer. Before he could ask what she was doing, she pressed her lips to his.","It wasn\u0027t a desperate, adrenaline-fueled kiss like the one before the dragon 1, or a relief-filled one like outside the Hospital Wing2. It was soft, deliberate, and lingered just long enough to make Harry’s heart kick-start a frantic rhythm against his ribs.","She pulled back, her face flushed even in the moonlight.","\u0026quot;Protocol,\u0026quot; she squeaked.","Then, with the efficiency of a ripping band-aid, she scrambled onto the bed, dove under the sheet, and buried her burning face into Harry’s shoulder.","Harry lay there for a second, stunned, tasting vanilla and mint. Then, a slow, wide grin spread across his face. He wrapped his arm around her, pulling her close until there was no space left between them.","\u0026quot;Protocol?\u0026quot; Harry whispered into her hair, chuckling. \u0026quot;Is that what we\u0027re calling it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shut up, Harry,\u0026quot; came the muffled reply from his deltoid. \u0026quot;I\u0027m checking off the requirements. Fleur was very specific.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m not complaining,\u0026quot; Harry murmured, tightening his hold.","They settled into the familiar, tangled embrace that had horrified Ron and delighted the twins. The tension of the summer night melted away, replaced by the perfect, safe weight of her against him.","But as Harry’s breathing slowed, a sudden, terrifying realization hit him.","He stiffened.","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry hissed, poking her side.","\u0026quot;Mmm?\u0026quot; she mumbled, already half-asleep.","\u0026quot;You can\u0027t stay all night.\u0026quot;","Hermione groaned, tightening her grip on his waist. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t wanna go. Comfy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Harry whispered urgently. \u0026quot;I know it\u0027s comfy. But you have to go back to the guest room before 6:00 AM.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Why?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because of Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice laced with genuine panic.","Hermione lifted her head slightly, blinking at him. \u0026quot;Mr. Dursley? He likes me. He called me \u0027efficient\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry said grimly. \u0026quot;But he is also a man who believes in \u0027proper courtship\u00273. If he walks in here tomorrow morning to wake me up for a jog and finds a \u0027Gryffindor Pretzel\u0027 in his house...\u0026quot;","Harry shuddered.","\u0026quot;He won\u0027t hex us, Hermione. He\u0027s worse. He\u0027ll \u003cem\u003electure\u003c/em\u003e us.\u0026quot;","He looked at her with wide, terrified green eyes. \u0026quot;He\u0027ll sit on the end of the bed. He\u0027ll talk about \u0027respectable boundaries.\u0027 He might even bring out the charts he uses for drill sales. He’ll start planning the wedding, Hermione. He’ll ask about your dowry.\u0026quot;","Hermione’s eyes widened. She remembered Vernon’s intense, loud, and thorough interrogation about the kiss during Harry’s third year4. She imagined being woken up not by a gentle shake, but by Vernon Dursley booming about \u0026quot;efficiency in romance.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh god,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;You\u0027re right.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s an early riser,\u0026quot; Harry warned, checking the glowing hands of the alarm clock. \u0026quot;You have four hours. Then you have to ninja-roll out of here and back to the guest room. If we get caught, Dudley will never let us live it down. He still has the cricket bat, but he\u0027ll use it to guard the door to make sure we don\u0027t \u0027sin\u0027 again.\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a stifled giggle, snuggling back down into the crook of his neck.","\u0026quot;Four hours,\u0026quot; she agreed sleepily. \u0026quot;Wake me up at 5:55. And Harry?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If he catches us... I\u0027m blaming the nightmares. Or the Nargles.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Deal,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, closing his eyes. \u0026quot;Goodnight, Mione.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Goodnight, Harry.\u0026quot;","They fell asleep quickly, resting in the peaceful silence of Privet Drive, blissfully unaware that in the master bedroom, Vernon Dursley had just set his alarm for 5:30 AM to get an early start on the lawn."]},{"num":23,"origNum":23,"title":"The Morning After","wordCount":1173,"paragraphs":["At 5:30 AM sharp, Vernon Dursley’s internal alarm clock went off. It was a biologically ingrained mechanism honed by years of drill sales meetings and the necessity of beating the rush hour traffic on the M25.","He hauled himself out of bed, careful not to wake Petunia, and pulled on his dressing gown. He felt invigorated. The lawn was calling to him. But first, he decided to check on the boy. Harry had been looking peaky yesterday, and Vernon wanted to make sure he was up for a spot of \u0026quot;character-building\u0026quot; fence painting later that morning.","He walked down the landing, his slippers silent on the carpet. He reached Harry’s door and turned the handle quietly, preparing his usual booming \u0026quot;Rise and shine!\u0026quot; greeting.","He pushed the door open. The greeting died in his throat.","The morning light filtering through the curtains illuminated the scene perfectly. There, in the center of the narrow bed, was a tangled mass of limbs and Gryffindor colors. Harry was asleep on his back, one arm thrown over his head. Hermione was curled into his side, her head resting on his chest, her arm draped possessively over his stomach. Their legs were woven together in a knot that defied anatomical logic.","Vernon’s mustache bristled. His face began to purple. The \u0026quot;Proper Conduct\u0026quot; lecture loaded itself into his throat. \u003cem\u003eUnmarried! Under his roof! Boundaries! Efficiency in sleeping arrangements!\u003c/em\u003e","He opened his mouth to roar.","But then, he paused.","He looked at Harry’s face. Usually, even in sleep, the boy’s brow was furrowed, twitching with the nightmares of graveyards and snakes. But today? Harry looked... peaceful. His breathing was deep and even. He looked like a normal fifteen-year-old boy who felt completely safe.","Vernon remembered the hollow, haunted look in Harry’s eyes when he returned from the maze1. He remembered the way Harry had stood in the kitchen, trembling, terrified that he was bringing death to their doorstep2. He remembered the boy standing alone against Dementors to save Dudley3.","Vernon let out a long, slow breath through his nose. The purple hue faded from his face.","\u003cem\u003eThey\u0027ve fought dragons,\u003c/em\u003e Vernon thought, his grip on the doorknob loosening. \u003cem\u003eThey\u0027ve fought maniacs. Let them have a lie-in.\u003c/em\u003e","A small, uncharacteristic smile tugged at the corner of his mouth under the mustache. It was a look of grudging, protective approval.","He stepped back and pulled the door shut with a click so soft it was barely a whisper.","He padded back to the master bedroom. Petunia was just stirring.","\u0026quot;Vernon?\u0026quot; she murmured. \u0026quot;Is it time?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Petunia,\u0026quot; Vernon whispered, a conspiratorial gleam in his eye. \u0026quot;Come and look at this. Quietly.\u0026quot;","Intrigued, Petunia followed him. They crept back to Harry’s door. Vernon opened it an inch. Petunia peered through the gap.","She saw the \u0026quot;Ostrich\u0026quot; maneuver in full effect. She saw the girl who had offered to sleep on the floor to protect her nephew, now sleeping soundly in his arms.","Petunia pressed her hand to her cheek. Her eyes softened into that same look she had worn on Platform Nine and Three-Quarters4.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; she whispered. \u0026quot;Bless them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shall I wake them?\u0026quot; Vernon asked, though he already knew the answer.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t you dare,\u0026quot; Petunia hissed, smiling. \u0026quot;Let them sleep. But Vernon... not a word to Dudley. He\u0027ll never let them hear the end of it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Agreed,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded. \u0026quot;Operation Silent Morning.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003e8:30 AM: The Panic\u003c/strong\u003e","Sunlight blasted Harry in the face. It wasn\u0027t the soft, grey light of dawn; it was the bright, aggressive yellow of a fully started day.","Harry groaned, trying to roll over, but found he was pinned down by a warm, heavy weight. He blinked his eyes open. He was staring at a messy bun of brown hair.","\u0026quot;Mmm,\u0026quot; the hair mumbled. \u0026quot;Five more minutes.\u0026quot;","Harry’s brain rebooted slowly. \u003cem\u003eSunlight. Heavy weight. Hermione. Bedroom.\u003c/em\u003e","He looked at the alarm clock.","\u003cstrong\u003e8:30.\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry’s heart stopped.","\u0026quot;SHIT!\u0026quot;","He sat up so fast he nearly headbutted Hermione.","\u0026quot;Wh-what? Voldemort?\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked, scrambling up, her hair exploding in every direction.","\u0026quot;Worse!\u0026quot; Harry hissed, grabbing his glasses with trembling fingers. \u0026quot;The time! It\u0027s eight-thirty! We missed the window! We missed it by two and a half hours!\u0026quot;","Hermione looked at the clock and gasped, turning pale. \u0026quot;Oh no! Mr. Dursley! The lecture! The charts! Harry, I can\u0027t discuss dowries before coffee!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go! Go! Go!\u0026quot; Harry urged, throwing the duvet off.","It was a frenzy of activity. Hermione grabbed her pillow and sprinted for the door, doing a commando roll into the hallway. She paused, listened for footsteps, and then dashed for the guest room.","Harry frantically smoothed the sheets, tried to flatten his hair (useless), and threw on a fresh t-shirt, his heart pounding louder than it had in the Department of Mysteries.","\u003cstrong\u003e8:45 AM: The Breakfast of Champions\u003c/strong\u003e","Ten minutes later, Harry walked into the kitchen. He was trying for a look of casual, well-rested nonchalance.","\u0026quot;Morning,\u0026quot; he croaked.","\u0026quot;Morning, Harry!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed. He was sitting at the table, newspaper spread out, looking suspiciously cheerful.","\u0026quot;Morning, dear,\u0026quot; Petunia chirped from the stove. She was humming. She never hummed.","Dudley was sitting opposite Vernon, staring at his grapefruit with a look of profound misery. He looked up when Harry entered.","\u0026quot;Alright, Harry?\u0026quot; Dudley grunted. \u0026quot;You slept late. Mum wouldn\u0027t let me turn on the TV. Said the noise would disturb the \u0027atmosphere\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh. Right. Sorry,\u0026quot; Harry muttered, sliding into his seat.","A moment later, Hermione entered. She was dressed, her hair was brushed (mostly), and she was carrying a book as a prop of innocence.","\u0026quot;Good morning, everyone,\u0026quot; she said brightly—too brightly. \u0026quot;I just woke up. In the guest room. Where I slept. All night.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good morning, Hermione!\u0026quot; Vernon declared, beaming at her. \u0026quot;Sleep well? Mattress comfortable? Enough... warmth?\u0026quot;","Hermione froze mid-step. \u0026quot;Y-yes. Perfectly adequate. Thank you.\u0026quot;","She sat down next to Harry. They exchanged a terrified glance.","Something was wrong. The Dursleys weren\u0027t angry. They weren\u0027t lecturing. They were... \u003cem\u003egrinning\u003c/em\u003e.","Vernon folded his newspaper slowly. He looked at Harry. Then he looked at Hermione. Then he looked at the ceiling, whistling a jaunty tune.","Petunia placed a stack of pancakes on the table—not grapefruit, actual pancakes—and gave Harry a wink. A literal wink.","Dudley looked between his parents, totally lost. \u0026quot;What\u0027s going on? Why are you two looking like the cat that got the cream?\u0026quot;0","\u0026quot;Nothing, Dudders,\u0026quot; Vernon said, his eyes twinkling. \u0026quot;Just enjoying a lovely family morning. Isn\u0027t that right, Petunia?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lovely,\u0026quot; Petunia agreed, pouring tea. \u0026quot;So quiet. So peaceful.\u0026quot;","Harry stared at his plate. He felt a bead of sweat roll down his neck. They knew. They definitely knew.","Hermione was gripping her fork so hard her knuckles were white. She was staring at the pancakes as if they were cursed objects.","Vernon cleared his throat. The sound echoed in the silent kitchen like a gavel strike.","He leaned forward, resting his elbows on the table, fixing Harry and Hermione with a look of triumphant, mischievous knowledge.","\u0026quot;Sooo........\u0026quot; Vernon drawled, prolonging the word until it hung in the air like a guillotine."]},{"num":24,"origNum":24,"title":"The Great Grill of Privet Drive","wordCount":872,"paragraphs":["\u0026quot;Sooo........\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley repeated, buttering his toast with the slow, deliberate precision of a man who held all the cards. \u0026quot;I was just wondering about the structural integrity of the house.\u0026quot;","Harry stared at his pancakes. \u0026quot;The... structural integrity?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded gravely. \u0026quot;I heard creaking. Significant creaking. Around 2:00 AM. It sounded like a stealth mission gone wrong. Tell me, Hermione, did you find the guest room... drafty? Or perhaps the gravitational pull was just stronger in the room down the hall?\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a sound like a deflating balloon. \u0026quot;I... the wind... the Nargles...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Nargles,\u0026quot; Petunia chimed in, sipping her tea with an innocent smile. \u0026quot;Are those the creatures that force young ladies to abandon their assigned beds and sneak into their boyfriends\u0027 rooms in the dead of night?\u0026quot;","Harry choked on his orange juice.","\u0026quot;We didn\u0027t sneak!\u0026quot; Harry protested, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;Well, we did sneak, but not for... not for \u003cem\u003ethat\u003c/em\u003e! It was nightmares! Just sleeping! Structural support!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Structural support,\u0026quot; Vernon mused, his eyes dancing. \u0026quot;Is that what the kids are calling it these days? In my day, we called it \u0027canoodling\u0027. And let me tell you, Harry, for a boy who sleeps like a log, you certainly looked very... \u003cem\u003ecomfortable\u003c/em\u003e when I checked on you at five-thirty.\u0026quot;","The silence that followed was absolute.","Harry’s jaw dropped. Hermione looked as if she wanted the floor to open up and swallow her whole.","\u0026quot;You... you checked?\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;I did,\u0026quot; Vernon confirmed. \u0026quot;And I must say, very efficient use of space. Not an inch of mattress wasted. A true marvel of spatial engineering.\u0026quot;","It was at this precise moment that Dudley Dursley’s brain finally finished processing the data.","He looked at Harry’s scarlet face. He looked at Hermione’s trembling hands. He looked at his father’s triumphant grin.","The realization hit him like a Bludger.","\u0026quot;NO WAY!\u0026quot; Dudley bellowed, dropping his spoon.","He looked from Harry to Hermione, his eyes bulging. \u0026quot;You two? In the bed? The whole night? And Dad caught you?\u0026quot;","Dudley’s face turned a violent shade of red, his cheeks puffed out, and then—","\u003cem\u003ePFFFFFT!\u003c/em\u003e","A spray of grapefruit juice erupted from his mouth, missing the table but hitting the kitchen cabinets.","\u0026quot;BWAHAHAHAHA!\u0026quot;","Dudley didn\u0027t just laugh; he detonated. He slammed his hand on the table, threw his head back, and roared. It was a deep, guttural sound of pure, unadulterated sibling mockery.","\u0026quot;The cricket bat!\u0026quot; Dudley wheezed, clutching his ribs, tears streaming down his face. \u0026quot;I forgot... the cricket bat! I left the post unmanned! The fortress was breached! Hahahaha!\u0026quot;","He was laughing so hard he slid slightly out of his chair. \u0026quot;Harry! You dog! And Hermione! The prefect! Sneaking around like... like ninjas! Oh my god, I can\u0027t breathe!\u0026quot;","Hermione could take no more. The combined force of Vernon’s interrogation and Dudley’s nuclear laughter broke her.","She dropped her fork. She turned in her chair. And with a speed that would have impressed a Seeker, she grabbed the front of Harry’s t-shirt, yanked him toward her, and buried her entire head into his chest, covering her ears with her hands.","She went completely still. If she couldn\u0027t see them, they couldn\u0027t see her.","The laughter cut off instantly, replaced by confusion.","The Dursleys stared at the sudden disappearance of Hermione’s face. Vernon blinked. Petunia leaned forward. Dudley paused mid-wheeze, wiping a tear from his eye.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Vernon asked, pointing his knife at the bundle of brown hair currently trying to merge with Harry’s sternum. \u0026quot;Is she... is she alright? Is she having a seizure?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is she looking for something in your shirt?\u0026quot; Dudley gasped, still giggling.","Harry sighed, a long, weary sound of a man accepting his fate. He awkwardly patted Hermione’s head, much like he had done at the Burrow.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry explained, his voice flat. \u0026quot;She\u0027s hiding. She refuses to acknowledge reality.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But... why is she in your chest?\u0026quot; Petunia asked, bewildered. \u0026quot;Is this a wizarding custom?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s a move,\u0026quot; Harry said tiredly. \u0026quot;The Weasleys invented the name. We call it \u0027The Ostrich\u0027.\u0026quot;","Vernon looked at the girl burying her head in his nephew’s shirt to escape social embarrassment. He looked at Harry, who was tolerating it with the patience of a saint.","For a second, there was silence.","Then, Vernon Dursley let out a snort.","\u0026quot;The Ostrich!\u0026quot; Vernon roared.","\u0026quot;The Ostrich!\u0026quot; Petunia shrieked, dissolving into giggles.","The dam broke. The three Dursleys erupted into a gale of laughter that shook the kitchen windows. It was louder than the TV, louder than the drill factory. They laughed until they were gasping for air, clutching their sides.","\u0026quot;Oh, that is rich!\u0026quot; Vernon wiped his eyes with a napkin, wheezing. \u0026quot;Head in the sand! Perfect! Absolutely perfect! Oh, Harry, she\u0027s a keeper! A literal Ostrich!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Stop iiiiiiiit!\u0026quot; Hermione wailed into Harry’s chest, her voice muffled and vibrating against his ribs.","\u0026quot;Never!\u0026quot; Dudley howled, banging the table. \u0026quot;This is the best breakfast ever!\u0026quot;","Harry looked down at the top of Hermione’s head, then at his roaring, red-faced, Muggle family. He couldn\u0027t help it. He started laughing too.","\u0026quot;You can come out now, Ostrich,\u0026quot; Harry whispered into her ear. \u0026quot;I think they approve.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am living in this shirt forever,\u0026quot; Hermione mumbled back. \u0026quot;Forward my mail.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":25,"origNum":25,"title":"The Ostrich Returns","wordCount":766,"paragraphs":["The laughter in the kitchen had finally subsided to occasional snorts and wipes of teary eyes. The Dursleys were catching their breath, and Hermione had tentatively emerged from the sanctuary of Harry’s t-shirt, her face a bright, blotchy pink, but regaining some semblance of dignity. She smoothed her hair, avoiding eye contact with everyone.","Vernon took a long sip of his cold tea, his mustache twitching with leftover mirth. He looked at Harry, rewinding the conversation in his head.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Vernon chuckled, shaking his head. \u0026quot;‘The Ostrich’. Very witty, those Weasley twins. I suppose they saw you doing... something similar?\u0026quot;","He paused. The smile froze on his face. The gears in his head turned with audible precision.","\u0026quot;Wait a minute,\u0026quot; Vernon said slowly, setting his cup down. \u0026quot;You said the Weasleys \u003cem\u003enamed\u003c/em\u003e the move.\u0026quot;","Harry froze. He had hoped, against all hope, that the detail would slip by. But Vernon Dursley, despite his aversion to magic, had the sharp instincts of a man who could spot a bad drill contract from a mile away.","\u0026quot;Did I?\u0026quot; Harry squeaked, his voice jumping an octave.","\u0026quot;You did,\u0026quot; Vernon confirmed, his eyes narrowing, though the twinkle remained. \u0026quot;You said, \u0027The Weasleys invented the name.\u0027 Which implies...\u0026quot;","Vernon leaned forward, the table creaking under his elbows.","\u0026quot;Harry. \u003cem\u003eWhat happened at the Burrow?\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a small, terrified whimper.","\u0026quot;Well?\u0026quot; Petunia asked, leaning in, her curiosity piqued. \u0026quot;You told us you were sleeping in Percy\u0027s room. Alone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I was!\u0026quot; Harry protested, holding his hands up. \u0026quot;I was! But... it was Christmas! And there were nightmares! And... well...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Spit it out, boy!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, though he looked ready to burst with glee.","\u0026quot;She came into my room!\u0026quot; Harry blurted out, abandoning all loyalty to save his own skin. \u0026quot;It was freezing! We fell asleep! And in the morning... Ron walked in.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ron walked in?\u0026quot; Dudley gasped, leaning forward, entranced.","\u0026quot;Ron walked in,\u0026quot; Harry confirmed, covering his face with his hands. \u0026quot;And we were... sort of... knotted. Like a pretzel. A Gryffindor Pretzel. He screamed. The twins came running with spatulas. Mr. Weasley had his wand out. They thought I was being strangled.\u0026quot;","Harry peeked through his fingers. \u0026quot;And then we went to breakfast... and Fleur asked Hermione if she’d kissed me first... and Hermione did \u003cem\u003ethis\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Harry pointed to his chest.","The kitchen went silent for one heartbeat.","Then, everyone looked at Hermione.","She was sitting perfectly still. But a color transformation was taking place that defied science. She went from pink, to red, to a shade of scarlet so deep she looked like she was about to spontaneously combust. She looked exactly as she had that morning at the Burrow—a tomato that had given up on life.","She made a small, high-pitched noise like a kettle boiling over.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;I simply can\u0027t.\u0026quot;","And with the speed of a striking cobra, she turned, grabbed Harry’s t-shirt again, and \u003cstrong\u003ethump\u003c/strong\u003e.","She was back. Head buried. Hands over ears. The Ostrich had returned to its natural habitat.","\u0026quot;I am not here,\u0026quot; her muffled voice vibrated against Harry’s ribs. \u0026quot;I am in the library. Leave a message.\u0026quot;","The sight of the brilliant, terrifyingly smart witch reducing herself to a human lawn dart for the second time in ten minutes was simply too much.","This time, the explosion was catastrophic.","\u0026quot;BWAH-HA-HA-HA!\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley didn\u0027t just laugh; he collapsed. He actually slid out of his chair and onto the linoleum floor, clutching his stomach, his legs kicking in the air.","\u0026quot;A PRETZEL!\u0026quot; Vernon roared at the ceiling, tears streaming down his face into his ears. \u0026quot;SPATULAS! SHE DID IT IN FRONT OF THE WHOLE FAMILY!\u0026quot;","Dudley was gone. He had fallen off his chair onto the floor next to his father, pounding the ground with his fist, wheezing silently because his lungs had stopped working.","\u0026quot;The... the Ostrich!\u0026quot; Dudley gasped, pointing a shaking finger at Harry’s chest. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s a lifestyle!\u0026quot;","Even Petunia lost the battle. She was clutching the edge of the sink to stay upright, her knees buckling, shrieking with laughter. \u0026quot;Oh! Oh, stop! My makeup! Harry, stop! Look at her!\u0026quot;","Harry sat in the middle of the chaos, shaking with laughter himself, one hand resting on the back of the girl currently hiding in his shirt.","\u0026quot;You realize,\u0026quot; Harry shouted over the noise of Vernon rolling around on the floor, \u0026quot;that you\u0027re making it worse, Mione?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t care!\u0026quot; came the stubborn, muffled reply. \u0026quot;Tell me when they\u0027re dead from lack of oxygen!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, Lord,\u0026quot; Vernon wheezed from the floor, wiping his eyes with his sleeve. \u0026quot;Best... best summer... ever.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":26,"origNum":26,"title":"The Art of the Deal","wordCount":1262,"paragraphs":["The heat of July mellowed into a pleasant, breezy August. With Hermione back at her parents’ house, Number Four, Privet Drive, felt significantly quieter, though the phantom echoes of the \u0026quot;Ostrich Incident\u0026quot; still lingered in the hallways.","Petunia, scandalized by the sheer volume of laughter that had occurred that morning, had issued a strict edict: \u003cem\u003eNo mention of flightless birds or pretzels at the dinner table.\u003c/em\u003e","Dudley, however, found ways around the ban. He would occasionally walk past Harry in the hallway, tuck his head into his collar, and make a soft \u003cem\u003ehonking\u003c/em\u003e noise. Harry didn\u0027t mind. In fact, he usually dissolved into silent giggles with his cousin. It was a shared joke, a battle scar from the war of romance, and it made the house feel more like a home than ever.","On a Tuesday afternoon, just as Petunia was setting out a lunch of cold cuts and potato salad, the doorbell rang. It wasn\u0027t the sharp, impatient ring of a salesman, but a polite, melodic chime.","Vernon wiped his mouth with a napkin. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll get it. Probably the package from the catalogue.\u0026quot;","He opened the door and stopped. Standing on the doorstep, wearing a violently purple velvet suit that somehow looked dashing rather than ridiculous, was Albus Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;Good afternoon, Vernon,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, bowing slightly.","Usually, the sight of a wizard on the doorstep would have sent Vernon into a panic about the neighbours. But this was Dumbledore—the man who had defended Harry in court, the man who was leading the fight against the maniac who had threatened Dudley.","\u0026quot;Headmaster!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, stepping back and opening the door wide. \u0026quot;Come in, come in! Don\u0027t stand on the ceremony. We were just sitting down to lunch.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I would be delighted to join you,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;I must confess, I have a weakness for Petunia’s potato salad. Harry mentioned it in a letter.\u0026quot;","The lunch was a surreal but pleasant affair. Dumbledore sat between Dudley and Harry, discussing the finer points of championship boxing with Dudley (\u0026quot;It sounds remarkably like dueling, only with more concussions,\u0026quot; Dumbledore noted) and complimenting Petunia on the crispness of her lettuce.","Once the plates were cleared and tea was poured, Dumbledore’s expression turned serious, though his eyes retained their twinkle.","\u0026quot;I am afraid, however, that this is not purely a social call,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, placing his teacup down. \u0026quot;I have a favor to ask of you, Harry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Anything, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said immediately.","\u0026quot;I need your help to recruit an old colleague of mine. A man named Horace Slughorn.\u0026quot;","Vernon leaned forward, his business instincts tingling. \u0026quot;Recruit? Is he a difficult hire?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is... retired,\u0026quot; Dumbledore explained delicately. \u0026quot;And he is determined to stay that way. Horace is a man who appreciates his comforts and his safety. With Voldemort back, he has gone into hiding.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Why him?\u0026quot; Petunia asked. \u0026quot;Is he a great fighter?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said darker. \u0026quot;But he was a teacher at Hogwarts for a long time. He taught Tom Riddle.\u0026quot;","The name sucked the warmth out of the room. Dudley stopped eating his biscuit.","\u0026quot;He taught Voldemort?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;He did. And he possesses information—memories—that are vital to our understanding of how Riddle became who he is today. I need him back at Hogwarts, where I can... encourage him to share them.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore turned his blue eyes to Harry. \u0026quot;But Horace has a weakness. He likes to collect people. Famous people, talented people, powerful people. He likes to be the spider in the center of the web, connecting the influential. He calls it his \u0027Slug Club\u0027.\u0026quot;","Vernon nodded slowly, a look of recognition dawning on his face. \u0026quot;Ah. A networker. A social climber. I know the type. We have them in the drill association. Men who don\u0027t want to do the work, but want to know the man who does.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled. \u0026quot;And you, Harry... you are the crown jewel he is missing. The Boy Who Lived. The Chosen One. If he sees you, if he thinks he can add you to his collection... he won\u0027t be able to resist returning to Hogwarts.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So, I\u0027m the bait,\u0026quot; Harry said flatly.","\u0026quot;You are the signing bonus,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected him, sitting up straighter.","Vernon Dursley’s face shifted. The jovial uncle vanished, replaced by the sharp, ruthless Executive of Grunnings Drills. He looked at Harry with a critical, appraising eye.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon declared, pushing his tea aside. \u0026quot;If we’re going to close this deal, Harry, you can\u0027t just walk in there and ask him nicely. You need a strategy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A strategy?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;This Slughorn fellow,\u0026quot; Vernon began, using his fork to emphasize his points. \u0026quot;He wants you. You are a high-value asset. Supply and demand, Harry. Right now, the demand is high, but if you look too eager, the value drops.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore watched Vernon with fascination, his eyebrows rising.","\u0026quot;Listen to me,\u0026quot; Vernon instructed, his voice dropping to a coaching growl. \u0026quot;When we go in there, you don\u0027t beg. You don\u0027t plead. You don\u0027t say, \u0027Please, sir, come back to teach.\u0027 You play it cool.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cool?\u0026quot; Harry repeated.","\u0026quot;Aloof!\u0026quot; Vernon clarified. \u0026quot;You act like you’re doing \u003cem\u003ehim\u003c/em\u003e a favor by being there. Let him look at you. Let him see the scar. But make him work for your attention. If he asks you a question, give him a mysterious answer. If he mentions your fame, shrug it off like it bores you.\u0026quot;","Vernon stood up, pacing the small kitchen like he was in a boardroom.","\u0026quot;It’s the Soft Sell, Harry. You dangle the carrot. You let him think that by coming to Hogwarts, he’ll get exclusive access to the Harry Potter brand. But you make him fear that if he \u003cem\u003edoesn\u0027t\u003c/em\u003e come, he’ll miss out on the biggest opportunity of his life.\u0026quot;","Vernon turned to Dumbledore. \u0026quot;Am I reading this man right, Headmaster? Does he fear irrelevance?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You have read him to the letter, Vernon,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, looking genuinely stunned. \u0026quot;I dare say you understand Horace better than I do.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;People are the same everywhere, magic or not,\u0026quot; Vernon sniffed dismissively. \u0026quot;Ego is a universal currency.\u0026quot;","He turned back to Harry, gripping his nephew\u0027s shoulders.","\u0026quot;Shoulders back, Harry. Look him in the eye. Be polite, but distant. Make him feel that you are the prize to be won. And when Dumbledore makes the offer... you just look at Slughorn and give him a little smile. Just a little one. Like you know something he doesn\u0027t.\u0026quot;","Harry took a deep breath, absorbing the lesson. He imagined he was Malfoy for a second—arrogant, important, untouchable.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Harry said, nodding. \u0026quot;I can do that. I\u0027ll be the prize.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That\u0027s my boy,\u0026quot; Vernon beamed, slapping Harry on the back. \u0026quot;Go get him. Close the deal.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore stood up, his robes swishing. He looked from Vernon—red-faced, large, and brimming with Muggle corporate tactics—to Harry, who was now standing with a newfound, calculated confidence.","\u0026quot;I must say,\u0026quot; Dumbledore murmured, offering his arm to Harry. \u0026quot;I have spent fifty years studying the complexities of the magical mind. And yet, I believe I have learned more about Slytherin negotiation tactics in the last ten minutes at a kitchen table in Surrey than I did in a lifetime at school. Vernon, you are a formidable man.\u0026quot;","Vernon puffed out his chest, adjusting his tie. \u0026quot;Just common sense, Headmaster. Now, go on. Don\u0027t let him haggle.\u0026quot;","Harry took Dumbledore’s arm. The kitchen dissolved into the squeezing darkness of Apparition, leaving the Dursleys to finish their potato salad, confident that whatever dark wizards lay ahead, they didn\u0027t stand a chance against the sales techniques of Grunnings Drills."]},{"num":27,"origNum":27,"title":"The Soft Sell","wordCount":1070,"paragraphs":["The house in Budleigh Babberton smelled of old dust and dragon blood. Horace Slughorn, wearing silk pajamas and looking remarkably like a walrus in distress, was standing in the middle of a living room that had, moments ago, been a scene of chaotic destruction.","Dumbledore had already performed the introductions, efficiently repairing the room with a wave of his wand. Now, the silence stretched. Slughorn was eyeing Harry with a mixture of wariness and hunger.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Slughorn said, his eyes darting to the lightning bolt scar on Harry’s forehead. \u0026quot;This is him. Harry Potter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hello, sir,\u0026quot; Harry said politely, but he didn\u0027t step forward. He stayed by the door, leaning casually against the frame, his hands in his pockets.","He channeled Vernon. \u003cem\u003eShoulders back. Aloof. You are the prize.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I’ve heard a great deal about you,\u0026quot; Slughorn murmured, moving closer. \u0026quot;The Boy Who Lived. And now... the Chosen One, they say?\u0026quot;","Harry shrugged, a motion of supreme indifference. \u0026quot;People say a lot of things. Usually to sell newspapers.\u0026quot;","Slughorn blinked. He had expected eagerness. He had expected a boy desperate to impress a former Head of House. Instead, he was looking at a young man who looked like he had better places to be.","\u0026quot;You are... modest,\u0026quot; Slughorn noted, tilting his head. \u0026quot;Very like your mother. Lily was a favorite of mine. Extraordinary talent. You have her eyes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Harry said simply. He checked his watch—a calculated move Vernon had suggested to imply his time was valuable. \u0026quot;Professor Dumbledore said you might be coming back to teach. It would be... interesting. Hogwarts has been rather dull lately.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dull?\u0026quot; Slughorn spluttered. \u0026quot;With You-Know-Who back? With the Ministry in shambles?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Like I said,\u0026quot; Harry said coolly, meeting Slughorn’s gaze. \u0026quot;Predictable. We need someone who understands talent. Real talent. Not just... politics.\u0026quot;","He gave Slughorn the smile—the small, knowing smile Vernon had coached him on. The smile that said, \u003cem\u003eI know where the power is, do you?\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I imagine,\u0026quot; Harry added softly, turning slightly as if to leave, \u0026quot;that a man of your... collection... would find the current crop of students quite fascinating. If you were there, of course.\u0026quot;","The hook was baited. Slughorn looked at Dumbledore, then at Harry—the most famous wizard in the age, standing there, offering a subtle invitation into the inner circle of history.","Slughorn’s resolve crumbled like dry parchment.","\u0026quot;Alright!\u0026quot; Slughorn barked, throwing his hands up. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll do it! I\u0027ll come out of retirement! But I want a salary increase, Dumbledore! And a new office! And... and Potter! I expect you in my class!\u0026quot;","Harry turned back, his expression neutral. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll see if I can fit it in my schedule, sir.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Debrief\u003c/strong\u003e","An hour later, the cool night air of Privet Drive greeted them. Dumbledore side-along Apparated Harry to the end of the street.","\u0026quot;A masterclass, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled, his eyes twinkling in the streetlamp light. \u0026quot;I believe poor Horace never stood a chance. He was practically packing his trunk before we walked out the door.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I had good coaching,\u0026quot; Harry grinned.","He walked up the garden path and opened the front door. The Dursleys were exactly where he had left them—sitting at the kitchen table, though the potato salad had been replaced by cups of tea.","Vernon looked up sharply as Harry entered. \u0026quot;Well? Did you close?\u0026quot;","Harry nodded, pouring himself a glass of water. \u0026quot;He\u0027s in. He asked for a raise and a new office, but he took the job.\u0026quot;","Vernon slammed his hand on the table, triumphant. \u0026quot;Hah! The Soft Sell! Works every time! You made him feel like he needed you more than you needed him, didn\u0027t you?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I checked my watch,\u0026quot; Harry recounted, sitting down. \u0026quot;I shrugged when he called me the Chosen One. And I told him I\u0027d \u0027see if I could fit him in\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Brilliant!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, beaming with pride. \u0026quot;Absolutely brilliant! That, Harry, is how you handle talent. You don\u0027t chase; you attract. You\u0027re learning, boy! You could have a future in drills yet!\u0026quot;","Petunia smiled, topping up Harry\u0027s tea. \u0026quot;We\u0027re just glad you\u0027re going back to a school that actually has teachers, dear.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And that you didn\u0027t have to fight him,\u0026quot; Dudley added, looking up from a comic book. \u0026quot;Did he look like a walrus? Dad said he sounded like a walrus type.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly like a walrus,\u0026quot; Harry confirmed.","\u003cstrong\u003eDiagon Alley\u003c/strong\u003e","A week later, the sky was a heavy, slate grey as Harry stepped out of the fireplace at the Leaky Cauldron. He brushed the soot from his robes and walked out into the courtyard.","He was alone this time. Mrs. Weasley had offered to accompany him, and Hagrid had sent an owl, but Harry had politely declined. He was sixteen now. He had faced Voldemort in the Ministry. He had faced Dementors in Little Whinging. He could handle school shopping.","Diagon Alley was changed. The vibrant, chaotic joy of his first visit was gone. The street was quieter, the shoppers moving quickly in tight clusters. Posters of wanted Death Eaters plastered the shop fronts, their moving faces sneering at passersby. Several shops were boarded up.","But Harry didn\u0027t feel the fear that seemed to radiate from the other shoppers. He walked with a steady, purposeful stride. He felt the wand in his pocket—the holly and phoenix feather that had saved him so many times. He felt the protection of the Dursleys\u0027 home still humming in his blood.","He stopped at Madam Malkin’s for new robes—he had grown a few inches over the summer, thanks to Petunia’s cooking. He visited Flourish and Blotts, picking up his books. Since he knew Slughorn was returning, he knew his \u0027Exceeds Expectations\u0027 in Potions 1 would be enough to continue to N.E.W.T. level, so he boldly purchased \u003cem\u003eAdvanced Potion-Making\u003c/em\u003e.","As he walked past the boarded-up windows of Ollivanders—the wandmaker having vanished weeks ago—Harry paused.","The war was here. The world was darker, colder, and more dangerous. People stared at him as he passed—some with hope, some with fear, whispering \u0026quot;The Chosen One\u0026quot; behind their hands.","Harry adjusted his bag on his shoulder. He didn\u0027t shrug it off this time. He didn\u0027t check his watch or feign indifference. He simply looked ahead, toward Gringotts and the future.","He had a prophecy to fulfil. He had a Dark Lord to defeat. And he had a Potions Master to charm.","Harry Potter blended into the crowd and headed for the station. He was ready."]},{"num":28,"origNum":28,"title":"Shadows and Steam","wordCount":1103,"paragraphs":["The trip to Diagon Alley had been efficient, largely thanks to Vernon’s advice on maintaining a \u0026quot;high-value\u0026quot; demeanor, which Harry had found worked just as well on shopkeepers as it did on Slughorn. But as the sun began to dip, casting long shadows over the cobblestones, Harry felt the familiar tug of suspicion.","He had spotted a shock of platinum blond hair disappearing down the turn toward Knockturn Alley.","Pulling his Invisibility Cloak tight around himself, Harry slipped away from the bustling crowds of Diagon Alley and plunged into the gloom. The air here was colder, smelling of mildew and dark magic. He moved silently, his trainers making no sound on the grime-streaked stones, tracking Draco Malfoy.","Malfoy was walking with a hurried, nervous energy, checking over his shoulder every few steps. He stopped in a narrow, dimly lit cul-de-sac between Borgin and Burkes and a shuttered storefront.","Harry pressed himself into a shadowy alcove, holding his breath.","A moment later, a second figure emerged from the darkness. It was Severus Snape.","Harry’s stomach gave a lurch. \u003cem\u003eSnape? Here?\u003c/em\u003e","He strained his ears, but the distance was too great, and the low hum of wind through the alley obscured their voices. He watched as Malfoy and Snape spoke—Malfoy looking agitated, his hands gesturing wildly, while Snape remained calm, his black eyes glittering in the low light.","Then, the dynamic changed. A woman Harry didn\u0027t recognize—tall, with heavy-lidded eyes similar to Bellatrix Lestrange—stepped out from the shadows near Snape. Narcissa Malfoy.","Harry watched, transfixed, as Narcissa grabbed Snape’s hand. Malfoy stood by, watching with a mixture of fear and pride. Snape placed his hand over Narcissa\u0027s. They stood close, heads bowed.","It looked like a wedding, or a funeral.","Thin, golden tongues of fire erupted from the tip of a wand held by Narcissa, winding their way around Snape and Narcissa\u0027s joined hands. It was a ceremony. A binding.","Harry didn\u0027t know what it meant, but the gravity of it was unmistakable. Snape wasn\u0027t just talking to them; he was making a pact.","The golden light faded. The hands unclasp. Snape swept his cloak around him and vanished into the shadows, leaving Malfoy and his mother alone. Harry stood frozen, his mind racing. \u003cem\u003eWhat had Snape promised?\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Hogwarts Express\u003c/strong\u003e","September 1st arrived with its usual chaotic fanfare. The Hogwarts Express billowed scarlet steam, and the platform was packed with students. Harry, Ron, and Hermione found a compartment, but Harry’s mind was still in Knockturn Alley.","\u0026quot;I’m telling you, it looked like an Unbreakable Vow,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Ron and Hermione as the train rattled through the countryside. \u0026quot;I read about them. You can\u0027t break them or you die.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But why would Snape make a Vow to Malfoy\u0027s mum?\u0026quot; Ron asked, frowning at a Chocolate Frog card.","\u0026quot;To protect him,\u0026quot; Harry said darkly. \u0026quot;Draco’s up to something. I can feel it.\u0026quot;","Midway through the journey, Harry made his move. He grabbed his Invisibility Cloak.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m going for a walk,\u0026quot; he announced.","\u0026quot;Harry, don\u0027t,\u0026quot; Hermione warned. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t go looking for trouble.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m not looking for trouble,\u0026quot; Harry said, pulling the cloak over his head. \u0026quot;I\u0027m looking for answers.\u0026quot;","He moved down the corridor, dodging trolley witches and first-years, until he reached the Slytherin carriage. The blinds were drawn on the compartment Malfoy was sharing with Pansy Parkinson, Crabbe, and Goyle.","Harry didn\u0027t barge in. He remembered Snape’s Occlumency lessons: \u003cem\u003epatience, discipline, silence.\u003c/em\u003e","He waited until Goyle opened the door to retrieve a fallen sweet. In that split second, Harry slipped inside, pressing himself into the luggage rack above Goyle’s head. He didn\u0027t gasp. He didn\u0027t shift his weight. He lay perfectly still, controlling his breathing, becoming part of the woodwork.","Below him, Malfoy was holding court.","\u0026quot;You don\u0027t know what I\u0027m capable of,\u0026quot; Malfoy was saying, spinning his wand between his fingers. He looked thinner than usual, his face pale and pointed.","\u0026quot;But Draco,\u0026quot; Pansy simpered, gazing at him adoringly. \u0026quot;What did \u003cem\u003eHe\u003c/em\u003e say to you? Is it true?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t talk about the details,\u0026quot; Malfoy said, his voice dropping to a whisper that barely carried to the luggage rack. \u0026quot;But let\u0027s just say... I might not be wasting my time in Charms class next year. I have... higher priorities.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What kind of priorities?\u0026quot; Blaise Zabini asked skeptically.","\u0026quot;The kind that change things,\u0026quot; Malfoy smirked. \u0026quot;The kind that matter.\u0026quot;","Harry strained to hear more, but Malfoy fell silent, looking out the window with a brooding expression. The conversation shifted to Quidditch and the incompetence of the new Gryffindor team captain.","Harry lay there for the rest of the journey, frustrated. Malfoy was boasting, yes. He was clearly involved in something dark. But he hadn\u0027t said \u003cem\u003ewhat\u003c/em\u003e. He hadn\u0027t mentioned a mission, or a target, or a plan. There was no confession. Just vague, arrogant posturing.","When the train began to slow for Hogsmeade, Harry waited. He didn\u0027t try to sneak out while the Slytherins were bustling with their trunks. He waited until the compartment was completely empty.","He dropped down from the rack, landing softly. He hadn\u0027t been caught. He hadn\u0027t been stomped on. But he also hadn\u0027t found the smoking gun he needed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Start-of-Term Feast\u003c/strong\u003e","The Great Hall was a sea of pointed hats and floating candles. The enchanted ceiling mirrored the clear, starry night outside.","Harry sat between Ron and Hermione at the Gryffindor table, attacking a plate of roast beef and Yorkshire pudding. He felt a profound sense of relief to be sitting there with his nose intact and his dignity preserved, unlike the previous timeline where he might have been discovered.","\u0026quot;See anything?\u0026quot; Ron asked through a mouthful of potato.","\u0026quot;Nothing concrete,\u0026quot; Harry muttered, stabbing a carrot. \u0026quot;He’s planning something. He thinks he’s special. But he didn\u0027t say what.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Maybe he\u0027s just showing off,\u0026quot; Hermione suggested, pouring pumpkin juice. \u0026quot;He likes attention, Harry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Maybe,\u0026quot; Harry said, his eyes drifting to the Slytherin table.","Malfoy wasn\u0027t eating. He was staring at the High Table, his eyes fixed on Dumbledore.","Harry followed his gaze up to the staff table. Dumbledore sat in his golden chair, looking older and frailer, his blackened hand resting on the velvet armrest. Next to him sat Horace Slughorn, looking extremely pleased with himself in emerald velvet robes, already toasting Professor McGonagall. And at the end of the table sat Snape, his expression unreadable as he watched the students.","Harry took a bite of his Yorkshire pudding. He didn\u0027t have proof yet. But he had instincts honed by the Dursleys and sharpened by war. Malfoy was a threat. Snape was involved. And Harry was going to be ready."]},{"num":29,"origNum":29,"title":"The Prince and the Prize","wordCount":965,"paragraphs":["The start of the term had been a whirlwind of schedule changes, but none so jarring as the moment Professor McGonagall intercepted Harry and Ron in the corridor during a free period.","\u0026quot;Potter, Weasley,\u0026quot; she said briskly, adjusting her spectacles. \u0026quot;Why are you loitering? You ought to be in Potions.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We didn\u0027t get the grades, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry explained. \u0026quot;Snape—er, Professor Snape—required an \u0027Outstanding\u0027 for N.E.W.T. level.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Professor Slughorn, however, is perfectly happy with \u0027Exceeds Expectations\u0027,\u0026quot; McGonagall corrected, a rare smile touching her lips. \u0026quot;And since you both managed to achieve that grade—miraculously, in some cases—I suggest you head to the dungeons immediately. He has already started.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But we haven\u0027t got books,\u0026quot; Ron panicked. \u0026quot;Or scales. Or ingredients.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Professor Slughorn will provide,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, waving them away. \u0026quot;Go. Don\u0027t waste talent.\u0026quot;","Harry and Ron exchanged a look and bolted for the dungeons.","The Potions classroom was filled with colorful vapors and strange, bubbling noises—a stark contrast to the gloomy, silent atmosphere Snape had cultivated. Slughorn was standing at the front, beaming at the class, looking like a large, velvet-clad bumblebee.","\u0026quot;Harry, m\u0027boy! And Ron!\u0026quot; Slughorn boomed as they skidded into the room. \u0026quot;Excellent! I was hoping you\u0027d join us. Don\u0027t worry about being late, just slip in, slip in.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We haven\u0027t got our books, sir,\u0026quot; Harry said.","\u0026quot;Not to worry!\u0026quot; Slughorn gestured to a cupboard in the corner. \u0026quot;There’s a stack of old copies in there. Grab a pair and get started.\u0026quot;","Harry and Ron hurried to the cupboard. There were two books left. One looked relatively new, its cover crisp and clean. The other was a tattered, binding-broken mess with peeling corners.","Ron, utilizing his Keeper reflexes, lunged forward. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll take the new one!\u0026quot;","He snatched the pristine copy, looking triumphant. Harry was left with the battered relic. He grumbled, checking the back cover to see if it would even hold together. Written in faded ink along the bottom of the back cover were the words: \u003cem\u003eThis Book is the Property of the Half-Blood Prince.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Right then,\u0026quot; Slughorn announced, clapping his hands. \u0026quot;Today, we are brewing the Draught of Living Death. A complex potion, very tricky. But to the winner... I have a little prize.\u0026quot;","He pulled a tiny bottle of golden liquid from his pocket. It swirled enticingly, looking like molten sunlight.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eFelix Felicis\u003c/em\u003e ,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered from the front row, her eyes wide. \u0026quot;Liquid Luck.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely!\u0026quot; Slughorn beamed. \u0026quot;One vial. Twelve hours of perfect luck. Everything you attempt will be successful. To the student who brews the best draught... the luck is yours. Begin!\u0026quot;","The room exploded into activity. Harry opened his battered book. The pages were yellowed and stained, but as he looked closer, he noticed something odd. The printed instructions were covered in handwriting. Someone had crossed out lines, added notes, and scribbled alternative instructions in the margins.","Harry looked at the first instruction: \u003cem\u003eCut the Sopophorous bean.\u003c/em\u003e","In the margin, the mysterious Prince had written: \u003cem\u003eCrush with flat side of silver dagger, releases juice better.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry hesitated. He looked at Hermione, who was aggressively sawing at her bean, which was skittering across the table like a marble. He looked at Ron, whose bean had just flown off the desk and hit Gregory Goyle in the head.","\u003cem\u003eVernon always says to work smarter, not harder,\u003c/em\u003e Harry thought.","He turned his dagger sideways and pressed down hard. \u003cem\u003eCrunch.\u003c/em\u003e The bean burst open, releasing a flood of precious juice. Harry scooped it into his cauldron.","\u0026quot;How did you do that?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, looking up from her mangled bean with a frown.","\u0026quot;Crushed it,\u0026quot; Harry murmured, stirring the cauldron.","\u0026quot;But the instructions say to \u003cem\u003ecut\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; Hermione pointed out, her voice rising in frustration.","\u0026quot;Instructions are guidelines, Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry grinned, feeling a strange kinship with the scribbler in his book.","He continued to follow the Prince’s notes. When the book said to stir counter-clockwise, the Prince suggested adding a clockwise stir after every seventh rotation. Harry did it. The potion, which was supposed to be a pale lilac, turned a perfect, clear pink—exactly as Slughorn had described.","Around him, the class was struggling. Ron’s potion looked like tar and smelled like rotten eggs. Hermione’s was a respectable shade of purple, but she was hair-frazzled and stressed. Malfoy was hacking at his roots with a look of desperate fury.","Harry, meanwhile, felt a strange sense of calm. It was like the Soft Sell tactics Vernon had taught him—intuitive, precise, and yielding results that seemed almost unfair.","\u0026quot;Time\u0027s up!\u0026quot; Slughorn called out.","He walked through the dungeon, peering into cauldrons. He grimaced at Ron’s tar (\u0026quot;A valiant effort, Weasley\u0026quot;). He nodded approvingly at Hermione’s (\u0026quot;Very good consistency, Miss Granger\u0026quot;).","Then, he reached Harry.","Slughorn stopped. He stared into the cauldron. He sniffed the steam. He dropped a small leaf into the liquid, watching it disintegrate instantly.","\u0026quot;By the beard of Merlin,\u0026quot; Slughorn breathed. He looked up at Harry, his eyes wide with delight.","\u0026quot;Perfect. Absolutely perfect. I haven\u0027t seen a Draught of Living Death this pure since... well, since your mother sat in this very classroom. She had an instinctive touch, just like this.\u0026quot;","Harry felt a rush of pride. It wasn\u0027t just about the book; it was about the connection.","\u0026quot;Here you are, Harry,\u0026quot; Slughorn announced, holding up the tiny bottle of gold. \u0026quot;One vial of \u003cem\u003eFelix Felicis\u003c/em\u003e. Use it well.\u0026quot;","Harry took the cool glass vial, slipping it into his pocket. He glanced at Ron, who looked jealous but impressed, and then at Hermione, who was staring at his battered textbook with a look of intense, suspicious scrutiny.","\u0026quot;I think,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Ron as they packed up, \u0026quot;that this year is going to be very interesting.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think,\u0026quot; Ron muttered, eyeing Harry\u0027s book, \u0026quot;that I should have fought you for the old one.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":30,"origNum":30,"title":"The Prince’s Secrets","wordCount":880,"paragraphs":["As autumn turned to winter, the battered copy of \u003cem\u003eAdvanced Potion-Making\u003c/em\u003e became Harry’s most prized possession. The Half-Blood Prince, whoever he was, was a genius. His shortcuts and scribbled incantations didn\u0027t just help Harry survive Slughorn’s class; they made him a star.","Hermione, naturally, was livid.","\u0026quot;It\u0027s dishonest, Harry,\u0026quot; she snapped one evening in the common room, watching Harry effortlessly complete a essay on Golpalott’s Third Law using the Prince’s notes. \u0026quot;You\u0027re relying on someone else\u0027s work. It\u0027s... it\u0027s academically bankrupt!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s efficient,\u0026quot; Harry countered, borrowing a phrase Vernon had used when Harry showed him the book over the Christmas holidays. \u0026quot;The official instructions are outdated. The Prince just found a better workflow.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s not a project manager, Harry!\u0026quot; Hermione huffed. \u0026quot;And that spell you found? \u003cem\u003eSectumsempra\u003c/em\u003e? \u0027For Enemies\u0027? It sounds dark.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I haven\u0027t used it,\u0026quot; Harry said, tracing the word with his quill. \u0026quot;It’s just a backup. Like Dudley’s cricket bat.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Security Breaches\u003c/strong\u003e","The playful rivalry over the book, however, was soon overshadowed by darker events. The war was seeping into the castle.","First came the incident in Hogsmeade. Katie Bell touched a cursed opal necklace and was thrown into the air, screaming in agony. Harry had acted instantly, tackling her friends to stop them from touching her, his reflexes honed by years of dodging Dudley (in the old timeline) and training with Sirius (in this one). He had accused Malfoy immediately to Professor McGonagall, but without proof, his claims were dismissed.","Then came Ron’s birthday. What should have been a celebration turned into a near-tragedy when a box of chocolate cauldrons spiked with love potion (courtesy of Romilda Vane) led to Ron accidentally drinking poisoned oak-matured mead in Slughorn’s office.","Harry hadn\u0027t panicked. While Slughorn froze in shock, Harry remembered a scribble in the Prince’s book: \u003cem\u003eJust shove a bezoar down their throat.\u003c/em\u003e","He had found the stone in Slughorn’s kit and jammed it into Ron’s mouth, saving his best friend’s life seconds before the poison stopped his heart.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Letter from Surrey\u003c/strong\u003e","When Harry wrote to the Dursleys about the incident, the response was immediate and furious.","\u003cem\u003eHarry,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003ePoison? In the Head of House’s office? Is there no Health and Safety Executive in the magical world?\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eI have half a mind to drive up there and inspect the kitchen facilities myself. If they can\u0027t guarantee the beverage supply chain is secure, they should stick to water. Good thinking with the stone, though. Quick decisive action. That\u0027s the Dursley way.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eKeep your eyes open. If they can get to the Weasley boy, they are getting sloppy. Watch your back.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eUncle Vernon\u003c/em\u003e","Harry took the advice to heart. He became obsessed with the Marauder’s Map. He watched Malfoy’s dot religiously. The Slytherin boy was disappearing. He would vanish from the map for hours at a time, only to reappear in the bathrooms on the sixth floor—Moaning Myrtle’s domain.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s mending something,\u0026quot; Harry told Ron and Hermione, pointing at the map. \u0026quot;Borgin and Burkes. The Vanishing Cabinet. It has to be.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But how is he getting things in?\u0026quot; Hermione argued. \u0026quot;Filch scans everything with Secrecy Sensors.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t know,\u0026quot; Harry admitted, staring at the little dot labeled \u003cem\u003eDraco Malfoy\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;But I’m going to catch him.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sixth Floor\u003c/strong\u003e","It was a dreary day in May when the opportunity finally arose. Harry was walking back from Defense Against the Dark Arts when he checked the map. Malfoy’s dot was in the bathroom again. And this time, he was accompanied by the grey, ghostly dot of Moaning Myrtle.","Harry didn\u0027t hesitate. He folded the map, gripped his wand, and broke into a run.","He reached the sixth-floor corridor. It was deserted. He slowed down as he approached the door to the boys\u0027 bathroom, his trainers making no sound on the stone floor.","He pressed his ear against the wood.","He didn\u0027t hear plotting. He didn\u0027t hear the cackle of a villain.","He heard crying.","It was a jagged, desperate sound—the sound of someone cracking under immense pressure. Harry frowned. This didn\u0027t fit the narrative of the arrogant Death Eater in training.","He pushed the door open.","The bathroom was dim and cold. Moaning Myrtle was floating near the ceiling, looking down with a sympathetic expression.","Standing at the sink, gripping the porcelain so hard his knuckles were white, was Draco Malfoy. He was shaking. Tears were streaming down his pale face, dripping into the grimy basin. He looked sick, terrified, and utterly alone.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t do it,\u0026quot; Malfoy sobbed to his reflection, not seeing Harry yet. \u0026quot;It’s not working... and he’ll kill me... he’ll kill my mother...\u0026quot;","Harry stepped fully into the room, the door clicking shut behind him.","Malfoy’s head snapped up. He saw Harry in the mirror. The vulnerability vanished instantly, replaced by a mask of panicked fury. He spun around, drawing his wand with a trembling hand.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Malfoy spat, though his voice cracked.","Harry raised his own wand, leveling it at the boy who had once been his bully, but who now looked like a ghost of himself.","\u0026quot;I know what you\u0027re doing, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry said calmly. \u0026quot;And I know you\u0027re scared.\u0026quot;","Malfoy didn\u0027t lower his wand. The air in the bathroom grew heavy with static, the silence broken only by the dripping of a leaking tap."]},{"num":31,"origNum":31,"title":"Blood and Bonds","wordCount":1074,"paragraphs":["The silence in the bathroom shattered.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eCruci—\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Malfoy screamed, his wand slashing through the air, desperation turning his voice into a shriek.","Harry didn\u0027t think. He reacted. His wand whipped out, the spell from the Prince’s book leaping to his lips before he could consider the consequences.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eSECTUMSEMPRA!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","A jet of white light erupted from Harry’s wand. It hit Malfoy square in the chest.","There was no bang, no flash of sparks. Instead, Malfoy’s face went blank with shock. He stumbled backward, his wand clattering to the wet floor. Then, deep gashes appeared across his chest and face, as if he had been slashed by an invisible sword.","Blood sprayed outward, soaking his white shirt, splashing onto the mirror, staining the water on the floor crimson. Malfoy collapsed into the water with a sickening splash, gasping, his eyes rolling back.","Harry stood frozen for a fraction of a second, horror washing over him. \u003cem\u003eFor Enemies.\u003c/em\u003e He hadn\u0027t known. He hadn\u0027t known.","But the paralysis didn\u0027t last. The instinct that Vernon had praised—the quick, decisive action—kicked in.","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Harry roared.","He dropped his wand. He didn\u0027t run. He threw himself onto the wet floor, sliding on his knees until he reached the convulsing Slytherin.","\u0026quot;Draco! Draco, look at me!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, his hands pressing hard onto the deepest gash on Malfoy’s chest. The blood was hot and slippery, coating Harry’s hands, soaking into his school robes.","\u0026quot;I didn\u0027t mean it! I didn\u0027t know!\u0026quot; Harry gasped, pressing down with all his weight, trying to stem the terrifying flow. Malfoy was pale, his lips turning blue, his breathing shallow and wet.","\u0026quot;Help!\u0026quot; Harry screamed at the ceiling. \u0026quot;Someone help!\u0026quot;","The door banged open. Severus Snape burst in, his black robes flying. His face was a mask of fury, his wand raised to hex the attacker.","He stopped dead.","He saw Malfoy dying on the floor. But he also saw Harry Potter—the boy he hated, the boy he thought was an arrogant bully—crouched over his enemy, his hands covered in blood, frantically trying to save his life.","\u0026quot;Get out of the way, Potter!\u0026quot; Snape barked, though his voice lacked its usual venom. It was sharp, professional.","Harry didn\u0027t argue. He scrambled back, leaving bloody handprints on the tiles, but he didn\u0027t leave. He watched, chest heaving, as Snape knelt beside Malfoy.","Snape traced his wand over the deep wounds, chanting a song-like incantation.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eVulnera Sanentur...\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The flow of blood slowed.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eVulnera Sanentur...\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The wounds began to knit together.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eVulnera Sanentur...\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Draco gasped, a ragged intake of air. His eyes fluttered open. He looked up, dazed and terrified. The first thing he saw was Snape’s pale, focused face. The second thing he saw was Harry Potter, kneeling a few feet away, covered in blood, looking utterly devastated.","Snape hauled Malfoy into a sitting position against the porcelain sink. He wiped the remaining blood from Draco’s face with a quick charm. Then, he turned his cold black eyes on Harry.","\u0026quot;You used dark magic, Potter,\u0026quot; Snape whispered dangerously. \u0026quot;That was \u003cem\u003eSectumsempra\u003c/em\u003e. Where did you learn that spell?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The book,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, still shaking. \u0026quot;I didn\u0027t know... it just said \u0027for enemies\u0027. I didn\u0027t want to kill him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You nearly did,\u0026quot; Snape said.","Draco let out a sob. It was a broken, childish sound. He pulled his knees to his chest, burying his face in his hands, trembling violently.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t do it,\u0026quot; Draco choked out. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t... I’m not like you, Professor. I’m not like him.\u0026quot;","He looked up at Harry, his eyes red and rimmed with dark circles. The mask of the pureblood prince was gone.","\u0026quot;Why didn\u0027t you let me die, Potter?\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;It would have been easier. He’s going to kill me anyway. He’s going to kill my mother.\u0026quot;","Harry moved closer, ignoring the warning look from Snape. \u0026quot;Who, Draco? Voldemort?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He wants me to kill Dumbledore,\u0026quot; Draco confessed, the words tumbling out in a rush of panic. \u0026quot;That’s the mission. Fix the cabinet... let the Death Eaters in... and kill the Headmaster. If I don\u0027t do it, he kills my family.\u0026quot;","Harry felt a chill that had nothing to do with the wet floor. \u003cem\u003eA sixteen-year-old boy. Ordered to kill the greatest wizard alive.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry looked at Snape. \u0026quot;You knew,\u0026quot; Harry accused, remembering the Vow. \u0026quot;That\u0027s what the Vow was for. You swore to help him.\u0026quot;","Snape didn\u0027t deny it. He looked at Draco, then at Harry. The lines on his face seemed to deepen. He looked tired.","\u0026quot;I swore to protect him,\u0026quot; Snape said softly. \u0026quot;Because I knew he could not complete the task. And because, unlike the Dark Lord, I do not wish to see a student’s soul ripped apart.\u0026quot;","Draco looked between them, sobbing quietly. \u0026quot;I tried... the necklace... the mead... I’m useless. I can\u0027t look him in the eye and say \u003cem\u003eAvada Kedavra\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly.","He reached out, ignoring the blood on his hand, and grabbed Draco’s wrist.","\u0026quot;That means you\u0027re not one of them, Draco. You\u0027re just scared.\u0026quot;","Draco stared at Harry’s grip. \u0026quot;He\u0027ll find me. There’s nowhere safe.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, there is,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;The Order. Dumbledore. My aunt and uncle’s house—it has blood protection. We can hide you.\u0026quot;","Snape stood up slowly. He looked at the two boys—Gryffindor and Slytherin, united by fear and blood. He realized that the game had shifted. Harry Potter wasn\u0027t just a pawn to be guarded; he was becoming a player. And Draco Malfoy was breaking.","\u0026quot;Potter is right, Draco,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice unusually low. \u0026quot;You have failed. The Dark Lord will not forgive this. But there are... alternatives.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re going to help us?\u0026quot; Harry asked, looking up at the Potions Master. \u0026quot;Really help us? Not just spy?\u0026quot;","Snape’s lip curled, but there was no malice in it. \u0026quot;I made a Vow, Potter. To save his life. If that requires conspiring with you and Dumbledore to fake a death or hide a fugitive... then so be it.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at the door. \u0026quot;We must go to the Headmaster. Immediately. The Vanishing Cabinet must be destroyed before anyone comes through. And we must figure out a way to save Draco Malfoy without getting us all killed tonight.\u0026quot;","Harry stood up, offering a hand to Draco. Draco hesitated, then took it. Harry pulled him up.","\u0026quot;Come on, Malfoy,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice grim but steady. \u0026quot;Let’s go tell the old man the truth.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":32,"origNum":32,"title":"The Grand Performance","wordCount":1202,"paragraphs":["The journey to the cave was a descent into a nightmare that tested even the new, hardened resolve of Harry Potter. The black lake, the army of Inferi, and the emerald potion that tortured Albus Dumbledore to the brink of insanity—it was a horror show.","But they had done it. Harry, channeling every ounce of strength he possessed, had forced the potion down Dumbledore’s throat, fought off the clammy, dead hands of the Inferi with a ring of fire, and dragged the weakened Headmaster back to the edge of the cliffs.","They Apparated back to Hogsmeade in the dead of night, the air smelling of ozone and impending rain.","Dumbledore was leaning heavily on Harry, his face ashen, his breath rattling in his chest.","\u0026quot;We need... Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore gasped, clutching the locket in his blackened hand. \u0026quot;Take me... to the school. To the Astronomy Tower. We can fly.\u0026quot;","Harry didn\u0027t argue. He hailed Madam Rosmerta, who looked terrified and pointed at the sky above Hogwarts. The Dark Mark was hanging there—a skull composed of emerald stars with a serpent protruding from its mouth.","\u0026quot;Go,\u0026quot; Harry gritted out.","They borrowed brooms and flew through the wind and rain, landing hard on the ramparts of the Astronomy Tower. Dumbledore collapsed against the parapet, his strength gone.","\u0026quot;Go, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore whispered, his eyes sliding shut. \u0026quot;Wake Severus. Tell him what happened. Do not... speak to anyone else.\u0026quot;","But before Harry could move, the door to the ramparts burst open.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eExpelliarmus!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Harry’s wand—and Dumbledore’s—flew from their hands. Draco Malfoy stood there, his wand shaking, his face pale. Behind him, footsteps thundered up the stairs.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said calmly, though he looked moments from death. \u0026quot;You are not an assassin.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have to be,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, his eyes darting to the door. \u0026quot;They\u0027re coming. Bellatrix... Greyback. I let them in through the Cabinet. I had to make it look real.\u0026quot;","Harry, who had thrown on his Invisibility Cloak the moment the door opened, pressed himself against the dark wall, his heart hammering. \u003cem\u003eDraco is stalling,\u003c/em\u003e he realized. \u003cem\u003eHe’s waiting for the Order.\u003c/em\u003e","But the Order didn\u0027t come. Instead, the door was flung wide, and four Death Eaters burst onto the tower.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Headmaster\u0027s Office: Three Hours Earlier\u003c/strong\u003e","While Harry had been packing his rucksack for the cave, a very different conversation had taken place in the circular office of the Headmaster.","Severus Snape stood by the window, his arms crossed, looking at Dumbledore with profound agitation.","\u0026quot;It is tonight, then?\u0026quot; Snape asked quietly.","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Dumbledore replied, testing the sharpness of a silver knife. \u0026quot;Harry and I will retrieve the Horcrux. I will likely return... diminished. The trap will be sprung. Draco will let the Death Eaters in.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the boy?\u0026quot; Snape sneered, though his voice was tight. \u0026quot;Draco expects me to step in. He expects me to kill you to save him. To fulfill the Vow.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And you must,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said simply.","Snape turned, his black eyes flashing. \u0026quot;I have agreed to hide the boy. I have agreed to protect Potter. But I will not fracture my soul for your grand design, Albus! I am not a butcher!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You will not be fracturing your soul, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said calmly, walking over to his pensieve. \u0026quot;Because you will not be killing me.\u0026quot;","Snape paused. \u0026quot;Explain.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Killing Curse,\u0026quot; Dumbledore lectured, as if discussing the weather, \u0026quot;relies entirely on intent. You must \u003cem\u003ewant\u003c/em\u003e the target dead. You must desire the severance of soul from body with absolute malice.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore looked up, his blue eyes piercing. \u0026quot;You do not hate me, Severus. You do not wish me dead.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am finding you exceptionally annoying at the moment,\u0026quot; Snape muttered.","\u0026quot;But not hateful,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled faintly. \u0026quot;When the moment comes, you will point your wand. You will say the words. You must say them clearly, for Bellatrix and the others will be watching. \u003cem\u003eAvada Kedavra\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Snape recoiled. \u0026quot;If I say those words—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But in your mind,\u0026quot; Dumbledore interrupted, raising a finger, \u0026quot;you will cast a Blasting Curse. You will focus your intent on \u003cem\u003epropulsion\u003c/em\u003e, not death. You will blast me from the tower. I will fall. To the watchers, it will look like the impact of the Killing Curse throwing a body backward.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the fall?\u0026quot; Snape asked skeptically. \u0026quot;It is the highest tower in the castle.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have arranged... cushioning,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said vaguely. \u0026quot;Fawkes will be waiting. I will vanish. To the world, Albus Dumbledore will be dead. It is the only way, Severus. Voldemort must believe he has won. He must believe you are his most loyal servant. Only then will he trust you enough to keep you close... and keep the students safe.\u0026quot;","Snape stared at the old man. It was madness. It was high-stakes theater with a lethal incantation as the script.","\u0026quot;And if you miss?\u0026quot; Snape asked. \u0026quot;If your \u0027cushioning\u0027 fails?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Then,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly, \u0026quot;death will come as a great adventure. But I have faith in you, Severus.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Astronomy Tower: Present Time\u003c/strong\u003e","The scene on the tower was reaching a fever pitch. Bellatrix Lestrange was cackling, urging Draco to finish it. Greyback was eyeing Dumbledore like a piece of meat.","\u0026quot;Do it, Draco!\u0026quot; Bellatrix shrieked. \u0026quot;Now!\u0026quot;","Draco’s hand was shaking so hard he could barely hold his wand. He looked at Dumbledore, terror in his eyes. He couldn\u0027t do it. He couldn\u0027t even fake it.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, lowering his wand.","\u0026quot;Coward!\u0026quot; Bellatrix snarled, raising her own wand. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll do it myself!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;NO!\u0026quot;","Severus Snape swept onto the ramparts, pushing Draco aside roughly. He took in the scene: the weakened Dumbledore, the terrified Draco, the bloodthirsty Death Eaters.","Harry, hidden beneath his cloak, watched with bated breath. \u003cem\u003eSnape is here. Snape will save him.\u003c/em\u003e","Snape looked at Dumbledore. The old man was slumped against the wall, defenseless. His blue eyes met Snape’s black ones.","\u0026quot;Severus...\u0026quot; Dumbledore pleaded.","To Harry, it sounded like a beg for mercy.","To Draco, it sounded like a beg for help.","To Snape, it was a cue. Do it. Now.","Snape raised his wand. His face was a mask of revulsion and hatred—perfectly acted. He pointed it directly at Dumbledore’s chest.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eAvada Kedavra!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","A jet of green light erupted from Snape’s wand.","It hit Dumbledore square in the chest.","Harry opened his mouth to scream, but no sound came out. He watched in horror as Dumbledore was blasted backward, up and over the battlements. For a second, he hung suspended in the air, pale and lifeless, before plummeting into the darkness below.","\u0026quot;Out of here!\u0026quot; Snape shouted, grabbing Draco by the scruff of his neck. \u0026quot;Quickly!\u0026quot;","Snape turned and sprinted for the stairs, dragging the stunned Draco with him. Bellatrix fired the Dark Mark into the sky with a triumphant scream and followed, cackling into the night.","Harry remained frozen under his cloak, his mind unable to process what he had just seen.","Snape had done it.","Snape had killed Albus Dumbledore.","Harry tore off the cloak. A roar of pure, unadulterated rage erupted from his throat. He didn\u0027t care about the odds. He didn\u0027t care about safety. He vaulted over the steps and sprinted after them, a single thought consuming his mind.","\u003cem\u003eKill Snape.\u003c/em\u003e"]},{"num":33,"origNum":33,"title":"The Dead Man’s Toast","wordCount":1090,"paragraphs":["The grass of the grounds flew beneath Harry’s feet. He was running on pure hate, ignoring the stitch in his side and the screams of the students behind him.","Ahead, the Death Eaters were sprinting toward the gates. Bellatrix Lestrange paused only to whip her wand toward Hagrid’s hut. A jet of orange flame erupted, and the wooden structure caught fire with a roar.","\u0026quot;Go!\u0026quot; Snape shouted at Bellatrix and Greyback. \u0026quot;Get to the boundary! Disapparate! I will bring the boy!\u0026quot;","The Death Eaters didn\u0027t argue; they vanished into the night, leaving Snape dragging a stumbling, sobbing Draco Malfoy toward the edge of the Forbidden Forest.","\u0026quot;SNAPE!\u0026quot; Harry screamed, skidding to a halt.","Snape turned, his face illuminated by the burning hut. He looked monstrous in the flickering light.","\u0026quot;He trusted you!\u0026quot; Harry roared, raising his wand. He didn\u0027t think of disarming. He thought of the spell that had nearly killed Draco, the spell of the Prince. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eSECTUM—\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, Potter!\u0026quot;","Snape whipped his wand with blinding speed. The spell was blocked before it even left Harry’s lips. Harry was blasted backward, hitting the turf hard. He scrambled up, wand raised again.","\u0026quot;You killed him! \u003cem\u003eCruci—\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Snape roared.","He moved faster than Harry had ever seen. He closed the distance, grabbed Harry’s wrist, and twisted. Harry’s wand flew into the grass. Snape slammed Harry against a tree, pinning him there with a forearm to the throat.","Draco was standing nearby, staring at them with wide, vacant eyes. \u0026quot;Professor... we have to go... the Dark Lord...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Silence!\u0026quot; Snape hissed at Draco. He leaned in close to Harry, his black eyes burning. \u0026quot;You are just like your father, Potter. Lazy. Emotional. You do not understand what you see.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I saw you murder him!\u0026quot; Harry spat, struggling against Snape’s grip.","\u0026quot;You saw,\u0026quot; Snape whispered dangerously, \u0026quot;what I \u003cem\u003ewanted\u003c/em\u003e you to see. Grab hold.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What?\u0026quot; Harry choked out.","Snape didn\u0027t explain. He grabbed Draco by the scruff of the neck with his other hand, yanked Harry forward, and turned on his heel.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The sensation was suffocating. They were being squeezed through a rubber tube. The smell of burning wood and grass vanished, replaced by the scent of sawdust, goats, and stale mead.","Harry hit a wooden floor hard. He scrambled backward, looking for his wand, but he didn\u0027t have it. He looked up, ready to fight with his bare hands.","He froze.","They were in a dingy, dimly lit room. There were dusty curtains drawn over the windows and a goat wandering aimlessly in the corner.","And sitting in a moth-eaten armchair by the fire, holding a glass of amber liquid, was Albus Dumbledore.","He looked terrible. His robes were scorched, his hair was windblown, and he was wincing as he adjusted his position in the chair. But he was breathing.","\u0026quot;Ah,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, raising his glass slightly. \u0026quot;Severus. You made excellent time. And I see you brought guests.\u0026quot;","Harry’s mouth opened and closed. He looked at the dead man. Then he looked at Snape, who was dusting off his robes with a look of immense irritation.","\u0026quot;Potter tried to curse me,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, throwing Harry’s wand onto a table. \u0026quot;Again.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy let out a high-pitched whimper. He slid down the wall and sat on the floor, staring at Dumbledore as if he were a ghost.","\u0026quot;But...\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;I saw... the green light... you fell...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A Blasting Curse, Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; Dumbledore explained gently, taking a sip of his drink. \u0026quot;Combined with a rather potent Freezing Charm and a well-timed cushion summoned by Fawkes at the base of the tower. I dare say the fall was still rather unpleasant. My back will never be the same.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re alive,\u0026quot; Harry breathed, the rage draining out of him so fast it left him dizzy. \u0026quot;But Snape... he said the words.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Performance art, Harry,\u0026quot; a gruff voice grunted from the shadows.","Aberforth Dumbledore stepped into the light, carrying a tray of dirty glasses. He glared at his brother. \u0026quot;Stupid plan, Albus. You nearly broke your neck. Next time, use a dummy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The visual had to be convincing, Abe,\u0026quot; Albus replied calmly.","Snape stepped forward, looming over Harry and Draco. \u0026quot;Listen to me closely. To the world, Albus Dumbledore is dead. The Order saw it. The Death Eaters saw it. You saw it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Why?\u0026quot; Harry asked, his voice shaking. \u0026quot;Why put us through that?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because Voldemort must believe he has won,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice cold and hard. \u0026quot;He must believe I am his most loyal servant. If he thinks I killed Dumbledore, he will trust me implicitly. He will let me stay at Hogwarts. He will let me protect the students from the Carrows.\u0026quot;","Snape turned to Draco, his expression softening slightly. \u0026quot;And he will believe you succeeded in your mission, Draco. He will not kill your mother. You are safe.\u0026quot;","Draco put his head in his hands and began to sob—deep, heaving sobs of relief. \u0026quot;I thought I was a killer... I thought I\u0027d killed you...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You are no killer, Draco,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly. \u0026quot;You are a boy who was given an impossible choice.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore turned his piercing blue eyes to Harry. \u0026quot;Harry, I need you to be strong. You cannot tell anyone. Not Ron. Not Hermione. Not your aunt and uncle. To the world, I am a martyr. This secrecy is the only weapon we have left.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at the Headmaster—the man he had mourned for the last twenty minutes with a grief that felt like dying. He looked at Snape, the \u0026quot;murderer\u0026quot; who had saved them all.","\u0026quot;You want us to lie,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;To everyone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I want you to win,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said simply. \u0026quot;Voldemort will now become overconfident. He will move into the open. And while he celebrates my death, you, Harry, will hunt his Horcruxes. And Severus will guard the castle.\u0026quot;","Harry took a deep breath. He looked at Draco, who was wiping his eyes. He looked at Snape, who watched him with an unreadable expression.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;We\u0027re dead to the world.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, setting down his glass. \u0026quot;Now, Severus, take them back to the gates. You must make a convincing escape. Try not to actually hurt anyone, but do make it look... dramatic.\u0026quot;","Snape nodded. He grabbed Harry and Draco by the arms again.","\u0026quot;Ready for the second act, Potter?\u0026quot; Snape sneered.","Harry looked at Dumbledore one last time. \u0026quot;Professor... don\u0027t drink too much of that stuff.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore smiled, raising his glass. \u0026quot;I believe, Harry, that for tonight, I have earned it.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":34,"origNum":34,"title":"The White Lie","wordCount":917,"paragraphs":["The staging at the gates was brief and brutal. Snape, holding a trembling Draco, looked at Harry one last time.","\u0026quot;Remember the plan, Potter,\u0026quot; Snape hissed. \u0026quot;Bellatrix cast the curse. I was overwhelmed and took Draco... as a hostage. Stick to the script.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice hard. He looked at Draco. \u0026quot;Stay safe, Malfoy.\u0026quot;","Draco nodded weakly. \u0026quot;You too, Potter.\u0026quot;","With a swirl of his cloak, Snape grabbed Draco and Disapparated into the darkness, leaving Harry alone at the edge of the grounds.","Harry took a deep breath, summoned the tears that were already threatening to fall for the sheer stress of the night, and began to run back toward the castle, shouting.","\u0026quot;Help! Someone help!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","The hospital wing was crowded and chaotic. Bill Weasley was being tended to for his werewolf bites; Tonks and Lupin were huddled in a corner, looking grim. When Harry burst in, covered in dust and soot, the room fell silent.","Professor McGonagall rushed forward, her face white. \u0026quot;Harry! Where is Albus? Where is Snape?\u0026quot;","Harry grabbed her robes, channeling every ounce of Vernon Dursley’s ability to sell a story.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s gone,\u0026quot; Harry choked out. \u0026quot;Dumbledore... he\u0027s gone.\u0026quot;","Gasps rippled through the room. Molly Weasley let out a shriek.","\u0026quot;What happened?\u0026quot; Lupin demanded, stepping forward.","\u0026quot;We came back from a mission,\u0026quot; Harry lied, the story flowing with terrifying ease. \u0026quot;The Dark Mark was over the tower. We flew up. Draco Malfoy was there... he let them in. But he couldn\u0027t do it. He lowered his wand.\u0026quot;","Harry paused, wiping his eyes.","\u0026quot;Then Bellatrix Lestrange... she blasted him. She used the Killing Curse. Snape tried to stop them... he tried to grab Draco, but there were too many of them. They took Draco. They took him and ran.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bellatrix,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered, clutching her chest. \u0026quot;And Albus?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He fell,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;Over the battlements. But when I got down there... he was gone. Fawkes was flying away. I think... I think the phoenix took him.\u0026quot;","It was the perfect cover for the missing body. A reverent silence descended on the room. Outside, a phoenix began to sing—a lament that echoed through the grounds. Harry knew it was likely Dumbledore’s way of selling the lie from afar (or perhaps Fawkes really was mourning the \u0026quot;death\u0026quot; of his master\u0027s public persona), but it broke the hearts of everyone listening.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Funeral\u003c/strong\u003e","The funeral was held three days later. It was a somber, grey affair by the lake.","A white marble tomb was raised, though everyone believed it contained the body of the greatest wizard of the age, brought back by the phoenix for a final rest (or simply a cenotaph, as the body was \u0026quot;lost\u0026quot;).","Harry sat between Ron and Hermione. He wore his dress robes, his face a mask of grief. Inside, however, he felt a strange, cold detachment. He watched the Ministry officials, including the new Minister, Rufus Scrimgeour, offer empty platitudes. He watched Hagrid sobbing into a tablecloth-sized handkerchief.","He felt guilty for the tears of his friends, but he held onto Dumbledore’s command: \u003cem\u003eSecrecy is the only weapon we have left.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t believe it,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, leaning her head on Harry\u0027s shoulder. \u0026quot;I just... I can\u0027t believe he\u0027s gone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s not really gone,\u0026quot; Harry said, staring at the white tomb. \u0026quot;As long as we\u0027re fighting... he\u0027s not gone.\u0026quot;","It wasn\u0027t a lie. Hermione squeezed his hand, thinking he was being metaphorical. Harry squeezed back, knowing he was being literal.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Journey Home\u003c/strong\u003e","The train ride back to King’s Cross was quieter than it had ever been. The sky outside was a relentless, dreary grey. The Prophet lay on the seat next to them, the headline screaming: \u003cstrong\u003eDUMBLEDORE DEAD: SLAIN BY DEATH EATER LESTRANGE.\u003c/strong\u003e","The article speculated wildly about Snape’s disappearance, labeling him a coward who fled the sinking ship, and listed Draco Malfoy as a \u0026quot;victim of kidnapping.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I still don\u0027t understand why Snape ran,\u0026quot; Ron muttered, kicking the seat opposite. \u0026quot;Cowardly git. He should have fought harder.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He was outnumbered, Ron,\u0026quot; Harry said, defending the man he had hated for six years. \u0026quot;He tried to save Malfoy. I saw it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well, now we\u0027re on our own,\u0026quot; Hermione said quietly. She looked at Harry. \u0026quot;Harry, you know we\u0027re coming with you, right? Whatever Dumbledore asked you to do next... we\u0027re coming.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at his two best friends. He thought of the Horcruxes. He thought of the long, dangerous road ahead. And he thought of the secret he was keeping from them.","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;But first... I have to go home.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Dursleys?\u0026quot; Ron asked.","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Harry nodded, a small, genuine smile breaking through his mask. \u0026quot;I need to talk to my uncle. I think I\u0027m going to need some more strategy advice.\u0026quot;","As the Hogwarts Express pulled into Platform Nine and Three-Quarters, the steam cleared to reveal the barrier. Harry stood up, hefting his trunk. He wasn\u0027t returning as a tragic orphan this summer. He was returning as a soldier on leave, going back to his headquarters.","He stepped off the train, scanning the crowd until he saw them.","Vernon Dursley was standing there, looking grim and serious, wearing a black tie as a mark of respect for the \u0026quot;Headmaster fellow.\u0026quot; Petunia stood beside him, her hand on Dudley’s arm.","They didn\u0027t wave manicially. They simply nodded. They knew.","Harry walked toward them, leaving the magical world behind for a few weeks. The war had begun, but for now, he was going home."]},{"num":35,"origNum":35,"title":"The Seven Potters","wordCount":1212,"paragraphs":["The summer heat hung heavy over Little Whinging, but inside Number Four, the temperature was dropping rapidly due to the icy standoff in the kitchen.","\u0026quot;For the last time, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry said, running a hand through his hair in frustration. \u0026quot;It’s not a suggestion. It’s a magical expiration date. When I turn seventeen tomorrow, the bond of blood breaks. The charm my mother left... it vanishes. Voldemort will be able to walk right through that front door.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley sat at the kitchen table, his arms crossed over his chest, looking like a bulldog refusing to give up a bone.","\u0026quot;And I say we stand our ground!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;We’ve fortified the perimeter! Dudley has been training with the boxing club! We have the element of surprise!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dad,\u0026quot; Dudley interjected, leaning against the counter. \u0026quot;I can punch a lot of things, but I can\u0027t punch a killing curse.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are not running away, Harry,\u0026quot; Petunia said, though her voice wavered. She was packing tea bags into a box with trembling hands. \u0026quot;This is our home. We raised you here. We protected you here.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And you did a brilliant job,\u0026quot; Harry said softly, stepping closer to his aunt. \u0026quot;You kept me safe for sixteen years. But now, I have to keep you safe. And I can\u0027t do that if you\u0027re here.\u0026quot;","The doorbell rang—a sharp, insistent series of taps.","Vernon jumped up. \u0026quot;If that’s a salesman, he’s going to get an earful about impeccable timing!\u0026quot;","He marched to the hallway and wrenched the door open.","Standing on the immaculate porch was not a salesman. It was a crowd. Alastor \u0026quot;Mad-Eye\u0026quot; Moody stood at the front, his magical eye spinning wildly, flanked by Arthur Weasley, Kingsley Shacklebolt, Remus Lupin, Tonks, and Hagrid, whose massive frame spilled over into the flowerbeds. Behind them were Ron, Hermione, Bill, Fleur, Fred, George, and a nervous-looking Mundungus Fletcher.","\u0026quot;Good evening,\u0026quot; Moody growled, his scarred face twisting into what might have been a polite grimace. \u0026quot;We’re the extraction team. Are you packed?\u0026quot;","Vernon stared at the magical army on his lawn. He looked at the scarred Auror, the half-giant, and the man with the spinning blue eye.","\u0026quot;You must be the security consultants,\u0026quot; Vernon said, sizing Moody up. \u0026quot;You look... experienced.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027ve seen things that would turn your hair white, Dursley,\u0026quot; Moody grunted, limping into the hall. \u0026quot;Now, we don\u0027t have time for a debate. The protection breaks at midnight. The Dark Lord knows it. He will hit this house with everything he has.\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley stepped forward, smiling kindly. \u0026quot;Vernon, Petunia. We have prepared a safe house for you. It’s unplottable, heavily warded, and stocked with enough food for a year. Dedalus Diggle and Hestia Jones will be your protection detail. Think of it not as fleeing, but as a strategic relocation to a secure command post.\u0026quot;","Vernon paused. The phrase \u0026quot;strategic relocation\u0026quot; appealed to his business sensibilities.","\u0026quot;A command post,\u0026quot; Vernon mused. \u0026quot;Well. That puts a different spin on it. We aren\u0027t retreating; we are consolidating our assets.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Kingsley Shacklebolt said in his deep, calming voice. \u0026quot;We need you safe so Harry can focus on the mission.\u0026quot;","Vernon looked at Petunia, then at Dudley. He sighed, the fight going out of him.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon decided, clapping his hands. \u0026quot;Petunia, Dudley. Upstairs. Get the essentials. Clothes, documents, the photo albums. And Dudley, bring the cricket bat. We move out in twenty minutes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, Dad,\u0026quot; Dudley said, looking relieved.","As the Dursleys thundered upstairs to begin a frantic final pack, the kitchen of Number Four transformed into a war room.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Moody barked, dumping a large sack onto the kitchen table. \u0026quot;Potter, you\u0027re underage, which means you\u0027ve still got the Trace on you. We can\u0027t Apparate you, we can\u0027t use the Floo Network, and we can\u0027t use a Portkey. The Ministry will know.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So how are we getting to the Burrow?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;We fly,\u0026quot; Moody said. \u0026quot;Brooms, Thestrals, and Hagrid’s motorbike. But even then, if they\u0027re waiting for us, they\u0027ll target you. So, we\u0027re going to use a decoy.\u0026quot;","Moody pulled a flask of mud-like liquid from his cloak.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry said immediately, recognizing the smell of Polyjuice Potion. \u0026quot;No way. I\u0027m not letting you—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I told you he\u0027d be noble,\u0026quot; Ron said to Hermione, rolling his eyes.","\u0026quot;Harry, be reasonable,\u0026quot; Hermione pleaded. \u0026quot;It\u0027s the only way to confuse them. If there are seven Harry Potters flying in different directions, they won\u0027t know which one is the real target.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Seven?\u0026quot; Harry looked around the room. \u0026quot;You\u0027re all mad.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re all volunteers,\u0026quot; Fred grinned. \u0026quot;Well, Mundungus was \u0027volunteered\u0027, wasn\u0027t he?\u0026quot;","Mundungus grumbled something about his back, but Moody silenced him with a glare.","\u0026quot;We need a bit of you, Potter,\u0026quot; Moody growled. \u0026quot;Hair. Now.\u0026quot;","Harry sighed. He knew he couldn\u0027t win this argument, not with the Order staring him down and the clock ticking. He reached up, plucked a tuft of black hair from his head, and dropped it into the flask.","The potion hissed, turned a clear, bright gold, and smoked.","\u0026quot;Ooh, you look tasty, Harry,\u0026quot; George winked.","\u0026quot;Right, line up,\u0026quot; Moody commanded. \u0026quot;Fake Potters, step forward.\u0026quot;","Ron, Hermione, Fred, George, Fleur, and Mundungus stepped up to the table. Moody poured the potion into six small cups.","\u0026quot;Bottoms up,\u0026quot; Ron said, grimacing, and downed it in one go.","The others followed suit.","What followed was a spectacle of groans, grimaces, and bubbling skin.","Hermione gasped, clutching her stomach. \u0026quot;It tastes like... like old socks!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think it tastes like goblin piss,\u0026quot; Mundungus gagged.","\u0026quot;Focus!\u0026quot; Moody barked.","Before Harry’s eyes, his friends began to melt and shift. Hermione’s bushy hair shrank and darkened into messy black spikes. Ron’s lanky frame shortened, his freckles vanishing as his skin turned pale. Fleur’s elegant features dissolved, replaced by Harry’s glasses and scar. Fred and George shrank down, losing their bulk.","Within moments, six identical copies of Harry Potter stood in the Dursleys\u0027 kitchen, all gasping and looking at their hands in horror or amusement.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Fred-Harry said, checking his reflection in the toaster. \u0026quot;We\u0027re identical!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t know though,\u0026quot; George-Harry said, squinting at Fred. \u0026quot;I think I look better.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bah,\u0026quot; Fleur-Harry muttered, examining herself. \u0026quot;Bill, look away. I am hideous.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re beautiful to me, Harry,\u0026quot; Bill quipped, handing her a set of clothes from the sack. \u0026quot;Now, get changed. We need everyone in the uniform. Glasses, t-shirts, jackets.\u0026quot;","The kitchen became a flurry of activity as the six doppelgangers began to strip off their own clothes and pull on the identical outfits Moody had provided.","\u0026quot;This is weird,\u0026quot; Ron-Harry muttered, pulling on a pair of jeans. \u0026quot;Really weird.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Harry, your eyesight is terrible,\u0026quot; Hermione-Harry complained, putting on the round glasses and blinking rapidly. \u0026quot;Everything is blurry!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah, well, try living with it,\u0026quot; the real Harry said, watching the surreal scene unfold.","Upstairs, the heavy thud of suitcases being dragged across the landing echoed. The Dursleys were packing their lives away, preparing to leave the only home they had ever known. Downstairs, seven versions of the boy they had raised stood ready to launch into the sky, bait for the most dangerous wizard alive.","Harry looked at his friends—his family—wearing his face, risking their lives. He swallowed the lump in his throat.","\u0026quot;Ready?\u0026quot; Moody growled.","\u0026quot;Ready,\u0026quot; six voices answered in unison."]},{"num":36,"origNum":36,"title":"The Mother\u0027s Heart","wordCount":746,"paragraphs":["The sound of heavy suitcases bumping down the stairs announced the return of the Dursleys. Vernon appeared first, wrestling a massive trunk around the banister, followed by Dudley carrying a duffel bag and the promised cricket bat.","Petunia came last. She was clutching her handbag and a travel coat, looking around the kitchen with wide, bewildered eyes.","She stopped dead.","Staring back at her were seven identical Harry Potters.","They were everywhere. One was checking his reflection in the microwave. Two were arguing over a pair of glasses. One was buttoning a shirt that looked too tight. Another was looking at Bill Weasley with a decidedly feminine expression of distaste.","\u0026quot;Good grief,\u0026quot; Vernon muttered, dropping the trunk with a thud. \u0026quot;It’s a nightmare. It’s a factory line of them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Which one is he?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, squinting. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t tell. They\u0027ve all got the sticky-uppy hair.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m the real one!\u0026quot; Fred-Harry shouted, grinning mischievously.","\u0026quot;No, I am!\u0026quot; George-Harry countered, winking at Dudley. \u0026quot;Ignore him, Big D, he\u0027s an impostor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am Harry,\u0026quot; Fleur-Harry stated, though her posture was far too elegant.","The real Harry, standing near the back door, opened his mouth to identify himself. He didn\u0027t want to drag this out; the pain of leaving was already sharp enough.","But before he could speak, Petunia moved.","She didn\u0027t look at the Harry making jokes. She didn\u0027t look at the Harrys adjusting their clothes. She walked straight past the chaos, weaving through the crowd of wizards and doppelgangers.","She stopped directly in front of the real Harry.","He was standing quietly, his hands in his pockets, looking at her with an expression of profound sadness. He wasn\u0027t trying to be brave, or funny, or noble. He was just a boy saying goodbye to his mum.","Petunia didn\u0027t hesitate. She reached out, cupping his face in her hands.","\u0026quot;You look thin,\u0026quot; she whispered, her eyes searching his. \u0026quot;You haven\u0027t eaten enough today.\u0026quot;","Then, she pulled him into a fierce, bone-crushing hug. It wasn\u0027t the awkward, stiff embrace of a reluctant guardian. It was the desperate, clinging hold of a parent sending their child to war.","She pulled back slightly, brushed the hair off his forehead to reveal the scar, and planted a firm, lingering kiss right on top of it.","\u0026quot;Be safe,\u0026quot; she choked out.","The kitchen had gone silent. The six fake Harrys were staring. Mad-Eye Moody’s magical eye had stopped spinning. Even Vernon looked moved, blowing his nose loudly into a handkerchief.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Fred-Harry broke the silence, adjusting his glasses. \u0026quot;How did you do that? Mrs. Dursley, we’re identical. Same hair, same scar, same glasses. Even I don\u0027t know which one I am anymore.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; George-Harry agreed, looking baffled. \u0026quot;Did you use a spell? A secret signal?\u0026quot;","Petunia turned to look at the twins. She kept her arm wrapped tightly around the real Harry’s waist, anchoring him to her. She looked at the wizards with a fierce, teary-eyed dignity.","\u0026quot;He is my sister\u0027s son,\u0026quot; Petunia said, her voice trembling but clear. \u0026quot;I have washed his clothes, bandaged his knees, and tucked him in for sixteen years. You can change his face, you can change his voice, and you can change his clothes.\u0026quot;","She squeezed Harry’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;But a mother\u0027s heart always knows her own. And he is mine.\u0026quot;","A profound stillness settled over the room.","Molly Weasley let out a small sob, pressing her hand to her mouth. Hermione-Harry looked down at her shoes, seemingly fighting back tears behind the round spectacles. Even Mad-Eye Moody looked at Petunia with a gruff, newfound respect.","They had always known Harry lived with his aunt. But in that moment, seeing the fierce, possessive love radiating from the Muggle woman, they realized that Harry Potter hadn\u0027t just been housed at Privet Drive. He had been loved.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Moody grunted, his voice unusually thick. \u0026quot;Well said, Mrs. Dursley. Well said.\u0026quot;","Vernon stepped forward, placing a heavy hand on Harry\u0027s other shoulder, completing the protective circle.","\u0026quot;You heard the woman,\u0026quot; Vernon said, his voice rough. \u0026quot;He\u0027s ours. You lot better bring him back in one piece. Or you\u0027ll have to answer to us.\u0026quot;","Harry looked from his aunt to his uncle, his heart swelling so much it felt like it might burst. He had spent years terrified that his magical life would destroy his Muggle one. Instead, in the end, they had simply merged into one singular, powerful force of love.","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll come back,\u0026quot; Harry promised them both. \u0026quot;I always come back.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":37,"origNum":37,"title":"The Empty Nest and the Full House","wordCount":1354,"paragraphs":["The moment of departure had arrived. Dedalus Diggle was checking his pocket watch with frantic, ticking glances, while Hestia Jones stood by the back door, wand drawn, looking tense.","\u0026quot;We must go, Dursleys,\u0026quot; Diggle squeaked. \u0026quot;The timing is precise. We cannot risk the protection falling while you are still within the perimeter.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley took a deep breath. He looked around the kitchen—the gleaming appliances, the polished table where he had taught Harry negotiation tactics, the spot on the floor where he had laughed until he cried over \u0026quot;The Ostrich.\u0026quot; He was leaving his castle.","He turned to Harry. The bluster, the sales tactics, the lectures on efficiency—they all fell away.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon said, his voice thick.","He stepped forward and didn\u0027t bother with a handshake. He pulled Harry into a crushing bear hug, thumping him on the back with a hand the size of a ham.","\u0026quot;You give them hell, son,\u0026quot; Vernon choked out. \u0026quot;You show them what a Potter—and a Dursley—is made of. We\u0027ll keep the kettle on for you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry whispered into the rough fabric of his uncle\u0027s jacket. \u0026quot;Take care of the car.\u0026quot;","Vernon pulled back, sniffing loudly. \u0026quot;The car can be replaced. You can\u0027t.\u0026quot;","Dudley was next. He looked massive in his travel coat, the cricket bat handle sticking out of his duffel bag like a weapon of war.","\u0026quot;See you, Harry,\u0026quot; Dudley said. He looked like he wanted to punch something to stop himself from crying. Instead, he grabbed Harry and squeezed him so hard Harry’s ribs creaked. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t you dare die. Who am I going to watch TV with?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m unkillable, Big D,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, patting his cousin\u0027s back. \u0026quot;You protect Mum and Dad.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Always,\u0026quot; Dudley promised.","Finally, Petunia. She stood before him, her face wet with tears, looking smaller than usual. She reached out, smoothing his unruly black hair one last time, her fingers lingering on the scar.","\u0026quot;He would be so proud of you,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, invoking James Potter, a man she had once despised but now honored through his son. \u0026quot;And Lily... she\u0027s watching, Harry. I know she is.\u0026quot;","She pulled him close, kissing his cheek. \u0026quot;Come home, Harry. Just come home.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I promise,\u0026quot; Harry said, his own vision blurring.","\u0026quot;Come along!\u0026quot; Diggle urged.","With one last, lingering look at the boy they had raised, the Dursleys stepped out into the night. They climbed into the car with the Order members, the engine roared to life, and within seconds, the headlights swept across the drive and vanished into the dark.","Harry stood in the silent kitchen. He felt a phantom ache in his chest. The house was empty.","\u0026quot;Right then,\u0026quot; Mad-Eye Moody growled, breaking the silence. \u0026quot;Sentimental bit over. Now the real work begins. Mount up!\u0026quot;","The seven Harrys and their protectors filed out into the back garden. The night air was cool and filled with the scent of exhaust fumes from Hagrid’s motorbike and the earthy smell of the Thestrals.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re with me, Harry,\u0026quot; Hagrid beamed, patting the sidecar. \u0026quot;Just like when I brought yeh here.\u0026quot;","Harry climbed into the sidecar, gripping his wand and his rucksack. He looked around.","Arthur Weasley was mounting a Thestral with Fred-Harry. Remus was with George-Harry. Tonks was with Ron-Harry. Kingsley was with Hermione-Harry. Bill was with Fleur-Harry. And Mad-Eye Moody was pairing up with Mundungus-Harry.","\u0026quot;Good luck, everyone,\u0026quot; Harry called out. \u0026quot;See you at the Burrow.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;See you there, mate,\u0026quot; Ron-Harry grinned nervously.","\u0026quot;On my mark!\u0026quot; Moody barked. \u0026quot;One... two... three!\u0026quot;","There was a deafening roar from the motorbike, and with a surge of acceleration that pinned Harry to the seat, they shot into the sky.","The wind whipped Harry’s face, tearing the tears from his eyes. They rose higher and higher, the lights of Little Whinging becoming a grid of orange dots below.","Then, the scream.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eDeath Eaters!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Hagrid roared.","Out of the clouds, black shapes swarmed like bats. Jets of green light sizzled through the air.","\u0026quot;Hold on, Harry!\u0026quot; Hagrid yelled, hitting a button that sent a wall of dragon fire erupting from the tailpipe.","Harry twisted in the seat, raising his wand. He didn\u0027t use \u003cem\u003eExpelliarmus\u003c/em\u003e. He remembered Vernon\u0027s advice about decisive action. He remembered Snape\u0027s lessons on intent.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eStupefy! Impedimenta! Confringo!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Harry fought with a ferocity that surprised even himself. He blasted a masked figure off a broomstick, sent a Blasting Curse into the path of another, and deflected a curse meant for Hagrid.","To his left, he saw a flash of red light—Kingsley and Hermione-Harry fighting back-to-back on a Thestral. Above, a broomstick spiraled—it was Tonks and Ron-Harry, diving to avoid a curse.","\u0026quot;Get us out of here, Hagrid!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, shattering the mask of a Death Eater who got too close.","\u0026quot;Using the boost!\u0026quot; Hagrid shouted.","The bike screamed, shooting forward with terrifying speed, leaving the battle behind in a trail of smoke and fire.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Burrow\u003c/strong\u003e","The garden of the Burrow was silent, the long grass rustling in the wind. Molly Weasley stood by the back door, clutching a tea towel, her eyes scanning the sky. Ginny stood beside her, wand drawn.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re late,\u0026quot; Molly whispered.","\u0026quot;They\u0027ll be here, Mum,\u0026quot; Ginny said, though her voice was tight.","Then, a sound. The roar of an engine.","A single light appeared in the sky, growing larger and louder. With a skid and a spray of mud, Hagrid’s motorbike touched down in the paddock.","Harry scrambled out of the sidecar before it even stopped moving. \u0026quot;Hagrid! Are you okay?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fine, Harry! Just a scratch!\u0026quot; Hagrid boomed, wiping blood from his forehead.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Molly screamed, running forward and crushing him into a hug. \u0026quot;You\u0027re safe! You\u0027re safe!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Who else is back?\u0026quot; Harry asked breathlessly, pulling away.","\u0026quot;No one yet,\u0026quot; Ginny said, scanning the dark clouds.","Then, \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e. \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e. \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e.","Figures began to materialize out of the darkness.","Kingsley and Hermione landed on the Thestral. Hermione slid off, shaking but unharmed, and immediately transformed back into herself. She ran to Harry, throwing her arms around him.","\u0026quot;We made it!\u0026quot; she gasped. \u0026quot;Kingsley was amazing!\u0026quot;","Next came Bill and Fleur on a Thestral. Then Arthur and Fred. Then Tonks and Ron.","Harry counted heads frantically. \u0026quot;Where\u0027s George? Where\u0027s Moody?\u0026quot;","A moment of terrifying silence stretched.","Then, a broomstick plummeted from the sky, pulling up at the last second to land in a heap of limbs. Lupin and George rolled onto the grass.","George sat up immediately, checking his head. He reached up, felt both his ears, and grinned.","\u0026quot;Still got \u0027em both!\u0026quot; George cheered. \u0026quot;Though a curse missed me by an inch! Remus flies like a maniac!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Where is Mad-Eye?\u0026quot; Bill asked grimly.","A final \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e echoed.","Mad-Eye Moody and a terrified-looking Mundungus Fletcher appeared at the edge of the wards. Moody was limping heavily, his clothes scorched, his magical eye spinning so fast it was a blue blur, but he was upright.","\u0026quot;Damn coward!\u0026quot; Moody roared, grabbing Mundungus by the collar. \u0026quot;Tried to Disapparate, did you? I told you I\u0027d hex you if you broke formation!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I panicked!\u0026quot; Mundungus wailed. \u0026quot;There were dozens of them!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And we beat them!\u0026quot; Moody shouted, shoving Mundungus onto the grass.","He limped over to the group, surveying them with his magical eye. He counted thirteen heads. Thirteen living, breathing people.","\u0026quot;Everyone?\u0026quot; Moody grunted.","\u0026quot;Everyone,\u0026quot; Harry said, feeling a wave of relief so strong his knees buckled.","\u0026quot;Miracle,\u0026quot; Bill breathed. \u0026quot;They were waiting for us. They knew we were moving tonight.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Someone talked,\u0026quot; Moody growled. \u0026quot;But that\u0027s a problem for later. Tonight... we made it.\u0026quot;","Mrs. Weasley looked at the group—battered, windblown, but alive. She burst into fresh tears, this time of pure joy.","\u0026quot;Inside!\u0026quot; she commanded, her voice trembling. \u0026quot;All of you! I have brandy! I have soup! Come inside!\u0026quot;","As they walked toward the crooked, glowing warmth of the Burrow, Harry looked back at the sky. He thought of the Dursleys, driving toward their safe house. He thought of Snape, playing his dangerous double game. And he thought of the road ahead.","They had survived the flight. The Order was intact. And Harry Potter was ready to finish this."]},{"num":38,"origNum":38,"title":"Something Old, Something New, Something Borrowed","wordCount":1227,"paragraphs":["The morning of the wedding dawned bright and breezy, a perfect day for Bill and Fleur. The Burrow, however, was in a state of controlled hysteria. Mrs. Weasley was shouting orders about napkins, Fred and George were threatening to slip a love potion into the punch, and Charlie was trying to darn a hole in his dress robes with a wand that kept sparking.","Harry, seeking a moment of peace before the madness truly began, had retreated to the small, sunlit sitting room downstairs. He was trying to tie his tie—a skill Vernon had taught him, but which required a mirror he didn\u0027t currently have—when the door creaked open.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot;","He turned. Hermione stood there, and Harry’s hands froze on his tie. She was wearing a floaty, lilac dress that seemed to shimmer in the morning light. Her hair was sleek and shiny, not bushy, knotted at the back of her head. She looked breathtaking.","\u0026quot;Hi,\u0026quot; Harry breathed, forgetting entirely what he was doing.","\u0026quot;Hi,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled, a nervous flush on her cheeks. She turned around, presenting her back to him. \u0026quot;Could you... help me? Ginny is busy fighting with her hair, and I can\u0027t reach the zip.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah. Of course.\u0026quot;","Harry stepped forward, his fingers brushing the warm skin of her back as he found the small zipper. He pulled it up slowly, the soft rasp of the fabric the only sound in the room. He smoothed the material at her shoulders, his hands lingering for a fraction of a second longer than necessary.","\u0026quot;Done,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","Hermione turned around slowly. She looked up at him, her brown eyes searching his green ones. The air between them crackled with the same electricity that had filled the guest room at Privet Drive.","\u0026quot;You look...\u0026quot; Harry started, but he couldn\u0027t find the word. \u0026quot;You look beautiful, Mione.\u0026quot;","Hermione didn\u0027t say anything. She stepped closer, rising on her tiptoes, and pressed her lips to his.","It wasn\u0027t a quick peck for \u0026quot;protocol.\u0026quot; It was slow, sweet, and full of promises for a future they hoped they’d get to see. Harry’s hands moved to her waist, pulling her closer, losing himself in the moment.","\u0026quot;Morning!\u0026quot;","The cheerful voice shattered the mood like a dropped plate.","Harry and Hermione sprang apart as if electrocuted. Hermione spun around, her hands flying to her mouth. Harry nearly tripped over his own feet.","George Weasley was leaning against the doorframe, wearing a dressing gown and a grin that stretched from ear to ear (or, well, ear to hole).","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t mind me,\u0026quot; George said brightly, winking. \u0026quot;Just passing through. Carry on with the... \u003cem\u003ezipper inspection\u003c/em\u003e. Very thorough work, Harry. Top marks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We were just...\u0026quot; Hermione stammered, turning the color of a ripe plum.","\u0026quot;Helping!\u0026quot; Harry blurted out. \u0026quot;With the dress!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Of course, of course,\u0026quot; George nodded sagely. \u0026quot;That\u0027s what they all say. Just be careful, Harry. If Mum catches you \u0027helping\u0027 before the ceremony, she\u0027ll turn you into a garden gnome. Ostrich maneuvers are strictly forbidden until after the cake.\u0026quot;","George chuckled and sauntered away toward the kitchen, whistling the wedding march.","Hermione buried her face in her hands. \u0026quot;I am going to live in the library. Forever.\u0026quot;","Harry grinned, straightening his crooked tie. \u0026quot;At least it wasn\u0027t Ron.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Last Will and Testament\u003c/strong\u003e","The mood shifted dramatically an hour later. The joy of the wedding preparation was interrupted by the arrival of Rufus Scrimgeour. The Minister for Magic looked old and war-weary as he limped into the Burrow’s garden, flanked by two grim Aurors.","He demanded a private audience with Harry, Ron, and Hermione. They sat at the kitchen table, the silence heavy and tense.","\u0026quot;I am here,\u0026quot; Scrimgeour rasped, pulling a scroll of parchment from his robes, \u0026quot;to execute the last will and testament of Albus Percival Wulfric Brian Dumbledore.\u0026quot;","Harry kept his face impassive. To Scrimgeour, Dumbledore was dead. Harry had to play the part of the grieving student, not the co-conspirator.","\u0026quot;To Ronald Bilius Weasley,\u0026quot; Scrimgeour read, \u0026quot;I leave my Deluminator. In the hope that he will remember me when the lights go out.\u0026quot;","Ron took the silver object, looking confused but reverent. \u0026quot;Cool. Thanks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To Hermione Jean Granger,\u0026quot; Scrimgeour continued, \u0026quot;I leave my copy of \u003cem\u003eThe Tales of Beedle the Bard\u003c/em\u003e. In the hope that she will find it entertaining and instructive.\u0026quot;","Hermione accepted the old, rune-covered book, her mind already racing with questions.","\u0026quot;And to Harry James Potter,\u0026quot; Scrimgeour said, his yellow eyes fixing on Harry. \u0026quot;I leave the Snitch he caught in his first Quidditch match at Hogwarts. As a reminder of the rewards of perseverance and skill.\u0026quot;","Harry took the tiny gold ball. It felt cold and dead in his hand. He knew there was more to it—flesh memories—but he didn\u0027t let his skin touch it yet.","\u0026quot;Is that it?\u0026quot; Harry asked coldly.","\u0026quot;Not quite,\u0026quot; Scrimgeour said, his voice tightening. \u0026quot;Dumbledore left you a second bequest, Mr. Potter. The Sword of Godric Gryffindor.\u0026quot;","Harry’s heart skipped a beat, but he kept his expression bored. \u0026quot;Where is it, then?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Unfortunately,\u0026quot; Scrimgeour sneered, \u0026quot;the sword was not Dumbledore\u0027s to give. It is a historical artifact of Hogwarts. Furthermore... it is missing. It has not been seen since the night of his death.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So you\u0027re saying,\u0026quot; Harry said, channeling Vernon’s aggressive negotiation tactics, \u0026quot;that you’ve lost it? The Ministry lost a priceless artifact? Sounds like typical incompetence to me.\u0026quot;","Scrimgeour stood up, furious. \u0026quot;Watch your tone, boy! I know you’re up to something! Dumbledore may be dead, but his plots live on in you!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dumbledore is gone,\u0026quot; Harry lied smoothly, looking the Minister in the eye. \u0026quot;And the only thing I\u0027m up to is attending a wedding. Now, if you don\u0027t mind, I have a tie to fix.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Crashed Party\u003c/strong\u003e","The wedding was beautiful. The marquee was filled with golden light, floating balloons, and laughter. Bill looked ruggedly happy; Fleur was radiant. For a few hours, the war felt far away.","Harry, disguised by Polyjuice Potion to look like a red-headed Weasley cousin (\u0026quot;Barny\u0026quot;), sat with Ron and Hermione. They watched the dancing, momentarily forgetting the Snitch and the book in their pockets.","Then, the air changed.","It wasn\u0027t a sound. It was a feeling. The golden light in the marquee dimmed, as if a cloud had passed over the sun. The temperature plummeted. The floating champagne glasses frosted over and shattered.","A silver lynx—Kingsley’s Patronus—landed in the center of the dance floor.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eThe Ministry has fallen. Scrimgeour is dead. They are coming.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Panic erupted. Guests screamed and scrambled for the exits.","Then, the sides of the marquee ripped open.","They didn\u0027t just walk in; they glided. Dozens of Dementors swarmed into the tent, their ragged cloaks trailing over the grass, bringing with them a suffocating wave of despair. Behind them, masked Death Eaters fired curses into the crowd.","\u0026quot;Harry! Go!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley shouted, fighting off a Dementor with his Patronus.","\u0026quot;Hermione!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, grabbing Ron’s arm.","Hermione was already moving. She grabbed Harry’s hand and Ron’s wrist. The cold of the Dementors was closing in, the screams of the guests fading into a dull roar in Harry\u0027s ears.","\u0026quot;Hold on!\u0026quot; Hermione screamed.","She turned on her heel.","The darkness of the marquee swirled and vanished, replaced by the crushing pressure of Disapparition. The music, the wedding, and the Burrow were gone. They were on the run."]},{"num":39,"origNum":39,"title":"The Noble House of Black","wordCount":508,"paragraphs":["The sensation of Disapparition ended with a sharp crack, dumping Harry, Ron, and Hermione onto the dusty pavement of a familiar square. The streetlamps flickered overhead.","\u0026quot;Grimmauld Place,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, checking the street for watchers. \u0026quot;Quickly.\u0026quot;","They scrambled up the steps of Number Twelve. Harry tapped his wand on the door—the sequence Sirius had taught him—and they tumbled into the hallway.","The gas lamps flared to life. And there, standing at the end of the hall with his wand raised and a look of fierce, terrified aggression, was Sirius Black.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Sirius lowered his wand, rushing forward to grab Harry by the shoulders. \u0026quot;I saw the Patronus... the Ministry fell... are you hurt?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re fine,\u0026quot; Harry said, breathless. \u0026quot;But we have to talk. We found something in the cave. It wasn\u0027t the Horcrux.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Truth About R.A.B.\u003c/strong\u003e","Ten minutes later, they were seated in the kitchen. Harry placed the fake locket on the wooden table. He had opened it to reveal the note signed by \u003cem\u003eR.A.B.\u003c/em\u003e.","Sirius stared at the parchment, his hand trembling.","\u0026quot;Regulus,\u0026quot; Sirius whispered, his voice thick with a mixture of grief and shock. \u0026quot;Regulus Arcturus Black. My idiot brother.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He stole the real Horcrux,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly. \u0026quot;He turned against Voldemort. He died trying to bring him down.\u0026quot;","Sirius looked up, his grey eyes shining with tears. \u0026quot;I thought he was just a follower. A coward. But he... he tried to finish it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We need to find the real one,\u0026quot; Hermione said gently. \u0026quot;Sirius, do you know if Regulus brought it here?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Kreacher!\u0026quot; Sirius barked.","The ancient house-elf appeared with a \u003cem\u003ecrack\u003c/em\u003e, looking miserable. But when he saw the locket, he collapsed into wailing sobs.","It took twenty minutes to coax the whole, agonizing story out of the trembling elf. Between ragged sobs on the flagstones, Kreacher spoke of a nineteen-year-old Regulus Black who had grown sickened by the Dark Lord’s cruelty—who had lent Kreacher to Voldemort, only to watch the elf return half-dead from a subterranean sea of corpses.","He told them of the second trip to the sea cave, when Regulus had ordered Kreacher to switch the lockets, drink nothing himself, and leave his young master behind to be dragged beneath the black water by the Inferi. By the time Kreacher finished, Hermione had a hand pressed to her mouth, Ron was pale, and Sirius was sitting with his head bowed, tears dripping onto the scarred wood of the kitchen table for the little brother he had misjudged for sixteen years.","\u0026quot;I tried to destroy it, Master Sirius,\u0026quot; Kreacher wailed, pounding his bony fists against the floor. \u0026quot;Nothing left a mark upon it! And then—and then the thief came in the night!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mundungus Fletcher,\u0026quot; Kreacher croaked, swaying. \u0026quot;He stole it, Master. He stole Master Regulus\u0027s locket from the cabinets!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And where is it now?\u0026quot; Harry demanded.","\u0026quot;Kreacher tracked him,\u0026quot; the elf sniffed. \u0026quot;A woman... a Ministry woman... she took it from him. She threatened him. A woman looking like a toad.\u0026quot;","Harry, Ron, and Hermione exchanged a dark look.","\u0026quot;Umbridge,\u0026quot; Harry spat."]},{"num":40,"origNum":40,"title":"Magic is Might","wordCount":624,"paragraphs":["The planning sessions took place over the next two weeks. Sirius was desperate to come with them.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t sit here while you break into the Ministry!\u0026quot; Sirius argued, pacing the kitchen. \u0026quot;I know the building!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re Undesirable Number Two, Sirius,\u0026quot; Harry reminded him firmly, channeling a bit of Vernon’s no-nonsense practicality. \u0026quot;Every Death Eater in the Atrium has your face memorized. If you walk in there and the Polyjuice slips, they\u0027ll lock down the building in ten seconds. We need you holding Grimmauld Place as our extraction point.\u0026quot;","Sirius hated it, but he relented. He spent the time drilling them on Ministry protocols and secret passages instead.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Infiltration\u003c/strong\u003e","On the chosen morning, the Trio engaged in their now-familiar routine of Polyjuice Potion. This time, they had ambushed three Ministry employees.","Harry transformed into the hulking Albert Runcorn.","Ron became the small, nervous Reg Cattermole.","Hermione became the squat Mafalda Hopkirk.","\u0026quot;Remember,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice deep and rumbling in Runcorn’s body. \u0026quot;In and out. Find Umbridge. Get the locket. Run.\u0026quot;","They flushed themselves down the public toilets and emerged into the Atrium of the Ministry of Magic.","It was a nightmare. The golden fountain was gone, replaced by a towering black statue of a witch and wizard sitting on thrones made of naked, twisted Muggles. The slogan \u003cem\u003eMAGIC IS MIGHT\u003c/em\u003e hung above them.","They were separated almost immediately. Yaxley, a Death Eater Harry recognized from the tower, ordered \u0027Cattermole\u0027 (Ron) to fix the rain in his office. Ron, looking terrified, was dragged away to the lifts.","Harry and Hermione, trying to blend in, stepped into the lift. Just as the doors were closing, a hand blocked them.","Dolores Umbridge stepped inside.","She looked exactly the same—the velvet bow, the pink cardigan—but around her neck, resting against her pale throat, glinted the heavy gold locket of Salazar Slytherin.","Harry felt a surge of rage so potent his wand hand twitched. He felt the locket humming, calling to the piece of soul Voldemort had accidentally left in him.","\u0026quot;Ah, Mafalda,\u0026quot; Umbridge simpered. \u0026quot;And Runcorn. Going down to the courtrooms? We have a heavy batch of Mudbloods today.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry grunted, staring straight ahead.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Courtroom\u003c/strong\u003e","The courtroom was freezing. Dementors glided in the corners, casting a pall of despair over the terrified Muggle-borns awaiting interrogation.","Umbridge sat on the high bench, flanked by Yaxley. She was toying with the locket.","\u0026quot;This?\u0026quot; she was saying to a weeping woman. \u0026quot;This is the Selwyn family crest. One of the Sacred Twenty-Eight. A symbol of pure blood. Something you would know nothing about.\u0026quot;","The lie was too much. The desecration of an object belonging to the founders, used to prop up her bigotry, snapped Harry’s control.","\u0026quot;It\u0027s a lie,\u0026quot; Harry said loudly, his voice echoing in the stone chamber.","Umbridge looked down, confused. \u0026quot;What did you say, Runcorn?\u0026quot;","Harry pulled out his wand. The Polyjuice was beginning to itch, but he didn\u0027t care.","\u0026quot;I said,\u0026quot; Harry roared, \u0026quot;IT\u0027S A LIE! \u003cem\u003eSTUPEFY!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The jet of red light hit Umbridge square in the chest. She collapsed over the bench.","Chaos erupted. Yaxley jumped up, but Hermione was faster.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eStupefy!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Yaxley crumpled.","Harry vaulted over the barrier. He snatched the locket from Umbridge’s unconscious neck, feeling the cold metal against his skin.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eExpecto Patronum!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Harry cast the spell not for Dementors, but to clear the room. The silver stag erupted from Runcorn’s wand, charging the Dementors and driving them back.","\u0026quot;Hermione, let\u0027s go!\u0026quot;","They freed the Muggle-borns, telling them to run, and sprinted for the door. They met Ron in the corridor—he was wet, dripping from the magical rain, but safe.","\u0026quot;Got it?\u0026quot; Ron gasped.","\u0026quot;Got it!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, holding up the locket. \u0026quot;To the Atrium!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":41,"origNum":41,"title":"The Clean Getaway","wordCount":423,"paragraphs":["They burst into the Atrium just as the alarms began to scream. The fireplaces were sealing themselves off.","\u0026quot;There!\u0026quot; Yaxley shouted, recovering and sprinting out of a lift. \u0026quot;Stop them!\u0026quot;","Spells flew across the hall. Harry deflected a curse meant for Hermione.","\u0026quot;Group together!\u0026quot; Harry commanded.","They grabbed hands. Harry seized Ron’s arm; Hermione grabbed Harry’s and Ron’s. They spun on their heels.","The world twisted. Darkness pressed in.","But Yaxley had lunged. His hand closed around Hermione’s arm just as they vanished.","Harry saw it happening in the suffocating darkness of the limbo between spaces. He saw Yaxley hitching a ride, trying to break their concentration, trying to follow them to Grimmauld Place.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eRELASHIO!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Harry screamed in the void, pointing his wand blindly at the weight dragging on Hermione.","A jet of sparks hit Yaxley in the face. With a silent scream, the Death Eater lost his grip, flung away into the nothingness of the inter-dimensional space.","The pressure lifted.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","They hit the ground hard. It wasn\u0027t the pavement of London. It was soft pine needles and earth.","They tumbled over each other, gasping for air. The silence of a forest surrounded them.","Harry scrambled up, wand raised, checking the perimeter. \u0026quot;Everyone okay? Ron? Hermione?\u0026quot;","Hermione was sitting up, checking her arm where Yaxley had grabbed her. It was bruised, but whole.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m fine,\u0026quot; she breathed. \u0026quot;He... he grabbed me. But you hit him, Harry. He let go.\u0026quot;","Harry turned to Ron. \u0026quot;Ron? You in one piece?\u0026quot;","Ron was lying on his back, panting, looking pale but grinning. He lifted his arms and legs, wiggling his fingers and toes.","\u0026quot;All here,\u0026quot; Ron said. \u0026quot;No eyebrows missing. No knees left behind. I think I\u0027m actually getting good at this.\u0026quot;","Harry slumped against a tree, pulling the heavy gold locket from his pocket. It gleamed innocently in the dappled sunlight filtering through the trees.","\u0026quot;We did it,\u0026quot; Harry said, feeling the adrenaline crash. \u0026quot;We have the locket. And we didn\u0027t lead them back to Sirius.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Where are we?\u0026quot; Ron asked, sitting up and looking at the dense woods.","\u0026quot;Forest of Dean,\u0026quot; Hermione said, standing up and brushing pine needles from her robes. \u0026quot;I brought us here. It was the first place I thought of. It’s safe.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at the locket, then at his friends. They were tired, scared, and hunted. But they were whole.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Harry said, slipping the locket around his neck for safekeeping. \u0026quot;First rule: we keep moving. Second rule: we figure out how to destroy this thing.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":42,"origNum":42,"title":"The Frequency of Fear","wordCount":1202,"paragraphs":["The weeks that followed their escape from the Ministry were a blur of rain, canvas, and gnawing hunger. They moved constantly, never staying in one forest for more than two nights. From the Forest of Dean to the moors of Yorkshire, they became ghosts in the landscape.","Harry took the lead on security, channeling Mad-Eye Moody’s paranoia and Vernon Dursley’s obsession with perimeter checks. He set wards that hummed with power, alarms that triggered if so much as a fox crossed the line.","But while Harry managed the safety and Hermione managed the logistics (and the food, though her mushrooms were becoming a source of quiet despair), Ron was managing the silence.","Or rather, he was trying to fill it.","He spent every waking hour huddled over the small, battered wireless radio he had packed, twisting the dial with obsessive precision. He wasn\u0027t listening for music; he was listening for names.","\u0026quot;Anything?\u0026quot; Harry asked one evening, dropping a bundle of dry firewood near the tent entrance.","\u0026quot;Just propaganda,\u0026quot; Ron muttered, his voice tight. \u0026quot;The Ministry is churning out lists of \u0027Undesirables\u0027. They\u0027re saying Dad is under investigation for \u0027muggle-loving tendencies\u0027. And Ginny... they say she\u0027s back at Hogwarts, but Snape is Headmaster. And the Carrows are in charge of discipline.\u0026quot;","Ron looked up, his eyes dark and rimmed with red. Around his neck, the heavy gold locket of Salazar Slytherin glinted in the firelight. It was his turn to wear it.","\u0026quot;And Luna,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, the name catching in his throat. \u0026quot;Xenophilius Lovegood published an article supporting you, Harry. Now the Quibbler\u0027s printer has been smashed. No one’s seen Luna since the train ride.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027ll find them, Ron,\u0026quot; Hermione said gently, stirring a pot of watery stew. \u0026quot;Once we destroy this thing... once we stop him...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Once? When?\u0026quot; Ron snapped. The locket pulsed against his chest, amplifying the fear that had been eating him alive since the wedding. \u0026quot;We don\u0027t know how to open it. We don\u0027t know where the other Horcruxes are. We\u0027re just camping!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re staying alive,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;That\u0027s step one.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is it?\u0026quot; Ron challenged, his hand going to the locket. \u0026quot;Because it feels like we\u0027re hiding while everyone else bleeds.\u0026quot;","The rain started in November and didn\u0027t stop. The dampness seeped into their bones. The locket’s influence grew stronger, a constant, whispering presence that fed on their exhaustion.","Harry found it hard to concentrate when he wore it; he kept seeing the image of Sirius falling through the veil (a false memory implanted by fear) or the Dursleys being tortured in their safe house. Hermione became weepy and anxious.","But Ron took it the hardest. His worry for his family wasn\u0027t just anxiety; it was a physical pain. Every time the radio crackled with news of a raid or a disappearance, Ron flinched as if struck.","One evening in a sodden wood near the Severn, the tension finally snapped.","Hermione was trying to strip the bark off a scavenged branch to make tea. Harry was studying the Marauder\u0027s Map, watching the dots at Hogwarts moving in patterns he couldn\u0027t decipher.","Ron was by the radio. \u003cem\u003eClick. Hiss. Click.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot; ...rumors of a raid in Ottery St. Catchpole... several injured... status of the Burrow unknown...\u0026quot;","The voice on the radio faded into static.","Ron froze. He stood up slowly, the radio clattering to the floor.","\u0026quot;Did you hear that?\u0026quot; Ron demanded, his voice shaking.","\u0026quot;I heard,\u0026quot; Harry said, standing up. \u0026quot;Ron, it\u0027s just rumors. The Order is protecting them. The Burrow has the strongest wards Bill could set.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Wards break!\u0026quot; Ron yelled, turning on Harry. The locket swung from his neck like a pendulum. \u0026quot;People die, Harry! My family is in the line of fire because of \u003cem\u003eyou\u003c/em\u003e! because we\u0027re out here playing camping trip while they\u0027re being hunted!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are not playing!\u0026quot; Harry shouted back, his own temper flaring. \u0026quot;We are hunting the only things that can kill him! What do you want me to do, Ron? Walk into the Ministry and ask Voldemort for a duel?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I want a plan!\u0026quot; Ron roared. He ripped the locket off his neck, but he didn\u0027t hand it over. He held it in his fist, his knuckles white. \u0026quot;You said you knew what you were doing! You said Dumbledore left you instructions! But he didn\u0027t, did he? He left you a Snitch and a sword we can\u0027t find! We have nothing!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We have each other!\u0026quot; Hermione cried, stepping between them. \u0026quot;Ron, please! It\u0027s the locket talking! Take it off!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s not the locket!\u0026quot; Ron spat, though his eyes were wild with the Horcrux\u0027s influence. \u0026quot;It\u0027s me! I\u0027m the one listening to the list of dead people every night! I\u0027m the one wondering if my sister is being tortured by Carrows! I\u0027m the one wondering if Luna is dead!\u0026quot;","He looked at Harry, and for a second, the friendship that had survived trolls, spiders, and werewolves seemed to shatter.","\u0026quot;You don\u0027t get it,\u0026quot; Ron said, his voice dropping to a cruel whisper. \u0026quot;You don\u0027t have a family to lose, do you? Your parents are dead. Sirius is hiding. The Dursleys are safe in a bunker. You\u0027re fine. You can afford to wait.\u0026quot;","Harry went cold. It was a low blow, aimed with surgical precision by the piece of Voldemort\u0027s soul in the locket.","\u0026quot;My parents,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly, his voice trembling with suppressed rage, \u0026quot;died to give me a chance to fight him. Don\u0027t you dare talk to me about losing family.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Then do something!\u0026quot; Ron screamed. \u0026quot;Lead us! Or are we just going to wait until there\u0027s no one left to save?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am doing my best!\u0026quot; Harry yelled. \u0026quot;But if that\u0027s not good enough for you... if you think you can do better... then go!\u0026quot;","The silence that followed was deafening. The rain drummed against the canvas roof.","Ron stood there, chest heaving. He looked at Hermione, who was sobbing silently. He looked at Harry, whose face was hard and closed.","He looked at the locket in his hand.","\u0026quot;Fine,\u0026quot; Ron said.","He threw the locket onto Harry’s bunk. He grabbed his rucksack.","\u0026quot;Ron, no!\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked, running to him. \u0026quot;You can\u0027t leave! You can\u0027t!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m going back,\u0026quot; Ron said, shaking her off gently but firmly. \u0026quot;I have to know if they\u0027re okay. I can\u0027t stay here anymore.\u0026quot;","He walked to the tent flap. He paused, looking back at Harry one last time.","\u0026quot;I hope you find it, Harry,\u0026quot; Ron said, his voice hollow. \u0026quot;Whatever it is you\u0027re looking for.\u0026quot;","He stepped out into the rain.","\u0026quot;Ron!\u0026quot; Hermione screamed, chasing after him.","Harry stood frozen in the tent. He heard Hermione calling Ron\u0027s name in the darkness. He heard the sound of the wind.","And then, a sharp, final \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e of Disapparition.","A minute later, Hermione returned alone. She was soaked, her hair plastered to her face, her eyes wide with shock. She looked at the empty space where Ron had been. She looked at Harry.","She collapsed onto the floor and wept.","Harry walked over and picked up the locket. It was cold. He put it in his pocket, feeling the weight of it like a stone.","They were two now. And the winter had only just begun."]},{"num":43,"origNum":43,"title":"The Silver Doe and the Sword","wordCount":1383,"paragraphs":["The weeks without Ron were a hollow, grey existence. The silence in the tent was deafening, broken only by the crackle of the radio or the turn of a page. Harry and Hermione moved around each other like ghosts, united by their mission and their love, but fractured by the absence of the third point of their triangle.","On a freezing night in the Forest of Dean, Harry sat on watch outside the tent. Hermione was asleep, her breath misting in the cold air. Harry stared into the darkness, the locket heavy and cold against his chest, listening to the wind in the trees.","Then, a light appeared.","It wasn\u0027t a lantern or a wand tip. It was a soft, silver glow that seemed to weave through the oaks. A silver doe stepped into the clearing. She was beautiful, ethereal, and silent. She looked at Harry with large, gentle eyes, and then turned, trotting away into the dense forest.","Harry didn\u0027t think; he followed.","He tracked the Patronus through the snow, his heart pounding. She led him deep into the woods, to a small, frozen pool surrounded by gnarled trees. As Harry approached, the doe vanished into nothingness.","Harry walked to the edge of the pool. The ice was thick and opaque, but something glittered beneath it. He raised his wand.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eLumos.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The light penetrated the ice. Lying on the bottom of the pool, gleaming with an inner rubied fire, was the Sword of Godric Gryffindor.","\u0026quot;You\u0027ve got to be joking,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to the empty forest.","He couldn\u0027t summon it; Dumbledore had told him that much. To possess the sword, one had to show valour. He had to retrieve it.","Harry stripped off his outer layers, shivering violently as the biting wind hit his skin. He pointed his wand at the ice. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eDiffindo.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","A triangular chunk of ice cracked and bobbed in the dark water. Harry took a deep breath, gripped the edge of the hole, and lowered himself in.","The cold was agonizing. It felt like fire against his skin. He kicked down, swimming toward the glimmer of silver. His fingers brushed the hilt.","Suddenly, the locket around his neck woke up.","It sensed the sword—the one thing that could destroy it. The golden chain constricted. It tightened around Harry’s windpipe like a steel wire. Harry gasped, inhaling water. He thrashed, clawing at his throat, but the metal was cutting into his skin. His vision began to swim. The sword slipped from his fingers. The darkness of the pool rushed in. \u003cem\u003eDrowning. Dying.\u003c/em\u003e","Then, a splash.","Arms—strong, human arms—wrapped around his chest. He was hauled upward with tremendous force. He broke the surface, coughing and retching, dragging air into his burning lungs.","He was dragged onto the snowy bank. He lay there, gasping, shaking uncontrollably.","\u0026quot;Are you mental?\u0026quot; a familiar voice roared. \u0026quot;Why didn\u0027t you take the thing off first?\u0026quot;","Harry rolled over, hacking up water. Standing over him, soaking wet, holding the sword of Gryffindor in one hand and the broken chain of the locket in the other, was Ron Weasley.","\u0026quot;Ron?\u0026quot; Harry croaked, his voice raw.","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Ron panted, shivering. \u0026quot;I came back.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You... you saved me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well, I couldn\u0027t let you drown, could I?\u0026quot; Ron said, his teeth chattering. \u0026quot;Hermione would kill me.\u0026quot;","Harry stared at him. The anger he had felt for weeks vanished, replaced by overwhelming relief. He stood up, shaking, and began to pull his clothes back on.","\u0026quot;The sword,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;You got it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Ron handed it to him. \u0026quot;Here.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry pushed it back. \u0026quot;You have to do it, Ron. You have to destroy the locket.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Me?\u0026quot; Ron stepped back, looking terrified. \u0026quot;No way. That thing... it talks to me, Harry. It knows me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That\u0027s why you have to do it,\u0026quot; Harry insisted. \u0026quot;You faced it. You came back. You\u0027re the one who needs to finish it.\u0026quot;","Harry walked over to a flat rock and placed the locket on it. It was twitching now, sensing the end.","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll open it,\u0026quot; Harry said, raising his wand. \u0026quot;You strike. Do it fast.\u0026quot;","Ron gripped the sword with both hands, his face pale. He nodded.","\u0026quot;One... two... three! \u003cem\u003eOpen!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The lid of the locket flew open.","It didn\u0027t release a monster. It released a cloud of black smoke that coalesced into three towering, terrifying figures.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eRon Weasley...\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; the voice hissed. It was Voldemort\u0027s voice, but twisted, echoing Ron\u0027s own thoughts.","The smoke formed into the shapes of Arthur, Molly, and Ginny Weasley. They looked dead. Their eyes were hollow, their bodies broken.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eYou ran,\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; the smoke-Arthur whispered, pointing a skeletal finger. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eYou left us to die. The Burrow is burning, and you are hiding in the woods.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Ron yelled, raising the sword, but he was shaking.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eUseless,\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; the smoke-Molly screeched. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eMy least loved son. You could not protect us. You are not a hero. You are nothing.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Then, the smoke shifted. It formed into Harry and Hermione. But they weren\u0027t kissing; they were looking at Ron with expressions of utter, cold disappointment.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eWe didn\u0027t need you,\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; the smoke-Harry sneered. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eWe were better off without you. You are weak. You are a burden.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eWhy did you come back?\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; the smoke-Hermione whispered, her voice cutting deeper than any knife. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eYou abandoned your family. You abandoned us. You are a coward, Ron Weasley. A coward.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Ron stood frozen, the sword trembling in his hands. The tears were streaming down his face. This wasn\u0027t jealousy; this was his deepest shame. The fear that he wasn\u0027t enough to save the people he loved.","\u0026quot;Do it, Ron!\u0026quot; the real Harry screamed from the side. \u0026quot;It\u0027s a lie! We love you! Kill it!\u0026quot;","Ron looked at the smoke-Hermione, who was turning away from him in disgust. He looked at the smoke-Arthur, lying dead on the floor.","A roar built up in Ron’s chest. It was the roar of a brother, a son, and a Gryffindor.","\u0026quot;I AM NOT LEAVING AGAIN!\u0026quot;","Ron swung the sword. The blade flashed silver in the moonlight.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The sword cleaved the locket in two. A long, piercing scream echoed through the forest, and the smoke vanished instantly.","Silence returned to the clearing. Ron dropped the sword and fell to his knees, sobbing into the snow.","Harry walked over slowly. He sat down next to his best friend and put a hand on his shoulder.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m sorry,\u0026quot; Ron choked out. \u0026quot;I\u0027m so sorry I left. I just... I thought you\u0027d be better off.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We weren\u0027t,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly. \u0026quot;We were lost without you, mate.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reunion\u003c/strong\u003e","The walk back to the tent was slow. When they pushed through the canvas flap, Hermione was sitting by the heater, reading \u003cem\u003eThe Tales of Beedle the Bard\u003c/em\u003e.","She looked up. She saw Harry, dry now but looking exhausted. And then she saw Ron, standing sheepishly in the entryway, holding the broken locket.","Her book slid from her fingers and hit the floor.","She stood up slowly. Her expression was unreadable.","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Ron started, taking a step forward. \u0026quot;I—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You,\u0026quot; she whispered.","She walked toward him. Ron braced himself, perhaps expecting a hug.","Instead, Hermione launched herself at him and began to pummel his chest with her fists.","\u0026quot;You... complete... \u003cem\u003earse\u003c/em\u003e!\u0026quot; she shrieked with every hit. \u0026quot;You left! You left us! We thought you were dead! We thought you were captured! How could you! You stupid, stupid, arrogant ginger idiot!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ow! Hermione! I know! I\u0027m sorry!\u0026quot; Ron yelped, trying to fend off the blows. \u0026quot;I destroyed the locket! I saved Harry!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t care!\u0026quot; she yelled, tears spilling over. \u0026quot;You walked away!\u0026quot;","She hit him one last time, hard, on the arm. And then, the anger broke. She threw her arms around his neck and buried her face in his shoulder, sobbing.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t you ever do that again,\u0026quot; she wept.","Ron looked at Harry over Hermione’s bushy head, his eyes wide with relief. He wrapped his arms around her, hugging her back tightly.","\u0026quot;I won\u0027t,\u0026quot; Ron promised, his voice thick. \u0026quot;I\u0027m staying. Until the end.\u0026quot;","Harry smiled, watching them. The locket was gone. The team was back together. And for the first time in months, the tent felt warm."]},{"num":44,"origNum":44,"title":"The Malfoy Gambit","wordCount":1125,"paragraphs":["The capture was sudden and brutal. One moment, they were discussing their next move in the tent; the next, Harry had slipped up. In a moment of frustration, the name \u0026quot;Voldemort\u0026quot; had slipped past his lips, triggering the Taboo.","Protective enchantments shattered like glass. Snatchers swarmed the campsite. Hermione hit Harry with a Stinging Hex, swelling his face beyond recognition, but it was a desperate, fleeting measure. Fenrir Greyback didn\u0027t care about faces; he cared about bounties. And when they found the Sword of Gryffindor in Harry’s bag, the destination was inevitable.","Malfoy Manor.","They were dragged through the iron gates and into the drawing room. The atmosphere was suffocating. Lucius Malfoy looked desperate, his face unshaven and gaunt. Narcissa looked terrified. Bellatrix Lestrange sat on a high chair like a queen, toying with a silver knife.","\u0026quot;Bring the boy closer,\u0026quot; Bellatrix ordered. \u0026quot;Draco! Look at him. Is this Potter?\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy stepped forward. He looked ill. He looked at the swollen, distorted face of his former rival. He looked into Harry’s bright green eyes—the only part of him the hex hadn\u0027t changed.","Harry stared back. He didn\u0027t plead. He just held Draco’s gaze, a silent message passing between them: \u003cem\u003eThe plan. Stick to the plan.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I... I can\u0027t be sure,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, turning away. \u0026quot;His face is messed up. It could be anyone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Look closer!\u0026quot; Lucius hissed, grabbing his son’s shoulder. \u0026quot;If we hand over Potter, all is forgiven! We will be rewarded!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I won\u0027t say it if I\u0027m not sure, Father!\u0026quot; Draco snapped, pulling away. \u0026quot;I’m not calling the Dark Lord for a random Mudblood and a swollen stranger!\u0026quot;","Bellatrix’s eyes narrowed. But before she could press him, she saw the sword in the Snatcher’s hand.","\u0026quot;That sword!\u0026quot; she shrieked. \u0026quot;Where did you get that? It’s supposed to be in my vault!\u0026quot;","Panic erupted. The Snatchers were stunned. Harry and Ron were dragged by the hair and thrown into the cellar, while Hermione was kept upstairs for interrogation.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dungeon Reunion\u003c/strong\u003e","The cellar was pitch black and damp. Harry and Ron hit the stone floor hard.","\u0026quot;Ron?\u0026quot; a dreamy, familiar voice whispered from the shadows.","Ron scrambled up, ignoring his own bruises. \u0026quot;Luna?\u0026quot;","Luna Lovegood stepped into the sliver of light from the grate above. She looked thin and pale, but her eyes were unclouded.","\u0026quot;Luna!\u0026quot; Ron choked out.","He didn\u0027t hesitate. He rushed forward and pulled her into a fierce embrace. Luna, usually so composed, let out a small sob and hugged him back.","Ron pulled back slightly, cupping her face in his hands. \u0026quot;I thought... the radio said... I thought you were gone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m here, Ronald,\u0026quot; she whispered. \u0026quot;It’s been quite boring, actually. Mr. Ollivander isn\u0027t much for conversation.\u0026quot;","Ron let out a wet laugh, and then, overwhelmed by the relief of finding her alive, he leaned down and kissed her. It was messy and desperate, full of months of fear and worry.","\u0026quot;Bloody hell,\u0026quot; came the voice of Dean Thomas from the corner. \u0026quot;About time, mate.\u0026quot;","Harry ignored them, pulling the two-way mirror shard from his sock. He saw a blue eye staring back.","\u0026quot;Help us,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to the glass. \u0026quot;We\u0027re in Malfoy Manor. They have Hermione.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Escape\u003c/strong\u003e","The rescue came in the form of a loud \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e. Dobby the house-elf appeared in the center of the cellar, his tennis-ball eyes wide.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked. \u0026quot;Dobby has come to rescue you!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Harry gasped. \u0026quot;Take Luna, Dean, and Ollivander to Shell Cottage. Then come back for us. We\u0027re going for Hermione.\u0026quot;","Dobby nodded, grabbed the hands of the prisoners, and vanished with a crack.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Harry said, looking at Ron. \u0026quot;Upstairs. On three.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;One... two... three!\u0026quot;","They burst out of the cellar just as Bellatrix was screaming at Hermione. The drawing room was chaos.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eExpelliarmus!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Ron roared, disarming Bellatrix.","Harry sprinted across the room, snatching wands from the stunned Snatchers.","Draco was standing near the fireplace, his wand raised. He locked eyes with Harry. He saw the desperation, the resolve.","Harry charged him. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eExpelliarmus!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Draco didn\u0027t block. He didn\u0027t dodge. He held his wand loosely, and the moment Harry’s spell hit, the hawthorn wand flew from Draco’s hand and smacked into Harry’s palm.","Harry felt a jolt of warmth. The allegiance had changed. The Elder Wand—wherever it was—now answered to him.","\u0026quot;Go!\u0026quot; Draco mouthed, backing away as if blown back by the force of the spell.","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Harry yelled.","The elf appeared on the chandelier, unscrewing it. It crashed to the floor, shattering crystal everywhere. Hermione scrambled away from the wreckage, running to Harry and Ron.","Bellatrix screamed in fury. \u0026quot;You dirty little monkey! You could have killed me!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby never meant to kill!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked defiantly from the mantelpiece. \u0026quot;Dobby only meant to maim, or seriously injure!\u0026quot;","Harry grabbed Hermione and Ron. He grabbed Dobby’s hand.","\u0026quot;GO!\u0026quot; Harry shouted.","They began to turn on the spot. The squeezing sensation of Disapparition took hold.","But Bellatrix, screaming with rage, whipped a silver knife from her robes and threw it across the room.","It flew end over end, shimmering in the firelight, aimed directly at the vanishing elf’s chest.","Harry saw it. His Seeker reflexes, honed by dodging Bludgers and Dudley’s punches, kicked in faster than conscious thought.","He didn\u0027t let go of the group, but he yanked Dobby backward violently, twisting his own body into the path of the blade.","\u003cem\u003eZING.\u003c/em\u003e","The knife sliced through the air where Dobby had been a millisecond before, burying itself harmlessly into the dark wainscoting of the manor walls.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The drawing room vanished.","\u003cstrong\u003eShell Cottage\u003c/strong\u003e","They hit the wet sand of a beach with a thud. The sound of crashing waves filled their ears. The salt air smelled like freedom.","Harry scrambled up, his heart hammering against his ribs. He looked around frantically.","\u0026quot;Hermione? Ron?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re okay,\u0026quot; Ron gasped, helping Hermione up. She was shaking, clutching her arm where Bellatrix had carved into her, but she was alive.","\u0026quot;Dobby?\u0026quot; Harry called out, panic rising in his throat.","The little elf was sitting in the sand a few feet away, looking dazed. He patted his chest. He looked at his tea-towel toga.","There was no blood. There was no knife.","Dobby looked up at Harry, his enormous eyes filling with tears of gratitude.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter... saved Dobby,\u0026quot; the elf whispered.","Harry fell to his knees in the sand, letting out a breath that felt like it had been held since Little Whinging.","\u0026quot;Of course I did, Dobby,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice thick. \u0026quot;I promised I wouldn\u0027t let anyone hurt you.\u0026quot;","Ron and Hermione crawled over, and the four of them sat huddled on the beach under the stars, battered, scarred, and hunted, but miraculously, impossibly, all alive."]},{"num":45,"origNum":45,"title":"The Dragon and the Deal","wordCount":910,"paragraphs":["The planning at Shell Cottage was brief and tense. Harry, remembering Vernon\u0027s lectures on \u0026quot;The Art of the Deal,\u0026quot; approached the negotiation with Griphook not as a desperate wizard, but as a pragmatic business partner.","\u0026quot;We need the Cup,\u0026quot; Harry told the goblin, sitting at Bill\u0027s kitchen table. \u0026quot;You want the Sword. We can make that trade. But the Sword is the only thing that destroys Horcruxes. You get it \u003cem\u003eafter\u003c/em\u003e the job is done. And in exchange, we ensure you get out alive. Voldemort is hunting anyone associated with this. You\u0027re safer with us.\u0026quot;","Griphook, surprised by the boy\u0027s blunt, transactional honesty, agreed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Infiltration\u003c/strong\u003e","Walking into Diagon Alley was like walking into a grave. But for Hermione Granger, the challenge wasn\u0027t the atmosphere; it was the acting.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t do it,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, tugging at the uncomfortable, heavy robes of Bellatrix Lestrange. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t be her. She\u0027s... she\u0027s evil.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t think of her as evil,\u0026quot; Harry whispered from under the Invisibility Cloak, where he was hiding with Griphook. \u0026quot;Think of her as... Aunt Petunia when the neighbors park in front of her driveway. Or Uncle Vernon when the waiter brings the wrong soup. Channel the entitlement, Hermione. You own this place.\u0026quot;","Hermione straightened her spine. She thought of Petunia Dursley sniffing at a dirty window. She thought of Bellatrix’s sneer.","She marched into Gringotts.","\u0026quot;I wish to enter my vault,\u0026quot; Hermione barked at the head goblin, her voice dripping with imperious disdain.","It worked. They were led deep into the bowels of the earth, Ron (disguised as a foreign wizard) looking sufficiently imposing beside her.","But the plan hit a snag at the Thief\u0027s Downfall. The waterfall washed away the Polyjuice Potion and the enchantments. The cart overturned, dumping them onto the tracks.","\u0026quot;Impostors!\u0026quot; the goblins yelled, backing away.","\u0026quot;Imperio!\u0026quot; Harry cast, taking control of the Bogrod, the goblin with the keys.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Vault\u003c/strong\u003e","They scrambled inside the Lestrange vault. It was a nightmare of searing heat and multiplying treasure. Every cup they touched burned their skin and duplicated, filling the room with scorching gold.","\u0026quot;There!\u0026quot; Harry shouted, spotting the small golden cup with the badger engraving on a high shelf.","\u0026quot;The Sword!\u0026quot; Griphook yelled, pointing at the blade hanging from Harry\u0027s belt. \u0026quot;Give it to me! I can unlock the containment charms!\u0026quot;","Harry didn\u0027t hesitate. He handed the Sword of Gryffindor to the goblin. \u0026quot;Do it!\u0026quot;","Griphook used the blade to pry open the magical barrier protecting the shelf. Hermione levitated Harry. He swung through the burning air, his hand snatching the Cup of Helga Hufflepuff.","\u0026quot;Got it!\u0026quot; Harry roared, dropping back down into the pile of burning gold.","\u0026quot;We have the Cup!\u0026quot; Ron yelled, kicking away a pile of hot galleons. \u0026quot;Let\u0027s go!\u0026quot;","They turned to the door.","Griphook stood there, clutching the Sword. In the original timeline, his instinct would have been to run, to lock them in and save himself. But he looked at Harry—the boy who had saved Dobby, the boy who had negotiated with honor.","\u0026quot;The guards are coming!\u0026quot; Griphook shouted, throwing the Sword back to Harry. \u0026quot;I cannot fight them! Use the beast!\u0026quot;","Harry caught the sword. \u0026quot;You\u0027re coming with us!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Great Escape\u003c/strong\u003e","They burst out of the vault. The corridor was swarming with armed goblins and wizards. There was no way back to the cart.","But there was a way up.","The Ukrainian Ironbelly dragon, blind and tortured, was chained in the center of the cavern.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eRelashio!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Hermione screamed, blasting the chains.","\u0026quot;Jump!\u0026quot; Harry ordered.","They scrambled onto the dragon\u0027s back. Harry pulled Hermione up. Ron hauled himself onto the neck. Griphook, looking terrified, hesitated on the ledge.","\u0026quot;Come on!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, reaching out his hand.","Griphook looked at the goblin guards rushing toward him, then at the hand of the wizard. He jumped. Harry caught the goblin’s wrist and hauled him onto the dragon\u0027s back, wedging him between himself and Ron.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eDefodio!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Harry cast, gouging the ceiling.","The dragon, sensing freedom, roared. It spread its massive, tattered wings and launched itself upward.","It was chaotic and terrifying. They smashed through the rock, through the marble floor of the lobby, and burst through the roof of Gringotts Bank.","Glass and debris rained down on Diagon Alley as the dragon clawed its way into the open sky, screaming its triumph.","They flew north, the wind whipping their faces, leaving a trail of destruction and stunned silence behind them. They held on for dear life—Harry, Ron, Hermione, and the goblin who had chosen the winning side.","As the adrenaline faded, the dragon began to descend, tiring from the flight. Below them, a cool, dark lake shimmered in the afternoon light.","\u0026quot;We have to jump!\u0026quot; Harry yelled over the wind. \u0026quot;The water will break the fall!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Are you mad?\u0026quot; Ron screamed.","\u0026quot;Now!\u0026quot;","They slid off the dragon’s sleek scales.","For a few seconds, they were weightless, falling through the cool air. Then—","\u003cem\u003eSPLASH.\u003c/em\u003e","They hit the water hard. The cold shock was exhilarating. They kicked to the surface, gasping for air, watching the dragon fly off toward the horizon.","Harry treaded water, clutching the Hufflepuff Cup in one hand and his wand in the other. He looked around. Ron was shaking water from his hair. Hermione was coughing. Griphook was clinging to a piece of drift wood, looking grumpy but very much alive.","They had the Cup. They had the Sword. And they were still in the fight."]},{"num":46,"origNum":46,"title":"The Ghost in the Pub","wordCount":966,"paragraphs":["The drying charms Hermione cast on the shore of the lake did little to warm the chill of the water, but the adrenaline kept them moving. After parting ways with Griphook—who, having received his freedom and a bag of gold Harry pressed on him, vanished into the countryside to find his own kind—the Trio held hands and turned on the spot.","They appeared in Hogsmeade, under the cover of the Invisibility Cloak.","Immediately, the air was rent by a scream. It wasn\u0027t a person; it was the Caterwauling Charm. It shrieked like a banshee, echoing off the mountains.","\u0026quot;Accio Cloak!\u0026quot; a rough voice roared.","Death Eaters swarmed out of the Three Broomsticks. Beams of light shot into the street, searching for them.","\u0026quot;In here!\u0026quot; a gruff voice hissed.","A door to their left swung open. A hand reached out into the empty air, grabbed Harry’s arm through the Cloak, and yanked them inside.","They tumbled into a dark, sawdust-strewn room. The door slammed shut and bolts were thrown.","\u0026quot;You bloody idiots!\u0026quot; the man growled. \u0026quot;Setting off the charm at this hour? Do you have a death wish?\u0026quot;","It was Aberforth Dumbledore. He looked furious, peering through a spyhole in the curtains.","\u0026quot;We didn\u0027t know about the charm,\u0026quot; Harry panted, pulling off the Cloak. \u0026quot;Thanks, Aberforth.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t thank me yet,\u0026quot; Aberforth grunted. \u0026quot;They\u0027re swarming. You\u0027re trapped.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We need to get into the school,\u0026quot; Harry said urgently. \u0026quot;Tonight.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Impossible,\u0026quot; Aberforth snapped. \u0026quot;Snape has the place locked down tight. And the Carrows are prowling the passages.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We have to,\u0026quot; Ron insisted, shivering. \u0026quot;We have a job to do. Dumbledore left us a mission.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Did he now?\u0026quot; Aberforth sneered. \u0026quot;My brother and his missions. Getting people killed for the \u0027Greater Good\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That\u0027s enough, Abe,\u0026quot; a calm, familiar voice said from the shadows near the hearth. \u0026quot;They have had a long journey. Offer them a drink.\u0026quot;","Ron froze. Hermione gasped, dropping her beaded bag.","Slowly, incredulously, they turned toward the back of the room.","Sitting in a high-backed chair, looking much healthier than the last time Harry had seen him (though still nursing a glass of firewhisky), was Albus Dumbledore.","The silence in the room was absolute.","Ron’s mouth opened and closed like a goldfish. He looked at the \u0026quot;dead\u0026quot; Headmaster, then at Harry, then back at Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Ron whispered. \u0026quot;Is that... are you a ghost?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I should hope not, Mr. Weasley,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled, his eyes twinkling in the firelight. \u0026quot;Ghosts cannot enjoy a good mead, and I find I have developed quite a taste for it in my retirement.\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a strangled sob. \u0026quot;Professor? But... we saw... the tower... the funeral...\u0026quot;","She looked at Harry. She saw the lack of surprise on his face. She saw the resignation.","\u0026quot;You knew,\u0026quot; Hermione accused, her voice trembling. She shoved Harry’s shoulder hard. \u0026quot;Harry James Potter! You knew!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I had to,\u0026quot; Harry said, holding his hands up in surrender. \u0026quot;He made me promise. On the night of the tower. It was the only way to protect Draco. To protect Snape.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Snape?\u0026quot; Ron sputtered. \u0026quot;But he killed him! We saw the green light!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A performance,\u0026quot; Dumbledore explained gently, standing up. \u0026quot;A Blasting Curse disguised as a Killing Curse. A Cushioning Charm. And a great deal of trust in Severus’s acting abilities. It was necessary, Ron. Voldemort had to believe I was gone. He had to believe Severus was his.\u0026quot;","Hermione stared at the Headmaster. Her logical mind was racing, reassembling the events of the last year. \u0026quot;The sword,\u0026quot; she breathed. \u0026quot;That\u0027s why it was missing. You had it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot; Dumbledore nodded. \u0026quot;And now, I see you have returned with a Cup and a very wet Goblin-made sword. You have done magnificently.\u0026quot;","Ron shook his head, a grin slowly spreading across his face. \u0026quot;You\u0027re alive. You crazy old... you\u0027re actually alive.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;For now,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said soberly. \u0026quot;But my survival must remain a secret. If Voldemort learns of this before the final piece is in place, everything Severus has done will be for nothing. Do you understand?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We won\u0027t tell a soul,\u0026quot; Hermione promised, wiping her eyes.","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. He looked at the portrait of the young girl above the mantelpiece. \u0026quot;Now, I believe you wanted to get into the school?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We need to find the... the other thing,\u0026quot; Harry said, glancing at Aberforth.","\u0026quot;Ariana,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said to the portrait. \u0026quot;You know what to do.\u0026quot;","The girl in the painting nodded and turned away, walking down a long painted tunnel until she vanished into darkness.","They waited in tense silence. A few minutes later, the portrait swung forward like a door.","A tunnel was revealed. And scrambling out of it, looking battered, bruised, but grinning wildly, was Neville Longbottom.","\u0026quot;I knew it!\u0026quot; Neville cheered, dusting off his robes. \u0026quot;I knew you\u0027d come! Hey, Harry! Ron! Hermione!\u0026quot;","He stopped, seeing the figure standing behind them. Neville’s eyes bulged.","\u0026quot;Pro... Professor Dumbledore?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hello, Neville,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;I hear you have been giving the Carrows quite a headache. Ten points to Gryffindor.\u0026quot;","Neville looked like he might faint, but he steadied himself. \u0026quot;Right. Okay. You\u0027re alive. That\u0027s... that\u0027s brilliant. That changes everything.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It changes nothing yet, Neville,\u0026quot; Harry said quickly. \u0026quot;No one can know. Not even the D.A. Not yet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Got it,\u0026quot; Neville nodded, understanding the gravity of the war instantly. \u0026quot;Lips sealed. But come on. You won\u0027t believe what it\u0027s like in there. We’ve been waiting for you.\u0026quot;","Harry turned to Dumbledore. \u0026quot;We\u0027ll finish it, Professor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know you will,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. \u0026quot;Go.\u0026quot;","Harry, Ron, and Hermione climbed into the tunnel behind Neville. As the portrait swung shut behind them, sealing off the room and the secret of the living Headmaster, Harry felt a surge of adrenaline.","They were back. And this time, they weren\u0027t just fighting for survival. They were fighting to win."]},{"num":47,"origNum":47,"title":"The Parting of Ways","wordCount":1049,"paragraphs":["The Great Hall was silent as a tomb. The house tables had been cleared away, leaving the students standing in four large masses, huddled together under the enchanted ceiling which swirled with dark, angry clouds.","Severus Snape stood on the raised platform, his black robes hanging still around him. He looked gaunt, his face a mask of impenetrable coldness. Flanking him were the Carrows—Alecto and Amycus—who grinned with sadistic anticipation, their wands drawn.","\u0026quot;It has come to my attention,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice low but echoing perfectly to the back of the hall, \u0026quot;that Harry Potter was sighted in Hogsmeade earlier this evening.\u0026quot;","A ripple of murmurs broke out. Snape waited for it to die down.","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Snape continued, pacing slowly. \u0026quot;Should anyone attempt to aid Mr. Potter... should anyone attempt to conceal him... they will be punished. Specifically, any student found to be in collusion with him will answer to me.\u0026quot;","He stopped, scanning the sea of faces.","\u0026quot;However... if anyone here has knowledge of his movements... and steps forward now... they will be treated with leniency.\u0026quot;","The silence stretched. No one moved. The fear of the Carrows was great, but the loyalty to Harry—and the memory of Dumbledore—was greater.","Then, from the center of the Gryffindor mass, a voice rang out.","\u0026quot;It seems, despite your exhaustive defensive strategies, you still have a bit of a security problem, Headmaster.\u0026quot;","The students gasped and parted. Harry Potter stepped into the aisle. He stood tall, looking directly at the man who had taught him Occlumency, the man who had saved his life a dozen times, and the man he now had to publicly destroy with words.","The doors to the Great Hall banged open.","Kingsley Shacklebolt, Remus Lupin, Arthur Weasley, Fred, George, and the rest of the Order of the Phoenix strode in, wands raised, flanking Harry.","\u0026quot;I’m afraid it’s a bit of a staff rebellion, Severus,\u0026quot; Kingsley said, his deep voice calm and dangerous.","Snape looked at Harry. He looked at the Order. For a split second, Harry saw something flicker in the Headmaster’s black eyes—not fear, but a grim satisfaction. \u003cem\u003eThe boy made it. The actors are in place.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Harry Potter,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, raising his wand.","Harry stepped forward, his heart pounding. He had to sell this. He had to make everyone believe the lie, or Dumbledore’s safety—and Snape’s life—would be forfeit.","\u0026quot;How dare you,\u0026quot; Harry shouted, his voice thick with a rage that felt real, channeled from the memory of the Astronomy Tower. \u0026quot;How dare you stand where he stood!\u0026quot;","The Carrows looked ready to curse, but they waited for Snape\u0027s command.","\u0026quot;You are a coward!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, pointing his wand at Snape. \u0026quot;You killed him! You killed Albus Dumbledore and you trusted him!\u0026quot;","It was the line Dumbledore had scripted for him, the accusation that cemented Snape’s cover.","Snape didn\u0027t flinch. He held his ground.","But before curses could fly, Professor McGonagall stepped out from the crowd of students. She moved in front of Harry, shoving him gently back.","\u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice devoid of emotion.","\u0026quot;Get back, Potter,\u0026quot; McGonagall snapped, her wand trembling with fury. She faced Snape. \u0026quot;You will not harm my students.\u0026quot;","She slashed her wand through the air. A torrent of fire erupted, spiraling toward Snape.","Snape raised a Shield Charm, deflecting the fire. He didn\u0027t counter-attack. He stepped back, parrying McGonagall’s furious assault. She sent daggers of ice; he melted them. She sent a lasso of smoke; he transmuted it to black vapor.","Harry, watching closely, noticed what no one else did. Snape wasn\u0027t just blocking; he was aiming his deflections.","McGonagall fired a piercing hex. Snape blocked it with a lazy flick, redirecting the jet of light directly behind him. It hit Alecto Carrow square in the chest. She slumped to the floor, unconscious.","\u0026quot;Traitor!\u0026quot; Amycus Carrow roared, raising his wand at McGonagall.","Snape, pretending to stagger back from another of McGonagall\u0027s spells, \u0026quot;accidentally\u0026quot; bumped into Amycus, shoving his wand arm upward just as he fired. The curse hit the ceiling, bringing down a heavy chandelier directly onto Amycus’s head. He crumbled instantly.","With the Carrows down, Snape swirled his cloak. He blocked one final spell from McGonagall, caught Harry’s eye for a fraction of a second, and then dissolved into a cloud of black smoke.","He smashed through the Great Hall window, shattering the glass, and flew out into the night.","\u0026quot;Coward!\u0026quot; Harry screamed after him, maintaining the ruse until the very end. \u0026quot;COWARD!\u0026quot;","McGonagall lowered her wand, her chest heaving. She looked at the broken window, then turned to the students. The torchlight illuminated the hall, now free of the oppressive shadow of the Death Eaters.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, her voice shaking slightly. \u0026quot;It is good to see you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And you, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;But he\u0027s coming. Voldemort. He\u0027s on his way. We need to barricade the school.\u0026quot;","McGonagall straightened up. The grief vanished, replaced by the steel of the Deputy Headmistress.","\u0026quot;I shall secure the castle,\u0026quot; she declared. \u0026quot;Potter, you have a mission?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;I need to find something. Something Ravenclaw.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Then go,\u0026quot; McGonagall ordered. \u0026quot;We will hold him off.\u0026quot;","She turned to the statues lining the walls of the hall. She raised her wand high.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003ePiertotum Locomotor!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","With a rumble that shook the floor, the stone statues hopped down from their plinths. Knights, kings, and creatures of stone marched toward the doors.","\u0026quot;Hogwarts is threatened!\u0026quot; McGonagall cried, her voice ringing out. \u0026quot;Man the boundaries! Protect us! Do your duty to our school!\u0026quot;","She looked at Molly Weasley, a small smile touching her lips. \u0026quot;I\u0027ve always wanted to use that spell.\u0026quot;","As the statues marched out to form a perimeter and the younger students were evacuated through the portrait hole, Harry looked at Ron and Hermione.","\u0026quot;Ravenclaw Tower,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;The Diadem. That’s the next one.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll go to the Chamber of Secrets,\u0026quot; Ron said suddenly, holding up the basilisk fangs he had pulled from his bag earlier. \u0026quot;We need something to destroy the Cup. The sword is with you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Smart,\u0026quot; Harry nodded. \u0026quot;Hermione, go with him. I\u0027ll find the Diadem.\u0026quot;","They split up, running through the corridors of the castle as the sky outside turned black with the arrival of the Death Eater army. The Battle of Hogwarts had begun."]},{"num":48,"origNum":48,"title":"The Fire and the Flood","wordCount":1105,"paragraphs":["The battle raged above, shaking the ancient stones of the castle, but deep in the bowels of Hogwarts, silence reigned.","Ron and Hermione stood in the damp, echoing cavern of the Chamber of Secrets. The massive stone face of Salazar Slytherin loomed over them, surrounded by the skeletons of small animals. In Ron’s hand was a basilisk fang, yellowed and deadly sharp. On the wet floor sat the golden Cup of Helga Hufflepuff.","\u0026quot;You do it,\u0026quot; Ron said, his voice echoing. He handed the fang to Hermione. \u0026quot;You haven\u0027t destroyed one yet.\u0026quot;","Hermione took the fang. Her hands were trembling, not with fear, but with the weight of the moment.","\u0026quot;This is for the Muggles,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, thinking of her parents who didn\u0027t remember her. \u0026quot;This is for the innocent.\u0026quot;","She raised the fang high. The Cup seemed to sense the danger; a dark smoke began to swirl inside it, sounding like a thousand screaming voices.","\u0026quot;Do it, Hermione!\u0026quot; Ron shouted.","She brought the fang down with a primal scream.","\u003cem\u003eCRUNCH.\u003c/em\u003e","The fang pierced the gold. A torrent of black ichor exploded from the Cup. A shockwave blasted outward, knocking them both off their feet.","Suddenly, the black water in the surrounding pools surged up, rising like a tsunami. It formed the shape of Voldemort’s face, roaring in agony, before crashing down on top of them.","They sputtered, soaked to the bone, as the water receded. The Cup lay on the stone, twisted and lifeless.","Ron wiped the slime from his face and looked at Hermione. She was shivering, hair plastered to her face, but she was smiling—a fierce, triumphant smile.","\u0026quot;One down,\u0026quot; she gasped.","Ron scrambled up and pulled her to her feet. For a moment, they stood close, adrenaline coursing through them. In another timeline, this might have been the moment.","But Ron just grinned, raised his hand, and slapped a high-five against Hermione’s palm that echoed like a gunshot.","\u0026quot;Brilliant!\u0026quot; Ron cheered. \u0026quot;Absolute genius!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We did it!\u0026quot; Hermione laughed.","She pulled him into a tight, sisterly hug, squeezing the water out of his robes.","\u0026quot;For Harry,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered into his shoulder.","\u0026quot;For Luna,\u0026quot; Ron replied, squeezing back.","They broke apart, grinning.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Ron said, picking up the broken Cup. \u0026quot;Let\u0027s go find the others. I hope Harry\u0027s having as much fun as we are.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Room of Hidden Things\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry was definitely not having fun.","He stood atop a mountain of precarious furniture in the Room of Requirement, the Diadem of Ravenclaw clutched in his hand. He had found it perched on a bust of an ugly warlock, humming with dark energy.","But he wasn\u0027t alone.","\u0026quot;Hold it, Potter!\u0026quot;","Harry turned slowly on the pile of vanity mirrors. Standing below him, wands drawn, were Draco Malfoy and Gregory Goyle.","Draco looked terrified, his wand shaking. Goyle, however, looked unhinged.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; Harry said calmly, pocketing the Diadem. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t do this. The school is falling. Get out while you can.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We can\u0027t,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, his eyes darting to Goyle. \u0026quot;He... he wants to bring you in.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Dark Lord wants him dead!\u0026quot; Goyle grunted stupidly. \u0026quot;If we bring him the head, we get rewarded!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Goyle, no,\u0026quot; Draco hissed. \u0026quot;We just need the wand!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shut it, Draco!\u0026quot; Goyle roared. \u0026quot;You\u0027ve gone soft! Like your father!\u0026quot;","Goyle raised his wand, a cruel, vacant look in his eyes. He didn\u0027t aim a stunner. He aimed to burn the world down.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eFiendfyre!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","A jet of cursed fire erupted from Goyle’s wand. It wasn\u0027t just flames; it was a menagerie of beasts—serpents, chimeras, and dragons made of living magma. The fire consumed a stack of books instantly and roared upward, devouring everything in its path.","\u0026quot;Run!\u0026quot; Harry yelled.","He scrambled up the pile of junk as the heat became blistering. The fire was growing exponentially, eating the centuries of hidden objects.","Harry spotted two broomsticks leaning against a cabinet. He grabbed them both and kicked off, soaring into the smoky air just as the pile of chairs he had been standing on disintegrated into ash.","Below, Goyle was screaming. The fire he had summoned was out of his control. It had circled back, trapping him and Draco on a fragile island of desks.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Draco screamed, looking up, his face soot-stained and desperate.","Harry gripped the broom handle. He could leave them. They were enemies. They had tried to capture him.","We Dursleys stand by our friends, Vernon had said.","But we also save the idiots, Harry thought.","\u0026quot;Hold on!\u0026quot; Harry yelled.","He dove. The heat seared his face. He swooped low over the island.","\u0026quot;Grab my hand!\u0026quot; Harry roared at Draco.","Draco reached up, jumping. His hand locked around Harry’s wrist. Harry strained, the broom groaning under the weight, and hauled Draco up behind him.","\u0026quot;Goyle!\u0026quot; Draco shouted, pointing down.","Goyle was clinging to the top of a wardrobe, the fire licking at his heels. He looked terrified.","Harry threw the spare broom down. \u0026quot;Catch!\u0026quot;","Goyle fumbled, catching the broom. He mounted it clumsily and kicked off, wobbling into the air just as the wardrobe was swallowed by a flaming chimera.","\u0026quot;To the door!\u0026quot; Harry commanded.","They flew through the inferno, the heat singeing their robes, the roar of the fire deafening. They blasted out of the Room of Requirement, tumbling onto the cool stone floor of the corridor. The door slammed shut behind them, the wood searing hot.","Harry rolled over, coughing smoke. Draco and Goyle were lying on the floor, gasping.","\u0026quot;You saved me,\u0026quot; Goyle wheezed, looking at Harry with wide, stupid eyes. \u0026quot;Why?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because I\u0027m not a murderer,\u0026quot; Harry snapped, standing up.","He pulled the Diadem from his pocket. It was vibrating violently. He pulled the Sword of Gryffindor from his belt—he had taken it from Hermione before they split up.","\u0026quot;It ends,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","He stabbed the sword through the center of the Diadem.","A black, blood-like substance leaked from the tiara. It screamed—a high, piercing shriek that made Draco and Goyle cover their ears. Harry kicked the dying Horcrux toward the Room of Requirement. The heat radiating from the door seemed to grasp it, and the Diadem dissolved into nothingness.","Harry sheathed the sword. He looked at Draco.","\u0026quot;Go,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;Get Goyle out of here. Hide.\u0026quot;","Draco stood up, shaky but alive. He looked at Harry, then gave a sharp, singular nod.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said. It was the only thank you he could manage.","He grabbed Goyle and ran down the corridor, vanishing into the smoke of the battle.","Harry stood alone for a second, wiping soot from his glasses. Two down. The snake left. And then the man himself."]},{"num":49,"origNum":49,"title":"The Resurrection and the Light","wordCount":1175,"paragraphs":["Deep in the dungeons of Hogwarts, far below the lake where the giant squid tapped nervously against the glass, the Malfoy family sat in a secure holding cell. It wasn\u0027t a prison; it was a bunker. The door was reinforced with goblin silver, and the walls hummed with protections Severus Snape had woven himself.","Lucius Malfoy paced the small stone room, his usually impeccable hair disheveled. Narcissa sat on a cot, holding Draco’s hand so tight her knuckles were white.","\u0026quot;He is coming,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, feeling the tremor in the floorboards. \u0026quot;The Dark Lord is here. If he finds us...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He won\u0027t,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice trembling but certain. \u0026quot;Snape promised. Potter promised.\u0026quot;","Lucius stopped pacing. He looked at his son—the boy who had failed to kill, the boy who had been saved by his enemies. \u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Lucius muttered, shaking his head. \u0026quot;To think our survival depends on Harry Potter and a dead Headmaster’s plan. It is... humbling.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is necessary,\u0026quot; Narcissa said sharply. \u0026quot;We stay put, Lucius. We survive.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sky Breaks\u003c/strong\u003e","Above ground, the world was ending.","Lord Voldemort stood on a precipice in the Forbidden Forest, overlooking the castle. He did not hold the Elder Wand; he held his own yew wand, its feather core vibrating with his rage. He didn\u0027t need a legendary stick to destroy a school.","\u0026quot;Begin,\u0026quot; Voldemort whispered.","He slashed his wand through the air. A bolt of raw, destructive power slammed into the shimmering dome of protective enchantments McGonagall had cast.","The shield groaned. It flickered. And then, with a sound like a breaking wine glass amplified a thousand times, it shattered. Fragments of the ward rained down like burning confetti.","\u0026quot;Attack!\u0026quot; Bellatrix screamed from his side.","The army surged forward. Giants lumbered onto the viaduct, smashing the stone statues McGonagall had animated. Acromantulas swarmed up the walls. Death Eaters flew in black clouds, raining curses down on the defenders in the courtyard.","Harry stood at the front of the courtyard, flanked by Ron, Hermione, Ginny, and Neville. He fired stunning spells and shield charms, his movements a blur.","\u0026quot;There\u0027s too many of them!\u0026quot; Ron yelled, blasting a werewolf backward.","Then, the temperature plummeted.","It wasn\u0027t the chill of the wind; it was the vacuum of the soul. From the dark clouds above, a swarm descended. It was a legion of Dementors, hundreds strong, far more than had attacked the wedding. They swooped down like vultures, their ragged cloaks trailing rot and despair.","The defenders faltered. Wands dropped. The sheer weight of the misery was crushing. Harry felt the cold seep into his chest, drowning out the fire of the battle. He raised his wand, trying to think of the Dursleys, of the Burrow, of Hermione—but the memories felt distant, like they belonged to someone else.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eExpecto...\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Harry gasped, stumbling. The silver mist from his wand was wispy and weak.","A Dementor glided toward him, its scabbed hand reaching out.","Then, a voice cut through the screaming wind. It was calm, precise, and impossible.","\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eExpecto Patronum.\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026quot;","A phoenix made of blinding silver fire erupted from the shadows of the viaduct entrance. It didn\u0027t just fly; it soared, growing larger with every beat of its wings, driving the Dementors back with a wave of searing warmth.","The combatants froze. Death Eaters and students alike turned to look at the source of the spell.","Walking out of the castle, wearing scorched grey robes and looking every bit, the general returning to his army, was Albus Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;Albus?\u0026quot; Professor McGonagall whispered from the balcony, her hand flying to her mouth. She staggered, clutching the stone rail. \u0026quot;It cannot be...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s dead!\u0026quot; a Death Eater screamed. \u0026quot;We saw him fall!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore didn\u0027t stop. He walked straight to Harry, who was staring at him with wide, relieved eyes. The Headmaster stepped up beside the boy, the silver phoenix circling high above them, holding the darkness at bay.","\u0026quot;Together, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly, his blue eyes piercing. \u0026quot;Show them what true power looks like.\u0026quot;","Harry felt the shock vanish, replaced by a surge of joy so potent it felt like liquid sunlight. He looked at Dumbledore. He looked at Hermione and Ron. He looked at the school he loved.","He raised his wand high, matching Dumbledore’s stance.","\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eEXPECTO PATRONUM!\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026quot;","\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eEXPECTO PATRONUM!\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026quot;","They shouted it in unison.","It wasn\u0027t just a spell; it was a cataclysm of light.","Harry’s stag burst forth, but it was colossal, standing twenty feet tall. It joined Dumbledore’s phoenix. The two guardians merged, their light combining into a shockwave of pure, blinding silver energy.","It expanded outward in a rapidly widening sphere. It washed over the courtyard, the viaduct, the forest edge, and the lake.","The Dementors didn\u0027t just flee; they were obliterated. The silver light tore through them, dissolving their shadows into nothingness. The shockwave rolled out for five miles, cleansing the air, vaporizing the despair, and knocking the Giants off their feet with the sheer force of the positive energy.","For a long moment, the battlefield was bathed in absolute, silent white light.","Then, the light faded. The Dementors were gone. The air was warm again.","Silence reigned. Total, stunned silence.","\u0026quot;Professor!\u0026quot; Hagrid bellowed from the forest edge, sobbing loudly. \u0026quot;You\u0027re alive! I knew it! I knew yeh weren\u0027t gone!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Albus!\u0026quot; McGonagall cried, running down the steps, tears streaming down her face. \u0026quot;You... you old fraud! You wonderful old fraud!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore smiled, lowering his wand. He looked tired but triumphant.","\u0026quot;My apologies, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled. \u0026quot;I had to play dead. It was the only way to get a bit of peace and quiet around here.\u0026quot;","He turned to Harry. The humor faded from his face, replaced by solemn purpose.","Dumbledore reached into his sleeve and pulled out a wand. It was knobby, ancient, and radiated power. The Elder Wand.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said quietly, so only Harry could hear. \u0026quot;I possessed this wand for many years. But on the night of the Astronomy Tower, Draco Malfoy disarmed me.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded, understanding dawning. \u0026quot;And I disarmed Draco at the Manor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. \u0026quot;Its allegiance is yours. It has been waiting for you.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore held out the Elder Wand handle-first. Harry reached out and took it. A warmth like hot wine flooded his hand, far more potent than his old holly wand. The wand hummed, recognizing its master.","\u0026quot;But what will you use, Professor?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;I believe,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, eyes twinkling, \u0026quot;that a fair trade is in order.\u0026quot;","He reached out and gently took Harry’s holly and phoenix feather wand from his other hand.","\u0026quot;This wand has served you well, Harry. It shares a core with Voldemort’s. It is a brother. In my hands... perhaps it will teach Tom Riddle a final lesson about the power of connection.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore gripped Harry’s wand. He turned to face the forest, where Voldemort’s army stood in disarray, terrified by the return of the only wizard their master ever feared.","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, his voice ringing out like a bell. \u0026quot;Shall we finish this?\u0026quot;"]},{"num":50,"origNum":50,"title":"The Walk to the End","wordCount":1657,"paragraphs":["The silence that followed Dumbledore’s challenge was not one of fear, but of cold, calculating assessment. Lord Voldemort stared across the expanse of the grounds at the man he had believed dead. For a moment, his red eyes widened, a flicker of genuine shock piercing his composure.","But it was gone as quickly as it came, replaced by a sneer of supreme arrogance.","\u0026quot;You persist,\u0026quot; Voldemort’s voice amplified, booming across the grounds like thunder. \u0026quot;You cling to life, Dumbledore, like a barnacle to a sinking ship. It changes nothing. I have conquered death in ways you cannot comprehend. You are merely an old man with a borrowed trick.\u0026quot;","Voldemort did not attack. He lowered his wand, his gaze shifting from Dumbledore to the boy standing beside him.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter,\u0026quot; Voldemort hissed. \u0026quot;You have allowed your friends to die for you. You have allowed your teachers to shield you. But I speak now directly to you. On this night, you have fought valiantly. But you cannot win. I do not wish to spill magical blood. I wish only for you.\u0026quot;","The army of Death Eaters stood still, waiting.","\u0026quot;Join me in the Forbidden Forest,\u0026quot; Voldemort commanded. \u0026quot;Come alone. And I shall spare the school. I shall spare your defenders. But if you do not come... I shall kill every last man, woman, and child who tries to hide you from me.\u0026quot;","The Dark Lord turned, his cloak swirling, and vanished into the treeline, his army retreating into the shadows like a receding tide.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Decision\u003c/strong\u003e","The Great Hall had become a triage center. The wounded were being tended to, the air thick with the smell of smoke and ozone.","Harry stood apart from the crowd, his heart beating a slow, heavy rhythm. He knew. He had looked into the Penseive earlier (using the memories Slughorn had finally yielded and Dumbledore had collected). He knew about the accidental Horcrux. He knew that as long as he lived, Voldemort could not die.","\u0026quot;I have to go,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly.","Hermione, who was bandaging Ron’s arm, froze. She turned, her eyes wide with panic. \u0026quot;No. Harry, no! You heard Dumbledore! We’re winning! We destroyed the Dementors!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We aren\u0027t winning, Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice steady. \u0026quot;Not while he’s alive. And he won\u0027t die unless I do.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I won\u0027t let you!\u0026quot; Hermione grabbed his arm, tears spilling over. \u0026quot;We\u0027ll fight him together! We\u0027ll find another way!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;There is no other way,\u0026quot; Harry said gently. He pulled her into a hug, feeling her shake. \u0026quot;You have to trust me one last time. Look after Ron. Look after the school.\u0026quot;","He pulled away and walked over to Dumbledore, who was sitting quietly on the steps of the dais, the Elder Wand resting on his knee.","\u0026quot;You are going,\u0026quot; Dumbledore stated. It wasn\u0027t a question.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry said. He looked at the Elder Wand—the Deathstick, the Wand of Destiny. Then he looked at the holly wand in Dumbledore’s hand—his own wand.","\u0026quot;I need that back, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said, holding out his hand.","Dumbledore looked confused. \u0026quot;The Elder Wand is yours, Harry. It is the most powerful wand in existence. It is your best chance of survival.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m not going there to survive,\u0026quot; Harry said softly. \u0026quot;And I\u0027m not taking the Elder Wand to him. If he kills me and takes it... he becomes invincible. I\u0027m taking my own wand. The one that chose me.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore gazed at Harry with profound respect. He handed the holly wand back.","\u0026quot;You possess a wisdom far beyond your years, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore whispered. \u0026quot;Go. And do not fear.\u0026quot;","Harry took his old wand. He didn\u0027t say goodbye to Ron; he couldn\u0027t bear it. He slipped the Invisibility Cloak over his shoulders and walked out into the cool night air.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Forest\u003c/strong\u003e","The walk was long. Harry moved through the trees, his mind strangely clear. He thought of the Dursleys in their safe house, hopefully watching television and arguing over the kettle, safe because he was doing this. He thought of Hermione—of her fierce brown eyes, the scent of parchment and vanilla, and her ridiculous, wonderful Ostrich maneuver whenever she hid her blushing face against his chest.","He reached the clearing. The firelight flickered on the faces of the Death Eaters. Hagrid was tied to a tree, sobbing silently.","Voldemort stood in the center, waiting. He looked up as Harry pulled off the cloak and dropped it to the forest floor.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter,\u0026quot; Voldemort whispered, a smile twisting his lipless mouth. \u0026quot;The Boy Who Lived. Come to die.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m here,\u0026quot; Harry said. He didn\u0027t raise his wand. He stood tall, shoulders back, just as Vernon had taught him to stand in a negotiation. But the deal here was his life.","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Hagrid roared, struggling against his ropes. \u0026quot;HARRY! NO!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Silence!\u0026quot; a Death Eater shouted, silencing Hagrid with a wave of his wand.","Voldemort raised the yew wand. He didn\u0027t offer a duel. He didn\u0027t offer a speech. He simply aimed.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eAvada Kedavra!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The flash of green light illuminated the forest. Harry didn\u0027t look away. He saw the beam coming. And then, the world dissolved into white.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Living Room\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry gasped, inhaling air that smelled of baking bread and lilies.","He was lying on a soft rug. He sat up, blinking. He wasn\u0027t in a train station. He was in a living room—warm, cozy, and bathed in golden sunlight. There was a fire crackling in the grate. On the mantelpiece were photos: a baby Harry on a broomstick, a wedding photo of a laughing couple, and... strangely... a photo of Petunia Dursley holding a garden trowel.","\u0026quot;Harry.\u0026quot;","He turned. Sitting on the sofa were a man and a woman.","The man had untidy black hair and glasses. The woman had dark red hair and bright green eyes—eyes exactly like Harry’s.","\u0026quot;Mum? Dad?\u0026quot; Harry’s voice trembled.","Lily Potter smiled, radiating a love so powerful it felt like physical warmth. \u0026quot;My brave, brave boy.\u0026quot;","James Potter stood up and walked over, pulling Harry up from the rug and into a crushing hug. \u0026quot;We are so proud of you, son. So incredibly proud.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Am I... am I dead?\u0026quot; Harry asked, looking at them. \u0026quot;Is this it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not quite,\u0026quot; Lily said, standing up to join the hug. \u0026quot;You were hit by the Killing Curse, yes. But Voldemort... he was a little too greedy. When he used your blood to rebuild his body, he took your protection inside him. He tethered you to life.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the piece of his soul,\u0026quot; James added, his expression grim. \u0026quot;The part that has been clinging to you since that night in Godric\u0027s Hollow... that is gone. He destroyed his own Horcrux.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at his hands. They felt solid. \u0026quot;So I can go back?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You can,\u0026quot; Lily said softly, cupping his face. \u0026quot;Or you can stay. You can rest. You’ve fought so hard, Harry. You’ve earned peace.\u0026quot;","Harry looked around the warm room. He looked at his parents, the family he had yearned for his entire life.","But then he thought of the family waiting for him. He thought of Petunia kissing his scar. He thought of Vernon checking on him in the middle of the night. He thought of Ron and Hermione fighting in the castle.","\u0026quot;I have to go back,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice firm. \u0026quot;I have to finish it. For them.\u0026quot;","James grinned, ruffling Harry’s hair. \u0026quot;That’s my boy. Give them hell, Harry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Harry?\u0026quot; Lily whispered, kissing his forehead—right where Petunia had kissed him. \u0026quot;Know that we are always with you. In every beat of your heart.\u0026quot;","The room began to fade. The warmth turned to cold. The smell of baking bread turned to the smell of damp earth.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Procession\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry hit the ground. He lay face down in the dirt, keeping his eyes shut, his body limp.","\u0026quot;My Lord...\u0026quot; Bellatrix’s voice whispered.","Harry braced himself. But Voldemort laughed—a high, cold sound.","\u0026quot;No need, to check for a pulse\u0026quot; Voldemort sneered. \u0026quot;I saw the light leave his eyes. No one survives the Killing Curse twice. Not even Harry Potter.\u0026quot;","His arrogance was absolute. He didn\u0027t need confirmation because he believed himself infallible.","\u0026quot;Tie him up,\u0026quot; Voldemort ordered. \u0026quot;Let the giant carry him. We shall present our trophy to the school.\u0026quot;","Rough hands bound Harry’s wrists and ankles. He was hoisted into the air.","\u0026quot;No...\u0026quot; Hagrid sobbed, his voice broken. \u0026quot;Harry... oh, Harry...\u0026quot;","Hagrid cradled Harry in his massive arms as if he were a baby. Harry wanted to whisper, to tell him he was alive, but he couldn\u0027t risk it. He had to lay limp, feeling the tremors of Hagrid’s grief rock him with every step.","They marched out of the forest as dawn broke over the mountains.","Voldemort led the procession, his army laughing and jeering behind him. They walked up to the edge of the castle grounds.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter is dead!\u0026quot; Voldemort’s voice was magically amplified, booming into the Great Hall, into the dormitories, into the hearts of every defender.","The doors of the castle swung open. The survivors poured out onto the steps—Ron, Hermione, Ginny, Neville, McGonagall, and Dumbledore.","They stopped.","They saw Hagrid walking slowly from the tree line, weeping. And in his arms, limp and broken, lay the body of Harry Potter.","\u0026quot;NO!\u0026quot;","The scream ripped from Hermione’s throat. It was a sound of pure agony.","\u0026quot;HARRY!\u0026quot; Ron roared, starting to run forward, but Arthur grabbed him, holding him back.","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Ginny shrieked.","Even Dumbledore faltered. The old wizard staggered, his face turning ashen as he looked at the boy he had sent to die.","\u0026quot;He was trying to escape!\u0026quot; Voldemort shouted gleefully, spreading his arms. \u0026quot;He was killed while fleeing the grounds! Your hero is dead!\u0026quot;","The silence that fell over Hogwarts was heavier than stone. It was the silence of hope extinguishing.","Harry lay in Hagrid’s arms, listening to the screams of his friends, his heart hammering against his ribs, waiting for the moment to breathe."]},{"num":51,"origNum":51,"title":"The Boy Who Returned","wordCount":1215,"paragraphs":["Voldemort’s laughter was a high, cruel sound that seemed to freeze the morning air. He stepped toward the castle, his arms spread wide in triumph.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter is dead!\u0026quot; he bellowed again, savoring the despair on the faces of the resistance. \u0026quot;From this day forth, you put your faith in me...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;HARRY! NO!\u0026quot; Neville shouted, charging forward with a broken wand, only to be blasted back by Voldemort.","\u0026quot;And who is this?\u0026quot; Voldemort sneered. \u0026quot;Who has volunteered to demonstrate what happens to those who—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eCONFRINGO!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The spell didn\u0027t come from the defenders on the steps. It came from Hagrid’s arms.","Harry Potter rolled out of the giant’s grasp, hitting the stone of the courtyard and tumbling into a crouch. He didn\u0027t wait for the shock to register. He fired a Blasting Curse straight at Nagini, who was draped around Voldemort’s shoulders.","Voldemort screamed in fury, deflecting the curse with a slash of his yew wand, but the force of the explosion knocked him backward.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s alive!\u0026quot; Ron roared, his voice cracking with disbelief and joy.","Pandemonium erupted. The Centaurs charged from the forest, arrows flying. The defenders on the steps raised their wands, a renewed roar of hope drowning out the Death Eaters\u0027 confusion.","Harry didn\u0027t stop. He scrambled up and sprinted toward the castle doors, firing stunning spells over his shoulder to keep Voldemort at bay.","\u0026quot;Potter!\u0026quot; Voldemort shrieked, his face twisting into a mask of pure, animalistic rage. \u0026quot;Kill him! Kill him now!\u0026quot;","Harry dashed up the steps, weaving through the chaos. Dumbledore was there, standing like a statue amidst the fray, blasting Dolohov backward. He saw Harry coming. He saw the fire in the boy\u0027s eyes.","\u0026quot;Professor!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, sprinting past him. \u0026quot;The trade!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore didn\u0027t hesitate. He tossed the Elder Wand high into the air.","At the same moment, Harry tossed the holly wand.","Time seemed to slow. The two wands arced through the smoke-filled air, passing each other. Harry reached up, his seeker reflexes snatching the Elder Wand from the sky. As his fingers closed around the knobby wood, a jolt of electricity surged through his arm, familiar and fiercely powerful.","He spun around, leveling the Deathstick at the Dark Lord.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eExpelliarmus!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","Voldemort blocked it, but the force of the spell cracked the flagstones beneath his feet.","\u0026quot;You cannot win!\u0026quot; Voldemort roared, pursuing Harry into the Great Hall.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Battle of Hogwarts\u003c/strong\u003e","The duel that followed tore through the castle like a hurricane. Harry and Voldemort moved through the corridors, blasting statues and shattering windows. Green light met red in explosive collisions that shook the foundations.","But Voldemort was relentless. Even without the Elder Wand, his mastery of dark magic was unparalleled. He summoned firedrifts, animated suits of armor to crush Harry, and apparated with terrifying speed. Harry was forced backward, deflecting and shielding, sweat pouring down his face. He was surviving, but Voldemort was driving him toward the edge.","Meanwhile, the castle had become a meat grinder for the Death Eaters.","Fred and George Weasley fought back-to-back near the marble staircase, grinning manically as they unleashed a barrage of fireworks and hexes that sent Yaxley and Rookwood tumbling down the stairs, very much alive and very much unconscious.","Remus Lupin and Tonks fought side-by-side in the charms corridor, their dueling styles perfectly synchronized, protecting each other’s blind spots from a pack of werewolves.","In the Great Hall, Molly Weasley was a force of nature. Bellatrix Lestrange, cackling as she fired a Killing Curse at Ginny that missed by an inch, suddenly found herself facing the matriarch of the Weasley clan.","\u0026quot;NOT MY DAUGHTER, YOU BITCH!\u0026quot; Molly screamed.","Her wand was a blur. Bellatrix’s laugh died in her throat as she was forced onto the defensive. Molly’s curse hit Bellatrix square in the chest with the force of a cannonball, shattering her heart. Bellatrix fell, her eyes wide with shock, dead before she hit the floor.","At the center of the hall, Albus Dumbledore moved with the grace of a man half his age. He did not kill; he dismantled. With swipes of the holly wand, he bound Death Eaters in chains of water, encased them in stone, or simply banished them through the windows. He was a conductor, and the battle was his symphony.","Then, the dungeon doors burst open.","Severus Snape emerged, his black robes billowing. But he wasn\u0027t alone. Flanking him were Lucius, Narcissa, and Draco Malfoy.","\u0026quot;Traitors!\u0026quot; Travers screamed, pointing his wand at Snape.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eSectumsempra!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Snape slashed his wand. Travers collapsed, bleeding.","Lucius Malfoy, looking desperate and fierce, fought not for Voldemort, but for his son, stunning Macnair as he tried to flank them. Draco stood shoulder-to-shoulder with Dean Thomas, firing hexes at the masked figures he had once called allies.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Stand\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry was blasted backward through the oak doors, landing hard in the center of the courtyard. He scrambled up, gasping for breath, clutching the Elder Wand.","Voldemort glided through the dust, his eyes burning red. Nagini hissed, coiling around his feet, protected by a shimmering magical sphere.","\u0026quot;It ends, Harry Potter,\u0026quot; Voldemort whispered, raising the yew wand. \u0026quot;You have no shields left. No mothers to die for you. No Dumbledores to save you.\u0026quot;","Harry stood his ground, though his legs shook. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t need them to save me, Tom. I just need to finish the job.\u0026quot;","Voldemort laughed. \u0026quot;Nagini... kill.\u0026quot;","The giant snake lunged. She struck faster than thought, her jaws opening wide, aiming for Harry’s neck while he was focused on Voldemort.","Harry couldn\u0027t turn in time.","But from the rubble to his right, a figure surged forward. It was Neville Longbottom, limping, bloodied, but holding the Sword of Godric Gryffindor in both hands.","He didn\u0027t scream. He swung.","\u003cem\u003eSHING.\u003c/em\u003e","The silver blade sliced through the air and shore the great snake\u0027s head cleanly from its body.","The head spun through the air. The body thrashed and dissolved into black smoke—the last Horcrux, gone.","Voldemort screamed—a sound of physical agony as his soul was finally, completely mortal. He clutched his chest, staggering backward, his wand dipping for a fraction of a second.","It was the opening Harry needed.","He didn\u0027t use the Disarming Charm. He didn\u0027t use a stunner. He channeled every ounce of pain, every loss, every hope, and every bit of magic the Elder Wand possessed into one final, decisive strike.","He slashed the wand diagonally.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eDIFFINDO!\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","The Severing Charm, powered by the Wand of Destiny, hit Voldemort with the force of a guillotine.","There was no green light. No collision of spells.","The spell struck Voldemort across the chest. The impact was absolute. The Dark Lord was lifted off his feet and thrown backward. He hit the stone ground with a heavy, final thud.","His yew wand rolled out of his hand, clattering uselessly against the cobblestones.","Voldemort lay still, his red eyes staring blankly at the sky, a mortal man who had forgotten that death was the one thing he could never defeat.","The courtyard fell silent. The wind died down. The sun began to peek over the horizon, bathing the castle in the first light of a new day.","Harry Potter lowered his wand, his chest heaving, and stared at the body of Tom Riddle. It was over."]},{"num":52,"origNum":52,"title":"The Sun Rises","wordCount":852,"paragraphs":["The silence that followed the thud of Voldemort’s body was not empty; it was heavy with disbelief. The survivors stood frozen, wands still raised, staring at the corpse of the monster who had haunted their nightmares for decades. He looked small. He looked human. He looked finished.","Then, the sun broke fully over the horizon, bathing the ruined courtyard in gold.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s dead,\u0026quot; Ron Weasley whispered, his voice cracking in the quiet air. \u0026quot;He\u0027s actually dead.\u0026quot;","The realization hit the crowd like a physical wave.","\u0026quot;HARRY!\u0026quot;","The scream of joy came from Hermione. She sprinted across the cobblestones, ignoring the rubble, and collided with Harry, wrapping her arms around his neck and nearly knocking him over.","\u0026quot;You did it!\u0026quot; she sobbed into his dirty robes. \u0026quot;You stupid, brave, brilliant idiot! You did it!\u0026quot;","Ron was there a second later, grabbing them both in a crushing hug, lifting them slightly off the ground.","\u0026quot;We thought you were gone,\u0026quot; Ron choked out, burying his face in Harry\u0027s shoulder. \u0026quot;When Hagrid carried you... we thought it was over.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I told you,\u0026quot; Harry wheezed, squeezed between his two best friends. \u0026quot;I always come back.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wave of Relief\u003c/strong\u003e","The dam broke. The courtyard swarmed. People were crying, laughing, and shouting.","Neville Longbottom sat down hard on a piece of masonry, the Sword of Gryffindor resting on his knees, laughing hysterically while Luna Lovegood patted his shoulder.","Near the castle doors, the Weasley family collapsed into a single, red-headed pile. Molly Weasley was clutching Fred and George, sobbing uncontrollably.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re alive,\u0026quot; she wept, pulling Fred\u0027s face down to kiss his forehead. \u0026quot;My boys... my boys...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Steady on, Mum,\u0026quot; Fred laughed, though there were tears tracking through the soot on his face. \u0026quot;Can\u0027t get rid of us that easily. We haven\u0027t even opened the branch in Hogsmeade yet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think I lost a bit of ear, though,\u0026quot; George grinned, checking the side of his head. \u0026quot;To match yours. Now we\u0027re even.\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley held Bill and Ginny, looking at his family—battered, bruised, but miraculously whole. Not a single empty chair at the table.","Further back, Remus Lupin and Nymphadora Tonks were leaning against a shattered pillar, holding each other up. Remus looked older, grayer, but the lines of worry that had defined his face for years were smoothing out.","\u0026quot;Teddy,\u0026quot; Tonks whispered, resting her head on his chest. \u0026quot;Teddy has a father. And a mother.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He does,\u0026quot; Remus smiled, closing his eyes. \u0026quot;He does.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Unlikely Allies\u003c/strong\u003e","In the shadow of the dungeon entrance, the Malfoys stood apart from the celebration. Lucius looked broken, stripped of his arrogance. Narcissa clung to Draco, her eyes darting nervously at the cheering crowd.","Harry pulled away from Ron and Hermione. He walked through the crowd, which parted respectfully for him, until he reached them.","Draco flinched as Harry approached, but he didn\u0027t back down.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice hoarse.","\u0026quot;Malfoy,\u0026quot; Harry nodded. He looked at Narcissa. \u0026quot;You stayed. You fought.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We fought for our son,\u0026quot; Narcissa said coldly, though her grip on Draco tightened.","\u0026quot;That\u0027s enough,\u0026quot; Harry said. He looked at Draco and extended a hand.","Draco stared at it. It was the inverse of their first meeting on the train all those years ago. Slowly, hesitantly, Draco reached out and shook Harry\u0027s hand.","\u0026quot;We\u0027re even,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly.","Severus Snape stood nearby, leaning against the stone wall, looking like a man who hadn\u0027t slept in twenty years. He watched the handshake with an unreadable expression.","Harry walked over to him.","\u0026quot;Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said.","Snape pushed himself off the wall. He looked down at Harry, his black eyes searching the boy\u0027s face—seeing Lily’s eyes, yes, but finally seeing the man Harry had become.","\u0026quot;You cut it close, Potter,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, though the venom was gone. \u0026quot;Walking into the forest... it was a foolish Gryffindor move.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It worked,\u0026quot; Harry shrugged.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Snape murmured, looking out at the sunrise. \u0026quot;It did. Do not expect me to award you points for dying, however.\u0026quot;","Harry laughed. \u0026quot;I wouldn\u0027t dream of it.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Mentor\u003c/strong\u003e","Finally, Albus Dumbledore approached. He had been speaking with McGonagall and Sprout, but he broke away as Harry drew near. He looked at the Elder Wand in Harry’s hand.","\u0026quot;It is done,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly.","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Harry agreed. He looked at the powerful wand. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t want it, Professor. It\u0027s too much trouble.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A wise decision,\u0026quot; Dumbledore nodded. \u0026quot;What will you do with it?\u0026quot;","Harry looked at the holly wand tucked in his belt—the wand Dumbledore had returned to him. Then he looked at the Elder Wand.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m going to put it back,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;Where it belongs. In your tomb. If I die a natural death... the power breaks. And the cycle ends.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore beamed, a look of pure pride. \u0026quot;Harry... you are a better man than I ever was.\u0026quot;","Harry smiled, looking back at the Great Hall, where breakfast was already being conjured by the house-elves. He saw Ron and Hermione waving at him. He saw the life returning to the castle.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m just Harry,\u0026quot; he said.","And for the first time in his life, that was enough."]},{"num":53,"origNum":53,"title":"The Architect and the Outcasts","wordCount":871,"paragraphs":["The victory celebration had quieted into a focused, weary effort to tend to the wounded and account for the dead. The sun was high now, illuminating the scars of Hogwarts in brutal detail. The Astronomy Tower was a jagged stump; the Great Hall was missing half its roof; the marble staircase was a pile of rubble.","Harry stood in the courtyard, the Elder Wand humming in his hand. Dumbledore stood beside him, surveying the damage with a heavy heart.","\u0026quot;It will take months to repair,\u0026quot; McGonagall sighed, wiping soot from her cheek. \u0026quot;Perhaps the school will not open in September.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. He looked at the wand in his hand—the wand that had repaired his own holly wand in the original timeline, the wand capable of miracles. \u0026quot;It won\u0027t take months.\u0026quot;","He stepped forward, raising the Elder Wand. He didn\u0027t think of destruction; he thought of the castle as it was—his first home, the place that had given him magic.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eReparo Maxima.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","It wasn\u0027t a standard mending charm. A stream of gold and silver magic erupted from the tip of the wand, thicker and more potent than anything a normal wand could produce.","The rubble on the ground began to shake. Huge blocks of stone defied gravity, lifting into the air and slotting back into the walls with a deep, grinding thrum. The shattered glass of the windows flew upward, fusing back into pristine panes. The gargoyles hopped back onto their perches.","\u0026quot;Incredible,\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked.","\u0026quot;Help me,\u0026quot; Harry said to the teachers. \u0026quot;Guide the stone. I\u0027ll provide the power.\u0026quot;","For the next three days, Hogwarts became a construction site of magic. Harry stood at the epicenter, channeling the immense power of the Elder Wand, while Dumbledore, McGonagall, Flitwick, and Sprout directed the flow.","They rebuilt the Astronomy Tower, stone by stone. They wove the protective enchantments back into the gates. They regrew the burned grass of the grounds. It was exhausting work, but Harry refused to stop. He felt a responsibility to the castle—to put the world back together before he laid down his weapon.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Long Walk Home\u003c/strong\u003e","While the castle healed, the wounds of its people remained raw.","The Malfoys had not joined the celebrations. They sat in a corner of the Great Hall, isolated by a perimeter of glare and whispers. Every time Lucius moved, wands twitched in the hands of students who had lost friends. Narcissa kept her head bowed. Draco stared at the table, looking hollow.","They were pariahs. Even though they had switched sides at the last moment, the years of terror they had inflicted were not easily forgotten.","On the third evening, as the sun set over the newly restored viaduct, the Malfoys rose. They moved quietly toward the doors, trying to slip away before the evening meal began.","Harry saw them. He handed the Elder Wand to Dumbledore and jogged across the hall.","\u0026quot;Malfoy! Wait.\u0026quot;","The family froze near the entrance. Lucius turned, looking terrified that Harry had come to arrest them.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice guarded.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re leaving?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;There is no place for us here,\u0026quot; Narcissa said softly, looking at the angry faces of the students watching them. \u0026quot;We are... unwelcome.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They just need time,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;The wounds are fresh.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We do not have time,\u0026quot; Lucius muttered, looking at his arm where the Dark Mark was fading to a scar. \u0026quot;The Ministry... the Aurors... they will come for us.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at the family. He saw the fear he had once seen in himself. He remembered Vernon’s advice about protecting those who stood with you, even if they were difficult assets.","\u0026quot;Go home,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;Go to the Manor. Lock the gates.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And then?\u0026quot; Draco asked. \u0026quot;Wait for them to drag us to Azkaban?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;I’ll fix it.\u0026quot;","Lucius blinked. \u0026quot;You... you would do that? After everything?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You saved me at the Manor,\u0026quot; Harry said to Draco. \u0026quot;Narcissa, you lied to him in the forest (in the original timeline, Harry knew she would have; in this one, she fought for Draco). And Lucius... you fought for your son in the end.\u0026quot;","Harry stepped closer, lowering his voice.","\u0026quot;I have the ear of the new Minister. I have Kingsley. And I have the truth about Snape and Dumbledore’s plan. I will testify for you. I will tell them you were coerced. I will make sure you stay free.\u0026quot;","Narcissa let out a shuddering breath, tears filling her eyes. \u0026quot;Thank you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But I need time,\u0026quot; Harry warned. \u0026quot;The public is angry. Lay low. Don\u0027t speak to the press. Let me handle the politics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We will be silent as the grave,\u0026quot; Lucius promised, clutching his cane.","Draco looked at Harry. He didn\u0027t offer a handshake this time; he simply nodded, a look of profound, grudging respect on his face.","\u0026quot;Goodbye, Potter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;See you, Draco.\u0026quot;","Harry watched them walk out of the castle gates, three dark figures disappearing into the twilight. They were bruised and hated, but they were free.","Harry turned back to the Great Hall, where the noise of dinner was starting to rise. The castle was whole. His friends were safe. And tomorrow, he would finally put the Elder Wand to rest."]},{"num":54,"origNum":54,"title":"The Return to Normalcy","wordCount":923,"paragraphs":["The car provided by the Order—a sensible, black sedan driven by Dedalus Diggle—turned onto Privet Drive just as the streetlamps flickered to life.","The street was quiet. Lawns were manicured, cars were gleaming in driveways, and the only sign of disturbance was a cat watching them from a garden wall. It was aggressively, beautifully normal.","Vernon Dursley was the first to step out. He looked at Number Four, his castle, which was still standing. The wards hadn\u0027t exploded; the roof hadn\u0027t caved in.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, straightening his jacket. \u0026quot;The lawn needs mowing. But otherwise... adequate.\u0026quot;","Petunia stepped out, clutching her handbag to her chest. She looked at the front door, her heart hammering a frantic rhythm against her ribs. They had been told it was over. They had been told he was safe. But until she saw him, she wouldn\u0027t believe it.","Dudley grabbed his duffel bag (the cricket bat still protruding from the top) and followed his parents.","Diggle tipped his hat. \u0026quot;Safe and sound. I\u0027ll leave you to it.\u0026quot;","He popped away into the night.","Vernon unlocked the front door. The familiar smell of lemon polish and floor wax washed over them. The hallway was exactly as they had left it months ago—the photos on the wall, the coats on the rack, the silence.","They walked into the living room.","Sitting on the floral sofa, wearing clean jeans and a fresh t-shirt, was Harry. He looked tired, and there were new scars on his hands and face that hadn\u0027t been there in the summer, but he was holding a mug of tea and looking at them with a soft, genuine smile.","\u0026quot;Hi,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;I told you I\u0027d be back.\u0026quot;","Petunia let out a sound that was half-laugh, half-sob. She dropped her handbag on the floor and ran.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot;","She collided with him on the sofa, wrapping her arms around his neck and burying her face in his shoulder. She shook with the force of her relief, crying openly.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re alive,\u0026quot; she wept. \u0026quot;You stupid, wonderful boy. You\u0027re alive.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m okay, Aunt Petunia,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, patting her back. \u0026quot;It\u0027s over. He\u0027s gone.\u0026quot;","Vernon stood in the doorway, his face working hard to maintain composure. He looked at his nephew—the boy who had walked into a forest to die and walked back out.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Vernon choked out, his voice thick. He abandoned dignity and crossed the room, pulling both Harry and Petunia into a massive, trembling bear hug.","\u0026quot;You did it,\u0026quot; Vernon said gruffly into Harry\u0027s hair. \u0026quot;You really did it. You beat the bastard.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I had help,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, squeezed between them.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted, dropping his bag and diving onto the pile. \u0026quot;Move over, Mum!\u0026quot;","The four of them sat there for a long moment, a tangled mess of Dursleys and Potter, united in the sheer, overwhelming joy of survival.","\u0026quot;I... I missed you lot,\u0026quot; Harry admitted, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;Even the cottage cheese.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re ordering pizza,\u0026quot; Dudley declared immediately. \u0026quot;Five of them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Agreed,\u0026quot; Vernon said, wiping his eyes with his sleeve. \u0026quot;And beer. Proper beer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I believe,\u0026quot; a calm, familiar voice drifted in from the hallway, \u0026quot;that there is already a pot of tea brewed, should you prefer a warmer beverage to start.\u0026quot;","The Dursleys froze.","Vernon’s head snapped up. Petunia gasped, pulling away from Harry.","Standing in the doorway to the kitchen, holding a floral teapot and wearing pristine grey robes, was Albus Dumbledore.","Vernon Dursley turned a shade of pale usually reserved for ghosts.","\u0026quot;You...\u0026quot; Vernon whispered, pointing a shaking finger. \u0026quot;You\u0027re dead. We read the papers. We saw the obituary! \u0027Slain by Death Eater Lestrange!\u0027\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ah, yes,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled, walking into the room and setting the teapot on the coffee table. \u0026quot;The reports of my death were, as they say, a strategic necessity. Sugar, Vernon?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Strategic necessity?\u0026quot; Vernon repeated, staring at the old wizard. \u0026quot;You... you faked it? To fool the maniac?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To fool everyone,\u0026quot; Dumbledore corrected gently. \u0026quot;It was the only way to ensure Harry’s safety and to secure the loyalty of... a mutual friend.\u0026quot;","Petunia stared at him. She remembered the letter he had left on her doorstep fifteen years ago. She remembered his voice in the Howler. And now, seeing him alive, standing in her living room, she realized the magnitude of the game that had been played.","\u0026quot;You left him alone,\u0026quot; Petunia accused, though her voice lacked its usual bite. \u0026quot;You let everyone think you were gone. You let Harry carry the burden.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Harry was never alone,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly, looking at the boy on the sofa. \u0026quot;And as it turns out, he carried the burden far better than I ever could.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore turned to Vernon and Petunia, his expression turning solemn.","\u0026quot;I must also thank you,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. \u0026quot;When I left Harry on your doorstep, I hoped you would care for him as a son. I hoped you would provide the shelter he needed.\u0026quot;","He looked around the living room—at the photos, the television, the mundane, beautiful normalcy of it all.","\u0026quot;You did more than that,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said. \u0026quot;You gave him a home. You gave him a reason to fight. And in the end, it was your love—loud, stubborn, and perfectly ordinary—that helped save the world.\u0026quot;","Vernon puffed out his chest, his shock replaced by a familiar sense of vindication.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Vernon huffed, adjusting his tie. \u0026quot;We Dursleys get the job done, Headmaster. Whether it\u0027s selling drills or defeating Dark Lords. It\u0027s all about efficiency.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled. \u0026quot;Now, about that pizza, Dudley... I have heard excellent things about \u0027pepperoni\u0027.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":55,"origNum":55,"title":"The Pizza Protocol","wordCount":960,"paragraphs":["The doorbell of Number Four, Privet Drive, didn\u0027t just ring; it surrendered.","Within twenty minutes of Dumbledore\u0027s arrival, the house was besieged. But this time, it wasn\u0027t by Death Eaters or Dementors. It was by the smell of pepperoni, mozzarella, and the chaotic joy of the Order of the Phoenix.","The Weasleys arrived first, tumbling out of the fireplace (which Dumbledore had politely unblocked for the evening). Arthur Weasley immediately cornered Vernon to discuss the \u0026quot;aerodynamics of the pizza delivery scooter,\u0026quot; while Molly Weasley hugged Petunia, crying about \u0026quot;our brave boys.\u0026quot;","Then came Remus and Tonks, looking exhausted but blissful. And finally, walking up the driveway with the reluctance of a man marching to the gallows, was Severus Snape, flanked by a stern-looking Minerva McGonagall.","\u0026quot;Come in, come in!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, ushering them into the hall. He looked at Snape, who was eyeing the floral wallpaper with deep suspicion.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Vernon said, extending a hand to the Potions Master. \u0026quot;You\u0027re the double agent. The actor. I must say, Snape, your performance on the tower... chilling. Absolutely chilling. You have the poker face of a CEO during a hostile takeover.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at Vernon’s hand, then at Harry, who gave him a small, encouraging nod. Snape shook the hand.","\u0026quot;It was... necessary, Mr. Dursley,\u0026quot; Snape drawled. \u0026quot;Though I could have done without the sheer volume of pizza boxes.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Feast\u003c/strong\u003e","The living room and kitchen were transformed into a riot of noise and food. Dumbledore had transfigured the coffee table into a long banquet table, and the Dursleys\u0027 fine china was currently holding slices of Meat Feast and Hawaiian.","The conversations were a bizarre, wonderful clash of worlds.","In the corner, Dudley was showing Fred and George his boxing stance.","\u0026quot;So you just hit them?\u0026quot; Fred asked, fascinated. \u0026quot;No wand? No sparks?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just a right hook,\u0026quot; Dudley grinned, shadow-boxing.","\u0026quot;George,\u0026quot; Fred said seriously. \u0026quot;We need to sell \u0027The Dudley\u0027. A boxing glove on a spring. It’s genius.\u0026quot;","At the table, Hermione was explaining the concept of a \u0026quot;gap year\u0026quot; to Arthur Weasley, while Ron tried to teach Vernon the rules of Quidditch using pepperoni slices as players.","\u0026quot;It’s inefficient!\u0026quot; Vernon argued, moving a pepperoni Beater. \u0026quot;Why chase the Snitch when you can just foul the Seeker? It’s a supply chain issue!\u0026quot;","Petunia sat with McGonagall and Molly.","\u0026quot;He’s too thin,\u0026quot; Petunia fretted, watching Harry laugh with Ginny. \u0026quot;I need to get him back on the roast beef.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s alive, Petunia,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, taking a sip of wine. \u0026quot;And thanks to you, he’s sane. That is no small feat.\u0026quot;","Even Snape had been dragged into a conversation. He was standing by the window, trying to look invisible, when Remus who approached him.","\u0026quot;You made it, Severus,\u0026quot; Remus smiled, raising a slice of pizza.","\u0026quot;Do not get sentimental, Lupin,\u0026quot; Snape sneered, though he accepted a glass of wine. \u0026quot;I am only here because Dumbledore threatened to sing the school song if I refused.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Last Lesson\u003c/strong\u003e","As the pizza boxes were emptied and the laughter settled into a contented hum, Albus Dumbledore stood up at the head of the table. He tapped his spoon against his goblet.","The room fell silent. All eyes turned to the greatest wizard history had ever known, who was currently wearing a paper party hat Dudley had forced onto him.","\u0026quot;A toast,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, raising his goblet. \u0026quot;To family. Born and chosen.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To family!\u0026quot; the room echoed.","Dumbledore smiled, his blue eyes resting on Harry.","\u0026quot;We have fought hard,\u0026quot; Dumbledore began. \u0026quot;We have sacrificed much. And we have earned this peace. However...\u0026quot;","He paused, the twinkle in his eye becoming dangerous.","\u0026quot;There is one final task that must be completed. One obstacle that not even the Chosen One has yet overcome.\u0026quot;","Harry tensed. Ron reached for his wand. Hermione leaned forward.","\u0026quot;What is it, Professor?\u0026quot; Harry asked, ready for battle. \u0026quot;Is it another Horcrux? A hidden Death Eater?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Worse,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said gravely. \u0026quot;It is the N.E.W.T.s.\u0026quot;","Harry blinked. \u0026quot;The what?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Education, Harry!\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed, spreading his arms. \u0026quot;You, Mr. Weasley, and Miss Granger—along with Mr. Malfoy and the rest of your year—have missed a significant amount of schooling due to your... extracurricular activities saving the world.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You can\u0027t be serious,\u0026quot; Ron groaned, his head hitting the table.","\u0026quot;I am quite serious,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled. \u0026quot;I have spoken with the Board of Governors. Hogwarts will be hosting a special \u0027Year Eight\u0027 starting in September. A chance to complete your education properly. No Dark Lords. No life-threatening mysteries. Just essays, exams, and perhaps a little bit of Quidditch.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore looked strictly at Harry. \u0026quot;I expect to see you there, Mr. Potter. You may have defeated Voldemort, but you have not yet defeated a N.E.W.T. level Potions exam.\u0026quot;","The room held its breath, waiting for Harry’s reaction. The boy who had walked into the forest to die, who had led an army, who had rebuilt the castle... was being told to go back to school.","Harry looked at Hermione, who was beaming with absolute delight.","He looked at Ron, who looked like he wanted to cry.","He looked at Vernon and Petunia.","\u0026quot;Go back,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded firmly. \u0026quot;Get the qualification, Harry. It looks good on the CV. You can\u0027t be a hero forever. You need a fallback plan.\u0026quot;","Harry looked back at Dumbledore. A slow smile spread across his face. A normal year. A year of just being a student. A year of breakfast with his friends and weekends at Hogsmeade.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Harry laughed. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll be there.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Excellent!\u0026quot; Dumbledore clapped his hands. \u0026quot;Now, who wants the last slice of \u0027Hawaiian\u0027? I find the pineapple quite exhilarating!\u0026quot;","The room erupted into laughter. The war was over. The scars were healing. And Harry Potter was going back to school—not to survive, but to live."]},{"num":56,"origNum":56,"title":"The Solitary Serpent and the Lioness","wordCount":1102,"paragraphs":["September returned to the Scottish Highlands, painting the mountains in russet and gold. The Hogwarts Express had chugged north once more, carrying a unique cargo: the returning first years, terrified and excited, and the \u0026quot;Eighth Years,\u0026quot; war veterans returning to finish what they started.","The atmosphere in the castle was lighter than it had been in decades. The House tables mingled more freely; inter-house unity wasn\u0027t just a slogan anymore, it was a survival tactic. Harry, Ron, and Hermione sat at the Gryffindor table, often joined by Ernie Macmillan or a surprisingly chill Blaise Zabini.","But there was one shadow that refused to blend into the new light.","Draco Malfoy moved through the castle like a ghost. Though he had been pardoned—thanks to the tireless testimony of Harry Potter and Albus Dumbledore—he wore his guilt like a heavy cloak. He sat at the very edge of the Slytherin table, ate quickly, and vanished into the library or the Astronomy Tower before dessert appeared. He spoke to no one. He looked at no one. He was a boy trying very hard to disappear.","Most people let him. The anger against the Death Eaters was still raw, and while they wouldn\u0027t hex him in the corridors (mostly out of fear of Harry Potter’s wrath), they certainly didn\u0027t invite him to Hogsmeade.","Ginny Weasley, however, had never been good at doing what most people did.","She noticed him first. She noticed how he flinched when people laughed too loudly. She noticed the dark circles under his grey eyes. She noticed that he was drowning in plain sight.","It started in the library. Draco was sitting in a secluded alcove, buried behind a stack of Arithmancy charts.","\u0026quot;This seat taken?\u0026quot;","Draco looked up, startled. Ginny Weasley stood there, her red hair bright against the dusty books, holding her bag.","\u0026quot;There are five hundred empty seats, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, turning back to his chart. \u0026quot;Go find one.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I like the light in this one,\u0026quot; Ginny said, dropping her bag onto the table with a heavy thud and sitting opposite him.","Draco glared. She ignored him, pulling out her Transfiguration essay.","That became the routine. Every day, Ginny would find him. She would sit. He would tell her to leave. She would refuse. He would sigh, pretending to hate it, while secretly, the sound of her scratching quill became the only thing anchoring him to the present.","He hated her persistence. He hated her loud, Gryffindor boldness. But most of all, he hated the way his heart did a traitorous little flip whenever he smelled her floral shampoo. He was a Malfoy; she was a Weasley. It was impossible. It was ridiculous. It was happening.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Breaking Point\u003c/strong\u003e","By November, the tension had wound itself so tight it hummed.","It happened after an Advanced Defense Against the Dark Arts class. The lesson had been intense—dueling practice. Draco had been paired with a Hufflepuff who had \u0026quot;accidentally\u0026quot; sent a Stinging Hex at Draco’s face after the bell rang.","Draco hadn\u0027t retaliated. He had just packed his bag and walked out, stone-faced.","Ginny found him in the third-floor corridor.","\u0026quot;Why didn\u0027t you hex him back?\u0026quot; she demanded, hurrying to keep up with his long strides. \u0026quot;He did it on purpose, Malfoy!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go away, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco snapped, staring straight ahead.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t ignore me! You’re one of the best duelists in the school. You could have disarmed him in a second. Why do you let them treat you like a punching bag?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because maybe I deserve it!\u0026quot; Draco shouted, spinning around so fast Ginny nearly crashed into him.","The corridor was empty, the torches flickering in the draft.","\u0026quot;I am a former Death Eater, Weasley!\u0026quot; Draco yelled, his voice echoing off the stone walls. \u0026quot;I let them into the school! I almost killed Dumbledore! I don\u0027t need you defending me like I’m some charity case! I don\u0027t need your pity!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s not pity, you ferret!\u0026quot; Ginny screamed back, her face flushing with anger. \u0026quot;I’m not doing this because I feel sorry for you! I’m doing it because you’re an idiot who thinks he has to suffer alone forever!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I \u003cem\u003eam\u003c/em\u003e alone!\u0026quot; Draco spat. \u0026quot;That is my lot! And you... you prancing around me, pretending we’re friends... it’s a joke! You’re a Weasley. You’re the golden girl. You shouldn\u0027t even be looking at me!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well, I am looking at you!\u0026quot; Ginny stepped closer, invading his personal space, her brown eyes blazing. \u0026quot;I’m looking right at you, Draco Malfoy, and I see a coward who is too scared to admit that maybe, just maybe, he wants to be happy!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t you dare call me a coward,\u0026quot; Draco hissed, his control snapping. \u0026quot;You don\u0027t know anything about me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know enough! I know you\u0027re punishing yourself! And I\u0027m sick of watching it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Then stop watching!\u0026quot; Draco roared. \u0026quot;Leave me alone! Go back to your precious Potter and your saint of a brother and leave me to rot!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I won\u0027t!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Why not?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because I care about you, you seeking, arrogant prat!\u0026quot;","The silence that followed was deafening. Draco stared at her, his chest heaving. Ginny looked shocked by her own admission, her breathing ragged.","The air between them crackled, hot and electric.","\u0026quot;You care about me,\u0026quot; Draco repeated, his voice a low, dangerous whisper. \u0026quot;You have no idea what you\u0027re saying.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know exactly what I\u0027m saying,\u0026quot; Ginny said, her voice shaking but defiant.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re a fool,\u0026quot; Draco sneered, trying to push her away with words because he couldn\u0027t bring himself to do it physically. \u0026quot;You\u0027re a naive little girl playing with fire.\u0026quot;","Ginny’s temper flared. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t you patronize me!\u0026quot;","She raised her hand, swinging hard, aiming a slap right for his pale cheek.","She never connected.","Draco’s hand shot up. His seeker reflexes were still sharp. He caught her wrist mid-air, inches from his face.","He held her hand there, gripping it firmly but not painfully. They froze.","Ginny looked up at him, her eyes wide, her chest heaving against her robes. Draco looked down, his grey eyes darkening, the anger in them swirling into something else entirely—something hungry and terrified and desperate.","The tension was palpable, a physical weight pressing down on them. The anger evaporated, leaving only the raw, terrifying attraction that had been simmering for months.","Draco looked at her lips. Then he looked into her eyes, searching for a reason to stop, a reason to run.","He didn\u0027t find one.","\u0026quot;Damn it,\u0026quot; Draco whispered.","He yanked her wrist, pulling her stumbling toward him. His other hand tangles into her fiery hair, tilting her head back.","He crushed his mouth to hers."]},{"num":57,"origNum":57,"title":"The Potions Master’s Headache","wordCount":940,"paragraphs":["The kiss was not a polite, Victorian peck. It was a collision. It was months of arguments, repressed glances, and stored-up wartime adrenaline releasing in a single, frantic moment. Draco’s hands were tangled in Ginny’s hair; her arms were locked around his neck as if he were a life raft.","They were so consumed by the sudden annihilation of the personal space between them that they failed to notice the bell had rung.","The corridor, empty a moment ago, began to fill with students spilling out of the nearby Charms and Transfiguration classrooms. First-years stopped dead, their eyes bulging. A group of Hufflepuffs gasped in unison.","Then, from around the corner, came the familiar trio.","\u0026quot;I’m telling you, Ron,\u0026quot; Hermione was saying, clutching a stack of books, \u0026quot;the N.E.W.T. syllabus for Ancient Runes is far more rigorous than—\u0026quot;","She stopped. She walked into Harry’s back, who had frozen mid-stride. Ron walked into Hermione’s back.","\u0026quot;Oi! What’s the hold-up?\u0026quot; Ron grumbled, peering over Harry’s shoulder. \u0026quot;Did Peeves drop a water balloon on—\u0026quot;","Ron’s voice died. His jaw unhinged. The books he was carrying slipped from his numb fingers and hit the stone floor with a thunderous crash.","\u0026quot;BLOODY HELL!\u0026quot; Ron shrieked, the sound echoing off the vaulted ceiling. \u0026quot;THAT’S MY SISTER! WITH THE FERRET!\u0026quot;","Harry stared, his glasses nearly sliding off his nose. \u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; he murmured, a slow grin spreading across his face. \u0026quot;I didn\u0027t see that coming. I thought they were going to kill each other.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They \u003cem\u003eare\u003c/em\u003e killing each other!\u0026quot; Ron yelled, trying to surge forward. \u0026quot;He\u0027s eating her face! Harry, let me go! I need to save her!\u0026quot;","Hermione grabbed the back of Ron’s robes, hauling him back. She looked shocked, but a delighted smile was twitching at the corners of her mouth. \u0026quot;Ron, stop it! I think... I think she’s fighting back quite effectively.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s unnatural!\u0026quot; Ron wailed. \u0026quot;It’s a crime against nature! Ginny! GET OFF HIM!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eEnter Severus\u003c/strong\u003e","The noise level in the corridor—comprised of student gasps, Ron’s shouting, and general teenage hysteria—reached a crescendo that pierced the heavy oak door of the nearby Defense Against the Dark Arts classroom.","The door flew open with a bang.","Severus Snape emerged like a giant bat disturbed from its slumber. He looked furious. He had been in the middle of grading a particularly abysmal essay on Vampires, and his patience was already nonexistent.","\u0026quot;What,\u0026quot; Snape hissed, his voice cutting through the noise like a scalpel, \u0026quot;is the meaning of this cacophony?\u0026quot;","He swept into the center of the corridor, his black eyes flashing. \u0026quot;If I find one more Weasley product detonating in my—\u0026quot;","He stopped.","He looked at the center of the crowd.","There, oblivious to the audience, oblivious to her brother’s screaming, and oblivious to the terrifying presence of the former spy, Draco Malfoy and Ginny Weasley were still locked in a passionate embrace against the stone wall.","Snape’s pale face went through a complex series of expressions: Confusion. Horror. Revulsion. And finally, a look of supreme, existential exhaustion.","He closed his eyes for a brief moment, as if praying to a deity he didn\u0027t believe in for strength. \u003cem\u003eI survived the Dark Lord,\u003c/em\u003e his expression seemed to say. \u003cem\u003eI survived the snake. I survived the Potters. And I survived it all for this? Teenage hormones?\u003c/em\u003e","He opened his eyes.","\u0026quot;MR. MALFOY!\u0026quot; Snape barked.","Draco didn\u0027t flinch. He didn\u0027t even open his eyes. He just pulled Ginny closer.","Snape’s eyebrow twitched. He stepped closer.","\u0026quot;MISS WEASLEY! CEASE THIS ABOMINATION IMMEDIATELY!\u0026quot;","Ginny, whose hand was currently gripping Draco’s tie, ignored the command entirely.","The students were now looking at Snape, terrified and gleeful in equal measure. Ron looked like he was about to faint.","\u0026quot;Five points from Slytherin!\u0026quot; Snape tried, his voice rising. \u0026quot;Ten points from Gryffindor! DETENTION FOR LIFE!\u0026quot;","Nothing. They were in their own world.","Snape let out a long, suffering sigh. He drew his wand. He looked weary. He looked like a man who needed a drink, a holiday, and perhaps a memory charm to erase the last thirty seconds.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eDepulso Minimus,\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot; Snape muttered lazily, flicking his wand.","A blast of compressed air, gentle but firm, erupted between the couple.","\u003cem\u003eWHUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","Draco and Ginny were blasted backward in opposite directions. Draco stumbled, hitting the opposite wall with a thud. Ginny staggered back, catching her balance just before she tripped over a first-year.","They stood there, chests heaving, lips swollen, hair thoroughly mussed. They blinked, looking around the corridor as if waking up from a trance. They saw the staring students. They saw the purple-faced Ron. They saw Harry giving them a thumbs-up.","And finally, they saw Snape.","Snape stared at them with profound distaste. \u0026quot;Have you quite finished?\u0026quot;","Draco straightened his tie, his face flushed but his grey eyes bright with a look of exhilaration Harry had never seen before. \u0026quot;Yes, Professor. Sorry, Professor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sorry, Professor,\u0026quot; Ginny echoed, smoothing her robes.","Neither of them sounded sorry. In fact, as they looked at each other across the corridor, they both broke into matching, breathless grins.","\u0026quot;Disgusting,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, turning on his heel, his robes billowing. \u0026quot;Absolutely revolting. Ten points from Gryffindor for public indecency. And ten points from Slytherin for... for lack of situational awareness. Clear the corridor! Or I shall turn you all into flobberworms!\u0026quot;","He stormed back into his classroom and slammed the door.","The corridor exploded into laughter. Harry clapped a hand on Ron’s shoulder as Ginny walked boldly over to Draco and took his hand, right in front of everyone.","\u0026quot;Come on, Ron,\u0026quot; Harry laughed. \u0026quot;Let\u0027s go. I think the Ostrich has been dethroned as the scandal of the year.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":58,"origNum":58,"title":"The War on Decency","wordCount":756,"paragraphs":["If Harry and Hermione were the definition of a quiet, cozy romance—soft whispers in the common room, holding hands under the table, and the occasional \u0026quot;Ostrich\u0026quot; maneuver to hide from embarrassment—Draco Malfoy and Ginny Weasley were a fireworks display set off inside a library.","They were loud. They were possessive. And they had absolutely no shame.","The \u0026quot;Solitary Serpent\u0026quot; had vanished, replaced by a Draco Malfoy who seemed intent on making up for lost time by being physically attached to Ginny Weasley at all times. And Ginny, the fiery lioness, didn\u0027t just allow it; she instigated it.","The castle, which had survived a siege of giants and dark wizards, was now under a different kind of assault: \u003cstrong\u003eThe Malfoy-Weasley PDA Tour.\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eIncident 1: The Transfiguration Trauma\u003c/strong\u003e","It was a Tuesday morning. Professor McGonagall walked into her classroom early to prepare for the N.E.W.T. revision class. She was carrying a stack of delicate porcelain teacups she intended to turn into tortoises.","She opened the door.","There, sitting on her pristine desk, was Draco Malfoy. Standing between his legs, her hands gripping the lapels of his robes, was Ginny Weasley. They were kissing with an intensity that suggested they were trying to fuse their souls together through their mouths.","McGonagall didn\u0027t scream. She simply dropped the stack of teacups.","\u003cem\u003eCRASH.\u003c/em\u003e","The shattering porcelain echoed through the room.","Draco broke the kiss, but he didn\u0027t jump off the desk. He didn\u0027t look embarrassed. He simply looked over Ginny’s shoulder, wiped a smudge of lipstick from his mouth, and nodded.","\u0026quot;Professor,\u0026quot; Draco said smoothly. \u0026quot;We were just... testing the durability of the mahogany. Solid craftsmanship.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, her voice trembling with a mixture of shock and Scottish fury. \u0026quot;That is an educator\u0027s desk! It is not a sacrificial altar to Aphrodite! Get off! GET OFF!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In a minute, Professor,\u0026quot; Ginny said breathlessly, turning back to Draco. \u0026quot;I missed a spot.\u0026quot;","McGonagall turned into a tabby cat and fled the room.","\u003cstrong\u003eIncident 2: The Greenhouse Gas\u003c/strong\u003e","Professor Sprout was tending to the Venomous Tentacula in Greenhouse Three. It was dangerous work, requiring focus and silence.","Suddenly, she heard a rustling from behind the Bubotubers. Thinking it was a stray gnome, she grabbed a trowel and marched over.","\u0026quot;Shoo! Get out of—Oh, my stars!\u0026quot;","Draco looked up, looking annoyed. \u0026quot;We\u0027re studying the stars, Professor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In the middle of the afternoon?\u0026quot; Flitwick asked.","\u0026quot;We see stars whenever we kiss,\u0026quot; Ginny declared, looking at Draco with glazed eyes.","\u0026quot;Oh, for the love of Ravenclaw,\u0026quot; Flitwick muttered, casting a Silencing Charm on himself so he wouldn\u0027t have to hear the \u0026quot;squelching\u0026quot; noises anymore.","\u003cstrong\u003eIncident 4: The Potions Master’s limit\u003c/strong\u003e","The final straw occurred in the staff room.","Severus Snape had had a long week. He walked into the staff room during his break, craving only silence and a cup of black coffee.","He opened the door.","The staff room was empty of teachers. But on the chintz sofa near the fire lay Draco Malfoy. And lying on top of him, effectively using the former Death Eater as a human mattress, was Ginny Weasley.","They weren\u0027t even kissing this time. They were just staring into each other\u0027s eyes and whispering things that made the skin on the back of Snape’s neck crawl.","\u0026quot;Your eyes are like storm clouds,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered.","\u0026quot;Your hair is like fire,\u0026quot; Draco murmured back.","Snape stood there. He looked at the coffee pot on the other side of the room. He looked at the couple blocking his path.","He thought about the war. He thought about the Vow. He thought about the fact that he was technically Draco\u0027s godfather.","\u0026quot;Twenty years,\u0026quot; Snape said aloud to the empty room. \u0026quot;I spent twenty years protecting the world from the Dark Lord. I mastered the Dark Arts. I deceived the greatest legilimens of the age.\u0026quot;","Draco and Ginny looked up, unbothered.","\u0026quot;Hi, Professor,\u0026quot; Ginny waved. \u0026quot;We\u0027re taking a mental health break.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If you do not separate,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice terrifyingly calm, \u0026quot;I will transmute you both into coat racks. And I will hang Filch’s undergarments on you.\u0026quot;","Draco sighed, tightening his arms around Ginny. \u0026quot;He\u0027s bluffing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Try me,\u0026quot; Snape snarled, raising his wand.","\u0026quot;Run!\u0026quot; Ginny giggled.","They scrambled off the sofa and bolted out of the room, hand in hand, laughing maniacally.","Snape walked to the sofa. He took out his wand.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eIncendio.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;","He set the sofa on fire.","Then he poured his coffee, sat in an armchair, and watched it burn, a small smile of satisfaction on his face."]},{"num":59,"origNum":59,"title":"The Interruption of the Century","wordCount":1217,"paragraphs":["It was a Tuesday afternoon, a time usually reserved for quiet study and the gentle scratching of quills on parchment. However, for Headmaster Albus Dumbledore and Deputy Headmistress Minerva McGonagall, it was a time for a very serious inspection of the castle’s newly repaired West Wing corridor.","\u0026quot;The masonry work is holding up splendidly, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, adjusting her spectacles as she marched briskly down the hallway. She carried a stack of parchment scrolls detailing the new prefect patrols. \u0026quot;Though I am still concerned about the gargoyle on the fourth floor. It keeps singing sea shanties when the first years walk past.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I find it adds character, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore replied serenely, his violet robes sweeping the floor. \u0026quot;A little nautical whimsy never hurt anyone. Besides, it has excellent pitch.\u0026quot;","They turned the corner toward the tapestry of Barnabas the Barmy.","\u0026quot;Be that as it may,\u0026quot; McGonagall continued, checking her list, \u0026quot;we must ensure decorum is maintained. The castle has been through enough chaos; we need order. We need discipline. We need—\u0026quot;","She stopped.","She stopped so abruptly that Dumbledore, who had been admiring a floating dust mote, nearly walked into her.","\u0026quot;Minerva?\u0026quot; Dumbledore asked politely. \u0026quot;Have we forgotten something?\u0026quot;","McGonagall did not answer. She could not answer. Her mouth had fallen open, her jaw practically unhinged. Her eyes were bulging behind her square spectacles. The scrolls in her arms slipped, one by one, cascading onto the stone floor with a series of soft \u003cem\u003eflump, flump, flumps\u003c/em\u003e.","Dumbledore followed her gaze.","There, in the middle of the corridor, was a large, ornate suit of armor—14th-century goblin-wrought steel, if one were being precise.","But the armor was not standing at attention. It was rattling. It was shaking violently against its plinth.","Pressed against the breastplate of the armor was Draco Malfoy. And pressed against Draco Malfoy, effectively pinning him to the metal with her entire body, was Ginny Weasley.","They were not merely kissing. It was a fusion event.","Ginny’s hands were fisted in Draco’s platinum hair, pulling his head down. Draco’s arms were wrapped tightly around her waist, lifting her slightly off the ground so that they were eye-to-eye. They were devouring each other with a ferocity that suggested they had just discovered oxygen and were trying to share the last lungful.","The sound of the armor rattling—\u003cem\u003eclank, clank, clang\u003c/em\u003e—was providing a rhythmic, metallic backing track to their activities.","\u0026quot;Good heavens,\u0026quot; Dumbledore murmured. He sounded delighted.","McGonagall, however, looked as though she was witnessing the end of civilization. Her face turned a shade of white usually reserved for the Bloody Baron, before rapidly flushing to a violent, tartan red.","She tried to speak. \u0026quot;M-M-Mr...\u0026quot;","The couple didn\u0027t hear her. Draco tilted his head, deepening the kiss, and the suit of armor let out a loud, groaning \u003cem\u003eSCREECH\u003c/em\u003e as it tipped dangerously backward under their combined weight.","\u0026quot;MR. MALFOY! MISS WEASLEY!\u0026quot;","McGonagall’s scream echoed down the corridor, shattering the romantic bubble with the force of a sonic boom.","Draco and Ginny froze. They didn\u0027t jump apart. They didn\u0027t scramble to fix their clothes. They simply stopped moving, their faces still inches apart, panting heavily.","Draco slowly turned his head. His hair was sticking up in wild spikes (courtesy of the Weasley grip). His tie was undone. His lips were swollen and red.","He looked at the Headmaster and the Deputy Headmistress. He blinked.","\u0026quot;Afternoon, Professors,\u0026quot; Draco rasped, his voice sounding like he had swallowed gravel.","\u0026quot;Afternoon?\u0026quot; McGonagall choked out. She pointed a shaking finger at them. \u0026quot;AFTERNOON? You are... you are attempting to... to smelt that suit of armor with your bodies!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We were just talking,\u0026quot; Ginny said breathlessly, resting her forehead against Draco’s chest. She didn\u0027t even look embarrassed. She looked annoyed at the interruption.","\u0026quot;Talking?\u0026quot; McGonagall repeated shrilly. \u0026quot;With your tongues? Miss Weasley, you are practically climbing him like a tree!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s very tall,\u0026quot; Ginny shrugged.","\u0026quot;This is a school!\u0026quot; McGonagall roared, losing the battle for her composure. She flapped her hands at them. \u0026quot;A place of learning! Not a... a breeding ground for rampant hormones! Look at you! You look like you’ve been through a hurricane!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hurricane Ginny,\u0026quot; Draco smirked, tightening his arm around her waist. \u0026quot;Category five.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Silence!\u0026quot; McGonagall snapped. She turned to Dumbledore, desperate for backup. \u0026quot;Albus! Do something! Look at them! It’s indecent! It’s flagrant! It’s... it’s Gryffindor and Slytherin!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore was beaming. He looked from the flushed, defiant couple to his apoplectic Deputy. He clasped his hands together.","\u0026quot;I must say, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said thoughtfully, \u0026quot;I have always advocated for inter-house unity. Though I admit, I envisioned something more along the lines of a shared study group, rather than... this passionate display of vertical wrestling.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Albus!\u0026quot; McGonagall gasped, betrayed.","Dumbledore stepped closer, peering at the suit of armor over Draco’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;Although,\u0026quot; Dumbledore mused, his eyes twinkling furiously, \u0026quot;I am somewhat concerned for Sir Cadogan’s cousin here. I believe you have dented his breastplate, Draco. That takes considerable... pressure.\u0026quot;","Draco actually looked proud. \u0026quot;Thank you, sir.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;THIS IS NOT A COMPLIMENT!\u0026quot; McGonagall shrieked. She looked like she was about to start transfiguring students into tea cozies just to make the world make sense again.","\u0026quot;Separate!\u0026quot; she commanded. \u0026quot;Immediately! I want at least three feet of air between you! And fix your tie, Mr. Malfoy! You look like you’ve been dragged through a hedge backward!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, looking at Ginny.","Ginny finally stepped back, though she kept hold of Draco’s hand. She smoothed her skirt, looking at McGonagall with a challenging tilt of her chin.","\u0026quot;We were just leaving, Professor,\u0026quot; Ginny said. \u0026quot;We have... studying to do.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I bet you do,\u0026quot; McGonagall muttered darkly. \u0026quot;Anatomy, I presume?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Astronomy,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, deadpan. \u0026quot;Heavenly bodies and all that.\u0026quot;","McGonagall closed her eyes. She took a deep breath. She massaged her temples.","\u0026quot;Go,\u0026quot; she whispered. \u0026quot;Just go. Before I give you both detention for the rest of your natural lives. And if I see you touching—if I see so much as a finger brush against a robe—I will turn you both into ferrets and put you in separate cages.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Understood,\u0026quot; Draco nodded.","He squeezed Ginny’s hand. \u0026quot;Come on, Red. Let’s go find a library. Or a broom closet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Draco!\u0026quot; Ginny giggled, slapping his arm.","They walked past the professors. As they passed Dumbledore, the Headmaster leaned in and whispered loudly, \u0026quot;The third-floor tapestry room is soundproofed. Just a tip.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Albus!\u0026quot; McGonagall hissed.","Draco winked at the Headmaster. Ginny grinned. And they disappeared around the corner, swinging their joined hands.","McGonagall stood alone in the corridor with Dumbledore and the dented suit of armor. She looked at the scattered scrolls on the floor. She looked at the ceiling.","\u0026quot;I miss the war,\u0026quot; McGonagall said flatly. \u0026quot;It was quieter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, come now, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled, picking up a scroll. \u0026quot;It warms the heart! Young love! Passion! It’s spring!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s November, Albus.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Details,\u0026quot; Dumbledore waved a hand. \u0026quot;Now, shall we discuss the gargoyle? I believe he knows a ballad about a sailor and a mermaid that is quite... pertinent to what we just witnessed.\u0026quot;","McGonagall turned on her heel and marched away. \u0026quot;I am going to have a biscuit. A very large biscuit. And perhaps some of that firewhisky you keep in your desk.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;An excellent suggestion!\u0026quot; Dumbledore called after her, following happily. \u0026quot;I’ll bring the glasses!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":60,"origNum":60,"title":"The Crisis Summit","wordCount":931,"paragraphs":["The circular office of the Headmaster was usually a place of quiet contemplation, filled with the gentle whirring of silver instruments and the soft snores of former Headmasters in their portraits.","Tonight, however, it looked like a war room.","The Heads of House had gathered. They sat in a semi-circle in front of Dumbledore’s desk, looking like a group of soldiers who had just returned from a particularly harrowing battle.","Professor McGonagall was pacing, her tartan hat askew. Professor Sprout was fanning herself with a large fern leaf. Professor Flitwick was standing on his chair to be heard. And Severus Snape was slumped in a chintz armchair, staring at the ceiling with the dead, hollow eyes of a man who had seen too much.","\u0026quot;It is an epidemic, Albus!\u0026quot; McGonagall declared, slamming a scroll onto the desk. \u0026quot;A pandemic of passion! We cannot go on like this. The castle is not safe!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Safe?\u0026quot; Dumbledore asked pleasantly, folding his hands over his stomach. \u0026quot;Minerva, surely you exaggerate. It is merely... romance.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Romance?\u0026quot; Snape whispered, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;Albus, I walked into the Potions supply cupboard this morning to retrieve beetle eyes. Do you know what I found?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Beetle eyes?\u0026quot; Dumbledore guessed hopefully.","\u0026quot;I found Mr. Malfoy and Miss Weasley,\u0026quot; Snape said, shuddering. \u0026quot;They were... \u003cem\u003emarinating\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Marinating?\u0026quot; Sprout asked, horrified.","\u0026quot;They were covered in flobberworm mucus because they had knocked over a jar, and they didn\u0027t even notice,\u0026quot; Snape said flatly. \u0026quot;I had to vanish the mucus \u003cem\u003eand\u003c/em\u003e them. I sent them to the dungeons. Ten minutes later, the Bloody Baron came to me to complain. He said they were \u0027making the chains rattle\u0027.\u0026quot;","Snape put his head in his hands. \u0026quot;I survived Nagini. I cannot survive this.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s not just the dungeons!\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked. \u0026quot;I found them in the Charms corridor! They were practicing the Levitation Charm. On \u003cem\u003eeach other\u003c/em\u003e. Miss Weasley was floating three feet in the air while Mr. Malfoy... anchored her. With his mouth.\u0026quot;","McGonagall let out a strangled noise. \u0026quot;The library!\u0026quot; she shouted. \u0026quot;Madam Pince is threatening to resign! She found them in the Restricted Section. Apparently, they were researching \u0027Human Transfiguration\u0027—practically.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the greenhouses!\u0026quot; Sprout wailed. \u0026quot;My Venomous Tentacula has developed a nervous tic! It’s seen things, Albus! It’s seen things no plant should see!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore listened to the litany of complaints, his blue eyes moving from one traumatized professor to the next. He nodded sympathetically, humming soft little notes of concern.","\u0026quot;I see,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said gravely. \u0026quot;This is indeed... a vigorous situation.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Vigorous?\u0026quot; McGonagall snapped. \u0026quot;It’s a hurricane! Hurricane Malfoy-Weasley is tearing through this school, leaving a trail of traumatized staff and detentions in its wake! You must do something, Albus. Ban them from being within ten feet of each other! Put tracking charms on them! Anything!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore sighed. He opened his bottom drawer.","\u0026quot;It sounds to me,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, pulling out a large, dust-covered bottle and a tin of shortbread, \u0026quot;that what we really need is a tactical readjustment.\u0026quot;","He uncorked the bottle. The smell of Ogden’s Old Firewhisky filled the room.","\u0026quot;Firewhisky?\u0026quot; McGonagall asked, eyeing the bottle. \u0026quot;Albus, it is Tuesday.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is a Tuesday in the era of Malfoy-Weasley,\u0026quot; Dumbledore corrected, conjuring five crystal glasses. He poured generous measures for everyone.","\u0026quot;Here you are, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, floating a glass to the Potions Master. \u0026quot;You look like you need a double.\u0026quot;","Snape didn\u0027t argue. He downed the amber liquid in one swallow and held out his glass for a refill.","Dumbledore passed the tin around. \u0026quot;Custard cream, Pomona? Filius, a nice digestive?\u0026quot;","He picked up his own glass and leaned back in his high-backed chair, beaming at his staff.","\u0026quot;Now, I understand your distress,\u0026quot; Dumbledore began, dipping a biscuit into his whisky. \u0026quot;However, let us look at the bigger picture. For years, we have watched Slytherin and Gryffindor tear each other apart. We have seen prejudice, hatred, and war.\u0026quot;","He gestured vaguely toward the door.","\u0026quot;And now? We have a Malfoy and a Weasley—the very symbols of that divide—loving each other with... ah... \u003cem\u003eenthusiasm\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are trying to swallow each other whole, Albus,\u0026quot; Snape muttered into his glass.","\u0026quot;Precisely!\u0026quot; Dumbledore chirped. \u0026quot;It is the ultimate unification! It is the healing of old wounds! It is poetic! It is beautiful!\u0026quot;","He looked at McGonagall with wide, innocent eyes.","\u0026quot;Can we really stand in the way of such powerful, history-changing love? Would we be the villains in their story?\u0026quot;","McGonagall stared at him. She looked at the whisky. She looked at Snape, who was now eating a custard cream with aggressive misery.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re enjoying this,\u0026quot; McGonagall accused. \u0026quot;You find it funny.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I find it delightful!\u0026quot; Dumbledore giggled. \u0026quot;Just yesterday, I saw them hiding behind a suit of armor on the third floor. They froze when they saw me. Do you know what I did?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What?\u0026quot; Sprout asked, dreading the answer.","\u0026quot;I cast a Disillusionment Charm on them so they wouldn\u0027t be disturbed,\u0026quot; Dumbledore confessed, biting into his biscuit. \u0026quot;It seemed the polite thing to do.\u0026quot;","The four Heads of House stared at him in silence.","\u0026quot;You... you helped them hide?\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered.","\u0026quot;I am a romantic at heart, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled. \u0026quot;Now, drink up. I believe the Hufflepuffs are organizing a betting pool on where they’ll be caught next. I have five galleons on the Quidditch pitch hoops.\u0026quot;","McGonagall let out a long, defeated sigh. She picked up her glass of firewhisky.","\u0026quot;To retirement,\u0026quot; she toasted grimly.","\u0026quot;To retirement,\u0026quot; the others echoed.","\u0026quot;To young love!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered, clinking his glass against Snape’s.","Snape just stared at him. \u0026quot;I hate you, Albus.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Have another biscuit, Severus.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":61,"origNum":61,"title":"The Unlikely Scholars","wordCount":941,"paragraphs":["The end of the term arrived with the golden languor of June. The Great Hall was buzzing, trunks were packed, and the air smelled of freedom and treacle tart. But before the boats and carriages could take them away, there was one final hurdle: The N.E.W.T. Results.","The parchment scroll appeared on the notice board outside the Great Hall at 10:00 AM sharp.","A stampede of Eighth Years surged forward. Hermione, naturally, elbowed her way to the front with a ferocity that would have scared a Death Eater.","\u0026quot;Oh!\u0026quot; she gasped, her hands flying to her mouth.","\u0026quot;Well?\u0026quot; Ron asked from the back of the crush, trying to jump to see over Goyle’s head. \u0026quot;Did we fail? Am I going to be a professional gnome-tosser?\u0026quot;","Hermione turned around, beaming so brightly she was practically bioluminescent.","\u0026quot;Outstanding,\u0026quot; she breathed. \u0026quot;In everything. Top of the year.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Standard,\u0026quot; Harry grinned, clapping her on the back. \u0026quot;Never a doubt, Mione.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But look!\u0026quot; Hermione squeaked, grabbing Harry’s arm and dragging him to the board. \u0026quot;Harry, look at you!\u0026quot;","Harry squinted at the list.","1. GRANGER, HERMIONE J.","2. POTTER, HARRY J.","Harry blinked. He cleaned his glasses and looked again. He hadn\u0027t just passed. He was second.","\u0026quot;I... I came second?\u0026quot; Harry stammered. \u0026quot;In the whole year?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the Occlumency,\u0026quot; Hermione said knowingly. \u0026quot;And the focus. You treated studying like a mission this year, Harry. You had a strategy.\u0026quot;","Harry thought of Vernon’s advice on \u0026quot;maximizing assets\u0026quot; and \u0026quot;delivering under pressure.\u0026quot; He smiled. \u003cem\u003eThanks, Uncle Vernon.\u003c/em\u003e","But the real shock was just below Harry’s name.","3. MALFOY, DRACO L.","3. WEASLEY, RONALD B.","The corridor fell silent.","Ron Weasley pushed his way to the front. He stared at the number three. He traced his name with a shaking finger.","\u0026quot;I...\u0026quot; Ron’s voice cracked. \u0026quot;I got... Outstandings? I’m third?\u0026quot;","On the other side of the crowd, Draco Malfoy stood frozen. He looked at the list. He looked at his name. And then he looked at the name next to his.","\u0026quot;I tied...\u0026quot; Draco whispered, horror dawning on his face. \u0026quot;I tied with \u003cem\u003eWeasley\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I tied with the \u003cem\u003eFerret\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot; Ron shouted, turning to face Draco.","The two boys stared at each other. This was worse than a duel. This was an academic stalemate.","\u0026quot;You must have cheated,\u0026quot; Draco narrowed his eyes. \u0026quot;You probably bribed the examiners with... with Weasley Wizard Wheezes products.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cheated?\u0026quot; Ron spluttered, puffing out his chest. \u0026quot;I studied my arse off! You were too busy snogging my sister in greenhouses to revise! That’s why you slipped, Malfoy! The \u0027Hurricane\u0027 blew your grades away!\u0026quot;","Draco opened his mouth to retort, but he stopped. His pale cheeks turned pink. He realized Ron was right. He \u003cem\u003ehad\u003c/em\u003e spent a significant amount of study time locked in broom closets with Ginny.","\u0026quot;Worth it,\u0026quot; Draco muttered under his breath.","Suddenly, Ginny appeared, pushing through the crowd. She looked at the board, then squealed.","\u0026quot;Third!\u0026quot; she cheered.","She grabbed Draco by the tie and pulled him down for a loud, smacking kiss on the cheek. Then, she spun around and grabbed Ron, crushing him in a hug.","\u0026quot;My two clever idiots!\u0026quot; Ginny beamed, holding them both. \u0026quot;I knew you could do it!\u0026quot;","Ron looked at Draco over Ginny’s shoulder. Draco looked at Ron. They were trapped in a hug with the girl they both loved (in very different ways), tied in academic ranking, and bound by a future that terrified them both.","\u0026quot;I hate you,\u0026quot; Ron mouthed at Draco.","\u0026quot;The feeling is mutual,\u0026quot; Draco mouthed back.","But as Ginny let them go, neither of them moved away. They stood there, united in their unexpected success, a reluctant respect settling between them.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Staff Room Shock\u003c/strong\u003e","Meanwhile, in the staff room, the professors were reviewing the master list with a bottle of sherry.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t believe it,\u0026quot; Professor McGonagall said, staring at the parchment through her square spectacles. \u0026quot;Weasley? Ronald Weasley? Third?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He has a surprisingly analytical mind when he applies it,\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked, looking delighted. \u0026quot;His tactical work in chess translates remarkably well to Charms theory.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Potter,\u0026quot; Slughorn chortled, pouring himself a drink. \u0026quot;Second! I knew he had it in him! The Prince\u0027s book or not, the boy has instincts! A true potion-maker! I shall have to send him a box of crystallized pineapple.\u0026quot;","But it was Severus Snape who had the most profound reaction.","He sat in the corner, holding the Potions results. He had graded them himself. He had re-graded them, assuming there was a mistake. He had checked the cauldron bottoms for cheat-notes.","There were none.","Harry Potter had brewed a flawless Felix Felicis for his final exam. Ron Weasley had identified every ingredient in a complex antidote.","Snape lowered the parchment. He looked at Dumbledore, who was smiling serenely over a lemon drop.","\u0026quot;They actually learned,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, looking genuinely disturbed.","\u0026quot;They did,\u0026quot; Dumbledore agreed.","\u0026quot;Potter... is competent,\u0026quot; Snape said, the word feeling foreign on his tongue. \u0026quot;He is... intelligent.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is his mother\u0027s son,\u0026quot; McGonagall said softly.","Snape looked back at the list. He stared at Harry’s name. For years, he had seen only James Potter’s arrogance. But this year... this year he had seen a boy who protected his friends, who saved his enemies, and who—miracle of miracles—had actually read the textbook.","Snape sighed, a long, rattling sound.","\u0026quot;I need a drink,\u0026quot; Snape declared, reaching for the sherry bottle. \u0026quot;If Weasley is an intellectual, the apocalypse is truly upon us.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Unlikely Scholars!\u0026quot; Dumbledore toasted, raising his glass.","\u0026quot;To the end of the term,\u0026quot; Snape corrected, downing his drink in one go. \u0026quot;And to never, ever having to grade a Malfoy-Weasley essay again.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":62,"origNum":62,"title":"The Lion’s Den","wordCount":1251,"paragraphs":["The summer sun beat down on the pavement of Privet Drive, but inside the kitchen of Number Four, the atmosphere was cool and celebratory.","Harry placed the parchment on the table with a quiet sense of satisfaction.","Vernon Dursley picked it up, adjusting his reading glasses. He scanned the list of \u0027Outstandings\u0027 and the number \u00272\u0027 next to Harry’s name. He looked at the parchment, then at Harry, then at Petunia.","\u0026quot;Second,\u0026quot; Vernon stated, his voice booming with approval. \u0026quot;Second in the entire school. That’s top-tier, Harry. That’s executive material.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s wonderful,\u0026quot; Petunia breathed, running her finger over the results. \u0026quot;Better than Snape. Better than... well, better than almost everyone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Who was first?\u0026quot; Vernon asked suspiciously. \u0026quot;Not that Malfoy boy?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry grinned.","\u0026quot;Ah, well,\u0026quot; Vernon conceded with a wave of his hand. \u0026quot;The girl is a machine. There’s no shame in losing to a walking encyclopedia. But this... this is excellent.\u0026quot;","He stood up, looking at Harry with a serious, businessman-like expression.","\u0026quot;Now, Harry. You’re eighteen. You’ve got the qualifications. You’ve saved the world. You’re a man of means.\u0026quot;","Vernon reached into his pocket and pulled out a brochure he had clearly been saving. He slid it across the table. It was for a brand new, gleaming silver Vauxhall Astra.","\u0026quot;I’ve spoken to the boys at the dealership,\u0026quot; Vernon said, puffing out his chest. \u0026quot;I can get you a friends-and-family discount. It’s time you had your own wheels, son. A man can’t keep relying on brooms and... fireplaces. It’s undignified.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at the car. It was a generous, incredibly normal offer. It was Vernon trying to give him the best start he knew how.","\u0026quot;Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry said gently, sliding the brochure back. \u0026quot;Thank you. Really. That means a lot.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But?\u0026quot; Vernon raised an eyebrow.","\u0026quot;But I can teleport,\u0026quot; Harry reminded him. \u0026quot;And I have a motorbike that flies. And the Firebolt.\u0026quot;","Vernon paused. He frowned at the brochure.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted. \u0026quot;Forgot about the teleporting. No traffic, I suppose. Tremendously efficient on fuel.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Harry smiled. \u0026quot;But I’ll take a lift to the station if you’re offering.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Done,\u0026quot; Vernon declared. \u0026quot;And we’re getting the leather seats for Dudley instead.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","Three weeks later, the Burrow was vibrating with the chaotic energy of a Sunday roast. The garden was filled with tables, gnomes were flying over the hedge (courtesy of Fred and George), and the smell of roasting chicken wafted through the open windows.","Harry and Hermione stood by the back gate, waiting.","\u0026quot;He’s going to faint,\u0026quot; Ron muttered, chewing on a blade of grass. \u0026quot;I’m telling you. He’s going to walk in there, see Fred holding a Beater’s bat, and pass out.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Be nice, Ron,\u0026quot; Hermione scolded, though she looked nervous too. \u0026quot;It’s brave of him to come.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s suicide,\u0026quot; Ron corrected.","Then, with a sharp \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e, Draco Malfoy appeared at the apparation point.","He was dressed immaculately in muggle clothes—a dark shirt and trousers—clearly an attempt to blend in, though he looked stiff and pale. He clutched a bottle of expensive wine like a shield.","He saw the trio and froze.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco nodded, his voice tight. \u0026quot;Weasley. Granger.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Relax, Malfoy,\u0026quot; Harry said, stepping forward. \u0026quot;We haven\u0027t eaten anyone in years.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Easy for you to say,\u0026quot; Draco muttered. \u0026quot;You\u0027re the Chosen One. I\u0027m the... ex-ferret.\u0026quot;","Before Harry could reply, the back door of the Burrow banged open.","\u0026quot;DRACO!\u0026quot;","Ginny Weasley sprinted across the lawn. She didn\u0027t slow down. She launched herself at him.","Draco dropped the wine (Harry caught it with a quick seeker reflex) just in time to catch her. She wrapped her legs around his waist and buried her face in his neck.","\u0026quot;You came!\u0026quot; Ginny squealed.","Draco held her tight, closing his eyes for a second, drawing strength from her. \u0026quot;I said I would, Red.\u0026quot;","She pulled back and kissed him—a loud, happy smack on the lips that made Ron groan and cover his eyes.","\u0026quot;Okay! Okay!\u0026quot; Ron shouted. \u0026quot;We get it! He\u0027s here! Put him down before Dad sees!\u0026quot;","Ginny slid to the ground, beaming. She took Draco’s hand, lacing her fingers through his.","\u0026quot;Ready?\u0026quot; she asked.","Draco took a deep breath. He looked at the crooked house. He looked at the family of blood traitors he had been raised to hate, who had defeated his master.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Draco said honestly. \u0026quot;Let\u0027s go.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Silence\u003c/strong\u003e","They walked into the kitchen.","It was packed. Arthur was carving the chicken. Molly was stirring gravy. Bill and Fleur were setting the table. Charlie was showing Fred and George a burn on his arm. Percy was polishing his glasses.","\u0026quot;Mum, Dad,\u0026quot; Ginny announced, her voice ringing clear over the clatter of cutlery. \u0026quot;Everyone.\u0026quot;","The room went quiet. Every Weasley head turned.","\u0026quot;I brought a guest,\u0026quot; Ginny said, stepping forward and pulling Draco with her. \u0026quot;This is Draco.\u0026quot;","The silence that followed was heavy enough to crush a diamond.","Fred and George exchanged a look. George gripped his wand; Fred gripped a bread roll. Molly froze with the ladle in mid-air. Arthur stared over his glasses.","Draco stood there, pale as a sheet, holding Ginny’s hand so hard his knuckles were white.","\u0026quot;Mrs. Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice shaking slightly but holding steady. \u0026quot;Mr. Weasley. Thank you for... having me.\u0026quot;","No one moved. The history of the two families—the fights in Flourish and Blotts, the war, the prejudice—hung in the air like smoke.","Then, Ginny squeezed Draco’s hand. She looked up at him, and for a second, she forgot the room. She smiled at him—a look of such fierce, protective, and obvious adoration that it lit up her face.","Molly Weasley saw it.","She looked at her daughter. She saw the way Ginny leaned into him. She saw the way Draco, despite his terror, shifted slightly to shield Ginny from the room\u0027s gaze.","The ice around Molly’s heart shattered.","She dropped the ladle into the gravy boat.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Molly said, her voice loud and brisk, breaking the spell. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t just stand there in the doorway, Draco. You look like you haven\u0027t eaten a proper meal in weeks. You\u0027re all cheekbones.\u0026quot;","She bustled forward, wiping her hands on her apron. She didn\u0027t hug him—that would be too much, too soon—but she reached out and patted his arm firmly.","\u0026quot;Sit down,\u0026quot; Molly commanded. \u0026quot;Next to Ginny. Harry, pass the wine.\u0026quot;","The tension in the room snapped.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Fred exhaled, tossing the bread roll to George. \u0026quot;I thought she was going to hex him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I thought \u003cem\u003ehe\u003c/em\u003e was going to hex \u003cem\u003eus\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; George grinned. He walked over to Draco and clapped him on the back, making Draco jump. \u0026quot;Welcome to the madhouse, Malfoy. Don\u0027t eat the purple ones. We\u0027re testing those.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hello, Draco,\u0026quot; Arthur said, stepping forward and offering his hand. He looked serious, searching Draco’s face. \u0026quot;Good to see you.\u0026quot;","Draco shook it, looking overwhelmed. \u0026quot;Sir.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Charlie called out from the table. \u0026quot;Is it true you fought a dragon? Or was that just Potter exaggerating?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I... I flew away from a dragon,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, sitting down as Ginny beamed at him. \u0026quot;On the same broom as Potter. It was... undignified.\u0026quot;","Laughter rippled around the table.","Molly piled roast potatoes onto Draco’s plate until it groaned under the weight. She watched him look at Ginny, watched him relax, watched him smile a genuine, small smile.","She caught Harry’s eye across the table. Harry raised his glass to her.","The war was truly over. The families were mending. And even a Malfoy could find a place at the Weasley table."]},{"num":63,"origNum":63,"title":"The Shift Change","wordCount":667,"paragraphs":["The Burrow settled into a silence that was punctuated only by the ghoul in the attic banging on a pipe and the distant hooting of owls.","Down in the living room, Draco Malfoy was discovering that while Molly Weasley’s hospitality was warm, her furniture was not. He was lying on the chintz sofa, his feet hanging off the end, staring at the ceiling. The blanket was hand-knitted and smelled of baking, which was comforting, but his mind was racing. He was sleeping in the home of blood traitors, his stomach full of their food, and he had just shaken hands with Arthur Weasley.","It was a strange new world.","Around 1:00 AM, the creak of a floorboard snapped Draco to full alertness. He reached for his wand on the coffee table, his old instincts flaring.","He peered into the darkness of the hallway.","A figure was creeping down the stairs from the first floor. It was Hermione Granger. She was wearing her pajamas and moving with the stealth of someone who had spent a year on the run. She didn\u0027t look toward the living room; she headed straight for the second flight of stairs—the ones leading up to Percy’s room, where Harry was sleeping.","Draco watched her ascend. He waited until he heard the soft \u003cem\u003eclick\u003c/em\u003e of a door opening and closing on the floor above.","Draco smirked in the dark. \u003cem\u003ePotter and Granger. Predictable.\u003c/em\u003e","Then, a thought occurred to him. A wonderful, opportunistic thought.","\u003cem\u003eIf Granger is with Potter... then Red is alone.\u003c/em\u003e","Draco sat up. He looked at the ceiling. He looked at the stairs. He weighed the risk of being murdered by Molly Weasley against the reward of a decent mattress and Ginny.","It wasn\u0027t even a contest.","He stood up, abandoning the lumpy sofa. He moved silently—years of sneaking out of dungeons serving him well—and crept up the stairs. He bypassed the master bedroom (holding his breath), crept past the bathroom, and stopped outside Ginny’s door.","He eased it open.","Ginny was awake. She was sitting up in bed, arms crossed, staring at the empty bed across the room where Hermione was supposed to be.","\u0026quot;Traitor,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered to the empty pillow.","\u0026quot;She’s gone to the Potter summit,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, slipping inside and closing the door softly.","Ginny jumped, then grinned as she saw him in the moonlight. \u0026quot;Draco? You’ll get killed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m a risk-taker,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, walking over to her bed. \u0026quot;Besides, the sofa is a crime against lumbar support. Move over.\u0026quot;","Ginny scooted back, lifting the duvet. \u0026quot;You know, Hermione usually sleeps there. But I suppose you\u0027re a slight upgrade.\u0026quot;","Draco climbed in. The bed was small, forcing them immediately into each other\u0027s space.","\u0026quot;Wait,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered, putting a hand on his chest.","\u0026quot;What?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fleur’s rules,\u0026quot; Ginny smirked. \u0026quot;Protocol. Hermione told me about the \u0027Ostrich requirements\u0027. You can\u0027t just jump in.\u0026quot;","Draco rolled his eyes, but a smile tugged at his lips. \u0026quot;You Weasleys and your bureaucracy.\u0026quot;","He leaned in, cupping her face in his hands. He kissed her—slow, deep, and lingering, a kiss that tasted of wine and forgiveness.","\u0026quot;Satisfied?\u0026quot; Draco murmured against her lips.","\u0026quot;For now,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered.","Draco settled down, pulling the duvet over them. They instantly tangled together—legs interlocking, arms wrapping around waists. It was less of an Ostrich and more of a Python constriction, possessive and tight.","\u0026quot;Night, Draco,\u0026quot; Ginny breathed into his neck.","\u0026quot;Night, Red.\u0026quot;","Upstairs, in Percy\u0027s room, Harry and Hermione were already asleep, locked in their own defensive knot, secure in the knowledge that they were safe.","Downstairs, the sofa was empty.","And in the attic room, the first rays of the morning sun pierced through the small round window. The beam of light traveled across the dusty floorboards, climbed the bedpost, and landed squarely on the sleeping face of Ron Weasley.","He twitched, grumbled something about spiders, and rolled over, blissfully unaware that he was currently the meat in a double-decker sandwich of illicit romance taking place directly above and below him."]},{"num":64,"origNum":64,"title":"The Return of the Pretzel","wordCount":724,"paragraphs":["Ron Weasley woke with a groan as the sun hit his face. He stretched, cracking his knuckles, and sat up. The house was quiet, smelling of frying sausages.","He swung his legs out of bed and padded downstairs, fully expecting to find a traumatized Draco Malfoy sitting stiffly on the sofa, or perhaps hovering by the back door waiting for an escape route.","But when Ron reached the living room, the sofa was empty. The blanket was neatly folded (Draco was tidy, if nothing else), but the Slytherin was nowhere to be seen.","\u0026quot;Legged it,\u0026quot; Ron muttered to himself, shaking his head. \u0026quot;Knew he wouldn\u0027t last the night. Probably halfway to the Manor by now.\u0026quot;","He grabbed an apple from the fruit bowl and headed back upstairs. Since Malfoy had bailed, Ron decided it was his duty to wake Harry so they could get a head start on flying before the twins monopolized the paddock.","He climbed to the second floor, whistling tunelessly. He reached Percy’s door and didn\u0027t bother knocking.","\u0026quot;Oi, Harry! Wake up! Malfoy’s done a runner and Mum’s making—\u0026quot;","Ron pushed the door open. The words died in his throat. The apple fell from his hand and rolled across the floorboards.","The bed was once again defying the laws of physics. The \u0026quot;Gryffindor Pretzel\u0026quot; had returned with a vengeance. Harry was asleep on his back, snoring softly. Hermione was sprawled on top of him, her head tucked under his chin, one leg thrown over his waist, and her arm wrapped around his neck in a death grip. They looked less like two people sleeping and more like a single entity undergoing mitosis.","Ron stared. His brain flashed back to Christmas. It flashed back to the laughter. It flashed back to the \u0026quot;Ostrich.\u0026quot;","He couldn\u0027t help it. The trauma was too deep.","\u0026quot;EEEEEEP!\u0026quot;","It wasn\u0027t a scream. It was a high-pitched, tea-kettle squeal that vibrated through the floorboards.","\u0026quot;IT\u0027S HAPPENING AGAIN!\u0026quot; Ron bellowed, backing into the hallway. \u0026quot;CODE RED! CODE PRETZEL!\u0026quot;","The response was immediate.","\u0026quot;What is it?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley shouted from the bathroom, rushing out with shaving foam on half his face.","\u0026quot;Death Eaters?\u0026quot; Bill yelled, charging up the stairs with his wand drawn.","\u0026quot;Snake?\u0026quot; Molly screamed from the kitchen, brandishing a frying pan as she thundered up the steps.","\u0026quot;Better!\u0026quot; Fred shouted, sliding down the banister from the attic. \u0026quot;It\u0027s the sequel!\u0026quot;","Within seconds, the landing outside Percy’s room was a traffic jam of Weasleys. They piled into the doorway, weapons and wands raised, ready for a threat.","Instead, they saw the bed.","Harry and Hermione, jolted awake by the squealing and the stampede, froze. Harry blinked, his glasses skew-whiff on his face. Hermione lifted her head groggily from Harry’s chest, blinking in the sudden influx of Weasleys.","She saw Arthur with the shaving foam. She saw Molly with the frying pan. She saw Bill with his wand. And she saw Fred and George, who were already leaning against each other, shaking with silent laughter.","\u0026quot;Good morning, campers!\u0026quot; George announced brightly. \u0026quot;Welcome to the show!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We really need to start charging admission,\u0026quot; Fred agreed. \u0026quot;Look at the technique. The limb placement is exquisite.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is zey... attached?\u0026quot; Fleur asked from the back, peering over Bill’s shoulder. \u0026quot;Did zey follow the protocol? Was there a kiss?\u0026quot;","Harry groaned, letting his head thud back onto the pillow. \u0026quot;Not again.\u0026quot;","Hermione’s eyes went wide. The sleep cleared instantly, replaced by the sheer, crushing weight of social mortification. She looked at the army of Weasleys staring at her morning hair and her intimate proximity to the Chosen One.","She didn\u0027t speak. She didn\u0027t argue. She didn\u0027t try to explain about nightmares or Nargles.","She simply turned.","\u0026quot;Nope,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered.","She grabbed the front of Harry’s t-shirt. She yanked him upward slightly. And with a practiced, fluid motion, she dove.","\u003cem\u003eTHUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","She buried her face into Harry’s chest, pulled the duvet up over her ears, and went completely still.","\u0026quot;THE OSTRICH!\u0026quot; Fred roared.","\u0026quot;SHE DID THE THING!\u0026quot; George cheered, clapping his hands.","\u0026quot;Oh, bless her heart,\u0026quot; Molly giggled, lowering the frying pan. \u0026quot;She’s gone back into the burrow!\u0026quot;","The room erupted into laughter, louder and more chaotic than Christmas, as Harry lay there, patting the bushy head buried in his sternum, his face burning bright red, resigning himself to his fate as a human hiding place."]},{"num":65,"origNum":65,"title":"The Bucket Challenge","wordCount":974,"paragraphs":["The laughter in Percy\u0027s room was dying down, replaced by the collective wheezing of the Weasley clan. Harry was still acting as a human shield for Hermione, who was refusing to emerge until at least 1999.","Ron, wiping tears of mirth from his eyes, leaned against the doorframe. He looked at the empty sofa downstairs in his mind\u0027s eye. He looked at the Ostrich on the bed. He looked at the time.","And then, the gears in his head clicked into place with a sickening thud.","The smile slid off Ron’s face like sludge. His complexion went from flushed to pasty white in a nanosecond.","\u0026quot;Wait,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, his voice trembling.","\u0026quot;What is it, Won-Won?\u0026quot; Fred asked, wiping his eyes.","\u0026quot;If Hermione is here...\u0026quot; Ron pointed a shaking finger at the bed. \u0026quot;And Malfoy wasn\u0027t on the sofa...\u0026quot;","He looked at the ceiling above them (the attic). He looked at the floor below them (the landing). And then he looked down the hall toward the only other occupied bedroom.","\u0026quot;GINNY!\u0026quot;","Ron didn\u0027t run; he exploded into motion. He shoved past George, nearly knocked Arthur over, and sprinted down the hallway like a man whose hair was on fire.","\u0026quot;Ronald!\u0026quot; Molly shouted, waving the frying pan. \u0026quot;What is the matter?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;HE’S IN THE LION’S DEN!\u0026quot; Ron screamed over his shoulder. \u0026quot;THE FERRET IS IN THE DEN!\u0026quot;","The rest of the family, sensing a new and potentially even more entertaining disaster, surged after him. Harry, sensing the danger, tapped Hermione on the head.","\u0026quot;Coast is clear, Ostrich. But I think Ron’s about to commit a murder.\u0026quot;","Hermione popped her head up, hair wild. \u0026quot;Oh no.\u0026quot;","They scrambled out of bed and joined the stampede.","Ron reached Ginny’s door. He didn\u0027t knock. He didn\u0027t ask permission. He gripped the handle and threw the door open with enough force to crack the plaster.","\u0026quot;AHA! I KNEW—\u0026quot;","Ron stopped.","The army of Weasleys piled up behind him—Arthur, Molly, Bill, Fleur, the twins, Harry, and Hermione.","They all froze.","Ginny’s room was bathed in morning sunlight. But the occupants of the bed seemed determined to block it out entirely.","Draco Malfoy and Ginny Weasley were awake. They were sitting up in the small single bed, wrapped in the duvet, but their upper bodies were very much exposed to the elements (clothed, thankfully, in pajamas, though rumpled).","They were locked in a kiss that defied physics. It wasn\u0027t just a kiss; it was a biological merger. Draco’s hands were cupping Ginny’s face, Ginny’s hands were fisted in Draco’s pajama shirt, and they were devouring each other with a single-minded intensity that suggested they were trying to suck the souls out of one another’s bodies.","They didn\u0027t hear the door open. They didn\u0027t hear Ron’s scream. They didn\u0027t hear the collective gasp of ten people.","\u0026quot;MY EYES!\u0026quot; Ron howled, clapping his hands over his face and turning away. \u0026quot;THEY BURN! MAKE IT STOP!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; George whispered, looking impressed. \u0026quot;They need to come up for air. Surely?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s not breathing,\u0026quot; Fred noted, checking his watch. \u0026quot;That’s oxygen transfer via osmosis.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;GINNY!\u0026quot; Mrs. Weasley shrieked, banging the frying pan against the doorframe. \u0026quot;GINEVRA MOLLY WEASLEY!\u0026quot;","Nothing. Draco tilted his head, deepening the kiss, completely oblivious to the fact that his girlfriend’s mother was armed with cookware three feet away.","Arthur Weasley turned bright red and started cleaning his glasses frantically. \u0026quot;I... I think I left the kettle on. Downstairs. Far away.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get them apart!\u0026quot; Ron yelled, peeking through his fingers. \u0026quot;Use a crowbar! Use a blasting curse!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Allow me,\u0026quot; Bill said grimly.","The eldest Weasley brother stepped forward. He didn\u0027t draw his wand. He looked around the room, spotted a large pitcher of water on the nightstand (left there for hydration, ironically), and pointed his wand at it.","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eGlacius\u003c/em\u003e ,\u0026quot; Bill muttered.","The water turned icy cold, chunks of ice clinking against the glass.","Bill picked up the pitcher. He walked over to the bed. He loomed over the oblivious couple.","\u003cem\u003eSPLOOSH.\u003c/em\u003e","He upended the entire pitcher of ice water directly onto their heads.","The effect was instantaneous.","\u0026quot;GAH!\u0026quot; Draco yelled, springing apart from Ginny as if he’d been electrocuted.","\u0026quot;BLOODY HELL!\u0026quot; Ginny screamed, wiping ice cubes out of her eyes.","They sat there, soaking wet, shivering, gasping for air, looking like two drowned rats. Draco’s platinum hair was plastered to his forehead. Ginny’s pajamas were soaked.","They looked at Bill. They looked at the assemblage of Weasleys in the doorway.","\u0026quot;What was that for?!\u0026quot; Ginny roared, shivering.","\u0026quot;You were eating him!\u0026quot; Ron shouted, pointing an accusing finger. \u0026quot;In our house! In the morning! Without a permit!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is called a good morning kiss, Ronald!\u0026quot; Ginny snapped, shaking wet hair at him.","\u0026quot;That wasn\u0027t a kiss,\u0026quot; Fred corrected. \u0026quot;That was an exorcism.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;William!\u0026quot; Fleur Delacour stepped forward, looking furious. She grabbed a towel from the dresser and threw it at the shivering Draco. \u0026quot;You are a barbarian! Look at zem! It was passionate! It was romantic! You do not douse l\u0027amour with ice water!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do when it’s my baby sister,\u0026quot; Bill grunted, crossing his arms.","Draco, wiping water from his face with the towel, looked at the Weasleys. He looked at Harry and Hermione (who were trying very hard not to laugh in the back). He looked at the frying pan in Molly’s hand.","He shivered, wrapped the towel around his shoulders, and looked at Ginny.","\u0026quot;Next time,\u0026quot; Draco chattered, his teeth clicking, \u0026quot;we lock the door.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Definitely,\u0026quot; Ginny agreed, picking an ice cube out of her ear.","\u0026quot;OUT!\u0026quot; Mrs. Weasley finally exploded, pointing the frying pan down the stairs. \u0026quot;ALL OF YOU! BREAKFAST! NOW! AND PUT ON DRY CLOTHES!\u0026quot;","As the family retreated, Harry caught Draco’s eye. Harry smirked.","Draco just glared, dripping wet. \u0026quot;Not a word, Potter. Not one word.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Didn\u0027t say a thing,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;Just... stay hydrated, Malfoy.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":66,"origNum":66,"title":"The Inquisition of Toast","wordCount":1012,"paragraphs":["The kitchen at the Burrow was usually a place of warmth, chaotic noise, and the smell of burnt toast. Today, however, it felt more like a courtroom where the jury was armed with sausages and the judge was wielding a ladle.","The four defendants entered slowly.","Draco and Ginny, now wearing dry clothes (Draco in one of Bill’s old jumpers which was too broad in the shoulders, making him look slightly swamped), took their seats at the far end of the table. They were holding hands under the table, defiant but quiet.","Harry and Hermione entered next. Hermione was using Harry as a human shield, walking so close behind him she was practically stepping on his heels. They sat opposite the wet couple.","Mrs. Weasley was at the stove. The red-faced screaming fury from ten minutes ago had vanished, replaced by a bustling, terrifyingly efficient maternal energy. She was slamming plates of eggs onto the table with a little more force than necessary. \u003cem\u003eClatter. Clatter. Clatter.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Eat,\u0026quot; she commanded. \u0026quot;You’ll need your strength.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;For what?\u0026quot; Ron mumbled, eyeing his mother warily. \u0026quot;The execution?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;For the explanation,\u0026quot; Molly said, turning around with the frying pan still in hand.","Her anger had faded, but her curiosity—and her need to establish the moral boundaries of her household—had ramped up to nuclear levels. She looked at Draco and Ginny, who were busy buttering toast and pretending to be invisible. Then, her gaze swung to Harry and Hermione.","Draco and Ginny had been caught \u003cem\u003ein flagrante delicto\u003c/em\u003e. It was shocking, yes, but at least it was straightforward passion. Harry and Hermione, however, presented a logistical puzzle that Molly Weasley needed to solve.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Molly began, her voice deceptively light. \u0026quot;Harry.\u0026quot;","Harry choked on his pumpkin juice. \u0026quot;Yes, Mrs. Weasley?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Percy\u0027s room,\u0026quot; she said, piling three sausages onto his plate. \u0026quot;The bed in Percy\u0027s room.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s... it\u0027s a bed,\u0026quot; Harry stammered.","\u0026quot;It is a \u003cem\u003esingle\u003c/em\u003e bed,\u0026quot; Molly corrected, leaning against the counter. \u0026quot;It is exactly two feet and six inches wide. I know this because I bought the mattress in 1991. It was on sale because it was deemed \u0027unusually narrow\u0027.\u0026quot;","She fixed Harry with a piercing look.","\u0026quot;Please explain to me, Harry, how two fully grown teenagers managed to sleep in a two-foot-wide space without one of you falling onto the floor? Was magic involved? An Expansion Charm? Or are you two simply... liquid?\u0026quot;","The table went silent. Fred and George leaned forward, fascinated.","\u0026quot;We... uh...\u0026quot; Harry looked at Hermione for help. Hermione was currently studying the grain of the wooden table with microscopic intensity.","\u0026quot;It was a structural necessity!\u0026quot; Harry blurted out, reusing his defense from the Dursleys. \u0026quot;It was cold! And I had a nightmare! And Hermione came in to check on me! And then... gravity happened!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Gravity?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley asked, looking up from his paper, intrigued. \u0026quot;You mean the gravitational pull between two bodies increased due to proximity? Fascinating muggle physics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It wasn\u0027t physics, Dad,\u0026quot; Fred grinned. \u0026quot;It was biology.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was Tetris,\u0026quot; George corrected. \u0026quot;Did you see them? They were interlocked. Knees in elbows. Chins in necks. It was an engineering marvel.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the \u0027Ostrich\u0027?\u0026quot; Bill asked, buttering a scone. He looked at Hermione. \u0026quot;We heard about the Dursley incident. Is that a standard defensive position now?\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a small, high-pitched whimper.","\u0026quot;It is not a position!\u0026quot; she squeaked without looking up. \u0026quot;It is a tactical retreat from social humiliation!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is it true?\u0026quot; Ginny asked, looking across the table, eager to take the heat off herself. \u0026quot;Did you really bury your head in his shirt at breakfast? In front of his uncle?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She did,\u0026quot; Harry confirmed, grinning despite the interrogation. \u0026quot;Twice. Vernon laughed so hard he fell off his chair.\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley’s eyes widened. \u0026quot;Vernon Dursley? The man who drills? He... \u003cem\u003elaughed\u003c/em\u003e? At a romantic entanglement?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He called it \u0027The Ostrich\u0027,\u0026quot; Harry nodded. \u0026quot;He thinks Hermione is hilarious.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Molly huffed, pouring tea. \u0026quot;I suppose if the muggles find it amusing... but Harry, dear. \u003cem\u003eProtocol\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Fleur Delacour, who had been feeding Bill bits of bacon, perked up.","\u0026quot;Oui!\u0026quot; Fleur declared, pointing a fork at Harry. \u0026quot;I \u0027ave been asking zis for years! The Ostrich is cute, yes. But did you kiss \u0027er? Or did you just... flop together like dead fish?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We didn\u0027t flop!\u0026quot; Harry protested.","\u0026quot;We kissed!\u0026quot; Hermione shouted, her patience finally snapping.","The table gasped. Hermione froze, realizing she had just shouted about her love life in front of the entire Weasley clan.","\u0026quot;Aha!\u0026quot; Fred cheered. \u0026quot;Confession!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We kissed!\u0026quot; Hermione repeated, her face burning a violent scarlet, but her chin held high. \u0026quot;I kissed him! Before I got into the bed! Because of \u003cem\u003eyou\u003c/em\u003e, Fleur! I was following your stupid French protocol!\u0026quot;","Fleur clapped her hands delightedly. \u0026quot;Magnifique! See? I teach zem civilization!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So let me get this straight,\u0026quot; Ron said, using a sausage to point. \u0026quot;You walked in. You kissed him. You climbed into a single bed. You turned into a pretzel. And you slept there all night?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes!\u0026quot; Hermione snapped.","\u0026quot;And you,\u0026quot; Ron pointed the sausage at Draco, \u0026quot;You walked in. You kissed my sister. You almost swallowed her head. And then you got soaked?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Succinct summary, Weasel,\u0026quot; Draco muttered.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Ron said. He looked at his parents. \u0026quot;Can we eat now? All this talk of snogging is putting me off my eggs.\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley looked at the two couples. She looked at Harry, blushing but protective of Hermione. She looked at Draco, wearing Bill’s jumper and holding Ginny’s hand under the table.","She sighed, the last of the sternness leaving her face.","\u0026quot;Pass the toast, Harry,\u0026quot; Molly said softly. \u0026quot;And next time... use an Engorgement Charm on the bed. For heaven\u0027s sake.\u0026quot;","Harry exhaled, slumping in his chair. \u0026quot;Yes, Mrs. Weasley.\u0026quot;","Hermione, sensing the danger had passed, slowly lifted her head. But before she took a bite of toast, she shot Harry a look and leaned over, whispering in his ear.","\u0026quot;If you ever mention the Ostrich again,\u0026quot; she hissed, \u0026quot;I will hex you into next week.\u0026quot;","Harry just laughed and passed her the jam. \u0026quot;Deal.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":67,"origNum":67,"title":"The Ostrich Epidemic","wordCount":856,"paragraphs":["The kitchen had barely recovered from the revelation of Hermione’s midnight maneuvers when the Eye of Sauron (also known as Molly Weasley) swiveled to the far end of the table.","Harry and Hermione, now happily eating their toast in relative safety, watched with bated breath.","\u0026quot;And now,\u0026quot; Molly said, pointing a butter knife down the table, \u0026quot;The Main Event.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy stiffened. He was currently wearing Bill’s old Gryffindor Quidditch jumper, which was several sizes too big, making him look like a platinum-haired child playing dress-up. Beside him, Ginny sat with her chin jutted out, ready for a fight.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley began, trying to look stern but mostly looking fascinated. \u0026quot;Draco. The sofa. Was it... insufficient?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was... structurally sound, sir,\u0026quot; Draco said carefully, his eyes darting to the frying pan still within Molly’s reach. \u0026quot;But I found the ambient temperature of the ground floor to be... disagreeable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He was cold!\u0026quot; Fred gasped, clutching his chest. \u0026quot;Another victim of the Weasley winter! It’s an epidemic!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So naturally,\u0026quot; George continued, leaning over the table, \u0026quot;you sought warmth. In the one room in the house that contained the only daughter. A bold navigational choice.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I invited him!\u0026quot; Ginny snapped, buttering her toast with aggressive force. \u0026quot;The sofa is lumpy. And the ghoul was banging pipes. I couldn\u0027t sleep.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So you invited him in to help you sleep?\u0026quot; Bill asked dryly. \u0026quot;Because from what I saw when I walked in with the ice bucket, there wasn\u0027t much \u003cem\u003esleeping\u003c/em\u003e going on. There was a lot of... face-eating.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a vacuum seal!\u0026quot; Ron shouted, pointing a fork. \u0026quot;I’m telling you! If Bill hadn\u0027t thrown the water, they would have suffocated! It was a safety hazard!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was passion!\u0026quot; Fleur sighed dreamily.","\u0026quot;It was disgusting!\u0026quot; Ron countered.","Molly crossed her arms. \u0026quot;Draco. You are a guest. Guests usually stay in their assigned beds. They do not sneak through the house at 1:00 AM to \u0027visit\u0027 their girlfriends.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I didn\u0027t sneak,\u0026quot; Draco lied smoothly. \u0026quot;I patrolled. I heard a noise. I investigated.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You investigated Ginny’s tonsils?\u0026quot; Fred asked.","Draco turned a faint shade of pink. \u0026quot;I was ensuring her safety.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;From what?\u0026quot; George grilled him. \u0026quot;The Nargles? Or were you checking for Dementors in her mouth?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Okay, that’s enough!\u0026quot; Ginny yelled, her face heating up. \u0026quot;We’re dating! We like each other! We wanted to be close! Is that a crime?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Arthur said gently. \u0026quot;But locking the door might have been a courtesy to your brother’s retinas.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We were going to lock it!\u0026quot; Ginny protested. \u0026quot;We just... got distracted!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Distracted by the magnetic pull of Malfoy’s face?\u0026quot; Ron gagged.","\u0026quot;Yes!\u0026quot; Ginny shouted. \u0026quot;He has a nice face! Deal with it!\u0026quot;","The table erupted into snickers. Draco looked simultaneously mortified and preening at the compliment.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Molly sighed, shaking her head. \u0026quot;I suppose I can\u0027t be too angry. At least you didn\u0027t break the bed. Unlike \u003cem\u003esome\u003c/em\u003e people who turn into pretzels.\u0026quot;","She shot a look at Harry and Hermione.","\u0026quot;However,\u0026quot; Molly continued, her eyes twinkling mischievously. \u0026quot;I do have one question, Ginny. Harry and Hermione have \u0027The Ostrich\u0027 to hide their shame. What do you have? You were caught soaking wet, in pajamas, staring down your entire family. Do you have no shame?\u0026quot;","Ginny looked around the table.","She saw Fred and George grinning like hyenas.","She saw Bill looking smug about his aim with the water pitcher.","She saw Ron looking traumatized.","She saw Harry and Hermione watching with sympathy.","And she saw Draco, sitting there in the oversized jumper, looking at her with a mixture of panic and adoration.","The sheer weight of the embarrassment finally hit her. The ice water. The shouting. The \u0026quot;face-eating\u0026quot; comments.","Ginny Weasley, the boldest of them all, finally cracked.","She made a small, whimpering noise.","She turned in her chair. She grabbed the excess fabric of Bill’s jumper that Draco was wearing.","And with a decisive \u003cem\u003eTHUMP\u003c/em\u003e, she buried her face directly into the center of Draco’s chest.","She pulled the wool over her ears and went completely limp.","The kitchen went dead silent for one second.","Then, chaos.","\u0026quot;SHE\u0027S DONE IT!\u0026quot; Fred screamed, jumping out of his chair.","\u0026quot;THE OSTRICH!\u0026quot; George roared, pounding the table. \u0026quot;IT\u0027S CONTAGIOUS!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;NO WAY!\u0026quot; Ron howled, throwing his head back. \u0026quot;GINNY? THE OSTRICH? I\u0027VE SEEN EVERYTHING!\u0026quot;","Draco sat there, frozen. He looked down at the red hair currently mashing into his sternum. He looked at the Weasleys, who were dissolving into hysteria.","He slowly, awkwardly, raised a hand and patted Ginny’s head.","\u0026quot;There, there, Red,\u0026quot; Draco murmured, trying to keep a straight face. \u0026quot;It’s dark in here. They can\u0027t see you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I hate them,\u0026quot; Ginny’s muffled voice vibrated against his chest. \u0026quot;I hate them all.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Draco soothed, looking at Harry across the table.","Harry met his gaze. He pointed to Hermione, who was still hiding in his own shirt, then to Ginny hiding in Draco’s.","Harry mouthed: \u003cem\u003eWelcome to the club.\u003c/em\u003e","Draco smirked.","\u0026quot;BWAHAHAHA!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley wiped tears from his eyes. \u0026quot;Oh, this is marvelous! Two Ostriches at one breakfast! Vernon Dursley would be losing his mind!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Best. Breakfast. Ever,\u0026quot; Ron wheezed, clutching his stomach."]},{"num":68,"origNum":68,"title":"Guess Who’s Coming to Dinner","wordCount":1028,"paragraphs":["The iron gates of Malfoy Manor did not screech as they swung open; they glided silently, undoubtedly oiled by a House-Elf who was now being paid a competitive hourly wage.","Harry, Hermione, and Ginny walked up the long gravel drive. The Manor, once a place of nightmares where Hermione had been tortured and Dobby had nearly died, looked different. The dark ivy had been trimmed back, the windows were clean, and the oppressive gloom seemed to have lifted, replaced by tentative summer sunshine.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re squeezing my hand off, Draco,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered.","Draco, who had met them at the gate, looked pale. He was wearing his best dress robes, his hair was perfectly coiffed, and he looked like he was marching to his execution.","\u0026quot;My father is... fragile,\u0026quot; Draco muttered. \u0026quot;He\u0027s trying to adjust to the new world order. But bringing a Weasley home... it\u0027s a bit like bringing a blast-ended skrewt to a tea party.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am delightful,\u0026quot; Ginny corrected him, smoothing her dress. \u0026quot;And I know how to use a fish fork. I\u0027ll be fine.\u0026quot;","They reached the massive front door. Before Draco could touch the handle, it flew open.","Standing there, wearing a mismatched ensemble of a tea-cozy hat, a bright red tie, and several pairs of socks, was Dobby.","\u0026quot;Harry Potter!\u0026quot; the elf squeaked, his ears flapping wildly. \u0026quot;And Harry Potter\u0027s Wheezy! And Grangy!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Harry grinned, crouching down to shake the elf\u0027s hand. \u0026quot;You\u0027re working here?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby is a freelance consultant!\u0026quot; Dobby proclaimed proudly, puffing out his small chest. \u0026quot;Master Draco asked Dobby to help with the... \u003cem\u003esensitive\u003c/em\u003e dinner. Dobby is paid one Galleon a week and gets weekends off!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;One Galleon?\u0026quot; Hermione beamed. \u0026quot;That\u0027s wonderful, Dobby.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Father is grinding his teeth about it,\u0026quot; Draco whispered to Ginny. \u0026quot;He says paying a House-Elf is the end of civilization.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Drawing Room\u003c/strong\u003e","They were ushered into the drawing room. It was unrecognizable from the room where the chandelier had fallen. The dark artifacts were gone, replaced by vases of white lilies.","Lucius and Narcissa Malfoy stood by the fireplace. Lucius looked thinner, leaning heavily on his cane, his eyes darting nervously to Harry. Narcissa looked regal but strained.","\u0026quot;Mr. Potter,\u0026quot; Lucius said, his voice stiff. \u0026quot;Miss Granger. Welcome to... our home.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; Harry said, shaking the hand that had once slipped a diary into Ginny’s cauldron. \u0026quot;The place looks... brighter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, well,\u0026quot; Lucius cleared his throat, eyeing Dobby, who was currently rearranging the tea set with excessive noise. \u0026quot;We are making... changes.\u0026quot;","Narcissa stepped forward. She looked at Harry, then at Draco. \u0026quot;We are grateful you came.\u0026quot;","They sat down. The tension was thick enough to cut with a knife. Dobby poured tea, deliberately giving Lucius a cup that had a chip in the rim, humming loudly as he did so. Lucius twitched but said nothing.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, her gaze landing on Ginny, who was sitting next to Draco. \u0026quot;You brought a friend, Draco? We haven\u0027t been introduced.\u0026quot;","This was it.","Draco took a deep breath. He set his teacup down. He reached out and took Ginny’s hand, lacing his fingers through hers in plain sight of his parents.","Lucius’s eyes dropped to the joined hands. His eyebrow began to tick.","\u0026quot;Mother, Father,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice steady. \u0026quot;This is Ginny. Ginny Weasley.\u0026quot;","Lucius froze mid-sip.","\u0026quot;Weasley?\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. The name came out like a curse word.","\u0026quot;Arthur Weasley\u0027s daughter?\u0026quot; Narcissa asked, her voice faint.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Draco said firmly. \u0026quot;And she is my girlfriend.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eCLINK.\u003c/em\u003e","Lucius’s teacup hit the saucer with a rattle that sounded like a gunshot in the silent room.","\u0026quot;Girlfriend?\u0026quot; Lucius repeated, looking from Draco to Ginny as if his son had just announced he was dating a mountain troll. \u0026quot;A... a Weasley? In this house? Voluntarily?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; Ginny spoke up, her chin high. She squeezed Draco’s hand. \u0026quot;I know we have... history. Your husband tried to kill me with a diary once. And you called my father a disgrace to the name of wizard. But Draco is different. And I quite like him.\u0026quot;","Lucius looked like he was having a stroke. He turned to Harry, desperate for a sanity check.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Lucius pleaded. \u0026quot;Surely... surely this is a joke? A prank? Is this one of those \u0027Weasley Wheezes\u0027?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No joke, Lucius,\u0026quot; Harry said, sipping his tea calmly. \u0026quot;They\u0027re very happy. You should have seen them at school. Inseparable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We call them the Hurricane,\u0026quot; Hermione added helpfully.","Narcissa stared at Ginny. She took in the red hair, the freckles, the determined set of the jaw. Then she looked at Draco. She saw the way he was leaning into Ginny, the way his thumb was rubbing the back of her hand to comfort \u003cem\u003eher\u003c/em\u003e, despite his own fear.","She saw her son, who had been a ghost in this manor for years, looking... alive.","\u0026quot;A Weasley,\u0026quot; Narcissa murmured. She closed her eyes for a moment, then opened them. \u0026quot;Well. At least she is a Pureblood.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Narcissa!\u0026quot; Lucius gasped. \u0026quot;Have you lost your senses? Her father loves Muggles! They live in a... a hovel!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s a Burrow, actually,\u0026quot; Ginny corrected sweetly. \u0026quot;And it\u0027s very cozy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Father,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice hardening. \u0026quot;You wanted us to survive. You wanted the Malfoy name to continue. Well, this is it. I love her. And if you can\u0027t accept that... then Harry has offered me a room at Grimmauld Place. I hear Sirius is looking for a roommate.\u0026quot;","The threat of losing their son to the House of Black—and specifically to Sirius Black—was the final straw.","Lucius slumped in his chair. He looked at Dobby, who was wearing two hats now. He looked at Harry Potter, drinking his tea. He looked at his son holding hands with a blood traitor.","\u0026quot;I...\u0026quot; Lucius sighed, a sound of utter defeat. \u0026quot;I suppose... if she can overlook the diary incident...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m working on it,\u0026quot; Ginny smiled.","\u0026quot;Then... welcome,\u0026quot; Lucius choked out. \u0026quot;More tea, Miss Weasley?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; Ginny said.","Dobby let out a loud cheer. \u0026quot;Master Draco is courting the Wheezy! Dobby must make a cake! A red and gold cake!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Green and silver, Dobby!\u0026quot; Draco corrected quickly.","\u0026quot;We\u0027ll compromise,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;Checkerboard.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":69,"origNum":69,"title":"The Melting of the Iceberg","wordCount":1127,"paragraphs":["Lunch at Malfoy Manor was a surreal exercise in diplomatic relations. The house-elves had served a roasted pheasant that was cooked to perfection, but the conversation was the main course.","Lucius Malfoy sat at the head of the table, watching Ginny Weasley with the eyes of a hawk. He expected her to be loud, uncultured, or perhaps start talking about knitting sweaters. Instead, she was dissecting the current lineup of the Holyhead Harpies with a tactical acumen that rivaled a seasoned general.","\u0026quot;The Seeker is fast,\u0026quot; Ginny argued, cutting her pheasant precisely. \u0026quot;But she lacks situational awareness. She flies like she’s in a vacuum. A Bludger to the left flank would take her out in three minutes.\u0026quot;","Lucius paused, his fork halfway to his mouth. He appreciated strategy. He appreciated ruthlessness.","\u0026quot;A Bludger to the flank?\u0026quot; Lucius mused. \u0026quot;Crude. But effective.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s not crude if it wins the match, Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; Ginny countered, meeting his gaze without flinching. \u0026quot;It’s decisive.\u0026quot;","Lucius’s lip twitched. He looked at Draco, who was watching Ginny with a look of terrified awe.","\u0026quot;She has... spirit,\u0026quot; Lucius admitted to Narcissa.","\u0026quot;She has fire,\u0026quot; Narcissa corrected softly.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Peacock Walk\u003c/strong\u003e","After lunch, while Draco dragged Harry and Hermione off to show them the library (which Hermione had been eyeing hungrily), Lucius cleared his throat.","\u0026quot;Miss Weasley,\u0026quot; Lucius said stiffly. \u0026quot;Perhaps... you would care to see the gardens? The white peacocks are particularly... aggressive this time of year. I suspect you would get along with them.\u0026quot;","Ginny wiped her mouth. \u0026quot;I’d love to.\u0026quot;","They walked out onto the terrace. The air was warm, smelling of roses and old money. They walked in silence for a few minutes, the crunch of gravel under their boots the only sound.","Lucius stopped by a marble fountain. He gripped the head of his cane, staring at the water.","\u0026quot;I am not a man who apologizes, Miss Weasley,\u0026quot; Lucius began, his voice low. \u0026quot;I find it... distasteful. A sign of weakness.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Ginny said calmly.","\u0026quot;However,\u0026quot; Lucius turned to look at her. \u0026quot;I am also a man who values his family above all else. And I see... I see that my son has made his choice.\u0026quot;","He took a breath, looking pained, as if the words were physically stuck in his throat.","\u0026quot;Years ago... in a bookshop... I placed a diary in your cauldron.\u0026quot;","Ginny stiffened, her hand instinctively going to her wand pocket. \u0026quot;I remember.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I did not care who took it,\u0026quot; Lucius confessed, his grey eyes looking old and tired. \u0026quot;I wanted to discredit your father. I wanted to purge the school. You were... collateral damage. A pawn in a game I thought I was controlling.\u0026quot;","He looked at her—really looked at her—for the first time. He saw the girl who had survived possession by the Dark Lord, who had fought in the Department of Mysteries, who had held the line at Hogwarts.","\u0026quot;I was wrong,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;To use a child as a weapon... it was beneath even me. And seeing how much you mean to Draco... seeing that you are the reason he is standing upright today... I find myself... regretting my actions.\u0026quot;","He straightened up, regaining a shred of his dignity.","\u0026quot;I am sorry, Ginny Weasley. For the diary. For the danger. For everything.\u0026quot;","Ginny stared at him. She had hated this man for years. She had dreamed of hexing him into a oblivion. But standing here, seeing the broken pride and the genuine love he had for his son... the anger drained away.","She felt a tear prick her eye. She sniffed.","\u0026quot;Oh, come here, you old peacock,\u0026quot; Ginny choked out.","Before Lucius could process the insult or the movement, Ginny surged forward. She didn\u0027t offer a handshake. She wrapped her arms around his waist (he was quite tall) and buried her face in his velvet robes, hugging him tight.","Lucius Malfoy froze. He went rigid. His eyes bulged. He held his cane out to the side like a weapon he didn\u0027t know how to use. He looked like a man being attacked by a very affectionate squid.","\u0026quot;There, there,\u0026quot; Lucius said frantically, patting the top of her head with two stiff fingers. \u0026quot;That will do. Protocol observed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hug me back, Lucius,\u0026quot; Ginny mumbled into his chest. \u0026quot;It’s customary.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is it?\u0026quot; Lucius squeaked. \u0026quot;It seems... excessive.\u0026quot;","But slowly, awkwardly, Lucius lowered his arms. He placed one hand tentatively on her back.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Audience\u003c/strong\u003e","At that precise moment, the French doors to the terrace swung open.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m telling you, Potter, the first edition of \u003cem\u003eMoste Potente Potions\u003c/em\u003e is—\u0026quot;","Draco stopped.","Harry stopped. Hermione stopped. Narcissa stopped. Even Dobby, carrying a tray of lemonade, stopped.","They stared.","There, by the fountain, Lucius Malfoy—former Death Eater, pureblood supremacist, and man who believed smiling caused wrinkles—was being embraced by a Weasley. And he was... \u003cem\u003ehugging her back\u003c/em\u003e.","Draco dropped the book he was holding. His jaw hit his chest.","\u0026quot;Father?\u0026quot; Draco whispered, his voice high and terrified. \u0026quot;Are you... are you dying? Is this a goodbye hug?\u0026quot;","Harry took off his glasses, cleaned them on his shirt, and put them back on. \u0026quot;Nope. Still seeing it. Hermione, am I under a Confundus Charm?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I... I don\u0027t think so,\u0026quot; Hermione breathed, looking delighted. \u0026quot;I think... I think it\u0027s a breakthrough.\u0026quot;","Dobby let out a wail of pure joy. \u0026quot;Master Lucius is feeling the love! The Wheezy has melted the ice heart!\u0026quot;","Lucius, hearing the audience, looked up. His face went from pale to a violent, blotchy red. He tried to pull away, but Ginny was holding on with Gryffindor strength.","\u0026quot;I am being attacked!\u0026quot; Lucius shouted at them, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;She is crushing my ribs! Narcissa, assistance!\u0026quot;","Narcissa smiled—a true, radiant smile. \u0026quot;Oh, hush, Lucius. You look charming.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I look ridiculous!\u0026quot; Lucius roared. \u0026quot;Potter! Make it stop! You\u0027re the hero! Save me!\u0026quot;","Harry leaned against the doorframe, grinning. \u0026quot;Sorry, Lucius. We Dursleys believe in letting family moments play out. It’s important for emotional growth.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Emotional growth?!\u0026quot; Lucius spluttered. \u0026quot;I am losing circulation!\u0026quot;","Ginny finally pulled back, wiping her eyes, beaming up at him. \u0026quot;See? That wasn\u0027t so bad, was it?\u0026quot;","Lucius straightened his robes, smoothed his hair, and looked at the group staring at him. He tried to summon his old sneer, but it crumbled into a flustered, embarrassed grimace.","\u0026quot;It was... adequate,\u0026quot; Lucius muttered, refusing to meet anyone\u0027s eyes. \u0026quot;Dobby! Lemonade! Immediately! I need sugar for the shock!\u0026quot;","As Lucius marched past them into the house, looking thoroughly ruffled, Draco looked at Ginny.","\u0026quot;You hugged him,\u0026quot; Draco said, stunned. \u0026quot;You actually hugged Lucius Malfoy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He needed it,\u0026quot; Ginny shrugged.","Draco shook his head, looking at Harry. \u0026quot;Potter, I think I\u0027m going to marry her.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get in line,\u0026quot; Harry laughed. \u0026quot;I think your dad might propose first.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":70,"origNum":70,"title":"The Eagle and the Weasel","wordCount":994,"paragraphs":["The breakfast table at the Burrow was a battlefield of toast crusts and pumpkin juice spills. Arthur Weasley was halfway through explaining the function of a \u0026quot;spark plug\u0026quot; to a fascinated Harry (who had popped over to pick up Ron) when the light in the kitchen dimmed.","A massive eagle owl, looking distinctively aristocratic and disdainful of the Weasley’s scruffy family owl, Errol, swooped through the window. It landed directly in the butter dish, extended a leg bound in velvet ribbon, and hooted imperiously.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Ron muttered, recoiling. \u0026quot;That bird costs more than our house.\u0026quot;","Arthur untied the heavy parchment envelope. He broke the wax seal—which bore the Malfoy crest—and read the letter. His eyebrows climbed so high they disappeared into his hairline.","\u0026quot;Arthur?\u0026quot; Molly asked, pausing with a frying pan. \u0026quot;Is it the Ministry? Has the car been spotted again?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Arthur said, his voice faint. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s Lucius Malfoy.\u0026quot;","The kitchen went dead silent. Fred and George lowered their wands.","\u0026quot;He says,\u0026quot; Arthur read aloud, adjusting his glasses, \u0026quot;that in light of recent developments—specifically the \u0027unexpected but adequate\u0027 union of our children—he requests the honor of the Weasley family’s presence for dinner this evening. Tonight. At the Manor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He wants us for dinner?\u0026quot; Fred asked. \u0026quot;As guests? Or as the main course?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It says \u0027To bury the hatchet\u0027,\u0026quot; Arthur continued.","\u0026quot;In our backs?\u0026quot; George suggested.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry spoke up, grinning. \u0026quot;He means it. I think the hug broke him, Mrs. Weasley. He’s trying.\u0026quot;","Molly wiped her hands on her apron. She looked at the letter, then at Ginny’s empty chair (she was already at the Manor), and finally at her husband.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Molly declared, straightening her spine. \u0026quot;If Lucius Malfoy wants to host the Weasleys, he’s going to get the Weasleys. But we are not going to look like ragamuffins. Everyone! Upstairs! Best robes! Wash your faces! George, take that extendable ear out of your nose!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Makeover\u003c/strong\u003e","Meanwhile, at Malfoy Manor, a different kind of panic was ensuing.","Draco Malfoy stood in the center of the guest suite, looking critically at Harry, Hermione, and Ginny. They were currently dressed in their usual attire: jeans, t-shirts, and comfortable jumpers.","\u0026quot;Absolutely not,\u0026quot; Draco said, shaking his head. \u0026quot;Father is already hyperventilating about the number of redheads entering the premises. If you walk downstairs looking like you just rolled out of a haystack, he will have an aneurysm.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What\u0027s wrong with jeans?\u0026quot; Harry asked, looking down at his Levis. \u0026quot;Vernon says denim is durable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are not drilling for oil, Potter,\u0026quot; Draco drawled. \u0026quot;We are dining.\u0026quot;","He clapped his hands. The wardrobe doors flew open.","Floaty, magnificent fabrics streamed out, suspending themselves in the air.","\u0026quot;For the Lady,\u0026quot; Draco announced, gesturing to a gown of emerald green silk that shimmered like dragon scales. \u0026quot;Tailored to fit.\u0026quot;","Ginny gasped, stepping forward. \u0026quot;Draco... this is beautiful.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;For the Scholar,\u0026quot; Draco pointed to a set of dress robes in a deep, midnight blue periwinkle—a nod to the Yule Ball, but far more sophisticated, with silver threading.","Hermione’s hand flew to her mouth. \u0026quot;Oh, Draco. You didn\u0027t have to.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And for the Chosen One,\u0026quot; Draco smirked, gesturing to a set of sleek, black acromantula-silk dress robes. They were cut in a modern style, sharp and imposing, looking more like something a Auror general would wear than a schoolboy.","\u0026quot;Try them on,\u0026quot; Draco commanded. \u0026quot;I refuse to be the only well-dressed person in the room.\u0026quot;","Harry took the robes. The silk felt cool and heavy—expensive. He thought of the oversized cast-offs he had grown up in. He thought of Vernon trying to buy him a Vauxhall Astra.","\u0026quot;Thanks, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t get sentimental, Potter. It ruins the line of the suit.\u0026quot;","Draco turned to the corner of the room, where Dobby was currently polishing his own tea-towel toga.","\u0026quot;And Dobby?\u0026quot; Draco said softly.","The elf looked up, his tennis-ball eyes wide.","Draco reached behind his back and pulled out a small, elf-sized hanger. On it hung a miniature black tuxedo, complete with a crisp white shirt and a tiny red bow tie.","\u0026quot;Dobby is a freelance consultant,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice devoid of its usual sneer. \u0026quot;Consultants wear suits.\u0026quot;","Dobby stared at the clothes. His lip began to tremble. Tears welled up in his enormous eyes.","\u0026quot;Master Draco...\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked. \u0026quot;Clothes? Master Draco is giving Dobby... a suit?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s not a sock, so you\u0027re not free-er,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, looking at the ceiling. \u0026quot;Just put it on, Dobby. You represent the House.\u0026quot;","Dobby burst into loud, wailing sobs of joy, clutching the tuxedo to his chest. \u0026quot;Dobby is looking like a gentleman! Dobby is handsome!\u0026quot;","Harry, Hermione, and Ginny watched, smiling. The clothes were magnificent, yes. But seeing Draco Malfoy treat a House-Elf with dignity? That was the best look of all.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","The sun was setting, casting long, golden shadows across the Wiltshire countryside, when the air outside the Manor gates rippled.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK. CRACK. CRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The Weasley clan appeared.","Arthur wore his best ministry robes (slightly frayed at the cuffs, but pressed). Molly wore her navy dress with a new hat. Bill and Fleur looked glamorous as always. Charlie had tried to clean the soot off his jacket. Percy was polishing his horn-rimmed glasses. Ron looked terrified, tugging at his collar. And the twins were wearing matching dragon-skin jackets they had undoubtedly bought with the profits from their joke shop.","They stood before the towering iron gates of Malfoy Manor.","\u0026quot;It’s big, isn\u0027t it?\u0026quot; Ron gulped.","\u0026quot;It’s just a house, Ron,\u0026quot; Arthur said bravely, squeezing Molly’s hand. \u0026quot;Just bricks and mortar. Now, remember. We are guests. We will be polite. And Fred, George... no explosions.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We promise nothing,\u0026quot; Fred whispered to George.","The gates swung open silently. The Weasleys took a collective breath and began the long walk up the drive, marching into the heart of the enemy territory, armed only with their charm, their chaos, and a fruitcake Molly had baked as a peace offering."]},{"num":71,"origNum":71,"title":"The Clash of Clans","wordCount":740,"paragraphs":["The massive oak front doors of Malfoy Manor swung open to reveal the Weasley clan standing on the doorstep like a colorful, slightly nervous invading army.","Lucius Malfoy stood in the center of the entrance hall, flanked by Narcissa. He was gripping his cane so tightly his knuckles were white. He looked like a man preparing to diffuse a bomb with a teaspoon.","\u0026quot;Arthur,\u0026quot; Lucius said, his voice straining for neutrality. \u0026quot;Molly. Welcome.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lucius,\u0026quot; Arthur replied, stepping over the threshold and clutching Molly’s fruitcake as if it were a shield. \u0026quot;Narcissa. Thank you for the invitation.\u0026quot;","The air in the hall was thick enough to choke a hippogriff. The history between the two families—fistfights in bookstores, insults about poverty, allegiance to Dark Lords—swirled around them like invisible smoke.","Fred and George were eyeing a bust of a Malfoy ancestor with expressions that suggested they were calculating its explosive potential. Ron was staring at the marble floor, looking afraid he might dirty it just by existing.","Then, Molly Weasley moved.","She handed her handbag to Arthur. She stepped forward, crossing the No Man\u0027s Land of the marble foyer. She looked at Narcissa Malfoy—the woman who had lied to Voldemort in the forest, the mother who had stood in the Great Hall with her wand drawn to protect her son.","Molly didn\u0027t see a Black or a Malfoy. She saw another mother who had almost lost everything.","\u0026quot;Narcissa,\u0026quot; Molly said warmly.","She didn\u0027t offer a hand. She opened her arms and pulled the elegant, stiff witch into a hug that smelled of baking and comfort.","Narcissa froze for a millisecond. Then, her shoulders slumped. The icy facade cracked. She wrapped her slim arms around Molly, returning the embrace with a desperate, silent gratitude.","\u0026quot;Thank you,\u0026quot; Narcissa whispered into Molly’s ear. \u0026quot;For welcoming him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s family now,\u0026quot; Molly whispered back, pulling away and patting Narcissa’s cheek.","The tension in the room released a fraction.","Then, it was Lucius’s turn.","He watched the hug. He looked at Arthur Weasley, who was standing awkwardly holding the fruitcake. Lucius’s mind flashed back to the terrace. \u003cem\u003eProtocol,\u003c/em\u003e he told himself. \u003cem\u003eGinny said it is customary.\u003c/em\u003e","Lucius took a deep breath. He steeled himself. He stepped forward.","\u0026quot;Arthur,\u0026quot; Lucius announced, his voice booming slightly too loud in the quiet hall.","\u0026quot;Lucius?\u0026quot; Arthur asked, extending a hand for a handshake.","Lucius ignored the hand. He spread his arms wide, his velvet robes billowing like bat wings.","\u0026quot;Come here, you old tinkerer,\u0026quot; Lucius declared grimly.","Before Arthur could react, Lucius Malfoy lunged. He enveloped Arthur Weasley in a stiff, awkward, but undeniably firm embrace.","The silence that followed was louder than an explosion.","Arthur’s eyes bulged behind his glasses. He stood there, arms pinned to his sides, the fruitcake crushed between his chest and Lucius’s expensive robes. He looked like a man being attacked by a very expensive coat rack.","\u0026quot;Uhh...\u0026quot; Arthur wheezed. \u0026quot;Lucius?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am embracing the new era,\u0026quot; Lucius gritted out near Arthur’s ear, patting him on the back with a rhythm that sounded like \u003cem\u003ethump-thump-thump\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;I am... mingling.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy, standing on the staircase with Ginny, Harry, and Hermione, made a noise like a dying cat.","\u0026quot;My eyes,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, clutching the banister. \u0026quot;My father is hugging a Weasley. The apocalypse is here. The Mayans were right.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s sweet!\u0026quot; Ginny beamed, squeezing Draco’s arm.","\u0026quot;It’s terrifying!\u0026quot; Draco countered. \u0026quot;He looks like he’s trying to crush him!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think it’s nice,\u0026quot; Hermione said, though she was biting her lip to keep from laughing.","Harry just shook his head. \u0026quot;The Ostrich has nothing on this.\u0026quot;","Down in the hall, Lucius released Arthur, stepping back quickly and smoothing his robes. He looked flushed and slightly dizzy.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Lucius gasped. \u0026quot;That’s done. Formalities concluded. Dobby! Wine! Immediately!\u0026quot;","Arthur blinked, adjusting his glasses which had been knocked askew. A slow, bewildered smile spread across his face.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Arthur chuckled, looking at the crushed fruitcake. \u0026quot;That was... unexpected, Lucius. But... appreciated.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Let us never speak of it again,\u0026quot; Lucius commanded, turning on his heel and marching toward the dining room. \u0026quot;Dinner is served. Try not to touch the tapestries; they bite.\u0026quot;","Fred leaned over to George. \u0026quot;Ten galleons says Dad hugs him back before dessert.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re on,\u0026quot; George grinned.","And with that, the Weasleys followed the Malfoys into the dining room, stepping over the threshold of a new world where hugs were weapons of mass affection and enemies broke bread instead of bones."]},{"num":72,"origNum":72,"title":"The Feast of the Pheasant","wordCount":1018,"paragraphs":["The dining room of Malfoy Manor was designed to intimidate. The table was a single slab of dark mahogany that stretched for twenty feet. The chandelier above was a constellation of crystal (a replacement for the one Dobby had destroyed). The walls were lined with portraits of Malfoy ancestors who usually sneered at guests.","Tonight, however, even the portraits looked hungry.","Dobby, looking dashing in his miniature tuxedo, snapped his fingers.","The feast appeared.","It was not the hearty, rustic fare of the Burrow. It was a culinary symphony. There were platters of roasted venison glazed in redcurrant reduction, silver trays of pheasant stuffed with truffles, tureens of lobster bisque that smelled of the sea and cognac, and mountains of roasted vegetables that glistened like jewels.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, staring at a potato that was cut into the shape of a rose. \u0026quot;I feel bad eating it. It looks like art.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Eat it, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco said from across the table, unfolding his napkin. \u0026quot;It tastes better than it looks.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Vintage\u003c/strong\u003e","Lucius Malfoy stood at the head of the table. He gestured to Dobby, who trotted forward holding a dusty, cobweb-covered bottle with the reverence one might show a holy relic.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Lucius announced, his voice regaining some of its old silky confidence, \u0026quot;is a bottle of Elf-Made Elderflower Wine from 1492. It has been in the cellar since before the Statute of Secrecy was signed.\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley’s eyes widened. \u0026quot;1492? Lucius, that’s... that’s older than my shed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is significantly more valuable than your shed, Arthur,\u0026quot; Lucius noted, but there was no bite in it. He poured the golden liquid into Arthur’s crystal goblet. \u0026quot;Please. A toast.\u0026quot;","Lucius raised his glass. The table followed suit. The crystal chimed as twenty glasses were lifted.","\u0026quot;To...\u0026quot; Lucius paused. He looked at his son, sitting next to a Weasley. He looked at his wife, smiling at another Weasley. He looked at Harry Potter, the boy who had saved them all.","\u0026quot;To survival,\u0026quot; Lucius said simply. \u0026quot;And to the unexpected flavor of change.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hear, hear!\u0026quot; Arthur cheered.","They drank. The wine was exquisite—like drinking liquid summer sunlight mixed with history. Even Ron, whose experience with alcohol was limited to Butterbeer and cheap Firewhisky, closed his eyes and sighed happily.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Breaking of Bread\u003c/strong\u003e","The meal began in earnest. The initial stiffness evaporated with the wine and the sheer quality of the food.","\u0026quot;Pass the potatoes, please, Narcissa,\u0026quot; Molly asked politely.","\u0026quot;Of course, Molly,\u0026quot; Narcissa replied, levitating the silver dish. \u0026quot;And I must ask... this fruitcake you brought. Is it a family recipe?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, yes,\u0026quot; Molly beamed. \u0026quot;Great-Aunt Muriel\u0027s. It’s soaked in rum for three months.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Three months?\u0026quot; Lucius interjected, eyeing the dense brick of cake sitting on the sideboard. \u0026quot;Is it a dessert or a building material?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a bit of both,\u0026quot; Fred grinned. \u0026quot;We used a slice to chock the wheels of the car once.\u0026quot;","Lucius let out a short, startled bark of laughter. He immediately covered his mouth with his napkin, looking horrified that he had made such a plebeian sound.","\u0026quot;Did you hear that?\u0026quot; George whispered to Harry. \u0026quot;He laughed. The gargoyle cracked.\u0026quot;","Harry grinned, slicing his venison. \u0026quot;I told you. He’s human. Mostly.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Conversations\u003c/strong\u003e","As the courses progressed, the conversations grew louder and more animated.","At one end, Hermione was engaging Narcissa in a surprisingly intense discussion about library organization spells. Narcissa, it turned out, was quite the bibliophile and was horrified to learn Hermione had been using \u003cem\u003eScourgify\u003c/em\u003e on ancient texts.","\u0026quot;No, my dear,\u0026quot; Narcissa corrected gently. \u0026quot;You must use \u003cem\u003ePura Pagina\u003c/em\u003e. It preserves the ink.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003ePura Pagina\u003c/em\u003e ,\u0026quot; Hermione repeated, eyes shining as she mentally cataloged the spell. \u0026quot;Brilliant.\u0026quot;","In the center, Bill and Fleur were discussing Gringotts security with Draco.","\u0026quot;The dragon was a nice touch,\u0026quot; Draco admitted, swirling his wine. \u0026quot;Though the hole in the roof was drafty for weeks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We did warn Griphook,\u0026quot; Bill shrugged. \u0026quot;Dragons don\u0027t like queues.\u0026quot;","And at the head of the table, the most impossible conversation of all was taking place.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Lucius said, loosening his tie slightly (a historic first). \u0026quot;You say this... \u0027spark plug\u0027... creates the fire?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly!\u0026quot; Arthur said, moving salt shakers around to demonstrate an engine. \u0026quot;It ignites the petrol! Boom! The piston moves! It’s purely mechanical combustion!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fascinating,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured, staring at the salt shakers. \u0026quot;And Muggles trust their lives to these... explosions?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Every day, Lucius! Every day!\u0026quot;","Lucius shook his head, pouring himself more wine. \u0026quot;Madness. Utter madness. Tell me more about the \u0027rubber ducks\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","By the time dessert arrived—a towering croquembouche made by the house-elves, alongside slices of Molly’s formidable fruitcake—the table was a mess of crumbs, empty bottles, and laughter.","Lucius was red-faced and listening to Arthur explain how airplanes stayed up. Narcissa was laughing at a story Molly was telling about Fred and George turning Ron’s teddy bear into a spider. Draco and Ginny were feeding each other profiteroles, ignoring the gagging noises from Ron.","Harry sat back, feeling full and warm. He looked around the table.","This was the room where Voldemort had sat. This was the room where Charity Burbage had died. But tonight, the shadows were gone, chased away by the clinking of glasses and the roar of Weasley laughter.","\u0026quot;Good food,\u0026quot; Harry said to Dobby, who was refilling his water glass.","\u0026quot; The best, Harry Potter!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked. \u0026quot;Master Lucius ordered the reserves! He wanted to impress the Wheezys!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He succeeded,\u0026quot; Harry smiled.","Lucius stood up, swaying slightly. He held up a slice of fruitcake.","\u0026quot;I have tasted the brick,\u0026quot; Lucius announced to the room. \u0026quot;And I must say... it pairs surprisingly well with the \u002792 Merlot. A triumph of density, Molly.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Lucius,\u0026quot; Molly beamed.","\u0026quot;To the chef!\u0026quot; Fred toasted.","\u0026quot;To the brick!\u0026quot; George added.","\u0026quot;To us,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, raising his glass.","The dinner at Malfoy Manor went down in history not for the politics, but for the party. It was the night the war truly ended, buried under an avalanche of roast pheasant and the undeniable power of a good meal shared between enemies who had become family."]},{"num":73,"origNum":73,"title":"The Collision of Worlds","wordCount":1223,"paragraphs":["Five years had passed since the Battle of Hogwarts, and the wizarding world had settled into a golden age of peace, prosperity, and extremely busy schedules for its heroes.","Harry Potter, at twenty-three, was the youngest Head Auror in history. He had reorganized the department, banished the Dementors, and implemented a strict \u0026quot;No Corruption\u0026quot; policy that Vernon Dursley would have approved of. He still wore glasses, his hair was still messy, but he walked with the easy confidence of a man who knew his place in the world.","Hermione Granger was currently the youngest Deputy Minister for Magic. She was single-handedly rewriting the legislature on House-Elf rights, Goblin relations, and the standardization of cauldron thickness (a passion project). She was terrifyingly efficient, and even the gargoyles in the Ministry atrium stood up straighter when she walked past.","Ron Weasley had left the Auror office after two years (\u0026quot;Too much paperwork, not enough laughs\u0026quot;) to join Fred and George at Weasleys\u0027 Wizard Wheezes. The trio of brothers had turned the joke shop into a global empire. Ron managed the strategy, Fred handled product development, and George managed the PR. They were currently working on a line of \u0026quot;Daydream Charms\u0026quot; for bored Ministry employees.","Ginny Weasley was the star Chaser for the Holyhead Harpies, her poster adorning bedroom walls across the country. She was fierce, fast, and still managed to terrify Draco whenever she flew too close to the ground.","And Draco Malfoy? He had surprised everyone by taking a job at the Ministry in the Department of International Magical Cooperation, specifically in Finance and Relations. He used his family’s old connections not for dark favors, but to secure trade deals and smooth over diplomatic incidents. He was good at it—charming, ruthless when necessary, and impeccably dressed.","Luna Lovegood was a Magizoologist, traveling the world to discover new species (she had recently found a Crumple-Horned Snorkack in Sweden, much to Hermione’s disbelief), but she always returned for the gatherings.","And tonight was the gathering.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Quarterly Summit\u003c/strong\u003e","The dinners at Malfoy Manor had evolved from a peace treaty into a tradition. Every three months, the group would descend upon Wiltshire for a night of food, wine, and arguments about Quidditch.","But tonight was special. Tonight, the guest list had expanded.","Harry stood by the front door of the Manor, adjusting his dress robes. Draco stood beside him, checking his pocket watch.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re late,\u0026quot; Draco muttered. \u0026quot;I thought Muggles prided themselves on punctuality.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Traffic, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;It’s a Muggle thing. Too many cars on the M25.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Barbarians,\u0026quot; Draco sighed. \u0026quot;Why can\u0027t they just fly?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because a Ford Mondeo doesn\u0027t have a broomstick mode,\u0026quot; Harry reminded him.","Just then, the sound of tires crunching on gravel echoed up the drive. A sleek, black executive car rolled through the open gates, passing the albino peacocks who strutted indignantly out of the way.","The car stopped. The doors opened.","Vernon Dursley stepped out. He had aged a bit—his mustache was greyer, his waistline slightly more managed thanks to Petunia’s diet regime—but he looked imposing in his best suit. He looked up at the facade of Malfoy Manor.","\u0026quot;Hm,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, nodding approvingly. \u0026quot;Impressive stonework. Pointing looks solid. Good guttering.\u0026quot;","Petunia stepped out next, clutching a bouquet of flowers. She looked nervous, her eyes darting to the peacocks.","Then came Dudley. He was huge—muscle, not fat, thanks to his boxing career. He was holding the hand of a pretty, petite woman with kind eyes and a bewildered expression.","\u0026quot;This is it, Chloe,\u0026quot; Dudley whispered to his wife. \u0026quot;Harry’s friend’s house. The rich one.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s... a castle, Dudley,\u0026quot; Chloe whispered back, eyes wide.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Welcome\u003c/strong\u003e","The front doors swung open.","Lucius Malfoy stepped out. He was leaning on his cane, but his posture was upright, his face less gaunt than it had been after the war. Narcissa glided beside him.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said, his voice smooth as silk. \u0026quot;Petunia. You made it.\u0026quot;","Vernon walked up the steps. He looked at the former Death Eater. He looked at the wizard who had once sneered at him.","Vernon extended his hand. \u0026quot;Lucius. Good to see you. The drive is a nightmare. Roadworks near Basingstoke.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Abominable,\u0026quot; Lucius agreed, shaking the hand firmly. \u0026quot;We really must lobby the Prime Minister for better infrastructure. Welcome back.\u0026quot;","Petunia walked up to Narcissa.","\u0026quot;Narcissa,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled, handing over the flowers. \u0026quot;Peonies. From the garden.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are lovely, Petunia,\u0026quot; Narcissa beamed, taking them. \u0026quot;And you look well. That shade of salmon suits you.\u0026quot;","Then, Harry stepped forward.","\u0026quot;Uncle Vernon! Aunt Petunia!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Petunia hugged him tightly. \u0026quot;You look tired. Are you eating? Being an Auror sounds exhausting.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m fine, Aunt Petunia,\u0026quot; Harry laughed.","Dudley stepped up, grinning. \u0026quot;Harry. Good to see you, mate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You too, Big D.\u0026quot; Harry looked at the woman beside him. \u0026quot;And this must be Chloe.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hi,\u0026quot; Chloe squeaked, looking at the wizard. \u0026quot;Dudley told me... well, he told me everything. But I didn\u0027t expect... peacocks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They\u0027re harmless,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, stepping forward and offering a hand. \u0026quot;Unless you\u0027re wearing blue. They get jealous. I\u0027m Draco.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Nice to meet you,\u0026quot; Chloe shook his hand.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grand Tour\u003c/strong\u003e","They moved into the entrance hall. The Dursleys stopped, staring at the chandelier, the marble staircase, and the moving portraits.","\u0026quot;Moving pictures,\u0026quot; Vernon noted, pointing at a portrait of Abraxas Malfoy, who was currently picking his teeth. \u0026quot;Bit distracting, isn\u0027t it? How do you watch the telly?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We don\u0027t have a \u0027telly\u0027, Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said, guiding them toward the drawing room. \u0026quot;Though Arthur Weasley keeps threatening to install one. Something about \u0027Eastenders\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, you have to watch Eastenders,\u0026quot; Chloe chimed in. \u0026quot;It’s gripping.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is it?\u0026quot; Narcissa asked politely. \u0026quot;Is there dueling?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lots of shouting in a pub,\u0026quot; Dudley explained.","\u0026quot;Sounds like the Weasleys,\u0026quot; Draco muttered to Harry.","Just then, the Floo network flared green in the drawing room fireplace.","Fred and George Weasley tumbled out, followed by Ron and a very dreamy-looking Luna.","\u0026quot;We have arrived!\u0026quot; Fred announced, dusting off his suit (which was purple and orange). \u0026quot;And we brought the entertainment!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No explosions!\u0026quot; Lucius barked instantly, a reflex honed over five years.","\u0026quot;Just sparklers, Lucius!\u0026quot; George winked. He spotted the Dursleys. \u0026quot;Vernon! Petunia! Dudley! And the new Mrs. D! Welcome to the lair of the aristocracy!\u0026quot;","Vernon looked at the twins—alive, chaotic, and successful. He looked at Lucius—rich, magical, and surprisingly tolerant. He looked at Harry—hero, Auror, and nephew.","Vernon Dursley took a deep breath of the expensive, magical air.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon said, rubbing his hands together. \u0026quot;Excellent spread. Now, Lucius, before we eat, I need to pick your brain about this \u0027Gringotts\u0027 investment portfolio. I hear Goblin gold is stable in a bear market.\u0026quot;","Lucius smiled—a genuine, amused smile. \u0026quot;It is indeed, Vernon. Shall we discuss it over the \u002792 Merlot?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lead the way,\u0026quot; Vernon beamed.","As the mismatched family of Muggles, Wizards, former Death Eaters, and war heroes moved into the dining room, Harry hung back for a moment with Hermione and Ron.","\u0026quot;Look at them,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, shaking his head. \u0026quot;If you told me ten years ago that Vernon Dursley would be discussing finance with Lucius Malfoy, I’d have checked you into St. Mungo’s.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a brave new world, mate,\u0026quot; Ron grinned, putting his arm around Harry. \u0026quot;And the food is fantastic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Come on,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled, pulling them both toward the door. \u0026quot;Dinner is served.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":74,"origNum":74,"title":"The Summit of Oddities","wordCount":856,"paragraphs":["The pre-dinner drinks were being served in the drawing room, but the social dynamics had fractured into small, fascinating clusters of cross-cultural exchange.","In the center of the room, Vernon Dursley found himself the center of attention. He was flanked on his left by Arthur Weasley, whose eyes were shining with unbridled excitement, and on his right by Lucius Malfoy, who was studying Vernon with the intense, scholarly focus of a man trying to decipher a particularly complex rune.","Vernon held a small, silver object in his hand. It was a retractable ballpoint pen.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Arthur breathed, leaning in close. \u0026quot;You say the ink is... contained? Inside a tube?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Plastic cartridge,\u0026quot; Vernon explained, clicking the pen. \u003cem\u003eClick-click.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;Press the top, the nib extends. Press again, it retracts. No mess, no ink pots, no sharpening feathers. Efficiency.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Extraordinary,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured. He reached out a pale hand, looking at Vernon. \u0026quot;May I?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go ahead,\u0026quot; Vernon said, handing it over like a king bestowing a sword.","Lucius held the Biro. He clicked it tentatively. \u003cem\u003eClick.\u003c/em\u003e He jumped slightly.","\u0026quot;It makes a sound,\u0026quot; Lucius noted, looking at Arthur. \u0026quot;A mechanical signal of readiness.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s genius, Lucius!\u0026quot; Arthur beamed. \u0026quot;Muggles have bypassed the need for quills entirely! They’ve industrialized writing!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the ink?\u0026quot; Lucius asked, narrowing his eyes at the tip. \u0026quot;It does not dry out?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not for months,\u0026quot; Vernon said proudly. \u0026quot;And you can clip it to your pocket. See the clip? Practical design.\u0026quot;","Lucius slid the pen into the breast pocket of his expensive wizarding robes. He patted it.","\u0026quot;I feel... prepared,\u0026quot; Lucius admitted, a strange look of wonder on his face. \u0026quot;Vernon, tell me again about the \u0027stapler\u0027. You said it binds paper with... metal teeth?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ah, the stapler,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded sagely. \u0026quot;A brutal but necessary tool. Remind me to show you the one in the car.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Council of Mothers\u003c/strong\u003e","On the plush velvet sofas near the fireplace, a different kind of summit was taking place. The Matriarchs—Molly Weasley, Narcissa Malfoy, and Petunia Dursley—sat with cups of tea (and a glass of sherry for Narcissa).","They were discussing the universal enemy of all households: stains.","\u0026quot;Dragon blood is the worst,\u0026quot; Molly sighed, shaking her head. \u0026quot;Charlie ruins his robes constantly. Scourgify usually works, but it leaves a smell.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I find soaking it in mooncalf solution helps,\u0026quot; Narcissa suggested elegantly. \u0026quot;Though it ruins the silk if you leave it too long.\u0026quot;","Petunia smoothed her skirt, looking between the two witches. She cleared her throat.","\u0026quot;Have you tried baking soda and white vinegar?\u0026quot; Petunia asked.","Narcissa blinked. \u0026quot;Baking... soda?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a powder,\u0026quot; Petunia explained, her voice gaining confidence. \u0026quot;You make a paste. Scrub it in. Let it sit. Then wash it with hot water. It lifts anything. Grass, wine, grease.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Scrub it?\u0026quot; Narcissa repeated the word as if it were in a foreign language. \u0026quot;With your... hands?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;With a brush, Cissy,\u0026quot; Molly interrupted, looking intrigued. \u0026quot;It sounds vigorous. I like it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s very effective,\u0026quot; Petunia nodded firmly. \u0026quot;And for white linens? Lemon juice and sunshine. No magic required.\u0026quot;","Narcissa looked at Petunia with a newfound respect. \u0026quot;You harness the sun to bleach your linens? That sounds... incredibly powerful. Is it ancient Muggle alchemy?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s just nature,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled. \u0026quot;And a bit of elbow grease.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I must try this \u0027elbow grease\u0027,\u0026quot; Narcissa decided, sipping her sherry. \u0026quot;Dobby! Note down \u0027vinegar\u0027 on the shopping list!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Kids\u0027 Table\u003c/strong\u003e","Over by the drinks cart, the younger generation watched the spectacle with a mixture of horror and hilarity.","Harry leaned against the wall, swirling his drink. \u0026quot;I never thought I\u0027d see the day. Lucius Malfoy is fascinated by a biro.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He stole my dad\u0027s thunder,\u0026quot; Ron grumbled, watching Lucius click the pen repeatedly near his ear. \u0026quot;Dad\u0027s been obsessing over pens for years. Now Malfoy thinks he discovered them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the stapler that’s going to break him,\u0026quot; Draco said, taking a sip of wine. He looked at his father with a pained expression. \u0026quot;If Vernon shows him a hole-puncher, I think my father might actually faint. He loves organized bureaucracy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Look at Mum,\u0026quot; Ginny giggled, pointing to the sofa. \u0026quot;She’s taking notes from Petunia. I think they’re discussing bleach.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bleach is dangerous stuff,\u0026quot; Hermione noted. \u0026quot;Though probably safer than half the potions Mrs. Weasley uses.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I like the new Mrs. D,\u0026quot; George said, watching Chloe chat happily with Luna about Nargles (Chloe thought they were a type of dog). \u0026quot;She fits right in.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Dudley,\u0026quot; Fred added, pointing to where Dudley was arm-wrestling Charlie Weasley on a side table (and winning). \u0026quot;Look at the size of him. He’s like a human Bludger.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at the room. He saw his cousin laughing with a dragon tamer. He saw his aunt teaching a pureblood aristocrat about cleaning. He saw his uncle explaining office supplies to a former Death Eater.","He felt Hermione slip her hand into his.","\u0026quot;It’s weird, isn\u0027t it?\u0026quot; she whispered.","\u0026quot;It’s mad,\u0026quot; Harry agreed.","\u0026quot;It’s perfect,\u0026quot; Ron said, grabbing a canapé.","\u0026quot;Cheers to that,\u0026quot; Draco said, raising his glass. \u0026quot;To the madness.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the madness,\u0026quot; they all echoed, watching their families collide and blend in the most unexpected, wonderful way possible."]},{"num":75,"origNum":75,"title":"The Feast of Two Worlds","wordCount":749,"paragraphs":["The dining table at Malfoy Manor groaned under the weight of a feast that seemed determined to bridge the cultural divide through the universal language of calories.","Dobby, orchestrating a team of house-elves from the sidelines, had outdone himself. He had clearly taken his new \u0026quot;consultant\u0026quot; role seriously, blending Malfoy extravagance with the hearty comfort food Harry and the Weasleys loved.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Menu\u003c/strong\u003e","At the center of the table sat a magnificent Roast Boar, glazed in honey and pomegranate, surrounded by a ring of crackling that Vernon Dursley eyed with something approaching religious devotion. Flanking the boar were silver platters of Beef Wellington, the pastry golden and flaky, and a mountain of Yorkshire puddings that defied gravity.","\u0026quot;It’s a structural marvel,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley commented, poking a Yorkshire pudding. \u0026quot;How does it stay so airy?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Magic, Arthur,\u0026quot; Molly whispered, though she was busy inspecting the consistency of the truffled mash potatoes.","There were bowls of Roasted Root Vegetables glistening with thyme butter, a tureen of Bouillabaisse that Fleur declared \u0026quot;acceptable\u0026quot; (which was high praise), and a peculiar dish of Mushy Peas that Lucius had ordered specifically for the Dursleys, though he looked at the green paste with deep suspicion.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Libations\u003c/strong\u003e","The drinks were flowing as freely as the conversation.","Lucius had opened the deep cellar. Crystal goblets refilled themselves with a 1912 Elf-Made Pinot Noir that tasted like blackberries and velvet. For the toast, he produced a bottle of Madame Rosmerta’s Oak-Matured Mead, but the \u003cem\u003epièce de résistance\u003c/em\u003e was reserved for Vernon.","\u0026quot;Dobby,\u0026quot; Lucius instructed with a flick of his hand.","The elf trotted forward holding a bottle of dusty, amber liquid.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Lucius said to Vernon, \u0026quot;is a bottle of 50-year-old Firewhisky. However, I am told you prefer... Brandy?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do enjoy a drop,\u0026quot; Vernon admitted, loosening his belt a notch.","\u0026quot;This was a gift from the French Minister,\u0026quot; Lucius explained. \u0026quot;It is infused with the essence of sun-dried plums. It does not burn; it warms.\u0026quot;","Vernon took a sip. His eyes widened. \u0026quot;Smooth. Very smooth. You know, Lucius, you might have a future in the import-export business.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I shall add it to my portfolio,\u0026quot; Lucius inclined his head.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Atmosphere\u003c/strong\u003e","As the main course was cleared and dessert appeared—a Treacle Tart for Harry, a tower of Eclairs for the French contingent, and a dense Fruitcake for the brave—the room was filled with a contented, sleepy hum.","Draco and Ginny were sharing a plate of strawberries, whispering and laughing. Ron was debating the merits of Cannons vs. Harpies with Dudley, who was surprisingly knowledgeable about \u0026quot;The Keepers\u0026quot; (he meant Goalkeepers, but Ron knew what he meant). Hermione and Narcissa were discussing the merits of magical preservation versus Muggle museums.","Harry sat back, nursing his mead. He looked at his uncle, whose face was flushed with brandy and good beef. He looked at his aunt, who was exchanging knitting patterns with Molly.","It was perfect. It was the \u0026quot;Happily Ever After\u0026quot; he hadn\u0027t dared to dream of during the darkest, coldest nights of the war.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Interruption\u003c/strong\u003e","The clock on the mantelpiece chimed ten.","Slowly, the laughter died down as Lucius Malfoy pushed back his heavy oak chair. The scrape of wood against the floor was loud in the sudden quiet.","Lucius stood up. He picked up a silver spoon and tapped it gently against his crystal goblet. \u003cem\u003eDing. Ding. Ding.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;If I could have your attention,\u0026quot; Lucius said.","His voice was devoid of the warmth that had filled the dinner. His face had settled into a mask of severe, aristocratic seriousness. The lines around his mouth tightened.","Vernon stopped chewing. Molly lowered her fork. Harry sat up straighter, his Auror instincts flaring. Draco frowned, looking at his father with concern.","\u0026quot;The dinner has been... adequate,\u0026quot; Lucius began, his grey eyes sweeping the room, lingering on Arthur, then Vernon, and finally Harry. \u0026quot;But we are not merely here to eat and discuss... staplers.\u0026quot;","He gripped the head of his cane with both hands.","\u0026quot;There is a serious matter we must discuss,\u0026quot; Lucius announced, his voice dropping an octave. \u0026quot;A matter of grave importance that concerns the future of our families. I have delayed it long enough.\u0026quot;","He looked at Draco, then at Ginny.","\u0026quot;It concerns the bloodlines,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered ominously.","The room went cold. Ron reached for his wand under the table. Vernon looked confused but alarmed. Harry narrowed his eyes.","Lucius took a deep breath, looking grim.","\u0026quot;I need to know,\u0026quot; Lucius said, staring directly at Arthur Weasley."]},{"num":76,"origNum":76,"title":"The Ultimatum of the Rings","wordCount":931,"paragraphs":["The silence stretched tight across the dining table. Lucius Malfoy stood like a judge delivering a verdict, his grey eyes locked onto Arthur Weasley.","\u0026quot;I need to know,\u0026quot; Lucius repeated, his voice heavy with gravitas. \u0026quot; regarding the... continuity of our houses.\u0026quot;","Harry’s hand drifted toward his wand. Ron stopped chewing his éclair. Molly held her breath.","\u0026quot;We have broken bread,\u0026quot; Lucius intoned. \u0026quot;We have shared wine. We have... embraced.\u0026quot; He shuddered slightly at the memory. \u0026quot;But there is a matter of propriety. A matter of \u003cem\u003ecommitment\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Lucius slammed his hand on the table (gently, so as not to break the crystal).","\u0026quot;When, precisely,\u0026quot; Lucius demanded, \u0026quot;are these children going to get married?\u0026quot;","The tension in the room didn\u0027t just break; it evaporated into a cloud of bewildered relief from the older generation and sheer panic from the younger.","\u0026quot;Oh, thank Morgana!\u0026quot; Molly Weasley exhaled, clutching her chest. \u0026quot;I thought you were going to say the Dark Lord had a secret brother!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Married?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley perked up, adjusting his glasses. \u0026quot;Yes! excellent point, Lucius! It has been... five years? Six?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Seven,\u0026quot; Narcissa corrected, sipping her wine with a serene smile. \u0026quot;And I have already picked out the floral arrangements for a winter ceremony. White roses and silver ribbons.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I was thinking summer,\u0026quot; Molly countered instantly, her eyes gleaming with matrimonial strategy. \u0026quot;The orchard. Gold and red. Very rustic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We can negotiate the season,\u0026quot; Narcissa conceded graciously.","Vernon Dursley wiped his mouth with a napkin, nodding vigorously. \u0026quot;Here, here! It’s about time. Tax brackets, Harry! Joint assets! Stability! You can’t go running around playing cops and robbers forever without a solid domestic infrastructure!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And grandchildren,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, her eyes misty. \u0026quot;I want to knit booties.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Defendants\u003c/strong\u003e","While the parents launched into a unified front of aggressive planning, the six young adults sitting at the table looked like they had been hit with a mass Stunning Spell.","Draco Malfoy choked on his wine. He coughed, his face turning pink, while Ginny thumped him hard on the back.","\u0026quot;Father!\u0026quot; Draco wheezed. \u0026quot;Are you... are you proposing on my behalf? In front of the Weasleys? In front of \u003cem\u003ePotter\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Someone has to,\u0026quot; Lucius sniffed. \u0026quot;You are moving at a glacial pace, Draco. At this rate, the Malfoy line will end with you and a houseful of cats.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are busy!\u0026quot; Ginny protested, her face matching her hair. \u0026quot;I have a Quidditch career! Draco has... international relations!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You can relate internationally while wearing a ring,\u0026quot; Lucius countered smoothly.","Harry sank low in his chair, trying to hide behind a centerpiece of lilies.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t look at me,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Hermione. \u0026quot;I’m invisible. I’m an Ostrich.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Harry James Potter,\u0026quot; Hermione hissed, her cheeks burning. \u0026quot;If you try to hide in your own shirt right now, I will hex you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But look at them!\u0026quot; Harry gestured to Vernon and Arthur, who were now discussing the cost of marquee rentals. \u0026quot;They’re organizing! It’s a pincer movement!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s efficient!\u0026quot; Vernon roared from across the table. \u0026quot;Economy of scale! Three weddings! One supplier! Think of the discount!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Three?\u0026quot; Ron squeaked.","He looked at Luna. Luna was currently making a necklace out of prawn tails on her plate, humming softly.","\u0026quot;Luna,\u0026quot; Ron whispered frantically. \u0026quot;They’re talking about... you know. Us.\u0026quot;","Luna looked up, her large, protuberant eyes dreamy. \u0026quot;Oh, I know, Ronald. Daddy has already written the ceremony. He wants us to be bound by a golden thread under the light of a Crumple-Horned Snorkack moon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A what moon?\u0026quot; Ron asked, terrified.","\u0026quot;It’s very rare,\u0026quot; Luna smiled. \u0026quot;We might have to wait a few decades. Or we could just do it next Tuesday.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Tuesday?\u0026quot; Ron’s voice cracked.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Pressure Cooker\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Now, see here,\u0026quot; Vernon said, pulling a notebook from his pocket (he always carried one). \u0026quot;Harry. You’re the eldest. You go first. Set the example.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I... I...\u0026quot; Harry stammered. He looked at Hermione.","Hermione looked at him. The panic in her eyes slowly faded, replaced by something softer. She reached under the table and squeezed his hand.","\u0026quot;We’re not in a rush,\u0026quot; Hermione said firmly to the room. \u0026quot;We are focusing on our careers.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Rubbish,\u0026quot; Petunia sniffed. \u0026quot;You can have a career and a husband. I managed a house and a garden and Vernon. And Vernon is a full-time job.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am a demanding enterprise,\u0026quot; Vernon agreed proudly.","\u0026quot;And you, Draco,\u0026quot; Narcissa turned her gaze on her son. \u0026quot;The Manor is large. It is empty. It needs life.\u0026quot;","Draco looked at Ginny. He saw the fire in her eyes, the way she challenged him, the way she loved him. He thought of the ring he had hidden in his sock drawer for six months, terrified to ask because he wasn\u0027t sure if a Weasley would ever truly want to be a Malfoy legally.","\u0026quot;Mother,\u0026quot; Draco said quietly. \u0026quot;Ginny and I... we’ll do it when we’re ready. Not because you want a party.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t want a party,\u0026quot; Lucius said gravely. \u0026quot;I want the guest list settled before the Minister changes again. Politics, Draco.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, honestly!\u0026quot; Molly threw her hands up. \u0026quot;Arthur, get the calendar. We’re picking dates. If we leave it to them, they’ll elope.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Eloping sounds fantastic,\u0026quot; Ron muttered.","\u0026quot;No eloping!\u0026quot; Fleur shouted. \u0026quot;I need to design ze dresses! I ‘ave visions! Silk! Lace! Feathers!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No feathers,\u0026quot; Harry and Draco said in unison.","The table dissolved into chaos again—Molly and Narcissa debating flowers, Vernon and Arthur debating costs, Fleur sketching on a napkin, and the six \u0026quot;children\u0026quot; drinking wine rapidly, realizing that their peaceful, unmarried existence was under siege by the most formidable force in the universe:","Their parents, united."]},{"num":77,"origNum":77,"title":"The September Ultimatum","wordCount":798,"paragraphs":["The chaos of the \u0026quot;Marriage Summit\u0026quot; was reaching a fever pitch. Molly Weasley was threatening to knit wedding favors immediately. Lucius was muttering about pre-nuptial binding contracts. Vernon was drawing a timeline on a napkin.","Narcissa Malfoy, who had been watching the pandemonium with the cool detachment of a woman who had hosted the Dark Lord in her living room and survived, finally decided that order must be restored.","She didn\u0027t shout. She didn\u0027t bang the table. She simply stood up.","The rustle of her silk robes was quiet, but the command radiating from her was absolute.","\u0026quot;Quiet,\u0026quot; Narcissa said softly.","The room fell silent instantly. Even Vernon stopped clicking his pen.","\u0026quot;We are going in circles,\u0026quot; Narcissa stated, her voice crisp. \u0026quot;Suggestions are lovely, but what we require is a schedule.\u0026quot;","She looked at the calendar hanging on the wall (a wizarding one, where the days waved at you).","\u0026quot;September 1st,\u0026quot; Narcissa announced.","She turned to the table, fixing the six young adults with a steel gaze.","\u0026quot;That is ten months from today. It avoids the winter gloom. It avoids the heat of mid-summer. And it provides ample time for tailoring, venue preparation, and...\u0026quot; she looked at Lucius, \u0026quot;...mental preparation.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;September 1st?\u0026quot; Harry asked weakly. \u0026quot;But that\u0027s... that\u0027s the day the Hogwarts Express leaves.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Narcissa smiled, a terrifyingly benevolent expression. \u0026quot;A day of new beginnings. A day of departures. A day of... \u003cem\u003ecommitment\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parental Ratification\u003c/strong\u003e","The parents exchanged looks. A silent, telepathic vote was cast across the table.","\u0026quot;September,\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley mused, tapping his chin. \u0026quot;End of the fiscal quarter. Good for tax planning. The weather is stable. I like it. Efficient.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It gives me enough time to bake three ceremonial cakes,\u0026quot; Molly calculated, counting on her fingers. \u0026quot;And the gnomes will be hibernating, so the garden will be clear. Agreed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can have the peacocks molted and groomed by then,\u0026quot; Lucius noted, checking his pocket watch. \u0026quot;And the Ministry usually breaks for session. We can secure the Minister’s attendance.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the flowers,\u0026quot; Petunia sighed happily. \u0026quot;Late summer roses. Asters. It will be lovely.\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley raised his glass. \u0026quot;Motion carried! The date is set!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Surrender\u003c/strong\u003e","The focus shifted to the \u0026quot;children.\u0026quot; They sat there, trapped between the immovable object of their parents\u0027 love and the unstoppable force of their parents\u0027 organizational skills.","\u0026quot;Ten months?\u0026quot; Ron squeaked. \u0026quot;That’s... that’s not very long.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is three hundred days, Ronald,\u0026quot; Hermione corrected automatically, her face pale. \u0026quot;It is plenty of time to organize a wedding. Logistically.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But emotionally?\u0026quot; Ron whispered.","\u0026quot;Draco?\u0026quot; Lucius prompted, his eyebrow raised. \u0026quot;Do you have a conflict? A diplomatic mission? A hair appointment?\u0026quot;","Draco looked at Ginny. Ginny looked at Draco. They realized, with dawning horror, that they weren\u0027t getting out of this room without a date.","\u0026quot;September 1st is... fine,\u0026quot; Draco managed to say, gripping his wine glass. \u0026quot;As long as I don\u0027t have to wear ruffles.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No ruffles,\u0026quot; Narcissa promised. \u0026quot;Ginny?\u0026quot;","Ginny looked at her mother, who was already mentally measuring her for a dress. She looked at her father, who was beaming. She looked at Draco.","\u0026quot;Fine,\u0026quot; Ginny sighed, surrendering to the tide. \u0026quot;September 1st. But if anyone tries to make me release doves, I will hex them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Noted,\u0026quot; Lucius said gravely. \u0026quot;Harry? Hermione?\u0026quot;","Harry looked at Vernon. Vernon gave him a thumbs-up. Harry looked at Petunia, who was crying happy tears again.","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, squeezing Hermione’s hand. \u0026quot;Why not? We’ve waited long enough.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;September 1st,\u0026quot; Hermione agreed, a small smile touching her lips. \u0026quot;It’s a good date.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Luna? Ron?\u0026quot; Molly asked, turning the spotlight on her youngest son.","Luna hummed, looking at the ceiling. \u0026quot;Daddy says September is a good month for binding souls. The Wrackspurts are less active.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If the Wrackspurts are okay with it, I\u0027m okay with it,\u0026quot; Ron gulped.","Narcissa clapped her hands together once. \u0026quot;Excellent. It is decided. Dobby!\u0026quot;","The elf appeared at her elbow. \u0026quot;Mistress Cissy?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bring the champagne,\u0026quot; Narcissa ordered. \u0026quot;The vintage stuff. We have three weddings to plan.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And bring a notepad,\u0026quot; Vernon added, clicking his pen. \u0026quot;We need to make a list. Lucius, do you have a projector? I have a slide deck on \u0027Event Management\u0027 in the car.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do not know what a slide deck is,\u0026quot; Lucius said, looking excited, \u0026quot;but I am eager to learn.\u0026quot;","As the parents dove into a frenzy of planning, clinking glasses and comparing schedules, Harry leaned back in his chair. He looked at his friends—terrified, engaged, and together.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Draco. \u0026quot;At least we have ten months.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ten months to plan an escape?\u0026quot; Draco whispered back.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;Ten months to figure out how to stop Vernon and Lucius from starting a business together.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re doomed,\u0026quot; Draco groaned, clinking his glass against Harry\u0027s.","\u0026quot;Cheers,\u0026quot; Harry laughed. \u0026quot;To September.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":78,"origNum":78,"title":"The Hurricane and the Ring","wordCount":1046,"paragraphs":["It was a freezing Tuesday evening in November. The floodlights of the Holyhead Harpies’ training stadium hummed against the encroaching darkness, illuminating the empty stands and the muddy pitch below.","Draco Malfoy stood near the changing room tunnel, shivering in his impeccable cashmere coat. He checked his pocket watch for the tenth time in two minutes. He checked the pocket of his trousers for the fifteenth time. The small velvet box was still there, burning a hole against his thigh.","\u0026quot;Two months,\u0026quot; Draco muttered to himself, his breath misting in the cold air. \u0026quot;Two months of Mother sending me fabric swatches. Two months of Father asking if I\u0027ve \u0027secured the asset\u0027. I cannot take another week of aggressive floral planning.\u0026quot;","A whistle blew from the air.","Draco looked up. A blur of green and gold plummeted from the sky. Ginny Weasley, hair flying like a banner behind her, pulled her broom out of a terrifying dive just inches above the grass. She dismounted while the broom was still moving, skidding to a halt in the mud.","She was covered in grime. Her Quidditch robes were torn at the shoulder. There was a smear of blood on her cheek. She looked wild, dangerous, and absolutely magnificent.","Draco felt his heart do that traitorous flip it always did when he saw her.","\u0026quot;Malfoy!\u0026quot; Ginny shouted, jogging over, her broom over her shoulder. \u0026quot;You came! Did you see that Wronski Feint? I nearly made the Keeper vomit!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I saw it,\u0026quot; Draco said, handing her a towel he had brought. \u0026quot;I also saw you nearly decapitate yourself on the goal hoop. Do you have a death wish, Weasley, or do you just enjoy raising my blood pressure?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Risk adds flavor, remember?\u0026quot; Ginny grinned, wiping the mud from her face. She stopped, looking at him. \u0026quot;You look fancy. Why are you wearing the \u0027Ministry Negotiation\u0027 coat?\u0026quot;","Draco straightened his collar. He felt sweating despite the freezing wind. This was it. He had rehearsed a speech. He had planned to take her to a nice restaurant in Paris. He had planned champagne.","But looking at her now—fierce, muddy, and smelling of broomstick polish and rain—he realized a restaurant was wrong. That wasn\u0027t them. \u003cem\u003eThey\u003c/em\u003e were the Hurricane. \u003cem\u003eThey\u003c/em\u003e were the dented armor and the ice water.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m wearing the coat,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice tight, \u0026quot;because I have a negotiation to close.\u0026quot;","Ginny raised an eyebrow. \u0026quot;Oh? Are you trading goblin securities again?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Draco said. He stepped forward, ignoring the mud on her boots that was threatening his Italian leather shoes. \u0026quot;I am negotiating a merger. A permanent one.\u0026quot;","Ginny paused, the towel lowered. She searched his face. The banter faded from her eyes, replaced by a sudden, intense awareness.","\u0026quot;Draco?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My mother has booked the florist,\u0026quot; Draco said rapidly, losing his cool. \u0026quot;My father is currently arguing with your father about the structural integrity of a marquee. The date is set. The train is leaving the station.\u0026quot;","He took a step closer, invading her personal space, just like she used to invade his in the library.","\u0026quot;But I don\u0027t want to do this because of a deadline,\u0026quot; Draco said, his grey eyes locking onto hers. \u0026quot;And I don\u0027t want to do it because our parents have formed a terrifying coalition government.\u0026quot;","He reached into his pocket. He didn\u0027t go down on one knee. The ground was muddy, yes, but mostly, kneeling felt too submissive for them. They were equals. They stood eye-to-eye.","He pulled out the box and snapped it open.","Inside sat a ring that was distinctly un-Malfoy. It wasn\u0027t a heavy, gaudy emerald. It was a band of goblin-wrought silver, delicate but unbreakable, set with a diamond that blazed with an inner fire—and wrapped around the diamond was a tiny, intricate snake made of rubies. The Serpent and the Lion.","Ginny gasped. Her hand flew to her mouth.","\u0026quot;I want to do this,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, \u0026quot;because you are the only person on this earth who makes me feel alive. You’re the only one who yells at me when I’m being an idiot. You’re the fire, Ginny. And I’m tired of being cold.\u0026quot;","He took a breath, his composure cracking.","\u0026quot;Marry me, Red. Let’s terrify our families together.\u0026quot;","Ginny stared at the ring. She stared at Draco—the boy who had been her enemy, the boy who had been broken, the man who was standing in the mud asking for her forever.","She didn\u0027t say yes.","She dropped her broom. She dropped the towel.","And then, she launched herself at him.","It was a tackle worthy of a Beater. She slammed into him, wrapping her legs around his waist and her arms around his neck.","\u0026quot;OOF!\u0026quot; Draco grunted as the air left his lungs.","He staggered back, his expensive shoes slipping in the mud. He tried to keep his balance, but the force of the Weasley affection was too strong.","\u003cem\u003eSPLAT.\u003c/em\u003e","They went down.","Draco landed flat on his back in the cold, wet mud of the pitch. Ginny landed on top of him, straddling his chest, pinning him to the ground.","She wasn\u0027t crying. She was beaming—a smile so bright it outshone the stadium lights.","\u0026quot;Yes!\u0026quot; she shouted, inches from his face. \u0026quot;Yes, you idiot! Yes!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re getting mud on the coat,\u0026quot; Draco wheezed, staring up at her, a ecstatic grin breaking across his face.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t care about the coat!\u0026quot; Ginny yelled. She grabbed the ring from the box, which was still clutched in Draco’s muddy hand, and shoved it onto her finger. It fit perfectly.","\u0026quot;It’s mine now,\u0026quot; she declared. \u0026quot;And so are you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I gathered that,\u0026quot; Draco laughed, reaching up to cup her face, not caring that his hands were filthy.","She leaned down and kissed him—hard, messy, and triumphant. It was a kiss that tasted of rain and victory.","\u0026quot;Get up,\u0026quot; Ginny commanded, pulling back. \u0026quot;We have to go tell them. Mum is going to scream. Your dad might actually faint.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Let\u0027s stay here a minute,\u0026quot; Draco murmured, pulling her back down. \u0026quot;I\u0027m already ruined. Might as well enjoy the view.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hurricane Malfoy,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered against his lips.","\u0026quot;Future Malfoy,\u0026quot; Draco corrected.","And there, lying in the mud of the Quidditch pitch, under the glare of the floodlights, the Serpent finally, permanently, caught the Lioness."]},{"num":79,"origNum":79,"title":"Code Black","wordCount":844,"paragraphs":["The Inter-Departmental memo that flew into Draco Malfoy’s office on Level Five was not the usual pale violet of diplomatic correspondence. It was black. It was smoking. And it was screaming.","\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eURGENT. OFFICE OF THE HEAD AUROR. CODE BLACK. IMMEDIATELY.\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026quot;","Draco didn\u0027t hesitate. He dropped his quill, ignoring the goblin delegation he was in the middle of negotiating a trade tariff with.","\u0026quot;Apologies,\u0026quot; Draco barked, grabbing his wand and his coat. \u0026quot;National security.\u0026quot;","He sprinted to the lifts. \u0026quot;Code Black\u0026quot; was the highest threat level. It meant an Azkaban breakout. It meant a new Dark Lord. It meant Harry Potter was in mortal peril.","Draco burst onto Level Two, ignoring the startled receptionist. He sprinted down the corridor, his dragon-hide boots skidding on the polished floor. He reached the heavy oak door at the end of the hall marked \u003cstrong\u003eHEAD AUROR\u003c/strong\u003e.","He didn\u0027t knock. He kicked the door open, his wand raised, a curse on his lips.","\u0026quot;Potter! I’ve got your back! Where are they? Who’s attacking—\u0026quot;","Draco stopped.","The office was not a war zone. There were no duelling Death Eaters. There was no fiendfyre.","Harry Potter was sitting behind his desk. He was uninjured. However, he looked like a man who had just gone ten rounds with a Hungarian Horntail and lost. His head was in his hands, his hair was standing up in tufts where he had clearly been pulling at it, and he was surrounded by piles of glossy brochures.","Harry looked up as Draco burst in. His green eyes were wild and desperate.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re here,\u0026quot; Harry croaked. \u0026quot;Thank god.\u0026quot;","Draco lowered his wand slowly. He checked the corners of the room. Nothing.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice dangerously low. \u0026quot;You sent a Code Black. I left a Goblin Ambassador mid-sentence. I thought you were dying.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am dying,\u0026quot; Harry groaned, slumping forward until his forehead hit the desk with a thud. \u0026quot;I’m dead. Narcissa is going to kill me. Hermione is going to leave me. And Vernon is going to take back the discount on the car.\u0026quot;","Draco holstered his wand. He walked over to the desk and picked up one of the brochures. It wasn\u0027t a dossier on dark wizards. It was a catalogue for \u003cem\u003eTwilfitt and Tattings: Fine Jewelry\u003c/em\u003e.","Draco stared at it. He looked at Harry.","\u0026quot;A ring,\u0026quot; Draco stated flatly.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t have one,\u0026quot; Harry mumbled into the wood of his desk. \u0026quot;It’s February, Draco. The wedding is in September. I haven\u0027t proposed. I don\u0027t have a ring. I went to a shop yesterday, and the man started talking about \u0027clarity\u0027 and \u0027cuts\u0027 and \u0027settings\u0027, and I panicked and bought a watch instead.\u0026quot;","He lifted his head, looking at Draco with sheer panic.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t know what to do. If I get her the wrong thing... she wears it forever, Draco. Forever. If it’s ugly, she’ll hate it, but she’s too polite to say so, and every time she looks at her hand she’ll think, \u0027Harry is an idiot\u0027.\u0026quot;","Draco stared at the Savior of the Wizarding World. The man who had defeated Voldemort. The man who was currently being defeated by the concept of jewelry shopping.","Draco pinched the bridge of his nose. He let out a long, suffering sigh.","\u0026quot;Absolute incompetence,\u0026quot; Draco declared.","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Harry whimpered.","\u0026quot;You are the Head Auror,\u0026quot; Draco lectured, pacing the office. \u0026quot;You organize global manhunts. And yet, you cannot secure a piece of carbon for the woman you have been practically married to since you were eleven?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s too much pressure!\u0026quot; Harry argued. \u0026quot;Ginny’s ring is perfect. You set the bar too high! The snake? The ruby? It was genius! How do I top that?\u0026quot;","Draco stopped pacing. He preened slightly, adjusting his cuffs. \u0026quot;It was rather good, wasn\u0027t it? Custom design. Goblin-wrought.\u0026quot;","He looked at Harry, who was looking at him with the eyes of a lost puppy.","\u0026quot;Help me,\u0026quot; Harry pleaded. \u0026quot;Please. You have taste. You know about... shiny things. If I do this alone, I’ll end up buying something with a snitch on it.\u0026quot;","Draco shuddered visibly. \u0026quot;A snitch. Merlin’s beard, Potter, you really are a danger to yourself.\u0026quot;","Draco walked to the coat rack. He grabbed Harry’s cloak and threw it at him.","\u0026quot;Get up,\u0026quot; Draco commanded.","\u0026quot;Where are we going?\u0026quot; Harry asked, catching the cloak.","\u0026quot;We are going to a private jeweler in Paris,\u0026quot; Draco announced, checking his watch. \u0026quot;He owes the Malfoy family a favor. We are going to find a stone that is worthy of the brightest witch of the age. Something classic. Something intelligent. And absolutely nothing with a snitch on it.\u0026quot;","Harry scrambled up, relief washing over him. \u0026quot;Paris? Now?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Draco said, opening the door. \u0026quot;Code Black, remember? This is a national emergency. If Granger doesn\u0027t get a ring by the end of the week, my mother will personally come down here and transfigure you into an ottoman.\u0026quot;","Harry grabbed his wand. \u0026quot;You\u0027re a lifesaver, Malfoy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Draco smirked, leading the way to the lifts. \u0026quot;Try to keep up, Potter. We have a deadline.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":80,"origNum":80,"title":"The Diamond and the Debt","wordCount":1032,"paragraphs":["The shop, \u003cem\u003eL\u0027Atelier des Étoiles\u003c/em\u003e, was hidden down a side street in magical Paris that didn\u0027t appear on any map. The interior was lined with black velvet and lit by floating orbs of soft, white light. There were no display cases; just a single, polished ebony table.","Harry Potter stood before the table, sweating in his Auror robes.","\u0026quot;There are no numbers,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Draco, staring at the small velvet tray the jeweler, a man named Monsieur Delacour (a distant cousin of Fleur’s), had placed before them. \u0026quot;Draco, there are no little tickets with galleon signs. How do I know if I can afford it? Do I need to sell the Firebolt?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco sighed, adjusting his cufflinks. \u0026quot;If you have to ask the price, you are in the wrong shop. But don\u0027t worry. You are the Chosen One. I imagine you have a discount.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at the rings. They were spectacular. Rubies the size of quail eggs. Emeralds that looked like frozen forests. But none of them felt like \u003cem\u003eHermione\u003c/em\u003e. They were too loud. Too flashy.","\u0026quot;She doesn\u0027t like big things,\u0026quot; Harry muttered. \u0026quot;She likes... books. And logic. And warm jumpers.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are not buying her a jumper, Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said. He looked at the jeweler. \u0026quot;Show us the \u0027Lumière\u0027 collection. The cuts that focus on clarity, not size.\u0026quot;","The jeweler nodded and brought out a new tray.","Harry’s eyes scanned the row. And then, they stopped.","It sat in the center. It wasn\u0027t a massive rock. It was a diamond, cut in a perfect square (an Asscher cut, Draco informed him), set on a simple, delicate band of platinum that twisted slightly, like a vine. It didn\u0027t sparkle aggressively; it glowed. It looked clean, sharp, and unbreakable.","\u0026quot;That one,\u0026quot; Harry said, pointing.","Draco leaned in. He pulled out a jeweler’s loupe (he apparently carried one) and inspected the stone.","\u0026quot;Flawless,\u0026quot; Draco murmured. \u0026quot;Geometric perfection. It’s rigorous. It’s brilliant. It’s... Granger.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s beautiful,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;Monsieur,\u0026quot; Harry said to the jeweler, pulling out his Gringotts money pouch. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll take it. How much?\u0026quot;","The jeweler smiled, closing the box with a satisfying snap. He placed it in a bag made of white silk.","\u0026quot;The bill has been settled, Monsieur Potter.\u0026quot;","Harry froze, his hand halfway into his pouch. \u0026quot;What? By who?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;By Monsieur Malfoy,\u0026quot; the jeweler said, bowing to Draco. \u0026quot;The transaction was completed upon selection.\u0026quot;","Harry spun around. Draco was examining his fingernails, looking bored.","\u0026quot;Malfoy,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice rising. \u0026quot;You didn\u0027t.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I did,\u0026quot; Draco drawled. \u0026quot;Consider it a finder\u0027s fee. Or a dowry. Or simply insurance that you won\u0027t back out.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a diamond ring, Draco! It must cost thousands!\u0026quot; Harry argued. \u0026quot;I have gold! My parents left me money! Sirius left me money!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And my parents left me a Manor and a lot of guilt,\u0026quot; Draco cut him off, his voice losing its drawl. He looked at Harry, his grey eyes serious. \u0026quot;You saved my life, Harry. You saved me from the fire. You saved my soul in that bathroom. You saved my family from Azkaban.\u0026quot;","Draco stepped closer, picking up the silk bag and shoving it into Harry’s chest.","\u0026quot;Let me buy the damn ring, Potter. Let me do this one good thing.\u0026quot;","Harry stared at him. He saw the vulnerability behind the arrogance. He saw the boy who had no choice, finally making one.","Harry didn\u0027t argue. He didn\u0027t offer to pay him back.","Instead, he stepped forward and wrapped his arms around Draco Malfoy in a tight, brotherly hug.","Draco stiffened for a second—old habits dying hard—but then, he relaxed. He patted Harry’s back, awkwardly but firmly.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re getting emotional again,\u0026quot; Draco muttered into Harry’s shoulder. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t ruin the suit.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shut up, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, pulling back and wiping his eyes. \u0026quot;And thank you. Brother.\u0026quot;","Draco smirked, straightening his jacket. \u0026quot;Come on. We have a proposal to plan. And if you suggest hiding the ring in a cake, I will take it back.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe War Room\u003c/strong\u003e","Two hours later, they were back in London, in the living room of Harry and Ron’s flat (Ron was currently out with Luna). Ginny had been summoned via Floo Powder.","The three of them stood around the coffee table, which was covered in maps of Godric\u0027s Hollow.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Ginny said, looking at the ring box with misty eyes. \u0026quot;It’s perfect, Harry. She’s going to faint. But the location... it has to be right.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I was thinking the restaurant?\u0026quot; Harry suggested weakly.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Draco and Ginny said in unison.","\u0026quot;Godric\u0027s Hollow,\u0026quot; Harry said, tracing the map. \u0026quot;It’s where it started. It’s where my parents are. It’s where we went that Christmas... when we almost died.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Romantic,\u0026quot; Draco noted dryly.","\u0026quot;It is!\u0026quot; Harry insisted. \u0026quot;Because we survived. We walked out of there together. I want to ask her there because... because that’s where I realized I couldn\u0027t do it without her.\u0026quot;","Ginny smiled, squeezing Harry’s arm. \u0026quot;That’s beautiful, Harry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Draco said, pulling out a quill. \u0026quot; Logistics. We need snow. Is it snowing?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s March,\u0026quot; Harry said.","\u0026quot;I can fix that,\u0026quot; Draco noted. \u0026quot;Atmospheric Charms. We need soft, cinematic snow. Not a blizzard. We don\u0027t want her freezing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The churchyard?\u0026quot; Ginny suggested. \u0026quot;By the kissing gate?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Too morbid,\u0026quot; Harry shook his head. \u0026quot;Not by the graves.\u0026quot;","He pointed to a spot on the map—a small clearing near the center of the village, where the statue of his parents stood, but hidden by a row of trees.","\u0026quot;Here,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;It’s quiet. We can see the house where it happened, but we’re not \u003cem\u003ein\u003c/em\u003e the wreckage. It’s... looking forward, but remembering the past.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Perfect,\u0026quot; Ginny agreed. \u0026quot;I’ll get her there. I’ll tell her we’re visiting the graves for the anniversary of the Battle or something.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will handle the lighting,\u0026quot; Draco declared. \u0026quot;Candlelight. Floating. Lots of it. And I’ll have Dobby on standby with champagne. Not the cheap stuff.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at his friends—the Weasley and the Malfoy, plotting together to ensure his happiness. He touched the ring box in his pocket.","\u0026quot;Tomorrow,\u0026quot; Harry said, his heart pounding. \u0026quot;We do it tomorrow.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t drop the ring,\u0026quot; Draco warned.","\u0026quot;And don\u0027t do the Ostrich,\u0026quot; Ginny added.","\u0026quot;I promise,\u0026quot; Harry grinned."]},{"num":81,"origNum":81,"title":"Where It Began, Where It Begins","wordCount":891,"paragraphs":["The snow that Draco had promised began to fall just as they Apparated, dusting the cobblestones of Godric’s Hollow with a fresh, glittering coat of white.","It was quiet. The village slept under a blanket of winter silence, broken only by the distant chime of the church bell marking seven o\u0027clock.","Harry took Hermione’s hand. Her fingers were warm in his, her mittens a bright red against the monochrome night.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; she asked softly, looking around at the familiar, heart-aching scenery. \u0026quot;Why are we here? Is it... is it the anniversary?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice steady. \u0026quot;It’s not about the past today. Not entirely.\u0026quot;","He didn\u0027t lead her to the graveyard. He led her down the lane, past the pub, past the war memorial that flickered into the statue of his parents as they walked by. He didn\u0027t stop to look at James and Lily. He kept walking until they reached the end of the village, where the dark hedge grew wild and the gate stood rusted and slightly ajar.","The Potter Cottage.","It stood exactly as it had the night Voldemort destroyed it—the right side of the top floor blown apart, the ivy claiming the blackened stones. It was a monument to tragedy.","Hermione squeezed his hand tight. \u0026quot;Harry, are you sure you want to be here? It’s... it’s heavy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I used to hate this place,\u0026quot; Harry admitted, looking at the ruins. \u0026quot;I used to think of it as the place where my life ended before it even began. The place where I lost everything.\u0026quot;","He turned to face her. The snow caught in her eyelashes. The streetlight cast a soft, orange glow on her face. She looked worried, her brow furrowed in that way he loved because it meant she was thinking about \u003cem\u003ehim\u003c/em\u003e, worrying about \u003cem\u003ehim\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;But I was wrong,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;This isn\u0027t just where they died, Hermione. This is where I survived. This is where my mother’s love was strong enough to stop a Killing Curse.\u0026quot;","He reached up and tucked a stray curl of hair behind her ear.","\u0026quot;And ever since I left this house... I’ve been trying to find my way back home. I thought home was Hogwarts. Then I thought it was the Burrow. I even found it at Privet Drive in the end.\u0026quot;","Harry took a deep breath. The ring box in his pocket felt heavy, anchoring him to the earth.","\u0026quot;But I realized something this year. Home isn\u0027t a house. It isn\u0027t a castle or a cupboard.\u0026quot;","He stepped closer, invading her personal space, blocking out the sight of the ruined cottage behind him.","\u0026quot;Home is wherever you are, Hermione.\u0026quot;","Hermione’s breath hitched. Her eyes widened, shimmering with sudden tears. \u0026quot;Harry...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You stayed,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;When Ron left, you stayed. When the world fell apart, you stayed. When I walked into the forest... you were the last thing I saw before I closed my eyes. And you were the first thing I wanted to see when I came back.\u0026quot;","He let go of her hand. He took a step back.","And there, in the snow, in front of the house where he was born, Harry Potter knelt.","He didn\u0027t feel foolish. He didn\u0027t feel nervous anymore. He felt sure.","He pulled the white silk bag from his pocket. He took out the ring—the clean, geometric, flawless diamond that Draco had paid for, the one that glowed with an inner light like a captured star.","Hermione let out a small, strangled sob, her hands flying to her mouth.","\u0026quot;Hermione Jean Granger,\u0026quot; Harry said, looking up at her. \u0026quot;You are the smartest, bravest, most beautiful witch I know. You saved my life a hundred times, but more importantly... you gave me a life worth saving.\u0026quot;","The wind whispered through the ivy of the cottage, a soft, approving rustle.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t want to run anymore without you,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t want to be the Chosen One. I just want to be yours. Will you marry me?\u0026quot;","Hermione didn\u0027t answer immediately. She couldn\u0027t. She was crying, happy, silent tears that tracked down her cheeks.","She dropped to her knees in the snow, ignoring the cold, until she was eye-level with him.","\u0026quot;You idiot,\u0026quot; she choked out, laughing through the tears. \u0026quot;You wonderful, brilliant idiot. Of course.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes?\u0026quot; Harry asked, his heart soaring.","\u0026quot;Yes!\u0026quot; Hermione cried.","Harry took her hand—her trembling, cold hand—and slid the ring onto her finger. It fit perfectly. The platinum band seemed to warm against her skin, the diamond catching the light of the streetlamp and throwing rainbows across the snow.","Hermione looked at the ring, then at Harry.","She didn\u0027t do the Ostrich. She didn\u0027t hide.","She threw her arms around his neck and kissed him. It was a kiss that held the history of seven years—the library study sessions, the terrified flights on dragon-back, the quiet moments in the tent, and the loud, chaotic breakfasts with their families.","They held each other in the snow, kneeling in front of the ruins of the past, building a future that was entirely their own.","\u0026quot;I love you,\u0026quot; Harry whispered against her lips.","\u0026quot;I love you,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered back.","Above them, the clouds parted slightly, revealing a clear, bright moon. And for the first time in thirty years, the Potter Cottage didn\u0027t look like a grave. It looked like a beginning."]},{"num":82,"origNum":82,"title":"The Hat Trick","wordCount":957,"paragraphs":["The snow continued to fall softly over Godric’s Hollow, dusting the statue of James and Lily Potter in white. Under the shelter of the trees, Harry and Hermione stood locked in an embrace, the new diamond ring on Hermione’s finger catching the candlelight Draco had arranged.","\u0026quot;Ahem.\u0026quot;","Harry and Hermione broke apart, though Harry kept his arm firmly around her waist.","Emerging from the shadows of the churchyard gate were Draco Malfoy and Ginny Weasley. Ginny was beaming, her face flushed with the cold and excitement. Draco looked smug, adjusting his scarf with the air of a man who had successfully orchestrated a military coup.","\u0026quot;Finally,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, stepping into the clearing. \u0026quot;I was beginning to think we’d freeze to death waiting for you to ask the question, Potter. The Warming Charms were wearing off.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You were watching?\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, wiping a happy tear from her cheek.","\u0026quot;Security detail,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned, rushing forward to crush Hermione in a hug. \u0026quot;And lighting crew. Let me see it! Let me see!\u0026quot;","Hermione held out her hand. The platinum band twisted delicately, holding the flawless, geometric diamond. It glowed with a quiet, intense fire against the snowy backdrop.","\u0026quot;It’s perfect,\u0026quot; Ginny sighed. \u0026quot; absolutely perfect for you, Hermione.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It really is,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, looking at Harry. \u0026quot;How did you find it? It’s so... me.\u0026quot;","Harry laughed, rubbing the back of his neck. \u0026quot;I had a consultant. I almost bought a watch, Mione. Draco saved you from a lifetime of checking the time on your ring finger.\u0026quot;","Hermione turned to Draco. She didn\u0027t hug him—Draco still had limits—but she reached out and squeezed his hand.","\u0026quot;Thank you, Draco.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a public service, Granger,\u0026quot; Draco said, inspecting his fingernails. \u0026quot;I couldn\u0027t have the savior of the wizarding world proposing with a Cracker Jack prize. It would reflect poorly on the administration.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Ron Report\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Harry said, looking at the group. \u0026quot;That’s two down. We just need Ron to—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Actually,\u0026quot; Ginny interrupted, her grin widening. \u0026quot;We’re three for three.\u0026quot;","Harry and Hermione froze. \u0026quot;What?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I got an owl this morning,\u0026quot; Ginny laughed. \u0026quot;Ron beat you by twelve hours, Harry. He proposed to Luna yesterday.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He did?\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked. \u0026quot;How? Where?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In Sweden,\u0026quot; Draco supplied, looking amused. \u0026quot; apparently, they were tracking a... what was it? A Snorack?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Crumple-Horned Snorkack,\u0026quot; Ginny corrected. \u0026quot;Ron wrote to say they were hiking up a mountain. He found a pebble that looked like a heart—or a potato, Ron wasn\u0027t clear—and he just did it. He said he realized he didn\u0027t want to look for imaginary creatures with anyone else.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Luna?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;She said yes, obviously,\u0026quot; Ginny said. \u0026quot;Although, apparently, she asked if the ring was Nargle-proof first. Ron assured her it was.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Brilliant,\u0026quot; Harry exhaled, shaking his head. \u0026quot;Ron and Luna. You and Draco. Me and Hermione. We actually did it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Coalition will be pleased,\u0026quot; Draco noted dryly. \u0026quot;Father might actually stop hyperventilating about the lineage.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Plan\u003c/strong\u003e","They stood in the quiet village, the snow settling on their shoulders. They were engaged. The war was a memory. Their parents were united in a terrifying organizational force.","\u0026quot;We have to tell them,\u0026quot; Hermione said, looking at the ring. \u0026quot;We can\u0027t keep this secret. Narcissa has probably already sensed a disturbance in the force.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The deadline is September,\u0026quot; Harry reminded them. \u0026quot;We\u0027re way ahead of schedule. It\u0027s only March.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If we tell them now,\u0026quot; Draco calculated, \u0026quot;it gives my mother and Molly Weasley six months to plan three weddings. That might actually be enough time to prevent bloodshed over the color of the napkins.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Let\u0027s do it together,\u0026quot; Ginny suggested. \u0026quot;Rip the plaster off. All three couples. All the parents. One room.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Manor?\u0026quot; Harry suggested. \u0026quot;It has the biggest table.\u0026quot;","Draco sighed. \u0026quot;I suppose. Dobby will be thrilled. He loves a \u0027Big News\u0027 dinner.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Let\u0027s say Saturday,\u0026quot; Harry decided. \u0026quot;Two days from now. That gives Ron and Luna time to get back from Sweden.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll send the invites,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll make it sound official so Vernon brings his notepad.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eMalfoy Manor: The Calm Before\u003c/strong\u003e","Later that evening, Draco walked into the drawing room of Malfoy Manor. Lucius was reading the \u003cem\u003eProphet\u003c/em\u003e by the fire, and Narcissa was embroidering a handkerchief.","\u0026quot;Mother, Father,\u0026quot; Draco announced, pouring himself a drink.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; Lucius acknowledged without looking up. \u0026quot;How was your... excursion?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Productive,\u0026quot; Draco said, fighting a smile. \u0026quot;I have sent owls to the Weasleys and the Dursleys. We are hosting a dinner on Saturday.\u0026quot;","Lucius lowered the paper. He didn\u0027t look annoyed; he looked resigned.","\u0026quot;Again?\u0026quot; Lucius asked. \u0026quot;We just saw them last month. I haven\u0027t even finished reading the pamphlet Vernon gave me on \u0027Double-Entry Bookkeeping\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is important,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;We need to discuss... logistics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Logistics,\u0026quot; Narcissa perked up. \u0026quot;Is this regarding the September deadline?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In a manner of speaking,\u0026quot; Draco said smoothly. \u0026quot;Harry, Hermione, Ron, and Luna will be there as well.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Lucius sighed, folding his paper. \u0026quot;I shall tell Dobby to order more of that Muggle \u0027Cola\u0027. Vernon becomes irritable without it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the wine,\u0026quot; Draco added. \u0026quot;The good stuff, Father. The \u003cem\u003ereally\u003c/em\u003e good stuff. We might need it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Is there a crisis?\u0026quot; Narcissa asked sharply, sensing the undertone.","\u0026quot;No, Mother,\u0026quot; Draco smiled, touching the engagement ring hidden in his pocket—the twin to the one currently on Ginny\u0027s finger. \u0026quot;Just... a progress report. I think you\u0027ll find it satisfactory.\u0026quot;","Lucius grunted, picking up his pamphlet on bookkeeping. \u0026quot;As long as Arthur doesn\u0027t try to explain the \u0027internet\u0027 to me again. I still have a headache from the last time.\u0026quot;","Draco took a sip of his drink, hiding his grin. \u003cem\u003eJust wait until they hear about the triple wedding,\u003c/em\u003e he thought. \u003cem\u003eFather is going to need something stronger than Cola.\u003c/em\u003e"]},{"num":83,"origNum":83,"title":"The Ring Cycle","wordCount":1036,"paragraphs":["The dining room of Malfoy Manor was set for a summit. The crystal gleamed, the silverware was aligned with military precision, and Dobby was hovering in the corner, vibrating with the secret he had overheard but was forbidden to tell (he had taken to wearing three hats to contain his excitement).","The parents sat on one side of the long table: Lucius and Narcissa, Arthur and Molly, Vernon and Petunia. They looked like a coalition government preparing for a difficult budget meeting.","Opposite them sat the \u0026quot;children\u0026quot;: Harry and Hermione, Draco and Ginny, Ron and Luna. They sat in pairs, hands hidden under the table.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy began, pouring wine with a steady hand. \u0026quot;We are gathered. You mentioned a \u0027progress report\u0027 regarding the September deadline. I trust you have not encountered... obstacles?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Obstacles?\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley scoffed, opening his notebook. \u0026quot;Nonsense. Obstacles are just opportunities for management. I assume you\u0027ve secured the venues?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Actually,\u0026quot; Harry spoke up, his voice echoing slightly in the large room. \u0026quot;We haven\u0027t booked a venue yet.\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley’s face fell. \u0026quot;Harry, dear! September is six months away! The good orchards go fast!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We haven\u0027t booked a venue,\u0026quot; Harry continued, looking at Draco and Ron, \u0026quot;because we needed to confirm the... participants first.\u0026quot;","Draco cleared his throat. He looked at his father. He looked at Molly.","\u0026quot;We have an update,\u0026quot; Draco said smoothly. \u0026quot;Regarding the \u0027continuity of the houses\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, get on with it!\u0026quot; Ginny burst out.","She slammed her hand onto the table.","\u003cem\u003eCLACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The goblin-wrought silver ring with the ruby snake sparkled violently under the chandelier.","Lucius froze. Narcissa inhaled sharply.","Before the parents could process the Malfoy-Weasley confirmation, Hermione placed her hand on the table next to Ginny’s.","\u003cem\u003eCLINK.\u003c/em\u003e","The flawless, geometric diamond caught the light, glowing with cool, intellectual fire.","And finally, Luna Lovegood drifted her hand onto the table.","\u003cem\u003eTHUD.\u003c/em\u003e","Her ring was... unique. It appeared to be a rough, uncut moonstone wrapped in what looked like silver wire and—if one squinted—perhaps a bit of dried root. It was wild, strange, and perfectly Luna.","Three hands. Three rings. Three couples.","The silence that descended on the room was absolute.","Lucius Malfoy stared at the rings. He looked at Draco. He looked at Ginny. He looked at the ruby snake.","\u0026quot;Is that...\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, squinting. \u0026quot;Is that the 18th-century goblin setting? The one my grandfather hid from the Ministry?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Draco smirked. \u0026quot;I dug it out of the vault. It seemed appropriate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s... adequate,\u0026quot; Lucius choked out, though his eyes were shining. \u0026quot;More than adequate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And you!\u0026quot; Molly Weasley shrieked, jumping up and knocking her chair over. She pointed at Harry and Hermione. \u0026quot;You finally did it! Oh, thank heavens! I was going to lock you in a cupboard until you figured it out!\u0026quot;","She ran around the table, pulling Hermione into a hug that threatened to crush the Deputy Minister’s ribs.","\u0026quot;And Ron!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley beamed, looking at the moonstone. \u0026quot;That looks... homemade, son?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Ron said proudly, holding Luna’s hand. \u0026quot;Found the stone in Sweden. Wrapped it myself. Luna likes it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It keeps away the Nargles,\u0026quot; Luna confirmed dreamily.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Explosion\u003c/strong\u003e","The room dissolved into pandemonium.","Petunia was weeping over Harry, clutching his face. \u0026quot;She said yes! My Harry is getting married!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Of course she said yes,\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, clapping Harry on the back so hard Harry’s glasses slipped. \u0026quot;He bought a diamond you could see from space! Good investment, son! Solid asset!\u0026quot;","Vernon then turned to Lucius, his face purple with excitement.","\u0026quot;Lucius! Look at this! Three engagements! Announced simultaneously! Do you know what this means?\u0026quot;","Lucius, who was currently being hugged by a crying Molly Weasley (he had stopped resisting years ago), looked over her shoulder. \u0026quot;That we need more wine?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It means EFFICIENCY!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, slamming his fist on the table in triumph. \u0026quot;We can bulk-buy the catering! We can negotiate a group rate on the marquee! We can streamline the entire operation! It’s a Triple Merger!\u0026quot;","Lucius’s eyes lit up with the fervor of a man who loved a good deal almost as much as he loved pureblood lineage.","\u0026quot;A Triple Merger,\u0026quot; Lucius repeated, tasting the words. \u0026quot;Vernon... you are a visionary. We shall form a committee. You and I shall handle the finances. Arthur can handle the... electricals. Narcissa and Molly shall manage the aesthetics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the peacocks?\u0026quot; Narcissa asked, wiping a tear from her eye as she embraced Draco.","\u0026quot;The peacocks will wear bow ties,\u0026quot; Lucius declared magnanimously. \u0026quot;Dobby! Champagne! The 1898 vintage! All of it!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e","The dinner that followed was less of a meal and more of a victory lap.","Dobby popped bottles of champagne with the speed of a machine gun, filling glasses before they were even empty. The house-elves brought out a cake that seemed to be confused about its identity—it was one-third chocolate (for Harry), one-third treacle tart (for Draco), and one-third... pudding (for Luna).","\u0026quot;It is a franken-cake,\u0026quot; Ron noted, eating a large slice. \u0026quot;I love it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Hermione said, leaning her head on Harry’s shoulder, watching Vernon and Lucius furiously sketching a seating chart on a napkin. \u0026quot;Do you think we’ll actually get a say in our own wedding?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not a chance,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, clinking his glass against hers. \u0026quot;Uncle Vernon is already calculating the tax write-offs for the flower arrangements.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And my mother is currently explaining to Petunia why we need ice sculptures of Slytherin serpents,\u0026quot; Draco added, joining them. \u0026quot;I think Ginny just agreed to let them wear Gryffindor scarves.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s going to be a circus,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned, leaning into Draco.","\u0026quot;It’s going to be a riot,\u0026quot; Ron corrected, kissing Luna’s temple.","\u0026quot;It’s going to be perfect,\u0026quot; Luna said serenely, staring at the chandelier. \u0026quot;The Wrackspurts are dancing.\u0026quot;","Harry looked around the table. He saw the Malfoys, the Weasleys, and the Dursleys—former enemies, strangers, and muggles—united by the three rings shining on the table.","He raised his glass.","\u0026quot;To the Triple Merger,\u0026quot; Harry toasted.","\u0026quot;To the Merger!\u0026quot; the table roared back.","And as Lucius Malfoy and Vernon Dursley shook hands over a plan to import wholesale confetti, Harry knew that the biggest battle of their lives was over. Now, they just had to survive the wedding planning."]},{"num":84,"origNum":84,"title":"The Malfoy Bailout","wordCount":1046,"paragraphs":["The drawing room of Malfoy Manor looked less like a home and more like the headquarters of a failing military campaign.","It was July. The heat was sweltering, even with Cooling Charms. The September deadline loomed like a thunderhead.","The \u0026quot;Triple Merger\u0026quot; committee was fracturing under the strain.","\u0026quot;The guest list is unmanageable!\u0026quot; Hermione stressed, her hair expanding with the humidity and anxiety. She pointed her wand at a floating chart that was currently red with conflicts. \u0026quot;If we invite the Department of Magical Law Enforcement, we have to invite the Goblin Liaison Office, or it’s a diplomatic incident. But if we invite the Goblins, Uncle Vernon insists on charging them an entry fee!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s standard corporate practice!\u0026quot; Vernon argued from the sofa, loosening his tie. He was sweating profusely. \u0026quot;You don\u0027t let the assets walk in for free! We’re bleeding galleons here! The marquee rental alone costs more than my house!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We cannot serve chicken at a Malfoy wedding!\u0026quot; Lucius roared, pacing the rug. \u0026quot;It is pedestrian! We need swan! Or peacock!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You leave those birds alone!\u0026quot; Narcissa snapped. \u0026quot;They are molting!\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley was fanning herself with a fabric swatch. \u0026quot;We can\u0027t afford three hundred swans, Lucius! We have to be practical. The orchard at the Burrow can hold two hundred if everyone breathes in.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am not breathing in on my wedding day,\u0026quot; Ginny declared from the floor, where she was lying in a starfish position. \u0026quot;I will be wearing a corset. Breathing is already optional.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a disaster,\u0026quot; Ron moaned, his head on the table. \u0026quot;Lets just elope. Luna found a nice cave in Wales.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No caves!\u0026quot; Fleur shouted. \u0026quot;The humidity ruins the lace!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Intervention\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy sat in a high-backed armchair in the corner. He held a glass of iced water. He watched his father hyperventilating about poultry. He watched Vernon Dursley sweating over a calculator. He watched Ginny looking ready to hex the ceiling.","He set his glass down. The sharp \u003cem\u003eclink\u003c/em\u003e on the coaster went unheard in the shouting match.","Draco stood up. He walked to the center of the room, stepping over a roll of parchment.","\u0026quot;Enough,\u0026quot; Draco said.","He didn\u0027t shout. He spoke with the quiet, bored authority of someone who owned the building.","The room ignored him. Vernon was currently shouting about \u0026quot;overhead costs.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I SAID ENOUGH!\u0026quot; Draco barked.","Silence fell. Everyone turned to look at him.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Draco gestured around the room, \u0026quot;is hideous. You all look terrible. Father, your vein is throbbing. Mr. Dursley, you look like you are about to melt. And Ginny looks ready to commit murder.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am,\u0026quot; Ginny confirmed.","\u0026quot;The problem,\u0026quot; Draco stated, clasping his hands behind his back, \u0026quot;is logistics. The venue is too small. The security is a nightmare. The cost is... contentious.\u0026quot;","He paused, letting the words hang in the hot air.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Draco continued, \u0026quot;I have fixed it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fixed it?\u0026quot; Hermione asked warily. \u0026quot;How?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have removed the variables,\u0026quot; Draco drawled. \u0026quot;First, regarding the bill. I am paying it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What?\u0026quot; Molly gasped. \u0026quot;Draco, dear, no! It’s too much! Three weddings?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pocket change,\u0026quot; Draco dismissed with a wave of his hand. \u0026quot;The Malfoy vaults have been gathering dust. Consider it a stimulus package for the wizarding economy. I am footing the bill. All of it. Flowers, food, swans—if we must—and the marquee.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley dropped his calculator. \u0026quot; All of it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Every knut,\u0026quot; Draco nodded. \u0026quot;You can put your calculator away, Vernon. The budget is infinite.\u0026quot;","Lucius looked like he wanted to argue about family pride, but then he looked at the budget estimate on the table and decided that family pride could take a nap. \u0026quot;Well. That is... generous, Draco.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Second,\u0026quot; Draco went on, \u0026quot;the venue. The Burrow is too small. The Manor is... historically complicated. And Godric\u0027s Hollow is public.\u0026quot;","He reached into his robe pocket and pulled out a rolled-up parchment. He tossed it onto the coffee table. It unrolled to reveal a magical map of a lush, green island surrounded by turquoise water.","\u0026quot;So, I bought this,\u0026quot; Draco said simply.","Everyone stared at the map.","\u0026quot;Is that...\u0026quot; Harry squinted. \u0026quot;Is that an island?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Isla de la Fortuna,\u0026quot; Draco confirmed. \u0026quot;In the Caribbean. It is unplottable. It has private beaches. It has a villa that sleeps fifty. And it has a climate that does not require Cooling Charms.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You... bought... an island?\u0026quot; Ron whispered.","\u0026quot;It was on the market,\u0026quot; Draco shrugged. \u0026quot;A distressed seller. I got a deal.\u0026quot;","He looked at the group.","\u0026quot;We fly everyone out. Portkeys for the guests. We have the weddings on the beach. No press. No paparazzi. No Ministry crashing the party. Just us, the sand, and an open bar.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","For three seconds, the only sound was the ticking of the clock.","Then, Vernon Dursley stood up. He walked over to the map. He looked at the villa. He looked at the private beach.","\u0026quot;An island,\u0026quot; Vernon breathed. \u0026quot;A private island. In the Caribbean. Tax-free jurisdiction?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Entirely,\u0026quot; Draco smirked.","Vernon turned to Draco. He grabbed Draco’s hand and shook it violently.","\u0026quot;You are a genius!\u0026quot; Vernon roared. \u0026quot;A visionary! Outsourcing the venue to a tropical tax haven! It’s brilliant! Why didn\u0027t I think of it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, Draco!\u0026quot; Molly wept, rushing forward to hug him. \u0026quot;Sunshine! No rain! No gnomes!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can wear linen!\u0026quot; Lucius realized, looking delighted. \u0026quot;I have a cream linen suit I have never had the occasion to wear!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Beach wedding!\u0026quot; Luna cheered. \u0026quot;The Wrackspurts hate salt water!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And I don\u0027t have to wear shoes!\u0026quot; Ginny shouted, jumping up and tackling Draco. \u0026quot;I love you! I love you so much!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Draco laughed, catching her.","Harry looked at the map, then at Hermione.","\u0026quot;He bought an island,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;He actually bought an island.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It solves everything,\u0026quot; Hermione admitted, looking at her schedule. \u0026quot;No security breaches. Total privacy. And... well... it is very romantic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the Malfoy Bailout,\u0026quot; Ron grinned. \u0026quot;I\u0027m not complaining. I need a tan.\u0026quot;","Draco looked over Ginny’s shoulder at the room. The stress had vanished, replaced by the giddy excitement of a holiday.","\u0026quot;Pack your bags,\u0026quot; Draco announced. \u0026quot;We leave in two weeks to \u0027inspect the facilities\u0027. I hear the rum punch is excellent.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Caribbean!\u0026quot; Vernon toasted with his empty glass.","\u0026quot;To the Caribbean!\u0026quot; the family roared."]},{"num":85,"origNum":85,"title":"The Black Card","wordCount":1067,"paragraphs":["The summons to Gringotts had been ominous. The memo Harry received simply read: \u003cstrong\u003eURGENT. VAULT 1. FINANCIAL EMERGENCY. 10:00 AM.\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry, Hermione, Ron, Luna, and Ginny stood in the gleaming marble lobby of the bank, looking nervous.","\u0026quot;Financial emergency?\u0026quot; Ron whispered, clutching his wand. \u0026quot;Do you think the dragon came back? Is it demanding back pay?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Draco works in Relations,\u0026quot; Ginny said, frowning. \u0026quot;He wouldn\u0027t call us unless it was serious. Maybe the Ministry is freezing assets again.\u0026quot;","A goblin—Griphook, looking older and wearing a tailored suit that suspiciously resembled the one Draco had given Dobby—approached them.","\u0026quot;Mr. Malfoy is expecting you,\u0026quot; Griphook said, bowing low (a sign of respect he reserved only for the Dragon Riders). \u0026quot;Follow me. The Executive Suite.\u0026quot;","They were led not to the carts, but up a spiral staircase Harry had never noticed before, into a room that smelled of money. The walls were lined with gold bars, the table was made of polished obsidian, and the chairs were upholstered in dragon hide.","Draco Malfoy sat at the head of the table. He was flanked by two senior goblins who were nodding respectfully at a scroll Draco was annotating.","\u0026quot;Thank you, Ragnok,\u0026quot; Draco said, signing the parchment with a flourish. \u0026quot;That will be all.\u0026quot;","The goblins bowed and scuttled out, leaving the five Gryffindors (and one Ravenclaw) standing in the doorway.","\u0026quot;Sit,\u0026quot; Draco commanded, not looking up.","They sat. The air was tense.","\u0026quot;What is it, Draco?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, her voice high. \u0026quot;Is it the wedding? Has the island sunk?\u0026quot;","Draco finished writing, capped his pen (a gift from Vernon), and looked up. His face was grave.","\u0026quot;We have a problem,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;The Shopping List.\u0026quot;","He reached into his briefcase.","\u0026quot;I have reviewed the projected expenses for your wedding attire,\u0026quot; Draco said, sliding a piece of paper across the table. \u0026quot;Ron, you were planning to rent robes? From \u003cem\u003eMadam Malkin\u0027s Discount Bin\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","Ron turned red. \u0026quot; It’s budget-friendly! We’re saving for a house!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Potter,\u0026quot; Draco sneered slightly. \u0026quot;You were going to wear your Auror dress uniform? To your own wedding on a tropical island? It’s wool, Potter. You will die of heatstroke before the vows.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s respectful!\u0026quot; Harry argued.","\u0026quot;It’s sweaty,\u0026quot; Draco corrected.","He reached into his briefcase again. He pulled out five small, sleek, rectangular objects made of a matte black metal that absorbed the light. They were edged in goblin gold.","He slid one to each of them.","\u003cem\u003eCLINK. CLINK. CLINK. CLINK. CLINK.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry picked his up. It was heavy. It was warm to the touch. In the center, in glowing silver script, was his name: \u003cem\u003eHarry James Potter\u003c/em\u003e. And below it, the Gringotts crest and the Malfoy crest, intertwined.","\u0026quot;What is this?\u0026quot; Ginny asked, turning hers over.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Draco announced, leaning back in his chair and crossing his arms, \u0026quot;is the Gringotts Infinite Card.\u0026quot;","The room went silent.","\u0026quot;The what?\u0026quot; Ron asked.","\u0026quot;It is a prototype,\u0026quot; Draco explained, looking pleased with himself. \u0026quot;I spent the last two days negotiating with the High Council. It connects directly to a consolidated fund I have established. It bypasses the need for carrying heavy gold. You tap it, the gold transfers.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the limit?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, her eyes narrowing suspiciously. \u0026quot;Every credit line has a ceiling, Draco.\u0026quot;","Draco smirked. It was the smirk of a man who owned an island.","\u0026quot;No limit,\u0026quot; Draco said softly.","Hermione dropped the card. \u0026quot;That... that is fiscally irresponsible! That is economic madness!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is \u003cem\u003eInfinite\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; Draco repeated, enjoying the word. \u0026quot;You walk into a shop. You see a dress. You tap the card. It is yours. You see a suit. Yours. You see a yacht? Yours.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron Weasley stared at the black rectangle in his hand. His hands were shaking.","\u0026quot;No limit?\u0026quot; Ron squeaked. \u0026quot;Like... zero limit? I could buy... a bakery? I could buy the Cannons?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Please don\u0027t buy the Cannons, Ron,\u0026quot; Draco sighed. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t want to own a losing team. But yes. Buy the robes. Buy the shoes. Buy the expensive cufflinks.\u0026quot;","Harry pushed the card back across the obsidian table.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t take this, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;I have money. My parents left me a vault. Sirius left me a vault.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco rolled his eyes. \u0026quot;Your vault is cute. It is quaint. This is \u003cem\u003egenerational wealth\u003c/em\u003e. This is \u0027I bought an island\u0027 money. Just take the card. Do not insult me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s too much,\u0026quot; Harry insisted.","\u0026quot;Consider it reparations,\u0026quot; Draco said sharply. \u0026quot;For the years I was a git. For the years my father was a git. For the... unpleasantness in my drawing room.\u0026quot;","He looked at Hermione, his expression softening.","\u0026quot;Buy the best dress in the world, Granger,\u0026quot; Draco said quietly. \u0026quot;You deserve it.\u0026quot;","Hermione bit her lip, looking at the card. Tears pricked her eyes. \u0026quot;Draco... this is... ridiculous.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Draco agreed. \u0026quot;But I insist.\u0026quot;","Ginny didn\u0027t argue. She stood up, walked to the head of the table, and kissed Draco hard on the mouth.","\u0026quot;I love you,\u0026quot; she said. \u0026quot;And I am going to buy shoes that cost more than a broomstick.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I expect nothing less,\u0026quot; Draco grinned.","Luna picked up her card and held it to her ear. \u0026quot;It hums,\u0026quot; she noted happily. \u0026quot;I think the goblins sang to it. I shall buy a dress made of sunlight.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You can buy the sun if you want, Luna,\u0026quot; Draco said generously.","Ron was still staring at the card, tranced. \u0026quot;I’m going to buy a suit made of silk. Acromantula silk. No... velvet. No... gold!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t look like a canary, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco warned. \u0026quot;Keep it tasteful.\u0026quot;","Draco stood up, clapping his hands.","\u0026quot;Meeting adjourned,\u0026quot; he declared. \u0026quot;You have forty-eight hours to procure wardrobes that will make the French Ministry weep with envy. Go. Shop. Spend my inheritance. It’s what it’s there for.\u0026quot;","As the group filed out of the room—Ron clutching the card to his chest like a holy relic, Hermione looking terrified but excited, and Ginny already making a list—Harry stopped at the door.","He looked back at Draco, who was gathering his papers.","\u0026quot;You really enjoy this, don\u0027t you?\u0026quot; Harry asked. \u0026quot;Playing the benefactor.\u0026quot;","Draco looked up. He smiled—a genuine, unguarded smile.","\u0026quot;It feels better than playing the villain, Harry,\u0026quot; Draco said.","Harry nodded, pocketing the black card. \u0026quot;I\u0027m buying the most expensive socks in London, Malfoy. Just to spite you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get cashmere, Potter,\u0026quot; Draco called after him. \u0026quot;Your feet deserve it.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":86,"origNum":86,"title":"The Paris Protocol","wordCount":1067,"paragraphs":["The cobblestones of \u003cem\u003ePlace Cachée\u003c/em\u003e—the magical district hidden deep within Paris—gleamed under the summer sun. It was a street of high fashion, smelling of expensive perfume, macaroons, and old money.","Ginny Weasley stood in the center of the thoroughfare, wearing sunglasses and a grin that could strip paint. She held the Gringotts Infinite Card between two fingers like a throwing star.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Ginny declared. \u0026quot;Draco said to make the French Ministry weep. I intend to make them sob uncontrollably.\u0026quot;","Hermione Granger stood beside her, clutching her beaded bag nervously. \u0026quot;Ginny, these shops... there are no price tags in the window. That means we can\u0027t afford to breathe the air in there.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Correction,\u0026quot; Ginny said, flashing the black card. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eWe\u003c/em\u003e can\u0027t afford it. \u003cem\u003eDraco\u003c/em\u003e can. And he specifically ordered us to be irresponsible. It would be rude to disobey a direct order from the host.\u0026quot;","Luna Lovegood drifted toward a shop window displaying a dress made entirely of floating peacock feathers. \u0026quot;I hope they sell shoes made of clouds. My feet have been feeling very heavy lately.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cloud shoes,\u0026quot; Ginny nodded decisively. \u0026quot;Added to the list. Let’s move.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Boutique\u003c/strong\u003e","They entered \u003cem\u003eL\u0027Étoile Filante\u003c/em\u003e (The Shooting Star), the most exclusive bridal boutique in Europe. The interior was all white velvet and floating mirrors.","A saleswitch with a nose so upturned she could see the ceiling glided over. She looked at Hermione’s sensible jeans, Ginny’s windblown hair, and Luna’s radish earrings.","\u0026quot;Can I... help you?\u0026quot; the witch asked, her tone suggesting she would rather help them find the exit. \u0026quot;The souvenir shop is two streets over.\u0026quot;","Ginny slowly removed her sunglasses. She channeled Lucius Malfoy. She channeled Narcissa. She channeled every ounce of pureblood arrogance she had observed at the Manor dinners.","\u0026quot;We are not here for souvenirs,\u0026quot; Ginny said, her voice cool and bored. \u0026quot;We are here for three wedding trousseaus. The theme is \u0027Caribbean Island Luxury\u0027. We require silk. We require lace. And we require champagne. Now.\u0026quot;","The witch blinked. \u0026quot;I am afraid appointments are required for the—\u0026quot;","Ginny placed the Black Card on the glass counter.","\u003cem\u003eCLINK.\u003c/em\u003e","The card glowed. The Gringotts crest pulsed. The magic of the Malfoy vault hummed through the glass, vibrating the perfume bottles on the shelves.","The witch looked at the card. Her eyes widened. Her nostrils flared. The sneer vanished, replaced by a look of terrified devotion.","\u0026quot;Mademoiselle,\u0026quot; the witch squeaked. \u0026quot;Welcome. I shall close the shop. Champagne is coming.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Montage\u003c/strong\u003e","What followed was a blur of fabric, laughter, and magical tailoring.","\u003cstrong\u003eHermione\u003c/strong\u003e was the hardest to crack. She spent the first twenty minutes looking at price tags and hyperventilating.","\u0026quot;Ginny!\u0026quot; Hermione hissed from behind a changing screen. \u0026quot;This veil costs three thousand Galleons! That’s... that’s a library wing!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Buy it!\u0026quot; Ginny shouted from a podium where she was being measured by measuring tapes that hummed appreciatively.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione Jean Granger,\u0026quot; Ginny commanded. \u0026quot;You saved the world. You lived in a tent for a year. You are marrying the Boy Who Lived. You are going to wear the expensive veil, and you are going to look like a queen, or I will hex you.\u0026quot;","A pause. Then, the rustle of silk.","Hermione stepped out.","She was wearing a gown of ivory silk chiffon. It was simple, elegant, and timeless, with sleeves of delicate lace that looked like frost patterns on a window. It didn\u0027t puff; it flowed.","She looked at herself in the floating mirror. She touched the expensive veil.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;I look... tall.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You look like a boss,\u0026quot; Ginny corrected. \u0026quot;Sold.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eLuna\u003c/strong\u003e was the easiest. She wandered through the racks until she found a dress that no one else would have looked twice at. It was made of layers of organza that shifted color—pale yellow like sunlight, then silver like the moon, then soft blue like the sky.","\u0026quot;It feels like a sunrise,\u0026quot; Luna said, spinning in circles.","\u0026quot;It’s weird,\u0026quot; Ginny admitted. \u0026quot;But it’s you. Get the shoes.\u0026quot;","Luna found a pair of heels that were invisible until she put them on, at which point they sparkled like trapped stars.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lioness\u003c/strong\u003e","Then, it was Ginny’s turn.","She didn\u0027t want simple. She didn\u0027t want ethereal. She wanted fire.","She found it in the back room—a dress that made the French saleswitch gasp.","It was a backless gown of liquid silk in a shade of white so bright it hurt to look at. It was cut dangerously low, fit like a second skin, and had a slit that went up to her thigh. It was daring. It was dramatic. It was a dress that said, \u003cem\u003eI tamed the Serpent.\u003c/em\u003e","Ginny stepped onto the podium. She looked at herself. She thought of Draco in the mud. She thought of the ice water.","\u0026quot;Does it come with a spell to prevent wardrobe malfunctions while flying?\u0026quot; Ginny asked.","\u0026quot;For you, Mademoiselle?\u0026quot; the witch beamed. \u0026quot;We will add the strongest Sticking Charms in existence.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Checkout\u003c/strong\u003e","Three hours later, they stood at the counter. The pile of boxes was taller than Luna.","There were dresses. There were shoes. There were robes for the rehearsal dinner. There were swimsuits made of charm-infused fabric that never got wet. There was a sun hat for Hermione that was the size of a small umbrella.","The saleswitch tallied the total. The number on the register spun higher and higher, reaching a sum that would have bought a small country.","Hermione looked faint.","\u0026quot;The total is...\u0026quot; the witch hesitated, looking at the astronomical figure.","Ginny didn\u0027t even look at the number. She tapped the Black Card on the counter.","\u003cem\u003eDING.\u003c/em\u003e","A sound like a golden bell rang through the shop. A shower of golden sparks erupted from the register.","\u0026quot;Transaction approved,\u0026quot; a smooth, goblin-like voice announced from the card itself. \u0026quot;Thank you, Mr. Malfoy.\u0026quot;","The saleswitch bowed so low her nose touched the counter. \u0026quot;Merci, Mesdames. Please, take some complimentary perfume samples. Take the whole display.\u0026quot;","They walked out onto the streets of Paris, laden with shrunken bags, blinking in the sunlight.","\u0026quot;We just spent a fortune,\u0026quot; Hermione breathed, clutching her chest.","\u0026quot;We just stimulated the economy,\u0026quot; Ginny corrected, putting her sunglasses back on. \u0026quot;Now, where’s that bakery? I need a croissant the size of my head. Shopping is hungry work.\u0026quot;","Luna skipped ahead, her star-shoes twinkling. \u0026quot;I think the Nargles are jealous of my dress.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They should be,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned. \u0026quot;They should be.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":87,"origNum":87,"title":"The Fellowship of the Suit","wordCount":1069,"paragraphs":["While the girls were conquering Paris, the boys had apparated to a narrow, cobblestone alleyway hidden behind a charmed brick wall just off Savile Row in London. This was \u003cem\u003eThreadneedle Passage\u003c/em\u003e, the home of wizarding bespoke tailoring.","Draco Malfoy stood before the polished mahogany doors of \u003cem\u003eGaston \u0026amp; Gambol: Tailors to the Elite\u003c/em\u003e. He adjusted his cuffs, checked his reflection in the window, and turned to his companions.","\u0026quot;Gentlemen,\u0026quot; Draco announced. \u0026quot;We are about to enter a place of worship. There will be no giggling. There will be no asking for \u0027stretchy waists\u0027. And Weasley...\u0026quot;","Ron looked up, currently trying to clean a smudge off his trainers. \u0026quot;Yeah?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If you ask if they sell Chudley Cannons socks, I will disown you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fair enough,\u0026quot; Ron shrugged. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll ask for Harpies socks. Keep it in the family.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Fitting\u003c/strong\u003e","They entered. The shop smelled of leather, lavender, and intimidation. A tailor with a mustache so waxed it defied gravity glided over. He took one look at Harry’s messy hair and Ron’s slightly short trousers and sniffed.","Then he saw Draco. And more importantly, he saw the Black Card Draco was casually tapping against his thigh.","\u0026quot;Monsieur Malfoy,\u0026quot; the tailor purred, bowing low. \u0026quot;And... guests. How may we serve you?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We require three wedding ensembles,\u0026quot; Draco commanded. \u0026quot;Tropical climate. Beach setting. But formal. We need linen that doesn\u0027t crease, silk that breathes, and cuts that make us look like gods.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Say no more,\u0026quot; the tailor beamed. \u0026quot;Release the measures!\u0026quot;","A swarm of enchanted tape measures flew at them.","\u0026quot;Chest, 38 inches!\u0026quot; a tape measure shouted near Harry. \u0026quot;Posture: Slouchy! Recommend structural reinforcement!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hey!\u0026quot; Harry protested, swatting it away.","\u0026quot;Inside leg, 34!\u0026quot; another tape yelled at Ron. \u0026quot;Diet: Carb-heavy! Recommend elasticated gusset!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m cultivating mass!\u0026quot; Ron argued, blushing.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Transformation of Ron Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e","The most dramatic transformation, however, was reserved for Ron.","For years, Ron had worn hand-me-downs. He was used to robes that were too short, jumpers that were too itchy, and dress robes that smelled of his Great Aunt Tessie.","Draco marched him to a mirror. He waved his wand, and fabrics began to fly.","\u0026quot;Try this,\u0026quot; Draco ordered. \u0026quot;Cream linen. Italian cut. No, not that one, you look like a milkman. This one. Bamboo fiber blend.\u0026quot;","Ron put on the jacket. He looked in the mirror. He straightened his shoulders. The jacket fit perfectly—tailored to his broad shoulders and tall frame. It didn\u0027t itch. It felt like wearing air.","\u0026quot;Bloody hell,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, turning side to side. \u0026quot;Is this what rich people feel like all the time?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Draco said simply. \u0026quot;Now, try the shoes. Dragon-hide loafers. They massage your feet while you walk.\u0026quot;","Ron slipped his feet into the shoes. He let out a low moan of pleasure. \u0026quot;Oh, that’s the stuff. I’m never taking these off. I’m going to sleep in these.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You need cufflinks,\u0026quot; Draco critiqued. \u0026quot;Gold. To match the... rustic vibe.\u0026quot;","Ron picked up a pair of solid gold cufflinks shaped like tiny lions. He didn\u0027t even look at the price tag (which would have bought a small house). He just tapped the Black Card.","\u003cem\u003eDING.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I love this card,\u0026quot; Ron declared, kissing the black metal. \u0026quot;I want to marry this card.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Luna might object,\u0026quot; Harry noted, trying on a crisp white shirt.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Chosen Suit\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry was harder to style. He kept reaching for the plain black robes.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco sighed, snatching a grey robe out of Harry\u0027s hand. \u0026quot;You are the groom. You are not attending a funeral. You are marrying Hermione Granger. You need to look sharp. Intelligent. Dashing.\u0026quot;","Draco selected a suit of midnight blue—a subtle nod to the dress robes Hermione had bought him for the Yule Ball years ago, but modernized. The fabric shimmered slightly, woven with protective threads that repelled sand and stains.","Harry put it on. The magical tape measure swooned. \u0026quot;Perfection! A hero\u0027s silhouette!\u0026quot;","Harry looked in the mirror. He looked... grown up. He looked like the Head Auror.","\u0026quot;Not bad,\u0026quot; Harry admitted, adjusting the collar.","\u0026quot;It’s adequate,\u0026quot; Draco smirked, which was high praise.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Malfoy Standard\u003c/strong\u003e","Finally, Draco dressed himself. He chose a suit of pale, dove-grey silk linen. It was understated, elegant, and probably cost more than the shop itself. He added a tie pin made of a single, perfect pearl.","He stood next to Harry and Ron in the triple mirror.","Three men. A Malfoy, a Potter, and a Weasley. Standing shoulder to shoulder, looking sharp, dangerous, and ready to get married.","\u0026quot;We look good,\u0026quot; Ron said, admiring his reflection. \u0026quot;Like... really good. We look like a boy band.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are not a boy band,\u0026quot; Draco sneered. \u0026quot;We are a power triumvirate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Can we be a boy band at the reception?\u0026quot; Harry asked. \u0026quot;I think the Weird Sisters are playing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll consider it,\u0026quot; Draco allowed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Spree\u003c/strong\u003e","Once the suits were secured, the power of the Black Card went to their heads.","\u0026quot;Sunnglasses!\u0026quot; Ron shouted, pointing at a display of enchanted shades. \u0026quot;I need ones that let me see behind my head!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eDING.\u003c/em\u003e Bought.","\u0026quot;Luggage!\u0026quot; Harry decided, eyeing a set of dragon-skin trunks that followed their owner like loyal dogs. \u0026quot;I’m tired of carrying bags.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eDING.\u003c/em\u003e Bought.","\u0026quot;Casual wear,\u0026quot; Draco insisted, steering them toward the silk shirts. \u0026quot;We cannot wear suits on the beach every day. We need... resort wear.\u0026quot;","They bought linen shirts that unbuttoned dangerously low. They bought swimming trunks that changed pattern depending on the water temperature. They bought hats. They bought colognes that smelled like \u0027Victory\u0027 and \u0027Old Spice\u0027.","By the time they left the shop, they were followed by a floating flotilla of bags and trunks. The tailor was bowing so low his nose scraped the pavement.","\u0026quot;Thank you, Monsieur Malfoy! Thank you, Monsieur Potter! Monsieur Weasley, enjoy the gusset!\u0026quot;","They walked out onto the street, blinking in the London sun.","Ron was wearing his new sunglasses. He looked at Harry. He looked at Draco.","\u0026quot;We just spent a fortune,\u0026quot; Ron said, grinning wildly.","\u0026quot;We stimulated the economy,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, checking his manicure.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m hungry,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;Let\u0027s go to that Muggle place Dudley talks about. Nando\u0027s?\u0026quot;","Draco looked horrified. \u0026quot;Fast food? In these suits?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s spicy chicken, Malfoy,\u0026quot; Ron said, clapping a hand on Draco\u0027s shoulder. \u0026quot;Risk adds flavor.\u0026quot;","Draco sighed, looking at his two best friends. \u0026quot;Fine. But if I get sauce on this linen, I am suing you both.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Put it on the card,\u0026quot; Harry laughed."]},{"num":88,"origNum":88,"title":"The Ledger of Laziness","wordCount":881,"paragraphs":["The private parlor of the Leaky Cauldron looked like a dragon’s hoard had exploded inside a haberdashery.","Shrunken bags were piled on the tables. Self-propelling trunks were parking themselves in the corners. The air smelled of expensive cologne, new leather, and the ozone scent of heavy spending.","Hermione Granger sat in the center of the chaos, surrounded by long scrolls of parchment receipts. She had a quill in one hand and a look of mounting horror on her face.","\u0026quot;I’ve tallied the Paris receipts,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, her voice trembling. \u0026quot;And I’ve added the London expenditures.\u0026quot;","She looked up at the group. Harry was leaning back in his chair, feet (clad in cashmere socks) on the table. Ron was admiring his cufflinks in the firelight. Ginny was eating a cauldron cake. Luna was wearing her star-shoes, watching them twinkle.","\u0026quot;The total,\u0026quot; Hermione gulped, \u0026quot;is astronomical. It’s... it’s the GDP of a small country. We have spent...\u0026quot;","She scribbled a final number and turned the parchment around.","\u003cstrong\u003e245,000 GALLEONS.\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron choked on his drink. He stared at the number. He looked down at his cream linen suit.","\u0026quot;I’m wearing a house,\u0026quot; Ron whispered. \u0026quot;I am literally wearing a house on my body. Take it off! I have to take it off!\u0026quot;","He started clawing at his jacket buttons. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t walk around in a mortgage! It’s immoral!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Leave the jacket alone, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco’s voice cut through the panic.","Draco Malfoy was lying on a chaise longue near the window. He looked the picture of aristocratic indolence. He held a glass of firewhisky in one hand and was idly tossing a grape into the air and catching it with the other. He hadn\u0027t looked at the receipts once.","\u0026quot;Draco!\u0026quot; Hermione stressed, waving the parchment. \u0026quot;Do you see this number? Two hundred and forty-five \u003cem\u003ethousand\u003c/em\u003e! That’s... that’s a quarter of a million! We went overboard! We abused the card! We have to return the swan-feather fans!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Keep the fans,\u0026quot; Draco yawned. \u0026quot;It gets hot in the tropics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But the money!\u0026quot; Hermione insisted. \u0026quot;It’s irresponsible! You can\u0027t just burn through that kind of capital in six hours without consequences!\u0026quot;","Draco sighed. He sat up slowly, looking as if the conversation was exhausting him. He set his glass down.","\u0026quot;Granger,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;Pass me the ledger.\u0026quot;","He pointed to a small, leather-bound book that had been sitting on the table, ignoring the mountain of receipts.","Hermione handed it to him. \u0026quot;What is this? Your bankruptcy filing?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a live-feed portfolio tracker,\u0026quot; Draco explained, opening the book. The pages were blank, but as he touched them, numbers began to scrawl themselves in glowing green ink, updating in real-time.","Draco ran a finger down the column.","\u0026quot;Hm,\u0026quot; he grunted. \u0026quot;Interesting.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What?\u0026quot; Harry asked, sitting up. \u0026quot;Is it bad? Do we need to sell the island?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, turning the book so they could see. \u0026quot;While you lot were running around Paris terrorizing sales assistants, and while Potter was buying—what was it? Four hundred pairs of socks?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They\u0027re cashmere,\u0026quot; Harry defended. \u0026quot;And I bought them for the whole Order.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Draco rolled his eyes. \u0026quot;Anyway. While you were doing that, the goblin markets opened in New York.\u0026quot;","He pointed to a line of green numbers that was ticking upward rapidly.","\u0026quot;I have a substantial holding in Peruvian Instant Darkness Powder futures,\u0026quot; Draco explained lazily. \u0026quot;And apparently, there’s been a surge in demand in Brazil. Plus, the dividends from the \u0027Spark Plug\u0027 factory Vernon convinced me to invest in just cleared.\u0026quot;","He looked at the bottom line of the ledger.","\u0026quot;In the six hours you were shopping,\u0026quot; Draco said, checking his pocket watch, \u0026quot;my portfolio generated a return of...\u0026quot;","He tapped the page. The number flashed.","\u003cstrong\u003e+ 310,000 GALLEONS.\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco looked at Hermione. He smirked.","\u0026quot;So, technically,\u0026quot; Draco said, picking up his drink again and settling back onto the chaise, \u0026quot;I made a profit today. We actually came in under budget. I’m sixty-five thousand galleons richer than I was when I woke up.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","The silence in the parlor was profound.","Hermione stared at the ledger. She looked at the receipts. She looked at Draco. Her brain, usually so sharp and logical, seemed to short-circuit.","\u0026quot;You...\u0026quot; Hermione sputtered. \u0026quot;You made... while we spent... you did nothing! You just sat there!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Passive income, Granger,\u0026quot; Draco winked. \u0026quot;Work smarter, not harder. Vernon taught me that.\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley stood up. He walked over to Draco. He looked at the former Slytherin Prince who was currently funding his wedding, his wardrobe, and apparently his entire future existence.","Ron fell to his knees.","\u0026quot;Teach me,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, clutching Draco’s leg. \u0026quot;I will do anything. I will wash your peacocks. I will name my firstborn Draco. Just teach me the way of the passive galleon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get off me, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco laughed, kicking him gently. \u0026quot;You\u0027re wrinkling the linen.\u0026quot;","Harry burst out laughing, throwing his head back. \u0026quot;Unbelievable. We try to bankrupt him, and he accidentally gets richer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the Nargles,\u0026quot; Luna noted happily, tapping the ledger. \u0026quot;They like the green ink.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Ginny said, grabbing the receipts from Hermione and tossing them into the fire. \u0026quot;What you\u0027re saying is... we should have bought the yacht?\u0026quot;","Draco swirled his drink, looking at his friends—laughing, happy, and dressed like royalty.","\u0026quot;Next time, Red,\u0026quot; Draco smiled. \u0026quot;Next time.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":89,"origNum":89,"title":"The Wedding Embargo","wordCount":845,"paragraphs":["The drawing room of Malfoy Manor was currently serving as a high-end fashion runway. The furniture had been pushed back (by magic, much to Lucius’s mild disapproval), and the center of the room was piled high with the spoils of Paris and London.","Narcissa Malfoy and Molly Weasley sat on the sofa like judges at a talent show, sipping tea and nodding approvingly as the girls modeled their purchases.","\u0026quot;The lace on that shawl is exquisite, Hermione,\u0026quot; Narcissa noted, touching the fabric. \u0026quot;Goblin-made?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;French elves,\u0026quot; Hermione corrected, beaming. \u0026quot;It\u0027s enchanted to repel wine stains.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Practical,\u0026quot; Molly nodded. \u0026quot;Very smart.\u0026quot;","Harry, Ron, and Draco were lounging near the fireplace, looking thoroughly exhausted by the mere act of watching the fashion show. Ron was currently trying to teach Lucius the rules of \u0026quot;Uno\u0026quot; using a deck of cards he had found in his pocket, while Arthur and Vernon debated the structural integrity of the manor\u0027s chimney.","\u0026quot;And now,\u0026quot; Ginny announced, her eyes shining with excitement. \u0026quot;The main event.\u0026quot;","She gestured to three large, white boxes that were floating in the corner, glowing with preservation charms.","\u0026quot;The dresses,\u0026quot; Luna hummed, drifting over to her box. \u0026quot;They are very shiny.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We wanted to show you,\u0026quot; Hermione said, looking at Harry. \u0026quot;Just to get... an opinion.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Opinion?\u0026quot; Draco perked up. \u0026quot;I have several. Let’s see the investment.\u0026quot;","Ginny reached for the lid of her box. Harry sat up straighter. Ron stopped trying to make Lucius draw a \u0027Wild Card\u0027.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Ginny said. \u0026quot;Ready?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;STOP!\u0026quot;","The shout was so loud it rattled the crystal chandelier.","Everyone froze. Ginny’s hand hovered inches from the box lid.","Vernon Dursley was standing in the center of the room, his face a alarming shade of purple, his arms waved frantically like he was trying to stop a train.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t you dare open that box!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed.","\u0026quot;Uncle Vernon?\u0026quot; Harry asked, bewildered. \u0026quot;What\u0027s wrong? Is it... is it a bomb?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Worse!\u0026quot; Vernon roared. \u0026quot;It\u0027s bad luck! It\u0027s catastrophic misfortune!\u0026quot;","He pointed a shaking finger at Harry, then Draco, then Ron.","\u0026quot;You cannot see the dress before the wedding day!\u0026quot; Vernon lectured, channeling generations of superstitious tradition. \u0026quot;It is the golden rule of matrimony! If the groom sees the bride in the dress before the ceremony, the marriage is doomed! Doomed to... to inefficiency! To structural failure!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s just a dress, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia tried to soothe him, though she looked secretly pleased he knew the rules.","\u0026quot;It is not just a dress, Petunia!\u0026quot; Vernon insisted. \u0026quot;It is the symbol of the surprise! The \u0027Wow\u0027 factor! If they see it now, the market value of the reveal drops to zero!\u0026quot;","He turned on the men.","\u0026quot;OUT!\u0026quot; Vernon commanded, pointing at the heavy oak doors. \u0026quot;All of you! Grooms! Out! Fathers! Out!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fathers?\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy repeated, looking affronted. \u0026quot;This is my house, Vernon. I live here.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Doesn\u0027t matter!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;You are male. You are a liability. You will see something, you will make a face, you will say something about \u0027too much lace\u0027, and you will ruin the diplomatic relations for decades! Out! To the library! To the garden! Anywhere but here!\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley stood up, looking terrified. \u0026quot;He\u0027s right, Lucius. Molly once hexed me for seeing a swatch of fabric before the wedding. It’s not worth the risk.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am not leaving my own drawing room because of a superstition,\u0026quot; Lucius sniffed.","\u0026quot;Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, her voice silky and dangerous. \u0026quot;Go.\u0026quot;","Lucius stood up immediately. \u0026quot;Right. The library. I have... books to read.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But I want to see!\u0026quot; Ron complained. \u0026quot;I paid for part of it! Well, Draco paid for it, but I picked the shoes!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;OUT!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, ushering them like a herd of sheep. \u0026quot;Go! Go! Go! Move, Harry! Don\u0027t look back! Or you\u0027ll turn to salt! Or worse—a bachelor!\u0026quot;","Harry laughed, holding his hands up in surrender. \u0026quot;Okay! We\u0027re going! Come on, Draco. Let\u0027s go look at your... books.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I hate this,\u0026quot; Draco grumbled, standing up and dusting off his trousers. \u0026quot;Expelled from my own drawing room by a Muggle drill salesman. The indignity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s for your own good!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted, practically pushing Draco out the door.","He herded the men—Harry, Ron, Draco, Lucius, and Arthur—into the hallway and slammed the double doors shut with a resounding \u003cem\u003eTHUD\u003c/em\u003e.","Inside the drawing room, the women looked at the closed doors.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Molly Weasley said, picking up her tea. \u0026quot;That was decisive.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He has his moments,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled proudly.","\u0026quot;Can we open them now?\u0026quot; Ginny asked.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, leaning forward. \u0026quot;Open them. I want to see where the galleons went.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Exile\u003c/strong\u003e","Out in the hallway, the six men stood in silence.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Ron said, looking at the closed doors. \u0026quot;We\u0027ve been banished.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It appears so,\u0026quot; Lucius sighed, adjusting his cuffs. \u0026quot;Vernon, you are a tyrant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am a project manager,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected, straightening his tie. \u0026quot;I just saved your son\u0027s marriage. You\u0027re welcome.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the library?\u0026quot; Arthur suggested. \u0026quot;I still want to know how the \u0027stapler\u0027 binds without magic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the library,\u0026quot; Lucius agreed defeatedly. \u0026quot;Dobby! Bring the whisky! The men are in exile!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":90,"origNum":90,"title":"Silk and Steel","wordCount":865,"paragraphs":["\u003cstrong\u003eThe Drawing Room: The Reveal\u003c/strong\u003e","With the men safely exiled behind heavy oak doors, the atmosphere in the drawing room shifted from tense negotiation to hushed reverence.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Ginny said, taking charge. \u0026quot;Hermione first. If we show mine first, Mum might faint, and I want her conscious for the others.\u0026quot;","Hermione stepped forward. She tapped her wand on the white box. The lid dissolved into mist, revealing the gown within.","It floated out, suspended by gentle magic. The ivory silk chiffon caught the light of the chandelier, glowing softly. It was modest yet striking, the lace sleeves intricate as spiderwebs, the skirt flowing like water.","The room went silent.","Molly Weasley pressed a hand to her mouth. \u0026quot;Oh, Hermione. It’s... it’s like something out of a fairytale.\u0026quot;","Petunia Dursley stood up. She walked over to the floating dress, her eyes scanning the delicate embroidery. She thought of the little boy she had raised, the one who slept in a cupboard, now marrying a woman who would wear \u003cem\u003ethis\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;He’s going to forget his own name when he sees you,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, wiping a tear from her cheek. \u0026quot;You look... regal.\u0026quot;","Narcissa Malfoy nodded slowly, her critical gaze softening. \u0026quot;It is elegant. Understated. It commands respect without demanding attention. Very fitting for a Deputy Minister.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Ginny said, taking a deep breath. \u0026quot;My turn. Mum... brace yourself.\u0026quot;","She opened her box.","The backless gown of liquid white silk drifted into the air. It was sleek, modern, and undeniably sexy. The slit in the skirt was high; the neckline was deep. It was a dress designed for a woman who flew broomsticks at high speeds and dated a Malfoy.","Molly Weasley’s eyes widened. She made a small, squeaking sound.","\u0026quot;Ginevra,\u0026quot; Molly choked out. \u0026quot;Where... where is the back? Did they forget to sew it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s for the tropics, Mum!\u0026quot; Ginny defended. \u0026quot;It’s ventilation!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is... bold,\u0026quot; Narcissa interjected smoothly, stepping in to save the peace. She looked at the dress with genuine approval. \u0026quot;It is confident, Molly. It says she is not afraid. And frankly, with a Malfoy, one must occasionally remind them who holds the power. That dress holds the power.\u0026quot;","Molly looked at Narcissa, then at the dress. She sighed, a smile breaking through. \u0026quot;I suppose... she does have the figure for it. And Harry did say Draco paid for it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Draco insisted,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned.","\u0026quot;And finally,\u0026quot; Luna hummed, opening her box.","The dress of shifting colors floated out—pale yellow, silver, and soft blue layers moving like clouds.","\u0026quot;It changes color!\u0026quot; Petunia gasped, stepping back. \u0026quot;Is it... battery operated?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s enchanted organza,\u0026quot; Hermione explained gently.","\u0026quot;It’s very... Luna,\u0026quot; Molly smiled warmly. \u0026quot;It looks like a sunrise.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It matches the Nargles,\u0026quot; Luna said happily.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Library: The Tailoring Summit\u003c/strong\u003e","In the library, the mood was decidedly more masculine, smelling of old leather books and the 50-year-old brandy Dobby had just served.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley announced, sitting in a leather armchair like a king. \u0026quot;Show us the goods. If we’re banished, we might as well critique the investment.\u0026quot;","Ron went first. He levitated his cream linen suit out of the garment bag.","Arthur Weasley gasped. He rushed forward, touching the fabric with trembling fingers.","\u0026quot;It’s so... smooth,\u0026quot; Arthur breathed. \u0026quot;And look at the buttons! Are they plastic?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mother of pearl, Dad,\u0026quot; Ron said, beaming. \u0026quot;And the shoes massage my feet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Massage your feet?\u0026quot; Vernon asked, impressed. \u0026quot;Now that is technology I can get behind. Good choice, Weasley. Practical for the heat, but sharp.\u0026quot;","Harry revealed his midnight blue suit. It hung in the air, sleek and modern.","Vernon nodded vigorously. \u0026quot;Excellent. Dark colors command authority. You look like a CEO, Harry. Or a Head Auror, I suppose. It’s a power suit.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy swirled his brandy, eyeing the cut of Harry’s jacket. \u0026quot;The lapels are... adequate. A modern cut. It suits you, Potter. It hides the slouch.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t slouch,\u0026quot; Harry protested.","\u0026quot;You do,\u0026quot; Draco corrected.","Finally, Draco displayed his dove-grey silk linen suit. It was a masterpiece of tailoring, sharp as a knife and soft as a cloud.","Lucius stood up. He walked over to the suit. He inspected the stitching on the hem. He checked the lining. He examined the pearl tie pin.","He turned to his son.","\u0026quot;Gaston \u0026amp; Gambol?\u0026quot; Lucius asked.","\u0026quot;Custom commission,\u0026quot; Draco nodded.","Lucius pursed his lips. He looked at the suit, then at Draco.","\u0026quot;It is...\u0026quot; Lucius paused. \u0026quot;It is impeccable. You will look like a Malfoy.\u0026quot;","Draco let out a breath he didn\u0027t know he was holding. \u0026quot;Thank you, Father.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;However,\u0026quot; Lucius added, poking the pocket square. \u0026quot;Ensure you do not spill \u0027hot sauce\u0027 on it. I heard you discussing \u0027Nando\u0027s\u0027 with Weasley. I do not know what a \u0027Peri-Peri\u0027 is, but it sounds like a stain waiting to happen.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll be careful,\u0026quot; Draco smirked.","Vernon raised his brandy snifter. \u0026quot;To the suits! And to keeping them clean!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the suits!\u0026quot; the men roared.","Arthur leaned over to Lucius. \u0026quot;So, about this \u0027zipper\u0027 on the garment bag... how does the metal teeth interlock without a Binding Spell?\u0026quot;","Lucius sighed, topping up his glass. \u0026quot;Vernon? You’re up.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Gladly,\u0026quot; Vernon beamed, pulling out his pen. \u0026quot;It’s all about the slide mechanism...\u0026quot;"]},{"num":91,"origNum":91,"title":"The Aluminium Bird","wordCount":931,"paragraphs":["The final logistics meeting was held in the library of Malfoy Manor. The floor was covered in maps, portkey schedules, and luggage tags.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley said, pointing his wand at a schedule. \u0026quot;We have obtained authorization for three Portkeys. One at the Burrow, one here, and one at... ah, Privet Drive. They depart at 6:00 AM. It will be a bit of a squeeze, and the sensation is, admittedly, like being pulled backwards through a garden hose by your navel, but it is fast.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley, who was reviewing a spreadsheet of catering costs, looked up. His face went a dangerous shade of puce.","\u0026quot;Pulled through a hose?\u0026quot; Vernon repeated. \u0026quot;By my navel?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s standard procedure, Vernon,\u0026quot; Arthur beamed. \u0026quot;A bit nauseating, yes. Sometimes people vomit upon arrival. And landing can be tricky—one often falls on one\u0027s face. But it’s magic!\u0026quot;","Vernon slammed his folder shut.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Vernon declared.","The room went quiet. Lucius looked up from a book on Muggle aviation laws he was pretending to read.","\u0026quot;I beg your pardon?\u0026quot; Arthur asked.","\u0026quot;I said no,\u0026quot; Vernon stood up, adjusting his suit jacket. \u0026quot;I am not having my family—or my guests—vomiting on a beach in the Caribbean because of some barbaric magical transport. We are civilized human beings. We are not socks in a dryer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry started. \u0026quot;It’s a long way. The only other way is...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We fly,\u0026quot; Vernon announced. \u0026quot;Properly. In a machine designed by engineers, not wizards.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A plane?\u0026quot; Hermione asked. \u0026quot;Mr. Dursley, booking a commercial flight for fifty people—half of whom are wizards carrying wands and owls—is impossible on this short notice. The security checks alone...\u0026quot;","Vernon held up a hand. \u0026quot;I am not talking about commercial, Hermione. I am talking about \u003cem\u003eexecutive transport\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","He reached into his pocket and pulled out a sleek mobile phone. He flipped it open.","\u0026quot;I am calling in a favor,\u0026quot; Vernon said, dialing a number. \u0026quot;A man named Henderson. I supplied him with the drill bits that saved his oil rig in the North Sea back in \u002798. He owes me. Big time.\u0026quot;","He held the phone to his ear. The room watched in fascinated silence. Lucius leaned forward, staring at the small black device.","\u0026quot;Henderson!\u0026quot; Vernon barked into the phone. \u0026quot;Vernon Dursley. Yes, yes, long time. Look, I’m calling in the chip. The North Sea. Yes. I need a plane. A big one. For a wedding party. Next week. Tuesday.\u0026quot;","Vernon paused, listening.","\u0026quot;No, Henderson, not a Learjet. Too small. I need capacity. I have guests with... large luggage. And peacocks.\u0026quot;","Another pause. Vernon grinned—a shark-like, business grin.","\u0026quot;An A380? The double-decker? Is it fueled? Excellent. Crew included? Good man. Send the bill to my office. We’ll call it a marketing expense.\u0026quot;","He snapped the phone shut.","\u0026quot;Done,\u0026quot; Vernon declared, looking around the room with immense satisfaction. \u0026quot;We have an Airbus A380. Private charter. It’s the largest passenger airliner in the world. It has a bar. It has beds. And it does not pull you by the navel.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Runway Problem\u003c/strong\u003e","The room stared at him.","\u0026quot;An A380?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, his mouth open. \u0026quot;Dad, that’s... that’s huge. That’s like a flying hotel.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Only the best for the Merger,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded. He turned to Draco. \u0026quot;However, there is a logistical issue. Henderson says we need a runway. A long one. Tarmac. Reinforced concrete. At least three kilometers.\u0026quot;","Vernon looked at the map of the island. \u0026quot;Does the villa have a runway, Draco?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It has a helipad,\u0026quot; Draco said slowly. \u0026quot;And a dock.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not good enough,\u0026quot; Vernon shook his head. \u0026quot;We need flat, hard ground. Can you get contractors out there in a week? It takes months to lay tarmac.\u0026quot;","Draco stood up. He walked over to the map. He traced a finger along the dense jungle running down the spine of the island.","\u0026quot;Three kilometers?\u0026quot; Draco asked. \u0026quot;Flat and hard?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Vernon said.","Draco smirked. He pulled out his wand—the hawthorn wand Harry had returned to him.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t need contractors, Vernon,\u0026quot; Draco drawled. \u0026quot;I have magic. I can vanish the trees, level the mountain, and transfigure the sand into stone. I’ll head out there tonight. Give me three hours.\u0026quot;","Vernon blinked. He looked at Draco, then at the phone in his hand.","\u0026quot;Three hours?\u0026quot; Vernon whispered. \u0026quot;To build an international airport runway?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Give or take,\u0026quot; Draco shrugged. \u0026quot;I might add a terminal building if I get bored.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","The room erupted.","\u0026quot;A plane!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley shouted, jumping up. \u0026quot;A real aeroplane! With engines? And wings that don\u0027t flap? Oh, Vernon! Can I sit in the cockpit? Can I press the buttons?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We will ask the captain, Arthur,\u0026quot; Vernon said benevolently.","Lucius Malfoy looked at Narcissa. \u0026quot;We are flying in a... metal tube? In the sky? Without magic?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It has champagne, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa soothed. \u0026quot;Vernon said there is a bar.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ah,\u0026quot; Lucius relaxed. \u0026quot;Then it is acceptable.\u0026quot;","Chloe, Dudley’s wife, looked at Vernon with wide eyes. \u0026quot;Mr. Dursley... you just... you just got a jumbo jet? With a phone call?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s about leverage, my dear,\u0026quot; Vernon said, puffing out his chest. \u0026quot;Networking.\u0026quot;","Dudley clapped his father on the back. \u0026quot;You\u0027re a legend, Dad.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at Hermione and Ron.","\u0026quot;We’re taking a private Airbus to our wedding,\u0026quot; Harry said, shaking his head. \u0026quot;With Lucius Malfoy and Arthur Weasley. And Draco is building the airport.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I love your family,\u0026quot; Hermione laughed.","\u0026quot;I hope the plane has enough room for the broomsticks,\u0026quot; Ron worried. \u0026quot;Do they check for dragons in the cargo hold?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027ll ask Henderson,\u0026quot; Vernon promised. \u0026quot;Right! Pack your bags! We fly on Monday! No vomiting allowed!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":92,"origNum":92,"title":"The Terminal Velocity","wordCount":1260,"paragraphs":["The sunrise over Heathrow Airport was a bleed of industrial grey and orange, illuminating the sleek glass façade of the Signature Elite Class Terminal. It was a place reserved for royalty, rock stars, and apparently, the most eclectic wedding party in British history.","Vernon Dursley stood at the curb, checking his watch against the clock on his phone. He was wearing a travel suit that cost more than his first car, and he was wielding a clipboard with the authority of a five-star general.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed, his voice cutting through the roar of distant jet engines. \u0026quot;The manifest is locked! The luggage is loaded! We have a departure slot in forty-five minutes, and I will not lose it because someone is dallying with a vending machine! Move!\u0026quot;","The convoy of Ministry cars (black limousines enchanted to look inconspicuous, which mostly meant they looked like funeral cars) began to unload.","It was a spectacle that made the airport staff behind the glass desk stop sorting passports and stare.","First came the Weasleys. Arthur Weasley stepped onto the pavement and immediately stopped dead, his mouth falling open. He stared at the automatic sliding doors of the terminal.","\u0026quot;Molly, look!\u0026quot; Arthur gasped, pointing. \u0026quot;They sense us! No wand, no words! Just... proximity!\u0026quot;","He stepped forward. The doors swooshed open. He stepped back. They swooshed shut.","\u0026quot;Incredible,\u0026quot; Arthur breathed. \u0026quot;It’s like the door wants to be helpful.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Move along, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon barked, shepherding him through. \u0026quot;It’s a motion sensor, not a sentient plank of wood!\u0026quot;","Next came the Malfoys. Lucius stepped out of the limousine, wearing a cream linen suit that cost more than the limousine. He looked at the tarmac, then at the terminal building, with deep suspicion.","\u0026quot;It smells of... kerosene,\u0026quot; Lucius noted, sniffing the air delicately.","\u0026quot;It smells of progress, Lucius,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected, ticking him off the list. \u0026quot;And duty-free perfume. Inside.\u0026quot;","Then came the Professors.","It was a sight that defied logic. Albus Dumbledore was wearing a floral Hawaiian shirt (gifted by Harry) tucked into purple velvet trousers. Minerva McGonagall was wearing a stiff tartan traveling coat and clutching a hatbox.","Severus Snape looked exactly the same as he always did—black, buttoned-up, and miserable—except he was wearing dark sunglasses to hide his glare.","Hagrid brought up the rear, ducking low to avoid hitting his head on the sky, wearing a suit the size of a marquee tent.","\u0026quot;Professor!\u0026quot; Harry called out, jogging over with Hermione and Ron. \u0026quot;You made it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Wouldn\u0027t miss it for the world, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed, adjusting his sunglasses. \u0026quot;I have always wanted to experience \u0027The Aviation\u0027. Filius tells me they serve peanuts in tiny bags.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They do,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;Come on. You have to see the security check.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wonder of the Walk-Through\u003c/strong\u003e","The private lounge was a sanctuary of beige leather and free espresso, but the wizarding contingent treated it like a museum of artifacts.","Horace Slughorn was currently mesmerized by a Nespresso machine.","\u0026quot;You put the pod in here?\u0026quot; Slughorn asked a terrified lounge hostess. \u0026quot;And it pierces it? Alchemy! Pure alchemy! And look at the crema! Severus, look at the foam stability!\u0026quot;","Snape, who was standing in the corner looking like a rock star trying to avoid paparazzi, merely grunted. \u0026quot;It is coffee, Horace. Not a potion.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s better than your coffee,\u0026quot; Slughorn sniffed, pressing the button again just to watch it whir.","Meanwhile, Professor Flitwick was having a crisis near the magazine rack.","\u0026quot;Pictures that don\u0027t move!\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked, holding up a copy of \u003cem\u003eVogue\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;How do they know when to smile? They are frozen in a single moment of time! It’s positively haunting!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s printing, Professor,\u0026quot; Hermione explained gently, guiding him away before he tried to charm the cover model.","Arthur Weasley, having conquered the automatic doors, had found the X-Ray machine. The security staff, briefed by Vernon’s \u0026quot;Henderson Connection,\u0026quot; had been paid handsomely to ignore the fact that the guests were carrying sticks instead of weapons.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Arthur said, leaning over the monitor. \u0026quot;You see my... skeleton? Without removing the skin?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, sir,\u0026quot; the security guard said, looking nervous. \u0026quot;It’s radiation.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Radiation,\u0026quot; Arthur tested the word. \u0026quot;Is that a type of vision spell?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dad, please,\u0026quot; Ron groaned, dragging him away. \u0026quot;You\u0027re holding up the line. Malfoy is waiting.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy was indeed waiting. He stood by the floor-to-ceiling windows looking out at the tarmac, sipping a glass of complimentary champagne. He looked entirely at ease, the picture of a young billionaire, until he saw what was pulling up to the gate.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice losing its drawl. \u0026quot;Come here.\u0026quot;","Harry walked over. \u0026quot;What?\u0026quot;","Draco pointed a shaking finger out the window. \u0026quot;Is that... is that it?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Beast\u003c/strong\u003e","Parked on the private tarmac, gleaming white under the morning sun, was the Airbus A380.","It was colossal. It was a building with wings. The tail fin alone seemed to scrape the clouds. The four massive engines hung from the wings like dormant dragons.","\u0026quot;That,\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley announced, appearing behind them with a look of supreme satisfaction, \u0026quot;is the A380. Double-decker. Four Rolls-Royce Trent 900 engines. Range of eight thousand nautical miles. It is the pinnacle of human engineering.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy walked up to the window. He leaned on his cane. He looked at the plane.","He looked at his wand.","\u0026quot;It is... big,\u0026quot; Lucius admitted, his voice small.","\u0026quot;It weighs nearly six hundred tons,\u0026quot; Hermione recited, her eyes shining. \u0026quot;And it flies.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Without magic?\u0026quot; Narcissa asked, looking pale. \u0026quot;Just... physics?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lift and thrust, Cissy,\u0026quot; Vernon said, clapping Lucius on the shoulder. \u0026quot;Lift and thrust. Come on. The Captain is waiting.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Tarmac Walk\u003c/strong\u003e","The doors to the tarmac slid open (Arthur gasped again), and the party walked out into the open air.","The noise was the first thing that hit them—the high-pitched whine of the auxiliary power units, the distant roar of takeoffs, the wind whipping across the concrete.","Hagrid stopped. He looked up at the plane. For the first time in his life, Rubeus Hagrid felt small.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Hagrid whispered. \u0026quot;That’s bigger than a Horntail. That’s bigger than Grawp.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It has a bar, Hagrid,\u0026quot; Harry assured him. \u0026quot;And we took out the middle row of seats in First Class for you. You’ll fit.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thanks, Harry,\u0026quot; Hagrid sniffed, wiping his eyes with a tablecloth-sized handkerchief.","As they walked closer, the sheer scale of the machine became overwhelming. The wheels were taller than Professor Flitwick. The wing was a roof over their heads.","McGonagall stopped at the foot of the stairs. She looked up at the fuselage, then at Vernon.","\u0026quot;Mr. Dursley,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, her voice filled with a rare, grudging respect. \u0026quot;Muggles built this? With no wands? No levitation charms?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Built it, tested it, and fly it every day,\u0026quot; Vernon said, adjusting his tie. \u0026quot;We might not be able to turn teacups into tortoises, Professor, but we know how to get from A to B.\u0026quot;","McGonagall nodded slowly. \u0026quot;Indeed. Ten points to... well, to Muggles.\u0026quot;","Vernon grinned—a shark-like, triumphant grin.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted over the wind, waving his arm toward the stairs. \u0026quot;Boarding call! Destination: Paradise! No broomsticks allowed in the cabin! Let’s move!\u0026quot;","One by one, the wizards of Britain climbed the steps, leaving the magic of their world behind for the magic of aerodynamics, led by a drill salesman who had finally found his perfect kingdom.","Harry paused at the top of the stairs. He looked back at the gray London skyline.","\u0026quot;Ready?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, taking his hand.","\u0026quot;Ready,\u0026quot; Harry smiled.","He stepped into the plane. The doors closed.","And the Flight of the Merger began."]},{"num":93,"origNum":93,"title":"The Metal Tube of Terror","wordCount":1515,"paragraphs":["The interior of the Airbus A380 was not a cabin; it was a flying palace.","Vernon Dursley stood at the top of the stairs, directing traffic with the efficiency of a man who had finally found his true calling.","\u0026quot;Right! First Class, turn left! Economy—ah, who am I kidding, it\u0027s all First Class today! Find a suite! Do not touch the emergency exit lever, Arthur! That is not a window crank!\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley froze, his hand inches from the red lever. \u0026quot;It says \u0027Pull to Open\u0027, Vernon. I was merely testing the hinge mechanism.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sit down, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;Suite 4F. Next to the window. You can watch the wing flaps.\u0026quot;","The wizards filed in, their eyes wide. To a people used to wooden benches and drafty carriages, the plush cream leather, walnut veneer, and ambient LED lighting of the private jet were overwhelming.","Lucius Malfoy approached his seat—Suite 1A—with the suspicion one might reserve for a Cursed Object. He poked the leather headrest with the tip of his cane.","\u0026quot;It is... soft,\u0026quot; Lucius muttered. \u0026quot;Suspiciously soft.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It reclines, Father,\u0026quot; Draco said, settling into 1B across the aisle and pressing a button. His seat hummed and transformed into a lounger. \u0026quot;Massages, too.\u0026quot;","Lucius jumped back. \u0026quot;It moves? On its own? Is it enchanted?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hydraulics,\u0026quot; Hermione explained as she passed by, dragging a terrified-looking Ron toward row 3. \u0026quot;Fluid mechanics. No magic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Muggles sit on fluids?\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, looking horrified. \u0026quot;Barbaric.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Struggle of the Belt\u003c/strong\u003e","Once everyone was seated, the real battle began: The Seatbelt.","\u0026quot;It’s a simple latch mechanism!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted from the front of the cabin, holding up a belt like a flight attendant. \u0026quot;Metal tongue into the buckle! Listen for the click! Tighten across the hips! It is not a torture device!\u0026quot;","Severus Snape sat in seat 6A, wearing his sunglasses and looking like a vampire on vacation. He held the two ends of the belt, staring at them with profound disdain.","\u0026quot;I have bound werewolves,\u0026quot; Snape murmured to McGonagall in 6B. \u0026quot;I have restrained Death Eaters. And yet, I am to be defeated by a strap of polyester?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just click it, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall snapped, though she was currently tangled in her own belt. \u0026quot;It keeps you from... flying about.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can fly about perfectly well on my own,\u0026quot; Snape grumbled, but he clicked the latch.","Hagrid, in the center of the cabin where three seats had been removed to accommodate him, was currently sitting on the floor on a pile of cushions. He held a seatbelt extender that looked like a tugboat rope.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m comfy, Harry!\u0026quot; Hagrid called out. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t worry \u0027bout me! It\u0027s like a cave, but with carpet!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Taxi\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Cabin crew, arm doors and cross check,\u0026quot; the pilot’s voice crackled over the intercom.","Every wizard in the plane jumped.","\u0026quot;The voice of God?\u0026quot; Luna asked, looking at the ceiling speakers.","\u0026quot;The Captain,\u0026quot; Harry said, buckling up. \u0026quot;We\u0027re moving.\u0026quot;","The massive plane lurched. A low, vibrating hum began to shudder through the floorboards.","Outside the window, the terminal building began to slide backward.","\u0026quot;We are moving,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley squeaked, pressing his face against the double-paned glass. \u0026quot;But the wheels... they are rolling? Without a horse?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Engines, Arthur,\u0026quot; Vernon called out from his seat (1C, naturally). \u0026quot;Thrust!\u0026quot;","As the plane turned onto the runway, the hum grew louder. The auxiliary power units whined. The flaps on the wings extended with a mechanical \u003cem\u003egroan\u003c/em\u003e that sounded ominously like a dragon waking up.","Lucius Malfoy gripped the armrests of his suite. His knuckles were white.","\u0026quot;Narcissa,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, staring straight ahead. \u0026quot;If I die in a Muggle tube, I want you to tell the Dark Lord I fought a battalion of Aurors. Do not tell him I was killed by... hydraulics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hush, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, though she had closed her eyes and was clutching her wand.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Spool Up\u003c/strong\u003e","The plane came to a halt at the end of the runway. The brakes hissed.","For a moment, there was silence.","Then, the pilot pushed the throttles forward.","The four Rolls-Royce Trent 900 engines did not just start; they \u003cem\u003escreamed\u003c/em\u003e. A noise like a thousand Banshees filled the cabin. The entire frame of the aircraft began to shake violently.","\u0026quot;By Merlin\u0027s Beard!\u0026quot; Slughorn yelled, spilling his pre-flight peanuts. \u0026quot; The boiler is going to explode!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s just the spool up!\u0026quot; Hermione shouted over the roar. \u0026quot;It’s normal!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;THIS IS NOT NORMAL!\u0026quot; Ron screamed, grabbing Harry’s arm. \u0026quot;NOTHING ABOUT THIS IS NORMAL!\u0026quot;","And then, the brakes released.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Doom\u003c/strong\u003e","The acceleration was brutal. Six hundred tons of metal surged forward.","The G-force slammed everyone back into their seats. To a wizard, speed was usually associated with the wind in your face, the freedom of a broom.","This was different. This was raw, industrial brute force. It felt like being sat on by a Giant.","\u0026quot;WE ARE TOO HEAVY!\u0026quot; Professor Sprout shrieked from row 4. \u0026quot;PHYSICS CANNOT SUPPORT THIS! WE ARE A BRICK! WE ARE A FLYING BRICK!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Slow down!\u0026quot; Flitwick squealed, his legs kicking in the air as the force pinned him. \u0026quot;Too fast! We are going to hit the hedge!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy stopped breathing. He stared out the window as the runway lights blurred into a single streak of terror. He saw the edge of the airport rushing toward them.","\u0026quot;This is it,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, a single tear leaking from his eye. \u0026quot;The Muggles have trapped us. It is a suicide pact.\u0026quot;","Snape gripped his seatbelt with both hands, his sunglasses sliding down his nose. His lips moved in a silent, desperate prayer to forces he hadn\u0027t believed in for years.","\u0026quot;Make it stop,\u0026quot; Ron moaned, his eyes squeezed shut. \u0026quot;I want a Portkey. I want the navel hook. I love the navel hook!\u0026quot;","The plane hit 180 miles per hour. The vibration was teeth-rattling. The noise was deafening.","And then, the nose lifted.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Ascent\u003c/strong\u003e","The floor tilted up at a forty-five-degree angle.","Every wizard in the cabin let out a collective wail of despair.","\u0026quot;WE ARE FALLING UPWARDS!\u0026quot; George Weasley yelled, actually looking terrified for the first time in his life.","\u0026quot;Gravity has been cancelled!\u0026quot; Fred shouted.","The plane shuddered as it left the ground. The wheels thumped into the bay. The wings flexed upward under the strain.","McGonagall clutched her tartan hat to her head. \u0026quot;Albus! Do something! Use a Levitation Charm! We are defying nature!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore, however, was laughing. He was shaking in his seat, beard flying, looking out the window with the glee of a child on a roller coaster.","\u0026quot;Marvelous!\u0026quot; Dumbledore roared over the engines. \u0026quot;Simply marvelous! The sheer audacity of it! Look at the cars, Minerva! They are ants!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I DON\u0027T CARE ABOUT THE ANTS!\u0026quot; McGonagall shrieked. \u0026quot;I CARE ABOUT THE GROUND!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Level Off\u003c/strong\u003e","For ten minutes, the cabin was a tube of pure, unadulterated magical terror.","But then, the roar of the engines faded to a steady, powerful hum.","The steep angle of the floor leveled out.","The \u0026quot;fasten seatbelt\u0026quot; sign dinged softly—a polite, musical note that sounded absurdly calm after the violence of the ascent.","\u0026quot;Ladies and gentlemen,\u0026quot; the pilot’s voice soothed from the speakers. \u0026quot;We have reached our cruising altitude of 35,000 feet. The bar is now open.\u0026quot;","Slowly, very slowly, the wizards opened their eyes.","They were not dead. They were not falling.","Lucius Malfoy peeled one eye open. He looked out the window.","Below them was a carpet of white clouds, bathed in brilliant sunshine. Above them was a sky of piercing, dark blue.","It was peaceful. It was steady. It was... smooth.","Lucius released his death grip on the armrest. He touched his chest, checking for a heartbeat.","\u0026quot;We... are floating?\u0026quot; Lucius asked, his voice trembling.","\u0026quot;Cruising, Lucius,\u0026quot; Vernon called out from 1C, popping a bag of crisps. \u0026quot;Smooth as silk. told you. Henderson gets the good pilots.\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley peeled his face off Harry’s shoulder. He looked out the window.","\u0026quot;We\u0027re higher than a broom,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, awestruck. \u0026quot;Harry... we\u0027re higher than the Quidditch World Cup.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re in the stratosphere,\u0026quot; Hermione beamed, smoothing her skirt. \u0026quot;Isn\u0027t it beautiful?\u0026quot;","Snape pushed his sunglasses back up his nose. He took a deep, shuddering breath. He adjusted his collar.","\u0026quot;Acceptable,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, though his hands were still shaking slightly. \u0026quot;Though the takeoff lacked... elegance.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Elegance?\u0026quot; Hagrid laughed from the floor, untying himself from the cushions. \u0026quot;It was like riding a dragon with a rocket up its bum! I loved it!\u0026quot;","A stewardess appeared, pushing a trolley filled with crystal glasses and champagne.","\u0026quot;Drinks?\u0026quot; she asked pleasantly.","The entire cabin answered in unison.","\u0026quot;YES.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy snatched a glass of champagne before the trolley had even stopped moving. He downed it in one gulp and held out the glass for a refill.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said, the color returning to his cheeks. \u0026quot;I withdraw my objection. The metal tube is... terrifying. But effective.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Metal Tube!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley cheered, raising a glass of orange juice.","\u0026quot;To the Metal Tube!\u0026quot; the wizards roared, as the A380 soared toward the Caribbean, carrying the most powerful, and currently the most relieved, magical assembly in history."]},{"num":94,"origNum":94,"title":"The Altitude Banquet","wordCount":1114,"paragraphs":["The roar of the engines had faded to a background hum, and the seatbelt sign flicked off with a polite \u003cem\u003eping\u003c/em\u003e.","Vernon Dursley unbuckled his belt and stood up, smoothing his suit jacket. He looked like a conductor preparing to lead an orchestra.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, rubbing his hands together. \u0026quot;We have reached cruising altitude. Now, the real show begins. The Henderson Package includes the \u0027Platinum Sky Dining\u0027 option. Prepare yourselves.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dining?\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy asked, peering suspiciously at the small folding table in his suite. \u0026quot;Vernon, we are inside a metal tube in the stratosphere. Surely we are not expecting... hot food? Perhaps a sandwich? A cold pasty?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A sandwich?\u0026quot; Vernon scoffed, looking offended. \u0026quot;Lucius, please. We are not flying economy. We are flying \u003cem\u003eDursley Class\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","He snapped his fingers at a stewardess who had appeared from the galley. \u0026quot;Release the service!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Transformation\u003c/strong\u003e","The cabin crew moved with a synchronized efficiency that rivaled the house-elves of Hogwarts.","They didn\u0027t just hand out trays. They laid white linen tablecloths over the walnut tray tables. They placed heavy silver cutlery—actual metal, not plastic—alongside crystal salt and pepper shakers.","Arthur Weasley picked up a fork, examining it closely. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s stainless steel,\u0026quot; he whispered to Molly. \u0026quot;And look at the napkin, Molly! It’s cotton! At thirty-five thousand feet!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s very civilized, Arthur,\u0026quot; Molly agreed, though she was eyeing the small galley at the front of the plane with professional curiosity. \u0026quot;But how do they cook? I don\u0027t see a chimney. I don\u0027t smell smoke.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Convection, Molly!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed from across the aisle. \u0026quot;Electricity and circulating hot air! No open flames required. Safe as houses.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe First Course\u003c/strong\u003e","The appetizers arrived.","It was a Lobster Thermidor, served in the shell, with a side of micro-greens and a lemon foam.","Ron Weasley stared at the lobster. He looked out the window at the clouds. He looked back at the lobster.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, poking the shellfish. \u0026quot;It’s steaming. It’s actually hot.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Eat it, Ron,\u0026quot; Harry grinned, slicing into his own.","Ron took a bite. His eyes rolled back in his head.","\u0026quot;Bloody hell,\u0026quot; Ron moaned. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s creamy. It’s cheesy. It tastes like it was caught five minutes ago.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was flash-frozen!\u0026quot; Vernon explained loudly to the cabin. \u0026quot;Cryogenic technology! Preserves the freshness instantly! Muggles mastered ice magic decades ago, we just call it \u0027The Freezer\u0027!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy took a tentative bite of lobster. He chewed slowly. He swallowed.","He looked at Narcissa.","\u0026quot;Cissy,\u0026quot; Lucius said, his voice hushed. \u0026quot;It is... exquisite. The sauce has a depth I have only tasted in Paris. And we are... floating?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are floating, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa confirmed, dabbing her mouth with the linen napkin. \u0026quot;It is remarkable.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Main Event\u003c/strong\u003e","The plates were cleared, and the main course appeared.","Fillet Mignon, seared to medium-rare perfection, accompanied by dauphinoise potatoes and glazed asparagus.","Horace Slughorn let out a small whimper of delight.","\u0026quot;Look at the sear!\u0026quot; Slughorn exclaimed, pointing his knife at the steak. \u0026quot;Severus! Look at the Maillard reaction! To achieve this crust without a wand... it is sorcery of a different kind!\u0026quot;","Snape, who was cutting his steak with surgical precision, paused. He tasted the meat. He took a sip of the heavy, oaky Cabernet Sauvignon the stewardess had just poured.","\u0026quot;It is... acceptable,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, which in Snape-speak meant it was the best thing he had ever eaten. \u0026quot;The wine breathing time is impressive given the pressure differential.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the decanter,\u0026quot; Draco noted from row 1. \u0026quot;Aerating spout. I bought one in London. Very efficient.\u0026quot;","Hagrid, sitting on his pile of cushions in the center aisle, was presented with a platter that usually held a whole turkey. Today, it held four steaks.","\u0026quot;Bless yeh,\u0026quot; Hagrid beamed at the terrified stewardess. \u0026quot;I was peckish.\u0026quot;","He ate a whole potato in one bite. \u0026quot;Better than the Great Hall,\u0026quot; Hagrid declared, spraying crumbs. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t tell the elves I said that, but this gravy is thicker.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Technology\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley could not eat. He was too busy interrogating the crew.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Arthur asked the stewardess, holding a bread roll. \u0026quot;You say there is a... \u0027microwave\u0027? It waves... barely? It waves small?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Micro-waves, sir,\u0026quot; the stewardess said, pouring water. \u0026quot;It agitates the water molecules to create heat.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It agitates the molecules!\u0026quot; Arthur shouted to the cabin. \u0026quot;Did you hear that, Lucius? They annoy the water until it gets hot! It’s brilliant!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Please eat your steak, Arthur,\u0026quot; Lucius sighed, cutting a piece of asparagus. \u0026quot;Before you agitate my digestion.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dessert\u003c/strong\u003e","Just when the wizards thought it couldn\u0027t get better, the lights dimmed slightly.","\u0026quot;Dessert,\u0026quot; Vernon announced, leaning back in his seat, a glass of port in his hand. \u0026quot;And for this, I made a special request.\u0026quot;","The crew brought out bowls. They were frosted. Mist curled off them.","Inside sat three scoops of Gelato—Dark Chocolate, Pistachio, and Raspberry.","\u0026quot;Ice cream?\u0026quot; Hermione gasped. \u0026quot;Harry, keeping ice cream frozen on a plane is incredibly difficult. The refrigeration units required...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s solid,\u0026quot; Ron reported, tapping it with a spoon. \u0026quot;Rock solid.\u0026quot;","Professor McGonagall took a spoonful of raspberry. Her stern expression melted instantly.","\u0026quot;Oh my,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered. \u0026quot;It tastes like summer. Albus, try the pistachio.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore was already halfway through his bowl. He had somehow acquired sprinkles (Vernon suspected he had brought them in his pocket).","\u0026quot;I must say,\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared, waving his spoon. \u0026quot;I have eaten at the finest wizarding banquets. I have dined with Vampires in Transylvania and Goblins in the deep vaults. But eating ice cream whilst flying faster than a broomstick in a metal tube filled with Muggle engineering... this is a unique magic.\u0026quot;","He looked at Vernon.","\u0026quot;You have outdone yourself, Mr. Dursley.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","As the trays were cleared and the cabin settled into a food comatose silence, the mood had shifted completely.","The fear of the takeoff was gone. The suspicion of the technology had vanished.","Now, there was only full bellies and a profound, bewildered respect for the Muggle world.","Lucius Malfoy reclined his seat fully flat. He pulled a cashmere blanket (provided by the airline) up to his chin.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius called out softly.","\u0026quot;Yes, Lucius?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The food,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured sleepily. \u0026quot;It was not just adequate. It was... superior. I may need to speak to this \u0027Henderson\u0027 about catering the next Solstice Ball.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll give you his number,\u0026quot; Vernon said, closing his eyes with a smile of absolute triumph. \u0026quot;But he charges extra for altitude.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Worth it,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled from row 3, clutching his stomach happily. \u0026quot;Totally worth it.\u0026quot;","And as the A380 roared through the night sky, carrying the wizarding elite toward the Caribbean, the only sound in the cabin was the soft, satisfied snoring of Rubeus Hagrid."]},{"num":95,"origNum":95,"title":"The Descent into Madness","wordCount":1356,"paragraphs":["The flight had been a lull of false security. For seven hours, the wizarding elite had been lulled into complacency by endless champagne, movies on tiny screens (Arthur Weasley had watched \u003cem\u003eHow It’s Made\u003c/em\u003e four times), and the smooth hum of the engines.","But then, the spell broke.","\u003cem\u003eBING-BONG.\u003c/em\u003e","The \u0026quot;Fasten Seatbelt\u0026quot; sign flashed on. The cabin lights flickered to bright. The pilot’s voice, which had previously been the voice of a benevolent sky-god, now sounded like a harbinger of doom.","\u0026quot;Ladies and gentlemen, we have begun our initial descent into Isla de la Fortuna. Please return your seats to the upright position and stow your tray tables. It looks like a bit of a breezy approach this afternoon.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley woke from a nap, instantly alert. He checked his watch. \u0026quot;Right on schedule! Efficiency! Upright, everyone! Chairs up! Lucius, stop playing with the recline button!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Drop\u003c/strong\u003e","The nose of the A380 dipped.","To a Muggle, this was a standard three-degree glideslope. To a wizard, it felt like the floor had simply decided to stop existing.","\u0026quot;WE ARE TIPPING!\u0026quot; Professor Sprout shrieked, clutching a potted plant she had refused to put in the overhead bin. \u0026quot;THE FRONT IS FALLING!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s just the descent angle!\u0026quot; Hermione shouted from row 2, though she was gripping Harry’s hand quite tightly. \u0026quot;It’s controlled gravity!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;There is no control here!\u0026quot; Snape hissed from behind his sunglasses, gripping the armrests so hard the leather groaned. \u0026quot;We are sliding out of the sky in a metal coffin!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy looked out the window. The clouds had parted, revealing the ocean far, far below.","\u0026quot;Water,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, his face turning a shade of green that matched the Dark Mark. \u0026quot;Endless water. Narcissa, if we splash, do not let my hair get wet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Focus on the horizon, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa commanded, though she had her wand drawn and was pointing it at the ceiling as if threatening the aircraft to stay airborne.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Gear and the Groan\u003c/strong\u003e","The plane descended through 10,000 feet. The air got thicker. The turbulence began.","\u003cem\u003eBump. Jolt. Shudder.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;It’s shivering!\u0026quot; Ron yelled. \u0026quot;The plane is scared! It knows it’s going to crash!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s wind shear, Ron!\u0026quot; Harry laughed, though it sounded a bit manic.","Then came the mechanical noises.","\u003cem\u003eWHIRRRRR-CLUNK.\u003c/em\u003e","The landing gear extended. The floor vibrated violently as the massive wheels locked into place.","\u0026quot;THE BOTTOM HAS FALLEN OUT!\u0026quot; Molly Weasley screamed, grabbing Arthur’s head and pulling it into her shoulder. \u0026quot;THE LEGS HAVE DROPPED OFF!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think they dropped \u003cem\u003eout\u003c/em\u003e, Molly!\u0026quot; Arthur shouted, looking thrilled and terrified. \u0026quot;Like a bird! A metal bird extending its talons!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eREEEEEE-GROAN.\u003c/em\u003e","The flaps extended on the wings. It sounded like a dragon dying in slow motion.","\u0026quot;What was that?\u0026quot; Draco Malfoy yelped, abandoning all pretense of cool. He grabbed Ginny’s hand. \u0026quot;That sounded structural! Potter! Did you pay for the maintenance package?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Vernon organized it!\u0026quot; Harry yelled back.","\u0026quot;VERNON IS A DRILL SALESMAN!\u0026quot; Draco roared. \u0026quot;HE IS NOT AN AERONAUTICAL ENGINEER!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Approach\u003c/strong\u003e","The ocean rushed up to meet them. The island appeared—a strip of green and gold in the blue.","The runway—the one Draco had carved out of the jungle with magic—loomed ahead.","From the cockpit’s perspective, it was a beautiful approach. From the passenger cabin, it looked like they were trying to land a whale on a postage stamp.","\u0026quot;TOO FAST!\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked, his feet kicking in the air. \u0026quot;WE ARE COMING IN HOT!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Brace positions!\u0026quot; Fred and George shouted simultaneously, throwing their hands up as if on a roller coaster. \u0026quot;WHEEEEEE!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;NOT WHEEE!\u0026quot; McGonagall barked, pressing her tartan hat firmly onto her head with both hands. \u0026quot;ALBUS! LEVITATE US!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore was peering out the window, counting palm trees. \u0026quot;Thirty-two... thirty-three... Oh, look, a coconut!\u0026quot;","The ground rushed up. The tarmac blurred.","\u003cem\u003eTHUD-SCREECH.\u003c/em\u003e","The tires hit the concrete. Smoke billowed. The plane bounced once—a terrifying, stomach-churning hop—and slammed down again.","\u0026quot;WE’VE CRASHED!\u0026quot; Hagrid bellowed, covering his head with his arms.","Then, the reverse thrusters engaged.","\u003cem\u003eROAAAAAR.\u003c/em\u003e","The engines, which had been loud before, now sounded like the apocalypse. The plane shuddered violently as it fought to stop six hundred tons of momentum.","\u0026quot;IT’S EXPLODING!\u0026quot; Ron screamed. \u0026quot;THE ENGINES ARE EATING THEMSELVES!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s braking!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted over the noise, looking manic with glee. \u0026quot;Feel that torque! Feel the stopping power! Henderson, you magnificent bastard!\u0026quot;","The plane slowed. The roar faded to a whine. The shaking stopped.","The A380 taxied smoothly to the end of the runway and came to a gentle halt.","\u003cem\u003eBing.\u003c/em\u003e","The seatbelt sign turned off.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Exodus\u003c/strong\u003e","For three seconds, there was absolute silence in the cabin.","Then, pandemonium.","\u0026quot;GET IT OPEN!\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy shouted, unbuckling his belt with fumbling fingers. \u0026quot;OPEN THE DOOR! I NEED AIR! I NEED SOIL!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Evacuate!\u0026quot; Professor Sprout cried, sprinting for the aisle with her plant.","\u0026quot;Out of my way!\u0026quot; Snape snarled, vaulting over the back of his seat rather than waiting for McGonagall to stand up.","The wizarding elite, who usually moved with grace and dignity, turned into a stampede. They jammed the aisle, pushing and shoving.","\u0026quot;Move, Arthur!\u0026quot; Molly urged, pushing her husband. \u0026quot;Before it takes off again!\u0026quot;","Vernon stood at the front, looking disappointed. \u0026quot;Wait for the stairs! The stairs are coming! Maintain discipline!\u0026quot;","Nobody listened. They crowded the door, staring at the handle as if it were the gate to heaven.","When the cabin crew finally opened the door and the mobile stairs (magically conjured by a waiting Bill Weasley) locked into place, it was like uncorking a bottle.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Kissing of the Concrete\u003c/strong\u003e","The tropical heat hit them first—a wall of humidity and the scent of hibiscus.","But the wizards didn\u0027t care about the weather. They cared about \u003cem\u003esolidity\u003c/em\u003e.","Lucius Malfoy stumbled down the stairs, his linen suit rumpled, his hair in disarray. He reached the bottom step, missed it, and stumbled onto the tarmac.","He didn\u0027t stand up. He fell to his knees.","He placed both palms flat on the hot concrete.","\u0026quot;Solid,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered brokenly. \u0026quot;Stationary. Non-vibrating ground.\u0026quot;","He leaned down and pressed his forehead against the runway. \u0026quot;I love you, ground. I shall never leave you. I shall build a house right here.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Father, get up,\u0026quot; Draco hissed, stepping over him. \u0026quot;You\u0027re hugging the tarmac.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am bonding with the earth!\u0026quot; Lucius shouted, clutching the concrete. \u0026quot;Go away! I live here now!\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley ran down the stairs, bypassed Lucius, and sprinted for the grass at the edge of the runway.","He threw himself face-down into the turf.","\u0026quot;Grass!\u0026quot; Ron sobbed, grabbing handfuls of it. \u0026quot;Real, non-flying grass! I missed you! I’m sorry I ever looked at the sky!\u0026quot;","Professor Flitwick tumbled down the stairs and simply sat on the bottom step, hyperventilating. \u0026quot;Too high,\u0026quot; he squeaked. \u0026quot;Too fast. Never again. I shall swim back. I shall swim.\u0026quot;","Severus Snape walked down the stairs with shaky dignity. He stepped onto the ground. He adjusted his sunglasses.","He looked at a palm tree. He walked over to it. He placed a hand on the trunk.","\u0026quot;You,\u0026quot; Snape said to the tree. \u0026quot;You are rooted. You do not move. I appreciate your commitment to stasis.\u0026quot;","He leaned his forehead against the bark and closed his eyes.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dursley Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","At the top of the stairs, Vernon, Petunia, and Dudley stood watching the chaos below.","Vernon looked at the wizards kissing the floor, hugging trees, and eating grass.","He adjusted his cuffs.","\u0026quot;Amateurs,\u0026quot; Vernon scoffed. \u0026quot;Didn\u0027t even appreciate the flap settings on the approach. Beautiful drag coefficient.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a lovely flight, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia agreed, putting on her sunhat. \u0026quot;Though the landing was a bit bumpy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Crosswinds, Petunia,\u0026quot; Vernon said knowingly. \u0026quot;Now, come along. Let’s go find the bar before Lucius tries to marry the runway.\u0026quot;","Harry stood beside them, watching his friends and family losing their minds on the tarmac.","Hermione was trying to pull Ron out of the grass. Draco was trying to peel his father off the concrete. Hagrid was hugging the landing gear of the plane, thanking it for not dying.","Harry laughed. He took a deep breath of the tropical air.","\u0026quot;Welcome to paradise,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;I think we need a drink.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":96,"origNum":96,"title":"The United Nations of Alcohol","wordCount":1196,"paragraphs":["The journey from the runway to the villa was short, accomplished by a fleet of enchanted golf carts that Vernon Dursley drove with the enthusiasm of a man commanding a tank division.","When they crested the hill, the villa revealed itself.","It wasn\u0027t a house; it was a limestone city. Sprawling across the cliffside, gleaming white against the turquoise ocean, stood \u003cem\u003eCasa Fortuna\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;One hundred and twelve rooms,\u0026quot; Draco announced from the lead cart, shouting over the wind. \u0026quot;Fourteen kitchens. Three infinity pools. And a dungeon, though I’ve had it converted into a wine cellar.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A dungeon?\u0026quot; Lucius sniffed, holding onto his hat. \u0026quot;Finally, a civilized feature.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grand Tour\u003c/strong\u003e","They parked in the courtyard, which was paved with marble imported from Italy (by Muggles) and enchanted to repel sand (by wizards).","The group dispersed into the cavernous hallway, their footsteps echoing.","\u0026quot;It’s bigger than the Department of Mysteries,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, spinning in a circle to look at the vaulted ceiling. \u0026quot;And less... murderous.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s efficient use of square footage,\u0026quot; Vernon noted, tapping a pillar. \u0026quot;Load-bearing. Solid.\u0026quot;","The tour took an hour. They saw the Master Suites (assigned to the parents), the Guest Wings (assigned to the couples), and the \u0026quot;Hagrid Annex,\u0026quot; which was actually a converted ballroom with a bed the size of a bouncy castle.","\u0026quot;I fit!\u0026quot; Hagrid cheered, bouncing on the mattress. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t have to sleep in the garden!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We wouldn\u0027t hear of it, Hagrid,\u0026quot; Harry smiled.","Hermione was discovered in the library, which had open walls facing the ocean. She was hyperventilating slightly.","\u0026quot; The books aren\u0027t getting wet,\u0026quot; she gasped, touching a spell-protected volume. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s atmospheric preservation. It’s glorious.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Come on, Granger,\u0026quot; Draco said, leaning against the doorframe. \u0026quot;You can live in here later. It’s cocktail hour.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Bar at the End of the Universe\u003c/strong\u003e","The sun began to set, painting the sky in violent shades of purple and gold.","The party migrated to the South Terrace.","This was the heart of the villa. A massive, open-air deck suspended over the ocean, centered around a bar that looked like it had been stolen from a Las Vegas casino and improved by alchemy.","Draco walked behind the counter. He took off his linen jacket, rolled up his sleeves, and looked at his guests.","\u0026quot;Welcome,\u0026quot; Draco announced, spreading his arms, \u0026quot;to the Universal Bar. I have stocked it with every spirit known to wizard and Muggle kind. If it ferments, distills, or bubbles, I have it.\u0026quot;","The shelves behind him were a dazzling mosaic. Bottles of Muggle Gin stood next to flasks of Ogden’s Old Firewhisky. Expensive Russian Vodka chilled beside Gillywater. There were bottles that smoked, bottles that glowed, and bottles that just looked very, very expensive.","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Draco called.","The elf popped up, wearing a tropical shirt over his tuxedo. \u0026quot;Ready to shake, Master Draco!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Open the tab,\u0026quot; Draco ordered.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe First Round\u003c/strong\u003e","The rush to the bar was dignified but eager.","Vernon Dursley approached the counter. He looked at the glowing bottles with suspicion, then at the familiar labels.","\u0026quot;You have... Glenfiddich?\u0026quot; Vernon asked. \u0026quot;The 30-year?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have the 50-year, Vernon,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, pulling down a bottle. \u0026quot;And I have a chaser of Elven Mead if you\u0027re feeling adventurous.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll stick to the scotch,\u0026quot; Vernon said. \u0026quot;Neat. Good lad.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy drifted over. He eyed Vernon’s drink.","\u0026quot;Is that the Muggle \u0027Scotch\u0027?\u0026quot; Lucius asked.","\u0026quot;Single malt,\u0026quot; Vernon educated him. \u0026quot;Made in Scotland. Aged in oak. Pure chemistry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I shall try it,\u0026quot; Lucius decided. \u0026quot;To show solidarity.\u0026quot;","He took a sip. His eyebrows rose. \u0026quot;It has... peat? Smoke? It is... remarkably complex.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It puts hair on your chest, Lucius,\u0026quot; Vernon clapped him on the back.","\u0026quot;I have quite enough hair, thank you,\u0026quot; Lucius choked, but he took another sip.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Mixology\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley was mesmerized by a blender.","\u0026quot;It spins?\u0026quot; Arthur asked Dobby. \u0026quot;It chops the ice? With blades?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, Mr. Wheezy!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked. \u0026quot;It makes the Pina Colada!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I want one!\u0026quot; Arthur declared. \u0026quot;A Pina Colada! With the spinning blades!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Make it two, Arthur,\u0026quot; Petunia Dursley chimed in. She was wearing a floral sundress and looked ten years younger. \u0026quot;I’ve always wanted to try a cocktail with an umbrella in it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Umbrellas for everyone!\u0026quot; Arthur cheered.","Meanwhile, Snape and McGonagall had secured a quiet table near the railing.","Snape was drinking a glass of deep red wine that smoked slightly—a Vampire vintage. McGonagall had a large Gin and Tonic.","\u0026quot;Peace, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall sighed, looking at the sunset. \u0026quot;Actual peace.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The dunderheads are quiet,\u0026quot; Snape agreed, looking at the group. \u0026quot;And the ocean is... tolerable. It drowns out Weasley’s voice.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Bonding\u003c/strong\u003e","As the stars came out, the groups began to merge in ways that would have been impossible a few years ago.","Harry, Ron, and Dudley sat on high stools, drinking Butterbeer (imported by the crate).","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Dudley said, gesturing to the ocean. \u0026quot;You guys fought giants? Like... Jack and the Beanstalk giants?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bigger,\u0026quot; Ron said, using his hands to show the size. \u0026quot;And uglier. Grawp is okay, though. He\u0027s Hagrid\u0027s brother.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Your friend has a giant brother?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, eyes wide. \u0026quot;Cool.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You box, right, Big D?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Dudley nodded. \u0026quot;Heavyweight division.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Reckon you could take a troll?\u0026quot; Ron asked seriously. \u0026quot;With a good right hook?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If he doesn\u0027t have a club,\u0026quot; Dudley grinned. \u0026quot;Maybe.\u0026quot;","On the sofas, Narcissa Malfoy and Molly Weasley were sharing a bottle of Elf-Made Rosé.","\u0026quot;The boys look happy,\u0026quot; Molly murmured, watching Draco and Harry laugh at something Dudley said.","\u0026quot;They do,\u0026quot; Narcissa agreed. She looked at Molly. \u0026quot;Your daughter... she is good for Draco. She does not let him brood.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’d hex him if he brooded too long,\u0026quot; Molly chuckled. \u0026quot;And Draco... he spoils her. But he listens to her. That’s what matters.\u0026quot;","Narcissa clinked her glass against Molly’s. \u0026quot;To the children. Who are smarter than we were.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Climax of Civility\u003c/strong\u003e","The highlight of the evening occurred when Lucius Malfoy, three glasses of 50-year-old Scotch deep, decided to engage Vernon Dursley in a debate about currency.","\u0026quot;I simply do not understand,\u0026quot; Lucius slurred slightly, waving a crystal tumbler. \u0026quot;Paper money? It tears! It burns! Gold is eternal!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Gold is heavy, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon argued passionately, his face flushed. \u0026quot;You can\u0027t carry a vault in your pocket! It’s about liquidity! Electronic transfer! The Black Card!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The card is magic,\u0026quot; Lucius insisted.","\u0026quot;It’s banking!\u0026quot; Vernon roared happily. \u0026quot;It’s the magic of compound interest!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I like this man,\u0026quot; Lucius announced to the room. \u0026quot;He understands the value of a Galleon. Dobby! Refill Mr. Dursley’s glass! He is teaching me about... \u0027inflation\u0027.\u0026quot;","Harry stood by the railing with Hermione, watching the scene.","Draco was behind the bar, shaking a martini for Fleur. Ginny was laughing with Charlie.","Vernon and Lucius were bonding over capitalism.","\u0026quot;It’s a madhouse,\u0026quot; Harry said softly.","\u0026quot;It’s paradise,\u0026quot; Hermione corrected, leaning her head on his shoulder.","\u0026quot;To the Merger,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, raising his Butterbeer to the stars.","\u0026quot;To the Merger,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled.","And as the waves crashed against the cliffs below and the sound of laughter drifted into the tropical night, the wizards and Muggles of the new world drank to a future that was finally, truly, their own."]},{"num":97,"origNum":97,"title":"The Sleep of the Righteous","wordCount":1273,"paragraphs":["As the night deepened and the last of the cocktails were drained, a pleasant lethargy settled over the villa. The sound of the ocean below was a rhythmic lullaby, promising rest before the chaos of the weddings began.","Draco, acting as the consummate host (and enforcing the strict \u0026quot;No Peeking\u0026quot; rule for the couples), directed everyone to their designated wings.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parents\u0027 Wing\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon and Petunia Dursley were escorted to the \u0026quot;Executive Suite.\u0026quot; It was a masterpiece of colonial architecture, featuring mahogany furniture and a four-poster bed high enough to require a small set of stairs.","Vernon immediately located the climate control panel on the wall.","\u0026quot;Digital,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded approvingly, tapping the screen. \u0026quot;Zoned cooling. I’m setting it to a crisp eighteen degrees, Petunia. Optimal sleeping temperature for maximum REM cycles.\u0026quot;","Petunia was already on the balcony, touching the petals of a night-blooming jasmine. \u0026quot;It’s like a postcard, Vernon. And look—the towels are folded into swans. Two of them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Efficient towel usage,\u0026quot; Vernon agreed, unbuttoning his shirt. \u0026quot;I like this place.\u0026quot;","Down the hall in the \u0026quot;Imperial Suite,\u0026quot; Lucius and Narcissa Malfoy were conducting a structural inspection.","Lucius ran a hand over the bedsheets. \u0026quot;Egyptian cotton,\u0026quot; he murmured. \u0026quot;High thread count. At least eight hundred. Acceptable.\u0026quot;","He walked to the window, where the sheer curtains were billowing in the sea breeze. He poked them with his cane.","\u0026quot;No drafts,\u0026quot; Lucius noted. \u0026quot;And the silence... Narcissa, I cannot hear Weasley snoring. The soundproofing is magical.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is literally magical, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa smiled, taking down her hair. \u0026quot;Draco said he had the walls enchanted. Come to bed. You have a big day of... \u0027relaxing\u0027 tomorrow.\u0026quot;","In the \u0026quot;Garden Suite,\u0026quot; Arthur and Molly Weasley were having a technological crisis.","\u0026quot;Arthur, leave it alone!\u0026quot; Molly called out from the bathroom, where she was marveling at the size of the tub.","Arthur was standing in the center of the bedroom, staring up at the ceiling fan.","\u0026quot;It spins,\u0026quot; Arthur whispered, mesmerized. \u0026quot;It creates wind. But if I pull this chain... does it reverse? Does it suck the air up?\u0026quot;","He pulled the chain. The fan wobbled.","\u0026quot;Ingenious!\u0026quot; Arthur beamed. \u0026quot;I shall sleep directly under the vortex!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Brides and Grooms (The Separation)\u003c/strong\u003e","Strictly adhering to the \u0026quot;Bad Luck\u0026quot; embargo enforced by Vernon and Molly, the couples were split into opposite wings of the villa.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grooms\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter walked into his room. It was simple, white-walled, and faced the ocean.","He sat on the edge of the bed. He looked at the space.","He lay back, spreading his arms. He couldn\u0027t touch the edges of the bed. He smiled at the ceiling. He missed Hermione already, but he knew she was just down the hall. He closed his eyes, listening to the waves, feeling lighter than he had in years.","Ron Weasley’s room was next door. It featured a mini-bar that Dobby had stocked exclusively with chocolate frogs and pumpkin pasties.","Ron was currently bouncing on the mattress.","\u0026quot;It’s a cloud!\u0026quot; Ron shouted through the wall to Harry. \u0026quot;Harry! The bed is a cloud! And I have a fridge! A personal cold cupboard for snacks!\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy took the Master Suite in the East Wing. It was sleek, modern, and lonely.","He flopped onto the bed, staring at the empty space beside him where Ginny should have been.","\u0026quot;Stupid traditions,\u0026quot; Draco grumbled, punching his pillow. \u0026quot;Stupid Vernon Dursley and his flowcharts.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Brides\u003c/strong\u003e","In the West Wing, Hermione Granger entered her room and gasped.","Draco knew his audience. The room didn\u0027t just have a bed; it had a reading nook built into a bay window, stocked with books that had been preserved with anti-humidity charms1.","Hermione ran her fingers over the spines. She picked up a copy of \u003cem\u003eHogwarts: A History\u003c/em\u003e (Tropical Edition) and curled up in the window seat. She wasn\u0027t going to sleep. She was going to read until sunrise.","Ginny Weasley’s room was vibrant, decorated with local flowers. She stripped off her dress and dove onto the bed, stretching out like a starfish.","\u0026quot;Freedom!\u0026quot; she sighed. Then she frowned. She reached for her wand and tapped the wall shared with the boys\u0027 wing.","\u003cem\u003eTap. Tap. Tap.\u003c/em\u003e","A moment later, a knock came back from the other side of the villa (magically amplified).","\u003cem\u003eTap. Tap. Tap.\u003c/em\u003e","Ginny grinned. \u0026quot;Night, Draco.\u0026quot;","Luna Lovegood’s room was in the turret. The ceiling was made of glass, revealing the entire Milky Way.","Luna didn\u0027t get into bed. She lay on the rug in the center of the room, staring up at the stars.","\u0026quot;The Wrackspurts are sleeping,\u0026quot; she whispered to the room. \u0026quot;Shhh.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Professors\u003c/strong\u003e","The faculty wing was a study in contrasts.","Albus Dumbledore’s room was... loud. The decor was bright yellow, and there was a hammock strung between two marble pillars instead of a bed.","\u0026quot;Perfect,\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared, climbing into the hammock with a surprising amount of grace. He produced a nightcap (both the drink and the hat) from thin air. \u0026quot;Rocked to sleep by the sea. Splendid.\u0026quot;","Minerva McGonagall’s room was pristine, featuring a stiff-backed armchair and a bed with hospital corners. She transformed into a tabby cat almost immediately and curled up on the fluffiest pillow, finally allowing herself a moment of pure, unadulterated comfort.","Severus Snape had been given a room in the basement level—at his own request.","It was cool, dark, and had blackout curtains that blocked every photon of tropical sun.","Snape walked in. He locked the door. He sealed it with a Silencing Charm. He checked the wardrobe for hidden Weasleys.","Finding none, he exhaled. He took off his sunglasses. He lay down on the bed in the absolute dark, crossed his arms over his chest like a vampire in a coffin, and fell asleep instantly.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Marauders\u003c/strong\u003e","Sirius Black (who had arrived via a separate Portkey earlier in the day to avoid the Ministry fanfare) had a room on the ground floor with French doors that opened directly onto the beach.","He walked out onto the sand, letting the cool water wash over his bare feet. He looked up at the moon—no longer a source of fear for his best friend, but just a beautiful object in the sky.","He walked back inside, leaving the doors wide open so he could smell the salt air. He slept sprawled diagonally across the bed, a man who had spent too long in a cage and now refused to be contained by blankets.","Remus and Tonks shared a cozy room filled with soft lighting.","Teddy (who was staying with Andromeda for the week to allow his parents a break) was missed, but the silence was a luxury.","Tonks changed her hair color to a soft, sleepy blue. Remus pulled her close. For the first time in forever, the werewolf didn\u0027t look tired. He looked at peace.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Giant\u003c/strong\u003e","And finally, the \u0026quot;Hagrid Annex\u0026quot;2.","The converted ballroom was vast. The bed was, as promised, the size of a bouncy castle, reinforced with ironwood and covered in furs and sail-cloth sheets.","Hagrid sat on the edge, and the mattress groaned but held.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Hagrid chuckled, looking around. \u0026quot;Draco did alrigh\u0027. Plenty o\u0027 leg room.\u0026quot;","He took off his massive boots (which sounded like boulders hitting the floor) and swung his legs up.","He lay back, his head hitting a pillow the size of a sheep.","\u0026quot;Harry\u0027s gettin\u0027 married,\u0026quot; Hagrid sniffed into the darkness, a tear leaking into his beard. \u0026quot;Little Harry.\u0026quot;","He closed his eyes. Within seconds, a snore like a rumbling thunderstorm echoed through the annex, vibrating the floorboards and settling over the island like a protective blanket.","The villa slept. The Merger was resting."]},{"num":98,"origNum":98,"title":"The Drill Sergeant of Paradise","wordCount":1229,"paragraphs":["The sun had barely cleared the horizon, painting the Caribbean sky in soft pastels of pink and gold. The waves lapped gently against the white sand. The villa was silent, a sanctuary of rest for the weary wedding party.","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","The sound was not a bird. It was not a magical alarm. It was a shrill, piercing, mechanical shriek that cut through the tropical air like a knife through butter.","It stopped for a breath, then started again.","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEEEEEET! TWEEEEEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","In the Master Suite, Draco Malfoy fell out of bed, tangling in his Egyptian cotton sheets.","In the Hagrid Annex, the giant snorted awake, looking around for a dragon attack.","In the basement, Severus Snape’s eyes snapped open in the pitch blackness. He did not move, but the temperature in the room dropped ten degrees.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Assembly\u003c/strong\u003e","Ten minutes later, the beach looked like the scene of a shipwreck involving a luxury pajama factory.","The guests stumbled onto the sand, shielding their eyes from the offensive brightness of the morning sun.","Harry Potter stood swaying on his feet, his hair sticking up at angles that defied gravity, wearing a t-shirt that was inside out. Hermione was leaning against him, her eyes closed, clutching a book she wasn\u0027t reading.","Ron Weasley was wearing pajama bottoms with Snitches on them and looked like he didn\u0027t know what year it was.","\u0026quot;Who died?\u0026quot; Ron mumbled. \u0026quot;Is it Voldemort? Did he come back? Why are we up?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a whistle,\u0026quot; Ginny groaned, rubbing her temples. \u0026quot;A Muggle torture whistle.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy emerged from the villa wearing a silk dressing gown that shimmered in the sunlight. He was wearing sunglasses and holding a cup of black coffee as if it were a weapon.","\u0026quot;If this is an attack,\u0026quot; Draco rasped, \u0026quot;I am surrendering. Take the island. Just stop the noise.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy walked onto the sand wearing a long nightshirt and a velvet cap. He looked at the sand touching his slippers with deep distaste.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said, spotting the source of the noise. \u0026quot;Explain yourself. It is... 8:00 AM. The sun has barely bothered to rise.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe General\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley stood in the center of the beach. He was fully dressed. Not in a suit, but in what appeared to be vintage 1980s athletic wear: khaki shorts pulled up high, a white polo shirt tucked in, and a whistle on a lanyard around his neck.","He held a clipboard. He looked energized. He looked dangerous.","\u0026quot;Rise and shine!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed, blowing the whistle again for emphasis.","Snape hissed at the sound, covering his ears.","\u0026quot;We have a schedule!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, tapping his watch. \u0026quot;You lot have been sleeping for hours! While you were dreaming, I have been assessing the terrain! It is perfect! Flat sand! Minimal wind resistance!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;For what?\u0026quot; Sirius Black asked, yawning and scratching his chest. \u0026quot;Are we building a fort?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;For \u003cem\u003eTeam Building\u003c/em\u003e!\u0026quot; Vernon roared. \u0026quot;We are merging three families! We need synergy! We need coordination! We need... Organized Fun!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Organized... fun?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley repeated, looking fascinated. \u0026quot;Is that like a Ministry raid, but with balloons?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, Arthur,\u0026quot; Vernon said. \u0026quot;It is competitive! It builds character! Today, we are hosting the Inaugural Dursley-Malfoy-Weasley Beach Games!\u0026quot;","He gestured to Dobby, who was standing by a table laden with strange objects, looking delighted to be wearing a sweatband over his ears.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Events\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Event Number One!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted. \u0026quot;The Lemon and Spoon Race!\u0026quot;","He pointed to a basket of lemons and a pile of soup spoons.","\u0026quot;You balance the citrus on the utensil! You run to that palm tree and back! If the lemon falls, you are disqualified! No Sticking Charms! No Levitation! Pure gravity and wrist stability!\u0026quot;","The wizards stared at the lemons.","\u0026quot;Why?\u0026quot; Narcissa Malfoy asked, her voice faint. \u0026quot;Why would we carry fruit with cutlery? Dobby can levitate the lemons.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s about \u003cem\u003ebalance\u003c/em\u003e, Narcissa!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;It’s about grace under pressure!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Event Number Two!\u0026quot; Vernon continued, ignoring the groans. \u0026quot;The Three-Legged Race!\u0026quot;","He held up several strips of fabric.","\u0026quot;You pair up! You bind one leg to your partner’s leg! You run as a single, three-legged organism! It teaches cooperation! Communication! If you fall, you drag your partner down with you! Just like a marriage!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy looked at the strips of cloth. He looked at Arthur Weasley. He looked back at the cloth.","\u0026quot;I am to be... bound?\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;Physically tied to another human? While running?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s strictly mechanical, Lucius,\u0026quot; Arthur said, looking eager. \u0026quot;I believe it simulates the gait of a Graphorn.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Event Number Three!\u0026quot; Vernon finished, gesturing to a pile of rough burlap sacks. \u0026quot;The Sack Race!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The what?\u0026quot; Draco asked, lowering his sunglasses to peer at the dirty bags.","\u0026quot;The Sack Race!\u0026quot; Vernon beamed. \u0026quot;You get inside the bag! You jump! Like a kangaroo! First one across the line wins!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Mutiny\u003c/strong\u003e","Silence descended on the beach. The only sound was the waves and the heavy breathing of Vernon Dursley.","Severus Snape stepped forward. He was wearing a long black nightgown that made him look like a dark monk.","\u0026quot;Let me clarify,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, his voice dripping with venom. \u0026quot;You woke us at dawn. To force us to hop in potato bags? And carry fruit?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s spirited competition, Severus!\u0026quot; Vernon insisted.","\u0026quot;It is indignity,\u0026quot; Snape spat. \u0026quot;I am a Potions Master. I do not \u003cem\u003ehop\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m with Snape,\u0026quot; Ron said, raising his hand. \u0026quot;I’m not jumping in a sack. I’m going back to bed. The bed has a fridge.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No one goes back to bed!\u0026quot; Vernon blew the whistle again. \u003cem\u003eTWEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;This is mandatory! We are building bridges! Now, pick your teams! Couples together! Parents mix it up! Professors... you’re the referees! Snape, you watch for cheating! I know you have the eye for it!\u0026quot;","Snape paused. The idea of disqualifying people appealed to him.","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;I shall... adjudicate. Ten points from anyone who drops a lemon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s the spirit!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reluctant Participants\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco stood by the pile of sacks, looking at them with the same expression he usually reserved for Blast-Ended Skrewts.","\u0026quot;I am wearing silk,\u0026quot; Draco hissed to Ginny. \u0026quot;Imported silk. I am not putting my legs inside a farm implement.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, come on, Ferret,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned, waking up at the prospect of competition. \u0026quot;Scared I’ll beat you? I have excellent balance.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am not scared,\u0026quot; Draco sniffed. \u0026quot;I am concerned about the thread count.\u0026quot;","Hermione picked up a spoon. She weighed it in her hand.","\u0026quot;It’s actually quite difficult,\u0026quot; Hermione analyzed. \u0026quot;The center of gravity on a lemon is unpredictable. We’ll need to calculate the optimal velocity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mione,\u0026quot; Harry sighed, rubbing his eyes. \u0026quot;Just run. Don\u0027t do math.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m going to win,\u0026quot; Dudley declared, tying a scarf around his leg. \u0026quot;I’ve been training for this my whole life. Dad used to make me do laps in the garden.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He did?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;Every Sunday,\u0026quot; Dudley confirmed grimly. \u0026quot;The Dursley Games are brutal, Harry. No mercy.\u0026quot;","Vernon clapped his hands. \u0026quot;Right! Lemons first! Line up! To the tree and back! On my whistle!\u0026quot;","The wizards of Britain, the heroes of the war, and the aristocratic elite shuffled to the starting line, holding spoons, glaring at lemons, and resigning themselves to the fact that Voldemort may have been defeated, but Vernon Dursley was a force of nature that could not be stopped.","\u0026quot;Ready!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed. \u0026quot;Steady!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e"]},{"num":99,"origNum":99,"title":"The Citrus Sprint","wordCount":1068,"paragraphs":["The lines were drawn in the sand. On one side stood the \u0026quot;Athletes\u0026quot;—a grumbling collection of wizards holding soup spoons. On the other side stood Vernon Dursley, clipboard in hand, looking like a general reviewing his troops.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;To the palm tree and back! No thumbs on the fruit! One hand behind the back for aerodynamic stability!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;One moment, Vernon,\u0026quot; a calm voice interrupted.","Albus Dumbledore stepped forward from the sidelines, where he had been sitting in a conjured deckchair sipping a coconut. He was wearing his bright yellow swim trunks and the Hawaiian shirt Harry had bought him.","\u0026quot;I cannot help but notice,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, his eyes twinkling behind his sunglasses, \u0026quot;that the faculty is... observing. This seems contrary to the spirit of \u0027Team Building\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are referees, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall said quickly, clutching her scorecard. \u0026quot;We are impartial observers.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Nonsense!\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;To lead is to serve! To teach is to participate! I believe the Professors should run the first heat alongside the students. For morale!\u0026quot;","A collective sound of agony rose from the Hogwarts staff.","\u0026quot;Albus, no,\u0026quot; Snape hissed, recoiling as if struck. \u0026quot;I am a Headmaster. I have dignity. I have black robes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have bad knees!\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked.","\u0026quot;I have a potted plant!\u0026quot; Sprout argued, holding up her fern.","\u0026quot;Put the fern down, Pomona,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said cheerfully. \u0026quot;Chop chop! Grab a spoon!\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley looked at Dumbledore. He nodded slowly.","\u0026quot;Leadership by example,\u0026quot; Vernon stated, writing something down on his clipboard. \u0026quot;I like it. Upper management getting their hands dirty. Good policy, Headmaster. Get in line, Snape! You heard the man!\u0026quot;","Snape looked at Dumbledore. He looked at Vernon. He looked at the lemon Dobby was holding out to him.","\u0026quot;I loathe you all,\u0026quot; Snape whispered. But he took the spoon.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Race\u003c/strong\u003e","The competitors lined up. It was a bizarre tableau.","In Lane 1: Harry Potter and Dudley Dursley. They stood differently from the others. They were crouched slightly, knees bent, spoons held with a loose, practiced grip. They exchanged a look—a flashback to the backyard of Number Four, where Vernon used to make them race for the last slice of cake1.","In Lane 2: Draco Malfoy, holding his spoon as far away from his body as possible, as if the lemon were radioactive.","In Lane 3: Ron Weasley, who was trying to balance the lemon by staring at it intensely.","In Lane 4: Hermione Granger, who was whispering \u0026quot;physics... center of mass... steady velocity...\u0026quot; to herself.","In Lane 5: The Professors. Snape held his spoon like a wand. McGonagall held hers like a scepter. Dumbledore held his like a party favor.","\u0026quot;On my whistle!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed. \u0026quot;Three... Two... One!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e 2","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Start\u003c/strong\u003e","The explosion of movement was chaotic.","Arthur Weasley immediately dropped his lemon. He didn\u0027t pick it up. He picked up the spoon instead.","\u0026quot;Fascinating!\u0026quot; Arthur shouted. \u0026quot;The concavity is perfect for the curvature of the fruit! Muggles have thought of everything!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy took one step. His lemon rolled off. He looked at it on the sand.","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Lucius barked instinctively. \u0026quot;Fetch.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;DISQUALIFIED!\u0026quot; Vernon roared. \u0026quot;No assistance! You\u0027re out, Malfoy!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Leaders\u003c/strong\u003e","At the front of the pack, it wasn\u0027t a race. It was a clinic.","Harry and Dudley moved in perfect synchronization. They didn\u0027t run; they used the \u0026quot;Dursley Shuffle\u0026quot;—a rapid, flat-footed glide that kept the upper body almost perfectly still.","\u0026quot;Knees soft!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted to Harry. \u0026quot;Watch the wind shear!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I got it, Big D!\u0026quot; Harry called back, his lemon rock-steady.","They had done this a hundred times. They had raced for chocolate bars. They had raced to avoid chores. This was muscle memory.","They reached the palm tree turn-around point simultaneously. They pivoted with the grace of ballet dancers (or very large, coordinated swans) and headed back.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Pack\u003c/strong\u003e","Behind them, chaos reigned.","Draco Malfoy was walking with agonizing slowness.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t fall,\u0026quot; Draco whispered to his fruit. \u0026quot;I am a Malfoy. We do not drop things. We hold onto power. You are power. You are a yellow orb of power.\u0026quot;","Ginny Weasley zoomed past him, her tongue sticking out in concentration. \u0026quot;Too slow, Ferret!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am going for accuracy!\u0026quot; Draco yelled back.","Snape was surprisingly good. He moved like a vampire gliding across a floor. His hand was stone still. He was actually in third place.","But then, disaster struck.","George Weasley, from the sidelines, whispered, \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eAccio Lemon\u003c/em\u003e .\u0026quot;","It wasn\u0027t a strong spell, just a nudge. But it was enough.","Snape’s lemon wobbled. It tipped. It fell.","Snape stopped. He stared at the lemon in the sand. He looked up at George.","\u0026quot;Detention,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice carrying over the waves. \u0026quot;Forever.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Finish\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry and Dudley crossed the finish line side-by-side, their lemons still perfectly perched.","\u0026quot;WINNERS!\u0026quot; Vernon blew the whistle. \u0026quot;The Potter-Dursley Alliance takes the gold! Textbook form! Look at that wrist stability!\u0026quot;","Harry grabbed the lemon and spiked it into the sand like a Quidditch ball. Dudley high-fived him so hard it echoed.","\u0026quot;Still got it!\u0026quot; Dudley laughed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Standings\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry Potter \u0026amp; Dudley Dursley:\u003c/strong\u003e (Tied). Experience triumphed over magic.","\u003cstrong\u003eGinny Weasley:\u003c/strong\u003e Her Seeker skills gave her excellent hand-eye coordination.","\u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore:\u003c/strong\u003e He hadn\u0027t run. He had sort of skipped. And he might have stuck the lemon to the spoon with a little bit of wandless magic, but nobody was brave enough to check.","\u003cstrong\u003eLuna Lovegood:\u003c/strong\u003e She had walked backward the entire time because \u0026quot;the Nargles expect you to go forward.\u0026quot; Her lemon stayed on.","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco Malfoy:\u003c/strong\u003e He finished, but he looked exhausted from the stress. \u0026quot;I need a drink,\u0026quot; Draco panted. \u0026quot;The citrus... it mocks me.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHermione Granger:\u003c/strong\u003e She had over-calculated the wind resistance and tripped over her own feet trying to adjust her vector.","\u003cstrong\u003eRon Weasley:\u003c/strong\u003e He ate his lemon halfway through. \u0026quot;I got hungry,\u0026quot; Ron shrugged. \u0026quot;And it looked like a Snitch.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Losers\u003c/strong\u003e","Lucius Malfoy was still at the starting line, poking his lemon with his cane.","\u0026quot;It is defective,\u0026quot; Lucius announced to Narcissa. \u0026quot;It is not spherical. It is lopsided. I demand a recount.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is a fruit, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa sighed.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon clapped his hands, looking at his stopwatch. \u0026quot;Excellent warm-up! But that was just the appetizer! Prepare yourselves! The Three-Legged Race is next! And for this... you need to get intimate!\u0026quot;","Draco groaned, burying his face in his hands. \u0026quot;If I have to be tied to Weasley, I am swimming home.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":100,"origNum":100,"title":"The Three-Legged Catastrophe","wordCount":1257,"paragraphs":["The sun beat down on the white sands of Isla de la Fortuna. The palm trees swayed. The ocean sparkled.","And fifty grown adults were currently hopping around on one leg, trying to maintain their dignity while Vernon Dursley tied them together with lengths of bright orange sash.","\u0026quot;Tight knots!\u0026quot; Vernon barked, yanking a knot so hard Lucius Malfoy gasped. \u0026quot;We want structural integrity! You are no longer two individuals! You are a single, three-legged entity! You must think as one! Move as one! And for the love of God, don\u0027t pull a hamstring!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Pairings\u003c/strong\u003e","The lineup was a recipe for disaster.","The Grooms: Harry Potter was tied to Draco Malfoy.","Draco was looking at his leg—encased in his dove-grey bespoke linen trousers—which was now lashed firmly to Harry’s denim-clad calf.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco hissed. \u0026quot;If you trip... if you drag me into the sand... I will sue you. I will sue you for emotional damages and dry cleaning.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just move your left leg when I move my right,\u0026quot; Harry muttered, testing the bond. \u0026quot;And don\u0027t elbow me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I make no promises. My elbows are sharp. It’s genetic.\u0026quot;","The Heavyweights: Ron Weasley was tied to Dudley Dursley.","They looked like a siege tower. Ron was tall and lanky; Dudley was a wall of muscle. Together, they blocked out the sun.","\u0026quot;Right, Big D,\u0026quot; Ron said, bouncing on his free leg. \u0026quot;We have the stride advantage. We’re basically a giant. We just need momentum.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll count,\u0026quot; Dudley grunted, looking focused. \u0026quot;One, two, STOMP. Got it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Got it.\u0026quot;","The Brides: Hermione Granger was tied to Ginny Weasley.","Hermione was currently stretching her hamstrings. \u0026quot;The key is rhythm, Ginny. A steady cadence of sixty beats per minute.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The key is speed, Hermione,\u0026quot; Ginny countered, tying her hair back. \u0026quot;We sprint. If we fall, we roll.\u0026quot;","The Wildcards: Luna Lovegood was tied to Chloe (Dudley’s wife).","They were both barefoot. Luna was braiding blades of grass into the binding sash.","\u0026quot;I think if we hop in a spiral pattern, we’ll confuse the sand,\u0026quot; Luna suggested.","\u0026quot;I’ve never hopped in a spiral,\u0026quot; Chloe admitted. \u0026quot;But I’m game. This is the weirdest honeymoon ever.\u0026quot;","The Parents: Arthur Weasley was tied to Lucius Malfoy.","Lucius looked like a man marching to the gallows. He stood stiff as a board, refusing to look down at his leg, which was intimately acquainted with Arthur’s worn robes.","\u0026quot;Fascinating friction,\u0026quot; Arthur noted, wiggling his ankle. \u0026quot;The sash creates a pivot point!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Arthur,\u0026quot; Lucius said through gritted teeth. \u0026quot;If you speak of pivots again, I shall hex you. Just... do not let me fall. The indignity would kill me.\u0026quot;","The Mothers: Molly Weasley was tied to Narcissa Malfoy.","\u0026quot;We are going to win,\u0026quot; Molly declared, her competitive spirit flaring. \u0026quot;I raised seven children. I can coordinate a three-legged run in my sleep.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I survived the Dark Lord,\u0026quot; Narcissa replied coolly, hiking up her silk skirt. \u0026quot;I can survive a sack race. Lead the way, Molly.\u0026quot;","The Professors: Severus Snape was tied to Minerva McGonagall.","Snape looked murderous. He was wearing his black robes (he refused to change), which were hitched up to reveal pale, knobby ankles and black socks.","\u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape growled. \u0026quot;If you attempt to skip, I will sever the bond.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We will march, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall snapped. \u0026quot;With military precision. Left, right, left. Do try to keep up.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Race Begins\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon stood at the finish line, whistle raised. \u0026quot;On your marks! Get set!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Start\u003c/strong\u003e","The beach exploded into chaos.","The Heavyweights: Ron and Dudley surged forward. They didn\u0027t hop; they galloped.","\u0026quot;ONE! TWO! STOMP!\u0026quot; Dudley roared.","\u0026quot;ONE! TWO! STOMP!\u0026quot; Ron echoed.","They were a freight train. Sand flew in their wake. They were gaining speed with every step, their sheer mass making them unstoppable.","The Grooms: Harry and Draco were a mess of conflicting strategies.","\u0026quot;Left!\u0026quot; Harry yelled.","\u0026quot;My left or your left?\u0026quot; Draco panicked.","\u0026quot;THE ONLY LEFT!\u0026quot;","They wobbled, corrected, and then Draco tried to be elegant while Harry tried to be fast. The result was a strange, loping gait that looked like a drunken crab.","\u0026quot;Pick up your knees, Potter!\u0026quot; Draco shouted. \u0026quot;You have the grace of a flobberworm!\u0026quot;","The Parents:","Arthur and Lucius were a tragedy in motion. Arthur was enthusiastic (\u0026quot;Weeee! Look at us go, Lucius!\u0026quot;). Lucius was trying to glide, which is impossible when attached to a man who runs like a excited puppy.","\u0026quot;Slow down!\u0026quot; Lucius gasped, clutching his cane. \u0026quot;My hip! My dignity!\u0026quot;","Arthur tripped. He went down. He dragged Lucius with him.","Lucius Malfoy, Patriarch of the House, hit the sand face-first.","\u0026quot;I resign!\u0026quot; Lucius’s muffled voice came from the beach. \u0026quot;Leave me here! I am a crab now!\u0026quot;","The Mothers:","Molly and Narcissa were a terrifyingly efficient unit. Molly shouted the cadence (\u0026quot;STEP! STEP! STEP!\u0026quot;), and Narcissa executed it with ruthless precision. They stepped over the fallen Lucius without breaking stride.","\u0026quot;Sorry, dear!\u0026quot; Narcissa called back to her husband. \u0026quot;We’re winning!\u0026quot;","The Professors:","Snape and McGonagall were not winning. They were arguing.","\u0026quot;You are dragging!\u0026quot; McGonagall scolded.","\u0026quot;I am pacing myself!\u0026quot; Snape snarled. \u0026quot;I am not a racehorse!\u0026quot;","In a fit of pique, Snape stopped moving entirely, forcing McGonagall to pivot around him like a tetherball.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Finish\u003c/strong\u003e","It came down to the wire.","Ahead of the pack, the Ron-Dudley Juggernaut was thundering toward the palm tree. They had built up so much momentum that stopping was no longer an option.","\u0026quot;WE CAN\u0027T STOP!\u0026quot; Ron screamed, seeing the tree rushing closer.","\u0026quot;HIT THE TREE!\u0026quot; Dudley commanded. \u0026quot;IT’S THE ONLY WAY!\u0026quot;","They slammed into the palm tree with a force that shook coconuts loose. They rebounded, spun around, and charged back toward the finish line.","Behind them, Harry and Draco had finally found their rhythm.","\u0026quot;Sync up!\u0026quot; Harry yelled. \u0026quot;Quidditch reflexes!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Seeker speed!\u0026quot; Draco agreed.","They matched strides. They accelerated. They were flying. They passed the fallen Lucius. They passed the arguing Professors.","\u0026quot;We’re going to catch them!\u0026quot; Draco shouted, his competitive streak erasing his vanity. \u0026quot;Run, Potter! Run like the Dark Lord is chasing you!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s dead!\u0026quot; Harry yelled back.","\u0026quot;Run like my mother is chasing you!\u0026quot;","But it was too late.","Ron and Dudley, red-faced, sweating, and roaring like berserkers, crossed the line.","They didn\u0027t stop. They couldn\u0027t. They ran past Vernon, ran past the buffet table, and plowed straight into the ocean.","\u003cem\u003eSPLASH.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Winners\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon blew the whistle. \u0026quot;WINNERS! WEASLEY AND DURSLEY! THE HEAVYWEIGHT DIVISION!\u0026quot;","Harry and Draco collapsed across the line a second later, gasping for air, untying the sash frantically.","\u0026quot;We lost,\u0026quot; Draco panted, lying on his back in the sand. \u0026quot;We lost to a Weasley and a Muggle boxer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They had... mass,\u0026quot; Harry wheezed. \u0026quot;Physics was on their side.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","Out in the ocean, Ron and Dudley surfaced, high-fiving each other in the waves.","\u0026quot;We are champions!\u0026quot; Ron cheered. \u0026quot;We are the Kings of the Three Legs!\u0026quot;","On the beach, Narcissa was helping Lucius up. He was covered in sand. He had sand in his hair. He had sand in his pockets.","\u0026quot;I loathe sand,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, shaking his robes. \u0026quot;It gets everywhere.\u0026quot;","McGonagall was glaring at Snape. \u0026quot;You sabotaged us, Severus.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I preserved my knees, Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape replied smoothly, vanishing the sash with a tap of his wand. \u0026quot;A strategic victory.\u0026quot;","And Vernon Dursley stood on the sidelines, ticking a box on his clipboard with a flourish.","\u0026quot;Excellent!\u0026quot; Vernon beamed. \u0026quot;Synergy achieved! Now... grab a sack! The Sack Race starts in two minutes! And this time... no mercy!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh god,\u0026quot; Draco groaned, covering his eyes. \u0026quot;Someone Stupefy me.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":101,"origNum":101,"title":"The Kangaroo and the Headmaster","wordCount":1375,"paragraphs":["The beach of Isla de la Fortuna had been transformed into a gauntlet of burlap.","Vernon Dursley stood by the pile of sacks, shaking one out to demonstrate its structural integrity. Dust flew into the sea breeze.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;The Sack Race! The ultimate test of lower-body plyometrics and rhythmic coordination! You get inside! You hold the rim! You hop! It is simple! It is brutal!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is degrading,\u0026quot; Severus Snape muttered, staring at the sack Dobby had laid at his feet.","\u0026quot;Come now, Severus!\u0026quot; Dumbledore called out cheerfully. He was already standing inside his sack, which he had pulled up to his armpits. With his sunglasses and Hawaiian shirt, he looked like a very festive potato.","\u0026quot;It’s good for the calves! Minerva, hop in! Pomona, secure your greenery!\u0026quot;","McGonagall sighed the sigh of a woman who had survived three wizarding wars only to be defeated by a team-building exercise. She stepped into her sack with immense dignity, hiking her tartan skirt up.","\u0026quot;If anyone takes a photograph,\u0026quot; McGonagall announced to the students, \u0026quot;I will transfigure their camera into a venomous snake.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Noted,\u0026quot; Colin Creevey (who was hiding in the bushes with a camera) whispered, lowering his lens.","Lucius Malfoy was examining his sack with the tip of his wand. \u0026quot;Is this... jute? It is incredibly scratchy. It will exfoliate my shins against my will.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get in the bag, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon ordered. \u0026quot;We’re burning daylight! On the line!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lineup\u003c/strong\u003e","Fifty sacks lined up on the sand.","Harry and Dudley stood next to each other. They exchanged a nod. They knew the drill. Low center of gravity. Short, rapid hops.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t go for height,\u0026quot; Dudley whispered. \u0026quot;Go for frequency. Machine gun hops.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Got it,\u0026quot; Harry said, gripping the burlap.","Draco Malfoy was standing next to Ginny. He looked miserable.","\u0026quot;I am a Malfoy,\u0026quot; Draco hissed. \u0026quot;I do not hop. I stride. I glide. This is undignified.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just don\u0027t fall on your face, Ferret,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned, tightening her grip on her sack. She looked focused. She looked dangerous.","Ron Weasley was trying to widen the bottom of his sack with his feet. \u0026quot;My feet are too big! I’m going to tip over! I’m a toppling tower!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ready!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, whistle in mouth. \u0026quot;Steady!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Launch\u003c/strong\u003e","The beach exploded into a flurry of brown fabric.","Harry and Dudley shot off the line like cannonballs.","\u003cem\u003eThump-thump-thump-thump.\u003c/em\u003e","Their technique was flawless. They didn\u0027t jump high; they barely cleared the sand, their feet moving like pistons. They surged ahead of the pack, leaving a cloud of sand in their wake.","\u0026quot;Look at them go!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered. \u0026quot;Dursley technique! Low drag!\u0026quot;","Behind them, chaos reigned.","Ron tried a massive leap, achieved impressive height, and then realized he had no way to land safely. He tipped forward and face-planted into the sand with a muffled \u0026quot;OOF.\u0026quot;","Hermione was trying to calculate the trajectory of each hop, which resulted in her moving very slowly and methodically.","\u0026quot;Hop... calculate... hop... calculate...\u0026quot;","Draco was shuffling. He refused to bend his knees. He looked like a penguin trying to march.","\u0026quot;I hate this,\u0026quot; Draco muttered with every shuffle. \u0026quot;I hate this. I hate this.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Kangaroo\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry and Dudley were halfway to the finish line. They were neck-and-neck.","\u0026quot;We got this!\u0026quot; Harry panted. \u0026quot;Easy win!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t look back!\u0026quot; Dudley warned.","Suddenly, a sound cut through the thumping.","\u003cem\u003eWHOOSH. BOING. WHOOSH. BOING.\u003c/em\u003e","It sounded like a hydraulic press.","Harry glanced to his left. His eyes widened.","Ginny Weasley was not hopping. She was launching herself.","She had somehow channeled her Quidditch strength into her legs. She was clearing six feet with every bound. She looked, quite literally, like a kangaroo on steroids.","\u0026quot;See ya!\u0026quot; Ginny yelled as she flew past them at altitude.","She hit the sand, compressed like a spring, and launched again. She was a blur of red hair and burlap.","\u0026quot;Blimey!\u0026quot; Dudley gasped, stumbling slightly. \u0026quot;She\u0027s got springs in her shoes!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Headmaster’s Secret\u003c/strong\u003e","But Ginny wasn\u0027t the only surprise.","Coming up on the right, moving with a bizarre, floaty grace, was Albus Dumbledore.","He wasn\u0027t sweating. He wasn\u0027t panting. He was bouncing.","His long white beard trailed behind him like a comet\u0027s tail. He seemed to hang in the air for a second longer than gravity should allow before touching down and popping back up.","\u0026quot;Wheeeee!\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled as he bounded past a struggling Lucius Malfoy (who had fallen over and was currently shouting for a lawyer).","\u0026quot;How is he doing that?\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, watching the Headmaster overtake Draco.","\u0026quot;Magic knees!\u0026quot; Ron shouted from the ground where he was still trying to stand up.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Finish\u003c/strong\u003e","Ginny Weasley crossed the finish line with a final, massive leap that carried her clear over the buffer zone and into the waiting arms of Bill Weasley.","\u0026quot;WINNER!\u0026quot; Vernon blew the whistle. \u0026quot;GINNY WEASLEY! UNSTOPPABLE!\u0026quot;","Seconds later, Harry and Dudley lunged for the line. Harry threw himself forward, just edging out his cousin.","\u0026quot;SECOND PLACE, HARRY POTTER!\u0026quot;","And then, with a soft \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e, Albus Dumbledore landed across the line, straightened his sunglasses, and bowed to the stunned crowd.","\u0026quot;THIRD PLACE, ALBUS DUMBLEDORE!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Rest of the Pack\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eDudley Dursley:\u003c/strong\u003e (Close fourth).","\u003cstrong\u003eLuna Lovegood:\u003c/strong\u003e She had hopped sideways. \u0026quot;It’s faster if you don\u0027t look where you\u0027re going.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eSeverus Snape:\u003c/strong\u003e He had adopted a strategy of tiny, furious hops fueled by pure rage. He crossed the line, ripped the sack off, and vanished it into non-existence with a slash of his wand.","\u003cstrong\u003eMcGonagall:\u003c/strong\u003e Dignified to the last.","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco Malfoy:\u003c/strong\u003e He crossed the line, stepped out of the sack, and immediately cast \u003cem\u003eScourgify\u003c/em\u003e on his trousers. \u0026quot;Burn it,\u0026quot; he ordered Dobby. \u0026quot;Burn the sack.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","The group collapsed on the sand, gasping for air.","Everyone was staring at Dumbledore. The centenarian wizard was not even out of breath. He was eating a sherbet lemon.","\u0026quot;Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall wheezed, leaning against a palm tree. \u0026quot;How? You are... one hundred and fifty.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yoga, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled. \u0026quot;And a healthy appreciation for rhythm. I found the sack quite liberating! Like a cocoon!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You moved like a rubber ball,\u0026quot; Ron said, eyeing the Headmaster suspiciously. \u0026quot;Did you use a Cheering Charm on your legs?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I merely embraced the bounce, Ronald,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled.","Vernon Dursley walked over to Dumbledore and shook his hand.","\u0026quot;Impressive form, Headmaster,\u0026quot; Vernon noted. \u0026quot;Good extension. You’d make a fine addition to the Grunnings softball team.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I shall keep my schedule open, Vernon,\u0026quot; Dumbledore promised.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Twist\u003c/strong\u003e","The sun was high in the sky. The games were done. The adrenaline was fading, replaced by the deep, grumbling hunger of fifty people who had spent the morning hopping on a beach.","\u0026quot;Breakfast!\u0026quot; Ron shouted, pointing toward the villa where the smell of bacon was wafting down. \u0026quot;I need eggs! I need toast! I need to eat my weight in sausages!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the villa!\u0026quot; Vernon agreed, wiping his forehead. \u0026quot;Games concluded! Excellent effort! Showers and food!\u0026quot;","The group began to move, a mass of weary but happy bodies trudging toward the promise of food.","\u0026quot;Wait!\u0026quot;","The voice was calm, but it stopped them in their tracks.","Albus Dumbledore was standing by the pile of discarded sacks. He held up a hand.","\u0026quot;Before we depart for sustenance,\u0026quot; Dumbledore announced, his eyes shining with a dangerous level of whimsy. \u0026quot;I have had... an idea.\u0026quot;","Harry froze. He knew that tone. That was the tone Dumbledore used before announcing they were hunting Horcruxes or breaking into the Ministry.","\u0026quot;An idea, Professor?\u0026quot; Harry asked warily.","\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;Watching us all... hopping... bounding... it reminded me of the importance of \u003cem\u003etrust\u003c/em\u003e. Of reliance on one\u0027s peers.\u0026quot;","He looked around the beach.","\u0026quot;We have raced with spoons. We have raced with legs tied. We have raced in sacks. But we have not yet tested the ultimate bond.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What is it?\u0026quot; Draco asked, narrowing his eyes. \u0026quot;If it involves blindfolds, I refuse.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, it is much better than blindfolds,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly.","He pointed a long, bony finger toward the ocean.","\u0026quot;One final event,\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared. \u0026quot;To truly seal the Merger.\u0026quot;","The group followed his finger. They looked at the ocean. They looked at Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;What is it?\u0026quot; Vernon asked, checking his clipboard. \u0026quot;I\u0027m out of events.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I call it,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled, \u0026quot;The 1 mile foot race.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":102,"origNum":102,"title":"The Dungeon Sprinter","wordCount":905,"paragraphs":["\u0026quot;The Mile Run,\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared. \u0026quot;To the rocks and back. Pure stamina. Pure grit. No sacks. No spoons. No partners. Just you, the sand, and the will to survive.\u0026quot;","A groan went up from the assembly that was loud enough to startle a flock of seagulls.","\u0026quot;Run?\u0026quot; Ron whimpered, clutching his stomach. \u0026quot;I just want sausages. I don\u0027t want to run a mile. I have short legs for my height!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You have long legs, Ronald,\u0026quot; Hermione corrected, tying her shoelaces tight. \u0026quot;Stop complaining. It’s aerobic exercise.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Judge\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;I shall stretch my hamstrings,\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared, rolling his shoulders and preparing to join the line. \u0026quot;I feel quite nimble after the sacks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh no you don\u0027t,\u0026quot; McGonagall interrupted, stepping firmly in front of him. \u0026quot;Albus, you are banned.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Banned?\u0026quot; Dumbledore blinked. \u0026quot;On what grounds?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;On the grounds that you are clearly using Performance Enhancing Charms on your knees,\u0026quot; McGonagall sniffed. \u0026quot;And you cheat. I saw you levitate over a crab in the last heat.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a very aggressive crab!\u0026quot; Dumbledore protested.","\u0026quot;You’re the Judge, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;We need an impartial eye at the finish line. Someone to time us.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore groaned, a sound of deep, childish disappointment. \u0026quot;Oh, very well. But I shall judge harshly. I want to see sweat! I want to see determination!\u0026quot;","He conjured a comfortable armchair and a large stopwatch, sitting down with a huff.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Preparation\u003c/strong\u003e","The beach became a flurry of activity as the competitors prepped for the final showdown.","Vernon Dursley was taking this deadly seriously. He stripped off his polo shirt to reveal a white vest. He began doing deep lunges that made his knees crack like pistol shots.","\u0026quot;Oil the joints!\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, dropping into a squat. \u0026quot;Petunia, check your laces! We are representing the non-magical community! We must show them superior cardio!\u0026quot;","Petunia was doing star jumps with surprising vigor. \u0026quot;I’m ready, Vernon. I’ve been power-walking to the shops for twenty years.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy was casting Cooling Charms on his face. \u0026quot;I refuse to sweat,\u0026quot; he informed Ginny. \u0026quot;Malfoy men do not perspire. We glow.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You’re going to glow red in a minute,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned, stretching her quads. \u0026quot;Try to keep up, Ferret.\u0026quot;","Harry and Dudley were doing synchronized high-knees.","\u0026quot;Pacing, Harry,\u0026quot; Dudley coached, bouncing on his toes. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t sprint the start. Save it for the turn.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Got it,\u0026quot; Harry nodded, focused.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dark Horse\u003c/strong\u003e","Amidst the stretching and the complaining, Severus Snape stood motionless.","He was still wearing his long, billowing black robes. He was wearing his black boots. He looked like a heatstroke victim waiting to happen.","\u0026quot;Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall called out, jogging in place. \u0026quot;You are not running in that? You will melt. It is thirty degrees.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am acclimatized to the heat of cauldrons,\u0026quot; Snape said continuously. \u0026quot;However...\u0026quot;","He looked at the distant rocks. He looked at Vernon Dursley doing squats. He looked at Harry Potter, who was looking fast.","A strange glint entered Snape’s black eyes. It was the look of a man who had been underestimated for the last time.","\u0026quot;Drag,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Aerodynamic inefficiency.\u0026quot;","He reached for the clasp of his heavy outer cloak.","\u0026quot;What’s he doing?\u0026quot; Ron whispered to Hermione. \u0026quot;Is he forfeiting?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think he\u0027s... disrobing,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered back, looking horrified.","Snape undid the clasp. He shrugged his shoulders. The heavy black cloak pooled onto the sand.","Then, he reached for the buttons of his frock coat.","\u0026quot;Oh god,\u0026quot; Draco covered his eyes. \u0026quot;My eyes. I don\u0027t want to see my godfather\u0027s ribs. Dobby, bring me a blindfold!\u0026quot;","Snape removed the frock coat. Then, he grabbed the hem of his black shirt and pulled it over his head.","The beach went silent. The waves seemed to stop crashing.","Underneath the layers of black wool and misery, Severus Snape was ripped.","He did not have the pale, sunken chest of a dungeon dweller. He had the torso of a Greek statue carved out of marble. His abs were defined. His arms were corded with lean muscle.","But it was the legs that truly defied logic. As Snape vanished his trousers to reveal black running shorts, the crowd gasped.","His quads were massive. His calves looked like they had been chiseled from granite. He didn\u0027t look like a Potions Master; he looked like an Olympic sprinter who hunted stag for sport.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Hagrid whispered. \u0026quot;He\u0027s built like a centaur.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Severus?\u0026quot; McGonagall choked out, her glasses steaming up. \u0026quot;When... how...?\u0026quot;","Snape adjusted his shorts. He looked at the stunned crowd with a sneer.","\u0026quot;You think running up and down seven flights of stairs to the dungeons five times a day is not exercise?\u0026quot; Snape drawled. \u0026quot;You think stirring viscous potions for hours does not build core strength?\u0026quot;","He shook out his legs. The muscles rippled.","\u0026quot;I am aerodynamic,\u0026quot; Snape declared. \u0026quot;And I am going to win.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley stopped lunging. He stared at Snape’s legs. He looked at his own legs.","\u0026quot;Petunia,\u0026quot; Vernon whispered, looking concerned. \u0026quot;The wizard has engine blocks for thighs. The strategy has changed.\u0026quot;","Harry stared at his former professor. \u0026quot;I think I\u0027m traumatized,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Ron. \u0026quot;But also... impressed?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m just scared,\u0026quot; Ron squeaked. \u0026quot;He looks like he could outrun a broom.\u0026quot;","Snape crouched at the starting line, assuming a perfect sprinter’s stance. He dug his boots into the sand. He looked like a panther preparing to pounce.","\u0026quot;On your marks!\u0026quot; Dumbledore called out, looking delighted by the turn of events. \u0026quot;Get set!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":103,"origNum":103,"title":"The Speed of Severus","wordCount":1206,"paragraphs":["The starting line looked like the finals of an Olympic event, if the Olympics were held on a private magical island and half the competitors were wearing transfigured beachwear.","Severus Snape, wearing his black running shorts and looking like a statue of a vengeful Greek god, drew his wand. He didn\u0027t hex anyone. Instead, he flicked it at the sand.","\u003cem\u003ePop. Pop. Pop.\u003c/em\u003e","A row of professional starting blocks appeared in the sand—steel, adjustable, and gleaming.","\u0026quot;Blocks?\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley gasped, stopping his lunges. \u0026quot;Starting blocks? That is professional grade! Snape, you are full of surprises. I respect a man who understands traction!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If one is to run,\u0026quot; Snape said, digging his heels into the blocks and shaking out his massive quadriceps, \u0026quot;one should launch properly. Newton’s Third Law, Dursley. Action and reaction.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;On your marks!\u0026quot; Dumbledore called out from his armchair, holding the stopwatch like a holy relic.","Harry, Ginny, and Dudley took their stances. They looked focused. They were the athletes.","Ron stood upright, looking confused. \u0026quot;Do I just... go?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get set!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Launch\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape didn\u0027t run; he exploded.","He fired out of the blocks with a force that kicked up a rooster tail of sand. His form was perfect—head down, knees driving, arms pumping.","Harry and Dudley, relying on their youth and training, sprinted hard. Ginny, fueled by competitive rage, was right with them.","The pack thinned out immediately.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Quarter Mile\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry was breathing hard, the hot air burning his lungs. He was matching Dudley stride for stride. Ginny was half a step ahead of them, her hair flying like a banner.","\u0026quot;We’re leading!\u0026quot; Dudley panted. \u0026quot;Keep the pace!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Where’s... Snape?\u0026quot; Harry gasped.","\u003cem\u003eWHOOSH.\u003c/em\u003e","It wasn\u0027t a wind. It was a person.","A black blur tore past them on the left. It was Severus Snape.","He wasn\u0027t jogging. He wasn\u0027t running. He was sprinting with a mechanical, terrifying efficiency. His face was a mask of grim determination. His legs were a blur of motion.","\u0026quot;On your left,\u0026quot; Snape sneered as he rocketed past, his stride devouring the sand.","\u0026quot;What the...?\u0026quot; Ginny yelled, almost tripping. \u0026quot;He’s fast! He’s really fast!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s not human!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted. \u0026quot;Look at his turnover rate!\u0026quot;","Behind the lead group, the rest of the pack was struggling.","Vernon and Petunia were power-walking with impressive speed, arms swinging wildly.","\u0026quot;Keep the rhythm, Petunia!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted. \u0026quot;Pump the arms! Engage the core!\u0026quot;","Ron was jogging alongside Hermione. \u0026quot;Why is he so fast?\u0026quot; Ron wheezed, watching Snape become a dot in the distance. \u0026quot;He lives in a dungeon! He smells fumes for a living!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Anaerobic capacity!\u0026quot; Hermione panted, clutching a stitch in her side. \u0026quot;He must have... incredible... fast-twitch... muscle fibers!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy was walking. He refused to run. He was using his cane to propel himself forward with dignity.","\u0026quot;I am strolling,\u0026quot; Lucius announced to Arthur Weasley, who was jogging backward to look at the ocean. \u0026quot;I am promenading. I do not sweat.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Turn\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape reached the rocky outcrop—the halfway mark—while the others were barely three-quarters of the way there.","He slapped the rock with a satisfying \u003cem\u003ethwack\u003c/em\u003e.","He didn\u0027t slow down to turn. He banked, kicking up a wall of sand, and accelerated into the return leg.","He passed the trio—Harry, Ginny, and Dudley—going the other way.","Harry stared. Snape wasn\u0027t even breathing hard. His nostrils were flared, his eyes were locked on the finish line, and he looked like a heat-seeking missile made of muscle and malice.","\u0026quot;How?\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;Afterburners,\u0026quot; Dudley groaned, seeing the dust cloud Snape left behind. \u0026quot;He’s kicking into high gear.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Finish\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape crossed the finish line alone.","He didn\u0027t collapse. He didn\u0027t gasp. He ran through the line, slowed to a jog, and then came to a precise halt in front of Dumbledore.","Dumbledore checked the watch. He looked at it. He shook it. He looked at Snape.","\u0026quot;Four minutes and twelve seconds,\u0026quot; Dumbledore read, stunned. \u0026quot;In sand. Severus... that is... superhuman.\u0026quot;","Snape grabbed a towel Dobby offered. He wiped his face. He didn\u0027t smile.","\u0026quot;I have spent seventeen years running from my past, Albus,\u0026quot; Snape said evenly, putting his black shirt back on. \u0026quot;A mile on a beach is trivial.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Battle for Second\u003c/strong\u003e","Far behind him, the battle for second place was heating up.","Dudley, built for power rather than distance, was fading. The soft sand was sapping his energy.","\u0026quot;Go!\u0026quot; Dudley gasped to Harry. \u0026quot;Save yourself! Beat the Weasley!\u0026quot;","Harry and Ginny surged forward. They were neck and neck.","\u0026quot;I’m going to beat you, Potter!\u0026quot; Ginny yelled.","\u0026quot;In your dreams, Weasley!\u0026quot; Harry laughed, pushing harder.","They crossed the line simultaneously, collapsing into the sand in a tangle of limbs.","\u0026quot;TIE!\u0026quot; Dumbledore shouted. \u0026quot;Harry Potter and Ginny Weasley! Joint Silver!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Battle for Fourth\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley was slowing down, his chest heaving.","From behind him, a sleek, grey figure emerged. It was Draco Malfoy.","He wasn\u0027t running fast, but he was running \u003cem\u003elight\u003c/em\u003e. He seemed to glide over the sand.","\u0026quot;Make way for the aristocracy!\u0026quot; Draco panted, passing Dudley.","\u0026quot;No way!\u0026quot; Dudley groaned, trying to sprint, but his legs were jelly.","Draco crossed the line, fell to his knees, and threw his hands up. \u0026quot;Fourth! I take Fourth! I beat the Muggle!\u0026quot;","Dudley stumbled across a second later, collapsing next to Harry. \u0026quot;Sand,\u0026quot; Dudley wheezed. \u0026quot;Hate... sand.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Rest of the Field\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eVernon Dursley:\u003c/strong\u003e He power-walked across the line with a roar of triumph. \u0026quot;Cardio! vascular! Health!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePetunia Dursley:\u003c/strong\u003e Right behind him, not a hair out of place.","\u003cstrong\u003eHermione Granger:\u003c/strong\u003e She calculated the optimal finish and jogged in.","\u003cstrong\u003eRon Weasley:\u003c/strong\u003e He crawled across the line. \u0026quot;I see a light,\u0026quot; Ron whispered. \u0026quot;Is it grandma?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eArthur Weasley:\u003c/strong\u003e He got distracted by a crab and finished late.","\u003cstrong\u003eLucius Malfoy:\u003c/strong\u003e He arrived ten minutes later, looking fresh because he hadn\u0027t broken a sweat. \u0026quot;I enjoyed the view,\u0026quot; Lucius lied.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The group gathered around Snape, who was currently drinking a glass of water with the air of a bored emperor.","Harry looked at his former professor’s legs (now covered by trousers, thankfully).","\u0026quot;Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said, still breathless. \u0026quot;That was... terrifying.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You run like a centaur,\u0026quot; Ron wheezed from the ground. \u0026quot;A very angry centaur.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is called discipline, Weasley,\u0026quot; Snape sneered, though he looked secretly pleased. \u0026quot;Something you lack.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You beat Dudley,\u0026quot; Harry pointed out. \u0026quot;Dudley is a boxing champion.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And I,\u0026quot; Snape adjusted his cuffs, \u0026quot;am the Half-Blood Prince. I do not lose footraces to Muggles.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley walked over. He looked Snape up and down. He nodded.","\u0026quot;Good form, Snape,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted. \u0026quot;Excellent glute activation. We should go for a run in Surrey sometime. Terrorize the neighborhood.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at Vernon. A corner of his mouth twitched.","\u0026quot;Perhaps, Dursley,\u0026quot; Snape said. \u0026quot;Perhaps.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore clapped his hands. \u0026quot;Wonderful! Events concluded! The Dursley-Malfoy-Weasley Games are officially closed! And now... I believe there is a breakfast buffet waiting that is in danger of going cold.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Food!\u0026quot; Ron shouted, resurrecting from the sand.","As the group moved toward the villa, Harry put his arm around Hermione. He looked at Draco helping his father up the stairs. He looked at Snape talking to Vernon about hamstring stretches.","\u0026quot;I love this family,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;We\u0027re weird,\u0026quot; Hermione laughed, leaning into him.","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Harry agreed. \u0026quot;But I’m fast.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":104,"origNum":104,"title":"The Star-Spangled Banquet","wordCount":938,"paragraphs":["The group stood on the sand, knees shaking, lungs burning. The villa, perched on the cliff above, looked like it was miles away.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t make it,\u0026quot; Ron wheezed, collapsing onto a piece of driftwood. \u0026quot;My legs are jelly. I shall perish here. Tell Luna I loved her.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You are not perishing, Ronald,\u0026quot; Hermione panted, leaning against Harry. \u0026quot;But... the incline... it is steep.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley wiped his forehead with a towel. He looked up at the villa. He looked at the tired group.","\u0026quot;Logistical failure,\u0026quot; Vernon announced breathlessly. \u0026quot;Refueling station is too far from the point of exertion. We are running on fumes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Draco called out, not even bothering to stand up from where he was kneeling in the sand.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The elf appeared, still wearing his sweatband. \u0026quot;Master Draco?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bring the breakfast to us,\u0026quot; Draco ordered, waving a hand at the beach. \u0026quot;Here. Now. The Full American package we discussed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;On the sand, sir?\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked.","\u0026quot;On the sand, Dobby. Before Weasley starts eating the palm trees.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","It happened in a blink. One moment, the beach was empty. The next, a long, low table—conjured from driftwood but covered in crisp red-and-white checkered cloths—appeared on the shoreline.","Dozens of house-elves popped into existence, carrying silver platters that smelled of butter, syrup, and freedom.","\u0026quot;Oh, my days,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, staring at the spread. \u0026quot;It’s beautiful.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Spread\u003c/strong\u003e","It was not a delicate continental breakfast. It was a monument to American excess.","There were stacks of buttermilk pancakes—some plain, some bursting with blueberries, others studded with chocolate chips—towering like edible skyscrapers.","There were waffles the size of dinner plates, indented deep enough to hold pools of warm maple syrup.","\u0026quot;Bacon,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, tears forming in his eyes.","It wasn\u0027t the thick British back bacon. It was American streaky bacon—fried until it was shattered-glass crispy, piled high in a greasy, glorious mountain.","There were hash browns—golden, fried triangles of potato joy.","There were scrambled eggs, sunny-side-up eggs, and Eggs Benedict drowning in hollandaise sauce.","And there were \u0026quot;Biscuits and Gravy.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Cultural Confusion\u003c/strong\u003e","Lucius Malfoy approached the table warily. He poked a fluffy, white buttermilk biscuit with his fork.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; Lucius asked, looking distressed. \u0026quot;Why have they covered these scones in... soup? It looks like cement.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s gravy, Father,\u0026quot; Draco explained, piling three hash browns onto his plate. \u0026quot;Sausage gravy. It is a heart attack on a plate. It is delicious.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Scones with sausage gravy?\u0026quot; Narcissa murmured, looking fascinated. \u0026quot;The Americans are a bold people.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley, however, was in his element.","\u0026quot;This is it!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered, grabbing a plate. \u0026quot;Portion control is for the weak! Look at the size of these pancakes! Efficiency of caloric intake!\u0026quot;","He poured syrup over his stack until it cascaded down the sides like a sticky waterfall.","\u0026quot;Syrup,\u0026quot; Vernon lectured a listening Arthur Weasley. \u0026quot;Liquid sugar. Instant energy recovery. Dig in, Arthur!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I shall try the... \u0027Hash Brown\u0027,\u0026quot; Arthur declared bravely. \u0026quot;It looks like a golden brick.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Feeding Frenzy\u003c/strong\u003e","The group descended on the food. They didn\u0027t sit at a table; they sprawled on the sand, plates balanced on their knees, eating with the desperation of people who had just run a mile in the tropical sun.","Severus Snape sat apart, leaning against a rock. He had put his black shirt back on (to the relief of Draco), but he was eating with a terrifying mechanical precision.","He was consuming protein. Eggs. Bacon. Sausages.","\u0026quot;Refueling the engine,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Ginny, watching Snape eat four sausages in under a minute.","\u0026quot;He earned it,\u0026quot; Ginny replied, her mouth full of waffle. \u0026quot;He ran a four-minute mile. He probably needs six thousand calories just to maintain that scowl.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore was constructing a masterpiece. He had taken a waffle, covered it in whipped cream, added strawberries, and was currently sprinkling it with colorful sugary loops he had found in a bowl labeled \u0027Froot Loops\u0027.","\u0026quot;Look at the colors, Minerva!\u0026quot; Dumbledore delighted. \u0026quot;It is breakfast and art combined! A textural symphony!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is sugar with a side of sugar, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall sighed, sipping a large mimosa. \u0026quot;But after that sack race... I believe we have earned a little decadence.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Drinks\u003c/strong\u003e","Dobby reappeared with a trolley sunk halfway into the sand.","\u0026quot;Mimosas!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked. \u0026quot;And Bloody Marys! And Coffee! Black as the night!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Coffee,\u0026quot; Draco groaned, reaching out a hand. \u0026quot;Intravenously, Dobby. Please.\u0026quot;","Ron was currently drinking a milkshake.","\u0026quot;It’s 9:00 AM, Ronald,\u0026quot; Hermione pointed out, dipping her bacon into syrup (a trick Harry had taught her).","\u0026quot;It’s a dairy smoothie,\u0026quot; Ron argued. \u0026quot;It’s healthy. It has calcium. And chocolate.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Satisfaction\u003c/strong\u003e","As the platters emptied and the sun climbed higher, a heavy, satisfied silence fell over the beach.","Vernon Dursley lay back on the sand, a napkin tucked into his collar, patting his stomach.","\u0026quot;Excellent,\u0026quot; Vernon rumbled. \u0026quot;Top tier catering. Henderson really came through.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I quite liked the... \u0027Grits\u0027,\u0026quot; Lucius admitted, looking surprised. \u0026quot;It is like a savory porridge. Very comforting.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I liked the crispy pig,\u0026quot; Hagrid mumbled, picking his teeth with a small twig. \u0026quot;Crunchy.\u0026quot;","Harry looked around at his family.","Draco and Ginny were sharing a plate of fruit, sticky with juice.","Ron was asleep, a half-eaten pancake resting on his chest.","Snape was looking at the ocean, looking almost... relaxed.","Harry leaned back, digging his toes into the warm sand. He held Hermione’s hand.","\u0026quot;Best breakfast ever?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;Best breakfast ever,\u0026quot; Hermione agreed, closing her eyes.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon yawned, checking his watch. \u0026quot;Schedule says... Nap Time. Mandatory. Recovery period. Wake up call at noon for the rehearsal.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mandatory nap?\u0026quot; Ron mumbled in his sleep. \u0026quot;Vernon... you are my king.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":105,"origNum":105,"title":"The Mediterranean Pivot","wordCount":1087,"paragraphs":["The \u0026quot;Mandatory Nap\u0026quot; had been a success, mostly because no one had the energy to argue. But as the sun climbed to its zenith, signaling high noon, Vernon Dursley stirred from his lounger on the terrace.","He checked his watch. He blew a tentative toot on his whistle.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, though he didn\u0027t stand up. \u0026quot;1200 hours! Schedule dictates: Rehearsal! Formation marching! Vow practice!\u0026quot;","From the collection of sunbeds and hammocks, a collective groan rose like a dying beast.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry said simply, eyes still closed behind his sunglasses.","\u0026quot;Vetoed,\u0026quot; Draco murmured, waving a hand. \u0026quot;The grooms are on strike.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The brides are comatose,\u0026quot; Ginny added, not moving a muscle.","Vernon looked at his clipboard. He looked at the exhausted group. He remembered the sheer physical toll of the sack race.","\u0026quot;Rehearsal cancelled,\u0026quot; Vernon declared decisively. \u0026quot;Rescheduled for T-minus 2 days. We must prioritize energy conservation. A tired workforce is an inefficient workforce.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hear, hear,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley mumbled, dozing under a palm tree.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Venue Change\u003c/strong\u003e","Lunch was served not on the beach, but on the Upper Terrace of the villa—a shaded, breezy colonnade overlooking the turquoise bay, draped in bougainvillea and smelling of jasmine.","After the heavy, greasy glory of the American breakfast, the house-elves (under Dobby’s direction) had pivoted hard.","\u0026quot;Light!\u0026quot; Narcissa had ordered. \u0026quot;Fresh! If I see another pancake, I shall scream.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Spread\u003c/strong\u003e","The table was a mosaic of Mediterranean color.","There were silver platters of \u003cem\u003eSalade Niçoise\u003c/em\u003e, arranged with geometric precision—seared tuna steaks, bright green beans, and jammy eggs.","There were wooden boards laden with \u003cem\u003eMezze\u003c/em\u003e: bowls of cool, garlicky Tzatziki, smoky Baba Ganoush, and Hummus topped with pine nuts and paprika.","There were baskets of crusty French baguettes and warm pita bread.","There were blocks of Feta cheese drizzled with honey and sesame, and flaky triangles of \u003cem\u003eSpanakopita\u003c/em\u003e (spinach pie).","And in the center, a massive platter of grilled octopus and calamari, charred with lemon and oregano.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Professors\u0027 Critique\u003c/strong\u003e","The Hogwarts staff approached the buffet with the wariness of people who had eaten their weight in bacon three hours prior.","Professor Sprout was the first to dive in. She picked up a sprig of oregano from the Greek salad and sniffed it deeply.","\u0026quot;Oh, Pomona,\u0026quot; she sighed happily. \u0026quot;Smell that! It’s fresh cut. And the basil in the Caprese? It was still growing ten minutes ago. I can feel the chlorophyll!\u0026quot;","She piled her plate with greens. \u0026quot;Finally! Vitamins! My constitution cannot handle any more fried dough.\u0026quot;","Professor Flitwick was mesmerized by the \u003cem\u003eSpanakopita\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;Look at the layers!\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked, peeling back the phyllo pastry. \u0026quot;Hundreds of them! Thinner than parchment! To achieve this without a Flattening Charm... the elves are artists!\u0026quot;","Minerva McGonagall bypassed the food entirely and went straight for the drink station, which was serving chilled Rosé and cloudy lemonade.","She poured a glass of wine. She took a sip. She leaned against a marble pillar and closed her eyes.","\u0026quot;Civilization,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered. \u0026quot;Actual civilization. No sacks. No running. Just cheese and wine. I may retire here. I shall live in the linen closet.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Potions Master’s Palate\u003c/strong\u003e","Severus Snape approached the table. He had showered and changed back into his usual black attire, though he had conceded to leaving the frock coat off, wearing just the black shirt and trousers.","He picked up a bottle of olive oil. He tilted it, watching the golden liquid slide against the glass.","\u0026quot;Viscosity,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Color. Clarity.\u0026quot;","He poured a small amount onto a piece of baguette. He tasted it.","Harry watched him nervously. \u0026quot;Is it okay, Professor?\u0026quot;","Snape chewed slowly. He looked at the bottle.","\u0026quot;Cold-pressed,\u0026quot; Snape deduced. \u0026quot;Extra virgin. Low acidity. Peppery finish. It is... chemically sound.\u0026quot;","He moved to the Greek salad. He inspected a Kalamata olive.","\u0026quot;The brine balance is precise,\u0026quot; Snape noted. \u0026quot;Sodium levels adequate for rehydration after... exertion.\u0026quot;","He filled his plate with olives, feta, and tuna.","\u0026quot;It is acceptable,\u0026quot; Snape declared. \u0026quot;It is not a heart attack on a plate. Unlike the morning’s abomination.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You ate four sausages, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore reminded him, drifting past with a plate full of halloumi.","\u0026quot;Fuel,\u0026quot; Snape dismissed. \u0026quot;This is gastronomy.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eDumbledore’s Discovery\u003c/strong\u003e","Albus Dumbledore was currently engaged in a battle of wits with a piece of grilled Halloumi cheese.","\u0026quot;It squeaks!\u0026quot; Dumbledore delighted, chewing enthusiastically. \u0026quot;Minerva! Listen! \u003cem\u003eSqueak, squeak!\u003c/em\u003e It is the musical cheese of Cyprus!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Please stop squeaking your food, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall sighed, eating a olive.","\u0026quot;And this,\u0026quot; Dumbledore pointed to the Tzatziki. \u0026quot;It is yogurt... but with cucumber? It is a savory custard! Genius!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Cultural Divide\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley was eyeing the Calamari.","\u0026quot;Squid,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted to Lucius Malfoy. \u0026quot;Grilled. Rubber rings.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is a delicacy, Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said, cutting a piece of octopus with elegant precision. \u0026quot;In the Mediterranean, they understand that seafood should not be battered and deep-fried.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Nonsense,\u0026quot; Vernon argued, grabbing a baguette. \u0026quot;Everything is better battered. But... for health reasons... I suppose I’ll try the leaf.\u0026quot;","He took a scoop of salad. \u0026quot;The Mediterranean Diet,\u0026quot; Vernon announced to the table. \u0026quot;Olive oil and fish. Good for the ticker. Executive health strategy.\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley sat down with a plate piled high with pita bread and Hummus.","\u0026quot;It’s dip,\u0026quot; Ron whispered to Harry. \u0026quot;But it’s made of beans? It’s bean dip?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Chickpeas, Ron,\u0026quot; Hermione corrected, buttering a baguette.","\u0026quot;Whatever,\u0026quot; Ron shrugged. \u0026quot;It’s brilliant. And look at this little pie.\u0026quot; He picked up a Spanakopita. \u0026quot;It’s like a Cornish Pasty went on holiday.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lull\u003c/strong\u003e","The lunch was a quiet, refined affair compared to the raucous breakfast. The heat of the day, the cool breeze, and the lighter food lulled everyone into a state of relaxed contentment.","Draco and Ginny sat on the wall of the terrace, feeding each other grapes and ignoring the view.","Harry and Hermione sat at a small table, sharing a bowl of olives.","\u0026quot;We have four days,\u0026quot; Harry said, looking out at the ocean. \u0026quot;Four days of this.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s going to be chaotic,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled, dipping bread in oil. \u0026quot;But I think... I think we might actually survive it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;As long as Vernon doesn\u0027t organize a triathlon,\u0026quot; Harry laughed.","From the buffet table, Vernon’s voice drifted over.","\u0026quot;Swimming!\u0026quot; Vernon was saying to Snape. \u0026quot;Low impact! High resistance! Tomorrow morning, Severus! We hit the waves! 0700 hours!\u0026quot;","Snape looked at Vernon. He looked at the ocean. He looked at his glass of wine.","\u0026quot;I do not swim, Dursley,\u0026quot; Snape drawled. \u0026quot;I sink with dignity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027ll get you armbands!\u0026quot; Vernon promised.","Harry sighed happily. \u0026quot;Yep. We\u0027re going to survive.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":106,"origNum":106,"title":"The Bass Drop","wordCount":1001,"paragraphs":["The sun had vanished into the Caribbean Sea, leaving behind a sky composed of velvet darkness and diamonds.","On the beach, the atmosphere had shifted from \u0026quot;post-lunch coma\u0026quot; to \u0026quot;pre-party anticipation.\u0026quot; The tiki torches were lit. The bar was glowing. Dobby was juggling cocktail shakers.","Vernon Dursley was currently explaining the concept of \u0026quot;Happy Hour\u0026quot; to Lucius Malfoy.","\u0026quot;It is an economic incentive, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted over the rising murmur of the crowd. \u0026quot;Half-price drinks to stimulate early consumption! It maximizes bar efficiency!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But the drinks are free, Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius pointed out, swirling a glass of Elf-Made Pinot Noir. \u0026quot;Draco owns the island.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the \u003cem\u003eprinciple\u003c/em\u003e!\u0026quot; Vernon insisted.","Suddenly, the lights on the terrace flickered and died.","\u0026quot;Dark Magic!\u0026quot; Moody (who was lurking in a palm tree) shouted.","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Dudley Dursley’s voice boomed through a magically amplified megaphone.","A spotlight hit the center of the beach. Dudley stood there. He had traded his boxing gear for a crisp linen shirt and sunglasses (at night). He looked massive, confident, and surprisingly cool.","\u0026quot;Ladies and Gentlemen!\u0026quot; Dudley bellowed. \u0026quot;Wizards and Witches! We’ve had the games. We’ve had the food. But a wedding isn\u0027t a wedding without a beat!\u0026quot;","He pointed to a massive structure that had appeared on the edge of the sand—a raised platform covered in black equipment, wires, and towering black monoliths.","\u0026quot;The elves built the stage,\u0026quot; Dudley announced. \u0026quot;But I brought the talent. Please welcome my mates from uni... SWEDISH HOUSE MAFIA!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sonic Boom\u003c/strong\u003e","Three men walked onto the stage. They waved at Dudley. They put on headphones.","\u0026quot;Muggles?\u0026quot; Ron asked, squinting. \u0026quot;What are they doing with those tables? are they cooking?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are mixing,\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, clutching Harry’s arm. \u0026quot;Harry! That’s Swedish House Mafia! They’re huge! How does Dudley know them?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Boxing club?\u0026quot; Harry guessed, bewildered.","The lead DJ raised a hand. He pressed a button.","\u003cem\u003eTHUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","A soundwave of pure bass rolled across the beach. It wasn\u0027t just a noise; it was a physical impact. It hit the wizards in the chest like a Stunning Spell.","Lucius Malfoy dropped his wine glass. \u0026quot;We are under attack! They have cannons!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the bass, Father!\u0026quot; Draco yelled, grinning wildly. \u0026quot;It’s Muggle music!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is... vigorous!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley shouted, rushing toward the speakers to inspect them. \u0026quot;Look at the vibration! The air is trembling!\u0026quot;","Then, the melody kicked in. A synth line that soared higher than a Firebolt.","\u003cem\u003eDon\u0027t you worry, don\u0027t you worry child...\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Rave\u003c/strong\u003e","The beat dropped.","The beach exploded.","It wasn\u0027t a waltz. It wasn\u0027t a Weird Sisters rock ballad. It was Electronic Dance Music—relentless, driving, and impossible to ignore.","Ginny Weasley was the first to succumb. She grabbed Draco’s hand and dragged him into the center of the sand.","\u0026quot;Jump!\u0026quot; Ginny screamed.","\u0026quot;Malfoy\u0027s do not jump!\u0026quot; Draco protested.","\u0026quot;They do now!\u0026quot;","Draco looked at her. He looked at the flashing lights Dumbledore had just conjured to match the beat. He shrugged.","He jumped.","And suddenly, the Aristocrat of Wiltshire was bouncing up and down in the sand, linen shirt unbuttoned, laughing as the bass rattled his teeth.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parents\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley was pumping his fist.","\u0026quot;Feel that rhythm!\u0026quot; Vernon roared at Petunia. \u0026quot;It’s a metronome! It’s precise! It’s industrial!\u0026quot;","Petunia, caught up in the madness, was swaying her hips. \u0026quot;It’s very catchy, Vernon!\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley was dancing like a man trying to put out a small fire with his feet, his arms flailing in pure joy.","\u0026quot;I am pulsating!\u0026quot; Arthur yelled to Molly. \u0026quot;The music is controlling my limbs!\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley grabbed her husband and spun him around. \u0026quot;Go on, Arthur! Shake it!\u0026quot;","Even Lucius Malfoy was affected. He wasn\u0027t dancing, exactly. But he was tapping his cane on the marble floor in perfect time with the beat.","\u003cem\u003eTap. Tap. Tap. Tap.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;It has... authority,\u0026quot; Lucius admitted to Narcissa. \u0026quot;It commands you to move. I respect the imperative nature of the sound.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Professors\u003c/strong\u003e","Albus Dumbledore had gone full rave.","He had transfigured his robes into a sequined jumpsuit that reflected the laser lights. He was in the middle of the dance floor, leading a conga line consisting of Hagrid, Luna, and a confused but happy Fleur Delacour.","\u0026quot;Higher, Hagrid!\u0026quot; Dumbledore shouted, throwing his hands up. \u0026quot;Feel the magic of the synthesizer!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I feel it, Professor!\u0026quot; Hagrid bellowed, stomping the sand so hard he was creating small earthquakes.","Minerva McGonagall stood by the bar, tapping her foot. She looked at Snape.","\u0026quot;It has a certain... energy,\u0026quot; McGonagall admitted.","Severus Snape stood in the shadows, arms crossed, wearing his blackest scowl.","He looked at the flashing lights. He looked at the bouncing crowd. He looked at Draco Malfoy sweating through his silk.","\u0026quot;It is noise,\u0026quot; Snape declared flatly. \u0026quot;It is repetitive, electronic noise designed to liquidate the brain.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, lighten up, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, finishing her drink. \u0026quot;I’m going in.\u0026quot;","She marched onto the sand and began to do a very spirited Highland Fling to the beat of \u003cem\u003eSave The World\u003c/em\u003e.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Peak\u003c/strong\u003e","The music swelled. The lights strobed.","Harry Potter stood in the middle of it all, holding Hermione’s hand, watching his world collide.","He saw Dudley DJing with his friends. He saw Ron trying to breakdance (and failing). He saw Draco spinning Ginny around.","He saw Vernon Dursley high-fiving Arthur Weasley.","It was loud. It was chaotic. It was perfect.","\u0026quot;This is it!\u0026quot; Harry shouted to Hermione over the music. \u0026quot;This is the best night ever!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t hear you!\u0026quot; Hermione laughed, shouting back. \u0026quot;But yes!\u0026quot;","As the final crescendo hit, Dumbledore shot fireworks from his wand that exploded in time with the music, showering the beach in gold and silver sparks.","The wizards, Muggles, and elves jumped in unison, a single, joyous mass of humanity and magic, united by the universal language of a sick beat.","Only Snape remained still, sipping his wine. But if one looked closely, very closely... his left index finger was tapping against his glass.","\u003cem\u003eTap. Tap. Tap.\u003c/em\u003e","It was the most he had ever danced in his life."]},{"num":107,"origNum":107,"title":"The Festival of Questions","wordCount":934,"paragraphs":["The final beat of \u003cem\u003eDon’t You Worry Child\u003c/em\u003e faded into the night air, replaced by the rhythmic hush of the Caribbean waves. The laser lights dimmed, leaving the beach bathed in the soft, golden glow of the floating candles Dumbledore had conjured.","Dudley Dursley stepped back from the decks, high-fiving Axwell, Steve, and Sebastian.","\u0026quot;Thanks, lads,\u0026quot; Dudley grinned, wiping sweat from his forehead. \u0026quot;You brought the house down. Literally, I think a coconut fell on Ron.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Anytime, Big D,\u0026quot; Axwell laughed, unplugging his headphones. \u0026quot;Best crowd we\u0027ve had in years. The guy with the beard? The one in the sequins? He’s got moves.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s the Headmaster,\u0026quot; Dudley explained. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t ask.\u0026quot;","They jumped down from the stage, walking across the sand toward the long dining tables that the house-elves had set up near the surf.","But before they could reach the sanctuary of the chairs, they were intercepted.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Interrogation\u003c/strong\u003e","It wasn\u0027t the wizards who swarmed them first. It was Vernon Dursley.","Vernon had been watching the performance with a mixture of confusion and grudging respect for the sheer volume of the sound system. He marched up to the three DJs, flanked by Petunia.","\u0026quot;You there!\u0026quot; Vernon barked, extending a hand. \u0026quot;Vernon Dursley. Dudley’s father. I must say, the... \u003cem\u003ethumping\u003c/em\u003e... was very efficient. Rattled the fillings right out of my head.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, sir,\u0026quot; Sebastian Ingrosso smiled, shaking the hand.","\u0026quot;Dudley tells me you do this professionally,\u0026quot; Vernon said, eyeing their t-shirts. \u0026quot;Is there a market for this... noise?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We do alright,\u0026quot; Steve Angello said modestly.","\u0026quot;They do better than alright, Dad,\u0026quot; Dudley interjected, putting an arm around his friend. \u0026quot;They just headlined Tomorrowland.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Tomorrowland?\u0026quot; Petunia repeated, smoothing her dress. \u0026quot;Is that a theme park? Is it like Disney?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a music festival, Mom,\u0026quot; Dudley said. \u0026quot;In Belgium.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A festival,\u0026quot; Vernon mused. \u0026quot;Like a village fete? A few tents? Some jam for sale?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not exactly,\u0026quot; Axwell chuckled. \u0026quot;It’s... bigger.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;How big?\u0026quot; Vernon pressed, his business instincts twitching. \u0026quot;Attendance figures?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Over one hundred thousand people,\u0026quot; Steve replied casually. \u0026quot;At once. Over the weekend, it’s closer to four hundred thousand.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Muggle Shock\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley stopped walking. He stared at the three men in t-shirts.","\u0026quot;Four... hundred... thousand?\u0026quot; Vernon whispered. \u0026quot;Paying customers?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, sir.\u0026quot;","Vernon’s eyes glazed over. He was doing mental arithmetic. Ticket prices. Concessions. Parking fees.","\u0026quot;Good Lord,\u0026quot; Vernon breathed. \u0026quot;That is not a fete. That is a small nation. The logistics alone... the sanitation requirements... the insurance premiums!\u0026quot;","He looked at the DJs with newfound reverence. They were no longer just noisemakers; they were titans of industry.","\u0026quot;And you manage this crowd?\u0026quot; Vernon asked breathlessly. \u0026quot;Without a riot?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ideally,\u0026quot; Sebastian grinned. \u0026quot;We just play the music. The energy keeps them together.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Energy,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded sagely. \u0026quot;Crowd psychology. Supply and demand of dopamine. Brilliant.\u0026quot;","Petunia looked concerned. \u0026quot;But... where do they all sleep? Is there enough bedding?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They camp, Mrs. Dursley,\u0026quot; Dudley said. \u0026quot;Tents. Mud. It’s glorious.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mud,\u0026quot; Petunia shuddered. \u0026quot;Well. You boys certainly clean up well for dinner.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wizarding Confusion\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley, who had been hovering nearby, couldn\u0027t hold back any longer.","\u0026quot;Excuse me,\u0026quot; Arthur said, stepping forward with wide eyes. \u0026quot;Did you say... one hundred thousand Muggles? In one field?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Axwell nodded.","\u0026quot;And they all listen to the same music?\u0026quot; Arthur asked, fascinated. \u0026quot;How? Do you use a \u003cem\u003eSonorus\u003c/em\u003e charm on the speakers?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We use amplifiers, Mr. Weasley,\u0026quot; Dudley explained. \u0026quot;Electricity. Big magnets pushing air.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Magnets!\u0026quot; Arthur gasped, grabbing Lucius Malfoy’s arm. \u0026quot;Did you hear that, Lucius? They use magnets to push the air! It’s elemental manipulation via metal!\u0026quot;","Lucius looked at the DJs. \u0026quot;And these... one hundred thousand people,\u0026quot; Lucius drawled. \u0026quot;They congregate voluntarily? To listen to... bleeps and bloops?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They love the bleeps and bloops,\u0026quot; Steve smiled.","\u0026quot;Fascinating,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured. \u0026quot;The Dark Lord struggled to gather a few hundred followers. Perhaps he needed a bass drop.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He needed better PR,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected, clapping Lucius on the back. \u0026quot;And a catchy slogan. \u0027Tomorrowland\u0027—now that’s branding!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Feast\u003c/strong\u003e","The interrogation continued all the way to the tables. Vernon wanted to know about the profit margins of merchandise; Arthur wanted to know how the cables didn\u0027t get tangled; Dumbledore wanted to know if they accepted requests for polka.","Finally, they reached the dining area.","It was a long, low table set directly on the sand, illuminated by floating lanterns. The tablecloths were white linen, fluttering in the breeze.","\u0026quot;Sit! Sit!\u0026quot; Draco called out from the head of the table. \u0026quot;The artists must be starving.\u0026quot;","The group took their seats. The DJs sat between Dudley and Ron (who was asking if they could remix \u0026quot;Weasley is Our King\u0026quot;).","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Draco announced. \u0026quot;Dinner!\u0026quot;","The food appeared with a soft \u003cem\u003epop\u003c/em\u003e.","After the heavy American breakfast and the light Mediterranean lunch, dinner was a celebration of the location.","Huge platters of Caribbean jerk chicken, blackened mahi-mahi, coconut rice, fried plantains, and bowls of spicy callaloo soup appeared.","There were baskets of johnnycakes and jugs of rum punch that refilled themselves.","\u0026quot;It smells spicy!\u0026quot; Ron warned, sniffing a piece of chicken. \u0026quot;Proceed with caution!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s flavor, Ron,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, piling his plate high.","Vernon Dursley raised a glass of punch.","\u0026quot;To Swedish House Mafia!\u0026quot; Vernon toasted loudly. \u0026quot;For teaching us about economies of scale! And to the bass!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Bass!\u0026quot; the table roared.","As the DJs dug into the magical feast, watching salt shakers march across the table and napkins fold themselves into swans, Axwell leaned over to Dudley.","\u0026quot;Your family is weird, man,\u0026quot; he whispered.","\u0026quot;You have no idea,\u0026quot; Dudley grinned, clinking his glass against Harry’s. \u0026quot;But they know how to throw a party.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":108,"origNum":108,"title":"The Echoes of the Past","wordCount":1257,"paragraphs":["As the platters of jerk chicken and blackened mahi-mahi were cleared away by a squad of efficient house-elves, a comfortable lull settled over the beach. The tiki torches flickered against the starlight, and the Caribbean sea whispered against the sand.","Steve Angello wiped his mouth with a linen napkin and looked at Dudley.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Steve said, gesturing to the villa, the wizards, and the peacocks sleeping in the palm trees. \u0026quot;This is... a lot to process. But the vibe? It’s unreal.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a unique demographic,\u0026quot; Dudley grinned.","\u0026quot;We were supposed to fly back to Miami tonight,\u0026quot; Axwell admitted, looking at his watch. He looked at the open bar. He looked at the happy, strange crowd.","\u0026quot;But... if there’s a spare room? We’d love to crash. I don\u0027t think I’m ready to leave this... magic.\u0026quot;","Dudley looked at Draco.","\u0026quot;The villa sleeps fifty,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, leaning back in his chair with a glass of wine. \u0026quot;And the West Wing is currently unoccupied. You are welcome to stay. Consider it a thank you for the... bass.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Brilliant,\u0026quot; Sebastian grinned. \u0026quot;Round two tomorrow?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;God help us,\u0026quot; Snape muttered into his goblet, though he didn\u0027t look entirely displeased.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Inquisition of Tomorrowland\u003c/strong\u003e","With the sleeping arrangements settled, the professors seized their chance. They had been stewing with curiosity since the first beat dropped.","Albus Dumbledore leaned across the table, his blue eyes piercing behind his half-moon spectacles.","\u0026quot;Tell me,\u0026quot; Dumbledore began, his voice filled with wonder. \u0026quot;This \u0027Tomorrowland\u0027. You say hundreds of thousands gather. Is there... a ritual? A shared incantation?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s called the \u0027Drop\u0027, Professor,\u0026quot; Steve explained. \u0026quot;We build the tension. The music gets faster, higher. The crowd waits. And then... we let it go. And everyone jumps at the exact same second.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Synchronization,\u0026quot; Professor Flitwick squeaked, scribbling on a napkin. \u0026quot;Without a \u003cem\u003eConfundus\u003c/em\u003e Charm? Without \u003cem\u003eImperio\u003c/em\u003e? Purely auditory stimulus?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pure feeling,\u0026quot; Axwell tapped his chest. \u0026quot;It’s about unity. People from every country, every background, holding flags and dancing together. No politics. No wars. Just music.\u0026quot;","Narcissa Malfoy paused, her glass halfway to her lips. She looked at the DJs.","\u0026quot;No wars?\u0026quot; she whispered. \u0026quot;Just... strangers standing together?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s the motto,\u0026quot; Sebastian nodded. \u0026quot;Live Today, Love Tomorrow, Unite Forever.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy stared at the Muggle musician. He looked at the Dark Mark faded on his arm. He looked at the unity at the table.","\u0026quot;Unite Forever,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured. \u0026quot;A noble house motto. I... I approve.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the pyrotechnics?\u0026quot; Professor Sprout asked eagerly. \u0026quot;The fire? Is it dragon-based?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fireworks, ma\u0027am,\u0026quot; Dudley answered. \u0026quot;Gunpowder and timing. Dad loves them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Efficient combustion,\u0026quot; Vernon confirmed, toasting the DJs. \u0026quot;Value for money.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Quiet Shore\u003c/strong\u003e","The dinner wound down. The heavy food and the emotional toll of the day began to weigh on eyelids.","\u0026quot;Bedtime,\u0026quot; Molly Weasley announced, standing up and yawning. \u0026quot;We have a wedding to plan in four days. And I need to figure out how to make a cake that doesn\u0027t melt in this humidity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Stasis charms, Molly,\u0026quot; Hermione suggested sleepily, standing up. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll show you in the morning.\u0026quot;","The group began the slow trek back up the path to the villa, a procession of tired, happy wizards and Muggles.","But Draco Malfoy didn\u0027t follow them.","He walked down toward the water’s edge, his shoes discarded, his toes sinking into the wet sand. He stood looking out at the endless, dark ocean, the moonlight painting a silver path on the waves.","Harry, who had been about to follow Hermione, stopped. He saw the solitary figure in the white linen shirt standing by the surf.","\u0026quot;Go on,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, kissing Harry’s cheek. \u0026quot;I’ll see you upstairs.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded. He walked down the beach, the sand cool under his feet.","He walked up to Draco and stood beside him. They didn\u0027t speak for a long moment, just listening to the rhythm of the tide.","\u0026quot;It’s quiet,\u0026quot; Harry said finally.","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Draco agreed, not looking away from the horizon. \u0026quot;After the noise of the last ten years... it’s strange.\u0026quot;","Draco took a sip of the wine he had carried with him.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said softly. \u0026quot;Do you remember the train? First year?\u0026quot;","Harry chuckled. \u0026quot;I remember. You told me I shouldn\u0027t go making friends with the wrong sort. You offered to help me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I was a prat,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;An arrogant, entitled, bigoted little prat.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You were,\u0026quot; Harry agreed easily. \u0026quot;And I was a scrawny kid who didn\u0027t know a pumpkin pasty from a potion.\u0026quot;","Draco turned to look at him. The moonlight softened the sharp angles of his face.","\u0026quot;I hated you,\u0026quot; Draco admitted. \u0026quot;For years. I hated that you were the hero. I hated that you had friends who would die for you. I hated that... that you saved me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I hated you too,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;I hated that you had a family. I hated that you were safe.\u0026quot;","They looked at each other. The memories of insults, hexes, and the Sectumsempra scars faded, replaced by the memory of a wand thrown in a manor, a broomstick ride out of a fire, and a ring bought in Paris.","\u0026quot;We were children,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;Fighting a war our fathers started.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And now we\u0027re ending it,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;For good.\u0026quot;","Draco looked back at the villa. The lights were glowing in the windows. He could see Ginny laughing in a window on the second floor. He could see his parents talking to the Weasleys on the terrace.","\u0026quot;Look at us, Harry,\u0026quot; Draco said, using his first name naturally, without the sneer. \u0026quot;The Boy Who Lived and the Death Eater\u0027s son. Standing on a beach in the Caribbean, planning our weddings to a Muggle-born and a Blood Traitor.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And your dad is drinking scotch with my uncle,\u0026quot; Harry added.","Draco let out a laugh—a real, free sound that carried over the water. \u0026quot;It’s madness. But... I think I’m happy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You deserve to be,\u0026quot; Harry said. He bumped Draco’s shoulder with his own. \u0026quot;We both do.\u0026quot;","Draco finished his wine. He tossed the glass into the sand (Dobby would get it later).","\u0026quot;Come on,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;If I stay out here much longer, Ginny will send a search party. Or a Bat-Bogey Hex.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Probably the hex,\u0026quot; Harry grinned.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe View from the Villa\u003c/strong\u003e","They turned and walked back toward the lights of the villa.","As they walked, Harry reached out and draped his arm around Draco’s shoulders.","Draco didn\u0027t flinch. He didn\u0027t shrug it off. He reached up and put his arm around Harry’s shoulders in return.","They walked in step, leaning on each other slightly—two brothers not by blood, but by fire.","Up on the terrace, the rest of the party had paused before going inside.","Molly Weasley stood by the railing, looking down at the beach.","\u0026quot;Oh, Arthur,\u0026quot; she whispered, her hand flying to her mouth.","Narcissa Malfoy stood beside her. She watched her son—her proud, difficult, broken, and healed son—walking arm-in-arm with Harry Potter.","A tear tracked down Narcissa’s pale cheek. She didn\u0027t wipe it away.","\u0026quot;They are safe,\u0026quot; Narcissa breathed. \u0026quot;Finally.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are friends,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled, leaning against the stone balustrade, her eyes shining.","Even Vernon Dursley, standing by the door with a final glass of port, looked down at the two figures.","He cleared his throat loudly.","\u0026quot;Good lads,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, his eyes suspiciously bright. \u0026quot;Good lads. Now... who knows how to turn off the lights in the Executive Suite? It’s too high-tech.\u0026quot;","As the two former enemies walked into the light of the villa, the war was not just over. It was history.","And the future was waiting upstairs."]},{"num":109,"origNum":109,"title":"Operation Tandoori","wordCount":923,"paragraphs":["04:00 hours.","The digital clock on Vernon Dursley’s bedside table flicked over in silent green neon.","Vernon did not groan. He did not hit the snooze button. He sat up with the fluid precision of a hydraulic piston.","He glanced at Petunia, who was sleeping soundly, dreaming of lemon-scented cleaning products. He slid out of the high four-poster bed, careful not to disturb the mattress tension.","He didn\u0027t put on his pajama dressing gown. He put on his \u0026quot;Site Inspection\u0026quot; attire: a beige safari suit with many pockets, sturdy boots, and a fresh clipboard.","He crept out of the Executive Suite, bypassed the sleeping guards (statues Dumbledore had animated to guard the hallway), and exited the villa.","He climbed into a golf cart and drove silently down the winding path toward the airstrip. The jungle was alive with the sound of insects, but Vernon was listening for something much louder.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","He parked the cart at the edge of the runway—the three-kilometer strip of concrete Draco had carved from the island1.","Vernon checked his watch. \u0026quot;04:15. Wind speed negligible. Visibility good.\u0026quot;","He looked at the horizon. A set of lights appeared, blinking in a steady rhythm.","A low drone began to vibrate in the air. It wasn\u0027t the high-pitched whine of the A380’s jet engines. It was the deep, thrumming growl of turboprops.","A Lockheed C-130 Hercules, painted in matte grey, descended from the darkness.","It touched down with a heavy, purposeful skid, its massive propellers chopping the humid air. It taxied to the end of the runway and turned, its rear cargo ramp facing Vernon.","Vernon nodded. \u0026quot;Beautiful,\u0026quot; he whispered. \u0026quot;Military surplus. Rugged. Reliable.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Asset\u003c/strong\u003e","The rear ramp whirred and lowered slowly, revealing the cavernous, lit interior of the cargo hold.","A man stepped out. He was not wearing military fatigues. He was wearing pristine chef\u0027s whites and a toque that added a foot to his height.","\u0026quot;Mr. Dursley,\u0026quot; the Chef called out, his voice echoing over the tarmac.","\u0026quot;Chef Kumar,\u0026quot; Vernon replied, marching up the ramp to shake his hand. \u0026quot;You made good time. Did you hit turbulence over the Atlantic?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Smooth sailing, sir,\u0026quot; Kumar smiled. \u0026quot;We used the tailwind. Patel from Logistics said this was a Priority One rush order.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Vernon confirmed. \u0026quot;We have a VIP client list. Wizards. Aristocrats. And my son, who eats like a horse. I need volume, Kumar. And I need spice.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You called for the \u0027Mumbai Morning\u0027 package,\u0026quot; Kumar noted, checking his own clipboard. \u0026quot;With the \u0027Delhi Upgrade\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Vernon rubbed his hands together. \u0026quot;We’ve done American. We’ve done Mediterranean. Now, I want to hit them with flavor. I want heat. I want complexity. I want them to weep with joy over a lentil.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Unloading\u003c/strong\u003e","Chef Kumar snapped his fingers (not magically, just authoritatively).","\u0026quot;Move out! Go! Go! Go!\u0026quot;","From the belly of the C-130, an army emerged. Thirty sous-chefs, kitchen porters, and tandoor masters jogged down the ramp.","They weren\u0027t carrying wands. They were carrying equipment that looked heavy enough to sink a ship.","Four massive clay Tandoor ovens were wheeled out on dollies.","Crates of Basmati rice, sacks of flour (Atta and Maida), and barrels of ghee were offloaded with assembly-line speed.","\u0026quot;Careful with the Saffron!\u0026quot; Vernon barked as a porter jogged past. \u0026quot;That’s worth more than gold!\u0026quot;","They set up a field kitchen right on the beach, adjacent to the runway. Stainless steel prep tables were unfolded. Gas burners were hooked up to industrial tanks.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Prep\u003c/strong\u003e","05:00 hours. Three hours to wake-up call.","The operation began.","\u0026quot;Fire up the Tandoors!\u0026quot; Kumar shouted. \u0026quot;I want them at 480 degrees Celsius in twenty minutes!\u0026quot;","Vernon walked the line, inspecting the ingredients.","\u0026quot;What’s this?\u0026quot; Vernon asked, peering into a large vat.","\u0026quot;Idli batter, sir,\u0026quot; a sous-chef explained, stirring the fermented rice and lentil mix. \u0026quot;Fermented overnight in transit. It will be fluffy like a cloud.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted. \u0026quot;And the Dosa?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We have three griddles dedicated to Masala Dosa,\u0026quot; Kumar pointed. \u0026quot;Crispy. Potato filling spiced with mustard seeds and curry leaves.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Excellent,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded. \u0026quot;Now, the breads. I promised Lucius Malfoy a culinary education. I want Naan. I want Paratha. I want Puri.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are doing Bhature as well, sir,\u0026quot; Kumar promised. \u0026quot;Fried balloon bread. To go with the Chole.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Balloon bread,\u0026quot; Vernon tasted the phrase. \u0026quot;Arthur Weasley is going to lose his mind.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aromas\u003c/strong\u003e","By 06:00 hours, the smell began to rise.","It wasn\u0027t the smell of bacon or croissants. It was a complex, heavy, intoxicating cloud of toasted cumin, coriander, turmeric, and cardamom.","The chefs were moving in a blur.","On one side, huge pots of Sambar were bubbling, releasing steam that smelled of tamarind and drumsticks.","On the other, skewers of paneer and vegetables were being lowered into the roaring Tandoors.","Vernon stood in the center of the chaos, inhaling deeply. The spices tickled his nose.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Vernon declared to the jungle, \u0026quot;is global trade at its finest. Importing culture via air freight.\u0026quot;","He checked his watch. Two hours left.","\u0026quot;Double time!\u0026quot; Vernon clapped his hands. \u0026quot;I want the chutneys plated! Coconut! Mint! Tamarind! A tricolor of efficiency! The wizards wake at eight, and I want their tastebuds to wake up at 8:01!\u0026quot;","As the sun began to peek over the horizon, illuminating the steam rising from the pots and the sweat on the chefs\u0027 brows, Vernon Dursley smiled.","He had secured the plane. He had secured the venue. And now, he was about to secure the most flavorful breakfast the Caribbean had ever seen."]},{"num":110,"origNum":110,"title":"The Spice Alarm","wordCount":832,"paragraphs":["Ron Weasley was dreaming. In his dream, he was swimming in a lake, but the water wasn\u0027t water. It was warm, golden gravy. And the clouds above weren\u0027t clouds; they were fluffy, fried pillows of dough raining down gently around him.","He inhaled deeply. The smell was intense—toasted cumin, rich butter, frying garlic, and something sweet and floral.","He opened one eye.","He sniffed the air of his luxury suite. The smell was real. It was wafting in through the open balcony door, riding the sea breeze like a delicious ghost.","Ron sat up. His stomach gave a roar that sounded like a captive dragon.","\u0026quot;It’s not a dream,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, swinging his legs out of bed. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s better.\u0026quot;","He sprinted to the connecting door and hammered on it.","\u0026quot;HARRY! HARRY, WAKE UP! THE AIR IS EDIBLE!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grooms\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter groaned, pulling a pillow over his head. \u0026quot;Ron? It’s... what time is it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Time to eat!\u0026quot; Ron yelled through the wood. \u0026quot;Can\u0027t you smell it? It smells like the Burrow on steroids!\u0026quot;","Harry sat up. He sniffed. Ron was right. The room smelled incredible—spicy, warm, and complex.","Within minutes, the three grooms were standing in the hallway in their pajamas. Draco Malfoy looked less like a groom and more like a disgruntled silk moth.","\u0026quot;Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco rasped, rubbing his eyes. \u0026quot;If this is a prank... if you are cooking kippers...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sniff, Malfoy!\u0026quot; Ron commanded, pointing his nose at the window. \u0026quot;Just sniff!\u0026quot;","Draco inhaled. His grey eyes widened.","\u0026quot;Cardamom,\u0026quot; Draco identified instantly. \u0026quot;Turmeric. And... is that ghee? That is definitely high-quality ghee.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s breakfast,\u0026quot; Harry realized, grabbing his glasses. \u0026quot;Vernon. It has to be Vernon.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Brides\u003c/strong\u003e","Across the villa, the brides were stirring.","Ginny Weasley was already on the balcony, leaning over the railing, trying to pinpoint the source.","\u0026quot;It’s coming from the beach,\u0026quot; Ginny called out to Hermione, who was emerging from her room rubbing her eyes.","\u0026quot;It smells spicy,\u0026quot; Hermione noted, sniffing delicately. \u0026quot;But warm. Like... comfort food, but dangerous.\u0026quot;","Luna Lovegood drifted out of her turret room. She was wearing pajamas covered in dirigible plums.","\u0026quot;The air is full of golden mist,\u0026quot; Luna observed happily. \u0026quot;I think the Heliopaths are baking.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t care who’s baking,\u0026quot; Ginny declared, grabbing her dressing gown. \u0026quot;I’m going down there before Ron eats it all.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Elders\u003c/strong\u003e","In the Imperial Suite, Lucius Malfoy woke with a start.","\u0026quot;Narcissa,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;Do you smell that?\u0026quot;","Narcissa inhaled. \u0026quot;It smells... vivid, Lucius. Like a bazaar.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It smells aggressive,\u0026quot; Lucius noted, sitting up. \u0026quot;But... enticing. It smells like it has personality.\u0026quot;","In the Garden Suite, Arthur Weasley was leaning out the window.","\u0026quot;Molly!\u0026quot; Arthur shouted. \u0026quot;It’s not bacon! It’s something else! It smells like... adventure!\u0026quot;","Molly sniffed the air with professional scrutiny. \u0026quot;Ginger. Chilies. Coriander. It’s a curry, Arthur! At breakfast!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A breakfast curry?\u0026quot; Arthur gasped. \u0026quot;What a time to be alive!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Faculty\u003c/strong\u003e","Severus Snape did not wake up; he activated.","He stood in his darkened room, analyzing the olfactory data.","\u003cem\u003eSaffron. Mustard seeds. Fermented lentils.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Complex,\u0026quot; Snape murmured to the darkness. \u0026quot;Multi-layered. A potion of sustenance.\u0026quot;","He put on his sunglasses (inside) and opened the door.","Dumbledore was already in the hallway, wearing a nightcap and a look of pure delight.","\u0026quot;Ah, Severus!\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;The nose knows! I believe we are being treated to the culinary magic of the East!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is pungent, Headmaster,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, emerging from her room tying her robe. \u0026quot;But I must admit... my stomach is intrigued.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Approach\u003c/strong\u003e","The entire wedding party, a ragtag group of pajamas, dressing gowns, and bedhead, flowed out of the villa and down the winding path toward the airstrip.","As they cleared the jungle line, the view opened up.","They stopped.","On the edge of the tarmac, next to the massive C-130 Hercules, was a scene of organized chaos.","Steam rose in great white clouds from massive steel vats. The Tandoor ovens were roaring, shooting sparks into the morning sky.","Chefs in pristine whites were flipping breads that puffed up like balloons. Others were spreading batter on sizzling griddles.","And standing in the center of it all, holding a clipboard and looking like the Emperor of Spice, was Vernon Dursley.","\u0026quot;Move it!\u0026quot; Vernon roared at his troops. \u0026quot;The assets are approaching! Plate the Puri! Garnish the Dahl! I want the Chutney station fully operational!\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley’s knees buckled. He clutched Harry for support.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Ron whimpered, staring at a mountain of fried bread. \u0026quot;Tell me that’s for us. Tell me we don\u0027t have to share with the plane.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s for us, Ron,\u0026quot; Harry grinned, smelling the Tandoori chicken. \u0026quot;It’s definitely for us.\u0026quot;","Vernon spotted them. He waved his clipboard.","\u0026quot;Timing!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed happily. \u0026quot;08:00 hours! Right on the dot! Welcome to Mumbai! Grab a plate! And be careful—the pickle is hot!\u0026quot;","The wizards stared at the feast. They didn\u0027t know what half of it was, but they knew one thing: it smelled like the best magic they had ever encountered."]},{"num":111,"origNum":111,"title":"The Symphony of Spice","wordCount":893,"paragraphs":["The buffet line was not a line; it was a fortification of flavor.","Vernon Dursley stood at the head of the stainless-steel tables, gesturing with a pair of tongs as if they were a field marshal’s baton. Beside him stood Chef Kumar, looking proud and imposing in his starch-white uniform.","\u0026quot;Listen up!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;This is not toast and marmalade! This is a tactical assault on the palate! We are dealing with heat, spice, and texture profiles you people have never dreamed of!\u0026quot;","He pointed to the first station, where a chef was ladling a thick, steaming batter onto a massive, sizzling flat-top grill.","\u0026quot;Chef Kumar,\u0026quot; Vernon deferred. \u0026quot;Brief the assets.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dosa Station\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Kumar announced, his voice carrying over the hiss of the griddle, \u0026quot;is the \u003cem\u003eMasala Dosa\u003c/em\u003e. Fermented rice and lentil crepe.\u0026quot;","The chef on the grill swirled the batter outward in perfect concentric circles. It thinned out, bubbling and turning a golden, lacy brown.","\u0026quot;Watch the structural integrity!\u0026quot; Vernon pointed out excitedly. \u0026quot;Thin as paper, strong as canvas! He fills it with a spiced potato mash—turmeric, mustard seeds, curry leaves—and rolls it. It is a cylinder of joy!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy stepped closer, squinting against the steam.","\u0026quot;It is... enormous,\u0026quot; Lucius noted. \u0026quot;It is the size of a scroll. And it is rigid?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Crispy, Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; Kumar smiled. \u0026quot;Served with Coconut Chutney and Sambar.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sambar?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley asked, leaning over a pot of bubbling vegetable stew. \u0026quot;Is that a potion base?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lentil and tamarind stew, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed. \u0026quot;Sour! Spicy! Savory! It wakes up the nervous system better than a bucket of cold water!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Idli Towers\u003c/strong\u003e","Next was the steamer station.","\u0026quot;Idli,\u0026quot; Kumar introduced, lifting a lid to reveal tiers of fluffy, white discs. \u0026quot;Steamed rice cakes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They look like clouds,\u0026quot; Luna Lovegood whispered, poking one gently. \u0026quot;Are they made of moonbeams?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fermentation, Luna,\u0026quot; Hermione explained, looking delighted. \u0026quot;It’s a chemical process that creates air pockets. Like leavening bread, but with bacteria.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bacteria?\u0026quot; Draco wrinkled his nose.","\u0026quot;Good bacteria, Draco!\u0026quot; Vernon corrected. \u0026quot;Probiotics! Gut health! Eat two, you’ll live forever. Dip it in the gunpowder.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Gunpowder?\u0026quot; Ron’s head snapped up. \u0026quot;Explosive?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Podi,\u0026quot; Kumar laughed. \u0026quot;Spiced lentil powder mixed with ghee. It is an explosion... of flavor.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Pneumatic Bread\u003c/strong\u003e","But the crowd-stopper was the frying station.","Two chefs were dropping flat discs of dough into a wok of roiling hot oil.","As soon as the dough hit the oil, it reacted instantly. It puffed up. It expanded. It transformed into a perfect, golden, hollow balloon.","\u0026quot;Behold!\u0026quot; Vernon roared. \u0026quot;The \u003cem\u003eBhatura\u003c/em\u003e! Pneumatic bread! Look at the inflation rate!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;By Merlin,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley gasped, clutching Molly’s arm. \u0026quot;It inflates itself! What gas is inside? Helium?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Steam, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon said. \u0026quot;Rapid evaporation! It’s engineering! You eat it with \u003cem\u003eChole\u003c/em\u003e—spicy chickpeas.\u0026quot;","Ron watched a chef fish a balloon-bread out of the oil. \u0026quot;I want to sleep on it,\u0026quot; Ron decided. \u0026quot;I want a mattress made of that.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Tandoor\u003c/strong\u003e","Further down, the clay ovens were radiating intense heat.","Chefs were slapping dough against the inside walls of the oven with their bare hands.","\u0026quot;The Tandoor,\u0026quot; Kumar gestured. \u0026quot;480 degrees. We are making \u003cem\u003eAloo Paratha\u003c/em\u003e—bread stuffed with spiced potatoes—and \u003cem\u003eNaan\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Snape approached the oven. He peered into the fiery depths.","\u0026quot;Primitive,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Yet... efficient. The heat distribution is spherical. It chars and bakes simultaneously.\u0026quot;","He watched a chef pull a blistered, smoky naan out with metal skewers.","\u0026quot;The Maillard reaction is accelerated,\u0026quot; Snape noted. \u0026quot;Acceptable.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sweet and the Sip\u003c/strong\u003e","At the end of the line, a chef was piping batter into hot oil in spiral shapes, then soaking them in saffron syrup.","\u0026quot;Jalebi,\u0026quot; Kumar said. \u0026quot;Pure sugar syrup. Crispy. Sticky.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore was already there. \u0026quot;It is a glowing orange pretzel,\u0026quot; Dumbledore marveled, picking one up. The syrup dripped down his fingers. \u0026quot;It is translucent! It glows with the light of the sun!\u0026quot;","And finally, the beverage station.","A chef was \u0026quot;pulling\u0026quot; tea—pouring the steaming, milky liquid from one cup to another with a meter of vertical distance, creating a frothy, aromatic waterfall.","\u0026quot;Masala Chai,\u0026quot; Vernon announced, inhaling the scent of ginger and cardamom. \u0026quot;Tea, but with a backbone. None of that weak leaf-water. This is tea that fights back.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The wizards stood before the feast, plates in hand, looking overwhelmed.","\u0026quot;Where do we start?\u0026quot; Harry asked, looking from the Dosa to the Bhatura.","\u0026quot;Tactical approach, Harry!\u0026quot; Vernon advised. \u0026quot;Start with the Dosa for crunch. Move to the Idli for stability. Hit the Bhatura for the main payload. And keep the Lassi—that yogurt drink—on standby as a coolant. The pickle is high-grade incendiary.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy picked up a piece of naan. He tore it. Steam escaped.","\u0026quot;It smells...\u0026quot; Draco hesitated. \u0026quot;It smells like magic. But you say Muggles invented this?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Muggles with good taste,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected.","\u0026quot;Kumar,\u0026quot; Vernon turned to the chef. \u0026quot;Deployment successful. The assets are engaged.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Mr. Dursley,\u0026quot; Kumar grinned. \u0026quot;Enjoy the heat.\u0026quot;","As the group moved to the tables, plates piled high with colorful, steaming, aromatic mountains of food, Ron Weasley took a bite of a Bhatura dipped in Chole.","He froze. His eyes watered. His face flushed.","\u0026quot;Ron?\u0026quot; Hermione asked worriedly. \u0026quot;Is it too hot?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s...\u0026quot; Ron wheezed, reaching for his Lassi. \u0026quot;It’s a party in my mouth. And everyone is invited.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dig in!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed, biting the head off a green chili. \u0026quot;No prisoners!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":112,"origNum":112,"title":"The Heat and the Harmony","wordCount":898,"paragraphs":["The beach fell into a strange, rhythmic silence, broken only by the crunch of crispy crepe, the tearing of naan, and the occasional gasp of someone discovering a green chili the hard way.","Vernon Dursley sat at the head of the table, watching his troops eat with the satisfaction of a commander who had just won a war.","\u0026quot;Use your hands!\u0026quot; Vernon instructed, demonstrating with a piece of Paratha. \u0026quot;Cutlery is for amateurs! You need tactile feedback! Tear, scoop, eat! It’s all in the wrist action!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grooms\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron Weasley was currently having a religious experience.","He held a piece of \u003cem\u003eBhatura\u003c/em\u003e—the fried balloon bread—in both hands. He bit into it. It deflated with a soft sigh of steam, soaking up the spicy chickpea \u003cem\u003eChole\u003c/em\u003e on his plate.","\u0026quot;It’s... it’s heavy,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, his eyes wide. \u0026quot;But it’s light. It defies gravity, Harry. It’s magic bread.\u0026quot;","He dipped a chunk into the curry and ate it.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Ron moaned. \u0026quot;The spices. They’re dancing. They’re doing a jig on my tongue. Hermione, why have we been eating toast for seven years? Why didn\u0027t you tell me about cumin?\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy was approaching his \u003cem\u003eMasala Dosa\u003c/em\u003e with the caution of a potioneer handling volatile ingredients.","The Dosa was two feet long, hanging off the edges of his plate.","\u0026quot;It is a scroll,\u0026quot; Draco murmured. \u0026quot;An edible parchment.\u0026quot;","He cut a piece with a fork (ignoring Vernon’s glare), dipped it tentatively in the Coconut Chutney, and placed it in his mouth.","He chewed. He stopped. His eyes watered slightly.","\u0026quot;It is... crunchy,\u0026quot; Draco rasped. \u0026quot;And soft. And... spicy.\u0026quot;","He reached for his Mango Lassi and took a long drink.","\u0026quot;It burns,\u0026quot; Draco announced, his pale cheeks flushing pink. \u0026quot;But... I cannot stop eating it. It is addictive. Potter, is this a potion?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s potatoes, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, tearing into a Garlic Naan. \u0026quot;Just spicy potatoes.\u0026quot;","Harry was in heaven. He remembered the bland, boiled vegetables of his childhood at Privet Drive. Seeing Vernon Dursley championing chili and turmeric felt like the ultimate redemption arc.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Brides\u003c/strong\u003e","Ginny Weasley had abandoned all pretense of decorum. She had discovered the \u003cem\u003ePickle\u003c/em\u003e—a fiery red condiment made of lime and chili.","\u0026quot;This stuff is rocket fuel!\u0026quot; Ginny cheered, slathering it on her bread. \u0026quot;It wakes you up! It’s like a Pepper-Up Potion, but tasty!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Careful, Ginny,\u0026quot; Hermione warned, though she was busy dissecting an \u003cem\u003eIdli\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;Look at the texture,\u0026quot; Hermione marveled. \u0026quot;Spongy. It absorbs the Sambar perfectly. It’s the ultimate delivery vehicle for liquid flavor.\u0026quot;","She took a bite. \u0026quot;And it’s fermented! It’s gut health!\u0026quot;","Luna Lovegood was eating a \u003cem\u003eJalebi\u003c/em\u003e. The sticky orange syrup was getting on her fingers.","\u0026quot;It tastes like sunshine trapped in a maze,\u0026quot; Luna hummed. \u0026quot;I think the Wrackspurts are getting stuck in the sticky parts.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parents: The Weasleys\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley was weeping.","Not from sadness, but from the sheer mechanical wonder of the Tandoori Chicken.","\u0026quot;Molly,\u0026quot; Arthur sniffed, holding up a bright red drumstick. \u0026quot;Look at the char. Look at the color. Vernon says they cook this in a clay pot at five hundred degrees! Without magic fire!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s delicious, Arthur,\u0026quot; Molly agreed, fanning her mouth. \u0026quot;A bit hot! A bit nippy! But the flavor... it’s deep. It’s not just heat; it’s warmth.\u0026quot;","She took a sip of Masala Chai. \u0026quot;And this tea! It’s thick! It’s like a meal in a cup! I need the recipe. I need to know how long to boil the ginger.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parents: The Malfoys\u003c/strong\u003e","Lucius Malfoy was currently engaged in a staring contest with a \u003cem\u003eSamosa\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;It is a pyramid,\u0026quot; Lucius observed. \u0026quot;A golden, fried pyramid.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just eat it, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa said elegantly. She was managing to eat curry with a fork without getting a single drop on her white dress, a feat of pure aristocratic skill.","Lucius bit into the corner of the Samosa. Steam escaped. He tasted the spiced potato and peas.","His eyebrows rose.","\u0026quot;Peas,\u0026quot; Lucius noted. \u0026quot;But... angry peas. Peas with an attitude.\u0026quot;","He looked at Vernon.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius called down the table. \u0026quot;This pastry... it is aggressive. I like it. It demands attention.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a Samosa, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted back, dunking a piece of naan into his gravy. \u0026quot;It’s the king of snacks!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Chef’s Verdict\u003c/strong\u003e","Chef Kumar stood by the Tandoors, watching the British wizards consuming his food.","\u0026quot;They are sweating, sir,\u0026quot; a sous-chef whispered nervously. \u0026quot;Is it too spicy?\u0026quot;","Kumar watched Draco Malfoy drink an entire glass of Lassi in one go, gasp, and then immediately reach for another piece of spicy Dosa.","Kumar smiled.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Kumar said. \u0026quot;That is the sweat of joy. Keep the Naan coming. They are hooked.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","As the meal wound down, the group sat back, collectively stunned by the influx of carbohydrates and capsaicin.","Ron was lying on the sand (again), rubbing his stomach. \u0026quot;I’m full. I’m so full. But I want one more Jalebi. Is that wrong?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s necessary,\u0026quot; Harry said, handing him one.","Vernon stood up, wiping his mouth. He looked at the empty platters. He looked at the happy, red-faced wizards.","\u0026quot;Mission accomplished,\u0026quot; Vernon declared. \u0026quot;Palates expanded. Horizons broadened. And not a single person asked for marmalade.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said, raising a cup of chai. \u0026quot;It was... an experience. I may require a Cooling Charm for my tongue, but it was magnificent.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Spice!\u0026quot; Arthur toasted.","\u0026quot;To the Spice!\u0026quot; the table roared."]},{"num":113,"origNum":113,"title":"The Order of the Tandoor","wordCount":862,"paragraphs":["While the younger generation was busy slipping into a carbohydrate coma on the sand, the \u0026quot;Adult Table\u0026quot; (a loose term, given Dumbledore was currently wearing a straw hat and Sirius was barefoot) was experiencing a culinary revelation.","Vernon Dursley moved among them like a sommelier of spice, directing them toward the dishes that would best suit their constitutions.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Headmaster’s Sweet Tooth\u003c/strong\u003e","Albus Dumbledore stood before the dessert station, his blue eyes twinkling so brightly they rivaled the Caribbean sun. He was holding a small bowl containing two dark, syrup-soaked spheres.","\u0026quot;Chef Kumar tells me these are called \u003cem\u003eGulab Jamun\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; Dumbledore announced to the faculty. \u0026quot;Milk solids, fried, and soaked in rose-water syrup.\u0026quot;","He popped one whole into his mouth.","He chewed. He stopped chewing. A look of transcendent bliss washed over his face.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Dumbledore breathed, syrup glistening on his lips. \u0026quot;Minerva! It is a sponge of nectar! It dissolves! It is like eating a sweet, happy cloud!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is pure sugar, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall noted, eyeing the bowl warily. \u0026quot;You will be vibrating for days.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I shall vibrate with joy!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered. \u0026quot;Severus, try the orange spirals! They are sticky!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Professors\u0027 Analysis\u003c/strong\u003e","Minerva McGonagall had opted for a more sensible approach. She held a cup of Masala Chai in one hand and a plate of \u003cem\u003eDhokla\u003c/em\u003e (steamed savory cakes) in the other.","She took a sip of the tea. Her eyes widened behind her square spectacles.","\u0026quot;It is... vigorous,\u0026quot; McGonagall gasped, a hand going to her throat. \u0026quot;The ginger. It kicks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It clears the sinuses, Minerva,\u0026quot; Pomona Sprout said happily.","Professor Sprout was currently dissecting a \u003cem\u003eSamosa\u003c/em\u003e with the precision of a Herbologist examining a rare specimen.","\u0026quot;Look at the seeds,\u0026quot; Sprout pointed out to Flitwick. \u0026quot;Ajwain. Cumin. Coriander. It’s an entire herbology lesson wrapped in pastry. And the peas! They are perfectly steamed inside the shell!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am fascinated by the structural integrity of the \u003cem\u003ePuri\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked, holding up a small, fried disc. \u0026quot;It is pressurized! If I poke it...\u0026quot;","He poked it. It hissed.","\u0026quot;Propulsion!\u0026quot; Flitwick delighted. \u0026quot;Muggle culinary aerodynamics!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Marauders’ Feast\u003c/strong\u003e","Further down the beach, the Marauders were treating the buffet like a challenge.","Sirius Black was sitting cross-legged on the sand, a plate of the spiciest \u003cem\u003eVindaloo\u003c/em\u003e (a special request from Vernon) balanced on his knees.","He took a bite. He stopped. His eyes watered. He took another bite.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Sirius wheezed, grinning wildly, \u0026quot;is better than Azkaban. This is better than freedom. This wakes you up.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s burning your face off, Padfoot,\u0026quot; Remus Lupin noted gently.","Remus was eating \u003cem\u003eDal Makhani\u003c/em\u003e—black lentils cooked with butter and cream—with a piece of Naan.","\u0026quot;This is extraordinary,\u0026quot; Remus whispered. \u0026quot;It’s... heavy. Warm. It settles in the stomach like a lead weight, but in a good way.\u0026quot;","He looked at Sirius. \u0026quot;It warms the bones. Even the wolf would sleep after this.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The wolf would want the lamb chops,\u0026quot; Sirius laughed, wiping his forehead. \u0026quot;Pass the raita. I think my tongue is melting.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Metamorphmagus Meltdown\u003c/strong\u003e","Nymphadora Tonks was sitting between Remus and Fleur. She had just bitten into a green chili pickle, mistaking it for a vegetable side dish.","\u0026quot;Oh!\u0026quot; Tonks gasped.","Her hair, usually a bubblegum pink, flashed violently to a bright, alarming chili-red.","\u0026quot;Hot!\u0026quot; Tonks wheezed, fanning her mouth. \u0026quot;Fire! Dragon fire!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Drink the Lassi!\u0026quot; Fleur commanded, handing her a yogurt drink. \u0026quot;It neutralizes ze capsicum!\u0026quot;","Tonks downed the drink. Her hair slowly faded back to a soothing cool blue.","\u0026quot;Wow,\u0026quot; Tonks breathed. \u0026quot;That was a rush. I want more.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eSnape’s Verdict\u003c/strong\u003e","Severus Snape had finished his protein-heavy first course and was now inspecting a bowl of \u003cem\u003eBiryani\u003c/em\u003e.","He picked up a grain of Basmati rice with his fork. He examined the length.","\u0026quot;Aged,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Long grain. Cooked separately from the meat to maintain texture, then layered. The \u0027Dum\u0027 method of sealing the pot to trap the steam...\u0026quot;","He looked at Vernon Dursley, who was hovering nearby, awaiting the verdict.","\u0026quot;Dursley,\u0026quot; Snape said evenly. \u0026quot;This layering technique. It is... akin to the brewing of Amortentia. The spiraling of scents. The distinct layers merging into a cohesive whole.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s just cooking, Snape,\u0026quot; Vernon shrugged modestly. \u0026quot;Rice and spice.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is chemistry,\u0026quot; Snape corrected. He took a forkful.","He chewed. He swallowed. He looked at the ocean.","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice devoid of its usual sneer, \u0026quot;the most competent thing I have encountered in years. Ten points to... the Chef.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Conclusion\u003c/strong\u003e","As the sun climbed higher, the group lay back on the sand, defeated by the sheer volume of ghee and love.","Sirius was lying on his back, tossing grapes into his mouth.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Sirius called out lazily. \u0026quot;Your uncle... he’s alright. For a Muggle.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s efficient,\u0026quot; Harry laughed from where he was lying next to Hermione.","\u0026quot;He’s a feeder,\u0026quot; Molly Weasley corrected, looking at the empty pots with professional respect. \u0026quot;And I need that Dal recipe.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll get you a copy, Molly,\u0026quot; Vernon promised from his deckchair, where he was sipping a chai. \u0026quot;I’ll have Kumar write it down. Standard Operating Procedure.\u0026quot;","The beach was quiet, save for the sound of waves and satisfied sighs. The Curry Coma had officially descended."]},{"num":114,"origNum":114,"title":"The Digestion March","wordCount":839,"paragraphs":["The sun was high and unforgiving. The beach of Isla de la Fortuna looked less like a wedding venue and more like the aftermath of a very calm, very full battle.","Bodies were strewn across the sand in various states of repose.","Ron Weasley was lying spread-eagled, a napkin still tucked into his collar. \u0026quot;I can feel the naan,\u0026quot; Ron whispered to the sky. \u0026quot;It’s expanding. I am 90% bread.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley was sitting in a deckchair, eyes closed, hands folded over his stomach. \u0026quot;It’s the fermentation,\u0026quot; he muttered in his sleep. \u0026quot;Gaseous expansion. Efficient but... uncomfortable.\u0026quot;","Severus Snape was sitting in the shade of a palm tree, staring at the ocean with the glazed look of a man who had eaten too much protein.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Drill Sergeant Returns\u003c/strong\u003e","Hermione Granger sat up. She brushed the sand off her legs. She looked at the comatose group. She checked her watch.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Hermione announced, clapping her hands.","The sound was sharp and irritatingly alert.","\u0026quot;Ugh,\u0026quot; Draco groaned, pulling his shirt over his face. \u0026quot;Granger. Stop being loud. It’s illegal.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We need to move,\u0026quot; Hermione declared, standing up and casting a shadow over Harry. \u0026quot;We have consumed approximately four thousand calories each. If we lay here, we will calcify. We need to aid digestion. A walk.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A walk?\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy cracked one eye open. \u0026quot;In this heat? To where? The horizon?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Around the headland,\u0026quot; Hermione pointed. \u0026quot;To the Blue Lagoon and back. It’s three miles. Gentle pace. Come on.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I refuse,\u0026quot; Ron stated flatly. \u0026quot;Leave me to the crabs.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Up!\u0026quot; Hermione ordered, pulling Harry by the hand. \u0026quot;Harry, help me. Motivation!\u0026quot;","Harry sighed, but he let her pull him up. He felt heavy, full of curry and contentment.","\u0026quot;She’s right,\u0026quot; Harry addressed the group. \u0026quot;If we don\u0027t move now, we’ll never make it to the pre-wedding dinner tonight.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;There’s \u003cem\u003emore\u003c/em\u003e food?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley gasped, scrambling up. \u0026quot;I need to make room! Come along, Molly! To the lagoon!\u0026quot;","Slowly, groaning and complaining, the wizarding elite hauled themselves upright.","\u0026quot;My calves,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, standing up stiffly. \u0026quot;They are protesting.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Walk it off, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, adjusting her hat. \u0026quot;Left, right, left.\u0026quot;","The procession began to shamble down the beach, looking like a very well-dressed, very full zombie apocalypse.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Straggler\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley Dursley stood up. He brushed the sand off his linen shorts.","He looked at the retreating backs of his parents and the wizards. He looked at the empty buffet tables.","A thought sparked in his brain. It was a dangerous thought. It was a stupid thought. It was a Dursley thought.","He stopped walking.","Harry, who was lagging behind with Draco, turned back. \u0026quot;Coming, Big D?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Dudley called out, waving a hand. \u0026quot;Just... got some sand in my shoe. You guys go ahead. I’ll jog to catch up.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Jog?\u0026quot; Draco raised an eyebrow. \u0026quot;After twelve pancakes? You’re braver than I am, Dursley.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go on!\u0026quot; Dudley urged. \u0026quot;I’ll be right behind you!\u0026quot;","Harry shrugged. \u0026quot;Okay. Don\u0027t get lost.\u0026quot;","Harry and Draco turned the corner of the rocky outcrop, disappearing from view.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Mastermind\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley was alone on the beach.","He looked around to make sure the coast was clear. He checked the jungle line. He checked the sky.","He grinned. It was a wicked, mischievous grin that reminded anyone watching of the time he threw his tortoise through a greenhouse roof, but with better intentions.","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Dudley whispered loudly.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","The elf appeared, still wearing his tuxedo t-shirt and sweatband. He was holding a half-eaten Jalebi.","\u0026quot;Master Dudley!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked. \u0026quot;Is you wanting more balloon bread?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, Dobby,\u0026quot; Dudley said, his voice low and conspiratorial. \u0026quot;I have a plan. An idea. A vision.\u0026quot;","He leaned down.","\u0026quot;The walk will take them an hour,\u0026quot; Dudley calculated. \u0026quot;That gives us time. I need you to set something up. Here. On the sand.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby can set up anything!\u0026quot; Dobby bounced on his toes. \u0026quot;Is it fireworks? Is it a statue?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Better,\u0026quot; Dudley said. \u0026quot;It’s a test. A Gauntlet.\u0026quot;","He looked Dobby in the eye.","\u0026quot;I need glasses, Dobby. Small ones. Shot glasses.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Glasses for drinking?\u0026quot; Dobby asked.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Dudley nodded. \u0026quot;But not just a few. I need five hundred.\u0026quot;","Dobby’s eyes went wide. \u0026quot;Five... hundred?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Five hundred,\u0026quot; Dudley confirmed. \u0026quot;And I need bottles. Every liquor Draco has. Tequila. Vodka. Rum. Firewhisky. We are going to line them up. A mile of shots. When they get back... they have to run the Gauntlet.\u0026quot;","Dobby stared at Dudley. He processed the request.","Five hundred glasses. A mile of alcohol. Unsuspecting wizards returning from a health walk.","Slowly, a manic smile spread across the elf’s face. His ears quivered with delight.","\u0026quot;A Gauntlet of Spirits!\u0026quot; Dobby whispered in awe. \u0026quot;To test their livers!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Dudley grinned. \u0026quot;Can you do it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby lives for the chaos!\u0026quot; the elf cheered, snapping his fingers. \u0026quot;Dobby will get the glass! Dobby will get the bottles! Dobby will arrange them in a pattern of doom!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good man,\u0026quot; Dudley said, rubbing his hands together. \u0026quot;Let’s get to work. We have an ambush to prepare.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":115,"origNum":115,"title":"The Architecture of Intoxication","wordCount":1052,"paragraphs":["\u003cstrong\u003eThe Walk of Wellness\u003c/strong\u003e","A mile down the coast, the \u0026quot;Digestion March\u0026quot; was actually working.","The group moved at a leisurely pace along the shoreline, the Caribbean breeze cooling their sun-drenched skin.","Ron Weasley patted his stomach. \u0026quot;It’s gone down,\u0026quot; he announced miraculously. \u0026quot;The bread has settled. I feel... nimble again. I could eat a biscuit.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t you dare,\u0026quot; Hermione warned, taking a deep breath of sea air. \u0026quot;Focus on the scenery, Ronald. Look at the blue.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley was walking with Lucius Malfoy, pointing out various rock formations.","\u0026quot;See that cliff face?\u0026quot; Vernon gestured. \u0026quot;Prime real estate. You could put a cantilevered hotel there. Infinity pool over the edge. Charge premium rates for the \u0027Risk Factor\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A cantilever,\u0026quot; Lucius mused, tapping his cane on a shell. \u0026quot;Defying gravity without magic. I am consistently baffled by your people, Vernon. You live life on the edge.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We live life on the margin, Lucius,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected. \u0026quot;Profit margin.\u0026quot;","Even Severus Snape looked relatively peaceful. He was walking at the back of the group with Dumbledore, inspecting a piece of washed-up coral.","\u0026quot;Calcium carbonate structure,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Porous. Useful for filtration potions.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is a pretty pink rock, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled, humming a tune. \u0026quot;Enjoy the aesthetics.\u0026quot;","They turned the headland, feeling refreshed, lighter, and ready to relax. They had no idea that they were walking straight into an ambush.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Construction Site\u003c/strong\u003e","Back at the main beach, Dudley Dursley was sweating. Not from exertion, but from the heat of scientific creation.","\u0026quot;Table, Dobby!\u0026quot; Dudley commanded. \u0026quot;Longer! We need fifty feet of surface area!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eSNAP.\u003c/em\u003e","Dobby conjured a table made of driftwood that stretched from the waterline back toward the palm trees. It was low, sleek, and dangerous.","\u0026quot;Glasses!\u0026quot; Dudley ordered.","\u003cem\u003eSNAP.\u003c/em\u003e","Five hundred shot glasses appeared. They weren\u0027t mismatched. They were uniform, crystal, and glinting menacingly in the sun.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Dudley said, rubbing his hands together. \u0026quot;The ratio is ten to one. Ten participants. Fifty shots each. It is the Olympian standard.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby is ready to pour!\u0026quot; the elf squeaked, holding a bottle of tequila in each hand. \u0026quot;Dobby loves the science of liquids!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 1: The Muggle Warm-Up (Shots 1-10)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;First ten,\u0026quot; Dudley directed. \u0026quot;The Warm-Up. Pure spirits. Tequila. Vodka. Gin. Rum. Sambuca. We ease them in.\u0026quot;","Dobby moved down the line like a blur, filling the first hundred glasses.","\u0026quot;Lemon drops for the tequila?\u0026quot; Dobby asked.","\u0026quot;No lemons,\u0026quot; Dudley said ruthlessly. \u0026quot;We ran with lemons. Now we drink without them.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 2: The Wizarding Kick (Shots 11-20)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Next ten,\u0026quot; Dudley said, pointing to the crates of magical booze Draco had imported. \u0026quot;Wizard stuff. Firewhisky. Gillywater with a Vodka chaser. And that stuff that smokes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dragon Barrel Brandy!\u0026quot; Dobby chirped, pouring a liquid that hissed as it hit the glass.","\u0026quot;Perfect,\u0026quot; Dudley grinned. \u0026quot;That’ll wake up Dad’s sinuses.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 3: The Hybrid Zone (Shots 21-40)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Now we mix,\u0026quot; Dudley said, channeling a mad scientist. \u0026quot;Muggle mixers with Wizard spirits. Coke and Firewhisky. Sprite and Elven Wine. Red Bull and... what is that blue stuff?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Romulan Ale!\u0026quot; Dobby said (confused about his universes, but the bottle was indeed blue). \u0026quot;It makes the drinker sing!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In it goes,\u0026quot; Dudley nodded. \u0026quot;Twenty shots of chaos.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 4: The Death Eaters (Shots 41-49)\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley stopped at the last section of the table. He looked grave.","\u0026quot;These,\u0026quot; Dudley whispered, \u0026quot;are the punishers. I call this section \u0027The Death Eaters\u0027. They are designed to hurt.\u0026quot;","He began to mix ingredients with terrifying creativity.","\u003cstrong\u003eShot 41: The Bellatrix.\u003c/strong\u003e Absinthe mixed with Tabasco sauce and a drop of black ink. \u0026quot;It’s crazy and it burns,\u0026quot; Dudley noted.","\u003cstrong\u003eShot 42: The Dementor.\u003c/strong\u003e Pure gin, chilled to absolute zero by Dobby’s magic, mixed with liquid nitrogen. \u0026quot;It sucks the happiness out of your throat.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eShot 43: The Greyback.\u003c/strong\u003e Hair of the Dog (literally, a hair from a werewolf potion) mixed with moonshine and raw egg.","\u003cstrong\u003eShot 44: The Cruciatus.\u003c/strong\u003e Chili-infused vodka mixed with popping candy. \u0026quot;It hurts, but it crackles.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eShots 45-49:\u003c/strong\u003e A blur of currdled cream liqueurs, sour mixes, and spirits so strong they had warning labels in Parseltongue.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Boss (Shot 50)\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley stood at the very end of the table. There were ten larger glasses waiting.","\u0026quot;And finally,\u0026quot; Dudley announced, his voice dropping to a reverent whisper. \u0026quot;The Voldemort.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Dark Lord Drink!\u0026quot; Dobby gasped, covering his eyes.","\u0026quot;Ingredients,\u0026quot; Dudley demanded.","Dobby levitated the components.","\u003cstrong\u003ePure Grain Alcohol (95% Muggle Spirit).\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eOgden’s Old Firewhisky (Cask Strength).\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eFresh Green Chillies (chopped).\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eRed Chilli Powder (Extra Hot).\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eA dash of Dragon Blood (for color).\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley mixed them. The liquid turned a violent, angry red. It didn\u0027t just sit in the glass; it seemed to throb. Fumes rose from it that made Dobby’s eyes water.","\u0026quot;It smells like death,\u0026quot; Dudley smiled, looking into the abyss of the glass. \u0026quot;It smells like victory.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Trap is Set\u003c/strong\u003e","Ten minutes later, the setup was complete.","A line of glass stretched down the beach like a shimmering snake. Five hundred shots. A rainbow of destruction.","Dudley stood at the finish line (the Voldemort end), arms crossed, wearing his sunglasses.","Dobby stood on the table, bouncing on his heels, vibrating with excitement.","\u0026quot;They is coming, Master Dudley!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked, his ears twitching. \u0026quot;Dobby hears the footsteps of the thirsty!\u0026quot;","Dudley checked his reflection in a spoon. \u0026quot;Let’s do this.\u0026quot;","Around the bend of the cliff, the voices of the returning walkers drifted over the sand.","\u0026quot;I’m just saying,\u0026quot; Ron’s voice carried, \u0026quot;a nap sounds good. Maybe a light snack.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Look!\u0026quot; Harry’s voice cut in. \u0026quot;What is... is that a barricade?\u0026quot;","The group rounded the corner. They stopped.","They saw the table. They saw the glistening rows of liquid. They saw Dudley Dursley standing like the guardian of a very alcoholic gate.","\u0026quot;Oh no,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, spotting the sheer volume of glass.","\u0026quot;Oh yes,\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley roared, spotting the sheer volume of alcohol. \u0026quot;DUDLEY! Is that... an open bar arrangement?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a Gauntlet, Dad!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted across the beach. \u0026quot;The Walk is over! The Crawl begins!\u0026quot;","Dobby jumped in the air. \u0026quot;PREPARE YOUR LIVERS! THE VOLDEMORT AWAITS!\u0026quot;","Snape stopped walking. He looked at the line of shots. He looked at the red, bubbling liquid at the end.","\u0026quot;I survived the war,\u0026quot; Snape said to McGonagall, his face pale. \u0026quot;I am not certain I will survive the nephew.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":116,"origNum":116,"title":"The Gauntlet of the Grooms and Brides","wordCount":1190,"paragraphs":["Dudley Dursley looked at the line of five hundred glasses. He looked at the six volunteers. He looked at the horizon where the parents were still walking, blissfully unaware of the liver damage awaiting them.","\u0026quot;Math,\u0026quot; Dudley muttered. \u0026quot;If Dad joins in... and Lucius... we’re going to run dry by Shot 30.\u0026quot;","He turned to his lieutenant.","\u0026quot;Dobby! We need a supply chain! The parents will want to prove they can keep up. We need a refill station! Active reloading!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Active reloading!\u0026quot; Dobby chirped, snapping his fingers.","A dozen house-elves popped out of the jungle. They were dressed in miniature Hawaiian shirts and sunglasses.","\u0026quot;Team!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked. \u0026quot;Operation Booze-Flow! When a glass is empty, you fills it! No glass stays dry!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Dudley said, turning to the six victims—Harry, Ron, Draco, Hermione, Ginny, and Luna.","They stood at the starting line. They looked determined. They looked terrified.","\u0026quot;The Rules,\u0026quot; Dudley barked, checking his stopwatch. \u0026quot;One shot every thirty seconds. I blow the whistle, you drink. You do not stop. You do not hesitate. If you vomit, you do it in the ocean, then you come back. Clear?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Crystal,\u0026quot; Harry said, loosening his tie.","\u0026quot;I’m scared,\u0026quot; Ron whispered to Hermione.","\u0026quot;It’s just chemistry, Ron,\u0026quot; Hermione said, though her voice was shaking. \u0026quot;Ethanol and... bravery.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;On my mark!\u0026quot; Dudley raised the whistle. \u0026quot;Three... Two... One!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 1: The Muggle Warm-Up (Shots 1-10)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cem\u003eShot 1: Tequila.\u003c/em\u003e","They downed it.","\u0026quot;Salt!\u0026quot; Draco gasped, licking his hand frantically. \u0026quot;Where is the salt? It tastes like liquid regret!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s the point, Malfoy!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted. \u0026quot;Thirty seconds! Go!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 5: Sambuca.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;It’s licorice,\u0026quot; Luna hummed, swallowing happily. \u0026quot;But it burns like a Nargle bite.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 10: Absinthe.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I can see sound,\u0026quot; Ron announced, his eyes dilating. \u0026quot;Harry, your voice is purple.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 2: The Wizarding Kick (Shots 11-20)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Wizard stuff!\u0026quot; Dudley yelled. \u0026quot;Firewhisky! Go!\u0026quot;","They hit the magical spirits. This was familiar territory, but the pace was relentless.","\u003cem\u003eShot 15: Dragon Barrel Brandy.\u003c/em\u003e","Steam shot out of Harry’s ears.","\u0026quot;Whoo!\u0026quot; Ginny yelled, slamming the glass down. \u0026quot;That hits the spot! Come on, Draco! Keep up!\u0026quot;","Draco was struggling. He was holding onto the table for support. His linen shirt was unbuttoned to his navel.","\u0026quot;I am a Malfoy,\u0026quot; Draco slurred to a coconut. \u0026quot;I have endurance. I have... breeding.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 20: Gillywater Vodka.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I feel like I have gills,\u0026quot; Hermione giggled, swaying dangerously. \u0026quot;Harry, look. I’m swimming on land.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 3: The Hybrid Zone (Shots 21-40)\u003c/strong\u003e","This is where the wheels started to come off.","The mix of sugar, caffeine, and heavy magic hit their bloodstreams like a runaway train.","\u003cem\u003eShot 25: The Red Bull \u0026amp; Elven Wine.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I AM VIBRATING!\u0026quot; Ron roared. He started doing jumping jacks between shots. \u0026quot;LOOK AT ME! I AM ENERGY!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 32: The Romulan Ale (Blue Stuff).\u003c/em\u003e","Hermione drank the blue liquid. She blinked.","\u0026quot;Logic,\u0026quot; Hermione announced loudly to the ocean. \u0026quot;Logic is a construct! Gravity is a suggestion! I am the Ostrich Queen!\u0026quot;","She tried to bury her head in Harry’s shoulder but missed and headbutted his arm.","\u0026quot;Ow,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, swaying. \u0026quot;Nice aim, Mione.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 38: The Sour Apple Schnapps \u0026amp; Potion No. 9.\u003c/em\u003e","Draco Malfoy was crying. He wasn\u0027t sad. He was just crying.","\u0026quot;It’s so beautiful,\u0026quot; Draco sobbed, holding up the empty glass. \u0026quot;The glass. It’s round. It’s perfect. I love you, glass.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 4: The Death Eaters (Shots 41-49)\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley looked at his watch. They were wobbling. They were sweating. But they were still standing.","\u0026quot;The Gauntlet gets mean now!\u0026quot; Dudley warned. \u0026quot;Shot 41! The Bellatrix!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 41: Absinthe, Tabasco, Ink.\u003c/em\u003e","They drank.","\u0026quot;AGH!\u0026quot; Ginny screamed. \u0026quot;SPICY! WHY IS IT SPICY?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s evil!\u0026quot; Ron yelled, fanning his tongue. \u0026quot;It tastes like she’s actually in my mouth! Get her out!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 42: The Dementor (Liquid Nitrogen Gin).\u003c/em\u003e","They drank the smoking, freezing liquid.","Harry shivered violently. \u0026quot;Cold,\u0026quot; he chattered. \u0026quot;So cold. Someone cast a Patronus!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am the Patronus!\u0026quot; Luna cheered, spinning in a circle. \u0026quot;I am a hare! Hop hop!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 44: The Cruciatus (Popping Candy).\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;MY MOUTH IS EXPLODING!\u0026quot; Draco screamed, clutching his jaw. \u0026quot;THE CRACKLING! IT’S INSIDE MY TEETH!\u0026quot;","By Shot 49, they were a mess. Hermione was holding onto Ginny to stay upright. Harry was leaning on the table. Ron was trying to duel a seagull with a celery stick. Draco was trying to re-button his shirt but had forgotten how buttons worked.","\u0026quot;Last one!\u0026quot; Dudley bellowed, looking impressed. \u0026quot;The Big Boss! The Voldemort!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Boss (Shot 50)\u003c/strong\u003e","Dobby handed them the large glasses.","The red liquid bubbled. The fumes of the pure grain alcohol and dragon blood rose up, stinging their eyes.","\u0026quot;To Tom!\u0026quot; Harry slurred, raising the glass. \u0026quot;The dead bastard!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To Tom!\u0026quot; they roared.","They drank.","It wasn\u0027t a drink. It was a tactical nuclear strike.","The grain alcohol burned the throat. The chili powder incinerated the tongue. The dragon blood added a metallic, heavy aftertaste that felt like licking a sword.","\u003cem\u003eGULP.\u003c/em\u003e","Silence.","Harry’s eyes bulged. He opened his mouth. No sound came out.","Ron turned a shade of red that defied nature. He clutched his throat.","\u0026quot;FIRE!\u0026quot; Ron rasped. \u0026quot;DRAGON FIRE!\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a squeak. Smoke—actual black smoke—puffed out of her ears.","\u0026quot;I think I melted,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, sliding slowly down the table leg until she was sitting in the sand.","Ginny Weasley stood stock still. She looked at Draco.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; she whispered.","\u0026quot;Yes, Red?\u0026quot; Draco croaked, his voice an octave lower than usual.","\u0026quot;I can’t feel my face.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Me neither,\u0026quot; Draco agreed.","Then, the chili hit Luna.","Luna Lovegood threw her head back and let out a sound that was half-sneeze, half-roar.","\u003cem\u003eCHOO-ROAR!\u003c/em\u003e","A jet of actual sparks shot from her nose.","\u0026quot;Oh, lovely,\u0026quot; Luna smiled hazily, smoke drifting from her nostrils. \u0026quot;The Nargles have fireworks.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","They had done it. Fifty shots.","Harry stumbled away from the table. He felt light. He felt heavy. He felt... invincible.","\u0026quot;We won,\u0026quot; Harry declared to the sand. \u0026quot;We beat the Gauntlet.\u0026quot;","He tried to high-five Ron, missed by a foot, and slapped Dudley on the chest instead.","\u0026quot;Good job, Big D,\u0026quot; Harry mumbled. \u0026quot;Good juice.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You guys are animals,\u0026quot; Dudley laughed, shaking his head. \u0026quot;Absolute units.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy was currently trying to negotiate with a crab.","\u0026quot;Listen,\u0026quot; Draco was saying seriously to the crustacean. \u0026quot;I have galleons. I will buy your shell. I need armor. The sun is attacking me.\u0026quot;","Hermione was lying on her back, making sand angels. \u0026quot;I’m flying, Harry! Look at me! I’m a aerodynamic equation!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You sure are, Mione,\u0026quot; Harry grinned, sliding down to join her in the sand.","They lay there, a pile of intoxicated heroes, watching the sky spin.","\u0026quot;Here they come,\u0026quot; Dudley warned, looking down the beach.","The parents and professors were rounding the headland, looking refreshed, healthy, and completely unaware that they were walking into a minefield of five hundred refilled shot glasses.","\u0026quot;Oh no,\u0026quot; Ron giggled from the sand. \u0026quot;Dad. Dad is going to die.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My father,\u0026quot; Draco whispered in horror, staring at the sky. \u0026quot;He’s going to drink the Voldemort. He’s going to explode.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shhh,\u0026quot; Ginny put a finger to her lips. \u0026quot;Let’s watch.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":117,"origNum":117,"title":"The Parental Apocalypse","wordCount":1380,"paragraphs":["The \u0026quot;Walk of Wellness\u0026quot; ended not with health, but with a confrontation.","Vernon Dursley rounded the corner, feeling invigorated by the sea air. He stopped. He saw the table. He saw the five hundred refilled glasses glinting in the sun.","He saw his son, standing like a bouncer at a club entrance, stopwatch in hand.","And he saw the six young heroes of the wizarding world lying in the sand, groaning, giggling, and occasionally emitting sparks.","\u0026quot;Dudley!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed. \u0026quot;What is the meaning of this infrastructure?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the Gauntlet, Dad!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted, waving the whistle. \u0026quot;The kids finished it! Fifty shots! They survived! Are you going to let them beat you?\u0026quot;","Vernon’s mustache bristled. He looked at Harry, who was currently trying to high-five a crab. He looked at the glasses.","\u0026quot;A challenge,\u0026quot; Vernon growled. \u0026quot;A drinking challenge. In the middle of the day.\u0026quot;","He looked at Lucius Malfoy.","\u0026quot;Well, Lucius?\u0026quot; Vernon challenged. \u0026quot;You talked a big game about the wine cellar. Can you handle the volume?\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy smoothed his linen suit. He looked at Draco, who was lying on his back singing the Hogwarts school song in a falsetto.","\u0026quot;A Malfoy does not decline a challenge,\u0026quot; Lucius sneered, though he eyed the table warily. \u0026quot;Especially when the honor of the House is at stake.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m in!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley cheered, rolling up his sleeves. \u0026quot;I want to taste the Muggle potions!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, for heaven\u0027s sake,\u0026quot; Molly sighed. She looked at Narcissa. \u0026quot;If we don\u0027t join them, they’ll die.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Agreed,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, taking off her sunhat. \u0026quot;We shall escort them.\u0026quot;","Just then, Xenophilius Lovegood wandered out of the jungle, wearing bright yellow robes and a wreath of seaweed.","\u0026quot;Is there a ceremony?\u0026quot; Xenophilius asked, blinking at the shot glasses. \u0026quot;The Plimpy told me there would be nectar.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Grab a glass, Xeno!\u0026quot; Arthur yelled. \u0026quot;We’re running the Gauntlet!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lineup\u003c/strong\u003e","Seven parents stood at the starting line: Vernon, Petunia, Lucius, Narcissa, Arthur, Molly, and Xenophilius.","\u0026quot;Same rules!\u0026quot; Dudley barked. \u0026quot;Thirty seconds! No hesitation! No mercy! Dobby, are the refills ready?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby is locked and loaded!\u0026quot; the elf screamed, holding two bottles of rum.","\u0026quot;GO!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 1: The Muggle Shock (Shots 1-10)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cem\u003eShot 1: Tequila.\u003c/em\u003e","Arthur Weasley drank it. His eyes bulged.","\u0026quot;It... it has teeth!\u0026quot; Arthur gasped, clutching his throat. \u0026quot;It bites the throat! It is aggressive water!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s Tequila, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, slamming his glass down. \u0026quot;It puts hair on your liver! Next!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 5: Gin.\u003c/em\u003e","Lucius Malfoy sniffed it. \u0026quot;It smells like a pine forest.\u0026quot; He drank. He shuddered elegantly.","\u0026quot;Peasant juice,\u0026quot; Lucius rasped. \u0026quot;But effective.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 8: Sambuca.\u003c/em\u003e","Petunia Dursley drank the aniseed spirit. She didn\u0027t wince. She didn\u0027t cough. She slammed the glass down.","\u0026quot;Licorice,\u0026quot; Petunia said calmly. \u0026quot;Vernon, this is child\u0027s play.\u0026quot;","Narcissa looked at Petunia with deep respect. \u0026quot;You have a stomach of iron, Petunia.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 2: The Wizarding Revenge (Shots 11-20)\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Wizard booze!\u0026quot; Dudley yelled. \u0026quot;Dad, watch out! This stuff kicks!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 12: Ogden’s Old Firewhisky.\u003c/em\u003e","Vernon drank. Smoke shot out of his ears. His face turned a shade of purple that defied the color spectrum.","\u0026quot;WHOO!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted, fanning his mouth. \u0026quot;Spicy! That’s good! That clears the pipes!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 16: Banshee Screech (A screeching liquid).\u003c/em\u003e","Xenophilius drank it. He let out a high-pitched giggle.","\u0026quot;It tickles the Wrackspurts!\u0026quot; Xeno beamed, swaying. \u0026quot;I feel floaty!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 19: Dragon Brandy.\u003c/em\u003e","Molly Weasley downed it like water. \u0026quot;Arthur, you’re lagging!\u0026quot; she scolded. \u0026quot;Drink up! Don\u0027t let Lucius beat you!\u0026quot;","Lucius was struggling. He was holding onto the table with one hand. His linen suit was unbuttoned at the collar (a historic first).","\u0026quot;I am... unaffected,\u0026quot; Lucius slurred, leaning heavily on his cane. \u0026quot;The Malfoy constitution is... impervious.\u0026quot;","He missed the table when he tried to put his glass down.","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 3: The Hybrid Zone (Shots 21-40)\u003c/strong\u003e","This was where the parents began to unravel.","\u003cem\u003eShot 25: Red Bull \u0026amp; Vodka.\u003c/em\u003e","Lucius drank the energy drink mix. His eyes snapped open. His pupils dilated.","\u0026quot;My heart,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, touching his chest. \u0026quot;It is beating... fast. Very fast. I feel... urgent. Narcissa, I need to organize something. I need to file paperwork. Right now.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s caffeine, Lucius!\u0026quot; Hermione shouted from the sand. \u0026quot;Ride the wave!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I AM VIBRATING!\u0026quot; Lucius roared. \u0026quot;I AM A BEING OF PURE ENERGY!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 30: The Blue Stuff (Romulan Ale).\u003c/em\u003e","Arthur Weasley drank the blue liquid. He looked at Vernon.","\u0026quot;Vernon!\u0026quot; Arthur shouted. \u0026quot;I understand now! The plug! The spark plug! It is the soul of the car!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You got it, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted back, putting an arm around him. \u0026quot;Combustion! We are combustible men!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 38: The Sour Apple.\u003c/em\u003e","Petunia and Narcissa were leaning on each other.","\u0026quot;It’s sour,\u0026quot; Narcissa giggled—an actual giggle. \u0026quot;Petunia, look at my shoes. They are spinning.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My shoes are spinning too, Cissy,\u0026quot; Petunia laughed. \u0026quot;Let’s spin with them!\u0026quot;","They did a little twirl, nearly knocking over Xenophilius, who was currently having a conversation with a coconut.","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 4: The Death Eaters (Shots 41-49)\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley watched with awe. They were not stopping.","\u0026quot;The punishers!\u0026quot; Dudley warned. \u0026quot;Shot 41! The Bellatrix!\u0026quot;","Lucius stared at the glass. \u0026quot;Bella,\u0026quot; he sneered. \u0026quot;She was always... spicy.\u0026quot;","He drank it. He screamed.","\u0026quot;SHE BIT ME!\u0026quot; Lucius yelled, clawing at his tongue. \u0026quot;THE HARPY BIT MY TONGUE!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Drink the milk!\u0026quot; Molly shouted, handing him a White Russian from the next line. \u0026quot;Neutralize the acid!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 42: The Dementor.\u003c/em\u003e","Vernon drank the freezing liquid. He shivered, his mustache frosting over.","\u0026quot;Chilly!\u0026quot; Vernon chattered. \u0026quot;Turn up the thermostat!\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley cast a Patronus—a silver weasel—that ran around the table, cheering them on.","\u0026quot;Go, Weasel, Go!\u0026quot; Arthur cheered, chasing it.","\u003cem\u003eShot 45: The Cruciatus.\u003c/em\u003e","Xenophilius drank the popping candy vodka.","\u0026quot;My head is full of nargles!\u0026quot; Xeno declared, eyes wide. \u0026quot;They are popping! Pop! Pop! Pop!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Boss (Shot 50)\u003c/strong\u003e","They reached the end. Fifty shots.","They were swaying. They were sweating. Lucius was vibrating from the Red Bull. Vernon was frosted. Molly was fanning herself.","\u0026quot;The Voldemort,\u0026quot; Dudley announced solemnly.","The seven parents picked up the large glasses of red, bubbling, dragon-blood-infused grain alcohol.","Arthur Weasley raised his glass. He swayed, but he held it high.","\u0026quot;To the kids,\u0026quot; Arthur slurred. \u0026quot;Who saved us all.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the kids!\u0026quot; the parents roared.","They drank.","\u003cem\u003eGULP.\u003c/em\u003e","The reaction was immediate and nuclear.","Vernon’s eyes watered. He let out a roar that sounded like a bear stepping on a Lego.","\u0026quot;HAAAAARGH!\u0026quot;","Petunia hiccuped, and a small puff of red smoke came out of her mouth.","Lucius Malfoy stood perfectly still. His eyes crossed.","\u0026quot;I can see time,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;It is... slippery.\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley grabbed Arthur’s tie to stay upright. \u0026quot;Arthur... I think... I think I need to sit down.\u0026quot;","Xenophilius Lovegood simply slowly, gracefully, toppled backward onto the sand like a felled tree.","\u0026quot;Soft,\u0026quot; Xeno murmured from the ground.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","The parents stumbled away from the table. They didn\u0027t make it to the villa.","They collapsed onto the sand next to their children.","Lucius fell next to Draco.","\u0026quot;Father?\u0026quot; Draco asked, looking at the vibrating man.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; Lucius said, staring at the sky with wide, caffeinated eyes. \u0026quot;I understand the Muggles now. They drink poison for fun. They are... formidable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We did it!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered from where he was lying next to Harry. \u0026quot;Dursley... stamina! Unbeatable!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re a machine, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, patting his arm.","Arthur Weasley was lying next to Ron, giggling. \u0026quot;The spark plug, Ron! I get it! It’s the fire!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go to sleep, Dad,\u0026quot; Ron chuckled.","Narcissa and Petunia were sitting together, braiding each other\u0027s hair (or trying to; their coordination was gone).","\u0026quot;We should open a bakery,\u0026quot; Petunia suggested. \u0026quot;Gin and Cake.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Brilliant,\u0026quot; Narcissa agreed. \u0026quot;We shall call it \u0027The Tipsy Tart\u0027.\u0026quot;","The beach was a battlefield of empty glasses and snoring bodies.","Dudley stood over them, triumphant.","\u0026quot;Dobby,\u0026quot; Dudley said, wiping his brow. \u0026quot;We need water. Lots of water. And aspirin. And maybe a Pepper-Up Potion.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby is on it!\u0026quot; the elf chirped.","As the sun began to dip, casting long shadows over the sleeping, intoxicated assembly of the Wizarding World\u0027s finest (and the Dursleys), peace reigned on Isla de la Fortuna.","They had survived the war. They had survived the wedding planning. And now, they had survived the Gauntlet.","Nothing could stop them now. Except, perhaps, the hangover."]},{"num":118,"origNum":118,"title":"The Tenure of Titanium Livers","wordCount":1175,"paragraphs":["The beach was now a landscape of carnage. The Parents were snoring in a pile near the palm trees. The \u0026quot;Children\u0026quot; were lying in the sand, groaning and throwing popcorn at each other.","But the bar was still open.","Dudley Dursley, looking like a weary general who had seen too much war, wiped down the driftwood table.","\u0026quot;Dobby,\u0026quot; Dudley croaked. \u0026quot;Reset. One last round. The Veterans.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby is ready!\u0026quot; the elf chirped, though he was now wearing five hats and a pair of swimming goggles.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lineup\u003c/strong\u003e","The final group approached the table.","On the left: The Marauders \u0026amp; Co.","Sirius Black cracked his knuckles, looking arrogant. Remus Lupin looked resigned but game. Nymphadora Tonks changed her hair to a vibrant \u0026quot;Party Purple.\u0026quot;","In the center: The Potions Master.","Severus Snape adjusted his black sleeves. He looked at the glasses with the clinical detachment of a man about to dissect a flobberworm.","On the right: The Administration.","Albus Dumbledore and Minerva McGonagall stepped up. Dumbledore was humming. McGonagall was checking her hat pin.","Sirius leaned over the table, grinning at McGonagall.","\u0026quot;You sure about this, Minnie?\u0026quot; Sirius teased, nudging Remus. \u0026quot;It’s high-proof stuff. Not your usual sherry. We don\u0027t want you breaking a hip.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Tonks giggled. \u0026quot;Maybe you should sit this one out, Professor Dumbledore. It’s a young person\u0027s game. Your heart rate, you know?\u0026quot;","Remus winced. \u0026quot;Padfoot, Tonks... don\u0027t poke the dragon.\u0026quot;","McGonagall slowly turned her head. She looked at Sirius over her square spectacles. A small, dangerous smile touched her lips.","She looked at Dumbledore. Dumbledore looked back, his eyes twinkling with the force of a supernova.","\u0026quot;The youth,\u0026quot; Dumbledore mused. \u0026quot;They believe they invented endurance.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shall we show them, Albus?\u0026quot; McGonagall asked pleasantly.","\u0026quot;I believe we shall, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;The game is on.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Start\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Dudley yelled, raising the whistle. \u0026quot;The rules are strict! One shot every thirty seconds! You must wait for the whis—\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTWEEEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","Before the whistle even finished sounding, Dumbledore and McGonagall moved.","They didn\u0027t drink. They \u003cem\u003einhaled\u003c/em\u003e.","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 1 \u0026amp; 2: The Speed Run\u003c/strong\u003e","While Sirius was dramatically toasting the ocean and Snape was sniffing the bouquet of the Tequila, the Headmaster and Deputy were blurring.","\u003cem\u003eClink. Gulp. Clink. Gulp.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Thirty seconds!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted. \u0026quot;Hey! You’re going too fast! Those are the guidelines!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Guidelines are for students, Mr. Dursley!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered, downing three shots of Vodka in a row. \u0026quot;Faculty have tenure!\u0026quot;","McGonagall was matching him shot for shot. She picked up the Gin. Down. The Rum. Down. The Sambuca. Down.","She didn\u0027t wince. She didn\u0027t cough. She adjusted her glasses.","\u0026quot;Peat,\u0026quot; McGonagall critiqued the whiskey. \u0026quot;A bit young. Needs more cask time.\u0026quot;","Sirius stared, his glass of rum halfway to his mouth. \u0026quot;Remus... are they... lapping us?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are on Shot 15, Sirius,\u0026quot; Remus whispered, terrified. \u0026quot;We are on Shot 4.\u0026quot;","Snape narrowed his eyes. He abandoned his clinical approach. He grabbed two glasses at once.","\u0026quot;I will not be out-drunk by a Gryffindor and a geriatric!\u0026quot; Snape snarled, downing them.","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 3: The Hybrid Chaos\u003c/strong\u003e","By the time they hit the mixed drinks, the Marauders were feeling it.","\u003cem\u003eShot 25: Red Bull \u0026amp; Firewhisky.\u003c/em\u003e","Tonks’s nose turned into a pig snout. \u0026quot;Oink!\u0026quot; she giggled. \u0026quot;I’m a pig! Remus, look! I’m a party pig!\u0026quot;","Remus swayed. \u0026quot;You’re beautiful, Dora. I think I’m vibrating.\u0026quot;","Sirius was singing. \u0026quot;OH, HOGWARTS, HOGWARTS, HOGGY WARTY HOGWARTS!\u0026quot;","Snape was angry. The alcohol had stripped away his stoicism.","\u0026quot;Potter!\u0026quot; Snape yelled at the ocean. \u0026quot;Your father was a swine! And this Gillywater tastes like bog water! Ten points from Hufflepuff!\u0026quot;","Meanwhile, Dumbledore and McGonagall were at Shot 35.","They were having a polite conversation while knocking back high-octane cocktails like they were water.","\u0026quot;I do think the curriculum needs updating,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, downing a \u003cem\u003eRomulan Ale\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;The third years are soft.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Agreed, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore nodded, drinking a \u003cem\u003eSour Apple Schnapps\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;Perhaps we should reintroduce the dangerous beasts. A manticore or two.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePhase 4: The Death Eaters\u003c/strong\u003e","The Marauders hit the wall.","\u003cem\u003eShot 41: The Bellatrix (Absinthe \u0026amp; Tabasco).\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;HOT!\u0026quot; Sirius screamed, running in a small circle. \u0026quot;MY TONGUE IS ON FIRE! AGUAMENTI! AGUAMENTI MY MOUTH!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eShot 42: The Dementor (Liquid Nitrogen).\u003c/em\u003e","Remus drank it. His eyes rolled back. The wolf inside him whimpered.","\u0026quot;Cold,\u0026quot; Remus whispered, hugging himself. \u0026quot;So cold. Chocolate. I need chocolate.\u0026quot;","Snape drank the \u003cem\u003eCruciatus\u003c/em\u003e (Popping Candy).","\u0026quot;IT POPS!\u0026quot; Snape roared, looking betrayed. \u0026quot;WHY DOES IT POP? IT IS INSOLENT CANDY!\u0026quot;","He threw the glass into the sand.","Ahead of them, Dumbledore and McGonagall were at the end.","McGonagall drank the \u003cem\u003eBellatrix\u003c/em\u003e. She smacked her lips.","\u0026quot;Spicy,\u0026quot; she noted. \u0026quot;Like a good haggis.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore drank the \u003cem\u003eDementor\u003c/em\u003e. He exhaled a puff of cold air.","\u0026quot;Refreshing!\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared. \u0026quot;Like a breath mint!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Boss\u003c/strong\u003e","The Marauders and Snape stumbled to the end of the table. They were a mess. Sirius was crying about a motorcycle. Tonks was a pig. Snape was arguing with a coconut.","They looked at the final shot. \u003cem\u003eThe Voldemort\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;We have to,\u0026quot; Sirius slurred. \u0026quot;For James.\u0026quot;","They drank.","\u003cem\u003eGULP.\u003c/em\u003e","Total devastation.","Sirius collapsed face-first into the sand. \u0026quot;I see stars. They are laughing at me.\u0026quot;","Remus sat down hard. \u0026quot;I think the wolf just passed out.\u0026quot;","Tonks changed her hair to invisible and fell asleep on Remus’s shoulder.","Snape drank it. His eyes crossed. He stiffened like a board. Then, slowly, he tipped backward, rigid as a plank, and landed in the sand with a \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;I resign,\u0026quot; Snape whispered to the universe.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Tenure\u003c/strong\u003e","Only two remained standing.","Albus Dumbledore and Minerva McGonagall picked up the massive glasses of dragon-blood grain alcohol.","The younger generation—Harry, Ron, Draco, Hermione—watched from the sand, eyes wide.","\u0026quot;They can\u0027t,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;That stuff killed Vernon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cheers, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled, clinking his glass against hers.","\u0026quot;Slàinte, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall replied.","They drank. The red liquid vanished.","The beach held its breath.","Dumbledore set the glass down gently. He patted his mouth with a handkerchief.","McGonagall set her glass down. She straightened her hat.","They looked at each other.","\u0026quot;A robust vintage,\u0026quot; Dumbledore commented. \u0026quot;Notes of... fire?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dragon blood,\u0026quot; McGonagall identified correctly. \u0026quot;And a hint of chili. Warming. Good for the joints.\u0026quot;","They turned to look at the carnage behind them. They looked at the unconscious Snape, the weeping Sirius, and the awestruck crowd.","Dumbledore clapped his hands together. He didn\u0027t sway. He didn\u0027t slur.","\u0026quot;Well!\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;That was a delightful aperitif! Is it time for dinner? I find myself quite peckish.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I could eat,\u0026quot; McGonagall agreed, checking her watch. \u0026quot;The walk built up an appetite.\u0026quot;","They turned and walked back toward the villa, moving in a perfectly straight line, discussing the transfiguration properties of sand.","Harry Potter stared at their retreating backs.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re monsters,\u0026quot; Harry whispered in pure awe.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re legends,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, staring at Snape’s unconscious body. \u0026quot;Remind me never, ever to challenge McGonagall to a drinking contest.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think,\u0026quot; Ron said, staring at the empty glasses, \u0026quot;that Dumbledore might actually be magic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He \u003cem\u003eis\u003c/em\u003e magic, Ron,\u0026quot; Hermione said, shaking her head. \u0026quot;He is pure magic.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":119,"origNum":119,"title":"The Toxicology Tribunal","wordCount":1080,"paragraphs":["The walk back to the villa was interrupted before it even began.","Albus Dumbledore and Minerva McGonagall had taken three steps toward the path when a groan from the sand stopped them.","\u0026quot;Stop,\u0026quot; a voice rasped. It sounded like gravel being ground in a mortar.","Severus Snape sat up. Sand cascaded off his black shirt. His hair was wild. His sunglasses were askew. He looked like a vampire who had woken up on a beach in Ibiza and was not happy about it.","\u0026quot;Do not,\u0026quot; Snape hissed, pointing a trembling finger at them, \u0026quot;move another inch.\u0026quot;","Behind him, the rest of the casualties began to stir.","Sirius Black rolled over, clutching his head. \u0026quot;Did we win? Did the motorbike fly?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We died, Padfoot,\u0026quot; Remus moaned, his face buried in his hands. \u0026quot;We died of chili powder.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;How?\u0026quot; Ron Weasley squeaked from the fetal position. \u0026quot;How are they standing? They drank the Voldemort. They drank \u003cem\u003etwo\u003c/em\u003e Voldemorts.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Confrontation\u003c/strong\u003e","The group rallied. Fueled by confusion and wounded pride, the parents, the children, and the Marauders dragged themselves into a semi-circle around the two professors.","Vernon Dursley, whose face was still a mottled shade of red, squinted at Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;Headmaster,\u0026quot; Vernon croaked. \u0026quot;I consider myself a man of capacity. I have closed deals over three-martini lunches. I have survived Christmas at the Rotary Club. But that red sludge... it reset my factory settings. And you... you look like you’ve just had a light spritzer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I demand a toxicology screen!\u0026quot; Snape roared (or tried to, it came out as a loud wheeze). He pulled himself to his feet, swaying dangerously.","\u0026quot;I am a Potions Master. I know chemistry. I know biology. I calculated the ethanol content of that gauntlet. It was sufficient to stun a Basilisk. It should have rendered a human comatose. Explain your metabolism!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a trick!\u0026quot; Draco Malfoy accused from the sand, where Ginny was currently using his stomach as a pillow. \u0026quot;Transfigured water? A Bezoar in the cheek?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cheating!\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy whispered, looking at his cane which was currently floating two feet to his left. \u0026quot;They cheated the Gauntlet.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Defense: Minerva\u003c/strong\u003e","Minerva McGonagall adjusted her tartan hat. She looked at the wreckage of the younger generations. She looked at Snape, swaying in the breeze.","She let out a sharp, derisive sniff.","\u0026quot;Cheating?\u0026quot; McGonagall said, her Scottish brogue thickening with disdain. \u0026quot;Mr. Malfoy, do not insult me. I do not cheat. I endure.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But the volume!\u0026quot; Hermione argued weakly, holding her head. \u0026quot;The liver capacity!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Miss Granger,\u0026quot; McGonagall said crisply. \u0026quot;I am a Scotsman. I was weaned on single malt. My christening water was 80 proof.\u0026quot;","She stepped forward, looking down at Sirius and Remus.","\u0026quot;Furthermore,\u0026quot; she continued, her eyes flashing. \u0026quot;I have served as the Head of Gryffindor House for forty years. I taught the Marauders.\u0026quot; She pointed at Sirius. \u0026quot;I taught the Weasley Twins.\u0026quot; She pointed at Fred and George. \u0026quot;And I taught Harry Potter.\u0026quot;","She smoothed her robes.","\u0026quot;Do you have any idea the level of chemical assistance required to grade essays written by Crabbe and Goyle without setting the castle on fire? Do you know how much sherry it takes to cope with students turning into canaries in the middle of a lecture?\u0026quot;","She looked at Snape.","\u0026quot;You hide in your dungeon, Severus. You brew your little calming draughts. I face the chaos head-on. My tolerance is not biological; it is \u003cem\u003eprofessional\u003c/em\u003e. I am made of tartan, grit, and gin. Now, pick yourself up. You’re making Slytherin look soft.\u0026quot;","Snape opened his mouth. He closed it. He looked at the sand.","\u0026quot;Soft,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, devastated.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Defense: Albus\u003c/strong\u003e","All eyes turned to Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;And you?\u0026quot; Vernon asked. \u0026quot;You\u0027re not Scottish. You\u0027re... ancient. No offense.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;None taken, Vernon,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled, checking his nails. \u0026quot;I am indeed one hundred and fifteen years old.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Then how?\u0026quot; Harry asked. \u0026quot;The Voldemort... it had dragon blood in it. It tasted like burning iron.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ah,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled. \u0026quot;The secret, Harry, is Alchemy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Alchemy?\u0026quot; Hermione perked up, despite her nausea. \u0026quot;You transmuted the alcohol?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, no,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled. \u0026quot;That would be cheating. No, I speak of the Alchemy of the Soul.\u0026quot;","He began to pace, looking like a philosopher lecturing a class of hungover students.","\u0026quot;You see,\u0026quot; Dumbledore explained, \u0026quot;when one reaches my age, one realizes that the body is merely a vessel. A vessel that has survived dark wizards, cursed rings, and Bertie Bott’s Vomit-Flavored Beans.\u0026quot;","He stopped in front of Lucius Malfoy.","\u0026quot;You drink to forget, Lucius. You drink to numb the senses.\u0026quot;","He looked at Ron. \u0026quot;You drink to celebrate.\u0026quot;","He looked at Snape. \u0026quot;You drink to tolerate existence.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore spread his arms wide.","\u0026quot;I drink... to \u003cem\u003eenhance\u003c/em\u003e. To feel the burn! To taste the fire! I do not fight the alcohol, my friends. I invite it in! I offer it a lemon drop! I let it mingle with the magic in my blood until it realizes it is outmatched!\u0026quot;","He leaned in close to Vernon.","\u0026quot;Also,\u0026quot; Dumbledore whispered loudly, \u0026quot;I have a sweet tooth. The sugar content in those cocktails was delightful. It was basically a liquid cake buffet. I feel energized!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Verdict\u003c/strong\u003e","The group stared at him.","\u0026quot;He runs on sugar,\u0026quot; Dudley realized, horrified. \u0026quot;He’s like a giant hummingbird.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s terrifying,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;He beat the Dark Lord, and now he beat the bar.\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley, who was currently lying on his back making sand angels, raised a hand.","\u0026quot;I have a theory,\u0026quot; Arthur slurred. \u0026quot;His beard. It acts as a filter. It absorbs the toxins.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t be ridiculous, Arthur,\u0026quot; Molly sighed, sitting up. \u0026quot;He’s just... Dumbledore. He plays by different rules.\u0026quot;","Snape sighed—a long, rattling sound of defeat. He straightened his spine. He brushed the sand from his black shorts.","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Snape conceded stiffly. \u0026quot;You possess... superior constitutions. I yield the title.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Gracious of you, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed.","\u0026quot;However,\u0026quot; Snape added, narrowing his eyes. \u0026quot;If I find out you used a Bezoar, Albus, I will poison your tea.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I wouldn\u0027t dream of it,\u0026quot; Dumbledore winked.","\u0026quot;Now!\u0026quot; McGonagall clapped her hands, the sound like a thunderclap to the hungover group. \u0026quot;Enough lounging! We have dinner to eat! And I believe there is a dessert course involving chocolate. Up! Up! Movement aids recovery!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s a monster,\u0026quot; Sirius whimpered, letting Remus pull him up. \u0026quot;A tartan monster.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s the best,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, watching his professors lead the way back to the villa, walking in a perfectly straight line while the rest of the world spun around them."]},{"num":120,"origNum":120,"title":"The Delayed Fuse","wordCount":889,"paragraphs":["The sun was dipping lower, casting long, golden shadows across the sand. Albus Dumbledore and Minerva McGonagall walked toward the villa with the posture of kings returning from a crusade.","Their backs were straight. Their steps were synchronized. They did not sway.","\u0026quot;Look at them,\u0026quot; Harry whispered from the sand, watching with reverence. \u0026quot;They are invincible. They drank pure ethanol and they are discussing dinner.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are superior beings,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, rubbing his temples. \u0026quot;I hate them.\u0026quot;","The two professors reached the edge of the paved courtyard, exactly ten feet from the villa entrance.","They stopped.","It was sudden, like a clockwork toy running out of spring.","Dumbledore paused mid-step. He looked at the villa. He tilted his head to the left.","McGonagall stopped. She looked at the villa. She tilted her head to the right.","\u0026quot;Albus?\u0026quot; McGonagall asked, her voice perfectly calm and polite. \u0026quot;I believe the ground has decided to become vertical.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I concur, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore replied pleasantly. \u0026quot;The gravity seems to be... misbehaving. Shall we nap?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We shall.\u0026quot;","And then, with the synchronized grace of two falling trees, they tipped forward.","They didn\u0027t stumble. They didn\u0027t crumple. They simply rotated ninety degrees at the ankle and fell, rigid as planks, face-first into the soft sand.","\u003cem\u003eFLUMP. FLUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","Total stillness.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Panic\u003c/strong\u003e","The beach erupted.","\u0026quot;PROFESSOR!\u0026quot; Harry screamed, scrambling to his feet and sprinting toward them.","\u0026quot;THEY’RE DEAD!\u0026quot; Ron howled, tripping over his own feet. \u0026quot;THE ALCOHOL KILLED THEM! IT WAS TOO MUCH!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;MEDIC!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, dropping his towel. \u0026quot;Man down! Two men down! Code Red!\u0026quot;","Snape forgot his dignity. He sprinted (well, stumbled quickly) toward the fallen Headmaster. Even Draco looked terrified.","They reached the bodies. Harry slid to his knees beside Dumbledore. Hermione grabbed McGonagall’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;Professor!\u0026quot; Harry shook Dumbledore. \u0026quot;Professor, breathe! Dobby! Get a Bezoar!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Check for a pulse!\u0026quot; Sirius yelled, looking pale. \u0026quot;Is it the heart?\u0026quot;","Harry leaned down, pressing his ear to Dumbledore’s back. He waited for the rattle of death.","Instead, he heard a hum.","\u0026quot;Sherbet...\u0026quot; Dumbledore mumbled into the sand. \u0026quot;I want... a pair of woolen socks... made of custard.\u0026quot;","Harry froze. \u0026quot;What?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Nitwit,\u0026quot; Dumbledore whispered happily. \u0026quot;Blubber. Oddment. Tweak. The nargles are tickling my beard.\u0026quot;","Across the sand, Hermione turned McGonagall over. The Deputy Headmistress’s eyes were open, but they were looking in two different directions. Her hat was askew.","\u0026quot;Minerva?\u0026quot; Hermione asked frantically. \u0026quot;Can you hear me?\u0026quot;","McGonagall smiled—a loopy, lopsided grin that looked terrifying on her face.","\u0026quot;Mr. Potter,\u0026quot; McGonagall giggled. \u0026quot;Why are you a badger? Five points to the badger. Turn Mr. Weasley into a pincushion. He squeaks when you poke him.\u0026quot;","She patted Hermione’s cheek. \u0026quot;You have excellent whiskers, Miss Granger. Have a biscuit.\u0026quot;","Then, her eyes rolled back, and she let out a snore that sounded like a bagpipe deflating.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Diagnosis\u003c/strong\u003e","The panic in the group evaporated, replaced by a stunned silence.","Vernon Dursley stood over them, hands on his hips. He looked at the snoring wizards.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re not dead,\u0026quot; Vernon announced, wiping sweat from his brow. \u0026quot;They\u0027re pickled.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pickled?\u0026quot; Draco asked.","\u0026quot;The Delayed Fuse,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded sagely. \u0026quot;Seen it happen to the best of them. The adrenaline keeps you upright. The pride keeps you walking. But once the brain realizes the stomach is full of rocket fuel... BLAM. System shutdown. Reboot required.\u0026quot;","Snape stood up, brushing sand off his knees. A look of supreme, vindictive satisfaction spread across his face.","\u0026quot;They did not win,\u0026quot; Snape whispered. \u0026quot;They merely postponed the defeat. They are mortal.\u0026quot;","He looked down at Dumbledore, who was now blowing bubbles in the sand.","\u0026quot;Look at him,\u0026quot; Snape sneered affectionately. \u0026quot;The greatest wizard of the age. Defeated by a cocktail called \u0027The Voldemort\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Transport\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;We can\u0027t leave them here,\u0026quot; Harry said, standing up. \u0026quot;The tide is coming in. We have to get them to bed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon took charge. \u0026quot;Heavy lifting! Hagrid! You take the Headmaster!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Got \u0027im,\u0026quot; Hagrid sniffed, picking up Dumbledore with one hand as if he were a ragdoll. Dumbledore dangled limply, muttering about lemon drops.","\u0026quot;Draco! Harry!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;You take McGonagall! Careful with the hat!\u0026quot;","Harry grabbed McGonagall’s shoulders. Draco grabbed her feet.","\u0026quot;She’s surprisingly heavy,\u0026quot; Draco grunted as they lifted her.","\u0026quot;It’s the authority,\u0026quot; Ron noted. \u0026quot;It adds weight.\u0026quot;","They formed a procession. Hagrid carried Dumbledore like a sack of potatoes. Harry and Draco hauled McGonagall like a battering ram. The rest of the group trailed behind, wobbling and swaying.","They reached the villa. They navigated the stairs (during which McGonagall told Draco he looked like a \u0026quot;handsome ferret\u0026quot;).","They dumped Dumbledore into his hammock. He immediately curled up and began to snore in iambic pentameter.","They laid McGonagall on her pristine bed. She grabbed her pillow, whispered \u0026quot;Mischief Managed,\u0026quot; and passed out cold.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","The group stumbled back out of the villa and onto the beach. They were exhausted. They were hungover. They were confused.","They stood in a circle on the sand, looking back at the silent house.","Harry rubbed the back of his neck. He looked at Ron. He looked at the empty shot glasses still lined up on the table.","He thought about Dumbledore striding confidently away from the table, only to collapse like a puppet with cut strings.","\u0026quot;What just happened?\u0026quot; Harry asked, bewildered. \u0026quot;They were fine, and then suddenly BLAM, face first into the sand.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":121,"origNum":121,"title":"The Glucose Knockout","wordCount":832,"paragraphs":["The fire crackled merrily, sending sparks up toward the Caribbean stars. The smell of caramelizing sugar mixed with the salty sea air.","Vernon Dursley was conducting a masterclass in structural engineering using graham crackers and chocolate.","\u0026quot;The key,\u0026quot; Vernon mumbled, his speech slurring slightly from the fifty shots, \u0026quot;is the squish factor. You have to compress the marshmallow enough to melt the chocolate, but not so much that it extrudes out the sides. It is a delicate equilibrium.\u0026quot;","He handed a finished S\u0027more to Lucius Malfoy.","Lucius accepted the sticky, messy sandwich with two hands. He looked at it. The marshmallow oozed. The chocolate dripped.","\u0026quot;It is... untidy,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;But it smells like happiness.\u0026quot;","He took a bite. His eyes widened. The sugar hit his bloodstream like a bolt of lightning.","\u0026quot;Sweet,\u0026quot; Lucius gasped. \u0026quot;So sweet. It makes my teeth vibrate.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Catalyst\u003c/strong\u003e","Around the fire, the consumption was aggressive.","Ron Weasley had abandoned the crackers and was just eating roasted marshmallows off the stick, five at a time.","\u0026quot;They’re pillows,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled happily, his face smeared with ash and sugar. \u0026quot;Edible pillows. I want to live inside one.\u0026quot;","Sirius Black was eating the chocolate straight from the wrapper. \u0026quot;It pairs well with the tequila,\u0026quot; Sirius noted dreamily. \u0026quot;It’s a balanced diet.\u0026quot;","Severus Snape sat rigid, holding his perfectly golden-brown marshmallow. He ate it in small, precise bites.","\u0026quot;Sucrose,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Glucose. Fructose. A triple threat.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Chemical Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","It started subtly.","A heavy silence descended over the circle. The chewing slowed. The laughter faded into soft sighs.","Hermione Granger blinked. Her eyelids felt heavy. They felt like they were made of lead.","She looked at the empty chocolate wrappers. She looked at the empty shot glasses on the table behind them.","Her brain, sluggish but still functioning, made the connection.","\u0026quot;Oh no,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered.","\u0026quot;What?\u0026quot; Harry asked, yawning so wide his jaw cracked.","\u0026quot;The synergy,\u0026quot; Hermione slurred, leaning heavily against him. \u0026quot;Alcohol is a depressant. Sugar causes an insulin spike... followed by a crash. We just... we just combined a sedative with a tranquilizer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;English, Granger,\u0026quot; Draco mumbled from where he was lying on his back, staring at the stars.","\u0026quot;We just knocked ourselves out,\u0026quot; Hermione clarified softly. \u0026quot;The sugar... it’s the catalyst. It’s the final blow.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Domino Effect\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron went first.","He was holding a marshmallow stick. His hand slowly lowered. The stick dropped into the sand.","\u0026quot;I’m a biscuit,\u0026quot; Ron announced to the fire. \u0026quot;I am crumbling.\u0026quot;","He tipped sideways. He landed on a pile of discarded towels. He was asleep before he stopped rolling.","\u003cem\u003eSnore.\u003c/em\u003e","Lucius Malfoy looked at Ron. He sneered—or tried to. It came out as a sleepy grimace.","\u0026quot;Weakness,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;A Malfoy never...\u0026quot;","His head drooped. His chin hit his chest.","\u0026quot;The sand,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured. \u0026quot;It looks... ergonomic.\u0026quot;","He slid out of his seated position. He curled up in the sand, clutching his cane like a teddy bear.","\u0026quot;Goodnight, Narcissa.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Goodnight, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa replied, already lying down, using her husband’s back as a pillow.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parents\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley fought it. He was a man of willpower.","\u0026quot;Must... maintain... perimeter,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, trying to stand up.","He got to one knee. He swayed.","\u0026quot;Power nap,\u0026quot; Vernon decided. \u0026quot;Strategic... shutdown.\u0026quot;","He collapsed onto his back, hands folded over his stomach.","Petunia simply sighed, smoothed her dress, and lay down next to him.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Marauders and Faculty\u003c/strong\u003e","Sirius Black was asleep with a half-eaten chocolate bar stuck to his chest. Remus was using Sirius as a mattress.","Tonks had changed her hair to match the sand and was camouflaged.","Severus Snape sat alone, the last sentinel.","He looked at the sleeping bodies. He looked at the fire.","\u0026quot;I could brew a Pepper-Up Potion,\u0026quot; Snape thought aloud. \u0026quot;I could... revitalize them.\u0026quot;","He tried to reach for his wand. His arm felt like it weighed a thousand pounds.","\u0026quot;Or,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, his eyes sliding shut behind his sunglasses. \u0026quot;I could... surrender.\u0026quot;","He didn\u0027t lie down. He simply slumped sideways against the log he was sitting on. His head lolled back.","A soft, rattling snore escaped the Potions Master.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Two\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry and Draco were the last ones conscious.","They sat side-by-side, leaning against each other for support.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco mumbled. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t move my legs. I think they belong to the island now.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Me neither,\u0026quot; Harry yawned. \u0026quot;The sugar... it’s heavy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We should go to the villa,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;There are beds. With sheets.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Too far,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;Miles away.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Draco agreed. \u0026quot;Miles.\u0026quot;","They looked at the fire, dying down to embers. They looked at their family—Muggles, wizards, former enemies—sleeping in a heap under the Caribbean sky.","\u0026quot;It’s a good party,\u0026quot; Harry said, his eyes closing.","\u0026quot;Adequate,\u0026quot; Draco whispered.","They slid down together, shoulders touching, and joined the collective slumber.","The waves washed against the shore. The palm trees swayed.","And on the beach of Isla de la Fortuna, the entire wedding party slept the deep, sugar-coated sleep of the victorious, defeated by a marshmallow."]},{"num":122,"origNum":122,"title":"The Walking Dead","wordCount":977,"paragraphs":["The sun over Isla de la Fortuna did not rise gently; it assaulted the villa.","Inside the bedrooms, fifty pairs of eyes cracked open, instantly regretted it, and slammed shut again.","Harry Potter woke up in his bed. He didn\u0027t remember getting there. He vaguely recalled a sensation of floating, likely Dobby levitating him up the stairs like a piece of luggage.","He tried to sit up. His head felt like it had been used as a Bludger during a particularly violent match. His tongue felt like it was made of wool.","\u0026quot;Water,\u0026quot; Harry croaked. \u0026quot;Aguamenti... my face.\u0026quot;","Next door, a groan echoed through the wall that sounded like a dying walrus.","\u0026quot;My brain,\u0026quot; Ron’s voice muffled through the plaster. \u0026quot;It’s too big for my skull. I can hear my hair growing.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Exodus of the Damned\u003c/strong\u003e","Slowly, painfully, the wedding party began to emerge.","They did not walk; they shambled.","Draco Malfoy exited the East Wing wearing sunglasses that covered half his face. He was using the wall for support.","\u0026quot;The sun,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, shielding his face. \u0026quot;Turn it off. Father, buy the sun and turn it off.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy was behind him, clutching his cane with a trembling hand. He looked grey.","\u0026quot;I cannot buy the sun, Draco,\u0026quot; Lucius rasped. \u0026quot;I cannot even buy a coherent thought. I believe the \u0027Red Bull\u0027 has betrayed me.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley emerged from the Executive Suite. He looked like a deflated balloon.","\u0026quot;Hydration,\u0026quot; Vernon mumbled, his eyes bloodshot. \u0026quot;Critical failure of fluid levels. The sugar... it was a tactical error.\u0026quot;","They converged in the hallway—a shuffling army of the hungover. No one spoke. They simply nodded grimly at one another and began the long, agonizing descent to the beach, drawn by the primal need for fresh air and perhaps to drown themselves in the ocean.","Snape brought up the rear. He walked with stiff, jerky movements.","\u0026quot;I am going to brew a poison,\u0026quot; Snape whispered to no one. \u0026quot;And I am going to drink it. It will be an improvement.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Beach Scene\u003c/strong\u003e","They stumbled out of the villa and onto the sand. The brightness was blinding.","They squinted against the glare.","And then, they stopped.","Sitting under a large white parasol near the water’s edge were Albus Dumbledore and Minerva McGonagall.","They looked pristine.","McGonagall was wearing a crisp linen dress and a sunhat. She was reading \u003cem\u003eTransfiguration Today\u003c/em\u003e.","Dumbledore was wearing a fresh Hawaiian shirt (this one featured dancing pineapples). He was buttering a scone.","There was a silver tea service on the table between them. They looked radiant, rested, and annoyingly healthy.","Dumbledore looked up. He spotted the horde of zombies.","\u0026quot;Good morning!\u0026quot; Dumbledore boomed cheerfully.","The zombies flinched physically. Ron covered his ears. Draco whimpered.","\u0026quot;A lovely day for it!\u0026quot; Dumbledore continued, pouring tea. \u0026quot;The sea air is quite invigorating! Who wants a scone? They are fresh!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Confrontation\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry staggered forward. He looked at Dumbledore. He looked at the empty bottles from last night still piled near the fire pit.","He remembered Dumbledore drinking the Voldemort. He remembered him face-planting into the sand.","\u0026quot;How?\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;How are you... loud?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We carried you,\u0026quot; Draco rasped, pointing a shaking finger. \u0026quot;We carried you to bed. You were unconscious. You were murmuring about socks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I often murmur about socks,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled pleasantly. \u0026quot;It is a sign of deep relaxation.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But the hangover!\u0026quot; Ron shouted (then immediately regretted the volume, clutching his head). \u0026quot;Ow. You drank the dragon blood! You should be dead! Or at least... suffering!\u0026quot;","Minerva McGonagall lowered her magazine. She peered at them over her spectacles. She looked at Snape, who was leaning against a palm tree with his eyes closed.","\u0026quot;Mr. Weasley,\u0026quot; McGonagall said briskly. \u0026quot;Professor Dumbledore and I have a schedule to keep. Weddings to officiate. Speeches to give.\u0026quot;","She took a sip of tea.","\u0026quot;A hangover,\u0026quot; McGonagall stated simply, \u0026quot;is not optimal.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The zombies stared at them.","\u0026quot;Not... optimal?\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley repeated, blinking slowly. \u0026quot;You just... decided not to have one? Is that an executive decision?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mind over matter, Vernon,\u0026quot; Dumbledore tapped his temple. \u0026quot;I simply explained to my head that aching would be inconvenient. It agreed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s not how biology works!\u0026quot; Hermione wailed, looking like she wanted to cry. \u0026quot;That’s medically impossible!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is magic, Miss Granger,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled. \u0026quot;And perhaps a small Pepper-Up Potion taken at 4:00 AM. Preventive maintenance.\u0026quot;","Snape opened one eye. He stared at Dumbledore with pure, unadulterated loathing.","\u0026quot;You brewed a cure,\u0026quot; Snape hissed. \u0026quot;And you did not share.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You were asleep, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said innocently. \u0026quot;You looked so peaceful. Like a bat in hibernation. I didn\u0027t want to disturb you.\u0026quot;","Snape let out a sound that was half-growl, half-sob.","\u0026quot;I hate you,\u0026quot; Snape whispered. \u0026quot;I hate you with the fire of a thousand suns.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Have a scone, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore offered. \u0026quot;It absorbs the acid.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Defeat\u003c/strong\u003e","The group collapsed onto the sand around the professors. They lay there, broken and jealous, watching Dumbledore eat his scone with vigor.","\u0026quot;They’re gods,\u0026quot; Dudley moaned, lying face down. \u0026quot;They’re actual gods.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I want to be them when I grow up,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, putting his sunglasses back on.","\u0026quot;I just want the tea,\u0026quot; Harry groaned, reaching out a hand. \u0026quot;Please, Professor. Mercy.\u0026quot;","McGonagall smiled—a small, benevolent smile.","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; she called out softly.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Yes, Mistress Minnie?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bring the relief supplies,\u0026quot; McGonagall ordered. \u0026quot;The hydration draughts. And perhaps some aspirin for the Muggles. They look pitiable.\u0026quot;","As the elves swarmed them with water and potions, Harry looked up at Dumbledore, who was humming to a seagull.","\u0026quot;You win,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;You win the Gauntlet. You win the morning. You win everything.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I usually do, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;Now, drink up. We have a wedding rehearsal at noon. And I expect enthusiasm!\u0026quot;","A collective groan rose from the beach, carried away by the tropical wind."]},{"num":123,"origNum":123,"title":"The Grease Shield and the Great Flush","wordCount":1066,"paragraphs":["Just as Dobby approached Harry with a tray of crystal vials filled with bubbling blue Pepper-Up Potion, a large, sunburnt hand clamped down on the elf’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;Hold it!\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley barked. His voice was hoarse, but his authority was intact.","\u0026quot;Vernon?\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, clutching her head. \u0026quot;Please. The blue juice. I need it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No!\u0026quot; Vernon declared, swaying slightly but holding his ground. \u0026quot;You do not put high-octane fuel into a dry tank, Petunia! You’ll strip the lining! You need ballast! You need absorption!\u0026quot;","He turned to the table where the professors sat.","\u0026quot;Headmaster! Conjure a table! We need carbs! We need grease! We need the \u0027Dursley Sunday Special\u0027!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore, looking amused, waved the Elder Wand (which he was holding for Harry).","\u003cem\u003ePOP.\u003c/em\u003e","A long wooden table appeared in the sand. But instead of delicate china and linen, it was laden with the holy grail of hangover cures.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grease Shield\u003c/strong\u003e","There were mountains of buttered toast, cut thick as doorstops.","There were platters of bacon—not the crispy American kind this time, but thick, salty British back bacon, dripping with curative grease.","There were fried eggs with runny yolks.","There were hash browns.","There were sausages.","And, at Vernon’s specific request, there were massive, foil-wrapped Bacon Buttys with brown sauce.","\u0026quot;Eat!\u0026quot; Vernon commanded, grabbing a sandwich. \u0026quot;Create a sponge! Soak up the poison!\u0026quot;","The zombies shambled to the seats.","Lucius Malfoy looked at a Bacon Butty. He picked it up. Grease coated his fingers.","\u0026quot;It is... leaking,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;It is entirely unrefined.\u0026quot;","He took a bite. He chewed. A look of religious ecstasy crossed his face.","\u0026quot;It is the nectar of the gods,\u0026quot; Lucius moaned. \u0026quot;The salt... it speaks to my soul.\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley was eating toast as if he hadn\u0027t seen food in years. \u0026quot;Butter,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled. \u0026quot;I love butter. I want to live in a churn.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy, usually the picture of dining etiquette, was eating a fried egg with a spoon, staring blankly at the horizon. \u0026quot;The yolk,\u0026quot; he murmured. \u0026quot;It soothes the pain.\u0026quot;","They ate with a primal, desperate hunger. The fat and the carbohydrates hit their stomachs, forming the protective layer Vernon had promised. The shaking slowed. The world stopped spinning quite so fast.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Science of Hydration\u003c/strong\u003e","Twenty minutes later, the table was a wasteland of crumbs and empty plates. The group sat back, groaning, clutching their stomachs.","\u0026quot;I’m full,\u0026quot; Harry gasped. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t move. I am a statue of toast.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Hermione Granger announced. She stood up. She looked a little better—the color had returned to her cheeks, though her hair was still a bird\u0027s nest.","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Hermione declared, pointing to the ocean of water bottles and potions Dobby was guarding. \u0026quot;We hydrate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t,\u0026quot; Ron whined. \u0026quot;No room. I am at capacity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You will make room, Ronald,\u0026quot; Hermione said sternly. \u0026quot;It is a biological necessity. Professor Snape?\u0026quot;","She turned to the Potions Master, who was currently nursing a cup of black coffee and looking significantly more human after a bacon sandwich.","\u0026quot;Would you please explain to these... amateurs... why they need to drink water right now? Before the headache returns?\u0026quot;","Snape lowered his coffee. He looked at the group of suffering wizards. He curled his lip.","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, slipping into lecture mode. \u0026quot;Since you clearly lack the basic understanding of your own physiology.\u0026quot;","He stood up, casting a long shadow over the table.","\u0026quot;Alcohol,\u0026quot; Snape began, pacing the sand, \u0026quot;is a diuretic. It inhibits the production of vasopressin. In layman\u0027s terms... you have urinated away your cerebral fluid.\u0026quot;","Ron crossed his legs instinctively.","\u0026quot;Your brain,\u0026quot; Snape continued, enjoying their horror, \u0026quot;is currently shrinking. It is pulling away from your skull because it is dehydrated. That is the pounding you feel. Your grey matter is drying out like a potions ingredient left in the sun.\u0026quot;","He leaned over Harry.","\u0026quot;The grease Mr. Dursley provided has stabilized your stomach acids. But unless you reintroduce fluids immediately... the ethanol metabolites—specifically acetaldehyde, which is thirty times more toxic than alcohol itself—will remain in your system.\u0026quot;","Snape straightened up.","\u0026quot;In short, Potter: You are currently poisoned. Drink the water, or your brain will continue to shrivel until it resembles a walnut. Which, in Weasley’s case, might be an improvement.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Great Flood\u003c/strong\u003e","The terror in the group was palpable.","\u0026quot;My brain is shrinking?\u0026quot; Dudley yelped, grabbing a pitcher of water. \u0026quot;Drink! Everyone drink!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t want a walnut brain!\u0026quot; Sirius shouted, downing a glass of pumpkin juice.","Despite being stuffed to the gills with bacon and toast, they drank.","They drank gallons of iced water. They drank the Pepper-Up Potions. They drank coconut water.","It was uncomfortable. It was sloshy.","\u0026quot;I’m going to pop,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, drinking his third glass of water. \u0026quot;I am a water balloon in a linen suit.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Keep going!\u0026quot; Vernon encouraged, chugging a sports drink. \u0026quot;Flush the system! Dilute the toxins!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Resurrection\u003c/strong\u003e","Slowly, miraculously, it happened.","The color returned to faces. The eyes became less bloodshot. The pounding in heads faded from a deafening roar to a dull throb, and then to nothing.","Harry sat up straighter. He took a deep breath. The air didn\u0027t hurt anymore.","\u0026quot;I think...\u0026quot; Harry tested his neck muscles. \u0026quot;I think I’m alive.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can see clearly now,\u0026quot; Draco announced, taking off his sunglasses. \u0026quot;The sun is no longer my enemy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My brain feels... moist,\u0026quot; Ron noted happily. \u0026quot;Thanks, Snape.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t thank me,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, sitting back down. \u0026quot;Just don\u0027t do it again.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We won\u0027t,\u0026quot; Ginny promised. \u0026quot;Until the wedding.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore clapped his hands. \u0026quot;Marvelous! You have survived the Gauntlet, the Sugar Crash, and the Resurrection! You are now fully trained for matrimony!\u0026quot;","He looked at the group, now sitting up, fed, watered, and ready to face the day.","\u0026quot;And just in time,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled. \u0026quot;Because, by my calculation, the wedding is in exactly forty-eight hours.\u0026quot;","A fresh wave of panic hit the table—not from hangovers, but from the sudden realization of the deadline.","\u0026quot;Two days?\u0026quot; Molly Weasley shrieked, jumping up. \u0026quot;I haven\u0027t frosted the cakes! The flowers! The seating chart!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Villa!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, energized by grease and water. \u0026quot;Move out! We have a schedule to keep!\u0026quot;","As the group scrambled up the hill, energized and terrified, Harry looked back at the beach.","\u0026quot;We survived,\u0026quot; he whispered to Hermione.","\u0026quot;We did,\u0026quot; she smiled. \u0026quot;Now comes the hard part.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Getting Ron into a dress robe without him fainting.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":124,"origNum":124,"title":"The Muggle Method","wordCount":1262,"paragraphs":["The sun was climbing high over Isla de la Fortuna, burning off the last remnants of the morning haze. The group stood on the edge of the pristine white sand, looking at the empty stretch of beach where three weddings were supposed to happen in forty-eight hours.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley announced, clapping his hands. The sound was sharp and authoritative. \u0026quot;The hangover is cured. The brains are rehydrated. Now, we build.\u0026quot;","He pointed to a massive pile of bamboo poles, white silk sheets, folding chairs, and boxes of flowers that the house-elves had deposited near the tree line.","\u0026quot;We have an arch to construct. We have an aisle to lay. We have two hundred chairs to deploy.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy pulled out his wand. \u0026quot; \u003cem\u003eLocomotor Chairs\u003c/em\u003e ,\u0026quot; he began.","\u0026quot;PUT IT AWAY!\u0026quot; Vernon roared.","Draco froze, wand raised. \u0026quot;I beg your pardon?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No magic!\u0026quot; Vernon declared, crossing his arms. \u0026quot;Not for this. Magic is... flighty. It’s impermanent. If we want this venue to mean something, we build it with our hands! Sweat equity! Structural integrity derived from nuts, bolts, and honest labor!\u0026quot;","A collective groan rose from the wizards. It was a sound of deep, existential despair.","\u0026quot;Manual labor?\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy whispered, looking at his hands. \u0026quot;Vernon, I have people for this. I have elves. I have... money.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You can\u0027t buy the satisfaction of a job well done, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon countered. \u0026quot;Now, strip off the jackets! Roll up the sleeves! We are going analog!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Assignments\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon assigned roles with the speed of a foreman on a deadline.","\u003cstrong\u003eHeavy Lifting Team:\u003c/strong\u003e Hagrid, Sirius, Remus, and Bill.","\u003cstrong\u003ePrecision Engineering (Chairs):\u003c/strong\u003e Harry, Draco, Ron, and Neville.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Decor Committee:\u003c/strong\u003e Narcissa, Molly, Petunia, Hermione, Ginny, Luna, and Fleur.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Tool Specialists:\u003c/strong\u003e Arthur Weasley (naturally) and Vernon.","\u003cstrong\u003eQuality Control:\u003c/strong\u003e Snape, McGonagall, and Dumbledore.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Joy of the Screw\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley was in nirvana. He was holding a cordless power drill Vernon had brought from home.","\u0026quot;It rotates,\u0026quot; Arthur breathed, pulling the trigger. \u003cem\u003eWhirrrr.\u003c/em\u003e \u0026quot;It spins without a spell! It is torque! Pure, mechanical torque!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Steady, Arthur,\u0026quot; Vernon instructed, handing him a screw. \u0026quot;Drive it home. Secure the trellis.\u0026quot;","Arthur approached a bamboo pole. He applied the drill. \u003cem\u003eZZZZZT.\u003c/em\u003e The screw went in crooked.","\u0026quot;Fascinating!\u0026quot; Arthur cheered. \u0026quot;It resists!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Chair Crisis\u003c/strong\u003e","Down on the sand, the grooms were discovering the unique hell of white folding chairs.","\u0026quot;Why do they fold?\u0026quot; Draco spat, wrestling with a chair that seemed determined to sever his finger. \u0026quot;It is a trap. It is a biting chair.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You have to snap it,\u0026quot; Harry explained, sweating through his t-shirt. \u0026quot;Push down on the seat.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eSNAP.\u003c/em\u003e","Draco’s chair locked into place. He looked at it with deep suspicion.","\u0026quot;It feels... flimsy,\u0026quot; Draco noted. \u0026quot;Is this safe for my mother? She is wearing vintage robes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’ll hold,\u0026quot; Ron grunted, carrying a stack of four chairs. \u0026quot;I’m moving bulk, boys. Efficiency.\u0026quot;","Ron took a step. His foot sank into soft sand. He tipped forward. The chairs went flying.","\u003cem\u003eCLATTER-BANG.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;My toe!\u0026quot; Ron howled, hopping on one foot. \u0026quot;The chair bit my toe!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Quality Control!\u0026quot; Snape shouted from the shade of a palm tree, where he was holding a tape measure. \u0026quot;Weasley, your alignment is atrocious. That row is crooked by three inches. Straighten it, or I shall dock points from a House you no longer attend.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Archway\u003c/strong\u003e","Hagrid was the heavy machinery. He was holding a twenty-foot bamboo beam over his head with one hand while Sirius and Remus tried to secure the uprights.","\u0026quot; a bit to the left, Hagrid!\u0026quot; Sirius shouted, hammering a peg into the sand with a rock (Vernon had taken the hammer).","\u0026quot;Left it is!\u0026quot; Hagrid turned. The beam swung like a boom gate, nearly decapitating Remus.","\u0026quot;Whoa!\u0026quot; Lupin ducked, his werewolf reflexes saving him. \u0026quot;Watch the swing, Hagrid!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sorry!\u0026quot; Hagrid boomed.","\u0026quot;This is barbaric,\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy muttered. He had been assigned the task of holding the nails. He stood there, looking like a dispossessed king, holding a small paper bag of galvanized steel.","\u0026quot;I am a Malfoy,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered to a nail. \u0026quot;I hold influence. I hold gold. I do not hold hardware.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pass me a nail, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted from the top of a ladder.","Lucius sighed and handed up a nail with two fingers, looking disgusted.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Floral Arrangement\u003c/strong\u003e","Under the shade of the veranda, the women were weaving garlands of orchids and lilies.","\u0026quot;No, Fleur,\u0026quot; Molly corrected gently. \u0026quot;Wire first, then tape. It has to hold against the sea breeze.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is sticky,\u0026quot; Fleur complained, looking at the floral tape. \u0026quot;My fingers are... glued.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It builds character,\u0026quot; Petunia said briskly, snapping a stem. \u0026quot;And it saves money on Sticking Charms. Look at Hermione.\u0026quot;","Hermione was weaving flowers with a speed and precision that was terrifying. She had created a production line.","\u0026quot;Stem, wire, tape, cut. Stem, wire, tape, cut,\u0026quot; Hermione muttered, her eyes glazed with focus.","\u0026quot;She’s a machine,\u0026quot; Ginny noted, lazily tying a ribbon. \u0026quot;She’s optimized the bouquet.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Supervisor\u003c/strong\u003e","Albus Dumbledore was not building. He was \u0026quot;supervising.\u0026quot;","This mostly involved walking around with his hands behind his back, humming, and occasionally pointing at things with a sherbet lemon.","\u0026quot;A little more to the right, Harry!\u0026quot; Dumbledore called out. \u0026quot;Feng Shui is important! The energy must flow!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m just trying to make straight lines, Professor!\u0026quot; Harry yelled back, wiping sweat from his eyes.","\u0026quot;And Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore added, turning to the Potions Master. \u0026quot;You missed a spot with the measuring tape. Precision is key.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at the tape measure. He looked at the sand. He looked at Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;I am measuring sand, Albus,\u0026quot; Snape said in a deadpan voice. \u0026quot;I am quantifying a beach. This is madness.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is teamwork!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Halftime Whistle\u003c/strong\u003e","By 1:00 PM, the beach looked transformed. Rows of white chairs gleamed in the sun. A bamboo arch stood tall (if slightly leaning to the left).","The wedding party was sweaty, covered in sawdust, and exhausted.","Vernon climbed down from his ladder. He surveyed the site.","\u0026quot;Not bad,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted. \u0026quot;Not bad at all. A bit rough around the edges, but it has heart.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","Dobby appeared on top of a stack of unused lumber.","\u0026quot;Lunch is served!\u0026quot; Dobby squeaked.","A collective sigh of relief went up that was loud enough to disturb the waves.","\u0026quot;Steak?\u0026quot; Ron asked hopefully. \u0026quot;Burgers? A cow on a spit?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Light lunch!\u0026quot; Dobby announced, snapping his fingers.","A table appeared. It was not laden with heavy meats.","It held platters of crisp green salads, bowls of quinoa, fruit skewers, and delicate finger sandwiches with the crusts cut off.","\u0026quot;Salad?\u0026quot; Ron stared at the lettuce. \u0026quot;Dobby... where is the meat? Where is the grease?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Miss Hermione said we needs the fiber!\u0026quot; Dobby explained. \u0026quot;To process the toxins! And to keep the energy steady! No naps!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fiber,\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy repeated, looking at a bowl of kale. \u0026quot;I am to rebuild my strength with... leaves?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Eat up!\u0026quot; Hermione chirped, grabbing a plate. \u0026quot;It’s high-energy fuel! Complex carbohydrates! We have the reception area to set up this afternoon!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The reception area?\u0026quot; Draco groaned, collapsing onto a chair he had just built. \u0026quot;I thought we were done.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The dance floor doesn\u0027t lay itself, Malfoy,\u0026quot; Harry grinned, handing him a cucumber sandwich. \u0026quot;Eat your greens. We’ve got work to do.\u0026quot;","As the wizards reluctantly picked at their salads, Vernon Dursley nodded approvingly.","\u0026quot;Light lunch,\u0026quot; Vernon agreed. \u0026quot;Prevents the afternoon slump. Keeps the productivity up. Hermione, you’re a natural manager.\u0026quot;","Hermione beamed. Ron looked at his sandwich.","\u0026quot;I miss the bacon,\u0026quot; Ron whispered to the cucumber. \u0026quot;I miss it so much.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":125,"origNum":125,"title":"The Sweat Equity","wordCount":861,"paragraphs":["The fiber-heavy lunch, much to Ron’s dismay, actually worked.","By 2:00 PM, the wedding party wasn\u0027t sluggish; they were energized. The salad had provided a slow-release fuel that powered them through the heat of the afternoon.","Vernon Dursley, revitalized by a quinoa wrap, was barking orders with renewed vigor.","\u0026quot;The dance floor!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted, pointing to a stack of interlocking wooden parquet tiles. \u0026quot;It’s a jigsaw puzzle, people! Snap and lock! No gaps! I don\u0027t want anyone tripping during the waltz!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Floor\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry and Draco found themselves on their knees, snapping the wooden squares together.","\u0026quot;Click,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, pressing a tile down. \u0026quot;Click. It is... strangely satisfying.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s like Lego,\u0026quot; Harry said, wiping sweat from his forehead with the back of his hand. \u0026quot;But for feet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have a blister,\u0026quot; Draco noted, examining his palm. He didn\u0027t whine. He looked at it with a strange sort of fascination. \u0026quot;I have physically damaged my own skin to build a floor. Is this... rugged?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s very rugged, Malfoy,\u0026quot; Ginny called out, carrying a stack of tiles. \u0026quot;You look like a laborer. It’s hot.\u0026quot;","Draco preened. He attacked the next tile with renewed ferocity.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lighting\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley and Sirius Black were in charge of the string lights.","They were wrestling with a ladder and a long, tangled string of Edison bulbs.","\u0026quot;No magic,\u0026quot; Sirius grunted, stretching to hook the wire over a palm frond. \u0026quot;Just height and hope.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The filament!\u0026quot; Arthur gasped, holding a bulb. \u0026quot;It glows because of resistance! It fights the electricity and creates light! It is a metaphor for life!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a lightbulb, Arthur,\u0026quot; Remus said from the bottom of the ladder, holding it steady. \u0026quot;Just screw it in.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Touches\u003c/strong\u003e","By 4:30 PM, the heavy lifting was done. The focus shifted to the details.","Narcissa Malfoy and Petunia Dursley were tying ribbons to the backs of the chairs.","\u0026quot;A double knot,\u0026quot; Petunia instructed. \u0026quot;Keeps it symmetrical. And the tails must be even.\u0026quot;","Narcissa, who usually employed house-elves for such tasks, was concentrating hard. She tied the silk ribbon. She fluffed the bow.","\u0026quot;I did it,\u0026quot; Narcissa whispered. She looked at the chair. \u0026quot;I adorned furniture. With my own hands.\u0026quot;","She looked at Petunia. \u0026quot;It feels... personal.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled. \u0026quot;It means you care.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Inspection\u003c/strong\u003e","At 5:00 PM sharp, Vernon blew his whistle.","\u0026quot;TOOLS DOWN!\u0026quot;","The hammering stopped. The shuffling stopped.","The wedding party stepped back. They gathered near the edge of the dunes, wiping dirt and sweat from their faces.","They looked at what they had created.","It was magnificent.","Rows of white chairs sat in perfect, military alignment on the sand. The bamboo archway stood tall and sturdy, draped in white silk and tropical flowers that Hermione and Luna had arranged by hand.","The dance floor gleamed in the late afternoon sun, a smooth expanse of wood waiting for music.","Strings of lights crisscrossed overhead, waiting for the night.","It wasn\u0027t held up by Levitation Charms. It wasn\u0027t stuck together with Sticking Spells. It stood because they had hammered the nails, dug the holes, and snapped the locks.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron Weasley leaned on a shovel. He looked at the venue.","\u0026quot;We built that,\u0026quot; Ron said, his voice filled with awe. \u0026quot;Us. We actually built a building. Well, a floor and an arch.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It feels... solid,\u0026quot; Harry noted, testing the stability of a bamboo pole. \u0026quot;Real.\u0026quot;","Severus Snape walked down the aisle. He inspected the chairs. He checked the spacing. He looked at the dance floor seams.","He turned to the group.","\u0026quot;The geometric alignment is... flawless,\u0026quot; Snape admitted. \u0026quot;There is no magical residue to decay. No charms to wear off. It is physics and friction.\u0026quot;","He looked at Vernon.","\u0026quot;It is... competent.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;High praise,\u0026quot; Vernon beamed, puffing out his chest. \u0026quot;Sweat equity, Severus! You can\u0027t buy that feeling!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy was looking at his hands. They were dirty. There was a smudge of grease on his linen trousers. He had broken a nail.","He looked at the venue.","\u0026quot;I could have paid a thousand galleons to have this done in a second,\u0026quot; Lucius mused.","He walked over to the archway he had helped hold upright. He touched the wood.","\u0026quot;But,\u0026quot; Lucius said softly, \u0026quot;I suppose... knowing that I helped secure this beam... it adds a certain... value. A sentimental amortization.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It means you built the place your son is getting married, Lucius,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley said gently, putting a hand on his shoulder.","Lucius looked at Arthur. He didn\u0027t flinch. He nodded.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;I suppose I did.\u0026quot;","Hermione looked at her hands, which were covered in floral tape residue. She looked at Harry, whose t-shirt was soaked through. She looked at Ron, who had sawdust in his hair.","\u0026quot;It’s perfect,\u0026quot; Hermione declared. \u0026quot;Because it’s imperfect. It’s human.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s ready,\u0026quot; Vernon announced, checking his watch. \u0026quot;T-minus 24 hours to the main event. Now... who needs a shower?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Me!\u0026quot; fifty voices shouted in unison.","As they walked back up the path to the villa, leaving the silent, hand-built venue waiting by the sea, there was a swagger in their step. They weren\u0027t just wizards anymore. They were builders.","And they had earned their dinner."]},{"num":126,"origNum":126,"title":"The Grill Master","wordCount":780,"paragraphs":["The sun had set, but the heat of the day lingered in the stones of the Upper Terrace. The air was filled with the smell of charcoal smoke, hickory wood, and searing meat.","Vernon Dursley stood before a massive stainless-steel barbecue grill that looked like the control panel of a nuclear power plant. He was wearing an apron that said \u003cem\u003eKISS THE COOK\u003c/em\u003e (gifted by Harry) and wielding a pair of tongs like a wand.","\u0026quot;Fire!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed. \u0026quot;The primal element! The caveman’s television! We have built shelter, and now we cook the beast!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s hamburger,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered to Ron. \u0026quot;Not a beast.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a beast of a burger,\u0026quot; Ron corrected, eyeing the patties sizzling on the grate.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sous-Chefs\u003c/strong\u003e","Dobby and his team were strictly relegated to side-dish duty. Vernon did not trust elves with the turning of the meat.","\u0026quot;Timing is everything!\u0026quot; Vernon lectured Arthur Weasley, who was staring mesmerized at the charcoal. \u0026quot;You have to wait for the juices to rise! Flip it once! Only once! If you press it with the spatula, you lose the flavor! You ruin the integrity!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Do not press,\u0026quot; Arthur repeated solemnly. \u0026quot;Respect the juice.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Feast of Labor\u003c/strong\u003e","The food was served buffet style, but this time, it felt earned.","There were cheeseburgers thick as dictionaries. There were sausages that snapped when broken. There were corn cobs dripping in butter and chili lime salt. There were bowls of potato salad (Petunia’s recipe) and coleslaw.","The group ate with a ferocity that superseded manners.","Draco Malfoy, the boy who used to sneer at anything less than a five-course banquet, was eating a hot dog with his hands.","\u0026quot;Mustard,\u0026quot; Draco declared, wiping a smear from his lip. \u0026quot;Yellow mustard. It is sharp. It cuts the grease. It is... tactical.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a hot dog, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, biting into a burger.","\u0026quot;It is a tube of mystery meat,\u0026quot; Draco corrected. \u0026quot;But after building a floor... it tastes like victory.\u0026quot;","Severus Snape sat by the railing. He had a plate of grilled vegetables and a steak cooked rare.","\u0026quot;The char,\u0026quot; Snape murmured, inspecting a zucchini slice. \u0026quot;Carbonization. It adds a bitterness that balances the natural sugars. Dursley... your control of the thermal gradient is adequate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;High heat, sear the outside, lock it in!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted from the grill. \u0026quot;It’s physics, Severus!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Exhaustion\u003c/strong\u003e","By 9:00 PM, the adrenaline of the build had faded, replaced by a bone-deep weariness that no amount of Pepper-Up Potion could fix.","This wasn\u0027t the spinning sickness of a hangover. It was the heavy, aching, satisfying tiredness of physical work.","Lucius Malfoy sat in a wicker chair, his eyes half-closed. He looked at his hands. There was a small scratch on his thumb.","\u0026quot;I am wounded,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;I have bled for this wedding.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a hangnail, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa smiled sleepily, finishing her wine. \u0026quot;You will survive.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I shall require a healing balm,\u0026quot; Lucius insisted. \u0026quot;And perhaps a pillow for my lower back. The hammering... it takes a toll.\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley was practically asleep at the table. \u0026quot;Bed,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled. \u0026quot;Soft bed. No sand. Just pillows.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dismissal\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon scraped the grill down with a wire brush. He took off his apron.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, his voice a little lower than usual. \u0026quot;The venue is set. The bellies are full. Tomorrow... is the Rehearsal.\u0026quot;","He looked at the three couples.","\u0026quot;We walk the aisle. We practice the vows. We time the music. It must be clockwork. No tripping. No giggling. And absolutely no turning into Ostriches.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Promised,\u0026quot; Harry yawned.","\u0026quot;08:00 hours breakfast,\u0026quot; Vernon ordered. \u0026quot;09:00 hours on the sand. Sharp. Dismissed!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Retreat\u003c/strong\u003e","The group stood up, groaning as stiff muscles protested.","\u0026quot;Ouch,\u0026quot; Draco winced, rubbing his shoulder. \u0026quot;I think I pulled a deltoid.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s from the hammering,\u0026quot; Ginny said, leaning on him. \u0026quot;Come on, tough guy. Let’s get you horizontal.\u0026quot;","They filed back into the villa. There were no parties tonight. No secret meetings on the beach.","They went to their rooms.","Harry fell into bed without even taking off his socks. He stared at the ceiling for three seconds before his eyes closed.","In the room next door, Ron was already snoring.","In the Master Suite, Draco fell asleep clutching a pillow, dreaming of floorboards snapping together perfectly.","And in the Executive Suite, Vernon Dursley adjusted the AC, climbed into bed, and sighed the sigh of a man who had conquered the elements, the appetite, and the logistical challenges of a magical wedding.","\u0026quot;Good work today, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, turning out the light.","\u0026quot;Solid work,\u0026quot; Vernon agreed in the dark. \u0026quot;Structural integrity. 100%.\u0026quot;","The villa went dark. The island slept.","Tomorrow, they would rehearse the rest of their lives."]},{"num":127,"origNum":127,"title":"The Walk of the Potions Master","wordCount":1194,"paragraphs":["The sun rose over Isla de la Fortuna, but this time, there were no whistles. There was no shouting. There was only the gentle chime of silver against china and the smell of freshness.","The wedding party gathered on the terrace at 08:00 hours sharp. They had slept deeply, the physical labor of the previous day having cured the last of the hangover.","Vernon Dursley stood by the buffet, but he wasn\u0027t serving grease. He was serving \u0026quot;Performance Fuel.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Breakfast of Vitality\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Light!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, gesturing to the spread. \u0026quot;Clean! Efficient! Today is a day of precision. We cannot be weighed down by starch!\u0026quot;","The table was a rainbow of health.","There were platters of exotic fruits—dragon fruit, starfruit, and mango slices that glistened with dew.","There were bowls of Acai, topped with granola and chia seeds.","\u0026quot;Superfoods!\u0026quot; Vernon lectured Arthur Weasley. \u0026quot;Antioxidants! It scrubs the cells, Arthur! It polishes the arteries!\u0026quot;","There were poached eggs on thin slices of sourdough, draped in smoked salmon.","There were avocados, mashed and seasoned with chili flakes.","\u0026quot;Green butter,\u0026quot; Ron marveled, eating a spoonful of avocado. \u0026quot;It tastes like grass, but... creamy grass? I feel faster already.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is Omega-3,\u0026quot; Hermione explained, drinking a green juice that smelled of kale and apple. \u0026quot;Brain food, Ron. We need to focus.\u0026quot;","They ate. And miraculously, despite consuming platters of food, they didn\u0027t feel heavy. They felt buoyant. The energy was buzzing under their skin.","\u0026quot;I feel like I could fly without a broom,\u0026quot; Harry said, flexing his hands. \u0026quot;I feel... optimized.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded, sipping a ginseng tea, \u0026quot;is the power of nutrition. Now... to the beach! 1200 hours! Rehearsal formations!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Formation\u003c/strong\u003e","At noon, the sun was high, turning the ocean into a sheet of diamonds.","The venue was perfect. The white chairs gleamed. The bamboo arch stood tall against the blue sky.","Vernon stood at the front, stopwatch in hand.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon commanded. \u0026quot;Places! Grooms at the altar! Brides at the start of the aisle! Parents in the front row! Professors... try not to look so menacing!\u0026quot;","Harry, Ron, and Draco took their places under the arch. They looked at each other. They grinned.","\u0026quot;This is it,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;The dry run.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t trip,\u0026quot; Harry warned.","\u0026quot;I never trip,\u0026quot; Draco sniffed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Procession Problem\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Cue the music!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted.","Dumbledore, standing behind the grooms as the Officiant, waved his wand. A string quartet (conjured instruments playing themselves) began a soft, melodic version of a Celestina Warbeck song.","\u0026quot;Brides!\u0026quot; Vernon yelled. \u0026quot;Deploy!\u0026quot;","Luna Lovegood stepped up. Xenophilius Lovegood, wearing a tuxedo made of yellow silk, took her arm. He was crying already.","\u0026quot;My little moon beam,\u0026quot; Xeno sobbed. \u0026quot;Walking toward the Nargle-free future!\u0026quot;","They walked down the aisle. Perfect.","Ginny Weasley stepped up. Arthur Weasley offered his arm. He looked proud enough to burst.","\u0026quot;Ready, Ginny-bug?\u0026quot; Arthur asked.","\u0026quot;Ready, Dad.\u0026quot;","They walked. Perfect.","Then, it was Hermione’s turn.","She stood at the start of the aisle, holding a bouquet of practice-flowers. She looked beautiful in her sundress.","But she stood alone.","She looked to her left. She looked to her right.","Her parents were safe in Australia, living happy lives without memories of the war, just as she had enchanted them. It was a sacrifice she had made to save them.","But now, standing on the white sand, the gap beside her felt enormous.","Vernon lowered his stopwatch. The music faltered.","Harry took a step forward from the altar, ready to run to her, protocol be damned.","\u0026quot;I... I can walk myself,\u0026quot; Hermione said, her voice shaking slightly. \u0026quot;I’m an independent woman. It’s fine.\u0026quot;","She gripped her bouquet, her knuckles white. She lifted her chin. She prepared to walk the loneliest twenty yards of her life.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Shadow\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Miss Granger.\u0026quot;","The voice came from the shade of the palm trees. It was deep, silky, and familiar.","Severus Snape stepped out of the shadows.","He was wearing his black dress robes, buttoned to the neck despite the heat. He looked stark against the white sand—a ink blot on a pristine page.","He walked over to Hermione. He stopped beside her.","The wedding party held its breath. Ron’s mouth fell open.","Snape looked down at Hermione. He didn\u0027t sneer. He didn\u0027t scowl.","His black eyes caught the light, and for the first time, they held a glimmer of genuine, grudging respect.","\u0026quot;It is... illogical,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, \u0026quot;for the brightest witch of her age to walk alone.\u0026quot;","Hermione stared at him. \u0026quot;Professor?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have spent seven years grading your essays, Granger,\u0026quot; Snape said, looking at the altar where Harry stood. \u0026quot;I have watched you keep Potter alive when he had no right to survive. I have watched you endure torture in my own drawing room.\u0026quot;","He paused. He adjusted his cuff.","\u0026quot;You possess a formidable intellect. A Gryffindor courage that is... tolerable. And you tied with Potter in my N.E.W.T. class.\u0026quot;","He held out his arm. It was stiff, angular, and offered with the supreme dignity of a Prince.","\u0026quot;It would be,\u0026quot; Snape murmured, \u0026quot;an honor. To ensure you reach your destination.\u0026quot;","Hermione’s eyes filled with tears. She looked at the man who had terrified her for years, the man who had saved them all, the man who had run a four-minute mile on this very beach.","\u0026quot;Thank you, Severus,\u0026quot; she whispered.","She took his arm.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Walk\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Music!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, wiping his own eyes with a handkerchief. \u0026quot;Go!\u0026quot;","The strings swelled.","Snape and Hermione began to walk.","They moved in perfect synchronization. Snape did not glide like a bat; he marched like a soldier escorting a queen. His head was high. His expression dared anyone to laugh.","Hermione held his arm tightly, beaming through her tears.","They passed the parents. Molly Weasley was sobbing into Arthur’s shoulder. Narcissa Malfoy looked at Snape with a soft smile.","They reached the altar.","Harry watched them come. He looked at Snape.","Snape looked at Harry. He stopped. He gently disengaged his arm from Hermione’s.","He took Hermione’s hand and placed it in Harry’s.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice low.","\u0026quot;Sir,\u0026quot; Harry replied.","\u0026quot;Do not mess this up,\u0026quot; Snape warned. \u0026quot;Or I shall deduct points. Retroactively.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I won\u0027t,\u0026quot; Harry promised.","Snape nodded once. He turned, his robes billowing in the sea breeze, and took his place in the front row next to McGonagall.","McGonagall leaned over. \u0026quot;That was... kind, Severus.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I merely ensured the schedule was maintained, Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, staring straight ahead. \u0026quot;Efficiency. Dursley taught me that.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Vows\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Dumbledore announced, clapping his hands. \u0026quot;Everyone is here! Let us practice the words! Repeat after me...\u0026quot;","The rehearsal continued. They practiced the \u0026quot;I Do\u0027s\u0026quot;. They practiced the ring exchange (Draco dropped the ruby snake once, and Lucius nearly had a heart attack).","But as the sun began to set, casting the rehearsal in golden light, no one was looking at the view.","They were looking at the Potions Master, sitting in the front row, looking miserable and terrifying, who had just proven that even the darkest dungeons could let in a little light.","\u0026quot;Good rehearsal!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted, clicking his stopwatch. \u0026quot;Timing was perfect! 18 minutes! Efficient emotion! Now... rest! Tomorrow... we execute!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":128,"origNum":128,"title":"The Chippy on the Beach","wordCount":851,"paragraphs":["The emotional weight of the rehearsal—the tears, the vows, and the sight of Severus Snape acting like a human being—had left the group drained but exhilarated.","Vernon Dursley clicked his stopwatch.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, his voice cracking slightly with emotion (which he masked by coughing loudly). \u0026quot;Emotion... processed. Tears... dried. Now, the stomach calls! It is 1:00 PM. We need sustenance that grounds us. We need... nostalgia.\u0026quot;","He whistled. \u003cem\u003eTWEEET!\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Dobby! Execute Operation: Seaside Special!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Setup\u003c/strong\u003e","The house-elves did not bring out silver platters or crystal bowls.","Instead, they levitated a wooden shack onto the sand. It looked like a boardwalk stall from Brighton, complete with a striped awning and a chalkboard menu.","The smell hit them instantly. It wasn\u0027t spices or charcoal. It was the distinct, sharp, mouth-watering scent of malt vinegar, hot oil, and sea salt.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, his eyes widening. \u0026quot;Is that...?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Fish and Chips,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;Proper ones.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Menu\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon stood by the stall, handing out wooden forks.","\u0026quot;Fresh catch!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed. \u0026quot;Local Grouper and Snapper, but given the British treatment! Beer batter! Thick cut chips! Mushy peas! And for the adventurous... Pickled Eggs!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pickled... eggs?\u0026quot; Draco Malfoy repeated, staring at a jar of floating, pale spheres. \u0026quot;They look like preserved eyes, Potter. Are we brewing potions or eating lunch?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a delicacy, Draco,\u0026quot; Hermione laughed, grabbing a fork. \u0026quot;It’s pub food.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Presentation\u003c/strong\u003e","The food wasn\u0027t served on china. It was served in cones made of newsprint.","But this being a wizarding wedding, the newsprint was special.","\u0026quot;Look!\u0026quot; Ginny laughed, holding her cone. \u0026quot;It’s the \u003cem\u003eDaily Prophet\u003c/em\u003e! But it’s... us!\u0026quot;","The paper wrapping showed moving photos of the group: Harry and Draco flying at the Manor, the \u0026quot;Ostrich\u0026quot; incident at the Burrow, and Vernon Dursley yelling at a cloud.","\u0026quot;I am eating off my own face,\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy noted, peeling a chip off a picture of himself hugging Arthur Weasley. \u0026quot;It is... meta-physical.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s recycling!\u0026quot; Vernon corrected. \u0026quot;Sustainable dining!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Consumption\u003c/strong\u003e","The group sat on the folding chairs they had set up earlier, digging into the feast.","The batter was shatteringly crisp, golden and airy (thanks to a little help from Flitwick’s Levitation Charm during the frying process). The fish inside was flaky and sweet.","The chips were thick, hot, and drowning in salt and vinegar.","\u0026quot;The vinegar,\u0026quot; Snape murmured, inspecting a chip. \u0026quot;Acetic acid. It cuts the lipids of the batter. A classic chemical pairing.\u0026quot;","He took a bite. He didn\u0027t smile, but he closed his eyes for a long second.","\u0026quot;Adequate,\u0026quot; Snape declared. \u0026quot;It reminds me of... Spinners End. In a tolerable way.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pass the tartar sauce, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, dipping a chip. \u0026quot;I find the capers delightful.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Mushy Pea Debate\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley was fascinated by the mushy peas.","\u0026quot;It is a paste,\u0026quot; Arthur marveled. \u0026quot;Green masonry mortar. Vernon, is this used to hold bricks together?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It holds the \u003cem\u003esoul\u003c/em\u003e together, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, scooping a large spoonful. \u0026quot;It’s marrowfat peas! Soaked in bicarbonate! It’s comfort in a cup!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It looks like something Longbottom brewed in First Year,\u0026quot; Draco sneered, poking it.","\u0026quot;Try it, Ferret,\u0026quot; Ginny challenged, feeding him a spoonful.","Draco chewed. He swallowed. He looked confused.","\u0026quot;It is... sweet?\u0026quot; Draco asked. \u0026quot;And savory? It is... not terrible. I feel strangely comforted. I want to wear a wool sweater.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s the British DNA kicking in,\u0026quot; Harry laughed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Beverage\u003c/strong\u003e","To wash it down, there was only one option.","\u0026quot;Shandy!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, popping the tops off chilled bottles. \u0026quot;Lager and Lemonade! Low alcohol, high refreshment! We have a wedding tomorrow; we need to stay vertical!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Beer and soda?\u0026quot; Lucius asked, looking at the mixture with deep suspicion. \u0026quot;You dilute the beer?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We \u003cem\u003eenhance\u003c/em\u003e it,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected.","Lucius took a sip. \u0026quot;It is... fizzy. It is... pleasant. Why do I feel the urge to sit in a garden chair and complain about the weather?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;One of us! One of us!\u0026quot; Ron chanted, clinking his bottle against Lucius’s.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lull\u003c/strong\u003e","As the cones emptied and the shandy bottles clinked, a contented silence fell over the beach.","They were full of grease, salt, and vinegar—the holy trinity of British comfort.","Harry sat with Hermione and Ron, watching the waves roll in.","\u0026quot;Tomorrow,\u0026quot; Harry said softly. \u0026quot;It’s really happening.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Ron said, wiping crumbs from his chin. \u0026quot;You’re getting married, mate. To Hermione. Finally.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And you’re marrying Luna,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled, leaning her head on Harry’s shoulder but holding Ron’s hand.","\u0026quot;And the Ferret is marrying Ginny,\u0026quot; Ron shook his head. \u0026quot;And eating mushy peas. The world has gone mad.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a good mad,\u0026quot; Harry said.","Vernon stood up, brushing crumbs off his vest.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced. \u0026quot;Lunch concluded! Grease intake optimal! Now... rest! Relax! Do not move a muscle! Tomorrow is the Big Show. I want everyone rested, polished, and ready to execute the Merger of the Century!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, sir!\u0026quot; the group chorused.","As they sat in the sun, listening to the ocean and the rustle of newsprint, they weren\u0027t the Saviors of the World, or the Boy Who Lived, or the Brightest Witch.","They were just a family, having chips on the beach."]},{"num":129,"origNum":129,"title":"The Raw and the Grilled","wordCount":859,"paragraphs":["The velvet rope dropped. The wedding party surged forward, finding their places at the tables centered around the glowing charcoal grills.","Harry, Ron, Hermione, Draco, Ginny, and Luna claimed a round table near the edge of the terrace.","On the table lay the tools of the trade: heavy porcelain bowls, metal chopsticks (which Ron eyed with deep suspicion), and a pair of steel tongs for the grill.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sushi First Strike\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter, emboldened by years of Vernon’s culinary boot camps, didn\u0027t hesitate. He reached for a slice of \u003cem\u003eO-Toro\u003c/em\u003e.","He didn\u0027t use soy sauce. He didn\u0027t use wasabi. He ate it pure.","He closed his eyes.","\u0026quot;It dissolves,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;It’s not fish. It’s... meat butter. It’s savory velvet.\u0026quot;","Ron looked at the raw slab on his own plate. He poked it with a chopstick.","\u0026quot;It’s definitely raw, Harry,\u0026quot; Ron noted nervously. \u0026quot;It’s glistening. Is it going to wriggle?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Eat it, Ronald,\u0026quot; Hermione commanded, dipping a piece of Salmon Sashimi into soy sauce with elegant precision. \u0026quot;It’s rich in omega-3s. And it’s delicious.\u0026quot;","Ron took a breath. He grabbed the tuna with his fingers (abandoning the sticks immediately). He threw it into his mouth.","He chewed once. He stopped. His eyes went wide.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Ron breathed. \u0026quot;Oh, wow. It... it just vanished. Where did it go? I want it back. I want ten more.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is acceptable,\u0026quot; Draco Malfoy sniffed, eating a piece of Yellowtail. \u0026quot;Fresh. The texture is... aristocratic. It does not fight back.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wagyu Revelation\u003c/strong\u003e","Then, the main event arrived. A chef placed a platter of the A5 Wagyu beef on the table. It was sliced thin, the marbling so intense it looked like pink lace.","\u0026quot;The happy cow,\u0026quot; Luna smiled, picking up a slice with her chopsticks (she used them perfectly, having apparently learned from a Nargle). \u0026quot;You can taste the classical music.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Harry said, picking up the tongs. \u0026quot;Vernon said ten seconds. High heat.\u0026quot;","He laid the beef onto the hot grill mesh.","\u003cem\u003eHISSSSSSS.\u003c/em\u003e","The sound was aggressive. Smoke billowed up, smelling of rendered fat and salt.","Harry flipped it. Five seconds later, he took it off.","He placed the sizzling strip onto Draco’s plate.","\u0026quot;Try that, Malfoy,\u0026quot; Harry challenged. \u0026quot;See if it beats the Manor kitchen.\u0026quot;","Draco looked at the meat. It was glistening with its own juices. He picked it up. He ate it.","Draco Malfoy stopped functioning for a solid three seconds. He stared at the ocean.","\u0026quot;My father,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, his voice trembling with emotion, \u0026quot;has lied to me. He told me the best beef came from Scotland. He was wrong. This cow... this cow is a god.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It melts,\u0026quot; Ginny moaned, eating her own piece. \u0026quot;It coats your mouth. It’s like eating a savory cloud.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe DIY BBQ\u003c/strong\u003e","Now came the \u003cem\u003eGalbi\u003c/em\u003e—the marinated short ribs.","\u0026quot;Lettuce wrap,\u0026quot; Hermione instructed, following Vernon’s briefing. \u0026quot;Meat. Garlic. Paste. Wrap. Eat.\u0026quot;","They loaded the grill. The smell of caramelizing soy and garlic filled the air.","\u0026quot;This requires coordination,\u0026quot; Draco complained, flipping meat with his silk sleeves rolled up. \u0026quot;I am essentially a line cook. I should be paid.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You own the island, Draco,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, wrapping a piece of rib in a lettuce leaf. \u0026quot;You’re paying yourself.\u0026quot;","Ron constructed a wrap the size of a Quaffle. He shoved the whole thing in his mouth.","\u0026quot;Mmph,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled, juice running down his chin. \u0026quot;Garlic. Sweet. Salty. Crunchy. It’s a flavor bomb, Harry! It exploded!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Kimchi Challenge\u003c/strong\u003e","Ginny Weasley reached for the bowl of red, fermented cabbage.","\u0026quot;The courage,\u0026quot; she quoted Vernon.","She took a large bite of Kimchi.","Her eyes watered instantly. \u0026quot;Whoa!\u0026quot; Ginny gasped, fanning her mouth. \u0026quot;It’s sour! It’s spicy! It’s... fizzing on my tongue!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s alive!\u0026quot; Ron panicked, backing away.","\u0026quot;It cuts the fat,\u0026quot; Hermione analyzed, eating a piece with her beef. \u0026quot;See? The Wagyu is rich, but the Kimchi is sharp. It cleans the palate so you can eat more beef. It’s tactical gastronomy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s brilliant,\u0026quot; Ginny decided, going back for seconds. \u0026quot;It wakes you up. I feel like I could fly a broom to the moon right now.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Verdict\u003c/strong\u003e","As the platters emptied and the grill cooled, the six friends sat back, utterly defeated by the richness of the meal.","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t move,\u0026quot; Harry admitted, staring at the stars. \u0026quot;I am made of tuna and happy cows.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have eaten raw fish,\u0026quot; Ron shook his head in disbelief. \u0026quot;And I liked it. Who am I? What have I become?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You have become cultured, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, sipping a cup of green tea. \u0026quot;Welcome to the club.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Nargles loved the barbecue,\u0026quot; Luna noted dreamily. \u0026quot;They like the smoke.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at his friends. He looked at the empty grill.","\u0026quot;Vernon was right,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;Operation Pacific Rim was a success.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Total victory,\u0026quot; Ron agreed, burping softly. \u0026quot;Now... pass the Wassabi. I want to see if it really clears the sinuses.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t do it, Ron,\u0026quot; Hermione warned.","Ron ate a spoonful of green paste.","\u0026quot;AAGH!\u0026quot; Ron screamed, clutching his nose. \u0026quot;MY BRAIN IS ON FIRE!\u0026quot;","The table erupted in laughter as Ron downed a pitcher of water.","\u0026quot;Idiot,\u0026quot; Draco smirked affectionately.","\u0026quot;My idiot,\u0026quot; Luna sighed, smiling."]},{"num":130,"origNum":130,"title":"The Diplomatic Palate","wordCount":894,"paragraphs":["At the \u0026quot;Senior Table,\u0026quot; the atmosphere was less about enthusiastic devouring and more about cautious negotiation with the cuisine.","Vernon Dursley sat at the head, tongs in one hand, a glass of Asahi beer in the other. He looked like a king holding court.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon announced. \u0026quot;Phase One. The Sashimi. Do not be afraid. It is dead. It is clean. It is softer than a cloud.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Raw Deal\u003c/strong\u003e","Molly Weasley stared at the platter of raw tuna with the expression of a woman who had spent forty years ensuring every piece of meat she served was roasted to within an inch of its life.","\u0026quot;It’s... pink,\u0026quot; Molly whispered. \u0026quot;Arthur, it’s entirely uncooked. It hasn\u0027t seen a flame. It hasn\u0027t even seen a warming charm.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s \u0027Au Naturel\u0027, Molly!\u0026quot; Arthur said excitedly, picking up a piece of salmon with his fingers (he had given up on the chopsticks immediately). \u0026quot;Muggle bravery! They eat the sea as it is!\u0026quot;","Arthur popped the salmon into his mouth. He chewed. He blinked.","\u0026quot;Oh!\u0026quot; Arthur gasped. \u0026quot;It’s cold! But... sweet? It tastes like the ocean, but without the salt water!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy was inspecting a slice of Yellowtail on the end of his fork.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said gravely. \u0026quot;If I contract a parasite, my lawyers will seize your drill factory.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Eat the fish, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa commanded gently. \u0026quot;It matches your dress robes. Pale and expensive.\u0026quot;","Lucius sighed. He ate the fish.","His eyes fluttered shut.","\u0026quot;Silk,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured involuntarily. \u0026quot;It is edible silk. I... I withdraw the threat of litigation. Pass the soy sauce.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Manual Labor Dispute\u003c/strong\u003e","Then came the Korean BBQ.","The charcoal grills in the center of the table roared to life.","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Vernon instructed. \u0026quot;We cook. You take the Galbi—the short rib—and you lay it on the mesh. You listen for the sizzle. That is the sound of flavor being born.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy recoiled. \u0026quot;I beg your pardon? \u003cem\u003eWe\u003c/em\u003e cook? I am wearing white linen, Vernon. I do not stand over open flames. That is what Dobby is for.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby is on break!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;He’s eating a Jalebi! Pick up the tongs, Lucius! Be a man! Sear your own destiny!\u0026quot;","Lucius looked at the raw, marinated meat. He looked at the tongs. He looked at Narcissa, who was already grilling a mushroom with elegant precision.","\u0026quot;Fine,\u0026quot; Lucius sneered. \u0026quot;But if I singe an eyebrow...\u0026quot;","He placed a strip of beef on the grill. \u003cem\u003eHISSSSSS.\u003c/em\u003e Smoke rose up.","Lucius jumped back, but then he leaned in. He sniffed.","\u0026quot;Garlic,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;Soy. Pear? It smells... intoxicated.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s marinaded!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered. \u0026quot;Flip it, Lucius! Don\u0027t let it burn!\u0026quot;","Lucius flipped the meat. He watched it turn a perfect, caramelized brown. A strange look crossed his face.","\u0026quot;I... I made that,\u0026quot; Lucius said, pointing at the cooked meat with his tongs. \u0026quot;I applied heat. I transformed it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You’re a chef, Lucius!\u0026quot; Arthur clapped. \u0026quot;A Muggle chef!\u0026quot;","Lucius put the meat on his plate. He ate it.","\u0026quot;It is better,\u0026quot; Lucius decided, \u0026quot;because I suffered for it.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wagyu Consensus\u003c/strong\u003e","When the A5 Wagyu arrived, the table fell silent. The marbling was so intense the meat looked like white marble.","\u0026quot;The Happy Cow,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled, picking up a slice. \u0026quot;It looks very rich, Vernon. Is it good for the cholesterol?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s good for the soul, Petunia!\u0026quot; Vernon promised. \u0026quot;Ten seconds per side!\u0026quot;","They seared the meat. They ate it.","Molly Weasley actually dropped her fork.","\u0026quot;Oh my,\u0026quot; Molly breathed, her hand going to her heart. \u0026quot;It’s... I don\u0027t even have to chew. It just... leaves.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is essence of beef,\u0026quot; Arthur agreed, eyes wide. \u0026quot;It is the Platonic ideal of a cow.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;This cow,\u0026quot; Lucius announced, wiping his mouth with a napkin, \u0026quot;lived a better life than most wizards. I can taste the privilege. I approve.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wasabi Incident\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley, emboldened by the beef, spotted the green mound on the sushi platter.","\u0026quot;Ah!\u0026quot; Arthur beamed. \u0026quot;Mint paste! To cleanse the palate! Like a toothpaste, but for dinner!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Arthur, no—\u0026quot; Vernon started, but it was too late.","Arthur took a teaspoon-sized scoop of Wasabi and put it in his mouth.","He froze.","His face turned the color of a tomato. His eyes bulged behind his glasses. Steam seemed to issue from his ears.","\u0026quot;HOOO!\u0026quot; Arthur wheezed, grabbing a pitcher of water. \u0026quot;IT’S ANGRY MINT! IT’S NOT MINT! IT’S FIRE PASTE!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s horseradish, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon roared with laughter. \u0026quot;It clears the tubes!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My tubes are cleared!\u0026quot; Arthur gasped, fanning his tongue. \u0026quot;My tubes are gone! I can see through time!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Verdict\u003c/strong\u003e","As the meal wound down, the parents sat back, loosened belts, and unbuttoned jackets.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Molly Weasley said, picking the last grain of rice from her plate. \u0026quot;I must admit, Vernon. You were right. It was... an adventure.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a triumph,\u0026quot; Narcissa corrected, sipping green tea. \u0026quot;I shall require the supplier for the \u0027Kimchi\u0027. It is invigorating.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy looked at the empty grill. He looked at his tongs, which he was still holding.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius said seriously. \u0026quot;This \u0027Barbecue\u0027... it creates a sense of... agency. I enjoyed controlling the heat.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You’re a natural, Lucius,\u0026quot; Vernon grinned.","\u0026quot;I shall have one installed at the Manor,\u0026quot; Lucius decided. \u0026quot;In the drawing room. For guests.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Maybe the garden, dear,\u0026quot; Narcissa suggested.","\u0026quot;The garden,\u0026quot; Lucius conceded. \u0026quot;To the Happy Cow!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Cow!\u0026quot; the parents toasted."]},{"num":131,"origNum":131,"title":"The Dragon Paste","wordCount":929,"paragraphs":["At the \u0026quot;High Table\u0026quot; (which was actually just a table closest to the ocean), the Hogwarts faculty and the Order members were navigating the culinary landscape with varying degrees of success.","Sirius Black was grilling short ribs with a reckless abandon, tossing garlic cloves onto the fire just to see them flare. Remus Lupin was quietly making perfect lettuce wraps. Nymphadora Tonks was trying to eat sushi with chopsticks and failing, eventually turning her fingers into chopsticks (a Metamorphmagus perk).","Albus Dumbledore, however, had found the condiment station.","He sat with a plate of \u003cem\u003eSashimi\u003c/em\u003e, a glass of Sake, and a small bowl filled entirely with the bright green paste that had nearly assassinated Arthur Weasley minutes earlier.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Headmaster’s Snack\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Pistachio?\u0026quot; Dumbledore mused, lifting the bowl. \u0026quot;Or perhaps a mint purée? The color is most vibrant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is \u003cem\u003eWasabi\u003c/em\u003e, Albus,\u0026quot; Severus Snape drawled from the next seat, slicing his Wagyu beef. \u0026quot;It is a rhizome. A root. Similar to horseradish, but significantly more... volatile.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Volatile,\u0026quot; Dumbledore repeated happily. \u0026quot;I do enjoy a spirited vegetable.\u0026quot;","He didn\u0027t take a dab. He didn\u0027t take a smear.","Albus Dumbledore took a dessert spoon, scooped up a golf-ball-sized mound of pure Wasabi, and put it in his mouth.","The table went silent.","McGonagall lowered her fork. Sirius stopped chewing. Even Snape paused, waiting for the inevitable explosion.","Dumbledore chewed. He swallowed. He blinked once, his blue eyes watering slightly behind his glasses.","Then, he smiled.","\u0026quot;Invigorating!\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared, breathing out a sigh that smelled of nasal clearing. \u0026quot;It tickles the sinuses! It is like a cold wind on a hot day! Severus, you must try it. It clears the mind wonderfully.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Skeptics\u003c/strong\u003e","Sirius Black laughed, shaking his head.","\u0026quot;I saw Arthur,\u0026quot; Sirius grinned, pointing down the beach where Arthur Weasley was still drinking water. \u0026quot;He turned purple. He was wheezing like a busted bagpipe. I thought he was dying.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Arthur is a Muggle enthusiast,\u0026quot; McGonagall sniffed, dipping a piece of sushi in soy sauce. \u0026quot;But his constitution is... gentle. He finds Earl Grey tea \u0027racy\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Tonks chimed in, her hair turning a hungry shade of purple. \u0026quot;Ron was screaming too. But they’re Weasleys. They exaggerate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It cannot be that bad,\u0026quot; Remus reasoned, looking at Dumbledore, who was currently spreading more Wasabi onto a tuna roll like it was butter. \u0026quot;Look at Albus. He’s eating it like pudding.\u0026quot;","Snape peered at the green paste.","\u0026quot;The chemical compound is allyl isothiocyanate,\u0026quot; Snape analyzed. \u0026quot;It produces a nasal sensation, not a tongue burn. It is fleeting. Weasley and his father were clearly engaging in theatrics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Sirius decided. \u0026quot;Challenge accepted. If the old man can handle it, the Marauders can handle it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the Faculty,\u0026quot; McGonagall added, her competitive streak flaring. \u0026quot;I am not going to be outdone by a root vegetable.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Group Taste Test\u003c/strong\u003e","They grabbed spoons.","\u0026quot;A teaspoon,\u0026quot; Sirius directed. \u0026quot;A proper dose. On three.\u0026quot;","Sirius, Remus, Tonks, McGonagall, and Snape all scooped up a generous dollop of Wasabi.","\u0026quot;One... two... three!\u0026quot;","They put the spoons in their mouths.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Detonation\u003c/strong\u003e","For one second, nothing happened.","Then, chemistry took over. The vapors rose through the back of their mouths, traveled up their nasal cavities, and hit their olfactory nerves with the force of a Cruciatus Curse.","\u003cem\u003eWHOOSH.\u003c/em\u003e","Sirius Black’s eyes bulged so far out of his head they looked like they might detach. He slammed his hands on the table.","\u0026quot;GAAAAAH!\u0026quot; Sirius screamed, but no sound came out, just a high-pitched wheeze.","Remus Lupin turned pale, then red, then a violent shade of maroon. He clutched his nose.","\u0026quot;The Wolf!\u0026quot; Remus choked out. \u0026quot;The Wolf is dying! It smells like pain!\u0026quot;","Tonks didn\u0027t scream. She changed. Her hair cycled rapidly through every color of the rainbow—red, green, blue, yellow—before settling on a shock of pure, distress-signal white. Her nose briefly turned into a pig snout, then a beak, before returning to normal.","\u0026quot;MY FACE!\u0026quot; Tonks yelled. \u0026quot;MY FACE IS FIZZING!\u0026quot;","Minerva McGonagall sat rigidly upright. Tears streamed down her face in silent rivers. She opened her mouth to speak, but all that came out was a small, dignified squeak.","\u0026quot;Water,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered. \u0026quot;Aguamenti... the ocean... bring the ocean.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Potions Master’s Regret\u003c/strong\u003e","But it was Severus Snape who had the most profound reaction.","He froze. His black eyes widened behind his sunglasses. His nostrils flared.","He didn\u0027t scream. He didn\u0027t flail.","He simply stood up, rigid as a board. He picked up his napkin. He dabbed his eyes.","\u0026quot;It is...\u0026quot; Snape gasped, his voice sounding like he had inhaled helium. \u0026quot;It is... not horseradish. It is... concentrated... hatred.\u0026quot;","He grabbed a pitcher of iced tea. He didn\u0027t pour it. He drank straight from the jug, dignity be damned.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Unbothered\u003c/strong\u003e","They sat there, gasping, crying, and chugging fluids, looking like the victims of a chemical attack.","And in the center of the carnage sat Albus Dumbledore.","He was eating another piece of sushi, topped with a fresh dollop of green paste.","\u0026quot;Is something the matter?\u0026quot; Dumbledore asked pleasantly, looking around at the weeping wizards. \u0026quot;Is the vintage too spicy?\u0026quot;","Sirius wiped his streaming eyes with his sleeve. He looked at Dumbledore. He looked at the empty spoon.","\u0026quot;You...\u0026quot; Sirius wheezed. \u0026quot;You are a monster. You have no nerve endings.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have excellent nerve endings,\u0026quot; Dumbledore corrected, beaming. \u0026quot;They simply enjoy a bit of excitement. Now, who wants to try the Kimchi? Vernon says it \u0027bites back\u0027!\u0026quot;","The Marauders and the Professors groaned in unison, pushing their plates away.","\u0026quot;I surrender,\u0026quot; Snape whispered into his pitcher. \u0026quot;I yield to the vegetables.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":132,"origNum":132,"title":"The Redemption of the Ribeye","wordCount":809,"paragraphs":["With the wasabi tears wiped away and the sinus passages of the Order of the Phoenix cleared for the first time in decades, the table turned its attention to the glowing charcoal grills set into the center of the mahogany.","The \u0026quot;Green Paste Incident\u0026quot; was forgotten the moment the raw A5 Wagyu hit the hot metal mesh.","\u003cem\u003eHISSS-CRACKLE.\u003c/em\u003e","The sound was hypnotic. The scent that rose up was heavy, rich, and intoxicating—the smell of rendering fat and searing protein.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Potions Master’s Precision\u003c/strong\u003e","Severus Snape, having recovered his dignity (and his vision), took possession of the tongs.","\u0026quot;Do not touch it,\u0026quot; Snape ordered Sirius, who was reaching for a slice with his fingers. \u0026quot;This is not a chicken leg, Black. It is a biological masterpiece. It requires thermal respect.\u0026quot;","Snape watched the meat. He didn\u0027t flip it immediately. He watched the edges turn from pink to a caramelized brown. He watched the white marbling liquify, basting the meat from the inside out.","\u0026quot;Ten seconds,\u0026quot; Snape murmured, counting down like he was brewing Felix Felicis. \u0026quot;Nine... eight...\u0026quot;","He flipped the slice. The underside was a perfect, lattice-work mahogany.","He placed the piece onto Professor McGonagall’s plate.","\u0026quot;Eat,\u0026quot; Snape commanded. \u0026quot;Before the lipid structure resolidifies.\u0026quot;","McGonagall picked up the beef. She didn\u0027t use sauce. She didn\u0027t wrap it. She simply placed the hot, seared strip on her tongue.","She closed her eyes. Her shoulders dropped three inches.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered. \u0026quot;Oh, my. It... it doesn\u0027t require teeth, Severus. It simply... yields.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is meat butter,\u0026quot; Remus Lupin agreed, tasting his own piece. \u0026quot;It coats the mouth. It’s savory, but sweet? Like... beef candy?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Beef candy,\u0026quot; Sirius laughed, chewing happily. \u0026quot;I like that. Remus, the Wolf is purring.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Galbi Glaze\u003c/strong\u003e","Next came the \u003cem\u003eGalbi\u003c/em\u003e—the diamond-cut short ribs marinated in Vernon’s vaunted pear and soy mixture.","These required a longer sear. The sugar in the marinade hit the grill, bubbling and turning sticky and dark.","\u0026quot;The smell,\u0026quot; Tonks groaned, her hair turning a hungry shade of barbeque-sauce brown. \u0026quot;It smells like a campfire made of sugar and garlic.\u0026quot;","She grabbed a piece straight off the grill, blowing on it frantically.","\u0026quot;Hot! Hot! But... mmmph.\u0026quot; She chewed. \u0026quot;The pear! You can taste the fruit! It cuts the salt!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore was constructing a \u003cem\u003eSsam\u003c/em\u003e—a lettuce wrap—with the architectural focus of a man building a house of cards.","He took a crisp leaf of red lettuce. He added a spoonful of rice. He added a dollop of \u003cem\u003eSsamjang\u003c/em\u003e (the soybean paste). He added a clove of grilled garlic.","And finally, he crowned it with a glistening, charred piece of Galbi.","He folded it into a neat parcel and took a massive bite.","\u0026quot;Crunch,\u0026quot; Dumbledore narrated with his mouth full. \u0026quot;Then soft. Then heat. Then sweet. It is a textural journey, Minerva! It is a story in a leaf!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Tempura Interlude\u003c/strong\u003e","A server elf arrived with a basket of \u003cem\u003eTempura\u003c/em\u003e.","Vegetables and massive prawns had been dipped in an batter so light and airy it looked like lace, then fried to a pale gold.","\u0026quot;Fried air,\u0026quot; Sirius marveled, picking up a sweet potato slice. \u0026quot;How does the batter stay on? It’s gossamer.\u0026quot;","He bit into it. The crunch was audible across the table.","\u0026quot;It shatters,\u0026quot; Sirius grinned. \u0026quot;It’s like eating glass, but tasty glass.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Return of the Rice\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape, meanwhile, had discovered the \u003cem\u003eBibimbap\u003c/em\u003e.","He was mixing the stone bowl with a long spoon, listening to the rice sizzle and crisp up against the hot rock. The egg yolk broke, coating the vegetables and beef in a rich, yellow sauce.","\u0026quot;The thermal retention of the stone vessel,\u0026quot; Snape observed, scraping up a layer of crispy, golden rice from the bottom (the \u003cem\u003enurungji\u003c/em\u003e). \u0026quot;It creates a secondary texture. The rice is soft above, but brittle below.\u0026quot;","He ate a spoonful of the crunchy rice.","\u0026quot;Texture,\u0026quot; Snape declared, a rare look of contentment on his face. \u0026quot;Crunch without hardness. Flavor without chaos. It is... adequate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;High praise,\u0026quot; Remus chuckled, stealing a prawn from Sirius’s plate.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Course\u003c/strong\u003e","As the fire in the grills died down to glowing embers, the group sat back, coated in the invisible, comforting weight of Umami.","There was no sugar crash this time. Just the deep, savory satisfaction of high-quality protein and complex carbohydrates.","McGonagall was sipping a cup of roasted barley tea.","\u0026quot;I feel...\u0026quot; she searched for the word. \u0026quot;Anchored. That meal... it had gravitas.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It had beef,\u0026quot; Sirius corrected, picking his teeth with a chopstick. \u0026quot;Lots of beef.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And not a single explosive bean in sight,\u0026quot; Dumbledore sighed happily, wiping a smear of soybean paste from his beard. \u0026quot;The Muggles really do know how to treat a cow.\u0026quot;","They sat in the warm Caribbean breeze, watching the smoke from the grills drift up toward the stars, fully recovered from the Wasabi, and fully prepared for the wedding to come."]},{"num":133,"origNum":133,"title":"The Watchers on the Wall","wordCount":1184,"paragraphs":["The charcoal grills had dimmed to soft, glowing embers. The smell of searing Wagyu had faded, replaced by the cool, salty tang of the midnight ocean.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley announced, checking his watch in the moonlight. \u0026quot;2200 hours. The caloric intake has been substantial. The protein synthesis will occur during sleep. Parents, Professors, and Marauders... to the barracks! We need to be fresh for the ceremony.\u0026quot;","He looked at the six young adults sitting on the sea wall, their legs dangling over the sand.","\u0026quot;You lot,\u0026quot; Vernon softened, his voice losing its drill-sergeant edge. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t stay up too late. Big day tomorrow. Biggest day.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We won\u0027t, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry promised.","\u0026quot;Good lad.\u0026quot;","The older generation filed up the stone steps toward the villa, leaving the three couples alone in the vast, quiet darkness of the Caribbean night.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Midnight Stroll\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry slid off the wall. He took off his shoes, dropping them in the sand.","\u0026quot;Walk?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;Walk,\u0026quot; Hermione agreed, taking his hand.","The six of them moved down to the water’s edge where the foam hissed against the shore. They walked in a loose line—Harry and Hermione, Ron and Luna, Draco and Ginny.","For a long time, nobody spoke. The silence wasn\u0027t awkward; it was heavy with history.","\u0026quot;I ate raw fish,\u0026quot; Ron whispered suddenly, breaking the spell. He looked at the moon. \u0026quot;I ate raw fish, and I liked it. And tomorrow, I’m getting married in a linen suit that cost more than my broomstick.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027ve changed, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, though he was holding Ginny’s hand so tight his knuckles were white. \u0026quot;You’ve become... sophisticated.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think I’ve just become... happy,\u0026quot; Ron said, sounding surprised by the realization.","He looked at Luna, who was walking with her eyes closed, humming a tune that sounded suspiciously like \u003cem\u003eWeasley is Our King\u003c/em\u003e but in waltz time.","\u0026quot;Luna,\u0026quot; Ron said softly.","\u0026quot;Yes, Ronald?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Are the Nargles gone?\u0026quot;","Luna opened her eyes. She looked at the ocean. She looked at her friends.","\u0026quot;Oh, no,\u0026quot; Luna smiled serenely. \u0026quot;They are everywhere. But they are party Nargles. They are wearing tiny hats.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reflection\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry stopped walking. He looked at the group.","He looked at Draco Malfoy—the boy he had obsessed over in Sixth Year, the boy he had fought in a bathroom. Now, Draco was standing barefoot in the sand, the sleeves of his silk shirt rolled up, looking at Ginny Weasley like she was the only source of light in the universe.","He looked at Ron and Hermione—the two people who had kept him alive when he had nothing.","\u0026quot;We made it,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;We did,\u0026quot; Hermione said, leaning her head on his shoulder. \u0026quot;Against all odds. Statistically, we shouldn\u0027t be here.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Screw statistics,\u0026quot; Ginny said fiercely. \u0026quot;We’re here because we’re stubborn.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And because Potter has the survival instincts of a cockroach,\u0026quot; Draco added, smirking.","\u0026quot;And because you threw me a wand,\u0026quot; Harry countered.","Draco’s smirk faded. He looked down at the sand. \u0026quot;Yeah. Well. Don\u0027t tell anyone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Everyone knows, Draco,\u0026quot; Hermione said gently. \u0026quot;It’s why we’re here.\u0026quot;","They stood in a circle, the waves washing over their feet.","\u0026quot;To us,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly. \u0026quot;To the ones who made it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the ones who didn\u0027t,\u0026quot; Ron added, his voice thick.","\u0026quot;To them,\u0026quot; Draco whispered.","They didn\u0027t raise glasses. They just stood there, six broken pieces of a war that had healed into something stronger, holding onto each other in the dark.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe View from the Terrace\u003c/strong\u003e","High above them, on the stone terrace of the villa, the lights were out.","But the \u0026quot;adults\u0026quot; hadn\u0027t gone to bed. They were lined up along the stone balustrade, looking down at the beach.","The moonlight illuminated the six small figures walking by the water.","Molly Weasley was crying openly, her head resting on Arthur’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;Look at them, Arthur,\u0026quot; Molly sobbed quietly. \u0026quot;They look so... grown up.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are, Mollywobbles,\u0026quot; Arthur whispered, wiping his own glasses. \u0026quot;They saved the world. I think they earned the right to grow up.\u0026quot;","Narcissa Malfoy stood beside them. She wasn\u0027t crying, but her hand was gripping the stone railing so hard her nails were white.","\u0026quot;He is laughing,\u0026quot; Narcissa whispered, watching Draco kick water at Ginny. \u0026quot;Lucius, look. Our son is laughing.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy, stripped of his Death Eater mask and his pureblood armor, looked down at his son. He saw Draco holding hands with a blood traitor. He saw him standing shoulder-to-shoulder with Harry Potter.","\u0026quot;He is safe, Cissy,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured, his voice breaking. \u0026quot;He is alive. That is all that matters.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Marauders’ Watch\u003c/strong\u003e","Further down the rail, Sirius Black and Remus Lupin stood together.","\u0026quot;James would have loved this,\u0026quot; Sirius said, his voice rough. \u0026quot;The beach. The food. The fact that Snivellus ate a burger.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lily would have loved Hermione,\u0026quot; Remus added softly. \u0026quot;She would have loved that Harry found his equal.\u0026quot;","They watched Harry stop and kiss Hermione in the moonlight.","\u0026quot;He did it, Moony,\u0026quot; Sirius wiped a tear from his eye with a knuckle. \u0026quot;He finished the mission. He got the girl. He got the life we couldn\u0027t have.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He did,\u0026quot; Remus smiled. \u0026quot;Mischief Managed.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Teachers\u003c/strong\u003e","At the end of the terrace, the Professors stood in a row.","McGonagall was dabbing her eyes with a tartan handkerchief.","\u0026quot;They were children yesterday,\u0026quot; she sniffed. \u0026quot;I remember sorting them. Potter looked like he was drowning in his robes. Malfoy looked like a terrified peacock.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Weasley looked like he was going to vomit,\u0026quot; Snape added from the shadows.","Everyone turned to look at Snape. He wasn\u0027t sneering. He was leaning against a pillar, arms crossed, watching the beach with an intensity that belied his casual posture.","\u0026quot;They are... tolerable adults,\u0026quot; Snape admitted quietly. \u0026quot;They have... evolved.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;High praise, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled, holding a nightcap.","Dumbledore looked down at the beach. He saw the unity. He saw the love. He saw the future he had died (and resurrected) to protect.","\u0026quot;It is a beautiful thing,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly. \u0026quot;To see the story end well.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Muggle Farewell\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon and Petunia stood a little apart from the wizards.","Petunia was watching Harry. She remembered the baby in the basket. She remembered the boy in the cupboard. She remembered the green eyes that haunted her.","\u0026quot;He looks happy, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered. \u0026quot;He looks... like he belongs.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He does,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted. He cleared his throat, which seemed to have a large lump in it. \u0026quot;He’s a good lad. Stubborn. messy hair. Terrible eyesight. But... a good lad.\u0026quot;","Vernon looked at the wizards—the Malfoys, the Weasleys, the teachers. He looked at the magical world that had terrified him for two decades.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re a weird bunch, Petunia,\u0026quot; Vernon sniffed. \u0026quot;Mad as hatters. But... they take care of their own.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled, leaning her head on his shoulder. \u0026quot;They do.\u0026quot;","Down on the beach, the three couples turned and began to walk back toward the lights of the villa, arm in arm, ready for the morning that would change everything.","Above them, the watchers wiped their eyes, took one last look at the peace they had fought for, and finally, quietly, went to bed."]},{"num":134,"origNum":134,"title":"The Sapphire Clip","wordCount":1011,"paragraphs":["The Bridal Suite of the villa was a storm of silk, perfume, and hairspray.","The morning sun flooded the room, illuminating the chaos of preparation. House-elves darted around the floor picking up discarded pins, while enchanted brushes worked furiously on three heads of hair.","Molly Weasley was everywhere at once. She was crying, she was laughing, and she was threatening a stubborn curl on Ginny’s head with her wand.","\u0026quot;It will curl, Ginevra!\u0026quot; Molly sobbed. \u0026quot;It will curl or I will cry!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re already crying, Mum,\u0026quot; Ginny laughed, sitting still while a brush attacked her mane.","Narcissa Malfoy stood by the window, steaming a veil with a graceful wave of her wand. She looked serene amidst the madness, the calm eye of the bridal hurricane.","Nymphadora Tonks was changing her hair color every five seconds to match the bridesmaids\u0027 dresses, trying to decide between \u0026quot;Subtle Lavender\u0026quot; and \u0026quot;Party Pink.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go with the pink, Dora,\u0026quot; Remus had said (via a message Patronus earlier). \u0026quot;It matches the sunrise.\u0026quot;","Minerva McGonagall sat in a high-backed chair, sipping tea. She wasn\u0027t fussing. She was observing her girls—the students she had protected, taught, and worried over—preparing for the happiest day of their lives.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lioness Rises\u003c/strong\u003e","Ginny was the first to step into her dress.","With Narcissa’s help (\u0026quot;Careful with the silk, Molly, do not pinch\u0026quot;), she slid into the backless, liquid-white gown1.","She turned to the mirror.","The dress fit like a second skin. The high slit revealed a flash of leg. The open back showed off her strength.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Molly breathed, her hands flying to her mouth. \u0026quot;Oh, Ginny.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s not too much?\u0026quot; Ginny asked, suddenly nervous. \u0026quot;Is it too... bare?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is magnificent,\u0026quot; Narcissa declared, fastening a diamond necklace around Ginny’s throat. \u0026quot;It is fierce. You look like a queen who conquered a dragon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Which you did,\u0026quot; Tonks winked. \u0026quot;Or at least, you conquered a Draco.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Moon Beam\u003c/strong\u003e","Luna Lovegood floated out from behind the screen next.","Her dress of shifting organza—pale yellow, silver, and blue—moved around her like a living cloud2. She wasn\u0027t wearing shoes yet, but she was wearing a crown of fresh wildflowers she had picked from the garden that morning.","\u0026quot;I feel like a sunbeam,\u0026quot; Luna hummed, spinning slowly.","\u0026quot;You look like magic, Luna,\u0026quot; McGonagall said softly, her stern face softening into a genuine smile. \u0026quot;Pure, wild magic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Nargles are staying away,\u0026quot; Luna noted happily. \u0026quot;They know it is a serious occasion.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Brightest Witch\u003c/strong\u003e","Finally, the screen parted for Hermione.","She stepped out into the center of the room.","The ivory silk chiffon flowed around her, the delicate lace sleeves looking like frost patterns3. Her hair, usually bushy and wild, had been tamed into an elegant, complex knot at the nape of her neck, leaving her neck bare.","She looked tall. She looked graceful. She looked breathtaking.","The room fell silent. Tonks stopped changing her hair color. Molly stopped crying for a full three seconds.","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered. \u0026quot;Harry is going to faint. We need to put a Sticking Charm on his knees.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You look beautiful, dear,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, her voice unusually warm. \u0026quot;Truly.\u0026quot;","Hermione looked in the mirror. Her hands were shaking slightly.","\u0026quot;I... I wish...\u0026quot; she started, then stopped. She wished her mum could remember this. She wished she wasn\u0027t doing this without her own parents, even if she had the Weasleys.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Something Blue\u003c/strong\u003e","Petunia Dursley had been standing quietly in the corner, holding a small velvet pouch.","She had been watching them—the magic, the wands, the flying brushes—with a look of wistful sadness.","When Hermione spoke, Petunia stepped forward.","The room watched her. The Muggle in the magical sanctuary.","Petunia walked up to Hermione. She looked at the young woman who had saved her nephew’s life, the woman who had slept on the floor of Number Four to protect him4.","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Petunia said, her voice trembling slightly.","\u0026quot;Mrs. Dursley?\u0026quot; Hermione turned.","\u0026quot;You need something blue,\u0026quot; Petunia said. \u0026quot;It’s tradition. Old, New, Borrowed, Blue.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I... I have a blue ribbon on my garter,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled weakly.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Petunia said firmly. \u0026quot;You need something that matters.\u0026quot;","She opened the velvet pouch.","Inside lay a hair clip. It was silver, shaped like a small lily flower, set with three deep, brilliant blue sapphires.","McGonagall gasped audibly. She recognized it.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, her fingers tracing the silver petals, \u0026quot;belonged to my sister. To Lily.\u0026quot;","Hermione’s breath hitched. \u0026quot;Harry’s mother?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She wore it,\u0026quot; Petunia continued, tears filling her eyes, \u0026quot;to her graduation. And she wore it... the day she married James.\u0026quot;","Petunia looked up at Hermione.","\u0026quot;I kept it. All these years. I don\u0027t know why. I hated... I tried to hate everything about her world. But I couldn\u0027t throw this away.\u0026quot;","She held it out to Hermione.","\u0026quot;She would have loved you, Hermione. You are just like her. Smart. Brave. And you love him so much.\u0026quot;","Petunia’s voice cracked.","\u0026quot;Please. Wear it. For her. And for Harry. Let his mother be at his wedding.\u0026quot;","Hermione burst into tears. She didn\u0027t try to stop them.","\u0026quot;Oh, Petunia,\u0026quot; Hermione sobbed.","She lowered her head. Petunia, with shaking hands, slid the silver lily into Hermione’s dark hair, just above the bun.","The sapphires caught the light, glowing against the dark locks.","Molly Weasley let out a wail and buried her face in a handkerchief. Narcissa wiped a tear from her cheek with a distinct lack of Malfoy composure.","Even McGonagall removed her glasses to wipe her eyes.","\u0026quot;There,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, stepping back and looking at Hermione. \u0026quot;Now you are ready.\u0026quot;","Hermione reached out and hugged Petunia Dursley—a fierce, daughterly hug.","\u0026quot;Thank you,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;Thank you so much.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Come now,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, her voice thick with emotion, clapping her hands gently. \u0026quot;We must not ruin the makeup. Dry your eyes, girls. The grooms are waiting.\u0026quot;","As Hermione looked in the mirror one last time, the blue lily glinting in her hair, she wasn\u0027t just a bride. She was a link in a chain of love that had survived death, war, and time.","She was ready to go home."]},{"num":135,"origNum":135,"title":"The Reflection of Prongs","wordCount":888,"paragraphs":["The Grooms\u0027 Suite was a study in nervous energy and expensive tailoring.","Unlike the chaotic storm of hairspray in the bridal suite, this room smelled of sandalwood, starch, and the faint, metallic scent of panic.","Ron Weasley was currently fighting a losing battle with his cuffs.","\u0026quot;It won\u0027t go through!\u0026quot; Ron hissed, wrestling with the gold lion cufflink. \u0026quot;The lion is stubborn! It’s refusing to enter the buttonhole! Is it enchanted to reject nervousness?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Here, son,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley stepped in, his hands steady despite his own excitement. He took Ron’s wrist.","\u0026quot;You have to angle the paw,\u0026quot; Arthur explained gently, sliding the gold through the linen. \u0026quot;There. Look at you. Cream linen. You look like a wizarding prince, Ron.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I look like I’m about to faint,\u0026quot; Ron admitted, checking his reflection. \u0026quot;But... a well-dressed one.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Malfoy Standard\u003c/strong\u003e","across the room, Lucius Malfoy was conducting a final inspection of his son.","Draco stood perfectly still in his dove-grey silk linen suit1. He looked sharp, elegant, and terrified.","Lucius reached out and adjusted Draco’s pearl tie pin by a millimeter.","\u0026quot;The line must be straight, Draco,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured. \u0026quot;Chaos is for the reception. The ceremony requires geometry.\u0026quot;","He stepped back. He looked at his son—the boy who had survived the war, the man who had bought an island to save his friends\u0027 wedding.","\u0026quot;You look...\u0026quot; Lucius cleared his throat. \u0026quot;You look impeccable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thanks, Father,\u0026quot; Draco breathed, touching his tie.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t lock your knees,\u0026quot; Lucius advised. \u0026quot;I did at my wedding. I wobbled. Your mother never let me forget it.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Manager\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley was pacing the room, checking his watch every thirty seconds.","\u0026quot;10:00 hours!\u0026quot; Vernon announced. \u0026quot;We move to the beach in fifteen minutes! Shoes tied? Pocket squares folded? Rings? Who has the rings?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I have them, Vernon,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said serenely.","The Headmaster was sitting in a plush armchair, wearing robes of blinding gold that matched the sun. He was currently levitating three velvet boxes in a slow orbit around his head.","\u0026quot;They are safe in my gravitational field,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled. \u0026quot;Severus, stop scowling. It will wrinkle your cravat.\u0026quot;","Severus Snape, standing in the corner in his high-collared black dress robes, merely curled his lip.","\u0026quot;I am not scowling, Albus. I am contemplating the statistical probability of Weasley tripping on the sand.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;High,\u0026quot; Ron piped up. \u0026quot;Very high.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reveal\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Where’s Harry?\u0026quot; Sirius Black asked, looking around. He was leaning against the mantelpiece, looking dashing in a Muggle suit he had insisted on wearing \u0026quot;to blend in with Vernon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s in the dressing room,\u0026quot; Remus Lupin said, straightening his own shabby-but-clean robes. \u0026quot;Putting on the jacket.\u0026quot;","The door to the inner dressing room clicked open.","The room went silent.","Harry Potter stepped out.","He was wearing the midnight blue suit Draco had forced him to buy2. It fit him perfectly, the dark fabric shimmering slightly, cutting a sharp, heroic silhouette that was a world away from the baggy cast-offs of Privet Drive.","He had tamed his hair (mostly). He stood tall. He looked ready.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Ghosts\u003c/strong\u003e","Sirius Black froze. The glass of firewhisky in his hand tilted dangerously.","He stared at Harry. But for a heartbreaking second, he didn\u0027t see Harry.","He saw a messy-haired young man in dress robes standing in a church in Godric\u0027s Hollow. He saw his best friend, grinning nervously, waiting for a red-headed girl to walk down the aisle.","\u0026quot;James,\u0026quot; Sirius whispered, the name slipping out before he could stop it.","Remus Lupin made a small, choked sound. He stepped forward, his eyes scanning Harry’s face—the messy hair, the glasses, the jawline that had hardened over the years of war.","\u0026quot;Prongs,\u0026quot; Remus breathed.","Harry stopped. He looked at his godfathers. He saw the raw, open grief and love on their faces.","\u0026quot;It’s just me,\u0026quot; Harry said softly, a small smile touching his lips. \u0026quot;Just Harry.\u0026quot;","Sirius blinked, the illusion breaking but the emotion remaining. He set his glass down with a clatter.","He walked over to Harry. He didn\u0027t embrace him like a cool uncle. He grabbed him like a lifeline.","\u0026quot;You look just like him,\u0026quot; Sirius choked out, holding Harry by the shoulders. \u0026quot;But you’ve got... you’ve got so much of her in you, too.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You did it, Harry,\u0026quot; Remus said, his voice thick, placing a hand on Harry’s back. \u0026quot;You lived. You grew up. James and Lily... they would be so unbearable today. James would be strutting around like he owned the island.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Lily would be fixing his tie,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, though his eyes were wet.","Vernon Dursley watched the scene. He blew his nose loudly into a handkerchief.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, his eyes suspicious bright. \u0026quot;Sharp suit, Harry. Good investment. You look... proper. Like a man who pays his taxes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thanks, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry beamed.","Dumbledore stood up, catching the floating ring boxes out of the air.","\u0026quot;The past is always with us,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said gently. \u0026quot;But today... today is about the future.\u0026quot;","He opened the door to the terrace, letting the bright Caribbean sunlight flood the room.","\u0026quot;Gentlemen,\u0026quot; Dumbledore announced. \u0026quot;It is time to go to the chapel. Or, in this case, the sand.\u0026quot;","Harry took a deep breath. He looked at Ron and Draco.","\u0026quot;Ready?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ready,\u0026quot; they said together.","They walked out into the sun, leaving the ghosts behind, walking toward the women who were their future."]},{"num":136,"origNum":136,"title":"The Procession of Light","wordCount":741,"paragraphs":["The beach was silent, save for the rhythmic hush of the waves and the soft rustle of palm fronds.","Under the bamboo archway, decorated with white orchids and drift-wood, the three grooms stood in a line.","Ron Weasley was vibrating. He was sweating in his cream linen suit, shifting his weight from foot to foot.","\u0026quot;I’m going to faint,\u0026quot; Ron whispered out of the side of his mouth. \u0026quot;Harry, catch me. I’m going down. My knees are liquid.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lock your knees, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco Malfoy hissed from the other side of Harry.","Draco looked composed in his dove-grey suit, but Harry could see a small muscle jumping in his jaw. He was gripping his hands behind his back so tightly his knuckles were white.","\u0026quot;I’m not locking them!\u0026quot; Ron argued. \u0026quot;Lucius said \u003cem\u003edon\u0027t\u003c/em\u003e lock them!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Quiet,\u0026quot; Harry said, smiling. He felt surprisingly calm. He checked his own midnight blue cuffs. He touched the ring in his pocket.","\u0026quot;Just breathe.\u0026quot;","In the front row, Vernon Dursley checked his stopwatch.","\u0026quot;11:00 hours,\u0026quot; Vernon whispered to Petunia. \u0026quot;Precision timing. Excellent.\u0026quot;","Albus Dumbledore, resplendent in gold robes that outshone the sun, raised his wand.","The string quartet (hidden in the palm grove) began to play. It wasn\u0027t a traditional march; it was a soft, ethereal melody that sounded like wind chimes and magic.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Moon Arrives\u003c/strong\u003e","At the top of the sand aisle, the first bride appeared.","Luna Lovegood walked barefoot on the sand. Her dress of shifting organza caught the sunlight, turning from pale yellow to soft blue with every step. She wore the crown of wildflowers in her hair.","Xenophilius Lovegood walked beside her, weeping openly into a yellow silk handkerchief, looking like a very proud, very bright sunflower.","Ron stopped vibrating. He stopped breathing. He just stared.","\u0026quot;She’s shining,\u0026quot; Ron whispered. \u0026quot;She’s actually shining.\u0026quot;","Luna drifted down the aisle. She wasn\u0027t looking at the guests; she was looking at Ron. She smiled—a serene, dreamy smile that anchored him to the earth.","She reached the altar. She kissed her father’s cheek.","She stepped up to Ron. She took his hand.","\u0026quot;Hello, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna said softly. \u0026quot;The Nargles are singing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You look beautiful, Luna,\u0026quot; Ron choked out.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Fire Arrives\u003c/strong\u003e","The music shifted. It became deeper, warmer.","Ginny Weasley stepped onto the aisle.","A collective intake of breath swept through the guests.","The backless white silk gown flowed around her like water. Her red hair was loose, a fiery cascade down her back. She didn\u0027t look like a princess; she looked like a warrior queen who had laid down her sword for a ring.","Arthur Weasley walked her down. He was beaming, his chest puffed out, walking with a bouncy step that threatened to turn into a skip.","Draco Malfoy felt his heart stop.","He watched her come toward him. He saw the fierce joy in her eyes. He saw the way she looked at him—not as a Malfoy, not as a Death Eater, but as \u003cem\u003eher\u003c/em\u003e Draco.","Lucius Malfoy, sitting in the front row, leaned forward on his cane.","\u0026quot;She commands the space,\u0026quot; Lucius murmured to Narcissa. \u0026quot;She has presence.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She has Draco’s heart,\u0026quot; Narcissa whispered back, smiling.","Ginny reached the altar. Arthur hugged her, then turned to Draco. He shook Draco’s hand firmly.","\u0026quot;Take care of her, son,\u0026quot; Arthur said.","\u0026quot;With my life, sir,\u0026quot; Draco promised.","Ginny stepped up beside him. She took his hand. Her grip was strong, grounding him.","\u0026quot;Hi,\u0026quot; she whispered.","\u0026quot;Hi, Red,\u0026quot; Draco breathed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Wait\u003c/strong\u003e","The two couples stood at the altar. The guests turned in their seats, waiting for the final piece of the trio.","Harry stood alone in the center. He looked down the long stretch of white sand.","The music swelled—a soaring, triumphant melody that Harry recognized. It was the song Fawkes used to sing.","At the entrance to the aisle, standing in the shade of the palms, stood Hermione Granger.","She adjusted the blue sapphire lily in her hair. She smoothed the skirt of her ivory chiffon dress.","Beside her, Severus Snape offered his arm. He looked stiff, formidable in his black robes, but his expression was calm.","\u0026quot;Ready, Miss Granger?\u0026quot; Snape asked quietly.","Hermione looked at the beach. She looked at the parents wiping their eyes. She looked at her friends standing under the arch.","And she looked at Harry, waiting for her in the sun.","She took a deep breath, filling her lungs with the salt air.","\u0026quot;It’s happening,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered."]},{"num":137,"origNum":137,"title":"The Guests in the Back Row","wordCount":606,"paragraphs":["The music swelled—a soaring melody that seemed to be carried by the sea breeze itself.","Severus Snape walked with a slow, measured cadence. He did not rush. He escorted Hermione Granger down the aisle of white sand as if he were delivering a precious, volatile potion to its final destination.","The guests turned. Gasps of admiration rippled through the crowd.","Vernon Dursley dabbed his eyes. \u0026quot;She looks expensive,\u0026quot; Vernon whispered to Petunia. \u0026quot;Classy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She looks lovely,\u0026quot; Petunia wept, clutching her handbag.","Harry stood at the altar. His heart was hammering against his ribs in a rhythm that drowned out the waves. He watched Hermione coming toward him—the girl who had corrected his pronunciation in First Year, the girl who had punched Malfoy, the girl who had stayed.","She was radiant. The ivory silk flowed around her, and the blue sapphire lily—his mother’s lily—glinted in her hair like a captured piece of the sky.","Harry felt his vision blur. He blinked, trying to clear the happy tears.","And that was when he saw them.","In the very back row, behind the chairs where the house-elves stood standing on crates to see, the air seemed to shimmer.","It wasn\u0027t a heat haze. It wasn\u0027t a glare from the sun.","Two figures stood there, bathed in a soft, silvery light that was brighter than the Caribbean morning.","Harry stopped breathing. He blinked hard, once, twice.","They didn\u0027t vanish.","A man with untidy black hair and glasses, wearing dress robes that looked suspiciously like the ones from his wedding photos, stood tall. He was grinning—a wide, mischievous, arrogant, wonderful grin.","Beside him stood a woman with dark red hair and eyes that matched Harry’s own. She was glowing with a love so potent Harry could feel it across the sand.","James and Lily Potter.","They weren\u0027t ghosts. They weren\u0027t memories from a stone. They were... present.","James raised a hand. He didn\u0027t speak. He simply nodded—a firm, decisive nod of a father looking at his son and saying, \u003cem\u003eYou did good, kid. You did good.\u003c/em\u003e","Lily raised her hand and gave a small, gentle wave. She mouthed something. Harry couldn\u0027t hear it, but he knew the shape of the words.","\u003cem\u003eWe are so proud.\u003c/em\u003e","The world tilted. The grief that Harry had carried for nineteen years—the hollow space in his chest where they should have been—suddenly filled up.","They hadn\u0027t missed it. They were here.","A sob trapped itself in Harry’s throat. His knees shook. He felt like he was going to collapse under the sheer weight of the moment.","Then, a warm hand touched his.","Harry snapped his eyes back to the altar.","Hermione was there. She had reached him.","Snape had stepped back, taking his seat with a swirl of black robes, leaving Hermione standing in front of Harry, her brown eyes wide with concern.","She saw the look on his face—the shock, the tears, the look of a man seeing ghosts.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, squeezing his hand tight, anchoring him back to the earth. \u0026quot;Harry, are you alright? You look... you’re crying.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at her. He looked back at the last row.","The light was fading, blending back into the sunshine. But the warmth remained.","He looked back at Hermione. At his future.","He took a deep, shuddering breath, wiping the tears from his cheeks with his thumb.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m fine,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his voice thick with emotion. \u0026quot;I\u0027m... I\u0027m perfect.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Then why are you crying?\u0026quot; Hermione asked softly, searching his face.","Harry smiled—a smile that reached his eyes and stayed there.","\u0026quot;It’s just...\u0026quot; Harry choked out, squeezing her hand. \u0026quot;It\u0027s just that \u003cstrong\u003eYOU ARE SO BEAUTIFUL!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot;"]},{"num":138,"origNum":138,"title":"Nargles and Hurricanes","wordCount":941,"paragraphs":["Albus Dumbledore stood under the bamboo arch, his golden robes billowing gently in the trade winds. He raised his hands, and the crowd of wizards, Muggles, and house-elves fell silent.","\u0026quot;We are gathered here,\u0026quot; Dumbledore began, his voice amplified without a wand, resonating with warmth, \u0026quot;on this island of fortune, to witness the binding of souls. We have built floors. We have raced with lemons. We have survived the \u0027Voldemort\u0027 cocktail. And now, we celebrate love.\u0026quot;","He twinkled at the front row.","\u0026quot;Vernon, please stop checking your watch. We are on schedule.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley lowered his wrist, looking caught. \u0026quot;Just ensuring efficiency, Headmaster.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;First,\u0026quot; Dumbledore announced. \u0026quot;Ronald Bilius Weasley and Luna Elizabeth Lovegood.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Moon and the King\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron and Luna stepped forward. They held hands loosely. Ron looked terrified but happy; Luna looked like she was floating an inch above the sand.","\u0026quot;Ronald,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled. \u0026quot;Your vows.\u0026quot;","Ron cleared his throat. He pulled a crumpled piece of parchment from his pocket. He looked at it. He looked at Luna. He stuffed the parchment back in his pocket.","\u0026quot;I wrote stuff down,\u0026quot; Ron said, his voice shaking slightly. \u0026quot;About stars and stuff. But... it didn\u0027t sound like me.\u0026quot;","He took a deep breath. He looked into Luna’s large, silvery eyes.","\u0026quot;Luna. You’re... mental. Properly bonkers.\u0026quot;","A ripple of laughter went through the crowd. Xenophilius Lovegood nodded vigorously, taking it as a compliment.","\u0026quot;But,\u0026quot; Ron continued, squeezing her hand. \u0026quot;You’re the best kind of mental. Before I met you, I worried about everything. I worried about being poor. I worried about Harry. I worried about spiders. But when I’m with you... the world just seems... quieter. Happier.\u0026quot;","Ron’s ears turned pink.","\u0026quot;I promise to listen to you about the Nargles, even if I can\u0027t see them. I promise to protect you from the world, even though you don\u0027t really need it. And I promise to share my food with you. Even the bacon. Especially the bacon.\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a wet sob in the background.","Luna beamed. She didn\u0027t need a parchment.","\u0026quot;Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna said, her voice dreamy and clear. \u0026quot;You are very warm. You are like a fresh loaf of bread from the oven. You ground me. When I float away, you hold the string.\u0026quot;","She reached up and touched his face.","\u0026quot;I promise to help you find your keys. I promise to paint your life in colors you haven\u0027t seen yet. And I promise to love you, even when you are being a \u0027git\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do,\u0026quot; Ron whispered.","\u0026quot;I do,\u0026quot; Luna hummed.","\u0026quot;Then by the power vested in me,\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared, \u0026quot;I pronounce you... delightfully odd. You may kiss!\u0026quot;","Ron leaned down. It wasn\u0027t a passionate Hollywood kiss; it was sweet, clumsy, and full of joy.","The crowd cheered. Xenophilius blew his nose into his yellow handkerchief with a sound like a trumpet.","\u0026quot;Beautiful!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley shouted. \u0026quot;They fit together like a plug and a socket!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Fire and the Ice\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;And now,\u0026quot; Dumbledore announced, as Ron and Luna stepped back, \u0026quot;The Union of the Houses. Draco Lucius Malfoy and Ginevra Molly Weasley.\u0026quot;","Draco and Ginny stepped into the center. The contrast was striking—Draco in his cool grey, Ginny in her blazing white.","They didn\u0027t look nervous. They looked intense.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; Dumbledore nodded.","Draco looked at Ginny. He didn\u0027t pull out a note. He spoke from memory, his voice low and serious.","\u0026quot;Ginny. I was raised to hate you. I was raised to think I was better than you.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy flinched in the front row, staring at his shoes. Narcissa placed a hand on his arm.","\u0026quot;I was an idiot,\u0026quot; Draco continued. \u0026quot;I was cold. I was hollow. I was a coward living in a manor full of ghosts.\u0026quot;","He stepped closer, his grey eyes locking onto her brown ones.","\u0026quot;Then you crashed into me. You yelled at me. You challenged me. You set fire to my world, Red. And I never want to put it out.\u0026quot;","Draco took a shaky breath.","\u0026quot;I promise to stand by you. I promise to be the man you saw when no one else did. I promise to buy you the best broomsticks, fly with you into the storm, and never, ever let you be bored. I am yours. Completely.\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley let out a wail that startled a seagull. \u0026quot;Oh, Arthur! He’s a poet!\u0026quot;","Ginny grinned. It was a fierce, dangerous grin.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; she said. \u0026quot;You are an arrogant, high-maintenance, dramatic ferret.\u0026quot;","Draco smirked. \u0026quot;Guilty.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But,\u0026quot; Ginny’s voice softened. \u0026quot;You are also brave. You saved Harry. You saved us. You fought your own family to stand with me.\u0026quot;","She grabbed his lapels, pulling him slightly closer.","\u0026quot;I promise to keep your ego in check. I promise to defend you when you’re being stupid. I promise to love you with everything I have. We are a hurricane, Draco. Let’s tear the roof off.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do,\u0026quot; Draco breathed.","\u0026quot;I do,\u0026quot; Ginny said firmly.","\u0026quot;Then,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed, \u0026quot;I pronounce you... a force of nature. You may kiss!\u0026quot;","They didn\u0027t wait. Draco grabbed her waist, Ginny grabbed his neck, and they kissed with the same intensity that had traumatized the Hogwarts corridors.","\u0026quot;GET A ROOM!\u0026quot; Ron shouted from the sidelines, though he was grinning.","\u0026quot;THEY HAVE A ROOM!\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley roared back happily. \u0026quot;IT HAS A BALCONY! EFFICIENCY!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy dabbed his eyes with a silk square. \u0026quot;He has the Malfoy eloquence,\u0026quot; Lucius sniffed. \u0026quot;And she has... volume. It will be a formidable alliance.\u0026quot;","As the couple broke apart, breathless and beaming, Dumbledore turned his eyes to the final pair.","\u0026quot;And finally,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly. \u0026quot;The Boy Who Lived... and the Brightest Witch of Her Age.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":139,"origNum":139,"title":"The Blessing of the Evans Sisters","wordCount":1023,"paragraphs":["The sun was directly overhead now, a halo of brilliance that seemed to center on the bamboo archway.","Harry Potter and Hermione Granger stood facing each other. The sapphire lily clip in Hermione’s hair caught the light, casting small blue reflections onto Harry’s face.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly. \u0026quot;Your vows.\u0026quot;","Harry took Hermione’s hands. They were shaking. He looked at her—really looked at her—and saw the girl on the train, the girl in the library, the girl in the tent, and the woman standing before him.","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry began, his voice thick but steady. \u0026quot;I grew up in a cupboard. I grew up thinking I was alone. But then I met you.\u0026quot;","He squeezed her hands.","\u0026quot;You taught me magic. You taught me logic. But mostly, you taught me that family isn\u0027t about blood. It’s about who stays. And you always stayed. When the world turned on me, you stayed. When Ron left, you stayed. When I walked to my death, you were the last voice I heard.\u0026quot;","A tear tracked down Hermione’s cheek.","\u0026quot;I promise to listen to you,\u0026quot; Harry vowed. \u0026quot;I promise to be the home you deserve. I promise to never go anywhere without you again. You are my best friend. You are my heart.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione?\u0026quot; Dumbledore prompted gently.","Hermione took a shuddering breath. She looked into Harry’s green eyes.","\u0026quot;Harry. You are the most infuriating, reckless, noble person I have ever met.\u0026quot;","A wet laugh rippled through the front row.","\u0026quot;You carry the weight of the world on your shoulders,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;But you don\u0027t have to carry it alone anymore. I promise to carry it with you. I promise to nag you about your safety. I promise to read the books you won\u0027t read.\u0026quot;","She smiled through her tears.","\u0026quot;I love you, Harry Potter. Always.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I pronounce you,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, his own eyes glistening, \u0026quot;bonded for life. You may—\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Light\u003c/strong\u003e","Dumbledore didn\u0027t finish the sentence.","The sunlight above the altar shifted. It didn\u0027t dim; it intensified. It coalesced.","A beam of pure, shimmering gold descended from the sky, bypassing the bamboo roof, bathing Harry and Hermione in a warmth that felt like a physical embrace.","The crowd gasped. Vernon Dursley dropped his stopwatch.","The light swirled and formed two distinct shapes hovering just above the altar.","They were translucent, made of starlight and memory, but they were as real as the sand beneath their feet.","James Potter, tall and messy-haired, stood with his arm around Lily Potter.","They weren\u0027t looking at the crowd. They were looking at the couple.","Lily was beaming, her hand pressed to her heart. James was nodding, a look of fierce, overwhelming pride on his face.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sisters\u003c/strong\u003e","In the front row, Petunia Dursley let out a sound that tore through the silence—a sharp, ragged intake of breath.","\u0026quot;Lily?\u0026quot; Petunia whispered.","The spirit of Lily Potter turned. She looked down at the front row. She looked at the sister she had left behind, the sister who had been jealous, bitter, and angry.","But Lily didn\u0027t see the bitterness. She saw the woman who had taken in a baby on a cold November night. She saw the woman who had kept the blood wards alive for seventeen years.","Lily smiled at Petunia. She mouthed two words, clear as day.","\u003cem\u003eThank you.\u003c/em\u003e","Petunia broke. She collapsed into Vernon’s chest, sobbing uncontrollably, years of guilt and grief washing away in the Caribbean sun. Vernon held her tight, staring up at the sister-in-law he had feared, nodding his respect.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Prince’s Peace\u003c/strong\u003e","Lily’s gaze shifted. She looked past the Weasleys. She looked past the students.","She found the man in black standing in the second row.","Severus Snape stood frozen. His face was pale, his black eyes wide with shock. He had spent half a life seeking redemption for her death.","Lily looked at him. She didn\u0027t look angry. She didn\u0027t look sad.","She reached out a hand toward him. It was a gesture of peace. Of forgiveness. Of letting go.","Snape staggered back a step, clutching the back of McGonagall’s chair. His mask crumbled. The sneer, the bitterness, the hardness—it all melted away, leaving just a man who had finally been absolved.","He lowered his head, a single, sharp nod of gratitude.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Marauders Reunited\u003c/strong\u003e","Beside Snape, Sirius Black and Remus Lupin were clutching each other.","James Potter looked at them. He grinned—that old, arrogant, brotherly grin that said, \u003cem\u003eWe managed it, didn\u0027t we?\u003c/em\u003e","He gave them a thumbs-up.","\u0026quot;Prongs,\u0026quot; Sirius choked out, tears streaming down his face. \u0026quot;You beautiful idiot.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We got him there, James,\u0026quot; Remus wept. \u0026quot;We got him there.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Collapse\u003c/strong\u003e","Finally, the spirits turned back to Harry.","Harry stood at the altar, paralyzed. He looked up at his parents. He saw them blessing him. He saw them happy. He saw them together.","The wall he had built to hold it all in—the war, the deaths, the pressure, the leadership—shattered.","\u0026quot;Mum,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;Dad.\u0026quot;","James nodded. Lily blew a kiss.","And then, as gently as they had arrived, they faded into the sunlight, leaving only the warmth of their blessing behind.","Harry’s legs gave out.","The emotion was too much. The sheer relief, the joy, the grief—it hit him like a physical blow.","His knees buckled. He started to fall backward into the sand.","He didn\u0027t hit the ground.","Two pairs of arms caught him instantly.","On his right, Ron Weasley grabbed him under the armpit, hauling him up.","On his left, Draco Malfoy caught his shoulder, steadying him with a grip of steel.","Harry hung there for a second, suspended between his first friend and his oldest enemy, his head hanging, sobbing into his chest.","\u0026quot;We got you, mate,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, holding him tight. \u0026quot;We got you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Stand up, Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said softly, his voice thick with emotion. \u0026quot;You’re not doing this alone. Never again.\u0026quot;","Hermione stepped forward, wrapping her arms around his waist, burying her face in his chest.","Harry looked up. He saw Ron. He saw Draco. He saw Hermione.","He stood up. He wiped his eyes. He took a breath.","He was supported. He was loved. He was home."]},{"num":140,"origNum":140,"title":"The Kiss of Light","wordCount":928,"paragraphs":["Harry stood upright, his hands trembling slightly as he held Hermione’s waist. The warmth of his parents\u0027 spirits still lingered on his skin, a phantom hug that fortified his soul.","He looked at Dumbledore. The Headmaster wiped a single, silver tear from his cheek and smiled—a smile that held a century of pride.","\u0026quot;I believe,\u0026quot; Dumbledore whispered, his voice thick, \u0026quot;that no further words are necessary. Harry... you may kiss your bride.\u0026quot;","Harry looked down at Hermione. Her eyes were swimming with tears, reflecting the Caribbean sky and the ghost of the gold light that had just vanished.","\u0026quot;Finally,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","He leaned down. Hermione rose on her tiptoes.","Their lips met.","It wasn\u0027t just a kiss. It was the sealing of a pact made in a troll-wrecked bathroom, forged in a time-loop, and solidified in a tent in the Forest of Dean.","And as they kissed, the magic of the island—fueled by the lingering presence of James and Lily, the ancient wards of the earth, and the sheer power of the gathered wizards—reacted.","A pulse of brilliant, white light erupted from the altar.","It didn\u0027t blind; it illuminated. It swept across the beach, washing over the guests, turning the sand to diamond dust and the ocean to liquid sapphire. It raced up the cliffside, lighting up the villa windows, and shot into the sky, chasing away the last wisps of clouds.","For a heartbeat, the entire island glowed like a star.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aunt’s Grief\u003c/strong\u003e","When the light faded, the silence broke.","In the front row, Petunia Dursley collapsed.","It wasn\u0027t a faint; it was a surrender. She fell into her chair, burying her face in her hands, her shoulders shaking with violent, racking sobs.","\u0026quot;She saw me,\u0026quot; Petunia wept, her voice muffled by her palms. \u0026quot;Vernon... she saw me. She smiled.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley, the man who had spent twenty years fearing magic, wrapped his massive arms around his wife. He didn\u0027t look at the wizards with suspicion. He looked at the altar with awe.","\u0026quot;She did, Petunia,\u0026quot; Vernon choked out, tears streaming into his mustache. \u0026quot;She thanked you. We did right by him. We did right.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I missed her,\u0026quot; Petunia wailed, the bitterness of decades dissolving into pure, agonizing grief. \u0026quot;I missed my sister.\u0026quot;","Dudley leaned over, putting a heavy hand on his mother’s back. \u0026quot;She knows, Mum. She knows.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Marauders’ Tears\u003c/strong\u003e","Sirius Black was not okay.","He had slumped onto the sand next to his chair, his legs unable to support him. He was clutching Remus Lupin’s robes like a drowning man.","\u0026quot;Did you see him, Moony?\u0026quot; Sirius gasped, his face wet and red. \u0026quot;He looked... he looked so happy. He gave me the thumbs up. The arrogant toe-rag gave me the thumbs up.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s proud, Padfoot,\u0026quot; Remus wept, tears tracking through the scars on his face. He held Sirius upright, though he was shaking just as hard. \u0026quot;He saw Harry. He saw the man he became.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I thought I failed him,\u0026quot; Sirius sobbed, hitting the sand with his fist. \u0026quot;I thought I failed them both.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You didn\u0027t,\u0026quot; Remus whispered, pulling his brother-in-arms into a hug. \u0026quot;Look at him, Sirius. Look at Harry. We didn\u0027t fail.\u0026quot;","Nymphadora Tonks, her hair a soft, sympathetic grey, wrapped her arms around both of them, resting her chin on Remus’s shoulder, crying silently for the family she had only known through stories.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Faculty’s Heart\u003c/strong\u003e","Rubeus Hagrid was making a sound like a wounded foghorn.","\u0026quot;BWA-HUH-HUH!\u0026quot;","He was blowing his nose into a handkerchief the size of a mainsail.","\u0026quot;I remember bringin\u0027 him to the doorstep,\u0026quot; Hagrid howled to the sky. \u0026quot;He was so small. Fits in me hand. And now... look at \u0027im. Married. With Lily and James watchin\u0027.\u0026quot;","Professor McGonagall had abandoned all pretense of sternness. She had removed her spectacles and was pressing a tartan handkerchief to her eyes, her shoulders trembling.","\u0026quot;He has her eyes,\u0026quot; Minerva whispered brokenly. \u0026quot;I always said it. But seeing them... seeing them together...\u0026quot;","She reached out and blindly gripped Dumbledore’s hand.","Albus Dumbledore, the man who had orchestrated the war, the death, and the victory, sat in his chair. He looked old. He looked tired. But he looked happier than anyone had ever seen him.","\u0026quot;Love,\u0026quot; Dumbledore murmured, squeezing Minerva’s hand. \u0026quot;It is the only magic that matters. We were right, Minerva. In the end... love won.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Potions Master\u003c/strong\u003e","And then, there was Severus Snape.","He stood apart from the others, near the edge of the bamboo arch. He was rigid. His hands were clenched at his sides so tightly that his fingernails bit into his palms.","He was not crying. He was Occluding.","He was building walls of stone and ice inside his mind, trying to contain the tsunami of emotion that threatened to shatter him.","\u003cem\u003eShe reached out,\u003c/em\u003e his mind whispered. \u003cem\u003eShe forgave.\u003c/em\u003e","He stared at Harry and Hermione kissing. He saw the happiness. He saw the lack of fear.","He felt a burning in his throat that had nothing to do with firewhisky. His chest ached with a physical pain—the breaking of a guilt he had carried since he was twenty-one years old.","He took a shallow breath. His mask slipped.","A single muscle jumped in his jaw. His eyes, black and bottomless, glistened.","He didn\u0027t sob. He didn\u0027t collapse.","But he slowly, deliberately, lowered his head in a bow toward the empty space where the spirits had hovered.","\u0026quot;Always,\u0026quot; Snape whispered to the air.","And for the first time in his life, the word didn\u0027t feel like a curse. It felt like a promise kept."]},{"num":141,"origNum":141,"title":"The Prince’s Surrender","wordCount":1045,"paragraphs":["The tears on the beach dried quickly in the tropical warmth, replaced by the infectious rhythm of celebration.","Vernon Dursley, having recovered from his emotional breakdown, was now directing the house-elves to open the champagne.","\u0026quot;Cork management!\u0026quot; Vernon barked, wiping his eyes. \u0026quot;Trajectory away from the guests! We don\u0027t need a black eye on the wedding photos!\u0026quot;","The string quartet switched from sentimental ballads to upbeat waltzes. The dance floor—the one they had snapped together piece by piece—filled up instantly.","Draco spun Ginny around, her white dress flaring like a cloud. Ron was trying to teach Luna a dance that looked suspiciously like a goal-keeper defending hoops. Vernon was waltzing with Petunia, counting the steps out loud (\u0026quot;One-two-three, efficiency-two-three\u0026quot;).","But at the edge of the joy, in the shadow of a palm tree near the bar, there was a void.","Severus Snape sat on a high stool. He was not looking at the party. He was looking at the amber liquid in his glass, his hand shaking so slightly it created ripples in the drink.","He felt hollowed out. Seeing Lily... seeing her smile... it had broken the dam he had built around his heart for seventeen years, but the wreckage was still there.","\u0026quot;Go away,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, sensing movement to his left.","\u0026quot;Not a chance, Snivellus,\u0026quot; a rough voice replied.","Snape stiffened. He didn\u0027t turn. \u0026quot;I am not in the mood for your childish taunts, Black. Go dance with your werewolf.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s right here,\u0026quot; Remus Lupin said softly, stepping up to Snape’s other side.","Snape looked up. Sirius Black and Remus Lupin stood flanking him. They weren\u0027t holding drinks. They weren\u0027t smiling. They looked... tired. And sad. And determined.","\u0026quot;What do you want?\u0026quot; Snape hissed, gripping his glass. \u0026quot;Do you want a confession? Do you want to gloat? \u0027We won, Snape lost\u0027? Get it over with.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We saw her,\u0026quot; Sirius said. His voice wasn\u0027t mocking. It was thick with unshed tears.","Snape flinched. \u0026quot;Do not speak of her.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She looked at you, Severus,\u0026quot; Remus said gently, using his first name. \u0026quot;She reached out to you. She didn\u0027t look angry. She looked... at peace.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She forgave you,\u0026quot; Sirius said, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;We saw it. She forgave you for the mudblood comment. She forgave you for the prophecy. She forgave you for everything.\u0026quot;","Snape squeezed his eyes shut. \u0026quot;Stop it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Why?\u0026quot; Sirius demanded, stepping closer. \u0026quot;Why should we stop? Because it hurts? Good. It should hurt. But you have to let it go.\u0026quot;","Sirius placed a hand on the bar, leaning in.","\u0026quot;James gave me the thumbs up,\u0026quot; Sirius whispered. \u0026quot;He forgave me for convincing them to switch Secret Keepers. He forgave me for failing him.\u0026quot;","Sirius looked at Snape, his grey eyes burning.","\u0026quot;If James Potter can forgive me... and Lily Potter can forgive you... then who the hell are we to keep this hate alive?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I cannot,\u0026quot; Snape choked out, his voice barely audible. \u0026quot;It is all I have.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, it isn\u0027t,\u0026quot; Remus said firmly. \u0026quot;You have a life, Severus. You saved Harry. You saved the school. You saved Draco.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You\u0027re not a Death Eater anymore,\u0026quot; Sirius said roughly. \u0026quot;You\u0027re just a miserable git. But you\u0027re \u003cem\u003eour\u003c/em\u003e miserable git.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at Sirius. He looked at the man who had tormented him in school, the man he had wanted kissed by Dementors.","He saw the grief in Sirius’s eyes that mirrored his own.","The wall crumbled.","It didn\u0027t crack; it disintegrated. The years of Occlumency, the years of spying, the years of holding his breath—it all rushed out of him in a single, agonizing gasp.","Snape dropped his glass. It shattered on the floor.","He let out a sob—a raw, ugly sound that had been trapped in his throat since Halloween 1981.","\u0026quot;I tried,\u0026quot; Snape wept, his shoulders shaking violently. \u0026quot;I tried to save her.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We know,\u0026quot; Sirius whispered.","Snape stumbled off the stool. He couldn\u0027t stand. He started to fall.","But he didn\u0027t hit the sand.","Sirius grabbed him. Remus grabbed him.","And then, Severus Snape did the impossible. He didn\u0027t push them away.","He grabbed the lapels of Sirius’s jacket. He grabbed Remus’s shoulder. And he pulled them in.","He buried his face in Sirius Black’s shoulder and broke down completely, sobbing like a child, holding onto the Marauders as if they were the only things keeping him from drowning.","Sirius froze for a second, shock written all over his face. Then, his face crumpled. He wrapped his arms around Snape, holding the shaking man tight.","\u0026quot;I’ve got you,\u0026quot; Sirius choked out. \u0026quot;We’ve got you.\u0026quot;","Remus wrapped his arms around both of them, resting his head on Snape’s shaking back, tears streaming down his own face.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Silence on the Floor\u003c/strong\u003e","On the dance floor, the music didn\u0027t stop because the band stopped playing. It stopped because the dancers stopped moving.","One by one, the guests froze.","Harry stopped dancing with Hermione. Draco stopped spinning Ginny. Vernon stopped counting steps.","They turned toward the bar.","They saw the impossible.","They saw the three enemies—the Werewolf, the Convict, and the Spy—locked in a desperate, three-way embrace, holding each other up, crying into each other\u0027s shoulders.","It was a tableau of grief and healing so powerful it sucked the air out of the beach.","McGonagall put a hand to her mouth. \u0026quot;Oh, Severus,\u0026quot; she whispered.","Dumbledore took off his glasses and wiped them, his hands shaking.","Draco stared. He had never seen his godfather cry. He had never seen him touch anyone without malice.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s letting go,\u0026quot; Draco whispered.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Son\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter stood in the middle of the dance floor. He watched the men who had shaped his life—his father’s best friends, and his mother’s oldest friend.","He saw the pain. He saw the love.","He felt a pull in his chest so strong it physically moved his feet.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Hermione asked softly.","Harry looked at her. His eyes were wet, but he was smiling.","\u0026quot;I need to go there,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;I need to be with them.\u0026quot;","Hermione nodded, letting go of his hand. She pushed him gently forward.","\u0026quot;Go,\u0026quot; she whispered.","Harry turned. He didn\u0027t walk. He ran.","He sprinted across the sand toward the bar, toward the three men who were finally, after all these years, burying the war."]},{"num":142,"origNum":142,"title":"The Boy and the Spy","wordCount":881,"paragraphs":["Sirius Black and Remus Lupin saw him coming.","They saw Harry sprinting across the sand, his dress robes flying behind him, his face set in a mask of fierce determination.","They looked at each other. They didn\u0027t need to speak. The Marauders stepped back.","They released their grip on Severus Snape, stepping aside to leave the Potions Master standing alone by the bar.","Snape swayed. He looked stripped raw, his chest heaving, his face wet with tears he hadn\u0027t bothered to wipe away. He looked like a man who had just survived a shipwreck.","He raised his head, sensing the movement.","\u0026quot;Potter?\u0026quot; Snape rasped, blinking against the salt and the grief. \u0026quot;Stay ba—\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eTHUD.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry didn\u0027t stop. He didn\u0027t slow down. He collided with Snape.","He wrapped his arms around the man’s waist (Snape was taller, always taller) and buried his face in the black robes that smelled of sea salt, old potions, and spilled firewhisky.","Snape went rigid. He stood like a statue, his arms pinned to his sides.","\u0026quot;Get off me,\u0026quot; Snape hissed, though his voice lacked any venom. It sounded terrified. \u0026quot;Release me, Potter. Do not make a scene.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry said into the robes.","\u0026quot;I said unhand me!\u0026quot; Snape tried to push Harry away. He placed his hands on Harry’s shoulders to shove him back.","But Harry didn\u0027t budge. He held on tighter. He held on with the strength of a Seeker who had caught the Snitch and refused to let go.","\u0026quot;I’m not letting go,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;You tried to make me hate you. It didn\u0027t work.\u0026quot;","Snape’s hands trembled on Harry’s shoulders. He tried to push, but his strength—the strength born of hatred and duty—was gone.","He looked down.","He saw the messy black hair. He saw the glasses.","And then, Harry looked up.","Green eyes. Bright, almond-shaped, brilliant green eyes.","Lily’s eyes.","They weren\u0027t looking at him with James’s arrogance. They weren\u0027t looking at him with fear.","They were looking at him with forgiveness.","Snape’s knees gave out.","He slumped against the bar, sliding down until he was eye-level with Harry. His hands moved from Harry’s shoulders to cup the back of Harry’s neck, his fingers tangling in the hair he had mocked for seven years.","\u0026quot;I was cruel,\u0026quot; Snape choked out, the confession tearing itself from his throat. \u0026quot;I was... a monster to you. Every day. Every lesson.\u0026quot;","He looked into the green eyes, searching for the judgment he felt he deserved.","\u0026quot;I saw him,\u0026quot; Snape wept. \u0026quot;I saw James. I wanted to hate you. I punished you for his sins. I am sorry, Harry. I am so... so sorry.\u0026quot;","It was the first time he had ever used Harry’s first name.","Harry shook his head, tears spilling onto his cheeks.","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;I know you were hurting. But you kept me safe. You watched over me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I failed you,\u0026quot; Snape sobbed.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;You didn\u0027t. You saved me.\u0026quot;","Harry pulled Snape into a hug again, but this time, Snape didn\u0027t resist.","The Potions Master, the spy, the man who had lived in the shadows, collapsed forward. He buried his face in Harry’s shoulder.","He cried. He cried for the boy he had bullied. He cried for the woman he had loved. He cried for the wasted years of bitterness.","And Harry held him up.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Witness\u003c/strong\u003e","The beach was silent. The only sound was the breaking of the waves and the quiet, racking sobs of Severus Snape.","Draco Malfoy stood on the dance floor, his hand gripping Ginny’s. He watched his godfather—the man who had taught him to be cold, to be shielded—breaking apart in the arms of his rival.","\u0026quot;He’s human,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, stunned. \u0026quot;He was human all along.\u0026quot;","Hermione Granger wiped her eyes, leaning against Ron. \u0026quot;He needed this,\u0026quot; she said softly. \u0026quot;He needed Harry to forgive him more than he needed anything.\u0026quot;","McGonagall stood with Dumbledore. She took off her glasses, unable to see through the tears.","\u0026quot;That boy,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered. \u0026quot;He has a heart too big for his body.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is the best of us, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore agreed, watching the scene with a peaceful smile. \u0026quot;He is the best of us all.\u0026quot;","Petunia Dursley watched from the table. She saw the man who had been the strange, greasy boy from Spinner\u0027s End. She saw him weeping on her nephew’s shoulder.","She remembered Lily defending him.","\u0026quot;She was right,\u0026quot; Petunia murmured to Vernon. \u0026quot;She was right about him.\u0026quot;","Sirius and Remus stood just a few feet away, guarding the moment. They didn\u0027t interfere. They just watched, bearing witness to the healing of the final scar of the war.","Snape pulled back slightly. He looked at Harry. He looked exhausted, old, and wrecked.","But his eyes were clear. The darkness was gone.","\u0026quot;Thank you,\u0026quot; Snape whispered.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re welcome, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry smiled. \u0026quot;Now... I think you need a drink. But maybe just water this time.\u0026quot;","Snape let out a wet, shaky laugh. \u0026quot;Water. Yes. That would be... prudent.\u0026quot;","Harry put his arm around Snape’s waist, supporting him. Sirius stepped in on the other side.","Together, the Boy Who Lived and the Marauder walked the Half-Blood Prince away from the bar and toward the chairs, surrounded by the silence of a family that had finally, truly, become whole."]},{"num":143,"origNum":143,"title":"The Waltz of the Half-Blood Prince","wordCount":842,"paragraphs":["The emotional storm had passed, leaving the beach cleansed and the guests exhausted but lighter.","Vernon Dursley, ever the master of ceremonies, clapped his massive hands.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, blowing his nose loudly. \u0026quot;Enough blubbering! We are at a wedding, not a funeral! We have paid for the band until midnight! Efficiency means dancing!\u0026quot;","The string quartet (now augmented by a saxophone player Dudley had found) struck up a lively, mid-tempo waltz.","Harry and Hermione moved back to the center of the floor. Draco took Ginny’s hand. Ron grabbed Luna.","But on the sidelines, Severus Snape did not retreat to the shadows. He did not go to the bar.","He smoothed his black robes. He adjusted his cuffs. He walked up to Minerva McGonagall, who was dabbing her eyes.","Snape extended a hand. He bowed—a stiff, formal, pureblood bow.","\u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice void of mockery. \u0026quot;May I?\u0026quot;","McGonagall stared at the hand. \u0026quot;Severus? You... dance?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am a man of many hidden depths,\u0026quot; Snape drawled. \u0026quot;Do not keep me waiting. The tempo is accelerating.\u0026quot;","McGonagall took his hand.","Snape swept her onto the floor.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Shock\u003c/strong\u003e","The guests stopped moving. The \u0026quot;children\u0026quot; froze mid-step.","Severus Snape was not just dancing. He was \u003cem\u003egliding\u003c/em\u003e.","His movements were precise, geometric, and fluid. He held his frame with the rigidity of a ruler, yet he moved across the sand as if he were made of smoke. He spun McGonagall—who was an excellent dancer herself—with a flourish that sent her tartan robes flying.","\u0026quot;He’s...\u0026quot; Ron whispered, watching Snape execute a perfect turn. \u0026quot;He’s good. Why is he good? It’s unnatural.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s geometry,\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, watching Snape’s feet. \u0026quot;Look at his footwork. It’s mathematical perfection. He’s dancing like he brews—exact measurements of movement.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go, Severus!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered from the sidelines, clapping in time. \u0026quot;Work the glutes!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Rotation\u003c/strong\u003e","The song ended. McGonagall was breathless and flushed.","\u0026quot;You lead well, Severus,\u0026quot; she admitted, fanning herself. \u0026quot;For a bat.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Old habits,\u0026quot; Snape murmured.","Before he could leave the floor, a drift of pale yellow organza appeared at his elbow.","\u0026quot;May I cut in, Professor?\u0026quot; Luna Lovegood asked, looking up at him with dreamy eyes.","Snape looked down at Luna. He didn\u0027t sneer.","\u0026quot;Miss Lovegood,\u0026quot; Snape nodded. \u0026quot;Try not to step on my boots.\u0026quot;","They danced. Luna moved like a leaf in the wind; Snape moved like the wind itself. It was a bizarre, beautiful contrast.","As he spun her, Snape leaned down.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Do not change,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e Snape whispered in her ear. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;The world is full of ordinary dunderheads. Remain... distinct.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","Luna beamed. \u0026quot;The Nargles like your rhythm, sir.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Fire\u003c/strong\u003e","Next came the Hurricane. Ginny Weasley practically tagged Luna out, grabbing Snape’s hand.","\u0026quot;My turn,\u0026quot; Ginny declared. \u0026quot;Let’s see if you can handle a Weasley tempo.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Do not challenge me, Red,\u0026quot; Snape warned, his eyes narrowing.","He spun her so fast her feet left the ground. He dipped her with a dramatic flair that made Draco drop his drink.","\u0026quot;That is my godfather!\u0026quot; Draco yelled. \u0026quot;And my fiancée! This is a conflict of interest!\u0026quot;","Snape pulled Ginny back up. As the music swelled, he leaned close to her ear.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;He is fragile,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e Snape whispered, his voice intense. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Beneath the arrogance, he is glass. Keep him safe, Weasley. He needs your fire more than he knows.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I will,\u0026quot; Ginny promised, her eyes fierce.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Partner\u003c/strong\u003e","Finally, Snape turned. He looked across the floor.","Hermione Granger was standing with Harry. She looked at Snape. She looked terrified but curious.","Snape walked over. He stopped in front of her.","\u0026quot;Mrs. Potter-to-be,\u0026quot; Snape said softly.","Harry let go of her hand. \u0026quot;Go on, Mione. He hasn\u0027t bitten anyone yet.\u0026quot;","Hermione placed her hand in Snape’s.","The music slowed to a gentle, melancholy ballad.","Snape danced with Hermione differently. He wasn\u0027t showy. He wasn\u0027t competitive. He was gentle. He guided her around the floor with a respectful distance, his movements soft.","The crowd watched in silence. The \u0026quot;Insufferable Know-It-All\u0026quot; and the teacher who had tormented her for being smart.","Snape looked over her head at the ocean. Then, he looked down.","He leaned in. He spoke for a long time, his voice a low rumble that only she could hear.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I called you insufferable,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e Snape whispered. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I mocked your intelligence. I punished you for knowing the answers. But you must understand... I did not hate you because you were wrong. I resented you... because you were always right.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","Hermione’s breath hitched.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You have a mind that rivals the founders,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e Snape continued, his voice rough. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Do not let the Ministry dull it. Do not let the bureaucracy silence you. You are the brightest witch of your age, Hermione. And I... I am sorry I never gave you the points you deserved.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","He pulled back.","Hermione was crying again, but she was smiling.","\u0026quot;Ten points to Gryffindor?\u0026quot; she whispered.","Snape’s lip curled into a genuine half-smile.","\u0026quot;Fifty,\u0026quot; Snape corrected.","He bowed to her, released her hand, and walked off the dance floor, leaving a stunned silence and a very happy witch in his wake."]},{"num":144,"origNum":144,"title":"The Gift of the Half-Blood Prince","wordCount":1032,"paragraphs":["The wedding feast was winding down. The tiered cakes—chocolate-treacle-pudding hybrid masterpieces—had been cut and devoured. The champagne flutes had been refilled more times than Lucius Malfoy cared to count (though he was currently counting quite happily).","It was time for the speeches.","Vernon Dursley went first, naturally. He stood up, tapping a spoon against a glass with the rhythm of a pile driver.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, his face flushed with pride and port. \u0026quot;To the happy couples! You have merged assets! You have consolidated families! You have secured the future! May your returns be high and your overheads low!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To low overheads!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley cheered, clinking his glass against Lucius’s.","Lucius stood next. He leaned on his cane, looking at Draco.","\u0026quot;To my son,\u0026quot; Lucius said, his voice surprisingly steady. \u0026quot;Who taught me that sometimes... tradition is just peer pressure from dead people. To Draco and Ginny. The House of Malfoy... approves.\u0026quot;","Sirius and Remus gave a joint toast that was mostly embarrassing stories about Harry’s hair, ending with a tearful salute to James and Lily.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Speaker\u003c/strong\u003e","Then, the room went quiet.","Severus Snape stood up.","He didn\u0027t tap his glass. He didn\u0027t clear his throat. He simply stood, a dark pillar in the candlelight.","He looked at the three couples sitting at the head table.","\u0026quot;I have spent the better part of two decades,\u0026quot; Snape began, his voice low and silky, \u0026quot;attempting to teach you dunderheads the subtle science and exact art of potion-making.\u0026quot;","A ripple of laughter went through the room.","\u0026quot;I have failed,\u0026quot; Snape continued. \u0026quot;Weasley still cannot distinguish between monkshood and wolfsbane. Potter relies on luck. And Malfoy... well, Malfoy at least knows how to chop.\u0026quot;","He paused. His black eyes softened, just a fraction.","\u0026quot;However... it appears you have learned something more important. You have learned survival. You have learned loyalty.\u0026quot;","He looked at Harry.","\u0026quot;You have learned forgiveness.\u0026quot;","Snape reached into his robes. He didn\u0027t pull out a speech. He pulled out his wand.","\u0026quot;I am not a man of sentiment,\u0026quot; Snape stated. \u0026quot;I value privacy. I value silence. And while I tolerate your presence in this villa... you are collectively deafening.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hey!\u0026quot; Ron protested.","\u0026quot;Therefore,\u0026quot; Snape swirled his wand in a wide, complex arc toward the dark end of the beach, away from the main villa. \u0026quot;I have arranged for... distance.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Construction\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cem\u003eRUMBLE.\u003c/em\u003e","The ground shook gently. The sand down the beach began to swirl.","Out of the darkness, shapes began to form. They weren\u0027t illusions; they were transfigurations of matter, pulled from the sand, the stone, and the wood of the island.","Three structures rose from the beach, glowing with fresh magic.","\u003cstrong\u003eCottage One: The Library\u003c/strong\u003e","The first cottage was built of warm, honey-colored stone. It had a wraparound porch and a chimney puffing gentle smoke. But the defining feature was the walls—they were mostly glass.","And through the glass, one could see shelves. Floor-to-ceiling bookshelves, already stocked.","\u0026quot;For Potter and Granger,\u0026quot; Snape announced. \u0026quot;A sanctuary. Where Miss Granger can read without Weasley breathing on her, and Potter can... rest.\u0026quot;","Hermione gasped, her hands flying to her mouth. \u0026quot;It’s beautiful.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eCottage Two: The Rookery\u003c/strong\u003e","The second cottage was... eccentric. It was round, painted in soft hues of orange and yellow. It had a thatched roof that looked like a bird\u0027s nest and a garden that was already blooming with strange, luminescent flowers. There was a telescope mounted on the roof.","\u0026quot;For Weasley and Lovegood,\u0026quot; Snape drawled. \u0026quot;A... habitat. It is Nargle-proofed. And the kitchen is reinforced for heavy usage.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a giant mushroom!\u0026quot; Ron cheered. \u0026quot;I love it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s perfect,\u0026quot; Luna hummed. \u0026quot;It has curved walls. The energy flows.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eCottage Three: The Fortress\u003c/strong\u003e","The third cottage was sleek. It was made of white marble and dark mahogany. It had a balcony that jutted out over the ocean and a private, walled courtyard. It looked expensive, private, and very Slytherin.","\u0026quot;For Malfoy and Weasley,\u0026quot; Snape nodded to Draco. \u0026quot;Soundproofed. Heavily. So you may conduct your... \u0027negotiations\u0027... without disturbing the peace.\u0026quot;","Ginny turned bright red. Draco smirked.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The three couples stared at the cottages. They weren\u0027t just houses; they were homes. Tailored, thoughtful, and permanent.","\u0026quot;You... you built us houses?\u0026quot; Harry asked, standing up and looking at Snape. \u0026quot;You?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I transfigured them,\u0026quot; Snape corrected, looking bored. \u0026quot;It was a simple matter of molecular rearrangement. Sand is silica; silica becomes glass and stone. It is elementary chemistry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Elementary chemistry,\u0026quot; Harry repeated, grinning. \u0026quot;Right.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a wedding gift,\u0026quot; Snape said stiffly. \u0026quot;Do not read into it. I simply require quiet in the main villa so I can drink my coffee in peace.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered, wiping her eyes again. \u0026quot;You soft old bat.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am not soft,\u0026quot; Snape snapped. \u0026quot;I am practical.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Hug (Again)\u003c/strong\u003e","It was Ron who moved first.","\u0026quot;That’s it,\u0026quot; Ron announced. \u0026quot;He gave me a kitchen. I’m hugging him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Weasley, do not—\u0026quot; Snape warned, raising a hand.","Too late. Ron launched himself at Snape. \u0026quot;THANK YOU, SEVERUS!\u0026quot;","Harry and Draco joined in. The three grooms—the Gryffindor, the Slytherin, and the Chosen One—surrounded the Potions Master in a group hug.","Snape stood there, stiff as a board, surrounded by linen suits and gratitude.","\u0026quot;Get off,\u0026quot; Snape ordered, though he didn\u0027t push them away. \u0026quot;You are wrinkling my robes. I will deduct points. I will deduct houses.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You can\u0027t deduct a house you just gave us!\u0026quot; Harry laughed.","\u0026quot;Watch me,\u0026quot; Snape muttered.","Lucius Malfoy leaned over to Vernon Dursley.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;Did... did Severus just give away real estate? Oceanfront real estate?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He did, Lucius,\u0026quot; Vernon nodded, looking at the cottages with a critical eye. \u0026quot;Solid foundations. Good roofing. The man knows his structural engineering. I might offer him a job.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Cottages!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley cheered, raising his glass.","\u0026quot;To the Cottages!\u0026quot; the room roared.","Snape finally extricated himself from the boys. He smoothed his robes. He looked at Harry. He looked at the house he had built for Lily’s son.","\u0026quot;Go,\u0026quot; Snape said softly. \u0026quot;Go home.\u0026quot;","And as the three couples ran down the beach toward their new lives, leaving footprints in the sand, Severus Snape picked up his glass of wine, sat down, and finally, truly, smiled."]},{"num":145,"origNum":145,"title":"The Supersonic Secret","wordCount":879,"paragraphs":["The sun rose over Isla de la Fortuna, but the A380 did not rise with it.","The massive white bird, which had been parked on the runway like a dormant dragon, was gone. It had departed in the dead of night, summoned back to London for an urgent corporate merger involving oil tycoons.","Vernon Dursley stood on the terrace, a satellite phone pressed to his ear. His face was a thundercloud.","\u0026quot;Breach of contract, Henderson!\u0026quot; Vernon roared at the horizon. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t care if the Sheikh needs to fly his falcons to Dubai! I have a wedding party stranded in the tropics! I have assets on the ground!\u0026quot;","He listened. His mustache twitched. His eyes narrowed.","\u0026quot;A replacement?\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;It had better be good. It had better be... significant.\u0026quot;","He listened again.","Slowly, the rage drained from Vernon’s face. His jaw slackened. A glint appeared in his eye—the glint of a man who had just been offered the Crown Jewels for the price of a drilled hole.","\u0026quot;Truly?\u0026quot; Vernon whispered. \u0026quot;Operational? With the afterburners?\u0026quot;","He listened one last time. Then, a smile spread across his face. It wasn\u0027t his usual shark-like business grin. It was a look of pure, boyish glee.","\u0026quot;Henderson,\u0026quot; Vernon said, his voice trembling with excitement. \u0026quot;You are forgiven. Send it. Send the bird.\u0026quot;","He snapped the phone shut. He looked at the empty runway.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Vernon chuckled to himself. \u0026quot;Lucius is going to lose his mind. Speed. Pure speed.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Brunch of Champions\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon turned back to the villa. \u0026quot;Dobby! Crisis averted! Deploy the breakfast! We are staying one more day! Make it celebratory!\u0026quot;","The house-elves, sensing the mood, pivoted from \u0026quot;Recovery Food\u0026quot; to \u0026quot;Honeymoon Brunch.\u0026quot;","The tables on the terrace were laden with a spread that screamed luxury.","There were towers of pastries—croissants so flaky they shattered when touched, Danishes glistening with apricot glaze, and \u003cem\u003ePain au Chocolat\u003c/em\u003e that smelled of melted dark chocolate.","There were silver warming trays of Eggs Florentine, the hollandaise sauce rich and lemony.","There were boards of smoked salmon, capers, and cream cheese.","There were carafes of iced coffee, freshly squeezed juices in every color of the rainbow, and—because it was a celebration—more champagne.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Emergence\u003c/strong\u003e","The parents and professors were already seated, enjoying the coffee and the view.","\u0026quot;One more day?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley asked, buttering a croissant. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t mind. I haven\u0027t finished inspecting the air conditioning vents.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s lovely,\u0026quot; Molly agreed. \u0026quot;I can get the recipe for the coconut cake.\u0026quot;","Then, the couples arrived.","They did not walk from the villa. They emerged from their respective cottages down the beach path.","Harry and Hermione came first.","They were holding hands. Harry’s hair was messier than usual (if that was possible), and his shirt was buttoned wrong. Hermione was wearing one of Harry’s shirts over her swimsuit.","They walked with a slow, synchronized lazy gait. They looked exhausted, but they were glowing with a happiness so bright it rivaled the sun.","\u0026quot;Morning,\u0026quot; Harry mumbled, shielding his eyes.","Next came Ron and Luna.","Ron looked dazed. He walked into a chair, apologized to it, and sat down. He had a flower chain around his neck.","\u0026quot;The Nargles were very active last night,\u0026quot; Luna hummed, drifting to her seat. \u0026quot;Very loud.\u0026quot;","Ron turned bright red and buried his face in a melon slice.","Finally, Draco and Ginny appeared from the \u0026quot;Fortress.\u0026quot;","Draco was wearing sunglasses and a silk robe. Ginny was wearing Draco’s linen shirt.","They looked... smug.","\u0026quot;Coffee,\u0026quot; Draco demanded, snapping his fingers. \u0026quot;Black. Strong. I require caffeine to function.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Rough night?\u0026quot; Sirius Black teased, winking at Ginny.","\u0026quot;Eventful,\u0026quot; Ginny smirked, stealing a piece of bacon from Draco’s plate. \u0026quot;Very eventful.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Inquisition\u003c/strong\u003e","As the caffeine kicked in and the pastries disappeared, the reality of their situation dawned on Hermione.","\u0026quot;Wait,\u0026quot; she said, looking at the empty sky. \u0026quot;Where’s the plane? The A380 is gone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Recalled,\u0026quot; Vernon announced calmly, sipping his tea. \u0026quot;Logistical hiccup. Henderson needed the capacity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So we\u0027re stranded?\u0026quot; Lucius asked, looking at his empty glass. \u0026quot;On an island? With no wine shipments?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The cellar is full, Lucius,\u0026quot; Draco reassured him.","\u0026quot;We are not stranded,\u0026quot; Vernon corrected. \u0026quot;Transport has been arranged. A replacement vessel is inbound. It arrives tomorrow morning at 0900 hours.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What kind of vessel?\u0026quot; Arthur asked eagerly. \u0026quot;A boat? A hovercraft?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;An aircraft, Arthur,\u0026quot; Vernon said.","\u0026quot;Is it another double-decker?\u0026quot; Ron asked. \u0026quot;I liked the stairs.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Vernon said, a mysterious smile playing on his lips. \u0026quot;It is smaller. Much smaller. It seats only one hundred.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Smaller?\u0026quot; Malfoy scoffed. \u0026quot;A downgrade? Vernon, I do not fly in \u0027regional\u0027 jets. My legs require room.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is not a downgrade, Lucius,\u0026quot; Vernon said softly. \u0026quot;It is an upgrade in... velocity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Velocity?\u0026quot; Harry asked. \u0026quot;Is it fast?\u0026quot;","Vernon leaned back in his chair. He looked at the sky. He looked at the wizards.","\u0026quot;Let’s just say,\u0026quot; Vernon murmured, \u0026quot;that we will arrive in London \u003cem\u003ebefore\u003c/em\u003e we leave the Caribbean. Theoretically speaking.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Time travel?\u0026quot; Hermione gasped. \u0026quot;Without a Time-Turner?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Physics, Hermione,\u0026quot; Vernon tapped his nose. \u0026quot;Supersonic physics. Now, eat up! Enjoy the beach! Tomorrow... we break the barrier!\u0026quot;","The group stared at him. They didn\u0027t know what \u0026quot;Supersonic\u0026quot; meant, but the glint in Vernon Dursley’s eye suggested it was going to be loud, fast, and entirely Dursley-approved."]},{"num":146,"origNum":146,"title":"The Tides of Change","wordCount":838,"paragraphs":["The midday sun turned the Caribbean Sea into a sheet of undulating turquoise glass. On the Lower Terrace, the lunch tables were set, shaded by white umbrellas fluttering in the breeze.","The parents, professors, and Marauders were seated, sipping iced tea and waiting.","\u0026quot;Where are they?\u0026quot; Molly Weasley fretted, shading her eyes. \u0026quot;They’ve been in the water for hours. They’ll turn into prunes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are newlyweds, Molly,\u0026quot; Sirius Black grinned, kicking his feet up on an empty chair. \u0026quot;Let them swim. It’s better than them hiding in the cottages.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Quiet,\u0026quot; Snape murmured, looking up from a book. \u0026quot;They are returning.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Emergence\u003c/strong\u003e","It was a scene straight out of a movie, but without the slow-motion effects.","The six young adults emerged from the surf. They weren\u0027t fighting a war. They weren\u0027t running from Snatchers. They were just swimming.","Draco and Ginny came out first.","Ginny Weasley, wearing a emerald green bikini that matched her team colors, walked with the powerful, athletic stride of a professional Chaser. She looked strong, fierce, and utterly confident.","Draco walked beside her, wearing expensive black swim trunks. He was pale, sleek, and for the first time in his life, he didn\u0027t look like he was carrying the weight of the Malfoy name on his shoulders. He looked light.","\u0026quot;Look at him,\u0026quot; Narcissa whispered, lowering her glass. \u0026quot;He stands differently. He stands... tall.\u0026quot;","Next came Ron and Luna.","Ron was towering, his broad chest and shoulders (built by years of Quidditch and recent manual labor) filling out the frame. He lifted Luna over a small wave, setting her down gently.","Luna, wearing a swimsuit with a pattern of sunflowers, was laughing, shaking water from her hair like a happy Niffler.","And finally, Harry and Hermione.","Harry walked out of the water, water streaming down his chest, highlighting the scars that crisscrossed his skin—the basilisk bite, the knife wound from the graveyard, the locket burn.","But he didn\u0027t hide them. He walked with his arm around Hermione’s waist.","Hermione, in a simple navy swimsuit, looked radiant. The anxiety that usually furrowed her brow was gone, washed away by the salt water. She looked relaxed, happy, and beautiful.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The terrace went silent.","It wasn\u0027t just that they looked good. It was what they represented.","Molly Weasley stared at her youngest son and daughter. She remembered scrubbing dirt off Ron’s nose. She remembered Ginny begging to fly a broom.","Now, they were adults. Powerful, married, beautiful adults.","\u0026quot;They grew up,\u0026quot; Molly whispered, her voice cracking. \u0026quot;Arthur... when did they grow up?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;While we were busy worrying, Mollywobbles,\u0026quot; Arthur said softly, taking her hand. \u0026quot;They grew up beautifully.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley lowered his binoculars (he was bird watching, or so he claimed). He looked at Harry.","He saw the physical strength in the boy. He saw the way Harry guided Hermione over the hot sand.","\u0026quot;He’s filled out,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted approvingly. \u0026quot;Good muscle tone. That’s the protein diet kicking in. He looks... capable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He looks like a man, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia said quietly, clutching her napkin. \u0026quot;He looks just like James did in the photos. But... happier.\u0026quot;","Sirius Black let out a low whistle.","\u0026quot;Prongslet got buff,\u0026quot; Sirius grinned, though his eyes were shining. \u0026quot;Must be all that running away from danger. Great cardio.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s peace, Sirius,\u0026quot; Remus noted, watching Tonks wave at Hermione. \u0026quot;It suits them. They don\u0027t look like soldiers anymore. They look like people.\u0026quot;","Severus Snape watched them approach. He saw Draco laughing at something Ron said. He saw Harry kiss Hermione’s temple.","He saw the scars on Harry’s chest and the Dark Mark fading on Draco’s arm.","\u0026quot;They survived,\u0026quot; Snape murmured to himself. \u0026quot;Against all probability... they survived.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Lunch\u003c/strong\u003e","The group walked up the steps to the terrace, dripping wet and beaming.","\u0026quot;Starving!\u0026quot; Ron announced, grabbing a towel. \u0026quot;Swimming is hungry work. What’s for lunch?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Seafood!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, pointing to the buffet. \u0026quot;Local catch! Grilled Snapper! Conch Fritters! And a salad... for balance!\u0026quot;","They sat down, wrapping towels around their shoulders, smelling of the ocean and sunscreen.","\u0026quot;You lot look...\u0026quot; Arthur searched for the word. \u0026quot;Shiny.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the salt,\u0026quot; Luna explained, stealing a fritter from Ron’s plate. \u0026quot;It cleanses the aura.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the happiness,\u0026quot; Hermione smiled, squeezing Harry’s wet hand.","\u0026quot;It’s the fact that we don\u0027t have to save the world tomorrow,\u0026quot; Harry added, taking a sip of iced tea. \u0026quot;The only thing on my schedule is a nap.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And a flight,\u0026quot; Vernon reminded him, his eyes glinting with the secret of the incoming aircraft. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t forget the flight. Tomorrow morning. 0900 hours. We break the sound barrier.\u0026quot;","Draco leaned back, putting his arm around Ginny’s chair. He looked at his parents, at the Weasleys, at the Potters.","\u0026quot;To the ocean,\u0026quot; Draco toasted, raising a glass of water.","\u0026quot;To the ocean,\u0026quot; they echoed.","As they ate, laughing and passing plates of grilled fish, the parents watched them with a mixture of pride and a bittersweet realization.","The children didn\u0027t need protecting anymore. The war was over. The wedding was done.","They were free."]},{"num":147,"origNum":147,"title":"The Liquidation of the Larder","wordCount":819,"paragraphs":["The sun began its final descent over Isla de la Fortuna, turning the sky into a bruising mix of violet and blood orange.","On the main terrace of the villa, the atmosphere was not one of sadness for the end of the holiday, but of grim determination.","Vernon Dursley stood before the assembled party. He was wearing his \u0026quot;Executive Dinner\u0026quot; suit (a white tuxedo jacket he had found in the closet that fit surprisingly well). He held a clipboard that was thick with inventory lists.","\u0026quot;Right!\u0026quot; Vernon announced, his voice echoing off the marble pillars. \u0026quot;Listen close! We depart at 0900 hours tomorrow. The aircraft has weight limits, but more importantly, we have a surplus problem.\u0026quot;","He tapped the clipboard aggressively.","\u0026quot;The pantries are at 40% capacity. The wine cellar is still holding three hundred bottles of vintage stock. The walk-in freezer contains ingredients that cannot be transported across international borders due to customs regulations.\u0026quot;","He looked at the group with a wild, manic glint in his eye.","\u0026quot;We cannot leave it. We cannot waste it. That is inefficiency! That is sunk cost!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So what is the plan, Vernon?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley asked, adjusting his bow tie.","\u0026quot;The plan,\u0026quot; Vernon roared, throwing his arms wide, \u0026quot;is \u003cstrong\u003eLiquidation\u003c/strong\u003e! Total consumption! If it is edible, we eat it tonight! If it is drinkable, we drink it! We are not leaving a single crumb for the seagulls!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Draco called out. \u0026quot;Execute the \u0027Grand Finale\u0027 protocol!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eSNAP.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reveal\u003c/strong\u003e","The terrace floor rumbled.","The long dining table, usually set for twenty, began to extend. Extra leaves shot out of the ends, elongating the wood until it stretched the entire length of the balcony.","Then, the food appeared.","It wasn\u0027t served course by course. It was an avalanche of gastronomy.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Cold Bar\u003c/strong\u003e","At the north end of the table, a glacier of crushed ice rose toward the ceiling.","Embedded in the ice were mountains of King Crab legs, thick as tree branches, already cracked and waiting.","There were oysters—hundreds of them—shimmering in their shells like wet pearls, topped with pearls of caviar.","There were lobsters, split down the middle, their meat sweet and white.","There were prawns the size of bananas.","\u0026quot;It is an aquarium,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, staring at the seafood. \u0026quot;A dead, delicious aquarium.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Hot Line\u003c/strong\u003e","In the center, silver cloches floated in mid-air, keeping their contents piping hot.","Vernon walked down the line, lifting lids with a flourish.","\u0026quot;Behold!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted. \u0026quot;Beef Wellington! But not just beef! It is stuffed with foie gras and truffles! It is decadence wrapped in pastry!\u0026quot;","Next to it sat a \u003cstrong\u003eCrown Roast of Lamb\u003c/strong\u003e, the bones interlocked like fingers, the center filled with a stuffing made of wild mushrooms and chestnuts.","There were whole roasted ducks, their skin lacquered to a mahogany shine with honey and soy.","There were tureens of truffle risotto that smelled so earthy and rich it made Snape’s nose twitch from ten feet away.","There were bowls of lobster mac and cheese, bubbling with gruyere and gold leaf (actual gold leaf).","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Magic Touch\u003c/strong\u003e","Dumbledore had apparently been allowed into the kitchen for the finale.","Floating above the table were bubbles of soup—Butternut Squash and Sage—drifting within reach. You simply had to pop them with a spoon to release the soup into your bowl.","\u0026quot;Edible bubbles!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered, popping one. \u0026quot;No bowl required if you are quick enough!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dessert Fortress\u003c/strong\u003e","At the south end, a fortress of sugar had been constructed.","A chocolate fountain, three tiers high, flowed with Belgian dark chocolate.","Surrounding it were towers of profiteroles, croquembouche, macarons in every house color, and a massive Pavlova topped with every tropical fruit grown on the island.","And in the center, spinning slowly, was a spinning wheel of cheese.","\u0026quot;It rotates,\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy gasped, clutching his cane. \u0026quot;The Brie... it spins.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wine Lake\u003c/strong\u003e","The bar was gone. In its place was a wall of wine.","Every bottle that had not been drunk was uncorked and breathing.","\u0026quot;1945 Mouton Rothschild,\u0026quot; Draco read a label, his voice trembling. \u0026quot;1982 Petrus. Father... we are drinking the inheritance.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are liquidating the asset, Draco!\u0026quot; Lucius cried, grabbing a goblet. \u0026quot;Pour it! Pour it all!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Challenge\u003c/strong\u003e","The group stood before the feast. It was overwhelming. It was excessive. It was magnificent.","\u0026quot;There is enough food here,\u0026quot; Hermione calculated, \u0026quot;to feed Hogwarts for a week.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We have four hours,\u0026quot; Vernon checked his watch. \u0026quot;Pacing is key. Start with the proteins. Move to the carbs. Use the sorbet to cleanse the palate. Do not fill up on bread!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m going in,\u0026quot; Ron said, rolling up his sleeves. \u0026quot;If I don\u0027t survive... bury me in the mac and cheese.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Liquidation!\u0026quot; Harry toasted, raising an empty glass that Dobby immediately filled with vintage champagne.","\u0026quot;To the Liquidation!\u0026quot; the wedding party roared.","They pulled out their chairs. The final feast of the island had begun."]},{"num":148,"origNum":148,"title":"The Gluttony Protocol","wordCount":780,"paragraphs":["The silence of the Caribbean night was broken by the sound of cracking shells, clinking silverware, and the collective groans of people who were enjoying themselves entirely too much.","Vernon Dursley sat at the head of the table, a lobster bib tucked into his tuxedo collar. He wielded a pair of silver crackers like a weapon of war.","\u0026quot;Structural weakness!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted, pointing at a King Crab leg. \u0026quot;Hit it at the joint! Leverage, Ron! Use the fulcrum!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Seafood Siege\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron Weasley was currently engaged in hand-to-hand combat with a crab leg the size of a bludger.","\u0026quot;It’s armored!\u0026quot; Ron grunted, snapping the shell.","White meat burst forth. Ron dipped it into a bowl of melted butter and garlic. He ate it.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Ron moaned, his eyes rolling back. \u0026quot;It’s sweet. It’s like the ocean turned into sugar. Harry, I think I love this crab more than I love Quidditch.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t let Ginny hear that,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, sliding a raw oyster into his mouth.","Lucius Malfoy was eating caviar with a mother-of-pearl spoon. He looked at the tin.","\u0026quot;Beluga,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered reverently. \u0026quot;From the Caspian Sea. Narcissa, we are eating the price of a small broomstick with every bite.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It pops,\u0026quot; Narcissa smiled, sipping champagne. \u0026quot;It is delightful.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wellington Evaluation\u003c/strong\u003e","Then came the Beef Wellington.","Vernon stood up to carve. The knife slid through the golden pastry, the mushroom duxelles, and the pink beef with zero resistance.","\u0026quot;Look at that cross-section!\u0026quot; Vernon presented a slice to the table. \u0026quot;Pastry integrity maintained! No soggy bottom! The moisture seal is absolute!\u0026quot;","Severus Snape accepted a slice. He inspected the layer of truffle and foie gras.","\u0026quot;The layering,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;It is distinct. The earthiness of the fungus... the richness of the liver... the iron of the beef. It is a flavor compound that should be illegal.\u0026quot;","He took a bite. He chewed slowly.","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; Snape announced to the room, \u0026quot;better than the Hogwarts feast. The house-elves have outdone themselves.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby is pleased!\u0026quot; the elf squeaked from the sidelines, popping a cork on a magnum of Bordeaux.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Bubble Buffet\u003c/strong\u003e","Albus Dumbledore was having the time of his life with the floating soup bubbles.","\u0026quot;Catch it, Minerva!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered, chasing a glowing orange sphere of Butternut Squash soup with his spoon.","\u0026quot;Albus, sit down,\u0026quot; McGonagall sighed, though she was smiling.","\u003cem\u003ePOP.\u003c/em\u003e","Dumbledore caught one. The soup splashed gently into his spoon. He slurped it up.","\u0026quot;Sage!\u0026quot; Dumbledore declared. \u0026quot;And nutmeg! It is a flying autumn hug! Filius, try the green one! I believe it is pea and mint!\u0026quot;","Professor Flitwick levitated himself to catch a high-flying bubble. \u0026quot;Got it! Oh, refreshing!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wine Lake\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy was staring at his goblet. It was filled with a deep, ruby-red liquid that smelled of old leather and dark fruit.","\u0026quot;1945,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;The Victory Vintage.\u0026quot;","He took a sip. He didn\u0027t swallow immediately. He let it coat his tongue.","\u0026quot;It tastes like time,\u0026quot; Draco said, looking at Ginny. \u0026quot;It tastes like dust and velvet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It tastes like purple,\u0026quot; Ginny said, taking a massive gulp. \u0026quot;Good purple.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You are a heathen, Weasley,\u0026quot; Draco sighed affectionately, refilling her glass.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Cheese Wheel\u003c/strong\u003e","The spinning wheel of Brie was mesmerizing.","Hermione Granger stood before it, holding a cracker.","\u0026quot;It’s centrifugal force,\u0026quot; Hermione analyzed. \u0026quot;As it spins, the cheese softens at the edges. If I time my scrape perfectly...\u0026quot;","She reached in with a knife. She scraped a layer of gooey, melting cheese onto her cracker.","She ate it.","\u0026quot;Oh no,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;It’s too good. I can\u0027t stop. I’m going to live here. I’m going to build a house inside the cheese wheel.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Room for two?\u0026quot; Harry asked, joining her with a plate of grapes.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Surrender\u003c/strong\u003e","Two hours later, the table was a ruin.","Lobster shells were piled high. The Beef Wellington was a memory. The wine bottles were empty.","The group sat back in their chairs, defeated by luxury.","Vernon Dursley undid the top button of his trousers.","\u0026quot;Capacity reached,\u0026quot; Vernon wheezed. \u0026quot;Storage tanks full. Efficiency... 110%.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t feel my legs,\u0026quot; Ron mumbled, his head resting on the table next to a bowl of mac and cheese. \u0026quot;But it was worth it.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy was staring at the empty caviar tin. \u0026quot;We ate it all,\u0026quot; he said, sounding shocked. \u0026quot;We consumed the asset.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a good investment, Lucius,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley hiccuped, patting his shoulder. \u0026quot;High yield of happiness.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Chef!\u0026quot; Sirius Black toasted from the floor, where he was lying with a bottle of wine.","\u0026quot;To the Chef!\u0026quot; the room groaned.","They sat in the warm night air, heavy, happy, and ready for the fastest flight of their lives."]},{"num":149,"origNum":149,"title":"The Rocket with Windows","wordCount":744,"paragraphs":["The interior of the Concorde was not a palace. It was a tube. A very narrow, very sleek tube designed for one thing: speed.","\u0026quot;It is... intimate,\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy noted, squeezing into his leather seat in Row 1. His knees were practically touching the bulkhead. \u0026quot;Where is the legroom, Vernon? Where is the lounge?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sacrificed for aerodynamics, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted from across the aisle, buckling his belt with a snap. \u0026quot;You don\u0027t need a lounge when you are a projectile! Strap in! It’s going to get loud!\u0026quot;","Hagrid was currently occupying the entire rear section of the cabin, sitting on the floor with his back against the galley wall, looking terrified.","\u0026quot;It’s tiny, Harry,\u0026quot; Hagrid whispered, his eyes darting around the narrow fuselage. \u0026quot;It feels like a metal coffin.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a fast coffin, Hagrid,\u0026quot; Ron whimpered, gripping his armrests so hard the leather creaked. \u0026quot;A supersonic coffin.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Roar\u003c/strong\u003e","The pilot’s voice crackled. \u0026quot;Cabin crew, take your seats for immediate departure. Reheat is armed.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Reheat?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, her voice trembling. \u0026quot;He means afterburners. Oh, dear.\u0026quot;","The four Rolls-Royce/Snecma Olympus engines spooled up.","It wasn\u0027t a hum. It wasn\u0027t a drone. It was a physical assault on the eardrums. The entire plane began to vibrate. The tea cups in the galley rattled like chattering teeth.","\u0026quot;IT SOUNDS LIKE IT IS BREAKING!\u0026quot; McGonagall shrieked over the noise, clutching her hat.","\u0026quot;IT IS RAW POWER, MINERVA!\u0026quot; Vernon roared back, looking maniacally happy. \u0026quot;IT IS KEROSENE AND THUNDER!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Kick\u003c/strong\u003e","The brakes released. The pilot engaged the afterburners.","\u003cem\u003eBOOOOOM.\u003c/em\u003e","The plane didn\u0027t accelerate; it was kicked.","It felt as though a giant had walked up behind the aircraft and punted it down the runway.","Every passenger was slammed back into their seats. Faces were pulled taut.","\u0026quot;MY CHEEKS!\u0026quot; Draco yelled, his face flattening against his skull. \u0026quot;MY FACE IS REARRANGING!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I CAN\u0027T BREATHE!\u0026quot; Ron screamed. \u0026quot;THE AIR HAS BEEN LEFT BEHIND!\u0026quot;","Petunia Dursley let out a high-pitched wail, grabbing Dudley’s hand. Even Dudley, the boxing champion, looked pale.","\u0026quot;It’s got torque, Dad!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted. \u0026quot;Too much torque!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Climb\u003c/strong\u003e","The plane rotated. It shot into the sky at a terrifying angle.","Unlike the A380, which lumbered into the air, the Concorde knifed through it. It climbed like a fighter jet.","The cabin tilted so steeply that Hagrid slid three feet down the aisle before wedging himself against a trolley.","\u0026quot;WE ARE VERTICAL!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley shouted, looking out the tiny window at the blurring ground. \u0026quot;WE ARE LEAVING THE PLANET!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hold on!\u0026quot; Vernon laughed, his face vibrating. \u0026quot;Here comes the boom!\u0026quot;","The plane punched through the clouds in seconds. The blue sky darkened. The roar of the engines changed pitch—a deep, tearing scream as they pushed past the sound barrier.","\u003cem\u003eTHUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","A small jolt rocked the cabin.","\u0026quot;What was that?\u0026quot; Hermione gasped. \u0026quot;Did we hit a bird?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That was sound!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered. \u0026quot;We just left the noise behind! We are faster than our own scream!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am still screaming!\u0026quot; Ron wailed. \u0026quot;Can you hear me? Or am I silent?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Edge of Space\u003c/strong\u003e","The plane kept climbing. 40,000 feet. 50,000 feet.","The vibration smoothed out. The roar dulled to a distant hiss of wind.","The plane leveled off.","\u0026quot;Ladies and gentlemen,\u0026quot; the Captain announced coolly. \u0026quot;We have reached our cruising altitude of 60,000 feet. Mach 2.0. Welcome to the edge of space.\u0026quot;","Slowly, the wizards peeled their fingers off the armrests.","Lucius Malfoy looked out the window. His eyes widened.","The sky wasn\u0027t blue. It was a deep, dark purple, fading to black at the top. And below them, the horizon wasn\u0027t straight. It curved.","\u0026quot;The world,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, pressing his hand against the glass. \u0026quot;It is... round. I mean, I knew it was round. But Vernon... I can see the curve.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Stratosphere, Lucius!\u0026quot; Vernon beamed, unbuckling his belt. \u0026quot;We are higher than the weather! We are practically astronauts!\u0026quot;","Snape took off his sunglasses. He looked at the black sky.","\u0026quot;It is... void,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Empty. Cold. Efficient.\u0026quot;","He looked at Vernon.","\u0026quot;I approve.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Drinks!\u0026quot; Vernon shouted, standing up in the narrow aisle. \u0026quot;Champagne! We need to hydrate at Mach 2!\u0026quot;","As the stewardesses (who looked remarkably calm compared to the passengers) began to pour, Harry looked at Ron.","Ron’s hair was standing on end. His face was pale. But he was grinning.","\u0026quot;We’re faster than sound, Harry,\u0026quot; Ron breathed. \u0026quot;We’re outrunning the scream.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We sure are, mate,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, clinking his glass against Ron’s. \u0026quot;Next stop: London. Yesterday.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":150,"origNum":150,"title":"The Time Machine","wordCount":675,"paragraphs":["The cabin of the Concorde was quiet, save for the hiss of air rushing over the fuselage at 1,350 miles per hour.","Vernon Dursley stood in the aisle, pointing a sausage-like finger at a digital display mounted on the bulkhead.","\u0026quot;Look at that!\u0026quot; Vernon demanded. \u0026quot;Read the numbers, Arthur! What does it say?\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley squinted at the glowing red digits.","\u0026quot;Mach 2.02,\u0026quot; Arthur read slowly. \u0026quot;And... Time to Destination: 02:15.\u0026quot;","Arthur frowned. He pulled out his pocket watch. He tapped it. He looked at the display again.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; Arthur whispered, looking disturbed. \u0026quot;That cannot be right. We left the Caribbean... forty minutes ago? London is thousands of miles away. It takes a ship weeks. It takes a broomstick days.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That is the beauty of supersonic transport, Arthur!\u0026quot; Vernon crowed, sipping his champagne. \u0026quot;We are traveling faster than the rotation of the Earth! We are essentially chasing the sunrise! By the time we land, we will have barely aged!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are traveling... faster... than the world turns?\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy asked from Row 1, looking at his glass of wine with deep suspicion. \u0026quot;Is this legal? Is there a Time-Turner in the engine?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s physics, Lucius!\u0026quot; Hermione Granger piped up from Row 2. \u0026quot;Velocity equals distance over time. If the velocity is high enough, the time shrinks. It’s simple math.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is not math,\u0026quot; Ron Weasley mumbled, clutching his armrests. \u0026quot;It is cheating. We are cheating nature. The sky is going to get angry.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Window Watch\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy was glued to the window. The sky outside was a deep, bruised indigo, fading into the black of space above.","\u0026quot;It’s dark up here,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;Harry, look. You can see the curve. The actual curve of the planet.\u0026quot;","Harry leaned over. \u0026quot;It makes you feel small, doesn\u0027t it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It makes me feel fast,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, a grin spreading across his face. \u0026quot;We are the fastest humans alive right now. Faster than Aurors. Faster than dragons.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are a silver bullet,\u0026quot; Harry agreed.","Severus Snape sat in Row 6, reading a brochure about the Rolls-Royce Olympus engines.","\u0026quot;Reheat,\u0026quot; Snape murmured appreciatively. \u0026quot;Thrust-to-weight ratio. It is... elegant. A potion of kerosene and fire.\u0026quot;","He looked at McGonagall.","\u0026quot;Minerva, we should install these on the Hogwarts Express. We could cut the travel time to Scotland to twelve minutes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And kill the trolley witch with the G-force, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall replied dryly, though she was looking at the Mach meter with begrudging respect.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Descent Call\u003c/strong\u003e","The two hours passed in a blur of champagne and awe. It felt like they had barely finished their drinks when the chime sounded.","\u003cem\u003eBING-BONG.\u003c/em\u003e","The Captain’s voice crackled over the intercom. It was calm, professional, and terrifying.","\u0026quot;Ladies and gentlemen, we are beginning our initial descent into London Heathrow. We will be decelerating from Mach 2 to subsonic speeds shortly. Please return your seats to the upright position and fasten your seatbelts. It’s going to be a sharp drop.\u0026quot;","Vernon checked his watch. \u0026quot;Two hours, fifty-five minutes! A new personal best! Henderson, you beautiful maniac!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Panic Returns\u003c/strong\u003e","The euphoria of speed instantly vanished, replaced by the memory of the takeoff.","\u0026quot;Decelerating?\u0026quot; Ron yelped. \u0026quot;That means stopping! Stopping at this speed means crashing!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It means slowing down, Ron!\u0026quot; Hermione said, buckling her belt with trembling hands. \u0026quot;Just... hold on.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Strap in!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, dropping into his seat and clicking the buckle. \u0026quot;Lock it down! We are coming down from the stratosphere! It’s going to get bumpy!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy gripped his cane. He looked at Narcissa.","\u0026quot;If we survive the deceleration,\u0026quot; Lucius said rapidly, \u0026quot;I am buying a boat. A slow boat. A barge. I never want to go faster than a walking pace again.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just breathe, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa said, closing her eyes.","The engine pitch changed. The roar deepened. The nose of the plane dipped.","The wizards of Britain, who had faced Dark Lords and Dementors, squeezed their eyes shut and gripped their seatbelts as the white needle dropped out of the sky toward London.","\u0026quot;Here we go!\u0026quot; Dudley shouted from the back. \u0026quot;Re-entry!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":151,"origNum":151,"title":"The Drop and the Stop","wordCount":802,"paragraphs":["The transition from the edge of space to the atmosphere of London was not a gentle glide. It was a controlled fall.","The Concorde slowed from Mach 2. The roar of the engines changed from a high-pitched scream to a deep, guttural growl. The deceleration force threw everyone forward against their seatbelts.","\u0026quot;WE’RE BRAKING!\u0026quot; Ron Weasley yelled, his hands braced against the seat in front of him. \u0026quot;WHY ARE WE BRAKING IN THE CLOUDS? THERE IS NO ROAD!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s air resistance, Ron!\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, her face pale. \u0026quot;Atmospheric drag!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I DON\u0027T LIKE THE DRAG!\u0026quot; Ron screamed. \u0026quot;I WANT THE SMOOTH!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Droop\u003c/strong\u003e","Then, the nose of the plane moved.","With a mechanical whine that vibrated through the floorboards, the entire front cockpit section hinged downward to give the pilots a view of the runway.","From Draco Malfoy’s window in Row 1, it looked like the plane was snapping its own neck.","\u0026quot;THE FRONT FELL OFF!\u0026quot; Draco shrieked, losing all Malfoy composure. \u0026quot;POTTER! THE BEAK BROKE! WE ARE HEADLESS!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the Droop Snoot!\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley roared happily, holding his champagne glass which was tilting at a forty-five-degree angle. \u0026quot;Maximum visibility! Look at the hydraulics, Draco! It’s engineering poetry!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is a broken bird!\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy whimpered, pressing his face into the leather headrest. \u0026quot;Narcissa, tell the elves to catch us. Tell them to bring a mattress.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grey Welcome\u003c/strong\u003e","They punched through the cloud layer. The brilliant Caribbean sun vanished, replaced instantly by the dark, drizzly grey of a London morning.","Rain streaked the windows horizontally because they were still moving at 200 miles per hour.","\u0026quot;London,\u0026quot; Sirius Black gasped, looking out the window. \u0026quot;It looks... wet. And miserable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It looks like safety,\u0026quot; Remus Lupin corrected, gripping the armrests.","\u0026quot;Albus!\u0026quot; McGonagall shouted from Row 4. \u0026quot;We are coming in too steep! The angle of attack is aggressive!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is exhilarating, Minerva!\u0026quot; Dumbledore cheered, his beard flying up as the plane dropped. \u0026quot;It is like a dive on a Hippogriff, but with better catering! Wheeeee!\u0026quot;","Snape sat in Row 6. He did not scream. He did not cheer.","He crossed his arms over his chest. He closed his eyes behind his sunglasses.","\u0026quot;If I die,\u0026quot; Snape stated calmly to the empty air, \u0026quot;I am haunting Dursley. I will be the poltergeist of his drill factory. I will rust his inventory.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Impact\u003c/strong\u003e","The runway rushed up. The tarmac looked dangerously close and dangerously fast.","Concorde didn\u0027t flare gently like a normal jet; it landed with a high nose attitude and a heavy thud.","\u003cem\u003eSLAM.\u003c/em\u003e","The main gear hit the concrete. The impact shuddered through the spine of every wizard on board.","\u0026quot;OOF!\u0026quot; Hagrid grunted from the back, bouncing off the galley wall.","\u0026quot;WE’RE DOWN!\u0026quot; Harry yelled, bracing himself.","Then, the reverse thrusters engaged. The noise was deafening—a roar that sounded like a dragon gargling rocks.","The braking force was violent. Everyone was thrown forward, held in place only by the seatbelts.","\u0026quot;MY ORGANS!\u0026quot; Ron howled. \u0026quot;MY STOMACH IS IN MY THROAT! I CAN TASTE THE LOBSTER AGAIN!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Feel the Gs!\u0026quot; Vernon laughed maniacally, vibrating in his seat. \u0026quot;Stopping power! British engineering!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Make it stop!\u0026quot; Narcissa Malfoy cried, clutching Lucius’s hand. \u0026quot;Lucius, bribe the pilot! Give him gold to stop!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Scramble\u003c/strong\u003e","The plane slowed. The roar faded. The vibration ceased.","The Concorde turned off the runway and taxied toward the private terminal. It came to a complete halt.","\u003cem\u003eBING.\u003c/em\u003e","The seatbelt sign turned off.","For one second, there was silence.","Then, the cabin erupted into a scene of panic usually reserved for escaping a collapsing building.","\u0026quot;GET ME OUT!\u0026quot; Draco yelled, fumbling with his buckle. \u0026quot;THE TUBE IS TOO SMALL! I NEED SPACE!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Unbuckle!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley shouted, wrestling with the latch. \u0026quot;Molly, flee! Flee the metal bird!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t get out!\u0026quot; Hagrid bellowed from the back. \u0026quot;I\u0027m wedged! The kitchen has me!\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley stood up calmly. He adjusted his jacket. He checked his watch.","\u0026quot;Three hours and four minutes,\u0026quot; Vernon announced with immense satisfaction. \u0026quot;A new record. Gentlemen, we have arrived before we left. Welcome to yesterday.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t care about time travel!\u0026quot; Ron scrambled over the seat back, ignoring the aisle. \u0026quot;I just want ground! Stationary ground!\u0026quot;","The wizards crowded the door. They pressed their faces against the porthole window. They clawed at the locking mechanism.","Lucius Malfoy was practically climbing over Harry to get to the front.","\u0026quot;Move, Potter!\u0026quot; Lucius hissed. \u0026quot;You are the Chosen One, choose to move faster! I need to kiss the tarmac! I need to buy the tarmac!\u0026quot;","They stood there, a crushed mass of terrified magic folk, waiting for the seal to break, desperate to escape the miracle of supersonic flight and return to the safety of teleportation.","\u0026quot;Open!\u0026quot; Draco banged on the door. \u0026quot;Open, you infernal aluminum can!\u0026quot;","Vernon chuckled, picking up his briefcase. \u0026quot;Amateurs.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":152,"origNum":152,"title":"The Tarmac Theatre","wordCount":714,"paragraphs":["The door of the Concorde hissed open. The mobile stairs locked into place with a mechanical \u003cem\u003eclunk\u003c/em\u003e.","For a moment, nothing happened. The open doorway framed the grey, drizzly London sky like a portal to another dimension.","Then, the dam broke.","Lucius Malfoy did not walk down the stairs. He practically fell down them, his cane clattering against the metal steps. He reached the bottom, stumbled onto the wet, oil-stained tarmac, and collapsed.","He didn\u0027t care about his linen suit. He didn\u0027t care about the puddles.","He spread his arms wide, hugging the asphalt.","\u0026quot;Grey,\u0026quot; Lucius sobbed into the ground. \u0026quot;Beautiful, flat, stationary grey. I love you, tarmac. I shall buy you. I shall pave the Manor with you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get out of the way, Father!\u0026quot; Draco yelled, stumbling over him.","Draco hit the ground and rolled. He ended up on his back, staring at the grey clouds.","\u0026quot;Clouds,\u0026quot; Draco wheezed. \u0026quot;Clouds that stay \u003cem\u003eabove\u003c/em\u003e us. That is the correct order of things. Clouds up. Malfoys down.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Spill\u003c/strong\u003e","The rest of the wedding party spilled out of the plane like clown cars unloading at a circus.","Ron Weasley crawled down the stairs on his hands and knees.","\u0026quot;The ground isn\u0027t moving,\u0026quot; Ron announced to a confused baggage handler. \u0026quot;Sir! The ground! It has stopped vibrating! It is a miracle!\u0026quot;","Hagrid had to squeeze through the door sideways. When he finally popped out, he took the stairs two at a time, his massive boots shaking the metal frame.","He reached the bottom and fell to his knees, kissing a painted white line.","\u0026quot;Terra Firma!\u0026quot; Hagrid bellowed. \u0026quot;Good ol\u0027 dirt! Even if it is concrete!\u0026quot;","Severus Snape descended slowly. He looked like a spectre of death who had just been on a roller coaster. His sunglasses were crooked. His hair was windblown.","He walked to the nearest solid object—the wheel of the mobile stairs—and leaned his forehead against the cold rubber.","\u0026quot;Friction,\u0026quot; Snape whispered to the tire. \u0026quot;Adhesion. Stasis. I appreciate you.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe View from the Terminal\u003c/strong\u003e","Inside the glass-walled Elite Terminal, a group of businessmen, tired travelers, and airport staff were staring out the window.","They were used to seeing celebrities. They were used to seeing royalty.","They were \u003cem\u003enot\u003c/em\u003e used to this.","\u0026quot;Is that...\u0026quot; a businessman asked, lowering his \u003cem\u003eFinancial Times\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;Is that a Concorde?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is,\u0026quot; his colleague replied, pressing his nose against the glass. \u0026quot;Henderson\u0027s bird. But... look at the passengers.\u0026quot;","The Muggles watched in baffled silence.","They saw a man in a bright yellow Hawaiian shirt and purple velvet trousers (Dumbledore) skipping down the stairs, humming.","They saw a woman in full tartan robes (McGonagall) adjusting a pointed hat.","They saw a giant who was twice the size of a normal human (Hagrid) weeping over a white line.","They saw a man in a tuxedo (Vernon) checking his watch and high-fiving a man in a tweed suit (Arthur).","And they saw a pale aristocrat in a ruined linen suit (Lucius) literally making snow angels in the puddles on the tarmac.","\u0026quot;Is it... a circus?\u0026quot; a tourist asked, snapping a photo. \u0026quot;Or a cult?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a rock band,\u0026quot; the businessman decided. \u0026quot;It has to be. Look at the one in black leather (Snape). That’s the bassist. He looks miserable. Bassists are always miserable.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Count\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley stood at the bottom of the stairs, surveying the carnage. Bodies were strewn everywhere.","He looked at his watch.","\u0026quot;London!\u0026quot; Vernon roared. \u0026quot;11:00 AM! We beat the rush hour! We beat the sun! Gentlemen, we have conquered the Atlantic!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We have conquered nausea,\u0026quot; Hermione groaned from where she was sitting on her suitcase. \u0026quot;Vernon, please. Never again.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Until the next merger!\u0026quot; Vernon grinned.","Harry Potter sat on the wet ground, rain dripping off his nose. He looked at the chaos. He looked at the Muggles staring from the terminal.","He looked at his family—Muggle and Magic—united in their absolute refusal to ever fly supersonic again.","He started to laugh. It started as a chuckle and grew into a roar.","\u0026quot;We’re home,\u0026quot; Harry laughed. \u0026quot;We’re actually home.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And we’re alive,\u0026quot; Draco added from a puddle. \u0026quot;Though my suit is ruined.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Put it on the card,\u0026quot; Harry gasped.","\u0026quot;I intend to,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;I intend to buy a new suit. And a train. A slow train.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":153,"origNum":153,"title":"The House That Love Rebuilt","wordCount":1277,"paragraphs":["The chaos of Heathrow Terminal 5 was fading behind them.","Sirius Black stood by a pile of dragon-skin trunks, grinning like a man who had just won the lottery.","\u0026quot;I’ve got the baggage duty,\u0026quot; Sirius declared, levitating three trunks at once. \u0026quot;Moony is driving the car with Tonks. We’ll meet you at the flat? Or are you two disappearing again?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;One last stop,\u0026quot; Harry said, gripping Hermione’s hand. \u0026quot;We’ll be a bit late.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t rush,\u0026quot; Sirius winked. \u0026quot;I’m going to teach Vernon Dursley how to play Exploding Snap. Take your time.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded. He turned to Hermione.","\u0026quot;Ready?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Always,\u0026quot; she smiled, though she looked curious.","Harry turned on his heel. The world twisted. The smell of jet fuel and damp tarmac vanished, replaced by the scent of woodsmoke and crisp autumn leaves.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Cottage\u003c/strong\u003e","They landed in a lane in Godric\u0027s Hollow.","Hermione opened her eyes. She gasped.","She was expecting the ruin—the ivy-choked, blast-shattered monument they had visited that snowy Christmas Eve.","But the house that stood before them was whole.","The roof was repaired, the slate tiles gleaming in the afternoon sun. The hedge was trimmed. The front gate, once rusted and hanging off its hinges, was painted a fresh, welcoming green.","Warm, golden light spilled from the downstairs windows.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;How?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Kingsley,\u0026quot; Harry explained, looking at the house with a lump in his throat. \u0026quot;And Vernon’s architect friends. I asked them to fix it. I didn\u0027t want it to be a monument to death anymore, Mione. I wanted it to be a home.\u0026quot;","He unlatched the gate. It swung open silently.","\u0026quot;Come on.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Living Room\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry unlocked the front door. The smell hit them instantly—not mustiness or decay, but beeswax, old books, and... tea.","They walked into the hallway. The floorboards didn\u0027t creak.","They stepped into the living room.","Harry stopped. Hermione grabbed his arm, her nails digging in.","The room was furnished with cozy, mismatched armchairs and a squashy sofa near the fire.","And sitting on the sofa, looking as if they were just waiting for a friend to pop round, were James and Lily Potter.","They weren\u0027t the translucent, silvery figures from the forest or the altar. Here, inside the house where their magic still lived in the very walls, they looked almost solid.","James was leaning back, his arm draped over the sofa, wearing jeans and a t-shirt. Lily was holding a steaming mug, her legs curled under her.","They looked up as the door opened. James’s jaw dropped.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; James said, looking around the room. \u0026quot;You fixed the roof. Lily, look. The hole is gone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I see it, James,\u0026quot; Lily whispered, her green eyes fixed on Harry.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reunion\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry walked into the room. He felt like he was walking into a dream, but the heat from the fire was real.","\u0026quot;Hi,\u0026quot; Harry croaked.","\u0026quot;Hi, son,\u0026quot; James grinned, standing up. \u0026quot;Nice place. A bit cleaner than when we left it. Did you get rid of the cat hair?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Working on it,\u0026quot; Harry smiled tearfully.","Lily stood up. She didn\u0027t look at the furniture. She looked at Hermione.","Hermione was standing in the doorway, frozen. She was the logical one. She was the one who knew that the Resurrection Stone was gone, that ghosts were imprints, that this shouldn\u0027t be possible.","But she also knew what love felt like.","Lily walked over to Hermione. She stopped a foot away.","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Lily said softly.","Hermione let out a sob. \u0026quot;Mrs. Potter... I... I tried. I tried to keep him safe.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Lily whispered.","Lily reached out. She cupped Hermione’s face. Her touch wasn\u0027t cold; it was like a cool breeze on a hot day.","\u0026quot;You didn\u0027t just keep him safe,\u0026quot; Lily said, her eyes shining. \u0026quot;You saved him. You stood beside him when the darkness closed in, and you guarded his heart when the weight of the world tried to crush it.\u0026quot;","Hermione broke. She buried her face in her hands and wept—years of fear, responsibility, and the crushing weight of being the \u0027strong one\u0027 finally releasing.","Lily pulled her into a hug. It was a spectral embrace, but Hermione felt it in her soul.","\u0026quot;Thank you,\u0026quot; Lily whispered into Hermione’s hair. \u0026quot;Thank you for my son.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sit-Down\u003c/strong\u003e","James walked over to Harry. He punched him lightly on the shoulder.","\u0026quot;Nice suit,\u0026quot; James noted, eyeing the midnight blue fabric. \u0026quot;Better than the dress robes I wore. Sirius tell you about the ruffles?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He mentioned them,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, wiping his eyes.","\u0026quot;Come sit,\u0026quot; James gestured to the armchairs. \u0026quot;Tell us everything. We saw the big stuff... the battle... the forest. But tell us the rest. Tell us about the dragon.\u0026quot;","Harry and Hermione sat down. James and Lily sat opposite them on the sofa.","It was the most normal, impossible thing in the world. A double date with the dead.","\u0026quot;The dragon,\u0026quot; Harry began, leaning forward. \u0026quot;Well, it started because Hermione had a crazy idea...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was \u003cem\u003enot\u003c/em\u003e crazy,\u0026quot; Hermione sniffed, smiling through her tears. \u0026quot;It was calculated.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She blew up a bank, Dad,\u0026quot; Harry told James.","James threw his head back and laughed—a barking, joyful sound that filled the room. \u0026quot;That\u0027s my girl! Sirius would have loved that!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He did,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;He hugged her for ten minutes.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Conversation\u003c/strong\u003e","They talked for hours. The sun went down outside, but the room stayed bright with firelight and magic.","They talked about the Dursleys (\u0026quot;Petunia put a blanket over you?\u0026quot; Lily asked, stunned. \u0026quot;She kept the blanket?\u0026quot;).","They talked about Snape (\u0026quot;He has a good right hook,\u0026quot; James admitted begrudgingly. \u0026quot;And he can dance. Who knew?\u0026quot;).","They talked about the wedding.","\u0026quot;I liked the vows,\u0026quot; Lily said, looking at Hermione. \u0026quot; \u0027Home is not a house.\u0027 That was beautiful.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s true,\u0026quot; Hermione said, reaching for Harry’s hand. \u0026quot;This place... it\u0027s wonderful. But it\u0027s just brick and mortar. He\u0027s my home.\u0026quot;","Harry squeezed her hand.","James looked at them—holding hands, scarred but whole, sitting in the living room he had died in.","He looked at the repaired ceiling. He looked at the fire.","\u0026quot;You reclaimed it,\u0026quot; James said softly. \u0026quot;You took the worst night of our lives and you turned it into a morning.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We had to,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;We needed a place to start over.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; James smiled, leaning back and putting his arm around Lily. \u0026quot;You couldn\u0027t have picked a better spot. The foundations are good. Built on love.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And structural integrity,\u0026quot; Harry added, channeling Vernon.","James laughed. \u0026quot;And structural integrity.\u0026quot;","Lily leaned forward. She touched Harry’s knee.","\u0026quot;We can\u0027t stay forever, Harry,\u0026quot; she said gently. \u0026quot;The veil is thin here, but it\u0027s not open.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;I just... I wanted you to see it. I wanted you to know we\u0027re okay.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We know,\u0026quot; Lily smiled. \u0026quot;We know.\u0026quot;","She looked at Hermione.","\u0026quot;Take care of him,\u0026quot; Lily said. \u0026quot;He\u0027s trouble.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will,\u0026quot; Hermione promised. \u0026quot;I\u0027m good at trouble.\u0026quot;","James stood up. He offered a hand to Harry.","\u0026quot;Go on,\u0026quot; James said. \u0026quot;Go live your life, Harry. Make it a loud one. Make it a happy one.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will, Dad.\u0026quot;","Harry stood up. He took Hermione’s hand.","They walked to the door. Harry looked back one last time.","James and Lily were sitting on the sofa, holding hands, watching them leave. They were smiling.","\u0026quot;Bye, Mum. Bye, Dad.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;See you, son.\u0026quot;","Harry closed the door.","He stood on the porch, inhaling the cool night air. He looked at Hermione.","\u0026quot;You okay?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m perfect,\u0026quot; she said.","They walked down the garden path, past the gate, and Disapparated into the night, leaving the cottage glowing warm and bright in the darkness, no longer a ruin, but a home."]},{"num":154,"origNum":154,"title":"The Ghosts of Privet Drive","wordCount":1258,"paragraphs":["The living room of Number Four, Privet Drive was aggressively normal.","The tropical heat of the Caribbean, the roar of the Concorde, and the taste of spicy curry felt like a fever dream from another life.","Here, the curtains were drawn against the English drizzle. The television was blaring a game show. The smell was not of sea salt, but of roast chicken and floor polish.","Vernon Dursley sat in his armchair, rustling the \u003cem\u003eEvening Standard\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;Petrol prices,\u0026quot; Vernon grumbled, stabbing the paper with a finger. \u0026quot;Up again. And the council has missed the bin collection. I tell you, Petunia, this country is going to the dogs. No efficiency.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, dear,\u0026quot; Petunia called from the kitchen, where she was vigorously scrubbing a baking tray. \u0026quot;Did you put the coasters out?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Coasters are deployed,\u0026quot; Vernon confirmed.","On the sofa, Dudley and Chloe were watching the TV.","\u0026quot;I still can\u0027t believe we rode a dragon,\u0026quot; Chloe whispered, leaning her head on Dudley’s massive shoulder. \u0026quot;Well, a plane that felt like a dragon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a good trip,\u0026quot; Dudley said, flexing his hand. \u0026quot;But it’s good to be back. The sofa doesn\u0027t spin here.\u0026quot;","It was a perfect tableau of suburban peace.","Then, the lamp in the corner flickered.","The television screen went fuzzy, the game show host dissolving into static.","\u0026quot;Ruddy signal,\u0026quot; Vernon muttered, reaching for the remote. \u0026quot;I told them the aerial needed—\u0026quot;","He stopped.","The air in the room changed. The smell of floor polish vanished, replaced by the scent of woodsmoke, lilies, and something electrical—like ozone before a storm.","Two pillars of soft, silvery light materialized on the rug, right between the television and the coffee table.","Vernon dropped the remote. Petunia dropped the baking tray in the kitchen with a deafening \u003cem\u003eCLANG\u003c/em\u003e.","Chloe gasped, shrinking behind Dudley.","The light coalesced. The forms solidified.","Standing in the middle of the Dursley living room were James and Lily Potter.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Sisters\u003c/strong\u003e","Petunia Dursley walked slowly out of the kitchen, wiping her hands on a tea towel. She looked pale, her eyes wide and fixed on the woman standing on her rug.","Lily Potter looked exactly as Petunia remembered her, yet entirely different. The anger was gone. The youth was eternal. She was glowing.","\u0026quot;Tuney,\u0026quot; Lily said softly.","Petunia let out a whimper. She gripped the doorframe.","\u0026quot;Lily,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered. \u0026quot;You... you\u0027re here. In my house.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a lovely house,\u0026quot; Lily smiled, looking around. \u0026quot;It’s clean. It’s safe. You kept it safe.\u0026quot;","She walked toward her sister. Petunia didn\u0027t back away. She stood trembling.","\u0026quot;I was jealous,\u0026quot; Petunia blurted out, the confession tearing itself free after thirty years. \u0026quot;I was so jealous, Lily. You were special. And I was... ordinary.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You weren\u0027t ordinary,\u0026quot; Lily said gently. \u0026quot;You were the one who had to be strong. You were the one who had to take him in when I couldn\u0027t.\u0026quot;","Lily stopped in front of her. She reached out a translucent hand and placed it on Petunia’s cheek. Petunia leaned into the touch, tears spilling over.","\u0026quot;You gave him a home,\u0026quot; Lily whispered. \u0026quot;You gave him a family. Thank you, Tuney. Thank you for raising my boy.\u0026quot;","Petunia broke into a sob that was half-laugh, half-cry. \u0026quot;He has your eyes, Lily. He has your stubborn, impossible eyes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Lily beamed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Fathers\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley was gripping the arms of his chair so hard the fabric was straining.","He was staring at James Potter.","He remembered James. He remembered the dinner where James had mocked him. He remembered the arrogance.","But the man standing before him now didn\u0027t look arrogant. He looked humble.","James walked over to Vernon’s chair. He looked at the moustache. He looked at the suit.","\u0026quot;Vernon,\u0026quot; James said.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Vernon croaked, trying to summon his bluster but failing. \u0026quot;You... you’re transparent. You’re getting ectoplasm on the carpet.\u0026quot;","James laughed—a warm, rich sound.","\u0026quot;Sorry about the carpet,\u0026quot; James grinned. \u0026quot;And sorry about... well, everything before.\u0026quot;","James looked Vernon in the eye.","\u0026quot;I used to think you were boring, Vernon. I used to think you were small.\u0026quot;","James shook his head.","\u0026quot;But I watched you. I watched you stand in front of him at the Ministry. I watched you build a wedding venue with your bare hands. I watched you fly a Concorde for him.\u0026quot;","James straightened up. He offered a spectral hand.","\u0026quot;You stepped up,\u0026quot; James said seriously. \u0026quot;You were the father I couldn\u0027t be. You taught him how to survive. You taught him... efficiency.\u0026quot;","Vernon stared at the hand. He swallowed the lump in his throat.","\u0026quot;Someone had to teach him about drill bits,\u0026quot; Vernon gruffed, sitting up straighter. \u0026quot;And taxes. The boy had no concept of fiscal responsibility.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He does now,\u0026quot; James smiled. \u0026quot;Thanks to you.\u0026quot;","Vernon nodded, a sharp, decisive jerk of his head. \u0026quot;He turned out alright. For a wizard.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He turned out magnificent,\u0026quot; James agreed. \u0026quot;For a Dursley.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Cousins\u003c/strong\u003e","James and Lily turned to the sofa.","Dudley was staring at them, mouth open. Chloe was peeking out from behind his arm.","\u0026quot;Big D,\u0026quot; James grinned. \u0026quot;You got big. Really big.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I box,\u0026quot; Dudley managed to say. \u0026quot;Heavyweight.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I saw,\u0026quot; James nodded appreciatively. \u0026quot;You’ve got a right hook that could knock out a mountain troll. I saw you standing out on that front lawn in your boxing wraps, ready to punch a Dementor in the jaw if it came near Harry.\u0026quot;","Dudley’s ears turned pink, though he sat up a little straighter. \u0026quot;He’s my cousin. Someone had to watch his blind side when the weirdos showed up.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You weren\u0027t just his cousin, Big D—you were his brother,\u0026quot; James said warmly. \u0026quot;And I couldn\u0027t have asked for a better one to guard my son.\u0026quot;","Lily drifted over to Chloe.","\u0026quot;Hello, dear,\u0026quot; Lily said warmly. \u0026quot;Welcome to the family. It’s a bit... loud, isn\u0027t it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s... amazing,\u0026quot; Chloe breathed, looking at the glowing woman. \u0026quot;Are you... are you really magic?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Love is the only magic that stays,\u0026quot; Lily said softly. \u0026quot;Remember that.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Farewell\u003c/strong\u003e","The light began to fade. The static on the TV started to hiss.","James moved back to Lily’s side. They took hands.","They looked at the Dursleys—the ordinary, normal, grumpy family that had become the most extraordinary guardians in history.","\u0026quot;We have to go,\u0026quot; Lily said, her voice fading like a distant radio station.","\u0026quot;Take care of him,\u0026quot; James said. \u0026quot;Keep the kettle on.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Always,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, wiping her eyes.","\u0026quot;And Vernon?\u0026quot; James added, his silhouette blurring.","\u0026quot;Yes?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The A380?\u0026quot; James grinned, fading into the light. \u0026quot;Nice choice.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003ePOP.\u003c/em\u003e","They were gone.","The lamp stopped flickering. The TV picture snapped back into focus—the game show host was spinning a wheel.","The room smelled of floor polish and roast chicken again.","Vernon sat in silence for a long moment.","He picked up the remote. He turned off the TV.","He looked at Petunia, who was smiling through her tears. He looked at Dudley.","Vernon Dursley cleared his throat. He picked up his newspaper. He snapped it open.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon announced, his voice steady but unusually gentle. \u0026quot;That’s that, then. Ghosts dealt with. Closure achieved.\u0026quot;","He looked over the top of the paper.","\u0026quot;Petunia, is that chicken ready? I’m famished. Spectres don\u0027t fill the stomach.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s ready, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia said softly.","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, hiding a small smile behind the \u003cem\u003eEvening Standard\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;Let’s eat. We have a quiet evening ahead. Finally.\u0026quot;","But as he read the sports section, Vernon Dursley felt a strange warmth in his chest that had nothing to do with brandy.","It was the feeling of a job well done."]}]},{"id":"book-2","title":"Book 2: The Next Generation","subtitle":"The Rise of the Pantheon \u0026 The New Era","badge":"Work in Progress","sourceFile":"Harry Potter Fan Fiction - Book 2 (WIP).docx","lastModified":"2026-11-09T08:17:19.0671788Z","fileSize":2334697,"wordCount":91395,"chapterCount":82,"chapters":[{"num":1,"origNum":1,"title":"The Toast of Confusion","wordCount":1141,"paragraphs":["The dining room of Malfoy Manor was no longer a place of dark brooding; it was the loudest room in Wiltshire.","Two years had passed since the \u0026quot;Triple Wedding\u0026quot; on Isla de la Fortuna, and the quarterly dinners had become a fixture of the calendar that was more unmovable than a Gringotts vault. The long mahogany table was extended to its full length to accommodate the growing congregation now known affectionately as \u003cstrong\u003eThe Alliance\u003c/strong\u003e (Harry, Hermione, Ron, Luna, Draco, Ginny, Dudley, and Chloe) and \u003cstrong\u003eThe Management\u003c/strong\u003e (the parents).","Dobby, wearing a silk tuxedo that Draco had commissioned for him, snapped his fingers.","\u0026quot;The Roast!\u0026quot; Dobby announced. \u0026quot;The Beef of Celebration!\u0026quot;","A platter the size of a shield floated onto the table. It held a rib of beef so perfectly roasted it looked like a sculpture1111.","Vernon Dursley, sitting at the head of the table opposite Lucius Malfoy, adjusted his napkin. He had aged comfortably into his role as the logistical patriarch of the group.","\u0026quot;Excellent crust,\u0026quot; Vernon noted, pointing his fork. \u0026quot;High heat sear. Locks in the juices. That is structural integrity, Lucius.\u0026quot; 2222","\u0026quot;It is acceptable,\u0026quot; Lucius agreed, pouring gravy from a silver boat with a flourish. \u0026quot;Though I believe the Yorkshire Puddings have achieved a new level of verticality. Arthur, did you assist with the airflow?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Convection, Lucius!\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley beamed from across the table. \u0026quot;I installed a fan in the oven! It circulates the heat! Muggles call it \u0027Fan-Assisted\u0027!\u0026quot; 3333","\u0026quot;It spins?\u0026quot; Lucius asked, delighted. \u0026quot;Inside the heat?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Like a propeller!\u0026quot;","The meal was a cacophony of passing plates and cross-table shouting. Ron Weasley was currently explaining the profit margins of his new \u0026quot;Skiving Snackbox Pro\u0026quot; line to Dudley, who was nodding and suggesting a tie-in with a boxing gym. Draco Malfoy was debating Ministry policy with Hermione, while Harry simply ate potatoes and looked around the table with deep contentment.","As the plates were cleared by the efficient house-elf team, the atmosphere shifted to the relaxant phase.","\u0026quot;The vintage,\u0026quot; Lucius announced, standing up. He held a dusty bottle of Elf-Made Pinot Noir. \u0026quot;1902. A good year for grapes. A bad year for Goblins. But the flavor is exquisite.\u0026quot; 4","The crystal goblets floated around the table, filling themselves with the ruby-red liquid.","The glasses landed in front of the men. Vernon took a large sip. Arthur swirled his enthusiastically. Ron downed half of his in one gulp.","But when the bottle floated toward the women of The Alliance, the rhythm broke.","Hermione Granger placed her hand over her glass.","\u0026quot;Not for me, thank you, Lucius,\u0026quot; Hermione said quickly. \u0026quot;I... I have a very early meeting with the Centaur Liaison Office tomorrow. I need a clear head. Caffeine only.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at her, surprised. Hermione usually enjoyed a glass of wine after a debate with Draco. \u0026quot;You sure? It’s the good stuff.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Quite sure,\u0026quot; Hermione said, reaching for a water pitcher.","Further down the table, Luna Lovegood pushed her goblet away.","\u0026quot;No thank you,\u0026quot; Luna hummed. \u0026quot;The Wrackspurts are particularly active tonight. Alcohol makes them fuzzy, and I need to keep my aura sharp for the Crumple-Horned Snorkack expedition planning.\u0026quot; 5","Ron shrugged. \u0026quot;More for me then.\u0026quot;","Next to Draco, Ginny Weasley shook her head as the bottle approached.","\u0026quot;Pass,\u0026quot; Ginny said firmly. \u0026quot;Coach’s orders. We have a match against the Wimbourne Wasps on Saturday. I’m on a strict hydration protocol. Electrolytes only.\u0026quot;","Draco raised an eyebrow. \u0026quot;Since when do you listen to the coach about diet? Last week you ate a bucket of wings.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Since we need to win, Draco,\u0026quot; Ginny snapped, grabbing a bread roll.","And finally, Chloe Dursley smiled apologetically at Lucius.","\u0026quot;I’m sitting this one out too, Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; Chloe said. \u0026quot;I think I ate some bad shellfish at lunch. My stomach is a bit... flippy. Stick to ginger ale.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shellfish?\u0026quot; Vernon frowned. \u0026quot;We didn\u0027t have shellfish. We had lamb.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was... yesterday,\u0026quot; Chloe lied smoothly. \u0026quot;Delayed reaction.\u0026quot;","Lucius looked at the four young women. He looked at the bottle of 1902 Pinot. He looked at Narcissa.","\u0026quot;More for The Management, then,\u0026quot; Lucius decided, filling his own glass to the brim. \u0026quot;To... hydration.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To hydration!\u0026quot; the men roared.","The conversation resumed, the volume rising as the wine flowed. But at the center of the table, a different kind of communication was happening.","Hermione was staring at Ginny. Ginny was staring at Luna. Luna was smiling dreamily at Chloe.","They didn\u0027t speak. They just looked.","Hermione tapped her water glass three times. Ginny’s eyes widened. She looked at Chloe, who gave a tiny, almost imperceptible nod. Luna simply hummed a high-pitched note and touched her stomach.","The realization hit them simultaneously. The math. The excuses. The water.","Without a word, the four women stood up.","\u0026quot;Excuse us,\u0026quot; Hermione announced abruptly.","\u0026quot;Bathroom,\u0026quot; Ginny blurted out.","\u0026quot;Nargle check,\u0026quot; Luna added.","\u0026quot;Fresh air,\u0026quot; Chloe finished.","They rushed away from the table, huddling together near the large bay window overlooking the peacocks.","The husbands—Harry, Ron, Draco, and Dudley—watched them go, forks suspended halfway to their mouths.","\u0026quot;What are they doing?\u0026quot; Ron asked, chewing a potato. \u0026quot;Is it a secret meeting? Are we in trouble?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Probably discussing our failures,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, sipping his wine. \u0026quot;I forgot our anniversary last week. I bought her a broomstick to make up for it, but she still looks at me with suspicion.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I left my socks on the floor,\u0026quot; Harry admitted. \u0026quot;Hermione hates that.\u0026quot;","Suddenly, a sound erupted from the bay window that silenced the entire room.","It wasn\u0027t a spell. It wasn\u0027t an explosion.","It was a scream. A high-pitched, collective, four-part harmony of pure, unadulterated squealing.","\u0026quot;EEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE!\u0026quot;","The men jumped. Vernon dropped his fork. Lucius spilled his wine.","They spun around.","By the window, Hermione, Ginny, Luna, and Chloe were jumping up and down in a tight circle, holding hands, bouncing like they were back on the starting line of the Sack Race6. They were screaming, laughing, and crying all at once.","\u0026quot;OH MY GOD!\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked.","\u0026quot;ALL OF US?\u0026quot; Ginny yelled.","\u0026quot;THE TIMING!\u0026quot; Chloe laughed hysterically.","\u0026quot;LITTLE WRACKSPURTS!\u0026quot; Luna cheered.","They hugged each other in a crushing embrace, a knot of silk robes and happy tears.","At the table, The Alliance and The Management sat in stunned silence.","Harry looked at Draco. Draco looked at Ron. Ron looked at Dudley.","\u0026quot;Did we miss something?\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;Did they win a bet?\u0026quot; Ron asked, bewildered.","\u0026quot;Is there a spider?\u0026quot; Dudley suggested.","Vernon Dursley stared at the jumping women. He looked at their empty wine glasses. He looked at his wife.","\u0026quot;Petunia,\u0026quot; Vernon said slowly. \u0026quot;Why are they jumping? Is it... aerobics?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t know, Vernon,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, clutching her napkin. \u0026quot;But it looks... expensive.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy swirled his wine, watching his wife jumping up and down.","\u0026quot;I think,\u0026quot; Draco murmured, \u0026quot;that we have just lost control of the narrative.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Again,\u0026quot; Harry agreed."]},{"num":2,"origNum":2,"title":"The Syncope Symphony","wordCount":970,"paragraphs":["The squeals by the bay window faded into a breathless, teary-eyed silence. Hermione, Ginny, Luna, and Chloe wiped their eyes, straightened their robes (and dresses), and turned back toward the dining table.","They walked in formation—a phalanx of glowing, terrifying maternal energy.","The dining room was dead silent. Every fork was lowered. Every wine glass was suspended in mid-air.","Harry Potter looked at Hermione. He saw the flush on her cheeks. He saw the way her hand was instinctively resting on her stomach.","\u0026quot;Everything alright?\u0026quot; Harry asked, his voice wavering slightly. \u0026quot;Is it... did we forget an anniversary again?\u0026quot;","Hermione stopped at the head of the table. She looked at Ginny. Ginny nodded. She looked at Luna. Luna hummed. She looked at Chloe. Chloe beamed.","\u0026quot;We have an announcement,\u0026quot; Hermione said, her voice trembling with happy logic. \u0026quot;We have cross-referenced the dates. We have confirmed the symptoms. The data is irrefutable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Spit it out, Granger,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, though he was gripping the tablecloth. \u0026quot;You look like you’ve swallowed a Lumos charm.\u0026quot;","Ginny stepped forward. She slammed her hand on the table, rattling the silverware.","\u0026quot;We’re pregnant,\u0026quot; Ginny declared.","Ron blinked. \u0026quot;Who is?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;All of us, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna smiled dreamily. \u0026quot;It’s a Nargle infestation of the womb.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are all expecting,\u0026quot; Chloe clarified, grabbing Dudley’s hand. \u0026quot;At the same time.\u0026quot;","The silence that followed lasted exactly three seconds.","Then, The Management exploded.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Chaos of the Elders\u003c/strong\u003e","Molly Weasley let out a shriek that shattered a crystal goblet.","\u0026quot;ARTHUR!\u0026quot; Molly screamed, leaping from her chair with the agility of a teenager. \u0026quot;GET THE WOOL! I NEED WOOL! FOUR BLANKETS! FOUR SWEATERS! BOOTIES! I NEED TO START KNITTING NOW!\u0026quot;","She practically vaulted over the table to hug Ginny, then Hermione, then Luna, then Chloe, sobbing hysterically. \u0026quot;GRANDBABIES! AN ARMY OF THEM!\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley stood up, looking stunned and delighted. \u0026quot;A quartet?\u0026quot; he gasped. \u0026quot;A synchronized generation? Vernon! Do you realize the statistical probability?\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley was already in motion. He pulled a notebook from his pocket and clicked his pen furiously.","\u0026quot;Expansion!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, his eyes gleaming with the fire of a project manager. \u0026quot;We need a nursery wing! No, a nursery complex! Four cots! Bulk buying of nappies! The economies of scale on baby powder alone will be astronomical!\u0026quot;","He pointed his pen at Lucius.","\u0026quot;Lucius! We need a trust fund structure! A consolidated asset portfolio for the next generation! Compound interest starts today!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy looked pale. He looked at Draco. He looked at the future of his quiet, dignified manor being overrun by four screaming infants.","Then, a slow, proud smile spread across his face.","\u0026quot;An heir,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;The Malfoy line continues.\u0026quot; He looked at the other girls. \u0026quot;And... allies. A cohort. Narcissa, we must commission a portrait. Immediately. Dobby! Champagne! No... Milk! Bring milk!\u0026quot;","Narcissa was already crying, holding Petunia’s hand.","\u0026quot;They will grow up together,\u0026quot; Petunia wept, dabbing her eyes with a napkin. \u0026quot;Just like... just like they should have.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We need to baby-proof the island,\u0026quot; Narcissa decided, her voice steeling with grandmotherly resolve. \u0026quot;Padding on the marble. Rounded corners on the tables. Lucius, put the peacocks in a sanctuary; toddlers pull feathers.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Silence of the Lambs\u003c/strong\u003e","While The Management was dissolving into a frenzy of knitting, financial planning, and safety protocols, the four husbands sat frozen in their chairs.","They had not moved. They had not spoken. They were processing.","Harry Potter stared at a candle.","I defeated Voldemort, Harry thought. I hunted Horcruxes. I died and came back to life.","But I have never changed a diaper.","I am responsible for a human. A tiny, fragile human.","Oh god. I have to teach it to fly.","Ron Weasley was staring at a chicken leg.","A baby, Ron’s mind raced. Another Weasley. It’s going to be loud. It’s going to be hungry.","Wait. If Luna is having a baby... and I am the father...","Does that mean I have to share my food? For eighteen years?","And what if it sees Nargles?","Dudley Dursley looked at his massive hands.","A kid, Dudley panicked. A little Big D. What if it boxes? What if it has magic?","What if it punches me?","I need to buy a smaller punching bag.","Draco Malfoy was staring at Ginny.","A Malfoy-Weasley, Draco’s brain short-circuited. It will have red hair. It will have platinum hair.","It will be a Ginger Malfoy.","It will rule the world.","It will vomit on my silk robes.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Synchronization\u003c/strong\u003e","Slowly, as if choreographed by Dumbledore himself, the four men turned their heads to look at each other.","Harry’s face was white.","Ron’s face was green.","Draco’s face was grey.","Dudley’s face was red.","\u0026quot;Four?\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;At once?\u0026quot; Ron squeaked.","\u0026quot;Expensive,\u0026quot; Draco croaked.","\u0026quot;Help,\u0026quot; Dudley mumbled.","Their eyes rolled back in unison.","There was no staggering. There was no swaying. It was a precise, military-grade collapse.","\u003cstrong\u003eTHUD. THUD. THUD. THUD.\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry slumped forward, face-planting into his mashed potatoes.","Ron tipped backward, chair and all, hitting the rug with a crash.","Draco slid elegantly out of his chair, sliding under the table in a puddle of silk.","Dudley simply fell sideways like a felled tree, landing on the soft carpet.","The room went silent again.","Hermione looked at the unconscious fathers. She looked at Ginny.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Hermione sighed, picking up her water glass. \u0026quot;At least they synchronized the fainting. That bodes well for the playdates.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Ginny called out, stepping over Draco’s legs. \u0026quot;We need four Pepper-Up Potions! And maybe a pillow for the Ferret!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And pickles!\u0026quot; Luna added happily. \u0026quot;The baby wants pickles!\u0026quot;","As the house-elves swarmed the fallen heroes, Vernon Dursley looked down at his unconscious son and nephew.","\u0026quot;Lightweights,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, writing in his notebook. \u0026quot;Petunia, remind me to schedule \u0027Fatherhood Boot Camp\u0027. 0600 hours tomorrow. We start with diaper drills.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":3,"origNum":3,"title":"The Culinary Crimes Unit","wordCount":1197,"paragraphs":["Four months had passed since the \u0026quot;Syncope Symphony.\u0026quot; The initial shock of the quadruple pregnancy had faded, replaced by the grim reality of the second trimester. The morning sickness was gone. In its place, a new terror had risen across the United Kingdom.","The Cravings.","These were not normal cravings. These were alchemical disasters. These were flavor profiles that defied God, Merlin, and the Food Standards Agency.","Incident 1: Godric\u0027s Hollow","Subject: Hermione Granger-Potter","Craving: The Texture Paradox","The reconstructed cottage at Godric\u0027s Hollow was usually a sanctuary of peace and tea1. But this morning, it smelled like a vinegar factory had exploded inside a dairy.","Harry Potter walked into the kitchen, rubbing sleep from his eyes. He found his wife sitting at the rustic wooden table, surrounded by books on magical neonatal care.","She was eating a bowl of porridge. But the porridge was… lumpy. And neon orange.","\u0026quot;Mione,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice tight. \u0026quot;What… what is in the oats?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s texture, Harry,\u0026quot; Hermione explained matter-of-factly, not looking up from her book. \u0026quot;The porridge is too soft. I needed a counter-balance.\u0026quot;","Harry looked closer. Mixed into the warm, milky oats were…","\u0026quot;Are those… Cheetos?\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;The Muggle cheese puffs Dudley sent us?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Wotsits,\u0026quot; Hermione corrected, stirring the melting, neon-orange snacks into the grey sludge. \u0026quot;And sliced gherkins. For the acidity.\u0026quot;","Harry gagged. He physically gagged.","\u0026quot;You are eating cheesy, pickled porridge,\u0026quot; Harry said, gripping the counter for support.","\u0026quot;It’s efficient,\u0026quot; Hermione said, taking a bite. The crunch echoed in the silent kitchen. \u0026quot;Carbohydrates, dairy, electrolytes from the pickle brine. It covers all the food groups.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It covers the definition of a war crime,\u0026quot; Harry muttered.","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t judge me,\u0026quot; Hermione pointed her spoon at him. \u0026quot;The baby wants salt and mush. Now, pass the hot sauce. It needs a kick.\u0026quot;","Incident 2: Malfoy Manor","Subject: Ginny Malfoy","Craving: The Sweet Heat","Draco Malfoy walked into the pristine, marble-floored dining room of Malfoy Manor. He was dressed for the Ministry, looking sharp and professional.","Lucius Malfoy was already seated, reading the \u003cem\u003eDaily Prophet\u003c/em\u003e with a look of extreme distress. Narcissa was staring at her daughter-in-law with morbid fascination.","Ginny was sitting at the head of the table (a spot she had claimed during the \u0026quot;Merger\u0026quot;). She was wearing one of Draco’s silk shirts. She was holding a chocolate éclair.","\u0026quot;Good morning, Red,\u0026quot; Draco said, eyeing the pastry. \u0026quot;That looks… acceptable. A standard breakfast pastry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was a bit dry,\u0026quot; Ginny admitted. \u0026quot;So I made a dipping sauce.\u0026quot;","Draco looked at the silver gravy boat next to her.","\u0026quot;Chocolate sauce?\u0026quot; Draco asked hopefully.","\u0026quot;Gravy,\u0026quot; Ginny beamed. \u0026quot;Beef gravy. With extra pepper. And a dash of Mint Sauce.\u0026quot;","Lucius made a small, high-pitched noise and hid behind his newspaper.","Draco stopped breathing. He watched, horrified, as his wife took the cream-filled, chocolate-topped pastry and dunked it deep into the salty, meaty, minty sludge.","She took a bite. Cream, chocolate, choux pastry, beef gravy, and mint vinegar mixed in her mouth.","\u0026quot;Mmm,\u0026quot; Ginny moaned. \u0026quot;Salty-sweet-savory. It’s the perfect balance.\u0026quot;","Draco turned a shade of pale usually reserved for the undead.","\u0026quot;Dobby!\u0026quot; Draco choked out.","CRACK.","\u0026quot;Master Draco?\u0026quot; Dobby appeared, wearing a chef\u0027s hat.","\u0026quot;Bring me a bucket,\u0026quot; Draco ordered, staring at the ceiling. \u0026quot;And a Memory Charm. I need to un-see the dipping.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dobby also made Mistress Ginny a sardine smoothie!\u0026quot; Dobby chirped happily. \u0026quot;With whipped cream!\u0026quot;","Draco walked out of the room. \u0026quot;I am going to work. I may never come back.\u0026quot;","Incident 3: The Burrow","Subject: Luna Weasley","Craving: The Chromatic Aberration","Ron Weasley was a man who loved food. He respected food2. He believed in the sanctity of a good meal.","He was currently standing in the kitchen of the Burrow, staring at his wife’s plate with tears in his eyes. Molly Weasley was at the stove, pretending to be very busy with the washing up so she didn\u0027t have to look.","\u0026quot;Luna,\u0026quot; Ron whispered. \u0026quot;Love. My moon and stars. What is that?\u0026quot;","Luna smiled dreamily. She was wearing her paint-splattered overalls.","\u0026quot;It’s a salad, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna hummed.","\u0026quot;Salad implies vegetables,\u0026quot; Ron pointed out. \u0026quot;That is… pink fluff.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s cotton candy,\u0026quot; Luna explained. \u0026quot;Wrapped around Brussels sprouts. And dipped in English mustard.\u0026quot;","Ron looked at the plate. The green sprouts were encased in a cocoon of pink spun sugar, then slathered in bright yellow mustard.","\u0026quot;The colors are very stimulating for the baby,\u0026quot; Luna said, popping one into her mouth. \u0026quot;It teaches them about the spectrum.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It teaches them about indigestion!\u0026quot; Ron cried. \u0026quot;Luna, sugar and mustard? It’s… it’s chemically unstable!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Nargles love it,\u0026quot; Luna offered him one. \u0026quot;Try it, Ronald. It tastes like a confusing circus.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t,\u0026quot; Ron whimpered, backing away. \u0026quot;I have a weak constitution. I’ll just… I’ll have toast. Plain toast. Outside.\u0026quot;","Incident 4: Little Whinging","Subject: Chloe Dursley","Craving: The Heavyweight Champion","A few streets away from Number Four, in a sensible semi-detached house, Dudley Dursley sat at his kitchen table. He was a big man. He had eaten raw eggs for training. He had eaten school dinners.","But he was struggling.","Chloe sat opposite him. She was eating a sandwich.","But the bread wasn\u0027t bread.","\u0026quot;Are those… Pop-Tarts?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, his voice trembling.","\u0026quot;Strawberry frosted,\u0026quot; Chloe confirmed.","\u0026quot;And inside?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Tuna mayo,\u0026quot; Chloe said happily. \u0026quot;And crushed Oreos for texture.\u0026quot;","She took a huge bite. The strawberry frosting mixed with the fish and the chocolate cookies.","Dudley looked at his protein shake. He looked at his wife. He thought of his father’s lectures on structural integrity.","\u0026quot;Is it… good?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, trying to be supportive.","\u0026quot;It’s amazing,\u0026quot; Chloe said. \u0026quot;Do you want a bite?\u0026quot;","Dudley remembered Vernon’s advice: \u003cem\u003eA Dursley never backs down from a challenge.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Sure,\u0026quot; Dudley said bravely.","He took a bite.","His taste buds screamed. His brain short-circuited. Strawberry. Fish. Chocolate. Mayonnaise.","He chewed. He swallowed. He forced a smile.","\u0026quot;Bold flavor profile,\u0026quot; Dudley wheezed, his face turning green. \u0026quot;Very… distinct.\u0026quot;","He stood up.","\u0026quot;I’m going for a run,\u0026quot; Dudley announced. \u0026quot;A long run. Maybe to Scotland.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Summit\u003c/strong\u003e","That evening, the four husbands met at the Leaky Cauldron. They sat in a dark corner booth. They did not order beer. They ordered water.","They looked like war veterans.","\u0026quot;Gravy,\u0026quot; Draco whispered into his hands. \u0026quot;She dipped a pastry in beef gravy. In my dining room. My father is weeping in the library.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cheetos in porridge,\u0026quot; Harry murmured, staring at the table. \u0026quot;The milk turned orange, Draco. It turned orange.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sprouts and cotton candy,\u0026quot; Ron shuddered. \u0026quot;The crunch… the squish… the mustard.\u0026quot;","Dudley stared at the wall. \u0026quot;Tuna. Pop. Tarts.\u0026quot;","The wizards looked at the Muggle.","\u0026quot;You win,\u0026quot; Ron said softly. \u0026quot;That is the worst thing I have ever heard.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My dad says it’s just \u0027fusion cuisine\u0027,\u0026quot; Dudley said hollowly. \u0026quot;He says we have to support the \u0027supply chain\u0027 of their appetites.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Your father,\u0026quot; Draco said, \u0026quot;has a stomach made of cast iron. We are mere mortals.\u0026quot;","Harry raised his glass of water.","\u0026quot;To the next five months,\u0026quot; Harry toasted grimly.","\u0026quot;May we survive the menu,\u0026quot; Draco agreed.","\u0026quot;And may the babies have normal taste buds,\u0026quot; Ron prayed.","They drank in silence, terrified of what dinner might bring."]},{"num":4,"origNum":4,"title":"The Splash Zone","wordCount":926,"paragraphs":["The dining room of Malfoy Manor was quiet, save for the rhythmic \u003cem\u003eclink\u003c/em\u003e of silver against china and the heavy, labored breathing of four women who looked ready to explode.","Eight months had passed since the Great Jump. The Alliance was heavy with child. The decision to remain ignorant of the sex and number of the babies had seemed romantic at the time. Now, staring down the barrel of imminent parenthood, it felt like a tactical error.","The Timeline","Hermione Granger-Potter was one week overdue. She was no longer walking; she was waddling with the fury of a woman betrayed by biology. She had read every book on magical obstetrics and was currently glaring at Harry as if he were personally responsible for the calendar.","Chloe Dursley was \u003cstrong\u003etwo days overdue\u003c/strong\u003e. She sat in a chair reinforced with cushioning charms, eating ice chips and looking like she wanted to punch the concept of time.","Luna Weasley was \u003cstrong\u003eone week away\u003c/strong\u003e from her due date. She was humming to her stomach, wearing a dress made entirely of elastic.","Ginny Malfoy still had \u003cstrong\u003etwo weeks\u003c/strong\u003e to go. She was smug about this fact, enjoying her mobility while the others groaned.","The Feast of Induction","The main table was laden with the usual Malfoy excellence—Roast Pheasant, Truffle Mash, Glazed Carrots.","But in the corner, set apart like a quarantine zone, was the \u003cstrong\u003e\u0026quot;Induction Station.\u0026quot;\u003c/strong\u003e","This table was not for the faint of heart. It was stocked with foods rumored by Muggles and Wizards alike to kickstart labor.","Hermione sat before a plate that defied culinary logic.","\u0026quot;Pineapple,\u0026quot; Hermione growled, stabbing a chunk of fruit. \u0026quot;Fresh. Contains bromelain. It softens the cervix.\u0026quot;","She dipped the pineapple into a bowl of Balsamic Vinegar mixed with crushed Ghost Peppers.","\u0026quot;And the capsaicin,\u0026quot; she added, taking a bite that made Harry’s eyes water from three feet away. \u0026quot;Stimulates the system. Get. It. Out.\u0026quot;","Chloe was attacking a bowl of \u0026quot;The Dursley Detonator\u0026quot;—a curry Vernon had commissioned from Chef Kumar specifically for this moment. It was red. It was bubbling.","\u0026quot;It hurts,\u0026quot; Chloe whispered, spooning the lava into her mouth. \u0026quot;But if it makes him come out, I’ll eat the bowl too.\u0026quot;","The Incident","Dinner wound down. The husbands were terrified.","\u0026quot;She’s looking at me like I’m a Dementor,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Draco.","\u0026quot;Ginny is kicking me under the table,\u0026quot; Draco winced. \u0026quot;And she’s not even due yet.\u0026quot;","Hermione pushed her chair back. It made a screeching sound on the marble.","\u0026quot;I need more pineapple,\u0026quot; she announced.","\u0026quot;I’ll come with you,\u0026quot; Ginny said, struggling to stand. \u0026quot;I want the pickles.\u0026quot;","They waddled to the Induction Station. Hermione reached for the tongs.","She froze.","She dropped the tongs.","She looked down at her feet. A clear puddle was spreading rapidly across the priceless Malfoy marble.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Hermione said, her voice strangely calm. \u0026quot;Harry.\u0026quot;","Harry jumped up. \u0026quot;What? What is it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My water,\u0026quot; Hermione stated. \u0026quot;It has broken.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eSPLASH.\u003c/strong\u003e","Three feet away, Chloe gasped. She looked down.","\u0026quot;Me too!\u0026quot; Chloe yelled. \u0026quot;Dudley! It’s happening!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eSPLASH.\u003c/strong\u003e","Luna, sitting at the table, blinked. She looked at the puddle forming under her chair.","\u0026quot;Oh, look,\u0026quot; Luna hummed. \u0026quot;The baby wants to join the party. My water has gone, Ronald.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eSPLASH.\u003c/strong\u003e","Ginny, standing next to Hermione, suddenly doubled over.","\u0026quot;You have got to be joking,\u0026quot; Ginny groaned. \u0026quot;I have two weeks! I’m not ready! I haven\u0027t packed the bag!\u0026quot;","Fluid hit the floor.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","For one second, there was absolute, stunned silence.","Four women. Four puddles. Four labors beginning at the exact same second.","Then, \u003cstrong\u003eThe Management\u003c/strong\u003e activated.","Vernon Dursley roared like a lion.","\u0026quot;GO TIME!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed, flipping his table. \u0026quot;Code Red! Transport! Dudley, get the car! Arthur, secure the perimeter! We are moving out!\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley shrieked with joy and terror.","\u0026quot;HOT WATER!\u0026quot; Molly screamed, running toward the kitchen. \u0026quot;I NEED TOWELS! AND BLANKETS! AND MAYBE A SEDATIVE FOR ARTHUR!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy stared at the floor.","\u0026quot;My marble,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, looking at the amniotic flood. \u0026quot;Antique Italian marble. Dobby... bring the mop. And the Healers. Bring St. Mungo\u0027s to us!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eNarcissa Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e was instantly at Ginny’s side, casting stabilizing charms. \u0026quot;Breathe, darling. Lucius, stop worrying about the floor! We are having heirs!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Husbands\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter went into Auror mode.","\u0026quot;Hermione!\u0026quot; he shouted, rushing to her and scooping her up (struggling slightly with the weight). \u0026quot;I’ve got you! Don\u0027t panic! I read the book! Breathing! Hee-hee-hoo!\u0026quot;","Dudley Dursley looked at Chloe. He looked at the door. He looked at his father.","\u0026quot;Dad!\u0026quot; Dudley yelled. \u0026quot;Do I drive fast? Or safe?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;FAST AND SAFE!\u0026quot; Vernon screamed. \u0026quot;DRIVE LIKE YOU STOLE IT, SON!\u0026quot;","Ron Weasley was staring at Luna’s puddle.","\u0026quot;Three weeks early?\u0026quot; Ron squeaked. \u0026quot;Luna, the bag isn\u0027t packed! I haven\u0027t finished the crib! I haven\u0027t eaten dessert!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Nargles don\u0027t wait for pudding, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna smiled, clutching her stomach.","Draco Malfoy stood paralyzed. He looked at Ginny, who was gripping the table and breathing through a contraction.","He looked at the puddle on his floor.","He looked at Harry holding Hermione.","He looked at Ron panicking.","Draco’s eyes rolled back.","\u0026quot;Four,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;At once. It’s a conspiracy.\u0026quot;","He swayed. He didn\u0027t faint—he was a Malfoy, after all. But he did sit down very abruptly on the floor, right in the splash zone.","\u0026quot;Someone,\u0026quot; Draco said calmly from the wet floor. \u0026quot;Get me a Firewhisky. I am about to become a father. And my shoes are ruined.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;MOVE!\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley shouted, leading the charge out the door. \u0026quot;TO THE HOSPITAL! CONVOY FORMATION! WE HAVE BABIES TO CATCH!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":5,"origNum":5,"title":"The Malfoy Maternity Ward","wordCount":964,"paragraphs":["\u0026quot;STOP!\u0026quot;","The command didn\u0027t come from Vernon Dursley. It didn\u0027t come from a wizard. It came from the top of the marble staircase.","Narcissa Malfoy stood there, looking down at the chaotic scene of wet floors, panicked husbands, and waddling wives. She held up a single, pale hand.","\u0026quot;Nobody,\u0026quot; Narcissa announced, her voice calm and imperious, \u0026quot;is going to a hospital.\u0026quot;","Vernon skidded to a halt, nearly dropping his car keys. \u0026quot;Narcissa! This is a medical emergency! We need sterile environments! We need professionals! We cannot deliver four babies on a rug!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My rugs are antique, Vernon,\u0026quot; Narcissa replied smoothly, descending the stairs. \u0026quot;And I have no intention of ruining them further. That is why we are not going to St. Mungo\u0027s. And we are certainly not going to a Muggle hospital in London traffic.\u0026quot;","She reached the bottom step and looked at the group.","\u0026quot;We are going,\u0026quot; Narcissa pointed a manicured finger down the long corridor to the left, \u0026quot;to the West Wing.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reveal\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;The West Wing?\u0026quot; Draco blinked, wiping sweat from his forehead. \u0026quot;Mother, the West Wing is guest suites and the gallery. It’s full of portraits of ancestors who judge people.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not anymore,\u0026quot; Narcissa smiled—a smile of supreme, logistical triumph that rivaled even Vernon’s best project management face.","She clapped her hands.","The double doors to the West Wing swung open.","A team of people marched out. But they weren\u0027t Death Eaters.","Half of them were wearing the lime-green robes of St. Mungo\u0027s Healers, carrying potions and wands.","The other half were wearing pristine white coats, carrying stethoscopes and medical bags. They were Muggles.","\u0026quot;I have hired them,\u0026quot; Narcissa explained casually. \u0026quot;The Head Healer of the Maternity Ward at St. Mungo\u0027s. And Dr. Thompson, the Chief of Obstetrics from St. Thomas\u0027 Hospital.\u0026quot;","Chloe Dursley gasped, clutching her stomach. \u0026quot;Dr. Thompson? He’s... he’s the Queen’s doctor. How did you...?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Malfoy name still opens doors, my dear,\u0026quot; Narcissa said softly. \u0026quot;And Galleons convert quite favorably to Pounds.\u0026quot;","She turned to the group.","\u0026quot;I have converted the entire wing. Four suites. Fully equipped. Magical monitoring for the witches. Muggle technology for Chloe. Pain relief potions. Epidurals. It is a state-of-the-art facility. And it is thirty seconds away.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","Silence descended on the hall, broken only by the drip-drip-drip of amniotic fluid on the marble.","Vernon Dursley stared at Narcissa. He looked at the team of doctors. He looked at the hallway.","He slowly lowered his car keys.","\u0026quot;In-house,\u0026quot; Vernon whispered reverently. \u0026quot;Zero transit time. Immediate access to specialists. Integrated magical and non-magical care.\u0026quot;","He looked at Narcissa with eyes full of tears.","\u0026quot;Narcissa,\u0026quot; Vernon choked out. \u0026quot;That is the most efficient contingency plan I have ever seen. You are... you are a Titan of Industry.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Vernon,\u0026quot; Narcissa dipped her head.","Molly Weasley burst into fresh tears. \u0026quot;Oh, Cissy! You did this? You prepared all this?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I had a feeling,\u0026quot; Narcissa admitted, looking at the four pregnant women. \u0026quot;And... I did not want my grandchildren born in a waiting room.\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy was looking at the Muggle doctors. One of them was checking a beeping machine.","\u0026quot;Electronics,\u0026quot; Lucius muttered, clutching his cane. \u0026quot;In the Manor. The ancestors will be spinning in their frames.\u0026quot; He paused, then sighed. \u0026quot;But... it is convenient. Well done, Narcissa.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Disbursement\u003c/strong\u003e","Narcissa clapped her hands again. \u0026quot;Right. Movement. Now.\u0026quot;","She pointed to the Healers.","\u0026quot;Suite 1: The Potter Suite. Hermione and Harry. Healer Smethwyck, you are with them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Suite 2: The Weasley Suite. Ron and Luna. Healer Pye, that is you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Suite 3: The Malfoy Suite. Draco and Ginny. I shall be supervising.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Suite 4: The Dursley Suite. Dudley and Chloe. Dr. Thompson, your team is ready. The electricity generator Arthur rigged up is fully operational.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Generator?\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley perked up from the back. \u0026quot;It’s working? The spark plugs held?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is humming beautifully, Arthur,\u0026quot; Narcissa assured him.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Walk\u003c/strong\u003e","The husbands mobilized. The panic was gone, replaced by purpose.","Harry grabbed Hermione’s hand. \u0026quot;Come on, Mione. The Library Cottage is nice, but I bet Narcissa has better pillows.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And doctors,\u0026quot; Hermione breathed, wincing as a contraction hit. \u0026quot;I love your aunt-in-law, Harry. I really do.\u0026quot;","Ron guided Luna. \u0026quot;Do you think the Nargles will follow us to the West Wing?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, no,\u0026quot; Luna smiled serenely, though she was squeezing his hand hard. \u0026quot;Narcissa has put up Anti-Nargle wards. She told me. It’s very thoughtful.\u0026quot;","Dudley lifted Chloe into his arms—bridal style—effortlessly. \u0026quot;We got the Queen’s doctor, Chlo. You’re basically royalty.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Just get me the drugs, Big D,\u0026quot; Chloe gritted out. \u0026quot;All of them.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy offered his arm to Ginny. He looked at his mother. He saw the planning, the expense, and the love that had gone into turning his ancestral home—a place of cold pureblood history—into a sanctuary for his mixed, chaotic family.","\u0026quot;Mother,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice thick.","\u0026quot;Go,\u0026quot; Narcissa ordered gently. \u0026quot;Make me a grandmother.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Doors Close\u003c/strong\u003e","The four couples walked down the corridor of the West Wing. The portraits on the walls—old wizards and witches who had once sneered at Muggles—watched in silence as the team of doctors and healers rushed past.","Harry and Hermione turned into the first door.","Ron and Luna took the second.","Draco and Ginny took the third.","Dudley and Chloe took the fourth.","Click. Click. Click. Click.","The four doors shut simultaneously.","In the hallway, The Management stood alone.","Vernon Dursley wiped his forehead with a handkerchief. He looked at Lucius.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Vernon said, exhaling a breath he’d held for twenty minutes. \u0026quot;The assets are secure. The facility is operational.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot; Lucius agreed, looking at the closed doors. \u0026quot;Now... Dobby?\u0026quot;","CRACK.","\u0026quot;Yes, Master Lucius?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Bring the Firewhisky,\u0026quot; Lucius ordered. \u0026quot;And the Brandy. And perhaps... the tea. It is going to be a long night.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":6,"origNum":6,"title":"The Quickest Round","wordCount":521,"paragraphs":["The West Wing of Malfoy Manor was usually a place of hushed whispers and art appreciation. Tonight, it was a battleground of biology.","Behind the door of Suite 4, the \u0026quot;Dursley Suite,\u0026quot; things were proceeding with alarming efficiency.","Dr. Thompson, the Royal Obstetrician, was checking a monitor. He looked calm. In fact, he looked bored.","\u0026quot;Push, Mrs. Dursley,\u0026quot; he said politely. \u0026quot;Just a little one.\u0026quot;","Chloe Dursley, lying on the bed surrounded by fluffy pillows and humming Muggle machines, took a deep breath. She didn\u0027t scream. She didn\u0027t curse. She engaged her core.","\u0026quot;One... two... three,\u0026quot; Chloe whispered, her face turning pink.","Dudley was holding her hand. He looked terrified. \u0026quot;Breathe, Chlo! Remember the Lamaze! Remember Mum\u0027s pelvic floor drills!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am remembering!\u0026quot; Chloe gasped. \u0026quot;Dudley, stop squeezing my hand, you\u0027ll break it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sorry!\u0026quot; Dudley yelped, letting go.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Dr. Thompson announced, looking over his spectacles. \u0026quot;One more push, please. The head is... well, it\u0027s practically falling out. Excellent muscle tone, Mrs. Dursley.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s the squats,\u0026quot; Chloe gritted out. \u0026quot;Petunia made me do a hundred squats a day.\u0026quot;","She pushed. It wasn\u0027t a roar of agony. It was a grunt of effort, like lifting a heavy box.","\u003cstrong\u003eWAAAAAAH!\u003c/strong\u003e","The sound cut through the room—a high, clear cry of indignation.","Dr. Thompson caught the baby with the practiced ease of a cricket player catching a slow ball.","\u0026quot;And... we are done,\u0026quot; the doctor smiled. \u0026quot;Congratulations. It is a boy.\u0026quot;","Dudley stared. He looked at the clock.","\u0026quot;An hour?\u0026quot; Dudley whispered. \u0026quot;It took an hour? I thought it took days! I brought snacks! I brought a pillow!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Your wife is very fit, Mr. Dursley,\u0026quot; Dr. Thompson said, wrapping the baby in a blanket. \u0026quot;Efficiency at its finest.\u0026quot;","He handed the bundle to Chloe. Chloe looked down. The baby was pink, squirming, and had a tuft of blonde fuzz on his head.","\u0026quot;Hi,\u0026quot; Chloe whispered, touching his cheek. \u0026quot;Hi there.\u0026quot;","Dudley leaned over. He looked at his son. Tears instantly filled his eyes.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s... he\u0027s perfect,\u0026quot; Dudley choked out. \u0026quot;Look at his fists. He\u0027s already got a guard up.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What shall we call him?\u0026quot; Chloe asked, looking up at her husband.","Dudley didn\u0027t hesitate. He had discussed this with his parents. He wanted a name that was strong, classic, and decidedly normal.","\u0026quot;Thomas,\u0026quot; Dudley said. \u0026quot;Thomas Vernon Dursley.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Tommy,\u0026quot; Chloe smiled. \u0026quot;I like it.\u0026quot;","Dudley kissed her forehead. Then he kissed the baby\u0027s head.","He walked to the door. He opened it.","The hallway was empty except for The Management, who were pacing nervously.","\u0026quot;Dudley?\u0026quot; Petunia asked, her hand flying to her throat. \u0026quot;Is everything...?\u0026quot;","Dudley grinned. He gave a thumbs up.","\u0026quot;It\u0027s a boy!\u0026quot; Dudley announced. \u0026quot;Thomas! And Chloe is eating a sandwich!\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley let out a roar of triumph.","\u0026quot;One hour!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered, checking his watch. \u0026quot;A Dursley record! Efficiency in the womb! Petunia, the squats worked!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, my grandson!\u0026quot; Petunia wept, hugging Vernon.","Lucius Malfoy looked at his pocket watch. \u0026quot;Impressive turnover,\u0026quot; he admitted to Narcissa. \u0026quot;The Muggles are setting a high bar.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We must hope the witches can keep up,\u0026quot; Narcissa murmured, looking anxiously at the other three doors."]},{"num":7,"origNum":7,"title":"The Humming Birth","wordCount":513,"paragraphs":["Thirty minutes after the triumphant arrival of Thomas Dursley, a very different sound drifted into the hallway from Suite 2.","It wasn\u0027t a scream. It wasn\u0027t a grunt of effort. It was a melody.","Inside the \u0026quot;Weasley Suite,\u0026quot; Luna Lovegood was lying on the bed, looking at the ceiling. She wasn\u0027t sweating. She wasn\u0027t gripping the sheets. She was humming a tune that sounded suspiciously like \u003cem\u003eWeasley is Our King\u003c/em\u003e, but slowed down to a lullaby tempo.","Ron Weasley was pacing.","\u0026quot;Luna,\u0026quot; Ron said, wringing his hands. \u0026quot;Are you... are you sure you don\u0027t want the potion? The Healer said it numbs the pain.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The pain is just the baby knocking, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna smiled, pausing her song. \u0026quot;If I numb it, she won\u0027t know I\u0027m home.\u0026quot;","Healer Pye, a wizard who had seen everything from dragon bites to Spattergroit, looked bewildered.","\u0026quot;Mrs. Weasley,\u0026quot; Healer Pye said tentatively. \u0026quot;The contractions are... well, they are peaking. You should be in agony.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Nargles are massaging my lower back,\u0026quot; Luna explained serenely. \u0026quot;And the humming helps the baby find the exit. It’s a sonic beacon.\u0026quot;","She took a deep breath and resumed humming. \u003cem\u003eHum-hum-hummmm.\u003c/em\u003e","Ron looked at the Healer. \u0026quot;Is she... is she okay?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Her vitals are perfect,\u0026quot; Healer Pye admitted, checking a floating orb. \u0026quot;It is unorthodox, Mr. Weasley, but she seems to be... vibrating the baby out.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Ron gulped. \u0026quot;Okay. Keep humming, Luna. Sing it out.\u0026quot;","Luna closed her eyes. Her humming grew louder, resonating in the room.","\u0026quot;Here she comes,\u0026quot; Luna said calmly.","\u0026quot;Push!\u0026quot; Healer Pye ordered.","Luna didn\u0027t push in the traditional sense. She hit a high note.","\u003cstrong\u003eHMMMMMMMM!\u003c/strong\u003e","The magic in the room seemed to shimmer. And then, with a soft slide and a small cry, the baby arrived.","Healer Pye caught the child, looking stunned.","\u0026quot;It’s a girl,\u0026quot; the Healer announced. \u0026quot;And she is... she is very calm.\u0026quot;","Ron rushed forward. He looked at his daughter. She had a tuft of Weasley-red hair, but her eyes, even squinting against the light, were wide and curious. She wasn\u0027t crying. She was looking around the room as if searching for invisible creatures.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, tears spilling over. \u0026quot;She’s here. She’s actually here.\u0026quot;","Luna sat up, taking the baby. She kissed the redhead.","\u0026quot;Hello,\u0026quot; Luna whispered. \u0026quot;I knew you were a girl. The moon told me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What’s her name?\u0026quot; Ron asked, stroking the baby\u0027s tiny hand.","\u0026quot;Pandora,\u0026quot; Luna said instantly. \u0026quot;After my mother. But we can call her Pan.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pandora Weasley,\u0026quot; Ron tested the name. \u0026quot;Pan. I love it.\u0026quot;","The door opened. Molly Weasley burst in, followed by Arthur.","\u0026quot;Is it...?\u0026quot; Molly gasped.","\u0026quot;A girl!\u0026quot; Ron shouted, beaming. \u0026quot;Pandora! And Luna sang her out!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sang her out?\u0026quot; Arthur asked, fascinated. \u0026quot;Like a siren?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Like a mother,\u0026quot; Luna smiled.","In the hallway, Lucius Malfoy leaned on his cane. \u0026quot;Singing,\u0026quot; he muttered. \u0026quot;Muggles doing squats. Witches singing. Is anyone going to give birth normally tonight?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Define normal, Lucius,\u0026quot; Narcissa smiled, listening to the soft cooing from the Weasley suite. \u0026quot;We are in a Manor full of Gryffindors. Normal left the building years ago.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":8,"origNum":8,"title":"The Viper\u0027s Strike","wordCount":633,"paragraphs":["The hallway outside Suite 3 was quiet for about an hour after Pandora\u0027s arrival. Then, the screaming started.","It wasn\u0027t the baby. It was Draco Malfoy.","\u0026quot;OW! OW! GINNY! THAT IS MY WRIST! I NEED THAT FOR WORK!\u0026quot;","Inside the \u0026quot;Malfoy Suite,\u0026quot; the atmosphere was significantly less serene than the humming birth of Luna Lovegood. Ginny Malfoy was not singing. She was not doing squats. She was gripping the bed rails with one hand and Draco’s forearm with the other, her face a mask of fierce, red-faced concentration.","\u0026quot;Shut up, Draco!\u0026quot; Ginny roared through a contraction. \u0026quot;Or I will break it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You \u003cem\u003eare\u003c/em\u003e breaking it!\u0026quot; Draco yelped, trying to pry her fingers off his expensive silk sleeve. \u0026quot;Mother! Help me! She\u0027s got a Beater\u0027s grip!\u0026quot;","Narcissa Malfoy, who was acting as the primary support (and enjoying it immensely), dabbed Ginny’s forehead with a cool cloth.","\u0026quot;Breathe through it, darling,\u0026quot; Narcissa soothed. \u0026quot;Ignore him. Men are fragile.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am not fragile!\u0026quot; Draco protested, wincing as Ginny squeezed again. \u0026quot;I am... structurally compromised! My circulation is cutting off!\u0026quot;","Healer Smethwyck (who had swapped in for Pye) looked at the monitor. \u0026quot;Fully dilated, Mrs. Malfoy. The baby is ready. On the next contraction, I need a big push.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You hear that, Ferret?\u0026quot; Ginny panted, sweat matting her red hair. \u0026quot;It’s time. And if you let go of my hand, I will hex you into a toad.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027m not letting go!\u0026quot; Draco said, tears of pain in his eyes. \u0026quot;I\u0027m just losing feeling in my fingers!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Push!\u0026quot; the Healer commanded.","Ginny pushed. She channeled every ounce of her Chaser strength, every bit of her Weasley temper. She screamed—a warrior\u0027s cry that echoed down the hall.","And as she screamed, she squeezed.","\u003cstrong\u003eCRACK.\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;GAH!\u0026quot; Draco shouted, dropping to his knees beside the bed. \u0026quot;My thumb! She dislocated my thumb!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Keep pushing!\u0026quot; Narcissa ordered, ignoring her son’s injury. \u0026quot;Focus, Ginny!\u0026quot;","One final, massive effort, and the baby slid into the Healer\u0027s hands.","A wail filled the room—loud, demanding, and immediate.","\u0026quot;It’s a girl!\u0026quot; Narcissa cried, clapping her hands.","Draco, clutching his throbbing hand, pulled himself up to look. The pain vanished.","The baby was tiny, furious, and covered in gunk. She had a tuft of platinum blonde hair, but when she blinked open her eyes, they weren\u0027t grey. They were a warm, vivid brown—pure Weasley eyes staring out from a Malfoy face.","\u0026quot;A girl,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, awestruck. \u0026quot;A Malfoy girl.\u0026quot;","Ginny collapsed back onto the pillows, panting. \u0026quot;Give her to me.\u0026quot;","The Healer handed the baby to Ginny. Ginny looked down.","\u0026quot;She’s perfect,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered. She looked at Draco, who was nursing his hand. \u0026quot;Sorry about the thumb.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Worth it,\u0026quot; Draco said, kissing Ginny’s sweaty forehead. \u0026quot;Totally worth it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;What shall we name her?\u0026quot; Ginny asked, tracing the baby\u0027s cheek.","\u0026quot;Cassiopeia,\u0026quot; Draco said softly. \u0026quot;The Queen. Cassie for short.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cassiopeia Malfoy,\u0026quot; Ginny tested it. \u0026quot;It sounds... regal. And a bit dangerous.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Like her mother,\u0026quot; Draco smiled.","The door opened. Lucius Malfoy peered in, looking terrified.","\u0026quot;Is it safe?\u0026quot; Lucius asked. \u0026quot;Is the screaming over?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Come in, Father,\u0026quot; Draco beamed, holding up his injured hand. \u0026quot;Meet your granddaughter. And call a Healer for my thumb.\u0026quot;","Lucius walked in. He looked at the baby. He looked at Ginny.","\u0026quot;A girl,\u0026quot; Lucius breathed. \u0026quot;The first Malfoy girl in three generations.\u0026quot;","He reached out a trembling finger. Cassie grabbed it with a surprisingly strong grip.","\u0026quot;She has the Weasley strength,\u0026quot; Lucius noted, wincing slightly.","\u0026quot;And the Malfoy attitude,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned.","In the hallway, Vernon Dursley checked his watch. \u0026quot;Three down! One to go! Hermione is lagging! Come on, Potter! Pick up the pace!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s not a race, Vernon,\u0026quot; Arthur Weasley said happily, handing out cigars. \u0026quot;But... Ron \u003cem\u003edid\u003c/em\u003e win.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Only because Luna sang!\u0026quot; Vernon argued. \u0026quot;Performance enhancing vocals! I\u0027m calling a stewards\u0027 inquiry!\u0026quot;"]},{"num":9,"origNum":9,"title":"The Faculty Inspection","wordCount":946,"paragraphs":["The West Wing hallway, now doubling as a nursery viewing gallery, was filled with the soft sounds of new life and the anxious shuffling of new parents.","Dudley and Chloe were cradling Thomas, who slept soundly, oblivious to the magical world surrounding him.","Ron and Luna were swaying with Pandora, who was wide awake, blinking at a portrait of a grumpy warlock.","Draco and Ginny were huddled over Cassie, who was currently gripping Draco\u0027s finger with a strength that suggested future Beater potential.","The double doors at the end of the corridor swung open with a flourish.","Albus Dumbledore swept in, his robes a celebratory azure blue that seemed to shimmer. He was flanked by Minerva McGonagall, crisp in her tartan, and Severus Snape, who wore his usual black but with an air of resigned tolerance. Behind them trailed the Marauders—Sirius Black, grinning widely; Remus Lupin, looking warm and paternal; and Nymphadora Tonks, whose hair had turned a soft, baby pink in solidarity.","\u0026quot;Reinforcements!\u0026quot; Sirius announced, clapping his hands. \u0026quot;We brought gifts. And noise. And possibly a unauthorized toy broomstick, but don\u0027t tell Molly.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Introductions\u003c/strong\u003e","The group descended on the new parents like a friendly swarm.","\u0026quot;Let me see him!\u0026quot; Sirius demanded, rushing to Dudley. He peered at Thomas. \u0026quot;Look at that. He\u0027s got the Dursley chin. Solid. Good for taking a punch, eh, Big D?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He\u0027s perfect,\u0026quot; Remus smiled, touching the baby\u0027s tiny hand with a gentle finger. \u0026quot;Welcome to the world, Thomas.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore was cooing over Pandora, his beard tickling her nose.","\u0026quot;A Weasley-Lovegood,\u0026quot; Dumbledore mused, his eyes twinkling furiously. \u0026quot;She will see things no one else does, Ronald. Filius will be delighted. She already looks like she\u0027s solving a riddle.\u0026quot;","McGonagall was inspecting Cassie with the critical eye of a Head of House assessing a new student. She looked at the platinum hair. She looked at the fierce brown eyes.","\u0026quot;She is... formidable,\u0026quot; McGonagall decided, adjusting her spectacles. \u0026quot;She looks like she\u0027s already planning a detention. Ten points to Slytherin. Or Gryffindor. It will be a battle for the Sorting Hat.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Potions Master\u0027s Blessing\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape hung back near the wall, arms crossed. He looked at the babies. He looked at the cooing adults.","\u0026quot;Noise,\u0026quot; Snape murmured to no one in particular. \u0026quot;So much noise. They are small. They are loud. They are... leaking fluids.\u0026quot;","Ginny, spotting him lurking, walked over. \u0026quot;Hold her, Professor.\u0026quot;","Snape recoiled as if she had offered him a Blast-Ended Skrewt. \u0026quot;I do not hold infants, Mrs. Malfoy. They are fragile. And sticky.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She\u0027s your god-granddaughter, Severus,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, stepping up beside Ginny. \u0026quot;It\u0027s protocol. You have to inspect the merchandise.\u0026quot;","Snape sighed—a long, suffering sound. He held out his arms stiffly. Ginny deposited Cassie into them.","Snape looked down. Cassie looked up. She frowned. Snape frowned back.","For a moment, they just stared at each other, two masters of the scowl.","\u0026quot;She has an acceptable glare,\u0026quot; Snape admitted, a corner of his mouth twitching. \u0026quot;She judges. Good.\u0026quot;","He handed her back to Ginny with impressive speed. \u0026quot;Do not let her brew anything until she is thirty. She has the look of someone who would add lacewing flies without measuring.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Missing Piece\u003c/strong\u003e","Tonks was bouncing Thomas (Dudley looked terrified she would drop him or morph into a clown to entertain him, but she was surprisingly gentle).","\u0026quot;Three down!\u0026quot; Tonks cheered. \u0026quot;Where\u0027s the last one? Where\u0027s Harry?\u0026quot;","The mood shifted instantly. The laughter died down. Everyone looked at the closed door of Suite 1.","\u0026quot;It\u0027s been hours,\u0026quot; Molly Weasley whispered, wringing her hands in her apron. \u0026quot;Four hours since Ginny finished. Why is it taking so long?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione reads too much,\u0026quot; Ron said nervously, rocking Pandora a little too fast. \u0026quot;She\u0027s probably arguing with the baby about the exit strategy. Or the lighting.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is... quiet,\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy noted, listening at the door with a frown. \u0026quot;Too quiet.\u0026quot;","Inside the Potter Suite, there was no screaming. There was no singing. There was only a tense, heavy silence that seemed to seep under the doorframe.","Slowly, the door handle turned.","Harry Potter stepped out.","He looked exhausted. His hair was wilder than usual, sticking up in sweaty spikes. His sleeves were rolled up, and his tie was gone. He looked pale, his green eyes wide and dark.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Petunia asked, stepping forward, her hand flying to her mouth. \u0026quot;Is she...?\u0026quot;","Harry leaned against the doorframe as if it were the only thing holding him up. He looked at the group of family and friends—holding their babies, celebrating life, bathed in the warm glow of the hallway lights.","\u0026quot;She\u0027s stuck,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;The baby is stuck. The Healer says... the Healer says it\u0027s complicated.\u0026quot;","The joy in the hallway evaporated instantly.","Draco handed Cassie to Narcissa without a word. Ron handed Pandora to Molly. Dudley handed Thomas to Chloe.","The three men walked over to Harry. They didn\u0027t ask questions. They stood around him, a wall of support—the Gryffindor, the Slytherin, and the Muggle.","\u0026quot;What do you need?\u0026quot; Draco asked, his voice low and serious.","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t know,\u0026quot; Harry said, rubbing his face. \u0026quot;I just... I\u0027m scared. She\u0027s in pain, and the magic isn\u0027t... it\u0027s taking too long.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore stepped forward. The twinkle was gone from his eyes, replaced by the sheer, radiating power of the greatest wizard alive.","\u0026quot;Fear not, Harry,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly. \u0026quot;We are here. And we have magic.\u0026quot;","He looked at the door, then at Snape and McGonagall.","\u0026quot;Shall we see what can be done?\u0026quot;","Harry nodded, looking small. He turned back into the room, leaving the celebration behind for the battle that was still being fought in the silence of Suite 1."]},{"num":10,"origNum":10,"title":"The Double Miracle","wordCount":1201,"paragraphs":["The silence in the West Wing hallway had stretched thin, taut as a piano wire. Four hours had passed since the faculty inspection. The other babies—Thomas, Pandora, and Cassie—had been taken to the nurseries to sleep, leaving the adults to pace the corridor in a vigil of worry.","Inside Suite 1, there were no screams. Hermione Granger did not scream. She worked.","She had banished everyone but Harry and Healer Smethwyck. She had refused the pain potions because she wanted to \u0026quot;monitor the contractions accurately.\u0026quot;","Harry sat by her head, wiping her brow with a cool cloth, whispering encouragement. He looked terrified.","\u0026quot;Almost there, Mrs. Potter,\u0026quot; Smethwyck said, his voice calm but urgent. \u0026quot;One more. Give me everything.\u0026quot;","Hermione gripped Harry’s hand so hard he felt a knuckle pop. She squeezed her eyes shut. She pushed with the same ferocity she had used to punch Draco Malfoy in Third Year, with the same determination that had kept them alive in a tent for months.","\u0026quot;WAAAAAAH!\u0026quot;","A cry. Loud, strong, and furious.","\u0026quot;It’s a boy!\u0026quot; Smethwyck announced, handing the baby to a floating self-swaddling blanket.","Harry let out a breath, laughing with relief. \u0026quot;A boy. Mione, we have a—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Wait,\u0026quot; Smethwyck said sharply. \u0026quot;Mrs. Potter. Stop smiling. We are not done.\u0026quot;","Hermione’s eyes snapped open. \u0026quot;What?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;There is another heartbeat,\u0026quot; Smethwyck said, checking the magical monitor. \u0026quot;And it is... impatient.\u0026quot;","Harry’s jaw dropped. \u0026quot;Another? But... we didn\u0027t check! We wanted a surprise!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Surprise,\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, clutching her stomach as a new wave hit her. \u0026quot;Oh, Harry. Twins.\u0026quot;","Ten minutes of chaotic, intense effort later, a second cry joined the first—this one softer, more musical, but just as alive.","\u0026quot;A girl,\u0026quot; Smethwyck smiled, wrapping the second bundle.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reveal\u003c/strong\u003e","The door to Suite 1 opened.","Harry Potter stood there. He was disheveled, sweat-soaked, and looked like he had been hit by a Bludger. But he was grinning so hard it looked painful.","\u0026quot;Well?\u0026quot; Sirius barked, jumping up from the floor.","Harry leaned against the doorframe. He held up two fingers.","\u0026quot;Two,\u0026quot; Harry croaked. \u0026quot;We have two.\u0026quot;","The hallway erupted. Molly Weasley shrieked. Arthur clapped Vernon on the back. Draco woke up from a nap on the bench.","\u0026quot;Come in,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;But... be quiet.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parade of Visitors\u003c/strong\u003e","They filed in. The room was dim, lit only by soft, floating orbs. Hermione was propped up against a mountain of pillows, looking exhausted but triumphant. In her arms, she held two bundles.","The Marauders were the first to reach the bedside.","Sirius looked at the boy in the blue blanket. He stopped dead.","The baby had a tuft of jet-black, messy hair that was already sticking up at the back. He had Harry’s nose. He had James’s chin.","\u0026quot;Prongs,\u0026quot; Sirius whispered, his hand shaking as he reached out. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s a clone. Harry, he looks more like you than \u003cem\u003eyou\u003c/em\u003e do.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He looks like James,\u0026quot; Remus corrected gently, smiling through his tears. \u0026quot;Hello, little Marauder.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We named him James,\u0026quot; Harry said softly. \u0026quot;James Sirius Potter.\u0026quot;","Sirius let out a wet, barking laugh, wiping his eyes. \u0026quot;No pressure, kid. No pressure at all.\u0026quot;","Then, Molly and Narcissa approached. They looked at the girl.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Molly breathed. \u0026quot;Look at her.\u0026quot;","The baby girl was awake. She had a fuzz of dark red hair—auburn, deep and rich.","\u0026quot;She’s beautiful,\u0026quot; Narcissa admitted, touching the baby\u0027s hand. \u0026quot;She has the Potter face structure, but the coloring...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the eyes,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Final Guests\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry stood up. He looked toward the door, where Petunia Dursley and Severus Snape were hanging back, unsure if they belonged in this inner circle of joy.","\u0026quot;Aunt Petunia,\u0026quot; Harry called softly. \u0026quot;Professor. Come here. You need to see her.\u0026quot;","Petunia walked forward slowly, clutching her handbag as if it were a shield. Snape followed, his face an unreadable mask, his black robes trailing silently on the floor.","They reached the bed.","Harry took the baby girl from Hermione. He turned to his aunt.","\u0026quot;Look,\u0026quot; Harry said.","Petunia looked down.","She saw the red hair. It was the exact shade of the autumn leaves in Cokeworth. It was the exact shade of the girl who used to swing on the playground swings.","Then, the baby blinked.","Green eyes. Almond-shaped, startlingly bright, brilliant green eyes stared up at Petunia.","Petunia gasped. She dropped her handbag. Her hands flew to her mouth to stifle a sob that was thirty years in the making.","\u0026quot;Lily,\u0026quot; Petunia whimpered. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s her. She came back.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Her name is Lily,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice thick. \u0026quot;Lily Luna Potter.\u0026quot;","Petunia reached out with trembling hands. \u0026quot;Can I?\u0026quot;","Harry placed the baby in her arms. Petunia cradled her niece’s granddaughter. She looked into the eyes of the sister she had lost, the sister she had envied, the sister she had loved too late.","\u0026quot;Hello, Lily,\u0026quot; Petunia wept, rocking her gently. \u0026quot;I’m your Auntie Tuney. And I am going to spoil you rotten. I promise.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley stood behind his wife, his hand on her shoulder, looking down at the baby with a softness that would have shocked his drill salesmen. \u0026quot;She’s a beauty, Pet. A real beauty.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Potions Master\u003c/strong\u003e","Then, it was Snape’s turn.","Petunia looked at Snape. She saw the way he was staring at the bundle in her arms. She saw the hunger, the grief, and the fear in his black eyes.","\u0026quot;Severus,\u0026quot; Petunia said gently, using his name for the first time in her life without a sneer. \u0026quot;She wants to meet you.\u0026quot;","Petunia stepped closer to him. She didn\u0027t hand him the baby—he looked too terrified to hold her—but she lowered the bundle so he could see.","Snape looked down.","He expected to see Potter. He expected to see James.","He saw the red hair. He saw the face shape.","And then, he saw the eyes.","The world seemed to stop for Severus Snape. The noise of the room faded. The war, the Dark Mark, the years of spying—it all dissolved.","He was looking at Lily Evans.","Not a memory. Not a ghost. A living, breathing piece of the only light he had ever known.","He stopped breathing. His hand raised slowly, involuntarily, trembling like a leaf in the wind.","He reached out. His long, pale finger hovered over the baby’s face.","Baby Lily reached up. Her tiny hand wrapped around Snape’s finger. She gripped it tight.","Snape let out a sound—a broken, ragged exhale that sounded like a soul shattering.","\u0026quot;Lily,\u0026quot; he whispered. It wasn\u0027t a question. It was a prayer.","A tear leaked from his eye, tracking through the harsh lines of his face, dripping off his nose, and landing on the blanket.","He didn\u0027t pull his finger away. He let her hold him. He looked at Harry.","\u0026quot;She is...\u0026quot; Snape’s voice failed. He cleared his throat. \u0026quot;She is... perfect.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She has her eyes,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, never looking away from the baby. \u0026quot;Always.\u0026quot;","He stood there, the Potions Master, the spy, the bravest man Harry knew, tethered to the world by the tiny grip of a baby girl with red hair and green eyes.","And in that moment, the debt was paid. The guilt was gone.","Severus Snape was finally, truly, free."]},{"num":11,"origNum":11,"title":"The Boy from Spinner\u0027s End and the Girl on the Swing","wordCount":1294,"paragraphs":["The West Wing was finally silent. The bustle of healers, the shouts of joy, and the chaotic parade of Weasleys had faded. In the nurseries, the four babies—Thomas, Pandora, Cassie, and the twins—slept the deep, innocent sleep of the newborn.","In the Potter Suite, Harry was sprawled on the chaise lounge, one arm hanging off the side, snoring softly. Hermione was asleep in the bed, a protective arm curled around the empty space where the bassinets had been before the babies were moved to the nursery.","Severus Snape stood on the stone balcony at the end of the corridor. The night air of Wiltshire was cool, carrying the scent of damp earth and the distant, manicured roses of the Malfoy gardens. He gripped the stone balustrade, his knuckles white.","He wasn\u0027t looking at the gardens. He was looking at the past.","He heard the soft click of the balcony door opening. He didn\u0027t turn. He knew the footsteps. They were light, hesitant, but familiar in a way that made his chest ache.","Petunia Dursley stepped out into the night. She pulled her cardigan tighter around herself. She walked up to the railing, standing a few feet away from him.","For a long time, neither of them spoke. They just watched the moon cast long shadows over the grounds.","\u0026quot;They are sleeping,\u0026quot; Petunia said finally, her voice quiet.","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Silence is a rare commodity in this family.\u0026quot;","Petunia let out a small, breathy laugh. \u0026quot;It is.\u0026quot;","She turned her head to look at his profile—the hooked nose, the severe lines, the curtain of black hair. She remembered him as a scrawny, mismatched boy in ill-fitting clothes, hiding behind a bush, watching her sister. She remembered calling him a freak. She remembered him making a branch fall on her.","\u0026quot;You held her,\u0026quot; Petunia said.","Snape stiffened. He didn\u0027t look at her. \u0026quot;I did.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Little Lily,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered the name like a benediction. \u0026quot;She... she is a carbon copy, Severus. It’s almost frightening.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is a ghost,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice rough. \u0026quot;A ghost given flesh.\u0026quot;","He finally turned to look at her. He saw the lines on her face, the grey in her hair. He saw the woman who had slammed the door in his face a thousand times in his mind.","\u0026quot;She has the eyes,\u0026quot; Snape said. \u0026quot;Potter... Harry... he has them. But on her? With that hair? It is... difficult to look at.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Petunia admitted. She leaned against the railing. \u0026quot;When I saw her... I felt like I was back in Cokeworth. By the river. Watching you two make flowers open and close.\u0026quot;","Snape flinched. \u0026quot;You were always watching from behind the tree, Tuney.\u0026quot;","The childhood nickname hung in the air between them—a relic of a time before magic and jealousy tore them apart.","\u0026quot;I was jealous,\u0026quot; Petunia said, her voice steady. \u0026quot;I told you that today. I wanted what you two had. Not the magic, really. But the... the belonging. You two belonged to a world I couldn\u0027t touch.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And so you punished her son,\u0026quot; Snape said. It wasn\u0027t an accusation; it was a statement of fact.","\u0026quot;And so did you,\u0026quot; Petunia countered gently.","Snape looked away, back to the dark horizon. \u0026quot;Yes. I did. I saw James Potter every time I looked at him. I saw the arrogance. The popularity. The man who stole her.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And I saw the sister who left me behind,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered. \u0026quot;I saw the reason my parents were so proud. I saw the danger that got her killed.\u0026quot;","She moved closer, sliding her hand along the stone rail until it was inches from his.","\u0026quot;We were both awful to him, Severus,\u0026quot; Petunia said. \u0026quot;We were two bitter, broken people, taking out our grief on a child who just wanted to be loved.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And yet,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice barely a whisper, \u0026quot;he forgave us. He ran across a beach to hold me up. He lets you knit him sweaters.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He has her heart,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled through fresh tears. \u0026quot;Lily’s heart. It was always too big for her body. She couldn\u0027t hold a grudge to save her life. And neither can he.\u0026quot;","Snape closed his eyes. He thought of the tiny hand gripping his finger. He thought of the feeling of peace that had washed over him when the baby looked at him.","\u0026quot;I promised her,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;By her body. I promised I would protect him. I spent seventeen years in the dark, doing terrible things, just to keep that promise.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You did,\u0026quot; Petunia said fiercely. \u0026quot;Vernon told me. About the war. About the spy work. You saved him, Severus. You saved my nephew when I couldn\u0027t.\u0026quot;","She reached out and placed her hand over his. Her skin was warm against his cold, pale hand.","\u0026quot;Thank you,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered. \u0026quot;From the sister who wasn\u0027t magical. Thank you for saving the last piece of her.\u0026quot;","Snape looked down at their joined hands—the Muggle and the Wizard, the two people who had loved Lily Evans most in the world, standing on a balcony in a house that used to hunt their kind.","He turned his hand over and squeezed hers.","\u0026quot;You gave him a home,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice thick. \u0026quot;Dumbledore told me. The blood wards. They only worked because you took him in. You sealed the bond. You kept him alive, Petunia. Just as much as I did.\u0026quot;","Petunia let out a sob. \u0026quot;I tried to stamp it out of him. The magic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It didn\u0027t work,\u0026quot; Snape said, a ghost of a smirk touching his lips. \u0026quot;He is relentlessly magical. And relentlessly Potter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is,\u0026quot; Petunia laughed, wiping her eyes. \u0026quot;He drives Vernon mad with the \u0027apparating\u0027 in the kitchen.\u0026quot;","They stood in silence for a moment, the bond of shared grief finally healing into something like friendship.","\u0026quot;Do you think...\u0026quot; Snape started, then hesitated. \u0026quot;Do you think she knows? About the name?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lily Luna,\u0026quot; Petunia said. \u0026quot;Oh, she knows, Severus. She was there today. I saw her. She knows that her daughter carries her name. And she knows that you... that you are part of this family now.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at the closed door of the nursery suite. He thought of the red-headed baby sleeping inside.","\u0026quot;I am not a grandfather,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, trying to regain his composure. \u0026quot;I am... a distant, terrifying uncle.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You are the man she held onto,\u0026quot; Petunia corrected. \u0026quot;You are the one she chose to grip. You don\u0027t get to be distant anymore, Severus. You’re trapped. Just like Vernon.\u0026quot;","Snape sighed, but it was a light sound. \u0026quot;Vernon. The man who tried to feed me \u0027Biscuits and Gravy\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He likes you,\u0026quot; Petunia smiled. \u0026quot;He says you have \u0027grit\u0027. And good calves.\u0026quot;","Snape snorted. \u0026quot;The world has gone mad, Tuney.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Petunia agreed, looking at the stars. \u0026quot;But it’s a good madness.\u0026quot;","She patted his hand and stepped back.","\u0026quot;I should go back to Vernon. He’s probably dreaming of crib assembly instructions.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Goodnight, Petunia,\u0026quot; Snape said softly.","\u0026quot;Goodnight, Severus.\u0026quot;","She walked back to the door. Before she left, she turned.","\u0026quot;You should come in tomorrow morning,\u0026quot; Petunia said. \u0026quot;For breakfast. Vernon is planning something involving \u0027waffles\u0027. And... Harry will want you there. To hold the baby again.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at the moon. He thought of the green eyes.","\u0026quot;I will be there,\u0026quot; Snape said.","Petunia nodded and slipped inside.","Severus Snape stood alone on the balcony. He wasn\u0027t looking at the past anymore. He was looking at the future. A future where he wasn\u0027t a spy, or a Death Eater, or a traitor.","He was just Severus. And he had a breakfast appointment.","\u0026quot;Lily,\u0026quot; he whispered to the night air. \u0026quot;We did it.\u0026quot;","And for the first time in forever, the silence didn\u0027t feel lonely. It felt like peace."]},{"num":12,"origNum":12,"title":"The Waffle Iron Throne","wordCount":1128,"paragraphs":["The dining hall of Malfoy Manor had seen many things over the centuries—Dark Lords, pureblood balls, and secret raids. It had never, however, seen a high-stakes waffle production line run by a Muggle drill executive.","It was 9:00 AM. The sun streamed through the high windows, illuminating a scene of absolute, joyful anarchy. The table had been extended so far it almost reached the front door.","Vernon Dursley stood at a side table that had been reinforced with iron. He was operating four industrial-sized waffle irons simultaneously.","\u0026quot;Rotation!\u0026quot; Vernon bellowed, flipping a handle. \u0026quot;Timing is critical! We need a golden crust, not a charcoal brick! Arthur, pass the batter!\u0026quot;","Arthur Weasley, wearing a \u0026quot;World’s Best Grandpa\u0026quot; apron that Molly had knitted overnight, handed over a pitcher. \u0026quot;The viscosity is perfect, Vernon! I added an extra egg for structural density!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parade of the Prams\u003c/strong\u003e","The double doors swung open.","\u0026quot;Make way!\u0026quot; Fred Weasley shouted, blowing a trumpet he had conjured. \u0026quot; The Heirs arrive!\u0026quot;","The Alliance entered, looking exhausted, disheveled, but glowing with pride. They were pushing a fleet of floating bassinets (except for Dudley, who was carrying Thomas in a Muggle carrier strapped to his chest like tactical armor).","Harry and Hermione led the charge with the twin pram. James Sirius was screaming at a volume that shook the chandelier crystals. Lily Luna was fast asleep, sucking her thumb.","\u0026quot;He has lungs,\u0026quot; Harry announced, looking shell-shocked. \u0026quot;He has Sirius’s volume.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s my boy!\u0026quot; Sirius Black cheered from the table, raising a mug of coffee. \u0026quot;Let it out, kid! Disturb the peace!\u0026quot;","Draco and Ginny followed. Cassie Malfoy was awake, sitting up in her floating crib, glaring at the room with a look of supreme judgment.","\u0026quot;She hates the morning,\u0026quot; Draco yawned, adjusting his silk pajamas. \u0026quot;She is definitely a Malfoy.\u0026quot;","Ron and Luna drifted in. Pandora was staring at the ceiling, trying to catch dust motes.","\u0026quot;She saw a Blibbering Humdinger,\u0026quot; Luna hummed happily. \u0026quot;It was hiding in the diaper bag.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Extended Cavalry\u003c/strong\u003e","The room was packed. The extended Weasley clan had arrived via Floo powder at dawn.","Bill Weasley was currently inspecting Thomas Dursley’s grip strength.","\u0026quot;Solid,\u0026quot; Bill noted, letting the baby squeeze his finger. \u0026quot;He’s got a grip like a goblin. Good for banking or curse-breaking.\u0026quot;","Fleur Delacour was hovering over Cassie, cooing in French. \u0026quot;Oh, zhe cheeks! Zey are magnificent! We must get \u0027er silk booties immediately. Cotton is too rough for zat skin!\u0026quot;","Charlie Weasley, fresh from Romania, was holding James. He held the screaming baby with the casual confidence of a man who wrestled Hungarian Horntails.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s feisty,\u0026quot; Charlie grinned as James kicked him. \u0026quot;A bit of a tail-lasher. Has he breathed fire yet?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not yet,\u0026quot; Hermione sighed, pouring herself a coffee. \u0026quot;Give him time.\u0026quot;","Percy Weasley sat at the end of the table, surrounded by stacks of parchment.","\u0026quot;I have the birth registration forms!\u0026quot; Percy announced, waving a quill. \u0026quot;We need signatures! Time of birth, weight, and blood status! Though the \u0027Half-Blood/Muggle-Born/Pureblood\u0027 section is going to be a nightmare to fill out for this lot. I might just write \u0027Complicated\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Waffle Distribution\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Order up!\u0026quot; Vernon roared.","House-elves sprinted from the waffle station, balancing stacks of golden, grid-patterned dough.","\u0026quot;Syrup!\u0026quot; Vernon commanded. \u0026quot;Berries! Whipped cream! We are building caloric mountains!\u0026quot;","Severus Snape sat near the window. He looked at the waffle placed in front of him. It was buried under a landslide of strawberries.","\u0026quot;It is... festive,\u0026quot; Snape murmured.","\u0026quot;Eat up, Severus!\u0026quot; Dumbledore chirped from the next seat. The Headmaster was currently bouncing Pandora on his knee while eating a waffle with his free hand. \u0026quot;It is brain food! And look at this little one! She has your contemplative frown.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at Pandora. Pandora looked at Snape. She reached out and grabbed his nose.","\u0026quot;Honk,\u0026quot; Dumbledore whispered.","Snape sighed, but he didn\u0027t pull away. \u0026quot;Ten points to Ravenclaw,\u0026quot; he muttered into his coffee. \u0026quot;For fearless aggression.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Muggle Artifact\u003c/strong\u003e","Arthur Weasley suddenly stood up, holding a white plastic box with an antenna.","\u0026quot;Everyone!\u0026quot; Arthur shouted. \u0026quot;Silence! I have activated the... Baby Monitor !\u0026quot;","The room went quiet. Static hissed from the box.","Then, a gurgle.","\u003cem\u003eGooo-ga.\u003c/em\u003e","It came from the box. But Thomas was across the room with Dudley.","\u0026quot;It transmits the soul!\u0026quot; Arthur gasped, his eyes wide with horror and delight. \u0026quot;It captures the baby\u0027s essence and shoots it through the air! Muggles have mastered telepathy via plastic!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s radio waves, Dad,\u0026quot; Hermione explained gently, buttering a waffle.","\u0026quot;Radio waves!\u0026quot; Arthur cheered. \u0026quot;Invisible waves of baby noises! Vernon, I’ll trade you a sneakoscope for it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Done,\u0026quot; Vernon grunted, flipping another waffle. \u0026quot;That thing never stops beeping anyway.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Malfoy Meltdown\u003c/strong\u003e","Lucius Malfoy was sitting next to Hagrid. It was a tight squeeze.","Hagrid was crying. Again.","\u0026quot;Look at \u0027em,\u0026quot; Hagrid sobbed into a napkin, gesturing to the babies. \u0026quot;Four of \u0027em. All friends. Just like you lot.\u0026quot;","He clapped Lucius on the back. Lucius face-planted into his fruit salad.","\u0026quot;Hagrid,\u0026quot; Lucius muffled through a melon slice. \u0026quot;Please. My skeletal structure is fragile.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sorry, Lucius!\u0026quot; Hagrid boomed, pulling him upright and dusting him off with a hand the size of a dustbin lid. \u0026quot;Just emotional, is all! Harry\u0027s got a pup! Draco\u0027s got a pup!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are children, Hagrid,\u0026quot; Narcissa corrected gently, though she was busy letting Cassie chew on her pearl necklace. \u0026quot;Not canines.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Quiet Moment\u003c/strong\u003e","Amidst the noise of cutlery, shouting Weasleys, and sizzling batter, Harry sat down next to Draco.","They both looked exhausted. They both had spit-up on their shirts.","\u0026quot;Tired?\u0026quot; Harry asked, cutting his waffle.","\u0026quot;I have forgotten what sleep feels like,\u0026quot; Draco admitted, staring at his coffee. \u0026quot;I think I hallucinated a Niffler at 3 AM.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That was Ron,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;He was looking for snacks.\u0026quot;","Draco smirked. He looked at the table—at his father eating fruit salad with a half-giant, at his mother holding a Weasley baby, at Snape letting a Lovegood child honk his nose.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Draco said quietly.","\u0026quot;Yeah?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We did it,\u0026quot; Draco gestured to the chaos. \u0026quot;We actually pulled it off. The Merger. The babies. The breakfast.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at Hermione, who was laughing as James threw a strawberry at Fred. He looked at Lily Luna, asleep in Petunia’s arms.","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, raising his coffee mug. \u0026quot;We did.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the next generation,\u0026quot; Draco toasted.","\u0026quot;To the next generation,\u0026quot; Harry agreed.","\u0026quot;And to Vernon,\u0026quot; Draco added, eyeing the waffle station. \u0026quot;Because these waffles are better than magic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t let Mrs. Weasley hear you say that,\u0026quot; Harry warned.","\u0026quot;TOO LATE!\u0026quot; Molly shouted from the other end of the table. \u0026quot;I heard that, Draco Malfoy! I’m knitting you an itchy jumper for Christmas!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I look forward to it, Molly!\u0026quot; Draco shouted back, and to his absolute shock, he meant it."]},{"num":13,"origNum":13,"title":"The Queen and the Puppy","wordCount":879,"paragraphs":["The garden of the Burrow was a riot of noise, color, and uncontrolled toddler magic.","It was a sunny Tuesday afternoon. The Alliance (minus the Dursleys, who were at a boxing tournament with Thomas) had gathered for the weekly playdate.","Arthur Weasley had \u0026quot;baby-proofed\u0026quot; the garden by enchanting the gnomes to be soft and plushy, but he hadn\u0027t accounted for the sheer volatility of the next generation.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe State of Play\u003c/strong\u003e","In the center of the rug, \u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e (age 2) was currently hovering six inches off the ground. She was cross-legged, staring intently at a blade of grass.","\u0026quot;Nargie,\u0026quot; Pan babbled, poking the air. \u0026quot;Fly fly.\u0026quot;","Next to her, \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter\u003c/strong\u003e (age 2) was sitting perfectly still. She radiated a sphere of such intense calm that a passing bumblebee had landed on her nose and fallen asleep. She simply giggled, her green eyes bright.","\u0026quot;Bee,\u0026quot; Lily cooed. \u0026quot;Sleeeepy.\u0026quot;","But the main event was happening near the gnome hole.","\u003cstrong\u003eCassiopeia Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e (age 2 and a half going on 40) was building a castle. She wasn\u0027t using magic; she was using wooden blocks. She placed each block with the surgical precision of a Malfoy and the fierce determination of a Weasley.","She wore a pristine white dress that Narcissa had sent. It was spotless.","\u0026quot;Foundation,\u0026quot; Cassie said clearly to herself. \u0026quot;Then the tower. Then the dungeon.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Instigator\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eJames Sirius Potter\u003c/strong\u003e (age 2, the elder twin by 12 minutes) was bored.","He had been running in circles for ten minutes, trying to break the sound barrier. He stopped. He looked at Cassie’s tower. He looked at Cassie’s clean dress.","A mischievous glint appeared in his brown eyes. He grinned—a grin that was pure James Potter Sr.","James scrunched up his face. He sneezed.","\u003cem\u003ePOOF.\u003c/em\u003e","Where a toddler had stood, a small, scruffy black puppy now sat. He had floppy ears and a tail that wagged so hard it shook his whole body.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Incident\u003c/strong\u003e","Puppy-James barked. He lowered his front paws, wiggled his bum, and launched himself.","He didn\u0027t attack Cassie. He attacked the castle.","CRASH.","The wooden blocks scattered. The tower fell. Puppy-James rolled through the wreckage, barking happily, and then shook himself, sending a cloud of dust onto Cassie’s white dress.","The parents, sitting on the porch with tea, froze.","\u0026quot;Oh no,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, lowering his mug.","\u0026quot;James,\u0026quot; Hermione sighed. \u0026quot;Not again.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Watch this,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned, leaning forward.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Elemental Tantrum\u003c/strong\u003e","Cassie did not cry. She did not wail for her mother.","She stood up slowly. She brushed the dust off her dress. She looked down at the yapping puppy.","Her grey eyes narrowed. Her jaw set.","\u0026quot;That,\u0026quot; Cassie announced, her voice crystal clear and dripping with icy disdain, \u0026quot;was very rude, James.\u0026quot;","Puppy-James stopped barking. He tilted his head.","\u0026quot;You are a bad dog,\u0026quot; Cassie declared.","She clenched her fists.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Shift\u003c/strong\u003e","The temperature in the garden dropped ten degrees in a second. Frost began to spread rapidly from Cassie’s left shoe, turning the green grass into crunchy white spikes. The lemonade pitcher on the picnic blanket froze solid with a loud \u003cem\u003eCRACK\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;Ice,\u0026quot; Ron shivered. \u0026quot;She\u0027s doing the ice thing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Wait for it,\u0026quot; Draco murmured, looking proud.","Puppy-James whimpered, backing away from the cold.","But Cassie wasn\u0027t done. The Weasley temper flared to meet the Malfoy cold.","Her hair seemed to lift with static. Her right hand glowed.","\u0026quot;Bad!\u0026quot; Cassie shouted.","WHOOSH.","A ring of fire erupted around her right side. It wasn\u0027t a destructive inferno, but a precise, controlled wall of flame that circled the ruined blocks.","The heat met the cold. Steam hissed into the air, creating a dramatic fog bank in the middle of the garden.","Puppy-James yelped, transformed back into a human boy with a \u003cem\u003epop\u003c/em\u003e, and scrambled backward on his bum.","\u0026quot;Hot!\u0026quot; James squeaked, eyes wide. \u0026quot;Cold! Cassie scary!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Intervention\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy strolled down the steps. He didn\u0027t run. He walked through the steam, waved his wand to vanish the fire, and then cancelled the frost with a flick of his wrist.","He knelt in front of his daughter.","\u0026quot;Cassiopeia,\u0026quot; Draco said gently. \u0026quot;We do not incinerate our cousins. It is bad form.\u0026quot;","Cassie looked at her father. She pointed at James.","\u0026quot;He broke the dungeon, Daddy,\u0026quot; she said, her sentence structure impeccable. \u0026quot;He is a chaotic element.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is,\u0026quot; Draco agreed, picking her up. \u0026quot;But we use words, not thermal shock.\u0026quot;","Harry ran over and scooped up James.","\u0026quot;You okay, Jamie?\u0026quot;","James looked at Cassie. He looked at the steam. He grinned.","\u0026quot;Again!\u0026quot; James cheered. \u0026quot;Puppy go zoom!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No zoom,\u0026quot; Harry sighed. \u0026quot;Time out.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","Cassie looked over Draco’s shoulder at the trembling, awe-struck James.","\u0026quot;Next time,\u0026quot; Cassie said, smoothing her dress, \u0026quot;I will freeze your tail.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She speaks in paragraphs,\u0026quot; Ron whispered to Hermione. \u0026quot;She\u0027s two. And she just threatened to freeze a body part. She really is a Malfoy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She has excellent diction,\u0026quot; Hermione admitted, looking impressed. \u0026quot;And her control of the elemental spectrum is fascinating.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She\u0027s terrifying,\u0026quot; Ron corrected.","Lily Luna, who had watched the whole thing from her spot on the rug, simply clapped her hands.","\u0026quot;Pwetty fire,\u0026quot; Lily gurgled. \u0026quot;Warm.\u0026quot;","Pan floated up a few inches higher to avoid the wet grass. \u0026quot;The Nargles like the steam,\u0026quot; she observed in baby-talk. \u0026quot;Fuzzy.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":14,"origNum":14,"title":"The Floating Prophet","wordCount":762,"paragraphs":["The steam from Cassie’s elemental tantrum had dissipated, but the adults were still on high alert. Harry was holding a squirming, human-shaped James by the back of his t-shirt, while Draco was re-pleating Cassie’s dress with a cleaning charm.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Ron exhaled, watching his niece. \u0026quot;So we have a blizzard-throwing toddler. Brilliant. What’s next? James turning into a dragon?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Puppy!\u0026quot; James shouted, trying to bite Harry’s hand.","\u0026quot;No puppy,\u0026quot; Harry sighed. \u0026quot;Human boy. Humans do not bite.\u0026quot;","While the attention was focused on the Potter-Malfoy skirmish, \u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e had drifted. Literally.","She had floated away from the picnic blanket, hovering about six inches off the grass, her toes dragging slightly through the daisies. She was heading for the hedge where the garden gnomes usually plotted their revenge against Crookshanks.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Conversation\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron spotted her first.","\u0026quot;Luna,\u0026quot; Ron whispered, nudging his wife. \u0026quot;She’s off-roading. She’s heading for the gnome hole.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s fine, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna smiled, sipping her tea. \u0026quot;The gnomes have a lot of interesting stories today. The Nargles told me they’re planning a festival.\u0026quot;","Pan reached the hedge. A particularly gnarly, potato-headed gnome popped out. Usually, these creatures would try to bite a child’s ankle.","Pan didn\u0027t flinch. She floated down until she was eye-level with the gnome. She reached out a chubby hand and patted its warty head.","\u0026quot;Nice Gnomey,\u0026quot; Pan babbled softly. \u0026quot;Eat worm? Yuck.\u0026quot;","The gnome blinked. It didn\u0027t bite. It made a chattering noise that sounded surprisingly polite.","\u0026quot;He says the soil is dry,\u0026quot; Pan announced to the garden, translating the gibberish. \u0026quot;Thirsty flower.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Did she just translate Gnomish?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, lowering her book.","\u0026quot;She listens,\u0026quot; Luna noted happily.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Prediction\u003c/strong\u003e","Suddenly, Pan stopped patting the gnome. She stiffened in mid-air. Her large, silvery eyes lost focus on the gnome and fixed on the empty garden gate.","She tilted her head.","\u0026quot;Pop,\u0026quot; Pan whispered.","\u0026quot;What’s that, Pan?\u0026quot; Ron called out, walking over to catch her tether (a long ribbon tied to her sash, just in case a strong wind picked up).","Pan pointed a finger at the empty gate.","\u0026quot;Grandpa,\u0026quot; Pan said, her voice serious. \u0026quot;Duck. Pop. Boom.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Grandpa’s at work, sweetie,\u0026quot; Ginny said, bouncing Cassie on her hip. \u0026quot;He won\u0027t be back for hours.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pop,\u0026quot; Pan insisted, frowning. \u0026quot;Duck.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","Three seconds later, the squeak of the garden gate echoed through the yard.","Arthur Weasley came stumbling in, looking flushed and excited, carrying a large cardboard box.","\u0026quot;Molly! Kids!\u0026quot; Arthur shouted. \u0026quot;Look what I found at the market! It’s a Muggle device for bath time! A Rubber Duck!\u0026quot;","He held up a bright yellow duck.","\u0026quot;Duck!\u0026quot; James cheered, clapping his hands.","\u0026quot;She called it,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, staring at Pan. \u0026quot;She said Duck.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Wait,\u0026quot; Ron said, looking at his daughter. \u0026quot;She also said \u0027Pop\u0027 and \u0027Boom\u0027.\u0026quot;","Arthur was fumbling with the box. \u0026quot;And that’s not all! I also acquired a... Toaster! The seller said it has a \u0027High Velocity Ejection\u0027 spring!\u0026quot;","Arthur set the toaster on the garden table. He pushed the lever down.","\u0026quot;Watch!\u0026quot; Arthur beamed.","\u003cstrong\u003eCLICK.\u003c/strong\u003e","For a moment, nothing happened.","Then—\u003cstrong\u003ePOP.\u003c/strong\u003e","The toaster didn\u0027t just eject the imaginary toast; the spring malfunctioned. The entire internal mechanism shot out of the top of the machine with a loud \u003cstrong\u003eBOOM\u003c/strong\u003e, flying ten feet into the air and landing in the birdbath with a splash.","\u0026quot;Excellent!\u0026quot; Arthur roared delightedly. \u0026quot;Such power!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The adults stared at the smoking toaster. Then they turned to look at the two-year-old floating by the hedge.","Pan clapped her hands. \u0026quot;Pop! Boom!\u0026quot; she giggled.","Cassie looked at Pan. She looked at the toaster.","\u0026quot;She told you,\u0026quot; Cassie stated clearly, smoothing her skirt. \u0026quot;Pan sees the future. It is very useful. She told me my juice would spill, and then James spilled it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She predicted a toaster explosion,\u0026quot; Hermione murmured, looking a mixture of terrified and academically fascinated. \u0026quot;A Seer. A verified Seer.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And she talks to gnomes,\u0026quot; Ron sighed, grabbing Pan’s ribbon and pulling her back down to earth like a balloon. \u0026quot;My daughter is going to be the weirdest girl at Hogwarts. I’m so proud.\u0026quot;","Luna kissed Ron’s cheek. \u0026quot;She’s just open-minded, Ronald.\u0026quot;","Lily Luna, sensing the sudden spike in amazement from the adults, let out a happy squeal. A small, shimmering bubble of golden light appeared around her and Pan, shielding them from the toaster smoke.","\u0026quot;Safe,\u0026quot; Lily gurgled.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Harry stood up, dusting off his jeans. \u0026quot;So we have an Elemental, a Seer, and a baby who creates forcefields. Should we just surrender the school to them now?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Draco agreed, picking up a book. \u0026quot;It saves time.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":15,"origNum":15,"title":"The Healer and the Hazard","wordCount":1030,"paragraphs":["The garden was buzzing with the chaotic energy of James Sirius Potter.","He was currently engaged in a high-speed game of tag with himself. He would sprint ten feet as a toddler, sneeze, transform into a black puppy with floppy ears, scramble under a bush, and then \u003cem\u003epop\u003c/em\u003e back into a boy to laugh at the confused gnomes.","\u0026quot;Zoom!\u0026quot; James shouted, running in circles around the apple tree. \u0026quot;Puppy fast!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Prediction\u003c/strong\u003e","On the picnic blanket, \u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e stopped playing with her grass blade. She floated up a few inches, her eyes fixing on a jagged grey stone protruding from the earth near the garden shed—a remnant of an old wall.","She tilted her head. Her expression went serious.","\u0026quot;Rock,\u0026quot; Pan stated clearly.","Ron looked up from his sandwich. \u0026quot;What\u0027s that, Pan? Found a nice rock?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sharp rock,\u0026quot; Pan clarified. She pointed a chubby finger at James, who was currently a puppy chasing a butterfly.","\u0026quot;James,\u0026quot; Pan counted. \u0026quot;Thirty seconds. Big ouch.\u0026quot;","Ron froze. \u0026quot;Thirty seconds? Pan, sweetie, is that a story or a... forecast?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Big ouch,\u0026quot; Pan repeated, drifting back down to the blanket. \u0026quot;Blood.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Ron shouted, scrambling up. \u0026quot;Grab him! Pan says he\u0027s going down!\u0026quot;","Harry looked up from his conversation with Draco. \u0026quot;What?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Fall\u003c/strong\u003e","It happened exactly as the clock ticked down.","James, currently in human form, tripped over a protruding root. He flailed, trying to catch himself, but momentum was against him. He pitched forward, landing hard on the exact jagged grey stone Pan had pointed out.","\u003cstrong\u003eCRUNCH.\u003c/strong\u003e","A scream pierced the air—sharp, high, and terrified.","\u0026quot;Mummy!\u0026quot; James shrieked.","Hermione was there in a split second, her wand already drawn. She skidded to her knees beside him.","The cut on his shin was deep—nasty and jagged. Blood was welling up rapidly, soaking his little jeans. Worse, his leg was bent at a sickening angle just below the knee. A compound fracture.","\u0026quot;Oh god,\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, her hands hovering. \u0026quot;Vulnera Sanentur! Episkey!\u0026quot;","The blood slowed, but it didn\u0027t stop. The bone didn\u0027t knit. The magic was fighting against the trauma, but the wound was deep and dirty.","\u0026quot;It’s deep, Harry!\u0026quot; Hermione cried, panic edging into her voice. \u0026quot;We need St. Mungo\u0027s! The bone is—\u0026quot;","James was sobbing, his face red, clutching his leg.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Intervention\u003c/strong\u003e","Suddenly, the crying stopped. Or rather, it echoed.","\u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter\u003c/strong\u003e had waddled over from the pond. She stood over her brother. Her face crumpled. She wasn\u0027t crying because she was scared; she was crying because \u003cem\u003ehe\u003c/em\u003e was hurting. The empathy washed over her, making her own leg throb in sympathy.","\u0026quot;Jamie hurt,\u0026quot; Lily sniffed.","\u0026quot;Lily, sweetie, move back,\u0026quot; Harry said gently, trying to reach for James. \u0026quot;Mummy is fixing it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Lily said firmly.","She pushed past Harry’s hand. She knelt in the dirt, her floral dress getting muddy.","She reached out with both hands and placed them directly over the bloody, broken mess of James’s leg.","She closed her eyes. A soft, white glow began to emanate from her palms—not the harsh light of a spell, but a warm, biological luminescence.","\u0026quot;Better,\u0026quot; Lily commanded.","\u003cstrong\u003eSNAP-KNIT.\u003c/strong\u003e","The sound was audible. Under Lily’s small hands, the bone audibly snapped back into alignment. The skin stitched itself together in a rapid, seamless zipper of flesh. The blood vanished, absorbed back into the body or evaporated by the magic.","Lily pulled her hands away.","There was no scar. There was no bruise. The leg was pristine.","James stopped crying instantly. He blinked. He looked at his leg. He kicked it out.","\u0026quot;All gone!\u0026quot; James cheered.","He scrambled up, tackled Lily in a fierce hug, getting mud all over her. \u0026quot;Thank you, Lil-Lil!\u0026quot;","Then, with the attention span of a goldfish, James sneezed, turned into a puppy, and sprinted off to chase a gnome.","Lily sat there for a moment. She let out a massive, jaw-cracking yawn.","\u0026quot;Nap,\u0026quot; she decided.","She stood up, waddled back to the edge of the pond, sat down, and began poking a butterfly, looking completely unbothered by the medical miracle she had just performed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","The garden was silent. The adults were staring at the toddler by the pond.","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry and Hermione (The Parents)\u003c/strong\u003e","Hermione was still kneeling in the dirt, her wand useless in her hand. She stared at the spot where the bone had been sticking out seconds ago.","\u0026quot;She...\u0026quot; Hermione stammered. \u0026quot;She reset a compound fracture. Without a wand. Without an incantation. Without a potion.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She said \u0027Better\u0027,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, looking at his daughter playing with the butterfly. \u0026quot;Hermione... that was pure white magic. That was... ancient stuff.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She didn\u0027t even look tired,\u0026quot; Hermione noted, her analytical mind racing to catch up with her shock. \u0026quot;Usually, healing that fast drains the caster. She just... yawned.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s a battery,\u0026quot; Harry realized. \u0026quot;A self-charging magical battery.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRon and Luna (The Seer’s Parents)\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron was sitting on the grass, looking pale. He looked at Pan, who was happily braiding grass.","\u0026quot;She knew,\u0026quot; Ron whispered. \u0026quot;Luna, she counted down. \u0027Thirty seconds.\u0027 She knew exactly when he’d fall.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She sees the threads, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna smiled, adjusting her radish earrings. \u0026quot;The Nargles tell her when time gets bumpy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And then Lily fixed it,\u0026quot; Ron shook his head. \u0026quot;We’re doomed. The kids are X-Men. We’re raising X-Men.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco and Ginny (The Strategists)\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy was leaning against the porch railing, his arms crossed. He had watched the entire sequence with eagle eyes.","\u0026quot;Did you see that?\u0026quot; Draco murmured to Ginny.","\u0026quot;I saw it,\u0026quot; Ginny said, her eyes wide. \u0026quot;She didn\u0027t just heal him, Draco. She erased the injury. It’s like she rewrote time for his leg.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;James breaks things,\u0026quot; Draco analyzed, looking at the chaotic puppy running in circles. \u0026quot;Cassie freezes or burns things. Pan predicts the disaster.\u0026quot;","He looked at Lily by the pond.","\u0026quot;And Potter’s daughter,\u0026quot; Draco concluded, a mix of fear and respect in his voice, \u0026quot;is the reset button. She is the fail-safe. If we ever go to war again, Ginny... we just put Lily in the middle and tell her to say \u0027Better\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s the most powerful one of them all,\u0026quot; Ginny agreed. \u0026quot;And she’s currently trying to eat a dandelion.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Terrifying,\u0026quot; Draco smirked. \u0026quot;Absolutely terrifying.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":16,"origNum":16,"title":"The Unbreakable Bubble","wordCount":650,"paragraphs":["The peace in the garden lasted exactly four minutes.","James Sirius Potter, having forgotten the trauma of a broken leg thanks to his sister\u0027s magic, was back to full speed. He was currently a human boy, but he was moving with the zoomies of a puppy.","\u0026quot;Tag!\u0026quot; James shouted, sprinting across the grass. \u0026quot;Tag Lily!\u0026quot;","He picked up speed. He lowered his head like a charging bull. He launched himself toward his sister, who was sitting near the pond, entranced by a blade of grass.","\u0026quot;James, slow down!\u0026quot; Hermione called out, instinctively reaching for her wand.","But she didn\u0027t need to.","Lily didn\u0027t flinch. She didn\u0027t look up. She didn\u0027t even blink.","Just as James was about to collide with her—a collision that would surely result in two crying toddlers—the air around Lily shimmered.","A soft, golden sphere of light materialized instantly, encasing her like an egg.","\u003cstrong\u003eBOING.\u003c/strong\u003e","It wasn\u0027t a hard impact. It sounded like someone dropping a marshmallow onto a pillow.","James hit the golden light. He didn\u0027t crash; he rebounded. He bounced backward a full three feet, landing softly on his bum in the grass. He looked confused, blinking dizzily.","Inside the bubble, Lily simply smiled. She giggled—a sound like silver bells—and went back to petting the grass, completely unbothered by the human projectile that had just attempted to tackle her.","The golden glow faded.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","The adults sat in stunned silence on the porch.","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry and Hermione (The Defense Analysts)\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter lowered his tea mug slowly. He looked at his son, who was shaking his head, trying to figure out why physics had stopped working. He looked at his daughter, who was humming to a beetle.","\u0026quot;She didn\u0027t even look,\u0026quot; Harry whispered. \u0026quot;Hermione, she didn\u0027t even know he was coming.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Passive magic,\u0026quot; Hermione breathed, her eyes wide with academic fascination mixed with maternal terror. \u0026quot;It’s an automatic defense mechanism. Like a \u003cem\u003eProtego\u003c/em\u003e, but... instinctual. It triggered based on threat assessment.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She has a forcefield,\u0026quot; Harry realized. \u0026quot;My two-year-old daughter has a permanent, unbreakable forcefield.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Hermione said, leaning back in her chair with a sigh of relief. \u0026quot;At least we don\u0027t have to worry about her getting tackled at Rugrats Rugby.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think we have to worry about the other kids bouncing off her into orbit,\u0026quot; Harry corrected.","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco and Ginny (The Power Brokers)\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy was smirking. It was a look of profound respect.","\u0026quot;Did you see the trajectory?\u0026quot; Draco asked Ginny, pointing his wand at the spot where James had landed. \u0026quot;He bounced. She repelled him with the force of a gentle breeze. It was elegant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was brilliant,\u0026quot; Ginny grinned. \u0026quot;James tries to bulldoze everything. Lily just... exists. And the world bends around her.\u0026quot;","Draco looked at Cassie, who was freezing a flower, and then at Lily.","\u0026quot;Cassie is the sword,\u0026quot; Draco murmured. \u0026quot;But Potter’s girl... she is the shield. The Unstoppable Force meets the Immovable Object. The playground politics are going to be fascinating.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s going to run the school, Draco,\u0026quot; Ginny said. \u0026quot;She won\u0027t even have to raise her voice. She’ll just smile, and people will bounce off her.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRon and Luna (The Audience)\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron Weasley had dropped his sandwich.","\u0026quot;She’s a rubber ball,\u0026quot; Ron said, staring at his niece. \u0026quot;She turned the air into a bouncy castle. How? Why?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s her aura, Ronald,\u0026quot; Luna observed happily, watching the golden light fade. \u0026quot;It’s very thick today. The Wrackspurts can\u0027t get through it. Neither can James.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So she’s invincible?\u0026quot; Ron asked. \u0026quot;Harry’s kid is invincible, and my kid talks to gnomes. We really are the sidekicks in this story, aren\u0027t we?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are the comic relief,\u0026quot; Luna smiled, patting his hand. \u0026quot;It’s a very important role.\u0026quot;","Ron looked at James, who was now poking the air around Lily, trying to find the invisible wall.","\u0026quot;Bloody hell,\u0026quot; Ron muttered. \u0026quot;I’m never playing Quidditch against her. I’d bounce off the goal hoops.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":17,"origNum":17,"title":"The Weight of the Soul","wordCount":735,"paragraphs":["The joy of the \u0026quot;bouncy castle\u0026quot; moment faded into a contemplative, heavy silence on the porch of the Burrow.","James was back to chasing a gnome, his leg completely forgotten. Cassie was building an ice-wall to protect her new tower. Pan was whispering to a beetle.","But Harry’s eyes were fixed on Lily, who was napping in the shade of the apple tree, her chest rising and falling in a peaceful rhythm.","\u0026quot;It’s not just the healing,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly, breaking the silence. He leaned forward, elbows on his knees. \u0026quot;Did you see her face before she touched him? She was crying. She wasn\u0027t scared... she was hurting. She felt his pain.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Empathy,\u0026quot; Hermione nodded, her brow furrowed. \u0026quot;True, unfiltered empathy. It’s a rare gift, Harry. But it’s also a burden.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s a curse,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, swirling his tea. \u0026quot;Think about it. She’s two. She’s in a garden with her family. What happens when she goes to Diagon Alley? Or Hogwarts?\u0026quot;","Harry flinched. \u0026quot;Hundreds of people. Fear. Anger. Jealousy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If she feels everything,\u0026quot; Ginny said, her voice tight, \u0026quot;she’ll drown. She won\u0027t have a moment of peace inside her own head. She’ll be feeling everyone else’s emotions.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the healing,\u0026quot; Ron added, looking at James’s leg. \u0026quot;Mum always said healing magic takes a toll. You can\u0027t just create bone and flesh from nothing. It has to come from somewhere. If she heals too much... will it drain her? Will it hurt her?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She yawned,\u0026quot; Hermione pointed out. \u0026quot;She was tired immediately after. It cost her energy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She needs shields,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;Stronger than physical ones. She needs mental shields. She needs Occlumency.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s a toddler, Harry,\u0026quot; Ron argued. \u0026quot;You can\u0027t teach a toddler to clear their mind. Their minds are pure chaos. Have you seen inside James’s head? It’s probably just loud noises and biscuits.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But Lily is different,\u0026quot; Hermione countered. \u0026quot;That bubble she made... that was a shield. It was instinctual. If she can shield her body without thinking, maybe she can shield her mind too. Maybe she’s already doing it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We don\u0027t know,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;And \u0027maybe\u0027 isn\u0027t good enough. If she goes out into the world with an open mind, she’s vulnerable. We need to know the strength of her walls.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at Draco. They exchanged a look of grim understanding. They both knew what it was like to have a mind that wasn\u0027t entirely safe.","\u0026quot;We need to test her,\u0026quot; Harry said.","\u0026quot;You want to use Legilimency on a baby?\u0026quot; Ron looked horrified.","\u0026quot;Not an attack,\u0026quot; Harry said quickly. \u0026quot;A check. A probe. We need someone who can touch her mind gently enough not to hurt her, but skillfully enough to see if she has defenses.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;There is only one person,\u0026quot; Hermione stated.","\u0026quot;Snape,\u0026quot; Harry and Draco said in unison.","\u0026quot;He’s going to hate this,\u0026quot; Ron sighed. \u0026quot;He hates playdates. He hates feelings. And he definitely hates probing the minds of Potter children.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He loves her,\u0026quot; Harry said, looking at the sleeping girl. \u0026quot;He’s the only one I trust to do it.\u0026quot;","Harry raised his wand. He didn\u0027t cast a Patronus; he sent a direct, encrypted message via the ethos, a trick he’d learned as Head Auror.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","Ten minutes later, the air at the edge of the garden shimmered.","There was no loud crack of Apparition. There was simply a displacement of air, a swirl of black robes, and the sudden, imposing presence of Severus Snape.","He stood by the garden gate. He was wearing his teaching robes, buttons done up to the chin despite the summer heat. His expression was one of profound irritation.","He unlatched the gate and swept up the path, the grass parting before him.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, stopping at the foot of the porch steps. \u0026quot;I was in the middle of a very delicate brewing process involving volatile armadillo bile. If this summons is because James has turned himself into a hamster and you cannot find him, I shall be exceedingly displeased.\u0026quot;","He looked at the group of adults staring at him with serious faces. He looked at the children playing. He looked at the sleeping form of Lily under the tree.","Snape’s scowl deepened, but his eyes sharpened.","\u0026quot;Why is the atmosphere so... heavy?\u0026quot; Snape asked, his voice dropping. \u0026quot;Has something happened to her?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We need your help, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said, standing up. \u0026quot;We need you to look inside her head.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":18,"origNum":18,"title":"The Fortress of Giggles","wordCount":1418,"paragraphs":["\u0026quot;You want me to do \u003cem\u003ewhat\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot;","Severus Snape did not shout. He did not need to. His whisper was cold enough to freeze the humid summer air of the Burrow’s garden.","\u0026quot;Legilimency,\u0026quot; Harry repeated, standing his ground though he looked like a schoolboy caught out of bed. \u0026quot;On Lily.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She is two years old, Potter,\u0026quot; Snape spat, his black eyes flashing. \u0026quot;Her mind is a forming galaxy of colors, shapes, and the urgent desire for biscuits. To intrude upon it is... invasive. It is crude. It is potentially damaging to \u003cem\u003emy\u003c/em\u003e sanity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She healed James,\u0026quot; Hermione interjected, stepping forward. \u0026quot;Fully. In seconds. She’s an Empath, Professor. A raw, unfiltered Empath.\u0026quot;","Snape paused. He looked at the sleeping toddler under the tree.","\u0026quot;If she feels everything,\u0026quot; Draco said quietly from the porch railing, \u0026quot;and she has no shields... she will burn out. She will be overwhelmed the moment she steps into a crowd.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at Draco. He looked at the worry etched into Harry and Hermione’s faces. He sighed, a sound like a deflating tire.","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Snape conceded, straightening his cuffs. \u0026quot;A cursory glance. A surface skim. I will check for... structural integrity. If I start weeping uncontrollably, pull me out.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Game\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape walked over to the apple tree. He knelt in the grass, heedless of the dirt staining his robes.","Lily Luna stirred. Her eyes fluttered open. She saw the dark figure looming over her.","Most toddlers would have cried. Lily beamed.","\u0026quot;Sev!\u0026quot; she chirped, reaching out with chubby hands.","Snape’s expression softened imperceptibly, though he looked around to make sure no one saw it. He took her small hands in his.","\u0026quot;Hello, little one,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice surprisingly gentle. \u0026quot;We are going to play a game. It is called \u0027The Staring Contest of Doom\u0027. You will lose.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Game!\u0026quot; Lily cheered, kicking her legs.","\u0026quot;I am going to look into your eyes,\u0026quot; Snape explained. \u0026quot;And I am going to try to guess what you are thinking. You must try to keep your thoughts... quiet. Can you do that?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Quiet,\u0026quot; Lily whispered, putting a finger to her lips. \u0026quot;Shhh.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Snape nodded. \u0026quot;Do not think about bunnies.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Attempts\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape focused. He raised his wand slightly, not pointing it at her, but holding it ready. He locked eyes with the brilliant green gaze.","\u003cem\u003eLegilimens.\u003c/em\u003e","He sent a feather-light probe, a mere wisp of mental inquiry, intending to brush against the surface of her mind.","He expected to find a chaotic swirl of toddler thoughts.","Instead, he hit... a marshmallow.","It wasn\u0027t a wall. It was a slippery, giggling surface. His thought slid right off.","Lily let out a peal of laughter.","\u0026quot;Tickle!\u0026quot; she squealed, rubbing her forehead. \u0026quot;Sev tickle!\u0026quot;","Snape frowned. He pulled back. \u0026quot;Tickle? I am a Master of the Mind Arts. I do not \u003cem\u003etickle\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","He looked at Harry. \u0026quot;She perceives the mental intrusion as a physical sensation. A tickle. It is... humiliating.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Try again,\u0026quot; Harry urged, biting his lip to keep from laughing.","Snape narrowed his eyes. He leaned in. He sharpened the probe. He put a little more weight behind it—the kind of force he would use on a first-year student who hadn\u0027t done their homework.","\u003cem\u003eLegilimens.\u003c/em\u003e","He pushed.","Still nothing. It was like trying to grab a bar of wet soap. His mind slid, bounced, and deflected. He couldn\u0027t get a foothold.","Lily giggled harder, her shoulders shaking. \u0026quot;Funny! Funny Sev!\u0026quot;","Snape withdrew, breathing slightly faster. He was a Master Occlumens. He was one of the most skilled Legilimens alive. And he was being defeated by a giggling baby who smelled like milk and grass.","\u0026quot;She is... elusive,\u0026quot; Snape muttered. \u0026quot;Her mind is naturally lubricated against intrusion. It is like trying to mentally wrestle a greased piglet.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Use the full weight,\u0026quot; Draco called out, eating an apple. \u0026quot;She can take it.\u0026quot;","Snape glared at his godson. \u0026quot;If I scramble her brains, Draco, I will hold you personally responsible.\u0026quot;","He looked back at Lily. She was smiling at him, trusting and happy.","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Snape whispered. \u0026quot;Forgive me, Lily. This is going to be... firm.\u0026quot;","He gathered his power. He focused his intent. He launched a full-strength, piercing Legilimency spell—a spear of mental energy designed to crack open the toughest spy.","\u003cem\u003eLEGILIMENS!\u003c/em\u003e","The spell connected.","For a split second, Snape broke through.","He didn\u0027t see memories. He didn\u0027t see thoughts.","He saw... light. Blinding, absolute, pure white light. It was a void of such immense, positive power that it was terrifying. It wasn\u0027t empty; it was full of everything. It was a supernova contained in a skull.","Lily blinked. She stopped giggling.","She looked at Snape. She felt the push. She didn\u0027t like the push. It wasn\u0027t a tickle anymore; it was a shove.","Her green eyes flashed gold.","She smiled—a small, mischievous smile.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Lily whispered.","She pushed back.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Splash\u003c/strong\u003e","It wasn\u0027t a spell. It was a mental eviction notice served with a battering ram.","Snape felt a force slam into his mind that felt like being hit by the Hogwarts Express. It threw him out of her head, but the momentum didn\u0027t stop there.","The psychic backlash manifested physically.","\u003cstrong\u003eWHOOSH.\u003c/strong\u003e","Severus Snape was lifted off his knees. He flew backward through the air, his black robes billowing like the wings of a startled bat. He sailed three clear feet, arms pinwheeling in a desperate attempt to grab dignity, which was currently out of reach.","\u003cstrong\u003eSPLASH.\u003c/strong\u003e","He landed flat on his back in the middle of the Weasleys\u0027 duck pond.","The water erupted, soaking the nearby gnomes. Ducks quacked in indignance and flapped away.","Snape sat up, dripping wet. A lily pad was stuck to his head like a jaunty beret. He spat out a mouthful of pond water and a small tadpole.","Silence descended on the garden.","Then, a small voice broke it.","Lily Luna clapped her hands, bouncing on her bottom.","\u0026quot;More!\u0026quot; she cheered. \u0026quot;More fly! Sev fly! Birdie!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry and Hermione\u003c/strong\u003e were clutching each other, faces red, shoulders shaking.","\u0026quot;She threw him,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, tears of laughter leaking from his eyes. \u0026quot;She threw Snape. Into the ducks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s physics!\u0026quot; Hermione wheezed, trying to sound academic but failing. \u0026quot;Newton’s Third Law! Equal and opposite reaction! But she... she treated him like a ragdoll!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRon and Luna\u003c/strong\u003e were staring at the pond.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s wet,\u0026quot; Ron noted unnecessarily. \u0026quot;He\u0027s very wet. Do we... do we help him? Or will he bite?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The ducks are confused,\u0026quot; Luna observed happily. \u0026quot;They think he is a giant black swan. Look, that one is trying to bond with him.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco and Ginny\u003c/strong\u003e were leaning on each other for support.","\u0026quot;Ten points to Gryffindor,\u0026quot; Draco choked out. \u0026quot;That was the best thing I have ever seen. My father will hear about this. I will make sure of it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He looked like a bat,\u0026quot; Ginny gasped. \u0026quot;A wet, angry bat. Oh, I love my niece.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Verdict\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape stood up in the pond. The water came up to his waist. He peeled the lily pad off his forehead with slow, dignified movements.","He waded out of the water, his boots squelching loudly on the grass—\u003cem\u003esquish, squish, squish\u003c/em\u003e. He dripped his way back to the apple tree, looking like a swamp monster in formal wear.","He looked down at Lily, who was still clapping.","Snape did not yell. He did not deduct points. He simply looked defeated.","He looked at Harry.","\u0026quot;Her shields,\u0026quot; Snape said, water dripping from his nose onto his shoes, \u0026quot;are adequate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Adequate?\u0026quot; Harry choked out. \u0026quot;She threw you in a pond! You have algae on your ear!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She is a mirror,\u0026quot; Snape said, wiping his face with a wet sleeve. \u0026quot;She reflects intent. If you come at her with love, she accepts it. If you come at her with force... she returns it with interest.\u0026quot;","He looked back at the baby. A look of profound respect crossed his face.","\u0026quot;She does not need training, Potter,\u0026quot; Snape declared, wringing out his cloak. \u0026quot;She needs a warning label. \u0027Caution: Reflective Surface\u0027.\u0026quot;","Lily reached up again. \u0026quot;Up! Up!\u0026quot;","Snape sighed. He was wet. He smelled of pond scum. But he bent down and picked her up.","\u0026quot;You are a menace,\u0026quot; Snape whispered to the baby. \u0026quot;Just like your grandmother. Though she never threw me in a duck pond.\u0026quot;","Lily patted his wet cheek and rested her head on his soggy shoulder.","\u0026quot;Wet,\u0026quot; she noted.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Snape agreed. \u0026quot;Very. Now, if you will excuse me, I am going to drip on your father\u0027s carpet.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":19,"origNum":19,"title":"The Mirror of Souls","wordCount":862,"paragraphs":["Severus Snape stood by the apple tree, his wand raised. He was not casting hexes; he was casting a complex sequence of Hot-Air Charms.","Steam rose from his black robes in billowing clouds. The smell of pond water and algae was slowly being replaced by the smell of ozone and irritated wizard.","The Alliance—Harry, Hermione, Ron, Luna, Draco, and Ginny—stood in a semi-circle around him, waiting. They looked like students waiting for exam results, if the exam involved throwing a teacher into a duck pond.","\u0026quot;Well?\u0026quot; Harry asked, breaking the silence. \u0026quot;Professor? What happened in there?\u0026quot;","Snape flicked his wand, blasting a jet of hot air at his boots. \u003cem\u003eSquelch.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;What happened,\u0026quot; Snape said, his voice low and devoid of its usual silky rhythm, \u0026quot;is that I attempted to breach a fortress, only to discover it was not a fortress at all. It was a trampoline.\u0026quot;","He turned to face them. His hair was dry now, though it stuck up in odd places. He looked at Hermione.","\u0026quot;You theorized she was an Empath,\u0026quot; Snape said. \u0026quot;You were incorrect.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I was?\u0026quot; Hermione blinked. \u0026quot;But the healing... the feelings...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She is not merely an Empath, Granger,\u0026quot; Snape corrected, vanishing a piece of duckweed from his sleeve. \u0026quot;An Empath feels what others feel. They absorb. They are sponges.\u0026quot;","He pointed a long finger at Lily, who was currently trying to put a flower in Pan’s hair a few yards away.","\u0026quot;That child is not a sponge. She is a \u003cstrong\u003eMirror\u003c/strong\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Explanation\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape began to pace, regaining his professorial air despite the damp trousers.","\u0026quot;Legilimency,\u0026quot; Snape lectured, \u0026quot;relies on finding a foothold. A crack in the emotional armor. Fear, anger, desire, shame. The Legilimens latches onto these hooks to pry the mind open.\u0026quot;","He stopped in front of Harry.","\u0026quot;When I entered her mind... there were no hooks. There was no fear. There was no darkness. There was only... light. Absolute, blinding, unadulterated benevolence.\u0026quot;","Snape shuddered slightly, as if the memory was physically painful.","\u0026quot;It was like staring into the sun. I could not find purchase. And when I applied force...\u0026quot;","He made a pushing motion with his hand.","\u0026quot;The laws of psychic physics took over. Every ounce of aggression I directed at her did not land. It was absorbed, inverted, and fired back at the source with exponential force.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Newton\u0027s Third Law,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, clutching Harry’s arm. \u0026quot;Equal and opposite reaction.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Amplified,\u0026quot; Snape corrected. \u0026quot;Because her core is pure magic. She didn\u0027t mean to throw me. She simply... rejected the negativity. My own power was used against me.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Verdict\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron stared at his niece. \u0026quot;So... she’s rubber and you’re glue?\u0026quot;","Snape glared at Ron. \u0026quot;If you wish to reduce high-level mind magic to a nursery rhyme, Weasley... yes. Essentially.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;So she’s safe?\u0026quot; Ginny asked, looking at the toddler. \u0026quot;If someone tries to hurt her?\u0026quot;","Snape let out a short, harsh laugh.","\u0026quot;Safe?\u0026quot; Snape sneered. \u0026quot;Mrs. Malfoy, she is not safe. She is \u003cstrong\u003edangerous\u003c/strong\u003e.\u0026quot;","He looked at the group, his black eyes serious.","\u0026quot;Do you understand what would happen if a Dark Wizard tried to possess her? If someone tried to use the Unforgivable Curses on her mind?\u0026quot;","The group shook their heads, terrified.","Snape looked at Harry. He stepped closer, lowering his voice.","\u0026quot;Potter. You remember the Dark Lord. You remember his mind. It was a sewer of hatred, suspicion, and malice. It was a void where love went to die.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded, the memory of the connection in his scar still a phantom ache. \u0026quot;I remember.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If the Dark Lord—at the height of his power—had attempted to use Legilimency on your daughter,\u0026quot; Snape said softly, \u0026quot;he would not have been thrown into a pond.\u0026quot;","Snape looked back at Lily.","\u0026quot;He would have crumbled,\u0026quot; Snape whispered. \u0026quot;He would have disintegrated. His fractured soul could not have existed in her presence for a millisecond. The purity of her mind would have burned him to ash from the inside out.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The silence in the garden was absolute.","Harry looked at his daughter. He saw a two-year-old girl in a muddy dress, giggling as she chased a butterfly.","He tried to reconcile that image with the force Snape had just described—a force capable of vaporizing Voldemort.","\u0026quot;She’s a weapon,\u0026quot; Draco breathed, horror and awe mixing in his voice. \u0026quot;A weapon made of... love.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is the Old Magic,\u0026quot; Luna hummed, smiling. \u0026quot;The magic that Lily Potter used to save Harry. But it didn\u0027t just save him. It grew.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She is the ultimate defense,\u0026quot; Snape agreed, finally holstering his wand. \u0026quot;She does not need Occlumency lessons, Potter. The world needs lessons on how not to provoke her.\u0026quot;","Harry let out a breath he felt he’d been holding for an hour. He leaned against Hermione.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;So... no one messes with Lily.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Snape said. He brushed a speck of dust from his robe. \u0026quot;Now, if you will excuse me... I believe I swallowed a tadpole. I require a strong cup of tea. And perhaps... a biscuit.\u0026quot;","He turned and marched toward the house, leaving The Alliance standing in the garden, staring at a toddler who could defeat a Dark Lord with a giggle."]},{"num":20,"origNum":20,"title":"The Balance of the Pack","wordCount":924,"paragraphs":["Severus Snape sat on the porch of the Burrow, holding a mug of tea that Molly Weasley had aggressively thrust into his hands. He was dry, but he still looked like a man who had gone twelve rounds with a Giant Squid.","The Alliance (minus the Dursleys) sat around him on the wooden steps. The mood had shifted from terror to a kind of heavy, awe-struck calculation.","\u0026quot;So,\u0026quot; Hermione started, her mind working furiously. \u0026quot;When James broke his leg... she was crying. She was sobbing before we even reached him. She felt the break.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Snape said, taking a sip of tea. \u0026quot;She felt the trauma. The biological distress signal.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But she didn\u0027t panic,\u0026quot; Harry pointed out. \u0026quot;She didn\u0027t freeze. She just... fixed it. And then she went back to playing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because of the Mirror,\u0026quot; Snape explained, gesturing with his free hand. \u0026quot;An ordinary empath absorbs pain and holds it. It festers. It overwhelms. But Lily...\u0026quot;","He looked at the toddler by the pond.","\u0026quot;She allowed the pain to enter, she acknowledged it, and then she rejected the trauma. She took the information—\u0027James is broken\u0027—and she reflected a correction—\u0027James is whole\u0027. Her mind is not a sponge, Granger. It is a prism. It takes in chaotic light and refracts it into order.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s why she yawned,\u0026quot; Draco realized. \u0026quot;It wasn\u0027t exhaustion from the magic. It was the effort of... filtering.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Correct,\u0026quot; Snape nodded. \u0026quot;She filtered a compound fracture into a nap.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Equation\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron looked at the other children. James was now trying to wrestle a gnome. Cassie was freezing a puddle. Pan was floating near the hedge.","\u0026quot;But Professor,\u0026quot; Ron asked, frowning. \u0026quot;If she’s that powerful... if she’s a walking mirror that can vaporize Dark Lords... how does she learn to turn it off? How does she not accidentally blast us all into the pond every time she has a tantrum?\u0026quot;","Snape’s black eyes moved to the other children. A look of grudging realization crossed his face.","\u0026quot;She does not learn it from you,\u0026quot; Snape said softly. \u0026quot;You are adults. You are careful with her. You treat her like glass.\u0026quot;","He pointed a long finger at \u003cstrong\u003eJames Sirius Potter\u003c/strong\u003e, who had just turned into a puppy and bitten a gnome\u0027s ear.","\u0026quot;She learns it from \u003cem\u003ethem\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","The parents looked at the chaotic scene.","\u0026quot;Look at the dynamic,\u0026quot; Snape commanded, his voice dropping to a lecture tone. \u0026quot;Potter’s son. The shapeshifter. He is chaos incarnate. He creates constant, unpredictable stimuli. He forces Lily to constantly adjust her shields. He is desensitizing her to shock.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at James. \u0026quot;He’s... training her?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is her sparring partner,\u0026quot; Snape confirmed. \u0026quot;He breaks things so she can learn to fix them. He rushes her so she can learn to bounce him.\u0026quot;","Snape’s gaze shifted to \u003cstrong\u003eCassie Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e.","\u0026quot;And the Malfoy girl,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Fire and Ice. She is volatile. Emotional. Powerful. She provides the raw elemental pressure. Lily cannot be overwhelmed by anger if she grows up wrestling a girl who throws fireballs when she drops her ice cream.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Cassie toughens her up,\u0026quot; Ginny whispered. \u0026quot;She makes sure Lily isn\u0027t soft.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the Weasley girl,\u0026quot; Snape finished, looking at \u003cstrong\u003ePan\u003c/strong\u003e. \u0026quot;The Seer. She provides the warning. The context. She translates the invisible world so Lily doesn\u0027t have to process it all alone.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Missing Variable\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape paused. He scanned the garden again, his brow furrowing.","\u0026quot;However,\u0026quot; Snape said slowly. \u0026quot;The equation is incomplete. There is too much energy here. Too much magic bouncing off magic. It needs a sink. It needs an anchor.\u0026quot;","He looked at Harry.","\u0026quot;Where is the Dursley boy? The Muggle-born\u0027s son?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thomas?\u0026quot; Harry asked. \u0026quot;He\u0027s at a tournament with Dudley and Chloe.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A pity,\u0026quot; Snape murmured. \u0026quot;Because he is the final variable. He provides the \u003cstrong\u003eGround\u003c/strong\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thomas?\u0026quot; Draco asked, surprised. \u0026quot;But he has no magic.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Snape snapped. \u0026quot;He is the structural integrity. He is the reality check. When James transforms, and Cassie burns, and Pan floats, and Lily reflects... Thomas Dursley is the earth beneath their feet. He absorbs the overflow. Without him, this group is a storm without a lightning rod.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Conclusion\u003c/strong\u003e","Snape set his tea down. He looked at the six parents.","\u0026quot;Do you understand?\u0026quot; Snape asked. \u0026quot;You were worried about protecting her \u003cem\u003efrom\u003c/em\u003e the world. You were worried about the world being safe \u003cem\u003efrom\u003c/em\u003e her.\u0026quot;","He leaned back, crossing his arms.","\u0026quot;Alone, Lily Luna Potter is a nuclear reactor without cooling rods. She would burn herself out, or she would inadvertently level a city with a burst of accidental magic.\u0026quot;","He gestured to the group of toddlers.","\u0026quot;But with them? With the Pack?\u0026quot;","Snape smirked.","\u0026quot;James provides the friction. Cassie provides the resistance. Pan provides the sight. And Thomas provides the gravity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are not just playmates,\u0026quot; Snape declared. \u0026quot;They are a containment field. They are a circuit. As long as they are together... she is safe. And the world is safe from her.\u0026quot;","Hermione let out a long, shuddering breath. She looked at the kids—the chaotic, messy, powerful future of their families.","\u0026quot;They balance the equation,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered.","\u0026quot;They do,\u0026quot; Snape agreed. He stood up, brushing off his robes. \u0026quot;Which is fortunate. Because I do not wish to spend my retirement being thrown into aquatic features.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at Snape. He looked at the kids.","\u0026quot;So we keep them together,\u0026quot; Harry said firmly. \u0026quot;Always.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Always,\u0026quot; Draco echoed.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Ron clapped his hands, looking relieved. \u0026quot;So, the kids are a bomb disposal unit. Good. Now... is there any cake left? I feel like I\u0027ve learned too much today.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":21,"origNum":21,"title":"The Cake of Truth","wordCount":1034,"paragraphs":["The red telephone on Harry Potter’s desk was not a magical artifact. It was a plastic, Muggle landline that Arthur Weasley had modified to ring at a volume that could wake the dead. It sat next to his piles of Auror reports, a silent sentinel connecting the Ministry to Little Whinging.","It had never rung. Until today.","\u003cstrong\u003eBRRRRRING-RING!\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry jerked, knocking over a bottle of ink. He grabbed the receiver.","\u0026quot;Potter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;HARRY!\u0026quot; Dudley’s voice was a high-pitched screech of pure panic. \u0026quot;CODE RED! CODE RED AT NUMBER FOUR!\u0026quot;","Harry’s blood ran cold. \u0026quot;Dudley? What is it? Death Eaters? Dark Marks?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;THE KITCHEN!\u0026quot; Dudley yelled. \u0026quot;IT’S HAPPENING! COME NOW! BRING THE WAND! BRING THE ARMY!\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eClick.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry didn\u0027t hesitate. He dropped the phone. He didn\u0027t walk to the Apparition point; he sprinted. He didn\u0027t think about protocol. He thought about the family that had raised him, the cousin who was his brother, and the toddler who was the Anchor of the Pack.","\u0026quot;Hold on, Big D,\u0026quot; Harry muttered, spinning on his heel.","\u003cstrong\u003eCRACK.\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry materialized on the front porch of Number Four, Privet Drive. He didn\u0027t knock. He blasted the door open with a non-verbal \u003cem\u003eAlohomora\u003c/em\u003e and burst into the hallway, his wand raised, a curse on his lips.","\u0026quot;STUPE—\u0026quot;","He froze.","He wasn\u0027t facing a legion of Dementors. He wasn\u0027t facing a resurrected Dark Lord.","He was facing the dining room.","The table had been overturned to form a barricade. Peeking over the top of the mahogany were four pairs of terrified eyes: Vernon, Petunia, Dudley, and Chloe. Vernon was clutching a spatula like a sword. Dudley was holding the cricket bat.","But the threat wasn\u0027t coming from the door. It was coming from the high chair in the center of the room.","Thomas Dursley, two years old, sat strapped in his chair. He was drooling slightly. He looked happy.","He had his chubby arms stretched out toward the kitchen counter.","And hovering in mid-air, floating steadily across the room toward his open hands, was a massive, three-layer Victoria Sponge cake.","It wasn\u0027t sliding. It was flying. It drifted over the carpet, cleared the overturned table (Vernon ducked with a yelp), and landed gently on the tray of the high chair.","Thomas clapped his hands. \u0026quot;Cake!\u0026quot; he giggled.","He plunged his face into the sponge.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Realization\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry stood in the hallway, his wand still raised. He looked at the cake-covered toddler. He looked at the terrified Dursleys hiding behind the furniture.","The tension in his chest didn\u0027t release; it snapped.","Harry lowered his wand. A sound escaped his throat. It started as a snort. Then a chuckle.","Then, Harry Potter, Head Auror, fell to his knees on the hallway carpet and began to wheeze.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Dudley whispered from behind the table. \u0026quot;Is it... is it a poltergeist? Is he possessed?\u0026quot;","Harry couldn\u0027t breathe. He was laughing so hard his ribs hurt. He pounded the floor with his fist. The irony. The absolute, cosmic irony.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s...\u0026quot; Harry gasped, wiping tears from his eyes. \u0026quot;He\u0027s not possessed, Dudley.\u0026quot;","Harry stood up, holstering his wand. He walked over to the high chair. Thomas looked up, face covered in jam and cream, and offered Harry a piece of cake.","\u0026quot;Ta,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, taking it.","He turned to the barricade.","\u0026quot;You can come out,\u0026quot; Harry said, grinning ear to ear. \u0026quot;It’s accidental magic. It happens when they\u0027re hungry or scared. Or when they really want cake.\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley slowly stood up. He brushed crumbs off his knees.","\u0026quot;Accidental... magic?\u0026quot; Vernon repeated.","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Harry said softly. He looked at Thomas.","\u0026quot;Thomas isn\u0027t a Muggle, Uncle Vernon. He’s a wizard.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dursley Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The silence in Number Four was heavier than the cake.","Vernon looked at his grandson. Petunia put a hand to her mouth. Dudley dropped the cricket bat.","\u0026quot;A... a wizard?\u0026quot; Vernon whispered. \u0026quot;A Dursley... wizard?\u0026quot;","Harry braced himself. He remembered the shouting matches. He remembered the fear. He remembered the \u0026quot;freak\u0026quot; comments of his childhood.","Vernon walked slowly toward the high chair. He looked at the boy who had just levitated a bakery product with his mind.","Vernon’s face went through a complex series of contortions. Shock. Confusion. Calculation.","Then, Vernon’s mustache twitched. He puffed out his chest.","\u0026quot;Well!\u0026quot; Vernon boomed. \u0026quot;Did you see that levitation? Stable! Smooth trajectory! He didn\u0027t drop a single crumb!\u0026quot;","Harry blinked. \u0026quot;Uncle Vernon?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Telekinesis!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, looking at Petunia with wild excitement. \u0026quot;Petunia! Do you realize what this means? The boy is a goldmine of efficiency! No more carrying groceries! He can float the furniture when we vacuum!\u0026quot;","He leaned in close to Thomas.","\u0026quot;Can you do remote controls, son? Can you fetch my slippers?\u0026quot;","Thomas burped.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s thinking about it!\u0026quot; Vernon cheered. \u0026quot;A wizard! My grandson has superpowers! Wait until I tell the boys at the club! \u0027Oh, your grandson plays football? Mine defies the laws of physics!\u0027\u0026quot;","Petunia walked forward. She was trembling. She looked at Harry, then at Thomas.","\u0026quot;He has it,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, tears filling her eyes. \u0026quot;He has... what Lily had.\u0026quot;","She reached out and touched Thomas’s sticky cheek.","\u0026quot;He\u0027s not ordinary,\u0026quot; Petunia said, her voice filled with a fierce, protective wonder. \u0026quot;He\u0027s special. Just like you, Harry.\u0026quot;","Dudley slumped into a chair. He looked at Chloe.","\u0026quot;I... I made magic?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, stunned. \u0026quot;Me? Big D?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Apparently so,\u0026quot; Chloe laughed, kissing his cheek. \u0026quot;We have a magic baby, Dudley.\u0026quot;","Dudley looked at Harry. \u0026quot;Does this mean... does he get the letter? The owl? The train?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah, Big D,\u0026quot; Harry smiled. \u0026quot;In nine years. He\u0027s going to Hogwarts.\u0026quot;","Dudley grinned. \u0026quot;Can I teach him to box? Magic boxing?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Please don\u0027t,\u0026quot; Harry laughed.","Vernon was already on his phone.","\u0026quot;Henderson! Yes! It’s Vernon! Cancel the drilling lessons for the boy! Yes! We’re pivoting! We need... what do we need, Harry? Wands? Cauldrons?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Not yet, Uncle Vernon,\u0026quot; Harry said.","\u0026quot;Right! We need theory books!\u0026quot; Vernon barked into the phone. \u0026quot;Get me a manual on \u0027Anti-Gravity Logistics\u0027! My grandson is going to run the world!\u0026quot;","Harry leaned against the doorframe, watching the Dursleys celebrate their magical heir.","The Anchor wasn\u0027t just the ground anymore. He was part of the sky.","And the Pack just got a lot more dangerous."]},{"num":22,"origNum":22,"title":"The High-Definition Heir","wordCount":941,"paragraphs":["Six months had passed since the Great Cake Levitation, and Number Four, Privet Drive had settled into a new, slightly surreal normal.","It was Sunday evening. The aroma of Petunia’s roast beef wafted from the kitchen, signaling that dinner was imminent. The living room was occupied by a unique blend of the magical and the mundane.","Harry and Hermione sat on the sofa, sipping tea. James and Lily (now three years and three months old) were building a fortress out of cushions on the rug. James was trying to turn the cushions into clouds, while Lily was reinforcing them with golden shimmers of protective light.","Vernon Dursley sat in his armchair, the king of his castle, watching the evening news. He was in a good mood. The drill market was up, and his grandson was a wizard. Life was efficient.","Thomas Dursley, also three and a bit, sat on the carpet near his grandfather\u0027s feet. He was a sturdy toddler, built like a miniature Dudley, with a calm, square face. He wasn\u0027t playing with magic. He was meticulously stacking coasters in a perfect vertical column.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Glitch\u003c/strong\u003e","Suddenly, a loud \u003cem\u003eZZZRT\u003c/em\u003e echoed through the room.","The television screen flickered violently. The newsreader’s face distorted into a jagged mess of static and horizontal lines. The audio dissolved into a high-pitched whine.","\u0026quot;Blast it!\u0026quot; Vernon barked, hitting the arm of his chair. \u0026quot;Infernal machine! I only bought this in \u002798! Japanese engineering is slipping!\u0026quot;","Harry winced. \u0026quot;Sorry, Uncle Vernon. might be us. The magical residue... electronics don\u0027t usually like me and Hermione being in the room.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the interference,\u0026quot; Hermione noted, looking at the static. \u0026quot;Magical energy disrupts electromagnetic fields. It’s why you can\u0027t have a TV at Hogwarts.\u0026quot;","Vernon grumbled, reaching for the remote to bang it against his palm—the universal Muggle fix. \u0026quot;I want to see the weather! If it rains on the golf course tomorrow, I need to know!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Touch\u003c/strong\u003e","Thomas stopped stacking coasters. He looked up at the noisy box. He frowned.","It was the frown of a Dursley who spotted a weed in the lawn. It was a frown that said: \u003cem\u003eDisorder.\u003c/em\u003e","Thomas stood up. He walked—sturdy, flat-footed steps—toward the television stand.","\u0026quot;Thomas, no,\u0026quot; Chloe called out from the doorway. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t touch, sweetie. It’s broken.\u0026quot;","Thomas ignored her. He stood directly in front of the screen, the static reflecting in his brown eyes. He didn\u0027t look scared of the noise. He looked offended by it.","He reached out his right hand. He placed his small, flat palm directly onto the center of the glass screen.","He didn\u0027t say a spell. He didn\u0027t wave a wand. He just... pushed. Not a physical push, but a conceptual one. He grounded the chaos.","\u003cstrong\u003eHUMMM-CLICK.\u003c/strong\u003e","The static didn\u0027t just fade; it was sucked away instantly. The whine vanished.","The picture snapped back. But it didn\u0027t just return to normal.","The colors exploded with vibrancy. The contrast deepened. The fuzzy edge of the analog signal sharpened into razor-sharp, impossible clarity. The newsreader’s tie wasn\u0027t just red; it was a high-definition crimson that seemed to have more pixels than the screen physically possessed. The sound became crisp, rich, and perfectly balanced.","Thomas patted the TV twice—\u003cem\u003epat, pat\u003c/em\u003e—as if telling a dog to sit. Then he turned around, walked back to his coasters, and resumed stacking.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","The room was silent, save for the crystal-clear voice of the newsreader discussing a cold front in Scotland.","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry and Hermione (The Experts)\u003c/strong\u003e","Hermione’s teacup was halfway to her mouth. She froze.","\u0026quot;That’s impossible,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered. \u0026quot;Harry... that’s impossible. Wizards \u003cem\u003ebreak\u003c/em\u003e technology. We blow fuses. We fry circuits. He just... he just upgraded the resolution.\u0026quot;","Harry was staring at the TV. \u0026quot;He didn\u0027t cast a repair charm, Hermione. Repair charms fix the parts. He... he improved the signal. He made the technology work \u003cem\u003ebetter\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Technomancy,\u0026quot; Hermione breathed, her eyes lighting up. \u0026quot;It’s theoretically possible but unheard of. He’s a bridge. He’s the Anchor, Harry! He grounded the magical interference and channeled it into the machine.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eVernon and Petunia (The Grandparents)\u003c/strong\u003e","Vernon Dursley was leaning forward in his chair, his mouth slightly open. He squinted at the screen.","\u0026quot;Look at that definition,\u0026quot; Vernon gasped. \u0026quot;Petunia! Look! I can see the pores on the weatherman’s nose!\u0026quot;","He looked down at Thomas, his chest swelling with pride.","\u0026quot;He fixed it!\u0026quot; Vernon roared. \u0026quot;No repairman! No service fee! And he upgraded the picture! The boy is a human antenna!\u0026quot;","Petunia clasped her hands to her chest. \u0026quot;He likes things tidy,\u0026quot; she said tearfully. \u0026quot;He just tidied up the picture. Oh, he’s such a good boy.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eDudley and Chloe (The Parents)\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley looked at Harry, wide-eyed.","\u0026quot;Is that... is that normal wizard stuff?\u0026quot; Dudley asked. \u0026quot;Can you guys do that?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, Big D,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, shaking his head in disbelief. \u0026quot;If I touch a computer, it usually catches fire. Thomas is... Thomas is something else entirely.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s practical,\u0026quot; Chloe said, looking at her son with amusement. \u0026quot;He saw it was broken, so he fixed it. No drama. No sparks.\u0026quot;","Vernon stood up and walked over to the TV, admiring the picture quality.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Vernon barked. \u0026quot;Forget the wands! Get the boy a screwdriver set! If he can do this to the telly, imagine what he can do to the toaster! We’ll have the most efficient appliances in Surrey!\u0026quot;","Harry looked at Hermione. They shared a look of realization.","The Pack had the Chaos (James), the Power (Cassie), the Sight (Pan), and the Soul (Lily).","But now, they realized the most terrifying thing of all: The Pack had a System Administrator.","And Thomas Dursley was going to make sure everything ran perfectly."]},{"num":23,"origNum":24,"title":"The Stick Debate","wordCount":1104,"paragraphs":["Diagon Alley was accustomed to crowds. It was accustomed to noise. But it was not accustomed to The Pack.","The cobblestones seemed to vibrate as the group approached the brick wall archway. The moment they stepped through, the noise of the magical street dipped for a second, then resumed with double the intensity.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Draco Malfoy announced, straightening his jacket. He reached into his pocket and pulled out a stack of sleek, black cards embossed with the Gringotts goblin crest in gold.","He handed one to Harry, one to Ron, one to Dudley, and one to Hermione.","\u0026quot;Draco,\u0026quot; Hermione sighed. \u0026quot;We have money. The royalties from \u0027Hogwarts: A History, Revised Edition\u0027 are doing quite well.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the Auror pension is fine,\u0026quot; Harry added.","\u0026quot;Hush,\u0026quot; Draco said, pressing the card into Harry’s hand. \u0026quot;This is the Malfoy \u0027Infinite\u0027 line. It connects directly to the Vault. I am not having my daughter’s cousins wearing second-hand robes or using budget cauldrons. We are outfitting an army. The army travels first class.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I like the sound of that,\u0026quot; Ron grinned, pocketing the card immediately. \u0026quot;Thanks, Ferret.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Infinite?\u0026quot; Vernon Dursley (who had insisted on coming to supervise the \u0027efficiency\u0027 of the trip) eyed the card. \u0026quot;Does it work at hardware stores?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Only magical ones, Vernon,\u0026quot; Draco said.","\u0026quot;Pity,\u0026quot; Vernon grumbled, but he pocketed it anyway.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Rampage of Retail\u003c/strong\u003e","The shopping trip was less of an errand and more of a tactical strike.","\u003cstrong\u003eMadam Malkin’s Robes for All Occasions\u003c/strong\u003e was the first casualty.","\u0026quot;I require a silk lining,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eCassie\u003c/strong\u003e (age 10) informed a terrified Madam Malkin. She was standing on the stool, arms outstretched. \u0026quot;And fireproofing. Double weave. If I get annoyed, I do not wish to scorch my hem.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Right, dear,\u0026quot; Madam Malkin squeaked, pinning the fabric with trembling hands.","Meanwhile, \u003cstrong\u003eJames\u003c/strong\u003e was vibrating. Literally. He was shifting his left ear into a beagle ear and back again just to annoy the tape measure, which was trying to strangle him in retaliation.","\u0026quot;Stand still, Potter!\u0026quot; the tape measure hissed.","\u0026quot;Make me!\u0026quot; James laughed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThomas\u003c/strong\u003e was inspecting the stitching on his plain black robes. He pulled a thread. It held. He nodded approvingly. \u0026quot;Good tensile strength,\u0026quot; he muttered to Dudley. \u0026quot;Should hold up in a grapple.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Bookstore and the Cauldron\u003c/strong\u003e","At \u003cstrong\u003eFlourish and Blotts\u003c/strong\u003e, Hermione was in heaven, but Thomas was the one drawing a crowd.","He picked up \u003cem\u003eThe Standard Book of Spells, Grade 1\u003c/em\u003e. He opened it, scanned the table of contents, and frowned.","\u0026quot;Inefficient,\u0026quot; Thomas stated.","\u0026quot;It’s the curriculum, Thomas,\u0026quot; Hermione said gently, stacking books for Lily.","\u0026quot;Chapter 4 can be condensed into Chapter 2,\u0026quot; Thomas argued, tapping the page. \u0026quot;And the diagram for the Levitation Charm has a structural flaw in the wrist movement vector. If you swish at 45 degrees, you lose 10% of the lift.\u0026quot;","A clerk overheard him and looked offended. Thomas ignored him and grabbed a book on \u003cem\u003eAdvanced Arithmancy\u003c/em\u003e instead.","At \u003cstrong\u003ePotage\u0027s Cauldron Shop\u003c/strong\u003e, \u003cstrong\u003ePan\u003c/strong\u003e caused a scene by floating into the rafters to inspect the pewter cauldrons from the inside.","\u0026quot;The bottom one has a Nargle nest,\u0026quot; Pan called down, hanging upside down by her knees. \u0026quot;We should take the copper ones. They sing better.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get down, Pan,\u0026quot; Ron sighed, paying for five copper cauldrons with Draco\u0027s card. \u0026quot;We\u0027ll take the singing ones.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wand Dilemma\u003c/strong\u003e","Finally, laden with bags that had been shrunk and lightened by Harry and Draco, the group stood before the most important shop of all.","\u003cstrong\u003eOllivanders: Makers of Fine Wands since 382 B.C.\u003c/strong\u003e","The peeling gold letters glinted in the afternoon sun. The shop looked dusty, quiet, and revered.","Harry stopped. \u0026quot;Right. This is it. The big moment.\u0026quot;","The Pack stopped. They looked at the shop. Then they looked at each other.","\u0026quot;Do we have to?\u0026quot; James asked, scratching his nose.","Harry blinked. \u0026quot;Do you have to what?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Get wands,\u0026quot; James said. He held up his hand. \u0026quot;I can turn into a dog. I can fly. I can unlock doors by sneezing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And I can freeze the pavement,\u0026quot; Cassie added, crossing her arms. \u0026quot;Why do I need a stick of wood to tell me how to do it?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It feels... clunky,\u0026quot; Thomas added. \u0026quot;I fixed the toaster with my hand. A wand seems like an unnecessary interface device. Like using a stylus when you have a touchscreen.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the wands are loud,\u0026quot; Pan whispered. \u0026quot;They shout.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t need it,\u0026quot; Lily said softly. She touched a wilting flower in a window box, and it bloomed instantly. \u0026quot;See? Better.\u0026quot;","The parents exchanged looks. They had anticipated excitement. They hadn\u0027t anticipated a philosophical rejection of the core tool of wizardry.","Harry knelt down to be eye-level with James and Lily. Draco knelt in front of Cassie.","\u0026quot;Listen,\u0026quot; Harry started. \u0026quot;You guys are powerful. We know that. You\u0027re stronger than we were at your age. Maybe stronger than we are now.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;But power without focus is just a mess,\u0026quot; Draco said smoothly. He pulled out his own hawthorn wand. \u0026quot;Cassie, you can freeze a puddle. But can you freeze a single drop of water falling from a tap without freezing the tap itself?\u0026quot;","Cassie frowned. \u0026quot;Maybe.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A wand isn\u0027t a crutch,\u0026quot; Harry said. \u0026quot;It’s a lens. It takes that massive ocean of magic you have inside and channels it into a laser beam. It gives you precision.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Think of it like this, Thomas,\u0026quot; Hermione added. \u0026quot;You like efficiency, right? Wandless magic leaks energy. It’s messy. Using a wand is 100% efficiency. Zero waste.\u0026quot;","Thomas’s eyes lit up. \u0026quot;Optimal energy transfer?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Exactly,\u0026quot; Hermione nodded.","\u0026quot;And James,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;You can do big stuff. But with a wand... you can do the cool stuff. Disarming charms. Shield charms. The stuff Aurors do.\u0026quot;","James’s eyes widened. \u0026quot;The cool stuff?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The really cool stuff,\u0026quot; Ron promised. \u0026quot;And they make a \u003cem\u003ewhoosh\u003c/em\u003e noise.\u0026quot;","The Pack looked at each other. The silent communication of the hive mind passed between them.","Precision. Efficiency. Cool noises.","\u0026quot;Okay,\u0026quot; James decided. \u0026quot;We\u0027ll take the sticks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;For the aesthetic,\u0026quot; Cassie agreed haughtily.","\u0026quot;For the efficiency,\u0026quot; Thomas nodded.","\u0026quot;The sticks want to meet us anyway,\u0026quot; Pan smiled.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Entry\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry stood up and opened the door. A tinkling bell rang somewhere in the depths of the shop.","The air inside was cool and smelled of dust, wood shavings, and ancient magic. Thousands of narrow boxes were piled to the ceiling.","The Pack stepped inside—five small, powerful children walking into the quiet domain of Garrick Ollivander.","From the shadows at the back of the shop, pale eyes shone.","\u0026quot;I wondered,\u0026quot; a soft, whispery voice echoed, \u0026quot;when the day would come.\u0026quot;","The Pack stepped forward. The wand choosing had begun."]},{"num":24,"origNum":25,"title":"The System Administrator\u0027s Baton","wordCount":718,"paragraphs":["Garrick Ollivander was old. He had seen thousands of eleven-year-olds. He had seen the Boy Who Lived. He had seen the Dark Lord.","But as Thomas Vernon Dursley stepped up to the counter, Ollivander blinked his silvery eyes. He didn\u0027t reach for a tape measure immediately. He leaned over the counter and sniffed.","\u0026quot;Curious,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered. \u0026quot;You do not hum, Mr. Dursley. You... vibrate. Like a bees\u0027 nest inside a lead box.\u0026quot;","Thomas stood squarely, feet shoulder-width apart. He looked at his father, Dudley, who gave him a supportive nod, before turning back to the wandmaker.","\u0026quot;I need a wand that is durable, sir. Low latency. High output. Preferably shatter-resistant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Quality,\u0026quot; Ollivander murmured, drifting into the shelves. \u0026quot;Yes. Let us see.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Failures\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander returned with a slender box. \u0026quot;Beech and unicorn hair. Nine inches. Flexible. Good for subtle artistry.\u0026quot;","Thomas took the wand. He didn\u0027t wave it. He just held it.","\u003cem\u003eFZZZT.\u003c/em\u003e","The wand didn\u0027t shoot sparks. It made a sound like a dying lightbulb. The wood turned grey, then crumbled into ash in Thomas’s hand.","\u0026quot;Overload,\u0026quot; Thomas noted, dusting the ash off his hands onto the floor. \u0026quot;Too much resistance in the circuit.\u0026quot;","Ollivander looked delighted. \u0026quot;Fascinating! You grounded the magic. You drank it dry!\u0026quot;","He ran back and fetched another. \u0026quot;Vine and phoenix feather. Spirited.\u0026quot;","Thomas grabbed it. The wand immediately drooped, bending like a wet noodle.","\u0026quot;Structural failure,\u0026quot; Thomas noted, handing back the limp stick. \u0026quot;It can\u0027t handle the weight.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Solution\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander stood still, tapping his chin. He looked at Thomas—the Anchor, the boy who fixed televisions by touching them, the boy who was more earth than air.","\u0026quot;I have not sold one of these in a century,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered. \u0026quot;It requires... a steady hand. A hand that does not waver.\u0026quot;","He went to the very back of the shop, to a dusty shelf near the floor. He pulled out a box that looked heavier than the others.","He opened it.","The wand inside was not polished or carved with runes. It was dark, almost black, and completely matte. It was thicker than a standard wand, resembling a small baton more than a twig.","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eLignum Vitae\u003c/strong\u003e,\u0026quot; Ollivander announced. \u0026quot;The hardest wood in the world. It sinks in water. It is used to build the shafts of ships.\u0026quot;","He handed it to Thomas.","\u0026quot;And the core... \u003cstrong\u003eDragon Heartstring\u003c/strong\u003e. But not just any dragon. This is from a Ukrainian Ironbelly. The heaviest dragon.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Connection\u003c/strong\u003e","Thomas took the wand.","It didn\u0027t emit a shower of gold and red sparks. It didn\u0027t shoot a rainbow.","\u003cstrong\u003eTHRUMMMMM.\u003c/strong\u003e","A deep, resonant bass note filled the shop. It sounded like a massive server booting up, or a high-voltage transformer humming to life.","The dust on the floor vibrated into perfect geometric circles around Thomas’s feet. The flickering gas lamp on the wall suddenly stabilized and burned with a perfect, unwavering blue flame.","Thomas gripped the wand. He felt the weight of it. It felt like a tool. It felt like a screwdriver, a hammer, and a circuit board all in one.","He gave it a single, sharp downward motion.","\u003cem\u003eClick.\u003c/em\u003e","Every open drawer in the shop slammed shut simultaneously. Every crooked box on the shelves straightened itself into perfect alignment. The scattered papers on Ollivander\u0027s desk stacked themselves by size.","\u0026quot;System optimized,\u0026quot; Thomas said, a satisfied smile crossing his face.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley Dursley’s jaw dropped. He looked at Harry. \u0026quot;Did he just... organize the magic shop?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He did,\u0026quot; Harry laughed, clapping Dudley on the back. \u0026quot;He tidied it up, Big D.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lignum Vitae and Dragon Heartstring,\u0026quot; Ollivander announced, looking a little pale but smiling. \u0026quot;Twelve inches. Unyielding. A wand for a builder... or a commander. It is a wand that enforces order.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It has good balance,\u0026quot; Thomas said, sliding the wand into his pocket. It didn\u0027t stick out; it seemed to vanish, integrated into his reality. \u0026quot;I’ll take it.\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy leaned forward, inspecting the perfectly aligned shelves. \u0026quot;I must say,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, looking at Thomas with approval. \u0026quot;I appreciate the aesthetic. Finally, a civilized wizard.\u0026quot;","Hermione whispered to Harry, \u0026quot;He just defragged the room, Harry. He’s going to drive the Poltergeist at Hogwarts absolutely insane.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t wait to see it,\u0026quot; Harry grinned.","\u0026quot;Next!\u0026quot; Ollivander called out, looking both excited and terrified for what was coming next."]},{"num":25,"origNum":26,"title":"The Wand That Wasn\u0027t There","wordCount":841,"paragraphs":["\u0026quot;Next!\u0026quot; Ollivander called out, his eyes gleaming with the thrill of Thomas’s selection.","There was no sound of footsteps. Instead, a slight draft blew through the shop, scattering a few loose feathers on the counter.","Ollivander looked down. No one was there.","He looked up.","Hovering three feet above the floor, drifting like a dandelion seed caught in a breeze, was Pandora Weasley. She was upside down, her red pigtails hanging towards the floorboards. She was peering intently at a cobweb in the corner.","\u0026quot;The spider is knitting a scarf,\u0026quot; Pan observed dreamily. \u0026quot;It’s going to be a cold winter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Miss Weasley,\u0026quot; Ollivander said, craning his neck. \u0026quot;If you could... descend?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Gravity is just a suggestion, Mr. Ollivander,\u0026quot; Luna Lovegood said happily from the back, where she was examining a box of wand polish. \u0026quot;But Pan, please come down. The wand chooses the wizard, and wands are usually on the ground floor.\u0026quot;","Pan flipped right-side up and drifted down, her toes barely brushing the dusty floorboards.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Trials\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander bustled away and returned with a pale, elegant box.","\u0026quot;Willow and unicorn hair. Good for healing. Gentle.\u0026quot;","Pan reached out. Before her fingers even brushed the wood, the wand let out a high-pitched \u003cem\u003eshriek\u003c/em\u003e. It sounded like a tea kettle boiling over.","Pan recoiled, floating up a few inches in surprise.","\u0026quot;Too loud,\u0026quot; Pan whispered, covering her ears. \u0026quot;It’s shouting at me. It says I’m too... floaty.\u0026quot;","Ollivander frowned. \u0026quot;Ebony and dragon heartstring? Impressive combat magic.\u0026quot;","He handed it to her. Pan took it. Immediately, the wand turned ice cold. Frost coated her fingers.","\u0026quot;It’s scared,\u0026quot; Pan said sadly. \u0026quot;It doesn\u0027t like the things I see. It wants to hide under the bed.\u0026quot;","She handed it back. \u0026quot;Do you have any that like ghosts?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Solution\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander stood very still. He looked at the girl who saw the unseen. He looked at her silver eyes, which were currently tracking something invisible flying around his head.","\u0026quot;I see,\u0026quot; Ollivander murmured. \u0026quot;You require a conduit. Something that bridges the gap between the here... and the elsewhere.\u0026quot;","He walked to a section of the shop that was shrouded in shadow. He didn\u0027t climb a ladder; he knelt down and pulled a box from a shelf that seemed to be made of mist rather than wood.","He returned, holding a wand that looked strange. It was incredibly pale, almost white, with a grain that seemed to swirl like smoke.","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eSilver Lime\u003c/strong\u003e,\u0026quot; Ollivander announced. \u0026quot;A rare wood. In the nineteenth century, these wands were highly sought after. They have a reputation for performing best for Seers and those skilled in Legilimency.\u0026quot;","He opened the box.","\u0026quot;And the core... \u003cstrong\u003eDemiguise Hair\u003c/strong\u003e.\u0026quot;","Ron frowned. \u0026quot;Demiguise? The invisible monkeys?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered. \u0026quot;Creatures that can turn invisible and see the immediate future. A core that is notoriously difficult to capture, and even harder to craft. It fades from view if the user is not... attuned.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Connection\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander held out the wand.","Pan didn\u0027t grab it. She held out her open palm, flat and waiting.","The wand rose from the box. It didn\u0027t shoot up; it drifted. It floated through the air like a piece of driftwood on a slow current.","It hovered over Pan’s hand.","Then, it dissolved.","For a second, it looked like it had vanished. But then, a soft, silvery mist began to swirl around Pan’s fingers. The wand reappeared, but it wasn\u0027t solid wood anymore. It looked like it was made of starlight and smoke. It orbited her hand, spinning slowly, trailing silver sparkles that didn\u0027t hit the floor but vanished into nothingness.","Pan giggled. She reached out and plucked the wand from the air. As soon as she touched it, her eyes turned a brilliant, glowing silver.","\u0026quot;Hello,\u0026quot; Pan whispered to the wand.","Around the shop, the shadows lengthened and waved. The dust motes in the air rearranged themselves to form the shape of a galloping horse for a brief second before scattering.","\u0026quot;It sings,\u0026quot; Pan beamed, looking at her parents. \u0026quot;It sings the song of the tomorrow.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","Ron Weasley looked at his daughter, who was now holding a wand made of smoke that helped her see the future.","\u0026quot;Silver Lime,\u0026quot; Ron muttered. \u0026quot;Demiguise hair. Right. Of course. Why would she get a stick when she can get a... ghost stick?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s beautiful,\u0026quot; Luna said, clapping her hands. \u0026quot;It matches your aura, Pan. It’s full of Nargle-repellent.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Curious,\u0026quot; Ollivander noted, looking at Pan with a mixture of professional pride and mild concern. \u0026quot;That wand has sat on my shelf for fifty years. It never moved for anyone. It seems it was waiting for someone who doesn\u0027t quite live in the present.\u0026quot;","Pan tucked the wand behind her ear. It stayed there, phasing in and out of visibility.","\u0026quot;Thank you, Mr. Wand Man,\u0026quot; Pan said politely. Then she floated back up to the ceiling to inspect the spider again.","\u0026quot;Two down,\u0026quot; Harry noted, looking at the floating girl and the system administrator. \u0026quot;This is going great. Absolutely normal.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Next!\u0026quot; Ollivander called, wiping his brow."]},{"num":26,"origNum":27,"title":"The Shifting Stick","wordCount":739,"paragraphs":["\u0026quot;Next!\u0026quot; Ollivander called, his voice trembling slightly. He eyed the group, wondering what fresh chaos awaited him after the floating girl and the system administrator.","James Sirius Potter didn\u0027t walk to the counter. He vaulted over a display of wand polish, did a forward roll, and landed with a *ta-da* pose.","\u0026quot;Me!\u0026quot; James grinned, bouncing on the balls of his feet. \u0026quot;I want one that goes *boom*.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We do not aim for *boom*, Mr. Potter,\u0026quot; Ollivander sighed, adjusting his spectacles. \u0026quot;We aim for control.\u0026quot;","He looked at James. Unlike Thomas (who was a solid wall) or Pan (who was a cloud), James was a vibrating coil of energy. His outline seemed to fuzz slightly, as if his body couldn\u0027t decide what shape it wanted to be.","\u0026quot;You are... unstable,\u0026quot; Ollivander noted. \u0026quot;In the most fascinating way. You are in a constant state of flux.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Failures\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander handed James a standard wand. \u0026quot;Holly and phoenix feather. Like your father.\u0026quot;","James grabbed it. \u0026quot;Expelliarmus!\u0026quot; he shouted, waving it vigorously.","The wand didn\u0027t disarm anyone. Instead, it melted. It turned into a puddle of brown goo that dripped through James\u0027s fingers onto the floor.","\u0026quot;Too rigid,\u0026quot; James complained, shaking his sticky hand. \u0026quot;It couldn\u0027t keep up.\u0026quot;","Ollivander frowned. \u0026quot;Blackthorn and dragon heartstring. A warrior\u0027s wand.\u0026quot;","James took it. He gave it a swish.","*POP.*","The wand vanished. In its place, James was holding a live, very confused ferret.","\u0026quot;Draco!\u0026quot; Harry shouted, laughing. \u0026quot;He turned the wand into you!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ha ha, Potter,\u0026quot; Draco drawled, though he looked impressed as the ferret chattered at him. \u0026quot;At least it\u0027s a ferret with excellent posture.\u0026quot;","James petted the ferret, which then turned back into a splintered stick.","\u0026quot;It tried to change *with* me,\u0026quot; James explained. \u0026quot;But it broke.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Solution\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander rubbed his temples. \u0026quot;A shapeshifter. A true polymorph. You need a wand that does not hold a shape, but flows with it.\u0026quot;","He went to a cabinet that was chained shut. He unlocked it with a tap of his own wand.","He pulled out a box that seemed to be vibrating.","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eDogwood\u003c/strong\u003e,\u0026quot; Ollivander announced. \u0026quot;A mischievous wood. It refuses to perform non-verbal spells and is known for being... loud. It craves excitement.\u0026quot;","He opened the box.","\u0026quot;And the core... this is exceedingly rare. \u003cstrong\u003eFragment of a Chimera Scale\u003c/strong\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A Chimera?\u0026quot; Hermione gasped. \u0026quot;But that\u0027s a hybrid beast. Lion, Goat, Snake. It’s incredibly volatile.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Ollivander smiled. \u0026quot;Three beasts in one. Just like our young Mr. Potter here, who seems to be a boy, a dog, a falcon, and a monkey all at once.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Connection\u003c/strong\u003e","James reached into the box.","The moment his fingers touched the wood, the wand didn\u0027t just glow. It *rippled*.","The wood seemed to turn to liquid in his hand, molding itself perfectly to his grip, then hardening again. It changed color—from a deep brown to a fiery red, then to a sleek black, cycling through textures.","**ROAR-SCREECH-BARK.**","A cacophony of animal sounds erupted from the tip—a lion\u0027s roar, a falcon\u0027s cry, a dog\u0027s bark.","A chaotic swirl of illusionary shapes burst forth: a spectral lion chased a spectral badger around James\u0027s head, while a ghostly snake coiled up his arm.","James laughed, tossing the wand into the air. It spun, turning into a blur of light, and when he caught it, it was a different shape—shorter, thicker—before settling back into its original form.","\u0026quot;It’s alive!\u0026quot; James cheered. \u0026quot;It changes when I change!\u0026quot;","He sneezed.","*POOF.*","James turned into a black dog. The wand didn\u0027t fall to the floor. It shrank, morphed, and became a sleek, silver collar around the dog\u0027s neck.","Dog-James barked happily, tail wagging.","*POOF.*","He turned back into a boy. The collar morphed back into the wand in his hand.","\u0026quot;Wicked,\u0026quot; James breathed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;It accommodates the Animagus transformation,\u0026quot; Harry said, wiping a tear from his eye. \u0026quot;Sirius would have loved this. That is the coolest thing I have ever seen.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dogwood and Chimera,\u0026quot; Ollivander shuddered. \u0026quot;It will never be boring, Mr. Potter. But do try not to turn your classmates into hamsters.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No promises!\u0026quot; James grinned, swinging the wand like a conductor\u0027s baton.","A shower of multi-colored sparks rained down, nearly hitting Dudley.","\u0026quot;Whoa!\u0026quot; Dudley ducked, shielding his face. \u0026quot;Watch the sparks, kiddo! I\u0027m not fireproof!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Sorry, Uncle D!\u0026quot; James laughed.","\u0026quot;Three down,\u0026quot; Ron counted, looking a bit green. \u0026quot;And the scary ones are left.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Next!\u0026quot; Ollivander called, pouring himself a glass of water."]},{"num":27,"origNum":28,"title":"The Empress’s Scepter","wordCount":1025,"paragraphs":["\u0026quot;Next,\u0026quot; Ollivander rasped, his voice sounding significantly older than it had ten minutes ago.","Cassiopeia Malfoy stepped forward. She didn\u0027t bounce like James, nor did she float like Pan. She glided. She looked at the piles of rejected wands on the floor—the ash from Thomas’s reject, the puddle from James’s reject—and wrinkled her nose.","\u0026quot;I trust,\u0026quot; Cassie said coolly, \u0026quot;that we can expedite this process. I require an instrument of precision, Mr. Ollivander. Not a toy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precision,\u0026quot; Ollivander nodded, sweat beading on his forehead. \u0026quot;Yes. The Malfoy blood. The Black blood. A potent mix.\u0026quot;","The Rejections","He handed her a wand. \u0026quot;Elm and dragon heartstring. Dignified.\u0026quot;","Cassie barely touched it.","SNAP.","The wand froze solid instantly, turning white with frost, and then shattered into a thousand diamond-dust splinters that chimed as they hit the floor.","\u0026quot;Too brittle,\u0026quot; Cassie critiqued, wiping frost from her glove.","Ollivander swallowed. He fetched another. \u0026quot;Cherry and unicorn hair. A wand of lethality.\u0026quot;","Cassie grasped it.","FOOM.","The wand didn\u0027t just catch fire; it vaporized. A burst of white-hot flame consumed the wood in a microsecond, leaving Cassie holding a handful of grey ash.","\u0026quot;Too flammable,\u0026quot; Cassie sighed, dusting her hands. \u0026quot;Do you have anything that isn\u0027t... kindling?\u0026quot;","She looked at her father. \u0026quot;Daddy, this is tedious.\u0026quot;","Draco leaned on his cane (purely aesthetic), looking proud. \u0026quot;Patience, star. Excellence cannot be rushed.\u0026quot;","The Secret Cabinet","Ollivander stopped. He looked at the girl who burned wood and froze steel. He looked at the pile of destroyed inventory.","He walked past the shelves. He walked past the dusty desk. He walked to the very back of the shop, to a section of the wall that looked like solid brick.","He tapped a specific brick with his own wand. The wall didn\u0027t open like Diagon Alley; a single, small stone drawer slid out with a grinding noise of stone-on-stone.","From it, Ollivander removed a box. It wasn\u0027t cardboard. It was carved from a single block of Obsidian—black, glassy, and cold.","The air in the shop dropped ten degrees.","\u0026quot;I do not offer this wand,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered, carrying the heavy box to the counter with both hands. \u0026quot;It is not for sale. It is usually... for safekeeping.\u0026quot;","The Alliance stepped closer. Harry felt a prickle on the back of his neck that he hadn\u0027t felt since the Battle of Hogwarts.","\u0026quot;What is it?\u0026quot; Harry asked sharply.","\u0026quot;It has no recorded maker,\u0026quot; Ollivander said, his voice trembling. \u0026quot;It predates my family business. It was found in the ruins of a fortress in the mountains of Eastern Europe. Some say it was an experiment by a wizard who sought to replicate the Deathstick.\u0026quot;","He opened the obsidian lid.","The wand inside was terrifyingly beautiful. It was jet black, but not like paint. It sucked the light out of the room. It was carved with jagged, angular runes that seemed to move if you looked at them out of the corner of your eye.","\u0026quot;African Blackwood,\u0026quot; Ollivander intoned. \u0026quot;The most expensive wood in the world. Dense enough to break iron.\u0026quot;","He looked at Cassie.","\u0026quot;And the core... The Heartstring of a Nundu.\u0026quot;","Hermione gasped, clutching Ron’s arm. \u0026quot;A Nundu? The beast that requires a hundred wizards to subdue? Their breath is toxic! That’s... that’s a weapon of mass destruction, not a core!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered. \u0026quot;It is a wand of conquest. In terms of raw magical output, it is believed to be second in power only to the Elder Wand itself.\u0026quot;","The Connection","Cassie looked at the wand. She didn\u0027t look scared. She looked... hungry.","She reached out her hand.","\u0026quot;Mine,\u0026quot; she whispered.","Her fingers closed around the handle.","BOOOOM.","There was no wind. There was no light. There was a shockwave of pure pressure.","The windows of the shop blew outwards. The shelves rattled violently. The gas lamps flickered and died, plunging the shop into darkness.","Then, the wand lit up.","A pulse of violet energy—the color of royalty and bruising—erupted from the tip. It didn\u0027t shoot out; it spiraled around Cassie like a tornado.","On her left side, the floorboards froze into black ice.","On her right side, blue flames licked the counter.","Cassie stood in the center of the storm, her hair floating in the magical updraft, her grey eyes glowing with the violet reflection. She raised the wand. The fire and ice swirled together, merging into a beam of pure, destructive energy that she held in check with a mere flick of her wrist.","She laughed. It wasn\u0027t a child\u0027s laugh. It was the laugh of a queen ascending her throne.","\u0026quot;Oh, yes,\u0026quot; Cassie purred, feeling the wand hum against her palm like a purring cat. \u0026quot;This will do nicely.\u0026quot;","She lowered the wand. The storm vanished instantly. The lights flickered back on.","The Reaction","The shop was silent. There was frost on the ceiling and scorch marks on the carpet.","Draco Malfoy looked at his daughter. He looked at the Nundu wand—the sister to the Elder Wand.","He turned to Harry. He looked pale.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;I think we need to be very, very nice to her during her teenage years.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She has a Nundu wand,\u0026quot; Ron squeaked, hiding behind Hermione. \u0026quot;She has a wand made of death and poison. And she’s ten.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It suits her,\u0026quot; Chloe noted, ever the pragmatist. \u0026quot;It matches her shoes.\u0026quot;","Harry stared at the wand. He felt the power radiating off it even from five feet away.","\u0026quot;Ollivander,\u0026quot; Harry said, his voice serious. \u0026quot;Is that thing safe?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Safe?\u0026quot; Ollivander let out a hysterical little giggle. \u0026quot;No, Mr. Potter. That wand is not safe. It is a catastrophe waiting for a direction.\u0026quot;","He looked at Cassie, who was admiring her reflection in the obsidian box.","\u0026quot;But,\u0026quot; Ollivander wiped his brow, \u0026quot;it seems she is the only one who can hold it without dying. So... seven Galleons, please.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll pay double,\u0026quot; Draco said, throwing a bag of gold on the counter. \u0026quot;Just... don\u0027t tell the Ministry she has it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Four down,\u0026quot; Dudley said, looking at the ceiling to make sure it was still there. \u0026quot;And the smallest one is left.\u0026quot;","They all turned to look at Lily Luna Potter."]},{"num":28,"origNum":29,"title":"The Genesis Wand","wordCount":1105,"paragraphs":["The shop was vibrating. The lingering energy of Thomas’s order, James’s chaos, Pan’s time-distortion, and Cassie’s destructive power made the air feel thick and electric.","\u0026quot;And finally,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered, leaning heavily on the counter. \u0026quot;The smallest one.\u0026quot;","Lily Luna Potter stepped forward. She was so short her chin barely cleared the countertop. She looked up at Ollivander with eyes that held the brightness of a spring morning.","\u0026quot;Hello, Mr. Ollivander,\u0026quot; she chirped. \u0026quot;You look tired. Would you like a hug?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I... I am fine, my dear,\u0026quot; Ollivander blinked, feeling a sudden urge to sit down and nap. \u0026quot;Let us find you a match.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Rejections\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander handed her a standard wand. \u0026quot;Willow and unicorn hair.\u0026quot;","Lily touched it.","\u003cem\u003eBLOOM.\u003c/em\u003e","The wand didn\u0027t spark. It instantly sprouted leaves, then flowers, then actual cherries. It grew so fast it twisted out of shape, the wood expanding into a small, living tree branch in seconds.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Lily said. \u0026quot;It grew.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Too much life,\u0026quot; Ollivander muttered. He handed her another. \u0026quot;Ebony and dragon heartstring.\u0026quot;","Lily grasped it.","The wand began to hum. It turned gold. Then it started to heat up. It glowed brighter and brighter until it was like holding a lightbulb filament.","\u0026quot;Hot,\u0026quot; Lily said, dropping it.","The wand hit the floor and dissolved into a pile of golden glitter.","\u0026quot;It can\u0027t hold the charge,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered. \u0026quot;She isn\u0027t channeling magic; she is flooding it. She is overfilling the vessel.\u0026quot;","He looked at Lily. He saw the aura around her—the sheer, unadulterated positive energy that kept the Alliance sane and healed broken bones with a touch.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Epiphany\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander stared at her for a long time. His pale eyes widened. He looked at the scorched floor where Cassie stood. He looked at the organized shelves where Thomas stood.","\u0026quot;The Balance,\u0026quot; Ollivander breathed. \u0026quot;If there is a Destroyer... there must be a Creator.\u0026quot;","He backed away from the counter.","\u0026quot;Wait here,\u0026quot; he commanded. \u0026quot;Do not touch anything. Do not breathe too hard.\u0026quot;","He didn\u0027t go to the back. He went to the floorboards behind his desk. He tapped a specific knot in the wood seven times. A trapdoor popped open.","A golden light spilled out from the hole, illuminating the dust motes.","Ollivander reached down and pulled out a box.","It was not made of cardboard, wood, or obsidian. It appeared to be carved from \u003cstrong\u003eAlabaster\u003c/strong\u003e, or perhaps solidified moonlight. It was translucent, glowing with a soft, pulsing white rhythm.","He placed it on the counter. The light from the box washed over the shop, making the scorch marks from Cassie’s wand fade slightly.","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Ollivander said, his voice trembling with a mixture of terror and reverence, \u0026quot;is a relic.\u0026quot;","He looked at Harry and Hermione.","\u0026quot;You know of the Deathly Hallows. You know of the Elder Wand. The Wand of Destiny. The Deathstick.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded, his throat dry.","\u0026quot;The Elder Wand,\u0026quot; Ollivander lectured, \u0026quot;was designed to be invincible in a duel. Its purpose is to conquer. To take. To sever the thread of life.\u0026quot;","He placed his hand on the glowing box.","\u0026quot;But before the Three Brothers... there were the First Makers. This wand is one of the \u003cstrong\u003eFirst Ten\u003c/strong\u003e. It is not a weapon of war.\u0026quot;","He opened the lid.","The wand inside was pure, pristine white. It looked like bone, or perhaps polished ivory, but it had a texture like living skin.","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eWhite Hazel from the Garden of the Ancients\u003c/strong\u003e,\u0026quot; Ollivander whispered. \u0026quot;And the core... \u003cstrong\u003eA single feather from the First Phoenix.\u003c/strong\u003e The Phoenix that did not burn, but ascended.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In terms of raw magical throughput,\u0026quot; Ollivander said, looking directly at Lily, \u0026quot;it is more powerful than the Elder Wand. Because the Elder Wand is limited by destruction. It can only end things. This wand... this wand \u003cstrong\u003eGives\u003c/strong\u003e. It creates. It restores. It is infinite.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Connection\u003c/strong\u003e","Lily reached out. Her small hand looked like a shadow against the brilliance of the wand.","She touched it.","There was no sound. There was no wind.","There was \u003cstrong\u003eSilence\u003c/strong\u003e.","But it wasn\u0027t an empty silence. It was the silence of a cathedral. The silence of deep space. The silence of perfect peace.","A pulse of white light expanded from Lily.","It passed through the room.","Where it touched the floor, the scorch marks vanished.","Where it touched the shattered glass of the window, the shards flew back together and sealed seamlessly.","Where it touched the adults, their old scars—Harry’s lightning bolt, Draco’s Dark Mark scar, Ron’s splinching scars—faded to almost nothing.","The light moved out of the shop. Outside, in Diagon Alley, the cobblestones scrubbed themselves clean. The cloudy sky parted to reveal a beam of pure sunshine.","Lily lifted the wand. It didn\u0027t look like a stick in her hand; it looked like an extension of her soul.","She giggled.","\u0026quot;Warm,\u0026quot; Lily said. \u0026quot;It feels like a hug.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","Ollivander collapsed into his chair. He looked ten years younger, but completely exhausted.","\u0026quot;The Wand of Grace,\u0026quot; Ollivander wept openly. \u0026quot;I never thought I would see it chosen. It has rejected every saint and healer for two thousand years.\u0026quot;","Harry Potter stared at his daughter. He looked at Cassie, who was holding the wand of a Destroyer. He looked at Thomas, holding the wand of Order. He looked at James, holding the wand of Chaos. He looked at Pan, holding the wand of Sight.","And he looked at Lily, holding the wand of Life.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, tears streaming down her face as the residual magic washed over her. \u0026quot;Do you realize what this means?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yeah,\u0026quot; Harry rasped, feeling the overwhelming love radiating from his daughter. \u0026quot;It means we have the Apocalypse in our living room. But at least we have the cure.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The Alliance,\u0026quot; Draco Malfoy said, his voice devoid of its usual sarcasm, staring at the children with genuine fear and awe. \u0026quot;We didn\u0027t raise a Pack, Potter. We raised a Pantheon.\u0026quot;","Lily hopped down from the stool, the white wand glowing softly in her hand. She walked over to Cassie.","\u0026quot;Your wand is scary,\u0026quot; Lily said, pointing her white wand at Cassie’s black one. \u0026quot;But mine likes yours. They are sisters.\u0026quot;","Cassie looked at her obsidian wand, then at Lily’s white one. She smirked, a genuine, protective smile.","\u0026quot;Day and Night, Lil,\u0026quot; Cassie said. \u0026quot;We cover everything.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Five wands,\u0026quot; Dudley said, shaking his head in disbelief. \u0026quot;And I thought getting them school shoes was going to be the hard part.\u0026quot;","They turned to leave the shop, the bell tinkling behind them. The shop was cleaner, brighter, and more magical than it had been in centuries.","The Pack was armed. And Hogwarts wasn\u0027t ready."]},{"num":29,"origNum":30,"title":"The Departure of the Pantheon","wordCount":1149,"paragraphs":["The Platform was a sea of steam, owls, and crying parents. But as The Pack moved through the crowd, the sea parted.","They didn\u0027t push. They didn\u0027t shout. They simply walked in a V-formation.","\u003cstrong\u003eThomas\u003c/strong\u003e was at the point, his Lignum Vitae wand tucked invisibly into his pocket, his steps heavy and rhythmic. \u003cstrong\u003eJames\u003c/strong\u003e bounced on his left, vibrating with energy. \u003cstrong\u003eCassie\u003c/strong\u003e glided on his right, looking like she owned the railway. \u003cstrong\u003ePan\u003c/strong\u003e drifted slightly behind, humming a tune that didn\u0027t exist yet, and \u003cstrong\u003eLily\u003c/strong\u003e walked in the center, radiating a glow that made everyone they passed suddenly feel like they’d just had a really good cup of hot chocolate.","They boarded the train. The corridors were packed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Eviction\u003c/strong\u003e","They reached a prime compartment in the middle of the train. It was currently occupied by four large Sixth Year Slytherins and two Ravenclaws. They were loud, they were taking up space, and they were laughing at a First Year who had dropped his trunk.","The door slid open.","The laughter stopped.","Cassiopeia Malfoy stood in the doorway. She was eleven. She was tiny compared to the sixteen-year-olds.","She didn\u0027t draw her wand. She didn\u0027t need the Nundu’s power for this; she just needed her face.","She looked at the tallest Slytherin boy. She tilted her head slightly. Her grey eyes went flat and cold—a look of absolute, terrifying boredom.","\u0026quot;You are sitting in our seats,\u0026quot; Cassie stated. Her voice was soft, silken, and carried the weight of a guillotine blade.","\u0026quot;Beat it, Firstie,\u0026quot; the boy sneered, though his voice wavered. \u0026quot;Go find the nursery.\u0026quot;","Cassie didn\u0027t blink. The air temperature in the compartment dropped fifteen degrees in a second. Frost began to creep across the glass of the window, cracking the pane with a loud \u003cem\u003esnap\u003c/em\u003e.","Behind her, James grinned, his teeth looking slightly too sharp.","Beside him, Thomas cracked his knuckles, the sound echoing like a gunshot.","And Pan leaned around the corner, her silver eyes glowing. \u0026quot;You should move,\u0026quot; she whispered. \u0026quot;Before the bad luck sticks to your shoelaces.\u0026quot;","The Sixth Years looked at the small girl who was freezing the room with her mood. They looked at the boy who vibrated. They felt the overwhelming pressure of \u003cem\u003epower\u003c/em\u003e radiating from the doorway.","Primitive survival instincts kicked in.","\u0026quot;We... uh... we were just leaving,\u0026quot; the Slytherin stammered.","They grabbed their trunks and scrambled past the first years, pressing themselves against the corridor walls to escape the aura of the Pack.","\u0026quot;Efficient,\u0026quot; Thomas noted, stepping inside and stowing his trunk with one smooth motion.","\u0026quot;I didn\u0027t even have to freeze their tea,\u0026quot; Cassie sighed, sitting down and crossing her legs.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Farewell\u003c/strong\u003e","Outside on the platform, The Alliance stood by the open window. The laughter of the shopping trip had faded, replaced by the heavy, aching lump in the throat that every parent knows.","\u003cstrong\u003eDudley and Chloe\u003c/strong\u003e","Dudley Dursley, the heavyweight boxing champion, looked like he was about to cry. He reached through the window and gripped Thomas’s hand.","\u0026quot;You got everything, champ?\u0026quot; Dudley asked, his voice thick. \u0026quot;Wand? Books? The screwdriver set?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Inventory checked twice, Dad,\u0026quot; Thomas said, his face calm. He squeezed Dudley’s hand—a grip that was shockingly strong for a boy. \u0026quot;Systems are green.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Take care of them, Tom,\u0026quot; Dudley whispered. \u0026quot;You\u0027re the Anchor. Keep their feet on the ground.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will,\u0026quot; Thomas promised. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll keep the team optimized.\u0026quot;","Chloe kissed Thomas’s forehead. \u0026quot;Don\u0027t forget to eat something other than sandwiches, sweetie.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRon and Luna\u003c/strong\u003e","Luna was adjusting a pair of Spectrespecs on Pan’s nose.","\u0026quot;Now, remember,\u0026quot; Luna said dreamily. \u0026quot; The Wrackspurts at Hogwarts are very aggressive during exams. Keep your aura fluffy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I will, Mummy,\u0026quot; Pan hummed, floating an inch off the seat.","Ron leaned in, looking at his daughter with fierce pride. \u0026quot;And Pan? If anyone gives you grief about being... you know, you...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll tell them their future?\u0026quot; Pan asked.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Ron grinned. \u0026quot;You tell them your Uncle Harry is the Head Auror and your cousin Cassie has a wand made of death. Okay?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco and Ginny\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy looked at his daughter. He saw the ice, the fire, and the Nundu wand hidden in her sleeve. He saw a queen in the making.","\u0026quot;Cassiopeia,\u0026quot; Draco said, his voice serious. \u0026quot;Ambition is a virtue. But cruelty is a weakness. Do not confuse the two.\u0026quot;","Cassie looked at her father. She softened. The ice melted from her eyes.","\u0026quot;I know, Father,\u0026quot; she said. \u0026quot;I will lead. I will not rule.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And if anyone pulls your pigtails,\u0026quot; Ginny added with a wicked grin, \u0026quot;you have my permission to turn their eyebrows into caterpillars.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mother,\u0026quot; Cassie smirked. \u0026quot;I aim much higher than eyebrows.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry and Hermione\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter stood looking at James and Lily. He saw his father’s chaos in James. He saw his mother’s love in Lily. And he saw himself and Hermione in all of them.","\u0026quot;James,\u0026quot; Harry said, pointing a finger. \u0026quot;Try... just try... to keep the detention letters to a minimum? At least for the first week?\u0026quot;","James laughed, hanging out the window. \u0026quot;I\u0027m going for the record, Dad! Marauders 2.0!\u0026quot;","Hermione was fussing over Lily, straightening her collar. \u0026quot;You have the extra cloak? And the potions kit?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, Mum,\u0026quot; Lily smiled. She reached out and took Harry’s hand and Hermione’s hand.","A pulse of warm, white light flowed from her skin to theirs. The anxiety of separation vanished. The fear of the future dissolved. They felt only peace and the certainty that everything would be alright.","\u0026quot;We’ll be okay,\u0026quot; Lily promised, her green eyes shining. \u0026quot;We have each other. We’re a Pack.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Departure\u003c/strong\u003e","A loud whistle blew. The steam billowed thicker, obscuring the scarlet engine.","\u0026quot;All aboard!\u0026quot;","The train jerked. The wheels began to turn.","\u0026quot;Bye!\u0026quot; James shouted, waving frantically.","\u0026quot;Optimizing route to Scotland,\u0026quot; Thomas stated, waving stoically.","\u0026quot;Goodbye,\u0026quot; Pan whispered to the steam.","Cassie gave a regal nod.","Lily blew a kiss that seemed to turn into a butterfly made of light before vanishing.","The Alliance stood on the platform. Harry put his arm around Hermione. Dudley rested his hand on Harry’s shoulder. Ron and Draco stood side by side.","They watched the train pick up speed, rounding the corner and disappearing into the tunnel.","The silence on the platform was heavy, but it wasn\u0027t sad.","\u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; Harry exhaled, a long, shaky breath. \u0026quot;They\u0027re gone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hogwarts won\u0027t know what hit it,\u0026quot; Draco murmured.","\u0026quot;The Pack has left the building,\u0026quot; Dudley smiled.","\u0026quot;Do you think they\u0027ll be okay?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, the worry creeping back in.","Harry looked at the empty track. He thought of the five wands. The five children. The perfect balance of Chaos, Order, Sight, Power, and Life.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry smiled. \u0026quot;They won\u0027t just be okay, Hermione. They\u0027re going to change the world.\u0026quot;","He turned to his family.","\u0026quot;Now... who wants a drink? I think we’re going to need it before the first owl arrives.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":30,"origNum":31,"title":"The Giant and the Guardian","wordCount":966,"paragraphs":["The train screeched to a halt in Hogsmeade Station. It was pitch black outside, the air biting with the chill of the Scottish highlands.","The doors opened, spilling noise and students onto the platform.","\u0026quot;Firs\u0027 years! Firs\u0027 years over here!\u0026quot;","The voice was a deep, rumbling boom that shook the soot off the station lamps. A giant of a man stood at the end of the platform, swinging a lantern as big as a beer barrel. His beard was wild, his coat was made of moleskin, and his eyes crinkled like black beetles in a smiling face.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reunion\u003c/strong\u003e","The crowd of terrified first years huddled together, intimidated by the sheer size of Rubeus Hagrid.","The Pack, however, did not huddle.","\u0026quot;Uncle Hagrid!\u0026quot; James shouted, his voice cracking with joy.","He didn\u0027t walk; he sprinted. He dodged a confused Hufflepuff, ducked under a Ravenclaw’s trunk, and launched himself at the half-giant.","\u0026quot;Whoa there!\u0026quot; Hagrid chuckled, catching James with one hand like he was a Quaffle.","But James wasn\u0027t alone.","Lily was right behind him, beaming. \u0026quot;Hagrid!\u0026quot; she squealed, hugging his massive leg since she couldn\u0027t reach any higher.","Pan floated—literally floated—over the heads of the other students and landed softly on Hagrid’s shoulder, patting his hair. \u0026quot; The bats in your beard are sleeping,\u0026quot; she whispered.","Cassie walked up with dignity, but her cool mask slipped into a genuine smile. She didn\u0027t tackle him, but she placed a hand on his coat. \u0026quot;Hello, Hagrid. You look... robust.\u0026quot;","And Thomas marched up, tilting his head back to look at the towering figure. He scanned Hagrid’s dimensions. \u0026quot;Structural integrity: Massive,\u0026quot; Thomas noted approvingly. He extended a hand. \u0026quot;Good evening, sir.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHagrid’s Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","Hagrid looked down. He saw Harry’s messy hair in James. He saw Lily’s eyes in Lily. He saw Draco’s chin in Cassie. He saw Ron’s freckles in Pan. And he saw a sturdy Dursley who looked at him with respect.","The giant froze. His beetle-black eyes filled with tears instantly.","\u0026quot;All of yeh,\u0026quot; Hagrid choked out, his voice thick and wobbly. \u0026quot;All of yeh together.\u0026quot;","He dropped the lantern (it didn\u0027t break; Thomas caught it with his reflexes). Hagrid opened his arms and scooped them up—James, Lily, Cassie, and Thomas—into a bone-crushing hug that lifted them all off the ground. Pan hugged his head from her perch on his shoulder.","\u0026quot;Look at yeh!\u0026quot; Hagrid sobbed openly, great tears splashing onto James\u0027s robes. \u0026quot;Just like yer mums and dads! Oh, I’ve been waitin’ for this! The Pack! At Hogwarts!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Can\u0027t breathe, Hagrid,\u0026quot; James wheezed happily.","\u0026quot;Ribs compressing,\u0026quot; Thomas noted, though he didn\u0027t struggle.","Hagrid set them down, sniffing loudly and wiping his eyes with a tablecloth-sized handkerchief.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Hagrid blew his nose with a sound like a foghorn. \u0026quot;Right then. No dawdlin\u0027. We got a schedule. Follow me! Mind yer step! Firs\u0027 years!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Black Lake\u003c/strong\u003e","The path down to the lake was steep and slippery. Thomas walked at the back, ensuring no one slipped. Lily walked in the middle, and the darkness seemed less scary around her.","They rounded a bend, and there was a collective gasp.","The Black Lake was a sheet of glass reflecting the stars. And atop the mountain on the other side, windows sparkling against the sky, was Hogwarts Castle.","\u0026quot;High ground advantage,\u0026quot; Thomas murmured, nodding at the fortifications. \u0026quot;Excellent defensive positioning.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s singing,\u0026quot; Pan whispered, staring at the stone turrets. \u0026quot;It remembers us.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Four to a boat!\u0026quot; Hagrid called out.","The Pack faced a logistical issue. There were five of them.","\u0026quot;I will take my own,\u0026quot; Cassie announced. She stepped into a boat. \u0026quot;Ice,\u0026quot; she whispered. The water around the hull froze slightly, stabilizing it.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m with her!\u0026quot; James jumped in.","\u0026quot;Me too,\u0026quot; Thomas stepped in, balancing the weight perfectly. \u0026quot;Center of gravity adjusted.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pan?\u0026quot; Lily asked.","\u0026quot;I\u0027ll fly,\u0026quot; Pan hummed, but Hagrid gently lifted her and Lily into the next boat. \u0026quot;No flyin\u0027, Pan. Yeh gotta arrive proper.\u0026quot;","The fleet of little boats pushed off all at once, gliding across the glass-smooth water.","As they approached the cliff face, silence fell over the group. The sheer scale of the magic washed over them. James stopped vibrating. Cassie stopped preening. Even Thomas stopped analyzing the masonry.","They were just children, staring at their destiny.","\u0026quot;Heads down!\u0026quot; Hagrid roared as they reached the ivy curtain.","They ducked, sailing through the dark tunnel and arriving at the underground harbor.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","They clambered out onto the rocks. Thomas checked everyone for wet shoes. Lily made sure a nervous Muggle-born boy who had lost his toad felt better.","Then, they walked up the flight of stone steps.","They crowded around the huge Oak Front Doors.","Hagrid raised a gigantic fist and knocked three times.","The door swung open immediately.","Standing there, bathed in the light of the entrance hall, was a tall, black-haired witch in emerald-green robes. Her face was stern, her glasses were square, and her hair was pulled back into a tight bun.","She looked exactly the same as she had in the stories their parents told.","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor Minerva McGonagall.\u003c/strong\u003e","She looked down at the sea of first years. Her eyes scanned the crowd.","She saw the messy black hair of a Potter.","She saw the platinum blonde of a Malfoy.","She saw the dreamy stare of a Weasley-Lovegood.","She saw the red hair of a Potter-Weasley.","And she saw the sturdy, serious face of a boy who looked remarkably like a polite version of Vernon Dursley.","McGonagall’s lips thinned. Her nostrils flared slightly.","She didn\u0027t just see five students. She saw twenty years of headaches, heart attacks, and gray hairs standing in a V-formation.","She saw The Pantheon.","\u0026quot;Welcome to Hogwarts,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, her voice crisp but with a tremor of deep, deep foreboding. \u0026quot;The Sorting Ceremony is about to begin.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":31,"origNum":32,"title":"The Assault on Dignity","wordCount":667,"paragraphs":["Professor Minerva McGonagall stood tall, her posture rigid, her expression one of severe, academic authority. She opened her mouth to deliver the speech she had given for decades—the one about House points, rule-breaking, and the utter necessity of decorum.","\u0026quot;The Sorting Ceremony,\u0026quot; she began, her voice echoing off the stone walls, \u0026quot;is a very serious—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;AUNT MINNIE!\u0026quot;","The scream didn\u0027t come from a terrified student. It came from James Sirius Potter.","Before McGonagall could process the breach of protocol, a small, black-haired missile launched itself from the crowd. James slammed into her midsection, wrapping his arms around her waist.","\u0026quot;Mr. Potter!\u0026quot; McGonagall gasped, the wind knocked out of her. \u0026quot;Release me this inst—\u0026quot;","She didn\u0027t finish.","\u0026quot;Minnie!\u0026quot; Lily squealed, waddling forward and hugging McGonagall’s knees, burying her face in the emerald robes.","\u0026quot;Hello, Professor,\u0026quot; Pan hummed, drifting up and wrapping her arms around McGonagall’s neck, her feet dangling a foot off the floor. \u0026quot;Your aura is very spiky today. Let me smooth it.\u0026quot;","Cassie, usually the picture of Malfoy reserve, stepped forward. She didn\u0027t run, but she moved with purpose. She stepped into the hug, wrapping her arms around McGonagall’s side and resting her head against the witch\u0027s arm.","\u0026quot;We missed you, Aunt Minerva,\u0026quot; Cassie said softy.","And finally, Thomas Dursley walked up. He didn\u0027t tackle her. He stood beside the pile of children, placed a sturdy hand on her shoulder, and gave it a reassuring squeeze.","\u0026quot;Good to see you, Ma\u0027am,\u0026quot; Thomas said earnestly. \u0026quot;You\u0027re looking structurally sound.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","For the other first years, this was like watching someone hug a hungry dragon.","A small Hufflepuff boy dropped his toad again. A Ravenclaw girl covered her eyes, expecting an explosion. The nervous Muggle-born boy whispered, \u0026quot;Are they insane? She\u0027s going to turn them into desk lamps!\u0026quot;","McGonagall stood there, encased in children. She was the Deputy Headmistress. She was a formidable witch. She was not a hugging post.","She stiffened. She sputtered.","\u0026quot;This... this is highly irregular!\u0026quot; McGonagall stammered, trying to pry James off her sash. \u0026quot;We are at school! I am your Professor! Unhand me!\u0026quot;","But then, she looked down.","She saw the top of James’s messy head (so like Harry’s). She felt the warmth radiating from Lily (so like her grandmother). She felt the cool dignity of Cassie and the dreamy weight of Pan.","Minerva McGonagall’s stern mouth twitched. The steel in her spine softened, just for a fraction of a second. She let out a sigh that was 10% annoyance and 90% suppressed affection.","Her hand came up, almost involuntarily, and patted James’s hair. She rested her other hand on Thomas’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;You are,\u0026quot; she whispered, her voice sounding suspicious wet, \u0026quot;a collection of menaces. The lot of you.\u0026quot;","She cleared her throat loudly—a sound like a cracking whip.","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; McGonagall announced, her voice returning to its usual steel. \u0026quot;Detach yourselves immediately. Or I shall deduct points before you are even Sorted.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Entry\u003c/strong\u003e","The Pack unpeeled themselves.","James grinned, straightening his robes. \u0026quot;Worth it.\u0026quot;","Lily beamed up at her.","Cassie smoothed her skirt, looking as if she had never hugged anyone in her life.","Pan floated back to the floor.","Thomas nodded respectfully and stepped back into formation.","McGonagall took a moment to adjust her spectacles and smooth her ruffled robes. She took a deep breath, composing herself. She looked at the terrified crowd of first years, then at the five smiling faces of the Pantheon.","\u0026quot;Follow me,\u0026quot; she commanded.","She turned and tapped the great oak doors with her wand.","\u003cstrong\u003eCREAAAK.\u003c/strong\u003e","The massive doors groaned open. A flood of golden light spilled into the entrance hall. The hum of hundreds of voices drifted out, along with the smell of roasting meats and pumpkin juice.","McGonagall strode forward.","Behind her, the first years shuffled nervously.","But at the front, walking in step with the Deputy Headmistress, The Pack marched in. They didn\u0027t look scared. They looked like they were coming home.","They stepped across the threshold and into the Great Hall."]},{"num":32,"origNum":33,"title":"The Walk of the Pantheon","wordCount":802,"paragraphs":["The Great Hall of Hogwarts was usually a cacophony of sound at the start of the term. Hundreds of students reunited, shouting across tables, while ghosts drifted through the air and enchanted candles flickered overhead.","But the moment the oak doors opened and The Pack crossed the threshold, the noise didn\u0027t taper off. It was severed.","Silence slammed into the room like a physical weight.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Atmosphere\u003c/strong\u003e","McGonagall led the way, but no one was looking at the Deputy Headmistress. Every eye was fixed on the five small eleven-year-olds walking in V-formation behind her.","It wasn\u0027t just that they were famous names. It was the air around them.","As \u003cstrong\u003eCassiopeia Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e glided past the Slytherin table, the air grew noticeably colder. The candles nearest to her dimmed, their flames turning a spectral blue. She didn\u0027t look at the students; she looked straight ahead at the High Table, her expression one of utter, regal indifference. The older Slytherins, usually quick to jeer at first years, sat up straighter, sensing a predator in their midst.","\u003cstrong\u003eJames Sirius Potter\u003c/strong\u003e walked with a bounce that seemed to vibrate the flagstones. The Gryffindors watched him, feeling a sudden spike in adrenaline, a restless urge to run, to jump, to \u003cem\u003edo\u003c/em\u003e something. He grinned at a Fifth Year, and the boy found himself grinning back, energized without knowing why.","\u003cstrong\u003eThomas Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e walked like a soldier. He scanned the structural supports of the ceiling. The Ravenclaws, usually lost in books or riddles, found their attention snapped to him. There was a solidity to him, a heavy reality that made the magic of the ceiling seem less whimsical and more like a calculated equation.","\u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e drifted. She wasn\u0027t looking at the tables; she was waving at the Bloody Baron, who actually stopped floating and bowed to her.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Wave of Peace\u003c/strong\u003e","But the true silence, the true awe, came from the center of the formation.","\u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter\u003c/strong\u003e.","She was the smallest student in the hall. But as she walked past the Hufflepuff and Ravenclaw tables, a phenomenon occurred.","A Fifth Year girl who had been crying about a breakup suddenly stopped. She wiped her eyes, took a deep breath, and felt a profound sense that everything was going to be fine.","A Seventh Year boy, stressed about his N.E.W.T.s, felt his shoulders drop three inches. The knot of anxiety in his chest untied itself.","The ghosts stopped bickering.","Even Mrs. Norris, the caretaker\u0027s hateful cat, rolled over on her back and purred as Lily passed.","Lily didn\u0027t notice the stares. She was just walking, radiating a blast radius of pure, unconditional wellness.","\u0026quot;Merlin\u0027s beard,\u0026quot; a Sixth Year Prefect whispered to his friend. \u0026quot;Do you feel that? It feels like... like Christmas morning.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It feels like a Cheering Charm,\u0026quot; the friend whispered back, looking at Lily. \u0026quot;But stronger. Who \u003cem\u003eis\u003c/em\u003e that?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That,\u0026quot; a voice whispered from the darkness of the Slytherin table, \u0026quot;is the Pantheon.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Stool\u003c/strong\u003e","The Pack reached the front of the hall. They stopped before the three-legged stool and the tattered, patched wizard’s hat.","The Sorting Hat, which usually sang a song about unity or bravery, had stayed silent this year. It seemed to be holding its breath.","McGonagall unfurled a long roll of parchment. She looked at the crowd of first years huddled behind The Pack—the normal children, the terrified Muggle-borns, the ones who didn\u0027t hold wands made of Nundu bone or Starlight.","\u0026quot;When I call your name,\u0026quot; McGonagall announced, her voice echoing in the unnatural silence, \u0026quot;you will put on the Hat and sit on the stool to be sorted.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Others\u003c/strong\u003e","The sorting began with the usual suspects, serving as a breaker for the tension.","\u0026quot;Ackerman, Dennis!\u0026quot;","A shaking boy walked up. The Hat barely touched his head. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;RAVENCLAW!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","The table cheered, but it was a polite cheer. They were still watching the five children at the front.","\u0026quot;Bones, Susan!\u0026quot; (A niece, perhaps). \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;HUFFLEPUFF!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Creevey, Colin II!\u0026quot; \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;GRYFFINDOR!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","The list went on. \u0026quot;Davis.\u0026quot; \u0026quot;Finnegan.\u0026quot; \u0026quot;Goldstein.\u0026quot;","The Hat was working quickly, almost impatiently. It shouted \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;SLYTHERIN!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e for a boy named Nott, and \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;RAVENCLAW!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e for a girl named Patil.","The Pack stood still. They didn\u0027t fidget. Thomas stood at parade rest. Cassie checked her nails. Pan hummed. James rocked on his heels. Lily watched the Hat with sympathy.","Finally, the crowd of un-sorted first years thinned out. The \u0026quot;normal\u0026quot; children had found their tables. The Hall was full.","Only five children remained standing in the center of the Great Hall.","McGonagall lowered the scroll slightly. She took a deep breath. She adjusted her glasses. She looked at the Hat.","The entire hall leaned forward. The teachers on the High Table—Flitwick, Sprout, Slughorn—sat up. Even the Headmaster\u0027s portrait behind the chair seemed to wake up.","The prelude was over. The main event was about to begin."]},{"num":33,"origNum":34,"title":"The Sorting of the Pantheon","wordCount":1272,"paragraphs":["The silence in the Great Hall was absolute. McGonagall unrolled the scroll further. Her voice was steady, but her eyes betrayed her anxiety. Behind her, at the center of the High Table, sat \u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore\u003c/strong\u003e. He was not a painting; he was alive, vibrant, and watching the proceedings with an intensity that made his blue eyes blaze behind his half-moon spectacles.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Architect\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Dursley, Thomas.\u0026quot;","A ripple of confusion went through the Muggle-borns and Half-bloods who knew the name. \u003cem\u003eDursley? A wizard?\u003c/em\u003e","Thomas walked up the steps. He sat on the stool. He looked at the Hat, then placed it squarely on his head.","The Hat didn\u0027t speak immediately. It hummed. A low, mechanical vibration.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Fascinating,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat’s voice whispered in Thomas’s ear, though it sounded clearer than usual, as if the connection had been scrubbed of static. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I have never seen a mind so... organized. There is no clutter here. No fear. Just pure, unadulterated structural integrity.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Efficiency is key,\u0026quot; Thomas thought back.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat agreed. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You do not seek glory. You do not seek power for power\u0027s sake. You seek to build. To optimize. To ensure the foundation holds. You are the Anchor.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","The Hat paused.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You have the loyalty of a Badger, but your method... your method is pure calculation. You are an architect of reality.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eRAVENCLAW!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot;","The Hat shouted the last word with a crisp, sharp tone. The Ravenclaw table applauded politely, though they looked confused by the broad-shouldered boy who didn\u0027t look like a typical bookworm. Thomas nodded, took off the Hat, and marched to the blue and bronze table. He sat down and immediately began organizing the silverware by size. Dumbledore clapped politely, his eyes twinkling.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Drifter\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Weasley, Pandora.\u0026quot;","Pan didn\u0027t walk; she drifted. She floated up the steps, humming a tune. She sat on the stool, and the Hat slid over her eyes.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Oh, my,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat chuckled nervously. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I usually look into your head, my dear. But you... you are looking into mine.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;You have a loose thread in 1994,\u0026quot; Pan thought dreamily.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I... yes, I suppose I do,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat stammered. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You are untethered in time. You see the ripples before the stone hits the water. A mind like this could go anywhere. You have the vision of a Ravenclaw, the daring of a Gryffindor...\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I want to be near the kitchen,\u0026quot; Pan thought. \u0026quot;And the plants. And the badger is fuzzy.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Loyalty,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat noted. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You bind them together. You are the glue that holds the Pack in the light.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eHUFFLEPUFF!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot;","The Hufflepuff table cheered wildly. Pan floated over, the Hat still perched crookedly on the stool behind her until McGonagall grabbed it.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Empress\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Malfoy, Cassiopeia.\u0026quot;","The air chilled. Cassie ascended the steps. She sat down with the grace of a queen taking her throne. She lowered the Hat onto her head.","The Hat gasped. It was audible.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Ice and Fire,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat whispered, its voice trembling. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;And the Shadow of the Nundu. You have ambition that would make Salazar himself take a step back. You desire to reshape the world.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;I desire to improve it,\u0026quot; Cassie corrected mentally. \u0026quot;Through order.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You are powerful,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat murmured. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Terrifyingly so. You could be great in Gryffindor... you have the nerve. But no... you are your father\u0027s daughter, but stronger. You are the blade in the darkness.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eSLYTHERIN!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot;","The Slytherin table erupted. They knew royalty when they saw it. Cassie removed the Hat, smoothed her hair, and glided to the table. As she passed the High Table, Dumbledore dipped his head in a respectful, solemn nod. Cassie returned it.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Hurricane\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Potter, James Sirius.\u0026quot;","James vaulted onto the stool before his name was fully called. He jammed the Hat onto his head.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Good heavens!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat shouted inside his head. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;It’s a zoo in here! Stop spinning! Is that a lion? A dog? A monkey? Boy, sit still!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Can\u0027t!\u0026quot; James laughed mentally.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You are a storm,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat said, sounding dizzy. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Chaos incarnate. You have bravery, yes. Recklessness in spades. You would charge a dragon with a teaspoon just to see what happens.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Sounds fun,\u0026quot; James thought.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;There is only one place for a hurricane.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eGRYFFINDOR!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot;","The Gryffindor table roared. James sprinted over, high-fiving the air.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Soul\u003c/strong\u003e","And then, there was one.","\u0026quot;Potter, Lily Luna.\u0026quot;","The Hall went silent again. Lily walked up. She looked tiny on the stool. The Hat dropped over her eyes, swallowing her whole head.","For a long moment, the Hat said nothing.","Then, a sound filled the Hall. The Hat... sighed.","It wasn\u0027t a sigh of boredom. It was a sigh of pure, unadulterated relief. It was the sound of a tired old man finally sitting in a comfortable chair by a fire.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Oh...\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e the Hat whispered, its voice projected to the whole room, soft and gentle. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I haven\u0027t felt this... ever. No shadows. No cracks. Just... light.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","Inside Lily’s head, the Hat was weeping tears of joy. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You heal me, child. Just by wearing me. You are the heart. The courage to love when the world is dark. The strength to be kind when it is hard.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Thank you, Mr. Hat,\u0026quot; Lily thought.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;You are the truest Lion I have ever met.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eGRYFFINDOR!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot;","The cheer was deafening. But it was also warm. Lily hopped down, beamed at McGonagall (who smiled back), and skipped to the Gryffindor table to sit next to James.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Speech\u003c/strong\u003e","The Pack was sorted. The four Houses were balanced. Chaos and Life in Gryffindor. Order in Slytherin. Vision in Hufflepuff. Structure in Ravenclaw.","Headmistress McGonagall rolled up her scroll and took her seat.","Albus Dumbledore stood up.","He wore robes of midnight blue embroidered with silver stars. His beard was as long and white as ever, and he looked positively radiant. The Hall fell silent instantly. Dumbledore had that effect—he didn\u0027t demand attention; he simply commanded it by existing.","He looked out over the sea of faces. His gaze lingered for a split second on the Ravenclaw table (Thomas), the Hufflepuff table (Pan), the Slytherin table (Cassie), and finally the Gryffindor table (James and Lily).","\u0026quot;Welcome,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, his voice deep and resonating without a charm. \u0026quot;To another year at Hogwarts.\u0026quot;","He smiled, and the twinkle in his eyes was blinding.","\u0026quot;We have new faces among us. And some old names with new energy.\u0026quot;","He clasped his hands together.","\u0026quot;The world outside these walls is changing. Magic itself seems to be evolving. But remember this...\u0026quot;","Dumbledore leaned forward over the golden owl lectern.","\u0026quot;Darkness is merely the absence of light. Chaos is merely the absence of Order. And as long as you find friendship across these four tables... as long as you realize that a Pack is stronger than a lone wolf...\u0026quot;","He beamed at the students.","\u0026quot;We shall weather any storm.\u0026quot;","He straightened up, spreading his arms wide in a gesture of welcome.","\u0026quot;But, before we get too heavy with philosophy, I believe there are empty stomachs to be filled! I have only four words to say to you!\u0026quot;","The returning students grinned, mouthing the words along with him.","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eNitwit! Blubber! Oddment! Tweak!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot;","Dumbledore sat down.","\u0026quot;Thank you!\u0026quot;","Golden platters filled instantly with roast beef, Yorkshire puddings, and mashed potatoes. The Feast began.","At the High Table, Dumbledore leaned over to McGonagall.","\u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; he whispered, buttering a roll. \u0026quot;I believe the castle is vibrating.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall sighed, watching James turn his goblet into a squirrel. \u0026quot;It is the Pantheon. I give it a week before the staircases start moving just to get out of their way.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore chuckled. \u0026quot;Oh, this is going to be a fun year.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":34,"origNum":35,"title":"The Malfoy Endowment","wordCount":1211,"paragraphs":["The Gargoyle guarding the Headmaster’s office had let the Pantheon pass earlier that evening, but now it stood guard over a much more somber meeting.","Inside the circular office, the delicate silver instruments whirred and puffed smoke. Fawkes the Phoenix was asleep on his perch, his head under his wing.","Albus Dumbledore sat behind his desk, unwrapping a Sherbet Lemon with calm precision.","Opposite him, Minerva McGonagall was massaging her temples as if trying to push a migraine back into her skull. Severus Snape was pacing the room like a caged panther, his black robes billowing with every angry turn.","\u0026quot;They have been here for three hours,\u0026quot; Snape hissed, stopping to glare at a sleeping portrait of Phineas Nigellus Black. \u0026quot;Three hours, Albus. And already, the Grey Lady has reported that the temperature in the dungeons has dropped to sub-zero because the Malfoy girl didn\u0027t like the humidity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Mr. Potter,\u0026quot; McGonagall added, her voice tight. \u0026quot;James. He was seen \u003cem\u003eracing\u003c/em\u003e the Moving Staircases. And winning. The stairs are now confused. They’ve stopped moving entirely.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And let us not forget the Dursley boy,\u0026quot; Snape sneered. \u0026quot;Filch found him in the trophy room. He wasn\u0027t polishing the trophies. He was \u003cem\u003ereorganizing\u003c/em\u003e them by metallurgical density. Filch is weeping in a cupboard because he can\u0027t find the Quidditch Cup.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore popped the sweet into his mouth and smiled.","\u0026quot;They are spirited,\u0026quot; Dumbledore agreed. \u0026quot;But the castle has weathered worse, Severus. It weathered the Founders. It weathered the War.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;This isn\u0027t a war, Headmaster,\u0026quot; Snape countered, slamming his hand on the back of a chair. \u0026quot;This is a hostile takeover by five eleven-year-olds with the power of gods. The Weasley girl... the \u003cem\u003efloating\u003c/em\u003e one... she told me I would find a missing sock in 1999. I don\u0027t even know what that means!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Arrival\u003c/strong\u003e","A knock interrupted Snape’s rant. The door opened.","Harry Potter and Draco Malfoy stepped inside.","They looked different from the frantic first-time parents on the platform. They looked like men who had dropped a bomb and were now coming to pay for the crater.","\u0026quot;Professors,\u0026quot; Harry said, giving a tired smile. \u0026quot;Headmaster.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ah, Harry, Draco,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed. \u0026quot;Come in. Tea?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No tea, Albus,\u0026quot; Draco said smoothly. He walked to the desk with the confidence of a man who owned the land the desk grew on. \u0026quot;We are here for... administrative purposes.\u0026quot;","They sat down. Harry looked apologetic. Draco looked like he was about to close a business deal.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Proposition\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco reached into the inner pocket of his tailored suit. He pulled out three slim, matte-black cards. They were edged in platinum and featured a moving, holographic crest of the Gringotts Bank, overlaid with the Malfoy \u0027M\u0027.","He placed one in front of McGonagall.","He placed one in front of Snape.","He slid the third across the desk to Dumbledore.","\u0026quot;What,\u0026quot; Snape asked, staring at the object with suspicion, \u0026quot;is this?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;This,\u0026quot; Draco announced, leaning back and crossing his legs, \u0026quot;is the \u003cstrong\u003eMalfoy Infinite\u003c/strong\u003e card.\u0026quot;","McGonagall picked it up. It felt heavy, warm to the touch. \u0026quot;Infinite?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are aware,\u0026quot; Draco began, his voice professional, \u0026quot;that The Pack... or the Pantheon, as I hear the ghosts are calling them... represents a significant strain on Hogwarts\u0027 resources.\u0026quot;","Harry nodded. \u0026quot;James breaks things. Cassie freezes things. Thomas... reconfigures things.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Lily,\u0026quot; Draco added, \u0026quot;while delightful, tends to cause structural anomalies by simply being too positive. I believe she accidentally healed a crack in the Astronomy Tower just by leaning on it.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Therefore,\u0026quot; Draco pointed to the cards. \u0026quot;These are for incidentals.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Explanation\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Incidentals?\u0026quot; Dumbledore asked, eyes twinkling.","\u0026quot;These cards are linked directly to the primary Malfoy Vault,\u0026quot; Draco explained. \u0026quot;Not the allowance vault. The \u003cem\u003eMain\u003c/em\u003e Vault. There is no spending limit. There is no overdraft fee. The goblins have been instructed to approve every transaction instantly, without question.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at the card. \u0026quot;Every transaction?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If James blows up a classroom,\u0026quot; Draco listed, ticking off fingers. \u0026quot;Swipe the card. Build a new one. Better stone. Italian marble if you like.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If Cassie freezes the Black Lake and kills the Giant Squid,\u0026quot; Draco continued (McGonagall gasped), \u0026quot;swipe the card. Import a new Squid. Get two.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If Thomas decides the library is inefficient and dismantles it,\u0026quot; Harry added, \u0026quot;swipe the card. Buy new books. Expand the wing.\u0026quot;","Draco leaned forward, his grey eyes serious.","\u0026quot;This covers structural damage, magical contamination, emotional distress for the staff, and hazard pay for Filch. If you need to hire a team of Curse-Breakers to undo something Pan did to the timeline? Swipe it.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reactions\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eMinerva McGonagall\u003c/strong\u003e looked at the card. She thought about the Transfiguration budget she had been fighting for since 1995. She thought about the drafty windows in Gryffindor Tower. She thought about the new broomsticks the school desperately needed.","Her hand closed tightly around the card.","\u0026quot;Mr. Malfoy,\u0026quot; she said, her voice shaking slightly. \u0026quot;Are you telling me I could repave the Quidditch Pitch with self-cushioning turf?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You could repave it with gold, Minerva,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;I don\u0027t care. Just keep them educated and keep the school standing.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eSeverus Snape\u003c/strong\u003e picked up the card. He turned it over. His dark eyes glittered with a sudden, predatory light.","\u0026quot;Rare ingredients,\u0026quot; Snape whispered. \u0026quot;Boomslang skin... Bicorn horn... Nundu breath...\u0026quot;","He looked at Draco.","\u0026quot;Infinite?\u0026quot; Snape clarified.","\u0026quot;If it exists on the market,\u0026quot; Draco promised, \u0026quot;you can buy it.\u0026quot;","Snape slipped the card into his sleeve. He sat down. He looked significantly less stressed.","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Snape drawled. \u0026quot;I suppose... accommodations can be made. If Potter\u0027s son turns a student into a badger, I shall simply purchase a better badger.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore\u003c/strong\u003e didn\u0027t pick up the card. He simply looked at the two fathers.","\u0026quot;You are bribing us,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled.","\u0026quot;We are investing, Headmaster,\u0026quot; Draco corrected, standing up. \u0026quot;This isn\u0027t a bribe. It\u0027s a disaster relief fund.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We know who they are, Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said quietly, standing up beside Draco. \u0026quot;We know what they can do. We just want to make sure Hogwarts survives the experience.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore smiled. He tapped the black card with a long finger.","\u0026quot;Generosity is a form of magic, too, Draco. Hogwarts accepts your... insurance policy.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Departure\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco buttoned his jacket.","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Draco said. \u0026quot;Oh, and Severus? If Cassie gives you trouble... do not deduct points. Just tell her I said she is acting like a Weasley. That usually corrects the behavior.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Noted,\u0026quot; Snape smirked.","\u0026quot;And Professor,\u0026quot; Harry said to McGonagall. \u0026quot;If James turns into a dog and pees on the rug... just put him outside. He hates that.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I shall keep that in mind, Potter,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, tucking the black card safely into her robes.","Harry and Draco turned and walked to the door.","\u0026quot;Do you think that was enough?\u0026quot; Harry whispered as they reached the exit.","\u0026quot;Harry,\u0026quot; Draco whispered back. \u0026quot;That card could buy France. They\u0027ll be fine.\u0026quot;","They stepped onto the spiral staircase.","Behind them, in the office, the mood had shifted.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m ordering a new cauldron,\u0026quot; Snape announced immediately. \u0026quot;Solid gold. Self-stirring.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think the Gryffindor common room needs a chandelier,\u0026quot; McGonagall mused.","Dumbledore popped another lemon drop. \u0026quot;I wonder if they sell wooly socks in bulk?\u0026quot;","The Pack had arrived. But thanks to the Malfoy fortune, the faculty was ready to face the storm in style."]},{"num":35,"origNum":36,"title":"The Engineer and the Druid","wordCount":1080,"paragraphs":["The first week of classes at Hogwarts was usually a time of adjustment. First years got lost on staircases, burned their eyebrows off in Transfiguration, and tried to remember which corridor led to a painful death.","But for the Pantheon, the first week wasn\u0027t an adjustment. It was an audit.","\u003cstrong\u003ePart I: The Optimization of Charms\u003c/strong\u003e","On Tuesday morning, the Ravenclaws and Hufflepuffs filed into the Charms classroom. Professor Filius Flitwick stood on his stack of books, beaming at the new students.","\u0026quot;Welcome!\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked. \u0026quot;Charms is the art of altering the properties of an object. It requires finesse, lightness, and precise wand work.\u0026quot;","He picked up his wand.","\u0026quot;Today, we start with the basics. The Levitation Charm. \u003cem\u003eWingardium Leviosa\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","He demonstrated the famous \u0026quot;swish and flick.\u0026quot; A feather on his desk rose gently into the air.","\u0026quot;Now, you try!\u0026quot;","The class erupted into the usual chorus of mispronounced incantations and clumsy waving. Feathers sat stubbornly on desks or, in one case, caught fire.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Critique\u003c/strong\u003e","In the front row, \u003cstrong\u003eThomas Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e did not pick up his feather. He was staring at Flitwick’s diagram on the blackboard with a deep frown.","He raised his hand.","\u0026quot;Yes, Mr. Dursley?\u0026quot; Flitwick asked, excited to teach the Anchor.","\u0026quot;Professor,\u0026quot; Thomas said, his voice polite but firm. \u0026quot;Your vector analysis is flawed.\u0026quot;","The class went silent.","\u0026quot;I beg your pardon?\u0026quot; Flitwick blinked.","Thomas stood up. He walked to the blackboard. He picked up a piece of chalk.","\u0026quot;The \u0027swish\u0027 creates unnecessary drag,\u0026quot; Thomas explained, drawing a sharp, angular diagram over Flitwick’s loops. \u0026quot;And the \u0027flick\u0027 dissipates 15% of the kinetic energy at the apex of the motion. It’s inefficient.\u0026quot;","He turned to the class.","\u0026quot;If you want optimal lift with minimal magical expenditure, you shouldn\u0027t swish. You should \u003cem\u003ethrust\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003etorque\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Demonstration\u003c/strong\u003e","Thomas returned to his desk. He pulled out his Lignum Vitae wand. It hummed with that deep, server-room bass note.","He looked at his feather.","He didn\u0027t say the incantation loudly. He didn\u0027t swish.","He stabbed his wand forward and twisted his wrist sharply—a movement like turning a key in a lock.","\u003cem\u003eWingardium.\u003c/em\u003e","He dropped the \u0026quot;Leviosa.\u0026quot; He deemed it redundant.","\u003cstrong\u003eSNAP.\u003c/strong\u003e","The feather didn\u0027t float. It shot upward as if pulled by a magnetic rail gun. It stopped exactly three feet in the air, freezing in perfect, absolute stillness. It didn\u0027t bob. It didn\u0027t drift. It looked like it was glued to the air molecules.","Thomas tapped the desk. The feather moved one foot to the left in a straight line. Tap. One foot forward. Tap. One foot down.","It was moving on a grid.","\u0026quot;Positional control established,\u0026quot; Thomas noted. \u0026quot;Latency is zero.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Grade\u003c/strong\u003e","Flitwick stared at the feather. He tried to summon it to him, but the feather refused to budge from Thomas’s grid.","\u0026quot;You... you re-engineered the spell,\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked, clutching his chest. \u0026quot;You stripped it of its whimsy and replaced it with... mathematics.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Whimsy is unpredictable, sir,\u0026quot; Thomas said, sitting down. \u0026quot;Structure is reliable.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ten points to Ravenclaw,\u0026quot; Flitwick gasped, fanning himself. \u0026quot;For... sheer, terrifying efficiency.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePart II: The Whisperer of Greenhouse One\u003c/strong\u003e","Wednesday afternoon brought Herbology with the Hufflepuffs and Gryffindors. The air in Greenhouse One was damp and smelled of earth and fertilizer.","Professor Sprout, a dumpy witch with a patched hat, stood behind a trestle table covered in pots of \u003cstrong\u003eBouncing Bulbs\u003c/strong\u003e.","\u0026quot;Right then!\u0026quot; Sprout barked cheerfully. \u0026quot;Bouncing Bulbs! Lively little things. The trick is to be firm! Grab them by the stem and force them into the pot before they smack you in the face!\u0026quot;","She demonstrated, wrestling a purple, wriggling bulb into a pot while it tried to headbutt her.","\u0026quot;Now, pairs! Gloves on! Watch your noses!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Conflict\u003c/strong\u003e","Chaos ensued. Gryffindors were shouting as bulbs bounced off the glass walls. Neville Longbottom’s grandson was currently being strangled by a particularly aggressive root.","But in the corner, \u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e stood alone. She wasn\u0027t wearing her dragon-hide gloves. She had taken them off and placed them neatly on the bench.","\u0026quot;Miss Weasley!\u0026quot; Sprout called out, wrestling a bulb. \u0026quot;Gloves! They bite!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They don\u0027t bite, Professor,\u0026quot; Pan’s dreamy voice floated across the greenhouse. \u0026quot;They’re just teething.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe lullaby\u003c/strong\u003e","Pan didn\u0027t grab her bulb. She didn\u0027t wrestle.","She floated up—her feet hovering six inches off the dirty floor—so she was eye-level with the writhing purple plant.","Her Silver Lime wand was tucked behind her ear, invisible. She didn\u0027t need it.","She reached out with her bare hands.","The Bouncing Bulb paused. It turned its eyeless top toward her.","\u0026quot;Shhh,\u0026quot; Pan whispered. She reached into her pocket and pulled out a small, shiny beetle. \u0026quot;Are you hungry? The soil is too acidic for you, isn\u0027t it? It makes your tummy hurt.\u0026quot;","She fed the beetle to the bulb. The plant swallowed it with a happy \u003cem\u003eglorp\u003c/em\u003e sound.","Then, Pan began to hum. It was a low, vibrating sound, like a bee in a jar.","The Bouncing Bulb stopped bouncing. It shivered. Then, it turned a soft, contented shade of lavender.","It climbed out of its nursery pot. It didn\u0027t attack Pan. It crawled into her hand, curled up like a cat, and went to sleep.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","The greenhouse went quiet. Students were freezing mid-wrestle to watch.","Sprout dropped her trowel.","\u0026quot;It... it\u0027s purring,\u0026quot; Sprout whispered. \u0026quot;I\u0027ve been a Herbologist for forty years. I have never seen a Bouncing Bulb \u003cem\u003epurr\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Pan floated over to Sprout, cradling the sleeping vegetable.","\u0026quot;He wants fresh compost, Professor,\u0026quot; Pan said softly. \u0026quot;And he says the Mandrakes in Greenhouse Three are waking up. They had a nightmare about a loud noise.\u0026quot;","As if on cue, a distant wailing started from Greenhouse Three.","Sprout looked at the small girl with silver eyes who floated above the mud.","\u0026quot;You speak to them,\u0026quot; Sprout breathed. \u0026quot;You don\u0027t just grow them. You \u003cem\u003eknow\u003c/em\u003e them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We are all just roots in the dark,\u0026quot; Pan smiled.","\u0026quot;Twenty points to Hufflepuff,\u0026quot; Sprout announced, wiping mud from her cheek. \u0026quot;For... well, for being a Druid, I suppose.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","That evening in the Great Hall, Thomas was creating a structural diagram of his peas and carrots, while Pan was feeding her salad from her own fork because \u0026quot;the lettuce asked nicely.\u0026quot;","At the High Table, Flitwick and Sprout exchanged looks.","\u0026quot;The boy treats magic like a machine,\u0026quot; Flitwick murmured, pouring wine with a shaking hand.","\u0026quot;And the girl treats the garden like a family,\u0026quot; Sprout replied, watching Pan.","\u0026quot;It’s only Wednesday,\u0026quot; Flitwick sighed. \u0026quot;I need a nap.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":36,"origNum":37,"title":"The Alchemist and The Predator","wordCount":1358,"paragraphs":["If Thomas was the engineer and Pan was the druid, Cassiopeia Malfoy was the scalpel.","Her first week at Hogwarts was a masterclass in elegant superiority. She didn\u0027t raise her hand eagerly like Hermione had; she simply waited to be called on, radiating an aura that suggested she already knew the answer and was merely waiting for the rest of the class to catch up.","\u003cstrong\u003ePart I: The Prince of Potions\u0027 Successor\u003c/strong\u003e","Thursday morning found the Slytherins and Gryffindors in the dungeons. The air was frigid, making the breath of the students mist in the gloom. Glass jars containing floating things lined the walls.","The door banged open. Professor Severus Snape swept into the room, his black robes billowing like bat wings. He stopped at the front, turning to face the class with a sneer.","\u0026quot;There will be no foolish wand-waving or silly incantations in this class,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, his voice silencing the room instantly. \u0026quot;I can teach you how to bottle fame, brew glory, and even stopper death... if you aren\u0027t as big a bunch of dunderheads as I usually have to teach.\u0026quot;","He set them a task: A Cure for Boils.","While James Potter was busy trying to make his cauldron bubble in time to a song he was humming (resulting in a cloud of pink, singing smoke that smelled like burnt rubber), Cassie worked in absolute silence.","She didn\u0027t chop her horned slugs; she sliced them with surgical exactness, each piece identical to the millimeter. She didn\u0027t dump her porcupine quills; she added them one by one, counting the seconds between each drop to allow for optimal diffusion.","Her cauldron didn\u0027t bubble violently. It simmered with a low, rhythmic hiss. The steam rising from it wasn\u0027t grey; it was a perfect, shimmering silver-blue.","Snape prowled the dungeon. He vanished James’s potion with a flick of his wand and a curled lip (\u0026quot;Scourgify. Mr. Potter, try not to poison your classmates before lunch\u0026quot;).","Then, he stopped at Cassie’s table.","He peered into her cauldron. He watched the silver steam rise. He looked at her workspace, which was meticulously organized, not a single drop spilled.","Snape’s black eyes moved from the cauldron to Cassie. For a moment, he saw Draco. For a moment, he perhaps even saw himself.","\u0026quot;Flawless,\u0026quot; Snape murmured, the word soft but carrying to the back of the room. \u0026quot;The viscosity is perfect. The color is exact.\u0026quot;","He looked at the Gryffindors with disdain, then back to Cassie.","\u0026quot;It seems competence is hereditary in some families,\u0026quot; Snape drawled. \u0026quot;Ten points to Slytherin. For a textbook execution.\u0026quot;","Cassie merely inclined her head. \u0026quot;Thank you, Professor. Precision is the better part of valor.\u0026quot;","Snape’s lips twitched—the closest he ever came to a smile. He moved on, leaving Cassie to bottle her masterpiece while James tried to scrub pink sludge off his eyebrows.","\u003cstrong\u003ePart II: The Wolf and the Wand\u003c/strong\u003e","But it was on Friday afternoon, in the Defense Against the Dark Arts classroom, that the true nature of Cassiopeia Malfoy was revealed.","The classroom was warm, lit by candles. At the front stood Professor Remus Lupin. His robes were shabby and patched, but his face was kind, though lined with years of hardship.","\u0026quot;Good afternoon,\u0026quot; Lupin smiled, leaning against his desk. \u0026quot;Defense Against the Dark Arts is not just about fighting. It is about understanding the nature of the threat. It is about control.\u0026quot;","He looked around the room.","\u0026quot;Today, we will start with the most fundamental defensive charm. \u003cem\u003eExpelliarmus\u003c/em\u003e. The Disarming Charm.\u0026quot;","He pushed himself off the desk.","\u0026quot;I need a volunteer to assist me. Someone to cast the spell against me so I can demonstrate how to block it.\u0026quot;","His eyes scanned the room. James’s hand shot up.","\u0026quot;Me! Pick me, Uncle Moony—I mean, Professor!\u0026quot;","Lupin smiled. \u0026quot;Perhaps someone a little... less enthusiastic for the first go, Mr. Potter. We don\u0027t want to blow a hole in the wall just yet.\u0026quot;","His gaze landed on the quiet, composed girl in the front row of the Slytherins.","\u0026quot;Miss Malfoy,\u0026quot; Lupin nodded. \u0026quot;Would you do the honors?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reveal\u003c/strong\u003e","Cassie stood up. She smoothed her robes. She walked to the dueling platform with a gliding step that made no sound.","She reached into her sleeve and drew her wand.","The moment the obsidian wood was exposed, the atmosphere in the room changed. The candlelight flickered and dimmed. A low, predatory thrum filled the air—not the mechanical hum of Thomas’s wand, but the deep, guttural growl of a beast waking up.","Lupin froze.","He was a werewolf. His senses were sharper than a normal wizard\u0027s. He didn\u0027t just see the wand; he \u003cem\u003esmelled\u003c/em\u003e it.","He smelled death. He smelled ancient, apex-predator power. He smelled a creature that even wolves feared.","\u0026quot;Miss Malfoy,\u0026quot; Lupin said, his voice dropping to a whisper. He took a half-step back, his eyes fixed on the black, jagged wood. \u0026quot;That wand...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;African Blackwood, Professor,\u0026quot; Cassie said calmly, holding the wand loosely at her side.","\u0026quot;And the core?\u0026quot; Lupin asked, his knuckles turning white as he gripped his own wand.","\u0026quot;Heartstring of a Nundu.\u0026quot;","The class gasped. Even the first years knew the name. The Nundu. The beast of East Africa. The breath that killed villages. The giant leopard that took a hundred wizards to subdue.","Lupin looked at the small, ten-year-old girl holding a weapon of mass destruction.","\u0026quot;A Nundu,\u0026quot; Lupin breathed. \u0026quot;I have not felt an aura like that since... well, in a very long time.\u0026quot;","He composed himself, forcing the teacher mask back on. But his stance shifted. He widened his footing. He raised his wand not in a casual block position, but in a serious, combat-ready guard.","\u0026quot;Very well,\u0026quot; Lupin said, his voice tight. \u0026quot;Cast the Disarming Charm. Do not hold back, Miss Malfoy. That wand will not allow you to be gentle.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Duel\u003c/strong\u003e","Cassie raised her arm.","She didn\u0027t shout. She didn\u0027t lunge.","She flicked her wrist. A tiny, minimalist movement.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Expelliarmus.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","She whispered it.","\u003cstrong\u003eCRACK-BOOM.\u003c/strong\u003e","It wasn\u0027t a jet of red light. It was a lance of violet lightning wrapped in black smoke. It tore through the air with a sound like a cracking whip.","Lupin reacted on instinct. He didn\u0027t cast a simple \u003cem\u003eProtego\u003c/em\u003e. He cast a full-powered \u003cem\u003eProtego Maxima\u003c/em\u003e, throwing his whole weight behind the shield.","The spell hit Lupin’s shield.","\u003cstrong\u003eSHATTER.\u003c/strong\u003e","The silver shield didn\u0027t just deflect the spell; it exploded into shards of light. The force of Cassie’s spell hammered through the defense, lifting the fully grown wizard off his feet.","Lupin flew backward, slamming into his desk and overturning it. His wand flew out of his hand, spinning through the air until Cassie caught it with her free hand.","Dust rained down from the ceiling.","The class was dead silent. James’s mouth was open.","Lupin groaned, sitting up amidst a pile of parchment. He rubbed his shoulder. He looked at the girl standing calmly in the center of the room, holding two wands.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;Ten points to Slytherin,\u0026quot; Lupin wheezed, getting to his feet with a wince.","He walked over to her. He looked at the obsidian wand with genuine wariness.","\u0026quot;That was not a Disarming Charm, Miss Malfoy,\u0026quot; Lupin said softly, taking his wand back. \u0026quot;That was a cannon blast.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I aimed for the wand, Professor,\u0026quot; Cassie said apologetically, though she didn\u0027t look sorry. \u0026quot;It... pulls. It wants to win.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Lupin nodded, rubbing his arm. \u0026quot;Nundus do not disarm. They conquer.\u0026quot;","He looked at the class, who were staring at Cassie with terrified awe.","\u0026quot;Lesson one,\u0026quot; Lupin announced, dusting off his robes. \u0026quot;A wand is a tool. But some tools are weapons. And Miss Malfoy...\u0026quot;","He looked down at her.","\u0026quot;...you are a natural duelist. Your stance was perfect. Your casting was silent. And your power is...\u0026quot; He paused. \u0026quot;...terrifying.\u0026quot;","Cassie smirked, a tiny, fleeting expression of Malfoy pride. She slid the black wand back into her sleeve.","\u0026quot;Thank you, Professor,\u0026quot; she said.","\u0026quot;Next!\u0026quot; Lupin called out, sounding like he needed a stiff drink. \u0026quot;And perhaps... someone with a wand made of wood, not nightmares?\u0026quot;","James jumped up. \u0026quot;My turn! My wand barks!\u0026quot;","Lupin sighed. \u0026quot;Of course it does.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":37,"origNum":38,"title":"The Alchemist of Life","wordCount":1104,"paragraphs":["Friday morning. Double Potions with the Gryffindors and Slytherins.","If the dungeons were cold for the other students, they seemed to freeze over completely when Severus Snape slammed the door shut. He turned to face the class, his black eyes seeking out one student in particular.","Lily Luna Potter sat in the front row. She was tiny, her chin barely clearing the edge of the cauldron. She had Harry’s messy hair (though red) and her grandmother’s eyes.","Snape hated those eyes. They reminded him of everything he had lost.","\u0026quot;Today,\u0026quot; Snape said softly, his voice silky with menace, \u0026quot;we attempt the \u003cstrong\u003eWiggenweld Potion\u003c/strong\u003e. A healing draught. It requires delicate timing. One mistake, and you will not wake the sleeper; you will put them in a coma.\u0026quot;","He chalked the instructions on the board.","\u0026quot;Begin.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Prodigy\u003c/strong\u003e","While James (sitting at the back) was trying to chop a Flobberworm with a blunt knife and making a mess, Lily worked with a rhythmic, almost musical grace.","She didn\u0027t look at the board. She didn\u0027t look at her book.","She looked at the ingredients.","She picked up a sprig of Dittany. \u003cem\u003eIt feels thirsty,\u003c/em\u003e she thought. She didn\u0027t chop it dry; she added a single drop of water to the leaf before slicing it, releasing a cloud of fresh, silver steam.","She picked up the Moly petals. The book said to crush them. Lily held them in her hand, warming them with her skin temperature first, then gently bruised them.","Her cauldron didn\u0027t smell like sulfur or swamp gas. It smelled like rain on hot pavement. It smelled like life.","Snape prowled the room. He vanished James’s sludge without a word. He sneered at a Slytherin’s lumpy mixture.","Then, he reached Lily’s desk.","He stopped. He looked into the cauldron.","The potion was a vibrant, glowing turquoise. It was perfect. No, it was \u003cem\u003emore\u003c/em\u003e than perfect. It possessed a luminosity that the textbook didn\u0027t even describe.","Snape’s hand twitched. He looked down at the small girl.","\u0026quot;You deviated from the instructions,\u0026quot; Snape whispered. \u0026quot;The book says to stir clockwise seven times. You stirred counter-clockwise once, then clockwise six times.\u0026quot;","Lily looked up, her green eyes wide and innocent.","\u0026quot;The Salamander blood was dizzy, Professor,\u0026quot; she explained softly. \u0026quot;It needed to be steadied before it could mix with the lionfish spines. Otherwise, they fight.\u0026quot;","Snape stared at her. \u0026quot;They... fight?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes,\u0026quot; Lily nodded. \u0026quot;Ingredients have feelings. You have to ask them nicely to work together.\u0026quot;","Snape felt a ghost walk over his grave. He remembered a red-haired girl in 1971 who used to talk to her ingredients. But this... this was different. This wasn\u0027t just talent; this was a fundamental connection to the essence of matter.","\u0026quot;It is...\u0026quot; Snape swallowed hard. \u0026quot;It is the most potent draught I have seen brewed in this classroom in twenty years.\u0026quot;","The class went silent. Snape \u003cem\u003enever\u003c/em\u003e complimented Gryffindors.","\u0026quot;Ten points,\u0026quot; Snape rasped, turning away quickly, \u0026quot;to Gryffindor.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Accident\u003c/strong\u003e","\u0026quot;AAAAH!\u0026quot;","The silence was shattered by a scream.","Nigel, a nervous Gryffindor boy two tables away, had panicked. Instead of adding a drop of Salamander blood, he had knocked the entire jar into his boiling cauldron.","\u003cstrong\u003eBOOM.\u003c/strong\u003e","The cauldron didn\u0027t just melt; it exploded. A wave of scalding, acidic green sludge erupted outward, splashing over Nigel’s face and chest.","\u0026quot;Idiot boy!\u0026quot; Snape roared, whipping out his wand to banish the potion.","But the damage was done. Nigel fell to the floor, screaming. His skin was sizzling, turning angry red and blistering before their eyes. The acid was eating through his robes.","\u0026quot;Stand back!\u0026quot; Snape shouted, rushing forward, his mind racing through counter-spells. \u003cem\u003eEpiskey\u003c/em\u003e wouldn\u0027t work on dark potion burns; he needed a neutralizing agent—","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Healer\u003c/strong\u003e","He didn\u0027t get there in time.","Lily Luna Potter was already there.","She didn\u0027t run; she seemed to simply appear beside Nigel. She knelt down, ignoring the acidic sludge on the floor that hissed against her shoes.","She pulled out the \u003cstrong\u003eWhite Hazel Wand\u003c/strong\u003e.","The moment the wand appeared, the dungeon stopped feeling cold. A soft, humming silence filled the room, pressing against the stone walls.","\u0026quot;It hurts!\u0026quot; Nigel sobbed, clutching his face.","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Lily whispered. She didn\u0027t look scared. She looked profoundly sad that he was in pain.","She touched the tip of the white wand to Nigel’s forehead.","She didn\u0027t shout a spell. She didn\u0027t need Latin. The wand was older than Latin.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Be whole,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e Lily whispered.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Miracle\u003c/strong\u003e","A pulse of pure, blinding white light flooded the dungeon. It was so bright that Snape had to shield his eyes.","It wasn\u0027t a spell of repair. It was a spell of \u003cem\u003ecreation\u003c/em\u003e.","Where the light touched Nigel’s skin, the burns didn\u0027t just fade; time seemed to reverse. The blisters vanished. The red, raw flesh knit itself back together into perfect, unblemished skin. The tears on his cheeks dried. Even his robes, which had been eaten by acid, wove themselves back together, the fabric looking newer than before.","The light faded.","Nigel lay on the floor, blinking. He touched his face. It was smooth. He took a deep breath.","\u0026quot;I...\u0026quot; Nigel sat up. \u0026quot;I feel... really good. I feel like I just had a nap.\u0026quot;","He looked at Lily. \u0026quot;My headache is gone. And my knee... I scraped my knee yesterday. It\u0027s gone too.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Aftermath\u003c/strong\u003e","Lily smiled, tucking the glowing white wand back into her pocket. She patted Nigel’s hand. \u0026quot;Be careful with the Salamander blood next time, Nigel. It gets angry if you rush it.\u0026quot;","She stood up.","Severus Snape was standing over her. His face was pale, his black eyes wide with shock. He looked from the perfectly healed boy to the small girl who held the power of the First Phoenix.","He had spent his life trying to stopper death. This girl... she simply dismissed it.","\u0026quot;That wand,\u0026quot; Snape whispered, his voice trembling slightly. \u0026quot;And that casting... that was not standard healing magic, Miss Potter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No, sir,\u0026quot; Lily said politely. \u0026quot;It was just... helping.\u0026quot;","Snape looked at her for a long, agonizing moment. He saw the power that Dumbledore had warned him about. The power of the Pack. The power of Life.","He straightened up, sweeping his robes around him to hide his shaking hands.","\u0026quot;Class dismissed,\u0026quot; Snape croaked. \u0026quot;Get out. All of you.\u0026quot;","As the students scrambled to leave, Nigel paused at the door.","\u0026quot;Thanks, Lily!\u0026quot;","Snape watched Lily walk away, holding hands with James. He slumped against his desk, staring at the empty cauldron where the miracle had happened.","\u0026quot;Lily,\u0026quot; Snape whispered to the empty room, closing his eyes. \u0026quot;She has your hands. And she has... everything else.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":38,"origNum":39,"title":"The Shapeshifter and the Sky","wordCount":1026,"paragraphs":["The final piece of the Pantheon puzzle was James Sirius Potter. And while his siblings and cousins conquered the classroom with intellect, empathy, or terrifying power, James conquered it with sheer, unadulterated kinetic energy.","\u003cstrong\u003ePart I: The Fluidity of Form\u003c/strong\u003e","Transfiguration with Professor McGonagall was considered the hardest subject. It required strict discipline, exact wand movements, and intense concentration.","\u0026quot;Transfiguration is some of the most complex and dangerous magic you will learn at Hogwarts,\u0026quot; McGonagall lectured, looking sternly over her square spectacles. \u0026quot;Anyone messing around in my class will leave and not come back. You have been warned.\u0026quot;","She tapped the blackboard, and diagrams of a match turning into a needle appeared.","\u0026quot;Begin.\u0026quot;","The class struggled. Matches stayed matches. Some became pointy matches. One student managed to make a match that looked like a silver toothpick.","James sat in the middle row. He looked at his match.","He pulled out his \u003cstrong\u003eDogwood and Chimera Scale wand\u003c/strong\u003e.","The wand rippled in his hand. It felt the intent of Transfiguration—the desire to change form—and it vibrated with excitement. It shifted texture, turning sleek and metallic to match the intended outcome.","James didn\u0027t just want a needle. That was boring.","He tapped the match. \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Mutatio.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Result\u003c/strong\u003e","The match didn\u0027t just turn silver. It liquefied.","It flowed into the air, a globule of quicksilver spinning rapidly. Then, it snapped into shape.","It became a needle. But then it shifted. It became a tiny silver snake. Then a miniature sword. Then a flower made of steel. Then back to a needle.","It was a cycle of continuous transfiguration, holding each form for a second before flowing into the next.","McGonagall stopped at his desk. She watched the metal object cycle through shapes.","\u0026quot;I asked for a needle, Mr. Potter,\u0026quot; she said, though her eyebrows were raised high.","\u0026quot;It is a needle, Professor,\u0026quot; James grinned, catching the object just as it turned back into a sharp point. \u0026quot;It’s just... an indecisive needle. Like my wand. It likes options.\u0026quot;","McGonagall looked at the boy. He didn\u0027t just change the object\u0027s appearance; he had destabilized its state of matter to allow for fluid shifting. It was advanced, chaotic, and brilliant.","\u0026quot;Transfiguration is indeed about change,\u0026quot; McGonagall murmured. \u0026quot;You seem to have mastered \u003cem\u003econtinuous\u003c/em\u003e change. Five points to Gryffindor. But do try to make it stop spinning before you sew a button with it.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePart II: The King of the Air\u003c/strong\u003e","Friday afternoon. The Flying Lesson.","The Gryffindors and Slytherins stood on the flat grounds outside the castle, facing twenty ancient, twiggy broomsticks lying on the grass. Madam Hooch, with her short grey hair and yellow hawk eyes, stalked between the lines.","\u0026quot;Stick out your right hand over your broom,\u0026quot; she barked, \u0026quot;and say \u0027Up!\u0027\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;UP!\u0026quot; everyone shouted.","James’s broom didn\u0027t just jump into his hand. It snapped into his palm with a \u003cem\u003ethwack\u003c/em\u003e so loud it echoed.","\u0026quot;Now,\u0026quot; Hooch commanded. \u0026quot;When I blow my whistle, you kick off hard from the ground. Keep your brooms steady, rise a few feet, and then come straight back down. Three... two...\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Launch\u003c/strong\u003e","She blew the whistle.","Most students wobbled three feet into the air. Neville’s grandson hovered nervously at shoulder height.","James Potter kicked off.","He didn\u0027t rise a few feet. He shot upward like a cork from a bottle.","\u0026quot;Mr. Potter!\u0026quot; Hooch screamed. \u0026quot;Come down this instant!\u0026quot;","James didn\u0027t hear her. The wind was rushing in his ears. His robes snapped behind him. He was fifty feet up in seconds.","He felt the old school broom vibrating beneath him. It was a terrible broom—a Cleansweep Seven that drifted to the left—but James didn\u0027t care. He was in the air. He was home.","\u0026quot;Wooooohooooo!\u0026quot; James yelled.","He pulled the broom handle up. He did a loop-the-loop. He rolled sideways. He flew hands-free, steering with his knees, laughing as the wind whipped his messy hair.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Dive\u003c/strong\u003e","High up in the Gryffindor Tower, in the Deputy Headmistress’s office, Minerva McGonagall was grading papers. She heard the whooping. She walked to the window.","Her eyes widened.","She saw a small black blur streak past the Astronomy Tower.","James had spotted something. A large hawk was circling the pitch, carrying a shiny beetle in its talons.","\u0026quot;Race you!\u0026quot; James shouted.","He tipped the broom forward. He went into a vertical dive.","McGonagall grabbed the window sill. \u0026quot;He\u0027s going to crash.\u0026quot;","James plummeted toward the earth. The wind screamed. The grass rushed up to meet him. Fifty feet. Thirty feet. Ten feet.","At the very last second—when impact seemed inevitable—James yanked the handle up.","He pulled out of the dive so hard the bristles of the broom scraped the grass. He shot back up, snatched the beetle from the surprised hawk (which squawked and dropped it), and did a victory lap around the goal posts.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Recruitment\u003c/strong\u003e","James landed smoothly, hopping off the broom.","\u0026quot;That was wicked!\u0026quot; he beamed at the terrified class.","\u0026quot;MR. POTTER!\u0026quot;","Professor McGonagall was sprinting across the grounds. Her robes were flying. She ran faster than anyone had ever seen her run.","James froze. He dropped the beetle. \u0026quot;I... I didn\u0027t mean to, Professor! The broom just... it went up!\u0026quot;","McGonagall stopped in front of him. She was breathless. Her glasses were askew. She clutched her chest.","She stared at him.","\u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; she gasped.","\u0026quot;I\u0027m sorry!\u0026quot; James pleaded. \u0026quot;I\u0027ll polish the trophies! I\u0027ll clean the owls!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Silence!\u0026quot; McGonagall snapped.","She pointed a shaking finger at him. Then she pointed at the castle.","\u0026quot;You will come with me.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Am I expelled?\u0026quot; James asked, his voice small.","\u0026quot;Expelled?\u0026quot; McGonagall looked at him as if he were mad. A manic gleam entered her eyes—the look of a woman who had lost the Quidditch Cup to Slytherin for too many years in a row.","\u0026quot;Expelled? Heavens no.\u0026quot;","She grabbed his shoulder and steered him toward the castle.","\u0026quot;I’m taking you to the Gryffindor Captain. I don\u0027t care about the First Year rule. I have the Malfoy Insurance Card. I will buy the rulebook and burn it if I have to.\u0026quot;","She looked down at James, beaming with fierce pride.","\u0026quot;You, Mr. Potter, are going to be the new Seeker.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":39,"origNum":40,"title":"The Year of the Pantheon","wordCount":1177,"paragraphs":["The First Year of the Pack did not follow the standard Hogwarts curriculum. It was less about learning magic and more about the school surviving the learning curve of five demigods.","As the seasons changed, a series of incidents cemented their legend. They weren\u0027t just students; they were a force of nature that the faculty—and the castle itself—had to learn to accommodate.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Halloween Optimization\u003c/strong\u003e","It started, traditionally, on Halloween. A Mountain Troll had been let into the dungeons (courtesy of a disgruntled former caretaker).","Teachers rushed toward the dungeons, Snape’s black robes flying, McGonagall’s face pale. They burst into the girl\u0027s bathroom, wands drawn, expecting carnage.","They found silence.","The Troll was there. It was standing in the middle of the room, encased in a block of solid, translucent ice from the waist down. It was shivering violently.","\u003cstrong\u003eCassiopeia Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e was leaning against a sink, examining her fingernails.","\u003cstrong\u003eThomas Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e was standing next to the Troll’s massive wooden club, which lay on the floor in three perfectly equal pieces.","\u0026quot;The structural integrity of the oak was compromised by a knot in the handle,\u0026quot; Thomas explained to the stunned teachers. \u0026quot;I applied percussive maintenance. It snapped.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And he was loud,\u0026quot; Cassie added, bored. \u0026quot;So I put him on ice. Literally.\u0026quot;","McGonagall lowered her wand. \u0026quot;Five points... for efficiency?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Poltergeist Whisperer\u003c/strong\u003e","In November, Peeves the Poltergeist decided to ambush the Hufflepuffs with a bag of water balloons. He swooped down, cackling.","\u0026quot;Ickle Firsties! Wet and weep!\u0026quot;","He threw a balloon at \u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e.","The balloon didn\u0027t hit her. It stopped in mid-air, inches from her face. Pan didn\u0027t blink. She drifted upward until she was eye-level with the chaotic spirit.","\u0026quot;You are very sad, Mr. Peeves,\u0026quot; Pan hummed, her silver eyes looking right through his translucent chest. \u0026quot;You make noise because the silence hurts your ears. You miss the Bloody Baron\u0027s jokes from 1892.\u0026quot;","Peeves froze. The water balloon dropped on his own head.","\u0026quot;I... I...\u0026quot; Peeves stammered.","\u0026quot;Shh,\u0026quot; Pan whispered, patting his cheek. \u0026quot;Go play in the Astronomy Tower. The wind sings there.\u0026quot;","Peeves floated away quietly, wiping a spectral tear. From that day on, whenever Pan walked down a corridor, Peeves would zoom ahead and polish the floor for her.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Quidditch Comet\u003c/strong\u003e","The first Quidditch match—Gryffindor vs. Slytherin—was the shortest in recorded history.","The whistle blew. The Quaffle was released.","\u003cstrong\u003eJames Sirius Potter\u003c/strong\u003e didn\u0027t wait. He didn\u0027t circle the pitch. He didn\u0027t look for the glimmer of gold.","His Dogwood wand was tucked in his boot, vibrating. His eyes—sharpened by his inner falcon—locked onto a pixel of gold near the Slytherin hoops.","He dove.","It wasn\u0027t a dive; it was a teleportation of speed. He was a black blur against the grey sky. The Slytherin Seeker was still pulling up on his broom handle when James streaked past him, the wind of his passing spinning the older boy around.","\u003cem\u003eTHWACK.\u003c/em\u003e","James pulled up, hovering in front of the stunned Slytherin Keeper. He held up the Snitch.","\u0026quot;Game over!\u0026quot; James shouted.","Total match time: 42 seconds.","Minerva McGonagall was seen in the stands, crying tears of joy into a tartan handkerchief while sliding the Malfoy Infinite Card to the Head of House elf. \u0026quot;Steak!\u0026quot; she sobbed. \u0026quot;Steak for everyone!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Infirmary Saint\u003c/strong\u003e","By January, Madame Pomfrey had a new problem. Her infirmary was empty.","Usually, winter brought colds, flu, and slip-and-fall injuries. But \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter\u003c/strong\u003e had started spending her free periods \u0026quot;visiting\u0026quot; the hospital wing.","She didn\u0027t cast spells. She just sat by the beds and told stories.","A Third Year with a nasty Dragon Pox outbreak found his spots vanishing within ten minutes of Lily sitting next to him.","A Beater with a broken arm felt the bone knit itself together when Lily handed him a glass of water.","\u0026quot;It’s bad for business, dear,\u0026quot; Madame Pomfrey sighed, watching a fully healed student skip out of the ward. \u0026quot;But... thank you.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Being sick is boring,\u0026quot; Lily smiled, radiating a warmth that made the drafty stone ward feel like a sunroom.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Exam Deconstruction\u003c/strong\u003e","Then came the End of Year Exams.","The Great Hall was silent, filled with scratching quills.","Thomas sat in the Ravenclaw section. He finished his Transfiguration theory paper in twenty minutes. He then flipped the parchment over and began writing a critique of the questions.","\u003cem\u003eQuestion 4 assumes a linear magical progression. This is inefficient. If one applies the Law of Gamp directly, the intermediate step is redundant.\u003c/em\u003e","When McGonagall graded it, she stared at the paper for an hour. Then she wrote \u003cem\u003e120%\u003c/em\u003e at the top and took an Aspirin.","In the Potions exam, Snape watched Cassie. She didn\u0027t use the provided scales. She measured ingredients by weight in her hand. Her Forgetfulness Potion was so potent that when Snape tested a drop, he forgot his own middle name for three hours.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Departure\u003c/strong\u003e","The year ended not with a whimper, but with the House Cup being awarded to everyone. Dumbledore, realizing that Gryffindor (James/Lily), Slytherin (Cassie), Ravenclaw (Thomas), and Hufflepuff (Pan) had all broken every point record in history, simply declared it a \u0026quot;Four-Way Tie.\u0026quot;","The Pack boarded the Hogwarts Express on a sunny June morning.","They claimed the same compartment. They were taller now. James had a few scars from adventures in the Forbidden Forest (which the Centaurs now avoided). Cassie’s aura was more controlled. Thomas had upgraded his trunk with hydraulic hinges.","The train chugged south, winding through the green hills of Scotland.","\u0026quot;Good year,\u0026quot; James said, kicking his feet up on the seat. \u0026quot;I only got detention twelve times.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thirteen,\u0026quot; Thomas corrected, checking a notebook. \u0026quot;You forgot the incident with the giant squid and the toaster.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That was a scientific experiment,\u0026quot; James defended.","\u0026quot;I liked the ghosts,\u0026quot; Pan hummed, looking out the window at the passing sheep. \u0026quot;They are happier now.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We didn\u0027t burn the school down,\u0026quot; Cassie noted, closing her book. \u0026quot;Father will be pleased. The Insurance Card balance is manageable.\u0026quot;","Lily looked at them all. She beamed. \u0026quot;I can\u0027t wait to tell Dad about the unicorn!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eKing\u0027s Cross\u003c/strong\u003e","The train slowed. The barrier of Platform 9 ¾ approached.","Steam billowed as the engines stopped. The doors opened.","The Pack stepped out.","Waiting for them was The Alliance. Harry, Hermione, Ron, Ginny, Draco, Dudley, and Chloe stood in a group, looking anxious.","They saw their children.","James ran to Harry, tackling him.","Lily jumped into Hermione’s arms.","Cassie walked up to Draco and allowed him to kiss her forehead (a rare display).","Pan floated into Ron’s hug.","Thomas shook Dudley’s hand firmly, then hugged Chloe.","\u0026quot;So?\u0026quot; Harry asked, looking at James. \u0026quot;How was it? Did you survive?\u0026quot;","James looked at his father. He grinned, and for a second, his eyes flashed with the wild, golden light of the Chimera.","\u0026quot;We didn\u0027t just survive, Dad,\u0026quot; James said. \u0026quot;We owned it.\u0026quot;","Harry laughed, looking at Dumbledore, who had stepped onto the platform to wave them off.","The First Year was over. The Pantheon had risen. And they had six more years to go.","\u003cstrong\u003eEnd of Year One.\u003c/strong\u003e"]},{"num":40,"origNum":41,"title":"Year Two - The War of Entropy","wordCount":413,"paragraphs":["Second Year was defined not by monsters, but by a philosophical disagreement between Gryffindor and Ravenclaw that escalated into a school-wide phenomenon.","They were twelve now—still children, still scabby-kneed and prone to running in the corridors, but their powers were becoming more defined.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Chaos\u003c/strong\u003e","On a rainy Tuesday in November, James Sirius Potter decided that walking between classes was \u0026quot;inefficient.\u0026quot; He tapped the main staircase with his Dogwood wand.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Lubricus Totalus.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","The marble stairs flattened. The friction coefficient vanished. The Grand Staircase became a giant, spiraling twisting slide. Gryffindors cheered, hurling themselves down the banisters, sliding from the seventh floor to the dungeons in seconds.","Filch slid past, screaming, clutching Mrs. Norris.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Order\u003c/strong\u003e","Thomas Dursley (carrying a set of brass calipers) was late for Arithmancy because of the slide. He did not find it amusing.","He stopped at the bottom of the slide. He pulled out his Lignum Vitae wand.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Stasis Grid.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","He didn\u0027t fix the stairs. Instead, he enchanted the air \u003cem\u003eabove\u003c/em\u003e the slide. As the Gryffindors came zooming down, laughing maniacally, they hit an invisible field of friction at the bottom.","They didn\u0027t crash. They simply... stopped. Instantly. Their momentum was zeroed out mathematically. They piled up gently like laundry in a basket.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Stalemate\u003c/strong\u003e","For the rest of the year, Hogwarts became a battleground of Physics.","James would turn a corridor into a zero-gravity zone to make carrying books easier.","Thomas would install \u0026quot;Magical Handrails\u0026quot; that forced students to walk in single file to optimize flow.","James would animate the suits of armor to dance the conga during passing periods.","Thomas would reprogram the armor to stand guard and check that everyone’s shoes were tied.","It culminated in Snape finding his potion store reorganized alphabetically by Thomas, while simultaneously, all the labels had been transfigured by James to read \u0026quot;Mysterious Goo.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore simply refused to intervene. \u0026quot;It is fascinating,\u0026quot; he told a stressed McGonagall. \u0026quot;It is a live demonstration of Thermodynamics versus Chaos Theory. I\u0027m taking notes.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eGrowing Pains\u003c/strong\u003e","By the end of the year, The Pack hadn\u0027t changed much physically. James was still a ball of wiry energy, buzzing like a hummingbird. Cassie was still petite, though her glare had sharpened. Thomas was a sturdy block of a boy, but he hadn\u0027t shot up in height yet.","And Lily... Lily remained tiny. She was still the size of an average nine-year-old, a pocket-sized powerhouse who still had to stand on a box to stir her cauldron properly."]},{"num":41,"origNum":42,"title":"Year Three - Prophecies and Boggarts","wordCount":538,"paragraphs":["Third Year brought Hogsmeade weekends, new electives, and the realization that they were now thirteen—though they certainly didn\u0027t look like teenagers yet. They were still very much a gang of kids.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Electives\u003c/strong\u003e","Thomas took Arithmancy and Ancient Runes. He horrified Professor Vector by pointing out that the number seven wasn\u0027t magical because of destiny, but because it was a prime number with structural stability.","Pan took Divination. It was a disaster for Professor Trelawney.","\u0026quot;My dear,\u0026quot; Trelawney gasped in the first class, misty-eyed. \u0026quot;I see... I see the Grim in your tea leaves!\u0026quot;","Pan looked into her cup. \u0026quot;No, Professor. That’s a dog. It’s my cousin James. He’s going to turn into a dog next Tuesday and chew on your shawl.\u0026quot;","(James did, in fact, accidentally partial-shift on Tuesday—sprouting ears and a tail—and chewed on a shawl).","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Boggart\u003c/strong\u003e","The defining moment of the year happened in Professor Lupin’s class. The Boggart—a shape-shifter that turns into your worst fear.","The line of third years moved forward.","Thomas stepped up. The Boggart turned into a Jenga tower. But it wasn\u0027t falling. It was slightly crooked. A single block was out of place, defying gravity.","Thomas twitched. \u0026quot;Asymmetry,\u0026quot; he whispered, horrified.","\u0026quot;Riddikulus!\u0026quot;","He forced the tower into a perfect, structurally sound cube. Thomas sighed with relief.","Cassie stepped up. The Boggart swirled and became... herself. But this version of Cassie was messy. Her robes were stained, her hair was unbrushed, and she had dirt on her nose.","Cassie’s eyes narrowed. She didn\u0027t shout. She sneered.","\u0026quot;Riddikulus.\u0026quot;","The messy Cassie was instantly scrubbed clean, her hair braiding itself perfectly. The real Cassie nodded approvingly and walked away.","James stepped up. The Boggart turned into a cage. A small, steel cage with no door.","James hated confinement. He hated stillness.","\u0026quot;Riddikulus!\u0026quot;","The cage turned into a hamster wheel. James laughed.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Light\u003c/strong\u003e","Then, \u003cstrong\u003eLily\u003c/strong\u003e stepped up. She was thirteen, but she looked ten.","The Boggart paused. It swirled. It tried to find a fear.","It turned into a Dementor. It towered over Lily, sucking the light from the room.","Lily didn\u0027t pull out her wand immediately. She looked at the creature of despair. She didn\u0027t look scared. She looked... pitying.","The Boggart hesitated. It fed on fear, but Lily wasn\u0027t offering any. She was radiating that constant, low-level hum of happiness.","The Dementor form wavered. It tried to become a dead flower. Lily smiled at it. It turned into a crying clown.","Lily raised her White Hazel wand.","\u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Riddikulus,\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e she whispered gently.","The clown didn\u0027t do something funny. It just stopped crying. It sat down, pulled out a bouquet of flowers, and handed them to her.","The Boggart, confused by the lack of fear, exploded into smoke.","Lupin ended the class early. \u0026quot;I think,\u0026quot; he told Harry later, \u0026quot;that Lily might be the only wizard in history who killed a Boggart with kindness.\u0026quot;","The end of the third year at Hogwarts had been a whirlwind of high-stakes exams, Boggart encounters that left Professor Lupin questioning the nature of the soul, and the general chaos that followed \u0026quot;The Pack\u0026quot; wherever they went.","But as the Hogwarts Express pulled into King’s Cross, the atmosphere wasn\u0027t one of exhaustion. It was one of anticipation."]},{"num":42,"origNum":12,"title":"The Island of Independence","wordCount":891,"paragraphs":["Isla de la Fortuna sat like a glittering emerald in the middle of a sapphire sea, shielded by a complex web of Muggle-repelling charms and high-end security wards that Vernon Dursley had personally \u0026quot;audited\u0026quot; for efficiency.","Usually, the arrival at the island was a logistical symphony led by \u0026quot;The Management.\u0026quot; Lucius Malfoy would typically be seen arguing with the portkey coordinators, while Vernon Dursley stood nearby with a clipboard, insisting that the \u0026quot;structural integrity\u0026quot; of the villa’s arrival gate was sub-par.","This time, however, the dock was strangely quiet.","\u0026quot;It feels... suspiciously calm,\u0026quot; Ron remarked, stepping off the private yacht Draco had commissioned (the \u0027Black Card\u0027 had been swiped so hard the teak wood groaned). Ron was carrying three suitcases and a bag of magical snacks that Pandora had already half-eaten.","\u0026quot;That’s because the ‘Management’ is currently embroiled in the \u0027Great Merger of 2005\u0027,\u0026quot; Hermione explained, checking her enchanted planner. \u0026quot;Aunt Petunia and Narcissa are overseeing the redesign of the Malfoy Manor gardens, and Vernon and Lucius are apparently trying to buy a small Muggle airline. Something about \u0027vertical integration\u0027.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank Merlin,\u0026quot; Draco sighed, adjusting his designer sunglasses. \u0026quot;If I had to hear my father and your Uncle Vernon debate the tax benefits of offshore Gringotts accounts one more time, I was going to jump into the Mediterranean without a Gillyweed.\u0026quot;","The Parents—Harry, Hermione, Draco, Ginny, Ron, and Luna—led the way up the white stone path toward the main mansion. Behind them followed The Pack, a formidable line of thirteen and fourteen-year-olds who seemed to have grown three inches since Easter.","Thomas Vernon Dursley walked at the front, his eyes scanning the villa’s electrical grid with the focus of a Technomancer. Beside him, James Sirius vibrated with so much excess energy that the nearby tropical flowers seemed to lean away from him. Cassie Malfoy walked with a regal stride that made the island look like it was her personal kingdom, while Pandora hummed a tune that caused the local seagulls to fly in synchronized circles. Bringing up the rear was Lily Luna, her very presence turning the humid air into a refreshing, joyful breeze.","The first night was a classic \u0026quot;Alliance\u0026quot; affair. They feasted on the terrace, the table groaning under the weight of food that would have satisfied a small giant. Harry and Hermione were already \u0026quot;knitted together\u0026quot; in their usual Gryffindor Pretzel style on the outdoor sofa, while Draco and Ginny—The Hurricane—were engaged in a high-stakes debate about Quidditch tactics that involved a lot of passionate gesturing and \u0026quot;The Ostrich\u0026quot; maneuvers whenever one of them made a particularly embarrassing point.","But throughout the dinner, a strange silence hung over the younger end of the table. The Pack wasn\u0027t fighting. They weren\u0027t playing pranks. They were \u003cem\u003ewhispering\u003c/em\u003e.","The next morning, the sun rose over the private beach, casting a golden glow over the infinity pool. The Parents were gathered in the breakfast nook, enjoying the rare luxury of a morning without Vernon’s \u0026quot;Strategy Briefings.\u0026quot;","The peace lasted exactly until the Five stood in the doorway.","They stood in a line, looking remarkably unified. Thomas, as the \u0026quot;Anchor,\u0026quot; stepped forward, but it was Cassie who spoke, her voice carrying the unmistakable authority of her mother and the cold confidence of her grandfather.","\u0026quot;We’ve had a meeting,\u0026quot; Cassie announced, crossing her arms.","\u0026quot;A meeting?\u0026quot; Harry asked, looking up from his coffee. \u0026quot;About what? The jet-ski schedule?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;About the living arrangements,\u0026quot; Thomas added, his voice deepening with the onset of his teenage years. \u0026quot;We love you all. Truly. But this villa is... crowded.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Crowded?\u0026quot; Ron choked on his bacon. \u0026quot;There are twelve bedrooms, three kitchens, and a cinema!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s not the space, Dad,\u0026quot; Pandora said, her eyes fixed on a point somewhere above Ron’s head. \u0026quot;It’s the \u003cem\u003eenergy\u003c/em\u003e. It’s very... parental. And loud. Mostly the PDA.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The point is,\u0026quot; James Sirius interjected, his snakewood wand sparking slightly in his pocket, \u0026quot;we’re not kids anymore. We’re third years. We’ve faced Boggarts, we’ve mastered Technomancy, and Lily... well, Lily is a literal beacon of light.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We want the East Mansion,\u0026quot; Cassie stated flatly.","The East Mansion was a separate, smaller but equally luxurious villa situated on the other side of the lagoon, connected only by a long rope bridge and a narrow sandbar.","\u0026quot;You want to live... alone?\u0026quot; Hermione asked, her logical brain already calculating the safety risks. \u0026quot;Without supervision?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We want privacy,\u0026quot; Cassie said, and for a fleeting second, her eyes flickered toward the others. \u0026quot;Our hormones are, as the Muggles say, \u0027acting up\u0027. James won\u0027t stop vibrating, Thomas is trying to wire the entire island for high-speed internet, and Pandora needs space to... vibrate out. We need our own sanctuary away from the \u0027Hurricane\u0027 and the \u0027Pretzel\u0027.\u0026quot;","The Parents looked at each other. The request was bold, unprecedented, and clearly something they had rehearsed.","\u0026quot;A separate mansion,\u0026quot; Draco mused, a smirk playing on his lips as he looked at his daughter. \u0026quot;Far enough away that we can’t hear you, but close enough that I can still cut off your Black Card access if you burn it down?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Cassie said.","The Pack stood their ground, five teenagers on the brink of becoming the most powerful magical unit the world had seen, and for the first time, The Parents realized that the \u0026quot;little kids\u0026quot; who used to hide in their sweaters were officially gone."]},{"num":43,"origNum":13,"title":"The Sovereign Republic of the East Mansion","wordCount":1052,"paragraphs":["The rope bridge connecting the main villa to the East Mansion wasn\u0027t just a physical walkway; to The Pack, it was a border crossing. Once they crossed the final slat of weathered wood and stepped onto the white sands of the East Beach, the atmosphere changed.","There were no reminders to \u0026quot;keep your elbows off the table.\u0026quot; There were no sudden, explosive arguments about Quidditch fouls from Draco and Ginny. Most importantly, there was no risk of walking into a room and seeing Harry and Hermione \u0026quot;knitted together\u0026quot; in a way that made everyone under the age of seventeen want to go for a long walk in the Forbidden Forest.","\u0026quot;Freedom,\u0026quot; James Sirius breathed, immediately vibrating so hard that he blurred at the edges. He didn\u0027t wait for the others; he sprinted toward the infinity pool, launched himself into a double-flip, and performed a cannonball that sent a ten-foot wall of water crashing over the sun loungers.","\u0026quot;Typical,\u0026quot; Cassie remarked, though she wasn\u0027t sneering. She dropped her designer beach bag—a gift from Narcissa that was larger on the inside—and claimed the prime cabana. \u0026quot;Thomas, the grid?\u0026quot;","Thomas Vernon Dursley didn\u0027t respond immediately. He was standing in the center of the open-plan living room, his hand pressed against the wall. To anyone else, it looked like he was daydreaming. To the Pack, they knew he was communicating with the island’s core.","\u0026quot;The ley lines are stable,\u0026quot; Thomas reported, his voice steady. \u0026quot;I’ve bridged the magical ward frequency with the satellite uplink Draco paid for. We have high-speed internet, but it’s being filtered through a prismatic shield. If James tries to download another chaotic prank video from the Muggle web, the router won’t explode this time.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Excellent,\u0026quot; Pandora said. She wasn\u0027t standing; she was currently drifting about six inches off the floor, her hair fanning out as if she were underwater. \u0026quot;The snorkelling will be vivid tomorrow. The fish are already talking about the \u0027vibrating boy\u0027 who just fell into their living room.\u0026quot;","The first few days of their independence were an exercise in controlled chaos. Without \u0026quot;The Management\u0026quot; to enforce a schedule, the Five developed their own strange, internal rhythm.","The Morning Rituals","Breakfast was a self-service affair managed by Lily Luna. While the others slept in, Lily would wake up with the sun, her presence making the tropical birds sing in complex, harmonious melodies. She didn\u0027t cook so much as she \u0026quot;persuaded\u0026quot; the food to be delicious. The fruit was always perfectly ripe when she touched it, and the pancakes seemed to fluff up just by being in her vicinity.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re doing that thing again, Lil,\u0026quot; James muttered one morning, stumbling into the kitchen. \u0026quot;The room smells like sunshine and optimism. It’s too early for optimism.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Eat your mango, James,\u0026quot; Lily smiled, handing him a bowl. \u0026quot;It’ll stop you from vibrating into the floorboards.\u0026quot;","The Laboratory of the Pack","By midday, the East Mansion transformed into a workshop. Thomas and James spent hours in the basement—which they had dubbed \u0027The Forge.\u0027 Using Thomas’s Technomancy and James’s raw, kinetic energy, they were trying to create a \u0026quot;Hover-Surfboard.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;If we can ground the levitation charm into the carbon-fiber deck,\u0026quot; Thomas explained, adjusting his glasses, \u0026quot;we don\u0027t need a wave. We can surf the air currents coming off the cliffs.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And if it fails?\u0026quot; James asked, his eyes gleaming.","\u0026quot;Then you’ll vibrate at a frequency that turns the board into shrapnel,\u0026quot; Thomas replied calmly. \u0026quot;So don\u0027t let it fail.\u0026quot;","The Afternoon Siesta and the \u0026quot;Hormones\u0026quot;","As the heat of the day peaked, the group would retreat to the shaded terraces. This was when the \u0026quot;privacy\u0026quot; they had requested became most apparent.","Cassie and Thomas often sat together, discussing the logistics of the wizarding world. There was a budding, quiet respect between them—the Malfoy precision meeting the Dursley pragmatism. They weren\u0027t \u0026quot;acting up\u0026quot; in the scandalous sense, but there was a new intensity in their conversations, a realization that they were the heirs to a very complicated, very powerful legacy.","Meanwhile, Pandora spent her time \u0026quot;observing\u0026quot; the group. Her Seer blood made her hyper-aware of the shifting dynamics. \u0026quot;The air is thick today,\u0026quot; she remarked to a confused James. \u0026quot;It tastes like growing pains and repressed shouting.\u0026quot;","The Night Shift","The nights were the best part. They didn\u0027t have a curfew. They stayed up watching Muggle movies on a giant screen Thomas had rigged to run on \u0026quot;Ambient Magic.\u0026quot;","On the fourth night, they sat on the roof of the East Mansion, looking across the lagoon at the main villa. They could see the distant glow of the Parents\u0027 dinner party—the soft sound of Harry’s laughter and the occasional \u0026quot;Hurricane\u0026quot; shout from Ginny.","\u0026quot;Do you think they miss us?\u0026quot; Lily asked, leaning her head on James’s shoulder.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re probably enjoying the silence,\u0026quot; Cassie said, though she was twisting a silver ring on her finger. \u0026quot;My dad is probably halfway through a bottle of Firewhisky, bragging to your dad about how he \u0027allowed\u0027 us to have our own house.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They\u0027re not just enjoying the silence,\u0026quot; Pandora whispered, her eyes turning that milky, prophetic white for a brief second. \u0026quot;They’re mourning the fact that we don\u0027t need them to hold our hands anymore. But they\u0027re also proud. The \u0027Pack\u0027 is a closed circle now.\u0026quot;","James stood up, looking out over the dark ocean. He felt the hum of the island, the buzz of the technology Thomas had installed, and the steady, warm light of Lily’s soul behind him.","\u0026quot;We’re doing okay, aren\u0027t we?\u0026quot; James asked. \u0026quot;No accidents. No Dark Lords. No one’s even set the kitchen on fire.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Speak for yourself,\u0026quot; Thomas muttered. \u0026quot;I saw Pandora trying to teach a crab how to use a fork earlier.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He was a very fast learner,\u0026quot; Pandora defended herself.","As the moon hung high over Isla de la Fortuna, the Five settled into their own home, proving that while they were born of \u0026quot;The Alliance,\u0026quot; they were something entirely new. They were independent, they were slightly hormonal, and they were—for the first time in their lives—the masters of their own destiny.","Across the water, the Parents watched the lights of the East Mansion stay on well past midnight.","\u0026quot;They\u0027re fine,\u0026quot; Harry whispered to Hermione as they stood on their balcony.","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; Hermione sighed, leaning into him. \u0026quot;That\u0027s the scary part.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":44,"origNum":14,"title":"The Sea Change","wordCount":816,"paragraphs":["The final forty-eight hours of the summer break arrived with a heavy, golden heat. On the terrace of the main villa, the \u0026quot;Six\u0026quot; were enjoying what Draco had termed \u0027The Final Peace.\u0027","With \u0026quot;The Management\u0026quot; (Vernon, Lucius, and the others) away on business, the atmosphere was relaxed. Harry and Hermione were, as usual, in a \u0026quot;Gryffindor Pretzel\u0026quot; on the oversized outdoor lounger—Hermione’s head was resting on Harry’s shoulder as she read a book on advanced arithmancy, while Harry mindlessly stroked her hair. Nearby, Draco and Ginny were sharing a bottle of chilled elfish wine, and Ron and Luna were debating whether the island’s sand was made of crushed dreams or silicate.","\u0026quot;Two days,\u0026quot; Ginny sighed, leaning back against Draco’s chest. \u0026quot;Two days before we have to deal with the chaos of the Hogwarts Express. I’ve almost forgotten what it’s like to not be in \u0027The Hurricane\u0027 mode.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They’ve been suspiciously quiet at the East Mansion,\u0026quot; Ron noted. \u0026quot;No explosions. No Technomancy-induced blackouts. Just... silence.\u0026quot;","Just as Hermione was about to comment on the psychological benefits of teenage independence, the surface of the lagoon broke.","Two figures were swimming toward the shore. They weren\u0027t using magic; they were using powerful, rhythmic strokes that cut through the water. As the water shallowed, the figures stood up and began to walk onto the white sand.","The terrace went dead silent. Hermione’s book slipped from her fingers, hitting the stone floor with a dull \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e. Harry froze, his hand stopping mid-stroke in Hermione’s hair.","It was James and Thomas. But it wasn\u0027t the boys who had left two weeks ago.","\u003cstrong\u003eJames Sirius Potter\u003c/strong\u003e stood nearly six feet tall. The \u0026quot;vibration\u0026quot; he usually emitted had manifested into visible, corded muscle across his chest and lean shoulders. His skin was tanned to a deep bronze, and his messy black hair—so like Harry’s—was slicked back by salt water, revealing a jawline that looked like it had been carved from granite. He moved with a raw, athletic power that made him look less like a third-year student and more like a professional Seeker in mid-season form.","Beside him, \u003cstrong\u003eThomas Vernon Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e was a revelation of physical strength. The Dursley \u0026quot;sturdiness\u0026quot; had evolved into its final, most impressive form. He was a mountain of functional muscle, standing even broader than James. His shoulders were like cannonballs, and his presence was so commanding he looked like a young Greek god of the forge. Even without magic, Thomas radiated a sense of absolute, unshakable power.","As they reached the terrace stairs, James shook his head, sending a spray of saltwater over the stone. Thomas wiped a hand across his face, his deep blue eyes calm and steady.","\u0026quot;We’re back,\u0026quot; James said. His voice had dropped an entire octave, landing in a rich, resonant baritone. \u0026quot;Is there any food left? Swimming across the lagoon twice a day makes you starving.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHermione\u003c/strong\u003e was the first to speak, her logical brain finally rebooting. \u0026quot;James Sirius Potter,\u0026quot; she whispered, her eyes wide as she looked at her son. \u0026quot;The biological rate of cell-regeneration required for that much vertical growth in fourteen days is... it\u0027s statistically impossible. Harry, look at him! He’s taller than you!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry\u003c/strong\u003e stood up, looking at his son with a mixture of immense pride and pure shock. He looked at James’s broad shoulders and then at Thomas. \u0026quot;I... I think the Dursley and Potter genes just had a secret meeting while we weren\u0027t looking. James, you look like your grandfather. But bigger.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eGinny\u003c/strong\u003e let out a low whistle, looking at her nephew with a predatory Quidditch-scout glint in her eyes. She nudged Hermione. \u0026quot;Hermione, stop worrying about the statistics and look at the wingspan! If he’s not Gryffindor Captain by next year, I’m retiring. But Harry, you better check Gringotts—you and Hermione are going to have to buy him an entirely new wardrobe. He’s literally bursting out of those trunks.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco\u003c/strong\u003e leaned forward, adjusting his sunglasses as he stared at Thomas, his godson’s cousin. \u0026quot;I have to admit,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, sounding genuinely impressed. \u0026quot;If this is what happens when Dursley \u0027efficiency\u0027 meets a summer at my island, I’m terrified of what the girls are going to look like. Thomas, you look like you could bench-press a Pensieve.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRon\u003c/strong\u003e looked at the two boys, then at his own midsection, then back at the \u0026quot;Greek Gods\u0026quot; standing on the terrace. He looked at Harry with a face of pure, fatherly terror. \u0026quot;Harry... we\u0027re in trouble. If they look like this at fourteen, we’re going to spend the next four years fending off half the wizarding world with a broomstick.\u0026quot;","James grinned, a flash of white teeth against his tanned skin, and looked at his mother and father. \u0026quot;We’re not kids anymore, Mum. The Pack has grown up.\u0026quot;","The two boys stood there, dripping wet and towering over the adults, the literal embodiments of a new, powerful era for the Alliance."]},{"num":45,"origNum":15,"title":"The Sirens of the Lagoon","wordCount":840,"paragraphs":["The terrace was already a disaster zone. Ron was still mourning his fallen meatball sub, Hermione was vibrating with \u0026quot;un-logical\u0026quot; stress, and Harry was staring at his son, James, wondering when exactly the boy had replaced his ribcage with a structural steel frame.","But then, the lagoon broke again.","If James and Thomas had arrived like a tectonic shift, what followed was a complete atomic collapse of the parental psyche.","Two figures emerged from the surf, walking with a synchronized, predatory grace that made the high-end Italian tiles of the terrace look like a runway in Milan. They weren’t just \u0026quot;tall\u0026quot;—they were five-foot-ten of distilled lethality and high-fashion elegance.","\u003cstrong\u003eCassie Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e led the way. She was wearing a sleek, obsidian-black bikini that shimmered like dragon scales (undoubtedly a limited-edition Malfoy vault piece). Her silver-blonde hair was slicked back, exposing a jawline so sharp it looked like it could cut through a Ministry decree. She had Ginny’s defiant, \u0026quot;I-will-crush-you\u0026quot; eyes and Draco’s arrogant, \u0026quot;I-own-this-beach\u0026quot; posture. She looked like a young queen returning from a very successful conquest.","Beside her, \u003cstrong\u003ePandora \u0026quot;Pan\u0026quot; Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e was an otherworldly vision. She was equally tall, but where Cassie was sharp, Pan was ethereal. She wore an iridescent lavender bikini that seemed to change color with the light, and her strawberry-blonde hair fell to her waist in salt-crusted waves. She possessed a natural, glowing aura that made it look as though she was walking in her own private spotlight. She looked less like a teenager and more like a celestial being who had accidentally wandered onto a mortal beach.","The reaction from the terrace was not just chaotic; it was \u003cstrong\u003eatomic.\u003c/strong\u003e","Draco Malfoy didn’t just drop his glass; it shattered against the stone, and he didn\u0027t even notice. His face turned a shade of white that Narcissa would have found impressively pale.","\u0026quot;No. Absolutely not. ACCIO PARKA!\u0026quot; he roared, waving his wand frantically at the air. \u0026quot;Ginny! Why does she have legs? Why are there so many legs? She’s only fourteen! I’m cancelling Hogwarts! I’m buying the castle and turning it into a fortress! I’ll build a wall! A Malfoy Wall!\u0026quot; He turned to the ocean and pointed his wand. \u0026quot;I CAST A CONCEALMENT CHARM ON THE ENTIRE MEDITERRANEAN!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eGinny Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e, however, was leaning back in her chair, laughing so hard she actually snorted her wine. \u0026quot;Oh, shut up, Draco! Look at her! She’s a Malfoy with my Quidditch build. She’s going to break every heart in Europe and then sue them for the emotional damages. That’s my girl!\u0026quot; She gave Cassie a thumbs-up. \u0026quot;Nice suit, Cass! Did your grandmother send that?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Obviously,\u0026quot; Cassie said, her voice a cool, bored Malfoy drawl. \u0026quot;She said the Dursley-Potter influence was making me too \u0027sturdy\u0027 and I needed to lean into the \u0027Lethal Aristocrat\u0027 aesthetic.\u0026quot;","Meanwhile, Ron Weasley had entered a state of catatonic shock. He looked at his daughter, Pandora—long-limbed, glowing, and looking like a supermodel from another dimension—and his brain simply stopped working.","\u0026quot;Pan?\u0026quot; he squeaked, his voice hitting a pitch only dogs could hear. \u0026quot;Why... why is there a lighthouse walking on our beach? Harry, lend me the Invisibility Cloak! I need to wrap her in it! I need to wrap the whole house in it! LUNA! Why is our daughter a celestial supermodel? I’m not ready for this! I haven\u0027t even finished my sandwich!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eLuna Lovegood\u003c/strong\u003e merely smiled, her eyes misty and calm as she watched Pandora. \u0026quot;Oh, don\u0027t be silly, Ron. She’s just finally aligning with her vertical frequency. The Gulping Plimpies told me she’d be tall this summer. She looks quite balanced, doesn\u0027t she? Like a very pretty, very dangerous heron.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHermione Granger\u003c/strong\u003e had achieved the \u0026quot;Ultimate Ostrich.\u0026quot; She had buried her face so deep into Harry’s chest that she was practically trying to merge with his ribcage. \u0026quot;It’s not possible,\u0026quot; she muffled into his shirt. \u0026quot;I checked the growth charts! I have the charts, Harry! Fourteen-year-olds are supposed to be awkward and gangly! They aren\u0027t supposed to look like they’ve been sculpted by Renaissance masters! It’s biologically rude!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry\u003c/strong\u003e, caught between a vibrating James, a mountain-like Thomas, a screaming Draco, and a muffled Hermione, just looked at the four of them standing in a row. The \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; was no longer a group of kids. They were a phalanx of beauty, power, and terrifying potential.","\u0026quot;Dad,\u0026quot; Cassie said, looking at Draco’s frantic wand-waving with supreme boredom as she tucked a strand of silver hair behind her ear. \u0026quot;Stop trying to summon a parka. It’s eighty degrees. And Thomas is hungry. If you don\u0027t feed the \u0027Anchor\u0027, he\u0027s going to start eating the furniture.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThomas\u003c/strong\u003e nodded, his deep, rumbling bass voice making the remaining glasses on the table rattle. \u0026quot;Steak. We need steak. Lots of it.\u0026quot;","The four of them stood there—James and Thomas like Greek titans, Cassie and Pan like high-fashion sirens—towering over the \u0026quot;Parents\u0026quot; who were currently a mess of spilled wine, shattered glass, and muffled logical protests.","The \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; hadn\u0027t just returned from the East Mansion. They had staged a biological coup."]},{"num":46,"origNum":16,"title":"The Final Eclipse (The Rise of Lily Luna)","wordCount":925,"paragraphs":["The terrace was no longer a place of relaxation; it was a theatre of the absurd. Draco was still frantically trying to summon winter wear in a tropical heatwave, Ron was staring at the space where his sandwich used to be as if it held the secrets to the universe, and Hermione was so deeply buried in Harry’s chest that she was practically part of his circulatory system.","But the \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; wasn\u0027t complete.","The four titans—James, Thomas, Cassie, and Pan—stood in a row, looking down at their parents with a mixture of pity and hunger. Then, they all turned as one toward the lagoon.","\u0026quot;Here she comes,\u0026quot; James rumbled in his new bass voice. \u0026quot;The Final Boss.\u0026quot;","The water didn\u0027t just break; it seemed to part in reverence. A figure emerged from the surf, moving with a fluid, haunting grace that made the previous four arrivals look like mere rehearsals.","It was \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter\u003c/strong\u003e.","Lily, who had left for the East Mansion looking like a delicate ten-year-old. Lily, who was the \u0026quot;baby\u0026quot; of the Alliance, the tiny beacon of light who usually sat on Harry’s lap.","That Lily was gone.","The girl walking onto the beach was a \u003cstrong\u003esix-foot-tall celestial phenomenon\u003c/strong\u003e. She stood exactly as tall as James and Thomas, her long, athletic limbs glowing with that signature \u0026quot;Lily aura\u0026quot; that was now amplified by her new stature. She wore a simple, white-and-gold bikini that made her look like a high-priestess of the sun. Her mahogany hair, thick and wavy, cascaded down her back like a waterfall of silk.","She didn\u0027t just look like a supermodel; she looked like the \u003cem\u003ereason\u003c/em\u003e supermodels were invented. She possessed a beauty so blindingly radiant and a stature so commanding that the very air around her seemed to hum with \u0026quot;The Light.\u0026quot;","She reached the terrace, stepped over Draco’s discarded wine glass, and looked at her parents.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Parental Atomic Meltdown:\u003c/strong\u003e","Harry Potter’s brain didn\u0027t just short-circuit; it experienced a total grid failure. He stared up—and he genuinely had to look up—at his daughter. His glasses didn\u0027t just slide down his nose; the right lens actually developed a hairline fracture from the sheer shock.","\u0026quot;Lily?\u0026quot; he whispered, his voice cracking like a boy in the middle of his own puberty. \u0026quot;Lily Luna? Where... where is my little girl? Who are you? Did someone use a Doubling Charm on you? Hermione! Look! She’s a giant! My baby is a giant!\u0026quot;","Hermione Granger finally detached herself from Harry’s chest, her hair now so frizzy it had its own weather system. She looked at Lily, looked at the height of the terrace railing, and then began to hyperventilate.","\u0026quot;Six feet,\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, her hands flying in frantic, logical gestures. \u0026quot;Harry, she’s six feet tall! She was four-foot-eleven in June! That is a growth rate of nearly an inch a day! It’s physically impossible! It defies the Law of Conservation of Mass! Lily Luna Potter, you return to your original dimensions this instant! It is biologically rude to grow this much without a permit!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRon Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e, seeing Harry’s breakdown, felt a surge of fraternal solidarity. He stood up, pointed at Lily, and looked at Harry. \u0026quot;Harry, give me your wand. We’re putting them all in a tower. A very tall tower with no doors and a lot of guard dogs. Thomas! Use your Technomancy to build a laser grid! No one is allowed to look at them! I’m going to go get my broom and start patrolling the perimeter!\u0026quot;","Draco Malfoy had stopped summoning parkas. He was now just sitting on the floor, staring at the five teenagers—the three six-foot-tall titans and the two five-foot-ten sirens.","\u0026quot;That’s it,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, his voice hollow. \u0026quot;The wizarding world is over. We’ve bred a master race. Between Thomas’s muscles, James’s chaos, the girls\u0027 lethality, and Lily... whatever Lily is... we’re basically just their assistants now. Ginny, fetch me the \u0027Black Card\u0027. I need to buy a private army just to escort them to Potions class.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eGinny Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e was the only one not panicking. She was looking at Lily with a look of pure, unadulterated awe. \u0026quot;Merlin\u0027s beard... she’s magnificent. Harry, look at her! She’s the perfect blend of your mother and Hermione’s intellect, wrapped in a frame that would make a Veela weep with envy.\u0026quot; She looked at Lily and winked. \u0026quot;Good summer, Lil?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was very peaceful, Aunt Ginny,\u0026quot; Lily said, her voice sounding like a silver bell—rich, calm, and utterly self-assured. She looked down at her father, who was still clutching his broken glasses. \u0026quot;Dad, stop staring. You’re vibrating more than James used to. And please don\u0027t let Uncle Ron build a tower. It would be very bad for the island’s aesthetic.\u0026quot;","Lily walked over and, in a move that shattered Harry’s heart into a million pieces, she didn\u0027t sit on his lap. She couldn\u0027t. She was too tall. Instead, she leaned down and kissed the top of his head.","\u0026quot;We’re ready for dinner now,\u0026quot; she announced, her aura of happiness washing over the terrace, momentarily drugging the parents into a state of stunned compliance.","The Five—the \u003cstrong\u003eNew Pantheon\u003c/strong\u003e—turned and walked toward the dining hall. James and Thomas acted as the pillars, Cassie and Pan as the blades, and Lily, at the center, as the blinding, six-foot-tall sun.","Behind them, the \u0026quot;Six\u0026quot; sat in the wreckage of their afternoon.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Ron whispered into the silence.","\u0026quot;Yeah, Ron?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re going to need a lot more security for the Hogwarts Express.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I know, Ron,\u0026quot; Harry sighed, finally leaning his head into his hands. \u0026quot;I know.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":47,"origNum":17,"title":"The Architecture of Men","wordCount":796,"paragraphs":["The main villa was quiet, but it was a vibrating, high-tension kind of quiet. Upstairs, \u0026quot;The Pack\u0026quot; was supposedly asleep, though the Parents suspected that Thomas was currently using his Technomancy to run a diagnostic on the island’s entire electrical grid while James hummed at a frequency that made the light fixtures rattle.","Downstairs in the lounge, the \u003cstrong\u003e\u0026quot;Eight\u0026quot;\u003c/strong\u003e—the core Alliance parents—were gathered in a state of collective shell-shock.","Harry and Hermione were in a maximum-security \u003cstrong\u003eGryffindor Pretzel\u003c/strong\u003e on the velvet sofa; Draco and Ginny were tangled together in a nearby armchair; Ron and Luna were on the rug sharing a plate of \u0026quot;stress biscuits\u0026quot;; and \u003cstrong\u003eDudley and Chloe\u003c/strong\u003e were sat on the love seat, Dudley staring at his own massive hands as if wondering where he had gone wrong in the genetic lottery.","\u0026quot;He’s six feet tall,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his voice cracking. \u0026quot;My son. My \u003cem\u003efourteen-year-old\u003c/em\u003e son. I have to look up to lecture him. How am I supposed to ground him if I’m craning my neck?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the Dursley-Potter intersection,\u0026quot; Hermione muffled into Harry\u0027s neck. \u0026quot;I’ve been running the numbers. Harry, the Potter kinetic energy combined with the Dursley structural density has created a... a biological fortress. James isn\u0027t just growing; he’s \u003cem\u003ereinforcing\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Reinforcing?\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eDudley\u003c/strong\u003e spoke up, his deep voice sounding strained. \u0026quot;Have you seen \u003cstrong\u003eThomas\u003c/strong\u003e? I was a heavyweight boxer, Harry. I was the biggest lad in Smeltings. But Thomas... I tried to give him a fatherly pat on the shoulder when he got back, and I felt like I was hitting a brick wall. He didn\u0027t even budge! He just looked at me and asked if I’d been keeping up with my cardio!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eChloe\u003c/strong\u003e leaned her head on Dudley’s shoulder, looking equally dazed. \u0026quot;I checked the laundry, Dudley. I had to throw away every single shirt he brought to the island. They’re all ripped at the seams. The shoulders... it’s like he grew a second set of muscles over the weekend. I asked him what he’d been eating at the East Mansion, and he just said \u0027Protein and ley-line energy.\u0027 What does that even mean?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It means we’re raising a tank,\u0026quot; Ron said, pointing a biscuit at Dudley. \u0026quot;Your son is a tank, Dursley. A very polite, very smart, Technomancing tank. He asked me if the villa’s foundations were \u0027structurally optimized for high-impact movement.\u0027 I thought he meant a workout. Now I realize he probably meant just \u003cem\u003ewalking\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And James!\u0026quot; Harry interjected, looking at Dudley. \u0026quot;He looks like my dad, but with your build. He’s got this... this \u003cem\u003epresence\u003c/em\u003e. He shook Ron\u0027s hand and I heard bones pop!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was three bones,\u0026quot; Ron confirmed solemnly. \u0026quot;I felt them.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eDraco Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e let out a shaky, aristocratic sigh. \u0026quot;Thomas is my godson’s cousin, but he looks like he belongs on a Malfoy tapestry from the Middle Ages—the ones where the knights are slaying dragons with their bare hands. I saw him lift three of the heavy oak lounge chairs at once earlier. He wasn\u0027t even using magic, Dudley. He just wanted to \u0027optimize the seating arrangement.\u0027 He’s fourteen! At fourteen, I was mostly a very stylish piece of parchment!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s the Vernon in him,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eGinny\u003c/strong\u003e noted, a wicked glint of amusement fighting through her shock. \u0026quot;Vernon always said he wanted the boy to be \u0027sturdy.\u0027 Well, Dudley, you and Chloe have produced a mountain. Thomas looks like he could bench-press the Ministry of Magic while James vibrates fast enough to power the lights. They’re a two-man power plant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think it’s wonderful,\u0026quot; Luna said, her eyes fixed on the ceiling. \u0026quot;The boys have stopped being saplings and have become oaks. It’s a very grounding energy. Although I suspect Thomas’s aura is so dense right now that he might actually be attracting his own small moon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m buying more protein,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eDudley\u003c/strong\u003e announced, standing up and pacing the room like a worried bear. \u0026quot;And a new gym set. If Thomas doesn\u0027t have something to lift, I’m afraid he’s going to start lifting the villa. Chloe, we’re going to need to call your tailor. And possibly a blacksmith.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Harry,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eChloe\u003c/strong\u003e added, looking over at the Potters. \u0026quot;You and Hermione better get ready. James and Thomas together? They’re going to be the most sought-after boys in the history of Hogwarts. We’re going to need a bigger owl-post box just for the love letters.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Harry and Dudley said in perfect, terrifying unison.","\u0026quot;I’m buying a dragon,\u0026quot; Draco repeated, clutching the Black Card. \u0026quot;A very large, very grumpy one. For the boys\u0027 own safety. And for mine.\u0026quot;","The Eight sat in the silence of the tropical night, a group of adults trying to come to terms with the fact that the boys they used to carry on their shoulders could now probably carry the entire family at once."]},{"num":48,"origNum":18,"title":"The Siren Protocol","wordCount":894,"paragraphs":["If the conversation about the boys had been about the \u0026quot;Architecture of Men,\u0026quot; the conversation about the girls was about the \u0026quot;Total Collapse of Parental Sanity.\u0026quot;","The \u0026quot;Eight\u0026quot; were still huddled in the lounge, but the atmosphere had shifted from shocked silence to a frantic, high-pitched state of emergency. Harry was currently cleaning his broken glasses with a trembling hand, while Draco was pacing the length of the room so fast he was leaving scorch marks on the rug.","\u0026quot;Six feet,\u0026quot; Harry whispered for the fortieth time. \u0026quot;She was the smallest. She was the \u003cem\u003elittlest\u003c/em\u003e one in the group. I used to carry her on my shoulders, Hermione! Now, if I tried that, we’d look like a circus act!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The biological audacity of it!\u0026quot; Hermione cried out, finally abandoning the \u003cstrong\u003eOstrich\u003c/strong\u003e maneuver. Her hair was now so charged with static that it was literally floating around her head like a halo. \u0026quot;She has grown thirteen inches in two months, Harry! Thirteen! I checked the Encyclopedia of Magical Development—this only happens to Giant-hybrids or people who have been hit by an accidental Engorgement Charm! But Lily isn\u0027t a giant. She’s... she’s a phenomenon!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Pan,\u0026quot; Ron groaned, his head buried in his hands. \u0026quot;She looks like she’s made of starlight and expensive perfume. I tried to tell her to put on a jumper for dinner—a nice, thick, woolly jumper—and she just looked at me with those big misty eyes and said, \u0027The moon doesn\u0027t wear a jumper, Daddy.\u0027 How do you argue with that? How do you put a jumper on the moon?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You don\u0027t, Ron,\u0026quot; Luna said serenely, braiding a piece of grass she’d found on the floor. \u0026quot;The moon is meant to be seen. Though I did notice her aura has become quite magnetic. She’ll probably start attracting metal objects and boy-wizards soon. It’s very natural.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eIt is NOT natural!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot; Draco roared, spinning on his heel. \u0026quot;Cassie is wearing a bikini that costs more than a Nimbus 2000 and has enough attitude to topple a government! She looked at me today—at \u003cem\u003eme\u003c/em\u003e, her father, the man who controls the Black Card—and she sneered! A perfect, Malfoy-grade sneer! She told me my panic was \u0027unbecoming of my station\u0027!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s got you there, Draco,\u0026quot; Ginny said, lounging back with a smirk. \u0026quot;She looked magnificent. She looks like she’s ready to lead an army or a runway show, possibly both. And let’s be honest—she’s a Malfoy-Weasley. We knew she’d be a heartbreaker. We just didn\u0027t expect her to be a heart-obliterater by the age of fourteen.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m calling Narcissa,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, reaching for the Floo powder. \u0026quot;No, wait. Narcissa sent her the suit. My own mother is a double agent! She’s arming the girl for social warfare!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eChloe\u003c/strong\u003e leaned forward, looking sympathetic. \u0026quot;It’s not just the magic, is it? Even in the Muggle world, when girls hit that stage... but this? This is different. They don\u0027t just look pretty. They look... powerful. Lily walked across that beach and I swear the waves actually calmed down just to watch her.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That’s the \u0027Light\u0027 in her,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eDudley\u003c/strong\u003e grunted, looking at Harry. \u0026quot;Your girl has always been special, Harry. But now? She’s like a beacon. If James and Thomas are the guards, Lily is the one they’re guarding. Not that she needs it. I saw her look at a coconut today and it practically peeled itself out of sheer respect.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m going to have to duel them,\u0026quot; Harry said suddenly, his eyes wide and glazed behind his cracked lenses.","\u0026quot;Who, Harry?\u0026quot; Hermione asked.","\u0026quot;Everyone,\u0026quot; Harry replied. \u0026quot;Every boy at Hogwarts. I’ll just stand at the front gates. \u0027Welcome to school. I’m Harry Potter. I’ve defeated a Dark Lord, and if you even \u003cem\u003ethink\u003c/em\u003e about asking my daughter to Hogsmeade, I will show you exactly how I did it.\u0027\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll help,\u0026quot; Ron stood up, looking determined. \u0026quot;I’ll bring the Cleansweep. We can do aerial patrols.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll fund the operation,\u0026quot; Draco added, finally stopping his pacing. \u0026quot;I’ll buy a fleet of stealth-brooms. We’ll call it \u0027Operation: No One Touches the Sirens.\u0027 We’ll need wards. Anti-boy wards. Wards that trigger a loud siren and a stinging hex if anyone under the age of seventeen gets within five feet of them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You three are pathetic,\u0026quot; Ginny laughed, though there was a soft look in her eyes as she looked at her husband and her brother. \u0026quot;They’re The Pack. They’ve got James and Thomas to look after them, and they’ve got each other. Besides, did you see Cassie’s face? She doesn\u0027t need a ward. She’s a Malfoy. One look from her and most boys will simply melt into a puddle of insecurity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And Lily,\u0026quot; Luna added softly, \u0026quot;Lily doesn\u0027t need protection because she is the protection. Her heart is so bright that darkness—and teenage boys—simply won\u0027t know how to handle her.\u0026quot;","Harry looked at Hermione, who was finally calming down, her hair slowly descending from its static-charged height.","\u0026quot;We’re in trouble, aren\u0027t we?\u0026quot; Harry asked.","\u0026quot;Statistically?\u0026quot; Hermione sighed, leaning her head on his shoulder. \u0026quot;We are in an unprecedented amount of trouble. The 4th year at Hogwarts is going to be a logistical and emotional catastrophe.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, closing his eyes. \u0026quot;At least we’re in it together.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;To the Alliance,\u0026quot; Ron said, raising a lukewarm butterbeer.","\u0026quot;To the Alliance,\u0026quot; they all echoed, eight parents bracing themselves for the storm that was their children."]},{"num":49,"origNum":19,"title":"The Management’s Audit","wordCount":798,"paragraphs":["The final morning on Isla de la Fortuna began with the roar of a private Gulfstream engine and the shimmer of a high-security Portkey arrival. \u003cstrong\u003e\u0026quot;The Management\u0026quot;\u003c/strong\u003e had arrived.","Vernon Dursley stepped onto the private dock, adjusting his beige safari suit and checking his gold watch with a frown of \u0026quot;efficiency.\u0026quot; Beside him, Lucius Malfoy looked as though he had been carved from ice, his walking stick clicking rhythmically against the wood. Behind them, Petunia, Narcissa, Molly, and Arthur followed, laden with gifts, high-end magical snacks, and enough \u0026quot;grandmotherly concern\u0026quot; to smother a dragon.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Vernon barked, looking up at the main villa. \u0026quot;I’ve checked the airline’s quarterly projections, fired three incompetent pilots, and Lucius has successfully bribed the Italian Ministry. Now, where are the youngsters? I want a full report on their summer progress!\u0026quot;","The \u0026quot;Eight\u0026quot; (the Parents) were standing at the top of the terrace stairs, wearing identical, mischievous smirks.","\u0026quot;Vernon, Lucius... everyone,\u0026quot; Harry said, stepping forward. His voice held a note of suppressed laughter. \u0026quot;Before you go inside, you might want to take a seat. And perhaps some smelling salts.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t be ridiculous, Harry,\u0026quot; Petunia tittered, adjusting her sun hat. \u0026quot;They’re just children. We’ve only been gone two months!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Actually,\u0026quot; Dudley said, looking at his father with a look of profound pity. \u0026quot;You might want to brace your core, Dad. The \u0027stock\u0027 has appreciated. Significantly.\u0026quot;","At that exact moment, the lagoon exploded.","James Sirius and Thomas Vernon had decided to finish their final swim practice with a synchronized sprint to the shore. They emerged from the water like two surfacing submarines, the sunlight glinting off their tanned, water-slicked skin.","As they stood up in the shallows and began the long walk toward the dock, \u0026quot;The Management\u0026quot; went into a state of total system failure.","Vernon Dursley actually dropped his leather briefcase. It hit the dock with a heavy thud, spilling spreadsheets into the sea. He stared at his grandson, Thomas, who was now a six-foot-tall wall of solid, functional muscle.","\u0026quot;Dudley...\u0026quot; Vernon wheezed, his face turning a dangerous shade of purple. \u0026quot;What... what have you done? Is that Thomas? Why is he built like a heavy-duty crane? He’s... he’s a mountain! He’s a fortress! That’s a Dursley! Look at those shoulders! You could land a helicopter on them!\u0026quot;","Lucius Malfoy didn\u0027t move, but his grip on his snake-headed cane tightened so hard his knuckles turned white. He looked at James Sirius—the boy who bore the Potter name but moved with the raw, terrifying power of a Dursley-steeled warrior.","\u0026quot;By the Founding Fathers,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered, his aristocratic poise momentarily shattered. \u0026quot;He’s... he’s a physical specimen of the highest order. Potter, did you put the boy through a Spartan training camp? He looks like he’s been sculpted by an angry deity.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eMolly Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e let out a shriek that startled the local seagulls. She dropped her bag of home-baked cookies and clutched her heart. \u0026quot;James! Thomas! Oh, my stars! They’re starving! Look at them! They’ve grown so much they must be hollow inside! Arthur, look! They’ve lost all their baby fat! They’re just... they\u0027re just muscles and bone! We need to get them a roast. Seven roasts! Immediately!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eArthur Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e reached for his spectacles, polished them frantically, and put them back on. \u0026quot;Fascinating... truly fascinating. Is this a Muggle growth-hormone? Or perhaps a localized gravitational anomaly? Harry, the boy’s wingspan is incredible! He’s a biological marvel!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePetunia Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e was weeping silently into a lace handkerchief, but she wasn\u0027t sad. She was terrified and proud. \u0026quot;He looks just like... he looks like a king,\u0026quot; she sobbed. \u0026quot;My little Thomas is a giant. And James... oh, Harry, Lily would have been so overwhelmed. He’s magnificent.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eNarcissa Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e was the only one who remained somewhat composed, though her eyes were wide. She looked at the two boys, then at the \u0026quot;Eight\u0026quot; parents. \u0026quot;I see,\u0026quot; she said smoothly. \u0026quot;The \u0027Pack\u0027 has decided to stop being puppies. Lucius, stop gawking. We are going to need to redo the entire Malfoy family wardrobe. And possibly reinforce the floors of the Manor.\u0026quot;","James and Thomas reached the dock, dripping water and towering over their grandparents. James shook his hair, spraying Lucius’s expensive robes with saltwater.","\u0026quot;Morning, Grandpa,\u0026quot; James rumbled, his new bass voice vibrating in Vernon’s chest. \u0026quot;Did you bring the airline? I want to see if I can fit in the cockpit.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eVernon\u003c/strong\u003e looked up at his grandson—actually had to tilt his head back—and let out a booming, hysterical laugh. \u0026quot;Fit in the cockpit? Lad, you look like you could \u003cem\u003ecarry\u003c/em\u003e the plane! That’s my boy! That’s a Dursley-Potter merger if I’ve ever seen one! Absolute efficiency!\u0026quot;","The Management stood there, surrounded by spilled cookies and dropped briefcases, staring at the two young titans who had officially outgrown the world they were born into."]},{"num":50,"origNum":20,"title":"The Sirens and the Shockwaves","wordCount":903,"paragraphs":["If the arrival of the boys had been a \u0026quot;structural audit\u0026quot; that left Vernon and Lucius reeling, the arrival of the girls was a full-scale atmospheric collapse.","The lagoon, seemingly sensing the impending drama, shimmered with a heat haze. The \u0026quot;Management\u0026quot; was still standing on the dock—Vernon clutching his spilled spreadsheets, Lucius leaning heavily on his cane, and Molly trying to gather her scattered cookies—when the water broke again.","Three figures emerged from the surf, walking in a synchronized, lethal V-formation. They didn\u0027t just walk; they glided with a high-fashion, predatory grace that turned the Mediterranean beach into a celestial runway.","\u003cstrong\u003eCassie Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e flanked the sides—two five-foot-ten visions of silver-blonde arrogance and ethereal lavender radiance. But at the center, leading them like a high-priestess of the sun, was \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter\u003c/strong\u003e.","At a towering six feet tall, Lily looked less like a fourteen-year-old and more like a goddess of legend. She was wearing the white-and-gold bikini that had already decimated Harry’s sanity, her mahogany hair trailing behind her like a royal cape. Her aura of \u0026quot;The Light\u0026quot; was so intense that the sunlight seemed to bend toward her, making her glow with a terrifying, beautiful brilliance.","The reaction from the \u0026quot;Management\u0026quot; was not just chaotic; it was \u003cstrong\u003eatomic.\u003c/strong\u003e","Lucius Malfoy made a sound like a violin string snapping at high tension. He stared at his granddaughter, Cassie, who was looking at him with a lethal Malfoy smirk.","\u0026quot;Narcissa!\u0026quot; Lucius gasped, his voice hitting a register that could have shattered crystal. \u0026quot;What is this? Why is my granddaughter a six-foot siren? Why is she wearing... is that dragon-hide silk? Who allowed this? ACCIO VELVET CURTAIN!\u0026quot; He waved his cane frantically, accidentally summoning a decorative tapestry from the villa’s lounge that flew through the air and hit Vernon in the face. \u0026quot;She’s a child! She was three feet tall and interested in potions kits yesterday! I’m moving the Malfoy vaults to a mountain peak! No one is allowed to look at her! Not even the portraits!\u0026quot;","Vernon Dursley, currently struggling with the tapestry Lucius had accidentally thrown at him, finally fought his way out and looked at Lily Luna. His eyes nearly popped out of his head.","\u0026quot;Harry!\u0026quot; Vernon roared, pointing a trembling finger. \u0026quot;Who is that? That’s not Lily! Lily is the little one! The one who likes the tea parties! This is a... this is a celestial event! Look at the height on her! She’s as tall as Thomas! She’s got the Dursley stature and the Potter... whatever-that-is! Petunia, get the checkbook! We need to hire a private security firm! A Muggle one with snipers! And possibly a tank!\u0026quot;","Molly Weasley had reached a level of high-pitched distress that was vibrating the dock. She was frantically trying to wrap her own shawl around Pandora, who was calmly drifting a few inches off the wood.","\u0026quot;Pan! Pandora! My goodness, look at your limbs! You\u0027re all legs and starlight! Where is your jumper? I don\u0027t care if it\u0027s a hundred degrees, you need a nice thick knit to hide all that... that... everything! And Lily! Oh, Lily dear, you’re so tall! How will I ever reach you to pinch your cheeks? Arthur, do something! They’re too beautiful! It’s a safety hazard! They’ll cause carriage accidents at Hogwarts!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eArthur Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e was holding his glasses on with both hands, looking at the girls with clinical, wide-eyed amazement. \u0026quot;Is this... is this the \u0027Supermodel\u0027 phenomenon I’ve read about in the Muggle papers? Petunia, is this normal for Muggle fourteen-year-olds? Do they all just turn into towering visions of grace overnight? It’s a fascinating biological upgrade!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003ePetunia Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e stood perfectly still, her hands clasped over her mouth. She wasn\u0027t yelling. She was staring at Lily Luna with tears streaming down her face. \u0026quot;She looks just like her,\u0026quot; Petunia whispered, her voice choked with a mixture of grief and wonder. \u0026quot;She looks like Lily... but if Lily had been a queen. She’s magnificent, Vernon. She’s the heart of the family, and she’s outgrown us all.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eNarcissa Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e stood beside Lucius, looking at the three girls with a cool, triumphant smile. She adjusted her sun hat and looked at her husband’s panicked face. \u0026quot;Lucius, stop trying to shroud the girl in tapestries. I sent her that suit. It was time the world realized that the Malfoy-Weasley line is the apex of the wizarding world. They aren\u0027t children anymore. They’re the New Pantheon. Deal with it.\u0026quot;","Lily reached the dock first, looking down—literally down—at her grandfather Lucius. She leaned in, her radiant aura making him blink, and kissed his cheek.","\u0026quot;Welcome to the island, Grandfather,\u0026quot; Lily said, her voice like a silver chime. \u0026quot;We’ve missed your efficiency.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eLucius\u003c/strong\u003e actually wobbled on his feet. \u0026quot;Efficiency,\u0026quot; he croaked. \u0026quot;Yes. We need... we need to audit the security. Immediately. And possibly the boys. Where are the boys? I want them in a defensive perimeter around this dock at all times!\u0026quot;","The three girls swept past the stunned Grandparents, followed by the towering forms of James and Thomas, who were trying very hard not to laugh at Lucius’s attempts to hide them behind the furniture.","The \u0026quot;Management\u0026quot; stood on the dock, surrounded by spilled cookies, floating lavender auras, and the shattered remains of their authority.","\u003cstrong\u003eVernon\u003c/strong\u003e looked at \u003cstrong\u003eLucius\u003c/strong\u003e. \u0026quot;Lucius?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, Vernon?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We’re going to need a bigger airline. And possibly a private army.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Agreed,\u0026quot; Lucius whispered. \u0026quot;For once, Vernon, I completely agree.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":51,"origNum":21,"title":"The War Council of the Elders","wordCount":951,"paragraphs":["The tropical night was thick with the scent of jasmine, expensive cigars, and the palpable, vibrating hum of parental anxiety. Upstairs, the \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; was asleep—or at least pretending to be—but downstairs in the grand lounge of the main villa, the \u0026quot;Fourteen\u0026quot; were gathered for what could only be described as an emergency summit.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Management\u003c/strong\u003e (Vernon, Petunia, Lucius, Narcissa, Molly, and Arthur) sat opposite \u003cstrong\u003eThe Eight\u003c/strong\u003e (Harry, Hermione, Dudley, Chloe, Draco, Ginny, Ron, and Luna). Between them sat several bottles of Firewhisky, a tray of Molly’s \u0026quot;calming\u0026quot; scones, and the shattered remains of everyone’s expectations.","\u003cstrong\u003eVernon Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e was the first to break the silence. He slammed a meaty hand onto the mahogany coffee table. \u0026quot;Dudley!\u0026quot; he barked, his face a vibrant shade of magenta. \u0026quot;I sent that boy to school as a sturdy lad. A lad with a good, solid Dursley frame. I come back, and what do I find? A skyscraper! A mahogany-tanned skyscraper with shoulders like a double-decker bus! That’s not a boy, Dudley, that’s a \u003cstrong\u003econstruction project\u003c/strong\u003e!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I told you, Dad,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eDudley\u003c/strong\u003e groaned, rubbing his temples. \u0026quot;The island air did something to them. Thomas hasn\u0027t stopped growing since June. He’s already eaten through three months\u0027 worth of steak in ten days.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the efficiency!\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eVernon\u003c/strong\u003e roared, though he looked secretly delighted. \u0026quot;He’s optimized his own growth! He’s a biological marvel of vertical integration! But James... Harry, your son is a menace! He shook my hand and nearly dislocated my rotator cuff! And the vibrating! Why is he vibrating so loud? Is he a human or a high-speed rail?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eLucius Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e, meanwhile, was staring into his glass of Firewhisky as if looking for an exit strategy from reality. \u0026quot;I have already been in contact with the Gringotts ward-specialists,\u0026quot; he whispered, his aristocratic poise hanging by a thread. \u0026quot;I am purchasing a private cloud. A thick, grey, impenetrable Malfoy-branded cloud that will follow Cassie and Pandora at all times. It will be charmed to drop rain—very cold rain—on any boy who gets within ten feet of them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, Lucius, don\u0027t be so dramatic,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eNarcissa\u003c/strong\u003e said, elegantly sipping her tea. \u0026quot;The girls look exactly as they should. They are Malfoys, Blacks, and Weasleys. They were never going to be \u0027cute.\u0027 They were always going to be \u003cstrong\u003eweaponized beauty\u003c/strong\u003e. I’ve already sent word to the Malfoy vaults to prepare the emerald collection. A six-foot-tall siren like Lily Luna requires jewels, not jumpers.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eNO JEWELS!\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eMolly Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e shrieked, her knitting needles clacking at a speed that could have powered a small village. \u0026quot;They need wool! Thick, chunky, non-form-fitting wool! I don\u0027t care if it\u0027s a heatwave! Did you see the girls? They look like... like... \u003cstrong\u003eSirens\u003c/strong\u003e! I saw Arthur nearly trip over a potted plant just because Pandora walked into the room! Arthur! At your age!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She’s very symmetrical, Molly!\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eArthur\u003c/strong\u003e defended himself, adjusting his spectacles. \u0026quot;It’s a fascinating Muggle-like phenomenon! The \u0027Supermodel Mutation\u0027! I’ve been reading about it! But Lily... Harry, Hermione... how? She was our tiny flower! She was the smallest of the lot!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHermione\u003c/strong\u003e let out a muffled whimper, her face currently buried in Harry’s shoulder in a textbook \u003cstrong\u003eSeated Ostrich\u003c/strong\u003e. \u0026quot;It’s the Law of Compensation!\u0026quot; she wailed into his shirt. \u0026quot;She spent thirteen years being small, so her magic decided to compensate for every missed millimeter in a single summer! She’s six feet tall, Arthur! She’s taller than me! She’s taller than Harry! I tried to give her a motherly hug and I ended up hugging her waist! It’s psychologically devastating!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHarry\u003c/strong\u003e patted Hermione’s hair, looking like a man who had seen the end of the world and found it oddly shiny. \u0026quot;I’ve accepted it,\u0026quot; he said, his voice hollow. \u0026quot;I’m just going to stand at the Hogwarts gates with a sign that says \u0027I HAVE A GOD-TIER BEYOND-LIFE CONTRACT AND I’M NOT AFRAID TO USE IT.\u0027 No one is asking Lily to Hogsmeade. No one.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, please,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eGinny\u003c/strong\u003e laughed, leaning into Draco’s side. \u0026quot;Harry, did you see the way Thomas was looking at the security wards? And the way Cassie was bossing James around? The \u0027Pack\u0027 isn\u0027t just hit by puberty; they’ve hit back. They’re a five-headed titan of hormones and high-magic. We aren\u0027t just in trouble at Hogwarts; we’re in trouble with the global economy once they graduate.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRon\u003c/strong\u003e sat up suddenly, his eyes wide. \u0026quot;Wait. If Lily is six feet tall... and James is six feet tall... and Thomas is a tank... does this mean I have to buy \u003cstrong\u003efive\u003c/strong\u003e new sets of Quidditch gear? In \u0027Titan\u0027 size?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’ll put it on the \u003cstrong\u003eBlack Card\u003c/strong\u003e, Ron,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eDraco\u003c/strong\u003e sighed, finally leaning back and closing his eyes. \u0026quot;At this point, I’m just waiting for the day they decide they don\u0027t need the island and just build their own out of sheer willpower.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I think,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eLuna\u003c/strong\u003e said softly, looking out at the moon, \u0026quot;that the meteor didn\u0027t just hit the children. I think it hit the whole world. The Alliance was powerful, but the Pantheon? They’re going to change everything. Though I do hope Thomas figures out how to make the internet work in the Forbidden Forest. James really wants to show the Centaurs some cat videos.\u0026quot;","The Fourteen sat in the flickering candlelight, a collection of the world\u0027s most powerful, wealthy, and influential witches, wizards, and Muggles—all of them utterly terrified of five teenagers sleeping upstairs.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eVernon\u003c/strong\u003e grunted, standing up. \u0026quot;First thing tomorrow: I’m ordering a hundredweight of bacon and a private security detail for the Hogwarts Express. Lucius, you handle the bribes. Petunia, help Molly with the \u0027modesty\u0027 sweaters. Harry, Draco... try to stop vibrating. It’s embarrassing.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We\u0027re not vibrating, Vernon,\u0026quot; \u003cstrong\u003eDraco\u003c/strong\u003e muttered. \u0026quot;That’s just the sound of our bank accounts and our sanity evaporating simultaneously.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":52,"origNum":22,"title":"The Calm Before the Hurricane","wordCount":673,"paragraphs":["The Great Hall was a sea of flickering candles and expectant faces, but for the first time in four years, the golden atmosphere felt strangely... light.","At the High Table, the faculty of Hogwarts sat in a row that could only be described as \u0026quot;cautiously optimistic.\u0026quot; Albus Dumbledore was currently wearing a Hawaiian shirt patterned with animated dancing pineapples and a cloak made entirely of shimmering silver sequins—a gift from the \u0026quot;Management\u0026quot; after the airline merger—and was humming a jaunty tune.","Beside him, Minerva McGonagall was checking her pocket watch every thirty seconds, her lips thinned into a line of professional concern. Severus Snape sat to her left, looking remarkably healthy for a man who lived in a dungeon, his dark eyes scanning the student tables with a predatory stillness.","\u0026quot;They weren\u0027t on the train, Albus,\u0026quot; Minerva whispered, her voice tight. \u0026quot;I’ve checked with the Prefects. I’ve checked with the conductor. Five seats in the premium cabin—commissioned and paid for by the Malfoy vault—were entirely empty. Even the trolley witch is distraught; apparently, James Sirius usually buys out her entire stock of Cauldron Cakes just to see if he can make them hover.\u0026quot;","Snape let out a long, slow breath that sounded suspiciously like a sigh of relief. \u0026quot;Perhaps,\u0026quot; he drawled, his voice silky and sharp, \u0026quot;they have finally decided that Hogwarts is too small for their collective ego. One can only hope they’ve moved on to colonizing a small moon. My stores of Potion ingredients might actually survive a semester without Lily Luna \u0027persuading\u0027 the Valerian roots to grow into the shape of hearts.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Now, now, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore twinkled, popping a lemon drop into his mouth. \u0026quot;The Pack has a flair for the dramatic. And given the reports from Isla de la Fortuna, I suspect their arrival will be... noteworthy.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Noteeworthy?\u0026quot; Remus Lupin interjected, leaning forward. He still had a faint look of haunting confusion in his eyes whenever he thought about Lily’s Boggart lesson. \u0026quot;Remus, the island’s magical signature has been spiking for weeks. Vernon Dursley sent me a letter—delivered by a private courier on a jet-ski, no less—warning me that the \u0027structural integrity\u0027 of the Great Hall might need reinforcement.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Reinforcement for what?\u0026quot; Hagrid asked, wiping a tear of worry from his beard. \u0026quot;They’re just kids! Little James, tiny Lily... they’re the heart of the school!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They were kids in June, Hagrid,\u0026quot; Snape muttered, his eyes flickering to the doors. \u0026quot;But if the rumors of the \u0027Meteor Puberty\u0027 are even half-true, we are no longer dealing with children. We are dealing with an environmental disaster.\u0026quot;","A wave of hushed whispers rippled through the student body. The Gryffindor table was looking at the empty seats where James and Lily should have been. The Slytherins were casting glances at the space reserved for Cassie. The absence of the five most powerful, chaotic, and beloved students was like a vacuum, sucking the energy out of the room.","\u0026quot;It’s peaceful, isn\u0027t it?\u0026quot; Filius Flitwick squeaked, looking around. \u0026quot;No one is vibrating. No one is accidentally Technomancing the chandeliers. No one is causing a localized \u0027Hurricane\u0027 in the corridors.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s the peace of the graveyard, Filius,\u0026quot; Snape countered. \u0026quot;Enjoy it. It usually lasts exactly until—\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eBOOM.\u003c/strong\u003e","The massive oak doors of the Great Hall didn\u0027t just open; they were slammed back against the stone walls with a force that made the enchanted ceiling flicker from a starry night to a thunderstorm.","The entire student body went silent. The forks of three hundred students hit their plates in a synchronized clatter.","Framed against the torchlight of the Entrance Hall, five towering silhouettes stood in the doorway.","Two massive, broad-shouldered titans stood on the flanks, their frames blocking out the light like pillars of a temple. Beside them, two long-limbed, elegant figures stood with a poise that made the very air in the Hall feel underdressed. And at the center, a sixth-foot-tall figure stood with an aura so bright, so radiant, that the candles in the Great Hall seemed to dim in submission.","The Pack had arrived."]},{"num":53,"origNum":23,"title":"The Walk of Titans","wordCount":622,"paragraphs":["The silence in the Great Hall wasn’t just a lack of noise; it was a physical weight, a vacuum created by the collective held breath of every soul in the room.","As the first two silhouettes stepped out of the shadows and into the golden, flickering light of the floating candles, the vacuum shattered into a thousand gasps.","\u003cstrong\u003eJames Sirius Potter\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003eThomas Vernon Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e didn’t just walk into the room; they occupied it. The heavy, rhythmic thud of their boots on the ancient stone sounded like the heartbeat of a giant.","James led the way, his pace carrying a predatory, athletic swagger. His white dress shirt—which had been tailored for him in June and was now visibly straining across his broad shoulders—was unbuttoned at the collar. His jaw was set, his green eyes scanning the hall with a calm, kinetic intensity that made several Gryffindor third-years forget how to breathe.","Beside him, Thomas was a wall of solid, immovable presence. He didn\u0027t have James’s restless energy; he had the terrifying stability of a mountain. His chest was so wide it seemed to block out the view of the Hufflepuff table entirely as he passed. He walked with a disciplined, heavy stride, his expression as unreadable and commanding as a king’s.","The reaction from the student body was instantaneous and \u003cstrong\u003echaotic.\u003c/strong\u003e","At the Gryffindor table, a group of fourth-year girls simultaneously dropped their forks. One girl, a usually articulate Beater for the team, let out a soft, whimpering sound and slowly slumped sideways into a bowl of mashed potatoes.","\u0026quot;Is that... James?\u0026quot; whispered a fifth-year, her eyes following the ripple of muscle in his back. \u0026quot;Is that the boy who used to vibrate so much he fell off his broom? He looks like... he looks like he could be the broom.\u0026quot;","At the Slytherin table, the usual cold composure was nowhere to be found. Several girls had stood up instinctively, their eyes wide as they appraised the two boys with a mixture of shock and intense, sudden interest.","\u0026quot;The Dursley boy,\u0026quot; one whispered, her voice trembling. \u0026quot;He’s not a Muggle-born, he’s a god of the forge. Look at those arms. He looks like he could pick up the Slytherin common room and move it to a better location.\u0026quot;","The male students fared no better. Most of them were staring at James and Thomas with looks of profound, soul-deep insecurity. A group of seventh-year Quidditch players, who had spent the summer feeling quite proud of their own physiques, suddenly began pulling their robes tighter and looking very intently at their pumpkin juice.","\u0026quot;What have they been eating?\u0026quot; one Ravenclaw boy muttered, frantically checking his own biceps. \u0026quot;Is it a potion? A hex? They’re fourteen! I’m seventeen and I look like a twig next to them!\u0026quot;","James and Thomas continued their march, oblivious to the carnage they were leaving in their wake. They didn\u0027t stop at the House tables. They didn\u0027t look for their friends. They walked straight down the center of the hall, their eyes fixed on the High Table.","As they reached the end of the aisle, just before the steps leading to the Professors\u0027 table, they came to a synchronized, military-perfect halt.","They stood there, two six-foot-tall pillars of bronze skin and hard muscle, the flickering candlelight catching the sharp angles of their faces. They looked less like students and more like a private security detail for the gods.","The Great Hall was silent once more, but this time, the silence was different. It was the silence of a kingdom waiting for its rulers to speak.","James tilted his head slightly, his eyes meeting his father’s stunned gaze at the High Table, a small, arrogant Potter smirk playing on his lips."]},{"num":54,"origNum":24,"title":"The High-Fashion Siege","wordCount":677,"paragraphs":["If the entrance of James and Thomas had been a tectonic shift, the entrance of \u003cstrong\u003eCassie Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e was a total atmospheric ignition.","The air in the Great Hall, already thin from the collective shock, seemed to suddenly smell of expensive French perfume and sea salt. The two girls stepped into the light, and for a terrifying second, the enchanted ceiling above swirled into a confused mess of silver and lavender, unable to decide which girl to reflect.","\u003cstrong\u003eCassie Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e walked three paces ahead, her silver-blonde hair caught in a perfectly sharp Malfoy braid that swayed against her back like a whip. She wasn\u0027t wearing standard school robes; she was in a tailored, obsidian-black traveling ensemble that hugged her five-foot-ten frame with lethal precision. Her gaze was a cold, aristocratic burn that made the Slytherin table collectively sit up as if they\u0027d been hit by a \u003cem\u003eStupefy\u003c/em\u003e.","Beside her, \u003cstrong\u003ePandora \u0026quot;Pan\u0026quot; Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e moved like a dream that had wandered into a nightmare. She was equally tall, her strawberry-blonde hair glowing with a faint, iridescent shimmer. She didn\u0027t just walk; she seemed to float over the stone, her eyes wide and misty, looking as if she were seeing through the walls of the castle and into the next century.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Male Student Meltdown (Atomic and Chaotic):\u003c/strong\u003e","The male population of Hogwarts didn\u0027t just notice them; they experienced a total system crash.","\u003cstrong\u003eSeamus Finnigan\u003c/strong\u003e, who had been mid-sentence about a new explosion he’d caused, simply stopped talking. His mouth stayed open so long that a nearby enchanted pea flew in. He didn\u0027t even chew. He just stared at Pandora, his face turning a shade of red that matched the Gryffindor banners.","\u003cstrong\u003eA group of Ravenclaw fourth-years\u003c/strong\u003e began whispering frantically, one of them pulling out a quill to try and calculate the \u0026quot;Golden Ratio\u0026quot; of Cassie’s facial structure before his hand shook so hard he snapped the nib.","\u003cstrong\u003eCormac McLaggen\u003c/strong\u003e, usually the most arrogant boy in school, actually stood up, knocked over his goblet of pumpkin juice, and blurted out, \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I think I’ve forgotten how to blink!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e to no one in particular.","One Hufflepuff boy was heard whispering a frantic prayer to Merlin, while another tried to fix his tie and ended up accidentally choking himself, falling off the bench with a loud \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e that no one noticed because they were too busy staring.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Female Student Reactions:\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eRomilda Vane\u003c/strong\u003e and her circle of friends, who had spent the last three years being the \u0026quot;it-girls\u0026quot; of the hallway, looked as if they had been told the library was moving into their dorms. \u0026quot;It’s not fair,\u0026quot; Romilda hissed, clutching her fork like a dagger. \u0026quot;They were awkward! Cassie was just \u0027the ferret’s daughter\u0027! Now she looks like she owns the Ministry!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Greengrass sisters\u003c/strong\u003e at the Slytherin table traded looks of pure, unadulterated respect. \u0026quot;The Malfoy-Weasley merger,\u0026quot; Astoria whispered. \u0026quot;It’s not a scandal anymore. It’s an empire.\u0026quot;","Cassie and Pan reached the end of the hall, the clicking of Cassie’s boots and the soft whisper of Pan’s steps cutting through the whimpers of the male students. They didn\u0027t look at the tables. They didn\u0027t acknowledge the chaos.","They reached the two pillars of muscle that were James and Thomas. Cassie stepped to the right of Thomas, and Pan stepped to the left of James.","They turned as one to face the High Table—four fourteen-year-olds who stood between five-foot-ten and six-feet tall, looking like a phalanx of young deities.","\u003cstrong\u003eSeverus Snape\u003c/strong\u003e gripped the arms of his chair so hard the wood groaned. \u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; he hissed out of the side of his mouth. \u0026quot;Tell me I am hallucinating. Tell me the Potter boy hasn\u0027t brought a professional fashion troupe into my Great Hall.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I can\u0027t, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered, her glasses slipping down her nose. \u0026quot;Because I think the Potter boy is currently the shortest person in that line.\u0026quot;","The four of them stood in perfect formation, a wall of bronze skin, silver hair, and sheer, intimidating presence. The Great Hall held its breath, waiting for the final piece of the puzzle."]},{"num":55,"origNum":25,"title":"The Solar Eclipse","wordCount":847,"paragraphs":["The Great Hall had already endured a tectonic shift and a high-fashion siege, but the atmosphere wasn\u0027t finished collapsing. The four titans—James, Thomas, Cassie, and Pan—didn’t sit down at their house tables. They didn’t even move. They stood like a royal guard in a perfect line at the foot of the High Table, their eyes fixed on the open oak doors, waiting for the center of their universe to arrive.","Then, the light in the Hall didn\u0027t just flicker; it seemed to bow.","A fifth figure stepped out of the shadows of the Entrance Hall. If the others were the storm, this was the sun. \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter\u003c/strong\u003e walked into the Great Hall, and the enchanted ceiling above instantly dissolved its twilight clouds into a blinding, golden sunrise.","She was \u003cstrong\u003esix feet tall\u003c/strong\u003e.","The \u0026quot;baby\u0026quot; of the Pack, the girl who had spent thirteen years being the smallest, most delicate member of the Alliance, was now a towering celestial phenomenon. She wore a traveling coat of cream and gold that flared behind her, her mahogany-red hair—the exact shade of her grandmother Lily’s—cascading down her back in thick, glowing waves.","She didn\u0027t just walk; she radiated a hum of pure, concentrated happiness that was so physical it made the students in the front rows feel like they’d just swallowed a gallon of liquid sunshine. She was, quite simply, the most beautiful thing the castle had ever seen.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Student Body Meltdown (Atomic, Funny, and Chaotic):\u003c/strong\u003e","The reaction was no longer just shock; it was a total biological and mental reset for every student in the room.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Male Students:\u003c/strong\u003e The carnage was absolute.","\u003cstrong\u003eSeamus Finnigan\u003c/strong\u003e, who had been leaning forward to get a better look, simply slid off his bench and landed on the floor with a muffled \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e. He didn\u0027t even try to get up; he just stared at Lily from floor-level, whispering, \u0026quot;I think I see angels.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eCormac McLaggen\u003c/strong\u003e, usually the most arrogant boy in Gryffindor, stopped mid-chew. A piece of chicken fell out of his mouth and into his lap. He didn\u0027t notice. He just smoothed his hair with a trembling hand and looked like he was about to burst into a spontaneous poem.","\u003cstrong\u003eA group of Ravenclaw fifth-years\u003c/strong\u003e simultaneously dropped their spectacles into their pumpkin juice. One was heard muttering, \u0026quot;It’s statistically impossible... beauty doesn\u0027t have that many lumens... she\u0027s breaking the laws of optics!\u0026quot;","One Hufflepuff boy actually began to weep quietly, clutching his heart as if he’d just been hit by a very friendly, very beautiful Blasting Curse.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Female Students:\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eRomilda Vane\u003c/strong\u003e and her circle of friends looked as if they had been petrified by a Basilisk. Romilda’s fork was frozen halfway to her mouth. \u0026quot;That\u0027s not Lily,\u0026quot; she hissed, her voice trembling with a mixture of awe and pure, unadulterated envy. \u0026quot;Lily was \u003cem\u003etiny\u003c/em\u003e. That\u0027s... that\u0027s a goddess. How can she be six feet tall? I\u0027m calling my mother. I\u0027m calling the Ministry. This is cheating!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eAstoria Greengrass\u003c/strong\u003e at the Slytherin table simply leaned back and sighed. \u0026quot;Well,\u0026quot; she whispered to her sister Daphne. \u0026quot;I suppose we can all stop trying now. The Potter-Evans genes have officially won the century.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe High Table Reactions:\u003c/strong\u003e","The Professors sat in a row of stunned, wide-eyed silence.","\u003cstrong\u003eSeverus Snape\u003c/strong\u003e gripped the arms of his chair so hard the wood began to spiderweb. He stared at the six-foot-tall girl walking toward him—the girl with James’s height and Lily’s eyes—and felt his soul attempt to leave his body through his ears. \u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; he hissed, his voice trembling. \u0026quot;Tell me that is not the Potter girl. Tell me she hasn\u0027t reached the ceiling. If she grows another inch, I am retiring to a cave. I cannot teach a student I have to use a ladder to look at.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor McGonagall\u003c/strong\u003e had her spectacles in her hand and was rubbing them frantically, as if she could polish the reality away. \u0026quot;Six feet,\u0026quot; she whispered. \u0026quot;She’s six feet tall. I shall have to order new Quidditch robes... and possibly a taller broom.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore\u003c/strong\u003e was the only one smiling. He stood up, his sequins shimmering, and clapped his hands once. \u0026quot;Magnificent!\u0026quot; he beamed. \u0026quot;A solar event in the Great Hall! I believe the term the Muggles use is \u0027Supermodel,\u0027 though I suspect even that is a bit of an understatement!\u0026quot;","Lily reached the front of the hall. She didn\u0027t look at the staring students or the fainting boys. She walked straight to the line where her brothers and cousins waited.","James and Thomas stepped aside with synchronized, respectful precision, opening a gap in the very center. Lily stepped into it, completing the phalanx.","The Five—the \u003cstrong\u003eNew Pantheon\u003c/strong\u003e—stood in a perfect row: James and Thomas as the pillars of muscle, Cassie and Pan as the lethal sirens, and Lily—six feet of glowing mahogany and gold—at the heart.","Lily turned slightly, her radiant aura washing over the Hall, and looked up at the High Table with a calm, regal smile.","\u0026quot;The Pack is present and accounted for, Professors,\u0026quot; she said, her voice like a silver bell ringing through the silence."]},{"num":56,"origNum":26,"title":"The Faculty Meltdown","wordCount":889,"paragraphs":["The \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; stood in their silent, magnificent line, looking for all the world like they had been sent by the gods to audit Hogwarts for its lack of aesthetic perfection. At the High Table, the silence was so thick it felt like a \u003cem\u003eSilencio\u003c/em\u003e charm had been cast on the entire room—until the collective faculty brain finally experienced a total, atomic reboot.","\u003cstrong\u003eSeverus Snape\u003c/strong\u003e was the first to physically react. He didn\u0027t just stand; he recoiled. He gripped the arms of his ornate chair so hard that the century-old oak began to crack under the pressure. He stared at James Sirius—who was currently broader than most of the castle\u0027s doorways—and then at Lily Luna, whose radiant aura was currently acting like a second sun inside the hall.","\u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape hissed, his voice trembling with a mixture of professional insult and existential dread. \u0026quot;Tell me I am hallucinating. Tell me that the Potter boy hasn\u0027t returned as a six-foot-tall Greek titan. And tell me—I beg of you—that his sister hasn\u0027t reached the ceiling. I cannot teach a student I have to look up to. I will not. I am moving to a cave in Albania. I shall live among the bats. They, at least, have the decency to be small and dark!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor McGonagall\u003c/strong\u003e wasn\u0027t listening. She had her spectacles off and was rubbing them frantically with her napkin, as if she could polish the reality of the situation away. She looked at the five of them—their height, their poise, the sheer \u0026quot;Management\u0026quot; energy they were radiating—and felt a logistical migraine bloom behind her eyes.","\u0026quot;The Quidditch robes,\u0026quot; she whispered, her voice a horrified squeak. \u0026quot;I’ve already ordered the standard fourth-year sizes. I shall have to cancel the order. I shall have to order adult-sized dragon-hide reinforcements! And the hoops! James is so tall now he could probably just stand on the ground and dunk the Quaffle! It’s unsporting! It’s... it’s a vertical insurrection!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor Flitwick\u003c/strong\u003e had climbed onto his stack of books to get a better look, only to realize that even with the extra height, he was still looking at Lily Luna’s waistline. \u0026quot;Merlin’s beard!\u0026quot; he squeaked, his voice hitting a pitch that made the nearby crystal goblets ring. \u0026quot;The lumens! The magical output from the Potter girl is off the charts! She’s not just a student, she’s a localized power grid! I’ll have to rewrite the entire Charms curriculum! How am I supposed to teach \u0027Wingardium Leviosa\u0027 to a girl who looks like she’s already mastered the art of being celestial?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHagrid\u003c/strong\u003e let out a sob that sounded like a tectonic plate shifting. He blew his nose into a tablecloth-sized handkerchief, the sound echoing like a foghorn. \u0026quot;Look at \u0027em!\u0026quot; he wailed happily. \u0026quot;They’re like beautiful, giant Centaurs, but with two legs! James! Thomas! You’ve finally grown into those hands of yours! I’ve got some blast-ended skrewts that need movin\u0027, and I think you two could just pick \u0027em up by the tails!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor Sprout\u003c/strong\u003e was looking at Thomas Vernon with a clinical, wide-eyed amazement. \u0026quot;He’s a mountain,\u0026quot; she muttered, her hands twitching as if she wanted to pot him in a giant barrel. \u0026quot;He looks like he’s been fed on nothing but Dragon-Dung Compost and pure sunlight. I’ve seen Mandrakes with less structural density! How is a Dursley-Potter merger this... this solid?\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRemus Lupin\u003c/strong\u003e, who had been quietly trying to process the fact that James now looked exactly like a more muscular version of his father, James Sr., looked at Lily and then back at Snape. \u0026quot;Severus, calm down. It’s just puberty. A very... enthusiastic puberty.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;\u003cstrong\u003eEnthusiastic?\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026quot; Snape roared, finally standing up, his black robes billowing in a way that looked distinctly less intimidating next to James’s wingspan. \u0026quot;Lupin, the girl is six feet tall! She is radiating enough positive energy to make my Potion cauldrons start brewing tea and biscuits out of pure spite! I will not have it! I will be in my dungeon! If anyone needs me, I’ll be sitting in the dark and waiting for the world to make sense again!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore\u003c/strong\u003e, ever the agent of chaos, simply stood up and spread his arms wide, his Hawaiian shirt sequins catching Lily’s light and creating a disco-ball effect across the ceiling.","\u0026quot;Magnificent!\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed, his eyes twinkling so hard they were practically glowing. \u0026quot;A growth spurt for the ages! Ten thousand points to Gryffindor, Slytherin, and Ravenclaw for sheer vertical excellence! I believe we shall have to raise the height of the Great Hall tables, or perhaps just give the Pack their own VIP section. Now, if you would be so kind as to sit down—if your new legs can fit under the benches—I believe we have a feast to attend to!\u0026quot;","The Pack shared a synchronized, knowing look. Lily smiled, the aura of \u0026quot;The Light\u0026quot; intensifying for a brief, mischievous second, before the five of them turned and walked toward their respective house tables.","Behind them, the Professors remained in a row of stunned, wide-eyed silence. Snape was still clutching his wine, McGonagall was still rubbing her glasses, and the student body was still trying to remember how to blink.","The Fourth Year had officially begun, and it was already clear: Hogwarts wasn\u0027t just a school anymore. It was a kingdom, and the Pantheon had just arrived to take the throne."]},{"num":57,"origNum":27,"title":"The Seating of the Pantheon","wordCount":920,"paragraphs":["The \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; had finished their performance at the foot of the High Table. With a synchronized nod that suggested they had rehearsed their departure as much as their arrival, the formation broke. They turned and began to walk toward their respective House tables, and the Great Hall descended into a new, more localized brand of pandemonium.","\u003cstrong\u003eSlytherin Table: The Return of the Queen\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eCassie Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e didn’t just walk to the Slytherin table; she reclaimed it. As she approached the green-and-silver banners, the younger years scrambled over one another to make room, nearly falling off their benches in their haste to vacate the prime middle seating.","The reaction was a mix of pure reverence and soul-deep intimidation. A group of sixth-year boys, who had previously been the \u0026quot;lords of the table,\u0026quot; suddenly looked like they were trying to hide behind their napkins.","\u0026quot;She’s wearing dragon-hide boots,\u0026quot; one girl whispered, her voice trembling with envy. \u0026quot;And did you see that look? That’s not just a Malfoy sneer; that’s a \u0027Management\u0027 sneer. She looks like she could fire the entire House by Tuesday.\u0026quot;","Cassie sat down, smoothed her obsidian traveling robes, and looked at a nearby plate of silver service. The nearest third-year immediately pushed the entire tray of smoked salmon toward her as if his life depended on it. Cassie didn\u0027t say a word; she just raised a perfectly arched eyebrow, and the boy looked like he might actually faint from the sheer honor of her presence.","\u003cstrong\u003eHufflepuff Table: The Ethereal Invasion\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003ePandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e drifted toward the Hufflepuff table, her strawberry-blonde hair glowing with a faint lavender shimmer. The Hufflepuffs, usually the most welcoming House, were currently frozen in a state of bewildered adoration.","As Pan sat down, she didn’t just sit; she seemed to settle into the space like a mist.","\u0026quot;Oh, hello,\u0026quot; she said to a group of gasping fourth-years. \u0026quot;The badgers under the floorboards told me there would be lemon tart tonight. I hope they’re right; the moon is very hungry.\u0026quot;","One boy, who had been holding a jug of pumpkin juice, was so mesmerized by the way Pan’s eyes seemed to contain actual starlight that he didn\u0027t notice he was pouring the juice directly into his own lap. He didn\u0027t even flinch at the cold. He just stared.","\u0026quot;She’s... she’s glowing,\u0026quot; a girl whispered, clutching her yellow tie. \u0026quot;Is she allowed to be that beautiful? Is it a Hufflepuff rule? I feel like I should be bowing or offering her my soul.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eRavenclaw Table: The Warrior-Scholar\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cstrong\u003eThomas Vernon Dursley\u003c/strong\u003e walked toward the Ravenclaw table, and for a second, the students there genuinely worried about the structural integrity of the furniture. Thomas was a six-foot-tall mountain of muscle, but he carried a stack of advanced Technomancy journals under one arm that suggested his brain was just as lethal as his biceps.","As he sat, the heavy oak bench let out a distinct creak of protest. The Ravenclaws, usually busy discussing arithmancy, were silent.","\u0026quot;Thomas?\u0026quot; a Prefect managed to squeak. \u0026quot;You... you’ve grown. Architecturally.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Optimized,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled, his deep voice making the salt shakers on the table rattle. \u0026quot;I found that the previous skeletal frame was inefficient for high-output magical channeling. I’ve made adjustments.\u0026quot;","A group of Ravenclaw girls were staring at the way his dress shirt was practically pleading for mercy across his shoulders. One girl was frantically scribbling in her notebook, trying to calculate the force of his grip strength, while another just stared at his jawline as if it were a particularly complex and beautiful geometric proof.","\u003cstrong\u003eGryffindor Table: The Twin Suns\u003c/strong\u003e","But the true atomic epicenter was the Gryffindor table. \u003cstrong\u003eJames Sirius\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna\u003c/strong\u003e walked toward the red-and-gold banners, and the House of the Brave suddenly lost its collective mind.","James led the way, his six-foot athletic frame vibrating with enough Potter-energy to light up the Forbidden Forest. He slammed a hand onto the table in greeting, and three pitchers of milk nearly jumped out of their skins.","\u0026quot;WE’RE BACK!\u0026quot; James roared, his grin flashing like a lightning strike.","The Gryffindor Quidditch team looked as if they had just seen a vision of a championship trophy. The Chasers were staring at James’s wingspan with predatory joy, while the rest of the table—particularly the girls—were experiencing a mass fainting spell.","However, the real shock was Lily. As she sat down next to James, her six-foot stature made her the tallest person at the table by a significant margin. She sat with a grace that made the wooden bench look like a throne, her mahogany hair catching the torchlight.","\u0026quot;Lily?\u0026quot; a third-year girl whispered, looking up—way up—at her. \u0026quot;You... you were my height last term. We were both small.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The island was very sunny,\u0026quot; Lily smiled, and the radiant aura of \u0027The Light\u0027 washed over the table so strongly that three boys in the immediate vicinity fell backward off their seats as if they’d been hit by a wave of pure happiness.","\u0026quot;She’s a giant!\u0026quot; one boy yelled from the end of the table, his eyes wide. \u0026quot;A beautiful, mahogany-haired giant! James, how are we supposed to play Quidditch against her? She can just reach up and grab the Snitch while standing on the ground!\u0026quot;","The Great Hall was a cacophony of dropped cutlery, frantic whispering, and the sound of teenage hearts breaking and reforming in the span of a single breath. The Pack had officially integrated, and as they reached for their golden plates, it was clear that the seating arrangements of Hogwarts had changed forever."]},{"num":58,"origNum":28,"title":"The Great Heart-Obliteration","wordCount":1165,"paragraphs":["The Great Hall was already a disaster zone of dropped forks and stunned silence, but as the feast truly began, the \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; didn\u0027t just eat; they engaged. Having spent the summer under the tutelage of the \u0026quot;Hurricane\u0026quot; (Ginny and Draco) and the \u0026quot;Logical Cozy\u0026quot; (Harry and Hermione), they possessed a natural, devastating charisma that they were now deploying with the casualness of someone passing the salt.","\u003cstrong\u003eSlytherin: The Malfoy Precision\u003c/strong\u003e","Cassie Malfoy sat amidst the silver and green, her obsidian robes rustling like a warning. Across from her sat a fifth-year boy named Adrian Pucey Jr., who had spent the last three years convinced he was the most handsome boy in his year.","Cassie reached for a crystal carafe of water, her fingers grazing Adrian’s hand for a split second. She didn\u0027t pull away immediately. Instead, she leaned in, her silver-blonde braid sliding over her shoulder.","\u0026quot;Adrian,\u0026quot; she murmured, her voice a cool, silken drawl that could have frozen a volcano. \u0026quot;You’re staring at my plate. If you wanted the dragon-tartare, you only had to ask. I don\u0027t bite... unless the Management authorizes it.\u0026quot;","She finished with a slow, razor-sharp Malfoy smirk and a single, deliberate wink.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction:\u003c/strong\u003e Adrian didn\u0027t just blush; he underwent a total physical transformation. His face turned a shade of purple that matched Vernon Dursley’s best rages. He tried to say \u0026quot;thank you,\u0026quot; but his vocal cords had evidently petrified. He made a sound like a choking Kneazle, accidentally knocked over his entire goblet of pumpkin juice into his lap, and then proceeded to stare at his napkin as if it were a Portkey that might save him. The Slytherins around him scrambled backward, terrified that the \u0026quot;Malfoy Lethality\u0026quot; was contagious.","\u003cstrong\u003eHufflepuff: The Dreamy Devastation\u003c/strong\u003e","Pandora Weasley was currently looking at a third-year boy named Cedric Diggory’s cousin, Toby. Toby was a sweet boy who liked Herbology and had never seen a girl who glowed with a literal lavender aura.","Pan tilted her head, her strawberry-blonde hair shimmering. She reached out and gently straightened Toby’s yellow-and-black tie, her fingers lingering near his collar.","\u0026quot;Toby,\u0026quot; she whispered, her eyes wide and misty. \u0026quot;The Nargles told me you have a very kind heart. And your aura... it tastes like cinnamon and summer rain today. It’s very... distracting.\u0026quot;","She leaned closer, inhaling softly as if catching his scent, before giving him a small, ethereal smile.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction:\u003c/strong\u003e Toby’s brain experienced a total catastrophic failure. He let out a soft, high-pitched \u003cem\u003e“eep!”\u003c/em\u003e and his eyes rolled back slightly. He attempted to butter a roll but was so mesmerized by Pan’s lavender light that he buttered his own thumb instead. When he finally realized it, he didn\u0027t stop—he just kept buttering his hand, nodding rhythmically while whispering, \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Cinnamon... rain... I am a moon-calf.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e The Hufflepuffs next to him had to physically hold him upright so he didn\u0027t slide under the table.","\u003cstrong\u003eRavenclaw: The Technical Knockout\u003c/strong\u003e","Thomas Vernon Dursley was focused on a Ravenclaw girl named Cho Chang’s niece, Mei. Mei was a brilliant arithmancer who prided herself on being unaffected by \u0026quot;jock\u0026quot; energy.","Thomas, whose shoulders were currently taking up the space of two regular humans, looked at the complex star-chart Mei was doodling on her napkin. He reached over, his massive, tanned hand covering her drawing as he pointed to a calculation.","\u0026quot;You’ve miscalculated the lunar trajectory for the Technomancy bridge,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled, his deep bass voice vibrating through the wooden table and, more importantly, through Mei’s chest. He leaned in so close his shoulder brushed hers. \u0026quot;But your logic is beautiful. Almost as efficient as your eyes.\u0026quot;","He looked at her with a steady, intense Dursley focus that was as unmovable as a mountain.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction:\u003c/strong\u003e Mei, a girl who lived for logic, found her internal circuitry fried. Her quill snapped in half. She tried to explain the arithmancy, but her tongue felt like a piece of dry parchment. She let out a squeak, her face turning a deep, scientific crimson, and then she buried her face into her textbook, literally trying to merge with the pages of \u003cem\u003eAdvanced Rune Calculations\u003c/em\u003e. Thomas just blinked, reached for a steak, and continued to eat as if he hadn\u0027t just committed a verbal homicide.","\u003cstrong\u003eGryffindor: The Double-Potter Pulsation\u003c/strong\u003e","The Gryffindor table was the center of the atomic blast. James and Lily were working in synchronized harmony.","\u003cstrong\u003eJames\u003c/strong\u003e turned to a sixth-year girl named Sarah, who had once called him \u0026quot;the vibrating toddler.\u0026quot; He leaned back, his white shirt straining, and ran a hand through his messy black hair.","\u0026quot;Hey, Sarah,\u0026quot; he said, his voice dropping into that rich, Potter baritone. He gave her a crooked, heart-melting grin. \u0026quot;I noticed you’re wearing the Gryffindor lion earrings I mentioned in second year. They look... better than I imagined. You should wear them when I’m playing Seeker. I’ll need something bright to look at while I’m catching the Snitch.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction:\u003c/strong\u003e Sarah’s jaw hit the table. She tried to toss her hair back, but she was trembling so much she accidentally swiped her own ear and knocked the earring into her soup. She didn\u0027t care. She just stared at James, her eyes glazing over, and whispered, \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;I’ll wear the earrings. I’ll wear the lion. I’ll wear the whole house, James.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","Meanwhile, \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna\u003c/strong\u003e—the six-foot-tall sun—turned to a boy named Leo, who was a fourth-year and currently looked like he was about to pass out just from the proximity to her aura.","Lily reached over and tucked a stray hair behind Leo’s ear, her touch leaving a literal trail of warmth on his skin. She looked into his eyes with the \u0026quot;Potter-Evans\u0026quot; emerald gaze.","\u0026quot;Leo,\u0026quot; she said, her voice like a silver chime. \u0026quot;You look so nervous. Are the candles too bright? Or is it me? Because I can dim my Light if it helps you breathe... but I’d rather you just look at me.\u0026quot;","She gave him a soft, radiant smile that felt like being wrapped in a warm blanket of pure joy.","\u003cstrong\u003eThe Reaction:\u003c/strong\u003e Leo didn\u0027t answer. He couldn\u0027t. He experienced what Ron would later call \u0026quot;The Full Lily Collapse.\u0026quot; His eyes went wide, he let out a strangled sob of pure adoration, and he simply fell backward off the bench, landing on the floor with his legs kicking in the air. He didn\u0027t even try to get up. He just lay there on the stone floor, staring at the ceiling and muttering, \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;The Light... she called me Leo... I am deceased.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e","Across the hall, the Professors watched as, one by one, the student body succumbed to the \u0026quot;Pack’s\u0026quot; effortless charm.","\u003cstrong\u003eSeverus Snape\u003c/strong\u003e closed his eyes and massaged his temples. \u0026quot;Potter,\u0026quot; he whispered to the empty air. \u0026quot;Your children are not students. They are biological weapons of mass seduction. I am calling the Ministry. This is a public health crisis.\u0026quot;","The Pack, meanwhile, just continued their dinner, sharing a knowing, synchronized glance. The summer lessons in \u0026quot;The Hurricane\u0026quot; and \u0026quot;The Ostrich\u0026quot; had paid off. The throne was theirs."]},{"num":59,"origNum":29,"title":"The Faculty Medical Emergency","wordCount":806,"paragraphs":["At the High Table, the feast had transitioned from a meal into a full-scale observation of a natural disaster. The Professors weren\u0027t eating; they were clutching their golden goblets with white-knuckled grips, watching as the \u0026quot;Pack\u0026quot; dismantled the student body’s composure with the casual ease of people peeling oranges.","\u003cstrong\u003eSeverus Snape\u003c/strong\u003e was currently experiencing what he internally called \u0026quot;The Malfoy-Potter Singularity.\u0026quot; He had just witnessed \u003cstrong\u003eCassie Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e wink at Adrian Pucey Jr., causing the boy to dump an entire pitcher of pumpkin juice into his own lap and then thank her for the privilege.","\u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape hissed, his voice reaching a frequency that only bats and particularly anxious House Elves could hear. \u0026quot;I am placing Slytherin House under a mandatory quarantine. The Malfoy girl is not a student; she is a biological weapon of mass seduction. I have just seen a Pucey—a boy whose family has a history of stoicism dating back to the Norman Conquest—attempt to apologize to a bread roll because she looked at him.\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor McGonagall\u003c/strong\u003e didn\u0027t answer because she was currently standing up, her hand over her mouth as she watched the Gryffindor table. At that exact moment, \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna\u003c/strong\u003e had reached out to tuck the hair behind Leo’s ear, and Leo had promptly slid off the bench like a stick of butter on a hot skillet.","\u0026quot;He’s down,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered, her voice trembling. \u0026quot;That’s the fourth one, Albus. Four boys in ten minutes. I’m going to have to call Poppy Pomfrey. We don\u0027t have enough Hospital Wing beds if the Potter girl continues to... to \u003cem\u003ebe\u003c/em\u003e like that. And James! James just told a girl she looked like a Snitch, and I believe she is currently trying to climb onto the table to fly! It’s anarchy! It’s vertical, charismatic anarchy!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor Flitwick\u003c/strong\u003e, who was still standing on his stack of books, was waving a frantic hand in the air. \u0026quot;Did you see the Hufflepuff table? The Weasley girl—Pandora—is radiating so much \u0027Light\u0027 that the candles are actually leaning toward her! And Toby Diggory is currently buttering his own wrist! His wrist, Minerva! The magical output of their collective flirtation is creating a localized high-pressure system! I can feel the atmospheric change from here!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eHagrid\u003c/strong\u003e let out a booming, watery chuckle that rattled the silverware. \u0026quot;They’re just findin\u0027 their feet, Professors! Though I reckon James\u0027s feet are about a size fourteen now. Look at \u0027em! It’s like watchin\u0027 young unicorns playin\u0027 in the forest... \u0027cept these unicorns have Malfoy bank accounts and Potter\u0027s luck. They\u0027re magnificent!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eProfessor Sprout\u003c/strong\u003e was looking at \u003cstrong\u003eThomas Vernon\u003c/strong\u003e with a mix of fear and horticultural respect. \u0026quot;He just told Mei her logic was beautiful. She’s currently trying to hide inside her Arithmancy textbook. I’ve seen Devil’s Snare retreat from light faster than that girl just retreated from that boy’s jawline. He’s too solid! He’s too... \u003cem\u003estructural\u003c/em\u003e! It’s not fair to the other Ravenclaws!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eAlbus Dumbledore\u003c/strong\u003e, meanwhile, had summoned a small, enchanted pair of binoculars from his sequined sleeve. He was leaning forward, delightedly watching the carnage.","\u0026quot;Oh, look!\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed, his Hawaiian shirt sequins flashing like a lighthouse. \u0026quot;Cassie has just made a seventh-year Prefect forget his own middle name! And Lily... oh, well done, Lily! She’s managed to make the Gryffindor Ghost, Sir Nicholas, blush. I didn\u0027t even think that was spiritually possible!\u0026quot;","\u003cstrong\u003eSnape\u003c/strong\u003e slammed his goblet onto the table. \u0026quot;Dumbledore, stop narrating the end of Western Civilization! The Potter boy is currently running his hand through his hair, and I can hear the girls in the first three rows vibrating! It’s a sonic hazard! I am leaving. I am going to my dungeon, I am locking the door, and I am brewing a Potion that induces temporary blindness and a total loss of romantic interest!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Now, now, Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled, lowering his binoculars. \u0026quot;You can’t brew your way out of puberty. Especially not when it hits with the force of a Malfoy-Dursley-Potter meteor. I believe the term the Muggles use is \u0027The Glow-Up.\u0027 Though in this case, I think it’s more of a \u0027The Blow-Up.\u0027 They’ve blown up the social order of Hogwarts in twenty minutes.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I’m doubling the duty of the Prefects,\u0026quot; McGonagall announced, her face set in a mask of professional terror. \u0026quot;No, wait. The Prefects are currently the ones fainting. I’m doubling the duty of the House Ghosts! They\u0027re the only ones who can\u0027t be affected by... by whatever \u0027Light\u0027 Lily Luna is emitting!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Actually, Minerva,\u0026quot; Flitwick squeaked, pointing toward the Gryffindor table. \u0026quot;The Fat Friar is currently trying to offer Pandora his dessert, and he’s been dead for six hundred years.\u0026quot;","The Faculty of Hogwarts sat in a row of stunned, wide-eyed defeat. They were the most powerful witches and wizards in the country, and they were currently being held hostage by five fourteen-year-olds who were merely being \u0026quot;polite\u0026quot; over dinner."]},{"num":60,"origNum":30,"title":"The Northern Front and the Double Faceplant","wordCount":1791,"paragraphs":["The Great Hall had barely begun to stabilize its atmospheric pressure following what Severus Snape was already documenting in his personal journal as \u0026quot;The Calamity of the Fourteen-Year-Olds.\u0026quot;","At the High Table, the Faculty was still in various stages of triage. Professor McGonagall was drinking iced pumpkin juice as if it were medicinal tonic, her lips pressed into a thin, white line. Professor Flitwick was busy casting localized calming draught charms over the Hufflepuff table, where Toby Diggory was still staring dreamily at his buttered wrist. And Snape sat with his quill poised menacingly over a roll of parchment, his dark eyes darting between the Gryffindor and Slytherin tables, drafting what looked suspiciously like an emergency restraining order against the entire Potter-Malfoy bloodline.","Only Albus Dumbledore remained entirely unbothered. His sequined Hawaiian-print outer robes caught the candlelight in a dazzling spray of magenta and neon green as he stood up, tapping the side of his goblet with a silver spoon.","\u003cem\u003eTing. Ting. Ting.\u003c/em\u003e","The sound echoed through the cavernous hall, cutting cleanly through the frantic teenage whispering and the occasional dazed sigh of a student who had made eye contact with Lily Luna.","\u0026quot;Quiet, please,\u0026quot; Dumbledore’s voice rolled across the room, warm and resonant. \u0026quot;Thank you. Now that our bellies are full—and our cardiovascular systems tested by the vigor of youth—it is time for a few start-of-term notices.\u0026quot;","He paused, his eyes twinkling brightly behind his half-moon spectacles.","\u0026quot;First, the caretaker, Mr. Filch, has asked me to remind you that Fanged Frisbees, Screaming Yo-yos, and any self-assembling Muggle electronics engineered by certain Ravenclaw second-cousins are strictly prohibited in the corridors.\u0026quot; Dumbledore directed a mild, benevolent glance toward Thomas Vernon Dursley, who sat unmoving at the Ravenclaw table, his expression completely blank, though his pocket gave off a faint, rhythmic electronic hum.","\u0026quot;Furthermore,\u0026quot; Dumbledore continued, his smile broadening, \u0026quot;it is my supreme honor to announce that Hogwarts has been chosen to host a legendary event this year. An event steeped in centuries of magical history, valor, and international camaraderie.\u0026quot;","A murmur rippled through the hall.","\u0026quot;Beginning this October, Hogwarts will play host to the Triwizard Tournament!\u0026quot;","The hall went dead silent for a single, stunned second, and then erupted.","\u0026quot;The Triwizard?!\u0026quot; Sarah shrieked from the Gryffindor table, momentarily forgetting her lost earring.","\u0026quot;Are you insane?\u0026quot; Hermione Granger\u0027s historical outrage seemed to echo spiritually through the stone walls, channeled instantly through her daughter. At the Gryffindor table, Lily Luna’s eyes widened in mild alarm, while across the room at the Ravenclaw table, Thomas Vernon immediately pulled out a brass caliper and a leather-bound ledger, already calculating the structural mortality rates of medieval arena games.","\u0026quot;Splendid,\u0026quot; Snape muttered aloud, his voice dripping with arsenic. \u0026quot;As if five feral teenagers weren\u0027t sufficient, we are now inviting foreign delegations to assist in the total destruction of my sanity.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Silence, please!\u0026quot; Dumbledore called out, raising both hands. The sequins on his sleeves flashed like emergency road flares. \u0026quot;The Tournament will see the selection of three champions—one from each school—to compete for the Triwizard Cup, eternal glory, and a personal cash prize of one thousand Galleons.\u0026quot;","Before the student body could fully process the prospect of international dueling and unmonitored dangerous beasts, Dumbledore gestured with a theatrical flourish toward the heavy oak doors at the back of the Great Hall.","\u0026quot;And now, please join me in extending a warm, Hogwarts welcome to our esteemed guests from the far north... the delegation of the Durmstrang Institute!\u0026quot;","The great double doors swung open with a resounding, thunderous boom.","A freezing draft of mountain air swept through the hall, carrying with it the sharp scent of pine needles, frost, and cured leather.","Into the hall marched the Durmstrang contingent.","They did not simply walk; they advanced with the unified, terrifying discipline of an elite military unit. Every student was dressed in heavy, blood-red robes trimmed with thick, dark manticore fur. On their feet were polished black boots that hit the flagstones in a synchronized, bone-rattling cadence.","\u003cem\u003eTHUMP. THUMP. THUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","Each student carried a tall, polished walking staff of carved ash. At every fourth stride, they slammed the butts of their staves into the stone floor in perfect unison.","\u003cem\u003eCLACK.\u003c/em\u003e","Sparks of silver and blue fire sprayed outward across the floor, sizzling in the air as two students in the front row launched into an explosive series of mid-air flips, landing in rigid, low crouches before rising without so much as a ruffle to their cloaks. The display of physical power and absolute northern stoicism had half the hall holding its breath.","And then, walking at the rear of the formation, came the leadership.","Walking with a heavy, deliberate gait that commanded instant respect was the Headmaster of Durmstrang: \u003cstrong\u003eViktor Krum\u003c/strong\u003e.","He was broader now than during his Quidditch days, his hair cropped close with flecks of silver at the temples, wearing high-collared black fur and leaning on an iron-tipped dragon-horn cane. The sharp, predatory hunch that had once terrified opposing Seekers had matured into pure, immovable northern authority.","But it was not Viktor Krum that stopped the hearts of the Gryffindor table.","Walking directly beside him was his daughter.","\u003cstrong\u003eValeria Krum\u003c/strong\u003e.","She was fourteen, but she possessed an icy, lethal poise that belonged on the deck of a Viking warship. Her raven-black hair was woven into an intricate, severe northern braid that hung down her back, fastened with silver clasps. Her cheekbones looked sharp enough to slice glass, and her eyes—a striking, stormy hazel-gold—scanned the Great Hall with the quiet, predatory focus of a Seeker surveying an open pitch. Over her tailored, charcoal-grey combat robes, she wore a short, fitted cloak of midnight-black snow-fox fur that swirled around her boots with every stride.","She walked like she owned the winter itself.","At the Gryffindor table, James Sirius Potter had been leaning back against the bench, radiating the absolute peak of post-dinner arrogance. His white shirt collar was casually unbuttoned, his messy black hair looked artfully chaotic, and he was basking in the residual glow of having reduced three girls to quivering puddles twenty minutes prior.","He had one eyebrow cocked, an easy, insolent Potter smirk curling his lips as he prepared to watch the northern \u0026quot;show-offs\u0026quot; march past.","Then Valeria Krum walked into his line of sight.","James’s eyes locked onto her.","And in that exact microsecond, every single system in James Sirius Potter’s brain experienced an immediate, catastrophic, blue-screen shutdown.","The smirk didn\u0027t just fade; it disintegrated. His chin dropped so hard and fast his jaw audibly clicked. The famous Potter kinetic vibration—the constant hum of energy that made him blur around the edges—stopped dead, freezing him in place like a statue carved from Surrey granite. His hazel-brown eyes dilated until they were practically black, staring at her with the unblinking, helpless terror of a rabbit that had just made eye contact with a golden eagle.","He forgot to breathe. He forgot to blink. He appeared to forget his own middle name.","Sitting two feet away, Lily Luna Potter glanced at her brother.","Her emerald eyes widened. She tracked his gaze, looked at Valeria Krum, and looked back at James’s slack-jawed, hypnotized face.","Down at the Slytherin table, Cassiopeia Malfoy had already caught the sudden shift in atmospheric gravity. Her silver eyes darted from Valeria’s sharp profile straight across to James, seeing the absolute, drooling ruins of his dignity.","Over at the Hufflepuff table, Pandora Weasley tilted her head, her misty eyes snapping into terrifyingly sharp focus. \u0026quot;Oh dear,\u0026quot; Pan murmured to the empty air. \u0026quot;The peacock just flew directly into a windmill.\u0026quot;","In that split second, the three girls shared a single, telepathic, horrifying realization: \u003cem\u003eThe cocky idiot is in love.\u003c/em\u003e","And then, in complete, synchronized horror:","\u003cstrong\u003eTHUD.\u003c/strong\u003e","Lily Luna folded her arms and dropped her face directly onto the Gryffindor table with enough force to rattle a basket of dinner rolls.","\u003cstrong\u003eTHUD.\u003c/strong\u003e","Cassie Malfoy dropped her forehead straight down onto the polished oak of the Slytherin table, burying her face in her hands with a muffled, aristocratic groan.","\u003cstrong\u003eCLATTER-THUMP.\u003c/strong\u003e","Pandora Weasley let her head drop straight forward onto her empty porcelain dessert plate at the Hufflepuff table, not even bothering to cushion the blow.","Across three separate house tables, the girls stayed faceplanted, their shoulders trembling in unified second-hand agony.","Meanwhile, Valeria Krum continued her measured, disciplined march toward the High Table. Her gaze was locked firmly ahead, ignoring the gasps and whispers of the British students with practiced northern indifference.","Except, as she drew level with the middle of the Gryffindor table, the sheer, burning intensity of James’s unblinking stare hit her like a physical wave of heat.","Valeria’s eyes flicked to the left.","She looked at James.","He was still frozen, his mouth slightly open, his chest barely moving, staring at her with an expression of pure, unadulterated, worshipping idiocy.","Valeria met his gaze for less than half a second.","Her hazel-gold eyes widened by a single millimeter.","And in that infinitesimal moment of distraction, the toe of her heavy combat boot clipped the uneven seam of an ancient stone flagstone.","Valeria Krum faltered.","Her left knee buckled by two inches. Her shoulder dipped. Her midnight-fur cloak swirled wildly as her balance slipped.","It was barely a stumble—a millisecond glitch in an otherwise flawless military parade. With lightning-fast Seeker reflexes, she recovered instantly, shifting her weight, squaring her broad, athletic shoulders, and snapping her chin back up. Her expression snapped back into icy, unyielding stone as she resumed her march toward Dumbledore, staring rigidly ahead as if the floor had merely offended her.","At the Gryffindor, Slytherin, and Hufflepuff tables, three pairs of eyes peeked up from their respective surfaces.","Lily, Cassie, and Pan saw the stumble.","They saw the micro-second hitch in the Seeker\u0027s stride.","They saw the faint, telltale flare of pink that dusted the high cheekbone of Viktor Krum’s daughter before she vanished into the crowd of northern fur.","Slowly, the three girls turned their heads toward each other across the Great Hall.","Their eyes met in a triangle of sheer, unadulterated panic.","\u003cem\u003eIt was mutual.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThe northern glacier had just melted.\u003c/em\u003e","And without a single word, in horrifying, synchronized dread:","\u003cstrong\u003eTHUMP.\u003c/strong\u003e","Lily slammed her forehead back down onto the Gryffindor table.","\u003cstrong\u003eTHUMP.\u003c/strong\u003e","Cassie hammered her face back into the Slytherin wood so hard her silver goblet jumped two inches into the air.","\u003cstrong\u003eCLANG.\u003c/strong\u003e","Pandora faceplanted straight back into her porcelain plate, letting out a long, wheezing squeak of despair.","Over at the Ravenclaw table, Thomas Vernon Dursley did not faceplant. He merely removed his steel-rimmed glasses, massaged the bridge of his nose, and let out a heavy, world-weary bass sigh.","\u0026quot;Structural failure imminent,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled into his collar. \u0026quot;God help the castle.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":61,"origNum":31,"title":"The Silk Storm and the Technomancer","wordCount":1464,"paragraphs":["Before the Great Hall could even begin to process the fact that Viktor Krum was scowling at the High Table, that Durmstrang was occupying the Slytherin benches, or that James Sirius Potter was still sitting with his mouth open like a broken mail slot, Albus Dumbledore clapped his hands once more.","\u0026quot;And now,\u0026quot; the Headmaster’s voice boomed cheerfully, the magenta sequins on his chest flashing in the candlelight, \u0026quot;let us welcome the radiant students of the Beauxbatons Academy of Magic, led by their esteemed Headmistress, Madame Maxime!\u0026quot;","The doors swung open again.","If Durmstrang had brought a blizzard, Beauxbatons brought spring in full, perfumed revolt.","A flock of shimmering, conjured silver butterflies fluttered into the Great Hall, scattering pastel sparkles across the tables. Following closely behind was a delegation of French students dressed in robes of fine, gossamer-thin powder-blue silk. They glided down the aisle not with boots and thumping staves, but with an ethereal, weightless grace that made them look as though they were drifting across water.","And they were, without exception, breathtaking.","\u0026quot;Bloody hell,\u0026quot; Ron Weasley’s ancestral voice seemed to whisper through the hall as half the male population of Hogwarts simultaneously forgot how to inhale.","Boys leaned so far over their tables to get a view that several goblets of gravy were tipped into adjacent laps. At the Hufflepuff table, a fifth-year boy attempted to smoothly rest his chin in his hand, missed entirely, and faceplanted into a bowl of mashed potatoes. At the Gryffindor table, boys were craning their necks so violently that Poppy Pomfrey in the corner was already reaching for muscle-relaxing salves.","Then came the rear of the procession.","If the girls in the front were stunning, the girl walking at the very end of the line was a localized magical phenomenon.","Her name was \u003cstrong\u003eCéleste Laurent\u003c/strong\u003e.","She was a pure-blooded Veela, and unlike part-Veelas whose magic was diluted into mere charm, Céleste radiated the ancient, undiluted glamour of the French Pyrenees. Her hair was a cascading waterfall of pure, liquid silver that shimmered with an inner moonlight, spilling past her waist in gossamer waves. Her eyes were deep, luminescent violets that seemed to hold the dusk sky, and her skin possessed the flawless, luminous sheen of freshly carved mother-of-pearl.","She didn\u0027t merely walk; she floated, an aura of intoxicating warmth, floral honey, and summer breezes trailing behind her in a tangible wake. In terms of sheer, devastating physical presence, she was the first girl to enter Hogwarts in a century who could genuinely rival the peerless triumvirate of Cassie Malfoy, Pandora Weasley, and Lily Luna Potter.","The effect on the hall was immediate, catastrophic, and completely undignified.","\u0026quot;Gah!\u0026quot; a Ravenclaw sixth-year croaked, his eyes bulging as he knocked his inkpot onto his bread roll.","\u0026quot;Marry me,\u0026quot; a boy at the Gryffindor table whined into his napkin, having completely forgotten his own house allegiance.","Two Slytherin fifth-years stood up simultaneously to offer her their seats, bumped heads with a hollow \u003cem\u003eCLONK\u003c/em\u003e, and tumbled backward over their bench in a heap of tangled green robes. Adrian Pucey Jr.—having barely survived Cassie’s lethal wink earlier—took one look at Céleste, closed his eyes, and simply slid underneath the Slytherin table, deciding that consciousness was an unnecessary liability for the rest of the evening.","Céleste smiled faintly, a serene, practiced expression. She was accustomed to this. Men were fragile, predictable creatures whose brains reliably melted into warm custard the moment she walked into an enclosed space. It was mildly flattering, occasionally useful, but mostly very boring.","Except as her violet gaze drifted across the tables, looking for a place to sit, she noticed an anomaly.","A statistical impossibility.","At the Ravenclaw table sat a boy.","He was broad-shouldered—built with the heavy, unshakeable solidity of an oak wardrobe—wearing crisp, perfectly ironed school robes. But unlike every other male in a fifty-yard radius, who was either drooling, choking on pumpkin juice, or pledging their family vaults to her, this boy was not looking at her.","He was not looking at anyone.","Thomas Vernon Dursley had a small, velvet-lined tool kit rolled out neatly beside his plate. In his large, steady hands, he was holding a miniature brass chronometer-regulator, using a precision micro-screwdriver the width of an eyelash to tighten a microscopic gear. A tiny, enchanted soldering stylus sat in a heat-proof ceramic stand next to his mashed peas, emitting a thin wisp of lavender smoke.","Céleste paused.","She turned her head. She released a subtle, concentrated pulse of pure Veela allure—the kind of invisible pheromonal wave that had brought French duelists to their knees in dueling pits.","The air around Thomas’s table shimmered faintly with lilac light.","Thomas didn\u0027t flinch. His hand didn\u0027t tremble. He simply adjusted the magnification lens attached to his steel-rimmed spectacles, gave the tiny screw a quarter-turn clockwise, and blew a speck of brass dust off the motherboard.","Céleste’s violet eyes widened in sheer, baffled curiosity.","\u003cem\u003eWho is this creature? Is he deaf? Is he carved out of Surrey sandstone?\u003c/em\u003e","Gliding forward with fluid grace, her powder-blue silk robes whispering against the flagstones, Céleste Laurent approached the Ravenclaw table. She stopped directly beside Thomas, the intoxicating scent of jasmine and enchanted honeysuckle enveloping his space.","She tilted her head, giving him an exquisite, dazzling smile that would have induced heart failure in the Minister of Magic.","\u0026quot;Pardon,\u0026quot; Céleste purred in a silken, honeyed French accent that made three nearby Ravenclaws fall off their stools. \u0026quot;Ze table is very crowded... may I sit beside you?\u0026quot;","Every boy at the table held his breath, expecting Thomas to stammer, explode into tears of joy, or throw his school robes at her feet like a carpet.","Thomas Vernon Dursley did not look up.","He did not raise his chin.","He did not even shift his eyes away from the micro-capacitor he was currently aligning with a pair of silver tweezers.","Without breaking his rhythm, Thomas reached down with his left hand and gave the end of the wooden Ravenclaw bench two firm, rhythmic taps with his knuckles.","\u003cem\u003eClick. Whirrrrr-clack.\u003c/em\u003e","The ancient wood groaned softly as a hidden Technomantic expansion charm—engineered by Thomas during his second week at Hogwarts to accommodate his heavy textbooks—smoothly slid outward. The bench extended by exactly thirty-six inches of polished, reinforced oak, complete with an ergonomically contoured backrest and a small brass cup holder.","\u0026quot;Bench load tolerance expanded,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled in his deep, unhurried bass voice, still squinting through his magnifying lens as he applied a dot of soldering flux. \u0026quot;Weight distribution is rated for up to three hundred pounds. Sit if you like. Just keep your silk clear of the flux stand; the residue stains.\u0026quot;","And that was it.","He picked up his micro-screwdriver again.","He didn\u0027t look at her face. He didn\u0027t look at her spun-silver hair. He didn\u0027t even look to see if she actually sat down. He just went straight back to calibrating his gear.","Céleste stood frozen beside the extended bench, her jaw parting in genuine, stunned shock. For the first time in her entire life, a boy had treated her presence not as a divine revelation, but as an incidental spatial variable in his workshop.","Across the Great Hall, three sets of eyes had witnessed the entire interaction.","At the Slytherin table, Cassiopeia Malfoy had her fork suspended halfway to her mouth. Her silver eyes were bulging in absolute, furious disbelief.","\u0026quot;Is he... is he serious?\u0026quot; Cassie hissed through gritted teeth, gripping her silver fork so hard the tines bent. \u0026quot;She is an elemental manifestation of French divinity, and he... he gave her thirty-six inches of oak and told her not to get solder on her dress?!\u0026quot;","Over at the Gryffindor table, Lily Luna Potter had both hands clapped over her mouth, her shoulders vibrating with a mixture of hysterical laughter and profound second-hand exhaustion.","\u0026quot;Thomas,\u0026quot; Lily groaned through her fingers, looking up at the enchanted ceiling as if seeking divine intervention. \u0026quot;You absolute, colossal dolt. You magnificent, blind, structural idiot.\u0026quot;","At the Hufflepuff table, Pandora Weasley had tilted her head so far to the side that her strawberry-blonde curls brushed the table. Her silvery eyes were wide with dreamy amusement.","\u0026quot;Oh, marvelous,\u0026quot; Pan whispered serenely to an utterly bewildered Hufflepuff first-year. \u0026quot;The silver swan just tried to charm a concrete pillar. The pillar offered her adequate seating and returned to its blueprints. It’s poetic, really.\u0026quot;","Cassie, Lily, and Pan looked across the Great Hall at each other once again.","First, James had suffered a total mental collapse over a northern glacier who tripped on a stone.","Now, Thomas had casually dismissed a French superweapon to tighten a clockwork screw.","Cassie dropped her head into her hands. Lily slumped over her goblet. Pan let out a soft, defeated wheeze.","\u003cem\u003eMen.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eAbsolute, hopeless, catastrophic dolts.\u003c/em\u003e"]},{"num":62,"origNum":32,"title":"Thermal Insulation and the Spark","wordCount":1291,"paragraphs":["\u003cem\u003eCRACK.\u003c/em\u003e","Underneath the heavy oak of the Ravenclaw table, a polished leather shoe made violent, unyielding contact with Thomas Vernon Dursley’s right shin.","Thomas flinched. The micro-screwdriver in his hand jerked by half a millimeter, missing the microscopic brass screw and leaving a tiny, scratch-like burr on the copper casing of his chronometer.","Thomas blinked through his magnifying lens, slowly lowered his hands, and looked down the bench with a heavy, deeply offended scowl.","\u0026quot;Ow!\u0026quot; Thomas’s deep bass voice carried an unmistakable tone of outraged Surrey practicality. \u0026quot;What was that for? Why did you kick me?!\u0026quot;","The seventh-year Ravenclaw Prefect, a lanky boy named Davies whose face had gone an alarming shade of blotchy scarlet, was leaning halfway across the table. Davies was sweating so profusely from the sheer atmospheric radiation of the Veela sitting three feet away that his prefect badge was slightly crooked.","\u0026quot;Thomas!\u0026quot; Davies hissed through clenched teeth, his voice a frantic, strangled whisper that sounded like a steam valve about to explode. \u0026quot;For the love of Rowena Ravenclaw, look to your left!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am currently calibrating a four-millimeter tension spring,\u0026quot; Thomas said evenly. \u0026quot;Left is irrelevant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A \u003cem\u003eVeela\u003c/em\u003e is sitting next to you!\u0026quot; Davies choked, his eyes bulging as he gestured wildly with a butter knife. \u0026quot;A French, silver-haired, celestial Veela! The most stunning girl on the European continent just asked to share your bench, and you treated her like an umbrella stand! Have you no decency?! Turn around and greet her!\u0026quot;","Several other Ravenclaws nodded frantically in furious agreement, looking as though they were ready to physically turn Thomas’s shoulders by force just to spare the house from international disgrace.","Thomas sighed. It was the long, put-upon sigh of a man whose productive workday had been needlessly interrupted by municipal bureaucracy.","\u0026quot;Fine,\u0026quot; Thomas muttered.","He set down his micro-screwdriver in its velvet groove. He carefully lifted the flip-down magnifying lens from his spectacles, smoothed the front of his robes, and slowly rotated his broad frame on the bench to face Céleste Laurent.","For the first time all evening, Thomas Vernon Dursley actually looked at her.","Céleste sat with her back straight, her chin slightly raised, waiting with cool, aristocratic expectation. Up close, her Veela beauty was blinding. Her cascading silver-white hair seemed to catch the candlelight and turn it into spun diamonds. Her violet eyes shimmered with ancient, captivating grace, and the delicate, intoxicating aroma of mountain honey and night-blooming jasmine drifted from her robes in an almost visible mist. Any other fourteen-year-old boy in Britain would have required an emergency blood transfusion just from the proximity.","Thomas evaluated her with the calm, methodical gaze of a building surveyor inspecting a newly delivered load of timber.","\u0026quot;Good evening,\u0026quot; Thomas said politely, giving her a brisk, crisp nod. \u0026quot;Welcome to Hogwarts. If you’re planning on sitting near the aisle, I recommend keeping your cloak on. The castle’s north-facing arched windows were installed in the fourteenth century and have atrocious thermal insulation. The cross-draft will give you a stiff neck.\u0026quot;","He paused, clearly considering his social obligations completely fulfilled.","\u0026quot;Have a pleasant dinner.\u0026quot;","With that, Thomas turned back to his napkin, flipped his magnifying lens down over his eye with a neat \u003cem\u003eclick\u003c/em\u003e, picked up his tweezers, and went straight back to aligning the micro-capacitor.","The silence that fell over the Ravenclaw table was deafening.","Davies looked like he was having a stroke. The sixth-year next to him simply let his forehead drop onto his dinner roll with a soft, hollow thud. Across the entire length of the table, thirty Ravenclaws simultaneously raised their hands and slapped their palms over their faces in a unified, synchronized wave of pure agony.","\u003cem\u003eSMACK.\u003c/em\u003e","And it wasn\u0027t just Ravenclaw.","Across the Great Hall, at the Gryffindor table, Lily Luna Potter watched the entire interaction. Her jaw unhinged. She slowly brought both hands up, pressed her palms against her eyes, and groaned so loudly that the candles above her table flickered.","At the Slytherin table, Cassiopeia Malfoy shoved her plate away, buried her face in her silver-embroidered sleeves, and let out a muffled, aristocratic shriek of despair that caused Adrian Pucey Jr.—still hiding under the bench—to flinch.","At the Hufflepuff table, Pandora Weasley didn\u0027t even use her hands. She simply tipped sideways, resting her cheek directly on the cold stone tabletop, staring blankly at the ceiling. \u0026quot;The pillar offered thermal analysis,\u0026quot; Pan whispered dreamily. \u0026quot;The universe is folding in on itself.\u0026quot;","Meanwhile, beside Thomas, Céleste Laurent was experiencing an entirely new sensation: utter, disbelieving bewilderment.","\u003cem\u003eThermal insulation?\u003c/em\u003e","He had looked directly into her eyes—eyes that had reduced the Beauxbatons dueling champions to stuttering wrecks—and he had warned her about a draft?","Her pride, which had been forged in the high courts of French magical society, should have been insulted. She should have sneered, flipped her shimmering silver hair, and glided over to the Slytherin table where half a dozen boys were currently waving their family signet rings at her like drowning men waving flares.","Instead, Céleste found herself completely, helplessly fascinated.","She looked at his massive, steady hands. She looked at the absolute, unflappable stillness of his posture. He wasn\u0027t nervous; his pulse wasn\u0027t racing, his hands weren\u0027t trembling, and his ears weren\u0027t even slightly pink. He was simply... genuinely, thoroughly immersed in whatever was sitting on that velvet cloth.","Curiosity won.","Slowly, carefully, Céleste leaned in. The silvery silk of her sleeve brushed against the dark wool of Thomas’s school robe. She leaned over his shoulder, her violet eyes dropping to the tiny, intricate metal contraption on the table.","It was a mesmerizing puzzle of spinning brass gears no larger than fleas, connected by gossamer-thin silver wires to a carved core of glowing blue lapis lazuli.","\u0026quot;Pardon,\u0026quot; Céleste whispered softly, her melodious French accent dipping into genuine curiosity. \u0026quot;What... what is zat you are building?\u0026quot;","The reaction was instantaneous.","Thomas froze.","He didn\u0027t freeze like James had frozen—struck dumb by romantic lightning.","He froze like a bloodhound catching a scent.","The micro-screwdriver hovered in the air. Slowly, Thomas lifted his magnifying lens. He turned his head back to Céleste, and for the very first time, his pale blue eyes weren\u0027t dull with civic politeness.","They were \u003cem\u003eablaze\u003c/em\u003e.","A massive, radiant, boyish grin—the kind of pure, unfiltered joy that usually only appeared when he found a particularly well-organized hardware store—spread across Thomas Vernon Dursley’s face.","\u0026quot;You\u0027re interested in the kinetic feedback loop?!\u0026quot; Thomas exclaimed, his deep voice suddenly booming with infectious, high-octane excitement.","Céleste blinked, startled by the sheer volume of his enthusiasm. \u0026quot;I... well, I noticed ze lapis core—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s a Technomantic harmonic dampener!\u0026quot; Thomas interrupted eagerly, practically vibrating with delight as he nudged his brass toolkit closer to her so she could see. \u0026quot;See, the problem with ambient Hogwarts magic is that it spikes during meal times because of the House Elves’ heating charms underneath the floorboards! It creates an irregular magnetic flutter! So what I’ve done here is bridge an enchanted copper coil with a standard Muggle step-down transformer—\u0026quot;","He grabbed his micro-tweezer, pointing excitedly at the flea-sized gears.","\u0026quot;—if you look right here, at the third escapement gear, I’ve shaved off half a millimeter to compensate for the lunar gravitational pull on the lapis crystal! Brilliant, right?! Look at that torque distribution!\u0026quot;","He looked at her, his broad face shining with absolute, unfiltered passion, entirely oblivious to the fact that half the Great Hall was staring at them in shock.","Céleste looked at the tiny, whirling brass gears. Then she looked at the radiant, totally unpretentious excitement in Thomas\u0027s eyes.","A slow, dazzling, genuinely amused smile curled the corners of her lips.","\u0026quot;Show me,\u0026quot; she murmured softly, leaning her chin on her hand. \u0026quot;Tell me about ze torque.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":63,"origNum":33,"title":"The Northern Diplomat and the Art of Verbal Collapse","wordCount":1440,"paragraphs":["While the Ravenclaw table was currently witnessing the unprecedented phenomenon of a pure-blooded French Veela taking notes on step-down transformers, Lily Luna Potter was engaged in a far more dangerous sport: observation.","Her six-foot frame allowed her an unobstructed, panoramic view of the Great Hall over the heads of the third-years. And Lily had not inherited the Evans intuition and the Potter Seeker vision just to stare at roast potatoes.","Down at the front of the hall, the Durmstrang delegation sat rigidly in their heavy, crimson robes. Viktor Krum was deep in quiet, guttural conversation with Severus Snape—two men whose collective capacity for scowling could have curdled cream at fifty paces.","Beside her father, Valeria Krum sat with impeccable, soldier-like poise. Her back was a plumb line of northern discipline. She cut her beef with razor precision. She did not chatter. She did not giggle.","Except.","Every ninety seconds—precisely when she calculated that the hall’s attention was drifting toward Dumbledore’s sequined sleeves or Thomas’s noisy Technomancy—Valeria’s chin would tilt by a fraction of an inch.","Her stormy, hazel-gold eyes would flick across the aisle.","Straight at the Gryffindor table.","More specifically, straight at James Sirius Potter, who was currently sitting with the vacant, glassy-eyed expression of a boy who had looked directly into an active solar flare. James was holding a fork upside down, attempting to spear a carrot that was three inches to the left of his plate, completely paralyzed by the mere fact that Valeria existed in the same hemisphere.","Valeria’s gaze would linger for two heartbeats—her dark lashes fluttering, a tiny, almost imperceptible softening in her fierce jawline—before snapping back to her plate with military severity.","She thought she was being subtle. She thought the northern arts of stealth and discipline were shielding her.","She had forgotten about Lily.","A slow, glorious, catastrophic grin spread across Lily Luna Potter’s face. It was the exact smile that had preceded James Sirius setting off thirty-two Whiz-bangs in the East Mansion swimming pool.","\u0026quot;Oh,\u0026quot; Lily whispered into her goblet of pumpkin juice. \u0026quot;Oh, this is too good. This is a gift from the gods.\u0026quot;","Beside her, James gave a pitiful, shuddering gasp as he dropped his fork entirely. \u0026quot;Lily,\u0026quot; he croaked, his voice cracking like a dry twig. \u0026quot;Is she... did she just... is the room spinning, or did she look at my hair? Does my hair look stupid? It feels stupid. My skull feels warm.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Your skull is empty, James,\u0026quot; Lily said sweetly.","She stood up.","When Lily Luna Potter stood up, the atmospheric pressure in the Gryffindor sector immediately shifted. The candlelight caught the radiant, warm copper-mahogany of her hair, and \u0026quot;The Light\u0026quot; that naturally hummed around her seemed to pulse like a cheerful beacon. Half a dozen boys in the vicinity reflexively straightened their ties, bracing for impact.","Lily didn\u0027t look at them.","She turned her dazzling, thousand-watt Evans smile directly toward the Durmstrang delegation.","She raised an arm and gave a bright, friendly, impossible-to-ignore wave.","\u0026quot;Valeria!\u0026quot; Lily’s voice chimed across the stone hall, clear, bell-like, and carrying the unshakeable, sunny authority of someone who had never known a stranger in her life. \u0026quot;Over here! There’s plenty of room between me and my brother! Come sit with us!\u0026quot;","The silence that fell over the aisle was immediate and absolute.","At the High Table, Viktor Krum’s head snapped around, his thick eyebrows knitting together in a heavy, thunderous V. Beside him, Snape closed his eyes and pinched the bridge of his nose, silently mouthing words that looked like \u003cem\u003eLord deliver me from this family.\u003c/em\u003e","At the Gryffindor table, James Sirius Potter simply died inside.","His eyes bulged to the size of Galleons. His soul visibly detached from his body, floated upward to inspect the charmed ceiling, and refused to come back down.","\u0026quot;Lily,\u0026quot; James hissed in a tone of pure, suffocating terror, grabbing at her sleeve with trembling fingers. \u0026quot;What are you doing? What are you—I’m going to throw you into the lake! I’m going to hex your eyebrows off! Cancel it! Tell her you meant another Valeria!\u0026quot;","It was too late.","Valeria Krum had frozen. For half a second, the stoic Durmstrang mask slipped, revealing the wide, startled eyes of a girl caught red-handed. But she was a Krum. She had flown in blizzards over the Black Sea; she did not retreat from a Gryffindor invitation.","Slowly, deliberately, Valeria set down her silver cutlery. She stood up, smoothed the midnight-black snow-fox fur of her cloak with a snap of leather, and stepped away from the northern delegation.","She walked across the central aisle.","Every stride was fluid, athletic, and devastatingly confident. Her heavy boots made a soft, rhythmic \u003cem\u003eclick-thud\u003c/em\u003e against the stone floor, her raven braid swaying against her spine.","As she reached the Gryffindor table, Lily smoothly slid two feet to the left, opening a wide, luxurious expanse of bench directly beside James.","Valeria stopped. She looked down at James.","Up close, the stormy gold flecks in her dark eyes were mesmerizing. Her scent—crisp mountain air, winter woodsmoke, and a hint of wild juniper—hit James like a physical blow to the sternum.","\u0026quot;Zdravei,\u0026quot; Valeria said. Her voice was low, rich, with a smoky, dark northern purr that vibrated right through the soles of James’s shoes. \u0026quot;I am Valeria Krum.\u0026quot;","She extended a slender, strong hand—a Seeker’s hand, calloused from broom-grips, with a silver snake ring coiled around her thumb.","James looked at the hand.","Then he looked at her face.","His mouth opened.","Nothing came out.","\u0026quot;James,\u0026quot; Lily prompted with a razor-sharp, sisterly elbow into his ribs. \u0026quot;Words. You use them every day. Try one.\u0026quot;","The elbow seemed to jump-start the rusted engine of James’s vocal cords. He bolted upright, nearly knocking his pumpkin juice onto his lap, his messy black hair sticking up in seven different directions.","He reached out to shake her hand, hesitated, panicked, tried to pull his hand back, realized how ridiculous that looked, and ended up executing an awkward, trembling claw-grip that shook her hand up and down like a rusted water pump.","\u0026quot;H-Hullo!\u0026quot; James barked. The volume was entirely wrong—it was the volume of a man shouting across a foggy Quidditch pitch in high gale winds.","His face flushed a violent, incandescent scarlet that rivaled the Gryffindor banner above his head.","\u0026quot;I’m... J-Jame,\u0026quot; he stammered, his baritone cracking into an undignified squeak. \u0026quot;I mean! Potter! James! James Potter. The... the third? No! Sirius! James Sirius Potter. I fly. I mean, I play! Quidditch! The brooms... in the air... with balls.\u0026quot;","He stopped.","He stared at her in horrified realization of what had just tumbled out of his mouth. He looked as though he wanted the stone floor to crack open, swallow him into the Chamber of Secrets, and seal itself with concrete.","Valeria blinked once.","Then, the razor-sharp line of her mouth twitched. A tiny, breathtaking dimple appeared on her left cheek—a flash of pure, genuine amusement that melted the northern frost right off her.","\u0026quot;I know who you are, James Potter,\u0026quot; Valeria murmured softly, her hazel-gold eyes dancing. \u0026quot;And I know how you fly.\u0026quot;","She withdrew her hand smoothly and swung her legs over the bench, settling onto the seat directly between Lily and the utterly destroyed James. She smoothed her fur cloak, reached for a warm bread roll, and turned her profile toward him as if they had been dining together for years.","Beside her, James slowly collapsed back onto the bench, staring straight ahead with unseeing eyes, breathing shallowly through his nose like an athlete in cardiac arrest.","Across the Great Hall, the show had not gone unnoticed.","At the Slytherin table, Cassiopeia Malfoy had leaned back against the high wooden partition. She was holding her silver goblet in one hand, watching the catastrophe with a slow, predatory smirk that was pure Narcissa Malfoy. She caught Lily’s eye across the hall and raised her goblet in a silent, mocking toast: \u003cem\u003eMagnificent cruelty, Potter.\u003c/em\u003e","At the Hufflepuff table, Pandora Weasley was practically humming. She tilted her head, watching James vibrate at a frequency so high that his silverware was actually rattling against the table. \u0026quot;Oh, the spirits are delighted,\u0026quot; Pan whispered to a bowl of mashed potatoes. \u0026quot;The dragon just invited the storm into her nest, and the storm forgot how to speak English. Best start-of-term feast in a decade.\u0026quot;","And Lily Luna Potter sat between the two of them, biting her bottom lip until it bruised, trying with every ounce of Evans willpower not to scream with hysterical laughter.","Her brother was in absolute, unmitigated hell.","And Lily had never been more entertained in her entire life."]},{"num":64,"origNum":34,"title":"The Wronski Feint and the Relief of the Seer","wordCount":1627,"paragraphs":["The Scottish October wind swept over the Quidditch pitch with the razor-sharp bite of impending winter, but the two figures circling a hundred feet above the turf were generating enough friction to melt the goalposts.","Over the past three weeks, James Sirius Potter had undergone a profound evolutionary leap. The stuttering, tongue-tied boy who had offered to play \u0026quot;brooms with balls\u0026quot; at the start-of-term feast had officially vanished.","When you placed James Potter on a broomstick, the awkwardness evaporated. The air was his natural habitat. And in Valeria Krum, he had met his absolute match.","For twenty-one days, the pitch had become their private arena. While the rest of the school was in the library or the Great Hall, James and Valeria had been flying late-night drills. They dived together at terrifying speeds, traded hair-raising Wronski Feints, and challenged each other to catch the Snitch within inches of the frosty grass.","In the air, they were flawless.","On the ground, however, they were an absolute, unmitigated catastrophe.","The romantic tension between them had escalated from a mild simmer into a category-five magical storm. They would walk back from the pitch side by side, their shoulders brushing with every stride, both of them vibrating with unspoken words, stolen glances, and desperate, agonizing hesitation. James would look at her like he wanted to swallow his own tongue; Valeria would look at him with a fierce, smoldering northern intensity that could have scorched the grass.","Neither of them had possessed the courage to say a single bloody word about it.","Which brought matters to the top row of the Gryffindor stands.","Crammed together on a narrow wooden bench, huddled beneath the legendary Invisibility Cloak that James had foolishly left in the common room three hours earlier, were three very cramped, very disgruntled teenage girls.","\u0026quot;My knee is wedged into your ribcage, Potter,\u0026quot; Cassiopeia Malfoy hissed in a venomous whisper, her breath fogging beneath the shimmering silver fabric. \u0026quot;If you do not shift your gargantuan, six-foot frame by three centimeters to the left, I am going to hex your kneecaps off. I did not spend four hundred Galleons on French silk robes to have them creased under a hand-me-down shroud.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Shh!\u0026quot; Lily Luna hissed back, her chin resting on Cassie’s shoulder as she peered through the microscopic gap in the fabric. \u0026quot;Shut up, Cassie! They just landed! They’re putting their brooms down!\u0026quot;","Between them sat Pandora Weasley.","Pan was not complaining about the space. Pan was currently curled into a tight, trembling ball, both of her hands clamped tightly over her temples, her strawberry-blonde curls spilling between her fingers. Her eyes were squeezed shut in pure, agonizing torment.","\u0026quot;The resonance,\u0026quot; Pan wheezed softly, her voice muffled against her knees. \u0026quot;It’s... it’s unbearable. Their repressed feelings are vibrating at ninety gigahertz. It tastes like copper and unfulfilled longing. My third eye is throbbing. I’ve had a headache since Tuesday week. If they don’t touch each other soon, I’m going to throw a Bludger at both of their heads.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Stay strong, Pan,\u0026quot; Lily whispered, patting her cousin’s arm sympathetically. \u0026quot;Look, they’re sitting on the grass.\u0026quot;","Down on the pitch, sixty feet below, the two Seekers had collapsed onto the frost-dusted turf near the center circle.","Both of them were breathless, their cheeks flushed pink from the wind. James had taken off his leather flying gloves, running a sweaty hand through his unruly black hair, leaning back on his palms. Valeria sat cross-legged beside him, her heavy Durmstrang training tunic unlaced at the throat, her raven braid messy and windswept.","\u0026quot;You cut the dive too sharp on the south hoop,\u0026quot; James said, trying for an easy, casual grin. His voice was slightly husky, lacking its usual bravado. \u0026quot;If I hadn’t pulled up, we would’ve collided.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I did not cut it sharp,\u0026quot; Valeria countered, her low, smoky accent cutting through the evening chill. She turned her head to look at him. \u0026quot;I knew your turn radius. You always bank three inches wider than you need to.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Do not,\u0026quot; James muttered, looking down at his boots.","\u0026quot;Do too.\u0026quot;","Silence fell over the pitch.","It wasn\u0027t a comfortable silence. It was that thick, suffocating, ozone-charged silence that preceded a lightning strike. James glanced at her profile—the sharp line of her jaw, the way her chest rose and fell with each breath, the stormy gold flecks in her dark eyes. His throat went dry. He opened his mouth, desperately trying to summon the courage that Gryffindor was supposed to provide, but the words stuck in his ribs like cold porridge.","Valeria watched him struggle.","She saw the clenching of his jaw. She saw the uncertainty in his hazel-brown eyes. She saw the boy who had just pulled off a ninety-mile-per-hour spiral drop looking at her as if she were a dragon he was terrified to wake.","Suddenly, Valeria’s eyes narrowed. A flicker of decisive, northern resolve flashed across her face.","\u003cem\u003eEnough.\u003c/em\u003e","She stood up.","James blinked, looking up at her from the turf in confusion. \u0026quot;Valeria? What’s wrong? Is your wrist hurting from that last catch?\u0026quot;","Valeria looked down at him intently, her stormy eyes dark, unwavering, and utterly predatory.","\u0026quot;Get up, James,\u0026quot; she commanded softly.","\u0026quot;What? Why? Did I do something—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Stand. Up.\u0026quot;","James scrambled to his feet, bewildered, dusting the dead grass off the seat of his Quidditch trousers. \u0026quot;All right, all right, I’m up. What is—\u0026quot;","He never finished the sentence.","The exact second James reached his full six-foot height, Valeria reached out with both hands, seized the thick leather collar of his practice jersey, and yanked him down toward her with the lethal, effortless strength of an international athlete.","James’s eyes widened in sheer panic for half a second.","Then her mouth crashed onto his.","It was not a soft, tentative, schoolyard kiss. It was a Durmstrang assault.","Her lips were cool from the wind but burned with an electric, fierce heat. She pulled him in tight, tilting her head, her fingers curling into the leather of his tunic, kissing him with all the pent-up frustration and fierce passion of the last three weeks.","Down on the pitch, every single circuit in James Sirius Potter’s nervous system blew out at once.","His leather gloves slipped from his limp fingers and fell onto the grass. His kinetic energy didn\u0027t just stop; it detonated. His mind flatlined. His hands hovered awkwardly in the air for two terrified seconds before gravity, instinct, and a century of Potter stubbornness took over. He let out a muffled, shuddering groan, wrapped his long arms around her waist, and pulled her flush against his chest, kissing her back with a desperate, breathless intensity that made his knees tremble.","Up in the stands, under the Invisibility Cloak, the world changed.","Pandora Weasley’s hands slowly, shakily peeled away from her temples.","She opened her silvery eyes. She took a deep, shuddering, oxygen-rich breath. A look of transcendent, heavenly bliss washed over her face, smoothing away weeks of psychic pain.","\u0026quot;It stopped,\u0026quot; Pan breathed, her voice filled with religious reverence. She slumped back against the wooden bench with a contented sigh. \u0026quot;The frequency... it smoothed out. The Wrackspurts have evacuated the airspace. The noise in my skull is gone. I can think again. I can \u003cem\u003ebreathe\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Beside her, Lily Luna Potter was engaged in a silent, violent victory dance.","She was pumping both fists in the air, biting her sleeve to keep from screaming with pure, unadulterated joy. \u0026quot;YES!\u0026quot; Lily hissed in a triumphant whisper, tears of laughter prickling her emerald eyes. \u0026quot;FINALLY! Oh, thank Merlin! She just tackled him! She didn\u0027t even wait for him to use his stupid brain, she just hauled him down like a sack of oats! Look at his feet! He’s standing on his tiptoes!\u0026quot;","Cassiopeia Malfoy slowly reached into her designer pocket and withdrew a small, sleek platinum pocket watch with an enchanted dial.","She clicked it open with a satisfying \u003cem\u003esnap\u003c/em\u003e, evaluated the time, and snapped it shut with a triumphant smirk.","\u0026quot;Three weeks, four days, and six hours,\u0026quot; Cassie announced smoothly, crossing her legs under the cloak with supreme aristocratic satisfaction. \u0026quot;I had the first week of October. Lily, you had Halloween. Pandora, you had the first snowfall. You both owe me five Galleons.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t care about the Galleons!\u0026quot; Lily wheezed, wiping a tear of laughter from her cheek as she watched her brother down below, who was currently clutching Valeria like a drowning man clutching a life raft. \u0026quot;Look at him! He looks like he’s about to faint! His brain has turned to porridge!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It was always porridge, darling,\u0026quot; Cassie remarked silkily, though a rare, genuine smile touched her lips as she watched the two flyers on the pitch. \u0026quot;At least now it’s porridge with a Bulgarian garnish. She has decent taste, I’ll give her that. Even if my father will have a coronary when he finds out Viktor Krum’s daughter is practically living in our family circle.\u0026quot;","Pan sighed dreamily, resting her head on Lily’s shoulder under the shimmering fabric. \u0026quot;Their auras are glowing gold and deep crimson now. It looks like a sunset over a bonfire. It’s very pretty.\u0026quot;","Down on the dark, windy pitch, the two figures finally broke apart. James was panting, his face incandescently red, resting his forehead against Valeria’s with a dazed, completely helpless smile. Valeria was looking up at him, a rare, breathtaking grin illuminating her fierce features, her fingers still tangled in the front of his shirt.","Up in the stands, the three girls leaned against each other under the cloak, laughing softly into the cold autumn wind.","The storm had broken. The idiot had been kissed.","And for the first time all term, the Great Hall was going to be an absolute riot tomorrow morning."]},{"num":65,"origNum":35,"title":"The Tensile Strength of French Silk","wordCount":1763,"paragraphs":["The walk back from the Quidditch pitch was a triumphal march.","Lily Luna Potter, Cassiopeia Malfoy, and Pandora Weasley strolled through the heavy castle doors, their Invisibility Cloak tucked safely into Cassie’s enchanted beaded handbag. Lily was still humming a buoyant, victorious tune, her emerald eyes dancing with glee. Cassie walked with the smug, languid grace of an empress whose investments had just paid a massive dividend. And Pan walked with her head tilted back, inhaling the cool castle air as if she had just emerged from a three-week underwater expedition.","\u0026quot;I still cannot believe she hauled him down by the collar,\u0026quot; Lily chuckled, shaking her head. \u0026quot;Our father is going to laugh until he chokes. Uncle Harry will probably buy her a Nimbus for Christmas.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My father will need a calming draught the size of a pumpkin,\u0026quot; Cassie remarked with immense satisfaction. \u0026quot;He spent ten years trying to avoid Viktor Krum at international Quidditch banquets because Krum once told him his hair was \u0027too shiny for flying.\u0027 Now Krum’s daughter is snogging James in the center circle. The Malfoy-Potter alliance has conquered Bulgaria.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The air tastes like peppermint now,\u0026quot; Pan said dreamily, skipping ahead a few steps. \u0026quot;No more screeching frequencies. Just quiet, happy little—wait.\u0026quot;","Pan stopped abruptly at the junction of the third-floor corridor. She held up a slender hand, her silvery eyes narrowing.","\u0026quot;What is it?\u0026quot; Lily asked, coming up behind her. \u0026quot;More Wrackspurts?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Pan murmured. \u0026quot;A low, mechanical hum. Like an electric drill trying to perform ballet.\u0026quot;","Cassie raised an eyebrow. \u0026quot;Thomas.\u0026quot;","The three girls peeked around the corner of the grand staircase gallery.","Sure enough, halfway down the corridor leading to the Arithmancy wing, Thomas Vernon Dursley was hard at work.","He was currently standing four rungs up on an extendable brass stepladder that he had clearly constructed himself, as it was fitted with pneumatic shock absorbers and a built-in cup holder. Thomas had his school robes neatly folded on a nearby stone plinth, leaving him in a crisp white shirt with the sleeves rolled past his thick forearms, a heavy leather tool belt strapped around his hips. He was holding a large monkey wrench in one hand, an enchanted spirit level in the other, and his wand tucked neatly behind his right ear like a carpenter’s pencil.","Hogwarts\u0027 famous trick stairs—the ones that had vanished under students\u0027 feet for ten centuries—had met their match. Thomas was systematically disassembling the gears beneath the third landing.","Standing at the foot of the ladder was Céleste Laurent.","Even in the dim, stone-lit corridor, Céleste looked like a vision from a Renaissance fresco. Her powdered-blue silk robes swirled around her ankles, and her cascades of liquid-silver hair shimmered with faint, gossamer light. She was holding a clipboard of Arithmancy schematics that Thomas had thrust into her hands twenty minutes prior, her luminescent violet eyes fixed on the boy above her.","And lurking about fifteen feet away, huddled behind a marble statue of a one-eyed witch, was an unofficial delegation that Lily immediately recognized.","\u0026quot;Look,\u0026quot; Lily whispered, pointing. \u0026quot;The Fan Club.\u0026quot;","Cassie snorted softly. \u0026quot;Pathetic.\u0026quot;","It was the \u003cstrong\u003eDursley Admiration Society\u003c/strong\u003e.","Over the last month, Thomas’s complete, towering immunity to typical teenage nonsense had turned him into an unexpected romantic sensation. A clandestine coalition of sixth-year Ravenclaws (who worshipped his intellect), fourth-year Hufflepuffs (who swooned over his dependable, oak-tree shoulders), and a cluster of Beauxbatons girls (who found his stoic, unbothered British masculinity completely exotic) had taken to following him at a respectful distance. To the French girls, Céleste had always been the untouchable peak of beauty back in the Pyrenees—at least until they arrived at Hogwarts and encountered the terrifying, runway-ready triad of Cassie, Lily, and Pan—and they were currently watching their schoolmate struggle with quiet, breathless anticipation.","Up on the ladder, Thomas gave a stubborn brass bolt a vicious turn with his wrench.","\u003cem\u003eSqueeee-CLACK.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;You see, Céleste,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled down from the ladder, his deep Surrey bass echoing off the stonework with absolute, professorial authority, \u0026quot;the primary defect in the counter-weight pulley system isn’t magical decay at all. It’s basic mechanical friction! The fourteenth-century stonemasons used soft limestone for the fulcrum! Limestone! It’s eroded by three millimeters on the northern axis, which creates a hitch in the pivot action every time someone weighing over ten stone steps on the tread.\u0026quot;","He adjusted his steel-rimmed spectacles with the back of his wrist, entirely absorbed.","\u0026quot;If we replace the limestone bushing with enchanted phosphor-bronze, we increase the load-bearing tolerance by four hundred percent! I’ve drafted a five-year maintenance schedule. It’ll cut down hospital wing visits for sprained ankles by eighty-two point six percent. Brilliant, isn\u0027t it?\u0026quot;","At the bottom of the ladder, Céleste Laurent did not look at the schematics.","She looked at him.","She had spent three solid weeks deploying every weapon in the Veela arsenal. She had worn perfume distilled from midnight lilies. She had brushed his shoulder with silk. She had offered him French pastries. She had listened to him explain gear ratios, torque differentials, circuit breakers, and the thermal properties of Scottish sandstone until her ears rang.","She had endured the polite nods. She had endured the casual taps on benches. She had endured being treated like a remarkably quiet junior apprentice in a Surrey garage.","Céleste Laurent had officially reached her limit.","Her violet eyes narrowed with a sudden, dangerous, feline intensity. A flush of pink rose to her flawless cheekbones.","Slowly, deliberately, she dropped the clipboard.","It hit the stone floor with a sharp \u003cem\u003eCLACK\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;Thomas,\u0026quot; Céleste commanded. Her melodious French accent was no longer soft and purring; it carried the sharp, ringing steel of a woman who was done negotiating.","Thomas blinked down from the ladder. \u0026quot;Careful with that, Céleste, those are the primary blueprints—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Down,\u0026quot; she said, pointing a slender, manicured finger at the stone floor. \u0026quot;Come down. \u003cem\u003eMaintenant\u003c/em\u003e.\u0026quot;","Thomas frowned in mild confusion. \u0026quot;Did the leveling bubble shift? I haven\u0027t torqued the retaining nut to specification yet—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eDown, Thomas!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","Recognizing that tone—it was the exact frequency Aunt Petunia used when Vernon tracked mud onto the front hallway carpet—Thomas sighed heavily, tucked his wrench into his belt, and stepped down the brass ladder.","\u0026quot;What is the matter?\u0026quot; Thomas asked as his boots hit the flagstones, wiping grease off his large hands with a rag. \u0026quot;If the draft from the stairs is bothering you again, I told you the wool cloak—\u0026quot;","Céleste didn\u0027t let him finish.","She reached up with both hands, grabbed the rolled collar of his crisp white shirt, and yanked him down.","And kissed him.","It wasn\u0027t a tentative, gentle peck. It was a pure-blooded Veela resorting to the final, desperate arrow in her quiver—a kiss of intoxicating warmth, floral honey, and raw, demanding frustration.","Thomas Vernon Dursley’s eyes went wide behind his spectacles.","His brain hit a total, catastrophic computational error. The blueprints, the gear ratios, the phosphor-bronze bushings, the Surrey property tax laws—all of it dissolved into static. He was being kissed by a creature of liquid silver and violet starlight, and the sensory overload threatened to blow every fuse in his skull.","For two seconds, he stood rigid as an iron girder.","And then... the Dursley genes took over.","Beneath the quiet, scholarly technician lived the blood of Vernon Dursley’s stubborn, bulldog ferocity and Dudley Dursley’s heavyweight boxing power. The sheer, instinctual reflex of a man who saw a problem, decided it was his, and handled it with overwhelming physical confidence.","Thomas dropped his oily rag.","He didn\u0027t stumble. He didn\u0027t hesitate.","His large, calloused hands reached down, gripped Céleste firmly by the waist, and with effortless, breathtaking strength, he simply \u003cstrong\u003elifted the pure-blooded Veela entirely off her feet\u003c/strong\u003e.","Céleste let out a muffled gasp against his mouth as she was hoisted into the air. Her powder-blue silk robes swirled around his knees, her delicate silver heels dangling six inches above the stone floor. Thomas pulled her flush against his chest, locking his massive arms around her back as he deepened the kiss with a fierce, possessive confidence that made the entire corridor seem to tilt on its axis.","Céleste’s hands, which had been gripping his collar in frustration, instantly tangled into his neatly combed hair, clinging to his broad shoulders as she kissed him back with a breathless, melting sigh.","Around the corner, behind the statue of the one-eyed witch, the Dursley Admiration Society imploded.","\u0026quot;No...\u0026quot; a fourth-year Hufflepuff whimpered, pressing her knuckles to her lips.","A sixth-year Ravenclaw girl’s quill snapped in half with a sickening \u003cem\u003ecrack\u003c/em\u003e.","Two Beauxbatons girls leaned against each other in dramatic, synchronized mourning, tears glistening in their mascara. It was over. The prize of the fourth-year class—the impenetrable, unbothered fortress of Ravenclaw—had fallen. He was officially, completely, irrevocably claimed. And worse, he had claimed her right back by lifting her into the air like a bag of enchanted feathers.","Watching from the shadows of the archway, Lily Luna Potter, Cassiopeia Malfoy, and Pandora Weasley stood shoulder to shoulder.","Cassie had a wicked, razor-sharp smirk curling her lips. \u0026quot;Well, well,\u0026quot; she murmured, crossing her arms. \u0026quot;Look at the builder. Who knew the Dursley boys had that kind of grip strength?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Uncle Dudley’s heavyweight training,\u0026quot; Lily beamed proudly, her emerald eyes sparkling with delight. \u0026quot;When a Dursley decides to hold onto something, they don\u0027t let go. Look at her shoes—she’s completely airborne!\u0026quot;","Beside them, Pandora Weasley let out a long, blissful, echoing sigh.","She rolled her shoulders, rotated her neck until it gave a soft, satisfying click, and smiled up at the vaulted stone ceiling.","\u0026quot;Gone,\u0026quot; Pan announced serenely. \u0026quot;All of it. The static has completely cleared.\u0026quot;","Lily looked at her with a grin. \u0026quot;Was Thomas’s tension giving you a headache too?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A little,\u0026quot; Pan admitted, tilting her head toward the couple down the hall, where Thomas had finally set Céleste back on her feet, though neither of them seemed in any hurry to let go of the other. \u0026quot;Nothing like James and Valeria, of course. James’s aura was like a thunderstorm trapped inside a tin can. Thomas’s aura was just... a very loud, stubborn diesel engine that refused to turn over. But now?\u0026quot;","Pan closed her eyes, basking in the peace.","\u0026quot;Now it’s purring like a kitten. Perfect harmony.\u0026quot;","Cassie pushed off the wall, smoothing her robes with a quiet chuckle. \u0026quot;Two down. One Seeker, one engineer. The Great Hall won’t survive the gossip at breakfast.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Breakfast?\u0026quot; Lily grinned, linking her arms through Cassie’s and Pan’s as they turned back toward the common rooms. \u0026quot;Darling, the Great Hall won’t survive until midnight.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":66,"origNum":36,"title":"The Bulgarian Shutdown and the Diplomatic Cable","wordCount":1837,"paragraphs":["The autumn frost of the Balkan mountains was unforgiving, coating the pine forests surrounding the Krum ancestral estate in a thick crust of rime. Inside the great timbered lodge, a roaring fire of birch logs crackled in the stone hearth, casting long, dancing shadows across walls lined with Quidditch memorabilia, polished brooms, and taxidermied mountain beasts.","Viktor Krum was sitting in a heavy, leather armchair, nursing a steaming mug of strong, spiced black tea.","He had been forced to return to Bulgaria for forty-eight hours on urgent Durmstrang administrative business—specifically, to yell at the Durmstrang Board of Governors for attempting to cut the delegation’s combat-robe budget, and to sign the official Triwizard Tournament liability waivers.","A sharp, authoritative tap sounded against the thick glass of the study window.","Viktor looked up, his thick, dark eyebrows rising in surprise. Perched on the sill outside was a massive Siberian eagle owl, its feathers dusted with Scottish snow, shaking its wings impatiently.","\u0026quot;Already?\u0026quot; Viktor muttered in his gravelly, low rumble.","He set his mug aside, pushed himself up from the leather chair, and unlatched the heavy iron window clasp. The owl swept inside, landed heavily on the mahogany desk, and extended a leg bearing a cylinder of parchment sealed with red Durmstrang wax.","Viktor took the letter, tossing the bird a dried strip of venison.","He examined the seal. It was Valeria’s neat, sharp handwriting.","A small, proud smile touched the corners of Viktor Krum’s severe mouth. His daughter was a champion. She was a Seeker of iron will, forged in northern blizzards, who did not waste parchment on frivolous teenage gossip.","\u0026quot;Aha,\u0026quot; Viktor grunted approvingly to the empty room. \u0026quot;She has flown the pitch. She has crushed the British Seekers. She writes to report her victory over the Potter boy.\u0026quot;","Technically, he was entirely correct. Valeria \u003cem\u003ehad\u003c/em\u003e captured the Seeker.","Viktor broke the wax seal, unrolled the thick parchment, and leaned against the edge of his desk to read.","\u003cem\u003eTatko,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThe Scottish air is damp, and their brooms are too light, but the castle is acceptable. The food lacks cabbage, but the bread is warm.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eQuidditch drills have concluded for the evening. James Sirius Potter is an extraordinary flyer. He banks too wide on the turns, but his dive is faster than mine. We have spent three weeks flying together.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eTonight, after practice, I stood him up on the turf.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eI kissed him.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eHe was very confused at first, but then he held me very tightly. He has strong hands. I am in love with him.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eSend more venison jerky.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eYour daughter,Valeria\u003c/em\u003e","Viktor Krum stopped breathing.","His dark, deep-set eyes remained fixed on the center of the parchment.","\u003cem\u003eI kissed him.I am in love with him.James Sirius Potter.\u003c/em\u003e","The words did not process through Viktor’s rational mind. Instead, they struck his cerebral cortex like a direct, high-speed collision with an iron Bludger.","His optical nerves completely severed communication with his brain. His heart, which had maintained an athlete\u0027s steady forty-eight beats per minute through three World Cup finals, gave a wild, violent \u003cem\u003eTHUMP\u003c/em\u003e and ceased operation.","His fingers went entirely limp. The parchment fluttered out of his hand, drifting lazily toward the floor.","Viktor Krum’s posture stiffened into a solid, unyielding board of six-foot-two Bulgarian oak. His jaw locked. His eyes glazed over into a flat, milky, catatonic stare directed at the taxidermied head of a wild boar above the mantelpiece.","And then, with the slow, majestic, terrifying grace of a felled redwood tree:","\u003cem\u003eTHUUUUUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","Viktor fell backward. He did not bend his knees. He did not put out his hands. He simply tipped over and hit the thick Persian rug flat on his back, his heavy leather boots pointing straight toward the ceiling, completely and utterly unconscious.","Ten seconds later, the heavy oak door of the study swung open.","Elena Krum—formerly Elena Petrova, a renowned Bulgarian potioneer with cheekbones every bit as sharp as her daughter’s and dark, laughing eyes—walked in carrying a silver tray with a plate of fresh \u003cem\u003ebanitsa\u003c/em\u003e pastries.","She took two steps into the study, paused, and looked down.","Her husband was lying spread-eagled on the rug, unmoving, his eyes wide and glassy, staring blankly at the chandelier.","Elena did not scream. She did not drop the tray. She had been married to Viktor Krum for twenty years; she had seen him hit by bludgeoning hexes, tackled off brooms by angry Irish Chasers, and trampled by an errant Hippogriff during a summer holiday in Greece.","She calmly set the pastry tray on the desk.","She walked around the desk, stepped delicately over Viktor’s left knee, and spotted the fallen piece of parchment lying by his hip.","Elena picked it up. She read it.","A slow, brilliant, utterly delighted smile spread across her face.","She let out a soft, musical laugh that echoed off the timber rafters. \u0026quot;Oh, Valeria,\u0026quot; Elena murmured warmly, her dark eyes shining with maternal pride. \u0026quot;A Potter. Of course. Just like your father... you couldn\u0027t pick an ordinary boy, could you?\u0026quot;","She looked down at her motionless husband.","She reached down, took Viktor’s wrist, and checked his pulse. It was faint, but returning to a steady rhythm.","\u0026quot;Take your time, Viktor,\u0026quot; Elena said pleasantly.","She stepped back over his legs, picked up a warm \u003cem\u003ebanitsa\u003c/em\u003e from the tray, settled into the leather armchair, and took a delicate bite while reading an Herbology journal.","Five minutes passed in peaceful silence.","Then, with a sudden, violent, gasping \u003cem\u003eGAAAAASP\u003c/em\u003e, Viktor Krum’s soul was violently sucked back into his mortal body.","His chest heaved. His hands clawed at the Persian rug. He bolted upright like a vampire rising from a crypt, his face transitioning from pale chalk to a violent, incandescent shade of beet purple.","\u0026quot;MY BROOM!\u0026quot; Viktor roared, his deep voice rattling the glass in the windows. \u0026quot;WHERE IS MY BROOM?! ELENA, WHERE IS MY RACING BROOM?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;In the shed, darling,\u0026quot; Elena said mildly, turning a page of her journal. \u0026quot;Behind the snow shovel.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I AM FLYING TO SCOTLAND!\u0026quot; Viktor bellowed, scrambling to his feet, knocking a chair over in his fury. \u0026quot;I WILL FLY SEVEN HUNDRED MILES! I WILL DESCEND UPON THAT CASTLE LIKE AN AVALANCHE! I WILL FEED THAT BOY TO THE GIANT SQUID! I WILL TEST THE DENSITY OF HIS SKULL WITH A BEATER\u0027S BAT! JAMES SIRIUS POTTER! I WILL TURN HIS TOENAILS INTO CABBAGES!\u0026quot;","He lunged toward the corner where his heavy dragon-horn walking cane stood, ready to summon his robes.","Elena did not flinch. She simply set her pastry down, stood up, walked over to her raging, broad-shouldered husband, and planted one hand flat against the center of his chest.","Viktor stopped dead, breathing like a wounded rhinoceros.","\u0026quot;Viktor,\u0026quot; Elena said, her voice dropping into that calm, lethal tone of absolute marital authority. \u0026quot;Sit.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Elena! He touched our daughter! He put his Gryffindor hands on her—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;She kissed \u003cem\u003ehim\u003c/em\u003e, Viktor. The letter clearly states she stood him up and kissed him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Because he bewitched her! With his... his messy hair and his arrogant British grin! Just like his father! His father was always doing that foolish thing with his glasses!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Harry Potter saved the world, Viktor,\u0026quot; Elena reminded him coolly, raising an eyebrow. \u0026quot;And as I recall, thirty years ago, an internationally famous Bulgarian Seeker flew across Europe, sat in the Hogwarts library for six weeks without saying a word, and invited a British girl named Hermione Granger to the Yule Ball.\u0026quot;","Viktor’s mouth opened.","He closed it.","He looked at his wife, his dark eyes bulging. \u0026quot;That was... that was different. I was a gentleman.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You grunted at her and gave her a water beetle,\u0026quot; Elena pointed out with a smirk. \u0026quot;Valeria is fourteen. She is happy. You are not flying to Scotland to commit murder in front of Albus Dumbledore.\u0026quot;","Viktor stared at the ceiling for a long, agonizing moment. He let out a low, defeated, guttural growl that shook the floorboards.","\u0026quot;Then I write,\u0026quot; Viktor hissed, storming behind his desk and slamming himself into his high-backed chair. \u0026quot;I write to Potter and Granger. Immediately. They will know what their spawn has done!\u0026quot;","He yanked a fresh sheet of heavy parchment toward him, grabbed an eagle-feather quill, dipped it so violently into the ink that black droplets splattered across the blotter, and began to write with furious, slashing strokes.","Elena walked around the desk and leaned over his shoulder, watching the quill fly.","\u003cem\u003ePOTTER.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eYOUR SON IS A MENACE. HE IS A DANGEROUS, IRRESPONSIBLE BROOM-MONKEY WHO LACKS PROPER DISCIPLINE. HE HAS AMBUSHED MY DAUGHTER IN THE DARK OF THE PITCH—\u003c/em\u003e","Elena reached down, calmly plucked the quill from his hand, dipped it in ink, drew a thick line through the words, and wrote in elegant, flowing script:","\u003cem\u003eDear Harry and Hermione,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWe hope this letter finds you both well and enjoying the autumn term.\u003c/em\u003e","Viktor snatched the quill back with a ferocious scowl.","\u003cem\u003eYOUR SON HAS PUT HIS LIPS UPON VALERIA. IF HE ENTERS HER DORMITORY OR BREATHES TOO CLOSELY TO HER FUR CLOAK, I WILL PERSONALLY FLY TO LONDON AND DISMANTLE HIS BROOMSTICK WITH MY BARE HANDS.\u003c/em\u003e","Elena sighed, gently took the quill again, crossed out the threat of violence, and added:","\u003cem\u003eViktor is currently undergoing an acute paternal stroke and has already fallen onto the carpet once today. Valeria has written to us with the very sweet news that she and James have shared their first kiss. She speaks very highly of his flying and his character.\u003c/em\u003e","Viktor snatched it back, his breathing ragged, muttering dark Bulgarian curses under his breath as he added his final, non-negotiable demands:","\u003cem\u003eCURFEW FOR JAMES POTTER MUST BE ENFORCED AT SEVEN O\u0027CLOCK. HE MUST KEEP BOTH FEET ON THE GROUND IN HER PRESENCE. NO UNCHAPERONED BROOM RIDES. I AM WATCHING HIM. I HAVE ENCHANTED BINOCULARS.V. KRUM\u003c/em\u003e","Elena smiled softly, took the quill one last time, and signed beneath his angry, jagged signature:","\u003cem\u003ePlease give our warmest regards to the family. We look forward to seeing you at the First Task in November.Warmly, Elena Krum.\u003c/em\u003e","Viktor folded the parchment with enough force to crease the fibers into dust. He dripped heavy, dark-red wax onto the seam and hammered the heavy Krum signet ring into it.","He stood up, walked over to the Siberian eagle owl, and tied the letter to its leg with tight, military knots.","\u0026quot;Fly,\u0026quot; Viktor commanded darkly, staring into the bird\u0027s amber eyes. \u0026quot;Fly directly to Godric’s Hollow. Deliver this to Harry Potter’s front door. And if his son is there... peck him on the ear.\u0026quot;","The great owl hooted softly, launched from the windowsill, and vanished into the snowy Balkan night, winging its way west toward England.","Viktor stood by the open window, the freezing mountain wind whipping his hair, his arms crossed over his broad chest as he glared out into the dark.","\u0026quot;A Potter,\u0026quot; Viktor growled to the mountains. \u0026quot;God help my blood pressure.\u0026quot;","Beside him, Elena took a bite of her warm pastry, leaned against his shoulder, and smiled serenely into the dark."]},{"num":67,"origNum":37,"title":"Temporal Stress and Diplomatic Cables","wordCount":1862,"paragraphs":["The morning sun filtered softly through the leaded bay windows of the Potter home in Godric’s Hollow, casting a warm, honeyed glow across stacks of Ministry briefings, empty teacups, and a half-eaten plate of Petunia’s homemade scones.","Harry Potter sat at the kitchen table in his shirtsleeves, his messy hair defying gravity as usual, enjoying the rare luxury of an uninterrupted Saturday morning off from the Auror Office.","A sharp, heavy \u003cem\u003eTHUMP\u003c/em\u003e against the glass startled him out of the sports section of the \u003cem\u003eDaily Prophet\u003c/em\u003e.","Perched on the outside sill was a bird that looked less like an owl and more like a feathered boulder. It was an enormous Siberian eagle owl, its piercing orange eyes glaring through the glass with the severe, unblinking discipline of a border guard.","Harry set his tea down, pushed his round glasses up his nose, and opened the window.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Harry murmured, admiring the bird’s massive wingspan as it stepped onto the sill. \u0026quot;Where did you fly in from, the Arctic Circle?\u0026quot;","The owl extended a thick, taloned leg. Attached to it was a heavy scroll of parchment, bound with crimson cord and stamped with a thick seal of dark red wax bearing the two-headed eagle and crossed Quidditch beaters of the Krum family crest.","Harry raised his eyebrows. He and Viktor had maintained a cordial, semi-regular correspondence over the decades—mostly brief, polite notes regarding international broom regulations or updates on junior league tournaments—but a letter arriving in the middle of October was highly unusual.","\u0026quot;Thanks, mate,\u0026quot; Harry said, tossing the owl a rasher of bacon from his breakfast plate.","He broke the wax seal, unrolled the parchment, and began to read.","His eyes scanned the opening lines.","\u003cem\u003ePOTTER.\u003c/em\u003e \u003cem\u003eYOUR SON IS A MENACE. HE IS A DANGEROUS, IRRESPONSIBLE BROOM-MONKEY...\u003c/em\u003e","Harry blinked.","Then his eyes traveled to the neat, elegant feminine handwriting that crossed out the insult:","\u003cem\u003eDear Harry and Hermione... Viktor is currently undergoing an acute paternal stroke and has already fallen onto the carpet once today. Valeria has written to us with the very sweet news that she and James have shared their first kiss...\u003c/em\u003e","Harry froze.","His brain processed the words: \u003cem\u003eValeria. James. First kiss. Quidditch pitch.\u003c/em\u003e","Then came Viktor’s manic, heavy scrawl at the bottom:","\u003cem\u003eHE HAS PUT HIS LIPS UPON VALERIA... CURFEW MUST BE ENFORCED AT SEVEN O\u0027CLOCK... I AM WATCHING HIM. I HAVE ENCHANTED BINOCULARS.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry stared at the parchment.","A single, quiet squeak escaped his throat.","Then his chest heaved.","The laughter didn\u0027t start in his mouth; it erupted from his core like an active volcano. His knees completely gave out. Harry lost his grip on the kitchen table, slid off his chair, and hit the wooden floorboards with a resounding, bone-rattling crash.","\u003cem\u003eTHUUUUMP.\u003c/em\u003e","He didn\u0027t get up. He couldn\u0027t. Harry was rolling on the Persian rug beneath the table, clutching his stomach with both hands, his glasses askew, howling with laughter so violent that he was practically suffocating. Tears of pure, unadulterated mirth streamed down his cheeks.","\u0026quot;A... a paternal stroke!\u0026quot; Harry wheezed, pounding his fist against the floorboards. \u0026quot;He... he fell on the carpet! Viktor Krum fell on his own carpet!\u0026quot;","The kitchen door swung open with a bang.","Hermione Granger-Potter strode into the room, a stack of Department of Magical Law Enforcement files balanced in one arm, her wand tucked into her messy topknot. She stopped dead, staring down at her husband, who was currently kicking his legs in the air like an overturned tortoise.","\u0026quot;Harry?\u0026quot; Hermione demanded, her brow furrowed in deep, practical concern. \u0026quot;What on earth was that thud?! Did the ceiling collapse? Are you having a seizure?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The... the letter!\u0026quot; Harry gasped, holding the parchment up toward her with a trembling, helpless hand. \u0026quot;Read it! Hermione, please... read it before my lungs explode!\u0026quot;","Hermione snatched the parchment with a sharp, exasperated sigh. \u0026quot;Honestly, Harry, if this is another one of George\u0027s exploding greeting cards—\u0026quot;","Her voice cut off.","Hermione’s eyes darted across the page.","The color drained from her face. Then it returned in a violent, furious, incandescent rush of crimson.","Her jaw dropped. The Ministry files in her arms slipped, scattering across the kitchen table in a chaotic blizzard of legal briefs.","\u0026quot;WHAT?!\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked.","It was not her normal voice. It was the terrifying, glass-shattering register she had previously reserved for Rita Skeeter and the Death Eaters.","\u0026quot;JAMES?!\u0026quot; she gasped, clutching the parchment to her chest as if shielding it from dark magic. \u0026quot;Our James?! He... he kissed a girl?! On a cold Quidditch pitch at night?! He is \u003cem\u003efourteen years old\u003c/em\u003e! He is a baby! He was playing with toy dragons and asking for extra toast in his pyjamas practically last Tuesday!\u0026quot;","She began pacing the kitchen floor like a caged panther, her slippers slapping violently against the wood.","\u0026quot;How could this happen?! Where was Minerva?! Where were the Prefects?! And what about his O.W.L. preparation?! He has double Arithmancy on Thursday! You cannot focus on Arithmancy when you are... when you are running around kissing Bulgarian Seekers in the frost! Who authorized this?!\u0026quot;","Harry, who had finally managed to haul himself into a sitting position against the leg of the kitchen table, wiped his streaming eyes with the sleeve of his shirt. He looked up at his pacing, hyperventilating wife with an expression of boundless, affectionate amusement.","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry said softly.","\u0026quot;I’m writing to Dumbledore immediately,\u0026quot; Hermione muttered, her hands waving frantically. \u0026quot;I’m going to have Minerva place an anti-flirtation ward around the Quidditch tower—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione, darling.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;—and curfew at seven o\u0027clock is entirely reasonable! In fact, make it six-thirty! And no unchaperoned—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione.\u0026quot; Harry’s voice dropped into that quiet, steady warmth that had anchored her through Horcrux hunts and Ministry revolutions.","She stopped pacing, glaring down at him with wide, flustered eyes. \u0026quot;What?!\u0026quot;","Harry gave her a slow, crooked, devastatingly familiar Potter grin.","\u0026quot;Remind me,\u0026quot; Harry murmured, resting his chin on his knees, \u0026quot;who was it that dragged me behind a tapestry near the Fat Lady’s portrait in the middle of our third year and kissed me so hard my glasses fell into an umbrella stand?\u0026quot;","Hermione froze.","The air vanished from the kitchen.","The crimson flush that had been confined to her cheeks suddenly detonated, spreading across her neck, over her ears, and straight into her hairline. Her mouth opened, closed, and opened again.","\u0026quot;That... that was entirely different!\u0026quot; Hermione sputtered, her voice leaping up an octave as she desperately tried to invoke the legendary Granger defense. \u0026quot;That was... there was intense temporal stress! There were Dementors surrounding the castle! Sirius was on the run! The atmospheric conditions were unprecedented!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You kissed me twice,\u0026quot; Harry pointed out, his green eyes dancing behind his spectacles. \u0026quot;And then you told me my hair was stupid and made me do my Charms essay.\u0026quot;","Hermione made a soft, strangled sound in the back of her throat.","Finding herself with zero logical counterarguments, the Deputy Head of Magical Law Enforcement executed the instinctive, ancestral maneuver she had perfected over two decades of marriage: she stepped forward, buried her burning face directly into Harry’s shoulder, and let out a long, muffled groan.","\u003cem\u003eThe Ostrich Maneuver.\u003c/em\u003e","Harry chuckled, wrapping his arms around her waist as she hid in his shirt. \u0026quot;He’s fourteen, Hermione. And he’s our son. If he’s anything like his father, he’s probably spent the last three weeks completely terrified of her.\u0026quot;","Hermione sighed into his collar, her tension finally melting away. \u0026quot;She’s Viktor’s daughter, Harry. She’s probably tougher than he is.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Which means James has met his match,\u0026quot; Harry smiled, kissing the crown of her head. \u0026quot;Come on. Let’s write back to Viktor before he actually charters a private flight to murder our boy.\u0026quot;","Hermione grumbled, but she pulled away, smoothing her hair with an authoritative sniff. She dragged a chair out, summoned a bottle of emerald ink and an eagle-feather quill from her desk, and pulled a fresh sheet of heavy parchment toward her.","\u0026quot;I am handling the diplomatic tone,\u0026quot; Hermione declared firmly. \u0026quot;You are not allowed to encourage him.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I would never,\u0026quot; Harry lied smoothly, pulling up a chair beside her and leaning over her shoulder, resting his chin in his hand.","Hermione dipped her quill and began to write:","\u003cem\u003eDear Viktor and Elena,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThank you for your letter, which Harry and I received this morning with a mixture of immense surprise, great relief, and—in Harry’s case—a rather undignified amount of laughter.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Tell him his threat about the Bludger was very nostalgic,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","\u0026quot;I am not writing that!\u0026quot; Hermione swatted his arm, continuing her script:","\u003cem\u003ePlease be assured that we share your desire for our children to remain safe, sensible, and focused on their academic studies. However, having known James for fourteen years, we can assure you that beneath his theatrical flying and chaotic hair, he is a boy of deep integrity and kindness.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Tell him James takes after his mother in being hopelessly bossed around by fierce women,\u0026quot; Harry piped up.","Hermione paused, glared at him sideways, and wrote:","\u003cem\u003eJames has, fortunately, inherited enough common sense to know when he is vastly outmatched. If Valeria is half as formidable as her parents, James will be on his best behavior.\u003c/em\u003e","Hermione glanced at Harry. \u0026quot;Now, regarding the curfew?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, absolutely,\u0026quot; Harry grinned. \u0026quot;Tell Viktor that if he wants to enforce a seven o\u0027clock curfew, he needs to talk to McGonagall. Minerva won\u0027t even let the House Ghosts enforce curfew before nine.\u0026quot;","Hermione shook her head, but added:","\u003cem\u003eWe will, of course, owl James this afternoon to remind him of the importance of manners, personal space, and respecting international delegations. We completely agree that broom rides should be strictly confined to daylight hours.\u003c/em\u003e","She paused, looking down at the letter with a soft, affectionate smile, and penned the final lines:","\u003cem\u003eElena, I hope you have managed to get Viktor off the floor. Tell him that Harry offers his deepest sympathies for his blood pressure, but suggests he invest in a mug of Chamomile tea rather than an international flight.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWe cannot wait to see you both at the First Task in November.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWith our warmest regards,Hermione and Harry\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Perfect,\u0026quot; Harry approved, reaching over to sign his messy, looping signature beside her neat cursive.","Hermione folded the parchment, sealed it with their family crest, and turned to the massive Siberian owl, who was currently preening its feathers on the back of a kitchen chair.","Harry tied the letter securely to the bird’s leg.","\u0026quot;Safe flight back to Sofia, big fellow,\u0026quot; Harry patted the owl’s broad head. \u0026quot;Tell Viktor his boy is in good hands.\u0026quot;","With a soft, resonant hoot, the Siberian eagle owl launched itself from the chair, spread its massive wings, and soared out through the open window, climbing high into the autumn sky toward the east.","Harry leaned against the windowsill, watching the speck vanish into the clouds. He slipped an arm around Hermione’s waist, pulling her close.","\u0026quot;Our boy\u0027s growing up, Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry whispered.","Hermione rested her head on his shoulder, letting out a quiet, bittersweet sigh.","\u0026quot;I know,\u0026quot; she murmured softly. \u0026quot;I just hope Hogwarts\u0027 roof is insured for when Viktor Krum arrives in November.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":68,"origNum":38,"title":"Silk, Solder, and the Pyrenean Accord","wordCount":1384,"paragraphs":["The powder-blue carriage of the Beauxbatons delegation, parked gracefully near the edge of the Forbidden Forest, was a masterpiece of French luxury. Inside, the space expanded into a sun-warmed Parisian salon of cream-colored silk, delicate gilded furniture, and the faint, perpetual scent of blooming lavender and white peaches.","At a small, Louis XIV writing desk by an oval window, Céleste Laurent dipped a slender silver quill into a pot of violet ink.","Her porcelain cheeks were still flushed with a delicate, rosy warmth. Her fingers trembled just enough to make the silver nib scatter microscopic specks of ink onto the heavy, scented vellum, but her violet eyes were shining with the calm, luminous certainty of an elemental force that had finally found its anchor.","She wrote with elegant, flowing French calligraphy:","\u003cem\u003eChers Maman et Papa,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThe Scottish highlands are as damp and unruly as Madame Maxime warned us, but the castle has a certain... ancient charm.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eI am writing to share news that will undoubtedly surprise you. For three weeks, I have endured the usual parade of English and Durmstrang boys whose faculties reliably dissolve the moment I breathe in their direction. It was, as always, exceptionally tedious.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eUntil I met Thomas.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eHis name is Thomas Vernon Dursley. He is a Ravenclaw.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eHe is not a duelist. He does not write poetry. He does not wear silk. He is broad-shouldered, immovable, and built with the solid, comforting strength of an ancient oak tree. While other boys recite terrible sonnets, Thomas repairs the castle’s moving staircases with enchanted bronze bushings and a leather tool belt.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003ePapa, my allure does not affect him. Not in the slightest. When I released the glamour of the Pyrenees, he merely adjusted his spectacles and told me the hall had poor thermal insulation.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eToday, on the third-floor landing, I grew tired of waiting. I asked him down from his stepladder, and I kissed him.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eMaman, his mind was confused for two seconds, and then he simply lifted me into the air. He held me off the floor with his bare hands as if I weighed no more than a feather, and he held me with such fierce, unshakeable certainty that the entire castle stopped spinning.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eHe looks at me, and he does not see a creature of myth to be worshipped. He sees me. He asks me to hold his blueprints, and he smiles when I ask him about gear ratios.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eI have chosen him.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWith all my love,Your daughter, Céleste\u003c/em\u003e","Céleste sealed the letter with a drop of shimmering mother-of-pearl wax, stamping it with the Laurent crest—a silver swan perched atop a blooming lily.","She walked to the carriage window, releasing her personal messenger: a pure-white dove whose feathers hummed with gentle, warm magic. The dove took flight into the crisp Scottish twilight, heading south across the Channel toward the sun-drenched valleys of southern France.","Six hundred miles away, perched high in the limestone cliffs overlooking the Dordogne river, stood the Château Laurent.","It was a palace of white stone, terraced vineyards, and cascading waterfalls that caught the warm Mediterranean breeze. In the sunlit morning room, Lord Jean-Luc Laurent and Lady Vivienne Laurent were taking their breakfast on the marble terrace.","Both were pure-blooded Veelas—tall, impossibly beautiful, with hair like spun platinum and silver, carrying the timeless, aristocratic poise of French magical nobility.","The white dove fluttered down from the azure sky, landing delicately on the silver marmalade dish.","\u0026quot;A letter from our little swan,\u0026quot; Vivienne smiled, her voice like chimes in the wind as she untied the vellum.","Jean-Luc, who was casually buttering a croissant with effortless elegance, looked up. \u0026quot;I assume she is writing to complain about the Scottish cuisine? Or perhaps to ask for more cashmere cloaks? The northern dampness is dreadful for the complexion.\u0026quot;","Vivienne broke the seal. She read the letter in silence.","Her violet eyes widened slightly. Her delicate eyebrows rose into high, graceful arches.","Then, Lady Vivienne Laurent did something she rarely did in the presence of the domestic staff: she pressed a manicured hand to her lips and let out a soft, delighted gasp.","\u0026quot;Jean-Luc,\u0026quot; she murmured, looking across the table at her husband. \u0026quot;Read this.\u0026quot;","Jean-Luc took the vellum, his brow furrowing in mild curiosity. As his eyes moved down the lines of elegant script, his expression cycled through several distinct phases: aristocratic bewilderment, utter astonishment, and finally, a deep, resonant, patrician chuckle.","\u0026quot;A... a builder?\u0026quot; Jean-Luc asked, looking at his wife in sheer, fascinated disbelief. \u0026quot;A boy named \u003cem\u003eThomas Vernon Dursley\u003c/em\u003e who carries monkey wrenches and lectures her on thermal insulation?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And who lifted her off the floor with his bare hands,\u0026quot; Vivienne pointed out, her eyes dancing with warm, maternal satisfaction. \u0026quot;Jean-Luc, you know how heavy our bloodline can be for young men. Most wizards either cower before our daughters or treat them like museum exhibits. But this boy... he treated our Céleste like an apprentice, and when she kissed him, he held her like a man.\u0026quot;","Jean-Luc leaned back in his wrought-iron chair, running a hand through his silvery hair, gazing out over their sunlit vineyards.","\u0026quot;Dursley,\u0026quot; Jean-Luc mused, tasting the English name. \u0026quot;I know the family lineage. Thomas’s father, Dudley Dursley, is a legendary Muggle heavyweight athlete who was knighted by their Queen for philanthropy, and his cousin is Harry Potter. The Dursleys are known for their formidable constitution and unshakeable practicality.\u0026quot;","A warm, fond smile settled onto the French patriarch’s handsome face.","\u0026quot;An unbothered Englishman,\u0026quot; Jean-Luc nodded slowly, satisfied. \u0026quot;A man who will not faint when she sneezes. A man whose feet are planted so firmly into the earth that even a Veela\u0027s storm cannot shake him. Yes... our Céleste has chosen exceptionally well.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We must write to his parents,\u0026quot; Vivienne decided immediately, pushing her teacup aside. \u0026quot;It is the proper way. The English value propriety, and Dudley and Chloe Dursley have raised a boy of remarkable substance.\u0026quot;","Jean-Luc summoned an embossed sheet of cream parchment with gilded edges and an antique French fountain pen.","Unlike the thunderous, manic threats of Viktor Krum, the Laurent family approached diplomacy with the velvet grace of seasoned courtiers. Jean-Luc drafted the letter with exquisite, formal penmanship, while Vivienne added touches of warm, motherly charm:","\u003cem\u003eTo Mr. Dudley and Mrs. Chloe Dursley,Number Four, Privet Drive, Little Whinging, Surrey\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eDear Mr. and Mrs. Dursley,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWe send you our most cordial greetings from Château Laurent in the south of France.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWe have this morning received a correspondence from our daughter, Céleste, who is currently residing at Hogwarts as part of the Beauxbatons delegation. She writes to us with profound affection regarding your son, Thomas Vernon.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eAs pure-blooded Veelas, our family has long understood that the greatest burden of magical beauty is the rarity with which one is truly seen. Céleste has informed us of Thomas’s extraordinary intellect, his devotion to his craft, and his complete, magnificent immunity to superficial charms.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eTo learn that your son offered her an expanded seat, explained the mechanics of castle architecture, and met her affections with such unhesitating, protective strength has brought immense joy and relief to our household. It is abundantly clear that Thomas possesses the noble character and unyielding fortitude of his parents.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWe understand that you may be attending the First Task of the Triwizard Tournament in November. We would be deeply honored if you would join us in the Beauxbatons hospitality pavilion for a glass of Château Laurent vintage and an exchange of acquaintance.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003ePlease convey our fondest regards to your family, and accept our deepest appreciation for the young man you have raised.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWith our highest esteem and warmest regards,Lord Jean-Luc and Lady Vivienne Laurent\u003c/em\u003e","Jean-Luc inspected the parchment, nodding with patrician approval, while Vivienne added a small, fragrant sprig of dried French lavender into the envelope before sealing it with their silver swan crest.","\u0026quot;There,\u0026quot; Vivienne smiled, handing the letter to their regal, silver-crested barn owl. \u0026quot;That should set the proper tone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Indeed,\u0026quot; Jean-Luc chuckled softly, watching the owl take off into the morning sky, winging its way toward the English suburbs. \u0026quot;I look forward to meeting this Mr. Dudley Dursley. A man whose son can lift a Veela by the waist and fix a staircase in the same afternoon is a man worth sharing a bottle of wine with.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":69,"origNum":39,"title":"The Surrey Blueprint and the French Lavender","wordCount":1641,"paragraphs":["Sunday morning at Number Four, Privet Drive was an institution of British suburban tranquility.","The front lawn was mowed to a precise three-eighths of an inch, the scent of sizzling bacon drifted from the kitchen, and the kettle on the stove was whistling its cheerful, domestic tune.","Dudley Dursley sat at the polished oak dining table, his massive, heavyweight boxer’s frame occupying nearly the entire width of a reinforced armchair. He was wearing a cozy grey woolen jumper with the sleeves pushed up over his thick, scarred forearms, carefully spreading thick strawberry jam across a piece of golden-brown toast.","Across from him, Chloe Dursley was humming softly as she poured two steaming mugs of strong breakfast tea, her brown hair pinned up in a loose, comfortable knot.","Over the years, the Dursleys had grown thoroughly accustomed to the magical postal system. They regularly received scuffed, soot-stained owls from Harry and Hermione, enthusiastic red envelopes from the Burrow that occasionally buzzed with Weasley clockwork, and the occasional terrifyingly brisk falcon from Draco Malfoy containing box-seat tickets to the Quidditch World Cup.","However, nothing in twenty years of marriage had prepared them for what landed on their kitchen windowsill at precisely nine-fifteen that morning.","There was no unceremonious crashing into the rhododendron bushes. There was no clattering against the glass.","Instead, three delicate, musical taps sounded against the window pane.","\u003cem\u003eTing. Ting. Ting.\u003c/em\u003e","Chloe turned around, tea mug in hand, and blinked. \u0026quot;Dudley... darling, look at this bird.\u0026quot;","Perched on the sill was the most aristocratic creature that had ever graced Little Whinging. It was a regal, silver-crested French barn owl with feathers that looked as though they had been individually brushed and shampooed. Its amber eyes were calm and dignified, and around its left leg was tied a thick envelope of heavy cream vellum, sealed with shimmering mother-of-pearl wax and tied with an azure silk ribbon.","Faintly, drifting through the seam of the window, was the undeniable aroma of wild French lavender and white peaches.","\u0026quot;Blimey,\u0026quot; Dudley muttered, setting his toast down. His broad face broke into a look of cautious bewilderment. \u0026quot;Did Harry send something from the Ministry? That bird looks like it costs more than my first car.\u0026quot;","Dudley walked over and pushed open the window.","The owl did not hop aggressively into the room. It stepped inside with a soft, elegant rustle of feathers, paused on the linoleum, and politely wiped both of its taloned feet against the corner of the tea towel on the counter before extending its leg.","\u0026quot;Well, aren\u0027t you polite,\u0026quot; Chloe smiled, reaching out to stroke the bird\u0027s silky chest feathers.","Dudley carefully untied the silk ribbon and took the envelope. He broke the pearlescent seal, releasing a small sprig of dried lavender that fluttered onto the table.","He unfolded the heavy, gold-edged vellum. Chloe leaned over his broad shoulder, and together, the two of them read the letter.","Silence descended over the kitchen.","The kettle gave a final hiss. The clock on the wall ticked.","Dudley’s jaw slowly dropped.","Chloe’s hands flew to her mouth, her eyes widening to the size of saucers.","\u0026quot;Lord... Lord Jean-Luc Laurent?\u0026quot; Dudley read aloud, his deep voice trembling with sheer, unadulterated shock. \u0026quot;Château Laurent? \u003cem\u003ePure-blooded Veelas?!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A Veela, Dudley!\u0026quot; Chloe gasped, clutching his shoulder with trembling fingers. \u0026quot;Thomas has... a French Veela is in love with our Tommy?!\u0026quot;","Dudley continued reading, his eyes scanning the lines of elegant French cursive:","\u003cem\u003e...To learn that your son offered her an expanded seat, explained the mechanics of castle architecture, and met her affections with such unhesitating, protective strength has brought immense joy and relief to our household...\u003c/em\u003e","Dudley stopped.","He stared at the words: \u003cem\u003emet her affections with such unhesitating, protective strength...\u003c/em\u003e","Then his eyes found the sentence Céleste had written to her parents: \u003cem\u003ehe simply lifted me into the air... held me with his bare hands as if I weighed no more than a feather...\u003c/em\u003e","A slow, colossal grin began to spread across Dudley Dursley’s face. It started in the corners of his eyes and erupted across his entire heavyweight features.","\u0026quot;HE LIFTED HER!\u0026quot; Dudley roared, slamming a massive fist onto the table so hard the marmalade jar bounced. \u0026quot;CHLOE! HE LIFTED HER OFF HER FEET!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Dudley, keep your voice down, the neighbors—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I don\u0027t care about the neighbors! The boy used the deadlift form! He bent his knees and drove through the hips! That’s the garage training! I told him core strength matters!\u0026quot; Dudley was practically vibrating in his chair, laughing with pure, bursting fatherly pride. \u0026quot;A French Veela princess, Chloe! And our boy gave her thirty-six inches of oak, told her the windows were drafty, and then hoisted her in the air like a sack of training weights!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, Dudley,\u0026quot; Chloe laughed, tears of pure joy and affection shining in her eyes as she re-read the letter. \u0026quot;Listen to how they write about him. They aren\u0027t angry. They’re... they’re grateful. They love that he’s so steady. That he treats her like a real person.\u0026quot;","She rested her forehead against Dudley’s cheek, her heart swelling with warmth. \u0026quot;He’s just like you, Dud. Big, solid, and so kind that even magic can\u0027t confuse him.\u0026quot;","Dudley softened, wrapping an arm around his wife’s waist and pulling her close against his side. \u0026quot;He’s a good lad, Chloe. The best.\u0026quot;","Beside them on the breakfast bar, the French barn owl gave a soft, patient hoot. It tilted its head, blinking its amber eyes.","\u0026quot;Oh, goodness,\u0026quot; Chloe gasped, stepping back and wiping a happy tear from her cheek. \u0026quot;The messenger is waiting for an answer! We can\u0027t send it back hungry.\u0026quot;","Chloe immediately went to the fridge, carved three thick slices of roast chicken breast from yesterday’s dinner, arranged them neatly on a small china saucer, and set it before the owl. The bird gave a low, appreciative coo and began to eat with delicate, refined pecks.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Dudley said, rolling up his jumper sleeves and pulling a heavy wooden stationery box from the sideboard. \u0026quot;We have to write back. Lord and Lady Laurent... blimey, Chloe, how do we write to French lords without sounding like complete plonkers?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We write from the heart, darling,\u0026quot; Chloe said gently, pulling up a chair beside him and handing him a nice pen. \u0026quot;Just tell them who we are, and how much we love their daughter already.\u0026quot;","Dudley took a deep breath, dipped his pen, and began to write in his neat, sturdy athlete’s handwriting:","\u003cem\u003eDear Lord Jean-Luc and Lady Vivienne Laurent,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThank you from the bottom of our hearts for your wonderful letter. Receiving it this morning at our breakfast table in Surrey was the greatest surprise of our lives.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWhen our son Thomas was born, he was the quietest baby we’d ever seen. He didn\u0027t cry; he just stared at the gears of the ceiling fan. By age five, he had disassembled every clock in our house to see how they worked. His grandfather Vernon has always been a man who respects solid craftsmanship and practical engineering, and Thomas definitely inherited that trait.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eHearing that he offered Céleste a seat and worried about her catching a draft made us laugh until we cried—that is Thomas through and through. But hearing how deeply he cares for her, and how safe she feels in his arms, means more to us than any magical title or trophy in the world.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThomas has always been a quiet boy who keeps his feelings locked behind his schematics. For him to lift Céleste off her feet means she has truly unlocked his heart. Please tell your daughter that she has already brought so much light into his life.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWe would be absolutely delighted and honored to join you in the Beauxbatons pavilion during the First Task in November. Dudley would be thrilled to share a glass of your French vintage—though you may have to explain to him which glass is for the wine and which is for the water!\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eThank you for your warmth, your kindness, and for raising such a brave, wonderful girl who could see the heart inside our gentle giant.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWith our deepest respect and warmest regards,Dudley and Chloe Dursley\u003c/em\u003e","Dudley paused, looked at the pen, and grinned. He added a small note at the very bottom:","\u003cem\u003eP.S. (From Dudley) - Tell Thomas that his deadlift form sounded impeccable, but he needs to make sure he keeps his lower back straight when lifting French nobility.\u003c/em\u003e","Chloe burst out laughing, swatting his shoulder affectionately. \u0026quot;Dudley! You did not just write that!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I had to!\u0026quot; Dudley chuckled unrepentantly. \u0026quot;It’s standard athletic coaching!\u0026quot;","Chloe shook her head, smiling fondly, and signed her name with a small, drawn heart beside Dudley’s bold signature.","She folded the letter, slipped it into an envelope, and tied it with a neat twine ribbon. She walked over to the silver owl, who had cleanly polished off the chicken and was now gently preening its chest feathers.","Dudley tied the letter securely to the bird’s leg.","\u0026quot;Safe flight back to France, mate,\u0026quot; Dudley patted the owl’s sleek head with a massive, gentle finger. \u0026quot;Give our best to the family.\u0026quot;","The silver owl gave a soft, melodic hoot of acknowledgment, spread its broad wings, and gracefully lifted off from the kitchen counter. It soared through the open window, climbing high into the clear Surrey morning, a streak of shimmering silver flying south toward the sunlit vineyards of the Dordogne.","Dudley stood by the window with his arm around Chloe’s shoulders, watching the bird disappear over the rooftops of Privet Drive.","\u0026quot;A French princess, Chloe,\u0026quot; Dudley murmured softly, shaking his head in quiet wonder. \u0026quot;Our Tommy.\u0026quot;","Chloe rested her head against his chest, listening to the steady, strong beat of his heart.","\u0026quot;Our Tommy,\u0026quot; she agreed softly, smiling into the autumn sunshine. \u0026quot;And she couldn\u0027t have picked a better boy.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":70,"origNum":40,"title":"The Parental Embargo and the Surveillance of Minerva","wordCount":1129,"paragraphs":["The official notification arrived at Godric’s Hollow, Malfoy Manor, the Burrow, and Number Four, Privet Drive via five identical, synchronized owls on the first of November.","It was not a request. It was an executive order.","Drafted with the chilling bureaucratic precision of Cassiopeia Malfoy, cross-referenced with the structural risk assessments of Thomas Vernon Dursley, and signed by all five members of The Pack, the document had come to be known as \u003cstrong\u003eThe First Task Exclusionary Decree\u003c/strong\u003e.","In short: \u003cstrong\u003eThe Parents were banned.\u003c/strong\u003e","\u003cem\u003eUnder no circumstances,\u003c/em\u003e the decree read in Cassie’s sharp, silver-embossed calligraphy, \u003cem\u003ewill \u0027The Management\u0027 be permitted on Hogwarts grounds for the First Task. This includes, but is not limited to: Vernon Dursley attempting to advise the Ministry on dragon-pen security; Lucius Malfoy attempting to purchase the arena concessions; Arthur Weasley attempting to interview the French carriage drivers regarding combustion engines; and Harry Potter hovering on a broomstick in full Auror tactical gear. We are fourteen. We are not toddlers. Stay home.\u003c/em\u003e","Naturally, the decree had caused an international parent crisis. Vernon had blustered about \u0026quot;taxpayer rights\u0026quot; until Petunia reminded him that Hogwarts was funded by an ancient magical endowment; Lucius had threatened to buy the surrounding hills of Hogsmeade just to set up a private viewing pavilion until Narcissa confiscated his cane; and Hermione had spent two solid days pacing her kitchen, drafting a fifteen-page counter-memorandum that Harry had quietly hidden behind the breadbox.","The decree held. The First Task would proceed without parental interference.","Inside the castle, however, an entirely different crisis was brewing: the rumor mill.","For two solid weeks, the corridors had been humming with an intensity that rivaled an overturned beehive. From the Slytherin dungeons to the Gryffindor common room, everyone was talking about the same two impossible, earth-shattering alliances:","\u003cem\u003eJames Sirius Potter had captured Viktor Krum’s daughter.Thomas Vernon Dursley was keeping company with the Beauxbatons Veela.\u003c/em\u003e","Yet, to the immense, agonizing frustration of the student body, nobody could prove a bloody thing.","Neither couple was flamboyant. They did not hold hands in the crowded corridors. They did not carve their initials into the desks in the Charms classroom. They did not disappear behind tapestries to snog like standard, reckless fourth-years.","Instead, they were infuriatingly, maddeningly subtle.","Up on the second floor of the castle, in her high-arched corner office overlooking the Transfiguration Courtyard, Professor Minerva McGonagall stood behind her leaded-glass window.","She was holding a small, brass enchanted spyglass to her eye, her thin lips pressed into a severe, contemplative line, a steaming cup of strong Scottish breakfast tea cooling on her mahogany desk.","Through the crosshairs of the spyglass, McGonagall observed the cobblestone courtyard below.","Walking side by side near the central fountain were James Sirius Potter and Valeria Krum.","They were walking with a precise eighteen inches of space between their shoulders. Both were dressed in standard, immaculate practice gear—James in his scarlet Gryffindor jumper, Valeria in her high-collared Durmstrang training tunic. Their hands were tucked loosely into their pockets.","McGonagall adjusted the focus.","\u0026quot;Look at them,\u0026quot; McGonagall muttered to herself in her sharp Scottish brogue. \u0026quot;Hands to themselves. Posture straight. Heads held high. If they were any more formal, they’d be signing the Treaty of Ghent.\u0026quot;","Down below, James was talking, gesturing with his thumb toward the Quidditch hoops in the distance, his messy black hair catching the crisp autumn breeze. Valeria nodded once, her sharp chin dipping in quiet agreement, her hazel-gold eyes tracking his hand. She said something brief—likely a critique of his turn radius, judging by the familiar, boyish scowl that crossed James’s face—and they continued their walk without a single brush of fingers, a single stolen glance, or a hint of teenage foolishness.","\u0026quot;Not a shred of evidence,\u0026quot; McGonagall mused, shaking her head. \u0026quot;They look like two professional Seekers discussing wind shear. Miss Parkinson swore to me yesterday that they were betrothed by northern blood-rites. Poppycock.\u0026quot;","She slowly panned the brass spyglass toward the eastern cloister.","There, strolling along the covered stone walkway, were Thomas Vernon Dursley and Céleste Laurent.","If James and Valeria were professional athletes, Thomas and Céleste looked like a visiting architect and his client.","Thomas was walking with his steady, heavy Surrey stride, a large leather-bound ledger open in the crook of his elbow, pointing with a wooden ruler at an arched doorway. Beside him, gliding with gossamer elegance in her powder-blue Beauxbatons cloak, was Céleste. She was looking at the ledger, nodding thoughtfully, her silver curls falling over her shoulder as she asked what appeared to be a serious, academic question.","Thomas adjusted his spectacles, made a note with a graphite pencil, and kept walking.","He didn\u0027t touch her. He didn\u0027t gawk at her spun-silver beauty. He didn\u0027t even lean in when she spoke. He maintained a respectful, immaculately calibrated distance of two feet, two inches.","McGonagall lowered the spyglass, blinking in utter bewilderment.","\u0026quot;It makes no sense,\u0026quot; she whispered to the empty office.","The rumors coming from the Prefects were hysterical. The Hufflepuff boys were in mourning. The sixth-year girls in Ravenclaw were holding vigil over snapped quills. Even the House Ghosts were gossiping—Sir Nicholas claimed that a \u0027wave of international amorous energy\u0027 had settled over the third floor.","And yet, watching them from her window, they appeared to be the most disciplined, well-behaved students in the history of the four houses.","\u003cem\u003eToo disciplined.\u003c/em\u003e","Minerva McGonagall had taught three generations of Potters. She had survived James Potter Senior and Sirius Black turning the Great Hall into a skating rink. She had survived Harry Potter, Ron Weasley, and Hermione Granger nearly dismantling the Ministry of Magic before their O.W.L.s.","A Potter did not walk with an eighteen-inch gap of stoic calm unless something monumental was being concealed.","And a Dursley who could engineer pneumatic shock absorbers for trick stairs did not take a French Veela on a walking tour of fourteenth-century doorframes without a motive.","There was a conspiracy. She could feel it in her Scottish bones. They were keeping their distance in public \u003cem\u003especifically\u003c/em\u003e because they were guilty as charged.","McGonagall set the brass spyglass down with a decisive \u003cem\u003eclack\u003c/em\u003e.","She picked up her tea, took a brisk sip, and set the cup back into its saucer.","She needed intelligence. She needed someone whose mind was naturally suspicious, fundamentally cynical, and utterly incapable of being blinded by teenage innocence. Someone who had spent twenty years running an underground intelligence network while brewing poison in the dark.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; McGonagall announced to her sleeping ginger cat on the hearth rug. \u0026quot;That settles it.\u0026quot;","She adjusted her high-collared emerald tartan robes, smoothed her sleeves with two sharp tugs, and strode briskly toward her heavy oak door.","Minerva McGonagall was going down to the dungeons.","It was time to consult Severus Snape."]},{"num":71,"origNum":41,"title":"The Duck Pond Protocol and the Pursuit of Peace","wordCount":1649,"paragraphs":["The dungeons of Hogwarts were, by design, the only part of the castle that remained utterly immune to the emotional climate of the upper floors.","Down here, twenty feet beneath the cold waters of the Black Lake, the stone walls wept silent droplets of mineral moisture. Rows of pickled flobberworms, bicorn horns, and lethifold skins floated in murky jars of preservative fluid, bathed in the sickly, flickering emerald glow of the hearth.","Severus Snape sat at his heavy black walnut desk, an eagle-feather quill in hand, meticulously marking a stack of third-year Potions essays with aggressive, slash-like strokes of red ink.","The heavy dungeon door did not knock. It swung open with the crisp, unmistakable snap of Scottish tartan and absolute academic authority.","Professor Minerva McGonagall strode into the subterranean gloom, her emerald traveling cloak swirling around her ankles. She closed the heavy door firmly behind her, cast a brisk \u003cem\u003eMuffliato\u003c/em\u003e toward the corridor with a flick of her wand, and marched straight to the edge of his desk.","Snape did not look up. His quill slashed another \u003cem\u003eT\u003c/em\u003e for \u003cem\u003eTroll\u003c/em\u003e across a parchment.","\u0026quot;Minerva,\u0026quot; Snape drawled, his voice a low, silky baritone that could have frozen boiling oil. \u0026quot;If you have come to complain about the Slytherin heating ducts again, I assure you, the cold builds character. It keeps them from growing soft, unlike your lions, who require plush cushions to complete their homework.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;This is not about the heating, Severus,\u0026quot; McGonagall said sharply, planting both hands on the front edge of his desk. She leaned in, her eyes narrowed behind her square spectacles. \u0026quot;It is about The Pack.\u0026quot;","The quill paused. A single drop of red ink bloomed on the parchment like a tiny, fresh bloodstain.","Slowly, Snape lifted his chin. His dark, obsidian eyes fixed on her face with profound, world-weary dread.","\u0026quot;I have already told you,\u0026quot; Snape whispered coldly. \u0026quot;I am not holding additional detentions for the Potter boy. If he chooses to fly his broomstick through the goalposts backwards, gravity will eventually resolve the problem on my behalf.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is not about flying,\u0026quot; McGonagall insisted, her voice dropping into a tense, conspiratorial whisper. \u0026quot;The castle is in an absolute frenzy, Severus. The corridors are rife with rumors. They say James Potter and Viktor Krum’s daughter are conducting an illicit, northern romance. They say young Thomas Dursley and the French Veela have formed an unbreakable alliance. Yet, when I observe them from my office window, they walk eighteen inches apart and discuss wind shear and stone masonry! It is unnatural. It is a coordinated, military-grade cover-up.\u0026quot;","Snape’s thin lips curled into a sneer of deep, familiar disdain. \u0026quot;Children walk beside other children, Minerva. It is, regrettably, how the species propagates. It is hardly grounds for a faculty tribunal.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;They are hiding something, Severus!\u0026quot; McGonagall pressed, tapping a finger on the wood. \u0026quot;A Potter does not display eighteen inches of civic modesty without an ulterior motive. You know this! You know what his father was like, and you know what Harry was like! I need proof. The Governors are already writing to me, asking if the Triwizard Tournament is being compromised by international fraternization.\u0026quot;","Snape raised an eyebrow. \u0026quot;And what, precisely, do you expect me to do about it?\u0026quot;","McGonagall stepped closer, her expression turning deadly serious.","\u0026quot;You are the most accomplished Legilimens in the British Isles,\u0026quot; she murmured. \u0026quot;One glance. A single, delicate, surface probe during dinner or when they pass you in the corridor. You don\u0027t need to break their minds, Severus. Just... skim them. A peek into James Potter’s thoughts. A tap on young Dursley’s consciousness. Find out what they are hiding.\u0026quot;","For a fleeting second, the old, dark instincts of the double agent flickered behind Severus Snape’s dark eyes.","A surface probe. It was child\u0027s play. He had picked through the minds of dark wizards, slippery politicians, and three generations of Gryffindor delinquents. James Potter Junior’s mind was undoubtedly an open, chaotic sewer of Quidditch plays, teenage vanity, and suppressed adrenaline—it would take less than half a second to rip through his surface thoughts and extract the truth.","\u0026quot;A simple Legilimency sweep,\u0026quot; Snape mused aloud, a cruel smirk playing on his lips. \u0026quot;It would certainly put an end to the—\u0026quot;","He stopped.","His breath caught in his throat.","The smirk on Snape’s face did not merely fade; it vanished into thin air, replaced by a sudden, ghastly, bloodless paleness.","A terrifying, suppressed memory—buried deep within the reinforced steel vaults of his subconscious—blasted through his mind like a thunderclap.","\u003cem\u003eThe Burrow. Fourteen years ago.\u003c/em\u003e","Snape remembered the crisp summer morning on Molly Weasley’s lawn. He remembered standing over a wooden pram, looking down at an infant girl with dark hair and startling emerald eyes. He had drawn his wand, sneering, intending to perform a routine, harmless Legilimency scan to evaluate the baby\u0027s magical core.","He had touched her mind for one-thousandth of a second.","And then... \u003cem\u003eThe Light.\u003c/em\u003e","The sheer, blinding, incomprehensible solar detonation of Lily Luna Potter’s infant soul. It hadn\u0027t just repelled him; the psychic backlash had hit him like an oncoming freight train of pure, unfiltered joy.","Severus Snape—a man who had stood toe-to-toe with the Dark Lord—had been blasted forty feet backward across the grass like an exploding umbrella, crashing headfirst into Molly Weasley’s ornamental duck pond. He had spent forty-five minutes picking duckweed out of his robes while a four-month-old infant giggled hysterically from her crib, waving her tiny fists in the air.","A cold, involuntary shiver traveled down Snape’s spine, making the hair on the back of his neck stand straight up.","\u003cem\u003eProbe their minds?\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eProbe a group that contained Lily Luna Potter’s solar flare, Cassiopeia Malfoy’s ancestral venom, and a Dursley who approached mental architecture like a reinforced concrete bunker?\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eNever. Not for all the Galleons in Gringotts.\u003c/em\u003e","Snape slammed his red-ink quill onto the desk with enough violence to crack the wood.","He leaned back, his black robes billowing, his face set into a rigid, icy mask of absolute, furious denial.","\u0026quot;No,\u0026quot; Snape snarled, his voice rising from a whisper to a sharp, biting hiss. \u0026quot;Absolutely not.\u0026quot;","McGonagall blinked, startled by the sudden hostility. \u0026quot;Severus? It is merely a surface skim—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is an unmitigated catastrophe waiting to happen!\u0026quot; Snape snapped, his dark eyes flashing. \u0026quot;Minerva, listen to yourself! You are a Deputy Headmistress of Hogwarts, not a bored village gossip! You are standing in my dungeon, asking me to perform high-level mental espionage on fourteen-year-olds because two adolescent girls didn\u0027t trip over their cloaks in the courtyard!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I am merely trying to protect the integrity of the school—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You are listening to the hysterical projections of twelve-year-old Hufflepuffs who believe that sharing a bread roll constitutes an international blood-oath!\u0026quot; Snape stood up, towering over his desk, his sneer returning with full, venomous force. \u0026quot;It is hormones, Minerva! Pointless, noisy, chemically induced adolescent foolishness! The Potter boy is thinking about Quidditch. The Dursley boy is thinking about spanners. If you wish to waste your afternoons staring through brass spyglasses at empty courtyards, that is your prerogative, but leave me out of your theatrical delusions!\u0026quot;","McGonagall stared at him, taken aback by the sheer, unyielding fury of his rebuttal.","She looked at the dark circles under his eyes. She looked at the stack of essays.","Slowly, the tension drained from her shoulders. She let out a long, weary Scottish sigh, adjusting her spectacles with a quiet sniff.","\u0026quot;Perhaps...\u0026quot; McGonagall murmured, her tone softening with reluctant embarrassment. \u0026quot;Perhaps you are right, Severus. The stress of hosting two foreign schools... it has made everyone somewhat jumpy. I apologize for disturbing your grading.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Accepted,\u0026quot; Snape bit out smoothly. \u0026quot;Now, if you will excuse me, I have seventy-four third-years who believe that powdered porcupine quills should be added \u003cem\u003ebefore\u003c/em\u003e the cauldron is taken off the fire. I must go prevent the east corridor from smelling of sulfur.\u0026quot;","McGonagall nodded briskly. \u0026quot;Good day, Severus.\u0026quot;","She turned and strode out of the dungeon, the heavy door clicking shut behind her with a dull, final \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e.","The silence of the subterranean office rushed back in, broken only by the crackle of the green hearth fire and the slow drip of water from the stones.","Severus Snape stood motionless behind his desk for a full minute, listening to her retreating footsteps fade down the corridor.","Then, his shoulders slumped.","He collapsed back into his leather armchair like a deflated accordion, burying his face in both of his long, pale hands, letting out a groan so deep and exhausted it sounded like it came from the center of the earth.","\u003cem\u003eOf course they were hiding it.\u003c/em\u003e","He had eyes. He had seen the way Viktor Krum’s daughter watched James from across the Great Hall. He had seen the Veela girl carrying a brass level behind young Dursley. He had survived the Marauders, he had survived the Golden Trio, and he knew with terrifying, metaphysical certainty that the next generation had already breached every perimeter of sensible behavior.","Something massive, chaotic, and utterly uncontrollable was brewing between The Pack and their foreign guests.","And Severus Snape was going to do absolutely, gloriously nothing about it.","He had survived a war. He had survived the Dark Lord. He had survived running a four-minute mile in the sand of Isla de la Fortuna.","He was fifty-six years old, his knees hurt when it rained, and he simply wanted his peace.","Reaching into the bottom drawer of his desk, Snape pushed aside three bottles of Veritaserum, grabbed a crystal flask of twenty-year-old Ogden’s Old Firewhisky, and poured two generous fingers into his empty teacup.","He raised the cup to the pickled flobberworms on the shelf.","\u0026quot;To complete and utter ignorance,\u0026quot; Snape muttered darkly.","He drank it down in one burning swallow, picked up his red quill, and went straight back to giving Gryffindors failing grades in blissful, deliberate silence."]},{"num":72,"origNum":42,"title":"The Locker Room Inspection and the Northern Bat","wordCount":1265,"paragraphs":["The Scottish November wind howled across the deserted Quidditch pitch, carrying with it the bitter, frosty bite of the approaching winter.","Severus Snape strode through the darkness like a solitary wraith, his heavy wool cloak billowing behind him in midnight-black wings. His routine evening patrol was an exercise in monastic solitude—he purposely chose the Quidditch grounds because it was cold, barren, and at eight-forty-five on a Tuesday evening, guaranteed to be free of the cheerful, noisy human existence he so thoroughly despised.","Or so he had thought.","As he swept past the shadowed arches beneath the wooden stands, his sharp, predatory ears caught an unmistakable, rhythmic disturbance.","\u003cem\u003eCLANG. Thud. Rustle.\u003c/em\u003e","Snape stopped dead in his tracks.","He tilted his head, his obsidian eyes narrowing into lethal slits.","The noise was coming from inside the Gryffindor boys\u0027 changing room. It was not the sound of wind. It was the distinct sound of heavy bodies colliding with metal lockers, accompanied by muffled, breathy gasps and hushed, chaotic rustling.","A cold, vicious smirk curled the corners of Snape’s thin lips.","\u003cem\u003eAha.\u003c/em\u003e","Finally. Contraband.","Undoubtedly, some third-year Gryffindor delinquents were attempting to smuggle dungbombs into the Slytherin showers, or perhaps testing out illegal Wheezes fireworks behind the towel racks.","In the span of three seconds, Snape had already assembled the opening salvo of his verbal execution: \u003cem\u003e\u0027Ten points from Gryffindor for every breath of oxygen you have wasted in this locker room, followed by three weeks of scrubbing flobberworm mucus with your fingernails...\u0027\u003c/em\u003e","Snape drew his wand with a silent, lethal flourish.","He marched to the heavy wooden door, raised a polished leather boot, and kicked the latch open with a thunderous, reverberating crash.","\u003cem\u003eBANG.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;CEASE THIS DEPLORABLE DISPLAY OF—\u0026quot;","The words did not finish.","The syllables choked in Severus Snape’s throat, turning into a strangled, gurgling squeak that died somewhere near his tonsils.","The scene illuminated by the flickering oil lantern was not a dungbomb deployment. It was not an illegal firework demonstration.","It was an Olympic-grade, high-impact, seismic snogging session.","Pinned firmly against a row of scarlet metal lockers was James Sirius Potter.","His Gryffindor practice jersey was half-unbuttoned at the throat, his messy black hair looked as though it had survived an electrical storm, and his long, athletic arms were wrapped with desperate, white-knuckled intensity around the waist of the girl currently occupying his entire personal airspace.","And that girl was Valeria Krum.","Valeria had one leather-booted knee hitched up onto the wooden changing bench for leverage, her short midnight-fox fur cloak cast carelessly over a broom rack, her fingers buried so deeply into James’s unruly black hair that she appeared to be using his scalp for balance. She was kissing him with the fierce, devastating ferocity of an avalanche roaring down the Balkan mountains.","Every time their lips collided, the metal lockers behind James’s shoulders gave a shuddering, violent \u003cem\u003eCLANG\u003c/em\u003e.","Snape stood frozen in the open doorway, his jaw slack, his wand trembling in his hand, his eyes bulging as if he had just witnessed the resurrection of an ancient, multi-headed demon.","\u0026quot;POTTER!\u0026quot; Snape’s voice shattered the locker room air, cracking into a shrill, hysterical roar. \u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eGET OFF THE METALWORK! FIVE HUNDRED FEET APART, THIS INSTANT!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The reaction was instantaneous.","James Sirius Potter detached from Valeria like a man who had just been struck by lightning. His eyes dilated in pure, suffocating terror. He tripped backward over his own Quidditch boots, scrambled for balance, knocked over a bucket of sponge-wash, and hit the wooden bench with a hollow \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e, his face glowing with a shade of scarlet that made his Gryffindor jersey look pale by comparison.","\u0026quot;P-Professor!\u0026quot; James choked out, clawing frantically at the unbuttoned collar of his shirt, his chest heaving as if he had just run a marathon. \u0026quot;We were... we weren\u0027t... we were reviewing! Aerodynamic positioning! The Wronski Feint... it requires a tight turning radius against the... the bulkhead—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;SILENCE!\u0026quot; Snape hissed, his face transitioning from pale chalk to a violent, mottled purple. \u0026quot;Do not dare insult my intelligence with your pathetic Gryffindor drivel, you miserable—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Excuse me.\u0026quot;","The voice cut through the damp locker room air like a chilled steel blade.","Snape’s tirade died instantly.","Valeria Krum did not scramble. She did not blush. She did not even blink.","Slowly, deliberately, she stepped off the wooden bench, standing at her full, imposing height. She casually reached up with both hands, smoothed the raven braid resting over her shoulder, and ran the back of her hand across her mouth, wiping away a trace of James\u0027s crooked smile.","She turned to face the terrifying Potions Master of Hogwarts.","Her stormy, hazel-gold eyes evaluated Severus Snape with the supreme, unbothered contempt of a northern warlord inspecting a mildly annoying insect.","\u0026quot;Under Section Fourteen of the International Educational Charter,\u0026quot; Valeria purred in her low, smoky Bulgarian accent, \u0026quot;faculty members are strictly prohibited from entering student changing facilities unannounced. Are you an international voyeur, Professor? Or simply an overgrown mountain bat with poor boundary management?\u0026quot;","James, who was still slumped on the bench, let out a tiny, whimpering wheeze of pure horror, instinctively covering his face with his hands. \u003cem\u003eShe did not just say that. We are dead. We are both going to be buried in the Forbidden Forest.\u003c/em\u003e","Snape’s mouth opened.","Nothing came out.","His obsidian eyes bulged so far they threatened to pop free from their sockets. A muscle beneath his left eye began to twitch with the violent, rhythmic frequency of a Morse-code transmitter. For thirty years, students had wept, fainted, and wet themselves in his presence.","And this fourteen-year-old Bulgarian girl had just called him an overgrown mountain bat.","\u0026quot;You...\u0026quot; Snape whispered, his voice trembling with an ungodly mixture of rage, shock, and catastrophic disbelief. \u0026quot;You... insolent... foreign...\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Go away, Professor,\u0026quot; Valeria interrupted calmly, crossing her arms over her chest, not giving him a single inch of ground. \u0026quot;We were in the middle of something. Your robes are drafty, and you are letting the cold in.\u0026quot;","She turned her back on him, stepped toward James, and calmly reached down to adjust the crooked collar of his shirt, brushing a stray black lock from his forehead with absolute, domestic casualness.","Severus Snape looked at Valeria.","Then he looked at James, who was staring up at his girlfriend with the dazed, terrified adoration of a puppy that had just watched its mother fight a dragon.","Snape’s hand was shaking so violently his wand tip left a streak of blue sparks in the air.","He didn\u0027t give a detention. He didn\u0027t deduct points. His brain had officially surpassed its capacity for administrative procedure and had entered the realm of apocalyptic despair.","\u0026quot;Dumbledore,\u0026quot; Snape croaked, his voice cracking like dry kindling.","He pointed a long, bony, trembling finger at the two of them.","\u0026quot;I am going to Dumbledore,\u0026quot; Snape snarled, his eyes wild. \u0026quot;If that man does not have you both placed in solitary confinement by sunrise, I will burn this castle to the foundations! I will dismantle the pitch! I WILL PERSONALLY THROW YOUR BROOMS INTO THE SEA!\u0026quot;","With a violent, theatrical sweep that knocked two towels off their hooks, Severus Snape wheeled around, his black cloak whipping like a hurricane.","He stormed out into the howling November gale, slamming the locker room door behind him with enough force to crack the oak lintel.","His boots hit the frosty grass at a full, frantic sprint.","The Dungeon Sprinter was back.","He was storming across the grounds, black robes billowing in the moonlight, heading straight for the Headmaster’s Tower to demand the end of Western Civilization."]},{"num":73,"origNum":43,"title":"Structural Shear and the Convergence of the Traumatized","wordCount":1343,"paragraphs":["At precisely nine o\u0027clock, while Severus Snape was being informed of his poor boundary management down on the Quidditch pitch, Professor Minerva McGonagall was patrolling the fourth-floor Arithmancy corridor.","Her wand tip was illuminated with a soft, steady \u003cem\u003eLumos\u003c/em\u003e, casting long, dancing shadows across the ancient stone walls. Her tartan traveling cloak was pulled tightly against the evening chill, her sensible leather shoes clicking in a calm, rhythmic cadence against the flagstones.","As she approached the shadowed alcove near the ancient tapestry of Barnabas the Barmy, a distinct and peculiar sound caught her ear.","\u003cem\u003eHnnngh. Thud. Gasp. Hrrrgh.\u003c/em\u003e","McGonagall stopped dead.","She cocked her head, her sharp brows knitting together in immediate, schoolmarm disapproval.","It was the sound of heavy, strained breathing, low grunts of physical exertion, and the muffled scrape of shoe leather against solid granite.","McGonagall let out a long, disappointed Scottish sigh, shaking her head in weary dismay.","\u003cem\u003eBoys,\u003c/em\u003e she thought, already rolling her eyes behind her square spectacles. \u003cem\u003eUndoubtedly some foolish fourth-year Gryffindors attempting to deadlift a marble gargoyle to prove their athletic prowess without using a simple Levitation Charm. Honestly, they’ll give themselves severe lumbar strain before their O.W.L.s.\u003c/em\u003e","Drawing her wand to cast an immediate \u003cem\u003eWingardium Leviosa\u003c/em\u003e—and prepare a brisk lecture on the virtues of using magic rather than adolescent muscle—McGonagall rounded the corner with crisp, commanding authority.","\u0026quot;Put that statue down this instant, you foolish boys, before you rupture your—\u0026quot;","The command died in her throat.","Her jaw detached from her skull. Her square spectacles slipped three inches down the bridge of her nose, dangling precariously by the ear-wires.","There was no marble gargoyle. There was no stone furniture being moved.","Pinned firmly against the ancient granite archway was Thomas Vernon Dursley.","Or, more accurately, pinned against the stone archway was Céleste Laurent, who was currently wrapped around Thomas like a gossamer-silk ribbon around an oak pillar.","Thomas had his heavy tool belt discarded on the floor, his shirtsleeves rolled to his thick elbows, his massive boxer’s arms locked securely around Céleste’s back and thighs, effortlessly holding the French Veela three feet in the air. Céleste’s slender legs were hooked firmly around his waist, her delicate silver heels dangling against his hips, her fingers tangled so deeply into his neatly parted brown hair that his spectacles were shoved crooked against his cheek.","And they were kissing.","It was not a sweet, innocent, corridor peck. It was a kiss of such devastating, soul-consuming, high-vacuum intensity that it looked as though they were attempting to extract each other’s internal organs through their teeth. Dementors across the Scottish highlands could only have looked upon the display with humble, professional admiration.","Every time Thomas hoisted her an inch higher to adjust his footing, his chest gave that low, heavy, heavyweight grunt that McGonagall had mistaken for manual labor.","Minerva McGonagall’s Scottish Presbyterian soul exploded into a million pieces.","\u0026quot;MR. DURSLEY!\u0026quot; McGonagall shrieked, her voice hitting a glass-shattering octave that set the suit of armor down the hall vibrating. \u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eMISS LAURENT! CEASE THIS SINFUL CONVULSION AT ONCE!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","The effect was instantaneous.","Thomas Vernon Dursley’s brain suffered a catastrophic structural collapse.","All six feet of broad, dependable Surrey logic vaporized into sheer, unmitigated terror. His grip slipped; he scrambled frantically, setting Céleste down so fast her silver heels clicked sharply against the flagstones. Thomas stumbled backward, knocked over his own brass stepladder with a deafening \u003cem\u003eCLANG\u003c/em\u003e, shoved his glasses frantically up his nose, and pressed his back flat against the wall, his face glowing with a shade of crimson that could have guided ships through heavy fog.","\u0026quot;P-Professor!\u0026quot; Thomas stammered, his deep Surrey bass cracking into a high-pitched squeak. \u0026quot;I... the archway... we were calculating! The dynamic shear resistance! The live load capacity of fourteenth-century mortar joints—my mother will kill me, Aunt Petunia will revoke my tea privileges, I am entirely deceased—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;SILENCE!\u0026quot; McGonagall gasped, clutching her chest, her tartan robes trembling with pure outrage. \u0026quot;Do not dare quote Arithmancy at me while holding a foreign national suspended in mid-air like a sack of oats! Fifty points from Ravenclaw! One hundred points! You will be scrubbing the owlery until your graduation!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Pardon.\u0026quot;","The voice was cool, smooth, and laced with pure, unapologetic Parisian frost.","McGonagall blinked, her fury momentarily interrupted.","Céleste Laurent did not look panicked. She did not blush. She calmly smoothed the front of her powder-blue silk robes, swept her cascading silver-white curls over one shoulder with a languid flick of her wrist, and turned her luminescent violet eyes upon the Deputy Headmistress.","She looked at McGonagall as if the professor were a poorly dressed pigeon that had wandered into a Michelin-starred restaurant.","\u0026quot;Is zere not an official European educational statute,\u0026quot; Céleste purred with icy, aristocratic disdain, \u0026quot;strictly prohibiting faculty members from voyeuring upon students during private personal hours? Because if zere is, Madame Deputy Headmistress, I am fully prepared to invoke it with Madame Maxime immediately. You are interrupting an extremely delicate cultural exchange.\u0026quot;","Thomas let out a faint, dying whimper against the wall, sliding down two inches. \u003cem\u003ePlease stop talking. She is going to transfigure us into teacups.\u003c/em\u003e","McGonagall stared at Céleste.","Her mouth opened. Her nostrils flared so wide they looked like twin dark tunnels.","\u0026quot;Cultural... \u003cem\u003ecultural exchange?!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot; McGonagall choked, her voice shaking with an ungodly mixture of fury and disbelief. \u0026quot;You were attempting to inhale his tonsils, young lady! In an open corridor! Before curfew!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He was testing my weight distribution,\u0026quot; Céleste replied smoothly, crossing her arms, her chin held high. \u0026quot;And his technique is flawless. Good evening, Professor.\u0026quot;","She reached out, casually took Thomas by his limp, trembling hand, and gave it a gentle, possessive squeeze.","Minerva McGonagall had reached her absolute, definitive limit.","Her Scottish patience, forged through fifty years of teaching, had finally snapped like dry heather in a wildfire.","\u0026quot;That is it,\u0026quot; McGonagall hissed, her eyes blazing behind her spectacles. She pointed a sharp, trembling finger down the corridor. \u0026quot;That is the absolute end! I have had enough of this international anarchy! I am going straight to Albus Dumbledore! We are placing this entire castle under martial law!\u0026quot;","With a furious, violent swish of her emerald robes, McGonagall wheeled around.","She didn\u0027t walk; she marched. She swept down the corridor like an angry Highland storm, her shoes striking the flagstones with the force of small artillery shells, heading straight for the central staircase toward the Headmaster’s Tower.","As she reached the grand third-floor landing near the gargoyle, the massive oak doors leading to the grounds burst open with a violent shudder.","Stumbling through the entrance hall, looking like a man who had barely escaped an artillery bombardment, was Severus Snape.","His black robes were soaked with river mist and wind, his hair was plastered wild across his forehead, and his chest was heaving with the ragged, desperate breath of a man who had sprinted three-quarters of a mile in heavy boots.","McGonagall stopped dead on the bottom stair.","Snape stopped dead on the flagstones.","The two professors stared at each other across the torchlit hall.","McGonagall’s spectacles were crooked, her face flushed red with Scottish fury. Snape’s robes were disheveled, his eyes wide with dark, twitching, unhinged madness.","\u0026quot;The locker room,\u0026quot; Snape gasped out between wheezing breaths, clutching his ribcage, his voice a ragged hiss. \u0026quot;Potter. The Bulgarian girl. Pinned to the lockers. She... she called me an overgrown mountain bat.\u0026quot;","McGonagall’s jaw dropped.","Then she pointed a shaking finger toward the upper stairs.","\u0026quot;The Arithmancy corridor,\u0026quot; McGonagall snarled, her voice vibrating with rage. \u0026quot;Young Dursley. The Veela. Hoisted in the air like a chandelier. She... she threatened me with international voyeurism statutes!\u0026quot;","The two ancient, battle-hardened educators stared into each other\u0027s eyes.","A silent, telepathic understanding passed between them: \u003cem\u003eThe asylum was officially being run by the inmates.\u003c/em\u003e","Without exchanging another word, in unified, synchronized, furious desperation, Minerva McGonagall and Severus Snape charged up the final flight of stairs toward the stone gargoyle.","They were going to Dumbledore.","And heaven help the Headmaster if he was wearing that bloody Hawaiian shirt."]},{"num":74,"origNum":44,"title":"The Diplomatic Miracle and the Titanium Livers","wordCount":1639,"paragraphs":["The gargoyle guarding the entrance to the Headmaster’s Tower barely had time to leap aside before the heavy oak door was kicked open with the combined, seismic fury of two senior faculty members on the verge of complete emotional disintegration.","Albus Dumbledore was sitting behind his claw-footed mahogany desk, comfortably draped in an eye-searing silk lounging robe patterned with neon-yellow pineapples and sequined hibiscus flowers. He was peacefully humming a bawdy muggle sea shanty while using silver tweezers to feed a candied lemon slice to Fawkes the phoenix.","He did not even have the opportunity to say \u0026quot;Sherbet Lemon.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;ALBUS!\u0026quot; Minerva McGonagall and Severus Snape bellowed in terrifying, overlapping, stereophonic harmony.","\u0026quot;Potter!\u0026quot; Snape hissed, slamming both palms onto the edge of Dumbledore\u0027s desk, his greasy hair flying wild, his dark eyes bulging with manic energy. \u0026quot;The Gryffindor locker room! Metal lockers! Unbuttoned to the sternum! The Krum girl was using his scalp for balance, Albus! And when I intervened, she looked me in the eye and called me an overgrown mountain bat with poor boundary management! I demand their immediate expulsion! I demand an international tribunal! I demand that pitch be salted so no grass may ever grow upon it again!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And the Arithmancy corridor!\u0026quot; McGonagall shrieked, her tartan cloak trembling as she shook a trembling fist in the air. \u0026quot;Young Dursley, Albus! Deadlifting the Veela against the archway like a chandelier! She had her legs wrapped around his waist, and they were engaged in a kiss of such terrifying vacuum intensity that I genuinely believed his internal organs were being extracted! And when I deducted points, the French girl threatened me with European voyeurism litigation! The boy claimed he was testing structural shear! It is anarchy! The school is lost!\u0026quot;","For a full thirty seconds, the circular office echoed with the sound of their ragged, gasping breaths.","On his golden perch, Fawkes blinked slowly, tucked his head under his wing, and went back to sleep. The portraits of former headmasters along the curved walls were leaning forward in their gilded frames, clutching their painted spectacles in sheer, delighted disbelief.","Albus Dumbledore did not shout. He did not jump.","He slowly set down his silver tweezers. He lowered his half-moon spectacles down the bridge of his crooked nose and evaluated his two most battle-hardened lieutenants with calm, unblinking, serene amusement.","\u0026quot;Minerva. Severus,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly, his voice a warm, gentle rumble of grandfatherly affection. \u0026quot;Please. Sit down before your cardiovascular systems stage an armed rebellion against your ribcages.\u0026quot;","With a languid wave of his slender wand, two plush, high-backed armchairs upholstered in velvet slid smoothly across the stone floor, bumping gently against the backs of their knees.","Neither of them sat. They stood, trembling with rage.","\u0026quot;Sit,\u0026quot; Dumbledore commanded with a pleasant, immovable smile.","Defeated by the furniture, McGonagall dropped into her chair with a sharp, furious huff, while Snape collapsed into his like a bundle of wet black laundry.","Dumbledore waved his wand again.","A silver tray floated from the sideboard, bearing a steaming porcelain pot of strong, restorative Earl Grey tea for McGonagall. And floating right beside it was a heavy, cut-crystal decanter of twenty-year-old Ogden’s Old Firewhisky, which tipped itself generously over a heavy glass tumbler and filled it to the brim with amber fire for Snape.","With a theatrical flick of his wrist, Dumbledore splashed three healthy fingers of the Firewhisky directly into McGonagall’s tea.","\u0026quot;Drink,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said cheerfully. \u0026quot;You both look as though you’ve just gone twelve rounds with a Hungarian Horntail.\u0026quot;","Snape didn\u0027t wait. He seized the tumbler and drained half of the burning liquid in one desperate, shuddering swallow, letting out a ragged wheeze. McGonagall gripped her teacup with white knuckles, took a massive gulp of the fortified Earl Grey, and glared over the rim.","\u0026quot;Well, Albus?!\u0026quot; McGonagall demanded, her voice tight. \u0026quot;What are you going to do about it?!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore leaned back in his high-backed chair, folded his hands over his pineapple-patterned stomach, and smiled.","It was not a smirk. It was a massive, beaming, radiant smile of pure, unfiltered, heartwarming joy. His blue eyes twinkled with so much light they could have illuminated a lighthouse.","\u0026quot;Isn\u0027t it wonderful?\u0026quot; Dumbledore murmured softly, sighing with profound contentment.","The silence that fell over the office was absolute.","Snape’s tumbler froze halfway to his mouth. A drop of amber Firewhisky dripped onto his black sleeve.","McGonagall’s jaw slowly dropped.","\u0026quot;W-Wonderful?\u0026quot; Snape croaked, his voice pitching up an octave into hysterical disbelief. \u0026quot;Did you... did your sequined robes constrict the blood flow to your brain, Albus?! I was called a \u003cem\u003emountain bat\u003c/em\u003e! In my own facility!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And I was threatened with the European Court of Human Rights!\u0026quot; McGonagall shouted, slamming her teacup into its saucer with a sharp \u003cem\u003eclatter\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;By a fourteen-year-old in powdered silk!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Oh, come now!\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled, waving a hand in airy dismissal. \u0026quot;For three centuries, the Triwizard Tournament was an unmitigated disaster of suspicion, bitterness, and dark hexes traded in the shadows! Schools arrived with armed guards! Champions poisoned each other\u0027s brooms! It was a geopolitical catastrophe disguised as an athletic competition!\u0026quot;","Dumbledore leaned forward, his eyes shining with pure delight.","\u0026quot;And now? Look at what has happened! A Potter is fostering deep, passionate diplomatic relations with Durmstrang in the privacy of the locker room! While a Dursley is demonstrating the unyielding, physical reliability of British engineering to the French aristocracy against our fourteenth-century archways! International magical cooperation has never been more vigorously, enthusiasm-filled, and thoroughly embraced!\u0026quot;","Snape choked on his tongue. He gripped the arms of his chair so hard the mahogany groaned. \u0026quot;Diplomatic relations?! Albus, he was practically fused to the metalwork! Her cloak was on the floor! They were vibrating at a frequency that was rattling the plumbing!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And young Dursley!\u0026quot; McGonagall gasped, her face flushing crimson. \u0026quot;He had her three feet in the air, Albus! He was holding her by the waist with his bare hands! The sheer... the sheer carnality of it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well, naturally,\u0026quot; Dumbledore noted with a fond, approving nod. \u0026quot;Dudley Dursley was a heavyweight boxing champion. Excellent deadlift form, from what I understand. One must admire a young man who does not skip his core exercises.\u0026quot;","Snape let out a sound that resembled a dying steam kettle. He buried his face in his hands, his shoulders heaving. \u0026quot;I cannot endure this. I am going to swallow a vial of Draught of Living Death. Wake me when they graduate.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Severus. Minerva.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore’s tone softened. The playful twinkle in his eyes shifted, replaced by that ancient, profound, and deeply gentle warmth that had seen them through the darkest nights of the wizarding world.","He looked at McGonagall, whose lips were trembling with exhausted frustration. He looked at Snape, whose dark silhouette was hunched in world-weary misery.","\u0026quot;Look at us,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said quietly, his voice like velvet. \u0026quot;Fourteen years ago, we were burying the dead. We were walking these very corridors in the dark, clutching our wands, wondering if the laughter of children would ever echo off these stones again without fear, without prejudice, without the shadow of war.\u0026quot;","McGonagall paused. Her gaze dropped to her teacup.","\u0026quot;And tonight?\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled softly, gesturing toward the star-filled window. \u0026quot;Tonight, the greatest crisis facing the Faculty of Hogwarts is that our boys are falling desperately, clumsily, and delightfully in love with remarkable young women from across the sea. Can you truly brew a potion to stop youth, Severus? Can you transfigure the fierce, beating heart of an adolescent into cold stone, Minerva?\u0026quot;","Snape remained silent, staring darkly at the Persian rug.","\u0026quot;They are safe,\u0026quot; Dumbledore continued gently. \u0026quot;They are fierce. They are loyal. And they have found people who see them for who they are—not as the children of war heroes, but simply as James and Thomas. Is that not precisely what we bled for?\u0026quot;","McGonagall stared into her fortified tea for a long, quiet moment.","She let out a long, shuddering, Scottish breath. The tension that had held her shoulders rigid for three weeks slowly, completely dissolved. She reached up, pushed her spectacles back onto the bridge of her nose, and rubbed the corners of her eyes.","\u0026quot;They are absolute terrors, Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered, though the sharpness was entirely gone from her voice, replaced by the tired, fond surrender of a grandmother who knew she was outmatched. \u0026quot;Both of them.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Of course they are,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed warmly, pouring another generous splash of Firewhisky into both of their cups. \u0026quot;They were raised by Harry, Hermione, Dudley, and Chloe. They could hardly be anything else.\u0026quot;","Snape slowly lowered his hands from his face.","He stared at his replenished tumbler of Firewhisky. He stared at Dumbledore’s neon pineapple robes.","He knew when a battle was lost. He knew when an entire castle had conspired against his peace of mind.","With a heavy, world-weary sigh that came from the very marrow of his bones, Severus Snape picked up his glass.","\u0026quot;If the Krum girl calls me a bat again,\u0026quot; Snape muttered into his drink, his voice flat with utter, unconditional surrender, \u0026quot;I am deducting five hundred points from Durmstrang. I do not care if they do not have a house hourglass. I will construct one out of spite.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore laughed—a rich, booming, joyful sound that echoed up into the rafters, making Fawkes ruffle his scarlet feathers in approval.","\u0026quot;A splendid compromise, Severus!\u0026quot; Dumbledore toasted, raising his own goblet of mulled mead. \u0026quot;To youth. To international diplomacy. And to the complete and utter impossibility of controlling the next generation.\u0026quot;","McGonagall clinked her teacup against his mead, letting out a small, reluctant chuckle. Snape merely raised his glass with a deadpan glare and drank the entire thing down.","There was no stopping them.","The Pack had conquered Hogwarts, the foreign schools had conquered The Pack, and the Faculty had officially, peacefully, and delightfully surrendered."]},{"num":75,"origNum":45,"title":"The Black Card Protocol and the Road to Paris","wordCount":1517,"paragraphs":["December had arrived at Hogwarts with the quiet, breathless magic of heavy Scottish snow.","Outside, the Black Lake had frozen into a sheet of dark jade ice, and the castle turrets wore thick caps of pristine white. Inside, the corridors were warmed by roaring hearths and the scent of roasted chestnuts, pine boughs, and festive anticipation.","Earlier that morning, Professor McGonagall had posted the official parchment notice on the board in the entrance hall: \u003cstrong\u003eThe Yule Ball\u003c/strong\u003e would be held on Christmas Eve, a formal night of international dining, dancing, and high magical celebration.","Down in the Great Hall, house segregation had officially, permanently surrendered.","At the center of the Gryffindor table, The Pack had constructed what could only be described as a sovereign domestic sanctuary. It was a lazy Saturday morning, and not a single one of them was wearing school robes.","James Sirius Potter was slouched in a pair of faded red flannel pyjama bottoms and a soft grey jumper, casually eating buttered pancakes with his arm lazily draped around Valeria Krum. Valeria, looking thoroughly at home in an oversized black Durmstrang fleece and wool lounge pants, had her boots propped on the bench, methodically spreading honey across a thick slice of toast.","Beside them sat Thomas Vernon Dursley in a navy blue thermal henley, his sleeves pushed up, reading a thick manual on goblin pneumatic seals while Céleste Laurent leaned comfortably against his broad shoulder. Céleste was dressed in powder-blue silk pyjamas under a thick cream cashmere cardigan, her cascading silver curls spilling across Thomas’s chest as she stole bacon from his plate with an amused, delicate smile.","Opposite them, Lily Luna was wrapped in a massive, hand-knitted Weasley sweater that could have housed a family of four, drinking hot cocoa with whipped cream; Pandora Weasley was floating about two inches above her seat in fluffy sheepskin slippers, humming to her scrambled eggs; and Cassiopeia Malfoy sat with queenly poise in tailored emerald-silk lounging robes, sipping black tea from a porcelain cup.","The Great Hall was quiet, warm, and pleasantly chaotic.","Until the owl arrived.","It was not a school owl. It was an enormous, imperious Great Horned Owl with feathers the color of polished silver slate, wearing a sleek leather harness stamped with the Malfoy crest.","The bird did not circle. It glided down the central aisle with the arrogant, patrician grace of a bird that owned the airspace, banked sharply over the Gryffindor table, and dropped a small, heavy parcel wrapped in black velvet directly into Cassiopeia Malfoy’s lap.","Cassie raised an eyebrow. \u0026quot;From Wiltshire,\u0026quot; she remarked coolly.","\u0026quot;Did Uncle Draco send more of those French chocolate truffles?\u0026quot; James mumbled around a mouthful of pancake. \u0026quot;The ones with the gold leaf? Those were brilliant.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Don\u0027t speak with your mouth full, Potter,\u0026quot; Cassie sighed.","She untied the silver silk cord and peeled back the black velvet.","Tucked inside was a crisp sheet of heavy parchment written in Draco Malfoy’s sharp, aristocratic script with black-and-silver ink. And resting beneath the letter was a set of sleek, cold, obsidian-black rectangular cards, forged from enchanted goblin-steel and inlaid with intricate, pulsing silver runes.","Cassie unfolded the letter and read it aloud with a slow, wicked smirk:","\u003cem\u003eDearest Cassiopeia,\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWord has reached Wiltshire regarding the Yule Ball.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eYour mother and I refuse, under any circumstances, to have a Malfoy or our extended family unit appear in anything less than bespoke, haute-couture perfection. Hogwarts functions have historically suffered from a tragic surplus of frilly second-hand lace and disastrous tailoring.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eI have enclosed the Black Cards. This applies to you, Pandora, and Lily, as well as your two new... international acquisitions.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eMy compliments to young James for securing the Bulgarian market; your grandfather Lucius is still bragging to his investment club that we have a Seeker in the family pipeline. And convey my highest regards to Thomas; his father’s deadlift form is legendary, and it appears the boy has inherited the proper grip strength.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eSpare no expense. Take them to Paris. If Gringotts complains about the liquidity drain, inform the Head Goblin that I will purchase their bank and convert it into a private stable.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eDress like deities.\u003c/em\u003e","\u003cem\u003eWith all our love,Father (and Mother)\u003c/em\u003e","Silence fell over the table.","James let out a low whistle. \u0026quot;Uncle Draco is an absolute madman.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He’s an artist,\u0026quot; Lily corrected, her emerald eyes sparkling with delight as she eyed the cards. \u0026quot;And he hates bad tailoring more than he hated Voldemort.\u0026quot;","At the end of the table, Valeria and Céleste were staring down at the sleek, obsidian cards with expressions of profound, uncharacteristic bewilderment.","Valeria picked one up. The enchanted metal was heavy, cold as ice, and buzzed faintly against her calloused fingertips with dormant, high-voltage magic.","\u0026quot;Cassie,\u0026quot; Valeria rumbled in her deep Bulgarian purr, her stormy eyes narrowing. \u0026quot;What is this? It looks like an ancient goblin runestone.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It\u0027s a Gringotts Black Card, darling,\u0026quot; Cassie replied smoothly, taking a delicate sip of her tea.","Céleste picked up another card, running a manicured fingernail over the inlaid silver runes. \u0026quot;I have seen gold vaults in Paris, and credit rings from the Swiss magical banks... but I have never heard of a \u0027Black Card.\u0027 What is ze credit limit on this?\u0026quot;","Cassie looked at Céleste.","Then she looked at Valeria.","A slow, predatory Malfoy smirk spread across Cassiopeia’s flawless face.","\u0026quot;Limit?\u0026quot; Cassie murmured, leaning forward. \u0026quot;There is no limit. It is an infinite, bottomless goblin-forged liquidity weapon backed by seven centuries of uncollateralized Malfoy and Black ancestral treasury debt.\u0026quot;","Valeria blinked. \u0026quot;Meaning?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Meaning,\u0026quot; Cassie said, tapping the card with a polished nail, \u0026quot;you could walk into Paris, purchase the Eiffel Tower, have it gold-plated by master goblin smiths, wrap it in acromantula silk, and the card wouldn\u0027t even ask for secondary identification.\u0026quot;","Valeria Krum’s mouth slowly parted.","Her father, Viktor Krum, was one of the wealthiest wizards in eastern Europe—a multi-millionaire in Galleons through sports contracts, broom sponsorships, and international estates. She was accustomed to private quidditch pitches and custom racing gear. But this? This was unhinged, bottomless, generational pure-blood lunacy.","Beside Thomas, Céleste Laurent let out a soft, stunned gasp.","As a pure-blooded French aristocrat whose family owned half the vineyards along the Dordogne, Céleste was intimately acquainted with luxury. She wore bespoke silk and summered in white marble châteaux. But the concept of a piece of goblin steel with zero financial ceiling—handed out like party favors to fourteen-year-olds for a school dance—was a level of wealth that defied rational comprehension.","\u0026quot;Mon dieu,\u0026quot; Céleste breathed, looking up at Thomas. \u0026quot;Is your family always like this?\u0026quot;","Thomas swallowed his bite of toast, adjusted his steel-rimmed spectacles, and sighed with deep, world-weary Surrey pragmatism.","\u0026quot;Only when Uncle Draco gets bored,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled. \u0026quot;Last Christmas, he sent my dad a solid gold set of socket wrenches. Dad tried to use the three-quarter inch on the lawnmower and bent the drive shaft because gold has terrible tensile strength. We had to use it as a doorstop.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Well, I am not using these as doorstops,\u0026quot; Lily declared firmly, scooping up three of the Black Cards and sliding them into her sweater pocket. Her green eyes were ablaze with pure, dangerous Evans determination. \u0026quot;London is completely out of the question. Twilfitt and Tatting’s has zero vision, and Madam Malkin smells of mothballs.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Agreed,\u0026quot; Cassie said, rising from the bench with the majestic grace of an empress taking her throne. \u0026quot;We are going to the Rue Saint-Honoré in Paris. Madame Vaneau’s private salon. I will have them close the boutique for the afternoon.\u0026quot;","Céleste’s violet eyes lit up with dazzling excitement. \u0026quot;Madame Vaneau?! She only designs for royalty and the Beauxbatons ministry elite! I know her chief enchantress!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The spirits are humming in French,\u0026quot; Pandora announced serenely, floating back down to her bench and sliding her sheepskin slippers across the floor. \u0026quot;The fabrics will be shimmering. The boys will be completely miserable carrying our bags. It will be glorious.\u0026quot;","James groaned, letting his forehead drop onto the wooden table with a hollow \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e. \u0026quot;Seven hours of dress shopping. Someone hex me. Please. Just cast a Stupefy and leave me in the snow.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You will carry the boxes, Potter,\u0026quot; Valeria commanded softly, reaching down and giving the back of his neck an affectionate, iron-gripped squeeze that made his spine straighten instantly. \u0026quot;And you will tell me I look magnificent.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, ma\u0027am,\u0026quot; James croaked, his face flushing pink.","Cassie smoothed her emerald silk robes, tucking her wand into her sleeve.","\u0026quot;Come along, children,\u0026quot; Cassie ordered, gesturing toward the great double doors of the hall. \u0026quot;We have an appointment with destiny. But first, we need an international Portkey.\u0026quot;","Still dressed in flannel pyjamas, oversized fleeces, silk robes, and sheepskin slippers, The Pack—flanked by their Bulgarian Seeker and French Veela—turned in unison and began their march through the Great Hall.","They were heading straight up to the Headmaster’s Tower.","It was time to inform Albus Dumbledore that five fourteen-year-olds were taking his foreign guests to Paris on an unlimited Malfoy shopping spree, and heaven help anyone who stood between them and the front door."]},{"num":76,"origNum":46,"title":"The Parisian Portkey and the Confectioner’s Tax","wordCount":1501,"paragraphs":["The spiral staircase ascended with a smooth, magical glide, delivering the seven teenagers directly to the threshold of the Headmaster’s Tower.","They were, without question, the most bizarrely dressed diplomatic delegation in the eight-century history of European magical governance.","Cassiopeia Malfoy led the procession in tailored emerald silk lounging robes and slippers that cost more than a Nimbus 2000. Flanking her was Lily Luna Potter, drowning in three yards of hand-knitted Weasley wool; Pandora Weasley, drifting an inch off the floor in fluffy sheepskin; James Sirius Potter, still clutching a half-eaten waffle in his flannel pyjamas; Valeria Krum, brooding with northern majesty in oversized Durmstrang training fleece; Thomas Vernon Dursley, carrying his pneumatic seal manual under his arm; and Céleste Laurent, looking like a French fashion advertisement that had accidentally wandered into a student dormitory.","Albus Dumbledore did not look up from his desk immediately.","He was wearing an eye-watering silk smoking jacket patterned with turquoise flamingos and gold glitter, humming softly as he used an antique silver magnifying glass to inspect a particularly stubborn crossword puzzle in the \u003cem\u003eDaily Prophet\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;Ah,\u0026quot; Dumbledore murmured serenely, not raising his eyes. \u0026quot;The seven-card battalion. I was wondering when you might arrive. Lemon Drop, James? Or have you finished eating your breakfast off your jumper?\u0026quot;","James looked down at his chest, quickly brushed away two stray waffle crumbs, and flushed pink. \u0026quot;Er. No, thank you, Professor.\u0026quot;","Cassie stepped forward. She did not fidget. She did not hesitate.","She reached into the pocket of her silk robe, withdrew the five gleaming, obsidian-steel Black Cards, and fanned them across the mahogany desk with the practiced, terrifying elegance of a high-stakes casino dealer.","The silver runes on the cards pulsed with faint, low-voltage goblin magic, reflecting in Dumbledore’s half-moon spectacles.","\u0026quot;Headmaster,\u0026quot; Cassie announced with cool, aristocratic authority. \u0026quot;The Yule Ball is in three weeks. As you are well aware, the general aesthetic standards of this institution are in critical, life-threatening jeopardy. My father has issued an emergency financial intervention. We require immediate, weekend international transit authorization.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore slowly lowered his magnifying glass.","His brilliant blue eyes traveled over the fanned Black Cards. Then they moved to the seven teenagers standing before him—fourteen years old, brimming with vibrant youth, and looking ready to wage economic warfare on a foreign capital.","A massive, radiant smile spread across Dumbledore’s wrinkled face. His eyes twinkled with so much amusement they could have powered the castle’s torches.","\u0026quot;Paris?\u0026quot; Dumbledore asked, his voice purring with delight. \u0026quot;On a crisp, snowy Saturday in December? With seven centuries of uncollateralized Malfoy treasury debt in your pockets?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Rue Saint-Honoré,\u0026quot; Cassie confirmed without blinking. \u0026quot;Madame Vaneau’s private salon. The London boutiques lack vision.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Naturally,\u0026quot; Dumbledore chuckled, clasping his hands over his flamingo robes. \u0026quot;It would be an unforgivable crime against international diplomacy to deny such an excursion. Young Mr. Potter must be properly fitted, Mr. Dursley requires robes that can withstand his... structural enthusiasm, and the ladies deserve nothing less than Parisian perfection.\u0026quot;","James and Thomas both let out synchronized sighs of relief.","\u0026quot;However,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said, raising a single, long, silver-ringed finger.","The temperature in the room instantly dropped. The teenagers tensed.","Valeria’s stormy hazel eyes narrowed into sharp, defensive slits; Thomas unconsciously stepped half an inch forward, bracing his shoulders; and Lily furrowed her brow, bracing for academic stipulations, curfews, or an emergency chaperone like Hagrid or McGonagall.","\u0026quot;There is one condition,\u0026quot; Dumbledore said softly, his expression turning solemn and conspiratorial. \u0026quot;A non-negotiable, high-priority international courier assignment.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Name it, Professor,\u0026quot; Lily said bravely. \u0026quot;We can handle it.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore leaned forward across his desk, lowering his voice to an urgent, dramatic whisper.","\u0026quot;In the fourth arrondissement, just off the Place des Vosges, tucked behind a curtain of enchanted violet wisteria, sits an ancient confiserie named \u003cem\u003eLa Dragée d\u0027Or\u003c/em\u003e. The proprietor, Monsieur Bonheur, crafts a very specific, limited-batch variety of Sherbet Lemons. They are crystallized with pure Sicilian citrus fire and enchanted with tiny, popping sparks that play Vivaldi’s \u003cem\u003eFour Seasons\u003c/em\u003e inside your ears as they dissolve.\u0026quot;","He looked at each of them with an intensity he usually reserved for ancient magical artifacts.","\u0026quot;Bring me four tins. Undamaged. And you have my unconditional blessing.\u0026quot;","A collective, stunned silence fell over the office.","Then James let out a snort of laughter that he desperately tried to turn into a cough. Valeria’s mouth twitched.","Céleste smiled dazzlingly, inclining her head with pure French grace. \u0026quot;Monsieur Bonheur is a second-cousin of my mother’s, Headmaster. You shall have six tins. And I will ensure he adds extra citrus sparks.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My dear Miss Laurent,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed, his hand over his heart as if deeply moved. \u0026quot;You are an absolute treasure. Viktor Krum’s daughter and a Laurent heiress... Hogwarts has never had finer ambassadors.\u0026quot;","Dumbledore pulled open the bottom drawer of his desk.","Being the Supreme Mugwump of the International Confederation of Wizards came with extraordinary, unchecked bureaucratic privileges. He withdrew a small, ornate, antique copper pocket watch with three winding stems and a faded velvet ribbon.","\u0026quot;An official, pre-cleared, bilateral international Portkey,\u0026quot; Dumbledore explained, setting it gently on the edge of the desk. \u0026quot;It is keyed to the coordinates of the Place Cachée—the hidden heart of magical Paris. It will activate at precisely twelve noon, and return you to this very rug at eight o\u0027clock this evening.\u0026quot;","He tapped the watch with his wand. A soft, golden chime echoed through the room.","\u0026quot;You have forty-five minutes to shed your nightwear and put on something suitable for the Continent,\u0026quot; Dumbledore smiled, his eyes twinkling brightly. \u0026quot;Off you go, children. Do not disappoint me with the lemon drops.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Thank you, Headmaster!\u0026quot; Lily cheered, grabbing James by the arm and spinning him toward the door.","Forty minutes later, the transformation was complete.","When the group reassembled at the base of the Headmaster’s Tower, the flannel pyjamas and fluffy slippers had been banished. In their place stood seven teenagers who looked as though they had stepped straight off the cover of \u003cem\u003eWitch Weekly International\u003c/em\u003e.","Cassie wore a sleek, high-collared winter coat of charcoal cashmere, trimmed with dark silver-fox fur around the neck and cuffs, paired with tall, polished black leather boots.","Lily Luna looked stunning in a rich, emerald-green wool trench coat that accentuated her six-foot frame, her copper-mahogany hair swept into an elegant, windblown updo fastened with silver pins.","Pandora drifted beside them in a breathtaking velvet mantle of dusk-blue, her strawberry-blonde curls woven with tiny enchanted silver stars that flickered like real constellations.","Valeria Krum had opted for northern military elegance: a fitted, double-breasted coat of midnight-black leather lined with wolf fur, her silver snake ring gleaming on her thumb, looking every bit the fierce, predatory Seeker queen.","Céleste Laurent was pure, effortless Parisian glamour—an ivory silk-wool capelet draped over a tailored ice-blue dress, her cascading silver curls catching the castle torches like liquid moonlight.","The boys had not been neglected.","James was wearing a sharp, dark-burgundy winter coat over a crisp white shirt, his collar slightly open, his messy black hair artfully disheveled, looking impossibly handsome and radiating nervous Potter energy.","Beside him, Thomas Vernon Dursley was a mountain of navy blue: a heavy, double-breasted woolen pea coat that accommodated his broad shoulders, crisp dark trousers, and heavy, polished boots, looking solid, dependable, and thoroughly unshakeable.","Dumbledore stood by his desk, holding the copper pocket watch by its ribbon, smiling warmly.","\u0026quot;Magnificent,\u0026quot; the Headmaster pronounced. \u0026quot;A triumph of tailoring. Gather round, please. One finger on the metal casing.\u0026quot;","All seven of them stepped in, reaching out.","James and Valeria linked fingers over the rim; Thomas’s large hand settled beside Céleste’s delicate fingers; Cassie, Lily, and Pan laid their hands across the silver winding stems.","\u0026quot;Three,\u0026quot; Dumbledore counted, his eyes gleaming.","\u0026quot;Hold on tight, Tommy,\u0026quot; Lily whispered with a grin.","\u0026quot;Two.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Mind the inertia on landing,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled practically.","\u0026quot;One.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eYANK.\u003c/em\u003e","It felt as though a giant, invisible hook had snagged behind their navels. The Headmaster’s office vanished in a blinding vortex of swirling blue and gold light. The wind roared in their ears, the stone walls melted into streaks of speed, and the freezing chill of the Scottish highlands was violently stripped away.","\u003cem\u003eSNAP.\u003c/em\u003e","Their boots slammed onto wet, glistening cobblestones.","The sudden scent of roasted chestnuts, rich dark coffee, melted chocolate, and expensive floral perfumes rushed into their lungs. The sound of distant accordion music, Parisian street chatter, and enchanted horse-drawn carriages echoed through the crisp December air.","Above them arched the magnificent, iron-and-glass ceiling of the \u003cstrong\u003ePlace Cachée\u003c/strong\u003e—the magical heart of Paris. Shimmering gas lamps illuminated rows of grand Haussmann-style boutiques, gilded café terraces, and floating crystalline globes of enchanted white snow.","They were in Paris.","Cassiopeia Malfoy adjusted the silver-fox fur at her collar. She slipped a hand into her coat, pulled out the gleaming obsidian Black Card, and let a slow, dangerous, beautiful smirk spread across her face.","\u0026quot;Ladies and gentlemen,\u0026quot; Cassie purred, looking down the grand boulevard of fashion. \u0026quot;Welcome to Paris. Let us go bankrupt a few boutiques.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":77,"origNum":47,"title":"The Triple Threat and the Hundred-Thousand-Galleon Receipt","wordCount":1979,"paragraphs":["The moment their boots had touched the glistening cobblestones of the Place Cachée, the seven-person Parisian expedition had immediately fractured into tactical units.","\u0026quot;There is an antique French artisan three streets over who specializes in enchanted hydraulic water-valves,\u0026quot; Céleste had purred, linking her arm possessively through Thomas’s heavy wool coat. \u0026quot;I thought you might like to inspect their fourteenth-century bronze casting.\u0026quot;","Thomas’s eyes had lit up behind his spectacles as if he had just been handed the keys to heaven. \u0026quot;Fourteenth-century bronze? With the original lead gaskets? Lead the way, Céleste.\u0026quot;","Meanwhile, James had barely taken two breaths of Parisian air before Valeria took him firmly by the collar of his burgundy coat. \u0026quot;There is a Bulgarian-French dueling boutique in the alley,\u0026quot; Valeria rumbled in her smoky accent, her eyes predatory. \u0026quot;They have new dragon-leather grip wraps for high-speed diving. You are coming with me, Potter.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes, ma\u0027am,\u0026quot; James had agreed instantly, completely helpless.","Which left the undisputed triumvirate of terror standing alone in the center of the boulevard: \u003cstrong\u003eCassiopeia Malfoy, Lily Luna Potter, and Pandora Weasley\u003c/strong\u003e.","Cassie had looked at the two of them, a slow, dangerous smile curling her lips.","\u0026quot;Good,\u0026quot; Cassie said, smoothing her silver-fox fur. \u0026quot;The amateurs are gone. Now we can shop in peace.\u0026quot;","When the three of them swept through the gilded doors of \u003cem\u003eMaison Vaneau\u003c/em\u003e on the Rue Saint-Honoré, it was not a shopping trip. It was a hostile financial takeover.","Without the boys or the other girls to moderate their pace, the three teenagers unleashed absolute, uninhibited havoc. Madame Vaneau took one look at the gleaming obsidian Black Card in Cassie’s manicured fingers, immediately locked the front doors, drew the heavy velvet curtains, and summoned her entire master staff of eighteen enchantresses and seamstresses.","For two solid hours, the boutique became a storm of spun starlight, celestial tulle, and diamond dust.","Cassie selected a structural marvel of midnight-emerald starlight velvet, woven with crushed celestial meteors that shifted from deep forest green to pitch black with every step, featuring an off-the-shoulder neckline tailored with pure white-acromantula silk.","Lily Luna Potter, whose six-foot frame and radiant \u0026quot;Light\u0026quot; had three French designers openly weeping into their tape measures, was fitted into a breathtaking, backless gown of liquid sunrise silk that flowed from pale champagne-gold at the bodice into a blazing, regal emerald at the floor-length hem, enchanted to hum with the soft, warm glow of her natural aura.","And Pandora Weasley stood laughing upon a rotating pedestal as eight seamstresses pinned a celestial gown of dusk-blue tulle—woven with real, microscopic shooting stars and singing dandelion fluff that hovered two inches off the carpet, accompanied by a delicate silver constellation tiara.","Add in three pairs of bespoke dragonhide dancing slippers, emerald hairpins, diamond-encrusted clasps, and private tailoring charms...","Cassie stepped up to the counter, dropped the Black Card, and signed her name with a gold quill without even checking the total.","Meanwhile, three hundred miles away in Wiltshire, the atmosphere in Malfoy Manor was deceptively tranquil.","Draco Malfoy was sitting in a high-backed leather armchair in his private study, legs casually crossed, swirling a glass of twenty-year-old Ogden’s Old Firewhisky.","Sitting opposite him was Harry Potter, who had dropped by to deliver some routine Auror security filings. The two former rivals—now brothers-in-arms and perpetual co-sufferers of teenage chaos—were peacefully debating the latest Quidditch league standings.","\u0026quot;I’m telling you, Harry,\u0026quot; Draco drawled smoothly, \u0026quot;the Harpies\u0027 new Beater has no discipline. If Ginny were still flying, she’d have knocked the girl into the third row by the second chukker.\u0026quot;","Harry chuckled into his butterbeer. \u0026quot;Ginny would have knocked her into the parking lot. You know how she gets.\u0026quot;","Suddenly, on the corner of Draco’s massive ebony desk, an antique silver Gringotts terminal gave a sharp, resonant, brassy \u003cem\u003ePING!\u003c/em\u003e","It was not a standard transaction chime. It was the frantic, high-frequency ring of an enchanted ledger recording a tectonic financial event.","A golden scroll of parchment began to feed out of the brass slot, clicking rapidly like a machine gun as line after line of enchanted ink printed in rapid succession.","Draco raised an eyebrow, amused. \u0026quot;Ah. It appears my daughter has located the silk counter.\u0026quot;","He set his drink down, reached across the desk with a languid hand, picked up the long receipt, and casually glanced at the bottom line.","Draco Malfoy froze.","His pale grey eyes widened by three distinct millimeters.","He blinked once. Twice.","He leaned forward, adjusting the parchment under the desk lamp to ensure the runes hadn\u0027t scrambled.","\u003cem\u003eTOTAL TRANSACTION: 112,650 GALLEONS.LOCATION: MAISON VANEAU, RUE SAINT-HONORÉ, PARIS.ITEMS: THREE (3) BESPOKE GOWNS \u0026amp; ACCESSORIES.CLIENTS: C. MALFOY, L. POTTER, P. WEASLEY.\u003c/em\u003e","A slow, breathless chuckle rumbled in Draco’s throat. A look of supreme, slightly terrified fatherly admiration spread across his aristocratic face.","\u0026quot;Salazar’s ghost,\u0026quot; Draco murmured, shaking his head. \u0026quot;One hundred and twelve thousand Galleons. On \u003cem\u003ethree\u003c/em\u003e dresses. She didn\u0027t even buy the shop. She just bought three frocks.\u0026quot;","Across the desk, Harry Potter had been in the middle of taking a peaceful swallow of butterbeer.","He stopped.","His head snapped around so fast his neck made an audible click.","\u0026quot;What did you just say?\u0026quot; Harry asked, his voice dropping into a dangerously quiet register. \u0026quot;How many Galleons?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;One hundred and twelve thousand, six hundred and fifty,\u0026quot; Draco repeated smoothly, admiring the golden scroll like a museum artifact. \u0026quot;And look at the breakdown—it’s just Cassie, Lily, and Pandora. The other two aren\u0027t even on the ticket. That is... frankly terrifying. Three fourteen-year-old girls have just expended the equivalent of an offshore naval frigate in ninety minutes.\u0026quot;","Harry’s brain suffered a total, blue-screen operational shutdown.","His Surrey middle-class instincts—forged through years of Uncle Vernon ranting about the cost of electricity, petrol, and school uniforms—collided violently with pure-blood financial lunacy.","\u0026quot;ONE HUNDRED AND TWELVE THOUSAND?!\u0026quot; Harry roared, practically vaulting out of his leather chair.","He lunged across the desk, snatched the parchment from Draco’s hand, and shoved his round glasses up his nose, his green eyes bulging so wide they threatened to shatter the lenses.","\u0026quot;ON THREE DRESSES?!\u0026quot; Harry shouted, his voice cracking with pure, unmitigated horror. \u0026quot;DRACO! THAT IS NOT DRESS SHOPPING! THAT IS AN ACT OF WAR! THAT IS MORE MONEY THAN MY ENTIRE FIRST-YEAR TRUST VAULT! WHAT ARE THEY WEARING, WOVEN PLUTONIUM?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Acromantula silk and powdered meteor dust, apparently,\u0026quot; Draco noted calmly, taking another sip of his Firewhisky. \u0026quot;Very tasteful.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;TASTEFUL?!\u0026quot; Harry was hyperventilating.","His Auror crisis protocols completely misfired. He didn\u0027t know what to do. His fourteen-year-old daughter was loose in France, armed with a piece of goblin plastic, spending astronomical fortunes with two Weasley and Malfoy conspirators.","In a state of pure, unthinking panic, Harry sprinted across the room toward the massive stone fireplace. He shoved his entire fist into the Floo powder urn, grabbed a massive handful, and hurled it into the grate.","\u003cem\u003eROOOOOOAR.\u003c/em\u003e","The flames erupted into a roaring emerald inferno. Harry stuck his head straight into the fire, screaming into the network with the volume of a man reporting a dragon invasion:","\u0026quot;HERMIONE! GODRIC’S HOLLOW! CODE BLACK! EMERGENCY AT MALFOY MANOR! GET THROUGH RIGHT NOW!\u0026quot;","Three seconds later, the green flames parted with a deafening \u003cem\u003eWHOOSH\u003c/em\u003e.","Hermione Granger-Potter exploded out of the fireplace onto the hearth rug.","Her wand was drawn in a razor-sharp dueling stance, sparks of blue light crackling at the tip, her hair billowing around her face, her eyes blazing with terrifying Ministry authority.","\u0026quot;HARRY!\u0026quot; Hermione barked, sweeping her wand across the room, ready to vaporize an army. \u0026quot;Where is the breach?! Is it a Death Eater remnant?! Have the children been ambushed in the Highlands?! Speak to me!\u0026quot;","She stopped.","There was no attack.","There was only Draco Malfoy, leaning back in his chair with one ankle resting on his knee, politely raising his glass to her.","And her husband, Harry, trembling like a leaf in the wind, holding a three-foot-long golden receipt toward her with both hands as if it were an unexploded magical warhead.","\u0026quot;The... the receipt, Hermione,\u0026quot; Harry choked out, his voice a dry, strangled squeak. \u0026quot;Look at the receipt.\u0026quot;","Hermione lowered her wand, her brow furrowing in deep, exasperated annoyance. \u0026quot;Harry James Potter, I was in the middle of a confidential briefing with the French Department of Magical Cooperation—\u0026quot;","She snatched the golden scroll.","She looked at the top: \u003cem\u003eMaison Vaneau, Paris.\u003c/em\u003e","She looked at the names: \u003cem\u003eCassie, Lily, Pandora.\u003c/em\u003e","Then her amber eyes hit the bottom line.","\u003cem\u003e112,650 GALLEONS.\u003c/em\u003e","The silence that fell over Draco’s study was so heavy, so suffocating, that even the grandfather clock in the corner seemed to pause its pendulum.","Hermione Granger’s face did not pale; it flushed an alarming, dangerous shade of purple-red that would have made Vernon Dursley proud.","Her jaw unhinged. Her eyes widened to the size of saucers. Her fingers tightened on the parchment so hard the gold foil began to crinkle and smoke.","\u0026quot;One...\u0026quot; Hermione whispered.","It was a terrifying, low vibration. The sound of an earthquake building beneath the tectonic plates.","\u0026quot;One hundred... and twelve thousand...\u0026quot;","Then, the volcano erupted.","\u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eONE HUNDRED AND TWELVE THOUSAND GALLEONS?!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked, her voice reaching a frequency that shattered two crystal tumblers on the side table and caused Draco’s silver inkpot to jump three inches into the air.","\u0026quot;My tumblers, Hermione,\u0026quot; Draco winced mildly, covering one ear.","\u0026quot;I DO NOT CARE ABOUT YOUR TUMBLERS, DRACO MALFOY!\u0026quot; Hermione roared, waving the parchment in the air like a battle standard, her Ministry robes whipping around her as she began to pace the Persian rug with manic, furious energy.","\u0026quot;THAT IS THREE YEARS OF SCHOLARSHIP FUNDING FOR UNDERPRIVILEGED MUGGLE-BORNS! THAT IS AN ENTIRE NEW WING FOR ST. MUNGO’S HOSPITAL! THAT IS FOURTEEN PUBLIC LIBRARIES AND A WATER TREATMENT PLANT IN CORNWALL!\u0026quot;","She whipped around on her heel, her wand pointing directly at Draco’s chest like a loaded cannon.","\u0026quot;ON THREE DRESSES?! THREE?! WHAT COULD POSSIBLY BE EMBROIDERED INTO A DRESS TO MAKE IT COST THIRTY-SEVEN THOUSAND GALLEONS A PIECE?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Lily\u0027s gown is woven with powdered starlight diamonds that amplify her magical Light,\u0026quot; Draco provided helpfully, thoroughly enjoying the greatest piece of live theater in Britain. \u0026quot;And Cassie’s has crushed celestial meteors. Really, Hermione, you can\u0027t put a price on proper solar radiation.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;POWDERED DIAMONDS?!\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, clutching her temples with both hands, looking as though her logical, academic brain was undergoing a complete meltdown.","\u0026quot;LILY LUNA POTTER IS FOURTEEN YEARS OLD! SHE LEAVES WET TOWELS ON HER BEDROOM FLOOR! SHE CANNOT WEAR POWDERED DIAMONDS TO A SCHOOL DANCE! SHE IS WALKING AROUND IN THE ANNUAL BUDGET OF THE ENTIRE WIZENGAMOT JUNIOR DIVISION!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione, love,\u0026quot; Harry attempted softly, creeping forward with his hands raised like a man approaching a wild Hippogriff. \u0026quot;Breathe. It’s... it’s Draco’s money—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I DO NOT CARE WHOSE MONEY IT IS!\u0026quot; Hermione snapped, whirling on him with wild eyes. \u0026quot;It is the principle! The sheer, unadulterated moral decadence! I am taking the Floo to Paris right now! I am going to the Rue Saint-Honoré, I am finding Madame Vaneau, and I am invoking the 1707 Fair Trade and Luxury Goods Embargo! I will dismantle those dresses seam by seam with my bare hands!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;All sales are final, darling,\u0026quot; Draco chuckled warmly, taking a leisurely sip of his Firewhisky. \u0026quot;Malfoy Black Card terms and conditions. Page forty-seven. Non-refundable.\u0026quot;","Hermione stared at the parchment.","She stared at Draco’s smug, smirking, unshakeable face.","She looked at Harry, who gave her a terrified, apologetic grimace.","Finding herself completely, utterly defeated by Malfoy generational wealth and the unholy vanity of her own daughter, the Deputy Head of Magical Law Enforcement let out a long, high-pitched, agonized groan.","She slowly pressed the crumpled golden receipt against her forehead, leaned back against the mantle of the fireplace, and slid three inches down the brickwork.","\u0026quot;God help this family,\u0026quot; Hermione whimpered into the parchment. \u0026quot;They haven\u0027t even gone to the shoe boutique yet.\u0026quot;"]},{"num":78,"origNum":48,"title":"The Aeronautical Laboratory and the Broken Tumbler","wordCount":1637,"paragraphs":["While Cassiopeia, Lily, and Pandora were busy holding the French textile industry hostage at wandpoint, James Sirius Potter and Valeria Krum were engaged in an entirely different kind of bloodsport.","Valeria had led James three blocks away from the perfume-choked boulevards of the Rue Saint-Honoré, down a cobblestone alley known as the \u003cem\u003eAllée des Champions\u003c/em\u003e—the ancient, high-security quarter of magical Paris dedicated exclusively to international dueling, aerial mechanics, and elite combat craftsmanship.","They had stopped in front of a grand, dark-timbered storefront with black wrought-iron gates: \u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eL’Atelier Flèche \u0026amp; Lame\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e (The Arrow \u0026amp; Blade Workshop).","Inside, it smelled of hot forge-fire, polished ashwood, expensive leather oil, and ozone.","The master broomwright, a retired French national Beater named Monsieur Delacroix, had initially looked down his hooked nose at the two fourteen-year-olds.","Until Valeria had casually stepped forward, unbuttoned her Durmstrang coat, and revealed the Krum family crest on her silver belt buckle.","And James, grinning his crooked Potter grin, had tossed Draco’s obsidian Black Card onto the polished glass counter like a skipping stone.","The gates had been locked immediately.","What followed was eighty-five minutes of pure, high-octane athletic madness.","They had not come for ribbons. They had come for performance.","First came the brooms. Delacroix had brought them into the vault to inspect a pair of unreleased, prototype racing brooms: the \u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eFlèche Boréale\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e (The Northern Arrow).","Carved from a single, unbroken bough of rare Siberian thunder-ash, reinforced with Scottish Highland oak along the spine, the handles were fitted with goblin-silver foot-stirrups and twin Phoenix-feather core twigs in the tail-twigs. They were enchanted with localized atmospheric dampeners, capable of accelerating from zero to one hundred and sixty miles per hour in three point two seconds without generating wind-drag.","James had touched the polished grain, and the broom had practically hummed in his hands.","\u0026quot;We\u0027ll take two,\u0026quot; James had said without a second\u0027s hesitation. \u0026quot;One with Bulgarian balance weighting, one with British turning radius.\u0026quot;","Then came the gear.","Full bespoke dueling and flying suits made from genuine, fire-cured Swedish Short-Snout dragonhide. The leather was midnight-black, thin as silk but tough enough to deflect high-velocity Bludgers, lined with enchanted thermal fleece that could maintain body temperature in an arctic blizzard, fitted with runic forearm guards and anti-jinx shielding.","Next, a matched pair of master-grade training Snitches, forged from solid goblin white-gold with enchanted hummingbird-wing flutter mechanisms that adjusted their evasion patterns based on the Seeker’s eye movements.","And finally, their Yule Ball formal wear.","Because they were in an elite dueling atelier, the formal wear was not merely fabric; it was wearable armor disguised as haute couture.","For Valeria: a breathtaking, floor-length battle-gown of charcoal-black shadow-silk, featuring a split-skirt over tailored dragonhide trousers, a high collar embroidered with silver dragon-scales, and an antique Bulgarian star-sapphire brooch that James had spotted in the display case and quietly bought for her while she was testing her broom grips.","For James: a razor-sharp, midnight-crimson dress coat tailored from heavy acromantula-blend wool with gold dragon-thread stitching along the cuffs, paired with a high-necked black silk waistcoat and polished dragonhide dress boots with silver buckles that made him look like an imperial dueling champion.","In return, Valeria had quietly purchased James a pair of antique, engraved dragon-bone wrist guards, inscribed with ancient northern runes of speed and protection.","James had stepped up to the counter, handed over the Black Card, and signed the receipt with a theatrical, boyish flourish.","\u0026quot;Charge it to the Malfoy account,\u0026quot; James beamed. \u0026quot;Uncle Draco said dress like deities. He didn\u0027t say we couldn\u0027t fly like them too.\u0026quot;","Back in Wiltshire, Draco Malfoy’s study was still recovering from the seismic shock of Hermione Granger’s maternal meltdown.","Hermione was currently sitting on the velvet sofa, a cold linen compress pressed firmly against her forehead, taking slow, deep, measured breaths through her nose like a woman in the final stages of labor.","Harry was standing beside her, dutifully rubbing her shoulder with one hand while holding a fresh mug of chamomile tea in the other.","Draco had just finished using his wand to clean up the shattered glass from his side table, settling back into his leather armchair with a fresh tumbler of Firewhisky, looking remarkably pleased with himself.","\u0026quot;I’m telling you, Hermione,\u0026quot; Draco drawled smoothly, swirling his amber drink, \u0026quot;it’s an investment in family prestige. When our children enter the Great Hall, the foreign delegations will weep. The Durmstrangs will look like mountain peasants, and the Beauxbatons girls will renounce their citizenship. It is a diplomatic victory.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It is a moral obscenity,\u0026quot; Hermione mumbled into her cold compress. \u0026quot;One hundred and twelve thousand Galleons on three girls. If Rita Skeeter gets wind of this, the \u003cem\u003eProphet\u003c/em\u003e will run an editorial on pure-blood oligarchy that will set my Ministry reforms back twenty years.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Rita Skeeter doesn\u0027t have the clearance to enter Wiltshire, darling,\u0026quot; Draco smirked. \u0026quot;I bought her printing press three years ago. She works for me.\u0026quot;","Before Hermione could open her mouth to unleash another furious tirade on journalistic ethics and corporate monopolies, the silver Gringotts terminal on Draco’s desk gave another sound.","\u003cem\u003ePING-PING-PING.\u003c/em\u003e","It was not the polite chime from earlier.","It was a frantic, metallic, triple-staccato alarm that sounded like a submarine diving beneath crush depth.","A fresh golden scroll began to spew from the brass slot, clicking with the terrifying velocity of an uncoiled spring.","Harry froze.","Hermione’s cold compress slipped from her forehead, landing in her lap with a wet \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e.","Draco chuckled softly, though there was a slight, puzzled twitch at the corner of his eye. \u0026quot;Well. It appears young James has found himself a scarf and a box of chocolate rooks. Let’s see... fifty Galleons? Perhaps seventy if he bought the heavy wool?\u0026quot;","Draco reached across the desk. He picked up the golden scroll.","He looked at the cardholder: \u003cem\u003eJAMES S. POTTER.\u003c/em\u003eHe looked at the merchant: \u003cem\u003eL\u0027ATELIER FLÈCHE \u0026amp; LAME, PARIS.\u003c/em\u003eHe looked at the bottom line.","Draco Malfoy’s hand completely ceased to function.","His fingers went entirely limp. The heavy crystal tumbler of twenty-year-old Ogden\u0027s slipped from his grasp, plummeted toward the floor, and detonated against the mahogany floorboards with a violent, alcohol-soaked \u003cem\u003eCRASH\u003c/em\u003e.","Firewhisky splashed across the toes of Draco\u0027s bespoke leather loafers.","Draco did not look down. He did not blink. He did not breathe.","His aristocratic, pale face transitioned from smug amusement to a state of utter, paralyzed, catatonic shock. His jaw dropped so far his teeth audibly parted.","\u0026quot;Draco?\u0026quot; Harry asked, his voice trembling with immediate, suffocating dread. \u0026quot;Draco... what is it? What did he buy?\u0026quot;","Draco slowly, mechanically lifted his head. He looked at Harry. His grey eyes were completely dilated.","\u0026quot;Ninety...\u0026quot; Draco croaked. His voice had lost all its silken charm; it sounded like two rusted gears grinding together in the desert. \u0026quot;Ninety-six... thousand... four hundred... Galleons.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;WHAT?!\u0026quot; Harry and Hermione roared in unified, ear-splitting horror.","\u0026quot;NINETY-SIX THOUSAND?!\u0026quot; Harry lunged across the desk, snatching the scroll from Draco’s numb fingers.","Hermione was on her feet in an instant, crowding over Harry\u0027s shoulder, her eyes wild with panic.","\u0026quot;ON WHAT?!\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked. \u0026quot;DID HE BUY A CASTLE?! DID HE PURCHASE THE VERSAILLES PALACE?!\u0026quot;","Harry read the itemized lines aloud, his voice climbing an octave with every syllable:","\u0026quot;Two... two \u003cem\u003eFlèche Boréale\u003c/em\u003e custom prototype racing brooms... with Phoenix-feather dampeners...\u0026quot;","Harry stopped.","He stared at the parchment.","A sudden, involuntary, utterly uncontrollable look of pure, raw, athletic awe washed over Harry Potter’s face.","\u0026quot;The \u003cem\u003eFlèche Boréale\u003c/em\u003e?\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his green eyes glowing behind his glasses. \u0026quot;The ones with the Siberian thunder-ash?! Draco... those aren\u0027t even released to the public! They have a six-month waiting list! The Bulgarian national team couldn\u0027t even get allocations!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;HARRY JAMES POTTER!\u0026quot; Hermione screamed, grabbing his face with both hands and forcing him to look away from the parchment. \u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eDO NOT DARE SOUND IMPRESSED! YOUR SON JUST SPENT NINETY-SIX THOUSAND GALLEONS ON TWO BROOMSTICKS AND LEATHER TROUSERS!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Swedish Short-Snout dueling suits,\u0026quot; Harry read weakly, his face flushing pink as he tried to suppress an enormous grin. \u0026quot;And... and a white-gold training Snitch. And an antique star-sapphire brooch for Valeria.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He bought her a star-sapphire?!\u0026quot; Hermione gasped, her hands flying to her hair, looking as though her nervous system was about to collapse entirely. \u0026quot;He is fourteen! He should be buying her a sugar quill! A butterbeer! A paper card with a moving heart! Who buys a fourteen-year-old girl an antique sapphire?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A Potter,\u0026quot; Draco muttered, staring down at the puddle of Firewhisky around his shoes, looking like a man whose world view had just been violently dismantled.","Draco slowly lifted a shaking hand and ran it through his white-blond hair.","\u0026quot;I gave them the cards to humiliate the French designers,\u0026quot; Draco whispered to the ceiling, dazed. \u0026quot;I gave them the cards to show them Malfoy grandeur. I did not expect Potter’s spawn to walk into the most expensive armory in Western Europe and buy out their entire tactical division.\u0026quot;","Draco looked up at Harry, his grey eyes wide with traumatized respect.","\u0026quot;Your son is a menace, Harry. A charismatic, high-velocity financial terrorist.\u0026quot;","Harry let out a nervous, breathless laugh, clutching the receipt. \u0026quot;Well... at least he has good taste in brooms?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;HARRY!\u0026quot; Hermione shrieked.","And then, right in the middle of their screaming match, a terrible, suffocating realization dawned across the room.","Silence fell over the study once again.","Hermione looked at Harry.","Harry looked at Draco.","Draco slowly turned his head toward the silent silver Gringotts terminal on the desk.","\u0026quot;Wait,\u0026quot; Harry whispered, his voice trembling with a fresh, deeper wave of absolute terror.","\u0026quot;There were five cards,\u0026quot; Hermione breathed, her eyes widening in horror.","Draco stared at the terminal.","\u0026quot;Thomas,\u0026quot; Draco whispered. \u0026quot;Thomas and the Veela are still in Paris.\u0026quot;","The three parents stared at the silent brass machine, waiting for the third strike of the hammer."]},{"num":79,"origNum":49,"title":"The Industrial Buyout and the Near-Death Experience","wordCount":1907,"paragraphs":["While James was busy equipping a private aerial strike force and the girls were depleting the European silk reserves, Thomas Vernon Dursley had spent his first two hours in Paris being intensely practical.","Céleste had taken him to an elite French boutique near the Place Vendôme, where Thomas had endured twenty minutes of measurements before politely selecting a single, dignified navy dress uniform with silver buttons. It had cost four hundred Galleons.","Thomas had considered his duties thoroughly concluded.","Then, as they were strolling along the Boulevard Beaumarchais toward a café, Thomas had stopped dead in the middle of the sidewalk.","His steel-rimmed spectacles had reflected the brass-and-copper sign of a massive, soot-stained industrial workshop: \u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eManufacture Royale des Tissus Enchantés\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.","Through the tall glass windows, Thomas had caught sight of something that made his engineer’s heart thrum like an electric dynamo.","It was an automated, twelve-foot-tall, steam-pneumatic magical loom.","The machine was an industrial marvel—woven from brass pistons, enchanted quartz crystals, and silver gears—spinning raw, molten strands of fire-resistant dragon-silk into whisper-thin sheets of fabric.","Thomas had walked inside without saying a single word. Céleste, amused and deeply fond, had followed closely behind.","Inside, an ancient French wizard named Monsieur Lafayette—a master inventor who looked like a cross between an eccentric clockmaker and a disgruntled badger—was currently screaming at three goblin mechanics because the loom’s secondary warp-spindle had jammed for the fifth time that morning.","Thomas hadn\u0027t looked at the silk.","He had walked straight up to the roaring machine, rolled up his sleeves, pulled a brass screwdriver from his pocket, and leaned over the primary drive-shaft.","\u0026quot;Your fulcrum is misaligned by four millimeters,\u0026quot; Thomas had rumbled calmly over the deafening clatter of the pistons. \u0026quot;The thermal expansion from the goblin-fire furnace is warping the bronze housing. If you replace the housing with cold-forged iron and recalibrate the gear ratio on the third escapement, the thread won\u0027t snap under high tension.\u0026quot;","Monsieur Lafayette had frozen. The goblins had dropped their wrenches.","For the next ninety minutes, Thomas and Lafayette had engaged in a high-octane, deeply passionate debate on thermodynamic stress, tensile elasticity, and magical-kinetic conductivity. Thomas had sketched three structural optimizations directly onto a napkin with a graphite pencil.","By the end of the conversation, the ancient French inventor was weeping tears of pure joy into his beard.","For twelve long years, both the British and French Ministries of Magic had been desperately trying to purchase the international commercial patent for Lafayette’s revolutionary \u003cstrong\u003eTechnomantic Dragon-Silk Process\u003c/strong\u003e—a miraculous fabric capable of deflecting high-level curses, regulating temperature, and self-repairing under magical stress. But Lafayette had stubbornly refused to sell to government bureaucrats, drowning their trade delegations in legal delays and red tape.","\u0026quot;You,\u0026quot; Lafayette had whispered, gripping Thomas’s large hands with trembling reverence. \u0026quot;You understand the soul of the machine! Not like those pompous Ministry fools! You see the torque! You see the beauty of the gear!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;It’s basic structural efficiency,\u0026quot; Thomas had shrugged modestly.","\u0026quot;Take it!\u0026quot; Lafayette had proclaimed, waving a fist in the air. \u0026quot;The exclusive global rights! The international patent! The six prototype industrial looms! Take it all before those French Ministry leeches steal it!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;How much?\u0026quot; Thomas had asked.","\u0026quot;Nine hundred thousand Galleons,\u0026quot; Lafayette had stated. \u0026quot;Everything. The blueprints, the global licensing, the manufacturing monopoly.\u0026quot;","Thomas had paused, calculating the economic viability in his head with the cold, unshakeable logic of Vernon Dursley assessing a bulk order of drill bits.","\u003cem\u003eEnchanted dragon-silk. Every Auror in Europe needs it. Every hospital requires it. Every Quidditch team uses it. Manufacturing yield increases by three hundred percent.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;Uncle Draco said to invest in quality materials,\u0026quot; Thomas had muttered to himself.","He reached into his pocket, pulled out the obsidian Black Card, and laid it flat on the grease-stained counter.","\u0026quot;Done,\u0026quot; Thomas said.","Meanwhile, back in Wiltshire, the atmosphere in Draco Malfoy’s study was thick with the suffocating silence of impending doom.","Harry, Hermione, and Draco were sitting around the ebony desk like three soldiers waiting in a trench for an artillery barrage.","Hermione was clutching a glass of cold water with both hands, her eyes fixed on the silver Gringotts terminal. Harry had his head resting against the back of his armchair, staring blankly at the ceiling. Draco was quietly nursing a fresh tumbler of Firewhisky, having finally accepted that his bank accounts were being dismantled by adolescents.","\u0026quot;He won\u0027t spend much,\u0026quot; Harry whispered into the silence, his voice hollow. \u0026quot;Thomas is Dudley\u0027s boy. Dudley wouldn\u0027t let him buy anything frivolous. He probably bought a sandwich and a brass bolt.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He is fourteen, Harry,\u0026quot; Hermione murmured, trembling. \u0026quot;He doesn\u0027t know the value of money. If he buys something extravagant—\u0026quot;","Suddenly, the silver terminal did not ping.","It \u003cem\u003escreamed\u003c/em\u003e.","A high-pitched, metallic siren shrieked from the brass casing. Sparks of violet and orange fire sprayed outward from the gears, sizzling against the mahogany desktop. The gears inside the terminal spun so violently that the entire machine began to shudder and smoke.","And then, the golden scroll unspooled.","It didn\u0027t click. It shot out of the slot like an uncoiled python, cascading over the edge of the desk, pooling across the Persian rug in five feet of glittering, gilded parchment.","Harry bolted upright.","Hermione’s glass of water slipped from her numb fingers, shattering against the floorboards.","Draco slowly, deliberately set his tumbler down. He reached out with two fingers, caught the end of the golden scroll, and pulled it toward him.","He looked at the cardholder: \u003cem\u003eTHOMAS V. DURSLEY.\u003c/em\u003eHe looked at the merchant: \u003cem\u003eMANUFACTURE ROYALE DES TISSUS ENCHANTÉS, PARIS.\u003c/em\u003eHe looked at the total.","Draco Malfoy’s jaw dropped.","His eyes widened until the whites showed entirely around his irises. The color drained from his face with the speed of an emptying bathtub, leaving him as pale as a ghost.","\u0026quot;Sweet... Mother... of... Merlin,\u0026quot; Draco whispered, his voice cracking into a dry wheeze.","\u0026quot;What is it?!\u0026quot; Hermione screamed, lunging across the desk. \u0026quot;DRACO, WHAT IS THE NUMBER?!\u0026quot;","Draco looked up. His hands were visibly, violently shaking.","\u0026quot;Eight hundred...\u0026quot; Draco whispered, swallowed hard, and tried again. \u0026quot;Eight hundred and ninety-four thousand... Galleons.\u0026quot;","The study went dead.","Harry Potter’s cardiovascular system simply gave up.","His knees buckled. His eyes rolled into the back of his head. He did not yell; he did not gasp. Harry simply folded forward at the waist and collapsed sideways onto the leather sofa like an empty laundry sack, clutching his chest, staring at the floor with a vacant, catatonic expression of pure, unadulterated shock.","\u0026quot;Nine... hundred... thousand...\u0026quot; Harry whispered to the carpet. \u0026quot;Nine hundred thousand Galleons...\u0026quot;","Hermione, meanwhile, underwent a full, terrifying, biological meltdown.","\u0026quot;NINE HUNDRED THOUSAND GALLEONS?!\u0026quot; she shrieked, the volume so devastating that two painted portraits on the wall threw their hands over their ears and fled into adjacent frames.","She grabbed Draco by the lapels of his bespoke robes, shaking the multi-millionaire patriarch back and forth like a rag doll.","\u0026quot;WHAT DID HE BUY?! DID HE BUY AN ENTIRE FRENCH PROVINCE?! IS MY NEPHEW THE KING OF BURGUNDY NOW?! I AM THE DEPUTY HEAD OF MAGICAL LAW ENFORCEMENT! I CANNOT HAVE A FOURTEEN-YEAR-OLD RELATIVE SPENDING THE ENTIRE GROSS NATIONAL PRODUCT OF SCOTLAND ON A SATURDAY AFTERNOON!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione, let go of my collar,\u0026quot; Draco gasped, prizing her fingers off his silk. \u0026quot;Let me read the breakdown!\u0026quot;","Hermione released him, stumbling backward against the sideboard, hyperventilating so hard she had to clutch her ribcage to keep from fainting onto Harry.","Draco smoothed his collar, his hands still trembling as he held the long golden parchment under the lamplight.","He read the first item:\u003cem\u003eItem 1: Bespoke Navy Dress Robes \u0026amp; Silver Hardware — 400 Galleons.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;See?!\u0026quot; Harry groaned from the floor. \u0026quot;He bought the robes! What is the other eight hundred and ninety-three thousand?!\u0026quot;","Draco read the second item.","He stopped.","His eyes scanned the line once. Twice. Three times.","The look of shock on Draco Malfoy’s face began to morph.","The color rushed back into his cheeks. His eyebrows climbed toward his hairline. And then, slowly, majestically, a massive, predatory, awe-struck grin spread across Draco Malfoy’s aristocratic face.","It was the smile of a dragon that had just discovered a mountain of gold guarded by a sleeping sheep.","Draco began to laugh.","It started as a low, breathless chuckle in his throat, and escalated into a booming, joyful, hysterical roar that echoed off the mahogany bookshelves.","\u0026quot;He didn\u0027t,\u0026quot; Draco laughed, wiping a tear from his eye. \u0026quot;Oh, by the blood of Salazar, he didn\u0027t!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;WHAT DID HE DO?!\u0026quot; Hermione yelled, grabbing a heavy brass paperweight, looking ready to bludgeon him with it. \u0026quot;DRACO, TELL ME BEFORE I CURSE YOU INTO A POND!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Hermione,\u0026quot; Draco said, holding up the scroll, his grey eyes blazing with pure, reverent financial awe. \u0026quot;You bureaucratic idiot. Look at the merchant. Look at the patent registration.\u0026quot;","Hermione snatched the scroll, her hands shaking, and read the itemized description:","\u003cem\u003ePURCHASE: Exclusive Global Commercial Patent, Manufacturing Rights, and Prototype Industrial Tooling for the \u0027Lafayette Technomantic Dragon-Silk Loom \u0026amp; Weaving Process.\u0027\u003c/em\u003e","Hermione froze.","Her jaw dropped so fast her teeth clicked.","Her amber eyes bulged. The paperweight slipped from her hand, landing on the desk with a heavy \u003cem\u003ethud\u003c/em\u003e.","\u0026quot;The... the Lafayette patent?\u0026quot; Hermione whispered, her voice trembling in utter, disbelieving shock. \u0026quot;The dragon-silk process?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Yes!\u0026quot; Draco beamed, throwing his hands in the air. \u0026quot;The exact patent the British Ministry has been trying to negotiate for twelve bloody years! The one the French Ministry blocked three different trade delegations from acquiring! The process that produces self-repairing, curse-deflecting dragon-silk at one-tenth of the manual labor cost!\u0026quot;","Harry weakly lifted his head from the sofa, blinking through his crooked glasses. \u0026quot;Wait... so he didn\u0027t buy clothes?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He bought an industrial monopoly, Harry!\u0026quot; Draco barked, laughing with pure, bursting pride. \u0026quot;Every Auror cloak in Europe! Every high-altitude Quidditch uniform! Every medical shield in St. Mungo\u0027s! The global licensing rights now belong exclusively to Thomas Vernon Dursley!\u0026quot;","Draco pointed a finger at the scroll, his business mind calculating at lightning speed.","\u0026quot;That patent will generate four million Galleons in net revenue in the first year alone! By year two, it will control twelve million! The British Ministry’s trade tax windfall alone will fund your entire department\u0027s budget for a decade, Hermione! He just made back the purchase price five times over before he’s even finished his fourth year!\u0026quot;","Draco collapsed back into his leather armchair, shaking his head in absolute, stunned wonder.","\u0026quot;Vernon Dursley\u0027s grandson,\u0026quot; Draco murmured with profound, solemn reverence. \u0026quot;I sent him to Paris with a credit line to buy a suit for a school dance, and the boy staged a hostile corporate takeover of the French textile industry.\u0026quot;","Draco picked up his Firewhisky glass, raised it toward the ceiling, and shook his head.","\u0026quot;The boy is an absolute, cold-blooded, industrial genius. I am doubling his allowance tomorrow.\u0026quot;","On the sofa, Harry Potter slowly rolled onto his back, staring up at the chandelier, letting out a long, dazed, exhausted breath.","Beside him, Hermione Granger-Potter slowly sank onto the edge of the cushions. She looked at the receipt. She looked at Draco’s triumphant, laughing face.","She let out a tiny, breathless squeak.","\u0026quot;My nephew,\u0026quot; Hermione whispered faintly to the empty air, \u0026quot;owns the European textile market.\u0026quot;","And with that, the Deputy Head of Magical Law Enforcement gently closed her eyes, leaned her head against Harry’s shoulder, and decided that for the rest of Saturday, consciousness was entirely optional.\u003cem\u003e[END OF CHAPTER]\u003c/em\u003e"]},{"num":80,"origNum":50,"title":"The Confectionery Subscription and the Vivaldi Citrus Crisis","wordCount":1308,"paragraphs":["The seven teenagers reconvened at the corner of the Rue Saint-Antoine at precisely half-past six, looking like a victorious military unit returning from the conquest of Western Europe.","Cassie, Lily, and Pandora were floating on the radiant, intoxicated high that could only be achieved by spending one hundred and twelve thousand Galleons on custom gowns.","James and Valeria strode down the cobblestones side by side, carrying two slender, velvet-wrapped cases containing prototype \u003cem\u003eFlèche Boréale\u003c/em\u003e racing brooms like royal standards, looking smug, athletic, and completely unapologetic.","And Thomas Vernon Dursley walked steadily with Céleste Laurent linked tightly to his arm, holding a thick, wax-sealed leather portfolio containing the global manufacturing patent to the European dragon-silk industry under his elbow, looking as content as a man who had just bought a particularly nice lawnmower.","\u0026quot;Right,\u0026quot; Lily announced, clapping her leather-gloved hands together with brisk authority. \u0026quot;We have the gowns. We have the dueling leathers. Tommy owns the industrial soul of France. We have one final, critical diplomatic mission before the Portkey activates at eight.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The lemon drops,\u0026quot; James said, his hazel eyes wide with sudden dread. \u0026quot;If we show up in Dumbledore\u0027s office without those sweets, he’s going to deduct fifty thousand points and make us clean the owlery with our teeth.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Relax, Potter,\u0026quot; Céleste smiled, her violet eyes dancing with Parisian amusement. \u0026quot;Follow me. It is just around the corner.\u0026quot;","Tucked behind a wrought-iron archway dripping with enchanted, fragrant violet wisteria, sat \u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eLa Dragée d’Or\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.","The shop looked like a fairytale brought to life. The bay windows were framed in polished copper and curved glass, showcasing floating spun-sugar carousels, crystal bell-jars filled with shimmering Turkish delights, and jars of candied violets that gave off a faint, harmonious humming sound. The warm, buttery aroma of melted caramel, vanilla pods, and pure Sicilian citrus oil spilled into the cold street like an invitation.","A brass bell chimed with a musical \u003cem\u003eding-dong\u003c/em\u003e as they pushed through the door.","Behind the marble counter stood Madame Éléonore Bonheur—a plump, cheerful French witch with rosy cheeks, powdered-sugar dusting her aprons, and grey curls pinned up with two silver sugar-tongs.","\u0026quot;Ah! \u003cem\u003eBonjour, mes enfants!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur beamed, wiping her hands on her apron. Then her eyes locked onto Céleste. \u0026quot;Céleste, \u003cem\u003ema petite colombe\u003c/em\u003e! What a marvelous surprise! Your mother told me you were freezing in the Scottish mountains!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Only slightly, Tante Éléonore,\u0026quot; Céleste laughed, leaning over the counter to exchange warm, double-cheek kisses. \u0026quot;We have come on an urgent, high-level diplomatic courier mission. From Scotland.\u0026quot;","Madame Bonheur’s eyes narrowed into sharp, knowing slits. A wide, conspiratorial smile spread across her face.","\u0026quot;Do not tell me,\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur whispered dramatically, leaning over the glass cases. \u0026quot;The tall, ancient Englishman? The one with the magnificent silver beard who dresses like an enchanted tropical sunset?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Albus Dumbledore,\u0026quot; the entire group chimed in unison.","Madame Bonheur threw her hands in the air, laughing with pure, nostalgic delight. \u0026quot;Albus! That magnificent lunatic! He has been buying my citrus drops since 1945! The man once attempted to trade me an enchanted goblin thimble and a pair of wool socks because he had run out of French francs at the station! How many tins does he desire? Four? Six?\u0026quot;","Lily and Céleste were about to answer when Thomas Vernon Dursley stepped forward.","Thomas pulled his graphite pencil from behind his ear and flipped open his small, grid-lined notebook. He adjusted his spectacles with the back of his thumb, evaluating the display of hexagonal brass tins with the unshakeable, analytical gravity of an air traffic controller.","\u0026quot;Six tins is completely inadequate,\u0026quot; Thomas rumbled in his deep Surrey bass.","The entire shop went silent. Madame Bonheur blinked.","\u0026quot;Pardon, young man?\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur asked, looking up at the broad-shouldered boy in the navy pea coat.","\u0026quot;I have been tracking the Headmaster’s consumption patterns since September,\u0026quot; Thomas explained calmly, tapping his pencil against the notebook. \u0026quot;Each tin contains precisely forty-eight drops. Under normal operating conditions, Professor Dumbledore consumes an average of six point four drops per waking day. However, during faculty emergencies—such as Professor Snape discovering students in locker rooms or Aunt Hermione receiving Gringotts receipts—his burn rate increases by forty-two percent.\u0026quot;","James let out a strangled snort and immediately covered his face with his sleeve.","\u0026quot;Furthermore,\u0026quot; Thomas continued methodically, \u0026quot;the winter term includes the Triwizard First Task, the Yule Ball, and three faculty administrative reviews. A supply of six tins will be fully depleted in precisely twenty-three point four days, resulting in an unacceptable citrus deficit during mid-January.\u0026quot;","Cassie raised an eyebrow, a slow, predatory Malfoy smirk spreading across her face. \u0026quot;Thomas is correct. We do not do things by halves. Madame Bonheur, how many tins are in a wholesale shipping carton?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Ten tins per carton, \u003cem\u003ema chère\u003c/em\u003e,\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur replied, utterly fascinated.","\u0026quot;Excellent,\u0026quot; Cassie declared, stepping up to the marble counter and withdrawing the gleaming obsidian Black Card. \u0026quot;We will take four entire wholesale cartons today. For immediate transport.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Four cartons?!\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur gasped, her hands flying to her cheeks. \u0026quot;That is forty tins! That is nearly two thousand drops of pure Sicilian citrus!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And,\u0026quot; Cassie continued smoothly, tapping the card against the marble with a crisp, authoritative \u003cem\u003eclick\u003c/em\u003e, \u0026quot;we wish to establish a permanent, standing, bilateral monthly subscription. One wholesale carton of ten tins, pre-paid, enchanted with featherlight and preservation wards, to be dispatched via international postal owl to the Headmaster’s Tower at Hogwarts on the first of every month.\u0026quot;","Madame Bonheur stared at the obsidian Black Card.","Then she looked at the seven teenagers.","Her jaw slowly dropped. \u0026quot;A... a permanent, lifetime subscription to Albus Dumbledore’s lemon drop addiction? Guaranteed by Gringotts sovereign debt?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Precisely,\u0026quot; Cassie purred. \u0026quot;Can you accommodate the volume?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Can I accommodate?!\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur shrieked with pure, unadulterated French joy. She grabbed the card, pressed it against the enchanted register, and watched it glow with vibrant, authorized blue light.","\u003cem\u003eCHING-CLATTER.\u003c/em\u003e","\u0026quot;This will pay for my granddaughter\u0027s mastery at the Beauxbatons Conservatory!\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur laughed, practically dancing behind the counter. \u0026quot;Albus will have lemon drops until he is two hundred years old! He will breathe Vivaldi\u0027s \u003cem\u003eWinter\u003c/em\u003e every time he exhales!\u0026quot;","With four swift, rhythmic waves of her wand, four massive, brass-bound wooden crates—stamped with the golden seal of \u003cem\u003eLa Dragée d’Or\u003c/em\u003e—floated down from the top shelves.","Madame Bonheur tapped each crate with a cheerful flourish.","\u003cem\u003eWhirrr-pop.\u003c/em\u003e","The crates shrank to the size of shoe boxes, hovering obediently in mid-air about three inches off the floor, glowing with gentle lavender preservation magic.","\u0026quot;Packed with extra popping sparks,\u0026quot; Madame Bonheur winked, handing the Black Card back to Cassie with a theatrical curtsy. \u0026quot;Tell Albus that Éléonore sends her love, and that he should wear the magenta robes with the gold fringe when he eats them!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;We will, Madame,\u0026quot; Lily laughed, giving the cheerful woman a warm hug over the counter.","As they stepped back out into the cold, crisp Parisian twilight, the four enchanted crates hovered neatly behind James and Thomas like a row of well-behaved, wooden ducklings.","James looked at the floating boxes, then at his prototype racing broom, and finally at Valeria, who was currently biting back a rare, stunning smile of pure amusement.","\u0026quot;We did it,\u0026quot; James grinned, running a hand through his windblown hair. \u0026quot;We bought out Paris, Thomas owns the textile industry, and we have enough lemon drops to keep Dumbledore completely sedated until graduation.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;A productive Saturday,\u0026quot; Cassie concluded with immense aristocratic satisfaction, checking her platinum pocket watch. \u0026quot;Seven-forty-five. Time to return to the Place Cachée.\u0026quot;","Linking arms, their boots clicking rhythmically against the wet cobblestones beneath the glowing gas lamps of the boulevard, the seven teenagers marched toward the Portkey.","Behind them lay a devastated French economy, an ecstatic confectionery owner, and three completely traumatized parents in Wiltshire.","Ahead of them lay the Yule Ball.","And Hogwarts was never, ever going to be the same."]},{"num":81,"origNum":51,"title":"The Seven-Figure Audit and the Citrus Shield","wordCount":1934,"paragraphs":["At precisely seven minutes to eight, Professor Minerva McGonagall and Severus Snape were sitting in the Headmaster’s Tower, engaged in what had become their daily evening ritual: attempting to talk Albus Dumbledore out of an administrative catastrophe.","McGonagall was holding a stack of revised patrol rosters, her tartan sleeves pulled back with severe Scottish focus. Snape sat across from her, his arms crossed over his chest like an irritated gargoyle, nursing a cup of black tea that had gone cold twenty minutes ago.","Dumbledore, meanwhile, was sitting behind his mahogany desk in his neon flamingo smoking jacket, humming a cheerful waltz while delicately polishing his antique pocket watch with a silk handkerchief.","\u0026quot;Albus,\u0026quot; McGonagall said, tapping her parchment with a sharp fingernail, \u0026quot;we cannot allow the Durmstrang students to swim in the Black Lake after nine o\u0027clock. The Giant Squid is becoming agitated. It tried to throw a stone bench back at them yesterday.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;The squid was merely returning their shot-put, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore replied mild-manneredly. \u0026quot;A splendid display of inter-species camaraderie.\u0026quot;","Snape sneered into his collar. \u0026quot;The squid was trying to drown them. Which, frankly, would have saved us considerable paperwork.\u0026quot;","Before McGonagall could issue a formal reprimand for Snape\u0027s lack of pedagogical empathy, the air in the center of the office suddenly turned violent.","\u003cem\u003eCRACK-WHIRRRRR.\u003c/em\u003e","The temperature in the room dropped ten degrees in a split second. A blinding, golden vortex of spinning magical energy erupted directly above the Persian rug, whipping Dumbledore\u0027s parchment across the desk and sending Fawkes fluttering into the air with an alarmed squawk.","McGonagall gasped, dropping her clipboard.","Snape was on his feet in half a heartbeat, his wand drawn in a lethal dueling strike, black robes billowing.","\u0026quot;DEFENSIVE STANCE!\u0026quot; Snape hissed.","\u003cem\u003eSNAP.\u003c/em\u003e","The vortex collapsed with a sharp, pneumatic pop.","Standing in the dead center of the Headmaster’s Persian rug, looking impeccably styled, flushed with cold December air, and smelling of Parisian hot chocolate and expensive French perfume, were seven teenagers.","Surrounding their boots was an absolute mountain of luxury: two slender velvet cases containing broomsticks, six gold-embossed garment bags from the Rue Saint-Honoré, a thick leather portfolio tied with red wax, and four floating, brass-bound wooden cartons hovering obediently at knee height.","Minerva McGonagall froze. Her wand arm slowly lowered, her jaw unhinging until her spectacles slid down her nose.","Severus Snape stared at the seven of them. His eye began its violent, rhythmic twitch.","\u0026quot;What...\u0026quot; McGonagall whispered, her Scottish brogue trembling with rising hysteria. \u0026quot;What in the name of the Four Founders is the meaning of this?! Why are seven students materializing out of the atmospheric ether directly into the Headmaster’s private office?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Good evening, Professors,\u0026quot; Dumbledore beamed from behind his desk, not even flinching. \u0026quot;Right on time. Eight o\u0027clock to the second. Excellent temporal navigation, children.\u0026quot;","Snape took two heavy, menacing strides toward the group, his obsidian eyes sweeping over the velvet cases and gilded bags.","\u0026quot;Where have you been?\u0026quot; Snape snarled, his voice dropping into a dangerous, icy purr. \u0026quot;And what, precisely, is in those packages? If I find a single illegal firework or dark artifact in this office—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;No fireworks, Professor,\u0026quot; Cassiopeia Malfoy replied smoothly, stepping to the front of the group with the languid, unshakeable poise of an empress addressing her domestic staff. \u0026quot;We have merely returned from Paris. Father authorized an emergency shopping excursion for the Yule Ball.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Paris?!\u0026quot; McGonagall shrieked, clutching her chest. \u0026quot;You went to \u003cem\u003eParis\u003c/em\u003e on a Saturday afternoon?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;On a school-sanctioned diplomatic mission, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore provided pleasantly, waving a hand.","\u0026quot;And I suppose,\u0026quot; Snape sneered, his lip curling with venomous disdain, \u0026quot;you squandered a small fortune of the Malfoy vanity fund on ribbons and lace? What was the damage, Miss Malfoy? Twenty Galleons? Fifty?\u0026quot;","Cassie raised an eyebrow. She reached into her coat, pulled out the golden Gringotts slips, and evaluated them with cool, aristocratic indifference.","\u0026quot;For our three gowns—mine, Lily’s, and Pandora’s—the total was one hundred and twelve thousand, six hundred and fifty Galleons.\u0026quot;","The silence that fell over the office was instantaneous.","Snape choked on his own tongue. He made a sound like a punctured bicycle tire.","McGonagall’s face transitioned through five distinct shades of white, grey, and alarming purple. Her hand flew to her throat. \u0026quot;One... one hundred... and twelve \u003cem\u003ethousand\u003c/em\u003e?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;That was just the silk, Professor,\u0026quot; James Sirius Potter piped up cheerfully, leaning against the back of the sofa with an easy, helpful grin. \u0026quot;Valeria and I spent ninety-six thousand, four hundred Galleons at \u003cem\u003eL’Atelier Flèche \u0026amp; Lame\u003c/em\u003e. We picked up two \u003cem\u003eFlèche Boréale\u003c/em\u003e prototype racing brooms with Siberian thunder-ash, matched Swedish Short-Snout dueling armor, and an antique star-sapphire brooch.\u0026quot;","McGonagall grabbed the edge of Dumbledore\u0027s desk to keep her knees from buckling. Her eyes bugged out behind her spectacles so wide they looked like dinner plates.","\u0026quot;Ninety-six... \u003cem\u003ethousand\u003c/em\u003e... on broomsticks?!\u0026quot; McGonagall gasped, her voice reaching a shrill, suffocating squeak. \u0026quot;You bought \u003cem\u003eprototypes\u003c/em\u003e?!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;And,\u0026quot; Thomas Vernon Dursley rumbled helpfully from the back, adjusting his steel-rimmed spectacles and consulting his neat, grid-lined notebook, \u0026quot;I spent eight hundred and ninety-four thousand Galleons to acquire the exclusive global patent, manufacturing rights, and prototype industrial looms for the Lafayette Technomantic Dragon-Silk weaving process.\u0026quot;","Thomas looked up, his expression completely blank, offering a polite Surrey nod.","\u0026quot;Bringing our total Saturday expenditure to precisely one million, one hundred and three thousand, eight hundred and fifty Galleons. Excluding the confectionery subscription.\u0026quot;","\u003cem\u003eONE. MILLION. GALLEONS.\u003c/em\u003e","The words did not process through Minerva McGonagall’s brain. They detonated like a nuclear warhead inside her skull.","Her Scottish Presbyterian thriftiness, honed through seventy years of budgeting tea bags and reusing parchment, suffered a catastrophic, total biological meltdown.","\u0026quot;\u003cem\u003eONE MILLION GALLEONS?!\u003c/em\u003e\u0026quot; McGonagall went completely, terrifyingly, apocalyptically ballistic.","She slammed both hands onto Dumbledore’s desk so hard the silver instruments rattled and shrieked. She began pacing the Persian rug with the violent, manic energy of a wildcat trapped in a phone booth, her tartan robes whipping through the air like storm clouds.","\u0026quot;ONE MILLION! THAT IS MORE THAN THE ENTIRE OPERATING ENDOWMENT OF HOGWARTS SINCE THE NORMAN CONQUEST! YOU COULD PURCHASE THE ENTIRE HEBRIDEAN ISLAND CHAIN FOR THAT! YOU ARE FOURTEEN YEARS OLD! FOURTEEN! I AM PLACING YOU ALL IN DETENTION UNTIL YOU ARE FORTY-FIVE YEARS OLD!\u0026quot;","She whirled on James, pointing a shaking, furious finger. \u0026quot;YOUR FATHER WILL LOCK YOU IN A CELL! YOUR MOTHER WILL PERSONALLY DISMANTLE YOU SEAM BY SEAM!\u0026quot;","Beside her, Severus Snape looked as though his optic nerves were about to rupture. A vein on his temple was throbbing so violently it could be seen through his hair.","\u0026quot;Dragon-silk monopolies?!\u0026quot; Snape roared, his voice cracking into a shrill, hysterical shriek. \u0026quot;Aeronautical prototypes?! They are not students, Albus! They are a rogue, international financial syndicate! They are an armed cartel disguised as fourth-years! I am calling the Wizengamot! I am calling the International Confederation! I AM BURNING THOSE BROOMSTICKS IN THE COURTYARD THIS VERY INSTANT!\u0026quot;","The office was an inferno of screaming professors, vibrating furniture, and raw, ballistic panic.","Through it all, Albus Dumbledore did not shout.","He slowly, majestically stood up from behind his mahogany desk.","His sequined pineapple robes caught the torchlight in a dazzling, blinding spray of yellow and gold. He raised a single, calm hand, his brilliant blue eyes locking onto Lily and Céleste with the laser-focused, razor-sharp intensity of a hawk sighting prey.","He completely, utterly ignored the one million Galleons.","He ignored the Scottish meltdown.","He ignored the threats of international tribunals.","\u0026quot;Minerva. Severus. Silence,\u0026quot; Dumbledore commanded softly.","The room went instantly dead. McGonagall froze mid-stride, hyperventilating. Snape stood with his wand raised, trembling with rage.","Dumbledore leaned forward across his desk, his voice dropping into a tense, desperate, deeply serious whisper.","\u0026quot;Never mind the dragon-silk, Minerva,\u0026quot; Dumbledore whispered intently. He looked at Lily. \u0026quot;The drops. Did you secure the lemon drops?\u0026quot;","The Pack collectively smiled.","Lily Luna stepped forward, gesturing with a flourish toward the four brass-bound wooden cartons hovering obediently above the rug.","Céleste Laurent inclined her head with pure Parisian elegance. \u0026quot;Four wholesale cartons of ten tins each, Headmaster. Sourced directly from Madame Bonheur. Crystallized with pure Sicilian citrus fire and packed with extra popping sparks.\u0026quot;","Lily reached into her coat and pulled out a gold-stamped parchment slip, laying it on the desk.","\u0026quot;And,\u0026quot; Lily grinned, her emerald eyes dancing with pure Evans mischief, \u0026quot;we established a standing, perpetual monthly subscription. One wholesale carton of ten tins delivered via international postal owl to your tower on the first of every month for the rest of your natural life. Pre-paid on the Malfoy account.\u0026quot;","Albus Dumbledore stared at the four hovering crates.","Then he stared at the golden subscription deed.","A look of transcendent, heavenly, almost spiritual ecstasy washed over the Headmaster’s face. His eyes filled with tears of pure, unadulterated bliss.","\u0026quot;Four... four cartons?\u0026quot; Dumbledore breathed, his voice trembling with reverent awe. \u0026quot;And a lifetime subscription? To the Vivaldi drops?\u0026quot;","He lunged forward with the agility of a man half his age, popped the brass latch on the nearest carton, withdrew a hexagonal tin, and flipped the lid.","He plucked a glowing, crystallized yellow drop, popped it into his mouth, and closed his eyes.","A split second later, a soft, cheerful, perfectly harmonized violin trill from Vivaldi’s \u003cem\u003eSpring\u003c/em\u003e played faintly from Dumbledore’s left ear, accompanied by a tiny, sparkling puff of harmless yellow smoke.","\u0026quot;Oh, magnificent,\u0026quot; Dumbledore sighed, a blissful, dreamy smile settling onto his face. \u0026quot;Absolute, unmitigated genius. A triumph of international diplomacy.\u0026quot;","Behind him, McGonagall’s mouth worked without sound. Her face turned an alarming shade of eggplant purple.","Snape looked as though he was on the verge of suffering a stroke so severe it would echo backwards through time. His wand hand shook with homicidal intent.","Dumbledore, opening one twinkling blue eye, evaluated the thermonuclear pressure building inside his two senior colleagues.","He realized they had precisely twelve seconds before McGonagall transformed into a roaring Scottish lion and Snape hexed the entire room into matchsticks.","Dumbledore clapped his hands together with cheerful, decisive urgency.","\u0026quot;Splendid work, children!\u0026quot; Dumbledore announced briskly, waving his hands in a frantic shooing motion toward the door. \u0026quot;Ten points to Gryffindor! Ten points to Slytherin! Ten points to Ravenclaw! Ten points to Hufflepuff! And twenty points each to Durmstrang and Beauxbatons for exemplary courier service!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;DUMBLEDORE!\u0026quot; McGonagall and Snape screamed in unified outrage.","\u0026quot;Off to bed with you!\u0026quot; Dumbledore shouted cheerfully over their roar, practically herding the teenagers toward the spiral staircase with sweeps of his flamingo sleeves. \u0026quot;Take your brooms! Take your dragon-silk! Run along before our esteemed Deputy Headmistress bursts a critical blood vessel! Chop, chop! Out, out, out!\u0026quot;","The seven teenagers didn\u0027t need to be told twice.","Grabbing their floating broom cases, garment bags, and industrial blueprints, they bolted through the door, their boots pounding down the moving spiral staircase.","\u003cem\u003eSLAM.\u003c/em\u003e","The heavy oak door of the Headmaster’s Tower shut firmly behind them.","Standing on the third-floor landing, surrounded by their bespoke Parisian treasures, the seven of them stopped.","They looked at each other.","Through the heavy oak door above, the muffled, hysterical, glass-shattering screams of Minerva McGonagall and Severus Snape could be heard echoing off the stone walls, accompanied by the cheerful, faint strains of Vivaldi\u0027s violin drifting through the keyhole.","James let out a breathless snort.","Lily clapped a hand over her mouth.","Valeria burst into a rare, ringing laugh, and within two seconds, all seven of them were leaning against the stone walls, weeping with hysterical, unstoppable laughter.","The heist was complete. The Headmaster was bribed.","And the Yule Ball was going to be the greatest night in Hogwarts history."]},{"num":82,"origNum":52,"title":"Pest Control and the Malfoy Audit","wordCount":2058,"paragraphs":["With the Yule Ball officially three weeks away, the student body of Hogwarts had entered a state of acute, hormonal madness that Severus Snape referred to in the staff room as \u0026quot;The Annual Collective Psychosis.\u0026quot;","In every corridor, behind every suit of armor, and near every staircase, adolescent boys were desperately attempting to summon the courage to secure a date before all the acceptable options were claimed.","Naturally, the apex of the castle’s romantic food chain consisted of exactly three girls: \u003cstrong\u003eLily Luna Potter, Pandora Weasley, and Cassiopeia Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e.","They had spent the better part of the last month holding court in the Library’s sunlit east annex—an unassailable sanctuary where the three of them studied, planned the logistical downfall of their peers, and systematically destroyed the self-esteem of any male foolish enough to cross their perimeter.","Each girl had her own distinct, lethal method of rejection.","Lily Luna Potter rejected suitors with blinding, cheerful Evans warmth that crushed souls like an affectionate steamroller. When a hopeful fifth-year Gryffindor Chaser had approached her during breakfast with a bouquet of enchanted singing lilies, Lily had simply beamed down at him from her magnificent six-foot height, patted him firmly on the top of his head like an overgrown golden retriever, and said, \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Oh, bless your sweet heart, Rory! But my posture is built for someone who doesn\u0027t vibrate when I hand them a muffin. Go ask Sarah—she loves boys with manageable heights!\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e Rory had spent the rest of the day sitting by the lake, staring into the middle distance.","Pandora Weasley, meanwhile, used psychological warfare disguised as mystical benevolence. When an earnest Hufflepuff sixth-year had asked her by the greenhouses, Pan had tilted her head, looked deeply into his left nostril, and whispered dreamily, \u003cem\u003e\u0026quot;Oh, I’d adore to, Nigel, but the Plimpies in the lake told me that if we dance on a Tuesday, your left ear will turn permanently inside out and smell of pickled turnip. It’s an astrological certainty. I couldn\u0027t bear the guilt of your auditory deformity.\u0026quot;\u003c/em\u003e Nigel had panicked, sprinted straight to the Hospital Wing, and begged Madam Pomfrey for a preventative ear wash.","However, while Lily crushed hearts with sunshine and Pan dismantled them with madness, \u003cstrong\u003eCassiopeia Malfoy\u003c/strong\u003e was an entirely different species of predator.","Cassie did not soften the blow. She did not consult the spirits.","Cassie conducted an \u003cstrong\u003eaudit\u003c/strong\u003e.","On a frigid Tuesday afternoon, the annex was quiet except for the crackle of the hearth and the scratching of quills. Cassie was sitting in a high-backed velvet armchair, legs crossed with imperial poise, sipping a cup of Earl Grey tea from an antique silver cup.","Beside her, Lily was sprawled across the sofa reviewing Arithmancy charts, and Pan was floating three inches above a pile of floor cushions, humming to an enchanted butterfly.","The heavy oak doors of the annex creaked open.","Suitor Number One had arrived.","It was Adrian Pucey Jr.—a fifth-year Slytherin whose family boasted pure-blood ancestry dating back to the Norman Conquest, currently wearing his crispest school robes, his hair slicked back with enough dragon-dung pomade to withstand a hurricane. He was holding a polished ebony box tied with a silver ribbon.","Adrian took a deep breath, walked with rehearsed, aristocratic swagger across the Persian rug, and stopped three feet from Cassie’s armchair.","\u0026quot;Cassiopeia,\u0026quot; Adrian drawled, attempting to summon the deep, gravelly baritone of a seasoned diplomat. He extended the ebony box. \u0026quot;The Yule Ball approaches. As the two premier families of the serpent house, it is only proper that we represent Slytherin together. Inside this box is a necklace of crushed Caspian sea-pearls. I expect you will wear them with your gown.\u0026quot;","Lily immediately buried her face in her Arithmancy textbook to stifle a hysterical snort.","Cassie did not look at the box.","She did not even set her teacup down.","Slowly, deliberately, her cool, silver eyes rose from the rim of her porcelain cup, traveling up the line of Adrian’s polished dragonhide boots, over his pressed robes, and settling squarely onto his face.","The evaluation lasted four agonizing seconds. It was the gaze of a master tax collector inspecting a fraudulent ledger.","\u0026quot;Adrian,\u0026quot; Cassie murmured. Her voice was silky, quiet, and possessed the cutting clarity of chilled glass. \u0026quot;Your family’s ancestral vaults in Nottingham have been mortgaged to Gringotts since the second goblin rebellion of 1894. Your father’s recent investments in Romanian dragon-meat futures have collapsed by twenty-four percent, and your left eyebrow twitches whenever you attempt to project confidence.\u0026quot;","Adrian’s face instantly froze. The ebony box wavered in his hand.","\u0026quot;Furthermore,\u0026quot; Cassie continued smoothly, taking an unhurried sip of tea, \u0026quot;my gown for the evening is woven from midnight-emerald starlight velvet and powdered celestial meteors. If you were to stand beside me under the chandeliers in that dreadful, second-hand off-the-rack wool, the contrast would cause permanent optical trauma to the visiting dignitaries.\u0026quot;","She gave him a tiny, razor-sharp smirk that felt like a blade sliding between his ribs.","\u0026quot;The answer is an emphatic, non-negotiable no. Take your sea-pearls and give them to Parkinson. Her aesthetic standards are significantly more forgiving than mine. Dismissed.\u0026quot;","Adrian Pucey Jr. didn\u0027t speak. He couldn\u0027t. His aristocratic posture completely caved in. He clutched the ebony box to his chest, executed an awkward, stumbling half-bow, and practically bolted from the library as if pursued by a pack of rabid Dementors.","\u0026quot;Pest control,\u0026quot; Cassie noted calmly, adjusting the cuff of her emerald silk blouse. \u0026quot;Efficient and necessary.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;You didn\u0027t just reject him, Cassie,\u0026quot; Lily wheezed from behind her book, tears of laughter streaming down her cheeks. \u0026quot;You audited his family’s liquid assets and liquidated his soul in forty seconds!\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;He wasted my airspace, darling,\u0026quot; Cassie replied. \u0026quot;He deserved the audit.\u0026quot;","Before Lily could finish laughing, the annex doors swung open again.","Suitor Number Two marched in.","This time, it was a seventh-year Ravenclaw Prefect named Sterling—tall, handsome, broad-shouldered, and radiating the insufferable, pompous arrogance of a boy who had received top marks on his Charms O.W.L.s. He strode over, resting one hand casually on the back of Lily’s sofa, giving Cassie a confident, condescending smirk.","\u0026quot;Malfoy,\u0026quot; Sterling said smoothly. \u0026quot;I know you’ve been dealing with the usual parade of boys who can\u0027t handle a real woman. But I thought it was time someone of actual status stepped up. I’m Head Boy material, top of my class in Advanced Defense, and I happen to know the French delegation is looking to meet people with genuine academic influence. Let’s do the ball together. You won\u0027t find a better match in this castle.\u0026quot;","Lily stared at Sterling in pure, jaw-dropped disbelief at the sheer audacity.","Cassie slowly set her teacup into its silver saucer with a tiny, musical \u003cem\u003eclink\u003c/em\u003e.","She leaned her chin on her hand, tilting her head, looking at Sterling as if he were a particularly strange mold sample growing on stale bread.","\u0026quot;Sterling,\u0026quot; Cassie purred, her voice dripping with venomous sweetness. \u0026quot;You have a stain of pumpkin paste on your left collar that has existed since Thursday week. Your wand movement in Defense resembles a drunken troll swatting at midges with a rolling pin. And your primary qualification for \u0027Head Boy material\u0027 appears to be that you have memorized curfew regulations that nobody bothers to follow.\u0026quot;","Sterling’s smirk flickered. \u0026quot;Now, see here, Malfoy—\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;I do not date boys whose crowning achievement in life is waking up on time, Sterling,\u0026quot; Cassie interrupted, her eyes turning to chips of arctic ice. \u0026quot;And as for \u0027academic influence\u0027... my second-cousin Thomas purchased the global commercial monopoly on the European dragon-silk industry before breakfast on Saturday. You, on the other hand, had to ask Professor Flitwick for an extension on your Cheering Charm essay.\u0026quot;","She pointed a single, perfectly manicured finger toward the heavy double doors.","\u0026quot;Remove yourself from my presence before I have my father buy your father’s broom-repair shop and turn it into a facility for training acromantulas.\u0026quot;","Sterling’s face flushed a violent, incandescent shade of beet purple. His jaw worked without sound. He looked at Lily, who offered him a cheerful little wave of goodbye, and then fled through the doors so fast his prefect badge rattled against his chest.","\u0026quot;Two down,\u0026quot; Pan whispered serenely, floating another inch into the air as she watched the door shut. \u0026quot;His aura turned the color of bruised cabbage. It was very educational.\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Honestly, Cassie,\u0026quot; Lily grinned, shaking her head. \u0026quot;Is there anyone in this castle who can survive your scrutiny?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;Standards, Lily,\u0026quot; Cassie sighed, picking up her tea once more. \u0026quot;One must maintain standards. Otherwise, we end up dancing with boys who think a bouquet of dead weeds constitutes a courtship.\u0026quot;","The annex doors opened for the third time that afternoon.","The temperature in the library seemed to drop by ten degrees.","Walking through the doorway with the heavy, arrogant strut of a gladiator was a towering, sixth-year Durmstrang student named Goran.","He was broad as a wardrobe, with close-cropped dark hair, wearing his heavy crimson tunic lined with wolf fur, his jaw squared in absolute, aggressive northern certainty. He had spent three months watching the British girls from afar and had clearly decided that the diplomatic approach was beneath him.","Goran marched straight up to Cassie’s armchair, crossing his massive, fur-clad arms over his chest, looking down at her with a heavy, predatory scowl.","\u0026quot;Malfoy,\u0026quot; Goran rumbled in a thick, guttural Bulgarian accent that vibrated the glassware on the side table. \u0026quot;In the north, we do not waste words like these English weaklings. You are fierce. You have fire. You will accompany me to the Yule Ball. I will permit you to dance on my arm.\u0026quot;","Lily sat bolt upright, her emerald eyes flashing with dangerous Evans heat, ready to draw her wand.","Cassie didn\u0027t even flinch.","She didn\u0027t raise her voice. She didn\u0027t draw her wand.","She simply leaned back into the velvet cushions of her armchair, her silver eyes locking onto Goran’s with the terrifying, absolute stillness of an uncoiled viper.","\u0026quot;How delightfully quaint,\u0026quot; Cassie drawled, her voice a low, silken whisper that made the hairs on the back of Goran’s thick neck stand straight up. \u0026quot;A northern barbarian with an apparent death wish.\u0026quot;","Goran blinked, startled by the utter lack of fear. \u0026quot;What did you say?\u0026quot;","\u0026quot;My father holds seventy-two bilateral trade agreements with your Ministry of Magic, Goran,\u0026quot; Cassie purred, each word enunciated with surgical precision. \u0026quot;My brother-in-arms, James Potter, currently flies circles around your national Seeker while holding a waffle in his teeth. And if you step three inches closer to my personal space with those muddy, unpolished combat boots, my cousin Lily will physically heave you out of that window into the Black Lake...\u0026quot;","She paused, offering him a slow, lethal, breathtaking smile that froze the blood in his veins.","\u0026quot;...and I will personally send an invoice to your parents in Sofia for the professional cleaning of my Persian rug. Turn around, Goran. March back down to your damp ship. And thank Salazar that I am feeling merciful this afternoon.\u0026quot;","Goran stared down at her.","He was six feet two inches of solid northern muscle. He had wrestled mountain goats in the Balkans. He had survived the dark dueling pits of Durmstrang.","And looking down at this fourteen-year-old girl in emerald silk, Goran felt a cold, primal terror that he had never experienced in his life.","He swallowed hard. His Adam\u0027s apple bobbed.","Without a single word, the giant Durmstrang warrior executed an immediate, robotic about-face and marched stiffly out of the library, the doors swinging shut behind him with a terrified, breathless hush.","For five seconds, the annex was silent.","Then, Lily Luna Potter simply collapsed face-first into the sofa cushions, shrieking with unstoppable, hysterical laughter.","\u0026quot;THREE!\u0026quot; Lily howled into the fabric, pounding her fist against the velvet. \u0026quot;THREE IN A ROW! You made a Durmstrang combatant retreat across the North Sea without even drawing your wand!\u0026quot;","Pan giggled softly from her cushions, her silvery eyes sparkling. \u0026quot;His aura didn\u0027t even turn into cabbage. It just... dissolved into snow. Pure, frozen defeat.\u0026quot;","Cassie took a slow, delicate sip of her Earl Grey tea, perfectly unbothered, a brilliant, satisfied smirk gracing her lips.","\u0026quot;As I said, darlings,\u0026quot; Cassiopeia Malfoy purred, looking toward the heavy library doors. \u0026quot;Standard pest control. The Yule Ball belongs to us. And heaven help the ballroom when we arrive.\u0026quot;"]}]}]};
